a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "He seized me by the coat-sleeve in his eagerness, and drew me over to the table at which he had been working.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "\\"Let us have some fresh blood,\\" he said, digging a long bodkin into his finger, and drawing off the resulting drop of blood in a chemical pipette.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "\\"Now, I add this small quantity of blood to a litre of water.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
