a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "His chin, too, had the prominence and squareness which mark the man of determination.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "—Nil.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "4.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "—Feeble.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "His hands were invariably blotted with ink and stained with chemicals, yet he was possessed of extraordinary delicacy of touch, as I frequently had occasion to observe when I watched him manipulating his fragile philosophical instruments.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "The reader may set me down as a hopeless busybody, when I confess how much this man stimulated my curiosity, and how often I endeavoured to break through the reticence which he showed on all that concerned himself.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "Before pronouncing judgment, however, be it remembered, how objectless was my life, and how little there was to engage my attention.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "My health forbade me from venturing out unless the weather was exceptionally genial, and I had no friends who would call upon me and break the monotony of my daily existence.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "Under these circumstances, I eagerly hailed the little mystery which hung around my companion, and spent much of my time in endeavouring to unravel it.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "He was not studying medicine.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "He had himself, in reply to a question, confirmed Stamford's opinion upon that point.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "Neither did he appear to have pursued any course of reading which might fit him for a degree in science or any other recognized portal which would give him an entrance into the learned world.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "Yet his zeal for certain studies was remarkable, and within eccentric limits his knowledge was so extraordinarily ample and minute that his observations have fairly astounded me.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "Surely no man would work so hard or attain such precise information unless he had some definite end in view.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "Desultory readers are seldom remarkable for the exactness of their learning.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "No man burdens his mind with small matters unless he has some very good reason for doing so.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "His ignorance was as remarkable as his knowledge.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "Of contemporary literature, philosophy and politics he appeared to know next to nothing.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "Upon my quoting Thomas Carlyle, he inquired in the naivest way who he might be and what he had done.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "My surprise reached a climax, however, when I found incidentally that he was ignorant of the Copernican Theory and of the composition of the Solar System.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "That any civilized human being in this nineteenth century should not be aware that the earth travelled round the sun appeared to be to me such an extraordinary fact that I could hardly realize it.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "\\"You appear to be astonished,\\" he said, smiling at my expression of surprise.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "\\"Now that I do know it I shall do my best to forget it.\\"", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "\\"To forget it!\\"", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "\\"You see,\\" he explained, \\"I consider that a man's brain originally is like a little empty attic, and you have to stock it with such furniture as you choose.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "A fool takes in all the lumber of every sort that he comes across, so that the knowledge which might be useful to him gets crowded out, or at best is jumbled up with a lot of other things so that he has a difficulty in laying his hands upon it.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "Now the skilful workman is very careful indeed as to what he takes into his brain-attic.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "5.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "After walks has shown me splashes upon his trousers, and told me by their colour and consistence in what part of London he had received them.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "7.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "—Profound.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "8.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "—Accurate, but unsystematic.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "9.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "—Immense.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "He appears to know every detail of every horror perpetrated in the century.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "10.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "Plays the violin well.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "11.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "Is an expert singlestick player, boxer, and swordsman.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "12.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "Has a good practical knowledge of British law.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "11. Is an expert singlestick player, boxer, and swordsman. 12. Has a good practical knowledge of British law.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "When I had got so far in my list I threw it into the fire in despair.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "\\"If I can only find what the fellow is driving at by reconciling all these accomplishments, and discovering a calling which needs them all,\\" I said to myself, \\"I may as well give up the attempt at once.\\"", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "I see that I have alluded above to his powers upon the violin.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "These were very remarkable, but as eccentric as all his other accomplishments.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "That he could play pieces, and difficult pieces, I knew well, because at my request he has played me some of Mendelssohn's Lieder, and other favourites.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "When left to himself, however, he would seldom produce any music or attempt any recognized air.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "Leaning back in his arm-chair of an evening, he would close his eyes and scrape carelessly at the fiddle which was thrown across his knee.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "Sometimes the chords were sonorous and melancholy.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "Occasionally they were fantastic and cheerful.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "Clearly they reflected the thoughts which possessed him, but whether the music aided those thoughts, or whether the playing was simply the result of a whim or fancy was more than I could determine.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "I might have rebelled against these exasperating solos had it not been that he usually terminated them by playing in quick succession a whole series of my favourite airs as a slight compensation for the trial upon my patience.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "During the first week or so we had no callers, and I had begun to think that my companion was as friendless a man as I was myself.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "Presently, however, I found that he had many acquaintances, and those in the most different classes of society.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "There was one little sallow rat-faced, dark-eyed fellow who was introduced to me as Mr. Lestrade, and who came three or four times in a single week.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "One morning a young girl called, fashionably dressed, and stayed for half an hour or more.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "The same afternoon brought a grey-headed, seedy visitor, looking like a Jew pedlar, who appeared to me to be much excited, and who was closely followed by a slip-shod elderly woman.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "On another occasion an old white-haired gentleman had an interview with my companion; and on another a railway porter in his velveteen uniform.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "When any of these nondescript individuals put in an appearance, Sherlock Holmes used to beg for the use of the sitting-room, and I would retire to my bed-room.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "He always apologized to me for putting me to this inconvenience.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "\\"I have to use this room as a place of business,\\" he said, \\"and these people are my clients.\\"", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "Again I had an opportunity of asking him a point blank question, and again my delicacy prevented me from forcing another man to confide in me.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "I imagined at the time that he had some strong reason for not alluding to it, but he soon dispelled the idea by coming round to the subject of his own accord.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "It was upon the 4th of March, as I have good reason to remember, that I rose somewhat earlier than usual, and found that Sherlock Holmes had not yet finished his breakfast.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "The landlady had become so accustomed to my late habits that my place had not been laid nor my coffee prepared.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "With the unreasonable petulance of mankind I rang the bell and gave a curt intimation that I was ready.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "Then I picked up a magazine from the table and attempted to while away the time with it, while my companion munched silently at his toast.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "One of the articles had a pencil mark at the heading, and I naturally began to run my eye through it.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "Its somewhat ambitious title was \\"The Book of Life,\\" and it attempted to show how much an observant man might learn by an accurate and systematic examination of all that came in his way.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "It struck me as being a remarkable mixture of shrewdness and of absurdity.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "The reasoning was close and intense, but the deductions appeared to me to be far-fetched and exaggerated.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "The writer claimed by a momentary expression, a twitch of a muscle or a glance of an eye, to fathom a man's inmost thoughts.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "Deceit, according to him, was an impossibility in the case of one trained to observation and analysis.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "His conclusions were as infallible as so many propositions of Euclid.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "So startling would his results appear to the uninitiated that until they learned the processes by which he had arrived at them they might well consider him as a necromancer.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "\\"From a drop of water,\\" said the writer, \\"a logician could infer the possibility of an Atlantic or a Niagara without having seen or heard of one or the other.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "So all life is a great chain, the nature of which is known whenever we are shown a single link of it.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "Like all other arts, the Science of Deduction and Analysis is one which can only be acquired by long and patient study nor, is life long enough to allow any mortal to attain the highest possible perfection in it.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "Before turning to those moral and mental aspects of the matter which present the greatest difficulties, let the enquirer begin by mastering more elementary problems.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "Let him, on meeting a fellow-mortal, learn at a glance to distinguish the history of the man, and the trade or profession to which he belongs.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "Puerile as such an exercise may seem, it sharpens the faculties of observation, and teaches one where to look and what to look for.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "By a man's finger nails, by his coat-sleeve, by his boot, by his trouser knees, by the callosities of his forefinger and thumb, by his expression, by his shirt cuffs—by each of these things a man's calling is plainly revealed.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "That all united should fail to enlighten the competent enquirer in any case is almost inconceivable.\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "\\"What ineffable twaddle!\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "I cried, slapping the magazine down on the table, \\"I never read such rubbish in my life.\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "\\"What is it?\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "asked Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "\\"Why, this article,\\" I said, pointing at it with my egg spoon as I sat down to my breakfast.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "\\"I see that you have read it since you have marked it.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "I don't deny that it is smartly written.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "It irritates me though.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "It is evidently the theory of some arm-chair lounger who evolves all these neat little paradoxes in the seclusion of his own study.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "It is not practical.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "I should like to see him clapped down in a third class carriage on the Underground, and asked to give the trades of all his fellow-travellers.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_55	section	\N	Section 55	54	{"wordCount": 603}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "The theories which I have expressed there, and which appear to you to be so chimerical are really extremely practical—so practical that I depend upon them for my bread and cheese.\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "\\"And how?\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "I asked involuntarily.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "\\"Well, I have a trade of my own.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "I suppose I am the only one in the world.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "I'm a consulting detective, if you can understand what that is.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "Here in London we have lots of Government detectives and lots of private ones.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "When these fellows are at fault they come to me, and I manage to put them on the right scent.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "They lay all the evidence before me, and I am generally able, by the help of my knowledge of the history of crime, to set them straight.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "There is a strong family resemblance about misdeeds, and if you have all the details of a thousand at your finger ends, it is odd if you can't unravel the thousand and first.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "Lestrade is a well-known detective.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "He got himself into a fog recently over a forgery case, and that was what brought him here.\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "\\"And these other people?\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "\\"They are mostly sent on by private inquiry agencies.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "They are all people who are in trouble about something, and want a little enlightening.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "I listen to their story, they listen to my comments, and then I pocket my fee.\\"", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "\\"But do you mean to say,\\" I said, \\"that without leaving your room you can unravel some knot which other men can make nothing of, although they have seen every detail for themselves?\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "\\"Quite so.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "I have a kind of intuition that way.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "Now and again a case turns up which is a little more complex.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "Then I have to bustle about and see things with my own eyes.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "You see I have a lot of special knowledge which I apply to the problem, and which facilitates matters wonderfully.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "Those rules of deduction laid down in that article which aroused your scorn, are invaluable to me in practical work.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "Observation with me is second nature.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "You appeared to be surprised when I told you, on our first meeting, that you had come from Afghanistan.\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "\\"You were told, no doubt.\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "\\"Nothing of the sort.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "I _knew_ you came from Afghanistan.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "From long habit the train of thoughts ran so swiftly through my mind, that I arrived at the conclusion without being conscious of intermediate steps.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "There were such steps, however.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "The train of reasoning ran, 'Here is a gentleman of a medical type, but with the air of a military man.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "Clearly an army doctor, then.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "He has just come from the tropics, for his face is dark, and that is not the natural tint of his skin, for his wrists are fair.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "He has undergone hardship and sickness, as his haggard face says clearly.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "His left arm has been injured.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "He holds it in a stiff and unnatural manner.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "Where in the tropics could an English army doctor have seen much hardship and got his arm wounded?", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "' The whole train of thought did not occupy a second.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "That trick of his of breaking in on his friends' thoughts with an apropos remark after a quarter of an hour's silence is really very showy and superficial.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "He had some analytical genius, no doubt; but he was by no means such a phenomenon as Poe appeared to imagine.\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "\\"Have you read Gaboriau's works?\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "\\"Does Lecoq come up to your idea of a detective?\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes sniffed sardonically.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "\\"Lecoq was a miserable bungler,\\" he said, in an angry voice; \\"he had only one thing to recommend him, and that was his energy.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "That book made me positively ill.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "The question was how to identify an unknown prisoner.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "I could have done it in twenty-four hours.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "Lecoq took six months or so.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "It might be made a text-book for detectives to teach them what to avoid.\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "I felt rather indignant at having two characters whom I had admired treated in this cavalier style.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "I walked over to the window, and stood looking out into the busy street.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "\\"This fellow may be very clever,\\" I said to myself, \\"but he is certainly very conceited.\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "\\"There are no crimes and no criminals in these days,\\" he said, querulously.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "\\"What is the use of having brains in our profession.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "I know well that I have it in me to make my name famous.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "No man lives or has ever lived who has brought the same amount of study and of natural talent to the detection of crime which I have done.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "And what is the result?", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "There is no crime to detect, or, at most, some bungling villainy with a motive so transparent that even a Scotland Yard official can see through it.\\"", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "I was still annoyed at his bumptious style of conversation.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "I thought it best to change the topic.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "\\"I wonder what that fellow is looking for?\\"", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "I asked, pointing to a stalwart, plainly-dressed individual who was walking slowly down the other side of the street, looking anxiously at the numbers.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "He had a large blue envelope in his hand, and was evidently the bearer of a message.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "\\"You mean the retired sergeant of Marines,\\" said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "\\"Brag and bounce!\\"", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "thought I to myself.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "\\"He knows that I cannot verify his guess.\\"", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "The thought had hardly passed through my mind when the man whom we were watching caught sight of the number on our door, and ran rapidly across the roadway.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "We heard a loud knock, a deep voice below, and heavy steps ascending the stair.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "\\"For Mr. Sherlock Holmes,\\" he said, stepping into the room and handing my friend the letter.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "Here was an opportunity of taking the conceit out of him.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "He little thought of this when he made that random shot.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "\\"May I ask, my lad,\\" I said, in the blandest voice, \\"what your trade may be?\\"", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "\\"Commissionaire, sir,\\" he said, gruffly.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_468	lexical	\N	\N	467	{"text": "\\"Uniform away for repairs.\\"", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_469	lexical	\N	\N	468	{"text": "\\"And you were?\\"", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_477	lexical	\N	\N	476	{"text": "I confess that I was considerably startled by this fresh proof of the practical nature of my companion's theories.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_478	lexical	\N	\N	477	{"text": "My respect for his powers of analysis increased wondrously.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_479	lexical	\N	\N	478	{"text": "There still remained some lurking suspicion in my mind, however, that the whole thing was a pre-arranged episode, intended to dazzle me, though what earthly object he could have in taking me in was past my comprehension.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_480	lexical	\N	\N	479	{"text": "When I looked at him he had finished reading the note, and his eyes had assumed the vacant, lack-lustre expression which showed mental abstraction.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_481	lexical	\N	\N	480	{"text": "\\"How in the world did you deduce that?\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_482	lexical	\N	\N	481	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_483	lexical	\N	\N	482	{"text": "\\"Deduce what?\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_484	lexical	\N	\N	483	{"text": "said he, petulantly.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_485	lexical	\N	\N	484	{"text": "\\"Why, that he was a retired sergeant of Marines.\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_486	lexical	\N	\N	485	{"text": "\\"I have no time for trifles,\\" he answered, brusquely; then with a smile, \\"Excuse my rudeness.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_487	lexical	\N	\N	486	{"text": "You broke the thread of my thoughts; but perhaps it is as well.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_488	lexical	\N	\N	487	{"text": "So you actually were not able to see that that man was a sergeant of Marines?\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_489	lexical	\N	\N	488	{"text": "\\"No, indeed.\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_490	lexical	\N	\N	489	{"text": "\\"It was easier to know it than to explain why I knew it.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_491	lexical	\N	\N	490	{"text": "If you were asked to prove that two and two made four, you might find some difficulty, and yet you are quite sure of the fact.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_492	lexical	\N	\N	491	{"text": "Even across the street I could see a great blue anchor tattooed on the back of the fellow's hand.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_493	lexical	\N	\N	492	{"text": "That smacked of the sea.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_494	lexical	\N	\N	493	{"text": "He had a military carriage, however, and regulation side whiskers.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_495	lexical	\N	\N	494	{"text": "There we have the marine.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_496	lexical	\N	\N	495	{"text": "He was a man with some amount of self-importance and a certain air of command.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_497	lexical	\N	\N	496	{"text": "You must have observed the way in which he held his head and swung his cane.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_498	lexical	\N	\N	497	{"text": "A steady, respectable, middle-aged man, too, on the face of him—all facts which led me to believe that he had been a sergeant.\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_499	lexical	\N	\N	498	{"text": "\\"Wonderful!\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_500	lexical	\N	\N	499	{"text": "I ejaculated.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_501	lexical	\N	\N	500	{"text": "\\"Commonplace,\\" said Holmes, though I thought from his expression that he was pleased at my evident surprise and admiration.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_502	lexical	\N	\N	501	{"text": "\\"I said just now that there were no criminals.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_503	lexical	\N	\N	502	{"text": "It appears that I am wrong—look at this!\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_504	lexical	\N	\N	503	{"text": "He threw me over the note which the commissionaire had brought.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_505	lexical	\N	\N	504	{"text": "\\"Why,\\" I cried, as I cast my eye over it, \\"this is terrible!\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_506	lexical	\N	\N	505	{"text": "\\"It does seem to be a little out of the common,\\" he remarked, calmly.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_507	lexical	\N	\N	506	{"text": "\\"Would you mind reading it to me aloud?\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_508	lexical	\N	\N	507	{"text": "This is the letter which I read to him—", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_509	lexical	\N	\N	508	{"text": "\\"MY DEAR MR.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_510	lexical	\N	\N	509	{"text": "SHERLOCK HOLMES,—", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_511	lexical	\N	\N	510	{"text": "\\"There has been a bad business during the night at 3, Lauriston Gardens, off the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_512	lexical	\N	\N	511	{"text": "Our man on the beat saw a light there about two in the morning, and as the house was an empty one, suspected that something was amiss.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_513	lexical	\N	\N	512	{"text": "He found the door open, and in the front room, which is bare of furniture, discovered the body of a gentleman, well dressed, and having cards in his pocket bearing the name of 'Enoch J.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_514	lexical	\N	\N	513	{"text": "' There had been no robbery, nor is there any evidence as to how the man met his death.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2512	lexical	\N	\N	2511	{"text": "“No, sir.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_516	lexical	\N	\N	515	{"text": "We are at a loss as to how he came into the empty house; indeed, the whole affair is a puzzler.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_517	lexical	\N	\N	516	{"text": "If you can come round to the house any time before twelve, you will find me there.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_518	lexical	\N	\N	517	{"text": "I have left everything _in statu quo_ until I hear from you.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_519	lexical	\N	\N	518	{"text": "If you are unable to come I shall give you fuller details, and would esteem it a great kindness if you would favour me with your opinion.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_520	lexical	\N	\N	519	{"text": "uld favour me with your opinion.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_521	lexical	\N	\N	520	{"text": "Yours faithfully, \\"TOBIAS GREGSON.\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_522	lexical	\N	\N	521	{"text": "\\"Gregson is the smartest of the Scotland Yarders,\\" my friend remarked; \\"he and Lestrade are the pick of a bad lot.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_523	lexical	\N	\N	522	{"text": "They are both quick and energetic, but conventional—shockingly so.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_524	lexical	\N	\N	523	{"text": "They have their knives into one another, too.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_525	lexical	\N	\N	524	{"text": "They are as jealous as a pair of professional beauties.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_526	lexical	\N	\N	525	{"text": "There will be some fun over this case if they are both put upon the scent.\\"", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_527	lexical	\N	\N	526	{"text": "I was amazed at the calm way in which he rippled on.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_528	lexical	\N	\N	527	{"text": "\\"Surely there is not a moment to be lost,\\" I cried, \\"shall I go and order you a cab?\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_529	lexical	\N	\N	528	{"text": "\\"I'm not sure about whether I shall go.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_530	lexical	\N	\N	529	{"text": "I am the most incurably lazy devil that ever stood in shoe leather—that is, when the fit is on me, for I can be spry enough at times.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_531	lexical	\N	\N	530	{"text": "\\"Why, it is just such a chance as you have been longing for.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_532	lexical	\N	\N	531	{"text": "\\"My dear fellow, what does it matter to me.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_533	lexical	\N	\N	532	{"text": "Supposing I unravel the whole matter, you may be sure that Gregson, Lestrade, and Co.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_534	lexical	\N	\N	533	{"text": "will pocket all the credit.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_535	lexical	\N	\N	534	{"text": "That comes of being an unofficial personage.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_536	lexical	\N	\N	535	{"text": "\\"But he begs you to help him.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_537	lexical	\N	\N	536	{"text": "\\"Yes.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_538	lexical	\N	\N	537	{"text": "He knows that I am his superior, and acknowledges it to me; but he would cut his tongue out before he would own it to any third person.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_539	lexical	\N	\N	538	{"text": "However, we may as well go and have a look.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_540	lexical	\N	\N	539	{"text": "I shall work it out on my own hook.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_541	lexical	\N	\N	540	{"text": "I may have a laugh at them if I have nothing else.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_542	lexical	\N	\N	541	{"text": "Come on!\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_543	lexical	\N	\N	542	{"text": "He hustled on his overcoat, and bustled about in a way that showed that an energetic fit had superseded the apathetic one.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_544	lexical	\N	\N	543	{"text": "\\"Get your hat,\\" he said.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_545	lexical	\N	\N	544	{"text": "\\"You wish me to come?\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_546	lexical	\N	\N	545	{"text": "\\"Yes, if you have nothing better to do.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_547	lexical	\N	\N	546	{"text": "A minute later we were both in a hansom, driving furiously for the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_548	lexical	\N	\N	547	{"text": "It was a foggy, cloudy morning, and a dun-coloured veil hung over the house-tops, looking like the reflection of the mud-coloured streets beneath.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_549	lexical	\N	\N	548	{"text": "My companion was in the best of spirits, and prattled away about Cremona fiddles, and the difference between a Stradivarius and an Amati.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_550	lexical	\N	\N	549	{"text": "As for myself, I was silent, for the dull weather and the melancholy business upon which we were engaged, depressed my spirits.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_551	lexical	\N	\N	550	{"text": "\\"You don't seem to give much thought to the matter in hand,\\" I said at last, interrupting Holmes' musical disquisition.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_552	lexical	\N	\N	551	{"text": "\\"No data yet,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_553	lexical	\N	\N	552	{"text": "\\"It is a capital mistake to theorize before you have all the evidence.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_554	lexical	\N	\N	553	{"text": "It biases the judgment.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_555	lexical	\N	\N	554	{"text": "\\"You will have your data soon,\\" I remarked, pointing with my finger; \\"this is the Brixton Road, and that is the house, if I am not very much mistaken.\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_556	lexical	\N	\N	555	{"text": "\\"So it is.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_557	lexical	\N	\N	556	{"text": "Stop, driver, stop!\\"", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_558	lexical	\N	\N	557	{"text": "We were still a hundred yards or so from it, but he insisted upon our alighting, and we finished our journey upon foot.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_559	lexical	\N	\N	558	{"text": "Number 3, Lauriston Gardens wore an ill-omened and minatory look.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_560	lexical	\N	\N	559	{"text": "It was one of four which stood back some little way from the street, two being occupied and two empty.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_561	lexical	\N	\N	560	{"text": "The latter looked out with three tiers of vacant melancholy windows, which were blank and dreary, save that here and there a \\"To Let\\" card had developed like a cataract upon the bleared panes.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_562	lexical	\N	\N	561	{"text": "A small garden sprinkled over with a scattered eruption of sickly plants separated each of these houses from the street, and was traversed by a narrow pathway, yellowish in colour, and consisting apparently of a mixture of clay and of gravel.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_563	lexical	\N	\N	562	{"text": "The whole place was very sloppy from the rain which had fallen through the night.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_564	lexical	\N	\N	563	{"text": "The garden was bounded by a three-foot brick wall with a fringe of wood rails upon the top, and against this wall was leaning a stalwart police constable, surrounded by a small knot of loafers, who craned their necks and strained their eyes in the vain hope of catching some glimpse of the proceedings within.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_565	lexical	\N	\N	564	{"text": "I had imagined that Sherlock Holmes would at once have hurried into the house and plunged into a study of the mystery.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_566	lexical	\N	\N	565	{"text": "Nothing appeared to be further from his intention.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_567	lexical	\N	\N	566	{"text": "With an air of nonchalance which, under the circumstances, seemed to me to border upon affectation, he lounged up and down the pavement, and gazed vacantly at the ground, the sky, the opposite houses and the line of railings.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_568	lexical	\N	\N	567	{"text": "Having finished his scrutiny, he proceeded slowly down the path, or rather down the fringe of grass which flanked the path, keeping his eyes riveted upon the ground.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_569	lexical	\N	\N	568	{"text": "Twice he stopped, and once I saw him smile, and heard him utter an exclamation of satisfaction.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_570	lexical	\N	\N	569	{"text": "There were many marks of footsteps upon the wet clayey soil, but since the police had been coming and going over it, I was unable to see how my companion could hope to learn anything from it.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_571	lexical	\N	\N	570	{"text": "Still I had had such extraordinary evidence of the quickness of his perceptive faculties, that I had no doubt that he could see a great deal which was hidden from me.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_572	lexical	\N	\N	571	{"text": "At the door of the house we were met by a tall, white-faced, flaxen-haired man, with a notebook in his hand, who rushed forward and wrung my companion's hand with effusion.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_573	lexical	\N	\N	572	{"text": "\\"It is indeed kind of you to come,\\" he said, \\"I have had everything left untouched.\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_574	lexical	\N	\N	573	{"text": "\\"Except that!\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_575	lexical	\N	\N	574	{"text": "my friend answered, pointing at the pathway.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_576	lexical	\N	\N	575	{"text": "\\"If a herd of buffaloes had passed along there could not be a greater mess.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_577	lexical	\N	\N	576	{"text": "No doubt, however, you had drawn your own conclusions, Gregson, before you permitted this.\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_578	lexical	\N	\N	577	{"text": "\\"I have had so much to do inside the house,\\" the detective said evasively.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_579	lexical	\N	\N	578	{"text": "\\"My colleague, Mr. Lestrade, is here.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_580	lexical	\N	\N	579	{"text": "I had relied upon him to look after this.\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_581	lexical	\N	\N	580	{"text": "Holmes glanced at me and raised his eyebrows sardonically.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_582	lexical	\N	\N	581	{"text": "\\"With two such men as yourself and Lestrade upon the ground, there will not be much for a third party to find out,\\" he said.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_583	lexical	\N	\N	582	{"text": "Gregson rubbed his hands in a self-satisfied way.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_584	lexical	\N	\N	583	{"text": "\\"I think we have done all that can be done,\\" he answered; \\"it's a queer case though, and I knew your taste for such things.\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_585	lexical	\N	\N	584	{"text": "\\"You did not come here in a cab?\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_586	lexical	\N	\N	585	{"text": "asked Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_587	lexical	\N	\N	586	{"text": "\\"No, sir.\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_588	lexical	\N	\N	587	{"text": "\\"Nor Lestrade?\\"", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_591	lexical	\N	\N	590	{"text": "With which inconsequent remark he strode on into the house, followed by Gregson, whose features expressed his astonishment.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_592	lexical	\N	\N	591	{"text": "A short passage, bare planked and dusty, led to the kitchen and offices.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_593	lexical	\N	\N	592	{"text": "Two doors opened out of it to the left and to the right.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_594	lexical	\N	\N	593	{"text": "One of these had obviously been closed for many weeks.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_595	lexical	\N	\N	594	{"text": "The other belonged to the dining-room, which was the apartment in which the mysterious affair had occurred.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_596	lexical	\N	\N	595	{"text": "Holmes walked in, and I followed him with that subdued feeling at my heart which the presence of death inspires.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_597	lexical	\N	\N	596	{"text": "It was a large square room, looking all the larger from the absence of all furniture.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_598	lexical	\N	\N	597	{"text": "A vulgar flaring paper adorned the walls, but it was blotched in places with mildew, and here and there great strips had become detached and hung down, exposing the yellow plaster beneath.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_599	lexical	\N	\N	598	{"text": "Opposite the door was a showy fireplace, surmounted by a mantelpiece of imitation white marble.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_600	lexical	\N	\N	599	{"text": "On one corner of this was stuck the stump of a red wax candle.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_601	lexical	\N	\N	600	{"text": "The solitary window was so dirty that the light was hazy and uncertain, giving a dull grey tinge to everything, which was intensified by the thick layer of dust which coated the whole apartment.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_602	lexical	\N	\N	601	{"text": "All these details I observed afterwards.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_603	lexical	\N	\N	602	{"text": "At present my attention was centred upon the single grim motionless figure which lay stretched upon the boards, with vacant sightless eyes staring up at the discoloured ceiling.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_604	lexical	\N	\N	603	{"text": "It was that of a man about forty-three or forty-four years of age, middle-sized, broad shouldered, with crisp curling black hair, and a short stubbly beard.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_605	lexical	\N	\N	604	{"text": "He was dressed in a heavy broadcloth frock coat and waistcoat, with light-coloured trousers, and immaculate collar and cuffs.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_606	lexical	\N	\N	605	{"text": "A top hat, well brushed and trim, was placed upon the floor beside him.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_607	lexical	\N	\N	606	{"text": "His hands were clenched and his arms thrown abroad, while his lower limbs were interlocked as though his death struggle had been a grievous one.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_608	lexical	\N	\N	607	{"text": "On his rigid face there stood an expression of horror, and as it seemed to me, of hatred, such as I have never seen upon human features.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_609	lexical	\N	\N	608	{"text": "This malignant and terrible contortion, combined with the low forehead, blunt nose, and prognathous jaw gave the dead man a singularly simious and ape-like appearance, which was increased by his writhing, unnatural posture.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_610	lexical	\N	\N	609	{"text": "I have seen death in many forms, but never has it appeared to me in a more fearsome aspect than in that dark grimy apartment, which looked out upon one of the main arteries of suburban London.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_611	lexical	\N	\N	610	{"text": "Lestrade, lean and ferret-like as ever, was standing by the doorway, and greeted my companion and myself.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_612	lexical	\N	\N	611	{"text": "\\"This case will make a stir, sir,\\" he remarked.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_613	lexical	\N	\N	612	{"text": "\\"It beats anything I have seen, and I am no chicken.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_614	lexical	\N	\N	613	{"text": "\\"There is no clue?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_615	lexical	\N	\N	614	{"text": "said Gregson.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_616	lexical	\N	\N	615	{"text": "\\"None at all,\\" chimed in Lestrade.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_617	lexical	\N	\N	616	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes approached the body, and, kneeling down, examined it intently.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_618	lexical	\N	\N	617	{"text": "\\"You are sure that there is no wound?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_619	lexical	\N	\N	618	{"text": "he asked, pointing to numerous gouts and splashes of blood which lay all round.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_620	lexical	\N	\N	619	{"text": "\\"Positive!\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_621	lexical	\N	\N	620	{"text": "cried both detectives.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_622	lexical	\N	\N	621	{"text": "\\"Then, of course, this blood belongs to a second individual—presumably the murderer, if murder has been committed.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_623	lexical	\N	\N	622	{"text": "It reminds me of the circumstances attendant on the death of Van Jansen, in Utrecht, in the year '34.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_624	lexical	\N	\N	623	{"text": "Do you remember the case, Gregson?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_625	lexical	\N	\N	624	{"text": "\\"No, sir.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_629	lexical	\N	\N	628	{"text": "As he spoke, his nimble fingers were flying here, there, and everywhere, feeling, pressing, unbuttoning, examining, while his eyes wore the same far-away expression which I have already remarked upon.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_630	lexical	\N	\N	629	{"text": "So swiftly was the examination made, that one would hardly have guessed the minuteness with which it was conducted.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_631	lexical	\N	\N	630	{"text": "Finally, he sniffed the dead man's lips, and then glanced at the soles of his patent leather boots.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_632	lexical	\N	\N	631	{"text": "\\"He has not been moved at all?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_633	lexical	\N	\N	632	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_634	lexical	\N	\N	633	{"text": "\\"No more than was necessary for the purposes of our examination.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_635	lexical	\N	\N	634	{"text": "\\"You can take him to the mortuary now,\\" he said.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_636	lexical	\N	\N	635	{"text": "\\"There is nothing more to be learned.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_637	lexical	\N	\N	636	{"text": "Gregson had a stretcher and four men at hand.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_638	lexical	\N	\N	637	{"text": "At his call they entered the room, and the stranger was lifted and carried out.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_639	lexical	\N	\N	638	{"text": "As they raised him, a ring tinkled down and rolled across the floor.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_640	lexical	\N	\N	639	{"text": "Lestrade grabbed it up and stared at it with mystified eyes.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_641	lexical	\N	\N	640	{"text": "\\"There's been a woman here,\\" he cried.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_642	lexical	\N	\N	641	{"text": "\\"It's a woman's wedding-ring.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_643	lexical	\N	\N	642	{"text": "He held it out, as he spoke, upon the palm of his hand.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_644	lexical	\N	\N	643	{"text": "We all gathered round him and gazed at it.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_645	lexical	\N	\N	644	{"text": "There could be no doubt that that circlet of plain gold had once adorned the finger of a bride.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_646	lexical	\N	\N	645	{"text": "\\"This complicates matters,\\" said Gregson.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_647	lexical	\N	\N	646	{"text": "\\"Heaven knows, they were complicated enough before.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_648	lexical	\N	\N	647	{"text": "\\"You're sure it doesn't simplify them?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_649	lexical	\N	\N	648	{"text": "observed Holmes.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_650	lexical	\N	\N	649	{"text": "\\"There's nothing to be learned by staring at it.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_651	lexical	\N	\N	650	{"text": "What did you find in his pockets?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_652	lexical	\N	\N	651	{"text": "\\"We have it all here,\\" said Gregson, pointing to a litter of objects upon one of the bottom steps of the stairs.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_653	lexical	\N	\N	652	{"text": "\\"A gold watch, No.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_654	lexical	\N	\N	653	{"text": "97163, by Barraud, of London.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_655	lexical	\N	\N	654	{"text": "Gold Albert chain, very heavy and solid.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_656	lexical	\N	\N	655	{"text": "Gold ring, with masonic device.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_657	lexical	\N	\N	656	{"text": "Gold pin—bull-dog's head, with rubies as eyes.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_658	lexical	\N	\N	657	{"text": "Russian leather card-case, with cards of Enoch J.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_659	lexical	\N	\N	658	{"text": "Drebber of Cleveland, corresponding with the E.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_660	lexical	\N	\N	659	{"text": "J.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_661	lexical	\N	\N	660	{"text": "D.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_662	lexical	\N	\N	661	{"text": "upon the linen.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_663	lexical	\N	\N	662	{"text": "No purse, but loose money to the extent of seven pounds thirteen.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_664	lexical	\N	\N	663	{"text": "Pocket edition of Boccaccio's _Decameron_, with name of Joseph Stangerson upon the fly-leaf.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_665	lexical	\N	\N	664	{"text": "Two letters—one addressed to E.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_666	lexical	\N	\N	665	{"text": "J.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_667	lexical	\N	\N	666	{"text": "Drebber and one to Joseph Stangerson.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_668	lexical	\N	\N	667	{"text": "\\"At what address?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_669	lexical	\N	\N	668	{"text": "\\"American Exchange, Strand—to be left till called for.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_670	lexical	\N	\N	669	{"text": "They are both from the Guion Steamship Company, and refer to the sailing of their boats from Liverpool.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_674	lexical	\N	\N	673	{"text": "\\"I have had advertisements sent to all the newspapers, and one of my men has gone to the American Exchange, but he has not returned yet.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_675	lexical	\N	\N	674	{"text": "\\"Have you sent to Cleveland?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_676	lexical	\N	\N	675	{"text": "\\"We telegraphed this morning.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_677	lexical	\N	\N	676	{"text": "\\"How did you word your inquiries?\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_678	lexical	\N	\N	677	{"text": "\\"We simply detailed the circumstances, and said that we should be glad of any information which could help us.\\"", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_679	lexical	\N	\N	678	{"text": "\\"You did not ask for particulars on any point which appeared to you to be crucial?\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_680	lexical	\N	\N	679	{"text": "\\"I asked about Stangerson.\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_681	lexical	\N	\N	680	{"text": "\\"Nothing else?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_682	lexical	\N	\N	681	{"text": "Is there no circumstance on which this whole case appears to hinge?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_683	lexical	\N	\N	682	{"text": "Will you not telegraph again?\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_684	lexical	\N	\N	683	{"text": "\\"I have said all I have to say,\\" said Gregson, in an offended voice.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_685	lexical	\N	\N	684	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes chuckled to himself, and appeared to be about to make some remark, when Lestrade, who had been in the front room while we were holding this conversation in the hall, reappeared upon the scene, rubbing his hands in a pompous and self-satisfied manner.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_686	lexical	\N	\N	685	{"text": "\\"Mr. Gregson,\\" he said, \\"I have just made a discovery of the highest importance, and one which would have been overlooked had I not made a careful examination of the walls.\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_687	lexical	\N	\N	686	{"text": "The little man's eyes sparkled as he spoke, and he was evidently in a state of suppressed exultation at having scored a point against his colleague.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_688	lexical	\N	\N	687	{"text": "\\"Come here,\\" he said, bustling back into the room, the atmosphere of which felt clearer since the removal of its ghastly inmate.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_689	lexical	\N	\N	688	{"text": "\\"Now, stand there!\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_690	lexical	\N	\N	689	{"text": "He struck a match on his boot and held it up against the wall.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_691	lexical	\N	\N	690	{"text": "\\"Look at that!\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_692	lexical	\N	\N	691	{"text": "he said, triumphantly.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_693	lexical	\N	\N	692	{"text": "I have remarked that the paper had fallen away in parts.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_694	lexical	\N	\N	693	{"text": "In this particular corner of the room a large piece had peeled off, leaving a yellow square of coarse plastering.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_695	lexical	\N	\N	694	{"text": "Across this bare space there was scrawled in blood-red letters a single word—", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_696	lexical	\N	\N	695	{"text": "RACHE.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_697	lexical	\N	\N	696	{"text": "\\"What do you think of that?\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_698	lexical	\N	\N	697	{"text": "cried the detective, with the air of a showman exhibiting his show.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_699	lexical	\N	\N	698	{"text": "\\"This was overlooked because it was in the darkest corner of the room, and no one thought of looking there.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_700	lexical	\N	\N	699	{"text": "The murderer has written it with his or her own blood.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_701	lexical	\N	\N	700	{"text": "See this smear where it has trickled down the wall!", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_702	lexical	\N	\N	701	{"text": "That disposes of the idea of suicide anyhow.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_703	lexical	\N	\N	702	{"text": "Why was that corner chosen to write it on?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_704	lexical	\N	\N	703	{"text": "I will tell you.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_705	lexical	\N	\N	704	{"text": "See that candle on the mantelpiece.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_706	lexical	\N	\N	705	{"text": "It was lit at the time, and if it was lit this corner would be the brightest instead of the darkest portion of the wall.\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_707	lexical	\N	\N	706	{"text": "\\"And what does it mean now that you _have_ found it?\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_708	lexical	\N	\N	707	{"text": "asked Gregson in a depreciatory voice.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_709	lexical	\N	\N	708	{"text": "\\"Mean?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_710	lexical	\N	\N	709	{"text": "Why, it means that the writer was going to put the female name Rachel, but was disturbed before he or she had time to finish.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_711	lexical	\N	\N	710	{"text": "You mark my words, when this case comes to be cleared up you will find that a woman named Rachel has something to do with it.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_712	lexical	\N	\N	711	{"text": "It's all very well for you to laugh, Mr. Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_713	lexical	\N	\N	712	{"text": "You may be very smart and clever, but the old hound is the best, when all is said and done.\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_714	lexical	\N	\N	713	{"text": "\\"I really beg your pardon!\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_715	lexical	\N	\N	714	{"text": "said my companion, who had ruffled the little man's temper by bursting into an explosion of laughter.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_716	lexical	\N	\N	715	{"text": "\\"You certainly have the credit of being the first of us to find this out, and, as you say, it bears every mark of having been written by the other participant in last night's mystery.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_717	lexical	\N	\N	716	{"text": "I have not had time to examine this room yet, but with your permission I shall do so now.\\"", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_718	lexical	\N	\N	717	{"text": "As he spoke, he whipped a tape measure and a large round magnifying glass from his pocket.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_719	lexical	\N	\N	718	{"text": "With these two implements he trotted noiselessly about the room, sometimes stopping, occasionally kneeling, and once lying flat upon his face.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_720	lexical	\N	\N	719	{"text": "So engrossed was he with his occupation that he appeared to have forgotten our presence, for he chattered away to himself under his breath the whole time, keeping up a running fire of exclamations, groans, whistles, and little cries suggestive of encouragement and of hope.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_721	lexical	\N	\N	720	{"text": "As I watched him I was irresistibly reminded of a pure-blooded well-trained foxhound as it dashes backwards and forwards through the covert, whining in its eagerness, until it comes across the lost scent.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_722	lexical	\N	\N	721	{"text": "For twenty minutes or more he continued his researches, measuring with the most exact care the distance between marks which were entirely invisible to me, and occasionally applying his tape to the walls in an equally incomprehensible manner.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_723	lexical	\N	\N	722	{"text": "In one place he gathered up very carefully a little pile of grey dust from the floor, and packed it away in an envelope.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_724	lexical	\N	\N	723	{"text": "Finally, he examined with his glass the word upon the wall, going over every letter of it with the most minute exactness.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_725	lexical	\N	\N	724	{"text": "This done, he appeared to be satisfied, for he replaced his tape and his glass in his pocket.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_726	lexical	\N	\N	725	{"text": "\\"They say that genius is an infinite capacity for taking pains,\\" he remarked with a smile.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_727	lexical	\N	\N	726	{"text": "\\"It's a very bad definition, but it does apply to detective work.\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_728	lexical	\N	\N	727	{"text": "Gregson and Lestrade had watched the manœuvres of their amateur companion with considerable curiosity and some contempt.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_729	lexical	\N	\N	728	{"text": "They evidently failed to appreciate the fact, which I had begun to realize, that Sherlock Holmes' smallest actions were all directed towards some definite and practical end.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_730	lexical	\N	\N	729	{"text": "\\"What do you think of it, sir?\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_731	lexical	\N	\N	730	{"text": "they both asked.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_732	lexical	\N	\N	731	{"text": "\\"It would be robbing you of the credit of the case if I was to presume to help you,\\" remarked my friend.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_733	lexical	\N	\N	732	{"text": "\\"You are doing so well now that it would be a pity for anyone to interfere.\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_734	lexical	\N	\N	733	{"text": "There was a world of sarcasm in his voice as he spoke.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_735	lexical	\N	\N	734	{"text": "\\"If you will let me know how your investigations go,\\" he continued, \\"I shall be happy to give you any help I can.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_736	lexical	\N	\N	735	{"text": "In the meantime I should like to speak to the constable who found the body.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_737	lexical	\N	\N	736	{"text": "Can you give me his name and address?\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_738	lexical	\N	\N	737	{"text": "Lestrade glanced at his note-book.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_739	lexical	\N	\N	738	{"text": "\\"John Rance,\\" he said.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_740	lexical	\N	\N	739	{"text": "\\"He is off duty now.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_741	lexical	\N	\N	740	{"text": "You will find him at 46, Audley Court, Kennington Park Gate.\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_742	lexical	\N	\N	741	{"text": "Holmes took a note of the address.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_743	lexical	\N	\N	742	{"text": "\\"Come along, Doctor,\\" he said; \\"we shall go and look him up.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_744	lexical	\N	\N	743	{"text": "I'll tell you one thing which may help you in the case,\\" he continued, turning to the two detectives.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_745	lexical	\N	\N	744	{"text": "\\"There has been murder done, and the murderer was a man.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_746	lexical	\N	\N	745	{"text": "He was more than six feet high, was in the prime of life, had small feet for his height, wore coarse, square-toed boots and smoked a Trichinopoly cigar.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_747	lexical	\N	\N	746	{"text": "He came here with his victim in a four-wheeled cab, which was drawn by a horse with three old shoes and one new one on his off fore leg.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_748	lexical	\N	\N	747	{"text": "In all probability the murderer had a florid face, and the finger-nails of his right hand were remarkably long.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_749	lexical	\N	\N	748	{"text": "These are only a few indications, but they may assist you.\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_750	lexical	\N	\N	749	{"text": "Lestrade and Gregson glanced at each other with an incredulous smile.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_751	lexical	\N	\N	750	{"text": "\\"If this man was murdered, how was it done?\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_752	lexical	\N	\N	751	{"text": "asked the former.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_753	lexical	\N	\N	752	{"text": "\\"Poison,\\" said Sherlock Holmes curtly, and strode off.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_754	lexical	\N	\N	753	{"text": "\\"One other thing, Lestrade,\\" he added, turning round at the door: \\"'Rache,' is the German for 'revenge'; so don't lose your time looking for Miss Rachel.\\"", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_755	lexical	\N	\N	754	{"text": "With which Parthian shot he walked away, leaving the two rivals open-mouthed behind him.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_756	lexical	\N	\N	755	{"text": "CHAPTER IV.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_757	lexical	\N	\N	756	{"text": "WHAT JOHN RANCE HAD TO TELL.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_758	lexical	\N	\N	757	{"text": "It was one o'clock when we left No.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_759	lexical	\N	\N	758	{"text": "3, Lauriston Gardens.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_760	lexical	\N	\N	759	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes led me to the nearest telegraph office, whence he dispatched a long telegram.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_761	lexical	\N	\N	760	{"text": "He then hailed a cab, and ordered the driver to take us to the address given us by Lestrade.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_762	lexical	\N	\N	761	{"text": "\\"There is nothing like first hand evidence,\\" he remarked; \\"as a matter of fact, my mind is entirely made up upon the case, but still we may as well learn all that is to be learned.\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_763	lexical	\N	\N	762	{"text": "\\"You amaze me, Holmes,\\" said I.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_764	lexical	\N	\N	763	{"text": "\\"Surely you are not as sure as you pretend to be of all those particulars which you gave.\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_765	lexical	\N	\N	764	{"text": "\\"There's no room for a mistake,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_766	lexical	\N	\N	765	{"text": "\\"The very first thing which I observed on arriving there was that a cab had made two ruts with its wheels close to the curb.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_767	lexical	\N	\N	766	{"text": "Now, up to last night, we have had no rain for a week, so that those wheels which left such a deep impression must have been there during the night.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_768	lexical	\N	\N	767	{"text": "There were the marks of the horse's hoofs, too, the outline of one of which was far more clearly cut than that of the other three, showing that that was a new shoe.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_769	lexical	\N	\N	768	{"text": "Since the cab was there after the rain began, and was not there at any time during the morning—I have Gregson's word for that—it follows that it must have been there during the night, and, therefore, that it brought those two individuals to the house.\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_770	lexical	\N	\N	769	{"text": "\\"That seems simple enough,\\" said I; \\"but how about the other man's height?\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_771	lexical	\N	\N	770	{"text": "\\"Why, the height of a man, in nine cases out of ten, can be told from the length of his stride.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_772	lexical	\N	\N	771	{"text": "It is a simple calculation enough, though there is no use my boring you with figures.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_773	lexical	\N	\N	772	{"text": "I had this fellow's stride both on the clay outside and on the dust within.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_774	lexical	\N	\N	773	{"text": "Then I had a way of checking my calculation.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_775	lexical	\N	\N	774	{"text": "When a man writes on a wall, his instinct leads him to write about the level of his own eyes.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_776	lexical	\N	\N	775	{"text": "Now that writing was just over six feet from the ground.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_777	lexical	\N	\N	776	{"text": "It was child's play.\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_778	lexical	\N	\N	777	{"text": "\\"And his age?\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_779	lexical	\N	\N	778	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_780	lexical	\N	\N	779	{"text": "\\"Well, if a man can stride four and a-half feet without the smallest effort, he can't be quite in the sere and yellow.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_781	lexical	\N	\N	780	{"text": "That was the breadth of a puddle on the garden walk which he had evidently walked across.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_782	lexical	\N	\N	781	{"text": "Patent-leather boots had gone round, and Square-toes had hopped over.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_783	lexical	\N	\N	782	{"text": "There is no mystery about it at all.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_784	lexical	\N	\N	783	{"text": "I am simply applying to ordinary life a few of those precepts of observation and deduction which I advocated in that article.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_785	lexical	\N	\N	784	{"text": "Is there anything else that puzzles you?\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_786	lexical	\N	\N	785	{"text": "\\"The finger nails and the Trichinopoly,\\" I suggested.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_787	lexical	\N	\N	786	{"text": "\\"The writing on the wall was done with a man's forefinger dipped in blood.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_788	lexical	\N	\N	787	{"text": "My glass allowed me to observe that the plaster was slightly scratched in doing it, which would not have been the case if the man's nail had been trimmed.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_789	lexical	\N	\N	788	{"text": "I gathered up some scattered ash from the floor.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_790	lexical	\N	\N	789	{"text": "It was dark in colour and flakey—such an ash as is only made by a Trichinopoly.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_791	lexical	\N	\N	790	{"text": "I have made a special study of cigar ashes—in fact, I have written a monograph upon the subject.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_792	lexical	\N	\N	791	{"text": "I flatter myself that I can distinguish at a glance the ash of any known brand, either of cigar or of tobacco.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_793	lexical	\N	\N	792	{"text": "It is just in such details that the skilled detective differs from the Gregson and Lestrade type.\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_794	lexical	\N	\N	793	{"text": "\\"And the florid face?\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_795	lexical	\N	\N	794	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_796	lexical	\N	\N	795	{"text": "\\"Ah, that was a more daring shot, though I have no doubt that I was right.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_797	lexical	\N	\N	796	{"text": "You must not ask me that at the present state of the affair.\\"", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_798	lexical	\N	\N	797	{"text": "I passed my hand over my brow.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_799	lexical	\N	\N	798	{"text": "\\"My head is in a whirl,\\" I remarked; \\"the more one thinks of it the more mysterious it grows.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_800	lexical	\N	\N	799	{"text": "How came these two men—if there were two men—into an empty house?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_801	lexical	\N	\N	800	{"text": "What has become of the cabman who drove them?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_802	lexical	\N	\N	801	{"text": "How could one man compel another to take poison?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_803	lexical	\N	\N	802	{"text": "Where did the blood come from?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_804	lexical	\N	\N	803	{"text": "What was the object of the murderer, since robbery had no part in it?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_805	lexical	\N	\N	804	{"text": "How came the woman's ring there?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_806	lexical	\N	\N	805	{"text": "Above all, why should the second man write up the German word RACHE before decamping?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_807	lexical	\N	\N	806	{"text": "I confess that I cannot see any possible way of reconciling all these facts.\\"", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_808	lexical	\N	\N	807	{"text": "My companion smiled approvingly.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_809	lexical	\N	\N	808	{"text": "\\"You sum up the difficulties of the situation succinctly and well,\\" he said.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_810	lexical	\N	\N	809	{"text": "\\"There is much that is still obscure, though I have quite made up my mind on the main facts.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_811	lexical	\N	\N	810	{"text": "As to poor Lestrade's discovery it was simply a blind intended to put the police upon a wrong track, by suggesting Socialism and secret societies.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_812	lexical	\N	\N	811	{"text": "It was not done by a German.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_813	lexical	\N	\N	812	{"text": "The A, if you noticed, was printed somewhat after the German fashion.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_814	lexical	\N	\N	813	{"text": "Now, a real German invariably prints in the Latin character, so that we may safely say that this was not written by one, but by a clumsy imitator who overdid his part.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_815	lexical	\N	\N	814	{"text": "It was simply a ruse to divert inquiry into a wrong channel.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_816	lexical	\N	\N	815	{"text": "I'm not going to tell you much more of the case, Doctor.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_817	lexical	\N	\N	816	{"text": "You know a conjuror gets no credit when once he has explained his trick, and if I show you too much of my method of working, you will come to the conclusion that I am a very ordinary individual after all.\\"", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_818	lexical	\N	\N	817	{"text": "\\"I shall never do that,\\" I answered; \\"you have brought detection as near an exact science as it ever will be brought in this world.\\"", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_819	lexical	\N	\N	818	{"text": "My companion flushed up with pleasure at my words, and the earnest way in which I uttered them.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_820	lexical	\N	\N	819	{"text": "I had already observed that he was as sensitive to flattery on the score of his art as any girl could be of her beauty.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_822	lexical	\N	\N	821	{"text": "\\"Patent-leathers and Square-toes came in the same cab, and they walked down the pathway together as friendly as possible—arm-in-arm, in all probability.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_823	lexical	\N	\N	822	{"text": "When they got inside they walked up and down the room—or rather, Patent-leathers stood still while Square-toes walked up and down.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_824	lexical	\N	\N	823	{"text": "I could read all that in the dust; and I could read that as he walked he grew more and more excited.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_825	lexical	\N	\N	824	{"text": "That is shown by the increased length of his strides.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_826	lexical	\N	\N	825	{"text": "He was talking all the while, and working himself up, no doubt, into a fury.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_827	lexical	\N	\N	826	{"text": "Then the tragedy occurred.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_828	lexical	\N	\N	827	{"text": "I've told you all I know myself now, for the rest is mere surmise and conjecture.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_829	lexical	\N	\N	828	{"text": "We have a good working basis, however, on which to start.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_830	lexical	\N	\N	829	{"text": "We must hurry up, for I want to go to Halle's concert to hear Norman Neruda this afternoon.\\"", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_831	lexical	\N	\N	830	{"text": "This conversation had occurred while our cab had been threading its way through a long succession of dingy streets and dreary by-ways.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_832	lexical	\N	\N	831	{"text": "In the dingiest and dreariest of them our driver suddenly came to a stand.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_833	lexical	\N	\N	832	{"text": "\\"That's Audley Court in there,\\" he said, pointing to a narrow slit in the line of dead-coloured brick.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_834	lexical	\N	\N	833	{"text": "\\"You'll find me here when you come back.\\"", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_835	lexical	\N	\N	834	{"text": "Audley Court was not an attractive locality.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_836	lexical	\N	\N	835	{"text": "The narrow passage led us into a quadrangle paved with flags and lined by sordid dwellings.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_837	lexical	\N	\N	836	{"text": "We picked our way among groups of dirty children, and through lines of discoloured linen, until we came to Number 46, the door of which was decorated with a small slip of brass on which the name Rance was engraved.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_838	lexical	\N	\N	837	{"text": "On enquiry we found that the constable was in bed, and we were shown into a little front parlour to await his coming.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_839	lexical	\N	\N	838	{"text": "He appeared presently, looking a little irritable at being disturbed in his slumbers.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_840	lexical	\N	\N	839	{"text": "\\"I made my report at the office,\\" he said.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_841	lexical	\N	\N	840	{"text": "Holmes took a half-sovereign from his pocket and played with it pensively.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_842	lexical	\N	\N	841	{"text": "\\"We thought that we should like to hear it all from your own lips,\\" he said.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_843	lexical	\N	\N	842	{"text": "\\"I shall be most happy to tell you anything I can,\\" the constable answered with his eyes upon the little golden disk.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_844	lexical	\N	\N	843	{"text": "\\"Just let us hear it all in your own way as it occurred.\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_845	lexical	\N	\N	844	{"text": "Rance sat down on the horsehair sofa, and knitted his brows as though determined not to omit anything in his narrative.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_846	lexical	\N	\N	845	{"text": "\\"I'll tell it ye from the beginning,\\" he said.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_847	lexical	\N	\N	846	{"text": "\\"My time is from ten at night to six in the morning.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_848	lexical	\N	\N	847	{"text": "At eleven there was a fight at the 'White Hart'; but bar that all was quiet enough on the beat.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_849	lexical	\N	\N	848	{"text": "At one o'clock it began to rain, and I met Harry Murcher—him who has the Holland Grove beat—and we stood together at the corner of Henrietta Street a-talkin'.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_850	lexical	\N	\N	849	{"text": "Presently—maybe about two or a little after—I thought I would take a look round and see that all was right down the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_851	lexical	\N	\N	850	{"text": "It was precious dirty and lonely.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_852	lexical	\N	\N	851	{"text": "Not a soul did I meet all the way down, though a cab or two went past me.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_853	lexical	\N	\N	852	{"text": "I was a strollin' down, thinkin' between ourselves how uncommon handy a four of gin hot would be, when suddenly the glint of a light caught my eye in the window of that same house.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_854	lexical	\N	\N	853	{"text": "Now, I knew that them two houses in Lauriston Gardens was empty on account of him that owns them who won't have the drains seen to, though the very last tenant what lived in one of them died o' typhoid fever.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_855	lexical	\N	\N	854	{"text": "I was knocked all in a heap therefore at seeing a light in the window, and I suspected as something was wrong.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_859	lexical	\N	\N	858	{"text": "Rance gave a violent jump, and stared at Sherlock Holmes with the utmost amazement upon his features.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_860	lexical	\N	\N	859	{"text": "\\"Why, that's true, sir,\\" he said; \\"though how you come to know it, Heaven only knows.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_861	lexical	\N	\N	860	{"text": "Ye see, when I got up to the door it was so still and so lonesome, that I thought I'd be none the worse for some one with me.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_862	lexical	\N	\N	861	{"text": "I ain't afeared of anything on this side o' the grave; but I thought that maybe it was him that died o' the typhoid inspecting the drains what killed him.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_863	lexical	\N	\N	862	{"text": "The thought gave me a kind o' turn, and I walked back to the gate to see if I could see Murcher's lantern, but there wasn't no sign of him nor of anyone else.\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_864	lexical	\N	\N	863	{"text": "\\"There was no one in the street?\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_865	lexical	\N	\N	864	{"text": "\\"Not a livin' soul, sir, nor as much as a dog.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_866	lexical	\N	\N	865	{"text": "Then I pulled myself together and went back and pushed the door open.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_867	lexical	\N	\N	866	{"text": "All was quiet inside, so I went into the room where the light was a-burnin'.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_868	lexical	\N	\N	867	{"text": "There was a candle flickerin' on the mantelpiece—a red wax one—and by its light I saw——\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_869	lexical	\N	\N	868	{"text": "\\"Yes, I know all that you saw.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_870	lexical	\N	\N	869	{"text": "You walked round the room several times, and you knelt down by the body, and then you walked through and tried the kitchen door, and then——\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_871	lexical	\N	\N	870	{"text": "John Rance sprang to his feet with a frightened face and suspicion in his eyes.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_872	lexical	\N	\N	871	{"text": "\\"Where was you hid to see all that?\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_873	lexical	\N	\N	872	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_874	lexical	\N	\N	873	{"text": "\\"It seems to me that you knows a deal more than you should.\\"", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_875	lexical	\N	\N	874	{"text": "Holmes laughed and threw his card across the table to the constable.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_876	lexical	\N	\N	875	{"text": "\\"Don't get arresting me for the murder,\\" he said.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_877	lexical	\N	\N	876	{"text": "\\"I am one of the hounds and not the wolf; Mr. Gregson or Mr. Lestrade will answer for that.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_878	lexical	\N	\N	877	{"text": "Go on, though.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_879	lexical	\N	\N	878	{"text": "What did you do next?\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_880	lexical	\N	\N	879	{"text": "Rance resumed his seat, without however losing his mystified expression.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_881	lexical	\N	\N	880	{"text": "\\"I went back to the gate and sounded my whistle.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_882	lexical	\N	\N	881	{"text": "That brought Murcher and two more to the spot.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_883	lexical	\N	\N	882	{"text": "\\"Was the street empty then?\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_884	lexical	\N	\N	883	{"text": "\\"Well, it was, as far as anybody that could be of any good goes.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_885	lexical	\N	\N	884	{"text": "\\"What do you mean?\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_886	lexical	\N	\N	885	{"text": "The constable's features broadened into a grin.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_887	lexical	\N	\N	886	{"text": "\\"I've seen many a drunk chap in my time,\\" he said, \\"but never anyone so cryin' drunk as that cove.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_888	lexical	\N	\N	887	{"text": "He was at the gate when I came out, a-leanin' up agin the railings, and a-singin' at the pitch o' his lungs about Columbine's New-fangled Banner, or some such stuff.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_889	lexical	\N	\N	888	{"text": "He couldn't stand, far less help.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_890	lexical	\N	\N	889	{"text": "\\"What sort of a man was he?\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_891	lexical	\N	\N	890	{"text": "asked Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_892	lexical	\N	\N	891	{"text": "John Rance appeared to be somewhat irritated at this digression.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_893	lexical	\N	\N	892	{"text": "\\"He was an uncommon drunk sort o' man,\\" he said.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_894	lexical	\N	\N	893	{"text": "\\"He'd ha' found hisself in the station if we hadn't been so took up.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_895	lexical	\N	\N	894	{"text": "\\"His face—his dress—didn't you notice them?\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_896	lexical	\N	\N	895	{"text": "Holmes broke in impatiently.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_897	lexical	\N	\N	896	{"text": "\\"I should think I did notice them, seeing that I had to prop him up—me and Murcher between us.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_910	lexical	\N	\N	909	{"text": "\\"There's a half-sovereign for you,\\" my companion said, standing up and taking his hat.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_911	lexical	\N	\N	910	{"text": "\\"I am afraid, Rance, that you will never rise in the force.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_912	lexical	\N	\N	911	{"text": "That head of yours should be for use as well as ornament.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_913	lexical	\N	\N	912	{"text": "You might have gained your sergeant's stripes last night.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_914	lexical	\N	\N	913	{"text": "The man whom you held in your hands is the man who holds the clue of this mystery, and whom we are seeking.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_915	lexical	\N	\N	914	{"text": "There is no use of arguing about it now; I tell you that it is so.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_916	lexical	\N	\N	915	{"text": "Come along, Doctor.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_917	lexical	\N	\N	916	{"text": "We started off for the cab together, leaving our informant incredulous, but obviously uncomfortable.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_918	lexical	\N	\N	917	{"text": "\\"The blundering fool,\\" Holmes said, bitterly, as we drove back to our lodgings.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_919	lexical	\N	\N	918	{"text": "\\"Just to think of his having such an incomparable bit of good luck, and not taking advantage of it.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_920	lexical	\N	\N	919	{"text": "\\"I am rather in the dark still.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_921	lexical	\N	\N	920	{"text": "It is true that the description of this man tallies with your idea of the second party in this mystery.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_922	lexical	\N	\N	921	{"text": "But why should he come back to the house after leaving it?", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_923	lexical	\N	\N	922	{"text": "That is not the way of criminals.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_924	lexical	\N	\N	923	{"text": "\\"The ring, man, the ring: that was what he came back for.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_925	lexical	\N	\N	924	{"text": "If we have no other way of catching him, we can always bait our line with the ring.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_926	lexical	\N	\N	925	{"text": "I shall have him, Doctor—I'll lay you two to one that I have him.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_927	lexical	\N	\N	926	{"text": "I must thank you for it all.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_928	lexical	\N	\N	927	{"text": "I might not have gone but for you, and so have missed the finest study I ever came across: a study in scarlet, eh?", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_929	lexical	\N	\N	928	{"text": "Why shouldn't we use a little art jargon.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_930	lexical	\N	\N	929	{"text": "There's the scarlet thread of murder running through the colourless skein of life, and our duty is to unravel it, and isolate it, and expose every inch of it.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_931	lexical	\N	\N	930	{"text": "And now for lunch, and then for Norman Neruda.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_932	lexical	\N	\N	931	{"text": "Her attack and her bowing are splendid.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_933	lexical	\N	\N	932	{"text": "What's that little thing of Chopin's she plays so magnificently: Tra-la-la-lira-lira-lay.\\"", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_934	lexical	\N	\N	933	{"text": "Leaning back in the cab, this amateur bloodhound carolled away like a lark while I meditated upon the many-sidedness of the human mind.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_935	lexical	\N	\N	934	{"text": "CHAPTER V.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_936	lexical	\N	\N	935	{"text": "OUR ADVERTISEMENT BRINGS A VISITOR.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_937	lexical	\N	\N	936	{"text": "Our morning's exertions had been too much for my weak health, and I was tired out in the afternoon.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_938	lexical	\N	\N	937	{"text": "After Holmes' departure for the concert, I lay down upon the sofa and endeavoured to get a couple of hours' sleep.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_939	lexical	\N	\N	938	{"text": "It was a useless attempt.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_940	lexical	\N	\N	939	{"text": "My mind had been too much excited by all that had occurred, and the strangest fancies and surmises crowded into it.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_941	lexical	\N	\N	940	{"text": "Every time that I closed my eyes I saw before me the distorted baboon-like countenance of the murdered man.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_942	lexical	\N	\N	941	{"text": "So sinister was the impression which that face had produced upon me that I found it difficult to feel anything but gratitude for him who had removed its owner from the world.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_943	lexical	\N	\N	942	{"text": "If ever human features bespoke vice of the most malignant type, they were certainly those of Enoch J.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_944	lexical	\N	\N	943	{"text": "Drebber, of Cleveland.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_945	lexical	\N	\N	944	{"text": "Still I recognized that justice must be done, and that the depravity of the victim was no condonement in the eyes of the law.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_946	lexical	\N	\N	945	{"text": "The more I thought of it the more extraordinary did my companion's hypothesis, that the man had been poisoned, appear.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_56	section	\N	Section 56	55	{"wordCount": 600}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_947	lexical	\N	\N	946	{"text": "I remembered how he had sniffed his lips, and had no doubt that he had detected something which had given rise to the idea.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_948	lexical	\N	\N	947	{"text": "Then, again, if not poison, what had caused the man's death, since there was neither wound nor marks of strangulation?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_949	lexical	\N	\N	948	{"text": "But, on the other hand, whose blood was that which lay so thickly upon the floor?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_950	lexical	\N	\N	949	{"text": "There were no signs of a struggle, nor had the victim any weapon with which he might have wounded an antagonist.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_951	lexical	\N	\N	950	{"text": "As long as all these questions were unsolved, I felt that sleep would be no easy matter, either for Holmes or myself.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_952	lexical	\N	\N	951	{"text": "His quiet self-confident manner convinced me that he had already formed a theory which explained all the facts, though what it was I could not for an instant conjecture.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_953	lexical	\N	\N	952	{"text": "He was very late in returning—so late, that I knew that the concert could not have detained him all the time.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_954	lexical	\N	\N	953	{"text": "Dinner was on the table before he appeared.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_955	lexical	\N	\N	954	{"text": "\\"It was magnificent,\\" he said, as he took his seat.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_956	lexical	\N	\N	955	{"text": "\\"Do you remember what Darwin says about music?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_957	lexical	\N	\N	956	{"text": "He claims that the power of producing and appreciating it existed among the human race long before the power of speech was arrived at.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_958	lexical	\N	\N	957	{"text": "Perhaps that is why we are so subtly influenced by it.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_959	lexical	\N	\N	958	{"text": "There are vague memories in our souls of those misty centuries when the world was in its childhood.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_960	lexical	\N	\N	959	{"text": "\\"That's rather a broad idea,\\" I remarked.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_961	lexical	\N	\N	960	{"text": "\\"One's ideas must be as broad as Nature if they are to interpret Nature,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_962	lexical	\N	\N	961	{"text": "\\"What's the matter?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_963	lexical	\N	\N	962	{"text": "You're not looking quite yourself.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_964	lexical	\N	\N	963	{"text": "This Brixton Road affair has upset you.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_965	lexical	\N	\N	964	{"text": "\\"To tell the truth, it has,\\" I said.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_966	lexical	\N	\N	965	{"text": "\\"I ought to be more case-hardened after my Afghan experiences.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_967	lexical	\N	\N	966	{"text": "I saw my own comrades hacked to pieces at Maiwand without losing my nerve.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_968	lexical	\N	\N	967	{"text": "\\"I can understand.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_969	lexical	\N	\N	968	{"text": "There is a mystery about this which stimulates the imagination; where there is no imagination there is no horror.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_970	lexical	\N	\N	969	{"text": "Have you seen the evening paper?\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_971	lexical	\N	\N	970	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_972	lexical	\N	\N	971	{"text": "\\"It gives a fairly good account of the affair.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_973	lexical	\N	\N	972	{"text": "It does not mention the fact that when the man was raised up, a woman's wedding ring fell upon the floor.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_974	lexical	\N	\N	973	{"text": "It is just as well it does not.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_975	lexical	\N	\N	974	{"text": "\\"Why?\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_976	lexical	\N	\N	975	{"text": "\\"Look at this advertisement,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_977	lexical	\N	\N	976	{"text": "\\"I had one sent to every paper this morning immediately after the affair.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_978	lexical	\N	\N	977	{"text": "He threw the paper across to me and I glanced at the place indicated.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_979	lexical	\N	\N	978	{"text": "It was the first announcement in the \\"Found\\" column.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_980	lexical	\N	\N	979	{"text": "\\"In Brixton Road, this morning,\\" it ran, \\"a plain gold wedding ring, found in the roadway between the 'White Hart' Tavern and Holland Grove.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_981	lexical	\N	\N	980	{"text": "Apply Dr. Watson, 221B, Baker Street, between eight and nine this evening.\\"", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_982	lexical	\N	\N	981	{"text": "\\"Excuse my using your name,\\" he said.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_983	lexical	\N	\N	982	{"text": "\\"If I used my own some of these dunderheads would recognize it, and want to meddle in the affair.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_984	lexical	\N	\N	983	{"text": "\\"That is all right,\\" I answered.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_985	lexical	\N	\N	984	{"text": "\\"But supposing anyone applies, I have no ring.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_990	lexical	\N	\N	989	{"text": "\\"Why, the man in the brown coat—our florid friend with the square toes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_991	lexical	\N	\N	990	{"text": "If he does not come himself he will send an accomplice.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_992	lexical	\N	\N	991	{"text": "\\"Would he not consider it as too dangerous?\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_993	lexical	\N	\N	992	{"text": "\\"Not at all.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_994	lexical	\N	\N	993	{"text": "If my view of the case is correct, and I have every reason to believe that it is, this man would rather risk anything than lose the ring.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_995	lexical	\N	\N	994	{"text": "According to my notion he dropped it while stooping over Drebber's body, and did not miss it at the time.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_996	lexical	\N	\N	995	{"text": "After leaving the house he discovered his loss and hurried back, but found the police already in possession, owing to his own folly in leaving the candle burning.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_997	lexical	\N	\N	996	{"text": "He had to pretend to be drunk in order to allay the suspicions which might have been aroused by his appearance at the gate.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_998	lexical	\N	\N	997	{"text": "Now put yourself in that man's place.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_999	lexical	\N	\N	998	{"text": "On thinking the matter over, it must have occurred to him that it was possible that he had lost the ring in the road after leaving the house.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1000	lexical	\N	\N	999	{"text": "What would he do, then?", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1462	lexical	\N	\N	1461	{"text": "I will give you a proof of my knowledge.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1001	lexical	\N	\N	1000	{"text": "He would eagerly look out for the evening papers in the hope of seeing it among the articles found.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1002	lexical	\N	\N	1001	{"text": "His eye, of course, would light upon this.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1003	lexical	\N	\N	1002	{"text": "He would be overjoyed.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1004	lexical	\N	\N	1003	{"text": "Why should he fear a trap?", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1005	lexical	\N	\N	1004	{"text": "There would be no reason in his eyes why the finding of the ring should be connected with the murder.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1006	lexical	\N	\N	1005	{"text": "He would come.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1007	lexical	\N	\N	1006	{"text": "He will come.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1008	lexical	\N	\N	1007	{"text": "You shall see him within an hour?\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1009	lexical	\N	\N	1008	{"text": "\\"And then?\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1010	lexical	\N	\N	1009	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1011	lexical	\N	\N	1010	{"text": "\\"Oh, you can leave me to deal with him then.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1012	lexical	\N	\N	1011	{"text": "Have you any arms?\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1013	lexical	\N	\N	1012	{"text": "\\"I have my old service revolver and a few cartridges.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1014	lexical	\N	\N	1013	{"text": "\\"You had better clean it and load it.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1015	lexical	\N	\N	1014	{"text": "He will be a desperate man, and though I shall take him unawares, it is as well to be ready for anything.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1016	lexical	\N	\N	1015	{"text": "I went to my bedroom and followed his advice.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1017	lexical	\N	\N	1016	{"text": "When I returned with the pistol the table had been cleared, and Holmes was engaged in his favourite occupation of scraping upon his violin.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1018	lexical	\N	\N	1017	{"text": "\\"The plot thickens,\\" he said, as I entered; \\"I have just had an answer to my American telegram.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1019	lexical	\N	\N	1018	{"text": "My view of the case is the correct one.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1020	lexical	\N	\N	1019	{"text": "\\"And that is?\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1021	lexical	\N	\N	1020	{"text": "I asked eagerly.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1022	lexical	\N	\N	1021	{"text": "\\"My fiddle would be the better for new strings,\\" he remarked.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1023	lexical	\N	\N	1022	{"text": "\\"Put your pistol in your pocket.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1024	lexical	\N	\N	1023	{"text": "When the fellow comes speak to him in an ordinary way.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1025	lexical	\N	\N	1024	{"text": "Leave the rest to me.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1026	lexical	\N	\N	1025	{"text": "Don't frighten him by looking at him too hard.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1027	lexical	\N	\N	1026	{"text": "\\"It is eight o'clock now,\\" I said, glancing at my watch.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1028	lexical	\N	\N	1027	{"text": "\\"Yes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1029	lexical	\N	\N	1028	{"text": "He will probably be here in a few minutes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1030	lexical	\N	\N	1029	{"text": "Open the door slightly.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1034	lexical	\N	\N	1033	{"text": "This is a queer old book I picked up at a stall yesterday—'De Jure inter Gentes'—published in Latin at Liege in the Lowlands, in 1642.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1035	lexical	\N	\N	1034	{"text": "Charles' head was still firm on his shoulders when this little brown-backed volume was struck off.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1036	lexical	\N	\N	1035	{"text": "\\"Who is the printer?\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1037	lexical	\N	\N	1036	{"text": "\\"Philippe de Croy, whoever he may have been.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1038	lexical	\N	\N	1037	{"text": "' I wonder who William Whyte was.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1039	lexical	\N	\N	1038	{"text": "Some pragmatical seventeenth century lawyer, I suppose.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1040	lexical	\N	\N	1039	{"text": "His writing has a legal twist about it.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1041	lexical	\N	\N	1040	{"text": "Here comes our man, I think.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1042	lexical	\N	\N	1041	{"text": "se. His writing has a legal twist about it. Here comes our man, I think.\\"", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1043	lexical	\N	\N	1042	{"text": "As he spoke there was a sharp ring at the bell.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1044	lexical	\N	\N	1043	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes rose softly and moved his chair in the direction of the door.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1045	lexical	\N	\N	1044	{"text": "We heard the servant pass along the hall, and the sharp click of the latch as she opened it.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1046	lexical	\N	\N	1045	{"text": "\\"Does Dr. Watson live here?\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1047	lexical	\N	\N	1046	{"text": "asked a clear but rather harsh voice.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1048	lexical	\N	\N	1047	{"text": "We could not hear the servant's reply, but the door closed, and some one began to ascend the stairs.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1049	lexical	\N	\N	1048	{"text": "The footfall was an uncertain and shuffling one.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1050	lexical	\N	\N	1049	{"text": "A look of surprise passed over the face of my companion as he listened to it.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1051	lexical	\N	\N	1050	{"text": "It came slowly along the passage, and there was a feeble tap at the door.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1052	lexical	\N	\N	1051	{"text": "\\"Come in,\\" I cried.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1053	lexical	\N	\N	1052	{"text": "At my summons, instead of the man of violence whom we expected, a very old and wrinkled woman hobbled into the apartment.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1054	lexical	\N	\N	1053	{"text": "She appeared to be dazzled by the sudden blaze of light, and after dropping a curtsey, she stood blinking at us with her bleared eyes and fumbling in her pocket with nervous, shaky fingers.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1055	lexical	\N	\N	1054	{"text": "I glanced at my companion, and his face had assumed such a disconsolate expression that it was all I could do to keep my countenance.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1056	lexical	\N	\N	1055	{"text": "The old crone drew out an evening paper, and pointed at our advertisement.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1057	lexical	\N	\N	1056	{"text": "\\"It's this as has brought me, good gentlemen,\\" she said, dropping another curtsey; \\"a gold wedding ring in the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1058	lexical	\N	\N	1057	{"text": "It belongs to my girl Sally, as was married only this time twelvemonth, which her husband is steward aboard a Union boat, and what he'd say if he come 'ome and found her without her ring is more than I can think, he being short enough at the best o' times, but more especially when he has the drink.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1059	lexical	\N	\N	1058	{"text": "If it please you, she went to the circus last night along with——\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1060	lexical	\N	\N	1059	{"text": "\\"Is that her ring?\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1061	lexical	\N	\N	1060	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1062	lexical	\N	\N	1061	{"text": "\\"The Lord be thanked!\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1063	lexical	\N	\N	1062	{"text": "cried the old woman; \\"Sally will be a glad woman this night.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1064	lexical	\N	\N	1063	{"text": "That's the ring.\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1065	lexical	\N	\N	1064	{"text": "\\"And what may your address be?\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1066	lexical	\N	\N	1065	{"text": "I inquired, taking up a pencil.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1067	lexical	\N	\N	1066	{"text": "\\"13, Duncan Street, Houndsditch.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1068	lexical	\N	\N	1067	{"text": "A weary way from here.\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1069	lexical	\N	\N	1068	{"text": "\\"The Brixton Road does not lie between any circus and Houndsditch,\\" said Sherlock Holmes sharply.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1070	lexical	\N	\N	1069	{"text": "The old woman faced round and looked keenly at him from her little red-rimmed eyes.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1071	lexical	\N	\N	1070	{"text": "\\"The gentleman asked me for _my_ address,\\" she said.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1072	lexical	\N	\N	1071	{"text": "\\"Sally lives in lodgings at 3, Mayfield Place, Peckham.\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1073	lexical	\N	\N	1072	{"text": "\\"And your name is——?\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1074	lexical	\N	\N	1073	{"text": "\\"My name is Sawyer—hers is Dennis, which Tom Dennis married her—and a smart, clean lad, too, as long as he's at sea, and no steward in the company more thought of; but when on shore, what with the women and what with liquor shops——\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1075	lexical	\N	\N	1074	{"text": "\\"Here is your ring, Mrs. Sawyer,\\" I interrupted, in obedience to a sign from my companion; \\"it clearly belongs to your daughter, and I am glad to be able to restore it to the rightful owner.\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1076	lexical	\N	\N	1075	{"text": "With many mumbled blessings and protestations of gratitude the old crone packed it away in her pocket, and shuffled off down the stairs.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1077	lexical	\N	\N	1076	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes sprang to his feet the moment that she was gone and rushed into his room.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1078	lexical	\N	\N	1077	{"text": "He returned in a few seconds enveloped in an ulster and a cravat.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1079	lexical	\N	\N	1078	{"text": "\\"I'll follow her,\\" he said, hurriedly; \\"she must be an accomplice, and will lead me to him.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1080	lexical	\N	\N	1079	{"text": "Wait up for me.\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1081	lexical	\N	\N	1080	{"text": "The hall door had hardly slammed behind our visitor before Holmes had descended the stair.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1082	lexical	\N	\N	1081	{"text": "Looking through the window I could see her walking feebly along the other side, while her pursuer dogged her some little distance behind.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1083	lexical	\N	\N	1082	{"text": "\\"Either his whole theory is incorrect,\\" I thought to myself, \\"or else he will be led now to the heart of the mystery.\\"", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1084	lexical	\N	\N	1083	{"text": "There was no need for him to ask me to wait up for him, for I felt that sleep was impossible until I heard the result of his adventure.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1085	lexical	\N	\N	1084	{"text": "It was close upon nine when he set out.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1086	lexical	\N	\N	1085	{"text": "I had no idea how long he might be, but I sat stolidly puffing at my pipe and skipping over the pages of Henri Murger's \\"Vie de Bohème.\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1087	lexical	\N	\N	1086	{"text": "Ten o'clock passed, and I heard the footsteps of the maid as they pattered off to bed.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1088	lexical	\N	\N	1087	{"text": "Eleven, and the more stately tread of the landlady passed my door, bound for the same destination.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1089	lexical	\N	\N	1088	{"text": "It was close upon twelve before I heard the sharp sound of his latch-key.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1090	lexical	\N	\N	1089	{"text": "The instant he entered I saw by his face that he had not been successful.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1091	lexical	\N	\N	1090	{"text": "Amusement and chagrin seemed to be struggling for the mastery, until the former suddenly carried the day, and he burst into a hearty laugh.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1092	lexical	\N	\N	1091	{"text": "\\"I wouldn't have the Scotland Yarders know it for the world,\\" he cried, dropping into his chair; \\"I have chaffed them so much that they would never have let me hear the end of it.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1093	lexical	\N	\N	1092	{"text": "I can afford to laugh, because I know that I will be even with them in the long run.\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1094	lexical	\N	\N	1093	{"text": "\\"What is it then?\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1095	lexical	\N	\N	1094	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1096	lexical	\N	\N	1095	{"text": "\\"Oh, I don't mind telling a story against myself.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1097	lexical	\N	\N	1096	{"text": "That creature had gone a little way when she began to limp and show every sign of being foot-sore.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1098	lexical	\N	\N	1097	{"text": "Presently she came to a halt, and hailed a four-wheeler which was passing.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1099	lexical	\N	\N	1098	{"text": "I managed to be close to her so as to hear the address, but I need not have been so anxious, for she sang it out loud enough to be heard at the other side of the street, 'Drive to 13, Duncan Street, Houndsditch,' she cried.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1100	lexical	\N	\N	1099	{"text": "This begins to look genuine, I thought, and having seen her safely inside, I perched myself behind.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1101	lexical	\N	\N	1100	{"text": "That's an art which every detective should be an expert at.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1102	lexical	\N	\N	1101	{"text": "Well, away we rattled, and never drew rein until we reached the street in question.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1103	lexical	\N	\N	1102	{"text": "I hopped off before we came to the door, and strolled down the street in an easy, lounging way.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1104	lexical	\N	\N	1103	{"text": "I saw the cab pull up.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1105	lexical	\N	\N	1104	{"text": "The driver jumped down, and I saw him open the door and stand expectantly.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1107	lexical	\N	\N	1106	{"text": "When I reached him he was groping about frantically in the empty cab, and giving vent to the finest assorted collection of oaths that ever I listened to.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1108	lexical	\N	\N	1107	{"text": "There was no sign or trace of his passenger, and I fear it will be some time before he gets his fare.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1109	lexical	\N	\N	1108	{"text": "On inquiring at Number 13 we found that the house belonged to a respectable paperhanger, named Keswick, and that no one of the name either of Sawyer or Dennis had ever been heard of there.\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1110	lexical	\N	\N	1109	{"text": "\\"You don't mean to say,\\" I cried, in amazement, \\"that that tottering, feeble old woman was able to get out of the cab while it was in motion, without either you or the driver seeing her?\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1111	lexical	\N	\N	1110	{"text": "\\"Old woman be damned!\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1112	lexical	\N	\N	1111	{"text": "said Sherlock Holmes, sharply.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1113	lexical	\N	\N	1112	{"text": "\\"We were the old women to be so taken in.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1114	lexical	\N	\N	1113	{"text": "It must have been a young man, and an active one, too, besides being an incomparable actor.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1115	lexical	\N	\N	1114	{"text": "The get-up was inimitable.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1116	lexical	\N	\N	1115	{"text": "He saw that he was followed, no doubt, and used this means of giving me the slip.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1117	lexical	\N	\N	1116	{"text": "It shows that the man we are after is not as lonely as I imagined he was, but has friends who are ready to risk something for him.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1118	lexical	\N	\N	1117	{"text": "Now, Doctor, you are looking done-up.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1119	lexical	\N	\N	1118	{"text": "Take my advice and turn in.\\"", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1120	lexical	\N	\N	1119	{"text": "I was certainly feeling very weary, so I obeyed his injunction.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1121	lexical	\N	\N	1120	{"text": "I left Holmes seated in front of the smouldering fire, and long into the watches of the night I heard the low, melancholy wailings of his violin, and knew that he was still pondering over the strange problem which he had set himself to unravel.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1122	lexical	\N	\N	1121	{"text": "CHAPTER VI.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1123	lexical	\N	\N	1122	{"text": "TOBIAS GREGSON SHOWS WHAT HE CAN DO.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1124	lexical	\N	\N	1123	{"text": "The papers next day were full of the \\"Brixton Mystery,\\" as they termed it.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1125	lexical	\N	\N	1124	{"text": "Each had a long account of the affair, and some had leaders upon it in addition.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1126	lexical	\N	\N	1125	{"text": "There was some information in them which was new to me.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1127	lexical	\N	\N	1126	{"text": "I still retain in my scrap-book numerous clippings and extracts bearing upon the case.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1128	lexical	\N	\N	1127	{"text": "Here is a condensation of a few of them:—", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1129	lexical	\N	\N	1128	{"text": "The _Daily Telegraph_ remarked that in the history of crime there had seldom been a tragedy which presented stranger features.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1130	lexical	\N	\N	1129	{"text": "The German name of the victim, the absence of all other motive, and the sinister inscription on the wall, all pointed to its perpetration by political refugees and revolutionists.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1131	lexical	\N	\N	1130	{"text": "The Socialists had many branches in America, and the deceased had, no doubt, infringed their unwritten laws, and been tracked down by them.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1132	lexical	\N	\N	1131	{"text": "After alluding airily to the Vehmgericht, aqua tofana, Carbonari, the Marchioness de Brinvilliers, the Darwinian theory, the principles of Malthus, and the Ratcliff Highway murders, the article concluded by admonishing the Government and advocating a closer watch over foreigners in England.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1133	lexical	\N	\N	1132	{"text": "The _Standard_ commented upon the fact that lawless outrages of the sort usually occurred under a Liberal Administration.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1134	lexical	\N	\N	1133	{"text": "They arose from the unsettling of the minds of the masses, and the consequent weakening of all authority.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1135	lexical	\N	\N	1134	{"text": "The deceased was an American gentleman who had been residing for some weeks in the Metropolis.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1136	lexical	\N	\N	1135	{"text": "He had stayed at the boarding-house of Madame Charpentier, in Torquay Terrace, Camberwell.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1137	lexical	\N	\N	1136	{"text": "He was accompanied in his travels by his private secretary, Mr. Joseph Stangerson.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1138	lexical	\N	\N	1137	{"text": ", and departed to Euston Station with the avowed intention of catching the Liverpool express.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1139	lexical	\N	\N	1138	{"text": "They were afterwards seen together upon the platform.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2535	lexical	\N	\N	2534	{"text": "I did not act, however, with undue precipitation.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1140	lexical	\N	\N	1139	{"text": "Nothing more is known of them until Mr. Drebber's body was, as recorded, discovered in an empty house in the Brixton Road, many miles from Euston.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1141	lexical	\N	\N	1140	{"text": "How he came there, or how he met his fate, are questions which are still involved in mystery.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1142	lexical	\N	\N	1141	{"text": "Nothing is known of the whereabouts of Stangerson.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1143	lexical	\N	\N	1142	{"text": "We are glad to learn that Mr. Lestrade and Mr. Gregson, of Scotland Yard, are both engaged upon the case, and it is confidently anticipated that these well-known officers will speedily throw light upon the matter.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1144	lexical	\N	\N	1143	{"text": "e well-known officers will speedily throw light upon the matter.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1145	lexical	\N	\N	1144	{"text": "The _Daily News_ observed that there was no doubt as to the crime being a political one.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1146	lexical	\N	\N	1145	{"text": "The despotism and hatred of Liberalism which animated the Continental Governments had had the effect of driving to our shores a number of men who might have made excellent citizens were they not soured by the recollection of all that they had undergone.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1147	lexical	\N	\N	1146	{"text": "Among these men there was a stringent code of honour, any infringement of which was punished by death.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1463	lexical	\N	\N	1462	{"text": "Could you lay your hand upon those pills?\\"", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1148	lexical	\N	\N	1147	{"text": "Every effort should be made to find the secretary, Stangerson, and to ascertain some particulars of the habits of the deceased.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1149	lexical	\N	\N	1148	{"text": "A great step had been gained by the discovery of the address of the house at which he had boarded—a result which was entirely due to the acuteness and energy of Mr. Gregson of Scotland Yard.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1150	lexical	\N	\N	1149	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes and I read these notices over together at breakfast, and they appeared to afford him considerable amusement.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1151	lexical	\N	\N	1150	{"text": "\\"I told you that, whatever happened, Lestrade and Gregson would be sure to score.\\"", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1152	lexical	\N	\N	1151	{"text": "\\"That depends on how it turns out.\\"", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1153	lexical	\N	\N	1152	{"text": "\\"Oh, bless you, it doesn't matter in the least.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1154	lexical	\N	\N	1153	{"text": "If the man is caught, it will be _on account_ of their exertions; if he escapes, it will be _in spite_ of their exertions.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1155	lexical	\N	\N	1154	{"text": "It's heads I win and tails you lose.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1156	lexical	\N	\N	1155	{"text": "Whatever they do, they will have followers.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1157	lexical	\N	\N	1156	{"text": "'Un sot trouve toujours un plus sot qui l'admire.'\\"", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1158	lexical	\N	\N	1157	{"text": "\\"What on earth is this?\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1159	lexical	\N	\N	1158	{"text": "I cried, for at this moment there came the pattering of many steps in the hall and on the stairs, accompanied by audible expressions of disgust upon the part of our landlady.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1160	lexical	\N	\N	1159	{"text": "\\"It's the Baker Street division of the detective police force,\\" said my companion, gravely; and as he spoke there rushed into the room half a dozen of the dirtiest and most ragged street Arabs that ever I clapped eyes on.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1161	lexical	\N	\N	1160	{"text": "\\"'Tention!\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1162	lexical	\N	\N	1161	{"text": "cried Holmes, in a sharp tone, and the six dirty little scoundrels stood in a line like so many disreputable statuettes.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1163	lexical	\N	\N	1162	{"text": "\\"In future you shall send up Wiggins alone to report, and the rest of you must wait in the street.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1164	lexical	\N	\N	1163	{"text": "Have you found it, Wiggins?\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1165	lexical	\N	\N	1164	{"text": "\\"No, sir, we hain't,\\" said one of the youths.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1166	lexical	\N	\N	1165	{"text": "\\"I hardly expected you would.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1167	lexical	\N	\N	1166	{"text": "You must keep on until you do.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1168	lexical	\N	\N	1167	{"text": "Here are your wages.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1169	lexical	\N	\N	1168	{"text": "He handed each of them a shilling.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1170	lexical	\N	\N	1169	{"text": "\\"Now, off you go, and come back with a better report next time.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1171	lexical	\N	\N	1170	{"text": "He waved his hand, and they scampered away downstairs like so many rats, and we heard their shrill voices next moment in the street.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1172	lexical	\N	\N	1171	{"text": "\\"There's more work to be got out of one of those little beggars than out of a dozen of the force,\\" Holmes remarked.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1173	lexical	\N	\N	1172	{"text": "\\"The mere sight of an official-looking person seals men's lips.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_57	section	\N	Section 57	56	{"wordCount": 621}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1174	lexical	\N	\N	1173	{"text": "These youngsters, however, go everywhere and hear everything.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1175	lexical	\N	\N	1174	{"text": "They are as sharp as needles, too; all they want is organisation.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1176	lexical	\N	\N	1175	{"text": "\\"Is it on this Brixton case that you are employing them?\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1177	lexical	\N	\N	1176	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1178	lexical	\N	\N	1177	{"text": "\\"Yes; there is a point which I wish to ascertain.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1179	lexical	\N	\N	1178	{"text": "It is merely a matter of time.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1180	lexical	\N	\N	1179	{"text": "Hullo!", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1181	lexical	\N	\N	1180	{"text": "we are going to hear some news now with a vengeance!", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1182	lexical	\N	\N	1181	{"text": "Here is Gregson coming down the road with beatitude written upon every feature of his face.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1183	lexical	\N	\N	1182	{"text": "Bound for us, I know.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1184	lexical	\N	\N	1183	{"text": "Yes, he is stopping.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1185	lexical	\N	\N	1184	{"text": "There he is!\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1186	lexical	\N	\N	1185	{"text": "There was a violent peal at the bell, and in a few seconds the fair-haired detective came up the stairs, three steps at a time, and burst into our sitting-room.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1187	lexical	\N	\N	1186	{"text": "\\"My dear fellow,\\" he cried, wringing Holmes' unresponsive hand, \\"congratulate me!", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1188	lexical	\N	\N	1187	{"text": "I have made the whole thing as clear as day.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1189	lexical	\N	\N	1188	{"text": "A shade of anxiety seemed to me to cross my companion's expressive face.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1190	lexical	\N	\N	1189	{"text": "\\"Do you mean that you are on the right track?\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1191	lexical	\N	\N	1190	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1192	lexical	\N	\N	1191	{"text": "\\"The right track!", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1193	lexical	\N	\N	1192	{"text": "Why, sir, we have the man under lock and key.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1194	lexical	\N	\N	1193	{"text": "\\"And his name is?\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1195	lexical	\N	\N	1194	{"text": "\\"Arthur Charpentier, sub-lieutenant in Her Majesty's navy,\\" cried Gregson, pompously, rubbing his fat hands and inflating his chest.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1196	lexical	\N	\N	1195	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes gave a sigh of relief, and relaxed into a smile.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1197	lexical	\N	\N	1196	{"text": "\\"Take a seat, and try one of these cigars,\\" he said.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1198	lexical	\N	\N	1197	{"text": "\\"We are anxious to know how you managed it.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1199	lexical	\N	\N	1198	{"text": "Will you have some whiskey and water?\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1200	lexical	\N	\N	1199	{"text": "\\"I don't mind if I do,\\" the detective answered.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1201	lexical	\N	\N	1200	{"text": "\\"The tremendous exertions which I have gone through during the last day or two have worn me out.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1202	lexical	\N	\N	1201	{"text": "Not so much bodily exertion, you understand, as the strain upon the mind.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1203	lexical	\N	\N	1202	{"text": "You will appreciate that, Mr. Sherlock Holmes, for we are both brain-workers.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1204	lexical	\N	\N	1203	{"text": "\\"You do me too much honour,\\" said Holmes, gravely.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1205	lexical	\N	\N	1204	{"text": "\\"Let us hear how you arrived at this most gratifying result.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1206	lexical	\N	\N	1205	{"text": "The detective seated himself in the arm-chair, and puffed complacently at his cigar.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1207	lexical	\N	\N	1206	{"text": "Then suddenly he slapped his thigh in a paroxysm of amusement.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1208	lexical	\N	\N	1207	{"text": "\\"The fun of it is,\\" he cried, \\"that that fool Lestrade, who thinks himself so smart, has gone off upon the wrong track altogether.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1209	lexical	\N	\N	1208	{"text": "He is after the secretary Stangerson, who had no more to do with the crime than the babe unborn.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1210	lexical	\N	\N	1209	{"text": "I have no doubt that he has caught him by this time.\\"", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1211	lexical	\N	\N	1210	{"text": "The idea tickled Gregson so much that he laughed until he choked.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1212	lexical	\N	\N	1211	{"text": "\\"And how did you get your clue?\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1213	lexical	\N	\N	1212	{"text": "\\"Ah, I'll tell you all about it.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1214	lexical	\N	\N	1213	{"text": "Of course, Doctor Watson, this is strictly between ourselves.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1215	lexical	\N	\N	1214	{"text": "The first difficulty which we had to contend with was the finding of this American's antecedents.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1216	lexical	\N	\N	1215	{"text": "Some people would have waited until their advertisements were answered, or until parties came forward and volunteered information.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1217	lexical	\N	\N	1216	{"text": "That is not Tobias Gregson's way of going to work.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1218	lexical	\N	\N	1217	{"text": "You remember the hat beside the dead man?\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1219	lexical	\N	\N	1218	{"text": "\\"Yes,\\" said Holmes; \\"by John Underwood and Sons, 129, Camberwell Road.\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1220	lexical	\N	\N	1219	{"text": "Gregson looked quite crest-fallen.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1221	lexical	\N	\N	1220	{"text": "\\"I had no idea that you noticed that,\\" he said.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1222	lexical	\N	\N	1221	{"text": "\\"Have you been there?\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1223	lexical	\N	\N	1222	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1224	lexical	\N	\N	1223	{"text": "\\"Ha!\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1225	lexical	\N	\N	1224	{"text": "cried Gregson, in a relieved voice; \\"you should never neglect a chance, however small it may seem.\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1226	lexical	\N	\N	1225	{"text": "\\"To a great mind, nothing is little,\\" remarked Holmes, sententiously.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1227	lexical	\N	\N	1226	{"text": "\\"Well, I went to Underwood, and asked him if he had sold a hat of that size and description.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1228	lexical	\N	\N	1227	{"text": "He looked over his books, and came on it at once.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1229	lexical	\N	\N	1228	{"text": "He had sent the hat to a Mr. Drebber, residing at Charpentier's Boarding Establishment, Torquay Terrace.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1230	lexical	\N	\N	1229	{"text": "Thus I got at his address.\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1231	lexical	\N	\N	1230	{"text": "\\"Smart—very smart!\\"", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1232	lexical	\N	\N	1231	{"text": "murmured Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1233	lexical	\N	\N	1232	{"text": "\\"I next called upon Madame Charpentier,\\" continued the detective.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1234	lexical	\N	\N	1233	{"text": "\\"I found her very pale and distressed.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1235	lexical	\N	\N	1234	{"text": "Her daughter was in the room, too—an uncommonly fine girl she is, too; she was looking red about the eyes and her lips trembled as I spoke to her.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1236	lexical	\N	\N	1235	{"text": "That didn't escape my notice.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1237	lexical	\N	\N	1236	{"text": "I began to smell a rat.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1238	lexical	\N	\N	1237	{"text": "You know the feeling, Mr. Sherlock Holmes, when you come upon the right scent—a kind of thrill in your nerves.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1239	lexical	\N	\N	1238	{"text": "'Have you heard of the mysterious death of your late boarder Mr. Enoch J.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1240	lexical	\N	\N	1239	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1241	lexical	\N	\N	1240	{"text": "f Cleveland?' I asked.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1242	lexical	\N	\N	1241	{"text": "\\"The mother nodded.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1243	lexical	\N	\N	1242	{"text": "She didn't seem able to get out a word.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1244	lexical	\N	\N	1243	{"text": "The daughter burst into tears.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1245	lexical	\N	\N	1244	{"text": "I felt more than ever that these people knew something of the matter.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1246	lexical	\N	\N	1245	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1247	lexical	\N	\N	1246	{"text": "o'clock did Mr. Drebber leave your house for the train?' I asked.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1248	lexical	\N	\N	1247	{"text": "\\"'At eight o'clock,' she said, gulping in her throat to keep down her agitation.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1249	lexical	\N	\N	1248	{"text": "15 and one at 11.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1250	lexical	\N	\N	1249	{"text": "r. Stangerson, said that there were two trains—one at 9.15 and one at 11. He was to catch the first.'", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1251	lexical	\N	\N	1250	{"text": "\\"'And was that the last which you saw of him?'", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1252	lexical	\N	\N	1251	{"text": "\\"A terrible change came over the woman's face as I asked the question.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1253	lexical	\N	\N	1252	{"text": "Her features turned perfectly livid.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1338	lexical	\N	\N	1337	{"text": "\\"'I do not know,' she answered, turning white to her very lips.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1254	lexical	\N	\N	1253	{"text": "It was some seconds before she could get out the single word 'Yes'—and when it did come it was in a husky unnatural tone.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1255	lexical	\N	\N	1254	{"text": "\\"There was silence for a moment, and then the daughter spoke in a calm clear voice.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1256	lexical	\N	\N	1255	{"text": "\\"'No good can ever come of falsehood, mother,' she said.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1257	lexical	\N	\N	1256	{"text": "'Let us be frank with this gentleman.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1258	lexical	\N	\N	1257	{"text": "We _did_ see Mr. Drebber again.'", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1259	lexical	\N	\N	1258	{"text": "' cried Madame Charpentier, throwing up her hands and sinking back in her chair.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1260	lexical	\N	\N	1259	{"text": "back in her chair. 'You have murdered your brother.'", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1261	lexical	\N	\N	1260	{"text": "\\"'Arthur would rather that we spoke the truth,' the girl answered firmly.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1262	lexical	\N	\N	1261	{"text": "\\"'You had best tell me all about it now,' I said.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1263	lexical	\N	\N	1262	{"text": "'Half-confidences are worse than none.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1264	lexical	\N	\N	1263	{"text": "Besides, you do not know how much we know of it.'", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1265	lexical	\N	\N	1264	{"text": "' cried her mother; and then, turning to me, 'I will tell you all, sir.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1266	lexical	\N	\N	1265	{"text": "Do not imagine that my agitation on behalf of my son arises from any fear lest he should have had a hand in this terrible affair.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1267	lexical	\N	\N	1266	{"text": "He is utterly innocent of it.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1268	lexical	\N	\N	1267	{"text": "My dread is, however, that in your eyes and in the eyes of others he may appear to be compromised.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1269	lexical	\N	\N	1268	{"text": "That however is surely impossible.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1270	lexical	\N	\N	1269	{"text": "owever is surely impossible. His high character, his profession, his antecedents would all forbid it.'", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1271	lexical	\N	\N	1270	{"text": "\\"'Your best way is to make a clean breast of the facts,' I answered.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1272	lexical	\N	\N	1271	{"text": "'Depend upon it, if your son is innocent he will be none the worse.'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1273	lexical	\N	\N	1272	{"text": "\\"'Perhaps, Alice, you had better leave us together,' she said, and her daughter withdrew.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1274	lexical	\N	\N	1273	{"text": "'Now, sir,' she continued, 'I had no intention of telling you all this, but since my poor daughter has disclosed it I have no alternative.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1275	lexical	\N	\N	1274	{"text": "Having once decided to speak, I will tell you all without omitting any particular.'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1276	lexical	\N	\N	1275	{"text": "\\"'It is your wisest course,' said I.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1277	lexical	\N	\N	1276	{"text": "\\"'Mr. Drebber has been with us nearly three weeks.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1278	lexical	\N	\N	1277	{"text": "He and his secretary, Mr. Stangerson, had been travelling on the Continent.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1279	lexical	\N	\N	1278	{"text": "I noticed a \\"Copenhagen\\" label upon each of their trunks, showing that that had been their last stopping place.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1280	lexical	\N	\N	1279	{"text": "Stangerson was a quiet reserved man, but his employer, I am sorry to say, was far otherwise.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1281	lexical	\N	\N	1280	{"text": "He was coarse in his habits and brutish in his ways.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1282	lexical	\N	\N	1281	{"text": "The very night of his arrival he became very much the worse for drink, and, indeed, after twelve o'clock in the day he could hardly ever be said to be sober.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1283	lexical	\N	\N	1282	{"text": "His manners towards the maid-servants were disgustingly free and familiar.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1284	lexical	\N	\N	1283	{"text": "Worst of all, he speedily assumed the same attitude towards my daughter, Alice, and spoke to her more than once in a way which, fortunately, she is too innocent to understand.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1285	lexical	\N	\N	1284	{"text": "On one occasion he actually seized her in his arms and embraced her—an outrage which caused his own secretary to reproach him for his unmanly conduct.'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1286	lexical	\N	\N	1285	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1287	lexical	\N	\N	1286	{"text": "did you stand all this?' I asked. 'I suppose that you can get rid of your boarders when you wish.'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1288	lexical	\N	\N	1287	{"text": "\\"Mrs. Charpentier blushed at my pertinent question.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1289	lexical	\N	\N	1288	{"text": "'Would to God that I had given him notice on the very day that he came,' she said.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_58	section	\N	Section 58	57	{"wordCount": 608}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1291	lexical	\N	\N	1290	{"text": "They were paying a pound a day each—fourteen pounds a week, and this is the slack season.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1292	lexical	\N	\N	1291	{"text": "I am a widow, and my boy in the Navy has cost me much.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1293	lexical	\N	\N	1292	{"text": "I grudged to lose the money.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1294	lexical	\N	\N	1293	{"text": "I acted for the best.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1295	lexical	\N	\N	1294	{"text": "This last was too much, however, and I gave him notice to leave on account of it.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1296	lexical	\N	\N	1295	{"text": "That was the reason of his going.'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1297	lexical	\N	\N	1296	{"text": "\\"'Well?'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1298	lexical	\N	\N	1297	{"text": "\\"'My heart grew light when I saw him drive away.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1299	lexical	\N	\N	1298	{"text": "My son is on leave just now, but I did not tell him anything of all this, for his temper is violent, and he is passionately fond of his sister.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1300	lexical	\N	\N	1299	{"text": "When I closed the door behind them a load seemed to be lifted from my mind.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1301	lexical	\N	\N	1300	{"text": "Alas, in less than an hour there was a ring at the bell, and I learned that Mr. Drebber had returned.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1302	lexical	\N	\N	1301	{"text": "He was much excited, and evidently the worse for drink.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1303	lexical	\N	\N	1302	{"text": "He forced his way into the room, where I was sitting with my daughter, and made some incoherent remark about having missed his train.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1304	lexical	\N	\N	1303	{"text": "He then turned to Alice, and before my very face, proposed to her that she should fly with him.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1305	lexical	\N	\N	1304	{"text": "\\"You are of age,\\" he said, \\"and there is no law to stop you.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1306	lexical	\N	\N	1305	{"text": "I have money enough and to spare.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1307	lexical	\N	\N	1306	{"text": "Never mind the old girl here, but come along with me now straight away.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1308	lexical	\N	\N	1307	{"text": "You shall live like a princess.\\"", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1309	lexical	\N	\N	1308	{"text": "Poor Alice was so frightened that she shrunk away from him, but he caught her by the wrist and endeavoured to draw her towards the door.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1310	lexical	\N	\N	1309	{"text": "I screamed, and at that moment my son Arthur came into the room.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1311	lexical	\N	\N	1310	{"text": "What happened then I do not know.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1312	lexical	\N	\N	1311	{"text": "I heard oaths and the confused sounds of a scuffle.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1313	lexical	\N	\N	1312	{"text": "I was too terrified to raise my head.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1314	lexical	\N	\N	1313	{"text": "When I did look up I saw Arthur standing in the doorway laughing, with a stick in his hand.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1315	lexical	\N	\N	1314	{"text": "\\"I don't think that fine fellow will trouble us again,\\" he said.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1316	lexical	\N	\N	1315	{"text": "\\"I will just go after him and see what he does with himself.\\"", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1317	lexical	\N	\N	1316	{"text": "With those words he took his hat and started off down the street.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1318	lexical	\N	\N	1317	{"text": "The next morning we heard of Mr. Drebber's mysterious death.'", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1319	lexical	\N	\N	1318	{"text": "\\"This statement came from Mrs. Charpentier's lips with many gasps and pauses.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1320	lexical	\N	\N	1319	{"text": "At times she spoke so low that I could hardly catch the words.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1321	lexical	\N	\N	1320	{"text": "I made shorthand notes of all that she said, however, so that there should be no possibility of a mistake.\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1322	lexical	\N	\N	1321	{"text": "\\"It's quite exciting,\\" said Sherlock Holmes, with a yawn.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1323	lexical	\N	\N	1322	{"text": "\\"What happened next?\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1324	lexical	\N	\N	1323	{"text": "\\"When Mrs. Charpentier paused,\\" the detective continued, \\"I saw that the whole case hung upon one point.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1325	lexical	\N	\N	1324	{"text": "Fixing her with my eye in a way which I always found effective with women, I asked her at what hour her son returned.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1326	lexical	\N	\N	1325	{"text": "\\"'I do not know,' she answered.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1327	lexical	\N	\N	1326	{"text": "\\"'Not know?'", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1328	lexical	\N	\N	1327	{"text": "\\"'No; he has a latch-key, and he let himself in.'", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1329	lexical	\N	\N	1328	{"text": "\\"'After you went to bed?'", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1339	lexical	\N	\N	1338	{"text": "\\"Of course after that there was nothing more to be done.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1340	lexical	\N	\N	1339	{"text": "I found out where Lieutenant Charpentier was, took two officers with me, and arrested him.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1341	lexical	\N	\N	1340	{"text": "When I touched him on the shoulder and warned him to come quietly with us, he answered us as bold as brass, 'I suppose you are arresting me for being concerned in the death of that scoundrel Drebber,' he said.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1342	lexical	\N	\N	1341	{"text": "We had said nothing to him about it, so that his alluding to it had a most suspicious aspect.\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1343	lexical	\N	\N	1342	{"text": "\\"Very,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1344	lexical	\N	\N	1343	{"text": "\\"He still carried the heavy stick which the mother described him as having with him when he followed Drebber.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1345	lexical	\N	\N	1344	{"text": "It was a stout oak cudgel.\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1346	lexical	\N	\N	1345	{"text": "\\"What is your theory, then?\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1347	lexical	\N	\N	1346	{"text": "\\"Well, my theory is that he followed Drebber as far as the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1348	lexical	\N	\N	1347	{"text": "When there, a fresh altercation arose between them, in the course of which Drebber received a blow from the stick, in the pit of the stomach, perhaps, which killed him without leaving any mark.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1349	lexical	\N	\N	1348	{"text": "The night was so wet that no one was about, so Charpentier dragged the body of his victim into the empty house.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1350	lexical	\N	\N	1349	{"text": "As to the candle, and the blood, and the writing on the wall, and the ring, they may all be so many tricks to throw the police on to the wrong scent.\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1351	lexical	\N	\N	1350	{"text": "\\"Well done!\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1352	lexical	\N	\N	1351	{"text": "said Holmes in an encouraging voice.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1353	lexical	\N	\N	1352	{"text": "\\"Really, Gregson, you are getting along.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1354	lexical	\N	\N	1353	{"text": "We shall make something of you yet.\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1355	lexical	\N	\N	1354	{"text": "\\"I flatter myself that I have managed it rather neatly,\\" the detective answered proudly.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1356	lexical	\N	\N	1355	{"text": "\\"The young man volunteered a statement, in which he said that after following Drebber some time, the latter perceived him, and took a cab in order to get away from him.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1357	lexical	\N	\N	1356	{"text": "On his way home he met an old shipmate, and took a long walk with him.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1358	lexical	\N	\N	1357	{"text": "On being asked where this old shipmate lived, he was unable to give any satisfactory reply.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1359	lexical	\N	\N	1358	{"text": "I think the whole case fits together uncommonly well.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1360	lexical	\N	\N	1359	{"text": "What amuses me is to think of Lestrade, who had started off upon the wrong scent.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1361	lexical	\N	\N	1360	{"text": "I am afraid he won't make much of it.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1362	lexical	\N	\N	1361	{"text": "Why, by Jove, here's the very man himself!\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1363	lexical	\N	\N	1362	{"text": "It was indeed Lestrade, who had ascended the stairs while we were talking, and who now entered the room.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1364	lexical	\N	\N	1363	{"text": "The assurance and jauntiness which generally marked his demeanour and dress were, however, wanting.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1365	lexical	\N	\N	1364	{"text": "His face was disturbed and troubled, while his clothes were disarranged and untidy.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1366	lexical	\N	\N	1365	{"text": "He had evidently come with the intention of consulting with Sherlock Holmes, for on perceiving his colleague he appeared to be embarrassed and put out.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1367	lexical	\N	\N	1366	{"text": "He stood in the centre of the room, fumbling nervously with his hat and uncertain what to do.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1368	lexical	\N	\N	1367	{"text": "\\"This is a most extraordinary case,\\" he said at last—\\"a most incomprehensible affair.\\"", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1369	lexical	\N	\N	1368	{"text": "\\"Ah, you find it so, Mr. Lestrade!\\"", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1370	lexical	\N	\N	1369	{"text": "cried Gregson, triumphantly.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1371	lexical	\N	\N	1370	{"text": "\\"I thought you would come to that conclusion.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1372	lexical	\N	\N	1371	{"text": "Have you managed to find the Secretary, Mr. Joseph Stangerson?\\"", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1373	lexical	\N	\N	1372	{"text": "\\"The Secretary, Mr. Joseph Stangerson,\\" said Lestrade gravely, \\"was murdered at Halliday's Private Hotel about six o'clock this morning.\\"", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1374	lexical	\N	\N	1373	{"text": "CHAPTER VII.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1376	lexical	\N	\N	1375	{"text": "The intelligence with which Lestrade greeted us was so momentous and so unexpected, that we were all three fairly dumfoundered.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1377	lexical	\N	\N	1376	{"text": "Gregson sprang out of his chair and upset the remainder of his whiskey and water.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1378	lexical	\N	\N	1377	{"text": "I stared in silence at Sherlock Holmes, whose lips were compressed and his brows drawn down over his eyes.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1379	lexical	\N	\N	1378	{"text": "\\"Stangerson too!\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1380	lexical	\N	\N	1379	{"text": "he muttered.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1381	lexical	\N	\N	1380	{"text": "\\"The plot thickens.\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1382	lexical	\N	\N	1381	{"text": "\\"It was quite thick enough before,\\" grumbled Lestrade, taking a chair.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1383	lexical	\N	\N	1382	{"text": "\\"I seem to have dropped into a sort of council of war.\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1384	lexical	\N	\N	1383	{"text": "\\"Are you—are you sure of this piece of intelligence?\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1385	lexical	\N	\N	1384	{"text": "stammered Gregson.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1386	lexical	\N	\N	1385	{"text": "\\"I have just come from his room,\\" said Lestrade.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1387	lexical	\N	\N	1386	{"text": "\\"I was the first to discover what had occurred.\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1388	lexical	\N	\N	1387	{"text": "\\"We have been hearing Gregson's view of the matter,\\" Holmes observed.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1389	lexical	\N	\N	1388	{"text": "\\"Would you mind letting us know what you have seen and done?\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1390	lexical	\N	\N	1389	{"text": "\\"I have no objection,\\" Lestrade answered, seating himself.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1391	lexical	\N	\N	1390	{"text": "\\"I freely confess that I was of the opinion that Stangerson was concerned in the death of Drebber.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1392	lexical	\N	\N	1391	{"text": "This fresh development has shown me that I was completely mistaken.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1393	lexical	\N	\N	1392	{"text": "Full of the one idea, I set myself to find out what had become of the Secretary.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1394	lexical	\N	\N	1393	{"text": "They had been seen together at Euston Station about half-past eight on the evening of the third.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1395	lexical	\N	\N	1394	{"text": "At two in the morning Drebber had been found in the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1396	lexical	\N	\N	1395	{"text": "30 and the time of the crime, and what had become of him afterwards.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1397	lexical	\N	\N	1396	{"text": "I telegraphed to Liverpool, giving a description of the man, and warning them to keep a watch upon the American boats.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1398	lexical	\N	\N	1397	{"text": "I then set to work calling upon all the hotels and lodging-houses in the vicinity of Euston.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1399	lexical	\N	\N	1398	{"text": "You see, I argued that if Drebber and his companion had become separated, the natural course for the latter would be to put up somewhere in the vicinity for the night, and then to hang about the station again next morning.\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1400	lexical	\N	\N	1399	{"text": "where in the vicinity for the night, and then to hang about the station again next morning.\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1401	lexical	\N	\N	1400	{"text": "\\"They would be likely to agree on some meeting-place beforehand,\\" remarked Holmes.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1402	lexical	\N	\N	1401	{"text": "\\"So it proved.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1403	lexical	\N	\N	1402	{"text": "I spent the whole of yesterday evening in making enquiries entirely without avail.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1404	lexical	\N	\N	1403	{"text": "This morning I began very early, and at eight o'clock I reached Halliday's Private Hotel, in Little George Street.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1405	lexical	\N	\N	1404	{"text": "On my enquiry as to whether a Mr. Stangerson was living there, they at once answered me in the affirmative.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1406	lexical	\N	\N	1405	{"text": "\\"'No doubt you are the gentleman whom he was expecting,' they said.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1407	lexical	\N	\N	1406	{"text": "'He has been waiting for a gentleman for two days.'", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1408	lexical	\N	\N	1407	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1409	lexical	\N	\N	1408	{"text": "he now?' I asked.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1410	lexical	\N	\N	1409	{"text": "\\"'He is upstairs in bed.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1411	lexical	\N	\N	1410	{"text": "He wished to be called at nine.'", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1412	lexical	\N	\N	1411	{"text": "\\"'I will go up and see him at once,' I said.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1413	lexical	\N	\N	1412	{"text": "\\"It seemed to me that my sudden appearance might shake his nerves and lead him to say something unguarded.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1414	lexical	\N	\N	1413	{"text": "The Boots volunteered to show me the room: it was on the second floor, and there was a small corridor leading up to it.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1415	lexical	\N	\N	1414	{"text": "The Boots pointed out the door to me, and was about to go downstairs again when I saw something that made me feel sickish, in spite of my twenty years' experience.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1416	lexical	\N	\N	1415	{"text": "From under the door there curled a little red ribbon of blood, which had meandered across the passage and formed a little pool along the skirting at the other side.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1417	lexical	\N	\N	1416	{"text": "I gave a cry, which brought the Boots back.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1418	lexical	\N	\N	1417	{"text": "He nearly fainted when he saw it.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1419	lexical	\N	\N	1418	{"text": "The door was locked on the inside, but we put our shoulders to it, and knocked it in.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1420	lexical	\N	\N	1419	{"text": "The window of the room was open, and beside the window, all huddled up, lay the body of a man in his nightdress.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1421	lexical	\N	\N	1420	{"text": "He was quite dead, and had been for some time, for his limbs were rigid and cold.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1422	lexical	\N	\N	1421	{"text": "When we turned him over, the Boots recognized him at once as being the same gentleman who had engaged the room under the name of Joseph Stangerson.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1423	lexical	\N	\N	1422	{"text": "The cause of death was a deep stab in the left side, which must have penetrated the heart.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1424	lexical	\N	\N	1423	{"text": "And now comes the strangest part of the affair.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1425	lexical	\N	\N	1424	{"text": "What do you suppose was above the murdered man?\\"", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1426	lexical	\N	\N	1425	{"text": "I felt a creeping of the flesh, and a presentiment of coming horror, even before Sherlock Holmes answered.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1427	lexical	\N	\N	1426	{"text": "\\"The word RACHE, written in letters of blood,\\" he said.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1428	lexical	\N	\N	1427	{"text": "\\"That was it,\\" said Lestrade, in an awe-struck voice; and we were all silent for a while.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1429	lexical	\N	\N	1428	{"text": "There was something so methodical and so incomprehensible about the deeds of this unknown assassin, that it imparted a fresh ghastliness to his crimes.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1430	lexical	\N	\N	1429	{"text": "My nerves, which were steady enough on the field of battle tingled as I thought of it.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1431	lexical	\N	\N	1430	{"text": "\\"The man was seen,\\" continued Lestrade.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1432	lexical	\N	\N	1431	{"text": "\\"A milk boy, passing on his way to the dairy, happened to walk down the lane which leads from the mews at the back of the hotel.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1433	lexical	\N	\N	1432	{"text": "He noticed that a ladder, which usually lay there, was raised against one of the windows of the second floor, which was wide open.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1434	lexical	\N	\N	1433	{"text": "After passing, he looked back and saw a man descend the ladder.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1435	lexical	\N	\N	1434	{"text": "He came down so quietly and openly that the boy imagined him to be some carpenter or joiner at work in the hotel.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1436	lexical	\N	\N	1435	{"text": "He took no particular notice of him, beyond thinking in his own mind that it was early for him to be at work.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1437	lexical	\N	\N	1436	{"text": "He has an impression that the man was tall, had a reddish face, and was dressed in a long, brownish coat.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1438	lexical	\N	\N	1437	{"text": "He must have stayed in the room some little time after the murder, for we found blood-stained water in the basin, where he had washed his hands, and marks on the sheets where he had deliberately wiped his knife.\\"", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1439	lexical	\N	\N	1438	{"text": "I glanced at Holmes on hearing the description of the murderer, which tallied so exactly with his own.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1440	lexical	\N	\N	1439	{"text": "There was, however, no trace of exultation or satisfaction upon his face.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1441	lexical	\N	\N	1440	{"text": "\\"Did you find nothing in the room which could furnish a clue to the murderer?\\"", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1442	lexical	\N	\N	1441	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1443	lexical	\N	\N	1442	{"text": "\\"Nothing.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1444	lexical	\N	\N	1443	{"text": "Stangerson had Drebber's purse in his pocket, but it seems that this was usual, as he did all the paying.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1445	lexical	\N	\N	1444	{"text": "There was eighty odd pounds in it, but nothing had been taken.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1446	lexical	\N	\N	1445	{"text": "Whatever the motives of these extraordinary crimes, robbery is certainly not one of them.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1447	lexical	\N	\N	1446	{"text": "There were no papers or memoranda in the murdered man's pocket, except a single telegram, dated from Cleveland about a month ago, and containing the words, 'J.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1454	lexical	\N	\N	1453	{"text": "The man's novel, with which he had read himself to sleep was lying upon the bed, and his pipe was on a chair beside him.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1455	lexical	\N	\N	1454	{"text": "There was a glass of water on the table, and on the window-sill a small chip ointment box containing a couple of pills.\\"", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1456	lexical	\N	\N	1455	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes sprang from his chair with an exclamation of delight.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1457	lexical	\N	\N	1456	{"text": "\\"The last link,\\" he cried, exultantly.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1458	lexical	\N	\N	1457	{"text": "\\"My case is complete.\\"", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1459	lexical	\N	\N	1458	{"text": "The two detectives stared at him in amazement.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1460	lexical	\N	\N	1459	{"text": "\\"I have now in my hands,\\" my companion said, confidently, \\"all the threads which have formed such a tangle.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1461	lexical	\N	\N	1460	{"text": "There are, of course, details to be filled in, but I am as certain of all the main facts, from the time that Drebber parted from Stangerson at the station, up to the discovery of the body of the latter, as if I had seen them with my own eyes.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1464	lexical	\N	\N	1463	{"text": "\\"I have them,\\" said Lestrade, producing a small white box; \\"I took them and the purse and the telegram, intending to have them put in a place of safety at the Police Station.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1465	lexical	\N	\N	1464	{"text": "It was the merest chance my taking these pills, for I am bound to say that I do not attach any importance to them.\\"", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1466	lexical	\N	\N	1465	{"text": "\\"Give them here,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1467	lexical	\N	\N	1466	{"text": "\\"Now, Doctor,\\" turning to me, \\"are those ordinary pills?\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1468	lexical	\N	\N	1467	{"text": "They certainly were not.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1469	lexical	\N	\N	1468	{"text": "They were of a pearly grey colour, small, round, and almost transparent against the light.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1470	lexical	\N	\N	1469	{"text": "\\"From their lightness and transparency, I should imagine that they are soluble in water,\\" I remarked.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1471	lexical	\N	\N	1470	{"text": "\\"Precisely so,\\" answered Holmes.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1472	lexical	\N	\N	1471	{"text": "\\"Now would you mind going down and fetching that poor little devil of a terrier which has been bad so long, and which the landlady wanted you to put out of its pain yesterday.\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1473	lexical	\N	\N	1472	{"text": "I went downstairs and carried the dog upstairs in my arms.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1474	lexical	\N	\N	1473	{"text": "Its laboured breathing and glazing eye showed that it was not far from its end.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1475	lexical	\N	\N	1474	{"text": "Indeed, its snow-white muzzle proclaimed that it had already exceeded the usual term of canine existence.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1476	lexical	\N	\N	1475	{"text": "I placed it upon a cushion on the rug.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1477	lexical	\N	\N	1476	{"text": "\\"I will now cut one of these pills in two,\\" said Holmes, and drawing his penknife he suited the action to the word.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1478	lexical	\N	\N	1477	{"text": "\\"One half we return into the box for future purposes.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1479	lexical	\N	\N	1478	{"text": "The other half I will place in this wine glass, in which is a teaspoonful of water.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1480	lexical	\N	\N	1479	{"text": "You perceive that our friend, the Doctor, is right, and that it readily dissolves.\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1481	lexical	\N	\N	1480	{"text": "\\"This may be very interesting,\\" said Lestrade, in the injured tone of one who suspects that he is being laughed at, \\"I cannot see, however, what it has to do with the death of Mr. Joseph Stangerson.\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1482	lexical	\N	\N	1481	{"text": "\\"Patience, my friend, patience!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1483	lexical	\N	\N	1482	{"text": "You will find in time that it has everything to do with it.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1484	lexical	\N	\N	1483	{"text": "I shall now add a little milk to make the mixture palatable, and on presenting it to the dog we find that he laps it up readily enough.\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1485	lexical	\N	\N	1484	{"text": "As he spoke he turned the contents of the wine glass into a saucer and placed it in front of the terrier, who speedily licked it dry.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1486	lexical	\N	\N	1485	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes' earnest demeanour had so far convinced us that we all sat in silence, watching the animal intently, and expecting some startling effect.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1487	lexical	\N	\N	1486	{"text": "None such appeared, however.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1522	lexical	\N	\N	1521	{"text": "Young Charpentier could not have been engaged in this second affair.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1488	lexical	\N	\N	1487	{"text": "The dog continued to lie stretched upon the cushion, breathing in a laboured way, but apparently neither the better nor the worse for its draught.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1489	lexical	\N	\N	1488	{"text": "Holmes had taken out his watch, and as minute followed minute without result, an expression of the utmost chagrin and disappointment appeared upon his features.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1490	lexical	\N	\N	1489	{"text": "He gnawed his lip, drummed his fingers upon the table, and showed every other symptom of acute impatience.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1491	lexical	\N	\N	1490	{"text": "So great was his emotion, that I felt sincerely sorry for him, while the two detectives smiled derisively, by no means displeased at this check which he had met.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1492	lexical	\N	\N	1491	{"text": "\\"It can't be a coincidence,\\" he cried, at last springing from his chair and pacing wildly up and down the room; \\"it is impossible that it should be a mere coincidence.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1493	lexical	\N	\N	1492	{"text": "The very pills which I suspected in the case of Drebber are actually found after the death of Stangerson.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1494	lexical	\N	\N	1493	{"text": "And yet they are inert.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1495	lexical	\N	\N	1494	{"text": "What can it mean?", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1496	lexical	\N	\N	1495	{"text": "Surely my whole chain of reasoning cannot have been false.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1497	lexical	\N	\N	1496	{"text": "It is impossible!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1498	lexical	\N	\N	1497	{"text": "And yet this wretched dog is none the worse.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1499	lexical	\N	\N	1498	{"text": "Ah, I have it!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1500	lexical	\N	\N	1499	{"text": "I have it!\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1501	lexical	\N	\N	1500	{"text": "With a perfect shriek of delight he rushed to the box, cut the other pill in two, dissolved it, added milk, and presented it to the terrier.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1502	lexical	\N	\N	1501	{"text": "The unfortunate creature's tongue seemed hardly to have been moistened in it before it gave a convulsive shiver in every limb, and lay as rigid and lifeless as if it had been struck by lightning.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1503	lexical	\N	\N	1502	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes drew a long breath, and wiped the perspiration from his forehead.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1504	lexical	\N	\N	1503	{"text": "\\"I should have more faith,\\" he said; \\"I ought to know by this time that when a fact appears to be opposed to a long train of deductions, it invariably proves to be capable of bearing some other interpretation.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1505	lexical	\N	\N	1504	{"text": "Of the two pills in that box one was of the most deadly poison, and the other was entirely harmless.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1506	lexical	\N	\N	1505	{"text": "I ought to have known that before ever I saw the box at all.\\"", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1507	lexical	\N	\N	1506	{"text": "This last statement appeared to me to be so startling, that I could hardly believe that he was in his sober senses.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1508	lexical	\N	\N	1507	{"text": "There was the dead dog, however, to prove that his conjecture had been correct.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1509	lexical	\N	\N	1508	{"text": "It seemed to me that the mists in my own mind were gradually clearing away, and I began to have a dim, vague perception of the truth.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1510	lexical	\N	\N	1509	{"text": "\\"All this seems strange to you,\\" continued Holmes, \\"because you failed at the beginning of the inquiry to grasp the importance of the single real clue which was presented to you.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1511	lexical	\N	\N	1510	{"text": "I had the good fortune to seize upon that, and everything which has occurred since then has served to confirm my original supposition, and, indeed, was the logical sequence of it.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1512	lexical	\N	\N	1511	{"text": "Hence things which have perplexed you and made the case more obscure, have served to enlighten me and to strengthen my conclusions.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1513	lexical	\N	\N	1512	{"text": "It is a mistake to confound strangeness with mystery.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1514	lexical	\N	\N	1513	{"text": "The most commonplace crime is often the most mysterious because it presents no new or special features from which deductions may be drawn.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1515	lexical	\N	\N	1514	{"text": "This murder would have been infinitely more difficult to unravel had the body of the victim been simply found lying in the roadway without any of those _outré_ and sensational accompaniments which have rendered it remarkable.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1516	lexical	\N	\N	1515	{"text": "These strange details, far from making the case more difficult, have really had the effect of making it less so.\\"", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1517	lexical	\N	\N	1516	{"text": "Mr. Gregson, who had listened to this address with considerable impatience, could contain himself no longer.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1518	lexical	\N	\N	1517	{"text": "\\"Look here, Mr. Sherlock Holmes,\\" he said, \\"we are all ready to acknowledge that you are a smart man, and that you have your own methods of working.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1519	lexical	\N	\N	1518	{"text": "We want something more than mere theory and preaching now, though.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1523	lexical	\N	\N	1522	{"text": "Lestrade went after his man, Stangerson, and it appears that he was wrong too.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1524	lexical	\N	\N	1523	{"text": "You have thrown out hints here, and hints there, and seem to know more than we do, but the time has come when we feel that we have a right to ask you straight how much you do know of the business.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1525	lexical	\N	\N	1524	{"text": "Can you name the man who did it?\\"", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1526	lexical	\N	\N	1525	{"text": "\\"I cannot help feeling that Gregson is right, sir,\\" remarked Lestrade.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1527	lexical	\N	\N	1526	{"text": "\\"We have both tried, and we have both failed.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1528	lexical	\N	\N	1527	{"text": "You have remarked more than once since I have been in the room that you had all the evidence which you require.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1529	lexical	\N	\N	1528	{"text": "Surely you will not withhold it any longer.\\"", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1530	lexical	\N	\N	1529	{"text": "\\"Any delay in arresting the assassin,\\" I observed, \\"might give him time to perpetrate some fresh atrocity.\\"", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1531	lexical	\N	\N	1530	{"text": "Thus pressed by us all, Holmes showed signs of irresolution.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	pills	entity	object	Pills	\N	{"description": "A couple of pills found in a chip ointment box and later produced in a white box.", "firstSection": "section_38"}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1532	lexical	\N	\N	1531	{"text": "He continued to walk up and down the room with his head sunk on his chest and his brows drawn down, as was his habit when lost in thought.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1533	lexical	\N	\N	1532	{"text": "\\"There will be no more murders,\\" he said at last, stopping abruptly and facing us.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1534	lexical	\N	\N	1533	{"text": "\\"You can put that consideration out of the question.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1535	lexical	\N	\N	1534	{"text": "You have asked me if I know the name of the assassin.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1536	lexical	\N	\N	1535	{"text": "I do.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1537	lexical	\N	\N	1536	{"text": "The mere knowing of his name is a small thing, however, compared with the power of laying our hands upon him.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1538	lexical	\N	\N	1537	{"text": "This I expect very shortly to do.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1539	lexical	\N	\N	1538	{"text": "I have good hopes of managing it through my own arrangements; but it is a thing which needs delicate handling, for we have a shrewd and desperate man to deal with, who is supported, as I have had occasion to prove, by another who is as clever as himself.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1540	lexical	\N	\N	1539	{"text": "As long as this man has no idea that anyone can have a clue there is some chance of securing him; but if he had the slightest suspicion, he would change his name, and vanish in an instant among the four million inhabitants of this great city.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1541	lexical	\N	\N	1540	{"text": "Without meaning to hurt either of your feelings, I am bound to say that I consider these men to be more than a match for the official force, and that is why I have not asked your assistance.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1542	lexical	\N	\N	1541	{"text": "If I fail I shall, of course, incur all the blame due to this omission; but that I am prepared for.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1543	lexical	\N	\N	1542	{"text": "At present I am ready to promise that the instant that I can communicate with you without endangering my own combinations, I shall do so.\\"", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1544	lexical	\N	\N	1543	{"text": "Gregson and Lestrade seemed to be far from satisfied by this assurance, or by the depreciating allusion to the detective police.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1545	lexical	\N	\N	1544	{"text": "The former had flushed up to the roots of his flaxen hair, while the other's beady eyes glistened with curiosity and resentment.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1546	lexical	\N	\N	1545	{"text": "Neither of them had time to speak, however, before there was a tap at the door, and the spokesman of the street Arabs, young Wiggins, introduced his insignificant and unsavoury person.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1547	lexical	\N	\N	1546	{"text": "\\"Please, sir,\\" he said, touching his forelock, \\"I have the cab downstairs.\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1548	lexical	\N	\N	1547	{"text": "\\"Good boy,\\" said Holmes, blandly.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1549	lexical	\N	\N	1548	{"text": "\\"Why don't you introduce this pattern at Scotland Yard?\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1550	lexical	\N	\N	1549	{"text": "he continued, taking a pair of steel handcuffs from a drawer.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1551	lexical	\N	\N	1550	{"text": "\\"See how beautifully the spring works.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1552	lexical	\N	\N	1551	{"text": "They fasten in an instant.\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1553	lexical	\N	\N	1552	{"text": "\\"The old pattern is good enough,\\" remarked Lestrade, \\"if we can only find the man to put them on.\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1554	lexical	\N	\N	1553	{"text": "\\"Very good, very good,\\" said Holmes, smiling.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1555	lexical	\N	\N	1554	{"text": "\\"The cabman may as well help me with my boxes.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1556	lexical	\N	\N	1555	{"text": "Just ask him to step up, Wiggins.\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_59	section	\N	Section 59	58	{"wordCount": 619}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1557	lexical	\N	\N	1556	{"text": "I was surprised to find my companion speaking as though he were about to set out on a journey, since he had not said anything to me about it.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1558	lexical	\N	\N	1557	{"text": "There was a small portmanteau in the room, and this he pulled out and began to strap.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1559	lexical	\N	\N	1558	{"text": "He was busily engaged at it when the cabman entered the room.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1560	lexical	\N	\N	1559	{"text": "\\"Just give me a help with this buckle, cabman,\\" he said, kneeling over his task, and never turning his head.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1561	lexical	\N	\N	1560	{"text": "The fellow came forward with a somewhat sullen, defiant air, and put down his hands to assist.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1562	lexical	\N	\N	1561	{"text": "At that instant there was a sharp click, the jangling of metal, and Sherlock Holmes sprang to his feet again.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1563	lexical	\N	\N	1562	{"text": "\\"Gentlemen,\\" he cried, with flashing eyes, \\"let me introduce you to Mr. Jefferson Hope, the murderer of Enoch Drebber and of Joseph Stangerson.\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1564	lexical	\N	\N	1563	{"text": "The whole thing occurred in a moment—so quickly that I had no time to realize it.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1565	lexical	\N	\N	1564	{"text": "I have a vivid recollection of that instant, of Holmes' triumphant expression and the ring of his voice, of the cabman's dazed, savage face, as he glared at the glittering handcuffs, which had appeared as if by magic upon his wrists.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1566	lexical	\N	\N	1565	{"text": "For a second or two we might have been a group of statues.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1567	lexical	\N	\N	1566	{"text": "Then, with an inarticulate roar of fury, the prisoner wrenched himself free from Holmes's grasp, and hurled himself through the window.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1568	lexical	\N	\N	1567	{"text": "Woodwork and glass gave way before him; but before he got quite through, Gregson, Lestrade, and Holmes sprang upon him like so many staghounds.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1569	lexical	\N	\N	1568	{"text": "He was dragged back into the room, and then commenced a terrific conflict.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1570	lexical	\N	\N	1569	{"text": "So powerful and so fierce was he, that the four of us were shaken off again and again.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1571	lexical	\N	\N	1570	{"text": "He appeared to have the convulsive strength of a man in an epileptic fit.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1572	lexical	\N	\N	1571	{"text": "His face and hands were terribly mangled by his passage through the glass, but loss of blood had no effect in diminishing his resistance.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1573	lexical	\N	\N	1572	{"text": "It was not until Lestrade succeeded in getting his hand inside his neckcloth and half-strangling him that we made him realize that his struggles were of no avail; and even then we felt no security until we had pinioned his feet as well as his hands.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1574	lexical	\N	\N	1573	{"text": "That done, we rose to our feet breathless and panting.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1575	lexical	\N	\N	1574	{"text": "\\"We have his cab,\\" said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1576	lexical	\N	\N	1575	{"text": "\\"It will serve to take him to Scotland Yard.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1577	lexical	\N	\N	1576	{"text": "And now, gentlemen,\\" he continued, with a pleasant smile, \\"we have reached the end of our little mystery.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1578	lexical	\N	\N	1577	{"text": "You are very welcome to put any questions that you like to me now, and there is no danger that I will refuse to answer them.\\"", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1579	lexical	\N	\N	1578	{"text": "PART II.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1580	lexical	\N	\N	1579	{"text": "_The Country of the Saints._", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1581	lexical	\N	\N	1580	{"text": "CHAPTER I.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1582	lexical	\N	\N	1581	{"text": "ON THE GREAT ALKALI PLAIN.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1583	lexical	\N	\N	1582	{"text": "In the central portion of the great North American Continent there lies an arid and repulsive desert, which for many a long year served as a barrier against the advance of civilisation.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1584	lexical	\N	\N	1583	{"text": "From the Sierra Nevada to Nebraska, and from the Yellowstone River in the north to the Colorado upon the south, is a region of desolation and silence.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1585	lexical	\N	\N	1584	{"text": "Nor is Nature always in one mood throughout this grim district.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1586	lexical	\N	\N	1585	{"text": "It comprises snow-capped and lofty mountains, and dark and gloomy valleys.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1587	lexical	\N	\N	1586	{"text": "There are swift-flowing rivers which dash through jagged cañons; and there are enormous plains, which in winter are white with snow, and in summer are grey with the saline alkali dust.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1588	lexical	\N	\N	1587	{"text": "They all preserve, however, the common characteristics of barrenness, inhospitality, and misery.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1589	lexical	\N	\N	1588	{"text": "There are no inhabitants of this land of despair.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_60	section	\N	Section 60	59	{"wordCount": 688}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1590	lexical	\N	\N	1589	{"text": "A band of Pawnees or of Blackfeet may occasionally traverse it in order to reach other hunting-grounds, but the hardiest of the braves are glad to lose sight of those awesome plains, and to find themselves once more upon their prairies.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1591	lexical	\N	\N	1590	{"text": "The coyote skulks among the scrub, the buzzard flaps heavily through the air, and the clumsy grizzly bear lumbers through the dark ravines, and picks up such sustenance as it can amongst the rocks.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1592	lexical	\N	\N	1591	{"text": "These are the sole dwellers in the wilderness.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1593	lexical	\N	\N	1592	{"text": "In the whole world there can be no more dreary view than that from the northern slope of the Sierra Blanco.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1594	lexical	\N	\N	1593	{"text": "As far as the eye can reach stretches the great flat plain-land, all dusted over with patches of alkali, and intersected by clumps of the dwarfish chaparral bushes.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1595	lexical	\N	\N	1594	{"text": "On the extreme verge of the horizon lie a long chain of mountain peaks, with their rugged summits flecked with snow.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1596	lexical	\N	\N	1595	{"text": "In this great stretch of country there is no sign of life, nor of anything appertaining to life.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1597	lexical	\N	\N	1596	{"text": "There is no bird in the steel-blue heaven, no movement upon the dull, grey earth—above all, there is absolute silence.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1598	lexical	\N	\N	1597	{"text": "Listen as one may, there is no shadow of a sound in all that mighty wilderness; nothing but silence—complete and heart-subduing silence.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1599	lexical	\N	\N	1598	{"text": "It has been said there is nothing appertaining to life upon the broad plain.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1600	lexical	\N	\N	1599	{"text": "That is hardly true.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1601	lexical	\N	\N	1600	{"text": "Looking down from the Sierra Blanco, one sees a pathway traced out across the desert, which winds away and is lost in the extreme distance.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1602	lexical	\N	\N	1601	{"text": "It is rutted with wheels and trodden down by the feet of many adventurers.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1603	lexical	\N	\N	1602	{"text": "Here and there there are scattered white objects which glisten in the sun, and stand out against the dull deposit of alkali.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1604	lexical	\N	\N	1603	{"text": "Approach, and examine them!", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1605	lexical	\N	\N	1604	{"text": "They are bones: some large and coarse, others smaller and more delicate.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1606	lexical	\N	\N	1605	{"text": "The former have belonged to oxen, and the latter to men.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1607	lexical	\N	\N	1606	{"text": "For fifteen hundred miles one may trace this ghastly caravan route by these scattered remains of those who had fallen by the wayside.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1608	lexical	\N	\N	1607	{"text": "Looking down on this very scene, there stood upon the fourth of May, eighteen hundred and forty-seven, a solitary traveller.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1609	lexical	\N	\N	1608	{"text": "His appearance was such that he might have been the very genius or demon of the region.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1610	lexical	\N	\N	1609	{"text": "An observer would have found it difficult to say whether he was nearer to forty or to sixty.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1611	lexical	\N	\N	1610	{"text": "His face was lean and haggard, and the brown parchment-like skin was drawn tightly over the projecting bones; his long, brown hair and beard were all flecked and dashed with white; his eyes were sunken in his head, and burned with an unnatural lustre; while the hand which grasped his rifle was hardly more fleshy than that of a skeleton.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1612	lexical	\N	\N	1611	{"text": "As he stood, he leaned upon his weapon for support, and yet his tall figure and the massive framework of his bones suggested a wiry and vigorous constitution.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1613	lexical	\N	\N	1612	{"text": "His gaunt face, however, and his clothes, which hung so baggily over his shrivelled limbs, proclaimed what it was that gave him that senile and decrepit appearance.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1614	lexical	\N	\N	1613	{"text": "The man was dying—dying from hunger and from thirst.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1615	lexical	\N	\N	1614	{"text": "He had toiled painfully down the ravine, and on to this little elevation, in the vain hope of seeing some signs of water.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1616	lexical	\N	\N	1615	{"text": "Now the great salt plain stretched before his eyes, and the distant belt of savage mountains, without a sign anywhere of plant or tree, which might indicate the presence of moisture.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1617	lexical	\N	\N	1616	{"text": "In all that broad landscape there was no gleam of hope.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1618	lexical	\N	\N	1617	{"text": "North, and east, and west he looked with wild questioning eyes, and then he realised that his wanderings had come to an end, and that there, on that barren crag, he was about to die.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1619	lexical	\N	\N	1618	{"text": "\\"Why not here, as well as in a feather bed, twenty years hence,\\" he muttered, as he seated himself in the shelter of a boulder.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1889	lexical	\N	\N	1888	{"text": "\\"Neither would I,\\" said her companion.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1620	lexical	\N	\N	1619	{"text": "Before sitting down, he had deposited upon the ground his useless rifle, and also a large bundle tied up in a grey shawl, which he had carried slung over his right shoulder.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1621	lexical	\N	\N	1620	{"text": "It appeared to be somewhat too heavy for his strength, for in lowering it, it came down on the ground with some little violence.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1622	lexical	\N	\N	1621	{"text": "Instantly there broke from the grey parcel a little moaning cry, and from it there protruded a small, scared face, with very bright brown eyes, and two little speckled, dimpled fists.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1623	lexical	\N	\N	1622	{"text": "\\"You've hurt me!\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1624	lexical	\N	\N	1623	{"text": "said a childish voice reproachfully.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1625	lexical	\N	\N	1624	{"text": "\\"Have I though,\\" the man answered penitently, \\"I didn't go for to do it.\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1626	lexical	\N	\N	1625	{"text": "As he spoke he unwrapped the grey shawl and extricated a pretty little girl of about five years of age, whose dainty shoes and smart pink frock with its little linen apron all bespoke a mother's care.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1627	lexical	\N	\N	1626	{"text": "The child was pale and wan, but her healthy arms and legs showed that she had suffered less than her companion.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1628	lexical	\N	\N	1627	{"text": "\\"How is it now?\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1629	lexical	\N	\N	1628	{"text": "he answered anxiously, for she was still rubbing the towsy golden curls which covered the back of her head.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1630	lexical	\N	\N	1629	{"text": "\\"Kiss it and make it well,\\" she said, with perfect gravity, showing the injured part up to him.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1631	lexical	\N	\N	1630	{"text": "\\"That's what mother used to do.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1632	lexical	\N	\N	1631	{"text": "Where's mother?\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1633	lexical	\N	\N	1632	{"text": "\\"Mother's gone.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1634	lexical	\N	\N	1633	{"text": "I guess you'll see her before long.\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1635	lexical	\N	\N	1634	{"text": "\\"Gone, eh!\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1636	lexical	\N	\N	1635	{"text": "said the little girl.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1637	lexical	\N	\N	1636	{"text": "\\"Funny, she didn't say good-bye; she 'most always did if she was just goin' over to Auntie's for tea, and now she's been away three days.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1638	lexical	\N	\N	1637	{"text": "Say, it's awful dry, ain't it?", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1639	lexical	\N	\N	1638	{"text": "Ain't there no water, nor nothing to eat?\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1640	lexical	\N	\N	1639	{"text": "\\"No, there ain't nothing, dearie.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1641	lexical	\N	\N	1640	{"text": "You'll just need to be patient awhile, and then you'll be all right.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1642	lexical	\N	\N	1641	{"text": "Put your head up agin me like that, and then you'll feel bullier.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1643	lexical	\N	\N	1642	{"text": "It ain't easy to talk when your lips is like leather, but I guess I'd best let you know how the cards lie.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1644	lexical	\N	\N	1643	{"text": "What's that you've got?\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1645	lexical	\N	\N	1644	{"text": "\\"Pretty things!", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1646	lexical	\N	\N	1645	{"text": "fine things!\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1647	lexical	\N	\N	1646	{"text": "cried the little girl enthusiastically, holding up two glittering fragments of mica.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1648	lexical	\N	\N	1647	{"text": "\\"When we goes back to home I'll give them to brother Bob.\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1649	lexical	\N	\N	1648	{"text": "\\"You'll see prettier things than them soon,\\" said the man confidently.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1650	lexical	\N	\N	1649	{"text": "\\"You just wait a bit.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1651	lexical	\N	\N	1650	{"text": "I was going to tell you though—you remember when we left the river?\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1652	lexical	\N	\N	1651	{"text": "\\"Oh, yes.\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1653	lexical	\N	\N	1652	{"text": "\\"Well, we reckoned we'd strike another river soon, d'ye see.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1654	lexical	\N	\N	1653	{"text": "But there was somethin' wrong; compasses, or map, or somethin', and it didn't turn up.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1655	lexical	\N	\N	1654	{"text": "Water ran out.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1656	lexical	\N	\N	1655	{"text": "Just except a little drop for the likes of you and—and——\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1657	lexical	\N	\N	1656	{"text": "\\"And you couldn't wash yourself,\\" interrupted his companion gravely, staring up at his grimy visage.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1658	lexical	\N	\N	1657	{"text": "\\"No, nor drink.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1659	lexical	\N	\N	1658	{"text": "And Mr. Bender, he was the fust to go, and then Indian Pete, and then Mrs. McGregor, and then Johnny Hones, and then, dearie, your mother.\\"", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1660	lexical	\N	\N	1659	{"text": "\\"Then mother's a deader too,\\" cried the little girl dropping her face in her pinafore and sobbing bitterly.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1661	lexical	\N	\N	1660	{"text": "\\"Yes, they all went except you and me.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1662	lexical	\N	\N	1661	{"text": "Then I thought there was some chance of water in this direction, so I heaved you over my shoulder and we tramped it together.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1663	lexical	\N	\N	1662	{"text": "It don't seem as though we've improved matters.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1664	lexical	\N	\N	1663	{"text": "There's an almighty small chance for us now!\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1665	lexical	\N	\N	1664	{"text": "\\"Do you mean that we are going to die too?\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1666	lexical	\N	\N	1665	{"text": "asked the child, checking her sobs, and raising her tear-stained face.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1667	lexical	\N	\N	1666	{"text": "\\"I guess that's about the size of it.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1668	lexical	\N	\N	1667	{"text": "\\"Why didn't you say so before?\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1669	lexical	\N	\N	1668	{"text": "she said, laughing gleefully.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1670	lexical	\N	\N	1669	{"text": "\\"You gave me such a fright.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1671	lexical	\N	\N	1670	{"text": "Why, of course, now as long as we die we'll be with mother again.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1672	lexical	\N	\N	1671	{"text": "\\"Yes, you will, dearie.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1673	lexical	\N	\N	1672	{"text": "\\"And you too.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1674	lexical	\N	\N	1673	{"text": "I'll tell her how awful good you've been.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1675	lexical	\N	\N	1674	{"text": "I'll bet she meets us at the door of Heaven with a big pitcher of water, and a lot of buckwheat cakes, hot, and toasted on both sides, like Bob and me was fond of.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1676	lexical	\N	\N	1675	{"text": "How long will it be first?\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1677	lexical	\N	\N	1676	{"text": "\\"I don't know—not very long.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1678	lexical	\N	\N	1677	{"text": "The man's eyes were fixed upon the northern horizon.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1679	lexical	\N	\N	1678	{"text": "In the blue vault of the heaven there had appeared three little specks which increased in size every moment, so rapidly did they approach.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1680	lexical	\N	\N	1679	{"text": "They speedily resolved themselves into three large brown birds, which circled over the heads of the two wanderers, and then settled upon some rocks which overlooked them.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1681	lexical	\N	\N	1680	{"text": "They were buzzards, the vultures of the west, whose coming is the forerunner of death.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1682	lexical	\N	\N	1681	{"text": "\\"Cocks and hens,\\" cried the little girl gleefully, pointing at their ill-omened forms, and clapping her hands to make them rise.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1683	lexical	\N	\N	1682	{"text": "\\"Say, did God make this country?\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1684	lexical	\N	\N	1683	{"text": "\\"In course He did,\\" said her companion, rather startled by this unexpected question.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1685	lexical	\N	\N	1684	{"text": "\\"He made the country down in Illinois, and He made the Missouri,\\" the little girl continued.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1686	lexical	\N	\N	1685	{"text": "\\"I guess somebody else made the country in these parts.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1687	lexical	\N	\N	1686	{"text": "It's not nearly so well done.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1688	lexical	\N	\N	1687	{"text": "They forgot the water and the trees.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1689	lexical	\N	\N	1688	{"text": "\\"What would ye think of offering up prayer?\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1690	lexical	\N	\N	1689	{"text": "the man asked diffidently.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1691	lexical	\N	\N	1690	{"text": "\\"It ain't night yet,\\" she answered.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1692	lexical	\N	\N	1691	{"text": "\\"It don't matter.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1693	lexical	\N	\N	1692	{"text": "It ain't quite regular, but He won't mind that, you bet.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1694	lexical	\N	\N	1693	{"text": "You say over them ones that you used to say every night in the waggon when we was on the Plains.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1695	lexical	\N	\N	1694	{"text": "\\"Why don't you say some yourself?\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1696	lexical	\N	\N	1695	{"text": "the child asked, with wondering eyes.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1697	lexical	\N	\N	1696	{"text": "\\"I disremember them,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_61	section	\N	Section 61	60	{"wordCount": 623}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1698	lexical	\N	\N	1697	{"text": "\\"I hain't said none since I was half the height o' that gun.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1699	lexical	\N	\N	1698	{"text": "I guess it's never too late.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1700	lexical	\N	\N	1699	{"text": "You say them out, and I'll stand by and come in on the choruses.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1701	lexical	\N	\N	1700	{"text": "\\"Then you'll need to kneel down, and me too,\\" she said, laying the shawl out for that purpose.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1702	lexical	\N	\N	1701	{"text": "\\"You've got to put your hands up like this.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1703	lexical	\N	\N	1702	{"text": "It makes you feel kind o' good.\\"", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1704	lexical	\N	\N	1703	{"text": "It was a strange sight had there been anything but the buzzards to see it.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1705	lexical	\N	\N	1704	{"text": "Side by side on the narrow shawl knelt the two wanderers, the little prattling child and the reckless, hardened adventurer.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1706	lexical	\N	\N	1705	{"text": "Her chubby face, and his haggard, angular visage were both turned up to the cloudless heaven in heartfelt entreaty to that dread being with whom they were face to face, while the two voices—the one thin and clear, the other deep and harsh—united in the entreaty for mercy and forgiveness.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1707	lexical	\N	\N	1706	{"text": "The prayer finished, they resumed their seat in the shadow of the boulder until the child fell asleep, nestling upon the broad breast of her protector.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1708	lexical	\N	\N	1707	{"text": "He watched over her slumber for some time, but Nature proved to be too strong for him.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1709	lexical	\N	\N	1708	{"text": "For three days and three nights he had allowed himself neither rest nor repose.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1710	lexical	\N	\N	1709	{"text": "Slowly the eyelids drooped over the tired eyes, and the head sunk lower and lower upon the breast, until the man's grizzled beard was mixed with the gold tresses of his companion, and both slept the same deep and dreamless slumber.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1711	lexical	\N	\N	1710	{"text": "Had the wanderer remained awake for another half hour a strange sight would have met his eyes.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1712	lexical	\N	\N	1711	{"text": "Far away on the extreme verge of the alkali plain there rose up a little spray of dust, very slight at first, and hardly to be distinguished from the mists of the distance, but gradually growing higher and broader until it formed a solid, well-defined cloud.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1713	lexical	\N	\N	1712	{"text": "This cloud continued to increase in size until it became evident that it could only be raised by a great multitude of moving creatures.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1714	lexical	\N	\N	1713	{"text": "In more fertile spots the observer would have come to the conclusion that one of those great herds of bisons which graze upon the prairie land was approaching him.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1715	lexical	\N	\N	1714	{"text": "This was obviously impossible in these arid wilds.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1716	lexical	\N	\N	1715	{"text": "As the whirl of dust drew nearer to the solitary bluff upon which the two castaways were reposing, the canvas-covered tilts of waggons and the figures of armed horsemen began to show up through the haze, and the apparition revealed itself as being a great caravan upon its journey for the West.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1717	lexical	\N	\N	1716	{"text": "But what a caravan!", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1718	lexical	\N	\N	1717	{"text": "When the head of it had reached the base of the mountains, the rear was not yet visible on the horizon.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1719	lexical	\N	\N	1718	{"text": "Right across the enormous plain stretched the straggling array, waggons and carts, men on horseback, and men on foot.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1720	lexical	\N	\N	1719	{"text": "Innumerable women who staggered along under burdens, and children who toddled beside the waggons or peeped out from under the white coverings.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1721	lexical	\N	\N	1720	{"text": "This was evidently no ordinary party of immigrants, but rather some nomad people who had been compelled from stress of circumstances to seek themselves a new country.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1722	lexical	\N	\N	1721	{"text": "There rose through the clear air a confused clattering and rumbling from this great mass of humanity, with the creaking of wheels and the neighing of horses.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1723	lexical	\N	\N	1722	{"text": "Loud as it was, it was not sufficient to rouse the two tired wayfarers above them.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1724	lexical	\N	\N	1723	{"text": "At the head of the column there rode a score or more of grave ironfaced men, clad in sombre homespun garments and armed with rifles.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1725	lexical	\N	\N	1724	{"text": "On reaching the base of the bluff they halted, and held a short council among themselves.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1726	lexical	\N	\N	1725	{"text": "\\"The wells are to the right, my brothers,\\" said one, a hard-lipped, clean-shaven man with grizzly hair.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1727	lexical	\N	\N	1726	{"text": "\\"To the right of the Sierra Blanco—so we shall reach the Rio Grande,\\" said another.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1728	lexical	\N	\N	1727	{"text": "\\"Fear not for water,\\" cried a third.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_62	section	\N	Section 62	61	{"wordCount": 614}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1729	lexical	\N	\N	1728	{"text": "\\"He who could draw it from the rocks will not now abandon His own chosen people.\\"", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1730	lexical	\N	\N	1729	{"text": "\\"Amen!", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1731	lexical	\N	\N	1730	{"text": "Amen!\\"", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1732	lexical	\N	\N	1731	{"text": "responded the whole party.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1733	lexical	\N	\N	1732	{"text": "They were about to resume their journey when one of the youngest and keenest-eyed uttered an exclamation and pointed up at the rugged crag above them.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1734	lexical	\N	\N	1733	{"text": "From its summit there fluttered a little wisp of pink, showing up hard and bright against the grey rocks behind.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1735	lexical	\N	\N	1734	{"text": "At the sight there was a general reining up of horses and unslinging of guns, while fresh horsemen came galloping up to reinforce the vanguard.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1736	lexical	\N	\N	1735	{"text": "The word \\"Redskins\\" was on every lip.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1737	lexical	\N	\N	1736	{"text": "\\"There can't be any number of Injuns here,\\" said the elderly man who appeared to be in command.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1738	lexical	\N	\N	1737	{"text": "\\"We have passed the Pawnees, and there are no other tribes until we cross the great mountains.\\"", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1739	lexical	\N	\N	1738	{"text": "\\"Shall I go forward and see, Brother Stangerson,\\" asked one of the band.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1740	lexical	\N	\N	1739	{"text": "\\"And I,\\" \\"and I,\\" cried a dozen voices.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1741	lexical	\N	\N	1740	{"text": "\\"Leave your horses below and we will await you here,\\" the Elder answered.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1742	lexical	\N	\N	1741	{"text": "In a moment the young fellows had dismounted, fastened their horses, and were ascending the precipitous slope which led up to the object which had excited their curiosity.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1743	lexical	\N	\N	1742	{"text": "They advanced rapidly and noiselessly, with the confidence and dexterity of practised scouts.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1744	lexical	\N	\N	1743	{"text": "The watchers from the plain below could see them flit from rock to rock until their figures stood out against the skyline.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1745	lexical	\N	\N	1744	{"text": "The young man who had first given the alarm was leading them.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1746	lexical	\N	\N	1745	{"text": "Suddenly his followers saw him throw up his hands, as though overcome with astonishment, and on joining him they were affected in the same way by the sight which met their eyes.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1747	lexical	\N	\N	1746	{"text": "On the little plateau which crowned the barren hill there stood a single giant boulder, and against this boulder there lay a tall man, long-bearded and hard-featured, but of an excessive thinness.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1748	lexical	\N	\N	1747	{"text": "His placid face and regular breathing showed that he was fast asleep.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1749	lexical	\N	\N	1748	{"text": "Beside him lay a little child, with her round white arms encircling his brown sinewy neck, and her golden haired head resting upon the breast of his velveteen tunic.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1750	lexical	\N	\N	1749	{"text": "Her rosy lips were parted, showing the regular line of snow-white teeth within, and a playful smile played over her infantile features.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1751	lexical	\N	\N	1750	{"text": "Her plump little white legs terminating in white socks and neat shoes with shining buckles, offered a strange contrast to the long shrivelled members of her companion.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1752	lexical	\N	\N	1751	{"text": "On the ledge of rock above this strange couple there stood three solemn buzzards, who, at the sight of the new comers uttered raucous screams of disappointment and flapped sullenly away.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1753	lexical	\N	\N	1752	{"text": "The cries of the foul birds awoke the two sleepers who stared about them in bewilderment.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1754	lexical	\N	\N	1753	{"text": "The man staggered to his feet and looked down upon the plain which had been so desolate when sleep had overtaken him, and which was now traversed by this enormous body of men and of beasts.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1755	lexical	\N	\N	1754	{"text": "His face assumed an expression of incredulity as he gazed, and he passed his boney hand over his eyes.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1756	lexical	\N	\N	1755	{"text": "\\"This is what they call delirium, I guess,\\" he muttered.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1757	lexical	\N	\N	1756	{"text": "The child stood beside him, holding on to the skirt of his coat, and said nothing but looked all round her with the wondering questioning gaze of childhood.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1758	lexical	\N	\N	1757	{"text": "The rescuing party were speedily able to convince the two castaways that their appearance was no delusion.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1759	lexical	\N	\N	1758	{"text": "One of them seized the little girl, and hoisted her upon his shoulder, while two others supported her gaunt companion, and assisted him towards the waggons.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1760	lexical	\N	\N	1759	{"text": "\\"My name is John Ferrier,\\" the wanderer explained; \\"me and that little un are all that's left o' twenty-one people.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1761	lexical	\N	\N	1760	{"text": "The rest is all dead o' thirst and hunger away down in the south.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1762	lexical	\N	\N	1761	{"text": "\\"Is she your child?\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1763	lexical	\N	\N	1762	{"text": "asked someone.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1764	lexical	\N	\N	1763	{"text": "\\"I guess she is now,\\" the other cried, defiantly; \\"she's mine 'cause I saved her.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1765	lexical	\N	\N	1764	{"text": "No man will take her from me.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1766	lexical	\N	\N	1765	{"text": "She's Lucy Ferrier from this day on.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1767	lexical	\N	\N	1766	{"text": "Who are you, though?\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1768	lexical	\N	\N	1767	{"text": "he continued, glancing with curiosity at his stalwart, sunburned rescuers; \\"there seems to be a powerful lot of ye.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1769	lexical	\N	\N	1768	{"text": "\\"Nigh upon ten thousand,\\" said one of the young men; \\"we are the persecuted children of God—the chosen of the Angel Merona.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1770	lexical	\N	\N	1769	{"text": "\\"I never heard tell on him,\\" said the wanderer.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1771	lexical	\N	\N	1770	{"text": "\\"He appears to have chosen a fair crowd of ye.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1772	lexical	\N	\N	1771	{"text": "\\"Do not jest at that which is sacred,\\" said the other sternly.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1773	lexical	\N	\N	1772	{"text": "\\"We are of those who believe in those sacred writings, drawn in Egyptian letters on plates of beaten gold, which were handed unto the holy Joseph Smith at Palmyra.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1774	lexical	\N	\N	1773	{"text": "We have come from Nauvoo, in the State of Illinois, where we had founded our temple.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1775	lexical	\N	\N	1774	{"text": "We have come to seek a refuge from the violent man and from the godless, even though it be the heart of the desert.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1776	lexical	\N	\N	1775	{"text": "The name of Nauvoo evidently recalled recollections to John Ferrier.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1777	lexical	\N	\N	1776	{"text": "\\"I see,\\" he said, \\"you are the Mormons.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1778	lexical	\N	\N	1777	{"text": "\\"We are the Mormons,\\" answered his companions with one voice.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1779	lexical	\N	\N	1778	{"text": "\\"And where are you going?\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1780	lexical	\N	\N	1779	{"text": "\\"We do not know.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1781	lexical	\N	\N	1780	{"text": "The hand of God is leading us under the person of our Prophet.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1782	lexical	\N	\N	1781	{"text": "You must come before him.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1783	lexical	\N	\N	1782	{"text": "He shall say what is to be done with you.\\"", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1784	lexical	\N	\N	1783	{"text": "They had reached the base of the hill by this time, and were surrounded by crowds of the pilgrims—pale-faced meek-looking women, strong laughing children, and anxious earnest-eyed men.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1785	lexical	\N	\N	1784	{"text": "Many were the cries of astonishment and of commiseration which arose from them when they perceived the youth of one of the strangers and the destitution of the other.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1786	lexical	\N	\N	1785	{"text": "Their escort did not halt, however, but pushed on, followed by a great crowd of Mormons, until they reached a waggon, which was conspicuous for its great size and for the gaudiness and smartness of its appearance.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1787	lexical	\N	\N	1786	{"text": "Six horses were yoked to it, whereas the others were furnished with two, or, at most, four a-piece.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1788	lexical	\N	\N	1787	{"text": "Beside the driver there sat a man who could not have been more than thirty years of age, but whose massive head and resolute expression marked him as a leader.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1789	lexical	\N	\N	1788	{"text": "He was reading a brown-backed volume, but as the crowd approached he laid it aside, and listened attentively to an account of the episode.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1790	lexical	\N	\N	1789	{"text": "Then he turned to the two castaways.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1791	lexical	\N	\N	1790	{"text": "\\"If we take you with us,\\" he said, in solemn words, \\"it can only be as believers in our own creed.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1792	lexical	\N	\N	1791	{"text": "We shall have no wolves in our fold.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1793	lexical	\N	\N	1792	{"text": "Better far that your bones should bleach in this wilderness than that you should prove to be that little speck of decay which in time corrupts the whole fruit.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1794	lexical	\N	\N	1793	{"text": "Will you come with us on these terms?\\"", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1795	lexical	\N	\N	1794	{"text": "\\"Guess I'll come with you on any terms,\\" said Ferrier, with such emphasis that the grave Elders could not restrain a smile.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1796	lexical	\N	\N	1795	{"text": "The leader alone retained his stern, impressive expression.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1797	lexical	\N	\N	1796	{"text": "\\"Take him, Brother Stangerson,\\" he said, \\"give him food and drink, and the child likewise.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1798	lexical	\N	\N	1797	{"text": "Let it be your task also to teach him our holy creed.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1799	lexical	\N	\N	1798	{"text": "We have delayed long enough.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1800	lexical	\N	\N	1799	{"text": "Forward!", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1801	lexical	\N	\N	1800	{"text": "On, on to Zion!\\"", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1802	lexical	\N	\N	1801	{"text": "\\"On, on to Zion!\\"", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1803	lexical	\N	\N	1802	{"text": "cried the crowd of Mormons, and the words rippled down the long caravan, passing from mouth to mouth until they died away in a dull murmur in the far distance.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	chip_ointment_box	entity	object	Chip ointment box	\N	{"description": "A small chip ointment box that contained a couple of pills.", "firstSection": "section_38"}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1804	lexical	\N	\N	1803	{"text": "With a cracking of whips and a creaking of wheels the great waggons got into motion, and soon the whole caravan was winding along once more.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1805	lexical	\N	\N	1804	{"text": "The Elder to whose care the two waifs had been committed, led them to his waggon, where a meal was already awaiting them.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1806	lexical	\N	\N	1805	{"text": "\\"You shall remain here,\\" he said.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1807	lexical	\N	\N	1806	{"text": "\\"In a few days you will have recovered from your fatigues.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1808	lexical	\N	\N	1807	{"text": "In the meantime, remember that now and for ever you are of our religion.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1809	lexical	\N	\N	1808	{"text": "Brigham Young has said it, and he has spoken with the voice of Joseph Smith, which is the voice of God.\\"", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1810	lexical	\N	\N	1809	{"text": "CHAPTER II.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1811	lexical	\N	\N	1810	{"text": "THE FLOWER OF UTAH.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1812	lexical	\N	\N	1811	{"text": "This is not the place to commemorate the trials and privations endured by the immigrant Mormons before they came to their final haven.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1813	lexical	\N	\N	1812	{"text": "From the shores of the Mississippi to the western slopes of the Rocky Mountains they had struggled on with a constancy almost unparalleled in history.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1814	lexical	\N	\N	1813	{"text": "The savage man, and the savage beast, hunger, thirst, fatigue, and disease—every impediment which Nature could place in the way, had all been overcome with Anglo-Saxon tenacity.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1815	lexical	\N	\N	1814	{"text": "Yet the long journey and the accumulated terrors had shaken the hearts of the stoutest among them.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1816	lexical	\N	\N	1815	{"text": "There was not one who did not sink upon his knees in heartfelt prayer when they saw the broad valley of Utah bathed in the sunlight beneath them, and learned from the lips of their leader that this was the promised land, and that these virgin acres were to be theirs for evermore.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1817	lexical	\N	\N	1816	{"text": "Young speedily proved himself to be a skilful administrator as well as a resolute chief.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1818	lexical	\N	\N	1817	{"text": "Maps were drawn and charts prepared, in which the future city was sketched out.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1819	lexical	\N	\N	1818	{"text": "All around farms were apportioned and allotted in proportion to the standing of each individual.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1820	lexical	\N	\N	1819	{"text": "The tradesman was put to his trade and the artisan to his calling.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1821	lexical	\N	\N	1820	{"text": "In the town streets and squares sprang up, as if by magic.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1822	lexical	\N	\N	1821	{"text": "In the country there was draining and hedging, planting and clearing, until the next summer saw the whole country golden with the wheat crop.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1823	lexical	\N	\N	1822	{"text": "Everything prospered in the strange settlement.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1824	lexical	\N	\N	1823	{"text": "Above all, the great temple which they had erected in the centre of the city grew ever taller and larger.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1825	lexical	\N	\N	1824	{"text": "From the first blush of dawn until the closing of the twilight, the clatter of the hammer and the rasp of the saw was never absent from the monument which the immigrants erected to Him who had led them safe through many dangers.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1826	lexical	\N	\N	1825	{"text": "The two castaways, John Ferrier and the little girl who had shared his fortunes and had been adopted as his daughter, accompanied the Mormons to the end of their great pilgrimage.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1827	lexical	\N	\N	1826	{"text": "Little Lucy Ferrier was borne along pleasantly enough in Elder Stangerson's waggon, a retreat which she shared with the Mormon's three wives and with his son, a headstrong forward boy of twelve.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1828	lexical	\N	\N	1827	{"text": "Having rallied, with the elasticity of childhood, from the shock caused by her mother's death, she soon became a pet with the women, and reconciled herself to this new life in her moving canvas-covered home.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1890	lexical	\N	\N	1889	{"text": "\\"You!", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1829	lexical	\N	\N	1828	{"text": "In the meantime Ferrier having recovered from his privations, distinguished himself as a useful guide and an indefatigable hunter.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1830	lexical	\N	\N	1829	{"text": "So rapidly did he gain the esteem of his new companions, that when they reached the end of their wanderings, it was unanimously agreed that he should be provided with as large and as fertile a tract of land as any of the settlers, with the exception of Young himself, and of Stangerson, Kemball, Johnston, and Drebber, who were the four principal Elders.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1831	lexical	\N	\N	1830	{"text": "On the farm thus acquired John Ferrier built himself a substantial log-house, which received so many additions in succeeding years that it grew into a roomy villa.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1832	lexical	\N	\N	1831	{"text": "He was a man of a practical turn of mind, keen in his dealings and skilful with his hands.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1833	lexical	\N	\N	1832	{"text": "His iron constitution enabled him to work morning and evening at improving and tilling his lands.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1834	lexical	\N	\N	1833	{"text": "Hence it came about that his farm and all that belonged to him prospered exceedingly.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1835	lexical	\N	\N	1834	{"text": "In three years he was better off than his neighbours, in six he was well-to-do, in nine he was rich, and in twelve there were not half a dozen men in the whole of Salt Lake City who could compare with him.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1836	lexical	\N	\N	1835	{"text": "From the great inland sea to the distant Wahsatch Mountains there was no name better known than that of John Ferrier.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1837	lexical	\N	\N	1836	{"text": "There was one way and only one in which he offended the susceptibilities of his co-religionists.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1838	lexical	\N	\N	1837	{"text": "No argument or persuasion could ever induce him to set up a female establishment after the manner of his companions.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1839	lexical	\N	\N	1838	{"text": "He never gave reasons for this persistent refusal, but contented himself by resolutely and inflexibly adhering to his determination.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1840	lexical	\N	\N	1839	{"text": "There were some who accused him of lukewarmness in his adopted religion, and others who put it down to greed of wealth and reluctance to incur expense.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1841	lexical	\N	\N	1840	{"text": "Others, again, spoke of some early love affair, and of a fair-haired girl who had pined away on the shores of the Atlantic.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1842	lexical	\N	\N	1841	{"text": "Whatever the reason, Ferrier remained strictly celibate.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1843	lexical	\N	\N	1842	{"text": "In every other respect he conformed to the religion of the young settlement, and gained the name of being an orthodox and straight-walking man.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1844	lexical	\N	\N	1843	{"text": "Lucy Ferrier grew up within the log-house, and assisted her adopted father in all his undertakings.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1845	lexical	\N	\N	1844	{"text": "The keen air of the mountains and the balsamic odour of the pine trees took the place of nurse and mother to the young girl.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1846	lexical	\N	\N	1845	{"text": "As year succeeded to year she grew taller and stronger, her cheek more ruddy, and her step more elastic.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1847	lexical	\N	\N	1846	{"text": "Many a wayfarer upon the high road which ran by Ferrier's farm felt long-forgotten thoughts revive in their mind as they watched her lithe girlish figure tripping through the wheatfields, or met her mounted upon her father's mustang, and managing it with all the ease and grace of a true child of the West.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1848	lexical	\N	\N	1847	{"text": "So the bud blossomed into a flower, and the year which saw her father the richest of the farmers left her as fair a specimen of American girlhood as could be found in the whole Pacific slope.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1849	lexical	\N	\N	1848	{"text": "It was not the father, however, who first discovered that the child had developed into the woman.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1850	lexical	\N	\N	1849	{"text": "It seldom is in such cases.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1851	lexical	\N	\N	1850	{"text": "That mysterious change is too subtle and too gradual to be measured by dates.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1852	lexical	\N	\N	1851	{"text": "Least of all does the maiden herself know it until the tone of a voice or the touch of a hand sets her heart thrilling within her, and she learns, with a mixture of pride and of fear, that a new and a larger nature has awoken within her.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1853	lexical	\N	\N	1852	{"text": "There are few who cannot recall that day and remember the one little incident which heralded the dawn of a new life.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1854	lexical	\N	\N	1853	{"text": "In the case of Lucy Ferrier the occasion was serious enough in itself, apart from its future influence on her destiny and that of many besides.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1855	lexical	\N	\N	1854	{"text": "It was a warm June morning, and the Latter Day Saints were as busy as the bees whose hive they have chosen for their emblem.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1856	lexical	\N	\N	1855	{"text": "In the fields and in the streets rose the same hum of human industry.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1857	lexical	\N	\N	1856	{"text": "Down the dusty high roads defiled long streams of heavily-laden mules, all heading to the west, for the gold fever had broken out in California, and the Overland Route lay through the City of the Elect.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1858	lexical	\N	\N	1857	{"text": "There, too, were droves of sheep and bullocks coming in from the outlying pasture lands, and trains of tired immigrants, men and horses equally weary of their interminable journey.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1859	lexical	\N	\N	1858	{"text": "Through all this motley assemblage, threading her way with the skill of an accomplished rider, there galloped Lucy Ferrier, her fair face flushed with the exercise and her long chestnut hair floating out behind her.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1860	lexical	\N	\N	1859	{"text": "She had a commission from her father in the City, and was dashing in as she had done many a time before, with all the fearlessness of youth, thinking only of her task and how it was to be performed.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	terrier	entity	character	Terrier	\N	{"description": "A small dog that is ill and later dies after being given a pill mixture.", "firstSection": "section_39"}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1861	lexical	\N	\N	1860	{"text": "The travel-stained adventurers gazed after her in astonishment, and even the unemotional Indians, journeying in with their pelties, relaxed their accustomed stoicism as they marvelled at the beauty of the pale-faced maiden.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1862	lexical	\N	\N	1861	{"text": "She had reached the outskirts of the city when she found the road blocked by a great drove of cattle, driven by a half-dozen wild-looking herdsmen from the plains.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1863	lexical	\N	\N	1862	{"text": "In her impatience she endeavoured to pass this obstacle by pushing her horse into what appeared to be a gap.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1864	lexical	\N	\N	1863	{"text": "Scarcely had she got fairly into it, however, before the beasts closed in behind her, and she found herself completely imbedded in the moving stream of fierce-eyed, long-horned bullocks.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1865	lexical	\N	\N	1864	{"text": "Accustomed as she was to deal with cattle, she was not alarmed at her situation, but took advantage of every opportunity to urge her horse on in the hopes of pushing her way through the cavalcade.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1866	lexical	\N	\N	1865	{"text": "Unfortunately the horns of one of the creatures, either by accident or design, came in violent contact with the flank of the mustang, and excited it to madness.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1867	lexical	\N	\N	1866	{"text": "In an instant it reared up upon its hind legs with a snort of rage, and pranced and tossed in a way that would have unseated any but a most skilful rider.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1868	lexical	\N	\N	1867	{"text": "The situation was full of peril.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1869	lexical	\N	\N	1868	{"text": "Every plunge of the excited horse brought it against the horns again, and goaded it to fresh madness.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1870	lexical	\N	\N	1869	{"text": "It was all that the girl could do to keep herself in the saddle, yet a slip would mean a terrible death under the hoofs of the unwieldy and terrified animals.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1871	lexical	\N	\N	1870	{"text": "Unaccustomed to sudden emergencies, her head began to swim, and her grip upon the bridle to relax.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1872	lexical	\N	\N	1871	{"text": "Choked by the rising cloud of dust and by the steam from the struggling creatures, she might have abandoned her efforts in despair, but for a kindly voice at her elbow which assured her of assistance.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1873	lexical	\N	\N	1872	{"text": "At the same moment a sinewy brown hand caught the frightened horse by the curb, and forcing a way through the drove, soon brought her to the outskirts.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1874	lexical	\N	\N	1873	{"text": "\\"You're not hurt, I hope, miss,\\" said her preserver, respectfully.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1875	lexical	\N	\N	1874	{"text": "She looked up at his dark, fierce face, and laughed saucily.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1876	lexical	\N	\N	1875	{"text": "\\"I'm awful frightened,\\" she said, naively; \\"whoever would have thought that Poncho would have been so scared by a lot of cows?\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1877	lexical	\N	\N	1876	{"text": "\\"Thank God you kept your seat,\\" the other said earnestly.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1878	lexical	\N	\N	1877	{"text": "He was a tall, savage-looking young fellow, mounted on a powerful roan horse, and clad in the rough dress of a hunter, with a long rifle slung over his shoulders.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1879	lexical	\N	\N	1878	{"text": "\\"I guess you are the daughter of John Ferrier,\\" he remarked, \\"I saw you ride down from his house.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1880	lexical	\N	\N	1879	{"text": "When you see him, ask him if he remembers the Jefferson Hopes of St. Louis.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1881	lexical	\N	\N	1880	{"text": "If he's the same Ferrier, my father and he were pretty thick.\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1882	lexical	\N	\N	1881	{"text": "\\"Hadn't you better come and ask yourself?\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1883	lexical	\N	\N	1882	{"text": "she asked, demurely.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1884	lexical	\N	\N	1883	{"text": "The young fellow seemed pleased at the suggestion, and his dark eyes sparkled with pleasure.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1885	lexical	\N	\N	1884	{"text": "\\"I'll do so,\\" he said, \\"we've been in the mountains for two months, and are not over and above in visiting condition.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1886	lexical	\N	\N	1885	{"text": "He must take us as he finds us.\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1887	lexical	\N	\N	1886	{"text": "\\"He has a good deal to thank you for, and so have I,\\" she answered, \\"he's awful fond of me.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1888	lexical	\N	\N	1887	{"text": "If those cows had jumped on me he'd have never got over it.\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1891	lexical	\N	\N	1890	{"text": "Well, I don't see that it would make much matter to you, anyhow.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1892	lexical	\N	\N	1891	{"text": "You ain't even a friend of ours.\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1893	lexical	\N	\N	1892	{"text": "The young hunter's dark face grew so gloomy over this remark that Lucy Ferrier laughed aloud.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1894	lexical	\N	\N	1893	{"text": "\\"There, I didn't mean that,\\" she said; \\"of course, you are a friend now.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1895	lexical	\N	\N	1894	{"text": "You must come and see us.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1896	lexical	\N	\N	1895	{"text": "Now I must push along, or father won't trust me with his business any more.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1897	lexical	\N	\N	1896	{"text": "Good-bye!\\"", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1898	lexical	\N	\N	1897	{"text": "\\"Good-bye,\\" he answered, raising his broad sombrero, and bending over her little hand.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1899	lexical	\N	\N	1898	{"text": "She wheeled her mustang round, gave it a cut with her riding-whip, and darted away down the broad road in a rolling cloud of dust.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1900	lexical	\N	\N	1899	{"text": "Young Jefferson Hope rode on with his companions, gloomy and taciturn.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1901	lexical	\N	\N	1900	{"text": "He and they had been among the Nevada Mountains prospecting for silver, and were returning to Salt Lake City in the hope of raising capital enough to work some lodes which they had discovered.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1902	lexical	\N	\N	1901	{"text": "He had been as keen as any of them upon the business until this sudden incident had drawn his thoughts into another channel.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1903	lexical	\N	\N	1902	{"text": "The sight of the fair young girl, as frank and wholesome as the Sierra breezes, had stirred his volcanic, untamed heart to its very depths.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1904	lexical	\N	\N	1903	{"text": "When she had vanished from his sight, he realized that a crisis had come in his life, and that neither silver speculations nor any other questions could ever be of such importance to him as this new and all-absorbing one.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1905	lexical	\N	\N	1904	{"text": "The love which had sprung up in his heart was not the sudden, changeable fancy of a boy, but rather the wild, fierce passion of a man of strong will and imperious temper.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1906	lexical	\N	\N	1905	{"text": "He had been accustomed to succeed in all that he undertook.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1907	lexical	\N	\N	1906	{"text": "He swore in his heart that he would not fail in this if human effort and human perseverance could render him successful.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1908	lexical	\N	\N	1907	{"text": "He called on John Ferrier that night, and many times again, until his face was a familiar one at the farm-house.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1909	lexical	\N	\N	1908	{"text": "John, cooped up in the valley, and absorbed in his work, had had little chance of learning the news of the outside world during the last twelve years.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1910	lexical	\N	\N	1909	{"text": "All this Jefferson Hope was able to tell him, and in a style which interested Lucy as well as her father.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1911	lexical	\N	\N	1910	{"text": "He had been a pioneer in California, and could narrate many a strange tale of fortunes made and fortunes lost in those wild, halcyon days.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1912	lexical	\N	\N	1911	{"text": "He had been a scout too, and a trapper, a silver explorer, and a ranchman.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1913	lexical	\N	\N	1912	{"text": "Wherever stirring adventures were to be had, Jefferson Hope had been there in search of them.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1914	lexical	\N	\N	1913	{"text": "He soon became a favourite with the old farmer, who spoke eloquently of his virtues.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1915	lexical	\N	\N	1914	{"text": "On such occasions, Lucy was silent, but her blushing cheek and her bright, happy eyes, showed only too clearly that her young heart was no longer her own.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1916	lexical	\N	\N	1915	{"text": "Her honest father may not have observed these symptoms, but they were assuredly not thrown away upon the man who had won her affections.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1917	lexical	\N	\N	1916	{"text": "It was a summer evening when he came galloping down the road and pulled up at the gate.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1918	lexical	\N	\N	1917	{"text": "She was at the doorway, and came down to meet him.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1919	lexical	\N	\N	1918	{"text": "He threw the bridle over the fence and strode up the pathway.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1920	lexical	\N	\N	1919	{"text": "\\"I am off, Lucy,\\" he said, taking her two hands in his, and gazing tenderly down into her face; \\"I won't ask you to come with me now, but will you be ready to come when I am here again?\\"", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1921	lexical	\N	\N	1920	{"text": "\\"And when will that be?\\"", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1922	lexical	\N	\N	1921	{"text": "she asked, blushing and laughing.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1923	lexical	\N	\N	1922	{"text": "\\"A couple of months at the outside.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_63	section	\N	Section 63	62	{"wordCount": 604}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1928	lexical	\N	\N	1927	{"text": "\\"He has given his consent, provided we get these mines working all right.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1929	lexical	\N	\N	1928	{"text": "I have no fear on that head.\\"", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1930	lexical	\N	\N	1929	{"text": "\\"Oh, well; of course, if you and father have arranged it all, there's no more to be said,\\" she whispered, with her cheek against his broad breast.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1931	lexical	\N	\N	1930	{"text": "\\"Thank God!\\"", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1932	lexical	\N	\N	1931	{"text": "he said, hoarsely, stooping and kissing her.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1933	lexical	\N	\N	1932	{"text": "\\"It is settled, then.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1934	lexical	\N	\N	1933	{"text": "The longer I stay, the harder it will be to go.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1935	lexical	\N	\N	1934	{"text": "They are waiting for me at the cañon.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1936	lexical	\N	\N	1935	{"text": "Good-bye, my own darling—good-bye.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1937	lexical	\N	\N	1936	{"text": "In two months you shall see me.\\"", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1938	lexical	\N	\N	1937	{"text": "He tore himself from her as he spoke, and, flinging himself upon his horse, galloped furiously away, never even looking round, as though afraid that his resolution might fail him if he took one glance at what he was leaving.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1939	lexical	\N	\N	1938	{"text": "She stood at the gate, gazing after him until he vanished from her sight.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1940	lexical	\N	\N	1939	{"text": "Then she walked back into the house, the happiest girl in all Utah.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1941	lexical	\N	\N	1940	{"text": "CHAPTER III.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1942	lexical	\N	\N	1941	{"text": "JOHN FERRIER TALKS WITH THE PROPHET.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1943	lexical	\N	\N	1942	{"text": "Three weeks had passed since Jefferson Hope and his comrades had departed from Salt Lake City.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1944	lexical	\N	\N	1943	{"text": "John Ferrier's heart was sore within him when he thought of the young man's return, and of the impending loss of his adopted child.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1945	lexical	\N	\N	1944	{"text": "Yet her bright and happy face reconciled him to the arrangement more than any argument could have done.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1946	lexical	\N	\N	1945	{"text": "He had always determined, deep down in his resolute heart, that nothing would ever induce him to allow his daughter to wed a Mormon.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1947	lexical	\N	\N	1946	{"text": "Such a marriage he regarded as no marriage at all, but as a shame and a disgrace.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1948	lexical	\N	\N	1947	{"text": "Whatever he might think of the Mormon doctrines, upon that one point he was inflexible.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1949	lexical	\N	\N	1948	{"text": "He had to seal his mouth on the subject, however, for to express an unorthodox opinion was a dangerous matter in those days in the Land of the Saints.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1950	lexical	\N	\N	1949	{"text": "Yes, a dangerous matter—so dangerous that even the most saintly dared only whisper their religious opinions with bated breath, lest something which fell from their lips might be misconstrued, and bring down a swift retribution upon them.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1951	lexical	\N	\N	1950	{"text": "The victims of persecution had now turned persecutors on their own account, and persecutors of the most terrible description.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1952	lexical	\N	\N	1951	{"text": "Not the Inquisition of Seville, nor the German Vehmgericht, nor the Secret Societies of Italy, were ever able to put a more formidable machinery in motion than that which cast a cloud over the State of Utah.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1953	lexical	\N	\N	1952	{"text": "Its invisibility, and the mystery which was attached to it, made this organization doubly terrible.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1954	lexical	\N	\N	1953	{"text": "It appeared to be omniscient and omnipotent, and yet was neither seen nor heard.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1955	lexical	\N	\N	1954	{"text": "The man who held out against the Church vanished away, and none knew whither he had gone or what had befallen him.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1956	lexical	\N	\N	1955	{"text": "His wife and his children awaited him at home, but no father ever returned to tell them how he had fared at the hands of his secret judges.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1957	lexical	\N	\N	1956	{"text": "A rash word or a hasty act was followed by annihilation, and yet none knew what the nature might be of this terrible power which was suspended over them.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1958	lexical	\N	\N	1957	{"text": "No wonder that men went about in fear and trembling, and that even in the heart of the wilderness they dared not whisper the doubts which oppressed them.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1959	lexical	\N	\N	1958	{"text": "At first this vague and terrible power was exercised only upon the recalcitrants who, having embraced the Mormon faith, wished afterwards to pervert or to abandon it.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1960	lexical	\N	\N	1959	{"text": "Soon, however, it took a wider range.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2273	lexical	\N	\N	2272	{"text": "Once safe in Carson we may rest for the remainder of our lives.\\"", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1961	lexical	\N	\N	1960	{"text": "The supply of adult women was running short, and polygamy without a female population on which to draw was a barren doctrine indeed.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1962	lexical	\N	\N	1961	{"text": "Strange rumours began to be bandied about—rumours of murdered immigrants and rifled camps in regions where Indians had never been seen.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1963	lexical	\N	\N	1962	{"text": "Fresh women appeared in the harems of the Elders—women who pined and wept, and bore upon their faces the traces of an unextinguishable horror.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1964	lexical	\N	\N	1963	{"text": "Belated wanderers upon the mountains spoke of gangs of armed men, masked, stealthy, and noiseless, who flitted by them in the darkness.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1965	lexical	\N	\N	1964	{"text": "These tales and rumours took substance and shape, and were corroborated and re-corroborated, until they resolved themselves into a definite name.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1966	lexical	\N	\N	1965	{"text": "To this day, in the lonely ranches of the West, the name of the Danite Band, or the Avenging Angels, is a sinister and an ill-omened one.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1967	lexical	\N	\N	1966	{"text": "Fuller knowledge of the organization which produced such terrible results served to increase rather than to lessen the horror which it inspired in the minds of men.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1968	lexical	\N	\N	1967	{"text": "None knew who belonged to this ruthless society.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1969	lexical	\N	\N	1968	{"text": "The names of the participators in the deeds of blood and violence done under the name of religion were kept profoundly secret.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1970	lexical	\N	\N	1969	{"text": "The very friend to whom you communicated your misgivings as to the Prophet and his mission, might be one of those who would come forth at night with fire and sword to exact a terrible reparation.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1971	lexical	\N	\N	1970	{"text": "Hence every man feared his neighbour, and none spoke of the things which were nearest his heart.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1972	lexical	\N	\N	1971	{"text": "One fine morning, John Ferrier was about to set out to his wheatfields, when he heard the click of the latch, and, looking through the window, saw a stout, sandy-haired, middle-aged man coming up the pathway.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1973	lexical	\N	\N	1972	{"text": "His heart leapt to his mouth, for this was none other than the great Brigham Young himself.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1974	lexical	\N	\N	1973	{"text": "Full of trepidation—for he knew that such a visit boded him little good—Ferrier ran to the door to greet the Mormon chief.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1975	lexical	\N	\N	1974	{"text": "The latter, however, received his salutations coldly, and followed him with a stern face into the sitting-room.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1976	lexical	\N	\N	1975	{"text": "\\"Brother Ferrier,\\" he said, taking a seat, and eyeing the farmer keenly from under his light-coloured eyelashes, \\"the true believers have been good friends to you.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1977	lexical	\N	\N	1976	{"text": "We picked you up when you were starving in the desert, we shared our food with you, led you safe to the Chosen Valley, gave you a goodly share of land, and allowed you to wax rich under our protection.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1978	lexical	\N	\N	1977	{"text": "Is not this so?\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1979	lexical	\N	\N	1978	{"text": "\\"It is so,\\" answered John Ferrier.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1980	lexical	\N	\N	1979	{"text": "\\"In return for all this we asked but one condition: that was, that you should embrace the true faith, and conform in every way to its usages.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1981	lexical	\N	\N	1980	{"text": "This you promised to do, and this, if common report says truly, you have neglected.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1982	lexical	\N	\N	1981	{"text": "\\"And how have I neglected it?\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1983	lexical	\N	\N	1982	{"text": "asked Ferrier, throwing out his hands in expostulation.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1984	lexical	\N	\N	1983	{"text": "\\"Have I not given to the common fund?", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1985	lexical	\N	\N	1984	{"text": "Have I not attended at the Temple?", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1986	lexical	\N	\N	1985	{"text": "Have I not——?\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1987	lexical	\N	\N	1986	{"text": "\\"Where are your wives?\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1988	lexical	\N	\N	1987	{"text": "asked Young, looking round him.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1989	lexical	\N	\N	1988	{"text": "\\"Call them in, that I may greet them.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1990	lexical	\N	\N	1989	{"text": "\\"It is true that I have not married,\\" Ferrier answered.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1991	lexical	\N	\N	1990	{"text": "\\"But women were few, and there were many who had better claims than I.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1992	lexical	\N	\N	1991	{"text": "I was not a lonely man: I had my daughter to attend to my wants.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1993	lexical	\N	\N	1992	{"text": "\\"It is of that daughter that I would speak to you,\\" said the leader of the Mormons.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2302	lexical	\N	\N	2301	{"text": "Even in the darkness he could recognize the outline of the cliffs which bounded it.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1994	lexical	\N	\N	1993	{"text": "\\"She has grown to be the flower of Utah, and has found favour in the eyes of many who are high in the land.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1995	lexical	\N	\N	1994	{"text": "John Ferrier groaned internally.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1996	lexical	\N	\N	1995	{"text": "\\"There are stories of her which I would fain disbelieve—stories that she is sealed to some Gentile.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1997	lexical	\N	\N	1996	{"text": "This must be the gossip of idle tongues.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1998	lexical	\N	\N	1997	{"text": "What is the thirteenth rule in the code of the sainted Joseph Smith?", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_1999	lexical	\N	\N	1998	{"text": "' This being so, it is impossible that you, who profess the holy creed, should suffer your daughter to violate it.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2000	lexical	\N	\N	1999	{"text": "This being so, it is impossible that you, who profess the holy creed, should suffer your daughter to violate it.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2001	lexical	\N	\N	2000	{"text": "John Ferrier made no answer, but he played nervously with his riding-whip.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2002	lexical	\N	\N	2001	{"text": "\\"Upon this one point your whole faith shall be tested—so it has been decided in the Sacred Council of Four.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2003	lexical	\N	\N	2002	{"text": "The girl is young, and we would not have her wed grey hairs, neither would we deprive her of all choice.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2004	lexical	\N	\N	2003	{"text": "We Elders have many heifers,[1] but our children must also be provided.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2005	lexical	\N	\N	2004	{"text": "Stangerson has a son, and Drebber has a son, and either of them would gladly welcome your daughter to their house.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2006	lexical	\N	\N	2005	{"text": "Let her choose between them.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2007	lexical	\N	\N	2006	{"text": "They are young and rich, and of the true faith.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2008	lexical	\N	\N	2007	{"text": "What say you to that?\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2009	lexical	\N	\N	2008	{"text": "[1] Heber C.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2010	lexical	\N	\N	2009	{"text": "Kemball, in one of his sermons, alludes to his hundred wives under this endearing epithet.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2011	lexical	\N	\N	2010	{"text": "Ferrier remained silent for some little time with his brows knitted.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2012	lexical	\N	\N	2011	{"text": "\\"You will give us time,\\" he said at last.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2013	lexical	\N	\N	2012	{"text": "\\"My daughter is very young—she is scarce of an age to marry.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2014	lexical	\N	\N	2013	{"text": "\\"She shall have a month to choose,\\" said Young, rising from his seat.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2015	lexical	\N	\N	2014	{"text": "\\"At the end of that time she shall give her answer.\\"", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2016	lexical	\N	\N	2015	{"text": "He was passing through the door, when he turned, with flushed face and flashing eyes.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2017	lexical	\N	\N	2016	{"text": "\\"It were better for you, John Ferrier,\\" he thundered, \\"that you and she were now lying blanched skeletons upon the Sierra Blanco, than that you should put your weak wills against the orders of the Holy Four!\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2018	lexical	\N	\N	2017	{"text": "With a threatening gesture of his hand, he turned from the door, and Ferrier heard his heavy step scrunching along the shingly path.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2019	lexical	\N	\N	2018	{"text": "He was still sitting with his elbows upon his knees, considering how he should broach the matter to his daughter when a soft hand was laid upon his, and looking up, he saw her standing beside him.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2020	lexical	\N	\N	2019	{"text": "One glance at her pale, frightened face showed him that she had heard what had passed.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2021	lexical	\N	\N	2020	{"text": "\\"I could not help it,\\" she said, in answer to his look.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2022	lexical	\N	\N	2021	{"text": "\\"His voice rang through the house.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2023	lexical	\N	\N	2022	{"text": "Oh, father, father, what shall we do?\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2024	lexical	\N	\N	2023	{"text": "\\"Don't you scare yourself,\\" he answered, drawing her to him, and passing his broad, rough hand caressingly over her chestnut hair.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2025	lexical	\N	\N	2024	{"text": "\\"We'll fix it up somehow or another.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2026	lexical	\N	\N	2025	{"text": "You don't find your fancy kind o' lessening for this chap, do you?\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2027	lexical	\N	\N	2026	{"text": "A sob and a squeeze of his hand was her only answer.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2028	lexical	\N	\N	2027	{"text": "\\"No; of course not.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2029	lexical	\N	\N	2028	{"text": "I shouldn't care to hear you say you did.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2334	lexical	\N	\N	2333	{"text": "His strong will and untiring energy should, he determined, be devoted to that one end.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2030	lexical	\N	\N	2029	{"text": "He's a likely lad, and he's a Christian, which is more than these folk here, in spite o' all their praying and preaching.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2031	lexical	\N	\N	2030	{"text": "There's a party starting for Nevada to-morrow, and I'll manage to send him a message letting him know the hole we are in.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2032	lexical	\N	\N	2031	{"text": "If I know anything o' that young man, he'll be back here with a speed that would whip electro-telegraphs.\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2033	lexical	\N	\N	2032	{"text": "Lucy laughed through her tears at her father's description.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2034	lexical	\N	\N	2033	{"text": "\\"When he comes, he will advise us for the best.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2035	lexical	\N	\N	2034	{"text": "But it is for you that I am frightened, dear.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2036	lexical	\N	\N	2035	{"text": "One hears—one hears such dreadful stories about those who oppose the Prophet: something terrible always happens to them.\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2037	lexical	\N	\N	2036	{"text": "\\"But we haven't opposed him yet,\\" her father answered.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2038	lexical	\N	\N	2037	{"text": "\\"It will be time to look out for squalls when we do.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2039	lexical	\N	\N	2038	{"text": "We have a clear month before us; at the end of that, I guess we had best shin out of Utah.\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2040	lexical	\N	\N	2039	{"text": "\\"Leave Utah!\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2041	lexical	\N	\N	2040	{"text": "\\"That's about the size of it.\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2042	lexical	\N	\N	2041	{"text": "\\"But the farm?\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2043	lexical	\N	\N	2042	{"text": "\\"We will raise as much as we can in money, and let the rest go.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2044	lexical	\N	\N	2043	{"text": "To tell the truth, Lucy, it isn't the first time I have thought of doing it.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2045	lexical	\N	\N	2044	{"text": "I don't care about knuckling under to any man, as these folk do to their darned prophet.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2046	lexical	\N	\N	2045	{"text": "I'm a free-born American, and it's all new to me.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2047	lexical	\N	\N	2046	{"text": "Guess I'm too old to learn.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2048	lexical	\N	\N	2047	{"text": "If he comes browsing about this farm, he might chance to run up against a charge of buckshot travelling in the opposite direction.\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2049	lexical	\N	\N	2048	{"text": "\\"But they won't let us leave,\\" his daughter objected.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2050	lexical	\N	\N	2049	{"text": "\\"Wait till Jefferson comes, and we'll soon manage that.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2051	lexical	\N	\N	2050	{"text": "In the meantime, don't you fret yourself, my dearie, and don't get your eyes swelled up, else he'll be walking into me when he sees you.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2052	lexical	\N	\N	2051	{"text": "There's nothing to be afeared about, and there's no danger at all.\\"", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2053	lexical	\N	\N	2052	{"text": "John Ferrier uttered these consoling remarks in a very confident tone, but she could not help observing that he paid unusual care to the fastening of the doors that night, and that he carefully cleaned and loaded the rusty old shotgun which hung upon the wall of his bedroom.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2054	lexical	\N	\N	2053	{"text": "CHAPTER IV.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2055	lexical	\N	\N	2054	{"text": "A FLIGHT FOR LIFE.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2056	lexical	\N	\N	2055	{"text": "On the morning which followed his interview with the Mormon Prophet, John Ferrier went in to Salt Lake City, and having found his acquaintance, who was bound for the Nevada Mountains, he entrusted him with his message to Jefferson Hope.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2057	lexical	\N	\N	2056	{"text": "In it he told the young man of the imminent danger which threatened them, and how necessary it was that he should return.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2058	lexical	\N	\N	2057	{"text": "Having done thus he felt easier in his mind, and returned home with a lighter heart.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2059	lexical	\N	\N	2058	{"text": "As he approached his farm, he was surprised to see a horse hitched to each of the posts of the gate.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2060	lexical	\N	\N	2059	{"text": "Still more surprised was he on entering to find two young men in possession of his sitting-room.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2061	lexical	\N	\N	2060	{"text": "One, with a long pale face, was leaning back in the rocking-chair, with his feet cocked up upon the stove.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2062	lexical	\N	\N	2061	{"text": "The other, a bull-necked youth with coarse bloated features, was standing in front of the window with his hands in his pocket, whistling a popular hymn.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2063	lexical	\N	\N	2062	{"text": "Both of them nodded to Ferrier as he entered, and the one in the rocking-chair commenced the conversation.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2064	lexical	\N	\N	2063	{"text": "\\"Maybe you don't know us,\\" he said.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_64	section	\N	Section 64	63	{"wordCount": 653}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2065	lexical	\N	\N	2064	{"text": "\\"This here is the son of Elder Drebber, and I'm Joseph Stangerson, who travelled with you in the desert when the Lord stretched out His hand and gathered you into the true fold.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	reginald_musgrave	entity	character	Reginald Musgrave	\N	{"description": "A named man mentioned in Holmes's explanation.", "firstSection": "section_40"}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2066	lexical	\N	\N	2065	{"text": "\\"As He will all the nations in His own good time,\\" said the other in a nasal voice; \\"He grindeth slowly but exceeding small.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2067	lexical	\N	\N	2066	{"text": "John Ferrier bowed coldly.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2068	lexical	\N	\N	2067	{"text": "He had guessed who his visitors were.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2069	lexical	\N	\N	2068	{"text": "\\"We have come,\\" continued Stangerson, \\"at the advice of our fathers to solicit the hand of your daughter for whichever of us may seem good to you and to her.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2070	lexical	\N	\N	2069	{"text": "As I have but four wives and Brother Drebber here has seven, it appears to me that my claim is the stronger one.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2071	lexical	\N	\N	2070	{"text": "\\"Nay, nay, Brother Stangerson,\\" cried the other; \\"the question is not how many wives we have, but how many we can keep.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2072	lexical	\N	\N	2071	{"text": "My father has now given over his mills to me, and I am the richer man.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2073	lexical	\N	\N	2072	{"text": "\\"But my prospects are better,\\" said the other, warmly.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2074	lexical	\N	\N	2073	{"text": "\\"When the Lord removes my father, I shall have his tanning yard and his leather factory.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2075	lexical	\N	\N	2074	{"text": "Then I am your elder, and am higher in the Church.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2076	lexical	\N	\N	2075	{"text": "\\"It will be for the maiden to decide,\\" rejoined young Drebber, smirking at his own reflection in the glass.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2077	lexical	\N	\N	2076	{"text": "\\"We will leave it all to her decision.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2078	lexical	\N	\N	2077	{"text": "During this dialogue, John Ferrier had stood fuming in the doorway, hardly able to keep his riding-whip from the backs of his two visitors.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2079	lexical	\N	\N	2078	{"text": "\\"Look here,\\" he said at last, striding up to them, \\"when my daughter summons you, you can come, but until then I don't want to see your faces again.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2080	lexical	\N	\N	2079	{"text": "The two young Mormons stared at him in amazement.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2081	lexical	\N	\N	2080	{"text": "In their eyes this competition between them for the maiden's hand was the highest of honours both to her and her father.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2082	lexical	\N	\N	2081	{"text": "\\"There are two ways out of the room,\\" cried Ferrier; \\"there is the door, and there is the window.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2083	lexical	\N	\N	2082	{"text": "Which do you care to use?\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2084	lexical	\N	\N	2083	{"text": "His brown face looked so savage, and his gaunt hands so threatening, that his visitors sprang to their feet and beat a hurried retreat.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2085	lexical	\N	\N	2084	{"text": "The old farmer followed them to the door.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2086	lexical	\N	\N	2085	{"text": "\\"Let me know when you have settled which it is to be,\\" he said, sardonically.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2087	lexical	\N	\N	2086	{"text": "\\"You shall smart for this!\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2088	lexical	\N	\N	2087	{"text": "Stangerson cried, white with rage.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2089	lexical	\N	\N	2088	{"text": "\\"You have defied the Prophet and the Council of Four.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2090	lexical	\N	\N	2089	{"text": "You shall rue it to the end of your days.\\"", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2091	lexical	\N	\N	2090	{"text": "\\"The hand of the Lord shall be heavy upon you,\\" cried young Drebber; \\"He will arise and smite you!\\"", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2092	lexical	\N	\N	2091	{"text": "\\"Then I'll start the smiting,\\" exclaimed Ferrier furiously, and would have rushed upstairs for his gun had not Lucy seized him by the arm and restrained him.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2093	lexical	\N	\N	2092	{"text": "Before he could escape from her, the clatter of horses' hoofs told him that they were beyond his reach.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2094	lexical	\N	\N	2093	{"text": "\\"The young canting rascals!\\"", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2095	lexical	\N	\N	2094	{"text": "he exclaimed, wiping the perspiration from his forehead; \\"I would sooner see you in your grave, my girl, than the wife of either of them.\\"", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2096	lexical	\N	\N	2095	{"text": "\\"And so should I, father,\\" she answered, with spirit; \\"but Jefferson will soon be here.\\"", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2097	lexical	\N	\N	2096	{"text": "\\"Yes.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2098	lexical	\N	\N	2097	{"text": "It will not be long before he comes.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2099	lexical	\N	\N	2098	{"text": "The sooner the better, for we do not know what their next move may be.\\"", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2371	lexical	\N	\N	2370	{"text": "No one won't have her very long though, for I saw death in her face yesterday.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2100	lexical	\N	\N	2099	{"text": "It was, indeed, high time that someone capable of giving advice and help should come to the aid of the sturdy old farmer and his adopted daughter.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2101	lexical	\N	\N	2100	{"text": "In the whole history of the settlement there had never been such a case of rank disobedience to the authority of the Elders.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2102	lexical	\N	\N	2101	{"text": "If minor errors were punished so sternly, what would be the fate of this arch rebel.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2103	lexical	\N	\N	2102	{"text": "Ferrier knew that his wealth and position would be of no avail to him.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2104	lexical	\N	\N	2103	{"text": "Others as well known and as rich as himself had been spirited away before now, and their goods given over to the Church.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2105	lexical	\N	\N	2104	{"text": "He was a brave man, but he trembled at the vague, shadowy terrors which hung over him.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2106	lexical	\N	\N	2105	{"text": "Any known danger he could face with a firm lip, but this suspense was unnerving.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2107	lexical	\N	\N	2106	{"text": "He concealed his fears from his daughter, however, and affected to make light of the whole matter, though she, with the keen eye of love, saw plainly that he was ill at ease.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2108	lexical	\N	\N	2107	{"text": "He expected that he would receive some message or remonstrance from Young as to his conduct, and he was not mistaken, though it came in an unlooked-for manner.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2109	lexical	\N	\N	2108	{"text": "Upon rising next morning he found, to his surprise, a small square of paper pinned on to the coverlet of his bed just over his chest.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2110	lexical	\N	\N	2109	{"text": "On it was printed, in bold straggling letters:—", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2111	lexical	\N	\N	2110	{"text": "\\"Twenty-nine days are given you for amendment, and then——\\"", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2112	lexical	\N	\N	2111	{"text": "The dash was more fear-inspiring than any threat could have been.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2113	lexical	\N	\N	2112	{"text": "How this warning came into his room puzzled John Ferrier sorely, for his servants slept in an outhouse, and the doors and windows had all been secured.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2114	lexical	\N	\N	2113	{"text": "He crumpled the paper up and said nothing to his daughter, but the incident struck a chill into his heart.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2115	lexical	\N	\N	2114	{"text": "The twenty-nine days were evidently the balance of the month which Young had promised.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2116	lexical	\N	\N	2115	{"text": "What strength or courage could avail against an enemy armed with such mysterious powers?", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2117	lexical	\N	\N	2116	{"text": "The hand which fastened that pin might have struck him to the heart, and he could never have known who had slain him.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2118	lexical	\N	\N	2117	{"text": "Still more shaken was he next morning.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2119	lexical	\N	\N	2118	{"text": "They had sat down to their breakfast when Lucy with a cry of surprise pointed upwards.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2120	lexical	\N	\N	2119	{"text": "In the centre of the ceiling was scrawled, with a burned stick apparently, the number 28.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2121	lexical	\N	\N	2120	{"text": "To his daughter it was unintelligible, and he did not enlighten her.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2122	lexical	\N	\N	2121	{"text": "That night he sat up with his gun and kept watch and ward.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2123	lexical	\N	\N	2122	{"text": "He saw and he heard nothing, and yet in the morning a great 27 had been painted upon the outside of his door.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2124	lexical	\N	\N	2123	{"text": "Thus day followed day; and as sure as morning came he found that his unseen enemies had kept their register, and had marked up in some conspicuous position how many days were still left to him out of the month of grace.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2125	lexical	\N	\N	2124	{"text": "Sometimes the fatal numbers appeared upon the walls, sometimes upon the floors, occasionally they were on small placards stuck upon the garden gate or the railings.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2126	lexical	\N	\N	2125	{"text": "With all his vigilance John Ferrier could not discover whence these daily warnings proceeded.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2127	lexical	\N	\N	2126	{"text": "A horror which was almost superstitious came upon him at the sight of them.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2128	lexical	\N	\N	2127	{"text": "He became haggard and restless, and his eyes had the troubled look of some hunted creature.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2129	lexical	\N	\N	2128	{"text": "He had but one hope in life now, and that was for the arrival of the young hunter from Nevada.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2130	lexical	\N	\N	2129	{"text": "Twenty had changed to fifteen and fifteen to ten, but there was no news of the absentee.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2131	lexical	\N	\N	2130	{"text": "One by one the numbers dwindled down, and still there came no sign of him.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2132	lexical	\N	\N	2131	{"text": "Whenever a horseman clattered down the road, or a driver shouted at his team, the old farmer hurried to the gate thinking that help had arrived at last.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2133	lexical	\N	\N	2132	{"text": "At last, when he saw five give way to four and that again to three, he lost heart, and abandoned all hope of escape.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2134	lexical	\N	\N	2133	{"text": "Single-handed, and with his limited knowledge of the mountains which surrounded the settlement, he knew that he was powerless.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2135	lexical	\N	\N	2134	{"text": "The more-frequented roads were strictly watched and guarded, and none could pass along them without an order from the Council.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2136	lexical	\N	\N	2135	{"text": "Turn which way he would, there appeared to be no avoiding the blow which hung over him.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2137	lexical	\N	\N	2136	{"text": "Yet the old man never wavered in his resolution to part with life itself before he consented to what he regarded as his daughter's dishonour.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2138	lexical	\N	\N	2137	{"text": "He was sitting alone one evening pondering deeply over his troubles, and searching vainly for some way out of them.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2139	lexical	\N	\N	2138	{"text": "That morning had shown the figure 2 upon the wall of his house, and the next day would be the last of the allotted time.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2140	lexical	\N	\N	2139	{"text": "What was to happen then?", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2141	lexical	\N	\N	2140	{"text": "All manner of vague and terrible fancies filled his imagination.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2142	lexical	\N	\N	2141	{"text": "And his daughter—what was to become of her after he was gone?", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2143	lexical	\N	\N	2142	{"text": "Was there no escape from the invisible network which was drawn all round them.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2144	lexical	\N	\N	2143	{"text": "He sank his head upon the table and sobbed at the thought of his own impotence.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2145	lexical	\N	\N	2144	{"text": "What was that?", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2146	lexical	\N	\N	2145	{"text": "In the silence he heard a gentle scratching sound—low, but very distinct in the quiet of the night.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2147	lexical	\N	\N	2146	{"text": "It came from the door of the house.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2148	lexical	\N	\N	2147	{"text": "Ferrier crept into the hall and listened intently.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2149	lexical	\N	\N	2148	{"text": "There was a pause for a few moments, and then the low insidious sound was repeated.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2150	lexical	\N	\N	2149	{"text": "Someone was evidently tapping very gently upon one of the panels of the door.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2151	lexical	\N	\N	2150	{"text": "Was it some midnight assassin who had come to carry out the murderous orders of the secret tribunal?", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2152	lexical	\N	\N	2151	{"text": "Or was it some agent who was marking up that the last day of grace had arrived.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2153	lexical	\N	\N	2152	{"text": "John Ferrier felt that instant death would be better than the suspense which shook his nerves and chilled his heart.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2154	lexical	\N	\N	2153	{"text": "Springing forward he drew the bolt and threw the door open.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2155	lexical	\N	\N	2154	{"text": "Outside all was calm and quiet.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2156	lexical	\N	\N	2155	{"text": "The night was fine, and the stars were twinkling brightly overhead.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2157	lexical	\N	\N	2156	{"text": "The little front garden lay before the farmer's eyes bounded by the fence and gate, but neither there nor on the road was any human being to be seen.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2158	lexical	\N	\N	2157	{"text": "With a sigh of relief, Ferrier looked to right and to left, until happening to glance straight down at his own feet he saw to his astonishment a man lying flat upon his face upon the ground, with arms and legs all asprawl.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2159	lexical	\N	\N	2158	{"text": "So unnerved was he at the sight that he leaned up against the wall with his hand to his throat to stifle his inclination to call out.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2160	lexical	\N	\N	2159	{"text": "His first thought was that the prostrate figure was that of some wounded or dying man, but as he watched it he saw it writhe along the ground and into the hall with the rapidity and noiselessness of a serpent.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2161	lexical	\N	\N	2160	{"text": "Once within the house the man sprang to his feet, closed the door, and revealed to the astonished farmer the fierce face and resolute expression of Jefferson Hope.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2162	lexical	\N	\N	2161	{"text": "\\"Good God!\\"", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2163	lexical	\N	\N	2162	{"text": "gasped John Ferrier.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2164	lexical	\N	\N	2163	{"text": "\\"How you scared me!", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2165	lexical	\N	\N	2164	{"text": "Whatever made you come in like that.\\"", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2166	lexical	\N	\N	2165	{"text": "\\"Give me food,\\" the other said, hoarsely.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2167	lexical	\N	\N	2166	{"text": "\\"I have had no time for bite or sup for eight-and-forty hours.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2168	lexical	\N	\N	2167	{"text": "He flung himself upon the cold meat and bread which were still lying upon the table from his host's supper, and devoured it voraciously.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2169	lexical	\N	\N	2168	{"text": "\\"Does Lucy bear up well?\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2170	lexical	\N	\N	2169	{"text": "he asked, when he had satisfied his hunger.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2171	lexical	\N	\N	2170	{"text": "\\"Yes.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2172	lexical	\N	\N	2171	{"text": "She does not know the danger,\\" her father answered.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2173	lexical	\N	\N	2172	{"text": "\\"That is well.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2174	lexical	\N	\N	2173	{"text": "The house is watched on every side.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2175	lexical	\N	\N	2174	{"text": "That is why I crawled my way up to it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2176	lexical	\N	\N	2175	{"text": "They may be darned sharp, but they're not quite sharp enough to catch a Washoe hunter.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2177	lexical	\N	\N	2176	{"text": "John Ferrier felt a different man now that he realized that he had a devoted ally.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2178	lexical	\N	\N	2177	{"text": "He seized the young man's leathery hand and wrung it cordially.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2179	lexical	\N	\N	2178	{"text": "\\"You're a man to be proud of,\\" he said.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2180	lexical	\N	\N	2179	{"text": "\\"There are not many who would come to share our danger and our troubles.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2181	lexical	\N	\N	2180	{"text": "\\"You've hit it there, pard,\\" the young hunter answered.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2182	lexical	\N	\N	2181	{"text": "\\"I have a respect for you, but if you were alone in this business I'd think twice before I put my head into such a hornet's nest.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2183	lexical	\N	\N	2182	{"text": "It's Lucy that brings me here, and before harm comes on her I guess there will be one less o' the Hope family in Utah.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2184	lexical	\N	\N	2183	{"text": "\\"What are we to do?\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2185	lexical	\N	\N	2184	{"text": "\\"To-morrow is your last day, and unless you act to-night you are lost.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2186	lexical	\N	\N	2185	{"text": "I have a mule and two horses waiting in the Eagle Ravine.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2187	lexical	\N	\N	2186	{"text": "How much money have you?\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2188	lexical	\N	\N	2187	{"text": "\\"Two thousand dollars in gold, and five in notes.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2189	lexical	\N	\N	2188	{"text": "\\"That will do.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2190	lexical	\N	\N	2189	{"text": "I have as much more to add to it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2191	lexical	\N	\N	2190	{"text": "We must push for Carson City through the mountains.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2192	lexical	\N	\N	2191	{"text": "You had best wake Lucy.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2193	lexical	\N	\N	2192	{"text": "It is as well that the servants do not sleep in the house.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2194	lexical	\N	\N	2193	{"text": "While Ferrier was absent, preparing his daughter for the approaching journey, Jefferson Hope packed all the eatables that he could find into a small parcel, and filled a stoneware jar with water, for he knew by experience that the mountain wells were few and far between.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2195	lexical	\N	\N	2194	{"text": "He had hardly completed his arrangements before the farmer returned with his daughter all dressed and ready for a start.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2196	lexical	\N	\N	2195	{"text": "The greeting between the lovers was warm, but brief, for minutes were precious, and there was much to be done.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2197	lexical	\N	\N	2196	{"text": "\\"We must make our start at once,\\" said Jefferson Hope, speaking in a low but resolute voice, like one who realizes the greatness of the peril, but has steeled his heart to meet it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2198	lexical	\N	\N	2197	{"text": "\\"The front and back entrances are watched, but with caution we may get away through the side window and across the fields.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2199	lexical	\N	\N	2198	{"text": "Once on the road we are only two miles from the Ravine where the horses are waiting.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2200	lexical	\N	\N	2199	{"text": "By daybreak we should be half-way through the mountains.\\"", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2201	lexical	\N	\N	2200	{"text": "\\"What if we are stopped,\\" asked Ferrier.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2202	lexical	\N	\N	2201	{"text": "Hope slapped the revolver butt which protruded from the front of his tunic.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2203	lexical	\N	\N	2202	{"text": "\\"If they are too many for us we shall take two or three of them with us,\\" he said with a sinister smile.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2204	lexical	\N	\N	2203	{"text": "The lights inside the house had all been extinguished, and from the darkened window Ferrier peered over the fields which had been his own, and which he was now about to abandon for ever.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2205	lexical	\N	\N	2204	{"text": "He had long nerved himself to the sacrifice, however, and the thought of the honour and happiness of his daughter outweighed any regret at his ruined fortunes.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2206	lexical	\N	\N	2205	{"text": "All looked so peaceful and happy, the rustling trees and the broad silent stretch of grain-land, that it was difficult to realize that the spirit of murder lurked through it all.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2207	lexical	\N	\N	2206	{"text": "Yet the white face and set expression of the young hunter showed that in his approach to the house he had seen enough to satisfy him upon that head.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2208	lexical	\N	\N	2207	{"text": "Ferrier carried the bag of gold and notes, Jefferson Hope had the scanty provisions and water, while Lucy had a small bundle containing a few of her more valued possessions.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2209	lexical	\N	\N	2208	{"text": "Opening the window very slowly and carefully, they waited until a dark cloud had somewhat obscured the night, and then one by one passed through into the little garden.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2210	lexical	\N	\N	2209	{"text": "With bated breath and crouching figures they stumbled across it, and gained the shelter of the hedge, which they skirted until they came to the gap which opened into the cornfields.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2211	lexical	\N	\N	2210	{"text": "They had just reached this point when the young man seized his two companions and dragged them down into the shadow, where they lay silent and trembling.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2212	lexical	\N	\N	2211	{"text": "It was as well that his prairie training had given Jefferson Hope the ears of a lynx.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2213	lexical	\N	\N	2212	{"text": "He and his friends had hardly crouched down before the melancholy hooting of a mountain owl was heard within a few yards of them, which was immediately answered by another hoot at a small distance.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2214	lexical	\N	\N	2213	{"text": "At the same moment a vague shadowy figure emerged from the gap for which they had been making, and uttered the plaintive signal cry again, on which a second man appeared out of the obscurity.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2215	lexical	\N	\N	2214	{"text": "\\"To-morrow at midnight,\\" said the first who appeared to be in authority.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2216	lexical	\N	\N	2215	{"text": "\\"When the Whip-poor-Will calls three times.\\"", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2217	lexical	\N	\N	2216	{"text": "\\"It is well,\\" returned the other.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2218	lexical	\N	\N	2217	{"text": "\\"Shall I tell Brother Drebber?\\"", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2219	lexical	\N	\N	2218	{"text": "\\"Pass it on to him, and from him to the others.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2220	lexical	\N	\N	2219	{"text": "Nine to seven!\\"", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2221	lexical	\N	\N	2220	{"text": "\\"Seven to five!\\"", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2222	lexical	\N	\N	2221	{"text": "repeated the other, and the two figures flitted away in different directions.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2223	lexical	\N	\N	2222	{"text": "Their concluding words had evidently been some form of sign and countersign.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2224	lexical	\N	\N	2223	{"text": "The instant that their footsteps had died away in the distance, Jefferson Hope sprang to his feet, and helping his companions through the gap, led the way across the fields at the top of his speed, supporting and half-carrying the girl when her strength appeared to fail her.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2225	lexical	\N	\N	2224	{"text": "\\"Hurry on!", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2226	lexical	\N	\N	2225	{"text": "hurry on!\\"", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2227	lexical	\N	\N	2226	{"text": "he gasped from time to time.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2228	lexical	\N	\N	2227	{"text": "\\"We are through the line of sentinels.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2229	lexical	\N	\N	2228	{"text": "Everything depends on speed.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2230	lexical	\N	\N	2229	{"text": "Hurry on!\\"", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2231	lexical	\N	\N	2230	{"text": "Once on the high road they made rapid progress.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2232	lexical	\N	\N	2231	{"text": "Only once did they meet anyone, and then they managed to slip into a field, and so avoid recognition.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2233	lexical	\N	\N	2232	{"text": "Before reaching the town the hunter branched away into a rugged and narrow footpath which led to the mountains.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2234	lexical	\N	\N	2233	{"text": "Two dark jagged peaks loomed above them through the darkness, and the defile which led between them was the Eagle Cañon in which the horses were awaiting them.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2235	lexical	\N	\N	2234	{"text": "With unerring instinct Jefferson Hope picked his way among the great boulders and along the bed of a dried-up watercourse, until he came to the retired corner, screened with rocks, where the faithful animals had been picketed.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2236	lexical	\N	\N	2235	{"text": "The girl was placed upon the mule, and old Ferrier upon one of the horses, with his money-bag, while Jefferson Hope led the other along the precipitous and dangerous path.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2237	lexical	\N	\N	2236	{"text": "It was a bewildering route for anyone who was not accustomed to face Nature in her wildest moods.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2238	lexical	\N	\N	2237	{"text": "On the one side a great crag towered up a thousand feet or more, black, stern, and menacing, with long basaltic columns upon its rugged surface like the ribs of some petrified monster.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2239	lexical	\N	\N	2238	{"text": "On the other hand a wild chaos of boulders and debris made all advance impossible.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2240	lexical	\N	\N	2239	{"text": "Between the two ran the irregular track, so narrow in places that they had to travel in Indian file, and so rough that only practised riders could have traversed it at all.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2241	lexical	\N	\N	2240	{"text": "Yet in spite of all dangers and difficulties, the hearts of the fugitives were light within them, for every step increased the distance between them and the terrible despotism from which they were flying.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2242	lexical	\N	\N	2241	{"text": "They soon had a proof, however, that they were still within the jurisdiction of the Saints.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2243	lexical	\N	\N	2242	{"text": "They had reached the very wildest and most desolate portion of the pass when the girl gave a startled cry, and pointed upwards.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2244	lexical	\N	\N	2243	{"text": "On a rock which overlooked the track, showing out dark and plain against the sky, there stood a solitary sentinel.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2245	lexical	\N	\N	2244	{"text": "He saw them as soon as they perceived him, and his military challenge of \\"Who goes there?\\"", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2246	lexical	\N	\N	2245	{"text": "rang through the silent ravine.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2247	lexical	\N	\N	2246	{"text": "\\"Travellers for Nevada,\\" said Jefferson Hope, with his hand upon the rifle which hung by his saddle.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2248	lexical	\N	\N	2247	{"text": "They could see the lonely watcher fingering his gun, and peering down at them as if dissatisfied at their reply.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2249	lexical	\N	\N	2248	{"text": "\\"By whose permission?\\"", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2250	lexical	\N	\N	2249	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2251	lexical	\N	\N	2250	{"text": "\\"The Holy Four,\\" answered Ferrier.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2252	lexical	\N	\N	2251	{"text": "His Mormon experiences had taught him that that was the highest authority to which he could refer.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2253	lexical	\N	\N	2252	{"text": "\\"Nine from seven,\\" cried the sentinel.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2254	lexical	\N	\N	2253	{"text": "\\"Seven from five,\\" returned Jefferson Hope promptly, remembering the countersign which he had heard in the garden.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2255	lexical	\N	\N	2254	{"text": "\\"Pass, and the Lord go with you,\\" said the voice from above.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2256	lexical	\N	\N	2255	{"text": "Beyond his post the path broadened out, and the horses were able to break into a trot.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2257	lexical	\N	\N	2256	{"text": "Looking back, they could see the solitary watcher leaning upon his gun, and knew that they had passed the outlying post of the chosen people, and that freedom lay before them.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2258	lexical	\N	\N	2257	{"text": "CHAPTER V.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2259	lexical	\N	\N	2258	{"text": "THE AVENGING ANGELS.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2260	lexical	\N	\N	2259	{"text": "All night their course lay through intricate defiles and over irregular and rock-strewn paths.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2261	lexical	\N	\N	2260	{"text": "More than once they lost their way, but Hope's intimate knowledge of the mountains enabled them to regain the track once more.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2262	lexical	\N	\N	2261	{"text": "When morning broke, a scene of marvellous though savage beauty lay before them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2263	lexical	\N	\N	2262	{"text": "In every direction the great snow-capped peaks hemmed them in, peeping over each other's shoulders to the far horizon.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2264	lexical	\N	\N	2263	{"text": "So steep were the rocky banks on either side of them, that the larch and the pine seemed to be suspended over their heads, and to need only a gust of wind to come hurtling down upon them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2265	lexical	\N	\N	2264	{"text": "Nor was the fear entirely an illusion, for the barren valley was thickly strewn with trees and boulders which had fallen in a similar manner.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2266	lexical	\N	\N	2265	{"text": "Even as they passed, a great rock came thundering down with a hoarse rattle which woke the echoes in the silent gorges, and startled the weary horses into a gallop.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2267	lexical	\N	\N	2266	{"text": "As the sun rose slowly above the eastern horizon, the caps of the great mountains lit up one after the other, like lamps at a festival, until they were all ruddy and glowing.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2268	lexical	\N	\N	2267	{"text": "The magnificent spectacle cheered the hearts of the three fugitives and gave them fresh energy.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2269	lexical	\N	\N	2268	{"text": "At a wild torrent which swept out of a ravine they called a halt and watered their horses, while they partook of a hasty breakfast.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2270	lexical	\N	\N	2269	{"text": "Lucy and her father would fain have rested longer, but Jefferson Hope was inexorable.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2274	lexical	\N	\N	2273	{"text": "During the whole of that day they struggled on through the defiles, and by evening they calculated that they were more than thirty miles from their enemies.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2275	lexical	\N	\N	2274	{"text": "At night-time they chose the base of a beetling crag, where the rocks offered some protection from the chill wind, and there huddled together for warmth, they enjoyed a few hours' sleep.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2276	lexical	\N	\N	2275	{"text": "Before daybreak, however, they were up and on their way once more.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2277	lexical	\N	\N	2276	{"text": "They had seen no signs of any pursuers, and Jefferson Hope began to think that they were fairly out of the reach of the terrible organization whose enmity they had incurred.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2278	lexical	\N	\N	2277	{"text": "He little knew how far that iron grasp could reach, or how soon it was to close upon them and crush them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2279	lexical	\N	\N	2278	{"text": "About the middle of the second day of their flight their scanty store of provisions began to run out.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2280	lexical	\N	\N	2279	{"text": "This gave the hunter little uneasiness, however, for there was game to be had among the mountains, and he had frequently before had to depend upon his rifle for the needs of life.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2281	lexical	\N	\N	2280	{"text": "Choosing a sheltered nook, he piled together a few dried branches and made a blazing fire, at which his companions might warm themselves, for they were now nearly five thousand feet above the sea level, and the air was bitter and keen.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2282	lexical	\N	\N	2281	{"text": "Having tethered the horses, and bade Lucy adieu, he threw his gun over his shoulder, and set out in search of whatever chance might throw in his way.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2283	lexical	\N	\N	2282	{"text": "Looking back he saw the old man and the young girl crouching over the blazing fire, while the three animals stood motionless in the back-ground.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2284	lexical	\N	\N	2283	{"text": "Then the intervening rocks hid them from his view.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2285	lexical	\N	\N	2284	{"text": "He walked for a couple of miles through one ravine after another without success, though from the marks upon the bark of the trees, and other indications, he judged that there were numerous bears in the vicinity.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2286	lexical	\N	\N	2285	{"text": "At last, after two or three hours' fruitless search, he was thinking of turning back in despair, when casting his eyes upwards he saw a sight which sent a thrill of pleasure through his heart.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2287	lexical	\N	\N	2286	{"text": "On the edge of a jutting pinnacle, three or four hundred feet above him, there stood a creature somewhat resembling a sheep in appearance, but armed with a pair of gigantic horns.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2288	lexical	\N	\N	2287	{"text": "The big-horn—for so it is called—was acting, probably, as a guardian over a flock which were invisible to the hunter; but fortunately it was heading in the opposite direction, and had not perceived him.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2289	lexical	\N	\N	2288	{"text": "Lying on his face, he rested his rifle upon a rock, and took a long and steady aim before drawing the trigger.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2290	lexical	\N	\N	2289	{"text": "The animal sprang into the air, tottered for a moment upon the edge of the precipice, and then came crashing down into the valley beneath.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2291	lexical	\N	\N	2290	{"text": "The creature was too unwieldy to lift, so the hunter contented himself with cutting away one haunch and part of the flank.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2292	lexical	\N	\N	2291	{"text": "With this trophy over his shoulder, he hastened to retrace his steps, for the evening was already drawing in.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2293	lexical	\N	\N	2292	{"text": "He had hardly started, however, before he realized the difficulty which faced him.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2294	lexical	\N	\N	2293	{"text": "In his eagerness he had wandered far past the ravines which were known to him, and it was no easy matter to pick out the path which he had taken.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2295	lexical	\N	\N	2294	{"text": "The valley in which he found himself divided and sub-divided into many gorges, which were so like each other that it was impossible to distinguish one from the other.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2296	lexical	\N	\N	2295	{"text": "He followed one for a mile or more until he came to a mountain torrent which he was sure that he had never seen before.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2297	lexical	\N	\N	2296	{"text": "Convinced that he had taken the wrong turn, he tried another, but with the same result.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2298	lexical	\N	\N	2297	{"text": "Night was coming on rapidly, and it was almost dark before he at last found himself in a defile which was familiar to him.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2299	lexical	\N	\N	2298	{"text": "Even then it was no easy matter to keep to the right track, for the moon had not yet risen, and the high cliffs on either side made the obscurity more profound.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2300	lexical	\N	\N	2299	{"text": "Weighed down with his burden, and weary from his exertions, he stumbled along, keeping up his heart by the reflection that every step brought him nearer to Lucy, and that he carried with him enough to ensure them food for the remainder of their journey.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2301	lexical	\N	\N	2300	{"text": "He had now come to the mouth of the very defile in which he had left them.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2303	lexical	\N	\N	2302	{"text": "They must, he reflected, be awaiting him anxiously, for he had been absent nearly five hours.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2304	lexical	\N	\N	2303	{"text": "In the gladness of his heart he put his hands to his mouth and made the glen re-echo to a loud halloo as a signal that he was coming.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2305	lexical	\N	\N	2304	{"text": "He paused and listened for an answer.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2306	lexical	\N	\N	2305	{"text": "None came save his own cry, which clattered up the dreary silent ravines, and was borne back to his ears in countless repetitions.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2307	lexical	\N	\N	2306	{"text": "Again he shouted, even louder than before, and again no whisper came back from the friends whom he had left such a short time ago.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2308	lexical	\N	\N	2307	{"text": "A vague, nameless dread came over him, and he hurried onwards frantically, dropping the precious food in his agitation.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2309	lexical	\N	\N	2308	{"text": "When he turned the corner, he came full in sight of the spot where the fire had been lit.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2310	lexical	\N	\N	2309	{"text": "There was still a glowing pile of wood ashes there, but it had evidently not been tended since his departure.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2311	lexical	\N	\N	2310	{"text": "The same dead silence still reigned all round.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2312	lexical	\N	\N	2311	{"text": "With his fears all changed to convictions, he hurried on.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2313	lexical	\N	\N	2312	{"text": "There was no living creature near the remains of the fire: animals, man, maiden, all were gone.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2314	lexical	\N	\N	2313	{"text": "It was only too clear that some sudden and terrible disaster had occurred during his absence—a disaster which had embraced them all, and yet had left no traces behind it.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2315	lexical	\N	\N	2314	{"text": "Bewildered and stunned by this blow, Jefferson Hope felt his head spin round, and had to lean upon his rifle to save himself from falling.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2316	lexical	\N	\N	2315	{"text": "He was essentially a man of action, however, and speedily recovered from his temporary impotence.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2317	lexical	\N	\N	2316	{"text": "Seizing a half-consumed piece of wood from the smouldering fire, he blew it into a flame, and proceeded with its help to examine the little camp.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2318	lexical	\N	\N	2317	{"text": "The ground was all stamped down by the feet of horses, showing that a large party of mounted men had overtaken the fugitives, and the direction of their tracks proved that they had afterwards turned back to Salt Lake City.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2319	lexical	\N	\N	2318	{"text": "Had they carried back both of his companions with them?", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2320	lexical	\N	\N	2319	{"text": "Jefferson Hope had almost persuaded himself that they must have done so, when his eye fell upon an object which made every nerve of his body tingle within him.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2321	lexical	\N	\N	2320	{"text": "A little way on one side of the camp was a low-lying heap of reddish soil, which had assuredly not been there before.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2322	lexical	\N	\N	2321	{"text": "There was no mistaking it for anything but a newly-dug grave.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2323	lexical	\N	\N	2322	{"text": "As the young hunter approached it, he perceived that a stick had been planted on it, with a sheet of paper stuck in the cleft fork of it.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2324	lexical	\N	\N	2323	{"text": "The inscription upon the paper was brief, but to the point:", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2325	lexical	\N	\N	2324	{"text": "JOHN FERRIER, FORMERLY OF SALT LAKE CITY, Died August 4th, 1860.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2326	lexical	\N	\N	2325	{"text": "The sturdy old man, whom he had left so short a time before, was gone, then, and this was all his epitaph.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2327	lexical	\N	\N	2326	{"text": "Jefferson Hope looked wildly round to see if there was a second grave, but there was no sign of one.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2328	lexical	\N	\N	2327	{"text": "Lucy had been carried back by their terrible pursuers to fulfil her original destiny, by becoming one of the harem of the Elder's son.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2329	lexical	\N	\N	2328	{"text": "As the young fellow realized the certainty of her fate, and his own powerlessness to prevent it, he wished that he, too, was lying with the old farmer in his last silent resting-place.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2330	lexical	\N	\N	2329	{"text": "Again, however, his active spirit shook off the lethargy which springs from despair.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2331	lexical	\N	\N	2330	{"text": "If there was nothing else left to him, he could at least devote his life to revenge.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2332	lexical	\N	\N	2331	{"text": "With indomitable patience and perseverance, Jefferson Hope possessed also a power of sustained vindictiveness, which he may have learned from the Indians amongst whom he had lived.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2333	lexical	\N	\N	2332	{"text": "As he stood by the desolate fire, he felt that the only one thing which could assuage his grief would be thorough and complete retribution, brought by his own hand upon his enemies.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_65	section	\N	Section 65	64	{"wordCount": 644}
a-study-in-scarlet	murder_assassin	entity	character	Assassin	\N	{"description": "An unnamed man identified as the killer in the discussion.", "firstSection": "section_40"}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2335	lexical	\N	\N	2334	{"text": "With a grim, white face, he retraced his steps to where he had dropped the food, and having stirred up the smouldering fire, he cooked enough to last him for a few days.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2336	lexical	\N	\N	2335	{"text": "This he made up into a bundle, and, tired as he was, he set himself to walk back through the mountains upon the track of the avenging angels.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2337	lexical	\N	\N	2336	{"text": "For five days he toiled footsore and weary through the defiles which he had already traversed on horseback.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2338	lexical	\N	\N	2337	{"text": "At night he flung himself down among the rocks, and snatched a few hours of sleep; but before daybreak he was always well on his way.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2339	lexical	\N	\N	2338	{"text": "On the sixth day, he reached the Eagle Cañon, from which they had commenced their ill-fated flight.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2340	lexical	\N	\N	2339	{"text": "Thence he could look down upon the home of the saints.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2341	lexical	\N	\N	2340	{"text": "Worn and exhausted, he leaned upon his rifle and shook his gaunt hand fiercely at the silent widespread city beneath him.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2342	lexical	\N	\N	2341	{"text": "As he looked at it, he observed that there were flags in some of the principal streets, and other signs of festivity.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2343	lexical	\N	\N	2342	{"text": "He was still speculating as to what this might mean when he heard the clatter of horse's hoofs, and saw a mounted man riding towards him.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2344	lexical	\N	\N	2343	{"text": "As he approached, he recognized him as a Mormon named Cowper, to whom he had rendered services at different times.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2345	lexical	\N	\N	2344	{"text": "He therefore accosted him when he got up to him, with the object of finding out what Lucy Ferrier's fate had been.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2346	lexical	\N	\N	2345	{"text": "\\"I am Jefferson Hope,\\" he said.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2347	lexical	\N	\N	2346	{"text": "\\"You remember me.\\"", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2348	lexical	\N	\N	2347	{"text": "The Mormon looked at him with undisguised astonishment—indeed, it was difficult to recognize in this tattered, unkempt wanderer, with ghastly white face and fierce, wild eyes, the spruce young hunter of former days.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2349	lexical	\N	\N	2348	{"text": "Having, however, at last, satisfied himself as to his identity, the man's surprise changed to consternation.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2350	lexical	\N	\N	2349	{"text": "\\"You are mad to come here,\\" he cried.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2351	lexical	\N	\N	2350	{"text": "\\"It is as much as my own life is worth to be seen talking with you.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2352	lexical	\N	\N	2351	{"text": "There is a warrant against you from the Holy Four for assisting the Ferriers away.\\"", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2353	lexical	\N	\N	2352	{"text": "\\"I don't fear them, or their warrant,\\" Hope said, earnestly.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2354	lexical	\N	\N	2353	{"text": "\\"You must know something of this matter, Cowper.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2355	lexical	\N	\N	2354	{"text": "I conjure you by everything you hold dear to answer a few questions.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2356	lexical	\N	\N	2355	{"text": "We have always been friends.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2357	lexical	\N	\N	2356	{"text": "For God's sake, don't refuse to answer me.\\"", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2358	lexical	\N	\N	2357	{"text": "\\"What is it?\\"", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2359	lexical	\N	\N	2358	{"text": "the Mormon asked uneasily.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2360	lexical	\N	\N	2359	{"text": "\\"Be quick.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2361	lexical	\N	\N	2360	{"text": "The very rocks have ears and the trees eyes.\\"", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2362	lexical	\N	\N	2361	{"text": "\\"What has become of Lucy Ferrier?\\"", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2363	lexical	\N	\N	2362	{"text": "\\"She was married yesterday to young Drebber.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2364	lexical	\N	\N	2363	{"text": "Hold up, man, hold up, you have no life left in you.\\"", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2365	lexical	\N	\N	2364	{"text": "\\"Don't mind me,\\" said Hope faintly.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2366	lexical	\N	\N	2365	{"text": "He was white to the very lips, and had sunk down on the stone against which he had been leaning.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2367	lexical	\N	\N	2366	{"text": "\\"Married, you say?\\"", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2368	lexical	\N	\N	2367	{"text": "\\"Married yesterday—that's what those flags are for on the Endowment House.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2369	lexical	\N	\N	2368	{"text": "There was some words between young Drebber and young Stangerson as to which was to have her.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2370	lexical	\N	\N	2369	{"text": "They'd both been in the party that followed them, and Stangerson had shot her father, which seemed to give him the best claim; but when they argued it out in council, Drebber's party was the stronger, so the Prophet gave her over to him.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2374	lexical	\N	\N	2373	{"text": "\\"Yes, I am off,\\" said Jefferson Hope, who had risen from his seat.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2375	lexical	\N	\N	2374	{"text": "His face might have been chiselled out of marble, so hard and set was its expression, while its eyes glowed with a baleful light.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2376	lexical	\N	\N	2375	{"text": "\\"Where are you going?\\"", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2377	lexical	\N	\N	2376	{"text": "\\"Never mind,\\" he answered; and, slinging his weapon over his shoulder, strode off down the gorge and so away into the heart of the mountains to the haunts of the wild beasts.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2378	lexical	\N	\N	2377	{"text": "Amongst them all there was none so fierce and so dangerous as himself.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2379	lexical	\N	\N	2378	{"text": "The prediction of the Mormon was only too well fulfilled.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2380	lexical	\N	\N	2379	{"text": "Whether it was the terrible death of her father or the effects of the hateful marriage into which she had been forced, poor Lucy never held up her head again, but pined away and died within a month.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2381	lexical	\N	\N	2380	{"text": "Her sottish husband, who had married her principally for the sake of John Ferrier's property, did not affect any great grief at his bereavement; but his other wives mourned over her, and sat up with her the night before the burial, as is the Mormon custom.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2382	lexical	\N	\N	2381	{"text": "They were grouped round the bier in the early hours of the morning, when, to their inexpressible fear and astonishment, the door was flung open, and a savage-looking, weather-beaten man in tattered garments strode into the room.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2383	lexical	\N	\N	2382	{"text": "Without a glance or a word to the cowering women, he walked up to the white silent figure which had once contained the pure soul of Lucy Ferrier.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2384	lexical	\N	\N	2383	{"text": "Stooping over her, he pressed his lips reverently to her cold forehead, and then, snatching up her hand, he took the wedding-ring from her finger.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2385	lexical	\N	\N	2384	{"text": "\\"She shall not be buried in that,\\" he cried with a fierce snarl, and before an alarm could be raised sprang down the stairs and was gone.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2386	lexical	\N	\N	2385	{"text": "So strange and so brief was the episode, that the watchers might have found it hard to believe it themselves or persuade other people of it, had it not been for the undeniable fact that the circlet of gold which marked her as having been a bride had disappeared.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2387	lexical	\N	\N	2386	{"text": "For some months Jefferson Hope lingered among the mountains, leading a strange wild life, and nursing in his heart the fierce desire for vengeance which possessed him.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2388	lexical	\N	\N	2387	{"text": "Tales were told in the City of the weird figure which was seen prowling about the suburbs, and which haunted the lonely mountain gorges.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2389	lexical	\N	\N	2388	{"text": "Once a bullet whistled through Stangerson's window and flattened itself upon the wall within a foot of him.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2390	lexical	\N	\N	2389	{"text": "On another occasion, as Drebber passed under a cliff a great boulder crashed down on him, and he only escaped a terrible death by throwing himself upon his face.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2391	lexical	\N	\N	2390	{"text": "The two young Mormons were not long in discovering the reason of these attempts upon their lives, and led repeated expeditions into the mountains in the hope of capturing or killing their enemy, but always without success.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2392	lexical	\N	\N	2391	{"text": "Then they adopted the precaution of never going out alone or after nightfall, and of having their houses guarded.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2393	lexical	\N	\N	2392	{"text": "After a time they were able to relax these measures, for nothing was either heard or seen of their opponent, and they hoped that time had cooled his vindictiveness.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2394	lexical	\N	\N	2393	{"text": "Far from doing so, it had, if anything, augmented it.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2395	lexical	\N	\N	2394	{"text": "The hunter's mind was of a hard, unyielding nature, and the predominant idea of revenge had taken such complete possession of it that there was no room for any other emotion.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2396	lexical	\N	\N	2395	{"text": "He was, however, above all things practical.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2397	lexical	\N	\N	2396	{"text": "He soon realized that even his iron constitution could not stand the incessant strain which he was putting upon it.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2398	lexical	\N	\N	2397	{"text": "Exposure and want of wholesome food were wearing him out.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2399	lexical	\N	\N	2398	{"text": "If he died like a dog among the mountains, what was to become of his revenge then?", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2400	lexical	\N	\N	2399	{"text": "And yet such a death was sure to overtake him if he persisted.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2401	lexical	\N	\N	2400	{"text": "He felt that that was to play his enemy's game, so he reluctantly returned to the old Nevada mines, there to recruit his health and to amass money enough to allow him to pursue his object without privation.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2402	lexical	\N	\N	2401	{"text": "His intention had been to be absent a year at the most, but a combination of unforeseen circumstances prevented his leaving the mines for nearly five.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2403	lexical	\N	\N	2402	{"text": "At the end of that time, however, his memory of his wrongs and his craving for revenge were quite as keen as on that memorable night when he had stood by John Ferrier's grave.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2404	lexical	\N	\N	2403	{"text": "Disguised, and under an assumed name, he returned to Salt Lake City, careless what became of his own life, as long as he obtained what he knew to be justice.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2405	lexical	\N	\N	2404	{"text": "There he found evil tidings awaiting him.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2406	lexical	\N	\N	2405	{"text": "There had been a schism among the Chosen People a few months before, some of the younger members of the Church having rebelled against the authority of the Elders, and the result had been the secession of a certain number of the malcontents, who had left Utah and become Gentiles.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2407	lexical	\N	\N	2406	{"text": "Among these had been Drebber and Stangerson; and no one knew whither they had gone.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2408	lexical	\N	\N	2407	{"text": "Rumour reported that Drebber had managed to convert a large part of his property into money, and that he had departed a wealthy man, while his companion, Stangerson, was comparatively poor.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2409	lexical	\N	\N	2408	{"text": "There was no clue at all, however, as to their whereabouts.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2410	lexical	\N	\N	2409	{"text": "Many a man, however vindictive, would have abandoned all thought of revenge in the face of such a difficulty, but Jefferson Hope never faltered for a moment.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2411	lexical	\N	\N	2410	{"text": "With the small competence he possessed, eked out by such employment as he could pick up, he travelled from town to town through the United States in quest of his enemies.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2412	lexical	\N	\N	2411	{"text": "Year passed into year, his black hair turned grizzled, but still he wandered on, a human bloodhound, with his mind wholly set upon the one object upon which he had devoted his life.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2413	lexical	\N	\N	2412	{"text": "At last his perseverance was rewarded.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2414	lexical	\N	\N	2413	{"text": "It was but a glance of a face in a window, but that one glance told him that Cleveland in Ohio possessed the men whom he was in pursuit of.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2415	lexical	\N	\N	2414	{"text": "He returned to his miserable lodgings with his plan of vengeance all arranged.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2416	lexical	\N	\N	2415	{"text": "It chanced, however, that Drebber, looking from his window, had recognized the vagrant in the street, and had read murder in his eyes.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2417	lexical	\N	\N	2416	{"text": "He hurried before a justice of the peace, accompanied by Stangerson, who had become his private secretary, and represented to him that they were in danger of their lives from the jealousy and hatred of an old rival.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2418	lexical	\N	\N	2417	{"text": "That evening Jefferson Hope was taken into custody, and not being able to find sureties, was detained for some weeks.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2419	lexical	\N	\N	2418	{"text": "When at last he was liberated, it was only to find that Drebber's house was deserted, and that he and his secretary had departed for Europe.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2420	lexical	\N	\N	2419	{"text": "Again the avenger had been foiled, and again his concentrated hatred urged him to continue the pursuit.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2421	lexical	\N	\N	2420	{"text": "Funds were wanting, however, and for some time he had to return to work, saving every dollar for his approaching journey.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2422	lexical	\N	\N	2421	{"text": "At last, having collected enough to keep life in him, he departed for Europe, and tracked his enemies from city to city, working his way in any menial capacity, but never overtaking the fugitives.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2423	lexical	\N	\N	2422	{"text": "When he reached St. Petersburg they had departed for Paris; and when he followed them there he learned that they had just set off for Copenhagen.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2424	lexical	\N	\N	2423	{"text": "At the Danish capital he was again a few days late, for they had journeyed on to London, where he at last succeeded in running them to earth.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2425	lexical	\N	\N	2424	{"text": "As to what occurred there, we cannot do better than quote the old hunter's own account, as duly recorded in Dr. Watson's Journal, to which we are already under such obligations.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2426	lexical	\N	\N	2425	{"text": "CHAPTER VI.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2427	lexical	\N	\N	2426	{"text": "A CONTINUATION OF THE REMINISCENCES OF JOHN WATSON, M.D.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2428	lexical	\N	\N	2427	{"text": "Our prisoner's furious resistance did not apparently indicate any ferocity in his disposition towards ourselves, for on finding himself powerless, he smiled in an affable manner, and expressed his hopes that he had not hurt any of us in the scuffle.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2429	lexical	\N	\N	2428	{"text": "\\"I guess you're going to take me to the police-station,\\" he remarked to Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2430	lexical	\N	\N	2429	{"text": "\\"My cab's at the door.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2431	lexical	\N	\N	2430	{"text": "If you'll loose my legs I'll walk down to it.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2432	lexical	\N	\N	2431	{"text": "I'm not so light to lift as I used to be.\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2433	lexical	\N	\N	2432	{"text": "Gregson and Lestrade exchanged glances as if they thought this proposition rather a bold one; but Holmes at once took the prisoner at his word, and loosened the towel which we had bound round his ankles.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2434	lexical	\N	\N	2433	{"text": "He rose and stretched his legs, as though to assure himself that they were free once more.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2435	lexical	\N	\N	2434	{"text": "I remember that I thought to myself, as I eyed him, that I had seldom seen a more powerfully built man; and his dark sunburned face bore an expression of determination and energy which was as formidable as his personal strength.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2436	lexical	\N	\N	2435	{"text": "\\"If there's a vacant place for a chief of the police, I reckon you are the man for it,\\" he said, gazing with undisguised admiration at my fellow-lodger.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2437	lexical	\N	\N	2436	{"text": "\\"The way you kept on my trail was a caution.\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2438	lexical	\N	\N	2437	{"text": "\\"You had better come with me,\\" said Holmes to the two detectives.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2439	lexical	\N	\N	2438	{"text": "\\"I can drive you,\\" said Lestrade.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2440	lexical	\N	\N	2439	{"text": "\\"Good!", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2441	lexical	\N	\N	2440	{"text": "and Gregson can come inside with me.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2442	lexical	\N	\N	2441	{"text": "You too, Doctor, you have taken an interest in the case and may as well stick to us.\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2443	lexical	\N	\N	2442	{"text": "I assented gladly, and we all descended together.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2444	lexical	\N	\N	2443	{"text": "Our prisoner made no attempt at escape, but stepped calmly into the cab which had been his, and we followed him.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2445	lexical	\N	\N	2444	{"text": "Lestrade mounted the box, whipped up the horse, and brought us in a very short time to our destination.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2446	lexical	\N	\N	2445	{"text": "We were ushered into a small chamber where a police Inspector noted down our prisoner's name and the names of the men with whose murder he had been charged.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2447	lexical	\N	\N	2446	{"text": "The official was a white-faced unemotional man, who went through his duties in a dull mechanical way.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2448	lexical	\N	\N	2447	{"text": "\\"The prisoner will be put before the magistrates in the course of the week,\\" he said; \\"in the mean time, Mr. Jefferson Hope, have you anything that you wish to say?", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2449	lexical	\N	\N	2448	{"text": "I must warn you that your words will be taken down, and may be used against you.\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2450	lexical	\N	\N	2449	{"text": "\\"I've got a good deal to say,\\" our prisoner said slowly.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2451	lexical	\N	\N	2450	{"text": "\\"I want to tell you gentlemen all about it.\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2452	lexical	\N	\N	2451	{"text": "\\"Hadn't you better reserve that for your trial?\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2453	lexical	\N	\N	2452	{"text": "asked the Inspector.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2454	lexical	\N	\N	2453	{"text": "\\"I may never be tried,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2455	lexical	\N	\N	2454	{"text": "\\"You needn't look startled.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2456	lexical	\N	\N	2455	{"text": "It isn't suicide I am thinking of.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2457	lexical	\N	\N	2456	{"text": "Are you a Doctor?\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2458	lexical	\N	\N	2457	{"text": "He turned his fierce dark eyes upon me as he asked this last question.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2459	lexical	\N	\N	2458	{"text": "\\"Yes; I am,\\" I answered.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2460	lexical	\N	\N	2459	{"text": "\\"Then put your hand here,\\" he said, with a smile, motioning with his manacled wrists towards his chest.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2461	lexical	\N	\N	2460	{"text": "I did so; and became at once conscious of an extraordinary throbbing and commotion which was going on inside.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2462	lexical	\N	\N	2461	{"text": "The walls of his chest seemed to thrill and quiver as a frail building would do inside when some powerful engine was at work.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2463	lexical	\N	\N	2462	{"text": "In the silence of the room I could hear a dull humming and buzzing noise which proceeded from the same source.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2464	lexical	\N	\N	2463	{"text": "\\"Why,\\" I cried, \\"you have an aortic aneurism!\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2465	lexical	\N	\N	2464	{"text": "\\"That's what they call it,\\" he said, placidly.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2466	lexical	\N	\N	2465	{"text": "\\"I went to a doctor last week about it, and he told me that it is bound to burst before many days passed.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2467	lexical	\N	\N	2466	{"text": "It has been getting worse for years.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2468	lexical	\N	\N	2467	{"text": "I got it from over-exposure and under-feeding among the Salt Lake Mountains.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2469	lexical	\N	\N	2468	{"text": "I've done my work now, and I don't care how soon I go, but I should like to leave some account of the business behind me.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2470	lexical	\N	\N	2469	{"text": "I don't want to be remembered as a common cut-throat.\\"", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2471	lexical	\N	\N	2470	{"text": "The Inspector and the two detectives had a hurried discussion as to the advisability of allowing him to tell his story.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2472	lexical	\N	\N	2471	{"text": "\\"Do you consider, Doctor, that there is immediate danger?\\"", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2473	lexical	\N	\N	2472	{"text": "the former asked.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2474	lexical	\N	\N	2473	{"text": "\\"Most certainly there is,\\" I answered.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2475	lexical	\N	\N	2474	{"text": "\\"In that case it is clearly our duty, in the interests of justice, to take his statement,\\" said the Inspector.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2476	lexical	\N	\N	2475	{"text": "\\"You are at liberty, sir, to give your account, which I again warn you will be taken down.\\"", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2477	lexical	\N	\N	2476	{"text": "\\"I'll sit down, with your leave,\\" the prisoner said, suiting the action to the word.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2478	lexical	\N	\N	2477	{"text": "\\"This aneurism of mine makes me easily tired, and the tussle we had half an hour ago has not mended matters.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2479	lexical	\N	\N	2478	{"text": "I'm on the brink of the grave, and I am not likely to lie to you.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2480	lexical	\N	\N	2479	{"text": "Every word I say is the absolute truth, and how you use it is a matter of no consequence to me.\\"", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2481	lexical	\N	\N	2480	{"text": "With these words, Jefferson Hope leaned back in his chair and began the following remarkable statement.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2482	lexical	\N	\N	2481	{"text": "He spoke in a calm and methodical manner, as though the events which he narrated were commonplace enough.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2483	lexical	\N	\N	2482	{"text": "I can vouch for the accuracy of the subjoined account, for I have had access to Lestrade's note-book, in which the prisoner's words were taken down exactly as they were uttered.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2484	lexical	\N	\N	2483	{"text": "\\"It don't much matter to you why I hated these men,\\" he said; \\"it's enough that they were guilty of the death of two human beings—a father and a daughter—and that they had, therefore, forfeited their own lives.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2485	lexical	\N	\N	2484	{"text": "After the lapse of time that has passed since their crime, it was impossible for me to secure a conviction against them in any court.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2486	lexical	\N	\N	2485	{"text": "I knew of their guilt though, and I determined that I should be judge, jury, and executioner all rolled into one.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2487	lexical	\N	\N	2486	{"text": "You'd have done the same, if you have any manhood in you, if you had been in my place.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2488	lexical	\N	\N	2487	{"text": "\\"That girl that I spoke of was to have married me twenty years ago.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2489	lexical	\N	\N	2488	{"text": "She was forced into marrying that same Drebber, and broke her heart over it.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2490	lexical	\N	\N	2489	{"text": "I took the marriage ring from her dead finger, and I vowed that his dying eyes should rest upon that very ring, and that his last thoughts should be of the crime for which he was punished.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2491	lexical	\N	\N	2490	{"text": "I have carried it about with me, and have followed him and his accomplice over two continents until I caught them.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2492	lexical	\N	\N	2491	{"text": "They thought to tire me out, but they could not do it.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2493	lexical	\N	\N	2492	{"text": "If I die to-morrow, as is likely enough, I die knowing that my work in this world is done, and well done.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2494	lexical	\N	\N	2493	{"text": "They have perished, and by my hand.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2495	lexical	\N	\N	2494	{"text": "There is nothing left for me to hope for, or to desire.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2496	lexical	\N	\N	2495	{"text": "\\"They were rich and I was poor, so that it was no easy matter for me to follow them.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2497	lexical	\N	\N	2496	{"text": "When I got to London my pocket was about empty, and I found that I must turn my hand to something for my living.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2498	lexical	\N	\N	2497	{"text": "Driving and riding are as natural to me as walking, so I applied at a cabowner's office, and soon got employment.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2499	lexical	\N	\N	2498	{"text": "I was to bring a certain sum a week to the owner, and whatever was over that I might keep for myself.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2500	lexical	\N	\N	2499	{"text": "There was seldom much over, but I managed to scrape along somehow.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2501	lexical	\N	\N	2500	{"text": "The hardest job was to learn my way about, for I reckon that of all the mazes that ever were contrived, this city is the most confusing.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2536	lexical	\N	\N	2535	{"text": "My plans were already formed.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2502	lexical	\N	\N	2501	{"text": "I had a map beside me though, and when once I had spotted the principal hotels and stations, I got on pretty well.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2503	lexical	\N	\N	2502	{"text": "\\"It was some time before I found out where my two gentlemen were living; but I inquired and inquired until at last I dropped across them.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2504	lexical	\N	\N	2503	{"text": "They were at a boarding-house at Camberwell, over on the other side of the river.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2505	lexical	\N	\N	2504	{"text": "When once I found them out I knew that I had them at my mercy.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2506	lexical	\N	\N	2505	{"text": "I had grown my beard, and there was no chance of their recognizing me.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2507	lexical	\N	\N	2506	{"text": "I would dog them and follow them until I saw my opportunity.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2508	lexical	\N	\N	2507	{"text": "I was determined that they should not escape me again.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2509	lexical	\N	\N	2508	{"text": "\\"They were very near doing it for all that.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2510	lexical	\N	\N	2509	{"text": "Go where they would about London, I was always at their heels.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2511	lexical	\N	\N	2510	{"text": "Sometimes I followed them on my cab, and sometimes on foot, but the former was the best, for then they could not get away from me.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2512	lexical	\N	\N	2511	{"text": "It was only early in the morning or late at night that I could earn anything, so that I began to get behindhand with my employer.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2513	lexical	\N	\N	2512	{"text": "I did not mind that, however, as long as I could lay my hand upon the men I wanted.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2514	lexical	\N	\N	2513	{"text": "\\"They were very cunning, though.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2515	lexical	\N	\N	2514	{"text": "They must have thought that there was some chance of their being followed, for they would never go out alone, and never after nightfall.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2516	lexical	\N	\N	2515	{"text": "During two weeks I drove behind them every day, and never once saw them separate.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2517	lexical	\N	\N	2516	{"text": "Drebber himself was drunk half the time, but Stangerson was not to be caught napping.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2518	lexical	\N	\N	2517	{"text": "I watched them late and early, but never saw the ghost of a chance; but I was not discouraged, for something told me that the hour had almost come.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2519	lexical	\N	\N	2518	{"text": "My only fear was that this thing in my chest might burst a little too soon and leave my work undone.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2520	lexical	\N	\N	2519	{"text": "\\"At last, one evening I was driving up and down Torquay Terrace, as the street was called in which they boarded, when I saw a cab drive up to their door.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2521	lexical	\N	\N	2520	{"text": "Presently some luggage was brought out, and after a time Drebber and Stangerson followed it, and drove off.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2522	lexical	\N	\N	2521	{"text": "I whipped up my horse and kept within sight of them, feeling very ill at ease, for I feared that they were going to shift their quarters.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2523	lexical	\N	\N	2522	{"text": "At Euston Station they got out, and I left a boy to hold my horse, and followed them on to the platform.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2524	lexical	\N	\N	2523	{"text": "I heard them ask for the Liverpool train, and the guard answer that one had just gone and there would not be another for some hours.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2525	lexical	\N	\N	2524	{"text": "Stangerson seemed to be put out at that, but Drebber was rather pleased than otherwise.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2526	lexical	\N	\N	2525	{"text": "I got so close to them in the bustle that I could hear every word that passed between them.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2527	lexical	\N	\N	2526	{"text": "Drebber said that he had a little business of his own to do, and that if the other would wait for him he would soon rejoin him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2528	lexical	\N	\N	2527	{"text": "His companion remonstrated with him, and reminded him that they had resolved to stick together.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2529	lexical	\N	\N	2528	{"text": "Drebber answered that the matter was a delicate one, and that he must go alone.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2530	lexical	\N	\N	2529	{"text": "I could not catch what Stangerson said to that, but the other burst out swearing, and reminded him that he was nothing more than his paid servant, and that he must not presume to dictate to him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2531	lexical	\N	\N	2530	{"text": "On that the Secretary gave it up as a bad job, and simply bargained with him that if he missed the last train he should rejoin him at Halliday's Private Hotel; to which Drebber answered that he would be back on the platform before eleven, and made his way out of the station.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2532	lexical	\N	\N	2531	{"text": "\\"The moment for which I had waited so long had at last come.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2533	lexical	\N	\N	2532	{"text": "I had my enemies within my power.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2534	lexical	\N	\N	2533	{"text": "Together they could protect each other, but singly they were at my mercy.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2537	lexical	\N	\N	2536	{"text": "There is no satisfaction in vengeance unless the offender has time to realize who it is that strikes him, and why retribution has come upon him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2538	lexical	\N	\N	2537	{"text": "I had my plans arranged by which I should have the opportunity of making the man who had wronged me understand that his old sin had found him out.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2539	lexical	\N	\N	2538	{"text": "It chanced that some days before a gentleman who had been engaged in looking over some houses in the Brixton Road had dropped the key of one of them in my carriage.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2540	lexical	\N	\N	2539	{"text": "It was claimed that same evening, and returned; but in the interval I had taken a moulding of it, and had a duplicate constructed.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2541	lexical	\N	\N	2540	{"text": "By means of this I had access to at least one spot in this great city where I could rely upon being free from interruption.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2542	lexical	\N	\N	2541	{"text": "How to get Drebber to that house was the difficult problem which I had now to solve.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2543	lexical	\N	\N	2542	{"text": "\\"He walked down the road and went into one or two liquor shops, staying for nearly half-an-hour in the last of them.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2544	lexical	\N	\N	2543	{"text": "When he came out he staggered in his walk, and was evidently pretty well on.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2545	lexical	\N	\N	2544	{"text": "There was a hansom just in front of me, and he hailed it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2546	lexical	\N	\N	2545	{"text": "I followed it so close that the nose of my horse was within a yard of his driver the whole way.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2547	lexical	\N	\N	2546	{"text": "We rattled across Waterloo Bridge and through miles of streets, until, to my astonishment, we found ourselves back in the Terrace in which he had boarded.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2548	lexical	\N	\N	2547	{"text": "I could not imagine what his intention was in returning there; but I went on and pulled up my cab a hundred yards or so from the house.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2549	lexical	\N	\N	2548	{"text": "He entered it, and his hansom drove away.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2550	lexical	\N	\N	2549	{"text": "Give me a glass of water, if you please.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2551	lexical	\N	\N	2550	{"text": "My mouth gets dry with the talking.\\"", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2552	lexical	\N	\N	2551	{"text": "I handed him the glass, and he drank it down.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2553	lexical	\N	\N	2552	{"text": "\\"That's better,\\" he said.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2554	lexical	\N	\N	2553	{"text": "\\"Well, I waited for a quarter of an hour, or more, when suddenly there came a noise like people struggling inside the house.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2555	lexical	\N	\N	2554	{"text": "Next moment the door was flung open and two men appeared, one of whom was Drebber, and the other was a young chap whom I had never seen before.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2556	lexical	\N	\N	2555	{"text": "This fellow had Drebber by the collar, and when they came to the head of the steps he gave him a shove and a kick which sent him half across the road.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2557	lexical	\N	\N	2556	{"text": "' He was so hot that I think he would have thrashed Drebber with his cudgel, only that the cur staggered away down the road as fast as his legs would carry him.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2558	lexical	\N	\N	2557	{"text": "He ran as far as the corner, and then, seeing my cab, he hailed me and jumped in.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2559	lexical	\N	\N	2558	{"text": "'Drive me to Halliday's Private Hotel,' said he.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2560	lexical	\N	\N	2559	{"text": "eeing my cab, he hailed me and jumped in. 'Drive me to Halliday's Private Hotel,' said he.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2561	lexical	\N	\N	2560	{"text": "\\"When I had him fairly inside my cab, my heart jumped so with joy that I feared lest at this last moment my aneurism might go wrong.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2562	lexical	\N	\N	2561	{"text": "I drove along slowly, weighing in my own mind what it was best to do.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2563	lexical	\N	\N	2562	{"text": "I might take him right out into the country, and there in some deserted lane have my last interview with him.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2564	lexical	\N	\N	2563	{"text": "I had almost decided upon this, when he solved the problem for me.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2565	lexical	\N	\N	2564	{"text": "The craze for drink had seized him again, and he ordered me to pull up outside a gin palace.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2566	lexical	\N	\N	2565	{"text": "He went in, leaving word that I should wait for him.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2567	lexical	\N	\N	2566	{"text": "There he remained until closing time, and when he came out he was so far gone that I knew the game was in my own hands.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2568	lexical	\N	\N	2567	{"text": "\\"Don't imagine that I intended to kill him in cold blood.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2569	lexical	\N	\N	2568	{"text": "It would only have been rigid justice if I had done so, but I could not bring myself to do it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2670	lexical	\N	\N	2669	{"text": "Until then I will be responsible for him.\\"", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2570	lexical	\N	\N	2569	{"text": "I had long determined that he should have a show for his life if he chose to take advantage of it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2571	lexical	\N	\N	2570	{"text": "Among the many billets which I have filled in America during my wandering life, I was once janitor and sweeper out of the laboratory at York College.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2572	lexical	\N	\N	2571	{"text": "One day the professor was lecturing on poisons, and he showed his students some alkaloid, as he called it, which he had extracted from some South American arrow poison, and which was so powerful that the least grain meant instant death.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2573	lexical	\N	\N	2572	{"text": "I spotted the bottle in which this preparation was kept, and when they were all gone, I helped myself to a little of it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2574	lexical	\N	\N	2573	{"text": "I was a fairly good dispenser, so I worked this alkaloid into small, soluble pills, and each pill I put in a box with a similar pill made without the poison.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2575	lexical	\N	\N	2574	{"text": "I determined at the time that when I had my chance, my gentlemen should each have a draw out of one of these boxes, while I ate the pill that remained.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2576	lexical	\N	\N	2575	{"text": "It would be quite as deadly, and a good deal less noisy than firing across a handkerchief.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2577	lexical	\N	\N	2576	{"text": "From that day I had always my pill boxes about with me, and the time had now come when I was to use them.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2578	lexical	\N	\N	2577	{"text": "\\"It was nearer one than twelve, and a wild, bleak night, blowing hard and raining in torrents.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2579	lexical	\N	\N	2578	{"text": "Dismal as it was outside, I was glad within—so glad that I could have shouted out from pure exultation.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2580	lexical	\N	\N	2579	{"text": "If any of you gentlemen have ever pined for a thing, and longed for it during twenty long years, and then suddenly found it within your reach, you would understand my feelings.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2581	lexical	\N	\N	2580	{"text": "I lit a cigar, and puffed at it to steady my nerves, but my hands were trembling, and my temples throbbing with excitement.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2582	lexical	\N	\N	2581	{"text": "As I drove, I could see old John Ferrier and sweet Lucy looking at me out of the darkness and smiling at me, just as plain as I see you all in this room.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2583	lexical	\N	\N	2582	{"text": "All the way they were ahead of me, one on each side of the horse until I pulled up at the house in the Brixton Road.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2584	lexical	\N	\N	2583	{"text": "\\"There was not a soul to be seen, nor a sound to be heard, except the dripping of the rain.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2585	lexical	\N	\N	2584	{"text": "When I looked in at the window, I found Drebber all huddled together in a drunken sleep.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2586	lexical	\N	\N	2585	{"text": "I shook him by the arm, 'It's time to get out,' I said.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2587	lexical	\N	\N	2586	{"text": "\\"'All right, cabby,' said he.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2588	lexical	\N	\N	2587	{"text": "\\"I suppose he thought we had come to the hotel that he had mentioned, for he got out without another word, and followed me down the garden.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2589	lexical	\N	\N	2588	{"text": "I had to walk beside him to keep him steady, for he was still a little top-heavy.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2590	lexical	\N	\N	2589	{"text": "When we came to the door, I opened it, and led him into the front room.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2591	lexical	\N	\N	2590	{"text": "I give you my word that all the way, the father and the daughter were walking in front of us.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2592	lexical	\N	\N	2591	{"text": "\\"'It's infernally dark,' said he, stamping about.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2593	lexical	\N	\N	2592	{"text": "\\"'We'll soon have a light,' I said, striking a match and putting it to a wax candle which I had brought with me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2594	lexical	\N	\N	2593	{"text": "'Now, Enoch Drebber,' I continued, turning to him, and holding the light to my own face, 'who am I?'", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2595	lexical	\N	\N	2594	{"text": "\\"He gazed at me with bleared, drunken eyes for a moment, and then I saw a horror spring up in them, and convulse his whole features, which showed me that he knew me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2596	lexical	\N	\N	2595	{"text": "He staggered back with a livid face, and I saw the perspiration break out upon his brow, while his teeth chattered in his head.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2597	lexical	\N	\N	2596	{"text": "At the sight, I leaned my back against the door and laughed loud and long.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2598	lexical	\N	\N	2597	{"text": "I had always known that vengeance would be sweet, but I had never hoped for the contentment of soul which now possessed me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2599	lexical	\N	\N	2598	{"text": "' I said; 'I have hunted you from Salt Lake City to St. Petersburg, and you have always escaped me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2600	lexical	\N	\N	2599	{"text": "' He shrunk still further away as I spoke, and I could see on his face that he thought I was mad.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2601	lexical	\N	\N	2600	{"text": "So I was for the time.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2602	lexical	\N	\N	2601	{"text": "The pulses in my temples beat like sledge-hammers, and I believe I would have had a fit of some sort if the blood had not gushed from my nose and relieved me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2603	lexical	\N	\N	2602	{"text": "-hammers, and I believe I would have had a fit of some sort if the blood had not gushed from my nose and relieved me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2604	lexical	\N	\N	2603	{"text": "' I cried, locking the door, and shaking the key in his face.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2605	lexical	\N	\N	2604	{"text": "' I saw his coward lips tremble as I spoke.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2606	lexical	\N	\N	2605	{"text": "He would have begged for his life, but he knew well that it was useless.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2607	lexical	\N	\N	2606	{"text": "w his coward lips tremble as I spoke. He would have begged for his life, but he knew well that it was useless.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2608	lexical	\N	\N	2607	{"text": "' he stammered.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2609	lexical	\N	\N	2608	{"text": "der me?' he stammered.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2610	lexical	\N	\N	2609	{"text": "\\"'There is no murder,' I answered.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2611	lexical	\N	\N	2610	{"text": "'Who talks of murdering a mad dog?", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2612	lexical	\N	\N	2611	{"text": "What mercy had you upon my poor darling, when you dragged her from her slaughtered father, and bore her away to your accursed and shameless harem.'", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2613	lexical	\N	\N	2612	{"text": "\\"'It was not I who killed her father,' he cried.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2614	lexical	\N	\N	2613	{"text": "\\"'But it was you who broke her innocent heart,' I shrieked, thrusting the box before him.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2615	lexical	\N	\N	2614	{"text": "'Let the high God judge between us.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2616	lexical	\N	\N	2615	{"text": "Choose and eat.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2617	lexical	\N	\N	2616	{"text": "There is death in one and life in the other.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2618	lexical	\N	\N	2617	{"text": "I shall take what you leave.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2619	lexical	\N	\N	2618	{"text": "Let us see if there is justice upon the earth, or if we are ruled by chance.'", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2620	lexical	\N	\N	2619	{"text": "\\"He cowered away with wild cries and prayers for mercy, but I drew my knife and held it to his throat until he had obeyed me.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2621	lexical	\N	\N	2620	{"text": "Then I swallowed the other, and we stood facing one another in silence for a minute or more, waiting to see which was to live and which was to die.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2622	lexical	\N	\N	2621	{"text": "Shall I ever forget the look which came over his face when the first warning pangs told him that the poison was in his system?", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2623	lexical	\N	\N	2622	{"text": "I laughed as I saw it, and held Lucy's marriage ring in front of his eyes.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2624	lexical	\N	\N	2623	{"text": "It was but for a moment, for the action of the alkaloid is rapid.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2625	lexical	\N	\N	2624	{"text": "A spasm of pain contorted his features; he threw his hands out in front of him, staggered, and then, with a hoarse cry, fell heavily upon the floor.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2626	lexical	\N	\N	2625	{"text": "I turned him over with my foot, and placed my hand upon his heart.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2627	lexical	\N	\N	2626	{"text": "There was no movement.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2628	lexical	\N	\N	2627	{"text": "He was dead!", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2629	lexical	\N	\N	2628	{"text": "\\"The blood had been streaming from my nose, but I had taken no notice of it.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2630	lexical	\N	\N	2629	{"text": "I don't know what it was that put it into my head to write upon the wall with it.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2631	lexical	\N	\N	2630	{"text": "Perhaps it was some mischievous idea of setting the police upon a wrong track, for I felt light-hearted and cheerful.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2632	lexical	\N	\N	2631	{"text": "I remembered a German being found in New York with RACHE written up above him, and it was argued at the time in the newspapers that the secret societies must have done it.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2633	lexical	\N	\N	2632	{"text": "I guessed that what puzzled the New Yorkers would puzzle the Londoners, so I dipped my finger in my own blood and printed it on a convenient place on the wall.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2634	lexical	\N	\N	2633	{"text": "Then I walked down to my cab and found that there was nobody about, and that the night was still very wild.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2635	lexical	\N	\N	2634	{"text": "I had driven some distance when I put my hand into the pocket in which I usually kept Lucy's ring, and found that it was not there.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2636	lexical	\N	\N	2635	{"text": "I was thunderstruck at this, for it was the only memento that I had of her.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2707	lexical	\N	\N	2706	{"text": "I approached the house, as you know, on foot, and with my mind entirely free from all impressions.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2637	lexical	\N	\N	2636	{"text": "Thinking that I might have dropped it when I stooped over Drebber's body, I drove back, and leaving my cab in a side street, I went boldly up to the house—for I was ready to dare anything rather than lose the ring.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2638	lexical	\N	\N	2637	{"text": "When I arrived there, I walked right into the arms of a police-officer who was coming out, and only managed to disarm his suspicions by pretending to be hopelessly drunk.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2639	lexical	\N	\N	2638	{"text": "\\"That was how Enoch Drebber came to his end.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2640	lexical	\N	\N	2639	{"text": "All I had to do then was to do as much for Stangerson, and so pay off John Ferrier's debt.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2641	lexical	\N	\N	2640	{"text": "I knew that he was staying at Halliday's Private Hotel, and I hung about all day, but he never came out.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2642	lexical	\N	\N	2641	{"text": "I fancy that he suspected something when Drebber failed to put in an appearance.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2643	lexical	\N	\N	2642	{"text": "He was cunning, was Stangerson, and always on his guard.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2644	lexical	\N	\N	2643	{"text": "If he thought he could keep me off by staying indoors he was very much mistaken.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2645	lexical	\N	\N	2644	{"text": "I soon found out which was the window of his bedroom, and early next morning I took advantage of some ladders which were lying in the lane behind the hotel, and so made my way into his room in the grey of the dawn.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2646	lexical	\N	\N	2645	{"text": "I woke him up and told him that the hour had come when he was to answer for the life he had taken so long before.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2647	lexical	\N	\N	2646	{"text": "I described Drebber's death to him, and I gave him the same choice of the poisoned pills.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2648	lexical	\N	\N	2647	{"text": "Instead of grasping at the chance of safety which that offered him, he sprang from his bed and flew at my throat.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2649	lexical	\N	\N	2648	{"text": "In self-defence I stabbed him to the heart.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2650	lexical	\N	\N	2649	{"text": "It would have been the same in any case, for Providence would never have allowed his guilty hand to pick out anything but the poison.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2651	lexical	\N	\N	2650	{"text": "\\"I have little more to say, and it's as well, for I am about done up.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2652	lexical	\N	\N	2651	{"text": "I went on cabbing it for a day or so, intending to keep at it until I could save enough to take me back to America.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2653	lexical	\N	\N	2652	{"text": "I was standing in the yard when a ragged youngster asked if there was a cabby there called Jefferson Hope, and said that his cab was wanted by a gentleman at 221B, Baker Street.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2654	lexical	\N	\N	2653	{"text": "I went round, suspecting no harm, and the next thing I knew, this young man here had the bracelets on my wrists, and as neatly shackled as ever I saw in my life.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2655	lexical	\N	\N	2654	{"text": "That's the whole of my story, gentlemen.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2656	lexical	\N	\N	2655	{"text": "You may consider me to be a murderer; but I hold that I am just as much an officer of justice as you are.\\"", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2657	lexical	\N	\N	2656	{"text": "So thrilling had the man's narrative been, and his manner was so impressive that we had sat silent and absorbed.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2658	lexical	\N	\N	2657	{"text": "Even the professional detectives, _blasé_ as they were in every detail of crime, appeared to be keenly interested in the man's story.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2659	lexical	\N	\N	2658	{"text": "When he finished we sat for some minutes in a stillness which was only broken by the scratching of Lestrade's pencil as he gave the finishing touches to his shorthand account.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2660	lexical	\N	\N	2659	{"text": "\\"There is only one point on which I should like a little more information,\\" Sherlock Holmes said at last.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2661	lexical	\N	\N	2660	{"text": "\\"Who was your accomplice who came for the ring which I advertised?\\"", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2662	lexical	\N	\N	2661	{"text": "The prisoner winked at my friend jocosely.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2663	lexical	\N	\N	2662	{"text": "\\"I can tell my own secrets,\\" he said, \\"but I don't get other people into trouble.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2664	lexical	\N	\N	2663	{"text": "I saw your advertisement, and I thought it might be a plant, or it might be the ring which I wanted.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2665	lexical	\N	\N	2664	{"text": "My friend volunteered to go and see.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2666	lexical	\N	\N	2665	{"text": "I think you'll own he did it smartly.\\"", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2667	lexical	\N	\N	2666	{"text": "\\"Not a doubt of that,\\" said Holmes heartily.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2668	lexical	\N	\N	2667	{"text": "\\"Now, gentlemen,\\" the Inspector remarked gravely, \\"the forms of the law must be complied with.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2669	lexical	\N	\N	2668	{"text": "On Thursday the prisoner will be brought before the magistrates, and your attendance will be required.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2671	lexical	\N	\N	2670	{"text": "He rang the bell as he spoke, and Jefferson Hope was led off by a couple of warders, while my friend and I made our way out of the Station and took a cab back to Baker Street.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2672	lexical	\N	\N	2671	{"text": "CHAPTER VII.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2673	lexical	\N	\N	2672	{"text": "THE CONCLUSION.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2674	lexical	\N	\N	2673	{"text": "We had all been warned to appear before the magistrates upon the Thursday; but when the Thursday came there was no occasion for our testimony.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2675	lexical	\N	\N	2674	{"text": "A higher Judge had taken the matter in hand, and Jefferson Hope had been summoned before a tribunal where strict justice would be meted out to him.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2676	lexical	\N	\N	2675	{"text": "On the very night after his capture the aneurism burst, and he was found in the morning stretched upon the floor of the cell, with a placid smile upon his face, as though he had been able in his dying moments to look back upon a useful life, and on work well done.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2677	lexical	\N	\N	2676	{"text": "\\"Gregson and Lestrade will be wild about his death,\\" Holmes remarked, as we chatted it over next evening.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2678	lexical	\N	\N	2677	{"text": "\\"Where will their grand advertisement be now?\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2679	lexical	\N	\N	2678	{"text": "\\"I don't see that they had very much to do with his capture,\\" I answered.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2680	lexical	\N	\N	2679	{"text": "\\"What you do in this world is a matter of no consequence,\\" returned my companion, bitterly.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2681	lexical	\N	\N	2680	{"text": "\\"The question is, what can you make people believe that you have done.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2682	lexical	\N	\N	2681	{"text": "Never mind,\\" he continued, more brightly, after a pause.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2683	lexical	\N	\N	2682	{"text": "\\"I would not have missed the investigation for anything.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2684	lexical	\N	\N	2683	{"text": "There has been no better case within my recollection.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2685	lexical	\N	\N	2684	{"text": "Simple as it was, there were several most instructive points about it.\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2686	lexical	\N	\N	2685	{"text": "\\"Simple!\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2687	lexical	\N	\N	2686	{"text": "I ejaculated.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2688	lexical	\N	\N	2687	{"text": "\\"Well, really, it can hardly be described as otherwise,\\" said Sherlock Holmes, smiling at my surprise.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2689	lexical	\N	\N	2688	{"text": "\\"The proof of its intrinsic simplicity is, that without any help save a few very ordinary deductions I was able to lay my hand upon the criminal within three days.\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2690	lexical	\N	\N	2689	{"text": "\\"That is true,\\" said I.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2691	lexical	\N	\N	2690	{"text": "\\"I have already explained to you that what is out of the common is usually a guide rather than a hindrance.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2692	lexical	\N	\N	2691	{"text": "In solving a problem of this sort, the grand thing is to be able to reason backwards.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2693	lexical	\N	\N	2692	{"text": "That is a very useful accomplishment, and a very easy one, but people do not practise it much.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2694	lexical	\N	\N	2693	{"text": "In the every-day affairs of life it is more useful to reason forwards, and so the other comes to be neglected.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2695	lexical	\N	\N	2694	{"text": "There are fifty who can reason synthetically for one who can reason analytically.\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2696	lexical	\N	\N	2695	{"text": "\\"I confess,\\" said I, \\"that I do not quite follow you.\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2697	lexical	\N	\N	2696	{"text": "\\"I hardly expected that you would.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2698	lexical	\N	\N	2697	{"text": "Let me see if I can make it clearer.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2699	lexical	\N	\N	2698	{"text": "Most people, if you describe a train of events to them, will tell you what the result would be.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2700	lexical	\N	\N	2699	{"text": "They can put those events together in their minds, and argue from them that something will come to pass.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2701	lexical	\N	\N	2700	{"text": "There are few people, however, who, if you told them a result, would be able to evolve from their own inner consciousness what the steps were which led up to that result.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2702	lexical	\N	\N	2701	{"text": "This power is what I mean when I talk of reasoning backwards, or analytically.\\"", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2703	lexical	\N	\N	2702	{"text": "\\"I understand,\\" said I.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2704	lexical	\N	\N	2703	{"text": "\\"Now this was a case in which you were given the result and had to find everything else for yourself.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2705	lexical	\N	\N	2704	{"text": "Now let me endeavour to show you the different steps in my reasoning.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2706	lexical	\N	\N	2705	{"text": "To begin at the beginning.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2708	lexical	\N	\N	2707	{"text": "I naturally began by examining the roadway, and there, as I have already explained to you, I saw clearly the marks of a cab, which, I ascertained by inquiry, must have been there during the night.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2709	lexical	\N	\N	2708	{"text": "I satisfied myself that it was a cab and not a private carriage by the narrow gauge of the wheels.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2710	lexical	\N	\N	2709	{"text": "The ordinary London growler is considerably less wide than a gentleman's brougham.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2711	lexical	\N	\N	2710	{"text": "\\"This was the first point gained.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2712	lexical	\N	\N	2711	{"text": "I then walked slowly down the garden path, which happened to be composed of a clay soil, peculiarly suitable for taking impressions.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2713	lexical	\N	\N	2712	{"text": "No doubt it appeared to you to be a mere trampled line of slush, but to my trained eyes every mark upon its surface had a meaning.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2714	lexical	\N	\N	2713	{"text": "There is no branch of detective science which is so important and so much neglected as the art of tracing footsteps.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2715	lexical	\N	\N	2714	{"text": "Happily, I have always laid great stress upon it, and much practice has made it second nature to me.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2716	lexical	\N	\N	2715	{"text": "I saw the heavy footmarks of the constables, but I saw also the track of the two men who had first passed through the garden.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2717	lexical	\N	\N	2716	{"text": "It was easy to tell that they had been before the others, because in places their marks had been entirely obliterated by the others coming upon the top of them.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2718	lexical	\N	\N	2717	{"text": "In this way my second link was formed, which told me that the nocturnal visitors were two in number, one remarkable for his height (as I calculated from the length of his stride), and the other fashionably dressed, to judge from the small and elegant impression left by his boots.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2719	lexical	\N	\N	2718	{"text": "\\"On entering the house this last inference was confirmed.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2720	lexical	\N	\N	2719	{"text": "My well-booted man lay before me.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2721	lexical	\N	\N	2720	{"text": "The tall one, then, had done the murder, if murder there was.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2722	lexical	\N	\N	2721	{"text": "There was no wound upon the dead man's person, but the agitated expression upon his face assured me that he had foreseen his fate before it came upon him.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2723	lexical	\N	\N	2722	{"text": "Men who die from heart disease, or any sudden natural cause, never by any chance exhibit agitation upon their features.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2724	lexical	\N	\N	2723	{"text": "Having sniffed the dead man's lips I detected a slightly sour smell, and I came to the conclusion that he had had poison forced upon him.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2725	lexical	\N	\N	2724	{"text": "Again, I argued that it had been forced upon him from the hatred and fear expressed upon his face.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2726	lexical	\N	\N	2725	{"text": "By the method of exclusion, I had arrived at this result, for no other hypothesis would meet the facts.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2727	lexical	\N	\N	2726	{"text": "Do not imagine that it was a very unheard of idea.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2728	lexical	\N	\N	2727	{"text": "The forcible administration of poison is by no means a new thing in criminal annals.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2729	lexical	\N	\N	2728	{"text": "The cases of Dolsky in Odessa, and of Leturier in Montpellier, will occur at once to any toxicologist.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2730	lexical	\N	\N	2729	{"text": "\\"And now came the great question as to the reason why.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2731	lexical	\N	\N	2730	{"text": "Robbery had not been the object of the murder, for nothing was taken.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2732	lexical	\N	\N	2731	{"text": "Was it politics, then, or was it a woman?", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2733	lexical	\N	\N	2732	{"text": "That was the question which confronted me.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2734	lexical	\N	\N	2733	{"text": "I was inclined from the first to the latter supposition.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2735	lexical	\N	\N	2734	{"text": "Political assassins are only too glad to do their work and to fly.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2736	lexical	\N	\N	2735	{"text": "This murder had, on the contrary, been done most deliberately, and the perpetrator had left his tracks all over the room, showing that he had been there all the time.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2737	lexical	\N	\N	2736	{"text": "It must have been a private wrong, and not a political one, which called for such a methodical revenge.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2738	lexical	\N	\N	2737	{"text": "When the inscription was discovered upon the wall I was more inclined than ever to my opinion.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2739	lexical	\N	\N	2738	{"text": "The thing was too evidently a blind.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2740	lexical	\N	\N	2739	{"text": "When the ring was found, however, it settled the question.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	afghanistan	entity	character	afghanistan	\N	{"firstSection": "section_9"}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2741	lexical	\N	\N	2740	{"text": "Clearly the murderer had used it to remind his victim of some dead or absent woman.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2742	lexical	\N	\N	2741	{"text": "It was at this point that I asked Gregson whether he had enquired in his telegram to Cleveland as to any particular point in Mr. Drebber's former career.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2743	lexical	\N	\N	2742	{"text": "He answered, you remember, in the negative.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2744	lexical	\N	\N	2743	{"text": "\\"I then proceeded to make a careful examination of the room, which confirmed me in my opinion as to the murderer's height, and furnished me with the additional details as to the Trichinopoly cigar and the length of his nails.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2745	lexical	\N	\N	2744	{"text": "I had already come to the conclusion, since there were no signs of a struggle, that the blood which covered the floor had burst from the murderer's nose in his excitement.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2746	lexical	\N	\N	2745	{"text": "I could perceive that the track of blood coincided with the track of his feet.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2747	lexical	\N	\N	2746	{"text": "It is seldom that any man, unless he is very full-blooded, breaks out in this way through emotion, so I hazarded the opinion that the criminal was probably a robust and ruddy-faced man.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2748	lexical	\N	\N	2747	{"text": "Events proved that I had judged correctly.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2749	lexical	\N	\N	2748	{"text": "\\"Having left the house, I proceeded to do what Gregson had neglected.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2750	lexical	\N	\N	2749	{"text": "I telegraphed to the head of the police at Cleveland, limiting my enquiry to the circumstances connected with the marriage of Enoch Drebber.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2751	lexical	\N	\N	2750	{"text": "The answer was conclusive.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2752	lexical	\N	\N	2751	{"text": "It told me that Drebber had already applied for the protection of the law against an old rival in love, named Jefferson Hope, and that this same Hope was at present in Europe.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2753	lexical	\N	\N	2752	{"text": "I knew now that I held the clue to the mystery in my hand, and all that remained was to secure the murderer.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2754	lexical	\N	\N	2753	{"text": "\\"I had already determined in my own mind that the man who had walked into the house with Drebber, was none other than the man who had driven the cab.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2755	lexical	\N	\N	2754	{"text": "The marks in the road showed me that the horse had wandered on in a way which would have been impossible had there been anyone in charge of it.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2756	lexical	\N	\N	2755	{"text": "Where, then, could the driver be, unless he were inside the house?", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2757	lexical	\N	\N	2756	{"text": "Again, it is absurd to suppose that any sane man would carry out a deliberate crime under the very eyes, as it were, of a third person, who was sure to betray him.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2758	lexical	\N	\N	2757	{"text": "Lastly, supposing one man wished to dog another through London, what better means could he adopt than to turn cabdriver.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2759	lexical	\N	\N	2758	{"text": "All these considerations led me to the irresistible conclusion that Jefferson Hope was to be found among the jarveys of the Metropolis.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2760	lexical	\N	\N	2759	{"text": "\\"If he had been one there was no reason to believe that he had ceased to be.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2761	lexical	\N	\N	2760	{"text": "On the contrary, from his point of view, any sudden change would be likely to draw attention to himself.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2762	lexical	\N	\N	2761	{"text": "He would, probably, for a time at least, continue to perform his duties.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2763	lexical	\N	\N	2762	{"text": "There was no reason to suppose that he was going under an assumed name.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2764	lexical	\N	\N	2763	{"text": "Why should he change his name in a country where no one knew his original one?", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2765	lexical	\N	\N	2764	{"text": "I therefore organized my Street Arab detective corps, and sent them systematically to every cab proprietor in London until they ferreted out the man that I wanted.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2766	lexical	\N	\N	2765	{"text": "How well they succeeded, and how quickly I took advantage of it, are still fresh in your recollection.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2767	lexical	\N	\N	2766	{"text": "The murder of Stangerson was an incident which was entirely unexpected, but which could hardly in any case have been prevented.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2768	lexical	\N	\N	2767	{"text": "Through it, as you know, I came into possession of the pills, the existence of which I had already surmised.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2769	lexical	\N	\N	2768	{"text": "You see the whole thing is a chain of logical sequences without a break or flaw.\\"", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2770	lexical	\N	\N	2769	{"text": "\\"It is wonderful!\\"", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2771	lexical	\N	\N	2770	{"text": "I cried.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2772	lexical	\N	\N	2771	{"text": "\\"Your merits should be publicly recognized.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2773	lexical	\N	\N	2772	{"text": "You should publish an account of the case.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2774	lexical	\N	\N	2773	{"text": "If you won't, I will for you.\\"", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2775	lexical	\N	\N	2774	{"text": "\\"You may do what you like, Doctor,\\" he answered.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2776	lexical	\N	\N	2775	{"text": "\\"See here!\\"", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2777	lexical	\N	\N	2776	{"text": "he continued, handing a paper over to me, \\"look at this!\\"", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2778	lexical	\N	\N	2777	{"text": "It was the _Echo_ for the day, and the paragraph to which he pointed was devoted to the case in question.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2779	lexical	\N	\N	2778	{"text": "\\"The public,\\" it said, \\"have lost a sensational treat through the sudden death of the man Hope, who was suspected of the murder of Mr. Enoch Drebber and of Mr. Joseph Stangerson.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2780	lexical	\N	\N	2779	{"text": "The details of the case will probably be never known now, though we are informed upon good authority that the crime was the result of an old standing and romantic feud, in which love and Mormonism bore a part.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2781	lexical	\N	\N	2780	{"text": "It seems that both the victims belonged, in their younger days, to the Latter Day Saints, and Hope, the deceased prisoner, hails also from Salt Lake City.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2782	lexical	\N	\N	2781	{"text": "If the case has had no other effect, it, at least, brings out in the most striking manner the efficiency of our detective police force, and will serve as a lesson to all foreigners that they will do wisely to settle their feuds at home, and not to carry them on to British soil.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2783	lexical	\N	\N	2782	{"text": "It is an open secret that the credit of this smart capture belongs entirely to the well-known Scotland Yard officials, Messrs.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2784	lexical	\N	\N	2783	{"text": "Lestrade and Gregson.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2785	lexical	\N	\N	2784	{"text": "The man was apprehended, it appears, in the rooms of a certain Mr. Sherlock Holmes, who has himself, as an amateur, shown some talent in the detective line, and who, with such instructors, may hope in time to attain to some degree of their skill.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2786	lexical	\N	\N	2785	{"text": "It is expected that a testimonial of some sort will be presented to the two officers as a fitting recognition of their services.\\"", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2787	lexical	\N	\N	2786	{"text": "\\"Didn't I tell you so when we started?\\"", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2788	lexical	\N	\N	2787	{"text": "cried Sherlock Holmes with a laugh.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2789	lexical	\N	\N	2788	{"text": "\\"That's the result of all our Study in Scarlet: to get them a testimonial!\\"", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2790	lexical	\N	\N	2789	{"text": "\\"Never mind,\\" I answered, \\"I have all the facts in my journal, and the public shall know them.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2791	lexical	\N	\N	2790	{"text": "In the meantime you must make yourself contented by the consciousness of success, like the Roman miser—", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	sentence_2792	lexical	\N	\N	2791	{"text": "\\"'Populus me sibilat, at mihi plaudo Ipse domi simul ac nummos contemplor in arca.'\\"", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
