a-study-in-scarlet	note	entity	document	Note from Tobias Gregson	\N	{"to": "sherlock_holmes", "from": "tobias_gregson", "description": "A note/letter brought by the commissionaire about the body at Lauriston Gardens.", "firstSection": "section_16", "document_type": "letter", "content_summary": "A bad business occurred during the night at 3 Lauriston Gardens off the Brixton Road. A man on the beat saw a light there about two in the morning, found the door open, and discovered the body of a well-dressed gentleman with cards in his pocket naming Enoch J. Drebber. There had been no robbery and no evidence how he died. There are marks of blood in the room, but no wound on the body. Gregson asks Holmes to come before twelve or send his opinion."}
