a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_5	event	\N	Watson explains that he is looking for lodgings	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_72", "sentence_73"], "communicatesContent": "Looking for lodgings. Trying to solve the problem as to whether it is possible to get comfortable rooms at a reasonable price."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_6	event	\N	Stamford says another man used the same expression earlier that day	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_74"], "communicatesContent": "you are the second man to-day that has used that expression to me"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_7	event	\N	Watson asks who the first man was	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_75", "sentence_76"], "communicatesContent": "And who was the first?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_8	event	\N	Stamford describes the first man as a laboratory worker at the hospital who could not afford his rooms alone	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_77", "sentence_78"], "communicatesContent": "A fellow who is working at the chemical laboratory up at the hospital. He was bemoaning himself this morning because he could not get someone to go halves with him in some nice rooms which he had found, and which were too much for his purse."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_9	event	\N	Watson says he is willing to share the rooms and expense	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_79", "sentence_80", "sentence_81"], "communicatesContent": "if he really wants someone to share the rooms and the expense, I am the very man for him. I should prefer having a partner to being alone."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_10	event	\N	Stamford looks strangely at Watson over his wine-glass	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_82"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_11	event	\N	Stamford warns Watson that Sherlock Holmes may not suit him as a constant companion	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_83"], "communicatesContent": "You don't know Sherlock Holmes yet; perhaps you would not care for him as a constant companion."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_12	event	\N	Watson asks what is against Sherlock Holmes	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_84"], "communicatesContent": "Why, what is there against him?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_13	event	\N	Stamford describes Holmes as a little queer, enthusiastic in some branches of science, and a decent fellow	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_85", "sentence_86", "sentence_87"], "communicatesContent": "I didn't say there was anything against him. He is a little queer in his ideas—an enthusiast in some branches of science. As far as I know he is a decent fellow enough."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_14	event	\N	Watson asks whether Holmes is a medical student	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_88", "sentence_89"], "communicatesContent": "A medical student, I suppose?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_15	event	\N	Stamford says Holmes has not taken systematic medical classes and is a chemist with desultory eccentric studies	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_90", "sentence_91", "sentence_92"], "communicatesContent": "No—I have no idea what he intends to go in for. I believe he is well up in anatomy, and he is a first-class chemist; but, as far as I know, he has never taken out any systematic medical classes. His studies are very desultory and eccentric, but he has amassed a lot of out-of-the-way knowledge which would astonish his professors."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_16	event	\N	Watson asks whether Stamford ever asked Holmes what he was going in for	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_93", "sentence_94"], "communicatesContent": "Did you never ask him what he was going in for?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_17	event	\N	Stamford says Holmes is hard to draw out but can be communicative when the fancy seizes him	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_95"], "communicatesContent": "No; he is not a man that it is easy to draw out, though he can be communicative enough when the fancy seizes him."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_18	event	\N	Watson says he would like to meet Holmes and prefers a studious quiet lodger	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_96", "sentence_97", "sentence_98", "sentence_99", "sentence_100"], "communicatesContent": "I should like to meet him. If I am to lodge with anyone, I should prefer a man of studious and quiet habits. I am not strong enough yet to stand much noise or excitement. I had enough of both in Afghanistan to last me for the remainder of my natural existence. How could I meet this friend of yours?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_19	event	\N	Stamford says Holmes is sure to be at the laboratory and suggests driving round together after luncheon	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_101", "sentence_102", "sentence_103"], "communicatesContent": "He is sure to be at the laboratory. He either avoids the place for weeks, or else he works there from morning to night. If you like, we shall drive round together after luncheon."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_20	event	\N	Watson agrees to drive round together after luncheon	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_104"], "communicatesContent": "Certainly."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_21	event	\N	Stamford gives Watson more particulars about Holmes while they go to the hospital from Holborn	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_105", "sentence_106", "sentence_107", "sentence_108"], "communicatesContent": "You mustn't blame me if you don't get on with him. I know nothing more of him than I have learned from meeting him occasionally in the laboratory. You proposed this arrangement, so you must not hold me responsible."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_22	event	\N	Watson says it will be easy to part company if they do not get on	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_108"], "communicatesContent": "If we don't get on it will be easy to part company."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_6_23	event	\N	Watson suggests Stamford has reason for distancing himself from the matter	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_109", "sentence_110", "sentence_111"], "communicatesContent": "it seems to me, Stamford, that you have some reason for washing your hands of the matter. Is this fellow's temper so formidable, or what is it? Don't be mealy-mouthed about it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_1	event	\N	Watson and Stamford enter the hospital chemical laboratory	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_127", "sentence_128", "sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_131", "sentence_132"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_2	event	\N	Holmes finds a reagent that is precipitated by hæmoglobin	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_133", "sentence_134", "sentence_135", "sentence_136"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_3	event	\N	Stamford introduces Watson and Holmes	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_138"], "communicatesContent": "Dr. Watson, Mr. Sherlock Holmes"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_4	event	\N	Holmes greets Watson	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_139", "sentence_140"], "communicatesContent": "How are you?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_5	event	\N	Holmes remarks that Watson has been in Afghanistan	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_141"], "communicatesContent": "You have been in Afghanistan, I perceive."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_6	event	\N	Watson asks how Holmes knew about Afghanistan	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_142", "sentence_143"], "communicatesContent": "How on earth did you know that?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_7	event	\N	Holmes dismisses the question and turns to hæmoglobin	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_144", "sentence_145", "sentence_146"], "communicatesContent": "Never mind. The question now is about hæmoglobin. No doubt you see the significance of this discovery of mine?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_8	event	\N	Watson comments on the discovery	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_147"], "communicatesContent": "It is interesting, chemically, no doubt, but practically——"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_9	event	\N	Holmes explains the practical importance of the discovery	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_148", "sentence_149", "sentence_150"], "communicatesContent": "Why, man, it is the most practical medico-legal discovery for years. Don't you see that it gives us an infallible test for blood stains. Come over here now!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_10	event	\N	Holmes draws Watson over to the table	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_151"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_11	event	\N	Holmes takes fresh blood from his finger into a pipette	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_152"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_7_12	event	\N	Holmes mixes blood with water and adds reagents	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_153", "sentence_154", "sentence_155", "sentence_156", "sentence_157", "sentence_158"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_1	event	\N	Holmes exclaims over the blood test and praises its value	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_159", "sentence_160", "sentence_161", "sentence_162", "sentence_163", "sentence_164", "sentence_165", "sentence_166", "sentence_167", "sentence_168", "sentence_169", "sentence_170"], "communicatesContent": "Ha! ha! What do you think of that? Beautiful! beautiful! The old Guiacum test was very clumsy and uncertain. So is the microscopic examination for blood corpuscles. The latter is valueless if the stains are a few hours old. Now, this appears to act as well whether the blood is old or new. Had this test been invented, there are hundreds of men now walking the earth who would long ago have paid the penalty of their crimes."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_2	event	\N	Holmes states that criminal cases hinge on identifying stains	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_171", "sentence_172", "sentence_173", "sentence_174", "sentence_175", "sentence_176", "sentence_177", "sentence_178", "sentence_179"], "communicatesContent": "Indeed! Criminal cases are continually hinging upon that one point. A man is suspected of a crime months perhaps after it has been committed. His linen or clothes are examined, and brownish stains discovered upon them. Are they blood stains, or mud stains, or rust stains, or fruit stains, or what are they? That is a question which has puzzled many an expert, and why? Because there was no reliable test. Now we have the Sherlock Holmes' test, and there will no longer be any difficulty."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes remarks on past cases that the test would have resolved	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_180", "sentence_181", "sentence_182", "sentence_183", "sentence_184", "sentence_185"], "communicatesContent": "You are to be congratulated. There was the case of Von Bischoff at Frankfort last year. He would certainly have been hung had this test been in existence. Then there was Mason of Bradford, and the notorious Muller, and Lefevre of Montpellier, and Samson of New Orleans. I could name a score of cases in which it would have been decisive."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_4	event	\N	Stamford jokes that Holmes is a walking calendar of crime	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_186", "sentence_187", "sentence_188"], "communicatesContent": "You seem to be a walking calendar of crime. You might start a paper on those lines. Call it the 'Police News of the Past.'"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_5	event	\N	Holmes explains that he uses plaster and works with poisons	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_189", "sentence_190", "sentence_191"], "communicatesContent": "Very interesting reading it might be made, too. I have to be careful, for I dabble with poisons a good deal."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_6	event	\N	Stamford brings Watson and Holmes together about sharing rooms	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_192", "sentence_193", "sentence_194"], "communicatesContent": "We came here on business. My friend here wants to take diggings, and as you were complaining that you could get no one to go halves with you, I thought that I had better bring you together."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_5	event	\N	Watson and Holmes unpack and lay out their property	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_243"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_7	event	\N	Holmes proposes a Baker Street suite and asks about tobacco smoke	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_195", "sentence_196"], "communicatesContent": "I have my eye on a suite in Baker Street, which would suit us down to the ground. You don't mind the smell of strong tobacco, I hope?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_8	event	\N	Watson answers Holmes about smoking	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_197", "sentence_198"], "communicatesContent": "I always smoke 'ship's' myself."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_9	event	\N	Holmes describes chemicals, experiments, moods, and requested confessions	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_199", "sentence_200", "sentence_201", "sentence_202", "sentence_203", "sentence_204", "sentence_205", "sentence_206", "sentence_207"], "communicatesContent": "That's good enough. I generally have chemicals about, and occasionally do experiments. Would that annoy you? By no means. Let me see—what are my other shortcomings. I get in the dumps at times, and don't open my mouth for days on end. You must not think I am sulky when I do that. Just let me alone, and I'll soon be right. What have you to confess now? It's just as well for two fellows to know the worst of one another before they begin to live together."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_8_10	event	\N	Watson laughs and states his own habits and vices	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_208", "sentence_209", "sentence_210"], "communicatesContent": "I keep a bull pup, and I object to rows because my nerves are shaken, and I get up at all sorts of ungodly hours, and I am extremely lazy. I have another set of vices when I'm well, but those are the principal ones at present."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_1	event	\N	Holmes asks whether violin-playing counts as rows	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_211", "sentence_212"], "communicatesContent": "Do you include violin-playing in your category of rows?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_2	event	\N	Watson answers that it depends on the player	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_213"], "communicatesContent": "It depends on the player."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_3	event	\N	Holmes says a well-played violin is pleasing and a badly played one is not	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_214"], "communicatesContent": "A well-played violin is a treat for the gods—a badly-played one——"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_4	event	\N	The man responds with a merry laugh	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_215"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, that's all right."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_5	event	\N	Holmes says the matter is settled if the rooms are agreeable	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_216"], "communicatesContent": "I think we may consider the thing as settled—that is, if the rooms are agreeable to you."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_6	event	\N	Watson asks when they shall see the rooms	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_217"], "communicatesContent": "When shall we see them?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_7	event	\N	Holmes arranges a noon meeting for the next day to settle everything	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_218"], "communicatesContent": "Call for me here at noon to-morrow, and we'll go together and settle everything."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_8	event	\N	Watson agrees to meet at noon exactly and shakes Holmes's hand	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_219"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_9	event	\N	Watson and Stamford leave Holmes working among his chemicals and walk toward the hotel	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_220"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_10	event	\N	Watson asks Stamford how Holmes knew about Afghanistan	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_221"], "communicatesContent": "How the deuce did he know that I had come from Afghanistan?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_11	event	\N	Stamford smiles enigmatically	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_222"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_12	event	\N	Stamford says that knowledge is Holmes's little peculiarity	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_223"], "communicatesContent": "That's just his little peculiarity."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_13	event	\N	Stamford says many people have wanted to know how Holmes finds things out	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_224"], "communicatesContent": "A good many people have wanted to know how he finds things out."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_14	event	\N	Watson exclaims that the matter is a mystery and expresses interest	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_225", "sentence_226", "sentence_227", "sentence_228", "sentence_229", "sentence_230"], "communicatesContent": "Oh! a mystery is it? This is very piquant. I am much obliged to you for bringing us together. 'The proper study of mankind is man,' you know."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_15	event	\N	Stamford tells Watson to study Holmes and says good-bye	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "stamford", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_231", "sentence_232", "sentence_233", "sentence_234"], "communicatesContent": "You must study him, then. You'll find him a knotty problem, though. I'll wager he learns more about you than you about him. Good-bye."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_9_16	event	\N	Watson replies good-bye and walks on to his hotel interested in Holmes	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_235"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_1	event	\N	Watson and Holmes inspect the rooms at 221B Baker Street	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_238", "sentence_239", "sentence_240"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_2	event	\N	Watson and Holmes conclude the bargain and enter into possession of the rooms	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_241"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_3	event	\N	Watson moves his things from the hotel to 221B Baker Street	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_242"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_4	event	\N	Holmes follows with several boxes and portmanteaus	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_242"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_6	event	\N	Watson and Holmes settle down and accommodate themselves to their new surroundings	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_244"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_904	lexical	\N	\N	903	{"text": "“On the contrary,” he answered, “it clears every instant.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_905	lexical	\N	\N	904	{"text": "I only require a few missing links to have an entirely connected case.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_7	event	\N	Watson observes Holmes's habits and movements	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_245", "sentence_246", "sentence_247", "sentence_248", "sentence_249", "sentence_250", "sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253", "sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256", "sentence_257", "sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260", "sentence_261", "sentence_262", "sentence_263", "sentence_264", "sentence_265", "sentence_266", "sentence_267"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_10_8	event	\N	Holmes works at the chemical laboratory, in the dissecting-rooms, and on long walks	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_248"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_11_1	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes says he will do his best to forget the Copernican Theory	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_273", "sentence_274", "sentence_275"], "communicatesContent": "Now that I do know it I shall do my best to forget it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_11_2	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes explains the brain as a little empty attic	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_276", "sentence_277", "sentence_278", "sentence_279", "sentence_280", "sentence_281", "sentence_282"], "communicatesContent": "I consider that a man's brain originally is like a little empty attic, and you have to stock it with such furniture as you choose. A fool takes in all the lumber of every sort that he comes across, so that the knowledge which might be useful to him gets crowded out, or at best is jumbled up with a lot of other things so that he has a difficulty in laying his hands upon it. Now the skilful workman is very careful indeed as to what he takes into his brain-attic. He will have nothing but the tools which may help him in doing his work, but of these he has a large assortment, and all in the most perfect order. It is a mistake to think that that little room has elastic walls and can distend to any extent. Depend upon it there comes a time when for every addition of knowledge you forget something that you knew before. It is of the highest importance, therefore, not to have useless facts elbowing out the useful ones."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_11_3	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes dismisses the importance of the Solar System to his work	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_283", "sentence_284", "sentence_285", "sentence_286", "sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": "What the deuce is it to me? you say that we go round the sun. If we went round the moon it would not make a pennyworth of difference to me or to my work."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_11_4	event	\N	John Watson writes down Holmes's points and then throws the list into the fire	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_292", "sentence_293", "sentence_294", "sentence_295", "sentence_296", "sentence_297", "sentence_298", "sentence_299", "sentence_300", "sentence_301", "sentence_302", "sentence_303", "sentence_304", "sentence_305", "sentence_306", "sentence_307", "sentence_308", "sentence_309", "sentence_310", "sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_313", "sentence_314", "sentence_315", "sentence_316", "sentence_317", "sentence_318", "sentence_319", "sentence_320", "sentence_321", "sentence_322", "sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325", "sentence_326", "sentence_327"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_12_1	event	\N	Watson notes Holmes's violin playing powers	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_329", "sentence_330", "sentence_331", "sentence_332", "sentence_333", "sentence_334", "sentence_335", "sentence_336", "sentence_337"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_12_2	event	\N	Watson and Holmes have no callers during the first week or so	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_338"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_12_3	event	\N	Holmes receives a series of visitors and acquaintances	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_339", "sentence_340", "sentence_341", "sentence_342", "sentence_343"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_12_4	event	\N	Holmes asks to use the sitting-room and explains that the visitors are his clients	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_344", "sentence_345", "sentence_346"], "communicatesContent": "I have to use this room as a place of business, and these people are my clients."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_12_5	event	\N	Watson reads an article titled The Book of Life in a magazine	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_349", "sentence_350", "sentence_351", "sentence_352", "sentence_353", "sentence_354", "sentence_355", "sentence_356", "sentence_357", "sentence_358", "sentence_359", "sentence_360"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_1	event	\N	The writer argues that one fact can reveal a larger system	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_361", "sentence_362"], "communicatesContent": "From a drop of water, a logician could infer the possibility of an Atlantic or a Niagara without having seen or heard of one or the other. So all life is a great chain, the nature of which is known whenever we are shown a single link of it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_2	event	\N	The writer describes deduction and analysis as a difficult art requiring long study	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_363", "sentence_364", "sentence_365", "sentence_366", "sentence_367", "sentence_368"], "communicatesContent": "The Science of Deduction and Analysis can only be acquired by long and patient study. The enquirer should begin with elementary problems, learn at a glance to distinguish a man's history and profession, and use physical signs such as nails, sleeves, boots, knees, callosities, expression, and cuffs to reveal a man's calling."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_3	event	\N	Watson condemns the article	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_369", "sentence_370"], "communicatesContent": "What ineffable twaddle! I never read such rubbish in my life."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_4	event	\N	Watson asks what the article is	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_371", "sentence_372", "sentence_373"], "communicatesContent": "Why, this article,"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_15_2	event	\N	The commissionaire carries a large blue envelope.	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_456"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_15_3	event	\N	The commissionaire runs across the roadway after seeing the number on the door.	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_461"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_906	lexical	\N	\N	905	{"text": "We had almost forgotten our companion’s presence since we entered the chamber.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_5	event	\N	Holmes says Watson has read the article because it is marked	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_374", "sentence_375", "sentence_376", "sentence_377", "sentence_378", "sentence_379", "sentence_380"], "communicatesContent": "I see that you have read it since you have marked it. I don't deny that it is smartly written. It irritates me though. It is evidently the theory of some arm-chair lounger who evolves all these neat little paradoxes in the seclusion of his own study. It is not practical. I should like to see him clapped down in a third class carriage on the Underground, and asked to give the trades of all his fellow-travellers. I would lay a thousand to one against him."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_6	event	\N	Holmes reveals that he wrote the article	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_381", "sentence_382"], "communicatesContent": "You would lose your money. As for the article, I wrote it myself."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_7	event	\N	Holmes explains that he has a turn for observation and deduction	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_383", "sentence_384", "sentence_385", "sentence_386", "sentence_387"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, I have a turn both for observation and for deduction. The theories which I have expressed there are really extremely practical, so practical that I depend upon them for my bread and cheese."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_8	event	\N	Holmes says he has a trade and identifies it as consulting detective work	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_388", "sentence_389", "sentence_390"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I have a trade of my own. I'm a consulting detective, if you can understand what that is."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_9	event	\N	Holmes describes how other detectives bring him difficult cases	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_391", "sentence_392", "sentence_393", "sentence_394"], "communicatesContent": "Here in London we have lots of Government detectives and lots of private ones. When these fellows are at fault they come to me, and I manage to put them on the right scent. They lay all the evidence before me, and I am generally able, by the help of my knowledge of the history of crime, to set them straight. There is a strong family resemblance about misdeeds, and if you have all the details of a thousand at your finger ends, it is odd if you can't unravel the thousand and first."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_10	event	\N	Holmes mentions Lestrade and the forgery case that brought him there	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_395", "sentence_396"], "communicatesContent": "Lestrade is a well-known detective. He got himself into a fog recently over a forgery case, and that was what brought him here."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_13_11	event	\N	Holmes explains that people from agencies come to consult him and pay him	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_397", "sentence_398", "sentence_399", "sentence_400"], "communicatesContent": "They are mostly sent on by private inquiry agencies. They are all people who are in trouble about something, and want a little enlightening. I listen to their story, they listen to my comments, and then I pocket my fee."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_14_1	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes explains how he inferred a client's origin from observation and deduction	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_402", "sentence_403", "sentence_404", "sentence_405", "sentence_406", "sentence_407", "sentence_408", "sentence_409", "sentence_410", "sentence_411", "sentence_412", "sentence_413", "sentence_414", "sentence_415", "sentence_416", "sentence_417", "sentence_418", "sentence_419", "sentence_420", "sentence_421", "sentence_422", "sentence_423"], "communicatesContent": "Quite so. I have a kind of intuition that way. Now and again a case turns up which is a little more complex. Then I have to bustle about and see things with my own eyes. You see I have a lot of special knowledge which I apply to the problem, and which facilitates matters wonderfully. Those rules of deduction laid down in that article which aroused your scorn, are invaluable to me in practical work. Observation with me is second nature. You appeared to be surprised when I told you, on our first meeting, that you had come from Afghanistan. Nothing of the sort. I knew you came from Afghanistan. From long habit the train of thoughts ran so swiftly through my mind, that I arrived at the conclusion without being conscious of intermediate steps. There were such steps, however. The train of reasoning ran, 'Here is a gentleman of a medical type, but with the air of a military man. Clearly an army doctor, then. He has just come from the tropics, for his face is dark, and that is not the natural tint of his skin, for his wrists are fair. He has undergone hardship and sickness, as his haggard face says clearly. His left arm has been injured. He holds it in a stiff and unnatural manner. Where in the tropics could an English army doctor have seen much hardship and got his arm wounded?' The whole train of thought did not occupy a second. I then remarked that you came from Afghanistan, and you were astonished."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_14_2	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes criticizes Dupin and Lecoq as detectives	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_428", "sentence_429", "sentence_430", "sentence_431", "sentence_432", "sentence_433", "sentence_434", "sentence_435", "sentence_436", "sentence_437", "sentence_438", "sentence_439", "sentence_440", "sentence_441", "sentence_442"], "communicatesContent": "No doubt you think that you are complimenting me in comparing me to Dupin. Now, in my opinion, Dupin was a very inferior fellow. That trick of his of breaking in on his friends' thoughts with an apropos remark after a quarter of an hour's silence is really very showy and superficial. He had some analytical genius, no doubt; but he was by no means such a phenomenon as Poe appeared to imagine. Lecoq was a miserable bungler; he had only one thing to recommend him, and that was his energy. That book made me positively ill. The question was how to identify an unknown prisoner. I could have done it in twenty-four hours. Lecoq took six months or so. It might be made a text-book for detectives to teach them what to avoid."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_14_3	event	\N	John Watson admires Holmes and feels indignant at his remarks	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_425", "sentence_426", "sentence_427", "sentence_443", "sentence_444", "sentence_445"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_14_4	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes complains about crime and his profession	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_446", "sentence_447", "sentence_448", "sentence_449", "sentence_450", "sentence_451"], "communicatesContent": "There are no crimes and no criminals in these days. What is the use of having brains in our profession. I know well that I have it in me to make my name famous. No man lives or has ever lived who has brought the same amount of study and of natural talent to the detection of crime which I have done. And what is the result? There is no crime to detect, or, at most, some bungling villainy with a motive so transparent that even a Scotland Yard official can see through it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_15_1	event	\N	A man walks slowly down the other side of the street looking at house numbers.	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_455"], "communicatesContent": null}
