a-study-in-scarlet	event_15_9	event	\N	The speaker asks the commissionaire about his previous rank and service.	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_469", "sentence_471"], "communicatesContent": "And you were?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_15_10	event	\N	The commissionaire states that he was a sergeant in the Royal Marine Light Infantry.	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "commissionaire", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_471", "sentence_473"], "communicatesContent": "A sergeant, sir, Royal Marine Light Infantry, sir."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_15_11	event	\N	The commissionaire salutes and leaves the room.	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_474"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_16_1	event	\N	Holmes finishes reading the note	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_480"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_16_2	event	\N	Holmes identifies the man in the street as a retired sergeant of Marines	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_481", "sentence_498"], "communicatesContent": "that he was a retired sergeant of Marines"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_16_3	event	\N	Holmes explains the deductions behind identifying the man as a sergeant of Marines	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_490", "sentence_498"], "communicatesContent": "It was easier to know it than to explain why I knew it. Even across the street I could see a great blue anchor tattooed on the back of the fellow's hand. That smacked of the sea. He had a military carriage, regulation side whiskers, self-importance, an air of command, and a steady respectable middle-aged appearance, which led me to believe that he had been a sergeant."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_16_4	event	\N	Holmes throws Watson the note	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_502", "sentence_504"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_16_5	event	\N	Watson reads the note aloud to Holmes	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_507", "sentence_521"], "communicatesContent": "My dear Mr. Sherlock Holmes,—There has been a bad business during the night at 3, Lauriston Gardens, off the Brixton Road. Our man on the beat saw a light there about two in the morning, and as the house was an empty one, suspected that something was amiss. He found the door open, and in the front room, which is bare of furniture, discovered the body of a gentleman, well dressed, and having cards in his pocket bearing the name of 'Enoch J. Drebber.' There had been no robbery, nor is there any evidence as to how the man met his death. There are marks of blood in the room, but there is no wound upon his person. We are at a loss as to how he came into the empty house; indeed, the whole affair is a puzzler. If you can come round to the house any time before twelve, you will find me there. I have left everything in statu quo until I hear from you. If you are unable to come I shall give you fuller details, and would esteem it a great kindness if you would favour me with your opinion. Yours faithfully, Tobias Gregson."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_16_6	event	\N	Holmes comments on Gregson and Lestrade as the pick of the Scotland Yarders	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_522", "sentence_526"], "communicatesContent": "Gregson is the smartest of the Scotland Yarders; he and Lestrade are the pick of a bad lot. They are both quick and energetic, but conventional—shockingly so. They have their knives into one another, too. They are as jealous as a pair of professional beauties. There will be some fun over this case if they are both put upon the scent."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_17_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson drive in a hansom toward Brixton Road	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_547"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_17_2	event	\N	Holmes orders the driver to stop and the pair alight	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_555", "sentence_556", "sentence_557", "sentence_558"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_17_3	event	\N	Holmes examines the ground and the front of Number 3, Lauriston Gardens	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_559", "sentence_560", "sentence_561", "sentence_562", "sentence_563", "sentence_564", "sentence_567", "sentence_568", "sentence_569", "sentence_570"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_1	event	\N	Gregson greets the visitors at the house door	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_572", "sentence_573"], "communicatesContent": "It is indeed kind of you to come, I have had everything left untouched."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_2	event	\N	Holmes points to the disturbed pathway	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_574", "sentence_575", "sentence_576"], "communicatesContent": "Except that! If a herd of buffaloes had passed along there could not be a greater mess. No doubt, however, you had drawn your own conclusions, Gregson, before you permitted this."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_3	event	\N	Gregson replies that he had much to do inside the house and relied on Lestrade	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_578", "sentence_579", "sentence_580"], "communicatesContent": "I have had so much to do inside the house. My colleague, Mr. Lestrade, is here. I had relied upon him to look after this."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_21	event	\N	Gregson points to the objects collected from the pockets.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_652"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_4	event	\N	Holmes comments on Gregson and Lestrade being on the ground	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_581", "sentence_582"], "communicatesContent": "With two such men as yourself and Lestrade upon the ground, there will not be much for a third party to find out."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_5	event	\N	Gregson states that they have done all they can and mentions Holmes's taste for such cases	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_583", "sentence_584"], "communicatesContent": "I think we have done all that can be done; it's a queer case though, and I knew your taste for such things."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_6	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Gregson and Lestrade came by cab and Gregson answers no	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_585", "sentence_586", "sentence_587", "sentence_588", "sentence_589"], "communicatesContent": "You did not come here in a cab? Nor Lestrade?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_7	event	\N	Holmes leads the way into the house and Gregson follows	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_590", "sentence_591"], "communicatesContent": "Then let us go and look at the room."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_18_8	event	\N	Holmes and the narrator enter the dining-room and see the dead man	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_596", "sentence_603", "sentence_604", "sentence_605", "sentence_606", "sentence_607", "sentence_608", "sentence_609", "sentence_610"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_1	event	\N	Lestrade stands by the doorway and greets Watson and Holmes.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_611"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_2	event	\N	Lestrade remarks that the case will make a stir.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_612"], "communicatesContent": "This case will make a stir, sir."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_3	event	\N	Lestrade remarks that the case beats anything he has seen.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_613"], "communicatesContent": "It beats anything I have seen, and I am no chicken."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_4	event	\N	Gregson asks whether there is a clue.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_614", "sentence_615"], "communicatesContent": "There is no clue?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_5	event	\N	Lestrade answers that there is no clue.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_616"], "communicatesContent": "None at all."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_6	event	\N	Holmes approaches the body, kneels down, and examines it.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_617"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_7	event	\N	Holmes asks whether there is no wound.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_618", "sentence_619"], "communicatesContent": "You are sure that there is no wound?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_8	event	\N	Both detectives answer that there is no wound.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_620", "sentence_621"], "communicatesContent": "Positive!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_9	event	\N	Holmes states that the blood belongs to a second individual.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_622", "sentence_623", "sentence_624"], "communicatesContent": "Then, of course, this blood belongs to a second individual—presumably the murderer, if murder has been committed."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_10	event	\N	Holmes asks Gregson whether he remembers the case of Van Jansen.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_623", "sentence_624", "sentence_625"], "communicatesContent": "Do you remember the case, Gregson?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_11	event	\N	Holmes tells Gregson to read the case up.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_626", "sentence_627", "sentence_628"], "communicatesContent": "Read it up—you really should. There is nothing new under the sun. It has all been done before."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_12	event	\N	Holmes examines the body minutely.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_629", "sentence_630", "sentence_631"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_13	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the body has been moved.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_632", "sentence_633", "sentence_634"], "communicatesContent": "He has not been moved at all?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_14	event	\N	Holmes says the body can be taken to the mortuary.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_635", "sentence_636"], "communicatesContent": "You can take him to the mortuary now. There is nothing more to be learned."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_15	event	\N	Gregson has a stretcher and four men ready.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_637"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_16	event	\N	The men enter and lift the stranger out of the room.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_638"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_17	event	\N	A ring falls to the floor as the body is raised.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_639"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_18	event	\N	Lestrade grabs the ring and identifies it as a woman's wedding ring.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_640", "sentence_641", "sentence_642", "sentence_643", "sentence_644", "sentence_645"], "communicatesContent": "There's been a woman here. It's a woman's wedding-ring."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_19	event	\N	Gregson says the ring complicates matters.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_646", "sentence_647"], "communicatesContent": "This complicates matters."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_20	event	\N	Holmes remarks that staring at the ring will not help and asks what was found in the pockets.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_648", "sentence_649", "sentence_650", "sentence_651"], "communicatesContent": "You're sure it doesn't simplify them? There's nothing to be learned by staring at it. What did you find in his pockets?"}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "The Statement of the Case Chapter III.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_22	event	\N	Gregson lists the objects found in the dead man's pockets.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_653", "sentence_654", "sentence_655", "sentence_656", "sentence_657", "sentence_658", "sentence_659", "sentence_660", "sentence_661", "sentence_662", "sentence_663", "sentence_664", "sentence_665", "sentence_666", "sentence_667"], "communicatesContent": "A gold watch, No. 97163, by Barraud, of London. Gold Albert chain, very heavy and solid. Gold ring, with masonic device. Gold pin—bull-dog's head, with rubies as eyes. Russian leather card-case, with cards of Enoch J. Drebber of Cleveland, corresponding with the E. J. D. upon the linen. No purse, but loose money to the extent of seven pounds thirteen. Pocket edition of Boccaccio's Decameron, with name of Joseph Stangerson upon the fly-leaf. Two letters—one addressed to E. J. Drebber and one to Joseph Stangerson."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_23	event	\N	Holmes asks the address of the letters.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_668", "sentence_669"], "communicatesContent": "At what address?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_24	event	\N	Gregson says the letters were to be left at the American Exchange and were from the Guion Steamship Company.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_669", "sentence_670", "sentence_671"], "communicatesContent": "American Exchange, Strand—to be left till called for. They are both from the Guion Steamship Company, and refer to the sailing of their boats from Liverpool. It is clear that this unfortunate man was about to return to New York."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_25	event	\N	Holmes asks whether inquiries have been made about Stangerson.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_672", "sentence_673"], "communicatesContent": "Have you made any inquiries as to this man, Stangerson?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_26	event	\N	Gregson says he has sent advertisements to newspapers and a man to the American Exchange.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_674"], "communicatesContent": "I have had advertisements sent to all the newspapers, and one of my men has gone to the American Exchange, but he has not returned yet."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_27	event	\N	Holmes asks whether a telegram has been sent to Cleveland.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_675", "sentence_676"], "communicatesContent": "Have you sent to Cleveland?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_28	event	\N	Gregson says they telegraphed to Cleveland that morning.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_676"], "communicatesContent": "We telegraphed this morning."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_29	event	\N	Holmes asks how the inquiries were worded.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_677", "sentence_678"], "communicatesContent": "How did you word your inquiries?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_19_30	event	\N	Gregson explains the wording of the inquiries.	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_678"], "communicatesContent": "We simply detailed the circumstances, and said that we should be glad of any information which could help us."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_1	event	\N	Lestrade reappears in the hall from the front room rubbing his hands self-satisfiedly	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_685", "sentence_686", "sentence_687", "sentence_688"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_2	event	\N	Lestrade announces that he has made a discovery of highest importance after examining the walls	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_686", "sentence_687"], "communicatesContent": "I have just made a discovery of the highest importance, and one which would have been overlooked had I not made a careful examination of the walls."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_3	event	\N	Lestrade shows the wall inscription to the others	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_688", "sentence_689", "sentence_690", "sentence_691", "sentence_692"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_4	event	\N	Lestrade explains that the word was written in blood and was overlooked in the darkest corner	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_699", "sentence_700", "sentence_701", "sentence_702", "sentence_703", "sentence_704", "sentence_705", "sentence_706"], "communicatesContent": "This was overlooked because it was in the darkest corner of the room, and no one thought of looking there. The murderer has written it with his or her own blood. See this smear where it has trickled down the wall! That disposes of the idea of suicide anyhow. Why was that corner chosen to write it on? I will tell you. See that candle on the mantelpiece. It was lit at the time, and if it was lit this corner would be the brightest instead of the darkest portion of the wall."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_5	event	\N	Gregson responds to Lestrade's explanation	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_707", "sentence_708"], "communicatesContent": "And what does it mean now that you have found it?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_6	event	\N	Lestrade says the writer was going to write the female name Rachel and that a woman named Rachel has something to do with the case	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_709", "sentence_710", "sentence_711", "sentence_712", "sentence_713"], "communicatesContent": "Mean? Why, it means that the writer was going to put the female name Rachel, but was disturbed before he or she had time to finish. You mark my words, when this case comes to be cleared up you will find that a woman named Rachel has something to do with it. It's all very well for you to laugh, Mr. Sherlock Holmes. You may be very smart and clever, but the old hound is the best, when all is said and done."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_7	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes apologizes and says he will examine the room	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_714", "sentence_715", "sentence_716", "sentence_717", "sentence_718"], "communicatesContent": "I really beg your pardon! You certainly have the credit of being the first of us to find this out, and, as you say, it bears every mark of having been written by the other participant in last night's mystery. I have not had time to examine this room yet, but with your permission I shall do so now."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_20_8	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes examines the room with a tape measure and magnifying glass	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_718", "sentence_719", "sentence_720", "sentence_721", "sentence_722", "sentence_723", "sentence_724", "sentence_725"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "In Quest of a Solution Chapter IV.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_1	event	\N	Holmes remarks that genius is an infinite capacity for taking pains and applies it to detective work	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_726", "sentence_727"], "communicatesContent": "They say that genius is an infinite capacity for taking pains. It's a very bad definition, but it does apply to detective work."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_2	event	\N	Gregson and Lestrade watch Holmes's manoeuvres with curiosity and contempt	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_728"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_3	event	\N	Gregson and Lestrade ask Holmes what he thinks of it	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_730", "sentence_731"], "communicatesContent": "What do you think of it, sir?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_4	event	\N	Holmes declines to interfere and says he may later help with the investigation	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_732", "sentence_733", "sentence_734", "sentence_735"], "communicatesContent": "It would be robbing you of the credit of the case if I was to presume to help you. You are doing so well now that it would be a pity for anyone to interfere. If you will let me know how your investigations go, I shall be happy to give you any help I can."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_5	event	\N	Holmes asks to speak to the constable who found the body and requests his name and address	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_735", "sentence_736", "sentence_737"], "communicatesContent": "In the meantime I should like to speak to the constable who found the body. Can you give me his name and address?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_6	event	\N	Lestrade identifies John Rance and gives his address	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_738", "sentence_739", "sentence_740", "sentence_741"], "communicatesContent": "John Rance. He is off duty now. You will find him at 46, Audley Court, Kennington Park Gate."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_7	event	\N	Holmes notes John Rance's address and decides to go look him up with Watson	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_742", "sentence_743"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_8	event	\N	Holmes states that murder has been done and describes the murderer	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_744", "sentence_745", "sentence_746", "sentence_747", "sentence_748", "sentence_749"], "communicatesContent": "There has been murder done, and the murderer was a man. He was more than six feet high, was in the prime of life, had small feet for his height, wore coarse, square-toed boots and smoked a Trichinopoly cigar. He came here with his victim in a four-wheeled cab, which was drawn by a horse with three old shoes and one new one on his off fore leg. In all probability the murderer had a florid face, and the finger-nails of his right hand were remarkably long. These are only a few indications, but they may assist you."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_9	event	\N	Lestrade and Gregson react with an incredulous smile	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_750"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_10	event	\N	Lestrade asks how the man was murdered	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_751", "sentence_752"], "communicatesContent": "If this man was murdered, how was it done?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_21_11	event	\N	Holmes answers that the murder was by poison and leaves	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_753", "sentence_754", "sentence_755"], "communicatesContent": "Poison. 'Rache,' is the German for 'revenge'; so don't lose your time looking for Miss Rachel."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_1	event	\N	Holmes leaves No. 3, Lauriston Gardens and goes to the telegraph office	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_758", "sentence_759", "sentence_760"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_2	event	\N	Holmes dispatches a long telegram	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_760"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_3	event	\N	Holmes hails a cab and orders the driver to take them to the address given by Lestrade	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_761"], "communicatesContent": "take us to the address given us by Lestrade"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_4	event	\N	Holmes explains his deductions about the cab, the two visitors, and the night arrival	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_762", "sentence_766", "sentence_767", "sentence_768", "sentence_769"], "communicatesContent": "There is nothing like first hand evidence; as a matter of fact, my mind is entirely made up upon the case, but still we may as well learn all that is to be learned. The cab had made two ruts close to the curb, and because there had been no rain for a week until last night, the wheels must have been there during the night. The cab must have brought those two individuals to the house."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_5	event	\N	Watson questions Holmes about the deductions	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_763", "sentence_764", "sentence_770", "sentence_778", "sentence_786", "sentence_794"], "communicatesContent": "You amaze me, Holmes. Surely you are not as sure as you pretend to be of all those particulars which you gave. But how about the other man's height? And his age? The finger nails and the Trichinopoly? And the florid face?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_6	event	\N	Holmes answers that there is no room for a mistake	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_765"], "communicatesContent": "There's no room for a mistake."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_7	event	\N	Holmes explains how he inferred the other man's height	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_766", "sentence_771", "sentence_772", "sentence_773", "sentence_774", "sentence_775", "sentence_776", "sentence_777"], "communicatesContent": "The height of a man can be told from the length of his stride. I had this fellow's stride both on the clay outside and on the dust within. A man writes on a wall about the level of his own eyes, and the writing was just over six feet from the ground."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_12	event	\N	Holmes asks what the man looked like	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_895", "sentence_896"], "communicatesContent": "His face—his dress—didn't you notice them?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_1	event	\N	The man carries the child while the pair tramps onward	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1662"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_8	event	\N	Holmes explains how he inferred the other man's age	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_778", "sentence_780", "sentence_781", "sentence_782", "sentence_783", "sentence_784"], "communicatesContent": "If a man can stride four and a-half feet without the smallest effort, he can't be quite in the sere and yellow. That was the breadth of a puddle on the garden walk which he had evidently walked across. Patent-leather boots had gone round, and Square-toes had hopped over. I am simply applying to ordinary life a few of those precepts of observation and deduction which I advocated in that article."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_9	event	\N	Watson suggests the finger nails and the Trichinopoly	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_786"], "communicatesContent": "The finger nails and the Trichinopoly."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_10	event	\N	Holmes explains the blood writing, trimmed nail, and cigar ash	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_787", "sentence_788", "sentence_789", "sentence_790", "sentence_791", "sentence_792", "sentence_793"], "communicatesContent": "The writing on the wall was done with a man's forefinger dipped in blood. The plaster was slightly scratched, which would not have been the case if the man's nail had been trimmed. I gathered up some scattered ash from the floor. It was dark in colour and flakey—such an ash as is only made by a Trichinopoly. I have made a special study of cigar ashes and can distinguish the ash of any known brand."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_11	event	\N	Watson asks about the florid face	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_794", "sentence_795"], "communicatesContent": "And the florid face?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_22_12	event	\N	Holmes says the florid-face deduction was a daring shot and cannot be explained yet	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_796", "sentence_797"], "communicatesContent": "That was a more daring shot, though I have no doubt that I was right. You must not ask me that at the present state of the affair."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_23_1	event	\N	The speaker summarizes the difficulties of the case and describes the German word RACHE as a deliberate ruse	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_799", "sentence_800", "sentence_801", "sentence_802", "sentence_803", "sentence_804", "sentence_805", "sentence_806", "sentence_807", "sentence_809", "sentence_810", "sentence_811", "sentence_812", "sentence_813", "sentence_814", "sentence_815"], "communicatesContent": "There is much that is still obscure, though I have quite made up my mind on the main facts. As to poor Lestrade's discovery it was simply a blind intended to put the police upon a wrong track, by suggesting Socialism and secret societies. It was not done by a German. The A, if you noticed, was printed somewhat after the German fashion. Now, a real German invariably prints in the Latin character, so that we may safely say that this was not written by one, but by a clumsy imitator who overdid his part. It was simply a ruse to divert inquiry into a wrong channel."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_23_2	event	\N	Watson praises Holmes's deduction	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_818"], "communicatesContent": "I shall never do that; you have brought detection as near an exact science as it ever will be brought in this world."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_23_3	event	\N	Holmes reacts with pleasure to Watson's praise	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_819", "sentence_820"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_23_4	event	\N	Holmes explains what he has inferred from the cab and the men's movements	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_821", "sentence_822", "sentence_823", "sentence_824", "sentence_825", "sentence_826", "sentence_827", "sentence_828", "sentence_829", "sentence_830"], "communicatesContent": "Patent-leathers and Square-toes came in the same cab, and they walked down the pathway together as friendly as possible—arm-in-arm, in all probability. When they got inside they walked up and down the room—or rather, Patent-leathers stood still while Square-toes walked up and down. I could read all that in the dust; and I could read that as he walked he grew more and more excited. That is shown by the increased length of his strides. He was talking all the while, and working himself up, no doubt, into a fury. Then the tragedy occurred. I've told you all I know myself now, for the rest is mere surmise and conjecture. We have a good working basis, however, on which to start. We must hurry up, for I want to go to Halle's concert to hear Norman Neruda this afternoon."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_23_5	event	\N	The cab travels through the streets and stops at Audley Court	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_831", "sentence_832", "sentence_833", "sentence_834"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_23_6	event	\N	Holmes and Watson arrive at Audley Court	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_835", "sentence_836", "sentence_837", "sentence_838"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_1	event	\N	Rance reports the night's events at the office	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_840"], "communicatesContent": "I made my report at the office."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_2	event	\N	Holmes handles a half-sovereign while asking to hear the account	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_841", "sentence_842", "sentence_843", "sentence_844"], "communicatesContent": "We thought that we should like to hear it all from your own lips."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_3	event	\N	Rance agrees to tell the account	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_843", "sentence_845", "sentence_846"], "communicatesContent": "I shall be most happy to tell you anything I can."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_13	event	\N	Rance says he noticed the man's appearance and had to prop him up with Murcher	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_897", "sentence_898", "sentence_899"], "communicatesContent": "I should think I did notice them, seeing that I had to prop him up—me and Murcher between us. He was a long chap, with a red face, the lower part muffled round——"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_14	event	\N	Holmes stops Rance from continuing	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_899"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_15	event	\N	Holmes asks what became of the man	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_900"], "communicatesContent": "What became of him?"}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "The Story of the Bald-Headed Man Chapter V.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_4	event	\N	Rance describes his beat and the night's events	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_847", "sentence_848", "sentence_849", "sentence_850", "sentence_851", "sentence_852", "sentence_853", "sentence_854", "sentence_855", "sentence_856", "sentence_861", "sentence_862", "sentence_863", "sentence_865", "sentence_866", "sentence_867", "sentence_868"], "communicatesContent": "My time is from ten at night to six in the morning. At eleven there was a fight at the 'White Hart'; but bar that all was quiet enough on the beat. At one o'clock it began to rain, and I met Harry Murcher—him who has the Holland Grove beat—and we stood together at the corner of Henrietta Street a-talkin'. Presently—maybe about two or a little after—I thought I would take a look round and see that all was right down the Brixton Road. It was precious dirty and lonely. Not a soul did I meet all the way down, though a cab or two went past me. I was a strollin' down, thinkin' between ourselves how uncommon handy a four of gin hot would be, when suddenly the glint of a light caught my eye in the window of that same house. Now, I knew that them two houses in Lauriston Gardens was empty on account of him that owns them who won't have the drains seen to, though the very last tenant what lived in one of them died o' typhoid fever. I was knocked all in a heap therefore at seeing a light in the window, and I suspected as something was wrong. When I got to the door——"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_5	event	\N	Holmes states that Rance stopped and walked back to the garden gate	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_857", "sentence_858"], "communicatesContent": "You stopped, and then walked back to the garden gate. What did you do that for?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_6	event	\N	Rance shows amazement and answers Holmes	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_859", "sentence_860"], "communicatesContent": "Why, that's true, sir; though how you come to know it, Heaven only knows."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_7	event	\N	Rance says he wanted someone with him at the door	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_861", "sentence_862", "sentence_863"], "communicatesContent": "When I got up to the door it was so still and so lonesome, that I thought I'd be none the worse for some one with me. I ain't afeared of anything on this side o' the grave; but I thought that maybe it was him that died o' the typhoid inspecting the drains what killed him. The thought gave me a kind o' turn, and I walked back to the gate to see if I could see Murcher's lantern, but there wasn't no sign of him nor of anyone else."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_8	event	\N	Holmes asks whether anyone was in the street	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_864"], "communicatesContent": "There was no one in the street?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_9	event	\N	Rance says the street was empty	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_865"], "communicatesContent": "Not a livin' soul, sir, nor as much as a dog."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_10	event	\N	Rance enters the house and sees a candle burning in the room	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_866", "sentence_867", "sentence_868"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_11	event	\N	Holmes states what Rance did inside the room	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_869", "sentence_870"], "communicatesContent": "You walked round the room several times, and you knelt down by the body, and then you walked through and tried the kitchen door, and then——"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_24_12	event	\N	Rance reacts with alarm and questions Holmes	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_871", "sentence_872", "sentence_873", "sentence_874"], "communicatesContent": "Where was you hid to see all that? It seems to me that you knows a deal more than you should."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_1	event	\N	Holmes throws his card across the table to the constable	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_875"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_2	event	\N	Holmes says he is one of the hounds and not the wolf	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_876", "sentence_877"], "communicatesContent": "Don't get arresting me for the murder. I am one of the hounds and not the wolf; Mr. Gregson or Mr. Lestrade will answer for that."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_3	event	\N	Holmes asks Rance what he did next	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_878", "sentence_879"], "communicatesContent": "Go on, though. What did you do next?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_4	event	\N	Rance resumes his seat	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_880"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_5	event	\N	Rance goes back to the gate and sounds his whistle	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_881"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_6	event	\N	Murcher and two more arrive at the spot	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_882"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_7	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the street was empty	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_883"], "communicatesContent": "Was the street empty then?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_8	event	\N	Rance replies that the street was empty as far as anyone useful goes	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_884"], "communicatesContent": "Well, it was, as far as anybody that could be of any good goes."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_9	event	\N	Holmes asks what sort of man he was	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_890", "sentence_891"], "communicatesContent": "What sort of a man was he?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_10	event	\N	Rance says the man was very drunk	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_887", "sentence_888", "sentence_889"], "communicatesContent": "I've seen many a drunk chap in my time, but never anyone so cryin' drunk as that cove. He was at the gate when I came out, a-leanin' up agin the railings, and a-singin' at the pitch o' his lungs about Columbine's New-fangled Banner, or some such stuff. He couldn't stand, far less help."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_11	event	\N	Rance becomes irritated at the digression	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_892"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "The Tragedy of Pondicherry Lodge Chapter VI.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_16	event	\N	Rance says they did not look after the man and that he probably went home	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_901", "sentence_902"], "communicatesContent": "We'd enough to do without lookin' after him. I'll wager he found his way home all right."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_17	event	\N	Holmes asks how the man was dressed	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_903"], "communicatesContent": "How was he dressed?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_18	event	\N	Rance answers that the man wore a brown overcoat	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_904"], "communicatesContent": "A brown overcoat."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_19	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the man had a whip in his hand	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_905"], "communicatesContent": "Had he a whip in his hand?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_20	event	\N	Rance says the man had no whip	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_906"], "communicatesContent": "A whip—no."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_21	event	\N	Holmes remarks that the man must have left the whip behind	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_907"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_22	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Rance saw or heard a cab after that	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_908"], "communicatesContent": "You didn't happen to see or hear a cab after that?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_23	event	\N	Rance says he saw or heard no cab	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_rance", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_909"], "communicatesContent": "No."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_24	event	\N	Holmes gives Rance a half-sovereign	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_910"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_25	event	\N	Holmes criticizes Rance and says he might have gained his sergeant's stripes	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_911", "sentence_912", "sentence_913", "sentence_914", "sentence_915", "sentence_916"], "communicatesContent": "I am afraid, Rance, that you will never rise in the force. That head of yours should be for use as well as ornament. You might have gained your sergeant's stripes last night. The man whom you held in your hands is the man who holds the clue of this mystery, and whom we are seeking. There is no use of arguing about it now; I tell you that it is so. Come along, Doctor."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_26	event	\N	Holmes and Watson leave for the cab together	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_917"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_27	event	\N	Holmes speaks bitterly about the blundering fool and the missed opportunity	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_918", "sentence_919"], "communicatesContent": "The blundering fool. Just to think of his having such an incomparable bit of good luck, and not taking advantage of it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_28	event	\N	Watson says he is still in the dark and questions the man's return to the house	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_920", "sentence_921", "sentence_922", "sentence_923"], "communicatesContent": "I am rather in the dark still. It is true that the description of this man tallies with your idea of the second party in this mystery. But why should he come back to the house after leaving it? That is not the way of criminals."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_25_29	event	\N	Holmes says the man came back for the ring and that he can bait his line with it	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_924", "sentence_925", "sentence_926", "sentence_927", "sentence_928", "sentence_929", "sentence_930", "sentence_931", "sentence_932", "sentence_933"], "communicatesContent": "The ring, man, the ring: that was what he came back for. If we have no other way of catching him, we can always bait our line with the ring. I shall have him, Doctor—I'll lay you two to one that I have him. I must thank you for it all. I might not have gone but for you, and so have missed the finest study I ever came across: a study in scarlet, eh? Why shouldn't we use a little art jargon. There's the scarlet thread of murder running through the colourless skein of life, and our duty is to unravel it, and isolate it, and expose every inch of it. And now for lunch, and then for Norman Neruda. Her attack and her bowing are splendid. What's that little thing of Chopin's she plays so magnificently: Tra-la-la-lira-lira-lay."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_26_1	event	\N	An amateur bloodhound leans back in a cab and carols away like a lark while the narrator meditates on the many-sidedness of the human mind	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_934"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_26_2	event	\N	The narrator meditates on the many-sidedness of the human mind	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_934"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_1	event	\N	Watson lies down to sleep and fails to sleep	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_937", "sentence_938", "sentence_939", "sentence_940", "sentence_941", "sentence_942", "sentence_943", "sentence_944", "sentence_945", "sentence_946", "sentence_947", "sentence_948", "sentence_949", "sentence_950", "sentence_951"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_2	event	\N	Holmes returns late from the concert and sits down to dinner	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_953", "sentence_954", "sentence_955"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_3	event	\N	Holmes speaks about music and Darwin	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_955", "sentence_956", "sentence_957", "sentence_958", "sentence_959"], "communicatesContent": "It was magnificent. Do you remember what Darwin says about music? He claims that the power of producing and appreciating it existed among the human race long before the power of speech was arrived at. Perhaps that is why we are so subtly influenced by it. There are vague memories in our souls of those misty centuries when the world was in its childhood."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_4	event	\N	Watson says the Brixton Road affair has upset him	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_960", "sentence_961", "sentence_962", "sentence_963", "sentence_964", "sentence_965", "sentence_966", "sentence_967"], "communicatesContent": "To tell the truth, it has. I ought to be more case-hardened after my Afghan experiences. I saw my own comrades hacked to pieces at Maiwand without losing my nerve."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_5	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Watson has seen the evening paper	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_968", "sentence_969", "sentence_970", "sentence_971"], "communicatesContent": "Have you seen the evening paper?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_6	event	\N	Holmes explains the newspaper account and points out the omitted wedding ring	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_972", "sentence_973", "sentence_974", "sentence_975", "sentence_976"], "communicatesContent": "It gives a fairly good account of the affair. It does not mention the fact that when the man was raised up, a woman's wedding ring fell upon the floor. It is just as well it does not. Look at this advertisement."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_7	event	\N	Holmes sends advertisements to every paper	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_977"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_27_8	event	\N	Holmes throws the paper across to Watson and Watson reads the advertisement	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_978", "sentence_979", "sentence_980", "sentence_981"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_1	event	\N	Holmes hands over a ring	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_986", "sentence_987", "sentence_988"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_2	event	\N	Holmes predicts the man in the brown coat will answer the advertisement	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_989", "sentence_990", "sentence_991", "sentence_992", "sentence_993", "sentence_994", "sentence_995", "sentence_996", "sentence_997", "sentence_998", "sentence_999", "sentence_1000", "sentence_1001", "sentence_1002", "sentence_1003", "sentence_1004", "sentence_1005", "sentence_1006", "sentence_1007", "sentence_1008"], "communicatesContent": "The man in the brown coat—our florid friend with the square toes—will come, or send an accomplice, because he would rather risk anything than lose the ring."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_3	event	\N	Watson says he has a revolver and cartridges	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1011", "sentence_1012", "sentence_1013"], "communicatesContent": "I have my old service revolver and a few cartridges."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_4	event	\N	Watson cleans and loads the revolver	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1014", "sentence_1015", "sentence_1016"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_5	event	\N	Watson returns with the pistol and Holmes is scraping his violin	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1017"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_6	event	\N	Holmes announces an answer to his American telegram	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1018", "sentence_1019", "sentence_1020", "sentence_1021"], "communicatesContent": "The plot thickens. I have just had an answer to my American telegram. My view of the case is the correct one."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_7	event	\N	Holmes gives Watson instructions for the encounter	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1022", "sentence_1023", "sentence_1024", "sentence_1025", "sentence_1026"], "communicatesContent": "Put your pistol in your pocket. When the fellow comes speak to him in an ordinary way. Leave the rest to me. Don't frighten him by looking at him too hard."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_8	event	\N	Watson says it is eight o'clock	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1027"], "communicatesContent": "It is eight o'clock now."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_9	event	\N	Holmes says the man will probably arrive soon and gives further instructions	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1028", "sentence_1029", "sentence_1030", "sentence_1031", "sentence_1032", "sentence_1033"], "communicatesContent": "He will probably be here in a few minutes. Open the door slightly. That will do. Now put the key on the inside. Thank you!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_10	event	\N	Holmes presents a Latin book and comments on its publication date	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1034", "sentence_1035"], "communicatesContent": "This is a queer old book I picked up at a stall yesterday—'De Jure inter Gentes'—published in Latin at Liege in the Lowlands, in 1642. Charles' head was still firm on his shoulders when this little brown-backed volume was struck off."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_28_11	event	\N	Holmes identifies the printer and speculates about William Whyte	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1036", "sentence_1037", "sentence_1038", "sentence_1039", "sentence_1040", "sentence_1041"], "communicatesContent": "Philippe de Croy, whoever he may have been. I wonder who William Whyte was. Some pragmatical seventeenth century lawyer, I suppose. His writing has a legal twist about it. Here comes our man, I think."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_1	event	\N	A bell rings at the door	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1043"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_2	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes rises and moves toward the door	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1044"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_3	event	\N	The servant opens the door after walking along the hall	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1045"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_4	event	\N	An unknown visitor asks whether Dr. Watson lives there	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "unknown_visitor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1046", "sentence_1047"], "communicatesContent": "Does Dr. Watson live here?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_5	event	\N	Someone ascends the stairs after the door closes	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1048", "sentence_1049"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_6	event	\N	The visitor taps at the door and is admitted into the apartment	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1051", "sentence_1052", "sentence_1053"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_7	event	\N	Mrs. Sawyer enters the apartment	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1053", "sentence_1054"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_8	event	\N	Mrs. Sawyer produces an evening paper and points to the advertisement	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1056"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	section_68	section	\N	Section 68	67	{"wordCount": 673}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_9	event	\N	Mrs. Sawyer explains that the ring belongs to Sally Dennis and gives the address and name	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sally_sawyer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1057", "sentence_1058", "sentence_1059", "sentence_1065", "sentence_1066", "sentence_1067", "sentence_1071", "sentence_1072", "sentence_1073", "sentence_1074"], "communicatesContent": "It's this as has brought me, good gentlemen; a gold wedding ring in the Brixton Road. It belongs to my girl Sally... 13, Duncan Street, Houndsditch. Sally lives in lodgings at 3, Mayfield Place, Peckham. My name is Sawyer—hers is Dennis, which Tom Dennis married her."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_10	event	\N	Watson asks whether the ring is hers	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1060", "sentence_1061"], "communicatesContent": "Is that her ring?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_11	event	\N	Mrs. Sawyer confirms that the ring is Sally's and rejoices	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sally_sawyer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1062", "sentence_1063", "sentence_1064"], "communicatesContent": "The Lord be thanked! Sally will be a glad woman this night. That's the ring."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_12	event	\N	Watson returns the wedding ring to Mrs. Sawyer	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1075", "sentence_1076"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_29_13	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes leaves to follow Mrs. Sawyer	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1077", "sentence_1078", "sentence_1079", "sentence_1080", "sentence_1081", "sentence_1082"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_30_1	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes leaves and later returns unsuccessful	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1085", "sentence_1089", "sentence_1090", "sentence_1091"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_30_2	event	\N	The maid goes to bed	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1087"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_30_3	event	\N	The landlady passes the speaker's door on the way to bed	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1088"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_30_4	event	\N	Holmes explains the cab chase and the disappearance	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1092", "sentence_1093", "sentence_1096", "sentence_1097", "sentence_1098", "sentence_1099", "sentence_1100", "sentence_1102", "sentence_1103", "sentence_1104", "sentence_1105", "sentence_1106", "sentence_1107", "sentence_1108", "sentence_1109", "sentence_1111", "sentence_1112", "sentence_1113", "sentence_1114", "sentence_1115", "sentence_1116", "sentence_1117", "sentence_1118", "sentence_1119"], "communicatesContent": "I wouldn't have the Scotland Yarders know it for the world; I have chaffed them so much that they would never have let me hear the end of it. I can afford to laugh, because I know that I will be even with them in the long run. That creature had gone a little way when she began to limp and show every sign of being foot-sore. Presently she came to a halt, and hailed a four-wheeler which was passing. Drive to 13, Duncan Street, Houndsditch. This begins to look genuine. I hopped off before we came to the door. Nothing came out though. There was no sign or trace of his passenger. On inquiring at Number 13 we found that the house belonged to a respectable paperhanger, named Keswick, and that no one of the name either of Sawyer or Dennis had ever been heard of there. Old woman be damned! We were the old women to be so taken in. It must have been a young man, and an active one, too, besides being an incomparable actor. The get-up was inimitable. He saw that he was followed, no doubt, and used this means of giving me the slip. It shows that the man we are after is not as lonely as I imagined he was, but has friends who are ready to risk something for him. Now, Doctor, you are looking done-up. Take my advice and turn in."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_30_5	event	\N	Watson goes to bed and Holmes remains up playing the violin	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1120", "sentence_1121"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_31_1	event	\N	Newspaper reports describe the Brixton Mystery	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1124", "sentence_1125", "sentence_1129", "sentence_1130", "sentence_1131", "sentence_1132", "sentence_1133", "sentence_1134", "sentence_1145", "sentence_1146", "sentence_1147", "sentence_1148", "sentence_1149"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_31_2	event	\N	Drebber stays at Madame Charpentier's boarding-house in Camberwell	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1135", "sentence_1136"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_31_3	event	\N	Drebber travels with Stangerson and goes to Euston Station	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1137", "sentence_1138", "sentence_1139", "sentence_1140"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_31_4	event	\N	Drebber's body is discovered in an empty house on Brixton Road	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1140", "sentence_1141"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_31_5	event	\N	Gregson and Lestrade work on the case	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1143", "sentence_1149", "sentence_1150", "sentence_1151", "sentence_1153", "sentence_1154", "sentence_1155", "sentence_1156", "sentence_1157"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_1	event	\N	Holmes summons and instructs the Baker Street irregulars	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1160", "sentence_1161", "sentence_1162", "sentence_1163", "sentence_1164", "sentence_1165", "sentence_1166", "sentence_1167", "sentence_1168", "sentence_1169", "sentence_1170", "sentence_1171"], "communicatesContent": "In future you shall send up Wiggins alone to report, and the rest of you must wait in the street. Have you found it, Wiggins? You must keep on until you do. Here are your wages. Now, off you go, and come back with a better report next time."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_2	event	\N	Holmes remarks on the usefulness of the street boys	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1172", "sentence_1173", "sentence_1174", "sentence_1175"], "communicatesContent": "There's more work to be got out of one of those little beggars than out of a dozen of the force. The mere sight of an official-looking person seals men's lips. These youngsters, however, go everywhere and hear everything. They are as sharp as needles, too; all they want is organisation."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_3	event	\N	Watson asks whether Holmes is employing the boys on the Brixton case	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1176", "sentence_1177"], "communicatesContent": "Is it on this Brixton case that you are employing them?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_4	event	\N	Holmes says he is using the boys to ascertain a point in the Brixton case	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1178", "sentence_1179"], "communicatesContent": "Yes; there is a point which I wish to ascertain. It is merely a matter of time."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_5	event	\N	Gregson arrives at Holmes's room and congratulates Holmes	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "tobias_gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1180", "sentence_1181", "sentence_1182", "sentence_1183", "sentence_1184", "sentence_1185", "sentence_1186", "sentence_1187", "sentence_1188"], "communicatesContent": "My dear fellow, congratulate me! I have made the whole thing as clear as day."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_6	event	\N	Holmes asks Gregson whether he is on the right track	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1189", "sentence_1190", "sentence_1191"], "communicatesContent": "Do you mean that you are on the right track?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_7	event	\N	Gregson says the police have the man under lock and key and names Arthur Charpentier	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "tobias_gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1192", "sentence_1193", "sentence_1194", "sentence_1195"], "communicatesContent": "The right track! Why, sir, we have the man under lock and key. Arthur Charpentier, sub-lieutenant in Her Majesty's navy."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_8	event	\N	Holmes invites Gregson to sit and offers cigars and whiskey and water	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1196", "sentence_1197", "sentence_1198", "sentence_1199"], "communicatesContent": "Take a seat, and try one of these cigars. We are anxious to know how you managed it. Will you have some whiskey and water?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_9	event	\N	Gregson accepts whiskey and water and explains his exertions	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "tobias_gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1200", "sentence_1201", "sentence_1202", "sentence_1203", "sentence_1204", "sentence_1205", "sentence_1206", "sentence_1207"], "communicatesContent": "I don't mind if I do. The tremendous exertions which I have gone through during the last day or two have worn me out. Not so much bodily exertion, you understand, as the strain upon the mind. You will appreciate that, Mr. Sherlock Holmes, for we are both brain-workers."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_32_10	event	\N	Gregson laughs and says Lestrade is on the wrong track after Stangerson	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "tobias_gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1208", "sentence_1209", "sentence_1210"], "communicatesContent": "The fun of it is that that fool Lestrade, who thinks himself so smart, has gone off upon the wrong track altogether. He is after the secretary Stangerson, who had no more to do with the crime than the babe unborn. I have no doubt that he has caught him by this time."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_1	event	\N	Gregson laughs until he chokes at the idea	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1211"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_2	event	\N	Holmes says he noticed the hat by the dead man	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1218", "sentence_1219"], "communicatesContent": "You remember the hat beside the dead man?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_3	event	\N	Gregson reports how he traced the hat to Drebber's address	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1227", "sentence_1230"], "communicatesContent": "I went to Underwood, asked about the hat, and found that it had been sent to Mr. Drebber at Charpentier's Boarding Establishment, Torquay Terrace, thus I got at his address."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_4	event	\N	Gregson visits Madame Charpentier and questions her about Drebber	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1233", "sentence_1248", "sentence_1258"], "communicatesContent": "Have you heard of the mysterious death of your late boarder Mr. Enoch J. Cleveland? At what o'clock did Mr. Drebber leave your house for the train? Was that the last which you saw of him?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_5	event	\N	Madame Charpentier answers that Drebber left at eight o'clock and that she last saw him then	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "madame_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1242", "sentence_1248", "sentence_1254"], "communicatesContent": "At eight o'clock."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_6	event	\N	The daughter reveals that they saw Drebber again	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "arthur_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1255", "sentence_1258"], "communicatesContent": "We did see Mr. Drebber again."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_33_7	event	\N	Madame Charpentier says she will tell all and states that her son is innocent	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "madame_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1265", "sentence_1270"], "communicatesContent": "I will tell you all, sir. My son is utterly innocent of it. My dread is that he may appear to be compromised."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_34_1	event	\N	Mrs. Charpentier tells the account of Mr. Drebber and Mr. Stangerson staying and behaving badly	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": "mrs_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1274", "sentence_1275", "sentence_1277", "sentence_1278", "sentence_1279", "sentence_1280", "sentence_1281", "sentence_1282", "sentence_1283", "sentence_1284", "sentence_1285"], "communicatesContent": "I had no intention of telling you all this, but since my poor daughter has disclosed it I have no alternative. Having once decided to speak, I will tell you all without omitting any particular. Mr. Drebber has been with us nearly three weeks. He and his secretary, Mr. Stangerson, had been travelling on the Continent. I noticed a \\"Copenhagen\\" label upon each of their trunks, showing that that had been their last stopping place. Stangerson was a quiet reserved man, but his employer was coarse in his habits and brutish in his ways. The very night of his arrival he became very much the worse for drink, and after twelve o'clock in the day he could hardly ever be said to be sober. His manners towards the maid-servants were disgustingly free and familiar. He speedily assumed the same attitude towards my daughter, Alice, and spoke to her more than once in a way which she is too innocent to understand. On one occasion he actually seized her in his arms and embraced her, an outrage which caused his own secretary to reproach him for his unmanly conduct."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_11	event	\N	Lestrade produces the pills, purse, and telegram and says he took them for safekeeping	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1464", "sentence_1465"], "communicatesContent": "I have them. I took them and the purse and the telegram, intending to have them put in a place of safety at the Police Station. It was the merest chance my taking these pills, for I am bound to say that I do not attach any importance to them."}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes Gives a Demonstration Chapter VII.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_34_2	event	\N	Mrs. Charpentier explains why she delayed giving Mr. Drebber notice	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": "mrs_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1289", "sentence_1290", "sentence_1291", "sentence_1292", "sentence_1293", "sentence_1294", "sentence_1295", "sentence_1296"], "communicatesContent": "Would to God that I had given him notice on the very day that he came. It was a sore temptation. They were paying a pound a day each—fourteen pounds a week, and this is the slack season. I am a widow, and my boy in the Navy has cost me much. I grudged to lose the money. I acted for the best. This last was too much, however, and I gave him notice to leave on account of it. That was the reason of his going."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_34_3	event	\N	Mrs. Charpentier describes Mr. Drebber's return and proposal to Alice	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": "mrs_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1298", "sentence_1299", "sentence_1300", "sentence_1301", "sentence_1302", "sentence_1303", "sentence_1304", "sentence_1305", "sentence_1306", "sentence_1307", "sentence_1308", "sentence_1309"], "communicatesContent": "My heart grew light when I saw him drive away. My son is on leave just now, but I did not tell him anything of all this, for his temper is violent, and he is passionately fond of his sister. In less than an hour there was a ring at the bell, and I learned that Mr. Drebber had returned. He was much excited, and evidently the worse for drink. He forced his way into the room, where I was sitting with my daughter, and made some incoherent remark about having missed his train. He then turned to Alice, and before my very face, proposed to her that she should fly with him. 'You are of age,' he said, 'and there is no law to stop you. I have money enough and to spare. Never mind the old girl here, but come along with me now straight away. You shall live like a princess.' Poor Alice was so frightened that she shrunk away from him, but he caught her by the wrist and endeavoured to draw her towards the door."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_34_4	event	\N	Arthur Charpentier enters the room during the struggle with Mr. Drebber	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": "arthur_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1310", "sentence_1311", "sentence_1312", "sentence_1313", "sentence_1314", "sentence_1315", "sentence_1316", "sentence_1317"], "communicatesContent": "I don't think that fine fellow will trouble us again. I will just go after him and see what he does with himself."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_34_5	event	\N	Arthur Charpentier leaves after the altercation	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1316", "sentence_1317"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_34_6	event	\N	Mr. Drebber's mysterious death is reported the next morning	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1318"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_35_1	event	\N	Mrs. Charpentier speaks haltingly about her son's return and absence	34	{"section": "section_35", "speakerId": "mrs_charpentier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1319", "sentence_1320", "sentence_1321", "sentence_1324", "sentence_1325", "sentence_1326", "sentence_1327", "sentence_1328", "sentence_1329", "sentence_1330", "sentence_1331", "sentence_1332", "sentence_1333", "sentence_1334", "sentence_1335", "sentence_1336", "sentence_1337", "sentence_1338"], "communicatesContent": "I do not know. He has a latch-key, and he let himself in. Yes, after you went to bed. About eleven. Yes. I do not know what he was doing during that time."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_35_2	event	\N	Gregson arrests Arthur Charpentier with two officers	34	{"section": "section_35", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1340", "sentence_1341", "sentence_1342"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_35_3	event	\N	Gregson states his theory about Charpentier and Drebber	34	{"section": "section_35", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1344", "sentence_1345", "sentence_1346", "sentence_1347", "sentence_1348", "sentence_1349", "sentence_1350"], "communicatesContent": "He still carried the heavy stick which the mother described him as having with him when he followed Drebber. It was a stout oak cudgel. My theory is that he followed Drebber as far as the Brixton Road. There, a fresh altercation arose between them, in the course of which Drebber received a blow from the stick, in the pit of the stomach, perhaps, which killed him without leaving any mark. The night was so wet that no one was about, so Charpentier dragged the body of his victim into the empty house. As to the candle, and the blood, and the writing on the wall, and the ring, they may all be so many tricks to throw the police on to the wrong scent."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_35_4	event	\N	Holmes praises Gregson's progress	34	{"section": "section_35", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1351", "sentence_1352", "sentence_1353", "sentence_1354"], "communicatesContent": "Well done! Really, Gregson, you are getting along. We shall make something of you yet."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_35_5	event	\N	Gregson explains Arthur Charpentier's volunteered statement	34	{"section": "section_35", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1355", "sentence_1356", "sentence_1357", "sentence_1358", "sentence_1359", "sentence_1360", "sentence_1361", "sentence_1362"], "communicatesContent": "The young man volunteered a statement, in which he said that after following Drebber some time, the latter perceived him, and took a cab in order to get away from him. On his way home he met an old shipmate, and took a long walk with him. On being asked where this old shipmate lived, he was unable to give any satisfactory reply. I think the whole case fits together uncommonly well. Lestrade had started off upon the wrong scent. I am afraid he won't make much of it. Why, by Jove, here's the very man himself!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_35_6	event	\N	Lestrade enters the room looking troubled	34	{"section": "section_35", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1363", "sentence_1364", "sentence_1365", "sentence_1366", "sentence_1367", "sentence_1368"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_36_1	event	\N	Gregson speaks triumphantly to Lestrade	35	{"section": "section_36", "speakerId": "gregson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1369", "sentence_1370", "sentence_1371"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, you find it so, Mr. Lestrade! I thought you would come to that conclusion. Have you managed to find the Secretary, Mr. Joseph Stangerson?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_36_2	event	\N	Lestrade states that Joseph Stangerson was murdered at Halliday's Private Hotel	35	{"section": "section_36", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1372", "sentence_1373"], "communicatesContent": "The Secretary, Mr. Joseph Stangerson, was murdered at Halliday's Private Hotel about six o'clock this morning."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_37_1	event	\N	Lestrade reports that he has discovered Stangerson dead in his room	36	{"section": "section_37", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1386", "sentence_1387"], "communicatesContent": "I have just come from his room. I was the first to discover what had occurred."}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "The Episode of the Barrel Chapter VIII.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_37_2	event	\N	Lestrade explains his earlier investigation of Stangerson and Drebber	36	{"section": "section_37", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1391", "sentence_1399"], "communicatesContent": "I freely confess that I was of the opinion that Stangerson was concerned in the death of Drebber. This fresh development has shown me that I was completely mistaken. Full of the one idea, I set myself to find out what had become of the Secretary. They had been seen together at Euston Station about half-past eight on the evening of the third. At two in the morning Drebber had been found in the Brixton Road. I telegraphed to Liverpool, giving a description of the man, and warning them to keep a watch upon the American boats. I then set to work calling upon all the hotels and lodging-houses in the vicinity of Euston. You see, I argued that if Drebber and his companion had become separated, the natural course for the latter would be to put up somewhere in the vicinity for the night, and then to hang about the station again next morning."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_37_3	event	\N	Lestrade arrives at Halliday's Private Hotel and is told Stangerson is upstairs in bed	36	{"section": "section_37", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1404", "sentence_1412"], "communicatesContent": "I asked whether a Mr. Stangerson was living there. I was told that he had been waiting for a gentleman for two days and was upstairs in bed, to be called at nine. I said I would go up and see him at once."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_37_4	event	\N	Lestrade discovers blood outside Stangerson's room and the room is forced open	36	{"section": "section_37", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1413", "sentence_1419", "sentence_1420"], "communicatesContent": "I said I would go up and see him at once."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_37_5	event	\N	Lestrade and the Boots find Stangerson dead in the room	36	{"section": "section_37", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1420", "sentence_1423"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_37_6	event	\N	Lestrade identifies the dead man as Joseph Stangerson and describes the wound	36	{"section": "section_37", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1422", "sentence_1423"], "communicatesContent": "The Boots recognized him at once as being the same gentleman who had engaged the room under the name of Joseph Stangerson. The cause of death was a deep stab in the left side, which must have penetrated the heart."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_1	event	\N	Holmes identifies the word RACHE written in blood	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1427"], "communicatesContent": "The word RACHE, written in letters of blood."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_2	event	\N	Lestrade confirms Holmes's statement	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1428"], "communicatesContent": "That was it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_3	event	\N	Lestrade describes the unknown assassin's methodical deeds	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1429"], "communicatesContent": "There was something so methodical and so incomprehensible about the deeds of this unknown assassin, that it imparted a fresh ghastliness to his crimes."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_4	event	\N	Lestrade reports that a milk boy sees a ladder at the hotel and a man descending it	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1431", "sentence_1432", "sentence_1433", "sentence_1434", "sentence_1435", "sentence_1436", "sentence_1437"], "communicatesContent": "The man was seen. A milk boy, passing on his way to the dairy, happened to walk down the lane which leads from the mews at the back of the hotel. He noticed that a ladder, which usually lay there, was raised against one of the windows of the second floor, which was wide open. After passing, he looked back and saw a man descend the ladder. He came down so quietly and openly that the boy imagined him to be some carpenter or joiner at work in the hotel. He took no particular notice of him, beyond thinking in his own mind that it was early for him to be at work. He has an impression that the man was tall, had a reddish face, and was dressed in a long, brownish coat."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_5	event	\N	Lestrade reports blood-stained water and knife marks	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1438"], "communicatesContent": "He must have stayed in the room some little time after the murder, for we found blood-stained water in the basin, where he had washed his hands, and marks on the sheets where he had deliberately wiped his knife."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_6	event	\N	Holmes asks whether anything found in the room could furnish a clue	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1441", "sentence_1442"], "communicatesContent": "Did you find nothing in the room which could furnish a clue to the murderer?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_7	event	\N	Lestrade says nothing was found except the purse, telegram, and other items	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1443", "sentence_1444", "sentence_1445", "sentence_1446", "sentence_1447", "sentence_1448", "sentence_1449"], "communicatesContent": "Nothing. Stangerson had Drebber's purse in his pocket, but it seems that this was usual, as he did all the paying. There was eighty odd pounds in it, but nothing had been taken. Whatever the motives of these extraordinary crimes, robbery is certainly not one of them. There were no papers or memoranda in the murdered man's pocket, except a single telegram, dated from Cleveland about a month ago, and containing the words, 'J. H.' There was no name appended to this message."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_8	event	\N	Holmes asks whether anything else was found	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1451", "sentence_1452"], "communicatesContent": "And there was nothing else?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_9	event	\N	Lestrade reports the novel, pipe, water, and pills in the room	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "lestrade", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1453", "sentence_1454", "sentence_1455"], "communicatesContent": "Nothing of any importance. The man's novel, with which he had read himself to sleep was lying upon the bed, and his pipe was on a chair beside him. There was a glass of water on the table, and on the window-sill a small chip ointment box containing a couple of pills."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_38_10	event	\N	Holmes springs up in delight and declares his case complete	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1456", "sentence_1457", "sentence_1458", "sentence_1459", "sentence_1460", "sentence_1461", "sentence_1462", "sentence_1463"], "communicatesContent": "The last link. My case is complete. I have now in my hands all the threads which have formed such a tangle. There are, of course, details to be filled in, but I am as certain of all the main facts, from the time that Drebber parted from Stangerson at the station, up to the discovery of the body of the latter, as if I had seen them with my own eyes. I will give you a proof of my knowledge. Could you lay your hand upon those pills?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_1	event	\N	Holmes asks for the pills and questions whether they are ordinary pills	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1466", "sentence_1467"], "communicatesContent": "Give them here. Now, Doctor, are those ordinary pills?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_2	event	\N	Watson states that the pills are not ordinary and describes their appearance	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1468", "sentence_1469"], "communicatesContent": "They certainly were not. They were of a pearly grey colour, small, round, and almost transparent against the light."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_3	event	\N	Watson suggests the pills are soluble in water and Holmes confirms it	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1470", "sentence_1471"], "communicatesContent": "From their lightness and transparency, I should imagine that they are soluble in water."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_4	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson to fetch the terrier	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1472"], "communicatesContent": "Now would you mind going down and fetching that poor little devil of a terrier which has been bad so long, and which the landlady wanted you to put out of its pain yesterday."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_5	event	\N	Watson carries the terrier upstairs and places it on a cushion on the rug	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1473", "sentence_1474", "sentence_1475", "sentence_1476"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_6	event	\N	Holmes cuts a pill in two and dissolves half of it in water	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1477", "sentence_1478", "sentence_1479", "sentence_1480"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_7	event	\N	Holmes places the dissolved pill mixture before the terrier and the terrier licks it up	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1484", "sentence_1485"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_8	event	\N	The observers watch the terrier and no effect appears	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1486", "sentence_1487", "sentence_1488", "sentence_1489", "sentence_1490", "sentence_1491"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_9	event	\N	Holmes exclaims that the pills suspected in Drebber's case were found after Stangerson's death and that one pill is inert	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1492", "sentence_1493", "sentence_1494", "sentence_1495", "sentence_1496", "sentence_1497", "sentence_1498", "sentence_1499", "sentence_1500"], "communicatesContent": "It can't be a coincidence. The very pills which I suspected in the case of Drebber are actually found after the death of Stangerson. And yet they are inert. What can it mean? Surely my whole chain of reasoning cannot have been false. It is impossible! And yet this wretched dog is none the worse. Ah, I have it! I have it!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_10	event	\N	Holmes prepares the other pill in the same way and gives it to the terrier, which dies	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1501", "sentence_1502", "sentence_1503"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_39_11	event	\N	Holmes states that one pill was deadly poison and the other harmless	38	{"section": "section_39", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1504", "sentence_1505", "sentence_1506"], "communicatesContent": "I should have more faith. I ought to know by this time that when a fact appears to be opposed to a long train of deductions, it invariably proves to be capable of bearing some other interpretation. Of the two pills in that box one was of the most deadly poison, and the other was entirely harmless. I ought to have known that before ever I saw the box at all."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_40_1	event	\N	Holmes says that the murder will not lead to more murders	39	{"section": "section_40", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1533", "sentence_1534"], "communicatesContent": "There will be no more murders."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_40_2	event	\N	Holmes says that he knows the assassin's name and expects to secure him shortly	39	{"section": "section_40", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1535", "sentence_1538"], "communicatesContent": "I do. ... This I expect very shortly to do."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_40_3	event	\N	Holmes says that the assassin is a shrewd and desperate man supported by another equally clever man	39	{"section": "section_40", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1539", "sentence_1540"], "communicatesContent": "we have a shrewd and desperate man to deal with, who is supported, as I have had occasion to prove, by another who is as clever as himself"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_1	event	\N	Wiggins enters the room and reports that the cab is downstairs	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": "wiggins", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1546", "sentence_1547"], "communicatesContent": "Please, sir, I have the cab downstairs."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_2	event	\N	Holmes shows handcuffs and comments on their use at Scotland Yard	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1549", "sentence_1550", "sentence_1551", "sentence_1552", "sentence_1553"], "communicatesContent": "Why don't you introduce this pattern at Scotland Yard? See how beautifully the spring works. They fasten in an instant."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_3	event	\N	Holmes asks the cabman to help with the boxes	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1555", "sentence_1556", "sentence_1558", "sentence_1559", "sentence_1560", "sentence_1561"], "communicatesContent": "The cabman may as well help me with my boxes. Just ask him to step up, Wiggins."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_4	event	\N	Holmes handcuffs Jefferson Hope and reveals his identity	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1562", "sentence_1563", "sentence_1565"], "communicatesContent": "Gentlemen, let me introduce you to Mr. Jefferson Hope, the murderer of Enoch Drebber and of Joseph Stangerson."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_5	event	\N	Jefferson Hope breaks free and leaps through the window	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1567", "sentence_1568", "sentence_1569", "sentence_1570", "sentence_1571", "sentence_1572", "sentence_1573", "sentence_1574"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_6	event	\N	Holmes states that they have Hope's cab and that it will take him to Scotland Yard	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1575", "sentence_1576"], "communicatesContent": "We have his cab. It will serve to take him to Scotland Yard."}
valley-of-fear	section_69	section	\N	Section 69	68	{"wordCount": 679}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_41_7	event	\N	Holmes says the mystery has reached its end and invites questions	40	{"section": "section_41", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1577", "sentence_1578"], "communicatesContent": "We have reached the end of our little mystery. You are very welcome to put any questions that you like to me now, and there is no danger that I will refuse to answer them."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_43_1	event	\N	A desert region lies across the central North American continent	42	{"section": "section_43", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1583", "sentence_1584"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_43_2	event	\N	The Great Alkali Plain has barrenness, inhospitality, and misery	42	{"section": "section_43", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1588"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_43_3	event	\N	Pawnees and Blackfeet traverse the land	42	{"section": "section_43", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1590"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_43_4	event	\N	Wild animals move through the wilderness	42	{"section": "section_43", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1591", "sentence_1592"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_43_5	event	\N	A pathway runs across the desert and is marked by bones	42	{"section": "section_43", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1601", "sentence_1602", "sentence_1603", "sentence_1605", "sentence_1606", "sentence_1607"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_43_6	event	\N	A solitary traveller stands on the plain on May 4, 1847	42	{"section": "section_43", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1608", "sentence_1609", "sentence_1610", "sentence_1611", "sentence_1612", "sentence_1613", "sentence_1614"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_1	event	\N	A man toils up from a ravine to a little elevation in search of water.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1615"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_2	event	\N	The man looks over the barren landscape and sees no signs of moisture.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1616", "sentence_1617", "sentence_1618"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_3	event	\N	The man sits down in the shelter of a boulder.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1619"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_4	event	\N	The man deposits his rifle and grey shawl bundle on the ground.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1620", "sentence_1621"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_5	event	\N	A crying child emerges from the grey shawl bundle after it is lowered.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1622"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_6	event	\N	The little girl complains that she has been hurt.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1623", "sentence_1624"], "communicatesContent": "You've hurt me!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_7	event	\N	The man unwraps the grey shawl and lifts out a little girl.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1625", "sentence_1626"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_8	event	\N	The man answers the girl's question about her hurt head.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1628", "sentence_1629", "sentence_1630", "sentence_1631", "sentence_1632", "sentence_1633", "sentence_1634"], "communicatesContent": "Mother's gone. I guess you'll see her before long."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_9	event	\N	The little girl says her mother did not say good-bye and asks whether there is water or food.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1635", "sentence_1636", "sentence_1637", "sentence_1638", "sentence_1639"], "communicatesContent": "Funny, she didn't say good-bye; she 'most always did if she was just goin' over to Auntie's for tea, and now she's been away three days. Say, it's awful dry, ain't it? Ain't there no water, nor nothing to eat?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_10	event	\N	The man replies that there is nothing and tells the girl to be patient.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1640", "sentence_1641", "sentence_1642", "sentence_1643"], "communicatesContent": "No, there ain't nothing, dearie. You'll just need to be patient awhile, and then you'll be all right. Put your head up agin me like that, and then you'll feel bullier. It ain't easy to talk when your lips is like leather, but I guess I'd best let you know how the cards lie."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_11	event	\N	The little girl shows two glittering pieces of mica.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1644", "sentence_1645", "sentence_1646", "sentence_1647"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_12	event	\N	The little girl says she will give the mica to Brother Bob when they return home.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1648"], "communicatesContent": "When we goes back to home I'll give them to brother Bob."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_13	event	\N	The man says the girl will soon see prettier things.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1649", "sentence_1650"], "communicatesContent": "You'll see prettier things than them soon. You just wait a bit."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_14	event	\N	The man explains that the party left the river, expected another river, but the navigation was wrong and the water ran out.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1651", "sentence_1652", "sentence_1653", "sentence_1654", "sentence_1655", "sentence_1656"], "communicatesContent": "I was going to tell you though—you remember when we left the river? Well, we reckoned we'd strike another river soon, d'ye see. But there was somethin' wrong; compasses, or map, or somethin', and it didn't turn up. Water ran out. Just except a little drop for the likes of you and—and——"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_15	event	\N	The little girl comments that the man could not wash himself.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1657"], "communicatesContent": "And you couldn't wash yourself."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_44_16	event	\N	The man says there was no water to wash or drink and names the dead members of the party.	43	{"section": "section_44", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1658", "sentence_1659", "sentence_1660"], "communicatesContent": "No, nor drink. And Mr. Bender, he was the fust to go, and then Indian Pete, and then Mrs. McGregor, and then Johnny Hones, and then, dearie, your mother."}
valley-of-fear	section_70	section	\N	Section 70	69	{"wordCount": 613}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_2	event	\N	The child asks whether they are going to die too	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1665", "sentence_1666"], "communicatesContent": "Do you mean that we are going to die too?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_3	event	\N	The child laughs and says they will be with mother again when they die	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1668", "sentence_1669", "sentence_1670", "sentence_1671"], "communicatesContent": "Why didn't you say so before? You gave me such a fright. Why, of course, now as long as we die we'll be with mother again."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_4	event	\N	The man answers that the child will be with mother again	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1672"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, you will, dearie."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_5	event	\N	The child says she will tell mother how good the man has been and imagines a welcome in Heaven	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1673", "sentence_1674", "sentence_1675", "sentence_1676"], "communicatesContent": "And you too. I'll tell her how awful good you've been. I'll bet she meets us at the door of Heaven with a big pitcher of water, and a lot of buckwheat cakes, hot, and toasted on both sides, like Bob and me was fond of. How long will it be first?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_6	event	\N	The man answers that he does not know and that it will not be very long	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1677"], "communicatesContent": "I don't know—not very long."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_7	event	\N	The man looks toward the northern horizon	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1678"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_8	event	\N	Three specks appear and become three large brown birds that settle on rocks near the wanderers	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1679", "sentence_1680"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_9	event	\N	The birds are identified as buzzards	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1681"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_10	event	\N	The child points at the birds and claps her hands	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1682"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_11	event	\N	The child asks whether God made this country	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1683", "sentence_1684"], "communicatesContent": "Say, did God make this country?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_12	event	\N	The man answers that God made the country in Illinois and Missouri	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1684", "sentence_1685"], "communicatesContent": "In course He did. He made the country down in Illinois, and He made the Missouri."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_13	event	\N	The child says somebody else made this country and that water and trees were forgotten	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1686", "sentence_1687", "sentence_1688"], "communicatesContent": "I guess somebody else made the country in these parts. It's not nearly so well done. They forgot the water and the trees."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_14	event	\N	The man suggests offering up prayer	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1689", "sentence_1690"], "communicatesContent": "What would ye think of offering up prayer?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_15	event	\N	The child says it is not night yet	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1691"], "communicatesContent": "It ain't night yet."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_16	event	\N	The man says it does not matter and asks her to say the prayers used in the wagon on the Plains	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1692", "sentence_1693", "sentence_1694"], "communicatesContent": "It don't matter. It ain't quite regular, but He won't mind that, you bet. You say over them ones that you used to say every night in the waggon when we was on the Plains."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_17	event	\N	The child asks why the man does not say some himself	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1695", "sentence_1696"], "communicatesContent": "Why don't you say some yourself?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_18	event	\N	The man says he has forgotten the prayers and has not said any since he was a child	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1697", "sentence_1698", "sentence_1699", "sentence_1700"], "communicatesContent": "I disremember them. I hain't said none since I was half the height o' that gun. I guess it's never too late. You say them out, and I'll stand by and come in on the choruses."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_19	event	\N	The child lays out the shawl for kneeling and instructs the man how to pray	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": "little_girl", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1701", "sentence_1702", "sentence_1703"], "communicatesContent": "Then you'll need to kneel down, and me too. You've got to put your hands up like this. It makes you feel kind o' good."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_20	event	\N	The two wanderers kneel side by side on the shawl and pray	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1704", "sentence_1705", "sentence_1706"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_21	event	\N	The child finishes the prayer and the pair resumes sitting until the child falls asleep on the man's breast	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1707"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_45_22	event	\N	The man watches over the child and then falls asleep beside her	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1708", "sentence_1709", "sentence_1710"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_1	event	\N	A great caravan approaches the bluff and stops below it	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1712", "sentence_1713", "sentence_1716", "sentence_1718", "sentence_1719", "sentence_1720", "sentence_1721", "sentence_1722", "sentence_1724", "sentence_1725"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_2	event	\N	The caravan leaders hold a short council	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1725"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_3	event	\N	One man says the wells are to the right	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1726"], "communicatesContent": "The wells are to the right, my brothers."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_4	event	\N	Another man says the route to the Rio Grande lies to the right of the Sierra Blanco	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1727"], "communicatesContent": "To the right of the Sierra Blanco—so we shall reach the Rio Grande."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_5	event	\N	A third man declares that their people will not be abandoned	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1728", "sentence_1729", "sentence_1730", "sentence_1731", "sentence_1732"], "communicatesContent": "Fear not for water. He who could draw it from the rocks will not now abandon His own chosen people."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_6	event	\N	The caravan members shout amen	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1730", "sentence_1731", "sentence_1732"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_7	event	\N	A young man points toward the crag above them	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1733", "sentence_1734"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_8	event	\N	The caravan halts and prepares weapons at the sight of the pink signal	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1735", "sentence_1736", "sentence_1737", "sentence_1738"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_9	event	\N	Young men dismount and climb the steep slope	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1739", "sentence_1740", "sentence_1741", "sentence_1742", "sentence_1743", "sentence_1744", "sentence_1745"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_46_10	event	\N	The scout group reaches the top and sees something startling	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1746"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_1	event	\N	John Ferrier and a little girl sleep beside a boulder on a plateau	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1747", "sentence_1748", "sentence_1749", "sentence_1750", "sentence_1751"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_2	event	\N	Buzzards scream and fly away when newcomers appear	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1752"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_3	event	\N	The cries of the buzzards wake the two sleepers	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1753"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_4	event	\N	John Ferrier stands up and looks over the plain at the large moving party	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1754", "sentence_1755"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_5	event	\N	John Ferrier mutters that the situation is what they call delirium	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1756"], "communicatesContent": "This is what they call delirium, I guess."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_6	event	\N	The child stands beside John Ferrier and looks around silently	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1757"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_7	event	\N	The rescuing party convinces the two castaways that their appearance is real	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1758"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_8	event	\N	Rescuers lift Lucy Ferrier onto a shoulder and support John Ferrier toward the wagons	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1759"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_9	event	\N	John Ferrier names himself and explains that only he and the girl remain alive from twenty-one people	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1760", "sentence_1761"], "communicatesContent": "My name is John Ferrier; me and that little un are all that's left o' twenty-one people. The rest is all dead o' thirst and hunger away down in the south."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_10	event	\N	Someone asks whether the girl is John Ferrier's child	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1762", "sentence_1763"], "communicatesContent": "Is she your child?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_11	event	\N	John Ferrier declares that Lucy is his and renames her Lucy Ferrier	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1764", "sentence_1765", "sentence_1766"], "communicatesContent": "I guess she is now; she's mine 'cause I saved her. No man will take her from me. She's Lucy Ferrier from this day on."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_12	event	\N	John Ferrier asks the rescuers who they are and comments on their number	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1767", "sentence_1768"], "communicatesContent": "Who are you, though? there seems to be a powerful lot of ye."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_13	event	\N	A rescuer states that the group numbers nearly ten thousand and identifies the Mormons	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1769"], "communicatesContent": "Nigh upon ten thousand. We are the persecuted children of God—the chosen of the Angel Merona."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_14	event	\N	John Ferrier says he has never heard of the Angel Merona and remarks on the crowd	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1770", "sentence_1771"], "communicatesContent": "I never heard tell on him. He appears to have chosen a fair crowd of ye."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_15	event	\N	A rescuer warns John Ferrier not to jest about what is sacred	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1772"], "communicatesContent": "Do not jest at that which is sacred."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_16	event	\N	A rescuer explains the group's beliefs, origin in Nauvoo, and search for refuge	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1773", "sentence_1774", "sentence_1775"], "communicatesContent": "We are of those who believe in those sacred writings, drawn in Egyptian letters on plates of beaten gold, which were handed unto the holy Joseph Smith at Palmyra. We have come from Nauvoo, in the State of Illinois, where we had founded our temple. We have come to seek a refuge from the violent man and from the godless, even though it be the heart of the desert."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_17	event	\N	John Ferrier recognizes the group as Mormons	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1776", "sentence_1777", "sentence_1778"], "communicatesContent": "I see, you are the Mormons."}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "The Baker Street Irregulars Chapter IX.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_18	event	\N	John Ferrier asks where the group is going and the rescuer answers that they do not know and must go before their Prophet	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1779", "sentence_1780", "sentence_1781", "sentence_1782", "sentence_1783"], "communicatesContent": "We do not know. The hand of God is leading us under the person of our Prophet. You must come before him. He shall say what is to be done with you."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_19	event	\N	The escort reaches the base of the hill and the crowd gathers around the castaways	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1784", "sentence_1785", "sentence_1786"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_20	event	\N	The escort and crowd move on toward a large ornate wagon	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1786", "sentence_1787"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_21	event	\N	The leader sits by the driver reading a brown-backed volume and listens to the account	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1788", "sentence_1789"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_47_22	event	\N	The leader turns to the two castaways	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1790"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_1	event	\N	The leader sets terms for taking Ferrier and the child with the Mormons.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1791", "sentence_1792", "sentence_1793", "sentence_1794"], "communicatesContent": "If we take you with us, it can only be as believers in our own creed. We shall have no wolves in our fold. Better far that your bones should bleach in this wilderness than that you should prove to be that little speck of decay which in time corrupts the whole fruit. Will you come with us on these terms?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_2	event	\N	Ferrier agrees to come with the Mormons on any terms.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1795"], "communicatesContent": "Guess I'll come with you on any terms."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_3	event	\N	The leader orders Brother Stangerson to take Ferrier, feed them, and teach the creed.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1796", "sentence_1797", "sentence_1798", "sentence_1799", "sentence_1800", "sentence_1801"], "communicatesContent": "Take him, Brother Stangerson, give him food and drink, and the child likewise. Let it be your task also to teach him our holy creed. We have delayed long enough. Forward! On, on to Zion!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_4	event	\N	The crowd of Mormons repeats the cry to go on to Zion.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "the_mormon_caravan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1802", "sentence_1803"], "communicatesContent": "On, on to Zion!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_5	event	\N	The caravan starts moving again.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1804"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_6	event	\N	The Elder leads Ferrier and the child to his wagon and provides a meal.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1805"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_48_7	event	\N	The Elder tells Ferrier and the child that they will remain in the wagon, recover, and be of the Mormon religion.	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1806", "sentence_1807", "sentence_1808", "sentence_1809"], "communicatesContent": "You shall remain here. In a few days you will have recovered from your fatigues. In the meantime, remember that now and for ever you are of our religion. Brigham Young has said it, and he has spoken with the voice of Joseph Smith, which is the voice of God."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_49_1	event	\N	Young administers the settlement and plans the future city	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1817", "sentence_1818", "sentence_1819", "sentence_1820", "sentence_1821", "sentence_1822", "sentence_1823", "sentence_1824", "sentence_1825"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_49_2	event	\N	The immigrant Mormons reach the Utah valley	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1816"], "communicatesContent": "this was the promised land, and that these virgin acres were to be theirs for evermore"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_49_3	event	\N	John Ferrier and Lucy Ferrier accompany the Mormons to the end of the pilgrimage	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1826", "sentence_1827", "sentence_1828", "sentence_1829", "sentence_1830"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_49_4	event	\N	John Ferrier receives a tract of land	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1830"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_49_5	event	\N	John Ferrier builds a log-house on his farm	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1831"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_49_6	event	\N	John Ferrier improves and tills his lands	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1833", "sentence_1834", "sentence_1835", "sentence_1836"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_50_1	event	\N	John Ferrier refuses to set up a female establishment	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1838", "sentence_1839"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_50_2	event	\N	John Ferrier remains strictly celibate	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1840", "sentence_1841", "sentence_1842"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_50_3	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier grows up in the log-house and assists John Ferrier	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1844"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_50_4	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier grows taller and stronger over the years	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1846"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_50_5	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier rides into the city on a commission from her father	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1859", "sentence_1860"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_1	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier reaches the outskirts of the city and finds the road blocked by a cattle drove	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1862"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_2	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier tries to pass the blockade by pushing her horse into a gap	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1863"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_3	event	\N	The cattle close in behind Lucy Ferrier and she becomes surrounded by the moving herd	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1864"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_4	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier urges her horse forward to force a path through the cattle	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1865"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_5	event	\N	A bullock's horns strike the flank of the mustang and excite it to madness	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1866"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_6	event	\N	The horse rears and tosses violently	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1867"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_7	event	\N	The excited horse continues to plunge and threaten Lucy Ferrier	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1869", "sentence_1870"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_8	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier grows dizzy, loosens her grip, and struggles to remain in the saddle	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1871"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_9	event	\N	A kindly voice at Lucy Ferrier's elbow assures her of assistance	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1872"], "communicatesContent": "assistance"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_10	event	\N	Jefferson Hope catches the frightened horse by the curb and brings Lucy Ferrier through the drove	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1873"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_11	event	\N	Jefferson Hope speaks to Lucy Ferrier and asks whether she is hurt	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1874"], "communicatesContent": "You're not hurt, I hope, miss"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_12	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier looks up at Jefferson Hope and laughs	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1875"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_13	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier speaks to Jefferson Hope and says she is frightened and that Poncho was scared by the cows	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "lucy_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1876"], "communicatesContent": "I'm awful frightened; whoever would have thought that Poncho would have been so scared by a lot of cows?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_14	event	\N	Jefferson Hope speaks earnestly and thanks God that Lucy Ferrier kept her seat	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1877"], "communicatesContent": "Thank God you kept your seat"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_15	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier observes Jefferson Hope's appearance and laughs saucily	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1878", "sentence_1879"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_16	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he saw Lucy Ferrier ride down from John Ferrier's house and asks her to tell John Ferrier if he remembers the Jefferson Hopes of St. Louis	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1879", "sentence_1880", "sentence_1881"], "communicatesContent": "I saw you ride down from his house. When you see him, ask him if he remembers the Jefferson Hopes of St. Louis. If he's the same Ferrier, my father and he were pretty thick."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_17	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier invites Jefferson Hope to come and ask John Ferrier himself	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "lucy_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1882", "sentence_1883"], "communicatesContent": "Hadn't you better come and ask yourself?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_18	event	\N	Jefferson Hope accepts the suggestion and says he will come	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1884", "sentence_1885", "sentence_1886"], "communicatesContent": "I'll do so; we've been in the mountains for two months, and are not over and above in visiting condition. He must take us as he finds us."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_19	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier speaks of John Ferrier's affection for her and says he would have been upset if the cows had attacked her	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "lucy_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1887", "sentence_1888"], "communicatesContent": "He has a good deal to thank you for, and so have I; he's awful fond of me. If those cows had jumped on me he'd have never got over it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_20	event	\N	Jefferson Hope replies that he would not have gotten over it either	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1889"], "communicatesContent": "Neither would I"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_51_21	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier tells Jefferson Hope that he is not even a friend of the family and then retracts it as he grows gloomy	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "lucy_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1890", "sentence_1891", "sentence_1892", "sentence_1893", "sentence_1894", "sentence_1895", "sentence_1896", "sentence_1897"], "communicatesContent": "You! Well, I don't see that it would make much matter to you, anyhow. You ain't even a friend of ours. There, I didn't mean that; of course, you are a friend now. You must come and see us. Now I must push along, or father won't trust me with his business any more. Good-bye!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_1	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says goodbye and departs the meeting	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1898", "sentence_1899"], "communicatesContent": "Good-bye."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_2	event	\N	Jefferson Hope rides on with his companions after leaving the meeting	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1900"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_3	event	\N	Jefferson Hope and his companions prospect for silver in the Nevada Mountains and return toward Salt Lake City seeking capital for their discovered lodes	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1901"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_4	event	\N	Jefferson Hope becomes distracted from the silver business by the encounter	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1902"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_5	event	\N	Jefferson Hope is stirred by the sight of Lucy Ferrier	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1903"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_6	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier vanishes from Jefferson Hope's sight	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1904"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_7	event	\N	Jefferson Hope resolves to pursue Lucy Ferrier over silver speculation	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1904", "sentence_1905", "sentence_1907"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_8	event	\N	Jefferson Hope calls on John Ferrier repeatedly until he becomes familiar at the farm-house	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1908"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_9	event	\N	John Ferrier lacks news of the outside world during the last twelve years	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1909"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_10	event	\N	Jefferson Hope tells John Ferrier his history and travels in a way that interests Lucy Ferrier	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1910", "sentence_1911", "sentence_1912", "sentence_1913"], "communicatesContent": "All this; he had been a pioneer in California and had also been a scout, trapper, silver explorer, and ranchman; wherever stirring adventures were to be had, he had been there in search of them."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_11	event	\N	Jefferson Hope becomes a favourite with John Ferrier	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1914"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_12	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier shows signs of affection for Jefferson Hope	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1915", "sentence_1916"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_13	event	\N	Jefferson Hope arrives galloping at John Ferrier's gate	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1917"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_14	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier comes down to meet Jefferson Hope	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1918"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_15	event	\N	Jefferson Hope ties up his horse and walks up the pathway	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1919"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_16	event	\N	Jefferson Hope asks Lucy Ferrier to be ready to come with him when he returns	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1920", "sentence_1921", "sentence_1923", "sentence_1924", "sentence_1925"], "communicatesContent": "I am off, Lucy; I won't ask you to come with me now, but will you be ready to come when I am here again? A couple of months at the outside. I will come and claim you then, my darling. There's no one who can stand between us."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_17	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier asks about her father	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "lucy_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1926", "sentence_1927"], "communicatesContent": "And how about father?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_18	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says John Ferrier has given consent if the mines work out	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1928", "sentence_1929"], "communicatesContent": "He has given his consent, provided we get these mines working all right. I have no fear on that head."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_19	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier accepts the arrangement and leans against Jefferson Hope	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1930"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_20	event	\N	Jefferson Hope thanks God and kisses Lucy Ferrier	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1931", "sentence_1932"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_52_21	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says the engagement is settled and he must leave for the cañon	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1933", "sentence_1934", "sentence_1935", "sentence_1936", "sentence_1937"], "communicatesContent": "It is settled, then. The longer I stay, the harder it will be to go. They are waiting for me at the cañon. Good-bye, my own darling—good-bye. In two months you shall see me."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_53_1	event	\N	John Ferrier tears himself away, mounts his horse, and rides off furiously	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1938"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_53_2	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier stands at the gate and watches John Ferrier until he disappears from sight	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1939"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_53_3	event	\N	Lucy Ferrier walks back into the house	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1940"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_54_1	event	\N	Three weeks pass after Jefferson Hope and his comrades depart from Salt Lake City	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1943"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_54_2	event	\N	John Ferrier worries about Jefferson Hope's return and the loss of his adopted child	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1944", "sentence_1945"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_54_3	event	\N	John Ferrier determines that his daughter shall never wed a Mormon	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1946", "sentence_1947", "sentence_1948"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_54_4	event	\N	John Ferrier keeps silent about his unorthodox opinion	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1949", "sentence_1950"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_54_5	event	\N	The story describes a secret persecuting organization in Utah	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1951", "sentence_1952", "sentence_1953", "sentence_1954", "sentence_1955", "sentence_1956", "sentence_1957", "sentence_1958"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_54_6	event	\N	The Danite Band becomes known as a terrible secret society	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1965", "sentence_1966", "sentence_1967", "sentence_1968", "sentence_1969", "sentence_1970", "sentence_1971"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_1	event	\N	John Ferrier prepares to leave for his wheatfields and sees Brigham Young approach	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1972", "sentence_1973"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_2	event	\N	John Ferrier greets Brigham Young at the door and leads him into the sitting-room	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1974", "sentence_1975"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_3	event	\N	Brigham Young says the Mormons had helped Ferrier and required him to embrace the true faith and conform to its usages	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "brigham_young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1976", "sentence_1977", "sentence_1978", "sentence_1980", "sentence_1981"], "communicatesContent": "Brother Ferrier, the true believers have been good friends to you. We picked you up when you were starving in the desert, we shared our food with you, led you safe to the Chosen Valley, gave you a goodly share of land, and allowed you to wax rich under our protection. In return for all this we asked but one condition: that was, that you should embrace the true faith, and conform in every way to its usages. This you promised to do, and this, if common report says truly, you have neglected."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_4	event	\N	John Ferrier answers that the Mormons' account is so	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1979"], "communicatesContent": "It is so."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_5	event	\N	Brigham Young asks about Ferrier's wives and calls them in	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "brigham_young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1987", "sentence_1988", "sentence_1989"], "communicatesContent": "Where are your wives? Call them in, that I may greet them."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_6	event	\N	John Ferrier says he has not married and has his daughter to attend to his wants	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1990", "sentence_1991", "sentence_1992"], "communicatesContent": "It is true that I have not married. But women were few, and there were many who had better claims than I. I was not a lonely man: I had my daughter to attend to my wants."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_7	event	\N	Brigham Young speaks about Ferrier's daughter, her social standing, rumors about her, and the thirteenth rule of Joseph Smith's code	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "brigham_young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1993", "sentence_1994", "sentence_1995", "sentence_1996", "sentence_1997", "sentence_1998", "sentence_1999", "sentence_2000", "sentence_2001"], "communicatesContent": "It is of that daughter that I would speak to you. She has grown to be the flower of Utah, and has found favour in the eyes of many who are high in the land. There are stories of her which I would fain disbelieve—stories that she is sealed to some Gentile. This must be the gossip of idle tongues. What is the thirteenth rule in the code of the sainted Joseph Smith? This being so, it is impossible that you, who profess the holy creed, should suffer your daughter to violate it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_8	event	\N	Brigham Young says the girl's fate will be decided by the Sacred Council of Four and offers her to Stangerson's son or Drebber's son	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "brigham_young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2002", "sentence_2003", "sentence_2004", "sentence_2005", "sentence_2006", "sentence_2007", "sentence_2008"], "communicatesContent": "Upon this one point your whole faith shall be tested—so it has been decided in the Sacred Council of Four. The girl is young, and we would not have her wed grey hairs, neither would we deprive her of all choice. We Elders have many heifers, but our children must also be provided. Stangerson has a son, and Drebber has a son, and either of them would gladly welcome your daughter to their house. Let her choose between them. They are young and rich, and of the true faith. What say you to that?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_9	event	\N	John Ferrier asks for time to consider and says his daughter is too young to marry	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2011", "sentence_2012", "sentence_2013"], "communicatesContent": "You will give us time. My daughter is very young—she is scarce of an age to marry."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_55_10	event	\N	Brigham Young grants Lucy Ferrier one month to choose and then rise from his seat	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "brigham_young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2014", "sentence_2015"], "communicatesContent": "She shall have a month to choose. At the end of that time she shall give her answer."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_56_1	event	\N	A man turns angrily while passing through the door and threatens John Ferrier	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "brigham_young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2016", "sentence_2017", "sentence_2018"], "communicatesContent": "It were better for you, John Ferrier, that you and she were now lying blanched skeletons upon the Sierra Blanco, than that you should put your weak wills against the orders of the Holy Four!"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_56_2	event	\N	John Ferrier sits with Lucy Ferrier and they discuss their situation	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2019", "sentence_2020", "sentence_2021", "sentence_2022", "sentence_2023", "sentence_2024", "sentence_2025", "sentence_2026", "sentence_2027", "sentence_2028", "sentence_2029", "sentence_2030", "sentence_2031", "sentence_2032", "sentence_2033", "sentence_2034", "sentence_2035", "sentence_2036", "sentence_2037", "sentence_2038", "sentence_2039", "sentence_2040", "sentence_2041", "sentence_2042", "sentence_2043", "sentence_2044", "sentence_2045", "sentence_2046", "sentence_2047", "sentence_2048", "sentence_2049", "sentence_2050", "sentence_2051", "sentence_2052", "sentence_2053"], "communicatesContent": "Don't you scare yourself. We'll fix it up somehow or another. You don't find your fancy kind o' lessening for this chap, do you? No; of course not. I shouldn't care to hear you say you did. He's a likely lad, and he's a Christian, which is more than these folk here, in spite o' all their praying and preaching. There's a party starting for Nevada to-morrow, and I'll manage to send him a message letting him know the hole we are in. If I know anything o' that young man, he'll be back here with a speed that would whip electro-telegraphs. When he comes, he will advise us for the best. But it is for you that I am frightened, dear. One hears—one hears such dreadful stories about those who oppose the Prophet: something terrible always happens to them. But we haven't opposed him yet. It will be time to look out for squalls when we do. We have a clear month before us; at the end of that, I guess we had best shin out of Utah. Leave Utah! That's about the size of it. But the farm? We will raise as much as we can in money, and let the rest go. To tell the truth, Lucy, it isn't the first time I have thought of doing it. I don't care about knuckling under to any man, as these folk do to their darned prophet. I'm a free-born American, and it's all new to me. Guess I'm too old to learn. If he comes browsing about this farm, he might chance to run up against a charge of buckshot travelling in the opposite direction. But they won't let us leave. Wait till Jefferson comes, and we'll soon manage that. In the meantime, don't you fret yourself, my dearie, and don't get your eyes swelled up, else he'll be walking into me when he sees you. There's nothing to be afeared about, and there's no danger at all."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_1	event	\N	John Ferrier goes to Salt Lake City and entrusts a message to his acquaintance for Jefferson Hope	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2056"], "communicatesContent": "John Ferrier sent a message to Jefferson Hope by his acquaintance."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_2	event	\N	John Ferrier tells Jefferson Hope about the danger and the need to return	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2057"], "communicatesContent": "the imminent danger which threatened them, and how necessary it was that he should return"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_3	event	\N	John Ferrier returns home from Salt Lake City	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2058"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_4	event	\N	John Ferrier sees two horses hitched at the farm gate	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2059"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_5	event	\N	John Ferrier finds two young Mormon men in his sitting-room	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2060"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_6	event	\N	The young men introduce themselves to John Ferrier	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "enoch_j_drebber", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2063", "sentence_2064", "sentence_2065"], "communicatesContent": "Maybe you don't know us. This here is the son of Elder Drebber, and I'm Joseph Stangerson, who travelled with you in the desert when the Lord stretched out His hand and gathered you into the true fold."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_7	event	\N	The other young man responds with a scriptural remark	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "enoch_j_drebber", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2066"], "communicatesContent": "As He will all the nations in His own good time; He grindeth slowly but exceeding small."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_8	event	\N	Stangerson and Drebber state their marriage proposal for Ferrier's daughter	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2069", "sentence_2070", "sentence_2071", "sentence_2072", "sentence_2073", "sentence_2074", "sentence_2075", "sentence_2076", "sentence_2077"], "communicatesContent": "We have come, at the advice of our fathers to solicit the hand of your daughter for whichever of us may seem good to you and to her. As I have but four wives and Brother Drebber here has seven, it appears to me that my claim is the stronger one."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_9	event	\N	John Ferrier rejects the visitors and orders them to leave until his daughter summons them	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2078", "sentence_2079", "sentence_2080", "sentence_2081", "sentence_2082", "sentence_2083", "sentence_2084", "sentence_2085", "sentence_2086"], "communicatesContent": "when my daughter summons you, you can come, but until then I don't want to see your faces again. There are two ways out of the room: there is the door, and there is the window. Which do you care to use?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_57_10	event	\N	The two visitors retreat and Stangerson threatens Ferrier	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2084", "sentence_2085", "sentence_2087", "sentence_2088", "sentence_2089", "sentence_2090"], "communicatesContent": "You shall smart for this! You have defied the Prophet and the Council of Four. You shall rue it to the end of your days."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_1	event	\N	Young Drebber threatens John Ferrier with divine punishment	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "enoch_j_drebber", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2091"], "communicatesContent": "The hand of the Lord shall be heavy upon you. He will arise and smite you."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_2	event	\N	John Ferrier tries to rush upstairs for his gun and Lucy restrains him	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2092"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_3	event	\N	Horses depart beyond John Ferrier's reach	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2093"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_4	event	\N	John Ferrier denounces the young men and says he would sooner see Lucy dead than married to either of them	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2094", "sentence_2095"], "communicatesContent": "The young canting rascals! I would sooner see you in your grave, my girl, than the wife of either of them."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_5	event	\N	Lucy says Jefferson Hope will soon be here	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "lucy_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2096"], "communicatesContent": "And so should I, father; but Jefferson will soon be here."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_6	event	\N	John Ferrier and Lucy Ferrier discuss Jefferson Hope's imminent arrival	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2097", "sentence_2098", "sentence_2099"], "communicatesContent": "Yes. It will not be long before he comes. The sooner the better, for we do not know what their next move may be."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_7	event	\N	A warning letter or notice is pinned to John Ferrier's bed coverlet	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2109", "sentence_2110", "sentence_2111"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_8	event	\N	John Ferrier crumples the warning paper and keeps silent to Lucy	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2114"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_9	event	\N	John Ferrier and Lucy Ferrier breakfast when Lucy notices the number 28 on the ceiling	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2119", "sentence_2120", "sentence_2121"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_10	event	\N	John Ferrier sits up with his gun and keeps watch through the night	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2122"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_11	event	\N	John Ferrier finds 27 painted on the outside of his door in the morning	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2123"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_12	event	\N	Days pass and unseen enemies keep marking numbers showing the remaining days of the month of grace	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2124", "sentence_2125", "sentence_2126"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_13	event	\N	John Ferrier becomes haggard and restless	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2127", "sentence_2128"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_58_14	event	\N	John Ferrier hopes for Jefferson Hope's arrival	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2129"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_59_1	event	\N	The old farmer watches the dwindling numbers and loses hope of escape	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2130", "sentence_2131", "sentence_2132", "sentence_2133", "sentence_2134", "sentence_2136", "sentence_2137", "sentence_2138", "sentence_2139", "sentence_2140", "sentence_2141", "sentence_2142", "sentence_2143", "sentence_2144"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_59_2	event	\N	John Ferrier hears scratching at the house door and opens it	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2145", "sentence_2146", "sentence_2147", "sentence_2148", "sentence_2149", "sentence_2150", "sentence_2153", "sentence_2154"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_67_16	event	\N	Jefferson Hope succeeds in running the fugitives to earth in London	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2424"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_59_3	event	\N	Jefferson Hope enters the house from outside	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2155", "sentence_2156", "sentence_2157", "sentence_2158", "sentence_2159", "sentence_2160", "sentence_2161"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_59_4	event	\N	John Ferrier speaks to Jefferson Hope in surprise	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2162", "sentence_2163", "sentence_2164", "sentence_2165"], "communicatesContent": "How you scared me! Whatever made you come in like that."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_1	event	\N	Jefferson Hope asks for food	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2166", "sentence_2167"], "communicatesContent": "Give me food. I have had no time for bite or sup for eight-and-forty hours."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_2	event	\N	Jefferson Hope eats the cold meat and bread on the table	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2168"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_3	event	\N	Jefferson Hope asks about Lucy Ferrier	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2169", "sentence_2170"], "communicatesContent": "Does Lucy bear up well?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_4	event	\N	John Ferrier answers that Lucy does not know the danger	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2171", "sentence_2172"], "communicatesContent": "Yes. She does not know the danger."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_5	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says the house is watched and explains his approach	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2173", "sentence_2174", "sentence_2175", "sentence_2176"], "communicatesContent": "That is well. The house is watched on every side. That is why I crawled my way up to it. They may be darned sharp, but they're not quite sharp enough to catch a Washoe hunter."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_6	event	\N	John Ferrier reacts cordially to Jefferson Hope	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2177", "sentence_2178", "sentence_2179", "sentence_2180"], "communicatesContent": "You're a man to be proud of. There are not many who would come to share our danger and our troubles."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_7	event	\N	Jefferson Hope explains that Lucy brought him there	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2181", "sentence_2182", "sentence_2183"], "communicatesContent": "You've hit it there, pard. I have a respect for you, but if you were alone in this business I'd think twice before I put my head into such a hornet's nest. It's Lucy that brings me here, and before harm comes on her I guess there will be one less o' the Hope family in Utah."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_8	event	\N	John Ferrier asks what they are to do	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2184"], "communicatesContent": "What are we to do?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_9	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says they must leave that night and travel to Carson City	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2185", "sentence_2186", "sentence_2187", "sentence_2188", "sentence_2189", "sentence_2190", "sentence_2191", "sentence_2192", "sentence_2193"], "communicatesContent": "To-morrow is your last day, and unless you act to-night you are lost. I have a mule and two horses waiting in the Eagle Ravine. How much money have you? That will do. I have as much more to add to it. We must push for Carson City through the mountains. You had best wake Lucy. It is as well that the servants do not sleep in the house."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_10	event	\N	Jefferson Hope prepares supplies for the journey	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2194"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_11	event	\N	John Ferrier returns with Lucy Ferrier ready to depart	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2195"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_12	event	\N	John Ferrier and Lucy Ferrier greet each other warmly	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2196"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_13	event	\N	Jefferson Hope urges an immediate departure and describes the escape route	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2197", "sentence_2198", "sentence_2199", "sentence_2200"], "communicatesContent": "We must make our start at once. The front and back entrances are watched, but with caution we may get away through the side window and across the fields. Once on the road we are only two miles from the Ravine where the horses are waiting. By daybreak we should be half-way through the mountains."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_14	event	\N	John Ferrier asks what happens if they are stopped	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "john_ferrier", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2201"], "communicatesContent": "What if we are stopped?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_15	event	\N	Jefferson Hope displays his revolver and threatens to kill pursuers with him	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2202", "sentence_2203"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_16	event	\N	Ferrier looks out from the darkened window at the fields he will abandon	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2204", "sentence_2205", "sentence_2206"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_60_17	event	\N	Jefferson Hope arrives at the house and shows a white face and set expression	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2207"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_61_1	event	\N	Ferrier, Jefferson Hope, and Lucy carry their supplies while escaping	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2208"], "communicatesContent": null}
