a-study-in-scarlet	event_67_14	event	\N	Jefferson Hope follows the fugitives to Paris and learns they have gone to Copenhagen	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2423"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_67_15	event	\N	Jefferson Hope reaches Copenhagen and finds the fugitives have already gone on to London	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2424"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_1	event	\N	The prisoner is escorted to the police-station by cab	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2428", "sentence_2429", "sentence_2430", "sentence_2431", "sentence_2433", "sentence_2434", "sentence_2443", "sentence_2444", "sentence_2445", "sentence_2446"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_2	event	\N	The police inspector records the prisoner's name and murder charges	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2446"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_3	event	\N	The police inspector tells the prisoner he will be put before the magistrates and warns him that his words may be used against him	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "police_inspector", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2448", "sentence_2449"], "communicatesContent": "The prisoner will be put before the magistrates in the course of the week; in the mean time, Mr. Jefferson Hope, have you anything that you wish to say? I must warn you that your words will be taken down, and may be used against you."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_4	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he wants to tell the gentlemen all about it	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2450", "sentence_2451"], "communicatesContent": "I've got a good deal to say. I want to tell you gentlemen all about it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_5	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he may never be tried and is not thinking of suicide	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2452", "sentence_2453", "sentence_2454", "sentence_2455", "sentence_2456"], "communicatesContent": "I may never be tried. It isn't suicide I am thinking of."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_6	event	\N	Jefferson Hope asks whether Watson is a doctor	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2457", "sentence_2458", "sentence_2459"], "communicatesContent": "Are you a Doctor?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_7	event	\N	Jefferson Hope asks Watson to place a hand on his chest and Watson does so	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2460", "sentence_2461", "sentence_2462", "sentence_2463", "sentence_2464"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_68_8	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he has an aortic aneurism, explains how he got it, and says he wants to leave an account of the business behind him	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2465", "sentence_2466", "sentence_2467", "sentence_2468", "sentence_2469", "sentence_2470"], "communicatesContent": "That's what they call it. I went to a doctor last week about it, and he told me that it is bound to burst before many days passed. It has been getting worse for years. I got it from over-exposure and under-feeding among the Salt Lake Mountains. I've done my work now, and I don't care how soon I go, but I should like to leave some account of the business behind me. I don't want to be remembered as a common cut-throat."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_1	event	\N	The Inspector and two detectives discuss whether to let Jefferson Hope tell his story	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2471"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_2	event	\N	The Inspector asks whether there is immediate danger	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "police_inspector", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2472", "sentence_2473"], "communicatesContent": "Do you consider, Doctor, that there is immediate danger?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_3	event	\N	Watson answers that there is immediate danger	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2474"], "communicatesContent": "Most certainly there is."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_4	event	\N	The Inspector orders that Jefferson Hope's statement be taken down	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "police_inspector", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2475", "sentence_2476"], "communicatesContent": "In that case it is clearly our duty, in the interests of justice, to take his statement. You are at liberty, sir, to give your account, which I again warn you will be taken down."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_5	event	\N	Jefferson Hope sits down and begins his statement	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2477", "sentence_2481"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_6	event	\N	Jefferson Hope states that his aneurism has made him tired and that the earlier struggle has worsened his condition	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2478", "sentence_2479", "sentence_2480"], "communicatesContent": "This aneurism of mine makes me easily tired, and the tussle we had half an hour ago has not mended matters. I'm on the brink of the grave, and I am not likely to lie to you. Every word I say is the absolute truth, and how you use it is a matter of no consequence to me."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_7	event	\N	Jefferson Hope speaks in a calm, methodical manner	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2482"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_8	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he hated the men who caused the death of a father and daughter and believes they forfeited their lives	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2484", "sentence_2485", "sentence_2486", "sentence_2487"], "communicatesContent": "It don't much matter to you why I hated these men; it's enough that they were guilty of the death of two human beings—a father and a daughter—and that they had, therefore, forfeited their own lives. After the lapse of time that has passed since their crime, it was impossible for me to secure a conviction against them in any court. I knew of their guilt though, and I determined that I should be judge, jury, and executioner all rolled into one. You'd have done the same, if you have any manhood in you, if you had been in my place."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_9	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says the girl was to have married him twenty years earlier	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2488"], "communicatesContent": "That girl that I spoke of was to have married me twenty years ago."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_10	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says the girl was forced to marry Drebber and broke her heart	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2489"], "communicatesContent": "She was forced into marrying that same Drebber, and broke her heart over it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_11	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he took the marriage ring from her dead finger and vowed revenge against Drebber	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2490"], "communicatesContent": "I took the marriage ring from her dead finger, and I vowed that his dying eyes should rest upon that very ring, and that his last thoughts should be of the crime for which he was punished."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_12	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he carried the ring and followed the men over two continents until he caught them	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2491", "sentence_2492"], "communicatesContent": "I have carried it about with me, and have followed him and his accomplice over two continents until I caught them. They thought to tire me out, but they could not do it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_13	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he will die soon and that his work is done	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2493", "sentence_2494", "sentence_2495"], "communicatesContent": "If I die to-morrow, as is likely enough, I die knowing that my work in this world is done, and well done. They have perished, and by my hand. There is nothing left for me to hope for, or to desire."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_14	event	\N	Jefferson Hope explains that the men were rich, he was poor, and he found cab-driving work in London	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2496", "sentence_2497", "sentence_2498", "sentence_2499", "sentence_2500"], "communicatesContent": "They were rich and I was poor, so that it was no easy matter for me to follow them. When I got to London my pocket was about empty, and I found that I must turn my hand to something for my living. Driving and riding are as natural to me as walking, so I applied at a cabowner's office, and soon got employment. I was to bring a certain sum a week to the owner, and whatever was over that I might keep for myself. There was seldom much over, but I managed to scrape along somehow."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_69_15	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says learning London's routes was difficult and that he used a map	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2501", "sentence_2502"], "communicatesContent": "The hardest job was to learn my way about, for I reckon that of all the mazes that ever were contrived, this city is the most confusing. I had a map beside me though, and when once I had spotted the principal hotels and stations, I got on pretty well."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_1	event	\N	Narrator finds the two gentlemen after searching for them	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2503", "sentence_2504", "sentence_2505"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_2	event	\N	Narrator grows a beard	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2506"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_3	event	\N	Narrator follows the two men around London	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2507", "sentence_2508", "sentence_2510", "sentence_2511", "sentence_2512", "sentence_2513"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_4	event	\N	The two men avoid going out alone or after nightfall for two weeks	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2514", "sentence_2515", "sentence_2516", "sentence_2517", "sentence_2518", "sentence_2519"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_5	event	\N	The men leave Torquay Terrace with luggage and drive away	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2520", "sentence_2521", "sentence_2522"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_6	event	\N	The men arrive at Euston Station and ask for the Liverpool train	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2523", "sentence_2524", "sentence_2525"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_7	event	\N	Drebber says he has private business and goes away alone	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": "enoch_j_drebber", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2527", "sentence_2528", "sentence_2529", "sentence_2530", "sentence_2531"], "communicatesContent": "he had a little business of his own to do, and that if the other would wait for him he would soon rejoin him"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_8	event	\N	Stangerson and Drebber agree that Drebber will rejoin Stangerson at Halliday's Private Hotel if he misses the last train	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": "stangerson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2528", "sentence_2531"], "communicatesContent": "they had resolved to stick together"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_9	event	\N	The narrator decides not to act immediately and keeps following	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2532", "sentence_2533", "sentence_2534", "sentence_2535", "sentence_2536", "sentence_2537", "sentence_2538", "sentence_2542"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_70_10	event	\N	A gentleman drops a key in the narrator's carriage and it is later claimed and returned	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2539", "sentence_2540", "sentence_2541"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_1	event	\N	He walks down the road, enters one or two liquor shops, and stays in the last one for nearly half an hour.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2543"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_2	event	\N	He comes out of the liquor shop and staggers in his walk.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2544"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_3	event	\N	He hails a hansom.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2545"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_4	event	\N	The cab is followed closely along Waterloo Bridge and through many streets until it reaches the Terrace where he had boarded.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2546", "sentence_2547"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_5	event	\N	He enters the house and his hansom drives away.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2549"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_6	event	\N	He asks for a glass of water and says that his mouth gets dry with the talking.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2550", "sentence_2551"], "communicatesContent": "Give me a glass of water, if you please. My mouth gets dry with the talking."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_7	event	\N	John Watson hands him the glass and he drinks the water.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2552"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_8	event	\N	After waiting, he hears a struggle inside the house and two men appear from the door, one being Drebber.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2554", "sentence_2555"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	section_26	section	\N	Section 26	25	{"wordCount": 669}
sign-of-the-four	section_27	section	\N	Section 27	26	{"wordCount": 651}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_10	event	\N	Drebber runs down the road, hails the cab, and jumps in.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2557", "sentence_2558"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_11	event	\N	Drebber orders the cab to drive him to Halliday's Private Hotel.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "enoch_j_drebber", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2559", "sentence_2560"], "communicatesContent": "Drive me to Halliday's Private Hotel."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_12	event	\N	Drebber is inside the cab and Jefferson Hope drives slowly while considering what to do.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2561", "sentence_2562"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_13	event	\N	Drebber orders the cab to stop outside a gin palace, goes in, and waits there until closing time.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2565", "sentence_2566", "sentence_2567"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_14	event	\N	Jefferson Hope states that he did not intend to kill Drebber in cold blood and that he had long determined to give him a chance for his life.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2568", "sentence_2569", "sentence_2570"], "communicatesContent": "Don't imagine that I intended to kill him in cold blood. It would only have been rigid justice if I had done so, but I could not bring myself to do it. I had long determined that he should have a show for his life if he chose to take advantage of it."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_15	event	\N	Jefferson Hope recounts having worked at York College, taking a little of a deadly alkaloid, and making it into pills in boxes with similar pills.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2571", "sentence_2572", "sentence_2573", "sentence_2574"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_71_16	event	\N	He says he planned that each of his opponents would draw from one of the boxes while he ate the remaining pill, and that he kept the pill boxes with him until now.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2575", "sentence_2576", "sentence_2577"], "communicatesContent": "I determined at the time that when I had my chance, my gentlemen should each have a draw out of one of these boxes, while I ate the pill that remained. It would be quite as deadly, and a good deal less noisy than firing across a handkerchief. From that day I had always my pill boxes about with me, and the time had now come when I was to use them."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_1	event	\N	A cab arrives at the house in Brixton Road	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2578", "sentence_2583"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_2	event	\N	The driver finds Drebber asleep in the cab and wakes him	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2585", "sentence_2586"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_3	event	\N	Drebber gets out of the cab and follows the driver into the garden and house	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2588", "sentence_2590"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_4	event	\N	The driver lights a candle and asks Drebber who he is	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "driver", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2593", "sentence_2594"], "communicatesContent": "Now, Enoch Drebber, who am I?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_5	event	\N	Drebber recognizes the driver and recoils in fear	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2595", "sentence_2596"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_6	event	\N	The driver laughs, locks the door, and confronts Drebber about his pursuit	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "driver", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2597", "sentence_2599", "sentence_2604"], "communicatesContent": "I have hunted you from Salt Lake City to St. Petersburg, and you have always escaped me."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_7	event	\N	The driver says he is temporarily mad	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "driver", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2601"], "communicatesContent": "So I was for the time."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_8	event	\N	The driver explains that his nosebleed relieves him and accuses Drebber of murder	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "driver", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2602", "sentence_2610", "sentence_2611", "sentence_2612"], "communicatesContent": "There is no murder. Who talks of murdering a mad dog? What mercy had you upon my poor darling, when you dragged her from her slaughtered father, and bore her away to your accursed and shameless harem."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_72_9	event	\N	Drebber stammers a question for mercy	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "enoch_j_drebber", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2608", "sentence_2609"], "communicatesContent": "[unclear]?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_1	event	\N	Speaker denies killing her father	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2613"], "communicatesContent": "It was not I who killed her father."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_2	event	\N	Narrator accuses speaker of breaking Lucy Ferrier's heart	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2614"], "communicatesContent": "But it was you who broke her innocent heart."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_3	event	\N	Narrator orders a choice between two pills	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2615", "sentence_2616", "sentence_2617", "sentence_2618", "sentence_2619"], "communicatesContent": "Let the high God judge between us. Choose and eat. There is death in one and life in the other. I shall take what you leave. Let us see if there is justice upon the earth, or if we are ruled by chance."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_4	event	\N	Jefferson Hope is forced to obey and choose a pill	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2620"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_5	event	\N	Narrator swallows the other pill	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2621"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_6	event	\N	Jefferson Hope shows signs of poisoning	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2622", "sentence_2624", "sentence_2625"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_7	event	\N	Narrator laughs and displays Lucy Ferrier's marriage ring	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2623"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_8	event	\N	Jefferson Hope falls dead on the floor	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2625", "sentence_2626", "sentence_2627", "sentence_2628"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_9	event	\N	Narrator notices blood from his nose and writes on the wall with it	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2629", "sentence_2630", "sentence_2631", "sentence_2633"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_10	event	\N	Narrator walks to his cab and discovers the night is wild and nobody is about	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2634"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_11	event	\N	Narrator discovers Lucy Ferrier's ring is missing from his pocket	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2635", "sentence_2636"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_12	event	\N	Narrator returns to the house and meets a police officer	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2637", "sentence_2638"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_13	event	\N	Narrator disguises himself as drunk to avoid suspicion	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2638"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_14	event	\N	Narrator states that Enoch Drebber came to his end	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2639"], "communicatesContent": "That was how Enoch Drebber came to his end."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_15	event	\N	Narrator decides to do the same to Stangerson	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2640"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_16	event	\N	Narrator waits outside Halliday's Private Hotel for Stangerson	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2641", "sentence_2642", "sentence_2643", "sentence_2644"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_17	event	\N	Narrator enters Stangerson's room at dawn using ladders	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2645"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_18	event	\N	Narrator wakes Stangerson and tells him to answer for his earlier killing	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2646"], "communicatesContent": "the hour had come when he was to answer for the life he had taken so long before"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_19	event	\N	Narrator describes Drebber's death and offers Stangerson the poisoned pills	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2647"], "communicatesContent": "Drebber's death and the same choice of the poisoned pills"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_20	event	\N	Stangerson attacks the narrator and the narrator stabs him	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2648", "sentence_2649"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_73_21	event	\N	Narrator states that Providence would not have allowed Stangerson to choose anything but the poison	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "john_watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2650"], "communicatesContent": "Providence would never have allowed his guilty hand to pick out anything but the poison"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_1	event	\N	Jefferson Hope says he has little more to say	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2651"], "communicatesContent": "I have little more to say, and it's as well, for I am about done up."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_2	event	\N	Jefferson Hope goes cabbing for a day or so	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2652"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_3	event	\N	A ragged youngster asks for Jefferson Hope at 221B Baker Street	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "young", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2653"], "communicatesContent": "there was a cabby there called Jefferson Hope, and his cab was wanted by a gentleman at 221B, Baker Street"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_4	event	\N	Jefferson Hope goes round to the address and is arrested	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2654"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_5	event	\N	Jefferson Hope calls himself a murderer and an officer of justice	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2656"], "communicatesContent": "You may consider me to be a murderer; but I hold that I am just as much an officer of justice as you are."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_6	event	\N	Lestrade writes up the account in shorthand	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2659"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_7	event	\N	Holmes asks who the accomplice was	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2660", "sentence_2661"], "communicatesContent": "Who was your accomplice who came for the ring which I advertised?"}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_8	event	\N	Jefferson Hope refuses to expose other people and explains the advertisement	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "jefferson_hope", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2662", "sentence_2663", "sentence_2664", "sentence_2665", "sentence_2666"], "communicatesContent": "I can tell my own secrets, but I don't get other people into trouble. I saw your advertisement, and I thought it might be a plant, or it might be the ring which I wanted. My friend volunteered to go and see. I think you'll own he did it smartly."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_9	event	\N	Holmes agrees that the accomplice acted smartly	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2667"], "communicatesContent": "Not a doubt of that."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_10	event	\N	The inspector announces the legal process and Jefferson Hope's detention	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "police_inspector", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2668", "sentence_2669", "sentence_2670"], "communicatesContent": "the forms of the law must be complied with. On Thursday the prisoner will be brought before the magistrates, and your attendance will be required. Until then I will be responsible for him."}
a-study-in-scarlet	event_74_11	event	\N	Jefferson Hope is led away by warders and Watson and Holmes leave for Baker Street by cab	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2671"], "communicatesContent": null}
