sign-of-the-four	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "A Break in the Chain Chapter X.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "The End of the Islander Chapter XI.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "The Great Agra Treasure Chapter XII.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "The Strange Story of Jonathan Small", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "Chapter I The Science of Deduction", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes took his bottle from the corner of the mantel-piece and his hypodermic syringe from its neat morocco case.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "With his long, white, nervous fingers he adjusted the delicate needle, and rolled back his left shirt-cuff.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "For some little time his eyes rested thoughtfully upon the sinewy forearm and wrist all dotted and scarred with innumerable puncture-marks.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "Finally he thrust the sharp point home, pressed down the tiny piston, and sank back into the velvet-lined arm-chair with a long sigh of satisfaction.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "Three times a day for many months I had witnessed this performance, but custom had not reconciled my mind to it.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "On the contrary, from day to day I had become more irritable at the sight, and my conscience swelled nightly within me at the thought that I had lacked the courage to protest.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "Again and again I had registered a vow that I should deliver my soul upon the subject, but there was that in the cool, nonchalant air of my companion which made him the last man with whom one would care to take anything approaching to a liberty.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "His great powers, his masterly manner, and the experience which I had had of his many extraordinary qualities, all made me diffident and backward in crossing him.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "Yet upon that afternoon, whether it was the Beaune which I had taken with my lunch, or the additional exasperation produced by the extreme deliberation of his manner, I suddenly felt that I could hold out no longer.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "“Which is it to-day?”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "I asked,—“morphine or cocaine?”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "He raised his eyes languidly from the old black-letter volume which he had opened.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "“It is cocaine,” he said,—“a seven-per-cent.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "solution.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "Would you care to try it?”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "“No, indeed,” I answered, brusquely.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "“My constitution has not got over the Afghan campaign yet.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "I cannot afford to throw any extra strain upon it.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "He smiled at my vehemence.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "“Perhaps you are right, Watson,” he said.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "“I suppose that its influence is physically a bad one.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "I find it, however, so transcendently stimulating and clarifying to the mind that its secondary action is a matter of small moment.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "“But consider!”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "I said, earnestly.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "“Count the cost!", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "Your brain may, as you say, be roused and excited, but it is a pathological and morbid process, which involves increased tissue-change and may at last leave a permanent weakness.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "You know, too, what a black reaction comes upon you.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "Surely the game is hardly worth the candle.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "Why should you, for a mere passing pleasure, risk the loss of those great powers with which you have been endowed?", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "Remember that I speak not only as one comrade to another, but as a medical man to one for whose constitution he is to some extent answerable.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "He did not seem offended.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "On the contrary, he put his finger-tips together and leaned his elbows on the arms of his chair, like one who has a relish for conversation.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "“My mind,” he said, “rebels at stagnation.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "Give me problems, give me work, give me the most abstruse cryptogram or the most intricate analysis, and I am in my own proper atmosphere.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "I can dispense then with artificial stimulants.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "But I abhor the dull routine of existence.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "I crave for mental exaltation.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "That is why I have chosen my own particular profession,—or rather created it, for I am the only one in the world.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "“The only unofficial detective?”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "I said, raising my eyebrows.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "“The only unofficial consulting detective,” he answered.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "“I am the last and highest court of appeal in detection.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "When Gregson or Lestrade or Athelney Jones are out of their depths—which, by the way, is their normal state—the matter is laid before me.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "I examine the data, as an expert, and pronounce a specialist’s opinion.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "I claim no credit in such cases.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "My name figures in no newspaper.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "The work itself, the pleasure of finding a field for my peculiar powers, is my highest reward.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "But you have yourself had some experience of my methods of work in the Jefferson Hope case.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "“Yes, indeed,” said I, cordially.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "“I was never so struck by anything in my life.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "I even embodied it in a small brochure with the somewhat fantastic title of ‘A Study in Scarlet.’”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "He shook his head sadly.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "“I glanced over it,” said he.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "“Honestly, I cannot congratulate you upon it.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "Detection is, or ought to be, an exact science, and should be treated in the same cold and unemotional manner.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "You have attempted to tinge it with romanticism, which produces much the same effect as if you worked a love-story or an elopement into the fifth proposition of Euclid.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "“But the romance was there,” I remonstrated.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "“I could not tamper with the facts.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "“Some facts should be suppressed, or at least a just sense of proportion should be observed in treating them.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "The only point in the case which deserved mention was the curious analytical reasoning from effects to causes by which I succeeded in unraveling it.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "I was annoyed at this criticism of a work which had been specially designed to please him.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "I confess, too, that I was irritated by the egotism which seemed to demand that every line of my pamphlet should be devoted to his own special doings.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "More than once during the years that I had lived with him in Baker Street I had observed that a small vanity underlay my companion’s quiet and didactic manner.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "I made no remark, however, but sat nursing my wounded leg.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "I had a Jezail bullet through it some time before, and, though it did not prevent me from walking, it ached wearily at every change of the weather.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "“My practice has extended recently to the Continent,” said Holmes, after a while, filling up his old brier-root pipe.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "“I was consulted last week by François Le Villard, who, as you probably know, has come rather to the front lately in the French detective service.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "He has all the Celtic power of quick intuition, but he is deficient in the wide range of exact knowledge which is essential to the higher developments of his art.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "The case was concerned with a will, and possessed some features of interest.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "I was able to refer him to two parallel cases, the one at Riga in 1857, and the other at St. Louis in 1871, which have suggested to him the true solution.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "Here is the letter which I had this morning acknowledging my assistance.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "He tossed over, as he spoke, a crumpled sheet of foreign notepaper.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "I glanced my eyes down it, catching a profusion of notes of admiration, with stray “magnifiques,” “coup-de-maîtres,” and “tours-de-force,” all testifying to the ardent admiration of the Frenchman.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "“He speaks as a pupil to his master,” said I.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "“Oh, he rates my assistance too highly,” said Sherlock Holmes, lightly.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "“He has considerable gifts himself.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "He possesses two out of the three qualities necessary for the ideal detective.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "He has the power of observation and that of deduction.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "He is only wanting in knowledge; and that may come in time.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "He is now translating my small works into French.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "“Your works?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "“Oh, didn’t you know?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "he cried, laughing.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "“Yes, I have been guilty of several monographs.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "They are all upon technical subjects.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "Here, for example, is one ‘Upon the Distinction between the Ashes of the Various Tobaccoes.’", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "In it I enumerate a hundred and forty forms of cigar-, cigarette-, and pipe-tobacco, with coloured plates illustrating the difference in the ash.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "It is a point which is continually turning up in criminal trials, and which is sometimes of supreme importance as a clue.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "If you can say definitely, for example, that some murder has been done by a man who was smoking an Indian lunkah, it obviously narrows your field of search.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "To the trained eye there is as much difference between the black ash of a Trichinopoly and the white fluff of bird’s-eye as there is between a cabbage and a potato.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "“You have an extraordinary genius for minutiæ,” I remarked.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "“I appreciate their importance.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "Here is my monograph upon the tracing of footsteps, with some remarks upon the uses of plaster of Paris as a preserver of impresses.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "Here, too, is a curious little work upon the influence of a trade upon the form of the hand, with lithotypes of the hands of slaters, sailors, corkcutters, compositors, weavers, and diamond-polishers.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "That is a matter of great practical interest to the scientific detective,—especially in cases of unclaimed bodies, or in discovering the antecedents of criminals.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "But I weary you with my hobby.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "“Not at all,” I answered, earnestly.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "“It is of the greatest interest to me, especially since I have had the opportunity of observing your practical application of it.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "But you spoke just now of observation and deduction.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "Surely the one to some extent implies the other.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "“Why, hardly,” he answered, leaning back luxuriously in his arm-chair, and sending up thick blue wreaths from his pipe.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "“For example, observation shows me that you have been to the Wigmore Street Post-Office this morning, but deduction lets me know that when there you dispatched a telegram.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "“Right!”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "said I.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_71	section	\N	Section 71	70	{"wordCount": 628}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "But I confess that I don’t see how you arrived at it.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "It was a sudden impulse upon my part, and I have mentioned it to no one.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "“It is simplicity itself,” he remarked, chuckling at my surprise,—“so absurdly simple that an explanation is superfluous; and yet it may serve to define the limits of observation and of deduction.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "Observation tells me that you have a little reddish mould adhering to your instep.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "Just opposite the Wigmore Street Office they have taken up the pavement and thrown up some earth which lies in such a way that it is difficult to avoid treading in it in entering.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "The earth is of this peculiar reddish tint which is found, as far as I know, nowhere else in the neighbourhood.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "So much is observation.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "The rest is deduction.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "“How, then, did you deduce the telegram?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "“Why, of course I knew that you had not written a letter, since I sat opposite to you all morning.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "I see also in your open desk there that you have a sheet of stamps and a thick bundle of post-cards.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "What could you go into the post-office for, then, but to send a wire?", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "Eliminate all other factors, and the one which remains must be the truth.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "“In this case it certainly is so,” I replied, after a little thought.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "“The thing, however, is, as you say, of the simplest.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "Would you think me impertinent if I were to put your theories to a more severe test?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "“On the contrary,” he answered, “it would prevent me from taking a second dose of cocaine.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "I should be delighted to look into any problem which you might submit to me.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "“I have heard you say that it is difficult for a man to have any object in daily use without leaving the impress of his individuality upon it in such a way that a trained observer might read it.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "Now, I have here a watch which has recently come into my possession.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "Would you have the kindness to let me have an opinion upon the character or habits of the late owner?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "I handed him over the watch with some slight feeling of amusement in my heart, for the test was, as I thought, an impossible one, and I intended it as a lesson against the somewhat dogmatic tone which he occasionally assumed.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "He balanced the watch in his hand, gazed hard at the dial, opened the back, and examined the works, first with his naked eyes and then with a powerful convex lens.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "I could hardly keep from smiling at his crestfallen face when he finally snapped the case to and handed it back.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "“There are hardly any data,” he remarked.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "“The watch has been recently cleaned, which robs me of my most suggestive facts.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "“You are right,” I answered.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "“It was cleaned before being sent to me.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "In my heart I accused my companion of putting forward a most lame and impotent excuse to cover his failure.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "What data could he expect from an uncleaned watch?", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "“Though unsatisfactory, my research has not been entirely barren,” he observed, staring up at the ceiling with dreamy, lack-lustre eyes.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "“Subject to your correction, I should judge that the watch belonged to your elder brother, who inherited it from your father.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "“That you gather, no doubt, from the H.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "W.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "upon the back?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "The date of the watch is nearly fifty years back, and the initials are as old as the watch: so it was made for the last generation.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "Jewelry usually descends to the eldest son, and he is most likely to have the same name as the father.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "Your father has, if I remember right, been dead many years.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "It has, therefore, been in the hands of your eldest brother.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "“Right, so far,” said I.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "“Anything else?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "“He was a man of untidy habits,—very untidy and careless.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "He was left with good prospects, but he threw away his chances, lived for some time in poverty with occasional short intervals of prosperity, and finally, taking to drink, he died.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "That is all I can gather.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "I sprang from my chair and limped impatiently about the room with considerable bitterness in my heart.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "“This is unworthy of you, Holmes,” I said.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "“I could not have believed that you would have descended to this.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "You have made inquires into the history of my unhappy brother, and you now pretend to deduce this knowledge in some fanciful way.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "You cannot expect me to believe that you have read all this from his old watch!", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "It is unkind, and, to speak plainly, has a touch of charlatanism in it.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "“My dear doctor,” said he, kindly, “pray accept my apologies.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "Viewing the matter as an abstract problem, I had forgotten how personal and painful a thing it might be to you.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "I assure you, however, that I never even knew that you had a brother until you handed me the watch.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "“Then how in the name of all that is wonderful did you get these facts?", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "They are absolutely correct in every particular.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "“Ah, that is good luck.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "I could only say what was the balance of probability.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "I did not at all expect to be so accurate.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "“But it was not mere guess-work?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "“No, no: I never guess.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "It is a shocking habit,—destructive to the logical faculty.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "What seems strange to you is only so because you do not follow my train of thought or observe the small facts upon which large inferences may depend.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "For example, I began by stating that your brother was careless.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "When you observe the lower part of that watch-case you notice that it is not only dinted in two places, but it is cut and marked all over from the habit of keeping other hard objects, such as coins or keys, in the same pocket.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "Surely it is no great feat to assume that a man who treats a fifty-guinea watch so cavalierly must be a careless man.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "Neither is it a very far-fetched inference that a man who inherits one article of such value is pretty well provided for in other respects.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "I nodded, to show that I followed his reasoning.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "“It is very customary for pawnbrokers in England, when they take a watch, to scratch the number of the ticket with a pin-point upon the inside of the case.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "It is more handy than a label, as there is no risk of the number being lost or transposed.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "There are no less than four such numbers visible to my lens on the inside of this case.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "Inference,—that your brother was often at low water.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_72	section	\N	Section 72	71	{"wordCount": 608}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "Secondary inference,—that he had occasional bursts of prosperity, or he could not have redeemed the pledge.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "Finally, I ask you to look at the inner plate, which contains the key-hole.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "Look at the thousands of scratches all round the hole,—marks where the key has slipped.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "What sober man’s key could have scored those grooves?", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "But you will never see a drunkard’s watch without them.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "He winds it at night, and he leaves these traces of his unsteady hand.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "Where is the mystery in all this?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "“It is as clear as daylight,” I answered.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "“I regret the injustice which I did you.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "I should have had more faith in your marvellous faculty.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "May I ask whether you have any professional inquiry on foot at present?”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "“None.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "Hence the cocaine.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "I cannot live without brain-work.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "What else is there to live for?", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "Stand at the window here.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "Was ever such a dreary, dismal, unprofitable world?", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "See how the yellow fog swirls down the street and drifts across the dun-coloured houses.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "What could be more hopelessly prosaic and material?", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "What is the use of having powers, doctor, when one has no field upon which to exert them?", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "Crime is commonplace, existence is commonplace, and no qualities save those which are commonplace have any function upon earth.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "I had opened my mouth to reply to this tirade, when with a crisp knock our landlady entered, bearing a card upon the brass salver.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "“A young lady for you, sir,” she said, addressing my companion.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "“Miss Mary Morstan,” he read.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "“Hum!", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "I have no recollection of the name.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "Ask the young lady to step up, Mrs. Hudson.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "Don’t go, doctor.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "I should prefer that you remain.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "Chapter II The Statement of the Case", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "Miss Morstan entered the room with a firm step and an outward composure of manner.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "She was a blonde young lady, small, dainty, well gloved, and dressed in the most perfect taste.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "There was, however, a plainness and simplicity about her costume which bore with it a suggestion of limited means.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "The dress was a sombre greyish beige, untrimmed and unbraided, and she wore a small turban of the same dull hue, relieved only by a suspicion of white feather in the side.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "Her face had neither regularity of feature nor beauty of complexion, but her expression was sweet and amiable, and her large blue eyes were singularly spiritual and sympathetic.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "In an experience of women which extends over many nations and three separate continents, I have never looked upon a face which gave a clearer promise of a refined and sensitive nature.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "I could not but observe that as she took the seat which Sherlock Holmes placed for her, her lip trembled, her hand quivered, and she showed every sign of intense inward agitation.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "“I have come to you, Mr. Holmes,” she said, “because you once enabled my employer, Mrs. Cecil Forrester, to unravel a little domestic complication.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "She was much impressed by your kindness and skill.”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "“Mrs. Cecil Forrester,” he repeated thoughtfully.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "“I believe that I was of some slight service to her.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "The case, however, as I remember it, was a very simple one.”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "“She did not think so.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "But at least you cannot say the same of mine.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "I can hardly imagine anything more strange, more utterly inexplicable, than the situation in which I find myself.”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "Holmes rubbed his hands, and his eyes glistened.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "He leaned forward in his chair with an expression of extraordinary concentration upon his clear-cut, hawklike features.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "“State your case,” said he, in brisk, business tones.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "I felt that my position was an embarrassing one.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "“You will, I am sure, excuse me,” I said, rising from my chair.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "To my surprise, the young lady held up her gloved hand to detain me.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "“If your friend,” she said, “would be good enough to stop, he might be of inestimable service to me.”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "I relapsed into my chair.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "“Briefly,” she continued, “the facts are these.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "My father was an officer in an Indian regiment who sent me home when I was quite a child.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "My mother was dead, and I had no relative in England.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "I was placed, however, in a comfortable boarding establishment at Edinburgh, and there I remained until I was seventeen years of age.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "In the year 1878 my father, who was senior captain of his regiment, obtained twelve months’ leave and came home.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "He telegraphed to me from London that he had arrived all safe, and directed me to come down at once, giving the Langham Hotel as his address.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "His message, as I remember, was full of kindness and love.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "On reaching London I drove to the Langham, and was informed that Captain Morstan was staying there, but that he had gone out the night before and had not yet returned.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "I waited all day without news of him.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "That night, on the advice of the manager of the hotel, I communicated with the police, and next morning we advertised in all the papers.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "Our inquiries led to no result; and from that day to this no word has ever been heard of my unfortunate father.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "He came home with his heart full of hope, to find some peace, some comfort, and instead—” She put her hand to her throat, and a choking sob cut short the sentence.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "“The date?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "asked Holmes, opening his note-book.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "“He disappeared upon the 3rd of December, 1878,—nearly ten years ago.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "“His luggage?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "“Remained at the hotel.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "There was nothing in it to suggest a clue,—some clothes, some books, and a considerable number of curiosities from the Andaman Islands.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "He had been one of the officers in charge of the convict-guard there.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "“Had he any friends in town?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "“Only one that we know of,—Major Sholto, of his own regiment, the 34th Bombay Infantry.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "The major had retired some little time before, and lived at Upper Norwood.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "“In this case, however—”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "We communicated with him, of course, but he did not even know that his brother officer was in England.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "“A singular case,” remarked Holmes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "“I have not yet described to you the most singular part.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "About six years ago—to be exact, upon the 4th of May, 1882—an advertisement appeared in the _Times_ asking for the address of Miss Mary Morstan and stating that it would be to her advantage to come forward.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "There was no name or address appended.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "I had at that time just entered the family of Mrs. Cecil Forrester in the capacity of governess.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "By her advice I published my address in the advertisement column.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "The same day there arrived through the post a small card-board box addressed to me, which I found to contain a very large and lustrous pearl.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "No word of writing was enclosed.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "Since then every year upon the same date there has always appeared a similar box, containing a similar pearl, without any clue as to the sender.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "They have been pronounced by an expert to be of a rare variety and of considerable value.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "You can see for yourselves that they are very handsome.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "She opened a flat box as she spoke, and showed me six of the finest pearls that I had ever seen.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "“Your statement is most interesting,” said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "“Has anything else occurred to you?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "“Yes, and no later than to-day.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "That is why I have come to you.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "This morning I received this letter, which you will perhaps read for yourself.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "“Thank you,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "“The envelope too, please.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "Postmark, London, S.W.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "Date, July 7.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "Hum!", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "Man’s thumb-mark on corner,—probably postman.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "Best quality paper.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "Envelopes at sixpence a packet.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "Particular man in his stationery.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "No address.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "‘Be at the third pillar from the left outside the Lyceum Theatre to-night at seven o’clock.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "If you are distrustful, bring two friends.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "You are a wronged woman, and shall have justice.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "Do not bring police.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "If you do, all will be in vain.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "Your unknown friend.’", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "Well, really, this is a very pretty little mystery.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "What do you intend to do, Miss Morstan?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "“That is exactly what I want to ask you.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "“Then we shall most certainly go.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "You and I and—yes, why, Dr. Watson is the very man.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "Your correspondent says two friends.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "He and I have worked together before.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "“But would he come?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "she asked, with something appealing in her voice and expression.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "“I should be proud and happy,” said I, fervently, “if I can be of any service.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "“You are both very kind,” she answered.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "“I have led a retired life, and have no friends whom I could appeal to.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "If I am here at six it will do, I suppose?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "“You must not be later,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "“There is one other point, however.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "Is this handwriting the same as that upon the pearl-box addresses?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "“I have them here,” she answered, producing half a dozen pieces of paper.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "“You are certainly a model client.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "You have the correct intuition.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "Let us see, now.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "He spread out the papers upon the table, and gave little darting glances from one to the other.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "“They are disguised hands, except the letter,” he said, presently, “but there can be no question as to the authorship.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "See how the irrepressible Greek _e_ will break out, and see the twirl of the final _s_.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "They are undoubtedly by the same person.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "I should not like to suggest false hopes, Miss Morstan, but is there any resemblance between this hand and that of your father?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "“Nothing could be more unlike.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "“I expected to hear you say so.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "We shall look out for you, then, at six.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "Pray allow me to keep the papers.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "I may look into the matter before then.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "It is only half-past three.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "_Au revoir_, then.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "“_Au revoir_,” said our visitor, and, with a bright, kindly glance from one to the other of us, she replaced her pearl-box in her bosom and hurried away.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "Standing at the window, I watched her walking briskly down the street, until the grey turban and white feather were but a speck in the sombre crowd.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "“What a very attractive woman!”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "I exclaimed, turning to my companion.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "He had lit his pipe again, and was leaning back with drooping eyelids.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "“Is she?”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "he said, languidly.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "“I did not observe.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "“You really are an automaton,—a calculating-machine!”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "I cried.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "“There is something positively inhuman in you at times.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "He smiled gently.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "“It is of the first importance,” he said, “not to allow your judgment to be biased by personal qualities.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "A client is to me a mere unit,—a factor in a problem.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "The emotional qualities are antagonistic to clear reasoning.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "I assure you that the most winning woman I ever knew was hanged for poisoning three little children for their insurance-money, and the most repellant man of my acquaintance is a philanthropist who has spent nearly a quarter of a million upon the London poor.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "An exception disproves the rule.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "Have you ever had occasion to study character in handwriting?", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "What do you make of this fellow’s scribble?”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "“It is legible and regular,” I answered.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "“A man of business habits and some force of character.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "Holmes shook his head.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "“Look at his long letters,” he said.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "“They hardly rise above the common herd.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "That _d_ might be an _a_, and that _l_ an _e_.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "Men of character always differentiate their long letters, however illegibly they may write.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "There is vacillation in his _k_’s and self-esteem in his capitals.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "I am going out now.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "I have some few references to make.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "Let me recommend this book,—one of the most remarkable ever penned.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "It is Winwood Reade’s ‘Martyrdom of Man.’", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "I shall be back in an hour.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "I sat in the window with the volume in my hand, but my thoughts were far from the daring speculations of the writer.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "My mind ran upon our late visitor,—her smiles, the deep rich tones of her voice, the strange mystery which overhung her life.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "If she were seventeen at the time of her father’s disappearance she must be seven-and-twenty now,—a sweet age, when youth has lost its self-consciousness and become a little sobered by experience.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "So I sat and mused, until such dangerous thoughts came into my head that I hurried away to my desk and plunged furiously into the latest treatise upon pathology.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "What was I, an army surgeon with a weak leg and a weaker banking-account, that I should dare to think of such things?", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "She was a unit, a factor,—nothing more.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "If my future were black, it was better surely to face it like a man than to attempt to brighten it by mere will-o’-the-wisps of the imagination.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "Chapter III In Quest of a Solution", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "It was half-past five before Holmes returned.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "He was bright, eager, and in excellent spirits,—a mood which in his case alternated with fits of the blackest depression.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "“There is no great mystery in this matter,” he said, taking the cup of tea which I had poured out for him.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "“The facts appear to admit of only one explanation.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "“What!", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "you have solved it already?”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "“Well, that would be too much to say.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "I have discovered a suggestive fact, that is all.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "It is, however, _very_ suggestive.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "The details are still to be added.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "I have just found, on consulting the back files of the _Times_, that Major Sholto, of Upper Norwood, late of the 34th Bombay Infantry, died upon the 28th of April, 1882.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "“I may be very obtuse, Holmes, but I fail to see what this suggests.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "“No?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "You surprise me.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "Look at it in this way, then.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "Captain Morstan disappears.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "The only person in London whom he could have visited is Major Sholto.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "Major Sholto denies having heard that he was in London.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "Four years later Sholto dies.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "_Within a week of his death_ Captain Morstan’s daughter receives a valuable present, which is repeated from year to year, and now culminates in a letter which describes her as a wronged woman.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "What wrong can it refer to except this deprivation of her father?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "And why should the presents begin immediately after Sholto’s death, unless it is that Sholto’s heir knows something of the mystery and desires to make compensation?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "Have you any alternative theory which will meet the facts?”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "“But what a strange compensation!", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "And how strangely made!", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "Why, too, should he write a letter now, rather than six years ago?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "Again, the letter speaks of giving her justice.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "What justice can she have?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "It is too much to suppose that her father is still alive.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "There is no other injustice in her case that you know of.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "“There are difficulties; there are certainly difficulties,” said Sherlock Holmes, pensively.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "“But our expedition of to-night will solve them all.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "Ah, here is a four-wheeler, and Miss Morstan is inside.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "Are you all ready?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "Then we had better go down, for it is a little past the hour.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "I picked up my hat and my heaviest stick, but I observed that Holmes took his revolver from his drawer and slipped it into his pocket.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "It was clear that he thought that our night’s work might be a serious one.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "Miss Morstan was muffled in a dark cloak, and her sensitive face was composed, but pale.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "She must have been more than woman if she did not feel some uneasiness at the strange enterprise upon which we were embarking, yet her self-control was perfect, and she readily answered the few additional questions which Sherlock Holmes put to her.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "“Major Sholto was a very particular friend of papa’s,” she said.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "“His letters were full of allusions to the major.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "He and papa were in command of the troops at the Andaman Islands, so they were thrown a great deal together.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "By the way, a curious paper was found in papa’s desk which no one could understand.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "I don’t suppose that it is of the slightest importance, but I thought you might care to see it, so I brought it with me.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "It is here.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "Holmes unfolded the paper carefully and smoothed it out upon his knee.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "He then very methodically examined it all over with his double lens.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "“It is paper of native Indian manufacture,” he remarked.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "“It has at some time been pinned to a board.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "The diagram upon it appears to be a plan of part of a large building with numerous halls, corridors, and passages.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "37 from left,’ in faded pencil-writing.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "In the left-hand corner is a curious hieroglyphic like four crosses in a line with their arms touching.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "Beside it is written, in very rough and coarse characters, ‘The sign of the four,—Jonathan Small, Mahomet Singh, Abdullah Khan, Dost Akbar.’", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "No, I confess that I do not see how this bears upon the matter.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "Yet it is evidently a document of importance.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "It has been kept carefully in a pocket-book; for the one side is as clean as the other.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "ully in a pocket-book; for the one side is as clean as the other.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "“It was in his pocket-book that we found it.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "“Preserve it carefully, then, Miss Morstan, for it may prove to be of use to us.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "I begin to suspect that this matter may turn out to be much deeper and more subtle than I at first supposed.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "I must reconsider my ideas.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "He leaned back in the cab, and I could see by his drawn brow and his vacant eye that he was thinking intently.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "Miss Morstan and I chatted in an undertone about our present expedition and its possible outcome, but our companion maintained his impenetrable reserve until the end of our journey.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "It was a September evening, and not yet seven o’clock, but the day had been a dreary one, and a dense drizzly fog lay low upon the great city.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "Mud-coloured clouds drooped sadly over the muddy streets.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "Down the Strand the lamps were but misty splotches of diffused light which threw a feeble circular glimmer upon the slimy pavement.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "The yellow glare from the shop-windows streamed out into the steamy, vaporous air, and threw a murky, shifting radiance across the crowded thoroughfare.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "There was, to my mind, something eerie and ghost-like in the endless procession of faces which flitted across these narrow bars of light,—sad faces and glad, haggard and merry.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "Like all human kind, they flitted from the gloom into the light, and so back into the gloom once more.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "I am not subject to impressions, but the dull, heavy evening, with the strange business upon which we were engaged, combined to make me nervous and depressed.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "I could see from Miss Morstan’s manner that she was suffering from the same feeling.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "Holmes alone could rise superior to petty influences.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "He held his open note-book upon his knee, and from time to time he jotted down figures and memoranda in the light of his pocket-lantern.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "At the Lyceum Theatre the crowds were already thick at the side-entrances.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "In front a continuous stream of hansoms and four-wheelers were rattling up, discharging their cargoes of shirt-fronted men and beshawled, bediamonded women.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "We had hardly reached the third pillar, which was our rendezvous, before a small, dark, brisk man in the dress of a coachman accosted us.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "“Are you the parties who come with Miss Morstan?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "“I am Miss Morstan, and these two gentlemen are my friends,” said she.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "He bent a pair of wonderfully penetrating and questioning eyes upon us.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "“You will excuse me, miss,” he said with a certain dogged manner, “but I was to ask you to give me your word that neither of your companions is a police-officer.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "“I give you my word on that,” she answered.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "He gave a shrill whistle, on which a street Arab led across a four-wheeler and opened the door.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "The man who had addressed us mounted to the box, while we took our places inside.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "We had hardly done so before the driver whipped up his horse, and we plunged away at a furious pace through the foggy streets.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "The situation was a curious one.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "We were driving to an unknown place, on an unknown errand.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_73	section	\N	Section 73	72	{"wordCount": 610}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "Yet our invitation was either a complete hoax,—which was an inconceivable hypothesis,—or else we had good reason to think that important issues might hang upon our journey.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_468	lexical	\N	\N	467	{"text": "Miss Morstan’s demeanor was as resolute and collected as ever.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_469	lexical	\N	\N	468	{"text": "I endeavored to cheer and amuse her by reminiscences of my adventures in Afghanistan; but, to tell the truth, I was myself so excited at our situation and so curious as to our destination that my stories were slightly involved.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_470	lexical	\N	\N	469	{"text": "To this day she declares that I told her one moving anecdote as to how a musket looked into my tent at the dead of night, and how I fired a double-barrelled tiger cub at it.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_471	lexical	\N	\N	470	{"text": "At first I had some idea as to the direction in which we were driving; but soon, what with our pace, the fog, and my own limited knowledge of London, I lost my bearings, and knew nothing, save that we seemed to be going a very long way.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_472	lexical	\N	\N	471	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes was never at fault, however, and he muttered the names as the cab rattled through squares and in and out by tortuous by-streets.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_473	lexical	\N	\N	472	{"text": "“Rochester Row,” said he.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_474	lexical	\N	\N	473	{"text": "“Now Vincent Square.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_475	lexical	\N	\N	474	{"text": "Now we come out on the Vauxhall Bridge Road.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_476	lexical	\N	\N	475	{"text": "We are making for the Surrey side, apparently.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_477	lexical	\N	\N	476	{"text": "Yes, I thought so.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_478	lexical	\N	\N	477	{"text": "Now we are on the bridge.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_479	lexical	\N	\N	478	{"text": "You can catch glimpses of the river.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_480	lexical	\N	\N	479	{"text": "We did indeed get a fleeting view of a stretch of the Thames with the lamps shining upon the broad, silent water; but our cab dashed on, and was soon involved in a labyrinth of streets upon the other side.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_481	lexical	\N	\N	480	{"text": "“Wordsworth Road,” said my companion.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_482	lexical	\N	\N	481	{"text": "“Priory Road.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_483	lexical	\N	\N	482	{"text": "Lark Hall Lane.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_484	lexical	\N	\N	483	{"text": "Stockwell Place.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_485	lexical	\N	\N	484	{"text": "Robert Street.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_486	lexical	\N	\N	485	{"text": "Cold Harbor Lane.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_487	lexical	\N	\N	486	{"text": "Our quest does not appear to take us to very fashionable regions.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_488	lexical	\N	\N	487	{"text": "We had, indeed, reached a questionable and forbidding neighbourhood.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_489	lexical	\N	\N	488	{"text": "Long lines of dull brick houses were only relieved by the coarse glare and tawdry brilliancy of public houses at the corner.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_490	lexical	\N	\N	489	{"text": "Then came rows of two-storied villas each with a fronting of miniature garden, and then again interminable lines of new staring brick buildings,—the monster tentacles which the giant city was throwing out into the country.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_491	lexical	\N	\N	490	{"text": "At last the cab drew up at the third house in a new terrace.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_492	lexical	\N	\N	491	{"text": "None of the other houses were inhabited, and that at which we stopped was as dark as its neighbours, save for a single glimmer in the kitchen window.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_493	lexical	\N	\N	492	{"text": "On our knocking, however, the door was instantly thrown open by a Hindoo servant clad in a yellow turban, white loose-fitting clothes, and a yellow sash.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_494	lexical	\N	\N	493	{"text": "There was something strangely incongruous in this Oriental figure framed in the commonplace doorway of a third-rate suburban dwelling-house.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_495	lexical	\N	\N	494	{"text": "“The Sahib awaits you,” said he, and even as he spoke there came a high piping voice from some inner room.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_496	lexical	\N	\N	495	{"text": "“Show them in to me, khitmutgar,” it cried.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_497	lexical	\N	\N	496	{"text": "“Show them straight in to me.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_498	lexical	\N	\N	497	{"text": "Chapter IV The Story of the Bald-Headed Man", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_499	lexical	\N	\N	498	{"text": "We followed the Indian down a sordid and common passage, ill-lit and worse furnished, until he came to a door upon the right, which he threw open.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_500	lexical	\N	\N	499	{"text": "A blaze of yellow light streamed out upon us, and in the centre of the glare there stood a small man with a very high head, a bristle of red hair all round the fringe of it, and a bald, shining scalp which shot out from among it like a mountain-peak from fir-trees.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_74	section	\N	Section 74	73	{"wordCount": 657}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_501	lexical	\N	\N	500	{"text": "He writhed his hands together as he stood, and his features were in a perpetual jerk, now smiling, now scowling, but never for an instant in repose.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_502	lexical	\N	\N	501	{"text": "Nature had given him a pendulous lip, and a too visible line of yellow and irregular teeth, which he strove feebly to conceal by constantly passing his hand over the lower part of his face.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_503	lexical	\N	\N	502	{"text": "In spite of his obtrusive baldness, he gave the impression of youth.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_504	lexical	\N	\N	503	{"text": "In point of fact he had just turned his thirtieth year.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_505	lexical	\N	\N	504	{"text": "“Your servant, Miss Morstan,” he kept repeating, in a thin, high voice.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_506	lexical	\N	\N	505	{"text": "“Your servant, gentlemen.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_507	lexical	\N	\N	506	{"text": "Pray step into my little sanctum.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_508	lexical	\N	\N	507	{"text": "A small place, miss, but furnished to my own liking.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_509	lexical	\N	\N	508	{"text": "An oasis of art in the howling desert of South London.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_510	lexical	\N	\N	509	{"text": "We were all astonished by the appearance of the apartment into which he invited us.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_511	lexical	\N	\N	510	{"text": "In that sorry house it looked as out of place as a diamond of the first water in a setting of brass.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_512	lexical	\N	\N	511	{"text": "The richest and glossiest of curtains and tapestries draped the walls, looped back here and there to expose some richly-mounted painting or Oriental vase.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_513	lexical	\N	\N	512	{"text": "The carpet was of amber-and-black, so soft and so thick that the foot sank pleasantly into it, as into a bed of moss.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_514	lexical	\N	\N	513	{"text": "Two great tiger-skins thrown athwart it increased the suggestion of Eastern luxury, as did a huge hookah which stood upon a mat in the corner.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_515	lexical	\N	\N	514	{"text": "A lamp in the fashion of a silver dove was hung from an almost invisible golden wire in the centre of the room.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_516	lexical	\N	\N	515	{"text": "As it burned it filled the air with a subtle and aromatic odour.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_517	lexical	\N	\N	516	{"text": "“Mr. Thaddeus Sholto,” said the little man, still jerking and smiling.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_518	lexical	\N	\N	517	{"text": "“That is my name.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_519	lexical	\N	\N	518	{"text": "You are Miss Morstan, of course.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_520	lexical	\N	\N	519	{"text": "And these gentlemen—”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_521	lexical	\N	\N	520	{"text": "“This is Mr. Sherlock Holmes, and this is Dr. Watson.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_522	lexical	\N	\N	521	{"text": "“A doctor, eh?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_523	lexical	\N	\N	522	{"text": "cried he, much excited.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_524	lexical	\N	\N	523	{"text": "“Have you your stethoscope?", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_525	lexical	\N	\N	524	{"text": "Might I ask you—would you have the kindness?", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_526	lexical	\N	\N	525	{"text": "I have grave doubts as to my mitral valve, if you would be so very good.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_527	lexical	\N	\N	526	{"text": "The aortic I may rely upon, but I should value your opinion upon the mitral.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_528	lexical	\N	\N	527	{"text": "I listened to his heart, as requested, but was unable to find anything amiss, save indeed that he was in an ecstasy of fear, for he shivered from head to foot.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_529	lexical	\N	\N	528	{"text": "“It appears to be normal,” I said.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_530	lexical	\N	\N	529	{"text": "“You have no cause for uneasiness.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_531	lexical	\N	\N	530	{"text": "“You will excuse my anxiety, Miss Morstan,” he remarked, airily.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_532	lexical	\N	\N	531	{"text": "“I am a great sufferer, and I have long had suspicions as to that valve.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_533	lexical	\N	\N	532	{"text": "I am delighted to hear that they are unwarranted.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_534	lexical	\N	\N	533	{"text": "Had your father, Miss Morstan, refrained from throwing a strain upon his heart, he might have been alive now.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_535	lexical	\N	\N	534	{"text": "I could have struck the man across the face, so hot was I at this callous and off-hand reference to so delicate a matter.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_536	lexical	\N	\N	535	{"text": "Miss Morstan sat down, and her face grew white to the lips.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_537	lexical	\N	\N	536	{"text": "“I knew in my heart that he was dead,” said she.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_575	lexical	\N	\N	574	{"text": "I had quite high words with him last night.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_538	lexical	\N	\N	537	{"text": "“I can give you every information,” said he, “and, what is more, I can do you justice; and I will, too, whatever Brother Bartholomew may say.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_539	lexical	\N	\N	538	{"text": "I am so glad to have your friends here, not only as an escort to you, but also as witnesses to what I am about to do and say.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_540	lexical	\N	\N	539	{"text": "The three of us can show a bold front to Brother Bartholomew.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_541	lexical	\N	\N	540	{"text": "But let us have no outsiders,—no police or officials.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_542	lexical	\N	\N	541	{"text": "We can settle everything satisfactorily among ourselves, without any interference.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_543	lexical	\N	\N	542	{"text": "Nothing would annoy Brother Bartholomew more than any publicity.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_544	lexical	\N	\N	543	{"text": "He sat down upon a low settee and blinked at us inquiringly with his weak, watery blue eyes.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_545	lexical	\N	\N	544	{"text": "“For my part,” said Holmes, “whatever you may choose to say will go no further.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_546	lexical	\N	\N	545	{"text": "I nodded to show my agreement.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_547	lexical	\N	\N	546	{"text": "“That is well!", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_548	lexical	\N	\N	547	{"text": "That is well!”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_549	lexical	\N	\N	548	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_550	lexical	\N	\N	549	{"text": "“May I offer you a glass of Chianti, Miss Morstan?", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_551	lexical	\N	\N	550	{"text": "Or of Tokay?", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_552	lexical	\N	\N	551	{"text": "I keep no other wines.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_553	lexical	\N	\N	552	{"text": "Shall I open a flask?", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_554	lexical	\N	\N	553	{"text": "No?", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_555	lexical	\N	\N	554	{"text": "Well, then, I trust that you have no objection to tobacco-smoke, to the mild balsamic odour of the Eastern tobacco.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_556	lexical	\N	\N	555	{"text": "I am a little nervous, and I find my hookah an invaluable sedative.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_557	lexical	\N	\N	556	{"text": "He applied a taper to the great bowl, and the smoke bubbled merrily through the rose-water.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_558	lexical	\N	\N	557	{"text": "We sat all three in a semi-circle, with our heads advanced, and our chins upon our hands, while the strange, jerky little fellow, with his high, shining head, puffed uneasily in the centre.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_559	lexical	\N	\N	558	{"text": "“When I first determined to make this communication to you,” said he, “I might have given you my address, but I feared that you might disregard my request and bring unpleasant people with you.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_560	lexical	\N	\N	559	{"text": "I took the liberty, therefore, of making an appointment in such a way that my man Williams might be able to see you first.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_561	lexical	\N	\N	560	{"text": "I have complete confidence in his discretion, and he had orders, if he were dissatisfied, to proceed no further in the matter.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_562	lexical	\N	\N	561	{"text": "You will excuse these precautions, but I am a man of somewhat retiring, and I might even say refined, tastes, and there is nothing more unæsthetic than a policeman.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_563	lexical	\N	\N	562	{"text": "I have a natural shrinking from all forms of rough materialism.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_564	lexical	\N	\N	563	{"text": "I seldom come in contact with the rough crowd.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_565	lexical	\N	\N	564	{"text": "I live, as you see, with some little atmosphere of elegance around me.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_566	lexical	\N	\N	565	{"text": "I may call myself a patron of the arts.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_567	lexical	\N	\N	566	{"text": "It is my weakness.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_568	lexical	\N	\N	567	{"text": "The landscape is a genuine Corot, and, though a connoisseur might perhaps throw a doubt upon that Salvator Rosa, there cannot be the least question about the Bouguereau.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_569	lexical	\N	\N	568	{"text": "I am partial to the modern French school.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_570	lexical	\N	\N	569	{"text": "“You will excuse me, Mr. Sholto,” said Miss Morstan, “but I am here at your request to learn something which you desire to tell me.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_571	lexical	\N	\N	570	{"text": "It is very late, and I should desire the interview to be as short as possible.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_572	lexical	\N	\N	571	{"text": "“At the best it must take some time,” he answered; “for we shall certainly have to go to Norwood and see Brother Bartholomew.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_573	lexical	\N	\N	572	{"text": "We shall all go and try if we can get the better of Brother Bartholomew.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_574	lexical	\N	\N	573	{"text": "He is very angry with me for taking the course which has seemed right to me.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_576	lexical	\N	\N	575	{"text": "You cannot imagine what a terrible fellow he is when he is angry.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_577	lexical	\N	\N	576	{"text": "“If we are to go to Norwood it would perhaps be as well to start at once,” I ventured to remark.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_578	lexical	\N	\N	577	{"text": "He laughed until his ears were quite red.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_579	lexical	\N	\N	578	{"text": "“That would hardly do,” he cried.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_580	lexical	\N	\N	579	{"text": "“I don’t know what he would say if I brought you in that sudden way.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_581	lexical	\N	\N	580	{"text": "No, I must prepare you by showing you how we all stand to each other.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_582	lexical	\N	\N	581	{"text": "In the first place, I must tell you that there are several points in the story of which I am myself ignorant.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_583	lexical	\N	\N	582	{"text": "I can only lay the facts before you as far as I know them myself.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_584	lexical	\N	\N	583	{"text": "“My father was, as you may have guessed, Major John Sholto, once of the Indian army.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_585	lexical	\N	\N	584	{"text": "He retired some eleven years ago, and came to live at Pondicherry Lodge in Upper Norwood.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_586	lexical	\N	\N	585	{"text": "He had prospered in India, and brought back with him a considerable sum of money, a large collection of valuable curiosities, and a staff of native servants.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_587	lexical	\N	\N	586	{"text": "With these advantages he bought himself a house, and lived in great luxury.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_588	lexical	\N	\N	587	{"text": "My twin-brother Bartholomew and I were the only children.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_589	lexical	\N	\N	588	{"text": "“I very well remember the sensation which was caused by the disappearance of Captain Morstan.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_590	lexical	\N	\N	589	{"text": "We read the details in the papers, and, knowing that he had been a friend of our father’s, we discussed the case freely in his presence.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_591	lexical	\N	\N	590	{"text": "He used to join in our speculations as to what could have happened.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_592	lexical	\N	\N	591	{"text": "Never for an instant did we suspect that he had the whole secret hidden in his own breast,—that of all men he alone knew the fate of Arthur Morstan.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_593	lexical	\N	\N	592	{"text": "“We did know, however, that some mystery—some positive danger—overhung our father.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_594	lexical	\N	\N	593	{"text": "He was very fearful of going out alone, and he always employed two prize-fighters to act as porters at Pondicherry Lodge.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_595	lexical	\N	\N	594	{"text": "Williams, who drove you to-night, was one of them.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_596	lexical	\N	\N	595	{"text": "He was once light-weight champion of England.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_597	lexical	\N	\N	596	{"text": "Our father would never tell us what it was he feared, but he had a most marked aversion to men with wooden legs.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_598	lexical	\N	\N	597	{"text": "On one occasion he actually fired his revolver at a wooden-legged man, who proved to be a harmless tradesman canvassing for orders.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_599	lexical	\N	\N	598	{"text": "We had to pay a large sum to hush the matter up.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_600	lexical	\N	\N	599	{"text": "My brother and I used to think this a mere whim of my father’s, but events have since led us to change our opinion.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_601	lexical	\N	\N	600	{"text": "“Early in 1882 my father received a letter from India which was a great shock to him.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_602	lexical	\N	\N	601	{"text": "He nearly fainted at the breakfast-table when he opened it, and from that day he sickened to his death.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_603	lexical	\N	\N	602	{"text": "What was in the letter we could never discover, but I could see as he held it that it was short and written in a scrawling hand.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_604	lexical	\N	\N	603	{"text": "He had suffered for years from an enlarged spleen, but he now became rapidly worse, and towards the end of April we were informed that he was beyond all hope, and that he wished to make a last communication to us.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_605	lexical	\N	\N	604	{"text": "“When we entered his room he was propped up with pillows and breathing heavily.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_606	lexical	\N	\N	605	{"text": "He besought us to lock the door and to come upon either side of the bed.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_607	lexical	\N	\N	606	{"text": "Then, grasping our hands, he made a remarkable statement to us, in a voice which was broken as much by emotion as by pain.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_608	lexical	\N	\N	607	{"text": "I shall try and give it to you in his own very words.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_609	lexical	\N	\N	608	{"text": "“‘I have only one thing,’ he said, ‘which weighs upon my mind at this supreme moment.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_610	lexical	\N	\N	609	{"text": "It is my treatment of poor Morstan’s orphan.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_611	lexical	\N	\N	610	{"text": "The cursed greed which has been my besetting sin through life has withheld from her the treasure, half at least of which should have been hers.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_612	lexical	\N	\N	611	{"text": "And yet I have made no use of it myself,—so blind and foolish a thing is avarice.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_613	lexical	\N	\N	612	{"text": "The mere feeling of possession has been so dear to me that I could not bear to share it with another.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_614	lexical	\N	\N	613	{"text": "See that chaplet dipped with pearls beside the quinine-bottle.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_615	lexical	\N	\N	614	{"text": "Even that I could not bear to part with, although I had got it out with the design of sending it to her.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_616	lexical	\N	\N	615	{"text": "You, my sons, will give her a fair share of the Agra treasure.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_617	lexical	\N	\N	616	{"text": "But send her nothing—not even the chaplet—until I am gone.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_618	lexical	\N	\N	617	{"text": "After all, men have been as bad as this and have recovered.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_619	lexical	\N	\N	618	{"text": "“‘I will tell you how Morstan died,’ he continued.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_620	lexical	\N	\N	619	{"text": "‘He had suffered for years from a weak heart, but he concealed it from every one.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_621	lexical	\N	\N	620	{"text": "I alone knew it.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_622	lexical	\N	\N	621	{"text": "When in India, he and I, through a remarkable chain of circumstances, came into possession of a considerable treasure.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_623	lexical	\N	\N	622	{"text": "I brought it over to England, and on the night of Morstan’s arrival he came straight over here to claim his share.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_624	lexical	\N	\N	623	{"text": "He walked over from the station, and was admitted by my faithful old Lal Chowdar, who is now dead.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_625	lexical	\N	\N	624	{"text": "Morstan and I had a difference of opinion as to the division of the treasure, and we came to heated words.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_626	lexical	\N	\N	625	{"text": "Morstan had sprung out of his chair in a paroxysm of anger, when he suddenly pressed his hand to his side, his face turned a dusky hue, and he fell backwards, cutting his head against the corner of the treasure-chest.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_627	lexical	\N	\N	626	{"text": "When I stooped over him I found, to my horror, that he was dead.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_628	lexical	\N	\N	627	{"text": "“‘For a long time I sat half distracted, wondering what I should do.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_629	lexical	\N	\N	628	{"text": "My first impulse was, of course, to call for assistance; but I could not but recognise that there was every chance that I would be accused of his murder.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_630	lexical	\N	\N	629	{"text": "His death at the moment of a quarrel, and the gash in his head, would be black against me.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_631	lexical	\N	\N	630	{"text": "Again, an official inquiry could not be made without bringing out some facts about the treasure, which I was particularly anxious to keep secret.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_632	lexical	\N	\N	631	{"text": "He had told me that no soul upon earth knew where he had gone.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_633	lexical	\N	\N	632	{"text": "There seemed to be no necessity why any soul ever should know.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_634	lexical	\N	\N	633	{"text": "“‘I was still pondering over the matter, when, looking up, I saw my servant, Lal Chowdar, in the doorway.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_635	lexical	\N	\N	634	{"text": "He stole in and bolted the door behind him.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_636	lexical	\N	\N	635	{"text": "“Do not fear, Sahib,” he said.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_637	lexical	\N	\N	636	{"text": "“No one need know that you have killed him.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_638	lexical	\N	\N	637	{"text": "Let us hide him away, and who is the wiser?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_639	lexical	\N	\N	638	{"text": "“I did not kill him,” said I.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_640	lexical	\N	\N	639	{"text": "Lal Chowdar shook his head and smiled.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_641	lexical	\N	\N	640	{"text": "“I heard it all, Sahib,” said he.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_642	lexical	\N	\N	641	{"text": "“I heard you quarrel, and I heard the blow.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_643	lexical	\N	\N	642	{"text": "But my lips are sealed.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_644	lexical	\N	\N	643	{"text": "All are asleep in the house.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_645	lexical	\N	\N	644	{"text": "Let us put him away together.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_646	lexical	\N	\N	645	{"text": "That was enough to decide me.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_647	lexical	\N	\N	646	{"text": "If my own servant could not believe my innocence, how could I hope to make it good before twelve foolish tradesmen in a jury-box?", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_749	lexical	\N	\N	748	{"text": "You surprise me!", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_648	lexical	\N	\N	647	{"text": "Lal Chowdar and I disposed of the body that night, and within a few days the London papers were full of the mysterious disappearance of Captain Morstan.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_649	lexical	\N	\N	648	{"text": "You will see from what I say that I can hardly be blamed in the matter.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_650	lexical	\N	\N	649	{"text": "My fault lies in the fact that we concealed not only the body, but also the treasure, and that I have clung to Morstan’s share as well as to my own.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_651	lexical	\N	\N	650	{"text": "I wish you, therefore, to make restitution.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_652	lexical	\N	\N	651	{"text": "Put your ears down to my mouth.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_653	lexical	\N	\N	652	{"text": "The treasure is hidden in—’", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_654	lexical	\N	\N	653	{"text": "“At this instant a horrible change came over his expression; his eyes stared wildly, his jaw dropped, and he yelled, in a voice which I can never forget, ‘Keep him out!", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_655	lexical	\N	\N	654	{"text": "For Christ’s sake keep him out!’", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_656	lexical	\N	\N	655	{"text": "We both stared round at the window behind us upon which his gaze was fixed.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_657	lexical	\N	\N	656	{"text": "A face was looking in at us out of the darkness.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_658	lexical	\N	\N	657	{"text": "We could see the whitening of the nose where it was pressed against the glass.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_659	lexical	\N	\N	658	{"text": "It was a bearded, hairy face, with wild cruel eyes and an expression of concentrated malevolence.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_660	lexical	\N	\N	659	{"text": "My brother and I rushed towards the window, but the man was gone.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_661	lexical	\N	\N	660	{"text": "When we returned to my father his head had dropped and his pulse had ceased to beat.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_662	lexical	\N	\N	661	{"text": "“We searched the garden that night, but found no sign of the intruder, save that just under the window a single footmark was visible in the flower-bed.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_663	lexical	\N	\N	662	{"text": "But for that one trace, we might have thought that our imaginations had conjured up that wild, fierce face.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_664	lexical	\N	\N	663	{"text": "We soon, however, had another and a more striking proof that there were secret agencies at work all round us.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_665	lexical	\N	\N	664	{"text": "The window of my father’s room was found open in the morning, his cupboards and boxes had been rifled, and upon his chest was fixed a torn piece of paper, with the words ‘The sign of the four’ scrawled across it.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_666	lexical	\N	\N	665	{"text": "What the phrase meant, or who our secret visitor may have been, we never knew.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_667	lexical	\N	\N	666	{"text": "As far as we can judge, none of my father’s property had been actually stolen, though everything had been turned out.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_668	lexical	\N	\N	667	{"text": "My brother and I naturally associated this peculiar incident with the fear which haunted my father during his life; but it is still a complete mystery to us.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_669	lexical	\N	\N	668	{"text": "The little man stopped to relight his hookah and puffed thoughtfully for a few moments.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_670	lexical	\N	\N	669	{"text": "We had all sat absorbed, listening to his extraordinary narrative.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_671	lexical	\N	\N	670	{"text": "At the short account of her father’s death Miss Morstan had turned deadly white, and for a moment I feared that she was about to faint.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_672	lexical	\N	\N	671	{"text": "She rallied however, on drinking a glass of water which I quietly poured out for her from a Venetian carafe upon the side-table.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_673	lexical	\N	\N	672	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes leaned back in his chair with an abstracted expression and the lids drawn low over his glittering eyes.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_674	lexical	\N	\N	673	{"text": "As I glanced at him I could not but think how on that very day he had complained bitterly of the commonplaceness of life.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_675	lexical	\N	\N	674	{"text": "Here at least was a problem which would tax his sagacity to the utmost.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_676	lexical	\N	\N	675	{"text": "Mr. Thaddeus Sholto looked from one to the other of us with an obvious pride at the effect which his story had produced, and then continued between the puffs of his overgrown pipe.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_677	lexical	\N	\N	676	{"text": "“My brother and I,” said he, “were, as you may imagine, much excited as to the treasure which my father had spoken of.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_678	lexical	\N	\N	677	{"text": "For weeks and for months we dug and delved in every part of the garden, without discovering its whereabouts.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_679	lexical	\N	\N	678	{"text": "It was maddening to think that the hiding-place was on his very lips at the moment that he died.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_680	lexical	\N	\N	679	{"text": "We could judge the splendour of the missing riches by the chaplet which he had taken out.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_681	lexical	\N	\N	680	{"text": "Over this chaplet my brother Bartholomew and I had some little discussion.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_682	lexical	\N	\N	681	{"text": "The pearls were evidently of great value, and he was averse to part with them, for, between friends, my brother was himself a little inclined to my father’s fault.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_683	lexical	\N	\N	682	{"text": "He thought, too, that if we parted with the chaplet it might give rise to gossip and finally bring us into trouble.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_684	lexical	\N	\N	683	{"text": "It was all that I could do to persuade him to let me find out Miss Morstan’s address and send her a detached pearl at fixed intervals, so that at least she might never feel destitute.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_685	lexical	\N	\N	684	{"text": "“It was a kindly thought,” said our companion, earnestly.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_686	lexical	\N	\N	685	{"text": "“It was extremely good of you.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_687	lexical	\N	\N	686	{"text": "The little man waved his hand deprecatingly.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_688	lexical	\N	\N	687	{"text": "“We were your trustees,” he said.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_689	lexical	\N	\N	688	{"text": "“That was the view which I took of it, though Brother Bartholomew could not altogether see it in that light.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_690	lexical	\N	\N	689	{"text": "We had plenty of money ourselves.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_691	lexical	\N	\N	690	{"text": "I desired no more.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_692	lexical	\N	\N	691	{"text": "Besides, it would have been such bad taste to have treated a young lady in so scurvy a fashion.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_693	lexical	\N	\N	692	{"text": "‘Le mauvais goût mène au crime.’", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_694	lexical	\N	\N	693	{"text": "The French have a very neat way of putting these things.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_695	lexical	\N	\N	694	{"text": "Our difference of opinion on this subject went so far that I thought it best to set up rooms for myself: so I left Pondicherry Lodge, taking the old khitmutgar and Williams with me.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_696	lexical	\N	\N	695	{"text": "Yesterday, however, I learn that an event of extreme importance has occurred.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_697	lexical	\N	\N	696	{"text": "The treasure has been discovered.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_698	lexical	\N	\N	697	{"text": "I instantly communicated with Miss Morstan, and it only remains for us to drive out to Norwood and demand our share.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_699	lexical	\N	\N	698	{"text": "I explained my views last night to Brother Bartholomew: so we shall be expected, if not welcome, visitors.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_700	lexical	\N	\N	699	{"text": "Mr. Thaddeus Sholto ceased, and sat twitching on his luxurious settee.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_701	lexical	\N	\N	700	{"text": "We all remained silent, with our thoughts upon the new development which the mysterious business had taken.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_702	lexical	\N	\N	701	{"text": "Holmes was the first to spring to his feet.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_703	lexical	\N	\N	702	{"text": "“You have done well, sir, from first to last,” said he.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_704	lexical	\N	\N	703	{"text": "“It is possible that we may be able to make you some small return by throwing some light upon that which is still dark to you.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_705	lexical	\N	\N	704	{"text": "But, as Miss Morstan remarked just now, it is late, and we had best put the matter through without delay.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_706	lexical	\N	\N	705	{"text": "Our new acquaintance very deliberately coiled up the tube of his hookah, and produced from behind a curtain a very long befrogged topcoat with Astrakhan collar and cuffs.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_707	lexical	\N	\N	706	{"text": "This he buttoned tightly up, in spite of the extreme closeness of the night, and finished his attire by putting on a rabbit-skin cap with hanging lappets which covered the ears, so that no part of him was visible save his mobile and peaky face.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_708	lexical	\N	\N	707	{"text": "“My health is somewhat fragile,” he remarked, as he led the way down the passage.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_709	lexical	\N	\N	708	{"text": "“I am compelled to be a valetudinarian.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_710	lexical	\N	\N	709	{"text": "Our cab was awaiting us outside, and our programme was evidently prearranged, for the driver started off at once at a rapid pace.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_711	lexical	\N	\N	710	{"text": "Thaddeus Sholto talked incessantly, in a voice which rose high above the rattle of the wheels.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_712	lexical	\N	\N	711	{"text": "“Bartholomew is a clever fellow,” said he.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_713	lexical	\N	\N	712	{"text": "“How do you think he found out where the treasure was?", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_714	lexical	\N	\N	713	{"text": "He had come to the conclusion that it was somewhere indoors: so he worked out all the cubic space of the house, and made measurements everywhere, so that not one inch should be unaccounted for.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_828	lexical	\N	\N	827	{"text": "“There is something amiss with Bartholomew!”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_715	lexical	\N	\N	714	{"text": "Among other things, he found that the height of the building was seventy-four feet, but on adding together the heights of all the separate rooms, and making every allowance for the space between, which he ascertained by borings, he could not bring the total to more than seventy feet.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_716	lexical	\N	\N	715	{"text": "There were four feet unaccounted for.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_717	lexical	\N	\N	716	{"text": "These could only be at the top of the building.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_718	lexical	\N	\N	717	{"text": "He knocked a hole, therefore, in the lath-and-plaster ceiling of the highest room, and there, sure enough, he came upon another little garret above it, which had been sealed up and was known to no one.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_719	lexical	\N	\N	718	{"text": "In the centre stood the treasure-chest, resting upon two rafters.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_720	lexical	\N	\N	719	{"text": "He lowered it through the hole, and there it lies.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_721	lexical	\N	\N	720	{"text": "He computes the value of the jewels at not less than half a million sterling.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_722	lexical	\N	\N	721	{"text": "At the mention of this gigantic sum we all stared at one another open-eyed.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_723	lexical	\N	\N	722	{"text": "Miss Morstan, could we secure her rights, would change from a needy governess to the richest heiress in England.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_724	lexical	\N	\N	723	{"text": "Surely it was the place of a loyal friend to rejoice at such news; yet I am ashamed to say that selfishness took me by the soul, and that my heart turned as heavy as lead within me.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_725	lexical	\N	\N	724	{"text": "I stammered out some few halting words of congratulation, and then sat downcast, with my head drooped, deaf to the babble of our new acquaintance.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_726	lexical	\N	\N	725	{"text": "He was clearly a confirmed hypochondriac, and I was dreamily conscious that he was pouring forth interminable trains of symptoms, and imploring information as to the composition and action of innumerable quack nostrums, some of which he bore about in a leather case in his pocket.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_727	lexical	\N	\N	726	{"text": "I trust that he may not remember any of the answers which I gave him that night.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_728	lexical	\N	\N	727	{"text": "Holmes declares that he overheard me caution him against the great danger of taking more than two drops of castor oil, while I recommended strychnine in large doses as a sedative.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_729	lexical	\N	\N	728	{"text": "However that may be, I was certainly relieved when our cab pulled up with a jerk and the coachman sprang down to open the door.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_730	lexical	\N	\N	729	{"text": "“This, Miss Morstan, is Pondicherry Lodge,” said Mr. Thaddeus Sholto, as he handed her out.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_731	lexical	\N	\N	730	{"text": "Chapter V The Tragedy of Pondicherry Lodge", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_732	lexical	\N	\N	731	{"text": "It was nearly eleven o’clock when we reached this final stage of our night’s adventures.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_733	lexical	\N	\N	732	{"text": "We had left the damp fog of the great city behind us, and the night was fairly fine.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_734	lexical	\N	\N	733	{"text": "A warm wind blew from the westward, and heavy clouds moved slowly across the sky, with half a moon peeping occasionally through the rifts.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_735	lexical	\N	\N	734	{"text": "It was clear enough to see for some distance, but Thaddeus Sholto took down one of the side-lamps from the carriage to give us a better light upon our way.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_736	lexical	\N	\N	735	{"text": "Pondicherry Lodge stood in its own grounds, and was girt round with a very high stone wall topped with broken glass.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_737	lexical	\N	\N	736	{"text": "A single narrow iron-clamped door formed the only means of entrance.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_738	lexical	\N	\N	737	{"text": "On this our guide knocked with a peculiar postman-like rat-tat.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_739	lexical	\N	\N	738	{"text": "“Who is there?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_740	lexical	\N	\N	739	{"text": "cried a gruff voice from within.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_741	lexical	\N	\N	740	{"text": "“It is I, McMurdo.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_742	lexical	\N	\N	741	{"text": "You surely know my knock by this time.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_743	lexical	\N	\N	742	{"text": "There was a grumbling sound and a clanking and jarring of keys.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_744	lexical	\N	\N	743	{"text": "The door swung heavily back, and a short, deep-chested man stood in the opening, with the yellow light of the lantern shining upon his protruded face and twinkling distrustful eyes.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_745	lexical	\N	\N	744	{"text": "“That you, Mr. Thaddeus?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_746	lexical	\N	\N	745	{"text": "But who are the others?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_747	lexical	\N	\N	746	{"text": "I had no orders about them from the master.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_748	lexical	\N	\N	747	{"text": "“No, McMurdo?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_750	lexical	\N	\N	749	{"text": "I told my brother last night that I should bring some friends.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_751	lexical	\N	\N	750	{"text": "“He ain’t been out o’ his room to-day, Mr. Thaddeus, and I have no orders.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_752	lexical	\N	\N	751	{"text": "You know very well that I must stick to regulations.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_753	lexical	\N	\N	752	{"text": "I can let you in, but your friends must just stop where they are.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_754	lexical	\N	\N	753	{"text": "This was an unexpected obstacle.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_755	lexical	\N	\N	754	{"text": "Thaddeus Sholto looked about him in a perplexed and helpless manner.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_756	lexical	\N	\N	755	{"text": "“This is too bad of you, McMurdo!”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_757	lexical	\N	\N	756	{"text": "he said.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_758	lexical	\N	\N	757	{"text": "“If I guarantee them, that is enough for you.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_759	lexical	\N	\N	758	{"text": "There is the young lady, too.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_760	lexical	\N	\N	759	{"text": "She cannot wait on the public road at this hour.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_761	lexical	\N	\N	760	{"text": "“Very sorry, Mr. Thaddeus,” said the porter, inexorably.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_762	lexical	\N	\N	761	{"text": "“Folk may be friends o’ yours, and yet no friends o’ the master’s.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_763	lexical	\N	\N	762	{"text": "He pays me well to do my duty, and my duty I’ll do.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_764	lexical	\N	\N	763	{"text": "I don’t know none o’ your friends.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_765	lexical	\N	\N	764	{"text": "“Oh, yes you do, McMurdo,” cried Sherlock Holmes, genially.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_766	lexical	\N	\N	765	{"text": "“I don’t think you can have forgotten me.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_767	lexical	\N	\N	766	{"text": "Don’t you remember the amateur who fought three rounds with you at Alison’s rooms on the night of your benefit four years back?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_768	lexical	\N	\N	767	{"text": "“Not Mr. Sherlock Holmes!”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_769	lexical	\N	\N	768	{"text": "roared the prize-fighter.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_770	lexical	\N	\N	769	{"text": "“God’s truth!", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_771	lexical	\N	\N	770	{"text": "how could I have mistook you?", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_772	lexical	\N	\N	771	{"text": "If instead o’ standin’ there so quiet you had just stepped up and given me that cross-hit of yours under the jaw, I’d ha’ known you without a question.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_773	lexical	\N	\N	772	{"text": "Ah, you’re one that has wasted your gifts, you have!", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_774	lexical	\N	\N	773	{"text": "You might have aimed high, if you had joined the fancy.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_775	lexical	\N	\N	774	{"text": "“You see, Watson, if all else fails me I have still one of the scientific professions open to me,” said Holmes, laughing.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_776	lexical	\N	\N	775	{"text": "“Our friend won’t keep us out in the cold now, I am sure.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_777	lexical	\N	\N	776	{"text": "“In you come, sir, in you come,—you and your friends,” he answered.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_778	lexical	\N	\N	777	{"text": "“Very sorry, Mr. Thaddeus, but orders are very strict.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_779	lexical	\N	\N	778	{"text": "Had to be certain of your friends before I let them in.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_780	lexical	\N	\N	779	{"text": "Inside, a gravel path wound through desolate grounds to a huge clump of a house, square and prosaic, all plunged in shadow save where a moonbeam struck one corner and glimmered in a garret window.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_781	lexical	\N	\N	780	{"text": "The vast size of the building, with its gloom and its deathly silence, struck a chill to the heart.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_782	lexical	\N	\N	781	{"text": "Even Thaddeus Sholto seemed ill at ease, and the lantern quivered and rattled in his hand.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_783	lexical	\N	\N	782	{"text": "“I cannot understand it,” he said.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_784	lexical	\N	\N	783	{"text": "“There must be some mistake.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_785	lexical	\N	\N	784	{"text": "I distinctly told Bartholomew that we should be here, and yet there is no light in his window.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_786	lexical	\N	\N	785	{"text": "I do not know what to make of it.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_787	lexical	\N	\N	786	{"text": "“Does he always guard the premises in this way?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_788	lexical	\N	\N	787	{"text": "asked Holmes.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_789	lexical	\N	\N	788	{"text": "“Yes; he has followed my father’s custom.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_790	lexical	\N	\N	789	{"text": "He was the favourite son, you know, and I sometimes think that my father may have told him more than he ever told me.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_791	lexical	\N	\N	790	{"text": "That is Bartholomew’s window up there where the moonshine strikes.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_792	lexical	\N	\N	791	{"text": "It is quite bright, but there is no light from within, I think.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_793	lexical	\N	\N	792	{"text": "“None,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_794	lexical	\N	\N	793	{"text": "“But I see the glint of a light in that little window beside the door.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_795	lexical	\N	\N	794	{"text": "“Ah, that is the housekeeper’s room.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_796	lexical	\N	\N	795	{"text": "That is where old Mrs. Bernstone sits.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_797	lexical	\N	\N	796	{"text": "She can tell us all about it.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_798	lexical	\N	\N	797	{"text": "But perhaps you would not mind waiting here for a minute or two, for if we all go in together and she has no word of our coming she may be alarmed.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_799	lexical	\N	\N	798	{"text": "But hush!", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_800	lexical	\N	\N	799	{"text": "what is that?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_801	lexical	\N	\N	800	{"text": "He held up the lantern, and his hand shook until the circles of light flickered and wavered all round us.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_802	lexical	\N	\N	801	{"text": "Miss Morstan seized my wrist, and we all stood with thumping hearts, straining our ears.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_803	lexical	\N	\N	802	{"text": "From the great black house there sounded through the silent night the saddest and most pitiful of sounds,—the shrill, broken whimpering of a frightened woman.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_804	lexical	\N	\N	803	{"text": "“It is Mrs. Bernstone,” said Sholto.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_805	lexical	\N	\N	804	{"text": "“She is the only woman in the house.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_806	lexical	\N	\N	805	{"text": "Wait here.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_807	lexical	\N	\N	806	{"text": "I shall be back in a moment.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_808	lexical	\N	\N	807	{"text": "He hurried for the door, and knocked in his peculiar way.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_809	lexical	\N	\N	808	{"text": "We could see a tall old woman admit him, and sway with pleasure at the very sight of him.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_810	lexical	\N	\N	809	{"text": "“Oh, Mr. Thaddeus, sir, I am so glad you have come!", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_811	lexical	\N	\N	810	{"text": "I am so glad you have come, Mr. Thaddeus, sir!”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_812	lexical	\N	\N	811	{"text": "We heard her reiterated rejoicings until the door was closed and her voice died away into a muffled monotone.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_813	lexical	\N	\N	812	{"text": "Our guide had left us the lantern.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_814	lexical	\N	\N	813	{"text": "Holmes swung it slowly round, and peered keenly at the house, and at the great rubbish-heaps which cumbered the grounds.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_815	lexical	\N	\N	814	{"text": "Miss Morstan and I stood together, and her hand was in mine.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_816	lexical	\N	\N	815	{"text": "A wondrous subtle thing is love, for here were we two who had never seen each other before that day, between whom no word or even look of affection had ever passed, and yet now in an hour of trouble our hands instinctively sought for each other.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_817	lexical	\N	\N	816	{"text": "I have marvelled at it since, but at the time it seemed the most natural thing that I should go out to her so, and, as she has often told me, there was in her also the instinct to turn to me for comfort and protection.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_818	lexical	\N	\N	817	{"text": "So we stood hand in hand, like two children, and there was peace in our hearts for all the dark things that surrounded us.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_819	lexical	\N	\N	818	{"text": "“What a strange place!”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_820	lexical	\N	\N	819	{"text": "she said, looking round.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_821	lexical	\N	\N	820	{"text": "“It looks as though all the moles in England had been let loose in it.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_822	lexical	\N	\N	821	{"text": "I have seen something of the sort on the side of a hill near Ballarat, where the prospectors had been at work.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_823	lexical	\N	\N	822	{"text": "“And from the same cause,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_824	lexical	\N	\N	823	{"text": "“These are the traces of the treasure-seekers.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_825	lexical	\N	\N	824	{"text": "You must remember that they were six years looking for it.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_826	lexical	\N	\N	825	{"text": "No wonder that the grounds look like a gravel-pit.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_827	lexical	\N	\N	826	{"text": "At that moment the door of the house burst open, and Thaddeus Sholto came running out, with his hands thrown forward and terror in his eyes.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_831	lexical	\N	\N	830	{"text": "My nerves cannot stand it.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_832	lexical	\N	\N	831	{"text": "He was, indeed, half blubbering with fear, and his twitching feeble face peeping out from the great Astrakhan collar had the helpless appealing expression of a terrified child.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_833	lexical	\N	\N	832	{"text": "“Come into the house,” said Holmes, in his crisp, firm way.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_834	lexical	\N	\N	833	{"text": "“Yes, do!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_835	lexical	\N	\N	834	{"text": "pleaded Thaddeus Sholto.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_836	lexical	\N	\N	835	{"text": "“I really do not feel equal to giving directions.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_837	lexical	\N	\N	836	{"text": "We all followed him into the housekeeper’s room, which stood upon the left-hand side of the passage.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_838	lexical	\N	\N	837	{"text": "The old woman was pacing up and down with a scared look and restless picking fingers, but the sight of Miss Morstan appeared to have a soothing effect upon her.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_839	lexical	\N	\N	838	{"text": "“God bless your sweet calm face!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_840	lexical	\N	\N	839	{"text": "she cried, with an hysterical sob.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_841	lexical	\N	\N	840	{"text": "“It does me good to see you.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_842	lexical	\N	\N	841	{"text": "Oh, but I have been sorely tried this day!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_843	lexical	\N	\N	842	{"text": "Our companion patted her thin, work-worn hand, and murmured some few words of kindly womanly comfort which brought the colour back into the other’s bloodless cheeks.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_844	lexical	\N	\N	843	{"text": "“Master has locked himself in and will not answer me,” she explained.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_845	lexical	\N	\N	844	{"text": "“All day I have waited to hear from him, for he often likes to be alone; but an hour ago I feared that something was amiss, so I went up and peeped through the key-hole.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_846	lexical	\N	\N	845	{"text": "You must go up, Mr. Thaddeus,—you must go up and look for yourself.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_847	lexical	\N	\N	846	{"text": "I have seen Mr. Bartholomew Sholto in joy and in sorrow for ten long years, but I never saw him with such a face on him as that.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_848	lexical	\N	\N	847	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes took the lamp and led the way, for Thaddeus Sholto’s teeth were chattering in his head.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_849	lexical	\N	\N	848	{"text": "So shaken was he that I had to pass my hand under his arm as we went up the stairs, for his knees were trembling under him.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_850	lexical	\N	\N	849	{"text": "Twice as we ascended Holmes whipped his lens out of his pocket and carefully examined marks which appeared to me to be mere shapeless smudges of dust upon the cocoa-nut matting which served as a stair-carpet.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_851	lexical	\N	\N	850	{"text": "He walked slowly from step to step, holding the lamp, and shooting keen glances to right and left.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_852	lexical	\N	\N	851	{"text": "Miss Morstan had remained behind with the frightened housekeeper.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_853	lexical	\N	\N	852	{"text": "The third flight of stairs ended in a straight passage of some length, with a great picture in Indian tapestry upon the right of it and three doors upon the left.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_854	lexical	\N	\N	853	{"text": "Holmes advanced along it in the same slow and methodical way, while we kept close at his heels, with our long black shadows streaming backwards down the corridor.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_855	lexical	\N	\N	854	{"text": "The third door was that which we were seeking.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_856	lexical	\N	\N	855	{"text": "Holmes knocked without receiving any answer, and then tried to turn the handle and force it open.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_857	lexical	\N	\N	856	{"text": "It was locked on the inside, however, and by a broad and powerful bolt, as we could see when we set our lamp up against it.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_858	lexical	\N	\N	857	{"text": "The key being turned, however, the hole was not entirely closed.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_859	lexical	\N	\N	858	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes bent down to it, and instantly rose again with a sharp intaking of the breath.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_860	lexical	\N	\N	859	{"text": "“There is something devilish in this, Watson,” said he, more moved than I had ever before seen him.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_861	lexical	\N	\N	860	{"text": "“What do you make of it?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_862	lexical	\N	\N	861	{"text": "I stooped to the hole, and recoiled in horror.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_863	lexical	\N	\N	862	{"text": "Moonlight was streaming into the room, and it was bright with a vague and shifty radiance.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_864	lexical	\N	\N	863	{"text": "Looking straight at me, and suspended, as it were, in the air, for all beneath was in shadow, there hung a face,—the very face of our companion Thaddeus.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_865	lexical	\N	\N	864	{"text": "There was the same high, shining head, the same circular bristle of red hair, the same bloodless countenance.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_866	lexical	\N	\N	865	{"text": "The features were set, however, in a horrible smile, a fixed and unnatural grin, which in that still and moonlit room was more jarring to the nerves than any scowl or contortion.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_867	lexical	\N	\N	866	{"text": "So like was the face to that of our little friend that I looked round at him to make sure that he was indeed with us.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_868	lexical	\N	\N	867	{"text": "Then I recalled to mind that he had mentioned to us that his brother and he were twins.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_869	lexical	\N	\N	868	{"text": "“This is terrible!”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_870	lexical	\N	\N	869	{"text": "I said to Holmes.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_871	lexical	\N	\N	870	{"text": "“What is to be done?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_872	lexical	\N	\N	871	{"text": "“The door must come down,” he answered, and, springing against it, he put all his weight upon the lock.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_873	lexical	\N	\N	872	{"text": "It creaked and groaned, but did not yield.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_874	lexical	\N	\N	873	{"text": "Together we flung ourselves upon it once more, and this time it gave way with a sudden snap, and we found ourselves within Bartholomew Sholto’s chamber.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_875	lexical	\N	\N	874	{"text": "It appeared to have been fitted up as a chemical laboratory.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_876	lexical	\N	\N	875	{"text": "A double line of glass-stoppered bottles was drawn up upon the wall opposite the door, and the table was littered over with Bunsen burners, test-tubes, and retorts.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_877	lexical	\N	\N	876	{"text": "In the corners stood carboys of acid in wicker baskets.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_878	lexical	\N	\N	877	{"text": "One of these appeared to leak or to have been broken, for a stream of dark-coloured liquid had trickled out from it, and the air was heavy with a peculiarly pungent, tar-like odour.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_879	lexical	\N	\N	878	{"text": "A set of steps stood at one side of the room, in the midst of a litter of lath and plaster, and above them there was an opening in the ceiling large enough for a man to pass through.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_880	lexical	\N	\N	879	{"text": "At the foot of the steps a long coil of rope was thrown carelessly together.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_881	lexical	\N	\N	880	{"text": "By the table, in a wooden arm-chair, the master of the house was seated all in a heap, with his head sunk upon his left shoulder, and that ghastly, inscrutable smile upon his face.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_882	lexical	\N	\N	881	{"text": "He was stiff and cold, and had clearly been dead many hours.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_883	lexical	\N	\N	882	{"text": "It seemed to me that not only his features but all his limbs were twisted and turned in the most fantastic fashion.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_884	lexical	\N	\N	883	{"text": "By his hand upon the table there lay a peculiar instrument,—a brown, close-grained stick, with a stone head like a hammer, rudely lashed on with coarse twine.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_885	lexical	\N	\N	884	{"text": "Beside it was a torn sheet of note-paper with some words scrawled upon it.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_886	lexical	\N	\N	885	{"text": "Holmes glanced at it, and then handed it to me.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_887	lexical	\N	\N	886	{"text": "“You see,” he said, with a significant raising of the eyebrows.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_888	lexical	\N	\N	887	{"text": "In the light of the lantern I read, with a thrill of horror, “The sign of the four.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_889	lexical	\N	\N	888	{"text": "“In God’s name, what does it all mean?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_890	lexical	\N	\N	889	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_891	lexical	\N	\N	890	{"text": "“It means murder,” said he, stooping over the dead man.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_892	lexical	\N	\N	891	{"text": "“Ah, I expected it.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_893	lexical	\N	\N	892	{"text": "Look here!”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_894	lexical	\N	\N	893	{"text": "He pointed to what looked like a long, dark thorn stuck in the skin just above the ear.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_895	lexical	\N	\N	894	{"text": "“It looks like a thorn,” said I.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_896	lexical	\N	\N	895	{"text": "“It is a thorn.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_897	lexical	\N	\N	896	{"text": "You may pick it out.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_898	lexical	\N	\N	897	{"text": "But be careful, for it is poisoned.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_899	lexical	\N	\N	898	{"text": "I took it up between my finger and thumb.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_900	lexical	\N	\N	899	{"text": "It came away from the skin so readily that hardly any mark was left behind.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_901	lexical	\N	\N	900	{"text": "One tiny speck of blood showed where the puncture had been.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_902	lexical	\N	\N	901	{"text": "“This is all an insoluble mystery to me,” said I.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_75	section	\N	Section 75	74	{"wordCount": 648}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_907	lexical	\N	\N	906	{"text": "He was still standing in the doorway, the very picture of terror, wringing his hands and moaning to himself.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_908	lexical	\N	\N	907	{"text": "Suddenly, however, he broke out into a sharp, querulous cry.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_909	lexical	\N	\N	908	{"text": "“The treasure is gone!”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_910	lexical	\N	\N	909	{"text": "he said.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_911	lexical	\N	\N	910	{"text": "“They have robbed him of the treasure!", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_912	lexical	\N	\N	911	{"text": "There is the hole through which we lowered it.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_913	lexical	\N	\N	912	{"text": "I helped him to do it!", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_914	lexical	\N	\N	913	{"text": "I was the last person who saw him!", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_915	lexical	\N	\N	914	{"text": "I left him here last night, and I heard him lock the door as I came downstairs.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_916	lexical	\N	\N	915	{"text": "“What time was that?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_917	lexical	\N	\N	916	{"text": "“It was ten o’clock.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_918	lexical	\N	\N	917	{"text": "And now he is dead, and the police will be called in, and I shall be suspected of having had a hand in it.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_919	lexical	\N	\N	918	{"text": "Oh, yes, I am sure I shall.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_920	lexical	\N	\N	919	{"text": "But you don’t think so, gentlemen?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_921	lexical	\N	\N	920	{"text": "Surely you don’t think that it was I?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_922	lexical	\N	\N	921	{"text": "Is it likely that I would have brought you here if it were I?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_923	lexical	\N	\N	922	{"text": "Oh, dear!", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_924	lexical	\N	\N	923	{"text": "oh, dear!", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_925	lexical	\N	\N	924	{"text": "I know that I shall go mad!”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_926	lexical	\N	\N	925	{"text": "He jerked his arms and stamped his feet in a kind of convulsive frenzy.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_927	lexical	\N	\N	926	{"text": "“You have no reason for fear, Mr. Sholto,” said Holmes, kindly, putting his hand upon his shoulder.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_928	lexical	\N	\N	927	{"text": "“Take my advice, and drive down to the station to report this matter to the police.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_929	lexical	\N	\N	928	{"text": "Offer to assist them in every way.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_930	lexical	\N	\N	929	{"text": "We shall wait here until your return.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_931	lexical	\N	\N	930	{"text": "The little man obeyed in a half-stupefied fashion, and we heard him stumbling down the stairs in the dark.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_932	lexical	\N	\N	931	{"text": "Chapter VI Sherlock Holmes Gives a Demonstration", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_933	lexical	\N	\N	932	{"text": "“Now, Watson,” said Holmes, rubbing his hands, “we have half an hour to ourselves.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_934	lexical	\N	\N	933	{"text": "Let us make good use of it.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_935	lexical	\N	\N	934	{"text": "My case is, as I have told you, almost complete; but we must not err on the side of over-confidence.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_936	lexical	\N	\N	935	{"text": "Simple as the case seems now, there may be something deeper underlying it.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_937	lexical	\N	\N	936	{"text": "“Simple!”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_938	lexical	\N	\N	937	{"text": "I ejaculated.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_939	lexical	\N	\N	938	{"text": "“Surely,” said he, with something of the air of a clinical professor expounding to his class.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_940	lexical	\N	\N	939	{"text": "“Just sit in the corner there, that your footprints may not complicate matters.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_941	lexical	\N	\N	940	{"text": "Now to work!", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_942	lexical	\N	\N	941	{"text": "In the first place, how did these folk come, and how did they go?", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_943	lexical	\N	\N	942	{"text": "The door has not been opened since last night.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_944	lexical	\N	\N	943	{"text": "How of the window?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_945	lexical	\N	\N	944	{"text": "He carried the lamp across to it, muttering his observations aloud the while, but addressing them to himself rather than to me.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_946	lexical	\N	\N	945	{"text": "“Window is snibbed on the inner side.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_947	lexical	\N	\N	946	{"text": "Framework is solid.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_948	lexical	\N	\N	947	{"text": "No hinges at the side.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_949	lexical	\N	\N	948	{"text": "Let us open it.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_950	lexical	\N	\N	949	{"text": "No water-pipe near.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_951	lexical	\N	\N	950	{"text": "Roof quite out of reach.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_952	lexical	\N	\N	951	{"text": "Yet a man has mounted by the window.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_953	lexical	\N	\N	952	{"text": "It rained a little last night.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_954	lexical	\N	\N	953	{"text": "Here is the print of a foot in mould upon the sill.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_955	lexical	\N	\N	954	{"text": "And here is a circular muddy mark, and here again upon the floor, and here again by the table.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_956	lexical	\N	\N	955	{"text": "See here, Watson!", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_957	lexical	\N	\N	956	{"text": "This is really a very pretty demonstration.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_958	lexical	\N	\N	957	{"text": "I looked at the round, well-defined muddy discs.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_959	lexical	\N	\N	958	{"text": "“This is not a footmark,” said I.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_960	lexical	\N	\N	959	{"text": "“It is something much more valuable to us.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_961	lexical	\N	\N	960	{"text": "It is the impression of a wooden stump.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_962	lexical	\N	\N	961	{"text": "You see here on the sill is the boot-mark, a heavy boot with the broad metal heel, and beside it is the mark of the timber-toe.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_963	lexical	\N	\N	962	{"text": "“It is the wooden-legged man.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_964	lexical	\N	\N	963	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_965	lexical	\N	\N	964	{"text": "But there has been some one else,—a very able and efficient ally.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_966	lexical	\N	\N	965	{"text": "Could you scale that wall, doctor?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_967	lexical	\N	\N	966	{"text": "I looked out of the open window.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_968	lexical	\N	\N	967	{"text": "The moon still shone brightly on that angle of the house.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_969	lexical	\N	\N	968	{"text": "We were a good sixty feet from the ground, and, look where I would, I could see no foothold, nor as much as a crevice in the brick-work.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_970	lexical	\N	\N	969	{"text": "“It is absolutely impossible,” I answered.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_971	lexical	\N	\N	970	{"text": "“Without aid it is so.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_972	lexical	\N	\N	971	{"text": "But suppose you had a friend up here who lowered you this good stout rope which I see in the corner, securing one end of it to this great hook in the wall.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_973	lexical	\N	\N	972	{"text": "Then, I think, if you were an active man, You might swarm up, wooden leg and all.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_974	lexical	\N	\N	973	{"text": "You would depart, of course, in the same fashion, and your ally would draw up the rope, untie it from the hook, shut the window, snib it on the inside, and get away in the way that he originally came.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_975	lexical	\N	\N	974	{"text": "As a minor point it may be noted,” he continued, fingering the rope, “that our wooden-legged friend, though a fair climber, was not a professional sailor.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_976	lexical	\N	\N	975	{"text": "His hands were far from horny.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_977	lexical	\N	\N	976	{"text": "My lens discloses more than one blood-mark, especially towards the end of the rope, from which I gather that he slipped down with such velocity that he took the skin off his hand.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_978	lexical	\N	\N	977	{"text": "“This is all very well,” said I, “but the thing becomes more unintelligible than ever.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_979	lexical	\N	\N	978	{"text": "How about this mysterious ally?", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_980	lexical	\N	\N	979	{"text": "How came he into the room?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_981	lexical	\N	\N	980	{"text": "“Yes, the ally!”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_982	lexical	\N	\N	981	{"text": "repeated Holmes, pensively.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_983	lexical	\N	\N	982	{"text": "“There are features of interest about this ally.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_984	lexical	\N	\N	983	{"text": "He lifts the case from the regions of the commonplace.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_76	section	\N	Section 76	75	{"wordCount": 645}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_985	lexical	\N	\N	984	{"text": "I fancy that this ally breaks fresh ground in the annals of crime in this country,—though parallel cases suggest themselves from India, and, if my memory serves me, from Senegambia.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_986	lexical	\N	\N	985	{"text": "“How came he, then?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_987	lexical	\N	\N	986	{"text": "I reiterated.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_988	lexical	\N	\N	987	{"text": "“The door is locked, the window is inaccessible.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_989	lexical	\N	\N	988	{"text": "Was it through the chimney?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_990	lexical	\N	\N	989	{"text": "“The grate is much too small,” he answered.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_991	lexical	\N	\N	990	{"text": "“I had already considered that possibility.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_992	lexical	\N	\N	991	{"text": "“How then?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_993	lexical	\N	\N	992	{"text": "I persisted.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_994	lexical	\N	\N	993	{"text": "“You will not apply my precept,” he said, shaking his head.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_995	lexical	\N	\N	994	{"text": "“How often have I said to you that when you have eliminated the impossible whatever remains, _however improbable_, must be the truth?", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_996	lexical	\N	\N	995	{"text": "We know that he did not come through the door, the window, or the chimney.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_997	lexical	\N	\N	996	{"text": "We also know that he could not have been concealed in the room, as there is no concealment possible.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_998	lexical	\N	\N	997	{"text": "Whence, then, did he come?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_999	lexical	\N	\N	998	{"text": "“He came through the hole in the roof,” I cried.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1000	lexical	\N	\N	999	{"text": "“Of course he did.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1001	lexical	\N	\N	1000	{"text": "He must have done so.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1002	lexical	\N	\N	1001	{"text": "If you will have the kindness to hold the lamp for me, we shall now extend our researches to the room above,—the secret room in which the treasure was found.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1003	lexical	\N	\N	1002	{"text": "He mounted the steps, and, seizing a rafter with either hand, he swung himself up into the garret.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1004	lexical	\N	\N	1003	{"text": "Then, lying on his face, he reached down for the lamp and held it while I followed him.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1005	lexical	\N	\N	1004	{"text": "The chamber in which we found ourselves was about ten feet one way and six the other.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1006	lexical	\N	\N	1005	{"text": "The floor was formed by the rafters, with thin lath-and-plaster between, so that in walking one had to step from beam to beam.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1007	lexical	\N	\N	1006	{"text": "The roof ran up to an apex, and was evidently the inner shell of the true roof of the house.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1008	lexical	\N	\N	1007	{"text": "There was no furniture of any sort, and the accumulated dust of years lay thick upon the floor.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1009	lexical	\N	\N	1008	{"text": "“Here you are, you see,” said Sherlock Holmes, putting his hand against the sloping wall.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1010	lexical	\N	\N	1009	{"text": "“This is a trap-door which leads out on to the roof.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1011	lexical	\N	\N	1010	{"text": "I can press it back, and here is the roof itself, sloping at a gentle angle.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1012	lexical	\N	\N	1011	{"text": "This, then, is the way by which Number One entered.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1013	lexical	\N	\N	1012	{"text": "Let us see if we can find any other traces of his individuality.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1014	lexical	\N	\N	1013	{"text": "He held down the lamp to the floor, and as he did so I saw for the second time that night a startled, surprised look come over his face.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1015	lexical	\N	\N	1014	{"text": "For myself, as I followed his gaze my skin was cold under my clothes.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1016	lexical	\N	\N	1015	{"text": "The floor was covered thickly with the prints of a naked foot,—clear, well defined, perfectly formed, but scarce half the size of those of an ordinary man.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1017	lexical	\N	\N	1016	{"text": "“Holmes,” I said, in a whisper, “a child has done the horrid thing.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1018	lexical	\N	\N	1017	{"text": "He had recovered his self-possession in an instant.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1019	lexical	\N	\N	1018	{"text": "“I was staggered for the moment,” he said, “but the thing is quite natural.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1020	lexical	\N	\N	1019	{"text": "My memory failed me, or I should have been able to foretell it.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1021	lexical	\N	\N	1020	{"text": "There is nothing more to be learned here.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1022	lexical	\N	\N	1021	{"text": "Let us go down.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1023	lexical	\N	\N	1022	{"text": "“What is your theory, then, as to those footmarks?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1024	lexical	\N	\N	1023	{"text": "I asked, eagerly, when we had regained the lower room once more.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1025	lexical	\N	\N	1024	{"text": "“My dear Watson, try a little analysis yourself,” said he, with a touch of impatience.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1026	lexical	\N	\N	1025	{"text": "“You know my methods.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1027	lexical	\N	\N	1026	{"text": "Apply them, and it will be instructive to compare results.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1028	lexical	\N	\N	1027	{"text": "“I cannot conceive anything which will cover the facts,” I answered.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1029	lexical	\N	\N	1028	{"text": "“It will be clear enough to you soon,” he said, in an off-hand way.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1030	lexical	\N	\N	1029	{"text": "“I think that there is nothing else of importance here, but I will look.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1031	lexical	\N	\N	1030	{"text": "He whipped out his lens and a tape measure, and hurried about the room on his knees, measuring, comparing, examining, with his long thin nose only a few inches from the planks, and his beady eyes gleaming and deep-set like those of a bird.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1032	lexical	\N	\N	1031	{"text": "So swift, silent, and furtive were his movements, like those of a trained blood-hound picking out a scent, that I could not but think what a terrible criminal he would have made had he turned his energy and sagacity against the law, instead of exerting them in its defence.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1033	lexical	\N	\N	1032	{"text": "As he hunted about, he kept muttering to himself, and finally he broke out into a loud crow of delight.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1034	lexical	\N	\N	1033	{"text": "“We are certainly in luck,” said he.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1035	lexical	\N	\N	1034	{"text": "“We ought to have very little trouble now.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1036	lexical	\N	\N	1035	{"text": "Number One has had the misfortune to tread in the creosote.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1037	lexical	\N	\N	1036	{"text": "You can see the outline of the edge of his small foot here at the side of this evil-smelling mess.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1038	lexical	\N	\N	1037	{"text": "The carboy has been cracked, You see, and the stuff has leaked out.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1039	lexical	\N	\N	1038	{"text": "“What then?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1040	lexical	\N	\N	1039	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1041	lexical	\N	\N	1040	{"text": "“Why, we have got him, that’s all,” said he.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1042	lexical	\N	\N	1041	{"text": "“I know a dog that would follow that scent to the world’s end.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1043	lexical	\N	\N	1042	{"text": "If a pack can track a trailed herring across a shire, how far can a specially-trained hound follow so pungent a smell as this?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1044	lexical	\N	\N	1043	{"text": "It sounds like a sum in the rule of three.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1045	lexical	\N	\N	1044	{"text": "The answer should give us the—But halloa!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1046	lexical	\N	\N	1045	{"text": "here are the accredited representatives of the law.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1047	lexical	\N	\N	1046	{"text": "Heavy steps and the clamour of loud voices were audible from below, and the hall door shut with a loud crash.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1048	lexical	\N	\N	1047	{"text": "“Before they come,” said Holmes, “just put your hand here on this poor fellow’s arm, and here on his leg.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1049	lexical	\N	\N	1048	{"text": "What do you feel?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1050	lexical	\N	\N	1049	{"text": "“The muscles are as hard as a board,” I answered.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1051	lexical	\N	\N	1050	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1052	lexical	\N	\N	1051	{"text": "They are in a state of extreme contraction, far exceeding the usual _rigor mortis_.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1053	lexical	\N	\N	1052	{"text": "Coupled with this distortion of the face, this Hippocratic smile, or ‘_risus sardonicus_,’ as the old writers called it, what conclusion would it suggest to your mind?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1054	lexical	\N	\N	1053	{"text": "“Death from some powerful vegetable alkaloid,” I answered,—“some strychnine-like substance which would produce tetanus.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1055	lexical	\N	\N	1054	{"text": "“That was the idea which occurred to me the instant I saw the drawn muscles of the face.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1056	lexical	\N	\N	1055	{"text": "On getting into the room I at once looked for the means by which the poison had entered the system.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1057	lexical	\N	\N	1056	{"text": "As you saw, I discovered a thorn which had been driven or shot with no great force into the scalp.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1058	lexical	\N	\N	1057	{"text": "You observe that the part struck was that which would be turned towards the hole in the ceiling if the man were erect in his chair.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1059	lexical	\N	\N	1058	{"text": "Now examine the thorn.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1060	lexical	\N	\N	1059	{"text": "I took it up gingerly and held it in the light of the lantern.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1061	lexical	\N	\N	1060	{"text": "It was long, sharp, and black, with a glazed look near the point as though some gummy substance had dried upon it.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1062	lexical	\N	\N	1061	{"text": "The blunt end had been trimmed and rounded off with a knife.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1063	lexical	\N	\N	1062	{"text": "“Is that an English thorn?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1064	lexical	\N	\N	1063	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1065	lexical	\N	\N	1064	{"text": "“No, it certainly is not.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1066	lexical	\N	\N	1065	{"text": "“With all these data you should be able to draw some just inference.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1067	lexical	\N	\N	1066	{"text": "But here are the regulars; so the auxiliary forces may beat a retreat.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1068	lexical	\N	\N	1067	{"text": "As he spoke, the steps which had been coming nearer sounded loudly on the passage, and a very stout, portly man in a grey suit strode heavily into the room.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1069	lexical	\N	\N	1068	{"text": "He was red-faced, burly and plethoric, with a pair of very small twinkling eyes which looked keenly out from between swollen and puffy pouches.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1070	lexical	\N	\N	1069	{"text": "He was closely followed by an inspector in uniform, and by the still palpitating Thaddeus Sholto.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1071	lexical	\N	\N	1070	{"text": "“Here’s a business!”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1072	lexical	\N	\N	1071	{"text": "he cried, in a muffled, husky voice.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1073	lexical	\N	\N	1072	{"text": "“Here’s a pretty business!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1074	lexical	\N	\N	1073	{"text": "But who are all these?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1075	lexical	\N	\N	1074	{"text": "Why, the house seems to be as full as a rabbit-warren!”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1076	lexical	\N	\N	1075	{"text": "“I think you must recollect me, Mr. Athelney Jones,” said Holmes, quietly.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1077	lexical	\N	\N	1076	{"text": "“Why, of course I do!”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1078	lexical	\N	\N	1077	{"text": "he wheezed.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1079	lexical	\N	\N	1078	{"text": "“It’s Mr. Sherlock Holmes, the theorist.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1080	lexical	\N	\N	1079	{"text": "Remember you!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1081	lexical	\N	\N	1080	{"text": "I’ll never forget how you lectured us all on causes and inferences and effects in the Bishopgate jewel case.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1082	lexical	\N	\N	1081	{"text": "It’s true you set us on the right track; but you’ll own now that it was more by good luck than good guidance.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1083	lexical	\N	\N	1082	{"text": "“It was a piece of very simple reasoning.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1084	lexical	\N	\N	1083	{"text": "“Oh, come, now, come!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1085	lexical	\N	\N	1084	{"text": "Never be ashamed to own up.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1086	lexical	\N	\N	1085	{"text": "But what is all this?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1087	lexical	\N	\N	1086	{"text": "Bad business!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1088	lexical	\N	\N	1087	{"text": "Bad business!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1089	lexical	\N	\N	1088	{"text": "Stern facts here,—no room for theories.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1090	lexical	\N	\N	1089	{"text": "How lucky that I happened to be out at Norwood over another case!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1091	lexical	\N	\N	1090	{"text": "I was at the station when the message arrived.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1092	lexical	\N	\N	1091	{"text": "What d’you think the man died of?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1093	lexical	\N	\N	1092	{"text": "“Oh, this is hardly a case for me to theorise over,” said Holmes, dryly.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1094	lexical	\N	\N	1093	{"text": "“No, no.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1095	lexical	\N	\N	1094	{"text": "Still, we can’t deny that you hit the nail on the head sometimes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1096	lexical	\N	\N	1095	{"text": "Dear me!", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1097	lexical	\N	\N	1096	{"text": "Door locked, I understand.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1098	lexical	\N	\N	1097	{"text": "Jewels worth half a million missing.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1099	lexical	\N	\N	1098	{"text": "How was the window?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1100	lexical	\N	\N	1099	{"text": "“Fastened; but there are steps on the sill.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1101	lexical	\N	\N	1100	{"text": "“Well, well, if it was fastened the steps could have nothing to do with the matter.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1103	lexical	\N	\N	1102	{"text": "Man might have died in a fit; but then the jewels are missing.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1104	lexical	\N	\N	1103	{"text": "Ha!", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1105	lexical	\N	\N	1104	{"text": "I have a theory.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1106	lexical	\N	\N	1105	{"text": "—Just step outside, sergeant, and you, Mr. Sholto.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1107	lexical	\N	\N	1106	{"text": "—What do you think of this, Holmes?", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1108	lexical	\N	\N	1107	{"text": "Sholto was, on his own confession, with his brother last night.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1109	lexical	\N	\N	1108	{"text": "The brother died in a fit, on which Sholto walked off with the treasure.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1110	lexical	\N	\N	1109	{"text": "How’s that?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1111	lexical	\N	\N	1110	{"text": "on which Sholto walked off with the treasure. How’s that?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1112	lexical	\N	\N	1111	{"text": "“On which the dead man very considerately got up and locked the door on the inside.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1113	lexical	\N	\N	1112	{"text": "“Hum!", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1114	lexical	\N	\N	1113	{"text": "There’s a flaw there.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1115	lexical	\N	\N	1114	{"text": "Let us apply common sense to the matter.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1116	lexical	\N	\N	1115	{"text": "This Thaddeus Sholto _was_ with his brother; there _was_ a quarrel; so much we know.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1117	lexical	\N	\N	1116	{"text": "The brother is dead and the jewels are gone.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1118	lexical	\N	\N	1117	{"text": "So much also we know.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1119	lexical	\N	\N	1118	{"text": "No one saw the brother from the time Thaddeus left him.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1120	lexical	\N	\N	1119	{"text": "His bed had not been slept in.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1121	lexical	\N	\N	1120	{"text": "Thaddeus is evidently in a most disturbed state of mind.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1122	lexical	\N	\N	1121	{"text": "His appearance is—well, not attractive.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1123	lexical	\N	\N	1122	{"text": "You see that I am weaving my web round Thaddeus.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1124	lexical	\N	\N	1123	{"text": "The net begins to close upon him.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1125	lexical	\N	\N	1124	{"text": "“You are not quite in possession of the facts yet,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1126	lexical	\N	\N	1125	{"text": "“This splinter of wood, which I have every reason to believe to be poisoned, was in the man’s scalp where you still see the mark; this card, inscribed as you see it, was on the table; and beside it lay this rather curious stone-headed instrument.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1127	lexical	\N	\N	1126	{"text": "How does all that fit into your theory?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1128	lexical	\N	\N	1127	{"text": "“Confirms it in every respect,” said the fat detective, pompously.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1129	lexical	\N	\N	1128	{"text": "“House is full of Indian curiosities.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1130	lexical	\N	\N	1129	{"text": "Thaddeus brought this up, and if this splinter be poisonous Thaddeus may as well have made murderous use of it as any other man.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1131	lexical	\N	\N	1130	{"text": "The card is some hocus-pocus,—a blind, as like as not.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1132	lexical	\N	\N	1131	{"text": "The only question is, how did he depart?", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1133	lexical	\N	\N	1132	{"text": "Ah, of course, here is a hole in the roof.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1134	lexical	\N	\N	1133	{"text": "With great activity, considering his bulk, he sprang up the steps and squeezed through into the garret, and immediately afterwards we heard his exulting voice proclaiming that he had found the trap-door.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1135	lexical	\N	\N	1134	{"text": "“He can find something,” remarked Holmes, shrugging his shoulders.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1136	lexical	\N	\N	1135	{"text": "“He has occasional glimmerings of reason.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1137	lexical	\N	\N	1136	{"text": "_Il n’y a pas des sots si incommodes que ceux qui ont de l’esprit!_”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1138	lexical	\N	\N	1137	{"text": "“You see!”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1139	lexical	\N	\N	1138	{"text": "said Athelney Jones, reappearing down the steps again.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1140	lexical	\N	\N	1139	{"text": "“Facts are better than mere theories, after all.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1141	lexical	\N	\N	1140	{"text": "My view of the case is confirmed.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1142	lexical	\N	\N	1141	{"text": "There is a trap-door communicating with the roof, and it is partly open.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1143	lexical	\N	\N	1142	{"text": "“It was I who opened it.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1146	lexical	\N	\N	1145	{"text": "He seemed a little crestfallen at the discovery.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1147	lexical	\N	\N	1146	{"text": "“Well, whoever noticed it, it shows how our gentleman got away.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1148	lexical	\N	\N	1147	{"text": "Inspector!”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1149	lexical	\N	\N	1148	{"text": "“Yes, sir,” from the passage.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1150	lexical	\N	\N	1149	{"text": "—Mr. Sholto, it is my duty to inform you that anything which you may say will be used against you.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1151	lexical	\N	\N	1150	{"text": "I arrest you in the Queen’s name as being concerned in the death of your brother.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1152	lexical	\N	\N	1151	{"text": "ed in the death of your brother.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1153	lexical	\N	\N	1152	{"text": "“There, now!", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1154	lexical	\N	\N	1153	{"text": "Didn’t I tell you!”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1155	lexical	\N	\N	1154	{"text": "cried the poor little man, throwing out his hands, and looking from one to the other of us.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1156	lexical	\N	\N	1155	{"text": "“Don’t trouble yourself about it, Mr. Sholto,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1157	lexical	\N	\N	1156	{"text": "“I think that I can engage to clear you of the charge.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1158	lexical	\N	\N	1157	{"text": "“Don’t promise too much, Mr. Theorist,—don’t promise too much!”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1159	lexical	\N	\N	1158	{"text": "snapped the detective.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1160	lexical	\N	\N	1159	{"text": "“You may find it a harder matter than you think.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1161	lexical	\N	\N	1160	{"text": "“Not only will I clear him, Mr. Jones, but I will make you a free present of the name and description of one of the two people who were in this room last night.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1162	lexical	\N	\N	1161	{"text": "His name, I have every reason to believe, is Jonathan Small.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1163	lexical	\N	\N	1162	{"text": "He is a poorly-educated man, small, active, with his right leg off, and wearing a wooden stump which is worn away upon the inner side.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1164	lexical	\N	\N	1163	{"text": "His left boot has a coarse, square-toed sole, with an iron band round the heel.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1165	lexical	\N	\N	1164	{"text": "He is a middle-aged man, much sunburned, and has been a convict.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1166	lexical	\N	\N	1165	{"text": "These few indications may be of some assistance to you, coupled with the fact that there is a good deal of skin missing from the palm of his hand.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1167	lexical	\N	\N	1166	{"text": "The other man—”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1168	lexical	\N	\N	1167	{"text": "“Ah!", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1169	lexical	\N	\N	1168	{"text": "the other man—?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1170	lexical	\N	\N	1169	{"text": "asked Athelney Jones, in a sneering voice, but impressed none the less, as I could easily see, by the precision of the other’s manner.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1171	lexical	\N	\N	1170	{"text": "“Is a rather curious person,” said Sherlock Holmes, turning upon his heel.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1172	lexical	\N	\N	1171	{"text": "—A word with you, Watson.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1173	lexical	\N	\N	1172	{"text": "o be able to introduce you to the pair of them.—A word with you, Watson.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1174	lexical	\N	\N	1173	{"text": "He led me out to the head of the stair.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1175	lexical	\N	\N	1174	{"text": "“This unexpected occurrence,” he said, “has caused us rather to lose sight of the original purpose of our journey.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1176	lexical	\N	\N	1175	{"text": "“I have just been thinking so,” I answered.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1177	lexical	\N	\N	1176	{"text": "“It is not right that Miss Morstan should remain in this stricken house.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1178	lexical	\N	\N	1177	{"text": "“No.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1179	lexical	\N	\N	1178	{"text": "You must escort her home.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1180	lexical	\N	\N	1179	{"text": "She lives with Mrs. Cecil Forrester, in Lower Camberwell: so it is not very far.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1181	lexical	\N	\N	1180	{"text": "I will wait for you here if you will drive out again.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1182	lexical	\N	\N	1181	{"text": "Or perhaps you are too tired?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1183	lexical	\N	\N	1182	{"text": "“By no means.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1184	lexical	\N	\N	1183	{"text": "I don’t think I could rest until I know more of this fantastic business.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1185	lexical	\N	\N	1184	{"text": "I have seen something of the rough side of life, but I give you my word that this quick succession of strange surprises to-night has shaken my nerve completely.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1186	lexical	\N	\N	1185	{"text": "I should like, however, to see the matter through with you, now that I have got so far.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1187	lexical	\N	\N	1186	{"text": "“Your presence will be of great service to me,” he answered.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1188	lexical	\N	\N	1187	{"text": "“We shall work the case out independently, and leave this fellow Jones to exult over any mare’s-nest which he may choose to construct.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1189	lexical	\N	\N	1188	{"text": "When you have dropped Miss Morstan I wish you to go on to No.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1190	lexical	\N	\N	1189	{"text": "3, Pinchin Lane, down near the water’s edge at Lambeth.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1191	lexical	\N	\N	1190	{"text": "The third house on the right-hand side is a bird-stuffer’s: Sherman is the name.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1192	lexical	\N	\N	1191	{"text": "You will see a weasel holding a young rabbit in the window.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1193	lexical	\N	\N	1192	{"text": "Knock old Sherman up, and tell him, with my compliments, that I want Toby at once.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1194	lexical	\N	\N	1193	{"text": "You will bring Toby back in the cab with you.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1195	lexical	\N	\N	1194	{"text": "“A dog, I suppose.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1196	lexical	\N	\N	1195	{"text": "“Yes,—a queer mongrel, with a most amazing power of scent.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1197	lexical	\N	\N	1196	{"text": "I would rather have Toby’s help than that of the whole detective force of London.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1198	lexical	\N	\N	1197	{"text": "“I shall bring him, then,” said I.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1199	lexical	\N	\N	1198	{"text": "“It is one now.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1200	lexical	\N	\N	1199	{"text": "I ought to be back before three, if I can get a fresh horse.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1201	lexical	\N	\N	1200	{"text": "“And I,” said Holmes, “shall see what I can learn from Mrs. Bernstone, and from the Indian servant, who, Mr. Thaddeus tell me, sleeps in the next garret.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1202	lexical	\N	\N	1201	{"text": "Then I shall study the great Jones’s methods and listen to his not too delicate sarcasms.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1203	lexical	\N	\N	1202	{"text": "_’ Goethe is always pithy.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1204	lexical	\N	\N	1203	{"text": "Menschen verhöhnen was sie nicht verstehen._’ Goethe is always pithy.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1205	lexical	\N	\N	1204	{"text": "Chapter VII The Episode of the Barrel", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1206	lexical	\N	\N	1205	{"text": "The police had brought a cab with them, and in this I escorted Miss Morstan back to her home.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1207	lexical	\N	\N	1206	{"text": "After the angelic fashion of women, she had borne trouble with a calm face as long as there was some one weaker than herself to support, and I had found her bright and placid by the side of the frightened housekeeper.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1208	lexical	\N	\N	1207	{"text": "In the cab, however, she first turned faint, and then burst into a passion of weeping,—so sorely had she been tried by the adventures of the night.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1209	lexical	\N	\N	1208	{"text": "She has told me since that she thought me cold and distant upon that journey.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1210	lexical	\N	\N	1209	{"text": "She little guessed the struggle within my breast, or the effort of self-restraint which held me back.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1211	lexical	\N	\N	1210	{"text": "My sympathies and my love went out to her, even as my hand had in the garden.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1212	lexical	\N	\N	1211	{"text": "I felt that years of the conventionalities of life could not teach me to know her sweet, brave nature as had this one day of strange experiences.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1213	lexical	\N	\N	1212	{"text": "Yet there were two thoughts which sealed the words of affection upon my lips.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1214	lexical	\N	\N	1213	{"text": "She was weak and helpless, shaken in mind and nerve.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1215	lexical	\N	\N	1214	{"text": "It was to take her at a disadvantage to obtrude love upon her at such a time.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1216	lexical	\N	\N	1215	{"text": "Worse still, she was rich.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1217	lexical	\N	\N	1216	{"text": "If Holmes’s researches were successful, she would be an heiress.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1218	lexical	\N	\N	1217	{"text": "Was it fair, was it honourable, that a half-pay surgeon should take such advantage of an intimacy which chance had brought about?", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1219	lexical	\N	\N	1218	{"text": "Might she not look upon me as a mere vulgar fortune-seeker?", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1220	lexical	\N	\N	1219	{"text": "I could not bear to risk that such a thought should cross her mind.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1221	lexical	\N	\N	1220	{"text": "This Agra treasure intervened like an impassable barrier between us.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1222	lexical	\N	\N	1221	{"text": "It was nearly two o’clock when we reached Mrs. Cecil Forrester’s.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1223	lexical	\N	\N	1222	{"text": "The servants had retired hours ago, but Mrs. Forrester had been so interested by the strange message which Miss Morstan had received that she had sat up in the hope of her return.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1224	lexical	\N	\N	1223	{"text": "She opened the door herself, a middle-aged, graceful woman, and it gave me joy to see how tenderly her arm stole round the other’s waist and how motherly was the voice in which she greeted her.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1225	lexical	\N	\N	1224	{"text": "She was clearly no mere paid dependant, but an honoured friend.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1226	lexical	\N	\N	1225	{"text": "I was introduced, and Mrs. Forrester earnestly begged me to step in and tell her our adventures.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1227	lexical	\N	\N	1226	{"text": "I explained, however, the importance of my errand, and promised faithfully to call and report any progress which we might make with the case.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1228	lexical	\N	\N	1227	{"text": "As we drove away I stole a glance back, and I still seem to see that little group on the step, the two graceful, clinging figures, the half-opened door, the hall-light shining through stained glass, the barometer, and the bright stair-rods.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1229	lexical	\N	\N	1228	{"text": "It was soothing to catch even that passing glimpse of a tranquil English home in the midst of the wild, dark business which had absorbed us.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1230	lexical	\N	\N	1229	{"text": "And the more I thought of what had happened, the wilder and darker it grew.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1231	lexical	\N	\N	1230	{"text": "I reviewed the whole extraordinary sequence of events as I rattled on through the silent gas-lit streets.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1232	lexical	\N	\N	1231	{"text": "There was the original problem: that at least was pretty clear now.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1233	lexical	\N	\N	1232	{"text": "The death of Captain Morstan, the sending of the pearls, the advertisement, the letter,—we had had light upon all those events.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1234	lexical	\N	\N	1233	{"text": "They had only led us, however, to a deeper and far more tragic mystery.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1235	lexical	\N	\N	1234	{"text": "The Indian treasure, the curious plan found among Morstan’s baggage, the strange scene at Major Sholto’s death, the rediscovery of the treasure immediately followed by the murder of the discoverer, the very singular accompaniments to the crime, the footsteps, the remarkable weapons, the words upon the card, corresponding with those upon Captain Morstan’s chart,—here was indeed a labyrinth in which a man less singularly endowed than my fellow-lodger might well despair of ever finding the clue.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1236	lexical	\N	\N	1235	{"text": "Pinchin Lane was a row of shabby two-storied brick houses in the lower quarter of Lambeth.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1237	lexical	\N	\N	1236	{"text": "I had to knock for some time at No.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1238	lexical	\N	\N	1237	{"text": "3 before I could make my impression.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1239	lexical	\N	\N	1238	{"text": "At last, however, there was the glint of a candle behind the blind, and a face looked out at the upper window.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1240	lexical	\N	\N	1239	{"text": "“Go on, you drunken vagabone,” said the face.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1241	lexical	\N	\N	1240	{"text": "“If you kick up any more row I’ll open the kennels and let out forty-three dogs upon you.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1242	lexical	\N	\N	1241	{"text": "“If you’ll let one out it’s just what I have come for,” said I.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1243	lexical	\N	\N	1242	{"text": "“Go on!”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1244	lexical	\N	\N	1243	{"text": "yelled the voice.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1245	lexical	\N	\N	1244	{"text": "“So help me gracious, I have a wiper in the bag, an’ I’ll drop it on your ’ead if you don’t hook it.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1246	lexical	\N	\N	1245	{"text": "“But I want a dog,” I cried.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1247	lexical	\N	\N	1246	{"text": "“I won’t be argued with!”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1248	lexical	\N	\N	1247	{"text": "shouted Mr. Sherman.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1249	lexical	\N	\N	1248	{"text": "“Now stand clear, for when I say ‘three,’ down goes the wiper.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1250	lexical	\N	\N	1249	{"text": "“Mr. Sherlock Holmes—” I began, but the words had a most magical effect, for the window instantly slammed down, and within a minute the door was unbarred and open.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1251	lexical	\N	\N	1250	{"text": "Mr. Sherman was a lanky, lean old man, with stooping shoulders, a stringy neck, and blue-tinted glasses.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1252	lexical	\N	\N	1251	{"text": "“A friend of Mr. Sherlock is always welcome,” said he.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1253	lexical	\N	\N	1252	{"text": "“Step in, sir.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1254	lexical	\N	\N	1253	{"text": "Keep clear of the badger; for he bites.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1255	lexical	\N	\N	1254	{"text": "Ah, naughty, naughty, would you take a nip at the gentleman?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1256	lexical	\N	\N	1255	{"text": "This to a stoat which thrust its wicked head and red eyes between the bars of its cage.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1257	lexical	\N	\N	1256	{"text": "“Don’t mind that, sir: it’s only a slow-worm.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
crooked-man	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "\\"What should I know about that?\\"", "section": "crooked-man-section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1258	lexical	\N	\N	1257	{"text": "It hain’t got no fangs, so I gives it the run o’ the room, for it keeps the beetles down.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1259	lexical	\N	\N	1258	{"text": "You must not mind my bein’ just a little short wi’ you at first, for I’m guyed at by the children, and there’s many a one just comes down this lane to knock me up.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1260	lexical	\N	\N	1259	{"text": "What was it that Mr. Sherlock Holmes wanted, sir?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1261	lexical	\N	\N	1260	{"text": "“He wanted a dog of yours.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1262	lexical	\N	\N	1261	{"text": "“Ah!", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1263	lexical	\N	\N	1262	{"text": "that would be Toby.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1264	lexical	\N	\N	1263	{"text": "“Yes, Toby was the name.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1265	lexical	\N	\N	1264	{"text": "“Toby lives at No.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1266	lexical	\N	\N	1265	{"text": "7 on the left here.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1267	lexical	\N	\N	1266	{"text": "He moved slowly forward with his candle among the queer animal family which he had gathered round him.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1268	lexical	\N	\N	1267	{"text": "In the uncertain, shadowy light I could see dimly that there were glancing, glimmering eyes peeping down at us from every cranny and corner.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1269	lexical	\N	\N	1268	{"text": "Even the rafters above our heads were lined by solemn fowls, who lazily shifted their weight from one leg to the other as our voices disturbed their slumbers.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1270	lexical	\N	\N	1269	{"text": "Toby proved to be an ugly, long-haired, lop-eared creature, half spaniel and half lurcher, brown-and-white in colour, with a very clumsy waddling gait.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1271	lexical	\N	\N	1270	{"text": "It accepted after some hesitation a lump of sugar which the old naturalist handed to me, and, having thus sealed an alliance, it followed me to the cab, and made no difficulties about accompanying me.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1272	lexical	\N	\N	1271	{"text": "It had just struck three on the Palace clock when I found myself back once more at Pondicherry Lodge.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1273	lexical	\N	\N	1272	{"text": "The ex-prize-fighter McMurdo had, I found, been arrested as an accessory, and both he and Mr. Sholto had been marched off to the station.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1274	lexical	\N	\N	1273	{"text": "Two constables guarded the narrow gate, but they allowed me to pass with the dog on my mentioning the detective’s name.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1275	lexical	\N	\N	1274	{"text": "Holmes was standing on the door-step, with his hands in his pockets, smoking his pipe.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1276	lexical	\N	\N	1275	{"text": "“Ah, you have him there!”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1277	lexical	\N	\N	1276	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1278	lexical	\N	\N	1277	{"text": "“Good dog, then!", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1279	lexical	\N	\N	1278	{"text": "Athelney Jones has gone.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1280	lexical	\N	\N	1279	{"text": "We have had an immense display of energy since you left.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1281	lexical	\N	\N	1280	{"text": "He has arrested not only friend Thaddeus, but the gatekeeper, the housekeeper, and the Indian servant.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1282	lexical	\N	\N	1281	{"text": "We have the place to ourselves, but for a sergeant upstairs.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1283	lexical	\N	\N	1282	{"text": "Leave the dog here, and come up.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1284	lexical	\N	\N	1283	{"text": "We tied Toby to the hall table, and re-ascended the stairs.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1285	lexical	\N	\N	1284	{"text": "The room was as he had left it, save that a sheet had been draped over the central figure.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1286	lexical	\N	\N	1285	{"text": "A weary-looking police-sergeant reclined in the corner.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1287	lexical	\N	\N	1286	{"text": "“Lend me your bull’s-eye, sergeant,” said my companion.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1288	lexical	\N	\N	1287	{"text": "“Now tie this bit of card round my neck, so as to hang it in front of me.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1289	lexical	\N	\N	1288	{"text": "Thank you.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1290	lexical	\N	\N	1289	{"text": "—Just you carry them down with you, Watson.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1291	lexical	\N	\N	1290	{"text": "I am going to do a little climbing.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1292	lexical	\N	\N	1291	{"text": "And dip my handkerchief into the creasote.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1293	lexical	\N	\N	1292	{"text": "That will do.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1294	lexical	\N	\N	1293	{"text": "Now come up into the garret with me for a moment.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1295	lexical	\N	\N	1294	{"text": "e up into the garret with me for a moment.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1296	lexical	\N	\N	1295	{"text": "We clambered up through the hole.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1297	lexical	\N	\N	1296	{"text": "Holmes turned his light once more upon the footsteps in the dust.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1298	lexical	\N	\N	1297	{"text": "“I wish you particularly to notice these footmarks,” he said.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1299	lexical	\N	\N	1298	{"text": "“Do you observe anything noteworthy about them?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1300	lexical	\N	\N	1299	{"text": "“They belong,” I said, “to a child or a small woman.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1301	lexical	\N	\N	1300	{"text": "“Apart from their size, though.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1302	lexical	\N	\N	1301	{"text": "Is there nothing else?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1303	lexical	\N	\N	1302	{"text": "“They appear to be much as other footmarks.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1304	lexical	\N	\N	1303	{"text": "“Not at all.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1305	lexical	\N	\N	1304	{"text": "Look here!", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1306	lexical	\N	\N	1305	{"text": "This is the print of a right foot in the dust.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1307	lexical	\N	\N	1306	{"text": "Now I make one with my naked foot beside it.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1308	lexical	\N	\N	1307	{"text": "What is the chief difference?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1309	lexical	\N	\N	1308	{"text": "“Your toes are all cramped together.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1310	lexical	\N	\N	1309	{"text": "The other print has each toe distinctly divided.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1311	lexical	\N	\N	1310	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1312	lexical	\N	\N	1311	{"text": "That is the point.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1313	lexical	\N	\N	1312	{"text": "Bear that in mind.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1314	lexical	\N	\N	1313	{"text": "Now, would you kindly step over to that flap-window and smell the edge of the wood-work?", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1315	lexical	\N	\N	1314	{"text": "I shall stay here, as I have this handkerchief in my hand.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1316	lexical	\N	\N	1315	{"text": "I did as he directed, and was instantly conscious of a strong tarry smell.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1317	lexical	\N	\N	1316	{"text": "“That is where he put his foot in getting out.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1318	lexical	\N	\N	1317	{"text": "If _you_ can trace him, I should think that Toby will have no difficulty.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1319	lexical	\N	\N	1318	{"text": "Now run downstairs, loose the dog, and look out for Blondin.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1320	lexical	\N	\N	1319	{"text": "By the time that I got out into the grounds Sherlock Holmes was on the roof, and I could see him like an enormous glow-worm crawling very slowly along the ridge.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1321	lexical	\N	\N	1320	{"text": "I lost sight of him behind a stack of chimneys, but he presently reappeared, and then vanished once more upon the opposite side.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1322	lexical	\N	\N	1321	{"text": "When I made my way round there I found him seated at one of the corner eaves.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1323	lexical	\N	\N	1322	{"text": "“That you, Watson?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1324	lexical	\N	\N	1323	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1325	lexical	\N	\N	1324	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1326	lexical	\N	\N	1325	{"text": "“This is the place.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1327	lexical	\N	\N	1326	{"text": "What is that black thing down there?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1328	lexical	\N	\N	1327	{"text": "“A water-barrel.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1329	lexical	\N	\N	1328	{"text": "“Top on it?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1330	lexical	\N	\N	1329	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1331	lexical	\N	\N	1330	{"text": "“No sign of a ladder?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1332	lexical	\N	\N	1331	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1333	lexical	\N	\N	1332	{"text": "“Confound the fellow!", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1334	lexical	\N	\N	1333	{"text": "It’s a most break-neck place.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1335	lexical	\N	\N	1334	{"text": "I ought to be able to come down where he could climb up.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1336	lexical	\N	\N	1335	{"text": "The water-pipe feels pretty firm.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1337	lexical	\N	\N	1336	{"text": "Here goes, anyhow.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1338	lexical	\N	\N	1337	{"text": "There was a scuffling of feet, and the lantern began to come steadily down the side of the wall.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1339	lexical	\N	\N	1338	{"text": "Then with a light spring he came on to the barrel, and from there to the earth.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
crooked-man	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "\\"That's what I want to ascertain.", "section": "crooked-man-section_8", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1340	lexical	\N	\N	1339	{"text": "“It was easy to follow him,” he said, drawing on his stockings and boots.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1341	lexical	\N	\N	1340	{"text": "“Tiles were loosened the whole way along, and in his hurry he had dropped this.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1342	lexical	\N	\N	1341	{"text": "It confirms my diagnosis, as you doctors express it.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1343	lexical	\N	\N	1342	{"text": "The object which he held up to me was a small pocket or pouch woven out of coloured grasses and with a few tawdry beads strung round it.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1344	lexical	\N	\N	1343	{"text": "In shape and size it was not unlike a cigarette-case.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1345	lexical	\N	\N	1344	{"text": "Inside were half a dozen spines of dark wood, sharp at one end and rounded at the other, like that which had struck Bartholomew Sholto.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1346	lexical	\N	\N	1345	{"text": "“They are hellish things,” said he.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1347	lexical	\N	\N	1346	{"text": "“Look out that you don’t prick yourself.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1348	lexical	\N	\N	1347	{"text": "I’m delighted to have them, for the chances are that they are all he has.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1349	lexical	\N	\N	1348	{"text": "There is the less fear of you or me finding one in our skin before long.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1350	lexical	\N	\N	1349	{"text": "I would sooner face a Martini bullet, myself.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1351	lexical	\N	\N	1350	{"text": "Are you game for a six-mile trudge, Watson?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1352	lexical	\N	\N	1351	{"text": "“Certainly,” I answered.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1353	lexical	\N	\N	1352	{"text": "“Your leg will stand it?”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1354	lexical	\N	\N	1353	{"text": "“Oh, yes.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1355	lexical	\N	\N	1354	{"text": "“Here you are, doggy!", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1356	lexical	\N	\N	1355	{"text": "Good old Toby!", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1357	lexical	\N	\N	1356	{"text": "Smell it, Toby, smell it!”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1358	lexical	\N	\N	1357	{"text": "He pushed the creasote handkerchief under the dog’s nose, while the creature stood with its fluffy legs separated, and with a most comical cock to its head, like a connoisseur sniffing the _bouquet_ of a famous vintage.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1359	lexical	\N	\N	1358	{"text": "Holmes then threw the handkerchief to a distance, fastened a stout cord to the mongrel’s collar, and led him to the foot of the water-barrel.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1360	lexical	\N	\N	1359	{"text": "The creature instantly broke into a succession of high, tremulous yelps, and, with his nose on the ground, and his tail in the air, pattered off upon the trail at a pace which strained his leash and kept us at the top of our speed.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1361	lexical	\N	\N	1360	{"text": "The east had been gradually whitening, and we could now see some distance in the cold grey light.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1362	lexical	\N	\N	1361	{"text": "The square, massive house, with its black, empty windows and high, bare walls, towered up, sad and forlorn, behind us.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1363	lexical	\N	\N	1362	{"text": "Our course led right across the grounds, in and out among the trenches and pits with which they were scarred and intersected.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1364	lexical	\N	\N	1363	{"text": "The whole place, with its scattered dirt-heaps and ill-grown shrubs, had a blighted, ill-omened look which harmonized with the black tragedy which hung over it.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1365	lexical	\N	\N	1364	{"text": "On reaching the boundary wall Toby ran along, whining eagerly, underneath its shadow, and stopped finally in a corner screened by a young beech.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1366	lexical	\N	\N	1365	{"text": "Where the two walls joined, several bricks had been loosened, and the crevices left were worn down and rounded upon the lower side, as though they had frequently been used as a ladder.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1367	lexical	\N	\N	1366	{"text": "Holmes clambered up, and, taking the dog from me, he dropped it over upon the other side.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1368	lexical	\N	\N	1367	{"text": "“There’s the print of wooden-leg’s hand,” he remarked, as I mounted up beside him.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1369	lexical	\N	\N	1368	{"text": "“You see the slight smudge of blood upon the white plaster.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1370	lexical	\N	\N	1369	{"text": "What a lucky thing it is that we have had no very heavy rain since yesterday!", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1371	lexical	\N	\N	1370	{"text": "The scent will lie upon the road in spite of their eight-and-twenty hours’ start.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1372	lexical	\N	\N	1371	{"text": "I confess that I had my doubts myself when I reflected upon the great traffic which had passed along the London road in the interval.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1373	lexical	\N	\N	1372	{"text": "My fears were soon appeased, however.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1374	lexical	\N	\N	1373	{"text": "Toby never hesitated or swerved, but waddled on in his peculiar rolling fashion.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_77	section	\N	Section 77	76	{"wordCount": 614}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1375	lexical	\N	\N	1374	{"text": "Clearly, the pungent smell of the creasote rose high above all other contending scents.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1376	lexical	\N	\N	1375	{"text": "“Do not imagine,” said Holmes, “that I depend for my success in this case upon the mere chance of one of these fellows having put his foot in the chemical.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1377	lexical	\N	\N	1376	{"text": "I have knowledge now which would enable me to trace them in many different ways.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1378	lexical	\N	\N	1377	{"text": "This, however, is the readiest and, since fortune has put it into our hands, I should be culpable if I neglected it.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1379	lexical	\N	\N	1378	{"text": "It has, however, prevented the case from becoming the pretty little intellectual problem which it at one time promised to be.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1380	lexical	\N	\N	1379	{"text": "There might have been some credit to be gained out of it, but for this too palpable clue.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1381	lexical	\N	\N	1380	{"text": "“There is credit, and to spare,” said I.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1382	lexical	\N	\N	1381	{"text": "“I assure you, Holmes, that I marvel at the means by which you obtain your results in this case, even more than I did in the Jefferson Hope Murder.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1383	lexical	\N	\N	1382	{"text": "The thing seems to me to be deeper and more inexplicable.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1384	lexical	\N	\N	1383	{"text": "How, for example, could you describe with such confidence the wooden-legged man?”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1385	lexical	\N	\N	1384	{"text": "“Pshaw, my dear boy!", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1386	lexical	\N	\N	1385	{"text": "it was simplicity itself.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1387	lexical	\N	\N	1386	{"text": "I don’t wish to be theatrical.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1388	lexical	\N	\N	1387	{"text": "It is all patent and above-board.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1389	lexical	\N	\N	1388	{"text": "Two officers who are in command of a convict-guard learn an important secret as to buried treasure.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1390	lexical	\N	\N	1389	{"text": "A map is drawn for them by an Englishman named Jonathan Small.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1391	lexical	\N	\N	1390	{"text": "You remember that we saw the name upon the chart in Captain Morstan’s possession.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1392	lexical	\N	\N	1391	{"text": "He had signed it in behalf of himself and his associates,—the sign of the four, as he somewhat dramatically called it.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1393	lexical	\N	\N	1392	{"text": "Aided by this chart, the officers—or one of them—gets the treasure and brings it to England, leaving, we will suppose, some condition under which he received it unfulfilled.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1394	lexical	\N	\N	1393	{"text": "Now, then, why did not Jonathan Small get the treasure himself?", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1395	lexical	\N	\N	1394	{"text": "The answer is obvious.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1396	lexical	\N	\N	1395	{"text": "The chart is dated at a time when Morstan was brought into close association with convicts.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1397	lexical	\N	\N	1396	{"text": "Jonathan Small did not get the treasure because he and his associates were themselves convicts and could not get away.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1398	lexical	\N	\N	1397	{"text": "“But that is mere speculation,” said I.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1399	lexical	\N	\N	1398	{"text": "“It is more than that.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1400	lexical	\N	\N	1399	{"text": "It is the only hypothesis which covers the facts.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1401	lexical	\N	\N	1400	{"text": "Let us see how it fits in with the sequel.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1402	lexical	\N	\N	1401	{"text": "Major Sholto remains at peace for some years, happy in the possession of his treasure.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1403	lexical	\N	\N	1402	{"text": "Then he receives a letter from India which gives him a great fright.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1404	lexical	\N	\N	1403	{"text": "What was that?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1405	lexical	\N	\N	1404	{"text": "“A letter to say that the men whom he had wronged had been set free.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1406	lexical	\N	\N	1405	{"text": "“Or had escaped.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1407	lexical	\N	\N	1406	{"text": "That is much more likely, for he would have known what their term of imprisonment was.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1408	lexical	\N	\N	1407	{"text": "It would not have been a surprise to him.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1409	lexical	\N	\N	1408	{"text": "What does he do then?", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1410	lexical	\N	\N	1409	{"text": "He guards himself against a wooden-legged man,—a white man, mark you, for he mistakes a white tradesman for him, and actually fires a pistol at him.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1411	lexical	\N	\N	1410	{"text": "Now, only one white man’s name is on the chart.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1412	lexical	\N	\N	1411	{"text": "The others are Hindoos or Mohammedans.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1413	lexical	\N	\N	1412	{"text": "There is no other white man.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1414	lexical	\N	\N	1413	{"text": "Therefore we may say with confidence that the wooden-legged man is identical with Jonathan Small.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1415	lexical	\N	\N	1414	{"text": "Does the reasoning strike you as being faulty?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1416	lexical	\N	\N	1415	{"text": "“No: it is clear and concise.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1417	lexical	\N	\N	1416	{"text": "“Well, now, let us put ourselves in the place of Jonathan Small.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1418	lexical	\N	\N	1417	{"text": "Let us look at it from his point of view.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1419	lexical	\N	\N	1418	{"text": "He comes to England with the double idea of regaining what he would consider to be his rights and of having his revenge upon the man who had wronged him.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1420	lexical	\N	\N	1419	{"text": "He found out where Sholto lived, and very possibly he established communications with some one inside the house.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1421	lexical	\N	\N	1420	{"text": "There is this butler, Lal Rao, whom we have not seen.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1422	lexical	\N	\N	1421	{"text": "Mrs. Bernstone gives him far from a good character.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1423	lexical	\N	\N	1422	{"text": "Small could not find out, however, where the treasure was hid, for no one ever knew, save the major and one faithful servant who had died.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1424	lexical	\N	\N	1423	{"text": "Suddenly Small learns that the major is on his death-bed.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1425	lexical	\N	\N	1424	{"text": "In a frenzy lest the secret of the treasure die with him, he runs the gauntlet of the guards, makes his way to the dying man’s window, and is only deterred from entering by the presence of his two sons.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1426	lexical	\N	\N	1425	{"text": "Mad with hate, however, against the dead man, he enters the room that night, searches his private papers in the hope of discovering some memorandum relating to the treasure, and finally leaves a momento of his visit in the short inscription upon the card.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1427	lexical	\N	\N	1426	{"text": "He had doubtless planned beforehand that should he slay the major he would leave some such record upon the body as a sign that it was not a common murder, but, from the point of view of the four associates, something in the nature of an act of justice.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1428	lexical	\N	\N	1427	{"text": "Whimsical and bizarre conceits of this kind are common enough in the annals of crime, and usually afford valuable indications as to the criminal.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1429	lexical	\N	\N	1428	{"text": "Do you follow all this?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1430	lexical	\N	\N	1429	{"text": "“Very clearly.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1431	lexical	\N	\N	1430	{"text": "“Now, what could Jonathan Small do?", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1432	lexical	\N	\N	1431	{"text": "He could only continue to keep a secret watch upon the efforts made to find the treasure.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1433	lexical	\N	\N	1432	{"text": "Possibly he leaves England and only comes back at intervals.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1434	lexical	\N	\N	1433	{"text": "Then comes the discovery of the garret, and he is instantly informed of it.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1435	lexical	\N	\N	1434	{"text": "We again trace the presence of some confederate in the household.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1436	lexical	\N	\N	1435	{"text": "Jonathan, with his wooden leg, is utterly unable to reach the lofty room of Bartholomew Sholto.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1437	lexical	\N	\N	1436	{"text": "He takes with him, however, a rather curious associate, who gets over this difficulty, but dips his naked foot into creasote, whence comes Toby, and a six-mile limp for a half-pay officer with a damaged tendo Achillis.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1438	lexical	\N	\N	1437	{"text": "“But it was the associate, and not Jonathan, who committed the crime.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1439	lexical	\N	\N	1438	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1440	lexical	\N	\N	1439	{"text": "And rather to Jonathan’s disgust, to judge by the way he stamped about when he got into the room.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1441	lexical	\N	\N	1440	{"text": "He bore no grudge against Bartholomew Sholto, and would have preferred if he could have been simply bound and gagged.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1442	lexical	\N	\N	1441	{"text": "He did not wish to put his head in a halter.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1443	lexical	\N	\N	1442	{"text": "There was no help for it, however: the savage instincts of his companion had broken out, and the poison had done its work: so Jonathan Small left his record, lowered the treasure-box to the ground, and followed it himself.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1444	lexical	\N	\N	1443	{"text": "That was the train of events as far as I can decipher them.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1445	lexical	\N	\N	1444	{"text": "Of course as to his personal appearance he must be middle-aged, and must be sunburned after serving his time in such an oven as the Andamans.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1446	lexical	\N	\N	1445	{"text": "His height is readily calculated from the length of his stride, and we know that he was bearded.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1447	lexical	\N	\N	1446	{"text": "His hairiness was the one point which impressed itself upon Thaddeus Sholto when he saw him at the window.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1448	lexical	\N	\N	1447	{"text": "I don’t know that there is anything else.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1449	lexical	\N	\N	1448	{"text": "“The associate?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1450	lexical	\N	\N	1449	{"text": "“Ah, well, there is no great mystery in that.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1451	lexical	\N	\N	1450	{"text": "But you will know all about it soon enough.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1452	lexical	\N	\N	1451	{"text": "How sweet the morning air is!", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1453	lexical	\N	\N	1452	{"text": "See how that one little cloud floats like a pink feather from some gigantic flamingo.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1454	lexical	\N	\N	1453	{"text": "Now the red rim of the sun pushes itself over the London cloud-bank.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1455	lexical	\N	\N	1454	{"text": "It shines on a good many folk, but on none, I dare bet, who are on a stranger errand than you and I.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1456	lexical	\N	\N	1455	{"text": "How small we feel with our petty ambitions and strivings in the presence of the great elemental forces of nature!", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1457	lexical	\N	\N	1456	{"text": "Are you well up in your Jean Paul?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1458	lexical	\N	\N	1457	{"text": "“Fairly so.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1459	lexical	\N	\N	1458	{"text": "I worked back to him through Carlyle.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1460	lexical	\N	\N	1459	{"text": "“That was like following the brook to the parent lake.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1461	lexical	\N	\N	1460	{"text": "He makes one curious but profound remark.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1462	lexical	\N	\N	1461	{"text": "It is that the chief proof of man’s real greatness lies in his perception of his own smallness.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1463	lexical	\N	\N	1462	{"text": "It argues, you see, a power of comparison and of appreciation which is in itself a proof of nobility.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1464	lexical	\N	\N	1463	{"text": "There is much food for thought in Richter.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1465	lexical	\N	\N	1464	{"text": "You have not a pistol, have you?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1466	lexical	\N	\N	1465	{"text": "“I have my stick.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1467	lexical	\N	\N	1466	{"text": "“It is just possible that we may need something of the sort if we get to their lair.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1468	lexical	\N	\N	1467	{"text": "Jonathan I shall leave to you, but if the other turns nasty I shall shoot him dead.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1469	lexical	\N	\N	1468	{"text": "He took out his revolver as he spoke, and, having loaded two of the chambers, he put it back into the right-hand pocket of his jacket.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1470	lexical	\N	\N	1469	{"text": "We had during this time been following the guidance of Toby down the half-rural villa-lined roads which lead to the metropolis.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1471	lexical	\N	\N	1470	{"text": "Now, however, we were beginning to come among continuous streets, where labourers and dockmen were already astir, and slatternly women were taking down shutters and brushing door-steps.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1472	lexical	\N	\N	1471	{"text": "At the square-topped corner public houses business was just beginning, and rough-looking men were emerging, rubbing their sleeves across their beards after their morning wet.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1473	lexical	\N	\N	1472	{"text": "Strange dogs sauntered up and stared wonderingly at us as we passed, but our inimitable Toby looked neither to the right nor to the left, but trotted onwards with his nose to the ground and an occasional eager whine which spoke of a hot scent.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1474	lexical	\N	\N	1473	{"text": "We had traversed Streatham, Brixton, Camberwell, and now found ourselves in Kennington Lane, having borne away through the side-streets to the east of the Oval.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1475	lexical	\N	\N	1474	{"text": "The men whom we pursued seemed to have taken a curiously zigzag road, with the idea probably of escaping observation.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1476	lexical	\N	\N	1475	{"text": "They had never kept to the main road if a parallel side-street would serve their turn.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1477	lexical	\N	\N	1476	{"text": "At the foot of Kennington Lane they had edged away to the left through Bond Street and Miles Street.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1478	lexical	\N	\N	1477	{"text": "Where the latter street turns into Knight’s Place, Toby ceased to advance, but began to run backwards and forwards with one ear cocked and the other drooping, the very picture of canine indecision.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1479	lexical	\N	\N	1478	{"text": "Then he waddled round in circles, looking up to us from time to time, as if to ask for sympathy in his embarrassment.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1480	lexical	\N	\N	1479	{"text": "“What the deuce is the matter with the dog?”", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1481	lexical	\N	\N	1480	{"text": "growled Holmes.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1482	lexical	\N	\N	1481	{"text": "“They surely would not take a cab, or go off in a balloon.”", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1483	lexical	\N	\N	1482	{"text": "“Perhaps they stood here for some time,” I suggested.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1484	lexical	\N	\N	1483	{"text": "“Ah!", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1485	lexical	\N	\N	1484	{"text": "it’s all right.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1486	lexical	\N	\N	1485	{"text": "He’s off again,” said my companion, in a tone of relief.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1487	lexical	\N	\N	1486	{"text": "He was indeed off, for after sniffing round again he suddenly made up his mind, and darted away with an energy and determination such as he had not yet shown.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1488	lexical	\N	\N	1487	{"text": "The scent appeared to be much hotter than before, for he had not even to put his nose on the ground, but tugged at his leash and tried to break into a run.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1489	lexical	\N	\N	1488	{"text": "I could see by the gleam in Holmes’s eyes that he thought we were nearing the end of our journey.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1490	lexical	\N	\N	1489	{"text": "Our course now ran down Nine Elms until we came to Broderick and Nelson’s large timber-yard, just past the White Eagle tavern.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1491	lexical	\N	\N	1490	{"text": "Here the dog, frantic with excitement, turned down through the side-gate into the enclosure, where the sawyers were already at work.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1492	lexical	\N	\N	1491	{"text": "On the dog raced through sawdust and shavings, down an alley, round a passage, between two wood-piles, and finally, with a triumphant yelp, sprang upon a large barrel which still stood upon the hand-trolley on which it had been brought.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1493	lexical	\N	\N	1492	{"text": "With lolling tongue and blinking eyes, Toby stood upon the cask, looking from one to the other of us for some sign of appreciation.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1494	lexical	\N	\N	1493	{"text": "The staves of the barrel and the wheels of the trolley were smeared with a dark liquid, and the whole air was heavy with the smell of creasote.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1495	lexical	\N	\N	1494	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes and I looked blankly at each other, and then burst simultaneously into an uncontrollable fit of laughter.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1496	lexical	\N	\N	1495	{"text": "Chapter VIII The Baker Street Irregulars", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1497	lexical	\N	\N	1496	{"text": "“What now?”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1498	lexical	\N	\N	1497	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1499	lexical	\N	\N	1498	{"text": "“Toby has lost his character for infallibility.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1500	lexical	\N	\N	1499	{"text": "“He acted according to his lights,” said Holmes, lifting him down from the barrel and walking him out of the timber-yard.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1501	lexical	\N	\N	1500	{"text": "“If you consider how much creasote is carted about London in one day, it is no great wonder that our trail should have been crossed.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1502	lexical	\N	\N	1501	{"text": "It is much used now, especially for the seasoning of wood.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1503	lexical	\N	\N	1502	{"text": "Poor Toby is not to blame.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1504	lexical	\N	\N	1503	{"text": "“We must get on the main scent again, I suppose.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1505	lexical	\N	\N	1504	{"text": "“Yes.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1506	lexical	\N	\N	1505	{"text": "And, fortunately, we have no distance to go.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1507	lexical	\N	\N	1506	{"text": "Evidently what puzzled the dog at the corner of Knight’s Place was that there were two different trails running in opposite directions.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1508	lexical	\N	\N	1507	{"text": "We took the wrong one.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1509	lexical	\N	\N	1508	{"text": "It only remains to follow the other.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1510	lexical	\N	\N	1509	{"text": "There was no difficulty about this.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1511	lexical	\N	\N	1510	{"text": "On leading Toby to the place where he had committed his fault, he cast about in a wide circle and finally dashed off in a fresh direction.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1512	lexical	\N	\N	1511	{"text": "“We must take care that he does not now bring us to the place where the creasote-barrel came from,” I observed.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1513	lexical	\N	\N	1512	{"text": "“I had thought of that.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1514	lexical	\N	\N	1513	{"text": "But you notice that he keeps on the pavement, whereas the barrel passed down the roadway.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1515	lexical	\N	\N	1514	{"text": "No, we are on the true scent now.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1516	lexical	\N	\N	1515	{"text": "It tended down towards the river-side, running through Belmont Place and Prince’s Street.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1517	lexical	\N	\N	1516	{"text": "At the end of Broad Street it ran right down to the water’s edge, where there was a small wooden wharf.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1518	lexical	\N	\N	1517	{"text": "Toby led us to the very edge of this, and there stood whining, looking out on the dark current beyond.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_78	section	\N	Section 78	77	{"wordCount": 638}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1519	lexical	\N	\N	1518	{"text": "“We are out of luck,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1520	lexical	\N	\N	1519	{"text": "“They have taken to a boat here.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1521	lexical	\N	\N	1520	{"text": "Several small punts and skiffs were lying about in the water and on the edge of the wharf.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1522	lexical	\N	\N	1521	{"text": "We took Toby round to each in turn, but, though he sniffed earnestly, he made no sign.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1523	lexical	\N	\N	1522	{"text": "Close to the rude landing-stage was a small brick house, with a wooden placard slung out through the second window.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1524	lexical	\N	\N	1523	{"text": "“Mordecai Smith” was printed across it in large letters, and, underneath, “Boats to hire by the hour or day.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1525	lexical	\N	\N	1524	{"text": "A second inscription above the door informed us that a steam launch was kept,—a statement which was confirmed by a great pile of coke upon the jetty.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1526	lexical	\N	\N	1525	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes looked slowly round, and his face assumed an ominous expression.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1527	lexical	\N	\N	1526	{"text": "“This looks bad,” said he.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1528	lexical	\N	\N	1527	{"text": "“These fellows are sharper than I expected.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1529	lexical	\N	\N	1528	{"text": "They seem to have covered their tracks.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1530	lexical	\N	\N	1529	{"text": "There has, I fear, been preconcerted management here.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1531	lexical	\N	\N	1530	{"text": "He was approaching the door of the house, when it opened, and a little, curly-headed lad of six came running out, followed by a stoutish, red-faced woman with a large sponge in her hand.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1532	lexical	\N	\N	1531	{"text": "“You come back and be washed, Jack,” she shouted.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1533	lexical	\N	\N	1532	{"text": "“Come back, you young imp; for if your father comes home and finds you like that, he’ll let us hear of it.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1534	lexical	\N	\N	1533	{"text": "“Dear little chap!”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1535	lexical	\N	\N	1534	{"text": "said Holmes, strategically.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1536	lexical	\N	\N	1535	{"text": "“What a rosy-cheeked young rascal!", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1537	lexical	\N	\N	1536	{"text": "Now, Jack, is there anything you would like?”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1538	lexical	\N	\N	1537	{"text": "The youth pondered for a moment.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1539	lexical	\N	\N	1538	{"text": "“I’d like a shillin’,” said he.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1540	lexical	\N	\N	1539	{"text": "“Nothing you would like better?”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1541	lexical	\N	\N	1540	{"text": "“I’d like two shillin’ better,” the prodigy answered, after some thought.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1542	lexical	\N	\N	1541	{"text": "“Here you are, then!", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1543	lexical	\N	\N	1542	{"text": "—A fine child, Mrs. Smith!”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1544	lexical	\N	\N	1543	{"text": "mith!”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1545	lexical	\N	\N	1544	{"text": "“Lor’ bless you, sir, he is that, and forward.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1546	lexical	\N	\N	1545	{"text": "He gets a’most too much for me to manage, ’specially when my man is away days at a time.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1547	lexical	\N	\N	1546	{"text": "“Away, is he?”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1548	lexical	\N	\N	1547	{"text": "said Holmes, in a disappointed voice.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1549	lexical	\N	\N	1548	{"text": "“I am sorry for that, for I wanted to speak to Mr. Smith.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1550	lexical	\N	\N	1549	{"text": "“He’s been away since yesterday mornin’, sir, and, truth to tell, I am beginnin’ to feel frightened about him.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1551	lexical	\N	\N	1550	{"text": "But if it was about a boat, sir, maybe I could serve as well.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1552	lexical	\N	\N	1551	{"text": "“I wanted to hire his steam launch.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1553	lexical	\N	\N	1552	{"text": "“Why, bless you, sir, it is in the steam launch that he has gone.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1554	lexical	\N	\N	1553	{"text": "That’s what puzzles me; for I know there ain’t more coals in her than would take her to about Woolwich and back.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1555	lexical	\N	\N	1554	{"text": "If he’d been away in the barge I’d ha’ thought nothin’; for many a time a job has taken him as far as Gravesend, and then if there was much doin’ there he might ha’ stayed over.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1556	lexical	\N	\N	1555	{"text": "But what good is a steam launch without coals?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1557	lexical	\N	\N	1556	{"text": "“He might have bought some at a wharf down the river.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1558	lexical	\N	\N	1557	{"text": "“He might, sir, but it weren’t his way.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1559	lexical	\N	\N	1558	{"text": "Many a time I’ve heard him call out at the prices they charge for a few odd bags.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1560	lexical	\N	\N	1559	{"text": "Besides, I don’t like that wooden-legged man, wi’ his ugly face and outlandish talk.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1561	lexical	\N	\N	1560	{"text": "What did he want always knockin’ about here for?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1562	lexical	\N	\N	1561	{"text": "“A wooden-legged man?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1563	lexical	\N	\N	1562	{"text": "said Holmes, with bland surprise.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1564	lexical	\N	\N	1563	{"text": "“Yes, sir, a brown, monkey-faced chap that’s called more’n once for my old man.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1565	lexical	\N	\N	1564	{"text": "It was him that roused him up yesternight, and, what’s more, my man knew he was comin’, for he had steam up in the launch.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1566	lexical	\N	\N	1565	{"text": "I tell you straight, sir, I don’t feel easy in my mind about it.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1567	lexical	\N	\N	1566	{"text": "“But, my dear Mrs. Smith,” said Holmes, shrugging his shoulders, “You are frightening yourself about nothing.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1568	lexical	\N	\N	1567	{"text": "How could you possibly tell that it was the wooden-legged man who came in the night?", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1569	lexical	\N	\N	1568	{"text": "I don’t quite understand how you can be so sure.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1570	lexical	\N	\N	1569	{"text": "“His voice, sir.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1571	lexical	\N	\N	1570	{"text": "I knew his voice, which is kind o’ thick and foggy.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1572	lexical	\N	\N	1571	{"text": "He tapped at the winder,—about three it would be.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1573	lexical	\N	\N	1572	{"text": "‘Show a leg, matey,’ says he: ‘time to turn out guard.’", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1574	lexical	\N	\N	1573	{"text": "My old man woke up Jim,—that’s my eldest,—and away they went, without so much as a word to me.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1575	lexical	\N	\N	1574	{"text": "I could hear the wooden leg clackin’ on the stones.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1576	lexical	\N	\N	1575	{"text": "“And was this wooden-legged man alone?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1577	lexical	\N	\N	1576	{"text": "“Couldn’t say, I am sure, sir.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1578	lexical	\N	\N	1577	{"text": "I didn’t hear no one else.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1579	lexical	\N	\N	1578	{"text": "“I am sorry, Mrs. Smith, for I wanted a steam launch, and I have heard good reports of the—Let me see, what is her name?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1580	lexical	\N	\N	1579	{"text": "“The _Aurora_, sir.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1581	lexical	\N	\N	1580	{"text": "“Ah!", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1582	lexical	\N	\N	1581	{"text": "She’s not that old green launch with a yellow line, very broad in the beam?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1583	lexical	\N	\N	1582	{"text": "“No, indeed.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1584	lexical	\N	\N	1583	{"text": "She’s as trim a little thing as any on the river.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1585	lexical	\N	\N	1584	{"text": "She’s been fresh painted, black with two red streaks.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1586	lexical	\N	\N	1585	{"text": "“Thanks.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1587	lexical	\N	\N	1586	{"text": "I hope that you will hear soon from Mr. Smith.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1588	lexical	\N	\N	1587	{"text": "I am going down the river; and if I should see anything of the _Aurora_ I shall let him know that you are uneasy.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1589	lexical	\N	\N	1588	{"text": "A black funnel, you say?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1590	lexical	\N	\N	1589	{"text": "“No, sir.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1591	lexical	\N	\N	1590	{"text": "Black with a white band.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1592	lexical	\N	\N	1591	{"text": "“Ah, of course.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1593	lexical	\N	\N	1592	{"text": "It was the sides which were black.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1594	lexical	\N	\N	1593	{"text": "—There is a boatman here with a wherry, Watson.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1595	lexical	\N	\N	1594	{"text": "We shall take it and cross the river.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1596	lexical	\N	\N	1595	{"text": "e it and cross the river.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1597	lexical	\N	\N	1596	{"text": "“The main thing with people of that sort,” said Holmes, as we sat in the sheets of the wherry, “is never to let them think that their information can be of the slightest importance to you.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1598	lexical	\N	\N	1597	{"text": "If you do, they will instantly shut up like an oyster.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1599	lexical	\N	\N	1598	{"text": "If you listen to them under protest, as it were, you are very likely to get what you want.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1600	lexical	\N	\N	1599	{"text": "“Our course now seems pretty clear,” said I.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1601	lexical	\N	\N	1600	{"text": "“What would you do, then?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1602	lexical	\N	\N	1601	{"text": "“I would engage a launch and go down the river on the track of the _Aurora_.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1603	lexical	\N	\N	1602	{"text": "“My dear fellow, it would be a colossal task.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1604	lexical	\N	\N	1603	{"text": "She may have touched at any wharf on either side of the stream between here and Greenwich.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1605	lexical	\N	\N	1604	{"text": "Below the bridge there is a perfect labyrinth of landing-places for miles.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1606	lexical	\N	\N	1605	{"text": "It would take you days and days to exhaust them, if you set about it alone.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1607	lexical	\N	\N	1606	{"text": "“Employ the police, then.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1608	lexical	\N	\N	1607	{"text": "“No.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1609	lexical	\N	\N	1608	{"text": "I shall probably call Athelney Jones in at the last moment.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1610	lexical	\N	\N	1609	{"text": "He is not a bad fellow, and I should not like to do anything which would injure him professionally.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1611	lexical	\N	\N	1610	{"text": "But I have a fancy for working it out myself, now that we have gone so far.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1612	lexical	\N	\N	1611	{"text": "“Could we advertise, then, asking for information from wharfingers?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1613	lexical	\N	\N	1612	{"text": "“Worse and worse!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1614	lexical	\N	\N	1613	{"text": "Our men would know that the chase was hot at their heels, and they would be off out of the country.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1615	lexical	\N	\N	1614	{"text": "As it is, they are likely enough to leave, but as long as they think they are perfectly safe they will be in no hurry.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1616	lexical	\N	\N	1615	{"text": "Jones’s energy will be of use to us there, for his view of the case is sure to push itself into the daily press, and the runaways will think that every one is off on the wrong scent.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1617	lexical	\N	\N	1616	{"text": "“What are we to do, then?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1618	lexical	\N	\N	1617	{"text": "I asked, as we landed near Millbank Penitentiary.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1619	lexical	\N	\N	1618	{"text": "“Take this hansom, drive home, have some breakfast, and get an hour’s sleep.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1620	lexical	\N	\N	1619	{"text": "It is quite on the cards that we may be afoot to-night again.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1621	lexical	\N	\N	1620	{"text": "Stop at a telegraph-office, cabby!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1622	lexical	\N	\N	1621	{"text": "We will keep Toby, for he may be of use to us yet.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1623	lexical	\N	\N	1622	{"text": "We pulled up at the Great Peter Street post-office, and Holmes despatched his wire.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1624	lexical	\N	\N	1623	{"text": "“Whom do you think that is to?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1625	lexical	\N	\N	1624	{"text": "he asked, as we resumed our journey.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1626	lexical	\N	\N	1625	{"text": "“I am sure I don’t know.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1627	lexical	\N	\N	1626	{"text": "“You remember the Baker Street division of the detective police force whom I employed in the Jefferson Hope case?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1628	lexical	\N	\N	1627	{"text": "“Well,” said I, laughing.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1629	lexical	\N	\N	1628	{"text": "“This is just the case where they might be invaluable.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1630	lexical	\N	\N	1629	{"text": "If they fail, I have other resources; but I shall try them first.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1631	lexical	\N	\N	1630	{"text": "That wire was to my dirty little lieutenant, Wiggins, and I expect that he and his gang will be with us before we have finished our breakfast.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1632	lexical	\N	\N	1631	{"text": "It was between eight and nine o’clock now, and I was conscious of a strong reaction after the successive excitements of the night.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1633	lexical	\N	\N	1632	{"text": "I was limp and weary, befogged in mind and fatigued in body.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1634	lexical	\N	\N	1633	{"text": "I had not the professional enthusiasm which carried my companion on, nor could I look at the matter as a mere abstract intellectual problem.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1635	lexical	\N	\N	1634	{"text": "As far as the death of Bartholomew Sholto went, I had heard little good of him, and could feel no intense antipathy to his murderers.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1636	lexical	\N	\N	1635	{"text": "The treasure, however, was a different matter.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1637	lexical	\N	\N	1636	{"text": "That, or part of it, belonged rightfully to Miss Morstan.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1638	lexical	\N	\N	1637	{"text": "While there was a chance of recovering it I was ready to devote my life to the one object.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1639	lexical	\N	\N	1638	{"text": "True, if I found it it would probably put her forever beyond my reach.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1640	lexical	\N	\N	1639	{"text": "Yet it would be a petty and selfish love which would be influenced by such a thought as that.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1641	lexical	\N	\N	1640	{"text": "If Holmes could work to find the criminals, I had a tenfold stronger reason to urge me on to find the treasure.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1642	lexical	\N	\N	1641	{"text": "A bath at Baker Street and a complete change freshened me up wonderfully.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1643	lexical	\N	\N	1642	{"text": "When I came down to our room I found the breakfast laid and Holmes pouring out the coffee.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1644	lexical	\N	\N	1643	{"text": "“Here it is,” said he, laughing, and pointing to an open newspaper.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1645	lexical	\N	\N	1644	{"text": "“The energetic Jones and the ubiquitous reporter have fixed it up between them.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1646	lexical	\N	\N	1645	{"text": "But you have had enough of the case.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1647	lexical	\N	\N	1646	{"text": "Better have your ham and eggs first.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1648	lexical	\N	\N	1647	{"text": "I took the paper from him and read the short notice, which was headed “Mysterious Business at Upper Norwood.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1649	lexical	\N	\N	1648	{"text": "“About twelve o’clock last night,” said the _Standard_, “Mr. Bartholomew Sholto, of Pondicherry Lodge, Upper Norwood, was found dead in his room under circumstances which point to foul play.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1650	lexical	\N	\N	1649	{"text": "As far as we can learn, no actual traces of violence were found upon Mr. Sholto’s person, but a valuable collection of Indian gems which the deceased gentleman had inherited from his father has been carried off.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1651	lexical	\N	\N	1650	{"text": "The discovery was first made by Mr. Sherlock Holmes and Dr. Watson, who had called at the house with Mr. Thaddeus Sholto, brother of the deceased.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1652	lexical	\N	\N	1651	{"text": "By a singular piece of good fortune, Mr. Athelney Jones, the well-known member of the detective police force, happened to be at the Norwood Police Station, and was on the ground within half an hour of the first alarm.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1653	lexical	\N	\N	1652	{"text": "His trained and experienced faculties were at once directed towards the detection of the criminals, with the gratifying result that the brother, Thaddeus Sholto, has already been arrested, together with the housekeeper, Mrs. Bernstone, an Indian butler named Lal Rao, and a porter, or gatekeeper, named McMurdo.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1654	lexical	\N	\N	1653	{"text": "It is quite certain that the thief or thieves were well acquainted with the house, for Mr. Jones’s well-known technical knowledge and his powers of minute observation have enabled him to prove conclusively that the miscreants could not have entered by the door or by the window, but must have made their way across the roof of the building, and so through a trap-door into a room which communicated with that in which the body was found.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1655	lexical	\N	\N	1654	{"text": "This fact, which has been very clearly made out, proves conclusively that it was no mere haphazard burglary.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1656	lexical	\N	\N	1655	{"text": "The prompt and energetic action of the officers of the law shows the great advantage of the presence on such occasions of a single vigorous and masterful mind.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1657	lexical	\N	\N	1656	{"text": "We cannot but think that it supplies an argument to those who would wish to see our detectives more decentralised, and so brought into closer and more effective touch with the cases which it is their duty to investigate.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1658	lexical	\N	\N	1657	{"text": "“Isn’t it gorgeous!”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1659	lexical	\N	\N	1658	{"text": "said Holmes, grinning over his coffee-cup.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1660	lexical	\N	\N	1659	{"text": "“What do you think of it?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1661	lexical	\N	\N	1660	{"text": "“I think that we have had a close shave ourselves of being arrested for the crime.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1662	lexical	\N	\N	1661	{"text": "“So do I.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1663	lexical	\N	\N	1662	{"text": "I wouldn’t answer for our safety now, if he should happen to have another of his attacks of energy.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1664	lexical	\N	\N	1663	{"text": "At this moment there was a loud ring at the bell, and I could hear Mrs. Hudson, our landlady, raising her voice in a wail of expostulation and dismay.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1665	lexical	\N	\N	1664	{"text": "“By heaven, Holmes,” I said, half rising, “I believe that they are really after us.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1666	lexical	\N	\N	1665	{"text": "“No, it’s not quite so bad as that.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1667	lexical	\N	\N	1666	{"text": "It is the unofficial force,—the Baker Street irregulars.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1709	lexical	\N	\N	1708	{"text": "“Perhaps one of those Indians who were the associates of Jonathan Small.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1668	lexical	\N	\N	1667	{"text": "As he spoke, there came a swift pattering of naked feet upon the stairs, a clatter of high voices, and in rushed a dozen dirty and ragged little street-Arabs.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1669	lexical	\N	\N	1668	{"text": "There was some show of discipline among them, despite their tumultuous entry, for they instantly drew up in line and stood facing us with expectant faces.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1670	lexical	\N	\N	1669	{"text": "One of their number, taller and older than the others, stood forward with an air of lounging superiority which was very funny in such a disreputable little scarecrow.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1671	lexical	\N	\N	1670	{"text": "“Got your message, sir,” said he, “and brought ’em on sharp.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1672	lexical	\N	\N	1671	{"text": "Three bob and a tanner for tickets.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1673	lexical	\N	\N	1672	{"text": "“Here you are,” said Holmes, producing some silver.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1674	lexical	\N	\N	1673	{"text": "“In future they can report to you, Wiggins, and you to me.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1675	lexical	\N	\N	1674	{"text": "I cannot have the house invaded in this way.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1676	lexical	\N	\N	1675	{"text": "However, it is just as well that you should all hear the instructions.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1677	lexical	\N	\N	1676	{"text": "I want to find the whereabouts of a steam launch called the _Aurora_, owner Mordecai Smith, black with two red streaks, funnel black with a white band.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1678	lexical	\N	\N	1677	{"text": "She is down the river somewhere.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1679	lexical	\N	\N	1678	{"text": "I want one boy to be at Mordecai Smith’s landing-stage opposite Millbank to say if the boat comes back.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1680	lexical	\N	\N	1679	{"text": "You must divide it out among yourselves, and do both banks thoroughly.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1681	lexical	\N	\N	1680	{"text": "Let me know the moment you have news.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1682	lexical	\N	\N	1681	{"text": "Is that all clear?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1683	lexical	\N	\N	1682	{"text": "“Yes, guv’nor,” said Wiggins.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1684	lexical	\N	\N	1683	{"text": "“The old scale of pay, and a guinea to the boy who finds the boat.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1685	lexical	\N	\N	1684	{"text": "Here’s a day in advance.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1686	lexical	\N	\N	1685	{"text": "Now off you go!”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1687	lexical	\N	\N	1686	{"text": "He handed them a shilling each, and away they buzzed down the stairs, and I saw them a moment later streaming down the street.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1688	lexical	\N	\N	1687	{"text": "“If the launch is above water they will find her,” said Holmes, as he rose from the table and lit his pipe.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1689	lexical	\N	\N	1688	{"text": "“They can go everywhere, see everything, overhear every one.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1690	lexical	\N	\N	1689	{"text": "I expect to hear before evening that they have spotted her.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1691	lexical	\N	\N	1690	{"text": "In the meanwhile, we can do nothing but await results.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1692	lexical	\N	\N	1691	{"text": "We cannot pick up the broken trail until we find either the _Aurora_ or Mr. Mordecai Smith.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1693	lexical	\N	\N	1692	{"text": "“Toby could eat these scraps, I dare say.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1694	lexical	\N	\N	1693	{"text": "Are you going to bed, Holmes?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1695	lexical	\N	\N	1694	{"text": "“No; I am not tired.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1696	lexical	\N	\N	1695	{"text": "I have a curious constitution.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1697	lexical	\N	\N	1696	{"text": "I never remember feeling tired by work, though idleness exhausts me completely.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1698	lexical	\N	\N	1697	{"text": "I am going to smoke and to think over this queer business to which my fair client has introduced us.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1699	lexical	\N	\N	1698	{"text": "If ever man had an easy task, this of ours ought to be.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1700	lexical	\N	\N	1699	{"text": "Wooden-legged men are not so common, but the other man must, I should think, be absolutely unique.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1701	lexical	\N	\N	1700	{"text": "“That other man again!”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1702	lexical	\N	\N	1701	{"text": "“I have no wish to make a mystery of him,—to you, anyway.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1703	lexical	\N	\N	1702	{"text": "But you must have formed your own opinion.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1704	lexical	\N	\N	1703	{"text": "Now, do consider the data.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1705	lexical	\N	\N	1704	{"text": "Diminutive footmarks, toes never fettered by boots, naked feet, stone-headed wooden mace, great agility, small poisoned darts.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1706	lexical	\N	\N	1705	{"text": "What do you make of all this?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1711	lexical	\N	\N	1710	{"text": "“When first I saw signs of strange weapons I was inclined to think so; but the remarkable character of the footmarks caused me to reconsider my views.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1712	lexical	\N	\N	1711	{"text": "Some of the inhabitants of the Indian Peninsula are small men, but none could have left such marks as that.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1713	lexical	\N	\N	1712	{"text": "The Hindoo proper has long and thin feet.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1714	lexical	\N	\N	1713	{"text": "The sandal-wearing Mohammedan has the great toe well separated from the others, because the thong is commonly passed between.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1715	lexical	\N	\N	1714	{"text": "These little darts, too, could only be shot in one way.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1716	lexical	\N	\N	1715	{"text": "They are from a blow-pipe.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1717	lexical	\N	\N	1716	{"text": "Now, then, where are we to find our savage?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1718	lexical	\N	\N	1717	{"text": "“South American,” I hazarded.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1719	lexical	\N	\N	1718	{"text": "He stretched his hand up, and took down a bulky volume from the shelf.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1720	lexical	\N	\N	1719	{"text": "“This is the first volume of a gazetteer which is now being published.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1721	lexical	\N	\N	1720	{"text": "It may be looked upon as the very latest authority.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1722	lexical	\N	\N	1721	{"text": "What have we here?", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1723	lexical	\N	\N	1722	{"text": "‘Andaman Islands, situated 340 miles to the north of Sumatra, in the Bay of Bengal.’", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1724	lexical	\N	\N	1723	{"text": "Hum!", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1725	lexical	\N	\N	1724	{"text": "hum!", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1726	lexical	\N	\N	1725	{"text": "What’s all this?", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1727	lexical	\N	\N	1726	{"text": "Moist climate, coral reefs, sharks, Port Blair, convict-barracks, Rutland Island, cottonwoods—Ah, here we are.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1728	lexical	\N	\N	1727	{"text": "‘The aborigines of the Andaman Islands may perhaps claim the distinction of being the smallest race upon this earth, though some anthropologists prefer the Bushmen of Africa, the Digger Indians of America, and the Terra del Fuegians.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1729	lexical	\N	\N	1728	{"text": "The average height is rather below four feet, although many full-grown adults may be found who are very much smaller than this.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1730	lexical	\N	\N	1729	{"text": "They are a fierce, morose, and intractable people, though capable of forming most devoted friendships when their confidence has once been gained.’", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1731	lexical	\N	\N	1730	{"text": "Mark that, Watson.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1732	lexical	\N	\N	1731	{"text": "Now, then, listen to this.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1733	lexical	\N	\N	1732	{"text": "‘They are naturally hideous, having large, misshapen heads, small, fierce eyes, and distorted features.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1734	lexical	\N	\N	1733	{"text": "Their feet and hands, however, are remarkably small.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1735	lexical	\N	\N	1734	{"text": "So intractable and fierce are they that all the efforts of the British official have failed to win them over in any degree.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1736	lexical	\N	\N	1735	{"text": "They have always been a terror to shipwrecked crews, braining the survivors with their stone-headed clubs, or shooting them with their poisoned arrows.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1737	lexical	\N	\N	1736	{"text": "These massacres are invariably concluded by a cannibal feast.’", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1738	lexical	\N	\N	1737	{"text": "Nice, amiable people, Watson!", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1739	lexical	\N	\N	1738	{"text": "If this fellow had been left to his own unaided devices this affair might have taken an even more ghastly turn.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1740	lexical	\N	\N	1739	{"text": "I fancy that, even as it is, Jonathan Small would give a good deal not to have employed him.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1741	lexical	\N	\N	1740	{"text": "“But how came he to have so singular a companion?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1742	lexical	\N	\N	1741	{"text": "“Ah, that is more than I can tell.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1743	lexical	\N	\N	1742	{"text": "Since, however, we had already determined that Small had come from the Andamans, it is not so very wonderful that this islander should be with him.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1744	lexical	\N	\N	1743	{"text": "No doubt we shall know all about it in time.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1745	lexical	\N	\N	1744	{"text": "Look here, Watson; you look regularly done.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1746	lexical	\N	\N	1745	{"text": "Lie down there on the sofa, and see if I can put you to sleep.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1747	lexical	\N	\N	1746	{"text": "He took up his violin from the corner, and as I stretched myself out he began to play some low, dreamy, melodious air,—his own, no doubt, for he had a remarkable gift for improvisation.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1748	lexical	\N	\N	1747	{"text": "I have a vague remembrance of his gaunt limbs, his earnest face, and the rise and fall of his bow.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1749	lexical	\N	\N	1748	{"text": "Then I seemed to be floated peacefully away upon a soft sea of sound, until I found myself in dreamland, with the sweet face of Mary Morstan looking down upon me.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1750	lexical	\N	\N	1749	{"text": "Chapter IX A Break in the Chain", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1751	lexical	\N	\N	1750	{"text": "It was late in the afternoon before I woke, strengthened and refreshed.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1752	lexical	\N	\N	1751	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes still sat exactly as I had left him, save that he had laid aside his violin and was deep in a book.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1753	lexical	\N	\N	1752	{"text": "He looked across at me, as I stirred, and I noticed that his face was dark and troubled.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1754	lexical	\N	\N	1753	{"text": "“You have slept soundly,” he said.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1755	lexical	\N	\N	1754	{"text": "“I feared that our talk would wake you.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1756	lexical	\N	\N	1755	{"text": "“I heard nothing,” I answered.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1757	lexical	\N	\N	1756	{"text": "“Have you had fresh news, then?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1758	lexical	\N	\N	1757	{"text": "“Unfortunately, no.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1759	lexical	\N	\N	1758	{"text": "I confess that I am surprised and disappointed.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1760	lexical	\N	\N	1759	{"text": "I expected something definite by this time.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1761	lexical	\N	\N	1760	{"text": "Wiggins has just been up to report.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1762	lexical	\N	\N	1761	{"text": "He says that no trace can be found of the launch.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1763	lexical	\N	\N	1762	{"text": "It is a provoking check, for every hour is of importance.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1764	lexical	\N	\N	1763	{"text": "“Can I do anything?", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1765	lexical	\N	\N	1764	{"text": "I am perfectly fresh now, and quite ready for another night’s outing.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1766	lexical	\N	\N	1765	{"text": "“No, we can do nothing.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1767	lexical	\N	\N	1766	{"text": "We can only wait.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1768	lexical	\N	\N	1767	{"text": "If we go ourselves, the message might come in our absence, and delay be caused.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1769	lexical	\N	\N	1768	{"text": "You can do what you will, but I must remain on guard.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1770	lexical	\N	\N	1769	{"text": "“Then I shall run over to Camberwell and call upon Mrs. Cecil Forrester.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1771	lexical	\N	\N	1770	{"text": "She asked me to, yesterday.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1772	lexical	\N	\N	1771	{"text": "“On Mrs. Cecil Forrester?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1773	lexical	\N	\N	1772	{"text": "asked Holmes, with the twinkle of a smile in his eyes.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1774	lexical	\N	\N	1773	{"text": "“Well, of course Miss Morstan too.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1775	lexical	\N	\N	1774	{"text": "They were anxious to hear what happened.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1776	lexical	\N	\N	1775	{"text": "“I would not tell them too much,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1777	lexical	\N	\N	1776	{"text": "“Women are never to be entirely trusted,—not the best of them.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1778	lexical	\N	\N	1777	{"text": "I did not pause to argue over this atrocious sentiment.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1779	lexical	\N	\N	1778	{"text": "“I shall be back in an hour or two,” I remarked.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1780	lexical	\N	\N	1779	{"text": "“All right!", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1781	lexical	\N	\N	1780	{"text": "Good luck!", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1782	lexical	\N	\N	1781	{"text": "But, I say, if you are crossing the river you may as well return Toby, for I don’t think it is at all likely that we shall have any use for him now.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1783	lexical	\N	\N	1782	{"text": "I took our mongrel accordingly, and left him, together with a half-sovereign, at the old naturalist’s in Pinchin Lane.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1784	lexical	\N	\N	1783	{"text": "At Camberwell I found Miss Morstan a little weary after her night’s adventures, but very eager to hear the news.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1785	lexical	\N	\N	1784	{"text": "Mrs. Forrester, too, was full of curiosity.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1786	lexical	\N	\N	1785	{"text": "I told them all that we had done, suppressing, however, the more dreadful parts of the tragedy.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1787	lexical	\N	\N	1786	{"text": "Thus, although I spoke of Mr. Sholto’s death, I said nothing of the exact manner and method of it.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_79	section	\N	Section 79	78	{"wordCount": 676}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1788	lexical	\N	\N	1787	{"text": "With all my omissions, however, there was enough to startle and amaze them.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1789	lexical	\N	\N	1788	{"text": "“It is a romance!”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1790	lexical	\N	\N	1789	{"text": "cried Mrs. Forrester.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1791	lexical	\N	\N	1790	{"text": "“An injured lady, half a million in treasure, a black cannibal, and a wooden-legged ruffian.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1792	lexical	\N	\N	1791	{"text": "They take the place of the conventional dragon or wicked earl.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1793	lexical	\N	\N	1792	{"text": "“And two knight-errants to the rescue,” added Miss Morstan, with a bright glance at me.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1794	lexical	\N	\N	1793	{"text": "“Why, Mary, your fortune depends upon the issue of this search.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1795	lexical	\N	\N	1794	{"text": "I don’t think that you are nearly excited enough.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1796	lexical	\N	\N	1795	{"text": "Just imagine what it must be to be so rich, and to have the world at your feet!”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1797	lexical	\N	\N	1796	{"text": "It sent a little thrill of joy to my heart to notice that she showed no sign of elation at the prospect.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1798	lexical	\N	\N	1797	{"text": "On the contrary, she gave a toss of her proud head, as though the matter were one in which she took small interest.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1799	lexical	\N	\N	1798	{"text": "“It is for Mr. Thaddeus Sholto that I am anxious,” she said.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1800	lexical	\N	\N	1799	{"text": "“Nothing else is of any consequence; but I think that he has behaved most kindly and honourably throughout.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1801	lexical	\N	\N	1800	{"text": "It is our duty to clear him of this dreadful and unfounded charge.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1802	lexical	\N	\N	1801	{"text": "It was evening before I left Camberwell, and quite dark by the time I reached home.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1803	lexical	\N	\N	1802	{"text": "My companion’s book and pipe lay by his chair, but he had disappeared.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1804	lexical	\N	\N	1803	{"text": "I looked about in the hope of seeing a note, but there was none.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1805	lexical	\N	\N	1804	{"text": "“I suppose that Mr. Sherlock Holmes has gone out,” I said to Mrs. Hudson as she came up to lower the blinds.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1806	lexical	\N	\N	1805	{"text": "“No, sir.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1807	lexical	\N	\N	1806	{"text": "He has gone to his room, sir.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1808	lexical	\N	\N	1807	{"text": "Do you know, sir,” sinking her voice into an impressive whisper, “I am afraid for his health?”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1809	lexical	\N	\N	1808	{"text": "“Why so, Mrs. Hudson?”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1810	lexical	\N	\N	1809	{"text": "“Well, he’s that strange, sir.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1811	lexical	\N	\N	1810	{"text": "After you was gone he walked and he walked, up and down, and up and down, until I was weary of the sound of his footstep.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1812	lexical	\N	\N	1811	{"text": "Then I heard him talking to himself and muttering, and every time the bell rang out he came on the stairhead, with ‘What is that, Mrs. Hudson?’", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1813	lexical	\N	\N	1812	{"text": "And now he has slammed off to his room, but I can hear him walking away the same as ever.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1814	lexical	\N	\N	1813	{"text": "I hope he’s not going to be ill, sir.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1815	lexical	\N	\N	1814	{"text": "I ventured to say something to him about cooling medicine, but he turned on me, sir, with such a look that I don’t know how ever I got out of the room.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1816	lexical	\N	\N	1815	{"text": "“I don’t think that you have any cause to be uneasy, Mrs. Hudson,” I answered.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1817	lexical	\N	\N	1816	{"text": "“I have seen him like this before.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1818	lexical	\N	\N	1817	{"text": "He has some small matter upon his mind which makes him restless.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1819	lexical	\N	\N	1818	{"text": "I tried to speak lightly to our worthy landlady, but I was myself somewhat uneasy when through the long night I still from time to time heard the dull sound of his tread, and knew how his keen spirit was chafing against this involuntary inaction.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1820	lexical	\N	\N	1819	{"text": "At breakfast-time he looked worn and haggard, with a little fleck of feverish colour upon either cheek.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1821	lexical	\N	\N	1820	{"text": "“You are knocking yourself up, old man,” I remarked.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1822	lexical	\N	\N	1821	{"text": "“I heard you marching about in the night.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1823	lexical	\N	\N	1822	{"text": "“No, I could not sleep,” he answered.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1824	lexical	\N	\N	1823	{"text": "“This infernal problem is consuming me.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_80	section	\N	Section 80	79	{"wordCount": 680}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1825	lexical	\N	\N	1824	{"text": "It is too much to be balked by so petty an obstacle, when all else had been overcome.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1826	lexical	\N	\N	1825	{"text": "I know the men, the launch, everything; and yet I can get no news.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1827	lexical	\N	\N	1826	{"text": "I have set other agencies at work, and used every means at my disposal.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1828	lexical	\N	\N	1827	{"text": "The whole river has been searched on either side, but there is no news, nor has Mrs. Smith heard of her husband.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1829	lexical	\N	\N	1828	{"text": "I shall come to the conclusion soon that they have scuttled the craft.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1830	lexical	\N	\N	1829	{"text": "But there are objections to that.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1831	lexical	\N	\N	1830	{"text": "“Or that Mrs. Smith has put us on a wrong scent.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1832	lexical	\N	\N	1831	{"text": "“No, I think that may be dismissed.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1833	lexical	\N	\N	1832	{"text": "I had inquiries made, and there is a launch of that description.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1834	lexical	\N	\N	1833	{"text": "“Could it have gone up the river?”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1835	lexical	\N	\N	1834	{"text": "“I have considered that possibility too, and there is a search-party who will work up as far as Richmond.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1836	lexical	\N	\N	1835	{"text": "If no news comes to-day, I shall start off myself to-morrow, and go for the men rather than the boat.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1837	lexical	\N	\N	1836	{"text": "But surely, surely, we shall hear something.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1838	lexical	\N	\N	1837	{"text": "We did not, however.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1839	lexical	\N	\N	1838	{"text": "Not a word came to us either from Wiggins or from the other agencies.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1840	lexical	\N	\N	1839	{"text": "There were articles in most of the papers upon the Norwood tragedy.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1841	lexical	\N	\N	1840	{"text": "They all appeared to be rather hostile to the unfortunate Thaddeus Sholto.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1842	lexical	\N	\N	1841	{"text": "No fresh details were to be found, however, in any of them, save that an inquest was to be held upon the following day.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1843	lexical	\N	\N	1842	{"text": "I walked over to Camberwell in the evening to report our ill success to the ladies, and on my return I found Holmes dejected and somewhat morose.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1844	lexical	\N	\N	1843	{"text": "He would hardly reply to my questions, and busied himself all evening in an abstruse chemical analysis which involved much heating of retorts and distilling of vapours, ending at last in a smell which fairly drove me out of the apartment.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1845	lexical	\N	\N	1844	{"text": "Up to the small hours of the morning I could hear the clinking of his test-tubes which told me that he was still engaged in his malodorous experiment.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1846	lexical	\N	\N	1845	{"text": "In the early dawn I woke with a start, and was surprised to find him standing by my bedside, clad in a rude sailor dress with a pea-jacket, and a coarse red scarf round his neck.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1847	lexical	\N	\N	1846	{"text": "“I am off down the river, Watson,” said he.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1848	lexical	\N	\N	1847	{"text": "“I have been turning it over in my mind, and I can see only one way out of it.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1849	lexical	\N	\N	1848	{"text": "It is worth trying, at all events.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1850	lexical	\N	\N	1849	{"text": "“Surely I can come with you, then?”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1851	lexical	\N	\N	1850	{"text": "said I.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1852	lexical	\N	\N	1851	{"text": "“No; you can be much more useful if you will remain here as my representative.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1853	lexical	\N	\N	1852	{"text": "I am loath to go, for it is quite on the cards that some message may come during the day, though Wiggins was despondent about it last night.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1854	lexical	\N	\N	1853	{"text": "I want you to open all notes and telegrams, and to act on your own judgment if any news should come.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1855	lexical	\N	\N	1854	{"text": "Can I rely upon you?”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1856	lexical	\N	\N	1855	{"text": "“Most certainly.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1857	lexical	\N	\N	1856	{"text": "“I am afraid that you will not be able to wire to me, for I can hardly tell yet where I may find myself.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1858	lexical	\N	\N	1857	{"text": "If I am in luck, however, I may not be gone so very long.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1859	lexical	\N	\N	1858	{"text": "I shall have news of some sort or other before I get back.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1860	lexical	\N	\N	1859	{"text": "I had heard nothing of him by breakfast-time.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1861	lexical	\N	\N	1860	{"text": "On opening the _Standard_, however, I found that there was a fresh allusion to the business.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1862	lexical	\N	\N	1861	{"text": "“With reference to the Upper Norwood tragedy,” it remarked, “we have reason to believe that the matter promises to be even more complex and mysterious than was originally supposed.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1863	lexical	\N	\N	1862	{"text": "Fresh evidence has shown that it is quite impossible that Mr. Thaddeus Sholto could have been in any way concerned in the matter.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1864	lexical	\N	\N	1863	{"text": "He and the housekeeper, Mrs. Bernstone, were both released yesterday evening.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1865	lexical	\N	\N	1864	{"text": "It is believed, however, that the police have a clue as to the real culprits, and that it is being prosecuted by Mr. Athelney Jones, of Scotland Yard, with all his well-known energy and sagacity.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1866	lexical	\N	\N	1865	{"text": "Further arrests may be expected at any moment.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1867	lexical	\N	\N	1866	{"text": "“That is satisfactory so far as it goes,” thought I.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1868	lexical	\N	\N	1867	{"text": "“Friend Sholto is safe, at any rate.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1869	lexical	\N	\N	1868	{"text": "I wonder what the fresh clue may be; though it seems to be a stereotyped form whenever the police have made a blunder.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1870	lexical	\N	\N	1869	{"text": "I tossed the paper down upon the table, but at that moment my eye caught an advertisement in the agony column.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1871	lexical	\N	\N	1870	{"text": "It ran in this way:", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1872	lexical	\N	\N	1871	{"text": "—Whereas Mordecai Smith, boatman, and his son, Jim, left Smith’s Wharf at or about three o’clock last Tuesday morning in the steam launch _Aurora_, black with two red stripes, funnel black with a white band, the sum of five pounds will be paid to any one who can give information to Mrs. Smith, at Smith’s Wharf, or at 221_b_ Baker Street, as to the whereabouts of the said Mordecai Smith and the launch _Aurora_.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1873	lexical	\N	\N	1872	{"text": "ora_.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1874	lexical	\N	\N	1873	{"text": "This was clearly Holmes’s doing.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1875	lexical	\N	\N	1874	{"text": "The Baker Street address was enough to prove that.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1876	lexical	\N	\N	1875	{"text": "It struck me as rather ingenious, because it might be read by the fugitives without their seeing in it more than the natural anxiety of a wife for her missing husband.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1877	lexical	\N	\N	1876	{"text": "It was a long day.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1878	lexical	\N	\N	1877	{"text": "Every time that a knock came to the door, or a sharp step passed in the street, I imagined that it was either Holmes returning or an answer to his advertisement.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1879	lexical	\N	\N	1878	{"text": "I tried to read, but my thoughts would wander off to our strange quest and to the ill-assorted and villainous pair whom we were pursuing.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1880	lexical	\N	\N	1879	{"text": "Could there be, I wondered, some radical flaw in my companion’s reasoning.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1881	lexical	\N	\N	1880	{"text": "Might he be suffering from some huge self-deception?", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1882	lexical	\N	\N	1881	{"text": "Was it not possible that his nimble and speculative mind had built up this wild theory upon faulty premises?", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1883	lexical	\N	\N	1882	{"text": "I had never known him to be wrong; and yet the keenest reasoner may occasionally be deceived.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1884	lexical	\N	\N	1883	{"text": "He was likely, I thought, to fall into error through the over-refinement of his logic,—his preference for a subtle and bizarre explanation when a plainer and more commonplace one lay ready to his hand.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1885	lexical	\N	\N	1884	{"text": "Yet, on the other hand, I had myself seen the evidence, and I had heard the reasons for his deductions.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1886	lexical	\N	\N	1885	{"text": "When I looked back on the long chain of curious circumstances, many of them trivial in themselves, but all tending in the same direction, I could not disguise from myself that even if Holmes’s explanation were incorrect the true theory must be equally _outré_ and startling.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1887	lexical	\N	\N	1886	{"text": "At three o’clock in the afternoon there was a loud peal at the bell, an authoritative voice in the hall, and, to my surprise, no less a person than Mr. Athelney Jones was shown up to me.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1888	lexical	\N	\N	1887	{"text": "Very different was he, however, from the brusque and masterful professor of common sense who had taken over the case so confidently at Upper Norwood.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1889	lexical	\N	\N	1888	{"text": "His expression was downcast, and his bearing meek and even apologetic.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1890	lexical	\N	\N	1889	{"text": "“Good-day, sir; good-day,” said he.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1891	lexical	\N	\N	1890	{"text": "“Mr. Sherlock Holmes is out, I understand.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1892	lexical	\N	\N	1891	{"text": "“Yes, and I cannot be sure when he will be back.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1893	lexical	\N	\N	1892	{"text": "But perhaps you would care to wait.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1894	lexical	\N	\N	1893	{"text": "Take that chair and try one of these cigars.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1895	lexical	\N	\N	1894	{"text": "“Thank you; I don’t mind if I do,” said he, mopping his face with a red bandanna handkerchief.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1896	lexical	\N	\N	1895	{"text": "“And a whiskey-and-soda?”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1897	lexical	\N	\N	1896	{"text": "“Well, half a glass.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1898	lexical	\N	\N	1897	{"text": "It is very hot for the time of year; and I have had a good deal to worry and try me.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1899	lexical	\N	\N	1898	{"text": "You know my theory about this Norwood case?”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1900	lexical	\N	\N	1899	{"text": "“I remember that you expressed one.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1901	lexical	\N	\N	1900	{"text": "“Well, I have been obliged to reconsider it.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1902	lexical	\N	\N	1901	{"text": "I had my net drawn tightly round Mr. Sholto, sir, when pop he went through a hole in the middle of it.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1903	lexical	\N	\N	1902	{"text": "He was able to prove an alibi which could not be shaken.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1904	lexical	\N	\N	1903	{"text": "From the time that he left his brother’s room he was never out of sight of some one or other.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1905	lexical	\N	\N	1904	{"text": "So it could not be he who climbed over roofs and through trap-doors.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1906	lexical	\N	\N	1905	{"text": "It’s a very dark case, and my professional credit is at stake.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1907	lexical	\N	\N	1906	{"text": "I should be very glad of a little assistance.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1908	lexical	\N	\N	1907	{"text": "“We all need help sometimes,” said I.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1909	lexical	\N	\N	1908	{"text": "“Your friend Mr. Sherlock Holmes is a wonderful man, sir,” said he, in a husky and confidential voice.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1910	lexical	\N	\N	1909	{"text": "“He’s a man who is not to be beat.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1911	lexical	\N	\N	1910	{"text": "I have known that young man go into a good many cases, but I never saw the case yet that he could not throw a light upon.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1912	lexical	\N	\N	1911	{"text": "He is irregular in his methods, and a little quick perhaps in jumping at theories, but, on the whole, I think he would have made a most promising officer, and I don’t care who knows it.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1913	lexical	\N	\N	1912	{"text": "I have had a wire from him this morning, by which I understand that he has got some clue to this Sholto business.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1914	lexical	\N	\N	1913	{"text": "Here is the message.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1915	lexical	\N	\N	1914	{"text": "He took the telegram out of his pocket, and handed it to me.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1916	lexical	\N	\N	1915	{"text": "It was dated from Poplar at twelve o’clock.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1917	lexical	\N	\N	1916	{"text": "“Go to Baker Street at once,” it said.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1918	lexical	\N	\N	1917	{"text": "“If I have not returned, wait for me.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1919	lexical	\N	\N	1918	{"text": "I am close on the track of the Sholto gang.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1920	lexical	\N	\N	1919	{"text": "You can come with us to-night if you want to be in at the finish.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1921	lexical	\N	\N	1920	{"text": "“This sounds well.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1922	lexical	\N	\N	1921	{"text": "He has evidently picked up the scent again,” said I.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1923	lexical	\N	\N	1922	{"text": "“Ah, then he has been at fault too,” exclaimed Jones, with evident satisfaction.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1924	lexical	\N	\N	1923	{"text": "“Even the best of us are thrown off sometimes.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1925	lexical	\N	\N	1924	{"text": "Of course this may prove to be a false alarm; but it is my duty as an officer of the law to allow no chance to slip.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1926	lexical	\N	\N	1925	{"text": "But there is some one at the door.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1927	lexical	\N	\N	1926	{"text": "Perhaps this is he.”", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1928	lexical	\N	\N	1927	{"text": "A heavy step was heard ascending the stair, with a great wheezing and rattling as from a man who was sorely put to it for breath.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1929	lexical	\N	\N	1928	{"text": "Once or twice he stopped, as though the climb were too much for him, but at last he made his way to our door and entered.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1930	lexical	\N	\N	1929	{"text": "His appearance corresponded to the sounds which we had heard.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1931	lexical	\N	\N	1930	{"text": "He was an aged man, clad in seafaring garb, with an old pea-jacket buttoned up to his throat.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1932	lexical	\N	\N	1931	{"text": "His back was bowed, his knees were shaky, and his breathing was painfully asthmatic.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1977	lexical	\N	\N	1976	{"text": "But where is the old man?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1933	lexical	\N	\N	1932	{"text": "As he leaned upon a thick oaken cudgel his shoulders heaved in the effort to draw the air into his lungs.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1934	lexical	\N	\N	1933	{"text": "He had a coloured scarf round his chin, and I could see little of his face save a pair of keen dark eyes, overhung by bushy white brows, and long grey side-whiskers.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1935	lexical	\N	\N	1934	{"text": "Altogether he gave me the impression of a respectable master mariner who had fallen into years and poverty.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1936	lexical	\N	\N	1935	{"text": "“What is it, my man?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1937	lexical	\N	\N	1936	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1938	lexical	\N	\N	1937	{"text": "He looked about him in the slow methodical fashion of old age.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1939	lexical	\N	\N	1938	{"text": "“Is Mr. Sherlock Holmes here?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1940	lexical	\N	\N	1939	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1941	lexical	\N	\N	1940	{"text": "“No; but I am acting for him.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1942	lexical	\N	\N	1941	{"text": "You can tell me any message you have for him.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1943	lexical	\N	\N	1942	{"text": "“It was to him himself I was to tell it,” said he.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1944	lexical	\N	\N	1943	{"text": "“But I tell you that I am acting for him.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1945	lexical	\N	\N	1944	{"text": "Was it about Mordecai Smith’s boat?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1946	lexical	\N	\N	1945	{"text": "“Yes.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1947	lexical	\N	\N	1946	{"text": "I knows well where it is.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1948	lexical	\N	\N	1947	{"text": "An’ I knows where the men he is after are.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1949	lexical	\N	\N	1948	{"text": "An’ I knows where the treasure is.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1950	lexical	\N	\N	1949	{"text": "I knows all about it.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1951	lexical	\N	\N	1950	{"text": "“Then tell me, and I shall let him know.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1952	lexical	\N	\N	1951	{"text": "“It was to him I was to tell it,” he repeated, with the petulant obstinacy of a very old man.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1953	lexical	\N	\N	1952	{"text": "“Well, you must wait for him.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1954	lexical	\N	\N	1953	{"text": "“No, no; I ain’t goin’ to lose a whole day to please no one.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1955	lexical	\N	\N	1954	{"text": "If Mr. Holmes ain’t here, then Mr. Holmes must find it all out for himself.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1956	lexical	\N	\N	1955	{"text": "I don’t care about the look of either of you, and I won’t tell a word.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1957	lexical	\N	\N	1956	{"text": "He shuffled towards the door, but Athelney Jones got in front of him.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1958	lexical	\N	\N	1957	{"text": "“Wait a bit, my friend,” said he.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1959	lexical	\N	\N	1958	{"text": "“You have important information, and you must not walk off.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1960	lexical	\N	\N	1959	{"text": "We shall keep you, whether you like or not, until our friend returns.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1961	lexical	\N	\N	1960	{"text": "The old man made a little run towards the door, but, as Athelney Jones put his broad back up against it, he recognised the uselessness of resistance.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1962	lexical	\N	\N	1961	{"text": "“Pretty sort o’ treatment this!”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1963	lexical	\N	\N	1962	{"text": "he cried, stamping his stick.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1964	lexical	\N	\N	1963	{"text": "“I come here to see a gentleman, and you two, who I never saw in my life, seize me and treat me in this fashion!”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1965	lexical	\N	\N	1964	{"text": "“You will be none the worse,” I said.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1966	lexical	\N	\N	1965	{"text": "“We shall recompense you for the loss of your time.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1967	lexical	\N	\N	1966	{"text": "Sit over here on the sofa, and you will not have long to wait.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1968	lexical	\N	\N	1967	{"text": "He came across sullenly enough, and seated himself with his face resting on his hands.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1969	lexical	\N	\N	1968	{"text": "Jones and I resumed our cigars and our talk.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1970	lexical	\N	\N	1969	{"text": "Suddenly, however, Holmes’s voice broke in upon us.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1971	lexical	\N	\N	1970	{"text": "“I think that you might offer me a cigar too,” he said.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1972	lexical	\N	\N	1971	{"text": "We both started in our chairs.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1973	lexical	\N	\N	1972	{"text": "There was Holmes sitting close to us with an air of quiet amusement.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1978	lexical	\N	\N	1977	{"text": "“Here is the old man,” said he, holding out a heap of white hair.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1979	lexical	\N	\N	1978	{"text": "“Here he is,—wig, whiskers, eyebrows, and all.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1980	lexical	\N	\N	1979	{"text": "I thought my disguise was pretty good, but I hardly expected that it would stand that test.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1981	lexical	\N	\N	1980	{"text": "“Ah, You rogue!”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1982	lexical	\N	\N	1981	{"text": "cried Jones, highly delighted.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1983	lexical	\N	\N	1982	{"text": "“You would have made an actor, and a rare one.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1984	lexical	\N	\N	1983	{"text": "You had the proper workhouse cough, and those weak legs of yours are worth ten pounds a week.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1985	lexical	\N	\N	1984	{"text": "I thought I knew the glint of your eye, though.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1986	lexical	\N	\N	1985	{"text": "You didn’t get away from us so easily, You see.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1987	lexical	\N	\N	1986	{"text": "“I have been working in that get-up all day,” said he, lighting his cigar.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1988	lexical	\N	\N	1987	{"text": "“You see, a good many of the criminal classes begin to know me,—especially since our friend here took to publishing some of my cases: so I can only go on the war-path under some simple disguise like this.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1989	lexical	\N	\N	1988	{"text": "You got my wire?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1990	lexical	\N	\N	1989	{"text": "“Yes; that was what brought me here.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1991	lexical	\N	\N	1990	{"text": "“How has your case prospered?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1992	lexical	\N	\N	1991	{"text": "“It has all come to nothing.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1993	lexical	\N	\N	1992	{"text": "I have had to release two of my prisoners, and there is no evidence against the other two.”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1994	lexical	\N	\N	1993	{"text": "“Never mind.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1995	lexical	\N	\N	1994	{"text": "We shall give you two others in the place of them.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1996	lexical	\N	\N	1995	{"text": "But you must put yourself under my orders.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1997	lexical	\N	\N	1996	{"text": "You are welcome to all the official credit, but you must act on the line that I point out.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1998	lexical	\N	\N	1997	{"text": "Is that agreed?”", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_1999	lexical	\N	\N	1998	{"text": "“Entirely, if you will help me to the men.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2000	lexical	\N	\N	1999	{"text": "“Well, then, in the first place I shall want a fast police-boat—a steam launch—to be at the Westminster Stairs at seven o’clock.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2001	lexical	\N	\N	2000	{"text": "“That is easily managed.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2002	lexical	\N	\N	2001	{"text": "There is always one about there; but I can step across the road and telephone to make sure.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2003	lexical	\N	\N	2002	{"text": "“Then I shall want two stanch men, in case of resistance.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2004	lexical	\N	\N	2003	{"text": "“There will be two or three in the boat.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2005	lexical	\N	\N	2004	{"text": "What else?”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2006	lexical	\N	\N	2005	{"text": "“When we secure the men we shall get the treasure.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2007	lexical	\N	\N	2006	{"text": "I think that it would be a pleasure to my friend here to take the box round to the young lady to whom half of it rightfully belongs.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2008	lexical	\N	\N	2007	{"text": "—Eh, Watson?”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2009	lexical	\N	\N	2008	{"text": "e first to open it.—Eh, Watson?”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2010	lexical	\N	\N	2009	{"text": "“It would be a great pleasure to me.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2011	lexical	\N	\N	2010	{"text": "“Rather an irregular proceeding,” said Jones, shaking his head.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2012	lexical	\N	\N	2011	{"text": "“However, the whole thing is irregular, and I suppose we must wink at it.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2013	lexical	\N	\N	2012	{"text": "The treasure must afterwards be handed over to the authorities until after the official investigation.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2014	lexical	\N	\N	2013	{"text": "“Certainly.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2015	lexical	\N	\N	2014	{"text": "That is easily managed.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2016	lexical	\N	\N	2015	{"text": "One other point.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2017	lexical	\N	\N	2016	{"text": "I should much like to have a few details about this matter from the lips of Jonathan Small himself.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2018	lexical	\N	\N	2017	{"text": "You know I like to work the detail of my cases out.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2019	lexical	\N	\N	2018	{"text": "There is no objection to my having an unofficial interview with him, either here in my rooms or elsewhere, as long as he is efficiently guarded?”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2020	lexical	\N	\N	2019	{"text": "“Well, you are master of the situation.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2021	lexical	\N	\N	2020	{"text": "I have had no proof yet of the existence of this Jonathan Small.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2022	lexical	\N	\N	2021	{"text": "However, if you can catch him I don’t see how I can refuse you an interview with him.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2023	lexical	\N	\N	2022	{"text": "“That is understood, then?”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2024	lexical	\N	\N	2023	{"text": "“Perfectly.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2025	lexical	\N	\N	2024	{"text": "Is there anything else?”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2026	lexical	\N	\N	2025	{"text": "“Only that I insist upon your dining with us.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2027	lexical	\N	\N	2026	{"text": "It will be ready in half an hour.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2028	lexical	\N	\N	2027	{"text": "—Watson, you have never yet recognised my merits as a housekeeper.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2029	lexical	\N	\N	2028	{"text": "e in white wines.—Watson, you have never yet recognised my merits as a housekeeper.”", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2030	lexical	\N	\N	2029	{"text": "Chapter X The End of the Islander", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2031	lexical	\N	\N	2030	{"text": "Our meal was a merry one.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2032	lexical	\N	\N	2031	{"text": "Holmes could talk exceedingly well when he chose, and that night he did choose.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2033	lexical	\N	\N	2032	{"text": "He appeared to be in a state of nervous exaltation.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2034	lexical	\N	\N	2033	{"text": "I have never known him so brilliant.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2035	lexical	\N	\N	2034	{"text": "He spoke on a quick succession of subjects,—on miracle-plays, on mediæval pottery, on Stradivarius violins, on the Buddhism of Ceylon, and on the war-ships of the future,—handling each as though he had made a special study of it.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2036	lexical	\N	\N	2035	{"text": "His bright humour marked the reaction from his black depression of the preceding days.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2037	lexical	\N	\N	2036	{"text": "Athelney Jones proved to be a sociable soul in his hours of relaxation, and faced his dinner with the air of a _bon vivant_.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2038	lexical	\N	\N	2037	{"text": "For myself, I felt elated at the thought that we were nearing the end of our task, and I caught something of Holmes’s gaiety.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2039	lexical	\N	\N	2038	{"text": "None of us alluded during dinner to the cause which had brought us together.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2040	lexical	\N	\N	2039	{"text": "When the cloth was cleared, Holmes glanced at his watch, and filled up three glasses with port.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2041	lexical	\N	\N	2040	{"text": "“One bumper,” said he, “to the success of our little expedition.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2042	lexical	\N	\N	2041	{"text": "And now it is high time we were off.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2043	lexical	\N	\N	2042	{"text": "Have you a pistol, Watson?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2044	lexical	\N	\N	2043	{"text": "“I have my old service-revolver in my desk.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2045	lexical	\N	\N	2044	{"text": "“You had best take it, then.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2046	lexical	\N	\N	2045	{"text": "It is well to be prepared.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2047	lexical	\N	\N	2046	{"text": "I see that the cab is at the door.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2048	lexical	\N	\N	2047	{"text": "I ordered it for half-past six.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2049	lexical	\N	\N	2048	{"text": "It was a little past seven before we reached the Westminster wharf, and found our launch awaiting us.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2050	lexical	\N	\N	2049	{"text": "Holmes eyed it critically.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2051	lexical	\N	\N	2050	{"text": "“Is there anything to mark it as a police-boat?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2052	lexical	\N	\N	2051	{"text": "“Yes,—that green lamp at the side.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2053	lexical	\N	\N	2052	{"text": "“Then take it off.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2054	lexical	\N	\N	2053	{"text": "The small change was made, we stepped on board, and the ropes were cast off.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2055	lexical	\N	\N	2054	{"text": "Jones, Holmes, and I sat in the stern.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2056	lexical	\N	\N	2055	{"text": "There was one man at the rudder, one to tend the engines, and two burly police-inspectors forward.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2057	lexical	\N	\N	2056	{"text": "“Where to?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2058	lexical	\N	\N	2057	{"text": "asked Jones.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_81	section	\N	Section 81	80	{"wordCount": 652}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2060	lexical	\N	\N	2059	{"text": "Tell them to stop opposite Jacobson’s Yard.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2061	lexical	\N	\N	2060	{"text": "Our craft was evidently a very fast one.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2062	lexical	\N	\N	2061	{"text": "We shot past the long lines of loaded barges as though they were stationary.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2063	lexical	\N	\N	2062	{"text": "Holmes smiled with satisfaction as we overhauled a river steamer and left her behind us.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2064	lexical	\N	\N	2063	{"text": "“We ought to be able to catch anything on the river,” he said.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2065	lexical	\N	\N	2064	{"text": "“Well, hardly that.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2066	lexical	\N	\N	2065	{"text": "But there are not many launches to beat us.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2067	lexical	\N	\N	2066	{"text": "“We shall have to catch the _Aurora_, and she has a name for being a clipper.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2068	lexical	\N	\N	2067	{"text": "I will tell you how the land lies, Watson.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2069	lexical	\N	\N	2068	{"text": "You recollect how annoyed I was at being balked by so small a thing?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2070	lexical	\N	\N	2069	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2071	lexical	\N	\N	2070	{"text": "“Well, I gave my mind a thorough rest by plunging into a chemical analysis.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2072	lexical	\N	\N	2071	{"text": "One of our greatest statesmen has said that a change of work is the best rest.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2073	lexical	\N	\N	2072	{"text": "So it is.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2074	lexical	\N	\N	2073	{"text": "When I had succeeded in dissolving the hydrocarbon which I was at work at, I came back to our problem of the Sholtos, and thought the whole matter out again.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2075	lexical	\N	\N	2074	{"text": "My boys had been up the river and down the river without result.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2076	lexical	\N	\N	2075	{"text": "The launch was not at any landing-stage or wharf, nor had it returned.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2077	lexical	\N	\N	2076	{"text": "Yet it could hardly have been scuttled to hide their traces,—though that always remained as a possible hypothesis if all else failed.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2078	lexical	\N	\N	2077	{"text": "I knew this man Small had a certain degree of low cunning, but I did not think him capable of anything in the nature of delicate finesse.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2079	lexical	\N	\N	2078	{"text": "That is usually a product of higher education.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2080	lexical	\N	\N	2079	{"text": "I then reflected that since he had certainly been in London some time—as we had evidence that he maintained a continual watch over Pondicherry Lodge—he could hardly leave at a moment’s notice, but would need some little time, if it were only a day, to arrange his affairs.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2081	lexical	\N	\N	2080	{"text": "That was the balance of probability, at any rate.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2082	lexical	\N	\N	2081	{"text": "“It seems to me to be a little weak,” said I.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2083	lexical	\N	\N	2082	{"text": "“It is more probable that he had arranged his affairs before ever he set out upon his expedition.”", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2084	lexical	\N	\N	2083	{"text": "“No, I hardly think so.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2085	lexical	\N	\N	2084	{"text": "This lair of his would be too valuable a retreat in case of need for him to give it up until he was sure that he could do without it.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2086	lexical	\N	\N	2085	{"text": "But a second consideration struck me.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2087	lexical	\N	\N	2086	{"text": "Jonathan Small must have felt that the peculiar appearance of his companion, however much he may have top-coated him, would give rise to gossip, and possibly be associated with this Norwood tragedy.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2088	lexical	\N	\N	2087	{"text": "He was quite sharp enough to see that.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2089	lexical	\N	\N	2088	{"text": "They had started from their head-quarters under cover of darkness, and he would wish to get back before it was broad light.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2090	lexical	\N	\N	2089	{"text": "Now, it was past three o’clock, according to Mrs. Smith, when they got the boat.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2091	lexical	\N	\N	2090	{"text": "It would be quite bright, and people would be about in an hour or so.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2092	lexical	\N	\N	2091	{"text": "Therefore, I argued, they did not go very far.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2093	lexical	\N	\N	2092	{"text": "They paid Smith well to hold his tongue, reserved his launch for the final escape, and hurried to their lodgings with the treasure-box.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2094	lexical	\N	\N	2093	{"text": "In a couple of nights, when they had time to see what view the papers took, and whether there was any suspicion, they would make their way under cover of darkness to some ship at Gravesend or in the Downs, where no doubt they had already arranged for passages to America or the Colonies.”", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2095	lexical	\N	\N	2094	{"text": "“But the launch?", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2096	lexical	\N	\N	2095	{"text": "They could not have taken that to their lodgings.”", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2097	lexical	\N	\N	2096	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2098	lexical	\N	\N	2097	{"text": "I argued that the launch must be no great way off, in spite of its invisibility.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2099	lexical	\N	\N	2098	{"text": "I then put myself in the place of Small, and looked at it as a man of his capacity would.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2100	lexical	\N	\N	2099	{"text": "He would probably consider that to send back the launch or to keep it at a wharf would make pursuit easy if the police did happen to get on his track.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2101	lexical	\N	\N	2100	{"text": "How, then, could he conceal the launch and yet have her at hand when wanted?", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2102	lexical	\N	\N	2101	{"text": "I wondered what I should do myself if I were in his shoes.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2103	lexical	\N	\N	2102	{"text": "I could only think of one way of doing it.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2104	lexical	\N	\N	2103	{"text": "I might hand the launch over to some boat-builder or repairer, with directions to make a trifling change in her.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2105	lexical	\N	\N	2104	{"text": "She would then be removed to his shed or yard, and so be effectually concealed, while at the same time I could have her at a few hours’ notice.”", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2106	lexical	\N	\N	2105	{"text": "“That seems simple enough.”", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2107	lexical	\N	\N	2106	{"text": "“It is just these very simple things which are extremely liable to be overlooked.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2108	lexical	\N	\N	2107	{"text": "However, I determined to act on the idea.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2109	lexical	\N	\N	2108	{"text": "I started at once in this harmless seaman’s rig and inquired at all the yards down the river.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2110	lexical	\N	\N	2109	{"text": "I drew blank at fifteen, but at the sixteenth—Jacobson’s—I learned that the _Aurora_ had been handed over to them two days ago by a wooden-legged man, with some trivial directions as to her rudder.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2111	lexical	\N	\N	2110	{"text": "‘There ain’t naught amiss with her rudder,’ said the foreman.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2112	lexical	\N	\N	2111	{"text": "‘There she lies, with the red streaks.’", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2113	lexical	\N	\N	2112	{"text": "At that moment who should come down but Mordecai Smith, the missing owner?", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2114	lexical	\N	\N	2113	{"text": "He was rather the worse for liquor.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2115	lexical	\N	\N	2114	{"text": "I should not, of course, have known him, but he bellowed out his name and the name of his launch.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2116	lexical	\N	\N	2115	{"text": "‘I want her to-night at eight o’clock,’ said he,—‘eight o’clock sharp, mind, for I have two gentlemen who won’t be kept waiting.’", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2117	lexical	\N	\N	2116	{"text": "They had evidently paid him well, for he was very flush of money, chucking shillings about to the men.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2118	lexical	\N	\N	2117	{"text": "I followed him some distance, but he subsided into an ale-house: so I went back to the yard, and, happening to pick up one of my boys on the way, I stationed him as a sentry over the launch.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2119	lexical	\N	\N	2118	{"text": "He is to stand at water’s edge and wave his handkerchief to us when they start.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2120	lexical	\N	\N	2119	{"text": "We shall be lying off in the stream, and it will be a strange thing if we do not take men, treasure, and all.”", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2121	lexical	\N	\N	2120	{"text": "“You have planned it all very neatly, whether they are the right men or not,” said Jones; “but if the affair were in my hands I should have had a body of police in Jacobson’s Yard, and arrested them when they came down.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2122	lexical	\N	\N	2121	{"text": "“Which would have been never.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2123	lexical	\N	\N	2122	{"text": "This man Small is a pretty shrewd fellow.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2124	lexical	\N	\N	2123	{"text": "He would send a scout on ahead, and if anything made him suspicious lie snug for another week.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2125	lexical	\N	\N	2124	{"text": "“But you might have stuck to Mordecai Smith, and so been led to their hiding-place,” said I.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2126	lexical	\N	\N	2125	{"text": "“In that case I should have wasted my day.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2127	lexical	\N	\N	2126	{"text": "I think that it is a hundred to one against Smith knowing where they live.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2128	lexical	\N	\N	2127	{"text": "As long as he has liquor and good pay, why should he ask questions?", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2129	lexical	\N	\N	2128	{"text": "They send him messages what to do.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2130	lexical	\N	\N	2129	{"text": "No, I thought over every possible course, and this is the best.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2131	lexical	\N	\N	2130	{"text": "While this conversation had been proceeding, we had been shooting the long series of bridges which span the Thames.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2132	lexical	\N	\N	2131	{"text": "As we passed the City the last rays of the sun were gilding the cross upon the summit of St. Paul’s.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2133	lexical	\N	\N	2132	{"text": "It was twilight before we reached the Tower.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2134	lexical	\N	\N	2133	{"text": "“That is Jacobson’s Yard,” said Holmes, pointing to a bristle of masts and rigging on the Surrey side.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2135	lexical	\N	\N	2134	{"text": "“Cruise gently up and down here under cover of this string of lighters.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2136	lexical	\N	\N	2135	{"text": "He took a pair of night-glasses from his pocket and gazed some time at the shore.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2137	lexical	\N	\N	2136	{"text": "“I see my sentry at his post,” he remarked, “but no sign of a handkerchief.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2138	lexical	\N	\N	2137	{"text": "“Suppose we go down-stream a short way and lie in wait for them,” said Jones, eagerly.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2139	lexical	\N	\N	2138	{"text": "We were all eager by this time, even the policemen and stokers, who had a very vague idea of what was going forward.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2140	lexical	\N	\N	2139	{"text": "“We have no right to take anything for granted,” Holmes answered.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2141	lexical	\N	\N	2140	{"text": "“It is certainly ten to one that they go down-stream, but we cannot be certain.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2142	lexical	\N	\N	2141	{"text": "From this point we can see the entrance of the yard, and they can hardly see us.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2143	lexical	\N	\N	2142	{"text": "It will be a clear night and plenty of light.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2144	lexical	\N	\N	2143	{"text": "We must stay where we are.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2145	lexical	\N	\N	2144	{"text": "See how the folk swarm over yonder in the gaslight.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2146	lexical	\N	\N	2145	{"text": "“They are coming from work in the yard.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2147	lexical	\N	\N	2146	{"text": "“Dirty-looking rascals, but I suppose every one has some little immortal spark concealed about him.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2148	lexical	\N	\N	2147	{"text": "You would not think it, to look at them.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2149	lexical	\N	\N	2148	{"text": "There is no _a priori_ probability about it.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2150	lexical	\N	\N	2149	{"text": "A strange enigma is man!”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2151	lexical	\N	\N	2150	{"text": "“Some one calls him a soul concealed in an animal,” I suggested.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2152	lexical	\N	\N	2151	{"text": "“Winwood Reade is good upon the subject,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2153	lexical	\N	\N	2152	{"text": "“He remarks that, while the individual man is an insoluble puzzle, in the aggregate he becomes a mathematical certainty.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2154	lexical	\N	\N	2153	{"text": "You can, for example, never foretell what any one man will do, but you can say with precision what an average number will be up to.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2155	lexical	\N	\N	2154	{"text": "Individuals vary, but percentages remain constant.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2156	lexical	\N	\N	2155	{"text": "So says the statistician.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2157	lexical	\N	\N	2156	{"text": "But do I see a handkerchief?", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2158	lexical	\N	\N	2157	{"text": "Surely there is a white flutter over yonder.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2159	lexical	\N	\N	2158	{"text": "“Yes, it is your boy,” I cried.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2160	lexical	\N	\N	2159	{"text": "“I can see him plainly.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2161	lexical	\N	\N	2160	{"text": "“And there is the _Aurora_,” exclaimed Holmes, “and going like the devil!", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2162	lexical	\N	\N	2161	{"text": "Full speed ahead, engineer.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2163	lexical	\N	\N	2162	{"text": "Make after that launch with the yellow light.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2164	lexical	\N	\N	2163	{"text": "By heaven, I shall never forgive myself if she proves to have the heels of us!”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2165	lexical	\N	\N	2164	{"text": "She had slipped unseen through the yard-entrance and passed behind two or three small craft, so that she had fairly got her speed up before we saw her.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2166	lexical	\N	\N	2165	{"text": "Now she was flying down the stream, near in to the shore, going at a tremendous rate.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2167	lexical	\N	\N	2166	{"text": "Jones looked gravely at her and shook his head.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2168	lexical	\N	\N	2167	{"text": "“She is very fast,” he said.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2169	lexical	\N	\N	2168	{"text": "“I doubt if we shall catch her.”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2170	lexical	\N	\N	2169	{"text": "“We _must_ catch her!”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_82	section	\N	Section 82	81	{"wordCount": 617}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2171	lexical	\N	\N	2170	{"text": "cried Holmes, between his teeth.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2172	lexical	\N	\N	2171	{"text": "“Heap it on, stokers!", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2173	lexical	\N	\N	2172	{"text": "Make her do all she can!", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2174	lexical	\N	\N	2173	{"text": "If we burn the boat we must have them!”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2175	lexical	\N	\N	2174	{"text": "We were fairly after her now.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2176	lexical	\N	\N	2175	{"text": "The furnaces roared, and the powerful engines whizzed and clanked, like a great metallic heart.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2177	lexical	\N	\N	2176	{"text": "Her sharp, steep prow cut through the river-water and sent two rolling waves to right and to left of us.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2178	lexical	\N	\N	2177	{"text": "With every throb of the engines we sprang and quivered like a living thing.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2179	lexical	\N	\N	2178	{"text": "One great yellow lantern in our bows threw a long, flickering funnel of light in front of us.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2180	lexical	\N	\N	2179	{"text": "Right ahead a dark blur upon the water showed where the _Aurora_ lay, and the swirl of white foam behind her spoke of the pace at which she was going.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2181	lexical	\N	\N	2180	{"text": "We flashed past barges, steamers, merchant-vessels, in and out, behind this one and round the other.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2182	lexical	\N	\N	2181	{"text": "Voices hailed us out of the darkness, but still the _Aurora_ thundered on, and still we followed close upon her track.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2183	lexical	\N	\N	2182	{"text": "“Pile it on, men, pile it on!”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2184	lexical	\N	\N	2183	{"text": "cried Holmes, looking down into the engine-room, while the fierce glow from below beat upon his eager, aquiline face.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2185	lexical	\N	\N	2184	{"text": "“Get every pound of steam you can.”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2186	lexical	\N	\N	2185	{"text": "“I think we gain a little,” said Jones, with his eyes on the _Aurora_.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2187	lexical	\N	\N	2186	{"text": "“I am sure of it,” said I.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2188	lexical	\N	\N	2187	{"text": "“We shall be up with her in a very few minutes.”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2189	lexical	\N	\N	2188	{"text": "At that moment, however, as our evil fate would have it, a tug with three barges in tow blundered in between us.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2190	lexical	\N	\N	2189	{"text": "It was only by putting our helm hard down that we avoided a collision, and before we could round them and recover our way the _Aurora_ had gained a good two hundred yards.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2191	lexical	\N	\N	2190	{"text": "She was still, however, well in view, and the murky uncertain twilight was setting into a clear starlit night.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2192	lexical	\N	\N	2191	{"text": "Our boilers were strained to their utmost, and the frail shell vibrated and creaked with the fierce energy which was driving us along.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2193	lexical	\N	\N	2192	{"text": "We had shot through the Pool, past the West India Docks, down the long Deptford Reach, and up again after rounding the Isle of Dogs.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2194	lexical	\N	\N	2193	{"text": "The dull blur in front of us resolved itself now clearly enough into the dainty _Aurora_.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2195	lexical	\N	\N	2194	{"text": "Jones turned our search-light upon her, so that we could plainly see the figures upon her deck.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2196	lexical	\N	\N	2195	{"text": "One man sat by the stern, with something black between his knees over which he stooped.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2197	lexical	\N	\N	2196	{"text": "Beside him lay a dark mass which looked like a Newfoundland dog.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2198	lexical	\N	\N	2197	{"text": "The boy held the tiller, while against the red glare of the furnace I could see old Smith, stripped to the waist, and shovelling coals for dear life.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2199	lexical	\N	\N	2198	{"text": "They may have had some doubt at first as to whether we were really pursuing them, but now as we followed every winding and turning which they took there could no longer be any question about it.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2200	lexical	\N	\N	2199	{"text": "At Greenwich we were about three hundred paces behind them.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2201	lexical	\N	\N	2200	{"text": "At Blackwall we could not have been more than two hundred and fifty.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2202	lexical	\N	\N	2201	{"text": "I have coursed many creatures in many countries during my checkered career, but never did sport give me such a wild thrill as this mad, flying man-hunt down the Thames.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2203	lexical	\N	\N	2202	{"text": "Steadily we drew in upon them, yard by yard.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2204	lexical	\N	\N	2203	{"text": "In the silence of the night we could hear the panting and clanking of their machinery.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2205	lexical	\N	\N	2204	{"text": "The man in the stern still crouched upon the deck, and his arms were moving as though he were busy, while every now and then he would look up and measure with a glance the distance which still separated us.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2207	lexical	\N	\N	2206	{"text": "Jones yelled to them to stop.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2208	lexical	\N	\N	2207	{"text": "We were not more than four boat’s lengths behind them, both boats flying at a tremendous pace.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2209	lexical	\N	\N	2208	{"text": "It was a clear reach of the river, with Barking Level upon one side and the melancholy Plumstead Marshes upon the other.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2210	lexical	\N	\N	2209	{"text": "At our hail the man in the stern sprang up from the deck and shook his two clinched fists at us, cursing the while in a high, cracked voice.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2211	lexical	\N	\N	2210	{"text": "He was a good-sized, powerful man, and as he stood poising himself with legs astride I could see that from the thigh downwards there was but a wooden stump upon the right side.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2212	lexical	\N	\N	2211	{"text": "At the sound of his strident, angry cries there was movement in the huddled bundle upon the deck.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2213	lexical	\N	\N	2212	{"text": "It straightened itself into a little black man—the smallest I have ever seen—with a great, misshapen head and a shock of tangled, dishevelled hair.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2214	lexical	\N	\N	2213	{"text": "Holmes had already drawn his revolver, and I whipped out mine at the sight of this savage, distorted creature.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2215	lexical	\N	\N	2214	{"text": "He was wrapped in some sort of dark ulster or blanket, which left only his face exposed; but that face was enough to give a man a sleepless night.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2216	lexical	\N	\N	2215	{"text": "Never have I seen features so deeply marked with all bestiality and cruelty.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2217	lexical	\N	\N	2216	{"text": "His small eyes glowed and burned with a sombre light, and his thick lips were writhed back from his teeth, which grinned and chattered at us with a half animal fury.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2218	lexical	\N	\N	2217	{"text": "“Fire if he raises his hand,” said Holmes, quietly.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2219	lexical	\N	\N	2218	{"text": "We were within a boat’s-length by this time, and almost within touch of our quarry.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2220	lexical	\N	\N	2219	{"text": "I can see the two of them now as they stood, the white man with his legs far apart, shrieking out curses, and the unhallowed dwarf with his hideous face, and his strong yellow teeth gnashing at us in the light of our lantern.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2221	lexical	\N	\N	2220	{"text": "It was well that we had so clear a view of him.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2222	lexical	\N	\N	2221	{"text": "Even as we looked he plucked out from under his covering a short, round piece of wood, like a school-ruler, and clapped it to his lips.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2223	lexical	\N	\N	2222	{"text": "Our pistols rang out together.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2224	lexical	\N	\N	2223	{"text": "He whirled round, threw up his arms, and with a kind of choking cough fell sideways into the stream.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2225	lexical	\N	\N	2224	{"text": "I caught one glimpse of his venomous, menacing eyes amid the white swirl of the waters.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2226	lexical	\N	\N	2225	{"text": "At the same moment the wooden-legged man threw himself upon the rudder and put it hard down, so that his boat made straight in for the southern bank, while we shot past her stern, only clearing her by a few feet.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2227	lexical	\N	\N	2226	{"text": "We were round after her in an instant, but she was already nearly at the bank.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2228	lexical	\N	\N	2227	{"text": "It was a wild and desolate place, where the moon glimmered upon a wide expanse of marsh-land, with pools of stagnant water and beds of decaying vegetation.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2229	lexical	\N	\N	2228	{"text": "The launch with a dull thud ran up upon the mud-bank, with her bow in the air and her stern flush with the water.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2230	lexical	\N	\N	2229	{"text": "The fugitive sprang out, but his stump instantly sank its whole length into the sodden soil.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2231	lexical	\N	\N	2230	{"text": "In vain he struggled and writhed.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2232	lexical	\N	\N	2231	{"text": "Not one step could he possibly take either forwards or backwards.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2233	lexical	\N	\N	2232	{"text": "He yelled in impotent rage, and kicked frantically into the mud with his other foot, but his struggles only bored his wooden pin the deeper into the sticky bank.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2234	lexical	\N	\N	2233	{"text": "When we brought our launch alongside he was so firmly anchored that it was only by throwing the end of a rope over his shoulders that we were able to haul him out, and to drag him, like some evil fish, over our side.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2235	lexical	\N	\N	2234	{"text": "The two Smiths, father and son, sat sullenly in their launch, but came aboard meekly enough when commanded.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2236	lexical	\N	\N	2235	{"text": "The _Aurora_ herself we hauled off and made fast to our stern.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2237	lexical	\N	\N	2236	{"text": "A solid iron chest of Indian workmanship stood upon the deck.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2238	lexical	\N	\N	2237	{"text": "This, there could be no question, was the same that had contained the ill-omened treasure of the Sholtos.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2239	lexical	\N	\N	2238	{"text": "There was no key, but it was of considerable weight, so we transferred it carefully to our own little cabin.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2240	lexical	\N	\N	2239	{"text": "As we steamed slowly up-stream again, we flashed our search-light in every direction, but there was no sign of the Islander.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2241	lexical	\N	\N	2240	{"text": "Somewhere in the dark ooze at the bottom of the Thames lie the bones of that strange visitor to our shores.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2242	lexical	\N	\N	2241	{"text": "“See here,” said Holmes, pointing to the wooden hatchway.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2243	lexical	\N	\N	2242	{"text": "“We were hardly quick enough with our pistols.”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2244	lexical	\N	\N	2243	{"text": "There, sure enough, just behind where we had been standing, stuck one of those murderous darts which we knew so well.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2245	lexical	\N	\N	2244	{"text": "It must have whizzed between us at the instant that we fired.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2246	lexical	\N	\N	2245	{"text": "Holmes smiled at it and shrugged his shoulders in his easy fashion, but I confess that it turned me sick to think of the horrible death which had passed so close to us that night.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2247	lexical	\N	\N	2246	{"text": "Chapter XI The Great Agra Treasure", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2248	lexical	\N	\N	2247	{"text": "Our captive sat in the cabin opposite to the iron box which he had done so much and waited so long to gain.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2249	lexical	\N	\N	2248	{"text": "He was a sunburned, reckless-eyed fellow, with a network of lines and wrinkles all over his mahogany features, which told of a hard, open-air life.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2250	lexical	\N	\N	2249	{"text": "There was a singular prominence about his bearded chin which marked a man who was not to be easily turned from his purpose.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2251	lexical	\N	\N	2250	{"text": "His age may have been fifty or thereabouts, for his black, curly hair was thickly shot with grey.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2252	lexical	\N	\N	2251	{"text": "His face in repose was not an unpleasing one, though his heavy brows and aggressive chin gave him, as I had lately seen, a terrible expression when moved to anger.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2253	lexical	\N	\N	2252	{"text": "He sat now with his handcuffed hands upon his lap, and his head sunk upon his breast, while he looked with his keen, twinkling eyes at the box which had been the cause of his ill-doings.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2254	lexical	\N	\N	2253	{"text": "It seemed to me that there was more sorrow than anger in his rigid and contained countenance.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2255	lexical	\N	\N	2254	{"text": "Once he looked up at me with a gleam of something like humour in his eyes.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2256	lexical	\N	\N	2255	{"text": "“Well, Jonathan Small,” said Holmes, lighting a cigar, “I am sorry that it has come to this.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2257	lexical	\N	\N	2256	{"text": "“And so am I, sir,” he answered, frankly.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2258	lexical	\N	\N	2257	{"text": "“I don’t believe that I can swing over the job.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2259	lexical	\N	\N	2258	{"text": "I give you my word on the book that I never raised hand against Mr. Sholto.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2260	lexical	\N	\N	2259	{"text": "It was that little hell-hound Tonga who shot one of his cursed darts into him.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2261	lexical	\N	\N	2260	{"text": "I had no part in it, sir.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2262	lexical	\N	\N	2261	{"text": "I was as grieved as if it had been my blood-relation.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2263	lexical	\N	\N	2262	{"text": "I welted the little devil with the slack end of the rope for it, but it was done, and I could not undo it again.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2264	lexical	\N	\N	2263	{"text": "“Have a cigar,” said Holmes; “and you had best take a pull out of my flask, for you are very wet.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2265	lexical	\N	\N	2264	{"text": "How could you expect so small and weak a man as this black fellow to overpower Mr. Sholto and hold him while you were climbing the rope?”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2266	lexical	\N	\N	2265	{"text": "“You seem to know as much about it as if you were there, sir.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2267	lexical	\N	\N	2266	{"text": "The truth is that I hoped to find the room clear.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2268	lexical	\N	\N	2267	{"text": "I knew the habits of the house pretty well, and it was the time when Mr. Sholto usually went down to his supper.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2269	lexical	\N	\N	2268	{"text": "I shall make no secret of the business.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2270	lexical	\N	\N	2269	{"text": "The best defence that I can make is just the simple truth.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2271	lexical	\N	\N	2270	{"text": "Now, if it had been the old major I would have swung for him with a light heart.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2272	lexical	\N	\N	2271	{"text": "I would have thought no more of knifing him than of smoking this cigar.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2273	lexical	\N	\N	2272	{"text": "But it’s cursed hard that I should be lagged over this young Sholto, with whom I had no quarrel whatever.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2274	lexical	\N	\N	2273	{"text": "“You are under the charge of Mr. Athelney Jones, of Scotland Yard.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2275	lexical	\N	\N	2274	{"text": "He is going to bring you up to my rooms, and I shall ask you for a true account of the matter.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2276	lexical	\N	\N	2275	{"text": "You must make a clean breast of it, for if you do I hope that I may be of use to you.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2277	lexical	\N	\N	2276	{"text": "I think I can prove that the poison acts so quickly that the man was dead before ever you reached the room.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2278	lexical	\N	\N	2277	{"text": "“That he was, sir.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2279	lexical	\N	\N	2278	{"text": "I never got such a turn in my life as when I saw him grinning at me with his head on his shoulder as I climbed through the window.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2280	lexical	\N	\N	2279	{"text": "It fairly shook me, sir.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2281	lexical	\N	\N	2280	{"text": "I’d have half killed Tonga for it if he had not scrambled off.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2282	lexical	\N	\N	2281	{"text": "That was how he came to leave his club, and some of his darts too, as he tells me, which I dare say helped to put you on our track; though how you kept on it is more than I can tell.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2283	lexical	\N	\N	2282	{"text": "I don’t feel no malice against you for it.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2284	lexical	\N	\N	2283	{"text": "But it does seem a queer thing,” he added, with a bitter smile, “that I who have a fair claim to nigh upon half a million of money should spend the first half of my life building a breakwater in the Andamans, and am like to spend the other half digging drains at Dartmoor.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2285	lexical	\N	\N	2284	{"text": "It was an evil day for me when first I clapped eyes upon the merchant Achmet and had to do with the Agra treasure, which never brought anything but a curse yet upon the man who owned it.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2286	lexical	\N	\N	2285	{"text": "To him it brought murder, to Major Sholto it brought fear and guilt, to me it has meant slavery for life.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2287	lexical	\N	\N	2286	{"text": "At this moment Athelney Jones thrust his broad face and heavy shoulders into the tiny cabin.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2288	lexical	\N	\N	2287	{"text": "“Quite a family party,” he remarked.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2289	lexical	\N	\N	2288	{"text": "“I think I shall have a pull at that flask, Holmes.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2290	lexical	\N	\N	2289	{"text": "Well, I think we may all congratulate each other.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2291	lexical	\N	\N	2290	{"text": "Pity we didn’t take the other alive; but there was no choice.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2292	lexical	\N	\N	2291	{"text": "I say, Holmes, you must confess that you cut it rather fine.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2293	lexical	\N	\N	2292	{"text": "It was all we could do to overhaul her.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2294	lexical	\N	\N	2293	{"text": "“All is well that ends well,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2295	lexical	\N	\N	2294	{"text": "“But I certainly did not know that the _Aurora_ was such a clipper.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2296	lexical	\N	\N	2295	{"text": "“Smith says she is one of the fastest launches on the river, and that if he had had another man to help him with the engines we should never have caught her.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2297	lexical	\N	\N	2296	{"text": "He swears he knew nothing of this Norwood business.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2298	lexical	\N	\N	2297	{"text": "“Neither he did,” cried our prisoner,—“not a word.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2299	lexical	\N	\N	2298	{"text": "I chose his launch because I heard that she was a flier.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2300	lexical	\N	\N	2299	{"text": "We told him nothing, but we paid him well, and he was to get something handsome if we reached our vessel, the _Esmeralda_, at Gravesend, outward bound for the Brazils.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2301	lexical	\N	\N	2300	{"text": "“Well, if he has done no wrong we shall see that no wrong comes to him.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2302	lexical	\N	\N	2301	{"text": "If we are pretty quick in catching our men, we are not so quick in condemning them.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2303	lexical	\N	\N	2302	{"text": "It was amusing to notice how the consequential Jones was already beginning to give himself airs on the strength of the capture.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2304	lexical	\N	\N	2303	{"text": "From the slight smile which played over Sherlock Holmes’s face, I could see that the speech had not been lost upon him.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2305	lexical	\N	\N	2304	{"text": "“We will be at Vauxhall Bridge presently,” said Jones, “and shall land you, Dr. Watson, with the treasure-box.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2306	lexical	\N	\N	2305	{"text": "I need hardly tell you that I am taking a very grave responsibility upon myself in doing this.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2307	lexical	\N	\N	2306	{"text": "It is most irregular; but of course an agreement is an agreement.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2308	lexical	\N	\N	2307	{"text": "I must, however, as a matter of duty, send an inspector with you, since you have so valuable a charge.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2309	lexical	\N	\N	2308	{"text": "You will drive, no doubt?”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2310	lexical	\N	\N	2309	{"text": "“Yes, I shall drive.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2311	lexical	\N	\N	2310	{"text": "“It is a pity there is no key, that we may make an inventory first.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2312	lexical	\N	\N	2311	{"text": "You will have to break it open.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2313	lexical	\N	\N	2312	{"text": "Where is the key, my man?”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2314	lexical	\N	\N	2313	{"text": "“At the bottom of the river,” said Small, shortly.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2315	lexical	\N	\N	2314	{"text": "“Hum!", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2316	lexical	\N	\N	2315	{"text": "There was no use your giving this unnecessary trouble.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2317	lexical	\N	\N	2316	{"text": "We have had work enough already through you.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2318	lexical	\N	\N	2317	{"text": "However, doctor, I need not warn you to be careful.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2319	lexical	\N	\N	2318	{"text": "Bring the box back with you to the Baker Street rooms.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2320	lexical	\N	\N	2319	{"text": "You will find us there, on our way to the station.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2321	lexical	\N	\N	2320	{"text": "They landed me at Vauxhall, with my heavy iron box, and with a bluff, genial inspector as my companion.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2322	lexical	\N	\N	2321	{"text": "A quarter of an hour’s drive brought us to Mrs. Cecil Forrester’s.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2323	lexical	\N	\N	2322	{"text": "The servant seemed surprised at so late a visitor.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2324	lexical	\N	\N	2323	{"text": "Mrs. Cecil Forrester was out for the evening, she explained, and likely to be very late.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2325	lexical	\N	\N	2324	{"text": "Miss Morstan, however, was in the drawing-room: so to the drawing-room I went, box in hand, leaving the obliging inspector in the cab.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2326	lexical	\N	\N	2325	{"text": "She was seated by the open window, dressed in some sort of white diaphanous material, with a little touch of scarlet at the neck and waist.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2327	lexical	\N	\N	2326	{"text": "The soft light of a shaded lamp fell upon her as she leaned back in the basket chair, playing over her sweet, grave face, and tinting with a dull, metallic sparkle the rich coils of her luxuriant hair.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2328	lexical	\N	\N	2327	{"text": "One white arm and hand drooped over the side of the chair, and her whole pose and figure spoke of an absorbing melancholy.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2329	lexical	\N	\N	2328	{"text": "At the sound of my foot-fall she sprang to her feet, however, and a bright flush of surprise and of pleasure coloured her pale cheeks.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2330	lexical	\N	\N	2329	{"text": "“I heard a cab drive up,” she said.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2331	lexical	\N	\N	2330	{"text": "“I thought that Mrs. Forrester had come back very early, but I never dreamed that it might be you.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2332	lexical	\N	\N	2331	{"text": "What news have you brought me?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2333	lexical	\N	\N	2332	{"text": "“I have brought something better than news,” said I, putting down the box upon the table and speaking jovially and boisterously, though my heart was heavy within me.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2334	lexical	\N	\N	2333	{"text": "“I have brought you something which is worth all the news in the world.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2335	lexical	\N	\N	2334	{"text": "I have brought you a fortune.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2336	lexical	\N	\N	2335	{"text": "She glanced at the iron box.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2337	lexical	\N	\N	2336	{"text": "“Is that the treasure, then?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2338	lexical	\N	\N	2337	{"text": "she asked, coolly enough.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2339	lexical	\N	\N	2338	{"text": "“Yes, this is the great Agra treasure.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2340	lexical	\N	\N	2339	{"text": "Half of it is yours and half is Thaddeus Sholto’s.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2341	lexical	\N	\N	2340	{"text": "You will have a couple of hundred thousand each.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2342	lexical	\N	\N	2341	{"text": "Think of that!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2343	lexical	\N	\N	2342	{"text": "An annuity of ten thousand pounds.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2344	lexical	\N	\N	2343	{"text": "There will be few richer young ladies in England.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2345	lexical	\N	\N	2344	{"text": "Is it not glorious?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2346	lexical	\N	\N	2345	{"text": "I think that I must have been rather overacting my delight, and that she detected a hollow ring in my congratulations, for I saw her eyebrows rise a little, and she glanced at me curiously.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2347	lexical	\N	\N	2346	{"text": "“If I have it,” said she, “I owe it to you.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2348	lexical	\N	\N	2347	{"text": "“No, no,” I answered, “not to me, but to my friend Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2349	lexical	\N	\N	2348	{"text": "With all the will in the world, I could never have followed up a clue which has taxed even his analytical genius.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2350	lexical	\N	\N	2349	{"text": "As it was, we very nearly lost it at the last moment.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2351	lexical	\N	\N	2350	{"text": "“Pray sit down and tell me all about it, Dr. Watson,” said she.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2352	lexical	\N	\N	2351	{"text": "I narrated briefly what had occurred since I had seen her last,—Holmes’s new method of search, the discovery of the _Aurora_, the appearance of Athelney Jones, our expedition in the evening, and the wild chase down the Thames.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2353	lexical	\N	\N	2352	{"text": "She listened with parted lips and shining eyes to my recital of our adventures.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2354	lexical	\N	\N	2353	{"text": "When I spoke of the dart which had so narrowly missed us, she turned so white that I feared that she was about to faint.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2355	lexical	\N	\N	2354	{"text": "“It is nothing,” she said, as I hastened to pour her out some water.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2356	lexical	\N	\N	2355	{"text": "“I am all right again.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2357	lexical	\N	\N	2356	{"text": "It was a shock to me to hear that I had placed my friends in such horrible peril.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2358	lexical	\N	\N	2357	{"text": "“That is all over,” I answered.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2359	lexical	\N	\N	2358	{"text": "“It was nothing.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2360	lexical	\N	\N	2359	{"text": "I will tell you no more gloomy details.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2361	lexical	\N	\N	2360	{"text": "Let us turn to something brighter.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2362	lexical	\N	\N	2361	{"text": "There is the treasure.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2363	lexical	\N	\N	2362	{"text": "What could be brighter than that?", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2364	lexical	\N	\N	2363	{"text": "I got leave to bring it with me, thinking that it would interest you to be the first to see it.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2365	lexical	\N	\N	2364	{"text": "“It would be of the greatest interest to me,” she said.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2366	lexical	\N	\N	2365	{"text": "There was no eagerness in her voice, however.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2367	lexical	\N	\N	2366	{"text": "It had struck her, doubtless, that it might seem ungracious upon her part to be indifferent to a prize which had cost so much to win.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2368	lexical	\N	\N	2367	{"text": "“What a pretty box!”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2369	lexical	\N	\N	2368	{"text": "she said, stooping over it.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2370	lexical	\N	\N	2369	{"text": "“This is Indian work, I suppose?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2371	lexical	\N	\N	2370	{"text": "“Yes; it is Benares metal-work.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2372	lexical	\N	\N	2371	{"text": "“And so heavy!”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2373	lexical	\N	\N	2372	{"text": "she exclaimed, trying to raise it.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2374	lexical	\N	\N	2373	{"text": "“The box alone must be of some value.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2375	lexical	\N	\N	2374	{"text": "Where is the key?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2376	lexical	\N	\N	2375	{"text": "“Small threw it into the Thames,” I answered.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2377	lexical	\N	\N	2376	{"text": "“I must borrow Mrs. Forrester’s poker.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2378	lexical	\N	\N	2377	{"text": "There was in the front a thick and broad hasp, wrought in the image of a sitting Buddha.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2379	lexical	\N	\N	2378	{"text": "Under this I thrust the end of the poker and twisted it outward as a lever.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2380	lexical	\N	\N	2379	{"text": "The hasp sprang open with a loud snap.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2381	lexical	\N	\N	2380	{"text": "With trembling fingers I flung back the lid.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2382	lexical	\N	\N	2381	{"text": "We both stood gazing in astonishment.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2383	lexical	\N	\N	2382	{"text": "The box was empty!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2384	lexical	\N	\N	2383	{"text": "No wonder that it was heavy.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2385	lexical	\N	\N	2384	{"text": "The iron-work was two-thirds of an inch thick all round.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2386	lexical	\N	\N	2385	{"text": "It was massive, well made, and solid, like a chest constructed to carry things of great price, but not one shred or crumb of metal or jewelry lay within it.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2387	lexical	\N	\N	2386	{"text": "It was absolutely and completely empty.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2388	lexical	\N	\N	2387	{"text": "“The treasure is lost,” said Miss Morstan, calmly.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2389	lexical	\N	\N	2388	{"text": "As I listened to the words and realised what they meant, a great shadow seemed to pass from my soul.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2390	lexical	\N	\N	2389	{"text": "I did not know how this Agra treasure had weighed me down, until now that it was finally removed.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2391	lexical	\N	\N	2390	{"text": "It was selfish, no doubt, disloyal, wrong, but I could realise nothing save that the golden barrier was gone from between us.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2392	lexical	\N	\N	2391	{"text": "“Thank God!”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2393	lexical	\N	\N	2392	{"text": "I ejaculated from my very heart.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2394	lexical	\N	\N	2393	{"text": "She looked at me with a quick, questioning smile.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2395	lexical	\N	\N	2394	{"text": "“Why do you say that?”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2396	lexical	\N	\N	2395	{"text": "she asked.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2397	lexical	\N	\N	2396	{"text": "“Because you are within my reach again,” I said, taking her hand.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2398	lexical	\N	\N	2397	{"text": "She did not withdraw it.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2399	lexical	\N	\N	2398	{"text": "“Because I love you, Mary, as truly as ever a man loved a woman.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2400	lexical	\N	\N	2399	{"text": "Because this treasure, these riches, sealed my lips.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2401	lexical	\N	\N	2400	{"text": "Now that they are gone I can tell you how I love you.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2402	lexical	\N	\N	2401	{"text": "That is why I said, ‘Thank God.’”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2403	lexical	\N	\N	2402	{"text": "“Then I say, ‘Thank God,’ too,” she whispered, as I drew her to my side.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2404	lexical	\N	\N	2403	{"text": "Whoever had lost a treasure, I knew that night that I had gained one.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2405	lexical	\N	\N	2404	{"text": "Chapter XII The Strange Story of Jonathan Small", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2406	lexical	\N	\N	2405	{"text": "A very patient man was that inspector in the cab, for it was a weary time before I rejoined him.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2407	lexical	\N	\N	2406	{"text": "His face clouded over when I showed him the empty box.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2408	lexical	\N	\N	2407	{"text": "“There goes the reward!”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2409	lexical	\N	\N	2408	{"text": "said he, gloomily.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2410	lexical	\N	\N	2409	{"text": "“Where there is no money there is no pay.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2411	lexical	\N	\N	2410	{"text": "This night’s work would have been worth a tenner each to Sam Brown and me if the treasure had been there.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2412	lexical	\N	\N	2411	{"text": "“Mr. Thaddeus Sholto is a rich man,” I said.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2413	lexical	\N	\N	2412	{"text": "“He will see that you are rewarded, treasure or no.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2414	lexical	\N	\N	2413	{"text": "The inspector shook his head despondently, however.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2415	lexical	\N	\N	2414	{"text": "“It’s a bad job,” he repeated; “and so Mr. Athelney Jones will think.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2416	lexical	\N	\N	2415	{"text": "His forecast proved to be correct, for the detective looked blank enough when I got to Baker Street and showed him the empty box.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2417	lexical	\N	\N	2416	{"text": "They had only just arrived, Holmes, the prisoner, and he, for they had changed their plans so far as to report themselves at a station upon the way.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2418	lexical	\N	\N	2417	{"text": "My companion lounged in his arm-chair with his usual listless expression, while Small sat stolidly opposite to him with his wooden leg cocked over his sound one.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2419	lexical	\N	\N	2418	{"text": "As I exhibited the empty box he leaned back in his chair and laughed aloud.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2420	lexical	\N	\N	2419	{"text": "“This is your doing, Small,” said Athelney Jones, angrily.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2421	lexical	\N	\N	2420	{"text": "“Yes, I have put it away where you shall never lay hand upon it,” he cried, exultantly.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2422	lexical	\N	\N	2421	{"text": "“It is my treasure; and if I can’t have the loot I’ll take darned good care that no one else does.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2423	lexical	\N	\N	2422	{"text": "I tell you that no living man has any right to it, unless it is three men who are in the Andaman convict-barracks and myself.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2424	lexical	\N	\N	2423	{"text": "I know now that I cannot have the use of it, and I know that they cannot.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2425	lexical	\N	\N	2424	{"text": "I have acted all through for them as much as for myself.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2426	lexical	\N	\N	2425	{"text": "It’s been the sign of four with us always.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2462	lexical	\N	\N	2461	{"text": "“I am a Worcestershire man myself,—born near Pershore.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2427	lexical	\N	\N	2426	{"text": "Well I know that they would have had me do just what I have done, and throw the treasure into the Thames rather than let it go to kith or kin of Sholto or of Morstan.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2428	lexical	\N	\N	2427	{"text": "It was not to make them rich that we did for Achmet.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2429	lexical	\N	\N	2428	{"text": "You’ll find the treasure where the key is, and where little Tonga is.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2430	lexical	\N	\N	2429	{"text": "When I saw that your launch must catch us, I put the loot away in a safe place.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2431	lexical	\N	\N	2430	{"text": "There are no rupees for you this journey.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2432	lexical	\N	\N	2431	{"text": "“You are deceiving us, Small,” said Athelney Jones, sternly.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2433	lexical	\N	\N	2432	{"text": "“If you had wished to throw the treasure into the Thames it would have been easier for you to have thrown box and all.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2434	lexical	\N	\N	2433	{"text": "“Easier for me to throw, and easier for you to recover,” he answered, with a shrewd, sidelong look.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2435	lexical	\N	\N	2434	{"text": "“The man that was clever enough to hunt me down is clever enough to pick an iron box from the bottom of a river.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2436	lexical	\N	\N	2435	{"text": "Now that they are scattered over five miles or so, it may be a harder job.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2437	lexical	\N	\N	2436	{"text": "It went to my heart to do it, though.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2438	lexical	\N	\N	2437	{"text": "I was half mad when you came up with us.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2439	lexical	\N	\N	2438	{"text": "However, there’s no good grieving over it.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2440	lexical	\N	\N	2439	{"text": "I’ve had ups in my life, and I’ve had downs, but I’ve learned not to cry over spilled milk.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2441	lexical	\N	\N	2440	{"text": "“This is a very serious matter, Small,” said the detective.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2442	lexical	\N	\N	2441	{"text": "“If you had helped justice, instead of thwarting it in this way, you would have had a better chance at your trial.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2443	lexical	\N	\N	2442	{"text": "“Justice!”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2444	lexical	\N	\N	2443	{"text": "snarled the ex-convict.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2445	lexical	\N	\N	2444	{"text": "“A pretty justice!", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2446	lexical	\N	\N	2445	{"text": "Whose loot is this, if it is not ours?", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2447	lexical	\N	\N	2446	{"text": "Where is the justice that I should give it up to those who have never earned it?", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2448	lexical	\N	\N	2447	{"text": "Look how I have earned it!", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2449	lexical	\N	\N	2448	{"text": "Twenty long years in that fever-ridden swamp, all day at work under the mangrove-tree, all night chained up in the filthy convict-huts, bitten by mosquitoes, racked with ague, bullied by every cursed black-faced policeman who loved to take it out of a white man.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2450	lexical	\N	\N	2449	{"text": "That was how I earned the Agra treasure; and you talk to me of justice because I cannot bear to feel that I have paid this price only that another may enjoy it!", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2451	lexical	\N	\N	2450	{"text": "I would rather swing a score of times, or have one of Tonga’s darts in my hide, than live in a convict’s cell and feel that another man is at his ease in a palace with the money that should be mine.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2452	lexical	\N	\N	2451	{"text": "Small had dropped his mask of stoicism, and all this came out in a wild whirl of words, while his eyes blazed, and the handcuffs clanked together with the impassioned movement of his hands.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2453	lexical	\N	\N	2452	{"text": "I could understand, as I saw the fury and the passion of the man, that it was no groundless or unnatural terror which had possessed Major Sholto when he first learned that the injured convict was upon his track.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2454	lexical	\N	\N	2453	{"text": "“You forget that we know nothing of all this,” said Holmes quietly.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2455	lexical	\N	\N	2454	{"text": "“We have not heard your story, and we cannot tell how far justice may originally have been on your side.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2456	lexical	\N	\N	2455	{"text": "“Well, sir, you have been very fair-spoken to me, though I can see that I have you to thank that I have these bracelets upon my wrists.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2457	lexical	\N	\N	2456	{"text": "Still, I bear no grudge for that.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2458	lexical	\N	\N	2457	{"text": "It is all fair and above-board.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2459	lexical	\N	\N	2458	{"text": "If you want to hear my story I have no wish to hold it back.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2460	lexical	\N	\N	2459	{"text": "What I say to you is God’s truth, every word of it.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2461	lexical	\N	\N	2460	{"text": "Thank you; you can put the glass beside me here, and I’ll put my lips to it if I am dry.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2463	lexical	\N	\N	2462	{"text": "I dare say you would find a heap of Smalls living there now if you were to look.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2464	lexical	\N	\N	2463	{"text": "I have often thought of taking a look round there, but the truth is that I was never much of a credit to the family, and I doubt if they would be so very glad to see me.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2465	lexical	\N	\N	2464	{"text": "They were all steady, chapel-going folk, small farmers, well-known and respected over the country-side, while I was always a bit of a rover.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2466	lexical	\N	\N	2465	{"text": "At last, however, when I was about eighteen, I gave them no more trouble, for I got into a mess over a girl, and could only get out of it again by taking the Queen’s shilling and joining the 3rd Buffs, which was just starting for India.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2467	lexical	\N	\N	2466	{"text": "“I wasn’t destined to do much soldiering, however.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2468	lexical	\N	\N	2467	{"text": "I had just got past the goose-step, and learned to handle my musket, when I was fool enough to go swimming in the Ganges.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2469	lexical	\N	\N	2468	{"text": "Luckily for me, my company sergeant, John Holder, was in the water at the same time, and he was one of the finest swimmers in the service.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2470	lexical	\N	\N	2469	{"text": "A crocodile took me, just as I was half-way across, and nipped off my right leg as clean as a surgeon could have done it, just above the knee.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2471	lexical	\N	\N	2470	{"text": "What with the shock and the loss of blood, I fainted, and should have drowned if Holder had not caught hold of me and paddled for the bank.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2472	lexical	\N	\N	2471	{"text": "I was five months in hospital over it, and when at last I was able to limp out of it with this timber toe strapped to my stump I found myself invalided out of the army and unfitted for any active occupation.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2473	lexical	\N	\N	2472	{"text": "“I was, as you can imagine, pretty down on my luck at this time, for I was a useless cripple though not yet in my twentieth year.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2474	lexical	\N	\N	2473	{"text": "However, my misfortune soon proved to be a blessing in disguise.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2475	lexical	\N	\N	2474	{"text": "A man named Abel White, who had come out there as an indigo-planter, wanted an overseer to look after his coolies and keep them up to their work.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2476	lexical	\N	\N	2475	{"text": "He happened to be a friend of our colonel’s, who had taken an interest in me since the accident.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2477	lexical	\N	\N	2476	{"text": "To make a long story short, the colonel recommended me strongly for the post and, as the work was mostly to be done on horseback, my leg was no great obstacle, for I had enough knee left to keep good grip on the saddle.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2478	lexical	\N	\N	2477	{"text": "What I had to do was to ride over the plantation, to keep an eye on the men as they worked, and to report the idlers.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2479	lexical	\N	\N	2478	{"text": "The pay was fair, I had comfortable quarters, and altogether I was content to spend the remainder of my life in indigo-planting.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2480	lexical	\N	\N	2479	{"text": "Mr. Abel White was a kind man, and he would often drop into my little shanty and smoke a pipe with me, for white folk out there feel their hearts warm to each other as they never do here at home.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2481	lexical	\N	\N	2480	{"text": "“Well, I was never in luck’s way long.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2482	lexical	\N	\N	2481	{"text": "Suddenly, without a note of warning, the great mutiny broke upon us.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2483	lexical	\N	\N	2482	{"text": "One month India lay as still and peaceful, to all appearance, as Surrey or Kent; the next there were two hundred thousand black devils let loose, and the country was a perfect hell.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2484	lexical	\N	\N	2483	{"text": "Of course you know all about it, gentlemen,—a deal more than I do, very like, since reading is not in my line.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2485	lexical	\N	\N	2484	{"text": "I only know what I saw with my own eyes.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2486	lexical	\N	\N	2485	{"text": "Our plantation was at a place called Muttra, near the border of the Northwest Provinces.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2487	lexical	\N	\N	2486	{"text": "Night after night the whole sky was alight with the burning bungalows, and day after day we had small companies of Europeans passing through our estate with their wives and children, on their way to Agra, where were the nearest troops.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2488	lexical	\N	\N	2487	{"text": "Mr. Abel White was an obstinate man.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2489	lexical	\N	\N	2488	{"text": "He had it in his head that the affair had been exaggerated, and that it would blow over as suddenly as it had sprung up.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2490	lexical	\N	\N	2489	{"text": "There he sat on his veranda, drinking whiskey-pegs and smoking cheroots, while the country was in a blaze about him.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2491	lexical	\N	\N	2490	{"text": "Of course we stuck by him, I and Dawson, who, with his wife, used to do the book-work and the managing.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2492	lexical	\N	\N	2491	{"text": "Well, one fine day the crash came.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2524	lexical	\N	\N	2523	{"text": "It was impossible for us, therefore, to station a strong guard at every one of the innumerable gates.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2493	lexical	\N	\N	2492	{"text": "I had been away on a distant plantation, and was riding slowly home in the evening, when my eye fell upon something all huddled together at the bottom of a steep nullah.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2494	lexical	\N	\N	2493	{"text": "I rode down to see what it was, and the cold struck through my heart when I found it was Dawson’s wife, all cut into ribbons, and half eaten by jackals and native dogs.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2495	lexical	\N	\N	2494	{"text": "A little further up the road Dawson himself was lying on his face, quite dead, with an empty revolver in his hand and four Sepoys lying across each other in front of him.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2496	lexical	\N	\N	2495	{"text": "I reined up my horse, wondering which way I should turn, but at that moment I saw thick smoke curling up from Abel White’s bungalow and the flames beginning to burst through the roof.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2497	lexical	\N	\N	2496	{"text": "I knew then that I could do my employer no good, but would only throw my own life away if I meddled in the matter.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2498	lexical	\N	\N	2497	{"text": "From where I stood I could see hundreds of the black fiends, with their red coats still on their backs, dancing and howling round the burning house.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2499	lexical	\N	\N	2498	{"text": "Some of them pointed at me, and a couple of bullets sang past my head; so I broke away across the paddy-fields, and found myself late at night safe within the walls at Agra.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2500	lexical	\N	\N	2499	{"text": "“As it proved, however, there was no great safety there, either.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2501	lexical	\N	\N	2500	{"text": "The whole country was up like a swarm of bees.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2502	lexical	\N	\N	2501	{"text": "Wherever the English could collect in little bands they held just the ground that their guns commanded.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2503	lexical	\N	\N	2502	{"text": "Everywhere else they were helpless fugitives.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2504	lexical	\N	\N	2503	{"text": "It was a fight of the millions against the hundreds; and the cruellest part of it was that these men that we fought against, foot, horse, and gunners, were our own picked troops, whom we had taught and trained, handling our own weapons, and blowing our own bugle-calls.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2505	lexical	\N	\N	2504	{"text": "At Agra there were the 3rd Bengal Fusiliers, some Sikhs, two troops of horse, and a battery of artillery.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2506	lexical	\N	\N	2505	{"text": "A volunteer corps of clerks and merchants had been formed, and this I joined, wooden leg and all.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2507	lexical	\N	\N	2506	{"text": "We went out to meet the rebels at Shahgunge early in July, and we beat them back for a time, but our powder gave out, and we had to fall back upon the city.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2508	lexical	\N	\N	2507	{"text": "“Nothing but the worst news came to us from every side,—which is not to be wondered at, for if you look at the map you will see that we were right in the heart of it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2509	lexical	\N	\N	2508	{"text": "Lucknow is rather better than a hundred miles to the east, and Cawnpore about as far to the south.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2510	lexical	\N	\N	2509	{"text": "From every point on the compass there was nothing but torture and murder and outrage.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2511	lexical	\N	\N	2510	{"text": "“The city of Agra is a great place, swarming with fanatics and fierce devil-worshippers of all sorts.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2512	lexical	\N	\N	2511	{"text": "Our handful of men were lost among the narrow, winding streets.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2513	lexical	\N	\N	2512	{"text": "Our leader moved across the river, therefore, and took up his position in the old fort at Agra.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2514	lexical	\N	\N	2513	{"text": "I don’t know if any of you gentlemen have ever read or heard anything of that old fort.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2515	lexical	\N	\N	2514	{"text": "It is a very queer place,—the queerest that ever I was in, and I have been in some rum corners, too.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2516	lexical	\N	\N	2515	{"text": "First of all, it is enormous in size.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2517	lexical	\N	\N	2516	{"text": "I should think that the enclosure must be acres and acres.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2518	lexical	\N	\N	2517	{"text": "There is a modern part, which took all our garrison, women, children, stores, and everything else, with plenty of room over.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2519	lexical	\N	\N	2518	{"text": "But the modern part is nothing like the size of the old quarter, where nobody goes, and which is given over to the scorpions and the centipedes.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2520	lexical	\N	\N	2519	{"text": "It is all full of great deserted halls, and winding passages, and long corridors twisting in and out, so that it is easy enough for folk to get lost in it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2521	lexical	\N	\N	2520	{"text": "For this reason it was seldom that any one went into it, though now and again a party with torches might go exploring.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2522	lexical	\N	\N	2521	{"text": "“The river washes along the front of the old fort, and so protects it, but on the sides and behind there are many doors, and these had to be guarded, of course, in the old quarter as well as in that which was actually held by our troops.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2523	lexical	\N	\N	2522	{"text": "We were short-handed, with hardly men enough to man the angles of the building and to serve the guns.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2525	lexical	\N	\N	2524	{"text": "What we did was to organise a central guard-house in the middle of the fort, and to leave each gate under the charge of one white man and two or three natives.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2526	lexical	\N	\N	2525	{"text": "I was selected to take charge during certain hours of the night of a small isolated door upon the southwest side of the building.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2527	lexical	\N	\N	2526	{"text": "Two Sikh troopers were placed under my command, and I was instructed if anything went wrong to fire my musket, when I might rely upon help coming at once from the central guard.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2528	lexical	\N	\N	2527	{"text": "As the guard was a good two hundred paces away, however, and as the space between was cut up into a labyrinth of passages and corridors, I had great doubts as to whether they could arrive in time to be of any use in case of an actual attack.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2529	lexical	\N	\N	2528	{"text": "“Well, I was pretty proud at having this small command given me, since I was a raw recruit, and a game-legged one at that.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2530	lexical	\N	\N	2529	{"text": "For two nights I kept the watch with my Punjaubees.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2531	lexical	\N	\N	2530	{"text": "They were tall, fierce-looking chaps, Mahomet Singh and Abdullah Khan by name, both old fighting-men who had borne arms against us at Chilian-wallah.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2532	lexical	\N	\N	2531	{"text": "They could talk English pretty well, but I could get little out of them.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2533	lexical	\N	\N	2532	{"text": "They preferred to stand together and jabber all night in their queer Sikh lingo.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2534	lexical	\N	\N	2533	{"text": "For myself, I used to stand outside the gateway, looking down on the broad, winding river and on the twinkling lights of the great city.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2535	lexical	\N	\N	2534	{"text": "The beating of drums, the rattle of tomtoms, and the yells and howls of the rebels, drunk with opium and with bang, were enough to remind us all night of our dangerous neighbours across the stream.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2536	lexical	\N	\N	2535	{"text": "Every two hours the officer of the night used to come round to all the posts, to make sure that all was well.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2537	lexical	\N	\N	2536	{"text": "“The third night of my watch was dark and dirty, with a small, driving rain.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2538	lexical	\N	\N	2537	{"text": "It was dreary work standing in the gateway hour after hour in such weather.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2539	lexical	\N	\N	2538	{"text": "I tried again and again to make my Sikhs talk, but without much success.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2540	lexical	\N	\N	2539	{"text": "At two in the morning the rounds passed, and broke for a moment the weariness of the night.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2541	lexical	\N	\N	2540	{"text": "Finding that my companions would not be led into conversation, I took out my pipe, and laid down my musket to strike the match.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2542	lexical	\N	\N	2541	{"text": "In an instant the two Sikhs were upon me.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2543	lexical	\N	\N	2542	{"text": "One of them snatched my firelock up and levelled it at my head, while the other held a great knife to my throat and swore between his teeth that he would plunge it into me if I moved a step.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2544	lexical	\N	\N	2543	{"text": "“My first thought was that these fellows were in league with the rebels, and that this was the beginning of an assault.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2545	lexical	\N	\N	2544	{"text": "If our door were in the hands of the Sepoys the place must fall, and the women and children be treated as they were in Cawnpore.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2546	lexical	\N	\N	2545	{"text": "Maybe you gentlemen think that I am just making out a case for myself, but I give you my word that when I thought of that, though I felt the point of the knife at my throat, I opened my mouth with the intention of giving a scream, if it was my last one, which might alarm the main guard.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2547	lexical	\N	\N	2546	{"text": "The man who held me seemed to know my thoughts; for, even as I braced myself to it, he whispered, ‘Don’t make a noise.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2548	lexical	\N	\N	2547	{"text": "The fort is safe enough.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2549	lexical	\N	\N	2548	{"text": "There are no rebel dogs on this side of the river.’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2550	lexical	\N	\N	2549	{"text": "There was the ring of truth in what he said, and I knew that if I raised my voice I was a dead man.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2551	lexical	\N	\N	2550	{"text": "I could read it in the fellow’s brown eyes.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2552	lexical	\N	\N	2551	{"text": "I waited, therefore, in silence, to see what it was that they wanted from me.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2553	lexical	\N	\N	2552	{"text": "“‘Listen to me, Sahib,’ said the taller and fiercer of the pair, the one whom they called Abdullah Khan.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2554	lexical	\N	\N	2553	{"text": "‘You must either be with us now or you must be silenced forever.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2555	lexical	\N	\N	2554	{"text": "The thing is too great a one for us to hesitate.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2556	lexical	\N	\N	2555	{"text": "Either you are heart and soul with us on your oath on the cross of the Christians, or your body this night shall be thrown into the ditch and we shall pass over to our brothers in the rebel army.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2558	lexical	\N	\N	2557	{"text": "Which is it to be, death or life?", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2559	lexical	\N	\N	2558	{"text": "We can only give you three minutes to decide, for the time is passing, and all must be done before the rounds come again.’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2560	lexical	\N	\N	2559	{"text": "“‘How can I decide?’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2561	lexical	\N	\N	2560	{"text": "said I.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2562	lexical	\N	\N	2561	{"text": "‘You have not told me what you want of me.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2563	lexical	\N	\N	2562	{"text": "But I tell you now that if it is anything against the safety of the fort I will have no truck with it, so you can drive home your knife and welcome.’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2564	lexical	\N	\N	2563	{"text": "“‘It is nothing against the fort,’ said he.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2565	lexical	\N	\N	2564	{"text": "‘We only ask you to do that which your countrymen come to this land for.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2566	lexical	\N	\N	2565	{"text": "We ask you to be rich.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2567	lexical	\N	\N	2566	{"text": "If you will be one of us this night, we will swear to you upon the naked knife, and by the threefold oath which no Sikh was ever known to break, that you shall have your fair share of the loot.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2568	lexical	\N	\N	2567	{"text": "A quarter of the treasure shall be yours.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2569	lexical	\N	\N	2568	{"text": "We can say no fairer.’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2570	lexical	\N	\N	2569	{"text": "“‘But what is the treasure, then?’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2571	lexical	\N	\N	2570	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2572	lexical	\N	\N	2571	{"text": "‘I am as ready to be rich as you can be, if you will but show me how it can be done.’", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2573	lexical	\N	\N	2572	{"text": "“‘You will swear, then,’ said he, ‘by the bones of your father, by the honour of your mother, by the cross of your faith, to raise no hand and speak no word against us, either now or afterwards?’", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2574	lexical	\N	\N	2573	{"text": "“‘I will swear it,’ I answered, ‘provided that the fort is not endangered.’", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2575	lexical	\N	\N	2574	{"text": "“‘Then my comrade and I will swear that you shall have a quarter of the treasure which shall be equally divided among the four of us.’", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2576	lexical	\N	\N	2575	{"text": "“‘There are but three,’ said I.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2577	lexical	\N	\N	2576	{"text": "“‘No; Dost Akbar must have his share.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2578	lexical	\N	\N	2577	{"text": "We can tell the tale to you while we await them.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2579	lexical	\N	\N	2578	{"text": "Do you stand at the gate, Mahomet Singh, and give notice of their coming.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2580	lexical	\N	\N	2579	{"text": "The thing stands thus, Sahib, and I tell it to you because I know that an oath is binding upon a Feringhee, and that we may trust you.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2581	lexical	\N	\N	2580	{"text": "Had you been a lying Hindoo, though you had sworn by all the gods in their false temples, your blood would have been upon the knife, and your body in the water.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2582	lexical	\N	\N	2581	{"text": "But the Sikh knows the Englishman, and the Englishman knows the Sikh.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2583	lexical	\N	\N	2582	{"text": "Hearken, then, to what I have to say.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2584	lexical	\N	\N	2583	{"text": "“‘There is a rajah in the northern provinces who has much wealth, though his lands are small.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2585	lexical	\N	\N	2584	{"text": "Much has come to him from his father, and more still he has set by himself, for he is of a low nature and hoards his gold rather than spend it.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2586	lexical	\N	\N	2585	{"text": "When the troubles broke out he would be friends both with the lion and the tiger,—with the Sepoy and with the Company’s Raj.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2587	lexical	\N	\N	2586	{"text": "Soon, however, it seemed to him that the white men’s day was come, for through all the land he could hear of nothing but of their death and their overthrow.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2588	lexical	\N	\N	2587	{"text": "Yet, being a careful man, he made such plans that, come what might, half at least of his treasure should be left to him.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2589	lexical	\N	\N	2588	{"text": "That which was in gold and silver he kept by him in the vaults of his palace, but the most precious stones and the choicest pearls that he had he put in an iron box, and sent it by a trusty servant who, under the guise of a merchant, should take it to the fort at Agra, there to lie until the land is at peace.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2590	lexical	\N	\N	2589	{"text": "Thus, if the rebels won he would have his money, but if the Company conquered his jewels would be saved to him.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2591	lexical	\N	\N	2590	{"text": "Having thus divided his hoard, he threw himself into the cause of the Sepoys, since they were strong upon his borders.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2628	lexical	\N	\N	2627	{"text": "“‘You will challenge him, Sahib, as usual,’ whispered Abdullah.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2592	lexical	\N	\N	2591	{"text": "By doing this, mark you, Sahib, his property becomes the due of those who have been true to their salt.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2593	lexical	\N	\N	2592	{"text": "“‘This pretended merchant, who travels under the name of Achmet, is now in the city of Agra, and desires to gain his way into the fort.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2594	lexical	\N	\N	2593	{"text": "He has with him as travelling-companion my foster-brother Dost Akbar, who knows his secret.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2595	lexical	\N	\N	2594	{"text": "Dost Akbar has promised this night to lead him to a side-postern of the fort, and has chosen this one for his purpose.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2596	lexical	\N	\N	2595	{"text": "Here he will come presently, and here he will find Mahomet Singh and myself awaiting him.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2597	lexical	\N	\N	2596	{"text": "The place is lonely, and none shall know of his coming.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2598	lexical	\N	\N	2597	{"text": "The world shall know of the merchant Achmet no more, but the great treasure of the rajah shall be divided among us.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2599	lexical	\N	\N	2598	{"text": "What say you to it, Sahib?’", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2600	lexical	\N	\N	2599	{"text": "“In Worcestershire the life of a man seems a great and a sacred thing; but it is very different when there is fire and blood all round you and you have been used to meeting death at every turn.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2601	lexical	\N	\N	2600	{"text": "Whether Achmet the merchant lived or died was a thing as light as air to me, but at the talk about the treasure my heart turned to it, and I thought of what I might do in the old country with it, and how my folk would stare when they saw their ne’er-do-well coming back with his pockets full of gold moidores.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2602	lexical	\N	\N	2601	{"text": "I had, therefore, already made up my mind.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2603	lexical	\N	\N	2602	{"text": "Abdullah Khan, however, thinking that I hesitated, pressed the matter more closely.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2604	lexical	\N	\N	2603	{"text": "“‘Consider, Sahib,’ said he, ‘that if this man is taken by the commandant he will be hung or shot, and his jewels taken by the government, so that no man will be a rupee the better for them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2605	lexical	\N	\N	2604	{"text": "Now, since we do the taking of him, why should we not do the rest as well?", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2606	lexical	\N	\N	2605	{"text": "The jewels will be as well with us as in the Company’s coffers.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2607	lexical	\N	\N	2606	{"text": "There will be enough to make every one of us rich men and great chiefs.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2608	lexical	\N	\N	2607	{"text": "No one can know about the matter, for here we are cut off from all men.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2609	lexical	\N	\N	2608	{"text": "What could be better for the purpose?", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2610	lexical	\N	\N	2609	{"text": "Say again, then, Sahib, whether you are with us, or if we must look upon you as an enemy.’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2611	lexical	\N	\N	2610	{"text": "“‘I am with you heart and soul,’ said I.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2612	lexical	\N	\N	2611	{"text": "“‘It is well,’ he answered, handing me back my firelock.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2613	lexical	\N	\N	2612	{"text": "‘You see that we trust you, for your word, like ours, is not to be broken.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2614	lexical	\N	\N	2613	{"text": "We have now only to wait for my brother and the merchant.’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2615	lexical	\N	\N	2614	{"text": "“‘Does your brother know, then, of what you will do?’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2616	lexical	\N	\N	2615	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2617	lexical	\N	\N	2616	{"text": "“‘The plan is his.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2618	lexical	\N	\N	2617	{"text": "He has devised it.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2619	lexical	\N	\N	2618	{"text": "We will go to the gate and share the watch with Mahomet Singh.’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2620	lexical	\N	\N	2619	{"text": "“The rain was still falling steadily, for it was just the beginning of the wet season.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2621	lexical	\N	\N	2620	{"text": "Brown, heavy clouds were drifting across the sky, and it was hard to see more than a stone-cast.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2622	lexical	\N	\N	2621	{"text": "A deep moat lay in front of our door, but the water was in places nearly dried up, and it could easily be crossed.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2623	lexical	\N	\N	2622	{"text": "It was strange to me to be standing there with those two wild Punjaubees waiting for the man who was coming to his death.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2624	lexical	\N	\N	2623	{"text": "“Suddenly my eye caught the glint of a shaded lantern at the other side of the moat.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2625	lexical	\N	\N	2624	{"text": "It vanished among the mound-heaps, and then appeared again coming slowly in our direction.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2626	lexical	\N	\N	2625	{"text": "“‘Here they are!’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2627	lexical	\N	\N	2626	{"text": "I exclaimed.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2629	lexical	\N	\N	2628	{"text": "‘Give him no cause for fear.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2630	lexical	\N	\N	2629	{"text": "Send us in with him, and we shall do the rest while you stay here on guard.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2631	lexical	\N	\N	2630	{"text": "Have the lantern ready to uncover, that we may be sure that it is indeed the man.’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2632	lexical	\N	\N	2631	{"text": "“The light had flickered onwards, now stopping and now advancing, until I could see two dark figures upon the other side of the moat.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2633	lexical	\N	\N	2632	{"text": "I let them scramble down the sloping bank, splash through the mire, and climb half-way up to the gate, before I challenged them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2634	lexical	\N	\N	2633	{"text": "“‘Who goes there?’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2635	lexical	\N	\N	2634	{"text": "said I, in a subdued voice.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2636	lexical	\N	\N	2635	{"text": "“‘Friends,’ came the answer.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2637	lexical	\N	\N	2636	{"text": "I uncovered my lantern and threw a flood of light upon them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2638	lexical	\N	\N	2637	{"text": "The first was an enormous Sikh, with a black beard which swept nearly down to his cummerbund.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2639	lexical	\N	\N	2638	{"text": "Outside of a show I have never seen so tall a man.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2640	lexical	\N	\N	2639	{"text": "The other was a little, fat, round fellow, with a great yellow turban, and a bundle in his hand, done up in a shawl.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2641	lexical	\N	\N	2640	{"text": "He seemed to be all in a quiver with fear, for his hands twitched as if he had the ague, and his head kept turning to left and right with two bright little twinkling eyes, like a mouse when he ventures out from his hole.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2642	lexical	\N	\N	2641	{"text": "It gave me the chills to think of killing him, but I thought of the treasure, and my heart set as hard as a flint within me.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2643	lexical	\N	\N	2642	{"text": "When he saw my white face he gave a little chirrup of joy and came running up towards me.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2644	lexical	\N	\N	2643	{"text": "“‘Your protection, Sahib,’ he panted,—‘your protection for the unhappy merchant Achmet.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2645	lexical	\N	\N	2644	{"text": "I have travelled across Rajpootana that I might seek the shelter of the fort at Agra.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2646	lexical	\N	\N	2645	{"text": "I have been robbed and beaten and abused because I have been the friend of the Company.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2647	lexical	\N	\N	2646	{"text": "It is a blessed night this when I am once more in safety,—I and my poor possessions.’", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2648	lexical	\N	\N	2647	{"text": "“‘What have you in the bundle?’", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2649	lexical	\N	\N	2648	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2650	lexical	\N	\N	2649	{"text": "“‘An iron box,’ he answered, ‘which contains one or two little family matters which are of no value to others, but which I should be sorry to lose.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2651	lexical	\N	\N	2650	{"text": "Yet I am not a beggar; and I shall reward you, young Sahib, and your governor also, if he will give me the shelter I ask.’", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2652	lexical	\N	\N	2651	{"text": "“I could not trust myself to speak longer with the man.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2653	lexical	\N	\N	2652	{"text": "The more I looked at his fat, frightened face, the harder did it seem that we should slay him in cold blood.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2654	lexical	\N	\N	2653	{"text": "It was best to get it over.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2655	lexical	\N	\N	2654	{"text": "“‘Take him to the main guard,’ said I.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2656	lexical	\N	\N	2655	{"text": "The two Sikhs closed in upon him on each side, and the giant walked behind, while they marched in through the dark gateway.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2657	lexical	\N	\N	2656	{"text": "Never was a man so compassed round with death.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2658	lexical	\N	\N	2657	{"text": "I remained at the gateway with the lantern.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2659	lexical	\N	\N	2658	{"text": "“I could hear the measured tramp of their footsteps sounding through the lonely corridors.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2660	lexical	\N	\N	2659	{"text": "Suddenly it ceased, and I heard voices, and a scuffle, with the sound of blows.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2661	lexical	\N	\N	2660	{"text": "A moment later there came, to my horror, a rush of footsteps coming in my direction, with the loud breathing of a running man.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2662	lexical	\N	\N	2661	{"text": "I turned my lantern down the long, straight passage, and there was the fat man, running like the wind, with a smear of blood across his face, and close at his heels, bounding like a tiger, the great black-bearded Sikh, with a knife flashing in his hand.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2663	lexical	\N	\N	2662	{"text": "I have never seen a man run so fast as that little merchant.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	athelney_jones	entity	character	Athelney Jones	\N	{"description": "A detective named by Holmes.", "firstSection": "section_3"}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2664	lexical	\N	\N	2663	{"text": "He was gaining on the Sikh, and I could see that if he once passed me and got to the open air he would save himself yet.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2665	lexical	\N	\N	2664	{"text": "My heart softened to him, but again the thought of his treasure turned me hard and bitter.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2666	lexical	\N	\N	2665	{"text": "I cast my firelock between his legs as he raced past, and he rolled twice over like a shot rabbit.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2667	lexical	\N	\N	2666	{"text": "Ere he could stagger to his feet the Sikh was upon him, and buried his knife twice in his side.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2668	lexical	\N	\N	2667	{"text": "The man never uttered moan nor moved muscle, but lay were he had fallen.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2669	lexical	\N	\N	2668	{"text": "I think myself that he may have broken his neck with the fall.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2670	lexical	\N	\N	2669	{"text": "You see, gentlemen, that I am keeping my promise.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2671	lexical	\N	\N	2670	{"text": "I am telling you every work of the business just exactly as it happened, whether it is in my favour or not.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2672	lexical	\N	\N	2671	{"text": "He stopped, and held out his manacled hands for the whiskey-and-water which Holmes had brewed for him.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2673	lexical	\N	\N	2672	{"text": "For myself, I confess that I had now conceived the utmost horror of the man, not only for this cold-blooded business in which he had been concerned, but even more for the somewhat flippant and careless way in which he narrated it.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2674	lexical	\N	\N	2673	{"text": "Whatever punishment was in store for him, I felt that he might expect no sympathy from me.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2675	lexical	\N	\N	2674	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes and Jones sat with their hands upon their knees, deeply interested in the story, but with the same disgust written upon their faces.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2676	lexical	\N	\N	2675	{"text": "He may have observed it, for there was a touch of defiance in his voice and manner as he proceeded.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2677	lexical	\N	\N	2676	{"text": "“It was all very bad, no doubt,” said he.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2678	lexical	\N	\N	2677	{"text": "“I should like to know how many fellows in my shoes would have refused a share of this loot when they knew that they would have their throats cut for their pains.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2679	lexical	\N	\N	2678	{"text": "Besides, it was my life or his when once he was in the fort.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2680	lexical	\N	\N	2679	{"text": "If he had got out, the whole business would come to light, and I should have been court-martialled and shot as likely as not; for people were not very lenient at a time like that.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2681	lexical	\N	\N	2680	{"text": "“Go on with your story,” said Holmes, shortly.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2682	lexical	\N	\N	2681	{"text": "“Well, we carried him in, Abdullah, Akbar, and I.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2683	lexical	\N	\N	2682	{"text": "A fine weight he was, too, for all that he was so short.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2684	lexical	\N	\N	2683	{"text": "Mahomet Singh was left to guard the door.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2685	lexical	\N	\N	2684	{"text": "We took him to a place which the Sikhs had already prepared.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2686	lexical	\N	\N	2685	{"text": "It was some distance off, where a winding passage leads to a great empty hall, the brick walls of which were all crumbling to pieces.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2687	lexical	\N	\N	2686	{"text": "The earth floor had sunk in at one place, making a natural grave, so we left Achmet the merchant there, having first covered him over with loose bricks.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2688	lexical	\N	\N	2687	{"text": "This done, we all went back to the treasure.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2689	lexical	\N	\N	2688	{"text": "“It lay where he had dropped it when he was first attacked.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2690	lexical	\N	\N	2689	{"text": "The box was the same which now lies open upon your table.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2691	lexical	\N	\N	2690	{"text": "A key was hung by a silken cord to that carved handle upon the top.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2692	lexical	\N	\N	2691	{"text": "We opened it, and the light of the lantern gleamed upon a collection of gems such as I have read of and thought about when I was a little lad at Pershore.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2693	lexical	\N	\N	2692	{"text": "It was blinding to look upon them.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2694	lexical	\N	\N	2693	{"text": "When we had feasted our eyes we took them all out and made a list of them.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2695	lexical	\N	\N	2694	{"text": "There were one hundred and forty-three diamonds of the first water, including one which has been called, I believe, ‘the Great Mogul’ and is said to be the second largest stone in existence.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2696	lexical	\N	\N	2695	{"text": "Then there were ninety-seven very fine emeralds, and one hundred and seventy rubies, some of which, however, were small.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2760	lexical	\N	\N	2759	{"text": "‘I’ve had a nasty facer myself, but—’ That was all I could hear, but it was enough to set me thinking.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2697	lexical	\N	\N	2696	{"text": "There were forty carbuncles, two hundred and ten sapphires, sixty-one agates, and a great quantity of beryls, onyxes, cats’-eyes, turquoises, and other stones, the very names of which I did not know at the time, though I have become more familiar with them since.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2698	lexical	\N	\N	2697	{"text": "Besides this, there were nearly three hundred very fine pearls, twelve of which were set in a gold coronet.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2699	lexical	\N	\N	2698	{"text": "By the way, these last had been taken out of the chest and were not there when I recovered it.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2700	lexical	\N	\N	2699	{"text": "“After we had counted our treasures we put them back into the chest and carried them to the gateway to show them to Mahomet Singh.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2701	lexical	\N	\N	2700	{"text": "Then we solemnly renewed our oath to stand by each other and be true to our secret.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2702	lexical	\N	\N	2701	{"text": "We agreed to conceal our loot in a safe place until the country should be at peace again, and then to divide it equally among ourselves.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2703	lexical	\N	\N	2702	{"text": "There was no use dividing it at present, for if gems of such value were found upon us it would cause suspicion, and there was no privacy in the fort nor any place where we could keep them.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2704	lexical	\N	\N	2703	{"text": "We carried the box, therefore, into the same hall where we had buried the body, and there, under certain bricks in the best-preserved wall, we made a hollow and put our treasure.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2705	lexical	\N	\N	2704	{"text": "We made careful note of the place, and next day I drew four plans, one for each of us, and put the sign of the four of us at the bottom, for we had sworn that we should each always act for all, so that none might take advantage.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2706	lexical	\N	\N	2705	{"text": "That is an oath that I can put my hand to my heart and swear that I have never broken.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2707	lexical	\N	\N	2706	{"text": "“Well, there’s no use my telling you gentlemen what came of the Indian mutiny.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2708	lexical	\N	\N	2707	{"text": "After Wilson took Delhi and Sir Colin relieved Lucknow the back of the business was broken.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2709	lexical	\N	\N	2708	{"text": "Fresh troops came pouring in, and Nana Sahib made himself scarce over the frontier.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2710	lexical	\N	\N	2709	{"text": "A flying column under Colonel Greathed came round to Agra and cleared the Pandies away from it.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2711	lexical	\N	\N	2710	{"text": "Peace seemed to be settling upon the country, and we four were beginning to hope that the time was at hand when we might safely go off with our shares of the plunder.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2712	lexical	\N	\N	2711	{"text": "In a moment, however, our hopes were shattered by our being arrested as the murderers of Achmet.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2713	lexical	\N	\N	2712	{"text": "“It came about in this way.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2714	lexical	\N	\N	2713	{"text": "When the rajah put his jewels into the hands of Achmet he did it because he knew that he was a trusty man.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2715	lexical	\N	\N	2714	{"text": "They are suspicious folk in the East, however: so what does this rajah do but take a second even more trusty servant and set him to play the spy upon the first?", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2716	lexical	\N	\N	2715	{"text": "This second man was ordered never to let Achmet out of his sight, and he followed him like his shadow.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2717	lexical	\N	\N	2716	{"text": "He went after him that night and saw him pass through the doorway.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2718	lexical	\N	\N	2717	{"text": "Of course he thought he had taken refuge in the fort, and applied for admission there himself next day, but could find no trace of Achmet.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2719	lexical	\N	\N	2718	{"text": "This seemed to him so strange that he spoke about it to a sergeant of guides, who brought it to the ears of the commandant.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2720	lexical	\N	\N	2719	{"text": "A thorough search was quickly made, and the body was discovered.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2721	lexical	\N	\N	2720	{"text": "Thus at the very moment that we thought that all was safe we were all four seized and brought to trial on a charge of murder,—three of us because we had held the gate that night, and the fourth because he was known to have been in the company of the murdered man.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2722	lexical	\N	\N	2721	{"text": "Not a word about the jewels came out at the trial, for the rajah had been deposed and driven out of India: so no one had any particular interest in them.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2723	lexical	\N	\N	2722	{"text": "The murder, however, was clearly made out, and it was certain that we must all have been concerned in it.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2724	lexical	\N	\N	2723	{"text": "The three Sikhs got penal servitude for life, and I was condemned to death, though my sentence was afterwards commuted into the same as the others.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2725	lexical	\N	\N	2724	{"text": "“It was rather a queer position that we found ourselves in then.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2726	lexical	\N	\N	2725	{"text": "There we were all four tied by the leg and with precious little chance of ever getting out again, while we each held a secret which might have put each of us in a palace if we could only have made use of it.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_83	section	\N	Section 83	82	{"wordCount": 604}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2727	lexical	\N	\N	2726	{"text": "It was enough to make a man eat his heart out to have to stand the kick and the cuff of every petty jack-in-office, to have rice to eat and water to drink, when that gorgeous fortune was ready for him outside, just waiting to be picked up.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2728	lexical	\N	\N	2727	{"text": "It might have driven me mad; but I was always a pretty stubborn one, so I just held on and bided my time.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2729	lexical	\N	\N	2728	{"text": "“At last it seemed to me to have come.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2730	lexical	\N	\N	2729	{"text": "I was changed from Agra to Madras, and from there to Blair Island in the Andamans.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2731	lexical	\N	\N	2730	{"text": "There are very few white convicts at this settlement, and, as I had behaved well from the first, I soon found myself a sort of privileged person.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2732	lexical	\N	\N	2731	{"text": "I was given a hut in Hope Town, which is a small place on the slopes of Mount Harriet, and I was left pretty much to myself.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2733	lexical	\N	\N	2732	{"text": "It is a dreary, fever-stricken place, and all beyond our little clearings was infested with wild cannibal natives, who were ready enough to blow a poisoned dart at us if they saw a chance.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2734	lexical	\N	\N	2733	{"text": "There was digging, and ditching, and yam-planting, and a dozen other things to be done, so we were busy enough all day; though in the evening we had a little time to ourselves.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2735	lexical	\N	\N	2734	{"text": "Among other things, I learned to dispense drugs for the surgeon, and picked up a smattering of his knowledge.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2736	lexical	\N	\N	2735	{"text": "All the time I was on the lookout for a chance of escape; but it is hundreds of miles from any other land, and there is little or no wind in those seas: so it was a terribly difficult job to get away.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2737	lexical	\N	\N	2736	{"text": "“The surgeon, Dr. Somerton, was a fast, sporting young chap, and the other young officers would meet in his rooms of an evening and play cards.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2738	lexical	\N	\N	2737	{"text": "The surgery, where I used to make up my drugs, was next to his sitting-room, with a small window between us.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2739	lexical	\N	\N	2738	{"text": "Often, if I felt lonesome, I used to turn out the lamp in the surgery, and then, standing there, I could hear their talk and watch their play.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2740	lexical	\N	\N	2739	{"text": "I am fond of a hand at cards myself, and it was almost as good as having one to watch the others.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2741	lexical	\N	\N	2740	{"text": "There was Major Sholto, Captain Morstan, and Lieutenant Bromley Brown, who were in command of the native troops, and there was the surgeon himself, and two or three prison-officials, crafty old hands who played a nice sly safe game.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2742	lexical	\N	\N	2741	{"text": "A very snug little party they used to make.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2743	lexical	\N	\N	2742	{"text": "“Well, there was one thing which very soon struck me, and that was that the soldiers used always to lose and the civilians to win.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2744	lexical	\N	\N	2743	{"text": "Mind, I don’t say that there was anything unfair, but so it was.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2745	lexical	\N	\N	2744	{"text": "These prison-chaps had done little else than play cards ever since they had been at the Andamans, and they knew each other’s game to a point, while the others just played to pass the time and threw their cards down anyhow.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2746	lexical	\N	\N	2745	{"text": "Night after night the soldiers got up poorer men, and the poorer they got the more keen they were to play.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2747	lexical	\N	\N	2746	{"text": "Major Sholto was the hardest hit.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2748	lexical	\N	\N	2747	{"text": "He used to pay in notes and gold at first, but soon it came to notes of hand and for big sums.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2749	lexical	\N	\N	2748	{"text": "He sometimes would win for a few deals, just to give him heart, and then the luck would set in against him worse than ever.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2750	lexical	\N	\N	2749	{"text": "All day he would wander about as black as thunder, and he took to drinking a deal more than was good for him.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2751	lexical	\N	\N	2750	{"text": "“One night he lost even more heavily than usual.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2752	lexical	\N	\N	2751	{"text": "I was sitting in my hut when he and Captain Morstan came stumbling along on the way to their quarters.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2753	lexical	\N	\N	2752	{"text": "They were bosom friends, those two, and never far apart.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2754	lexical	\N	\N	2753	{"text": "The major was raving about his losses.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2755	lexical	\N	\N	2754	{"text": "“‘It’s all up, Morstan,’ he was saying, as they passed my hut.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2756	lexical	\N	\N	2755	{"text": "‘I shall have to send in my papers.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2757	lexical	\N	\N	2756	{"text": "I am a ruined man.’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2758	lexical	\N	\N	2757	{"text": "“‘Nonsense, old chap!’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2759	lexical	\N	\N	2758	{"text": "said the other, slapping him upon the shoulder.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2761	lexical	\N	\N	2760	{"text": "“A couple of days later Major Sholto was strolling on the beach: so I took the chance of speaking to him.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2762	lexical	\N	\N	2761	{"text": "“‘I wish to have your advice, major,’ said I.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2763	lexical	\N	\N	2762	{"text": "“‘Well, Small, what is it?’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2764	lexical	\N	\N	2763	{"text": "he asked, taking his cheroot from his lips.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2765	lexical	\N	\N	2764	{"text": "“‘I wanted to ask you, sir,’ said I, ‘who is the proper person to whom hidden treasure should be handed over.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2766	lexical	\N	\N	2765	{"text": "I know where half a million worth lies, and, as I cannot use it myself, I thought perhaps the best thing that I could do would be to hand it over to the proper authorities, and then perhaps they would get my sentence shortened for me.’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2767	lexical	\N	\N	2766	{"text": "“‘Half a million, Small?’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2768	lexical	\N	\N	2767	{"text": "he gasped, looking hard at me to see if I was in earnest.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2769	lexical	\N	\N	2768	{"text": "“‘Quite that, sir,—in jewels and pearls.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2770	lexical	\N	\N	2769	{"text": "It lies there ready for any one.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2771	lexical	\N	\N	2770	{"text": "And the queer thing about it is that the real owner is outlawed and cannot hold property, so that it belongs to the first comer.’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2772	lexical	\N	\N	2771	{"text": "“‘To government, Small,’ he stammered,—‘to government.’", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2773	lexical	\N	\N	2772	{"text": "But he said it in a halting fashion, and I knew in my heart that I had got him.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2774	lexical	\N	\N	2773	{"text": "“‘You think, then, sir, that I should give the information to the Governor-General?’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2775	lexical	\N	\N	2774	{"text": "said I, quietly.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2776	lexical	\N	\N	2775	{"text": "“‘Well, well, you must not do anything rash, or that you might repent.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2777	lexical	\N	\N	2776	{"text": "Let me hear all about it, Small.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2778	lexical	\N	\N	2777	{"text": "Give me the facts.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2779	lexical	\N	\N	2778	{"text": "“I told him the whole story, with small changes so that he could not identify the places.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2780	lexical	\N	\N	2779	{"text": "When I had finished he stood stock still and full of thought.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2781	lexical	\N	\N	2780	{"text": "I could see by the twitch of his lip that there was a struggle going on within him.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2782	lexical	\N	\N	2781	{"text": "“‘This is a very important matter, Small,’ he said, at last.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2783	lexical	\N	\N	2782	{"text": "‘You must not say a word to any one about it, and I shall see you again soon.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2784	lexical	\N	\N	2783	{"text": "“Two nights later he and his friend Captain Morstan came to my hut in the dead of the night with a lantern.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2785	lexical	\N	\N	2784	{"text": "“‘I want you just to let Captain Morstan hear that story from your own lips, Small,’ said he.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2786	lexical	\N	\N	2785	{"text": "“I repeated it as I had told it before.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2787	lexical	\N	\N	2786	{"text": "“‘It rings true, eh?’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2788	lexical	\N	\N	2787	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2789	lexical	\N	\N	2788	{"text": "‘It’s good enough to act upon?’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2790	lexical	\N	\N	2789	{"text": "“Captain Morstan nodded.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2791	lexical	\N	\N	2790	{"text": "“‘Look here, Small,’ said the major.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2792	lexical	\N	\N	2791	{"text": "‘We have been talking it over, my friend here and I, and we have come to the conclusion that this secret of yours is hardly a government matter, after all, but is a private concern of your own, which of course you have the power of disposing of as you think best.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2793	lexical	\N	\N	2792	{"text": "Now, the question is, what price would you ask for it?", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2794	lexical	\N	\N	2793	{"text": "We might be inclined to take it up, and at least look into it, if we could agree as to terms.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2795	lexical	\N	\N	2794	{"text": "He tried to speak in a cool, careless way, but his eyes were shining with excitement and greed.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2796	lexical	\N	\N	2795	{"text": "“‘Why, as to that, gentlemen,’ I answered, trying also to be cool, but feeling as excited as he did, ‘there is only one bargain which a man in my position can make.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2797	lexical	\N	\N	2796	{"text": "I shall want you to help me to my freedom, and to help my three companions to theirs.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	gregson	entity	character	Gregson	\N	{"description": "A detective named by Holmes.", "firstSection": "section_3"}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2798	lexical	\N	\N	2797	{"text": "We shall then take you into partnership, and give you a fifth share to divide between you.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2799	lexical	\N	\N	2798	{"text": "“‘Hum!’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2800	lexical	\N	\N	2799	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2801	lexical	\N	\N	2800	{"text": "‘A fifth share!", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2802	lexical	\N	\N	2801	{"text": "That is not very tempting.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2803	lexical	\N	\N	2802	{"text": "“‘It would come to fifty thousand apiece,’ said I.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2804	lexical	\N	\N	2803	{"text": "“‘But how can we gain your freedom?", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2805	lexical	\N	\N	2804	{"text": "You know very well that you ask an impossibility.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2806	lexical	\N	\N	2805	{"text": "“‘Nothing of the sort,’ I answered.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2807	lexical	\N	\N	2806	{"text": "‘I have thought it all out to the last detail.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2808	lexical	\N	\N	2807	{"text": "The only bar to our escape is that we can get no boat fit for the voyage, and no provisions to last us for so long a time.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2809	lexical	\N	\N	2808	{"text": "There are plenty of little yachts and yawls at Calcutta or Madras which would serve our turn well.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2810	lexical	\N	\N	2809	{"text": "Do you bring one over.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2811	lexical	\N	\N	2810	{"text": "We shall engage to get aboard her by night, and if you will drop us on any part of the Indian coast you will have done your part of the bargain.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2812	lexical	\N	\N	2811	{"text": "“‘If there were only one,’ he said.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2813	lexical	\N	\N	2812	{"text": "“‘None or all,’ I answered.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2814	lexical	\N	\N	2813	{"text": "‘We have sworn it.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2815	lexical	\N	\N	2814	{"text": "The four of us must always act together.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2816	lexical	\N	\N	2815	{"text": "“‘You see, Morstan,’ said he, ‘Small is a man of his word.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2817	lexical	\N	\N	2816	{"text": "He does not flinch from his friend.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2818	lexical	\N	\N	2817	{"text": "I think we may very well trust him.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2819	lexical	\N	\N	2818	{"text": "“‘It’s a dirty business,’ the other answered.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2820	lexical	\N	\N	2819	{"text": "‘Yet, as you say, the money would save our commissions handsomely.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2821	lexical	\N	\N	2820	{"text": "“‘Well, Small,’ said the major, ‘we must, I suppose, try and meet you.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2822	lexical	\N	\N	2821	{"text": "We must first, of course, test the truth of your story.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2823	lexical	\N	\N	2822	{"text": "Tell me where the box is hid, and I shall get leave of absence and go back to India in the monthly relief-boat to inquire into the affair.’", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2824	lexical	\N	\N	2823	{"text": "“‘Not so fast,’ said I, growing colder as he got hot.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2825	lexical	\N	\N	2824	{"text": "‘I must have the consent of my three comrades.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2826	lexical	\N	\N	2825	{"text": "I tell you that it is four or none with us.’", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2827	lexical	\N	\N	2826	{"text": "“‘Nonsense!’", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2828	lexical	\N	\N	2827	{"text": "he broke in.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2829	lexical	\N	\N	2828	{"text": "‘What have three black fellows to do with our agreement?’", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2830	lexical	\N	\N	2829	{"text": "“‘Black or blue,’ said I, ‘they are in with me, and we all go together.’", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2831	lexical	\N	\N	2830	{"text": "“Well, the matter ended by a second meeting, at which Mahomet Singh, Abdullah Khan, and Dost Akbar were all present.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2832	lexical	\N	\N	2831	{"text": "We talked the matter over again, and at last we came to an arrangement.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2833	lexical	\N	\N	2832	{"text": "We were to provide both the officers with charts of the part of the Agra fort and mark the place in the wall where the treasure was hid.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2834	lexical	\N	\N	2833	{"text": "Major Sholto was to go to India to test our story.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2835	lexical	\N	\N	2834	{"text": "If he found the box he was to leave it there, to send out a small yacht provisioned for a voyage, which was to lie off Rutland Island, and to which we were to make our way, and finally to return to his duties.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2836	lexical	\N	\N	2835	{"text": "Captain Morstan was then to apply for leave of absence, to meet us at Agra, and there we were to have a final division of the treasure, he taking the major’s share as well as his own.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_84	section	\N	Section 84	83	{"wordCount": 608}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2837	lexical	\N	\N	2836	{"text": "All this we sealed by the most solemn oaths that the mind could think or the lips utter.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2838	lexical	\N	\N	2837	{"text": "I sat up all night with paper and ink, and by the morning I had the two charts all ready, signed with the sign of four,—that is, of Abdullah, Akbar, Mahomet, and myself.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2839	lexical	\N	\N	2838	{"text": "“Well, gentlemen, I weary you with my long story, and I know that my friend Mr. Jones is impatient to get me safely stowed in chokey.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2840	lexical	\N	\N	2839	{"text": "I’ll make it as short as I can.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2841	lexical	\N	\N	2840	{"text": "The villain Sholto went off to India, but he never came back again.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2842	lexical	\N	\N	2841	{"text": "Captain Morstan showed me his name among a list of passengers in one of the mail-boats very shortly afterwards.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2843	lexical	\N	\N	2842	{"text": "His uncle had died, leaving him a fortune, and he had left the army, yet he could stoop to treat five men as he had treated us.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2844	lexical	\N	\N	2843	{"text": "Morstan went over to Agra shortly afterwards, and found, as we expected, that the treasure was indeed gone.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2845	lexical	\N	\N	2844	{"text": "The scoundrel had stolen it all, without carrying out one of the conditions on which we had sold him the secret.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2846	lexical	\N	\N	2845	{"text": "From that day I lived only for vengeance.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2847	lexical	\N	\N	2846	{"text": "I thought of it by day and I nursed it by night.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2848	lexical	\N	\N	2847	{"text": "It became an overpowering, absorbing passion with me.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2849	lexical	\N	\N	2848	{"text": "I cared nothing for the law,—nothing for the gallows.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2850	lexical	\N	\N	2849	{"text": "To escape, to track down Sholto, to have my hand upon his throat,—that was my one thought.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2851	lexical	\N	\N	2850	{"text": "Even the Agra treasure had come to be a smaller thing in my mind than the slaying of Sholto.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2852	lexical	\N	\N	2851	{"text": "“Well, I have set my mind on many things in this life, and never one which I did not carry out.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2853	lexical	\N	\N	2852	{"text": "But it was weary years before my time came.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2854	lexical	\N	\N	2853	{"text": "I have told you that I had picked up something of medicine.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2855	lexical	\N	\N	2854	{"text": "One day when Dr. Somerton was down with a fever a little Andaman Islander was picked up by a convict-gang in the woods.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2856	lexical	\N	\N	2855	{"text": "He was sick to death, and had gone to a lonely place to die.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2857	lexical	\N	\N	2856	{"text": "I took him in hand, though he was as venomous as a young snake, and after a couple of months I got him all right and able to walk.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2858	lexical	\N	\N	2857	{"text": "He took a kind of fancy to me then, and would hardly go back to his woods, but was always hanging about my hut.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2859	lexical	\N	\N	2858	{"text": "I learned a little of his lingo from him, and this made him all the fonder of me.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2860	lexical	\N	\N	2859	{"text": "“Tonga—for that was his name—was a fine boatman, and owned a big, roomy canoe of his own.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2861	lexical	\N	\N	2860	{"text": "When I found that he was devoted to me and would do anything to serve me, I saw my chance of escape.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2862	lexical	\N	\N	2861	{"text": "I talked it over with him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2863	lexical	\N	\N	2862	{"text": "He was to bring his boat round on a certain night to an old wharf which was never guarded, and there he was to pick me up.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2864	lexical	\N	\N	2863	{"text": "I gave him directions to have several gourds of water and a lot of yams, cocoa-nuts, and sweet potatoes.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2865	lexical	\N	\N	2864	{"text": "“He was stanch and true, was little Tonga.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2866	lexical	\N	\N	2865	{"text": "No man ever had a more faithful mate.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2867	lexical	\N	\N	2866	{"text": "At the night named he had his boat at the wharf.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2868	lexical	\N	\N	2867	{"text": "As it chanced, however, there was one of the convict-guard down there,—a vile Pathan who had never missed a chance of insulting and injuring me.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2869	lexical	\N	\N	2868	{"text": "I had always vowed vengeance, and now I had my chance.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2870	lexical	\N	\N	2869	{"text": "It was as if fate had placed him in my way that I might pay my debt before I left the island.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2871	lexical	\N	\N	2870	{"text": "He stood on the bank with his back to me, and his carbine on his shoulder.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2872	lexical	\N	\N	2871	{"text": "I looked about for a stone to beat out his brains with, but none could I see.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2873	lexical	\N	\N	2872	{"text": "Then a queer thought came into my head and showed me where I could lay my hand on a weapon.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2874	lexical	\N	\N	2873	{"text": "I sat down in the darkness and unstrapped my wooden leg.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2875	lexical	\N	\N	2874	{"text": "With three long hops I was on him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2876	lexical	\N	\N	2875	{"text": "He put his carbine to his shoulder, but I struck him full, and knocked the whole front of his skull in.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2877	lexical	\N	\N	2876	{"text": "You can see the split in the wood now where I hit him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2878	lexical	\N	\N	2877	{"text": "We both went down together, for I could not keep my balance, but when I got up I found him still lying quiet enough.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2879	lexical	\N	\N	2878	{"text": "I made for the boat, and in an hour we were well out at sea.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2880	lexical	\N	\N	2879	{"text": "Tonga had brought all his earthly possessions with him, his arms and his gods.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2881	lexical	\N	\N	2880	{"text": "Among other things, he had a long bamboo spear, and some Andaman cocoa-nut matting, with which I made a sort of sail.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2882	lexical	\N	\N	2881	{"text": "For ten days we were beating about, trusting to luck, and on the eleventh we were picked up by a trader which was going from Singapore to Jiddah with a cargo of Malay pilgrims.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2883	lexical	\N	\N	2882	{"text": "They were a rum crowd, and Tonga and I soon managed to settle down among them.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2884	lexical	\N	\N	2883	{"text": "They had one very good quality: they let you alone and asked no questions.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2885	lexical	\N	\N	2884	{"text": "“Well, if I were to tell you all the adventures that my little chum and I went through, you would not thank me, for I would have you here until the sun was shining.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2886	lexical	\N	\N	2885	{"text": "Here and there we drifted about the world, something always turning up to keep us from London.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2887	lexical	\N	\N	2886	{"text": "All the time, however, I never lost sight of my purpose.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2888	lexical	\N	\N	2887	{"text": "I would dream of Sholto at night.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2889	lexical	\N	\N	2888	{"text": "A hundred times I have killed him in my sleep.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2890	lexical	\N	\N	2889	{"text": "At last, however, some three or four years ago, we found ourselves in England.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2891	lexical	\N	\N	2890	{"text": "I had no great difficulty in finding where Sholto lived, and I set to work to discover whether he had realised the treasure, or if he still had it.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2892	lexical	\N	\N	2891	{"text": "I made friends with someone who could help me,—I name no names, for I don’t want to get any one else in a hole,—and I soon found that he still had the jewels.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2893	lexical	\N	\N	2892	{"text": "Then I tried to get at him in many ways; but he was pretty sly, and had always two prize-fighters, besides his sons and his khitmutgar, on guard over him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2894	lexical	\N	\N	2893	{"text": "“One day, however, I got word that he was dying.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2895	lexical	\N	\N	2894	{"text": "I hurried at once to the garden, mad that he should slip out of my clutches like that, and, looking through the window, I saw him lying in his bed, with his sons on each side of him.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2896	lexical	\N	\N	2895	{"text": "I’d have come through and taken my chance with the three of them, only even as I looked at him his jaw dropped, and I knew that he was gone.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2897	lexical	\N	\N	2896	{"text": "I got into his room that same night, though, and I searched his papers to see if there was any record of where he had hidden our jewels.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2898	lexical	\N	\N	2897	{"text": "There was not a line, however: so I came away, bitter and savage as a man could be.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2899	lexical	\N	\N	2898	{"text": "Before I left I bethought me that if I ever met my Sikh friends again it would be a satisfaction to know that I had left some mark of our hatred; so I scrawled down the sign of the four of us, as it had been on the chart, and I pinned it on his bosom.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2900	lexical	\N	\N	2899	{"text": "It was too much that he should be taken to the grave without some token from the men whom he had robbed and befooled.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2901	lexical	\N	\N	2900	{"text": "“We earned a living at this time by my exhibiting poor Tonga at fairs and other such places as the black cannibal.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2902	lexical	\N	\N	2901	{"text": "He would eat raw meat and dance his war-dance: so we always had a hatful of pennies after a day’s work.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2903	lexical	\N	\N	2902	{"text": "I still heard all the news from Pondicherry Lodge, and for some years there was no news to hear, except that they were hunting for the treasure.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2904	lexical	\N	\N	2903	{"text": "At last, however, came what we had waited for so long.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2905	lexical	\N	\N	2904	{"text": "The treasure had been found.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	section_85	section	\N	Section 85	84	{"wordCount": 654}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2906	lexical	\N	\N	2905	{"text": "It was up at the top of the house, in Mr. Bartholomew Sholto’s chemical laboratory.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2907	lexical	\N	\N	2906	{"text": "I came at once and had a look at the place, but I could not see how with my wooden leg I was to make my way up to it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2908	lexical	\N	\N	2907	{"text": "I learned, however, about a trap-door in the roof, and also about Mr. Sholto’s supper-hour.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2909	lexical	\N	\N	2908	{"text": "It seemed to me that I could manage the thing easily through Tonga.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2910	lexical	\N	\N	2909	{"text": "I brought him out with me with a long rope wound round his waist.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2911	lexical	\N	\N	2910	{"text": "He could climb like a cat, and he soon made his way through the roof, but, as ill luck would have it, Bartholomew Sholto was still in the room, to his cost.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2912	lexical	\N	\N	2911	{"text": "Tonga thought he had done something very clever in killing him, for when I came up by the rope I found him strutting about as proud as a peacock.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2913	lexical	\N	\N	2912	{"text": "Very much surprised was he when I made at him with the rope’s end and cursed him for a little blood-thirsty imp.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2914	lexical	\N	\N	2913	{"text": "I took the treasure-box and let it down, and then slid down myself, having first left the sign of the four upon the table, to show that the jewels had come back at last to those who had most right to them.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2915	lexical	\N	\N	2914	{"text": "Tonga then pulled up the rope, closed the window, and made off the way that he had come.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2916	lexical	\N	\N	2915	{"text": "“I don’t know that I have anything else to tell you.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2917	lexical	\N	\N	2916	{"text": "I had heard a waterman speak of the speed of Smith’s launch the _Aurora_, so I thought she would be a handy craft for our escape.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2918	lexical	\N	\N	2917	{"text": "I engaged with old Smith, and was to give him a big sum if he got us safe to our ship.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2919	lexical	\N	\N	2918	{"text": "He knew, no doubt, that there was some screw loose, but he was not in our secrets.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2920	lexical	\N	\N	2919	{"text": "All this is the truth, and if I tell it to you, gentlemen, it is not to amuse you,—for you have not done me a very good turn,—but it is because I believe the best defence I can make is just to hold back nothing, but let all the world know how badly I have myself been served by Major Sholto, and how innocent I am of the death of his son.”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2921	lexical	\N	\N	2920	{"text": "“A very remarkable account,” said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2922	lexical	\N	\N	2921	{"text": "“A fitting wind-up to an extremely interesting case.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2923	lexical	\N	\N	2922	{"text": "There is nothing at all new to me in the latter part of your narrative, except that you brought your own rope.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2924	lexical	\N	\N	2923	{"text": "That I did not know.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2925	lexical	\N	\N	2924	{"text": "By the way, I had hoped that Tonga had lost all his darts; yet he managed to shoot one at us in the boat.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2926	lexical	\N	\N	2925	{"text": "“He had lost them all, sir, except the one which was in his blow-pipe at the time.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2927	lexical	\N	\N	2926	{"text": "“Ah, of course,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2928	lexical	\N	\N	2927	{"text": "“I had not thought of that.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2929	lexical	\N	\N	2928	{"text": "“Is there any other point which you would like to ask about?”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2930	lexical	\N	\N	2929	{"text": "asked the convict, affably.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2931	lexical	\N	\N	2930	{"text": "“I think not, thank you,” my companion answered.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2932	lexical	\N	\N	2931	{"text": "“Well, Holmes,” said Athelney Jones, “You are a man to be humoured, and we all know that you are a connoisseur of crime, but duty is duty, and I have gone rather far in doing what you and your friend asked me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2933	lexical	\N	\N	2932	{"text": "I shall feel more at ease when we have our story-teller here safe under lock and key.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2934	lexical	\N	\N	2933	{"text": "The cab still waits, and there are two inspectors downstairs.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2935	lexical	\N	\N	2934	{"text": "I am much obliged to you both for your assistance.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2936	lexical	\N	\N	2935	{"text": "Of course you will be wanted at the trial.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2937	lexical	\N	\N	2936	{"text": "Good-night to you.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2938	lexical	\N	\N	2937	{"text": "“Good-night, gentlemen both,” said Jonathan Small.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2939	lexical	\N	\N	2938	{"text": "“You first, Small,” remarked the wary Jones as they left the room.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2940	lexical	\N	\N	2939	{"text": "“I’ll take particular care that you don’t club me with your wooden leg, whatever you may have done to the gentleman at the Andaman Isles.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2941	lexical	\N	\N	2940	{"text": "“Well, and there is the end of our little drama,” I remarked, after we had set some time smoking in silence.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2942	lexical	\N	\N	2941	{"text": "“I fear that it may be the last investigation in which I shall have the chance of studying your methods.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2943	lexical	\N	\N	2942	{"text": "Miss Morstan has done me the honour to accept me as a husband in prospective.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2944	lexical	\N	\N	2943	{"text": "He gave a most dismal groan.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2945	lexical	\N	\N	2944	{"text": "“I feared as much,” said he.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2946	lexical	\N	\N	2945	{"text": "“I really cannot congratulate you.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2947	lexical	\N	\N	2946	{"text": "I was a little hurt.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2948	lexical	\N	\N	2947	{"text": "“Have you any reason to be dissatisfied with my choice?”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2949	lexical	\N	\N	2948	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2950	lexical	\N	\N	2949	{"text": "“Not at all.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2951	lexical	\N	\N	2950	{"text": "I think she is one of the most charming young ladies I ever met, and might have been most useful in such work as we have been doing.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2952	lexical	\N	\N	2951	{"text": "She had a decided genius that way: witness the way in which she preserved that Agra plan from all the other papers of her father.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2953	lexical	\N	\N	2952	{"text": "But love is an emotional thing, and whatever is emotional is opposed to that true cold reason which I place above all things.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2954	lexical	\N	\N	2953	{"text": "I should never marry myself, lest I bias my judgment.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2955	lexical	\N	\N	2954	{"text": "“I trust,” said I, laughing, “that my judgment may survive the ordeal.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2956	lexical	\N	\N	2955	{"text": "But you look weary.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2957	lexical	\N	\N	2956	{"text": "“Yes, the reaction is already upon me.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2958	lexical	\N	\N	2957	{"text": "I shall be as limp as a rag for a week.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2959	lexical	\N	\N	2958	{"text": "“Strange,” said I, “how terms of what in another man I should call laziness alternate with your fits of splendid energy and vigour.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2960	lexical	\N	\N	2959	{"text": "“Yes,” he answered, “there are in me the makings of a very fine loafer and also of a pretty spry sort of fellow.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2961	lexical	\N	\N	2960	{"text": "I often think of those lines of old Goethe,—", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2962	lexical	\N	\N	2961	{"text": "Schade dass die Natur nur _einen_ Mensch aus Dir schuf, Denn zum würdigen Mann war und zum Schelmen der Stoff.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2963	lexical	\N	\N	2962	{"text": "“By the way, _à propos_ of this Norwood business, you see that they had, as I surmised, a confederate in the house, who could be none other than Lal Rao, the butler: so Jones actually has the undivided honour of having caught one fish in his great haul.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2964	lexical	\N	\N	2963	{"text": "“The division seems rather unfair,” I remarked.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2965	lexical	\N	\N	2964	{"text": "“You have done all the work in this business.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2966	lexical	\N	\N	2965	{"text": "I get a wife out of it, Jones gets the credit, pray what remains for you?”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2967	lexical	\N	\N	2966	{"text": "“For me,” said Sherlock Holmes, “there still remains the cocaine-bottle.”", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	sentence_2968	lexical	\N	\N	2967	{"text": "And he stretched his long white hand up for it.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	the_sign_of_the_four	entity	case	The Sign of the Four	\N	{"client": "unknown", "source": "the-sign-of-the-four", "outcome": "unresolved", "crime_type": "other", "description": "The story's investigation case.", "firstSection": "section_1", "primary_location": "unknown"}
sign-of-the-four	chapter_i_the_science_of_deduction	entity	document	Chapter I: The Science of Deduction	\N	{"description": "Chapter heading named in the section.", "firstSection": "section_3", "document_type": "manuscript", "content_summary": "Chapter I titled The Science of Deduction."}
sign-of-the-four	morphine	entity	object	Morphine	\N	{"description": "A drug named in the dialogue.", "firstSection": "section_3"}
