sign-of-the-four	event_3_1	event	\N	Holmes takes up his bottle and hypodermic syringe	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_18"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_2	event	\N	Holmes adjusts the needle and rolls back his shirt-cuff	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_19"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_3	event	\N	Holmes injects himself with the syringe	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_21"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_4	event	\N	Watson asks whether Holmes is taking morphine or cocaine	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_27", "sentence_28"], "communicatesContent": "Which is it to-day? morphine or cocaine?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_5	event	\N	Holmes states that he is using cocaine	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_29", "sentence_30", "sentence_31"], "communicatesContent": "It is cocaine, a seven-per-cent solution."}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_6	event	\N	Holmes invites Watson to try the cocaine	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_32"], "communicatesContent": "Would you care to try it?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_7	event	\N	Watson refuses to try the cocaine	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_33", "sentence_34", "sentence_35"], "communicatesContent": "No, indeed. My constitution has not got over the Afghan campaign yet. I cannot afford to throw any extra strain upon it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_8	event	\N	Watson warns Holmes against cocaine use	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_40", "sentence_41", "sentence_42", "sentence_43", "sentence_44", "sentence_45", "sentence_46", "sentence_47"], "communicatesContent": "But consider! Count the cost! Your brain may, as you say, be roused and excited, but it is a pathological and morbid process, which involves increased tissue-change and may at last leave a permanent weakness. You know, too, what a black reaction comes upon you. Surely the game is hardly worth the candle. Why should you, for a mere passing pleasure, risk the loss of those great powers with which you have been endowed? Remember that I speak not only as one comrade to another, but as a medical man to one for whose constitution he is to some extent answerable."}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_9	event	\N	Holmes responds that he does not feel offended and assumes a conversational posture	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_48", "sentence_49"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_10	event	\N	Holmes says his mind rebels at stagnation and that he craves mental work	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_50", "sentence_51", "sentence_52", "sentence_53", "sentence_54", "sentence_55"], "communicatesContent": "My mind rebels at stagnation. Give me problems, give me work, give me the most abstruse cryptogram or the most intricate analysis, and I am in my own proper atmosphere. I can dispense then with artificial stimulants. But I abhor the dull routine of existence. I crave for mental exaltation. That is why I have chosen my own particular profession,—or rather created it, for I am the only one in the world."}
sign-of-the-four	event_3_11	event	\N	Holmes identifies himself as the only unofficial consulting detective	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_56", "sentence_57", "sentence_58", "sentence_59", "sentence_60", "sentence_61", "sentence_62", "sentence_63", "sentence_64", "sentence_65"], "communicatesContent": "The only unofficial consulting detective. I am the last and highest court of appeal in detection. When Gregson or Lestrade or Athelney Jones are out of their depths—which, by the way, is their normal state—the matter is laid before me. I examine the data, as an expert, and pronounce a specialist’s opinion. I claim no credit in such cases. My name figures in no newspaper. The work itself, the pleasure of finding a field for my peculiar powers, is my highest reward. But you have yourself had some experience of my methods of work in the Jefferson Hope case."}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_1	event	\N	Watson says he was never so struck by anything in his life	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_66", "sentence_67", "sentence_68"], "communicatesContent": "I was never so struck by anything in my life. I even embodied it in a small brochure with the somewhat fantastic title of 'A Study in Scarlet.'"}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_2	event	\N	Holmes shakes his head sadly	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_69"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_3	event	\N	Holmes says he glanced over Watson's brochure and criticizes it	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_70", "sentence_71", "sentence_72", "sentence_73", "sentence_74", "sentence_75", "sentence_76", "sentence_77"], "communicatesContent": "I glanced over it. Honestly, I cannot congratulate you upon it. Detection is, or ought to be, an exact science, and should be treated in the same cold and unemotional manner. You have attempted to tinge it with romanticism. Some facts should be suppressed, or at least a just sense of proportion should be observed in treating them. The only point in the case which deserved mention was the curious analytical reasoning from effects to causes by which I succeeded in unraveling it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_4	event	\N	Watson feels annoyed and irritated by Holmes's criticism	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_78", "sentence_79"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_5	event	\N	Watson nurses his wounded leg	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_80", "sentence_81", "sentence_82"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_6	event	\N	Holmes speaks about his recent continental practice and François Le Villard	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_83", "sentence_84", "sentence_85", "sentence_86", "sentence_87", "sentence_88", "sentence_89", "sentence_90", "sentence_91", "sentence_92", "sentence_93", "sentence_94", "sentence_95", "sentence_96", "sentence_97"], "communicatesContent": "My practice has extended recently to the Continent. I was consulted last week by François Le Villard, who has come rather to the front lately in the French detective service. He has all the Celtic power of quick intuition, but he is deficient in the wide range of exact knowledge which is essential to the higher developments of his art. The case was concerned with a will, and possessed some features of interest. I was able to refer him to two parallel cases, the one at Riga in 1857, and the other at St. Louis in 1871, which have suggested to him the true solution. Here is the letter which I had this morning acknowledging my assistance."}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_7	event	\N	Holmes tosses over a crumpled sheet of foreign notepaper	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_88", "sentence_89"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_8	event	\N	Watson glances down the note and sees the Frenchman's praise	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_90", "sentence_91"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_1	event	\N	The group follows the Indian into a passage and through a door	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_499"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_9	event	\N	Holmes says François Le Villard rates his assistance too highly and describes his abilities	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_92", "sentence_93", "sentence_94", "sentence_95", "sentence_96", "sentence_97"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, he rates my assistance too highly. He has considerable gifts himself. He possesses two out of the three qualities necessary for the ideal detective. He has the power of observation and that of deduction. He is only wanting in knowledge; and that may come in time. He is now translating my small works into French."}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_10	event	\N	Watson asks about Holmes's works and Holmes laughs	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_98", "sentence_99", "sentence_100"], "communicatesContent": "Your works?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_4_11	event	\N	Holmes says he has written several technical monographs and describes one on tobacco ashes	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_101", "sentence_102", "sentence_103", "sentence_104", "sentence_105", "sentence_106", "sentence_107"], "communicatesContent": "I have been guilty of several monographs. They are all upon technical subjects. Here, for example, is one 'Upon the Distinction between the Ashes of the Various Tobaccoes.' In it I enumerate a hundred and forty forms of cigar-, cigarette-, and pipe-tobacco, with coloured plates illustrating the difference in the ash. It is a point which is continually turning up in criminal trials, and which is sometimes of supreme importance as a clue. If you can say definitely, for example, that some murder has been done by a man who was smoking an Indian lunkah, it obviously narrows your field of search. To the trained eye there is as much difference between the black ash of a Trichinopoly and the white fluff of bird's-eye as there is between a cabbage and a potato."}
sign-of-the-four	event_5_1	event	\N	Holmes explains observation and deduction using the post office example	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_119", "sentence_125", "sentence_126", "sentence_127", "sentence_128", "sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_132", "sentence_133", "sentence_134", "sentence_135"], "communicatesContent": "Observation shows me that you have been to the Wigmore Street Post-Office this morning, but deduction lets me know that when there you dispatched a telegram. Observation tells me that you have a little reddish mould adhering to your instep. Just opposite the Wigmore Street Office they have taken up the pavement and thrown up some earth of a peculiar reddish tint. I knew that you had not written a letter, since I sat opposite to you all morning. I see also in your open desk there that you have a sheet of stamps and a thick bundle of post-cards. What could you go into the post-office for, then, but to send a wire? Eliminate all other factors, and the one which remains must be the truth."}
sign-of-the-four	event_5_2	event	\N	Watson confirms the inference about the telegram	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_120", "sentence_121", "sentence_122", "sentence_123", "sentence_124", "sentence_136", "sentence_137"], "communicatesContent": "Right! Right on both points! But I confess that I don’t see how you arrived at it. It was a sudden impulse upon my part, and I have mentioned it to no one. In this case it certainly is so. The thing, however, is, as you say, of the simplest."}
sign-of-the-four	event_5_3	event	\N	Watson asks Holmes to test the theory on a watch	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_138", "sentence_139", "sentence_140", "sentence_141", "sentence_142", "sentence_143"], "communicatesContent": "Would you think me impertinent if I were to put your theories to a more severe test? I have here a watch which has recently come into my possession. Would you have the kindness to let me have an opinion upon the character or habits of the late owner?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_5_4	event	\N	Watson hands Holmes the watch	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_144"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_5_5	event	\N	Holmes examines the watch	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_145", "sentence_146"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_1	event	\N	Holmes remarks that there are hardly any data	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_147"], "communicatesContent": "There are hardly any data."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_2	event	\N	Holmes says the watch has been recently cleaned	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_148"], "communicatesContent": "The watch has been recently cleaned, which robs me of my most suggestive facts."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_3	event	\N	Watson agrees with Holmes	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_149"], "communicatesContent": "You are right."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_4	event	\N	Watson says the watch was cleaned before it was sent	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_150"], "communicatesContent": "It was cleaned before being sent to me."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_5	event	\N	Holmes deduces the watch belonged to Watson's elder brother and was inherited from the father	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_153", "sentence_154", "sentence_157", "sentence_158", "sentence_159", "sentence_160", "sentence_161", "sentence_162", "sentence_163", "sentence_164"], "communicatesContent": "Subject to your correction, I should judge that the watch belonged to your elder brother, who inherited it from your father."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_6	event	\N	Watson confirms Holmes's deduction so far	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_165"], "communicatesContent": "Right, so far."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_7	event	\N	Holmes says Watson's brother was untidy and careless, squandered his chances, lived in poverty, took to drink, and died	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_167", "sentence_168", "sentence_169"], "communicatesContent": "He was a man of untidy habits,—very untidy and careless. He was left with good prospects, but he threw away his chances, lived for some time in poverty with occasional short intervals of prosperity, and finally, taking to drink, he died. That is all I can gather."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_8	event	\N	Watson angrily accuses Holmes of making an unworthy deduction	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_170", "sentence_171", "sentence_172", "sentence_173", "sentence_174", "sentence_175"], "communicatesContent": "This is unworthy of you, Holmes. I could not have believed that you would have descended to this. You have made inquires into the history of my unhappy brother, and you now pretend to deduce this knowledge in some fanciful way. You cannot expect me to believe that you have read all this from his old watch! It is unkind, and, to speak plainly, has a touch of charlatanism in it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_9	event	\N	Holmes apologizes and says he did not know Watson had a brother until the watch was handed to him	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_176", "sentence_177", "sentence_178"], "communicatesContent": "My dear doctor, pray accept my apologies. Viewing the matter as an abstract problem, I had forgotten how personal and painful a thing it might be to you. I assure you, however, that I never even knew that you had a brother until you handed me the watch."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_10	event	\N	Watson asks how Holmes obtained the facts	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_179", "sentence_180"], "communicatesContent": "Then how in the name of all that is wonderful did you get these facts? They are absolutely correct in every particular."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_11	event	\N	Holmes says he used probability rather than guesswork and explains that small facts support large inferences	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_181", "sentence_182", "sentence_183", "sentence_184", "sentence_185", "sentence_186", "sentence_187"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, that is good luck. I could only say what was the balance of probability. I did not at all expect to be so accurate. No, no: I never guess. It is a shocking habit,—destructive to the logical faculty. What seems strange to you is only so because you do not follow my train of thought or observe the small facts upon which large inferences may depend."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_12	event	\N	Holmes explains that the watch-case's dents and scratches indicate careless handling	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_188", "sentence_189", "sentence_190", "sentence_191"], "communicatesContent": "I began by stating that your brother was careless. When you observe the lower part of that watch-case you notice that it is not only dinted in two places, but it is cut and marked all over from the habit of keeping other hard objects, such as coins or keys, in the same pocket. Surely it is no great feat to assume that a man who treats a fifty-guinea watch so cavalierly must be a careless man. Neither is it a very far-fetched inference that a man who inherits one article of such value is pretty well provided for in other respects."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_13	event	\N	Watson acknowledges Holmes's reasoning	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_192"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_14	event	\N	Holmes explains that scratch marks inside the watch-case indicate pawned pledges and irregular finances	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_193", "sentence_194", "sentence_195", "sentence_196", "sentence_197"], "communicatesContent": "It is very customary for pawnbrokers in England, when they take a watch, to scratch the number of the ticket with a pin-point upon the inside of the case. It is more handy than a label, as there is no risk of the number being lost or transposed. There are no less than four such numbers visible to my lens on the inside of this case. Inference,—that your brother was often at low water. Secondary inference,—that he had occasional bursts of prosperity, or he could not have redeemed the pledge."}
sign-of-the-four	event_6_15	event	\N	Holmes points to the key-hole scratches and attributes them to a drunkard's watch	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_198", "sentence_199", "sentence_200", "sentence_201", "sentence_202", "sentence_203"], "communicatesContent": "Finally, I ask you to look at the inner plate, which contains the key-hole. Look at the thousands of scratches all round the hole,—marks where the key has slipped. What sober man’s key could have scored those grooves? But you will never see a drunkard’s watch without them. He winds it at night, and he leaves these traces of his unsteady hand. Where is the mystery in all this?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_1	event	\N	Watson apologises for an injustice and says he should have had more faith in Holmes's faculty	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_204", "sentence_205", "sentence_206"], "communicatesContent": "It is as clear as daylight. I regret the injustice which I did you. I should have had more faith in your marvellous faculty."}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_2	event	\N	Watson asks Holmes whether he has any professional inquiry on foot	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_207"], "communicatesContent": "May I ask whether you have any professional inquiry on foot at present?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_3	event	\N	Holmes says he has none and explains his cocaine use	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_208", "sentence_209", "sentence_210", "sentence_211", "sentence_212", "sentence_213", "sentence_214", "sentence_215", "sentence_216", "sentence_217"], "communicatesContent": "None. Hence the cocaine. I cannot live without brain-work. What else is there to live for? Stand at the window here. Was ever such a dreary, dismal, unprofitable world? See how the yellow fog swirls down the street and drifts across the dun-coloured houses. What could be more hopelessly prosaic and material? What is the use of having powers, doctor, when one has no field upon which to exert them? Crime is commonplace, existence is commonplace, and no qualities save those which are commonplace have any function upon earth."}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_4	event	\N	Mrs. Hudson enters with a visiting card	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_218"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_5	event	\N	Mrs. Hudson identifies a young lady for Holmes	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "mrs_hudson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_219"], "communicatesContent": "A young lady for you, sir."}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_6	event	\N	Holmes reads the name on the card	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_220"], "communicatesContent": "Miss Mary Morstan."}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_7	event	\N	Holmes says he has no recollection of the name and tells Mrs. Hudson to show the visitor up	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_221", "sentence_222", "sentence_223"], "communicatesContent": "Hum! I have no recollection of the name. Ask the young lady to step up, Mrs. Hudson."}
sign-of-the-four	event_7_8	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson not to go and says he should remain	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_224", "sentence_225"], "communicatesContent": "Don't go, doctor. I should prefer that you remain."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_1	event	\N	Mary Morstan enters the room	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_227"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_2	event	\N	Mary Morstan sits in the chair Holmes places for her	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_233"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_3	event	\N	Mary Morstan speaks to Holmes about her employer's prior case	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_234", "sentence_235"], "communicatesContent": "I have come to you, Mr. Holmes, because you once enabled my employer, Mrs. Cecil Forrester, to unravel a little domestic complication. She was much impressed by your kindness and skill."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_4	event	\N	Holmes replies about Mrs. Cecil Forrester's case	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_236", "sentence_237", "sentence_238"], "communicatesContent": "Mrs. Cecil Forrester. I believe that I was of some slight service to her. The case, however, as I remember it, was a very simple one."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_5	event	\N	Mary Morstan says her situation is strange and inexplicable	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_239", "sentence_240", "sentence_241"], "communicatesContent": "She did not think so. But at least you cannot say the same of mine. I can hardly imagine anything more strange, more utterly inexplicable, than the situation in which I find myself."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_6	event	\N	Holmes invites Mary Morstan to state her case	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_242", "sentence_243", "sentence_244"], "communicatesContent": "State your case."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_7	event	\N	Mary Morstan asks Watson to remain	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_246", "sentence_247", "sentence_248", "sentence_249"], "communicatesContent": "If your friend would be good enough to stop, he might be of inestimable service to me."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_8	event	\N	Mary Morstan tells the facts of her father and childhood	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_250", "sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253"], "communicatesContent": "Briefly, the facts are these. My father was an officer in an Indian regiment who sent me home when I was quite a child. My mother was dead, and I had no relative in England. I was placed, however, in a comfortable boarding establishment at Edinburgh, and there I remained until I was seventeen years of age."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_9	event	\N	Captain Morstan returns home and telegraphs Mary Morstan from London	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "captain_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256"], "communicatesContent": "I have arrived all safe. Come down at once. Langham Hotel."}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_10	event	\N	Mary Morstan travels to the Langham Hotel and learns Captain Morstan is absent	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_257"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_11	event	\N	Mary Morstan waits all day for news of Captain Morstan	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_258"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_12	event	\N	Mary Morstan contacts the police and advertises for Captain Morstan	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_259"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_8_13	event	\N	The inquiries produce no result and Captain Morstan remains missing	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_260", "sentence_261"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_1	event	\N	Major Sholto is identified as the only known friend in town	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_269", "sentence_270"], "communicatesContent": "Only one friend in town is known: Major Sholto, of the 34th Bombay Infantry."}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_2	event	\N	A newspaper advertisement appears seeking Mary Morstan's address	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "the_times", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_275", "sentence_276"], "communicatesContent": "Asks for the address of Miss Mary Morstan and states that it would be to her advantage to come forward."}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_3	event	\N	Mary Morstan publishes her address in the advertisement column	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_277", "sentence_278"], "communicatesContent": "Mary Morstan's address is published in the advertisement column."}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_4	event	\N	Mary Morstan receives a pearl in a cardboard box	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_279", "sentence_280"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_5	event	\N	A similar pearl box arrives every year on the same date	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_281", "sentence_282"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_6	event	\N	Mary Morstan receives a letter by post	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_289", "sentence_290", "sentence_291", "sentence_305"], "communicatesContent": "Be at the third pillar from the left outside the Lyceum Theatre to-night at seven o’clock. If you are distrustful, bring two friends. You are a wronged woman, and shall have justice. Do not bring police. If you do, all will be in vain. Your unknown friend."}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_7	event	\N	Holmes examines the envelope	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_291", "sentence_292", "sentence_299"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_8	event	\N	Holmes and the others agree to go to the meeting	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_307", "sentence_308", "sentence_309", "sentence_310", "sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_315", "sentence_316", "sentence_318", "sentence_319"], "communicatesContent": "We shall most certainly go; Holmes, Watson, and Mary Morstan will attend, and Miss Morstan must not be later than six."}
sign-of-the-four	event_9_9	event	\N	Holmes inspects the handwriting samples	8	{"section": "section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_320", "sentence_321", "sentence_322", "sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325", "sentence_326", "sentence_327", "sentence_328", "sentence_329", "sentence_330"], "communicatesContent": "The handwriting on the letter and the pearl-box addresses is the same; he asks whether it resembles her father's hand."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_1	event	\N	The visitor says farewell and leaves	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "our_visitor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_338", "sentence_339"], "communicatesContent": "Au revoir."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_2	event	\N	Watson comments on the visitor's attractiveness	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_340", "sentence_341"], "communicatesContent": "What a very attractive woman!"}
valley-of-fear	section_87	section	\N	Section 87	86	{"wordCount": 602}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_3	event	\N	Watson criticizes Holmes for not observing the woman	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_343", "sentence_344", "sentence_345", "sentence_346", "sentence_347", "sentence_348"], "communicatesContent": "You really are an automaton,—a calculating-machine! There is something positively inhuman in you at times."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_4	event	\N	Holmes explains his method of avoiding bias	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_349", "sentence_350", "sentence_351", "sentence_352", "sentence_353", "sentence_354", "sentence_355", "sentence_356"], "communicatesContent": "It is of the first importance not to allow your judgment to be biased by personal qualities. A client is to me a mere unit, a factor in a problem. The emotional qualities are antagonistic to clear reasoning. I assure you that the most winning woman I ever knew was hanged for poisoning three little children for their insurance-money, and the most repellant man of my acquaintance is a philanthropist who has spent nearly a quarter of a million upon the London poor. I never make exceptions. An exception disproves the rule."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_5	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson about handwriting and points to a scribble	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_357", "sentence_358"], "communicatesContent": "Have you ever had occasion to study character in handwriting? What do you make of this fellow’s scribble?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_6	event	\N	Watson describes the handwriting	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_359", "sentence_360"], "communicatesContent": "It is legible and regular. A man of business habits and some force of character."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_7	event	\N	Holmes analyzes the handwriting in detail	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_361", "sentence_362", "sentence_363", "sentence_364", "sentence_365", "sentence_366"], "communicatesContent": "Look at his long letters. They hardly rise above the common herd. That d might be an a, and that l an e. Men of character always differentiate their long letters, however illegibly they may write. There is vacillation in his k’s and self-esteem in his capitals."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_8	event	\N	Holmes leaves to make references and recommends a book	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_367", "sentence_368", "sentence_369", "sentence_370", "sentence_371"], "communicatesContent": "I am going out now. I have some few references to make. Let me recommend this book, one of the most remarkable ever penned. It is Winwood Reade’s ‘Martyrdom of Man.’ I shall be back in an hour."}
sign-of-the-four	event_10_9	event	\N	Watson sits by the window and reads the book while thinking about the visitor	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_372", "sentence_373", "sentence_374", "sentence_375", "sentence_376", "sentence_377", "sentence_378"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_1	event	\N	Holmes returns home	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_380"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_2	event	\N	Holmes speaks about the matter and the facts	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_382", "sentence_383"], "communicatesContent": "There is no great mystery in this matter. The facts appear to admit of only one explanation."}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_3	event	\N	Watson responds that Holmes has not solved it	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_384", "sentence_385", "sentence_386", "sentence_387", "sentence_388", "sentence_389"], "communicatesContent": "What! you have solved it already?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_4	event	\N	Holmes states that he found a suggestive fact in The Times	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_390"], "communicatesContent": "I have just found, on consulting the back files of the Times, that Major Sholto, of Upper Norwood, late of the 34th Bombay Infantry, died upon the 28th of April, 1882."}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_5	event	\N	Holmes explains the sequence involving Captain Morstan, Major Sholto, and the daughter's gifts	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_395", "sentence_396", "sentence_397", "sentence_398", "sentence_399", "sentence_400", "sentence_401", "sentence_402"], "communicatesContent": "Captain Morstan disappears. The only person in London whom he could have visited is Major Sholto. Major Sholto denies having heard that he was in London. Four years later Sholto dies. Within a week of his death Captain Morstan’s daughter receives a valuable present, which is repeated from year to year, and now culminates in a letter which describes her as a wronged woman. What wrong can it refer to except this deprivation of her father? And why should the presents begin immediately after Sholto’s death, unless it is that Sholto’s heir knows something of the mystery and desires to make compensation? Have you any alternative theory which will meet the facts?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_6	event	\N	Holmes says the expedition will solve the difficulties	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_410", "sentence_411", "sentence_412", "sentence_413", "sentence_414"], "communicatesContent": "There are difficulties; there are certainly difficulties. But our expedition of to-night will solve them all. Ah, here is a four-wheeler, and Miss Morstan is inside. Are you all ready? Then we had better go down, for it is a little past the hour."}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_7	event	\N	Holmes takes his revolver from his drawer and pockets it	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_415", "sentence_416"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_8	event	\N	Miss Morstan arrives by four-wheeler with Watson and Holmes	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_412", "sentence_417", "sentence_418"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_9	event	\N	Miss Morstan says Major Sholto was a friend of her father and that they served together in the Andaman Islands	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_419", "sentence_420", "sentence_421"], "communicatesContent": "Major Sholto was a very particular friend of papa’s. His letters were full of allusions to the major. He and papa were in command of the troops at the Andaman Islands, so they were thrown a great deal together."}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_10	event	\N	Miss Morstan presents the curious paper from her father's desk	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_422", "sentence_423", "sentence_424"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_2	event	\N	The Indian opens the door on the right	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_499"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_11_11	event	\N	Holmes examines the curious paper	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_425", "sentence_426", "sentence_427", "sentence_428", "sentence_429", "sentence_430", "sentence_431", "sentence_432", "sentence_433", "sentence_434", "sentence_435"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_1	event	\N	A pocket-book contains the found item	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_437"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_2	event	\N	Holmes tells Miss Morstan to preserve the item carefully	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_438"], "communicatesContent": "Preserve it carefully, then, Miss Morstan, for it may prove to be of use to us."}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_3	event	\N	Holmes says he begins to suspect the matter is deeper and subtler than he first supposed	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_439"], "communicatesContent": "I begin to suspect that this matter may turn out to be much deeper and more subtle than I at first supposed."}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_4	event	\N	Holmes says he must reconsider his ideas	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_440"], "communicatesContent": "I must reconsider my ideas."}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_5	event	\N	Holmes leans back in the cab and thinks intently	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_441"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_6	event	\N	Miss Morstan and Watson chat in an undertone during the expedition	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_442"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_7	event	\N	Holmes maintains reserve until the end of the journey	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_442"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_8	event	\N	Holmes jots figures and memoranda in his notebook by lantern light	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_452"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_9	event	\N	The travelers arrive at the Lyceum Theatre	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_453"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_10	event	\N	A stream of hansoms and four-wheelers arrives at the theatre and discharges passengers	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_454"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_11	event	\N	The travelers reach the third pillar and are approached by a coachman	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_455", "sentence_456", "sentence_457"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_12	event	\N	Miss Morstan identifies herself and her companions to the coachman	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_458"], "communicatesContent": "I am Miss Morstan, and these two gentlemen are my friends."}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_13	event	\N	The coachman asks Miss Morstan for her word that neither companion is a police-officer	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "coachman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_460"], "communicatesContent": "I was to ask you to give me your word that neither of your companions is a police-officer."}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_14	event	\N	Miss Morstan gives her word	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_461"], "communicatesContent": "I give you my word on that."}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_15	event	\N	A street Arab leads across a four-wheeler and opens the door	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_462"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_16	event	\N	The coachman mounts the box and the travelers take their places inside the carriage	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_463"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_17	event	\N	The driver whips up the horse and the carriage departs at a furious pace through the foggy streets	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_464"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_18	event	\N	Holmes and Watson travel to an unknown place on an unknown errand	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_466"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_12_19	event	\N	Holmes mutters names while the cab moves through squares and by-streets	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_472"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_1	event	\N	The cab passes Vincent Square and comes out on Vauxhall Bridge Road	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_474", "sentence_475"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_2	event	\N	The cab reaches the Surrey side and crosses the bridge	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_476", "sentence_478"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_3	event	\N	The cab gives a fleeting view of the Thames	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_479", "sentence_480"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_4	event	\N	The cab travels through Wordsworth Road, Priory Road, Lark Hall Lane, Stockwell Place, Robert Street, and Cold Harbor Lane	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_481", "sentence_486"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_5	event	\N	The cab reaches a questionable and forbidding neighbourhood	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_487", "sentence_488"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_6	event	\N	The cab draws up at the third house in a new terrace	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_491"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_7	event	\N	A Hindoo servant opens the door	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_493"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_8	event	\N	The Hindoo servant says that the Sahib awaits the visitors	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "hindoo_servant", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_495"], "communicatesContent": "The Sahib awaits you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_13_9	event	\N	An unseen voice tells the khitmutgar to show them in straight in	12	{"section": "section_13", "speakerId": "the_sahib", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_496", "sentence_497"], "communicatesContent": "Show them in to me, khitmutgar. Show them straight in to me."}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_3	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto stands in the lit room and repeatedly greets Miss Morstan and the gentlemen	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_500", "sentence_505", "sentence_506"], "communicatesContent": "Your servant, Miss Morstan. Your servant, gentlemen."}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_4	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto invites the visitors into his sanctum	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_507", "sentence_508", "sentence_509"], "communicatesContent": "Pray step into my little sanctum. A small place, miss, but furnished to my own liking. An oasis of art in the howling desert of South London."}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_5	event	\N	The visitors enter Thaddeus Sholto's richly furnished apartment	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_510", "sentence_512", "sentence_513", "sentence_514", "sentence_515", "sentence_516"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_6	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto identifies himself to Miss Morstan and the gentlemen	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_517", "sentence_518", "sentence_519", "sentence_520", "sentence_521"], "communicatesContent": "Mr. Thaddeus Sholto. That is my name. You are Miss Morstan, of course. And these gentlemen—"}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_7	event	\N	Watson examines Thaddeus Sholto's heart	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_522", "sentence_523", "sentence_524", "sentence_525", "sentence_526", "sentence_527", "sentence_528", "sentence_529", "sentence_530"], "communicatesContent": "It appears to be normal. You have no cause for uneasiness."}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_8	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto explains his anxiety and speaks about Miss Morstan's father	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_531", "sentence_532", "sentence_533", "sentence_534"], "communicatesContent": "You will excuse my anxiety, Miss Morstan. I am a great sufferer, and I have long had suspicions as to that valve. I am delighted to hear that they are unwarranted. Had your father, Miss Morstan, refrained from throwing a strain upon his heart, he might have been alive now."}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_9	event	\N	Miss Morstan reacts to the reference to her father	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_536", "sentence_537"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_10	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto offers information and asks for secrecy and witnesses	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_538", "sentence_539", "sentence_540", "sentence_541", "sentence_542", "sentence_543"], "communicatesContent": "I can give you every information, and, what is more, I can do you justice; and I will, too, whatever Brother Bartholomew may say. I am so glad to have your friends here, not only as an escort to you, but also as witnesses to what I am about to do and say. The three of us can show a bold front to Brother Bartholomew. But let us have no outsiders,—no police or officials. We can settle everything satisfactorily among ourselves, without any interference. Nothing would annoy Brother Bartholomew more than any publicity."}
sign-of-the-four	event_14_11	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto sits on a low settee and looks at the visitors	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_544"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_1	event	\N	Holmes assures that what is said will go no further	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_545", "sentence_546", "sentence_547", "sentence_548", "sentence_549"], "communicatesContent": "whatever you may choose to say will go no further."}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_2	event	\N	Holmes offers Miss Morstan wine and tobacco-smoke	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_550", "sentence_551", "sentence_552", "sentence_553", "sentence_554", "sentence_555", "sentence_556"], "communicatesContent": "May I offer you a glass of Chianti, Miss Morstan? Or of Tokay? I keep no other wines. Shall I open a flask? No? Well, then, I trust that you have no objection to tobacco-smoke, to the mild balsamic odour of the Eastern tobacco. I am a little nervous, and I find my hookah an invaluable sedative."}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_3	event	\N	Holmes lights his hookah and smokes it	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_557", "sentence_558"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_4	event	\N	Sholto explains his precautions and preferences	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_559", "sentence_560", "sentence_561", "sentence_562", "sentence_563", "sentence_564", "sentence_565", "sentence_566", "sentence_567", "sentence_568", "sentence_569"], "communicatesContent": "When I first determined to make this communication to you, I might have given you my address, but I feared that you might disregard my request and bring unpleasant people with you. I took the liberty, therefore, of making an appointment in such a way that my man Williams might be able to see you first. I have complete confidence in his discretion, and he had orders, if he were dissatisfied, to proceed no further in the matter. You will excuse these precautions, but I am a man of somewhat retiring, and I might even say refined, tastes, and there is nothing more unæsthetic than a policeman. I have a natural shrinking from all forms of rough materialism. I seldom come in contact with the rough crowd. I live, as you see, with some little atmosphere of elegance around me. I may call myself a patron of the arts. It is my weakness. The landscape is a genuine Corot, and, though a connoisseur might perhaps throw a doubt upon that Salvator Rosa, there cannot be the least question about the Bouguereau. I am partial to the modern French school."}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_5	event	\N	Miss Morstan asks for a short interview and says she is there to learn what he wants to tell her	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_570", "sentence_571"], "communicatesContent": "but I am here at your request to learn something which you desire to tell me. It is very late, and I should desire the interview to be as short as possible."}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_6	event	\N	Sholto says the meeting will take time and that they will go to Norwood to see Brother Bartholomew	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_572", "sentence_573", "sentence_574", "sentence_575", "sentence_576"], "communicatesContent": "At the best it must take some time, for we shall certainly have to go to Norwood and see Brother Bartholomew. We shall all go and try if we can get the better of Brother Bartholomew. He is very angry with me for taking the course which has seemed right to me. I had quite high words with him last night. You cannot imagine what a terrible fellow he is when he is angry."}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_8	event	\N	The cab pulls up and the coachman opens the door	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_729"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_7	event	\N	Watson suggests they start at once for Norwood	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_577"], "communicatesContent": "If we are to go to Norwood it would perhaps be as well to start at once."}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_8	event	\N	Sholto laughs and says starting at once would not do	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_578", "sentence_579", "sentence_580", "sentence_581", "sentence_582", "sentence_583"], "communicatesContent": "That would hardly do. I don’t know what he would say if I brought you in that sudden way. No, I must prepare you by showing you how we all stand to each other. In the first place, I must tell you that there are several points in the story of which I am myself ignorant. I can only lay the facts before you as far as I know them myself."}
sign-of-the-four	event_15_9	event	\N	Sholto describes his father and family history	14	{"section": "section_15", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_584", "sentence_585", "sentence_586", "sentence_587", "sentence_588"], "communicatesContent": "My father was, as you may have guessed, Major John Sholto, once of the Indian army. He retired some eleven years ago, and came to live at Pondicherry Lodge in Upper Norwood. He had prospered in India, and brought back with him a considerable sum of money, a large collection of valuable curiosities, and a staff of native servants. With these advantages he bought himself a house, and lived in great luxury. My twin-brother Bartholomew and I were the only children."}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_1	event	\N	Captain Morstan disappears	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_589", "sentence_590", "sentence_592"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_2	event	\N	Family discusses the disappearance in Captain Morstan's presence	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_590", "sentence_591"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_3	event	\N	Captain Morstan joins the family's speculations	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_591"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_4	event	\N	The family suspects Captain Morstan hides the secret	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_592"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_5	event	\N	A mystery and danger overhang the father	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_593"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_6	event	\N	The father employs two prize-fighters as porters at Pondicherry Lodge	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_594", "sentence_595", "sentence_596"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_7	event	\N	The father fears going out alone	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_594"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_8	event	\N	The father shows aversion to men with wooden legs	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_597"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_9	event	\N	The father fires his revolver at a wooden-legged man	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_598", "sentence_599"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_10	event	\N	The family pays money to hush up the shooting incident	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_599"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_11	event	\N	The family revises its view of the father's behavior	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_600"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_12	event	\N	The father receives a letter from India	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_601"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_13	event	\N	The father nearly faints at the breakfast-table after opening the letter	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_602"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_14	event	\N	The father sickens from that day to his death	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_602", "sentence_604"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_15	event	\N	The father becomes rapidly worse	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_604"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_16	event	\N	The father makes a last communication to his children	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "father_of_watson_and_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_604", "sentence_605", "sentence_606", "sentence_607"], "communicatesContent": "He asks them to lock the door and come to either side of the bed, then makes a remarkable statement."}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_17	event	\N	The father speaks of his treatment of Morstan's orphan	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "father_of_watson_and_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_609", "sentence_610", "sentence_611", "sentence_612", "sentence_613", "sentence_614", "sentence_615", "sentence_616", "sentence_617", "sentence_618"], "communicatesContent": "I have only one thing which weighs upon my mind: my treatment of poor Morstan's orphan. My greed withheld from her the treasure, at least half of which should have been hers. See that chaplet dipped with pearls beside the quinine-bottle. Even that I could not bear to part with, although I had got it out with the design of sending it to her. You, my sons, will give her a fair share of the Agra treasure. But send her nothing—not even the chaplet—until I am gone. After all, men have been as bad as this and have recovered."}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_18	event	\N	The father explains how Morstan died	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "father_of_watson_and_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_619"], "communicatesContent": "I will tell you how Morstan died."}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_19	event	\N	Morstan and the father come into possession of a considerable treasure in India	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_620", "sentence_621", "sentence_622"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_20	event	\N	The father brings the treasure over to England	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_623"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_21	event	\N	Morstan arrives and comes straight to the house to claim his share	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_623", "sentence_624"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_22	event	\N	Morstan and the father argue over division of the treasure	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_625"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_16_23	event	\N	Morstan collapses and dies after pressing his hand to his side	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_626", "sentence_627"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_1	event	\N	The narrator considers calling for assistance and worries about being accused of murder	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_628", "sentence_629", "sentence_630", "sentence_631"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_2	event	\N	Lal Chowdar enters, bolts the door, and urges hiding the body	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": "lall_chowdar", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_634", "sentence_635", "sentence_636", "sentence_637", "sentence_638"], "communicatesContent": "Do not fear, Sahib. No one need know that you have killed him. Let us hide him away, and who is the wiser?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_3	event	\N	The narrator denies killing Captain Morstan	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_639"], "communicatesContent": "I did not kill him."}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_4	event	\N	Lal Chowdar claims he heard the quarrel and the blow and asks to hide the body	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": "lall_chowdar", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_640", "sentence_641", "sentence_642", "sentence_643", "sentence_644", "sentence_645"], "communicatesContent": "I heard it all, Sahib. I heard you quarrel, and I heard the blow. But my lips are sealed. All are asleep in the house. Let us put him away together."}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_5	event	\N	The narrator decides to conceal the death	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_646", "sentence_647"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_6	event	\N	Lal Chowdar and the narrator dispose of the body and the London papers report Captain Morstan's mysterious disappearance	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_648"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_7	event	\N	The narrator asks for restitution and says the treasure is hidden	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_650", "sentence_651", "sentence_652", "sentence_653"], "communicatesContent": "My fault lies in the fact that we concealed not only the body, but also the treasure, and that I have clung to Morstan’s share as well as to my own. I wish you, therefore, to make restitution. Put your ears down to my mouth. The treasure is hidden in—"}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_8	event	\N	A face appears at the window and the father dies	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_654", "sentence_655", "sentence_656", "sentence_657", "sentence_658", "sentence_659", "sentence_660", "sentence_661"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_9	event	\N	The narrator and his brother search the garden and find a footmark	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_662", "sentence_663"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_17_10	event	\N	The narrator's father room is found open, rifled, and marked with a paper bearing 'The sign of the four'	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_664", "sentence_665"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_1	event	\N	The little man stops to relight his hookah and puffs thoughtfully	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_669"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_2	event	\N	The group sits absorbed listening to Thaddeus Sholto's narrative	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_670"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_3	event	\N	Miss Morstan turns deadly white at the account of her father's death	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_671"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_4	event	\N	Watson pours a glass of water for Miss Morstan from the Venetian carafe	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_672"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_5	event	\N	Miss Morstan drinks the glass of water and rallies	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_672"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_6	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes leans back in his chair with an abstracted expression	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_673"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_7	event	\N	Mr. Thaddeus Sholto looks at the others with pride and continues speaking	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_676"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_8	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says that he and his brother were excited about the treasure their father had spoken of	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_677"], "communicatesContent": "My brother and I were much excited as to the treasure which my father had spoken of."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_9	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says that he and his brother dig in the garden for weeks and months without finding the treasure	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_678"], "communicatesContent": "For weeks and for months we dug and delved in every part of the garden, without discovering its whereabouts."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_10	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says it is maddening that the hiding-place was on his father's lips when he died	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_679"], "communicatesContent": "It was maddening to think that the hiding-place was on his very lips at the moment that he died."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_11	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says the missing riches can be judged by the chaplet	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_680"], "communicatesContent": "We could judge the splendour of the missing riches by the chaplet which he had taken out."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_12	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says he and Bartholomew discuss the chaplet	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_681"], "communicatesContent": "Over this chaplet my brother Bartholomew and I had some little discussion."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_13	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says the pearls were valuable and that Bartholomew was averse to parting with them	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_682", "sentence_683"], "communicatesContent": "The pearls were evidently of great value, and he was averse to part with them."}
sign-of-the-four	event_52_10	event	\N	The Smiths board the launch when commanded	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2235"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_14	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says he persuaded Bartholomew to let him find Miss Morstan's address and send her a detached pearl at intervals	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_684"], "communicatesContent": "It was all that I could do to persuade him to let me find out Miss Morstan’s address and send her a detached pearl at fixed intervals, so that at least she might never feel destitute."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_15	event	\N	The companion remarks that Thaddeus Sholto acted kindly	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_685", "sentence_686"], "communicatesContent": "It was a kindly thought. It was extremely good of you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_16	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says that he and Bartholomew were the trustees	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_687", "sentence_688"], "communicatesContent": "We were your trustees."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_17	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says he took the matter as trusteeship even though Bartholomew did not	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_689"], "communicatesContent": "That was the view which I took of it, though Brother Bartholomew could not altogether see it in that light."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_18	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says they had plenty of money and wanted no more	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_690", "sentence_691"], "communicatesContent": "We had plenty of money ourselves. I desired no more."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_19	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says it would have been bad taste to treat a young lady so	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_692", "sentence_693", "sentence_694"], "communicatesContent": "Besides, it would have been such bad taste to have treated a young lady in so scurvy a fashion. Le mauvais goût mène au crime. The French have a very neat way of putting these things."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_20	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says he set up rooms for himself and left Pondicherry Lodge with the khitmutgar and Williams	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_695"], "communicatesContent": "Our difference of opinion on this subject went so far that I thought it best to set up rooms for myself: so I left Pondicherry Lodge, taking the old khitmutgar and Williams with me."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_21	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says he learned the treasure had been discovered	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_696", "sentence_697"], "communicatesContent": "Yesterday, however, I learn that an event of extreme importance has occurred. The treasure has been discovered."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_22	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto says he communicated with Miss Morstan and must drive to Norwood to demand a share	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_698", "sentence_699"], "communicatesContent": "I instantly communicated with Miss Morstan, and it only remains for us to drive out to Norwood and demand our share. I explained my views last night to Brother Bartholomew: so we shall be expected, if not welcome, visitors."}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_23	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto stops speaking and sits twitching on his settee	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_700"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_18_24	event	\N	Holmes springs to his feet and speaks to the company	17	{"section": "section_18", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_702", "sentence_703", "sentence_704", "sentence_705"], "communicatesContent": "You have done well, sir, from first to last. It is possible that we may be able to make you some small return by throwing some light upon that which is still dark to you. But, as Miss Morstan remarked just now, it is late, and we had best put the matter through without delay."}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_1	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto dresses himself in coat and cap	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_706", "sentence_707"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_2	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto leads the way down the passage	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_708", "sentence_709"], "communicatesContent": "My health is somewhat fragile. I am compelled to be a valetudinarian."}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_3	event	\N	The cab starts off at a rapid pace	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_710"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_4	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto talks about Bartholomew Sholto and the treasure	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_711", "sentence_712", "sentence_713", "sentence_714", "sentence_715", "sentence_716", "sentence_717", "sentence_718", "sentence_719", "sentence_720", "sentence_721"], "communicatesContent": "Bartholomew is a clever fellow. How do you think he found out where the treasure was? He had come to the conclusion that it was somewhere indoors: so he worked out all the cubic space of the house, and made measurements everywhere, so that not one inch should be unaccounted for. Among other things, he found that the height of the building was seventy-four feet, but on adding together the heights of all the separate rooms, and making every allowance for the space between, which he ascertained by borings, he could not bring the total to more than seventy feet. There were four feet unaccounted for. These could only be at the top of the building. He knocked a hole, therefore, in the lath-and-plaster ceiling of the highest room, and there, sure enough, he came upon another little garret above it, which had been sealed up and was known to no one. In the centre stood the treasure-chest, resting upon two rafters. He lowered it through the hole, and there it lies. He computes the value of the jewels at not less than half a million sterling."}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_5	event	\N	The group reacts to the reported sum and Miss Morstan's change in fortune	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_722", "sentence_723", "sentence_724", "sentence_725"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_6	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto speaks about his symptoms and medicines	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_726", "sentence_727", "sentence_728"], "communicatesContent": "I am a confirmed hypochondriac and have symptoms, quack nostrums, and a leather case in my pocket."}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_7	event	\N	Watson and Holmes give contradictory medicine advice	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_728"], "communicatesContent": "I overheard Watson caution him against the great danger of taking more than two drops of castor oil, while Watson recommended strychnine in large doses as a sedative."}
sign-of-the-four	event_19_9	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto identifies the house as Pondicherry Lodge and hands Miss Morstan out	18	{"section": "section_19", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_730"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_1	event	\N	The party arrives at Pondicherry Lodge	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_732", "sentence_733", "sentence_734", "sentence_735", "sentence_736", "sentence_737"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_2	event	\N	McMurdo speaks from inside and asks who is there	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_739", "sentence_740"], "communicatesContent": "Who is there?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_3	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto identifies himself as McMurdo's caller	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_741", "sentence_742"], "communicatesContent": "It is I, McMurdo. You surely know my knock by this time."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_4	event	\N	McMurdo opens the door and faces the visitors	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_743", "sentence_744"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_5	event	\N	McMurdo refuses entry to Thaddeus's companions without orders	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_745", "sentence_747", "sentence_748", "sentence_749", "sentence_750", "sentence_751", "sentence_752", "sentence_753"], "communicatesContent": "That you, Mr. Thaddeus? But who are the others? I had no orders about them from the master. He ain't been out o' his room to-day, Mr. Thaddeus, and I have no orders. You know very well that I must stick to regulations. I can let you in, but your friends must just stop where they are."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_6	event	\N	Thaddeus protests that the companions should be admitted	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_755", "sentence_756", "sentence_757", "sentence_758", "sentence_759", "sentence_760"], "communicatesContent": "This is too bad of you, McMurdo! If I guarantee them, that is enough for you. There is the young lady, too. She cannot wait on the public road at this hour."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_7	event	\N	McMurdo remains unwilling but explains his strict duty	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_761", "sentence_762", "sentence_763", "sentence_764"], "communicatesContent": "Very sorry, Mr. Thaddeus. Folk may be friends o' yours, and yet no friends o' the master's. He pays me well to do my duty, and my duty I'll do. I don't know none o' your friends."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_8	event	\N	Holmes addresses McMurdo and reminds him of a past boxing match	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_765", "sentence_766", "sentence_767"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, yes you do, McMurdo. I don't think you can have forgotten me. Don't you remember the amateur who fought three rounds with you at Alison's rooms on the night of your benefit four years back?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_9	event	\N	McMurdo recognizes Holmes and praises his boxing talent	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_768", "sentence_769", "sentence_770", "sentence_771", "sentence_772", "sentence_773", "sentence_774"], "communicatesContent": "Not Mr. Sherlock Holmes! God's truth! how could I have mistook you? If instead o' standin' there so quiet you had just stepped up and given me that cross-hit of yours under the jaw, I'd ha' known you without a question. Ah, you're one that has wasted your gifts, you have! You might have aimed high, if you had joined the fancy."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_10	event	\N	Holmes jokes about having a scientific profession open to him	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_775", "sentence_776"], "communicatesContent": "Watson, if all else fails me I have still one of the scientific professions open to me. Our friend won't keep us out in the cold now, I am sure."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_11	event	\N	McMurdo admits the visitors and allows them in	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_777", "sentence_778", "sentence_779"], "communicatesContent": "In you come, sir, in you come,—you and your friends. Very sorry, Mr. Thaddeus, but orders are very strict. Had to be certain of your friends before I let them in."}
sign-of-the-four	event_20_12	event	\N	The visitors enter the grounds and approach the house	19	{"section": "section_20", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_780", "sentence_781", "sentence_782"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_1	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Bartholomew always guards the premises in that way	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_787", "sentence_788"], "communicatesContent": "Does he always guard the premises in this way?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_2	event	\N	Sholto explains that Bartholomew follows his father's custom and has the favourite-son position	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_789", "sentence_790"], "communicatesContent": "Yes; he has followed my father’s custom. He was the favourite son, you know, and I sometimes think that my father may have told him more than he ever told me."}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_3	event	\N	Holmes points out the lit window and the housekeeper's room	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_793", "sentence_794", "sentence_795", "sentence_796"], "communicatesContent": "But I see the glint of a light in that little window beside the door."}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_4	event	\N	Sholto says Mrs. Bernstone can explain the matter and asks the others to wait outside	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_797", "sentence_798", "sentence_799", "sentence_800"], "communicatesContent": "She can tell us all about it. But perhaps you would not mind waiting here for a minute or two, for if we all go in together and she has no word of our coming she may be alarmed. But hush! what is that?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_5	event	\N	A frightened woman's whimpering sounds from inside the house	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_801", "sentence_802", "sentence_803"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_6	event	\N	Sholto identifies the sound as Mrs. Bernstone and says she is the only woman in the house	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_804", "sentence_805", "sentence_806", "sentence_807"], "communicatesContent": "It is Mrs. Bernstone. She is the only woman in the house. Wait here. I shall be back in a moment."}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_7	event	\N	Sholto enters the house and is admitted by the housekeeper	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_808", "sentence_809", "sentence_810", "sentence_811", "sentence_812"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_8	event	\N	Holmes peers at the house and the rubbish-heaps with the lantern	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_813", "sentence_814"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_9	event	\N	Holmes and Miss Morstan stand together holding hands	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_815", "sentence_816", "sentence_817", "sentence_818"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_10	event	\N	Miss Morstan remarks that the place looks strange and like a gravel-pit	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "mary_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_819", "sentence_820", "sentence_821", "sentence_822"], "communicatesContent": "What a strange place! It looks as though all the moles in England had been let loose in it. I have seen something of the sort on the side of a hill near Ballarat, where the prospectors had been at work."}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_11	event	\N	Holmes attributes the ground traces to treasure-seekers	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_823", "sentence_824", "sentence_825", "sentence_826"], "communicatesContent": "And from the same cause. These are the traces of the treasure-seekers. You must remember that they were six years looking for it. No wonder that the grounds look like a gravel-pit."}
sign-of-the-four	event_21_12	event	\N	Thaddeus Sholto runs out of the house in terror and reports that something is wrong with Bartholomew	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "thaddeus_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_827", "sentence_828", "sentence_829", "sentence_830", "sentence_831", "sentence_832"], "communicatesContent": "There is something amiss with Bartholomew! I am frightened! My nerves cannot stand it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_1	event	\N	Holmes invites the others into the house	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_833", "sentence_834", "sentence_835", "sentence_836"], "communicatesContent": "Come into the house."}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_2	event	\N	The group follows Thaddeus Sholto into the housekeeper's room	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_837"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_3	event	\N	The old housekeeper reacts to Miss Morstan and expresses relief	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "old_woman_housekeeper", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_838", "sentence_839", "sentence_840", "sentence_841", "sentence_842"], "communicatesContent": "God bless your sweet calm face! It does me good to see you. Oh, but I have been sorely tried this day!"}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_4	event	\N	Miss Morstan comforts the housekeeper	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_843"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_5	event	\N	The housekeeper explains that her master is locked in and will not answer	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "old_woman_housekeeper", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_844", "sentence_845", "sentence_846", "sentence_847"], "communicatesContent": "Master has locked himself in and will not answer me. All day I have waited to hear from him, for he often likes to be alone; but an hour ago I feared that something was amiss, so I went up and peeped through the key-hole. You must go up, Mr. Thaddeus,—you must go up and look for yourself. I have seen Mr. Bartholomew Sholto in joy and in sorrow for ten long years, but I never saw him with such a face on him as that."}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_6	event	\N	Holmes leads the party up the stairs with the lamp	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_848", "sentence_849", "sentence_850", "sentence_851"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_7	event	\N	Miss Morstan remains behind with the housekeeper	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_852"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_8	event	\N	Holmes reaches the third-floor passage and approaches the third door	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_853", "sentence_854", "sentence_855"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_9	event	\N	Holmes knocks at the third door and tries to force it open	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_856", "sentence_857"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_10	event	\N	Holmes looks through the keyhole and recoils	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_858", "sentence_859", "sentence_860"], "communicatesContent": "There is something devilish in this, Watson."}
sign-of-the-four	event_22_11	event	\N	Watson looks through the keyhole and sees a face in the room	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_861", "sentence_862", "sentence_863", "sentence_864", "sentence_865", "sentence_866", "sentence_867", "sentence_868"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson force the chamber door down	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_872", "sentence_873", "sentence_874"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson enter Bartholomew Sholto’s chamber	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_874"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_3	event	\N	The chamber is discovered fitted out as a chemical laboratory	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_875", "sentence_876", "sentence_877", "sentence_879", "sentence_880"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_4	event	\N	Bartholomew Sholto is found dead in a chair	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_881", "sentence_882", "sentence_883"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_5	event	\N	Holmes examines the instrument by the dead man’s hand	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_884", "sentence_885", "sentence_886", "sentence_887"], "communicatesContent": "You see"}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_6	event	\N	Watson reads the note saying "The sign of the four"	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_888"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_7	event	\N	Watson asks what the scene means	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_889", "sentence_890"], "communicatesContent": "In God’s name, what does it all mean?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_8	event	\N	Holmes states that the death was murder	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_891"], "communicatesContent": "It means murder"}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_9	event	\N	Holmes points out a thorn in the skin above the ear	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_893", "sentence_894"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_10	event	\N	Watson identifies the object as a thorn and picks it out	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_895", "sentence_899", "sentence_900", "sentence_901"], "communicatesContent": "It looks like a thorn"}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_11	event	\N	Holmes explains that the thorn is poisoned	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_896", "sentence_897", "sentence_898"], "communicatesContent": "It is a thorn. You may pick it out. But be careful, for it is poisoned."}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_12	event	\N	Watson says the mystery is insoluble to him	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_902", "sentence_903"], "communicatesContent": "This is all an insoluble mystery to me. It grows darker instead of clearer."}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_13	event	\N	Holmes says the case is clearing and needs missing links	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_904", "sentence_905"], "communicatesContent": "On the contrary, it clears every instant. I only require a few missing links to have an entirely connected case."}
sign-of-the-four	event_23_14	event	\N	The companion reveals that the treasure is gone and that he fears suspicion	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "our_visitor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_906", "sentence_907", "sentence_908", "sentence_909", "sentence_910", "sentence_911", "sentence_912", "sentence_913", "sentence_914", "sentence_915", "sentence_916", "sentence_917", "sentence_918", "sentence_919", "sentence_920", "sentence_921", "sentence_922", "sentence_923", "sentence_924", "sentence_925", "sentence_926"], "communicatesContent": "The treasure is gone! They have robbed him of the treasure! There is the hole through which we lowered it. I helped him to do it! I was the last person who saw him! I left him here last night, and I heard him lock the door as I came downstairs. It was ten o’clock. And now he is dead, and the police will be called in, and I shall be suspected of having had a hand in it. Oh, yes, I am sure I shall. But you don’t think so, gentlemen? Surely you don’t think that it was I? Is it likely that I would have brought you here if it were I? Oh, dear! oh, dear! I know that I shall go mad!"}
sign-of-the-four	event_24_1	event	\N	Holmes reassures Mr. Sholto and advises him to report the matter to the police	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_927", "sentence_928", "sentence_929", "sentence_930"], "communicatesContent": "You have no reason for fear, Mr. Sholto. Take my advice, and drive down to the station to report this matter to the police. Offer to assist them in every way. We shall wait here until your return."}
sign-of-the-four	event_24_2	event	\N	Mr. Sholto leaves and goes down the stairs in the dark	23	{"section": "section_24", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_931"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_25_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson spend half an hour alone and Holmes begins examining the room	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_933", "sentence_934", "sentence_935", "sentence_936", "sentence_939", "sentence_940", "sentence_941", "sentence_942", "sentence_943", "sentence_944"], "communicatesContent": "Now, Watson, we have half an hour to ourselves. Let us make good use of it. My case is, as I have told you, almost complete; but we must not err on the side of over-confidence. Simple as the case seems now, there may be something deeper underlying it. Just sit in the corner there, that your footprints may not complicate matters. Now to work! In the first place, how did these folk come, and how did they go? The door has not been opened since last night. How of the window?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_25_2	event	\N	Holmes inspects the window and identifies signs of access by a man	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_945", "sentence_946", "sentence_947", "sentence_948", "sentence_949", "sentence_950", "sentence_951", "sentence_952", "sentence_953", "sentence_954", "sentence_955", "sentence_956", "sentence_957"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_25_3	event	\N	Watson examines the muddy marks and identifies the impression as a wooden stump	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_958", "sentence_959", "sentence_960", "sentence_961", "sentence_962", "sentence_963"], "communicatesContent": "This is not a footmark. It is something much more valuable to us. It is the impression of a wooden stump. It is the wooden-legged man."}
sign-of-the-four	event_25_4	event	\N	Holmes explains how the wooden-legged man and an ally could have used the rope to enter and leave through the window	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_964", "sentence_965", "sentence_966", "sentence_967", "sentence_968", "sentence_969", "sentence_970", "sentence_971", "sentence_972", "sentence_973", "sentence_974", "sentence_975", "sentence_976", "sentence_977"], "communicatesContent": "Quite so. But there has been some one else,—a very able and efficient ally. Could you scale that wall, doctor? Without aid it is so. But suppose you had a friend up here who lowered you this good stout rope which I see in the corner, securing one end of it to this great hook in the wall. Then, I think, if you were an active man, You might swarm up, wooden leg and all. You would depart, of course, in the same fashion, and your ally would draw up the rope, untie it from the hook, shut the window, snib it on the inside, and get away in the way that he originally came. As a minor point it may be noted that our wooden-legged friend, though a fair climber, was not a professional sailor. His hands were far from horny. My lens discloses more than one blood-mark, especially towards the end of the rope, from which I gather that he slipped down with such velocity that he took the skin off his hand."}
sign-of-the-four	event_25_5	event	\N	Watson asks how the ally entered the room and Holmes reflects on the ally	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_978", "sentence_979", "sentence_980", "sentence_981", "sentence_982", "sentence_983", "sentence_984", "sentence_985"], "communicatesContent": "This is all very well, but the thing becomes more unintelligible than ever. How about this mysterious ally? How came he into the room?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_26_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson climb into the garret above the room	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1002", "sentence_1003", "sentence_1004"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_26_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson search the garret	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1005", "sentence_1006", "sentence_1007", "sentence_1008", "sentence_1009", "sentence_1010", "sentence_1011", "sentence_1012", "sentence_1013"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_26_3	event	\N	Holmes notices the naked footmarks on the garret floor	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1014", "sentence_1015", "sentence_1016"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	section_88	section	\N	Section 88	87	{"wordCount": 610}
sign-of-the-four	event_26_4	event	\N	Watson says that a child has done the horrid thing	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1017"], "communicatesContent": "a child has done the horrid thing"}
sign-of-the-four	event_26_5	event	\N	Holmes tells Watson to apply his methods and compare results	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1018", "sentence_1019", "sentence_1020", "sentence_1021", "sentence_1022", "sentence_1023", "sentence_1024", "sentence_1025", "sentence_1026", "sentence_1027", "sentence_1028", "sentence_1029"], "communicatesContent": "I was staggered for the moment, but the thing is quite natural. My memory failed me, or I should have been able to foretell it. There is nothing more to be learned here. Let us go down. My dear Watson, try a little analysis yourself. You know my methods. Apply them, and it will be instructive to compare results. It will be clear enough to you soon."}
sign-of-the-four	event_26_6	event	\N	Holmes searches the lower room with lens and tape measure	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1030", "sentence_1031", "sentence_1032", "sentence_1033"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_1	event	\N	Holmes says they are in luck and that there will be very little trouble now	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1034", "sentence_1035"], "communicatesContent": "We are certainly in luck. We ought to have very little trouble now."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_2	event	\N	Holmes says Number One has trodden in the creosote and the leaking carboy has left a trail	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1036", "sentence_1037", "sentence_1038"], "communicatesContent": "Number One has had the misfortune to tread in the creosote. You can see the outline of the edge of his small foot here at the side of this evil-smelling mess. The carboy has been cracked, You see, and the stuff has leaked out."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_3	event	\N	Holmes says they have got him	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1041"], "communicatesContent": "Why, we have got him, that’s all."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_4	event	\N	Holmes says a trained hound could follow the scent	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1042", "sentence_1043"], "communicatesContent": "I know a dog that would follow that scent to the world’s end. If a pack can track a trailed herring across a shire, how far can a specially-trained hound follow so pungent a smell as this?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_5	event	\N	Holmes announces the police have arrived	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1045", "sentence_1046"], "communicatesContent": "But halloa! here are the accredited representatives of the law."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_6	event	\N	Heavy steps and voices are heard and the hall door slams shut	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1047"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_7	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson to examine the body and asks what he feels	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1048", "sentence_1049", "sentence_1050"], "communicatesContent": "Before they come, just put your hand here on this poor fellow’s arm, and here on his leg. What do you feel?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_8	event	\N	Watson feels the body and answers	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1049", "sentence_1050"], "communicatesContent": "The muscles are as hard as a board."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_9	event	\N	Holmes explains the body shows extreme contraction and a Hippocratic smile	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1051", "sentence_1052", "sentence_1053"], "communicatesContent": "Quite so. They are in a state of extreme contraction, far exceeding the usual rigor mortis. Coupled with this distortion of the face, this Hippocratic smile, or risus sardonicus, as the old writers called it, what conclusion would it suggest to your mind?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_10	event	\N	Watson identifies the cause of death as a powerful vegetable alkaloid	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1054"], "communicatesContent": "Death from some powerful vegetable alkaloid, some strychnine-like substance which would produce tetanus."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_11	event	\N	Holmes explains he looked for the means of poison entry and found a thorn in the scalp	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1055", "sentence_1056", "sentence_1057", "sentence_1058", "sentence_1059"], "communicatesContent": "That was the idea which occurred to me the instant I saw the drawn muscles of the face. On getting into the room I at once looked for the means by which the poison had entered the system. As you saw, I discovered a thorn which had been driven or shot with no great force into the scalp. You observe that the part struck was that which would be turned towards the hole in the ceiling if the man were erect in his chair. Now examine the thorn."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_12	event	\N	Watson examines the thorn	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1060", "sentence_1061", "sentence_1062"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_13	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the thorn is English and Watson answers no	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1063", "sentence_1064", "sentence_1065"], "communicatesContent": "Is that an English thorn?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_14	event	\N	Holmes says the data should support an inference and that the regular police are arriving	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1066", "sentence_1067"], "communicatesContent": "With all these data you should be able to draw some just inference. But here are the regulars; so the auxiliary forces may beat a retreat."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_15	event	\N	A very stout man enters the room with an inspector and Thaddeus Sholto	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1068", "sentence_1069", "sentence_1070"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_16	event	\N	The stout man speaks about the business and the crowded house	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1071", "sentence_1072", "sentence_1073", "sentence_1074", "sentence_1075"], "communicatesContent": "Here’s a business! Here’s a pretty business! But who are all these? Why, the house seems to be as full as a rabbit-warren!"}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_17	event	\N	Holmes reminds Athelney Jones of their acquaintance	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1076"], "communicatesContent": "I think you must recollect me, Mr. Athelney Jones."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_18	event	\N	Athelney Jones identifies Holmes and comments on the Bishopgate jewel case	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1077", "sentence_1078", "sentence_1079", "sentence_1080", "sentence_1081", "sentence_1082"], "communicatesContent": "Why, of course I do! It’s Mr. Sherlock Holmes, the theorist. Remember you! I’ll never forget how you lectured us all on causes and inferences and effects in the Bishopgate jewel case. It’s true you set us on the right track; but you’ll own now that it was more by good luck than good guidance."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_19	event	\N	Holmes says the reasoning was simple	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1083"], "communicatesContent": "It was a piece of very simple reasoning."}
sign-of-the-four	event_27_20	event	\N	Athelney Jones remarks on the case and asks what the man died of	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1084", "sentence_1085", "sentence_1086", "sentence_1087", "sentence_1088", "sentence_1089", "sentence_1090", "sentence_1091", "sentence_1092"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, come, now, come! Never be ashamed to own up. But what is all this? Bad business! Bad business! Stern facts here,—no room for theories. How lucky that I happened to be out at Norwood over another case! I was at the station when the message arrived. What d’you think the man died of?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_1	event	\N	Holmes and Athelney Jones discuss the missing jewels, the locked door, and the fastened window with steps on the sill	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1093", "sentence_1094", "sentence_1095", "sentence_1096", "sentence_1097", "sentence_1098", "sentence_1099", "sentence_1100"], "communicatesContent": "Door locked, I understand. Jewels worth half a million missing. How was the window?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_2	event	\N	Athelney Jones states a theory about Thaddeus Sholto and his brother	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1105", "sentence_1106", "sentence_1107", "sentence_1108", "sentence_1109", "sentence_1110", "sentence_1111"], "communicatesContent": "I have a theory. Sholto was, on his own confession, with his brother last night. The brother died in a fit, on which Sholto walked off with the treasure. How’s that?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_3	event	\N	Holmes rebuts the theory with another statement	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1112", "sentence_1113", "sentence_1114", "sentence_1115", "sentence_1116", "sentence_1117", "sentence_1118", "sentence_1119", "sentence_1120", "sentence_1121", "sentence_1122", "sentence_1123", "sentence_1124"], "communicatesContent": "On which the dead man very considerately got up and locked the door on the inside."}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_4	event	\N	Holmes points out the splinter, card, and instrument and asks how they fit the theory	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1125", "sentence_1126", "sentence_1127"], "communicatesContent": "You are not quite in possession of the facts yet. This splinter of wood, which I have every reason to believe to be poisoned, was in the man’s scalp where you still see the mark; this card, inscribed as you see it, was on the table; and beside it lay this rather curious stone-headed instrument. How does all that fit into your theory?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_5	event	\N	Athelney Jones asserts that the facts confirm his view and discovers the trap-door in the garret	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1128", "sentence_1129", "sentence_1130", "sentence_1131", "sentence_1132", "sentence_1133", "sentence_1134"], "communicatesContent": "Confirms it in every respect. House is full of Indian curiosities. Thaddeus brought this up, and if this splinter be poisonous Thaddeus may as well have made murderous use of it as any other man. The card is some hocus-pocus,—a blind, as like as not. The only question is, how did he depart? Ah, of course, here is a hole in the roof."}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_6	event	\N	Athelney Jones reports that he has found the trap-door and that it is partly open	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1135", "sentence_1136", "sentence_1137", "sentence_1138", "sentence_1139", "sentence_1140", "sentence_1141", "sentence_1142"], "communicatesContent": "You see! Facts are better than mere theories, after all. My view of the case is confirmed. There is a trap-door communicating with the roof, and it is partly open."}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_7	event	\N	Holmes says that he opened the trap-door	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1143", "sentence_1144", "sentence_1145", "sentence_1146", "sentence_1147"], "communicatesContent": "It was I who opened it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_8	event	\N	Athelney Jones calls for the inspector and arrests Mr. Sholto for being concerned in his brother's death	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1148", "sentence_1149", "sentence_1150", "sentence_1151", "sentence_1152"], "communicatesContent": "Mr. Sholto, it is my duty to inform you that anything which you may say will be used against you. I arrest you in the Queen’s name as being concerned in the death of your brother."}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_9	event	\N	Mr. Sholto reacts to the arrest	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1153", "sentence_1154", "sentence_1155"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_28_10	event	\N	Holmes tells Mr. Sholto not to trouble himself and says he can clear him of the charge	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1156", "sentence_1157"], "communicatesContent": "Don’t trouble yourself about it, Mr. Sholto. I think that I can engage to clear you of the charge."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_1	event	\N	The detective warns against overpromising	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1158", "sentence_1159", "sentence_1160"], "communicatesContent": "Don’t promise too much, Mr. Theorist,—don’t promise too much! You may find it a harder matter than you think."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_2	event	\N	Holmes identifies Jonathan Small and describes him	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1161", "sentence_1162", "sentence_1163", "sentence_1164", "sentence_1165", "sentence_1166"], "communicatesContent": "Not only will I clear him, Mr. Jones, but I will make you a free present of the name and description of one of the two people who were in this room last night. His name, I have every reason to believe, is Jonathan Small. He is a poorly-educated man, small, active, with his right leg off, and wearing a wooden stump which is worn away upon the inner side. His left boot has a coarse, square-toed sole, with an iron band round the heel. He is a middle-aged man, much sunburned, and has been a convict. These few indications may be of some assistance to you, coupled with the fact that there is a good deal of skin missing from the palm of his hand."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_3	event	\N	Jones asks about the other man	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1167", "sentence_1168", "sentence_1169", "sentence_1170"], "communicatesContent": "the other man—?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_4	event	\N	Holmes says the other man is a curious person and calls Watson aside	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1171", "sentence_1172", "sentence_1173"], "communicatesContent": "Is a rather curious person. —A word with you, Watson."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_5	event	\N	Holmes leads Watson out to the head of the stair	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1174"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_6	event	\N	Holmes and Watson discuss escorting Miss Morstan home and continuing the case	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1175", "sentence_1176", "sentence_1177", "sentence_1178", "sentence_1179", "sentence_1180", "sentence_1181", "sentence_1182", "sentence_1183", "sentence_1184", "sentence_1185", "sentence_1186", "sentence_1187", "sentence_1188"], "communicatesContent": "This unexpected occurrence has caused us rather to lose sight of the original purpose of our journey. It is not right that Miss Morstan should remain in this stricken house. You must escort her home. She lives with Mrs. Cecil Forrester, in Lower Camberwell: so it is not very far. I will wait for you here if you will drive out again. Or perhaps you are too tired? Your presence will be of great service to me. We shall work the case out independently, and leave this fellow Jones to exult over any mare’s-nest which he may choose to construct."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_7	event	\N	Holmes instructs Watson to go to Pinchin Lane and fetch Toby	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1189", "sentence_1190", "sentence_1191", "sentence_1192", "sentence_1193", "sentence_1194", "sentence_1195", "sentence_1196", "sentence_1197", "sentence_1198"], "communicatesContent": "When you have dropped Miss Morstan I wish you to go on to No. 3, Pinchin Lane, down near the water’s edge at Lambeth. The third house on the right-hand side is a bird-stuffer’s: Sherman is the name. You will see a weasel holding a young rabbit in the window. Knock old Sherman up, and tell him, with my compliments, that I want Toby at once. You will bring Toby back in the cab with you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_8	event	\N	Watson agrees to bring Toby back	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1198"], "communicatesContent": "I shall bring him, then."}
sign-of-the-four	event_29_9	event	\N	Holmes states his and Watson's next plans	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1199", "sentence_1200", "sentence_1201", "sentence_1202", "sentence_1203", "sentence_1204"], "communicatesContent": "It is one now. I ought to be back before three, if I can get a fresh horse. And I shall see what I can learn from Mrs. Bernstone, and from the Indian servant, who, Mr. Thaddeus tell me, sleeps in the next garret. Then I shall study the great Jones’s methods and listen to his not too delicate sarcasms. Goethe is always pithy. Menschen verhöhnen was sie nicht verstehen."}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_1	event	\N	The police bring a cab and escort Miss Morstan home	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1206"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_2	event	\N	Miss Morstan turns faint and then weeps in the cab	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1208"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_3	event	\N	They reach Mrs. Cecil Forrester's home	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1222"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_4	event	\N	Mrs. Forrester opens the door and greets Miss Morstan warmly	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1224"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_5	event	\N	Mrs. Forrester begs Watson to step in and tell the adventures	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "mrs_cecil_forrester", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1226"], "communicatesContent": "step in and tell her our adventures"}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_6	event	\N	Watson explains the importance of the errand and promises to report progress	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1227"], "communicatesContent": "the importance of my errand, and promised faithfully to call and report any progress which we might make with the case"}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_7	event	\N	Watson drives away and looks back at the group on the step	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1228"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_30_8	event	\N	Watson reviews the sequence of events while riding through the streets	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1231"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_1	event	\N	The speaker knocks for some time at No. 3.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1237", "sentence_1238"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_2	event	\N	A candle glints behind the blind and a face looks out at the upper window.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1239"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_3	event	\N	The face threatens to release dogs if the row continues.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "face_at_window", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1240", "sentence_1241"], "communicatesContent": "Go on, you drunken vagabone. If you kick up any more row I’ll open the kennels and let out forty-three dogs upon you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_4	event	\N	Watson says he has come for one dog to be let out.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1242"], "communicatesContent": "If you’ll let one out it’s just what I have come for."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_5	event	\N	The face orders Watson to go on.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "face_at_window", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1243", "sentence_1244"], "communicatesContent": "Go on!"}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_6	event	\N	The voice threatens to drop a wiper on Watson's head.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "face_at_window", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1245"], "communicatesContent": "So help me gracious, I have a wiper in the bag, an’ I’ll drop it on your ’ead if you don’t hook it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_7	event	\N	Watson says he wants a dog.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1246"], "communicatesContent": "But I want a dog."}
silver-blaze	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "\\"My dear Watson, you would confer a great favour upon me by coming.", "section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_8	event	\N	Mr. Sherman refuses to be argued with and orders the window clear.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1247", "sentence_1248", "sentence_1249"], "communicatesContent": "I won’t be argued with! Now stand clear, for when I say ‘three,’ down goes the wiper."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_9	event	\N	Watson mentions Sherlock Holmes, and the window slams down and the door is unbarred and opened.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1250"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_10	event	\N	Sherman welcomes a friend of Mr. Sherlock and invites the visitor to step in.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1252", "sentence_1253"], "communicatesContent": "A friend of Mr. Sherlock is always welcome. Step in, sir."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_11	event	\N	Sherman warns the visitor to keep clear of the badger and addresses the stoat.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1254", "sentence_1255", "sentence_1256"], "communicatesContent": "Keep clear of the badger; for he bites. Ah, naughty, naughty, would you take a nip at the gentleman?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_12	event	\N	Sherman identifies the stoat as only a slow-worm and explains that he lets it roam the room to keep the beetles down.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1257", "sentence_1258"], "communicatesContent": "Don’t mind that, sir: it’s only a slow-worm. It hain’t got no fangs, so I gives it the run o’ the room, for it keeps the beetles down."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_13	event	\N	Sherman explains that children tease him and people come down the lane to knock him up.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1259", "sentence_1260"], "communicatesContent": "You must not mind my bein’ just a little short wi’ you at first, for I’m guyed at by the children, and there’s many a one just comes down this lane to knock me up. What was it that Mr. Sherlock Holmes wanted, sir?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_14	event	\N	Watson says Holmes wanted one of Sherman’s dogs.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1261"], "communicatesContent": "He wanted a dog of yours."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_15	event	\N	Sherman identifies the dog as Toby and says Toby lives at No. 7 on the left.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1262", "sentence_1263", "sentence_1264", "sentence_1265", "sentence_1266"], "communicatesContent": "Ah! that would be Toby. Yes, Toby was the name. Toby lives at No. 7 on the left here."}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_16	event	\N	Sherman moves forward with his candle among the animals.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1267", "sentence_1268", "sentence_1269"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_17	event	\N	Watson sees Toby and gives it sugar.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1270", "sentence_1271"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_18	event	\N	Toby follows Watson to the cab and accompanies him.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1271"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_19	event	\N	Watson returns to Pondicherry Lodge at three o'clock.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1272"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_20	event	\N	Watson finds McMurdo arrested as an accessory and Sholto marched off to the station.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1273"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_21	event	\N	Two constables guard the gate and allow Watson to pass with the dog after he mentions the detective’s name.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1274"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_31_22	event	\N	Holmes stands on the doorstep smoking his pipe and speaks to Watson.	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1275", "sentence_1276", "sentence_1277", "sentence_1278", "sentence_1279", "sentence_1280", "sentence_1281", "sentence_1282", "sentence_1283"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, you have him there! Good dog, then! Athelney Jones has gone. We have had an immense display of energy since you left. He has arrested not only friend Thaddeus, but the gatekeeper, the housekeeper, and the Indian servant. We have the place to ourselves, but for a sergeant upstairs. Leave the dog here, and come up."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_1	event	\N	Watson ties Toby to the hall table and goes back upstairs	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1284"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_2	event	\N	Holmes asks the sergeant for the bull's-eye lantern and a card is tied round his neck	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1287", "sentence_1288", "sentence_1289"], "communicatesContent": "Lend me your bull’s-eye, sergeant."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_3	event	\N	Holmes instructs Watson to carry items down, climb, and dip his handkerchief into creasote	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1290", "sentence_1291", "sentence_1292", "sentence_1293", "sentence_1294"], "communicatesContent": "Just you carry them down with you, Watson. I am going to do a little climbing. And dip my handkerchief into the creasote. That will do. Now come up into the garret with me for a moment."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_4	event	\N	Watson and Holmes clamber up into the garret through the hole	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1296"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_5	event	\N	Holmes examines the footmarks in the dust	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1297", "sentence_1298", "sentence_1299"], "communicatesContent": "I wish you particularly to notice these footmarks. Do you observe anything noteworthy about them?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_6	event	\N	Holmes compares a right-foot print with his own naked foot	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1304", "sentence_1305", "sentence_1306", "sentence_1307", "sentence_1308", "sentence_1309", "sentence_1310", "sentence_1311", "sentence_1312", "sentence_1313"], "communicatesContent": "Look here! This is the print of a right foot in the dust. Now I make one with my naked foot beside it. What is the chief difference?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_38_4	event	\N	Mrs. Smith rejects that explanation and remarks on the prices charged for coal.	37	{"section": "section_38", "speakerId": "mrs_smith", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1558", "sentence_1559"], "communicatesContent": "It weren’t his way. Many a time I’ve heard him call out at the prices they charge for a few odd bags."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_7	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson to smell the edge of the woodwork and stay with the handkerchief	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1314", "sentence_1315"], "communicatesContent": "Now, would you kindly step over to that flap-window and smell the edge of the wood-work? I shall stay here, as I have this handkerchief in my hand."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_8	event	\N	Watson smells a strong tarry smell at the flap-window edge	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1316"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_9	event	\N	Holmes tells Watson that the place is where the man put his foot and orders him to loose Toby and look out for Blondin	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1317", "sentence_1318", "sentence_1319"], "communicatesContent": "That is where he put his foot in getting out. If you can trace him, I should think that Toby will have no difficulty. Now run downstairs, loose the dog, and look out for Blondin."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_10	event	\N	Holmes moves onto the roof and crawls along the ridge	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1320", "sentence_1321"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_11	event	\N	Watson finds Holmes seated at the corner eaves	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1322", "sentence_1323", "sentence_1324", "sentence_1325", "sentence_1326"], "communicatesContent": "That you, Watson?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_12	event	\N	Holmes questions Watson about a water-barrel, a ladder, and the place he can descend from	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1327", "sentence_1328", "sentence_1329", "sentence_1330", "sentence_1331", "sentence_1332", "sentence_1333", "sentence_1334", "sentence_1335", "sentence_1336", "sentence_1337"], "communicatesContent": "What is that black thing down there? Top on it? No sign of a ladder? Confound the fellow! It’s a most break-neck place. I ought to be able to come down where he could climb up. The water-pipe feels pretty firm. Here goes, anyhow."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_13	event	\N	Holmes descends the wall with the lantern and lands on the barrel and then the earth	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1338", "sentence_1339"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_14	event	\N	Holmes identifies loosened tiles and holds up a pouch found on the route	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1340", "sentence_1341", "sentence_1342", "sentence_1343", "sentence_1344"], "communicatesContent": "It was easy to follow him. Tiles were loosened the whole way along, and in his hurry he had dropped this. It confirms my diagnosis, as you doctors express it."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_15	event	\N	Holmes opens the pouch and shows the wooden spines inside it	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1345", "sentence_1346", "sentence_1347", "sentence_1348", "sentence_1349", "sentence_1350"], "communicatesContent": "They are hellish things. Look out that you don’t prick yourself. I’m delighted to have them, for the chances are that they are all he has. There is the less fear of you or me finding one in our skin before long. I would sooner face a Martini bullet, myself."}
sign-of-the-four	event_32_16	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson if he is game for a six-mile trudge	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1351"], "communicatesContent": "Are you game for a six-mile trudge, Watson?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_1	event	\N	Holmes pushes the creasote handkerchief under Toby's nose	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1355", "sentence_1356", "sentence_1357", "sentence_1358"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_2	event	\N	Holmes throws the handkerchief away and fastens Toby to a cord	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1359"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_3	event	\N	Holmes leads Toby to the foot of the water-barrel	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1359"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_4	event	\N	Toby follows the scent trail at speed	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1360", "sentence_1374", "sentence_1375"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_5	event	\N	Holmes and Watson travel across the grounds toward the boundary wall	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1361", "sentence_1362", "sentence_1363", "sentence_1364", "sentence_1365"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_6	event	\N	Toby stops in a corner screened by a young beech	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1365"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_7	event	\N	Holmes clambers up the wall and drops Toby over to the other side	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1366", "sentence_1367"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_8	event	\N	Holmes remarks on the hand print and blood smudge on the wall	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1368", "sentence_1369"], "communicatesContent": "There’s the print of wooden-leg’s hand. You see the slight smudge of blood upon the white plaster."}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_9	event	\N	Holmes says the scent will remain on the road despite the elapsed time	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1370", "sentence_1371"], "communicatesContent": "What a lucky thing it is that we have had no very heavy rain since yesterday! The scent will lie upon the road in spite of their eight-and-twenty hours’ start."}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_10	event	\N	Watson expresses doubt and later has his fears appeased	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1372", "sentence_1373"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_11	event	\N	Holmes explains that he does not depend on chance and describes the clue as the easiest route	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1376", "sentence_1377", "sentence_1378", "sentence_1379", "sentence_1380"], "communicatesContent": "Do not imagine that I depend for my success in this case upon the mere chance of one of these fellows having put his foot in the chemical. I have knowledge now which would enable me to trace them in many different ways. This, however, is the readiest and, since fortune has put it into our hands, I should be culpable if I neglected it. It has, however, prevented the case from becoming the pretty little intellectual problem which it at one time promised to be. There might have been some credit to be gained out of it, but for this too palpable clue."}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_12	event	\N	Watson praises Holmes's results and asks how he described the wooden-legged man	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1381", "sentence_1382", "sentence_1383", "sentence_1384"], "communicatesContent": "There is credit, and to spare. I assure you, Holmes, that I marvel at the means by which you obtain your results in this case, even more than I did in the Jefferson Hope Murder. The thing seems to me to be deeper and more inexplicable. How, for example, could you describe with such confidence the wooden-legged man?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_33_13	event	\N	Holmes explains his deduction about the treasure and the sign of the four	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1385", "sentence_1386", "sentence_1387", "sentence_1388", "sentence_1389", "sentence_1390", "sentence_1391", "sentence_1392", "sentence_1393", "sentence_1394", "sentence_1395", "sentence_1396", "sentence_1397"], "communicatesContent": "it was simplicity itself. I don’t wish to be theatrical. It is all patent and above-board. Two officers who are in command of a convict-guard learn an important secret as to buried treasure. A map is drawn for them by an Englishman named Jonathan Small. You remember that we saw the name upon the chart in Captain Morstan’s possession. He had signed it in behalf of himself and his associates,—the sign of the four, as he somewhat dramatically called it. Aided by this chart, the officers—or one of them—gets the treasure and brings it to England, leaving, we will suppose, some condition under which he received it unfulfilled. Now, then, why did not Jonathan Small get the treasure himself? The answer is obvious. The chart is dated at a time when Morstan was brought into close association with convicts. Jonathan Small did not get the treasure because he and his associates were themselves convicts and could not get away."}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_1	event	\N	Major Sholto remains at peace for some years while possessing his treasure	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1402"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_2	event	\N	Major Sholto receives a letter from India	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1403"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_3	event	\N	The letter states that the men whom the recipient had wronged had been set free or had escaped	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": "letter_from_india", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1405", "sentence_1406", "sentence_1407", "sentence_1408"], "communicatesContent": "The men whom he had wronged had been set free. Or had escaped."}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_4	event	\N	Major Sholto guards himself against a wooden-legged man and fires a pistol at a harmless tradesman	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1410"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_5	event	\N	Jonathan Small comes to England with the aims of regaining his rights and taking revenge	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1419"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_6	event	\N	Jonathan Small finds where Sholto lived and may establish communications with someone inside the house	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1420", "sentence_1421", "sentence_1422"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_7	event	\N	Jonathan Small learns that Major Sholto is on his death-bed	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1424"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_8	event	\N	Jonathan Small runs past the guards and reaches the dying man's window	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1425"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_34_9	event	\N	Jonathan Small is deterred from entering by the presence of Major Sholto's two sons	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1425"], "communicatesContent": null}
