sign-of-the-four	event_59_14	event	\N	English forces go out to meet the rebels at Shahgunge and then fall back to the city	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2507"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_60_1	event	\N	Our leader moves across the river and takes up his position in the old fort at Agra	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2513"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_60_2	event	\N	The force organises a central guard-house in the middle of the fort and assigns each gate to guards	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2525"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_60_3	event	\N	The narrator is selected to take charge of a small isolated door on the southwest side during certain hours of the night	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2526", "sentence_2527"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_60_4	event	\N	Two Sikh troopers are placed under the narrator's command	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2527"], "communicatesContent": null}
