sign-of-the-four	event_67_1	event	\N	Dr. Somerton and several officers meet in his rooms and play cards	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2737"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_2	event	\N	The surgery stands next to Dr. Somerton's sitting-room	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2738"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_3	event	\N	The narrator turns out the lamp and listens to the card game	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2739", "sentence_2740"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_4	event	\N	Major Sholto, Captain Morstan, Lieutenant Bromley Brown, Dr. Somerton, and prison-officials form a card-playing party	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2741", "sentence_2742"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_5	event	\N	The soldiers repeatedly lose at cards while the civilians win	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2743", "sentence_2744", "sentence_2745", "sentence_2746"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_6	event	\N	Major Sholto loses heavily and pays with notes, gold, and promissory notes	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2747", "sentence_2748", "sentence_2749", "sentence_2750", "sentence_2751"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_7	event	\N	Major Sholto and Captain Morstan walk toward their quarters after cards	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2752", "sentence_2753"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_8	event	\N	Major Sholto complains about his losses and says he must send in his papers	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "major_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2754", "sentence_2755", "sentence_2756", "sentence_2757", "sentence_2758", "sentence_2759", "sentence_2760"], "communicatesContent": "It's all up, Morstan. I shall have to send in my papers. I am a ruined man."}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_9	event	\N	The narrator speaks to Major Sholto on the beach about hidden treasure	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "narrator", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2761", "sentence_2762", "sentence_2763", "sentence_2764", "sentence_2765", "sentence_2766", "sentence_2767", "sentence_2768", "sentence_2769", "sentence_2770", "sentence_2771", "sentence_2772", "sentence_2773"], "communicatesContent": "I wanted to ask you, sir, who is the proper person to whom hidden treasure should be handed over. I know where half a million worth lies, and, as I cannot use it myself, I thought perhaps the best thing that I could do would be to hand it over to the proper authorities, and then perhaps they would get my sentence shortened for me."}
sign-of-the-four	event_67_10	event	\N	Major Sholto tells the narrator that hidden treasure should go to government	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "major_sholto", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2767", "sentence_2768", "sentence_2772", "sentence_2773"], "communicatesContent": "To government, Small — to government."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_1	event	\N	Jonathan Small says he should give the information to the Governor-General	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2774", "sentence_2775"], "communicatesContent": "You think, then, sir, that I should give the information to the Governor-General?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_2	event	\N	The major asks Small for the facts	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2776", "sentence_2777", "sentence_2778"], "communicatesContent": "Let me hear all about it, Small. Give me the facts."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_3	event	\N	Small tells the whole story with small changes to hide the places	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2779"], "communicatesContent": "the whole story"}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_4	event	\N	The major warns Small not to say anything and says he will see him again soon	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2782", "sentence_2783"], "communicatesContent": "This is a very important matter, Small. You must not say a word to any one about it, and I shall see you again soon."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_5	event	\N	The major and Captain Morstan come to Small's hut at night with a lantern	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2784"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_6	event	\N	The major asks Small to let Captain Morstan hear the story	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2785"], "communicatesContent": "I want you just to let Captain Morstan hear that story from your own lips, Small."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_7	event	\N	Small repeats the story	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2786"], "communicatesContent": "the story"}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_8	event	\N	The major asks whether the story rings true and is good enough to act upon	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2787", "sentence_2788", "sentence_2789", "sentence_2790"], "communicatesContent": "It rings true, eh? It's good enough to act upon?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_9	event	\N	Captain Morstan nods	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2790"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_9	event	\N	The speaker resolves to seek vengeance against Sholto	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2846", "sentence_2847", "sentence_2848", "sentence_2849", "sentence_2850", "sentence_2851"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	sentence_513	lexical	\N	\N	512	{"text": "Five to fifteen against Desborough!", "section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "entities": []}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_10	event	\N	The major explains that the secret is a private concern and asks what price Small would ask for it	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2791", "sentence_2792", "sentence_2793", "sentence_2794", "sentence_2795"], "communicatesContent": "We have been talking it over, my friend here and I, and we have come to the conclusion that this secret of yours is hardly a government matter, after all, but is a private concern of your own, which of course you have the power of disposing of as you think best. Now, the question is, what price would you ask for it? We might be inclined to take it up, and at least look into it, if we could agree as to terms."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_11	event	\N	Small proposes a bargain for his freedom and the freedom of his three companions	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2796", "sentence_2797", "sentence_2798"], "communicatesContent": "there is only one bargain which a man in my position can make. I shall want you to help me to my freedom, and to help my three companions to theirs. We shall then take you into partnership, and give you a fifth share to divide between you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_12	event	\N	The major objects that a fifth share is not very tempting	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2799", "sentence_2800", "sentence_2801", "sentence_2802"], "communicatesContent": "A fifth share! That is not very tempting."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_13	event	\N	Small says the share would come to fifty thousand apiece	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2803"], "communicatesContent": "It would come to fifty thousand apiece."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_14	event	\N	The major says gaining Small's freedom is impossible	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2804", "sentence_2805"], "communicatesContent": "But how can we gain your freedom? You know very well that you ask an impossibility."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_15	event	\N	Small explains the plan to escape by boat with provisions	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2806", "sentence_2807", "sentence_2808", "sentence_2809", "sentence_2810", "sentence_2811"], "communicatesContent": "Nothing of the sort. I have thought it all out to the last detail. The only bar to our escape is that we can get no boat fit for the voyage, and no provisions to last us for so long a time. There are plenty of little yachts and yawls at Calcutta or Madras which would serve our turn well. Do you bring one over. We shall engage to get aboard her by night, and if you will drop us on any part of the Indian coast you will have done your part of the bargain."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_16	event	\N	The major says he could agree only if there were one prisoner	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2812"], "communicatesContent": "If there were only one."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_17	event	\N	Small replies that it must be all or none and that the four must act together	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2813", "sentence_2814", "sentence_2815"], "communicatesContent": "None or all. We have sworn it. The four of us must always act together."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_18	event	\N	The major tells Morstan that Small is a man of his word and may be trusted	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2816", "sentence_2817", "sentence_2818"], "communicatesContent": "Small is a man of his word. He does not flinch from his friend. I think we may very well trust him."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_19	event	\N	Captain Morstan says the business is dirty but the money would help their commissions	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "captain_morstan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2819", "sentence_2820"], "communicatesContent": "It's a dirty business, yet, as you say, the money would save our commissions handsomely."}
sign-of-the-four	event_68_20	event	\N	The major agrees to try to meet Small and asks him where the box is hidden	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "major", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2821", "sentence_2822", "sentence_2823"], "communicatesContent": "We must, I suppose, try and meet you. We must first, of course, test the truth of your story. Tell me where the box is hid, and I shall get leave of absence and go back to India in the monthly relief-boat to inquire into the affair."}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_1	event	\N	The speaker demands the consent of his three comrades before agreeing	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "narrator", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2824", "sentence_2825", "sentence_2826", "sentence_2830"], "communicatesContent": "I must have the consent of my three comrades. I tell you that it is four or none with us. Black or blue, they are in with me, and we all go together."}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_2	event	\N	A second meeting is held with the three comrades present	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2831", "sentence_2832"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_3	event	\N	The parties agree on the treasure-plan arrangement	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "narrator", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2832", "sentence_2833", "sentence_2834", "sentence_2835", "sentence_2836", "sentence_2837", "sentence_2838"], "communicatesContent": "We were to provide both the officers with charts of the part of the Agra fort and mark the place in the wall where the treasure was hid. Major Sholto was to go to India to test our story. If he found the box he was to leave it there, to send out a small yacht provisioned for a voyage, which was to lie off Rutland Island, and to which we were to make our way, and finally to return to his duties. Captain Morstan was then to apply for leave of absence, to meet us at Agra, and there we were to have a final division of the treasure, he taking the major’s share as well as his own. All this we sealed by the most solemn oaths that the mind could think or the lips utter."}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_4	event	\N	The two charts are prepared and signed	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2838"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_5	event	\N	Major Sholto goes to India	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2841"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_6	event	\N	Captain Morstan appears on a passenger list in a mail-boat	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2842"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_7	event	\N	Major Sholto inherits a fortune and leaves the army	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2843"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_8	event	\N	Captain Morstan goes to Agra and finds the treasure gone	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2844", "sentence_2845"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_69_10	event	\N	The speaker takes an Andaman Islander into his care and cures him	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2853", "sentence_2854", "sentence_2855", "sentence_2856", "sentence_2857", "sentence_2858", "sentence_2859"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_70_1	event	\N	The narrator arranges an escape with Tonga	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": "narrator", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2861", "sentence_2862", "sentence_2863", "sentence_2864"], "communicatesContent": "He is to bring his boat round on a certain night to an old wharf which is never guarded, and there he is to pick me up. He is to have several gourds of water and a lot of yams, cocoa-nuts, and sweet potatoes."}
sign-of-the-four	event_70_2	event	\N	Tonga brings his boat to the wharf	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2867"], "communicatesContent": null}
