sign-of-the-four	event_71_19	event	\N	The narrator hears about Smith's launch Aurora and decides it is suitable for escape	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2917"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_71_20	event	\N	The narrator engages with Mordecai Smith and offers a large sum if he gets them safe to their ship	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "narrator", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2918"], "communicatesContent": "I engage with old Smith, and was to give him a big sum if he got us safe to our ship."}
sign-of-the-four	event_71_21	event	\N	Mordecai Smith remains outside the narrator's secrets	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2919"], "communicatesContent": null}
sign-of-the-four	event_71_22	event	\N	The narrator tells gentlemen that he is telling the truth and explains his defence	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "narrator", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2920"], "communicatesContent": "All this is the truth, and if I tell it to you, gentlemen, it is not to amuse you,—for you have not done me a very good turn,—but it is because I believe the best defence I can make is just to hold back nothing, but let all the world know how badly I have myself been served by Major Sholto, and how innocent I am of the death of his son."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_1	event	\N	Holmes comments that Tonga had lost all his darts except the one in his blow-pipe and that one was shot at them in the boat	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2923", "sentence_2925", "sentence_2926", "sentence_2927", "sentence_2928"], "communicatesContent": "There is nothing at all new to me in the latter part of your narrative, except that you brought your own rope. That I did not know. By the way, I had hoped that Tonga had lost all his darts; yet he managed to shoot one at us in the boat."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_2	event	\N	The convict replies that Tonga had lost all the darts except the one in his blow-pipe	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "convict", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2926"], "communicatesContent": "He had lost them all, sir, except the one which was in his blow-pipe at the time."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_3	event	\N	The convict asks whether there is any other point to ask about	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "convict", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2929", "sentence_2930"], "communicatesContent": "Is there any other point which you would like to ask about?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_4	event	\N	Watson answers that he does not think so and thanks the convict	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2931"], "communicatesContent": "I think not, thank you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_5	event	\N	Athelney Jones says he will feel more at ease when the story-teller is safe under lock and key, notes that the cab still waits and two inspectors are downstairs, thanks Holmes and Watson, says they will be wanted at the trial, and bids good-night	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2932", "sentence_2933", "sentence_2934", "sentence_2935", "sentence_2936", "sentence_2937"], "communicatesContent": "You are a man to be humoured, and we all know that you are a connoisseur of crime, but duty is duty, and I have gone rather far in doing what you and your friend asked me. I shall feel more at ease when we have our story-teller here safe under lock and key. The cab still waits, and there are two inspectors downstairs. I am much obliged to you both for your assistance. Of course you will be wanted at the trial. Good-night to you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_6	event	\N	Jonathan Small bids the gentlemen good-night	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "jonathan_small", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2938"], "communicatesContent": "Good-night, gentlemen both."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_7	event	\N	Jones warns Jonathan Small to go first and says he will take care that Small does not club him with his wooden leg	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "athelney_jones", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2939", "sentence_2940"], "communicatesContent": "You first, Small. I’ll take particular care that you don’t club me with your wooden leg, whatever you may have done to the gentleman at the Andaman Isles."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_8	event	\N	Watson remarks that the little drama has ended and that they have sat smoking in silence	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2941"], "communicatesContent": "Well, and there is the end of our little drama."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_9	event	\N	Watson says he fears it may be the last investigation in which he shall study Holmes's methods	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2942"], "communicatesContent": "I fear that it may be the last investigation in which I shall have the chance of studying your methods."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_10	event	\N	Watson says Miss Morstan has accepted him as a husband in prospective	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2943"], "communicatesContent": "Miss Morstan has done me the honour to accept me as a husband in prospective."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_11	event	\N	Holmes groans, says he feared as much, and says he cannot congratulate Watson	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2944", "sentence_2945", "sentence_2946"], "communicatesContent": "I feared as much. I really cannot congratulate you."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_12	event	\N	Watson asks whether Holmes has any reason to be dissatisfied with his choice	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2947", "sentence_2948", "sentence_2949"], "communicatesContent": "Have you any reason to be dissatisfied with my choice?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_13	event	\N	Holmes says he thinks Miss Morstan charming, praises her usefulness, cites her preservation of the Agra plan, explains that love is emotional and opposed to cold reason, and says he would never marry	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2950", "sentence_2951", "sentence_2952", "sentence_2953", "sentence_2954"], "communicatesContent": "Not at all. I think she is one of the most charming young ladies I ever met, and might have been most useful in such work as we have been doing. She had a decided genius that way: witness the way in which she preserved that Agra plan from all the other papers of her father. But love is an emotional thing, and whatever is emotional is opposed to that true cold reason which I place above all things. I should never marry myself, lest I bias my judgment."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_14	event	\N	Watson says he trusts his judgment may survive the ordeal and remarks that Holmes looks weary	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2955", "sentence_2956"], "communicatesContent": "I trust that my judgment may survive the ordeal. But you look weary."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_15	event	\N	Holmes says the reaction is already upon him and that he will be limp as a rag for a week	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2957", "sentence_2958"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, the reaction is already upon me. I shall be as limp as a rag for a week."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_16	event	\N	Watson remarks on Holmes's alternation of laziness with energy and vigour	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2959"], "communicatesContent": "Strange, how terms of what in another man I should call laziness alternate with your fits of splendid energy and vigour."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_17	event	\N	Holmes says he has the makings of a loafer and a spry fellow and quotes Goethe	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2960", "sentence_2961", "sentence_2962"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, there are in me the makings of a very fine loafer and also of a pretty spry sort of fellow. I often think of those lines of old Goethe,— Schade dass die Natur nur einen Mensch aus Dir schuf, Denn zum würdigen Mann war und zum Schelmen der Stoff."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_18	event	\N	Holmes says Lal Rao was the confederate in the house and that Jones has the undivided honour of having caught one fish in his haul	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2963"], "communicatesContent": "By the way, à propos of this Norwood business, you see that they had, as I surmised, a confederate in the house, who could be none other than Lal Rao, the butler: so Jones actually has the undivided honour of having caught one fish in his great haul."}
sign-of-the-four	event_72_19	event	\N	Watson says the division seems unfair, Holmes did all the work, Jones gets the credit, and Watson gets a wife	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2964", "sentence_2965", "sentence_2966"], "communicatesContent": "The division seems rather unfair. You have done all the work in this business. I get a wife out of it, Jones gets the credit, pray what remains for you?"}
sign-of-the-four	event_73_1	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes says that the cocaine-bottle remains	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2967"], "communicatesContent": "For me, there still remains the cocaine-bottle."}
sign-of-the-four	event_73_2	event	\N	Holmes stretches up his hand for the cocaine-bottle	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2968"], "communicatesContent": null}
