silver-blaze	event_1_1	event	\N	Holmes says he must go to Dartmoor and King's Pyland	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3", "sentence_6"], "communicatesContent": "I shall have to go. To Dartmoor; to King's Pyland."}
silver-blaze	event_1_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson discuss Holmes's departure	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4", "sentence_5", "sentence_14", "sentence_18"], "communicatesContent": "Go! Where to?"}
silver-blaze	event_1_3	event	\N	Watson agrees to go with Holmes and Holmes invites him to do so	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_14", "sentence_15", "sentence_16", "sentence_18"], "communicatesContent": "My dear Watson, you would confer a great favour upon me by coming. And I think that your time will not be misspent, for there are points about the case which promise to make it an absolutely unique one. We have, I think, just time to catch our train at Paddington, and I will go further into the matter upon our journey. You would oblige me by bringing with you your very excellent field-glass."}
silver-blaze	event_1_4	event	\N	Holmes and Watson depart by train for Exeter	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_19", "sentence_20"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_1_5	event	\N	Holmes reads fresh papers during the train journey	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_19", "sentence_20"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_1_6	event	\N	Holmes speaks about the train's speed and calculates it from telegraph posts	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_21", "sentence_22", "sentence_23", "sentence_24", "sentence_25"], "communicatesContent": "We are going well. Our rate at present is fifty-three and a half miles an hour. Nor have I. But the telegraph posts upon this line are sixty yards apart, and the calculation is a simple one."}
silver-blaze	event_1_7	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson whether he has looked into the murder of John Straker and the disappearance of Silver Blaze	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_26", "sentence_27"], "communicatesContent": "I presume that you have looked into this matter of the murder of John Straker and the disappearance of Silver Blaze?"}
silver-blaze	event_1_8	event	\N	Holmes explains how he will approach the case	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_28", "sentence_29", "sentence_30", "sentence_31"], "communicatesContent": "It is one of those cases where the art of the reasoner should be used rather for the sifting of details than for the acquiring of fresh evidence. The tragedy has been so uncommon, so complete and of such personal importance to so many people, that we are suffering from a plethora of surmise, conjecture, and hypothesis. The difficulty is to detach the framework of fact—of absolute undeniable fact—from the embellishments of theorists and reporters. Then, having established ourselves upon this sound basis, it is our duty to see what inferences may be drawn and what are the special points upon which the whole mystery turns."}
silver-blaze	event_1_9	event	\N	Holmes receives telegrams from Colonel Ross and Inspector Gregory inviting his cooperation	0	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_32"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_2_1	event	\N	Holmes says Silver Blaze is from the Isonomy stock and has a brilliant record	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_46"], "communicatesContent": "Silver Blaze is from the Isonomy stock, and holds as brilliant a record as his famous ancestor."}
silver-blaze	event_2_2	event	\N	Holmes says Silver Blaze is in his fifth year and has won prizes for Colonel Ross	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_47"], "communicatesContent": "He is now in his fifth year, and has brought in turn each of the prizes of the turf to Colonel Ross, his fortunate owner."}
silver-blaze	event_2_3	event	\N	Holmes says Silver Blaze is the first favourite for the Wessex Cup	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_48"], "communicatesContent": "Up to the time of the catastrophe he was the first favourite for the Wessex Cup, the betting being three to one on him."}
silver-blaze	event_2_4	event	\N	Holmes says many people had an interest in preventing Silver Blaze from appearing	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_49", "sentence_50"], "communicatesContent": "It is obvious, therefore, that there were many people who had the strongest interest in preventing Silver Blaze from being there at the fall of the flag next Tuesday."}
silver-blaze	event_2_5	event	\N	Holmes says the danger was appreciated at King's Pyland and precautions were taken	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_51", "sentence_52"], "communicatesContent": "The fact was, of course, appreciated at King's Pyland. Every precaution was taken to guard the favourite."}
silver-blaze	event_2_6	event	\N	Holmes says John Straker was a retired jockey and served Colonel Ross	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_53", "sentence_54"], "communicatesContent": "The trainer, John Straker, is a retired jockey who rode in Colonel Ross's colours before he became too heavy for the weighing-chair. He has served the Colonel for five years as jockey and for seven as trainer, and has always shown himself to be a zealous and honest servant."}
silver-blaze	event_2_7	event	\N	Holmes says the establishment had three lads and four horses	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_55", "sentence_56", "sentence_57"], "communicatesContent": "Under him were three lads; for the establishment was a small one, containing only four horses in all. One of these lads sat up each night in the stable, while the others slept in the loft. All three bore excellent characters."}
silver-blaze	event_2_8	event	\N	Holmes says John Straker lived in a small villa with a maid-servant	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_58", "sentence_59"], "communicatesContent": "John Straker, who is a married man, lived in a small villa about two hundred yards from the stables. He has no children, keeps one maid-servant, and is comfortably off."}
silver-blaze	event_2_9	event	\N	Holmes describes the lonely country, the villas, Tavistock, Mapleton, and roaming gypsies	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_60", "sentence_61", "sentence_62"], "communicatesContent": "The country round is very lonely, but about half a mile to the north there is a small cluster of villas built by a Tavistock contractor for the use of invalids and others who may wish to enjoy the pure Dartmoor air. Tavistock itself lies two miles to the west, while across the moor, also about two miles distant, is the larger training establishment of Mapleton, which belongs to Lord Backwater, and is managed by Silas Brown. In every other direction the moor is a complete wilderness, inhabited only by a few roaming gypsies."}
silver-blaze	event_2_10	event	\N	Holmes says the general situation was as it was last Monday night when the catastrophe occurred	1	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_63"], "communicatesContent": "Such was the general situation last Monday night when the catastrophe occurred."}
silver-blaze	event_3_1	event	\N	The horses are exercised and watered and the stables are locked up	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_64"], "communicatesContent": null}
