silver-blaze	event_3_6	event	\N	The man steps into the lantern light and is seen to carry a heavy stick and wear a grey tweed suit, a cloth cap, and gaiters	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_70", "sentence_71", "sentence_72", "sentence_73"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_3_7	event	\N	The man asks Edith Baxter where he is and says he had nearly decided to sleep on the moor	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": "unnamed_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_74", "sentence_75"], "communicatesContent": "Tell me where I am? I had almost made up my mind to sleep on the moor, when I saw the light of your lantern."}
silver-blaze	event_3_8	event	\N	Edith Baxter says the man is close to the King's Pyland training-stables	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": "edith_baxter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_76"], "communicatesContent": "You are close to the King's Pyland training-stables."}
silver-blaze	event_3_9	event	\N	The man says he understands that a stable-boy sleeps there alone every night and asks for the boy's supper	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": "unnamed_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_77", "sentence_78", "sentence_79", "sentence_80"], "communicatesContent": "I understand that a stable-boy sleeps there alone every night. Perhaps that is his supper which you are carrying to him."}
silver-blaze	event_3_10	event	\N	The man takes a folded white paper from his waistcoat pocket and offers it to Edith Baxter for the boy	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": "unnamed_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_81", "sentence_82"], "communicatesContent": "See that the boy has this to-night, and you shall have the prettiest frock that money can buy."}
silver-blaze	event_3_11	event	\N	Edith Baxter runs past the man to the meal window	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_83"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_3_12	event	\N	Edith Baxter finds the window already opened and sees Ned Hunter seated inside	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_84"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_3_13	event	\N	Edith Baxter begins to tell Ned Hunter what happened while the stranger comes up again	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_85"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_3_14	event	\N	The stranger greets them at the window	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": "unnamed_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_86"], "communicatesContent": "Good-evening."}
silver-blaze	event_3_15	event	\N	The stranger makes a business proposal and mentions the Wessex Cup horses Silver Blaze and Bayard and the weights	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": "unnamed_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_91", "sentence_92", "sentence_93", "sentence_94"], "communicatesContent": "It's business that may put something into your pocket. You've two horses in for the Wessex Cup—Silver Blaze and Bayard. Let me have the straight tip and you won't be a loser. Is it a fact that at the weights Bayard could give the other a hundred yards in five furlongs, and that the stable have put their money on him?"}
silver-blaze	event_3_16	event	\N	Ned Hunter springs up and rushes across the stable to unloose the dog	2	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_95", "sentence_96"], "communicatesContent": null}
