silver-blaze	event_5_1	event	\N	Holmes recapitulates the police actions in the case	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_132"], "communicatesContent": "I shall now recapitulate what the police have done in the matter."}
silver-blaze	event_5_2	event	\N	Inspector Gregory arrests Fitzroy Simpson	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_132", "sentence_133", "sentence_134"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_5_3	event	\N	Fitzroy Simpson is identified by name	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_134"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_5_4	event	\N	Fitzroy Simpson's betting-book shows registered bets against the favourite	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_136"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_5_5	event	\N	Fitzroy Simpson speaks after arrest about coming to Dartmoor to seek information	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": "fitzroy_simpson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_137", "sentence_138"], "communicatesContent": "I had come down to Dartmoor in the hope of getting some information about the King's Pyland horses, and also about Desborough, the second favourite, which was in charge of Silas Brown at the Mapleton stables."}
silver-blaze	event_5_6	event	\N	Fitzroy Simpson denies sinister intent and says he wanted first-hand information	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": "fitzroy_simpson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_138"], "communicatesContent": "I had no sinister designs, and had simply wished to obtain first-hand information."}
silver-blaze	event_5_7	event	\N	Fitzroy Simpson is confronted with the cravat and turns pale	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_139"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_5_8	event	\N	Fitzroy Simpson's wet clothing and stick are noted as matching the storm and possible weapon	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_140"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_5_9	event	\N	Police theory is stated that Fitzroy Simpson drugged the lad and took the horse	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_150", "sentence_151", "sentence_152", "sentence_153", "sentence_154", "sentence_155"], "communicatesContent": "The police imagine that Fitzroy Simpson drugged the lad, obtained a duplicate key, opened the stable door, took out the horse, put on the bridle, led the horse away over the moor, was met or overtaken by the trainer, fought with him, beat out the trainer's brains with his heavy stick, and then either hid the horse or the horse bolted."}
silver-blaze	event_5_10	event	\N	Holmes says he will test the matter on the spot	4	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_5", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_156"], "communicatesContent": "I shall very quickly test the matter when I am once upon the spot."}
silver-blaze	event_6_1	event	\N	Holmes, Watson, Colonel Ross, and Inspector Gregory arrive at Tavistock by evening	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_157", "sentence_158", "sentence_159"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_6_2	event	\N	Colonel Ross greets Holmes and says he wants to avenge Straker and recover his horse	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_160", "sentence_161"], "communicatesContent": "I am delighted that you have come down, Mr. Holmes. The Inspector here has done all that could possibly be suggested, but I wish to leave no stone unturned in trying to avenge poor Straker and in recovering my horse."}
silver-blaze	event_6_3	event	\N	Holmes asks whether there are fresh developments	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_162", "sentence_163"], "communicatesContent": "Have there been any fresh developments?"}
silver-blaze	event_6_4	event	\N	Inspector Gregory says that little progress has been made	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_164"], "communicatesContent": "We have made very little progress."}
silver-blaze	event_6_5	event	\N	The group drives through Tavistock in an open carriage	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_165", "sentence_166"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_6_6	event	\N	Inspector Gregory discusses his case while Holmes asks questions and interjects	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_167", "sentence_168"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_6_7	event	\N	Gregory states that Fitzroy Simpson is the likely suspect	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_169", "sentence_170", "sentence_171"], "communicatesContent": "The net is drawn pretty close round Fitzroy Simpson, and I believe myself that he is our man. At the same time I recognise that the evidence is purely circumstantial, and that some new development may upset it."}
silver-blaze	event_6_8	event	\N	Holmes asks about Straker's knife	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_172"], "communicatesContent": "How about Straker's knife?"}
silver-blaze	event_6_9	event	\N	Gregory says that Straker wounded himself in his fall	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_173"], "communicatesContent": "We have quite come to the conclusion that he wounded himself in his fall."}
silver-blaze	event_6_10	event	\N	Watson suggests that Straker wounded himself in his fall	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_174", "sentence_175"], "communicatesContent": "My friend Dr. Watson made that suggestion to me as we came down. If so, it would tell against this man Simpson."}
silver-blaze	event_6_11	event	\N	Gregory says Simpson has no knife and no wound and is strongly suspected	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_176", "sentence_177", "sentence_178", "sentence_179", "sentence_180", "sentence_181"], "communicatesContent": "Undoubtedly. He has neither a knife nor any sign of a wound. The evidence against him is certainly very strong. He had a great interest in the disappearance of the favourite. He lies under suspicion of having poisoned the stable-boy, he was undoubtedly out in the storm, he was armed with a heavy stick, and his cravat was found in the dead man's hand. I really think we have enough to go before a jury."}
silver-blaze	event_6_12	event	\N	Holmes rejects Gregory's case against Simpson and raises objections	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_182", "sentence_183", "sentence_184", "sentence_185", "sentence_186", "sentence_187", "sentence_188", "sentence_189"], "communicatesContent": "A clever counsel would tear it all to rags. Why should he take the horse out of the stable? If he wished to injure it why could he not do it there? Has a duplicate key been found in his possession? What chemist sold him the powdered opium? Above all, where could he, a stranger to the district, hide a horse, and such a horse as this? What is his own explanation as to the paper which he wished the maid to give to the stable-boy?"}
silver-blaze	event_6_13	event	\N	Gregory says Simpson claimed the paper was a ten-pound note and that one was found in his purse	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_190", "sentence_191"], "communicatesContent": "He says that it was a ten-pound note. One was found in his purse."}
silver-blaze	event_6_14	event	\N	Gregory says Simpson is not a stranger to Tavistock and had lodged there twice	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_192", "sentence_193", "sentence_194"], "communicatesContent": "But your other difficulties are not so formidable as they seem. He is not a stranger to the district. He has twice lodged at Tavistock in the summer."}
silver-blaze	event_6_15	event	\N	Gregory says the opium probably came from London, the key was thrown away, and the horse may be in a pit or old mine	5	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_6", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_195", "sentence_196", "sentence_197"], "communicatesContent": "The opium was probably brought from London. The key, having served its purpose, would be hurled away. The horse may be at the bottom of one of the pits or old mines upon the moor."}
silver-blaze	event_7_1	event	\N	The inspector says the cravat belongs to Simpson and that Simpson lost it	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_199"], "communicatesContent": "He acknowledges that it is his, and declares that he had lost it."}
silver-blaze	event_7_2	event	\N	A new element is introduced into the case	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_200"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_3	event	\N	Holmes pricks up his ears	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_201"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_4	event	\N	The police find traces of gypsies camping near the murder scene	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_202", "sentence_203"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_5	event	\N	The inspector says the gypsies were gone on Tuesday	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_203"], "communicatesContent": "On Tuesday they were gone."}
silver-blaze	event_7_6	event	\N	The inspector proposes that Simpson may have led the horse to the gypsies	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_204"], "communicatesContent": "Now, presuming that there was some understanding between Simpson and these gypsies, might he not have been leading the horse to them when he was overtaken, and may they not have him now?"}
silver-blaze	event_7_7	event	\N	Holmes agrees that the possibility exists	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_205"], "communicatesContent": "It is certainly possible."}
silver-blaze	event_7_8	event	\N	The police scour the moor for the gypsies and examine stables and out-houses around Tavistock	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_206", "sentence_207"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_9	event	\N	Holmes asks about the nearby training-stable	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_208"], "communicatesContent": "There is another training-stable quite close, I understand?"}
silver-blaze	event_7_10	event	\N	The inspector says the nearby stable is a factor and notes its owners' interest in the favourite's disappearance	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_209", "sentence_210", "sentence_211", "sentence_212"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, and that is a factor which we must certainly not neglect. As Desborough, their horse, was second in the betting, they had an interest in the disappearance of the favourite. Silas Brown, the trainer, is known to have had large bets upon the event, and he was no friend to poor Straker. We have, however, examined the stables, and there is nothing to connect him with the affair."}
silver-blaze	event_7_11	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Simpson is connected with the Mapleton stables	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_213"], "communicatesContent": "And nothing to connect this man Simpson with the interests of the Mapleton stables?"}
silver-blaze	event_7_12	event	\N	The inspector says there is nothing at all to connect Simpson with Mapleton	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_214"], "communicatesContent": "Nothing at all."}
silver-blaze	event_7_13	event	\N	The carriage stops at the villa by the road	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_216"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_14	event	\N	The party arrives at the villa and Holmes remains in the carriage until roused	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_219", "sentence_220"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_15	event	\N	Holmes explains that he had been day-dreaming	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_221", "sentence_222"], "communicatesContent": "Excuse me. I was day-dreaming."}
silver-blaze	event_7_16	event	\N	Watson notes Holmes's excitement and inferred clue-hunting	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_223"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_7_17	event	\N	Gregory asks Holmes whether he would rather go to the crime scene	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_224", "sentence_225"], "communicatesContent": "Perhaps you would prefer at once to go on to the scene of the crime, Mr. Holmes?"}
silver-blaze	event_7_18	event	\N	Holmes says he prefers to stay and ask details	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_226", "sentence_227", "sentence_232", "sentence_233", "sentence_234"], "communicatesContent": "I think that I should prefer to stay here a little and go into one or two questions of detail. Straker was brought back here, I presume? He has been in your service some years, Colonel Ross? I presume that you made an inventory of what he had in his pockets at the time of his death, Inspector? I should be very glad."}
silver-blaze	event_7_19	event	\N	Gregory says Straker lies upstairs, the inquest is tomorrow, and he has the pocket contents in the sitting-room	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_228", "sentence_229", "sentence_233"], "communicatesContent": "Yes; he lies upstairs. The inquest is to-morrow. I have the things themselves in the sitting-room, if you would care to see them."}
silver-blaze	event_7_20	event	\N	The Inspector unlocks a tin box and lays Straker's pocket contents out on the table	6	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_235", "sentence_236", "sentence_237", "sentence_238"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_1	event	\N	Holmes examines the knife closely	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_239"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_2	event	\N	Holmes states that the knife has blood-stains and was found in the dead man's grasp	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_240", "sentence_241"], "communicatesContent": "I presume, as I see blood-stains upon it, that it is the one which was found in the dead man's grasp. Watson, this knife is surely in your line?"}
silver-blaze	event_8_3	event	\N	Watson identifies the knife as a cataract knife	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_242"], "communicatesContent": "It is what we call a cataract knife."}
silver-blaze	event_8_4	event	\N	Holmes comments on the knife's delicacy and awkwardness for travel	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_243", "sentence_244", "sentence_245"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_5	event	\N	The Inspector states that the cork tip was found beside the body	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_246"], "communicatesContent": "The tip was guarded by a disk of cork which we found beside his body."}
silver-blaze	event_8_6	event	\N	The Inspector reports Mrs. Straker's account of the knife	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_247", "sentence_248"], "communicatesContent": "His wife tells us that the knife had lain upon the dressing-table, and that he had picked it up as he left the room. It was a poor weapon, but perhaps the best that he could lay his hands on at the moment."}
silver-blaze	event_8_7	event	\N	Holmes asks about the papers	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_249", "sentence_250"], "communicatesContent": "Very possible. How about these papers?"}
silver-blaze	event_8_8	event	\N	The Inspector identifies the papers	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253"], "communicatesContent": "Three of them are receipted hay-dealers' accounts. One of them is a letter of instructions from Colonel Ross. This other is a milliner's account for thirty-seven pounds fifteen made out by Madame Lesurier, of Bond Street, to William Derbyshire."}
silver-blaze	event_8_9	event	\N	The Inspector reports Mrs. Straker's statement about Derbyshire	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_254"], "communicatesContent": "Mrs. Straker tells us that Derbyshire was a friend of her husband's and that occasionally his letters were addressed here."}
silver-blaze	event_8_10	event	\N	Holmes remarks on Derbyshire's expensive tastes and the cost of the costume	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_255", "sentence_256"], "communicatesContent": "Madam Derbyshire had somewhat expensive tastes. Twenty-two guineas is rather heavy for a single costume."}
silver-blaze	event_8_11	event	\N	Holmes and the others go down to the scene of the crime	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_257"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_12	event	\N	Mrs. Straker steps forward and grips the Inspector's sleeve	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_258"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_13	event	\N	Mrs. Straker appears haggard and eager	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_259"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_14	event	\N	Mrs. Straker asks whether the missing things have been found	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "mrs_straker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_260", "sentence_261", "sentence_262"], "communicatesContent": "Have you got them? Have you found them?"}
silver-blaze	event_8_15	event	\N	The Inspector says Holmes has come from London to help	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_263", "sentence_264"], "communicatesContent": "No, Mrs. Straker. But Mr. Holmes here has come from London to help us, and we shall do all that is possible."}
silver-blaze	event_8_16	event	\N	Holmes asks Mrs. Straker whether he met her in Plymouth	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_265", "sentence_266"], "communicatesContent": "Surely I met you in Plymouth at a garden-party some little time ago, Mrs. Straker?"}
silver-blaze	event_8_17	event	\N	Mrs. Straker denies Holmes's identification	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "mrs_straker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_267"], "communicatesContent": "No, sir; you are mistaken."}
silver-blaze	event_8_18	event	\N	Holmes claims he recognized Mrs. Straker by her costume	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_268", "sentence_269", "sentence_270"], "communicatesContent": "Dear me! Why, I could have sworn to it. You wore a costume of dove-coloured silk with ostrich-feather trimming."}
silver-blaze	event_8_19	event	\N	Mrs. Straker denies owning such a dress	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "mrs_straker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_271"], "communicatesContent": "I never had such a dress, sir."}
silver-blaze	event_8_20	event	\N	Holmes accepts the denial and follows the Inspector outside	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_272", "sentence_273"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_21	event	\N	Holmes and the others reach the hollow where the body was found	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_274"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_22	event	\N	Holmes comments on the lack of wind	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_276"], "communicatesContent": "There was no wind that night, I understand."}
silver-blaze	event_8_23	event	\N	The Inspector states that there was heavy rain	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_277"], "communicatesContent": "None; but very heavy rain."}
silver-blaze	event_8_24	event	\N	Holmes says the overcoat was placed on the furze-bush	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_278"], "communicatesContent": "In that case the overcoat was not blown against the furze-bush, but placed there."}
silver-blaze	event_8_25	event	\N	The Inspector says the overcoat was laid across the bush	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_279"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, it was laid across the bush."}
silver-blaze	event_8_26	event	\N	Holmes notes the trampled ground	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_280", "sentence_281"], "communicatesContent": "You fill me with interest, I perceive that the ground has been trampled up a good deal. No doubt many feet have been here since Monday night."}
silver-blaze	event_8_27	event	\N	The Inspector states that matting was laid at the side and everyone stood on it	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_282"], "communicatesContent": "A piece of matting has been laid here at the side, and we have all stood upon that."}
silver-blaze	event_8_28	event	\N	The Inspector presents the boot, shoe, and horseshoe in a bag	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_284"], "communicatesContent": "In this bag I have one of the boots which Straker wore, one of Fitzroy Simpson's shoes, and a cast horseshoe of Silver Blaze."}
silver-blaze	event_8_29	event	\N	Holmes praises the Inspector and takes the bag	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_285", "sentence_286"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_30	event	\N	Holmes studies the trampled mud	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_8_31	event	\N	Holmes notices a half-burned wax vesta in the mud	7	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_288", "sentence_289", "sentence_290", "sentence_291"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_9_1	event	\N	Inspector finds the hidden object in the mud	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_292", "sentence_293", "sentence_294"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_9_2	event	\N	Inspector compares the boots with marks on the ground	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_298"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_9_3	event	\N	Inspector climbs to the rim of the hollow and searches the ferns and bushes	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_299"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_9_4	event	\N	Inspector reports that no more tracks are present	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": "inspector_gregory", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_300", "sentence_301"], "communicatesContent": "there are no more tracks; I have examined the ground very carefully for a hundred yards in each direction"}
silver-blaze	event_12_6	event	\N	Colonel Ross says he would prefer to have the horse	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_451"], "communicatesContent": "I should prefer to have the horse."}
a-case-of-identity	section_18	section	\N	Section 18	17	{"wordCount": 172}
silver-blaze	event_9_5	event	\N	Holmes rises and says he will walk over the moor and pocket the horseshoe	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_303", "sentence_304", "sentence_305"], "communicatesContent": "I should not have the impertinence to do it again after what you say. But I should like to take a little walk over the moor before it grows dark, that I may know my ground to-morrow, and I think that I shall put this horseshoe into my pocket for luck."}
silver-blaze	event_9_6	event	\N	Colonel Ross invites the Inspector to return with him and asks advice about the Cup entry	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_306", "sentence_307", "sentence_308"], "communicatesContent": "I wish you would come back with me, Inspector. There are several points on which I should like your advice, and especially as to whether we do not owe it to the public to remove our horse's name from the entries for the Cup."}
silver-blaze	event_9_7	event	\N	Holmes tells Colonel Ross to let the horse's name stand	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_309", "sentence_310"], "communicatesContent": "Certainly not. I should let the name stand."}
silver-blaze	event_9_8	event	\N	Colonel Ross thanks Holmes and says they will be at Straker's house	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_313"], "communicatesContent": "I am very glad to have had your opinion, sir. You will find us at poor Straker's house when you have finished your walk, and we can drive together into Tavistock."}
silver-blaze	event_9_9	event	\N	Colonel Ross and the Inspector turn back while Holmes and Watson walk across the moor	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_314", "sentence_315", "sentence_316"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_9_10	event	\N	Holmes explains his hypothesis about the horse's destination	8	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_317", "sentence_318", "sentence_319", "sentence_320", "sentence_321", "sentence_322", "sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325", "sentence_326", "sentence_327", "sentence_328", "sentence_329", "sentence_330", "sentence_331", "sentence_332", "sentence_333", "sentence_334", "sentence_335", "sentence_336"], "communicatesContent": "It's this way, Watson. We may leave the question of who killed John Straker for the instant, and confine ourselves to finding out what has become of the horse. Now, supposing that he broke away during or after the tragedy, where could he have gone to? The horse is a very gregarious creature. If left to himself his instincts would have been either to return to King's Pyland or go over to Mapleton. Why should he run wild upon the moor? He would surely have been seen by now. And why should gypsies kidnap him? These people always clear out when they hear of trouble, for they do not wish to be pestered by the police. They could not hope to sell such a horse. They would run a great risk and gain nothing by taking him. Surely that is clear. Where is he, then? I have already said that he must have gone to King's Pyland or to Mapleton. He is not at King's Pyland. Therefore he is at Mapleton. Let us take that as a working hypothesis and see what it leads us to. This part of the moor, as the Inspector remarked, is very hard and dry. But it falls away towards Mapleton, and you can see from here that there is a long hollow over yonder, which must have been very wet on Monday night. If our supposition is correct, then the horse must have crossed that, and there is the point where we should look for his tracks."}
silver-blaze	event_10_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson reach the hollow	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson split up to inspect the ground	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_338"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_3	event	\N	Holmes discovers a horse track and fits a shoe to the impression	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_339"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_4	event	\N	Holmes comments on imagination and Gregory	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_340", "sentence_341", "sentence_342", "sentence_343"], "communicatesContent": "See the value of imagination. It is the one quality which Gregory lacks. We imagined what might have happened, acted upon the supposition, and find ourselves justified. Let us proceed."}
silver-blaze	event_10_5	event	\N	Holmes and Watson cross the marshy ground and follow the tracks	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_344", "sentence_345", "sentence_346"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_6	event	\N	Holmes finds the tracks near Mapleton	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_347"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_7	event	\N	A man's track appears beside the horse's track	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_348"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_8	event	\N	Watson remarks that the horse had been alone before	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_349", "sentence_350", "sentence_351"], "communicatesContent": "The horse was alone before."}
silver-blaze	event_10_9	event	\N	The double track turns toward King's Pyland	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_352", "sentence_353"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_10	event	\N	Holmes and Watson follow the returning track	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_354", "sentence_355", "sentence_356", "sentence_357", "sentence_358"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_11	event	\N	The track ends at the Mapleton stables	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_359", "sentence_360"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_12	event	\N	Holmes questions the groom at the stables	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_361", "sentence_362", "sentence_363", "sentence_364"], "communicatesContent": "I only wished to ask a question. Should I be too early to see your master, Mr. Silas Brown, if I were to call at five o'clock to-morrow morning?"}
silver-blaze	event_12_7	event	\N	Holmes announces he is ready for Tavistock	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_452", "sentence_453"], "communicatesContent": "Now, gentlemen, I am quite ready for Tavistock."}
yellow-face	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
silver-blaze	event_10_13	event	\N	The groom identifies Silas Brown as being present	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": "stable_lad", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_365", "sentence_366", "sentence_367", "sentence_368"], "communicatesContent": "Bless you, sir, if any one is about he will be, for he is always the first stirring. But here he is, sir, to answer your questions for himself. No, sir, no; it is as much as my place is worth to let him see me touch your money. Afterwards, if you like."}
silver-blaze	event_10_14	event	\N	Silas Brown confronts Holmes and orders them away	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": "silas_brown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_369", "sentence_370", "sentence_371", "sentence_372", "sentence_373", "sentence_374"], "communicatesContent": "What's this, Dawson! No gossiping! Go about your business! And you, what the devil do you want here?"}
silver-blaze	event_10_15	event	\N	Holmes whispers to Silas Brown and gets an angry reaction	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_375", "sentence_376", "sentence_377", "sentence_378", "sentence_379", "sentence_380", "sentence_381", "sentence_382", "sentence_383", "sentence_384", "sentence_385", "sentence_386", "sentence_387", "sentence_388"], "communicatesContent": "Ten minutes' talk with you, my good sir."}
silver-blaze	event_10_16	event	\N	Holmes and Silas Brown speak in Brown's parlour	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_384", "sentence_385", "sentence_386", "sentence_387", "sentence_388", "sentence_389"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_10_17	event	\N	Holmes and Silas Brown reappear after twenty minutes	9	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_389", "sentence_390", "sentence_391", "sentence_392"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_11_1	event	\N	Holmes confronts Silas Brown and warns against mistakes or tricks	10	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_393", "sentence_394", "sentence_395", "sentence_396", "sentence_397", "sentence_398", "sentence_399", "sentence_400", "sentence_401", "sentence_402", "sentence_403", "sentence_404", "sentence_405", "sentence_406"], "communicatesContent": "There must be no mistake. No, don't. I shall write to you about it. No tricks, now, or—"}
silver-blaze	event_11_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson set off for King's Pyland	10	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_406"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_11_3	event	\N	Holmes describes Silas Brown's actions on the morning of the horse's disappearance	10	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_407", "sentence_408", "sentence_409", "sentence_410", "sentence_411", "sentence_412", "sentence_413", "sentence_414", "sentence_415"], "communicatesContent": "He tried to bluster out of it, but I described to him so exactly what his actions had been upon that morning that he is convinced that I was watching him. Of course you observed the peculiarly square toes in the impressions, and that his own boots exactly corresponded to them. Again, of course no subordinate would have dared to do such a thing. I described to him how, when according to his custom he was the first down, he perceived a strange horse wandering over the moor. How he went out to it, and his astonishment at recognising, from the white forehead which has given the favourite its name, that chance had put in his power the only horse which could beat the one upon which he had put his money. Then I described how his first impulse had been to lead him back to King's Pyland, and how the devil had shown him how he could hide the horse until the race was over, and how he had led it back and concealed it at Mapleton. When I told him every detail he gave it up and thought only of saving his own skin."}
silver-blaze	event_11_4	event	\N	Holmes says Silas Brown will guard the horse to obtain mercy	10	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_416", "sentence_417", "sentence_418", "sentence_419", "sentence_420"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, an old horse-faker like him has many a dodge. My dear fellow, he will guard it as the apple of his eye. He knows that his only hope of mercy is to produce it safe."}
silver-blaze	event_11_5	event	\N	Holmes says Colonel Ross will not be told about the horse and that he will use his own methods	10	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_421", "sentence_422", "sentence_423", "sentence_424", "sentence_425", "sentence_426", "sentence_427", "sentence_428", "sentence_429", "sentence_430", "sentence_431"], "communicatesContent": "The matter does not rest with Colonel Ross. I follow my own methods, and tell as much or as little as I choose. That is the advantage of being unofficial. I don't know whether you observed it, Watson, but the Colonel's manner has been just a trifle cavalier to me. I am inclined now to have a little amusement at his expense. Say nothing to him about the horse. And of course this is all quite a minor point compared to the question of who killed John Straker. On the contrary, we both go back to London by the night train."}
silver-blaze	event_11_6	event	\N	Holmes and Watson return to the trainer's house and find Colonel Ross and Inspector Gregory waiting in the parlour	10	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_434", "sentence_435"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_12_1	event	\N	Holmes says he and Watson will return to town by the night-express	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_436", "sentence_437"], "communicatesContent": "My friend and I return to town by the night-express."}
silver-blaze	event_12_2	event	\N	Holmes asks for a photograph of John Straker	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_443", "sentence_444"], "communicatesContent": "Might I ask for a photograph of Mr. John Straker?"}
silver-blaze	event_12_3	event	\N	Holmes asks Gregory to wait while he questions the maid	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_445", "sentence_446"], "communicatesContent": "If I might ask you to wait here for an instant, I have a question which I should like to put to the maid."}
silver-blaze	event_12_4	event	\N	Colonel Ross says he is disappointed in Holmes and sees no progress	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_447", "sentence_448"], "communicatesContent": "I must say that I am rather disappointed in our London consultant. I do not see that we are any further than when he came."}
silver-blaze	event_12_5	event	\N	Watson says Holmes has assured them the horse will run	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_449", "sentence_450"], "communicatesContent": "At least you have his assurance that your horse will run."}
yellow-face	yellow-face-section_5	section	\N	Section 5	4	{"wordCount": 677}
silver-blaze	event_12_8	event	\N	A stable-lad holds open the carriage door for the party	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_454"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_12_9	event	\N	Holmes questions the stable-lad about the sheep in the paddock	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_455", "sentence_456", "sentence_457", "sentence_458", "sentence_459", "sentence_460"], "communicatesContent": "You have a few sheep in the paddock. Who attends to them? Have you noticed anything amiss with them of late?"}
silver-blaze	event_12_10	event	\N	The stable-lad says three sheep have gone lame	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "stable_lad", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_460"], "communicatesContent": "Well, sir, not of much account; but three of them have gone lame, sir."}
silver-blaze	event_12_11	event	\N	Holmes praises the observation and orders the coach to drive on	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_461", "sentence_462", "sentence_463", "sentence_464"], "communicatesContent": "A long shot, Watson; a very long shot. Gregory, let me recommend to your attention this singular epidemic among the sheep. Drive on, coachman!"}
silver-blaze	event_12_12	event	\N	Holmes points Gregory to the dog's silence in the night-time	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_466", "sentence_467", "sentence_468", "sentence_469", "sentence_470", "sentence_471", "sentence_472"], "communicatesContent": "Exceedingly so. To the curious incident of the dog in the night-time."}
silver-blaze	event_12_13	event	\N	Holmes and Watson travel by train to Winchester for the Wessex Cup race	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_473"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_12_14	event	\N	Colonel Ross meets Holmes and Watson outside the station and drives them to the course	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_474"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_12_15	event	\N	Colonel Ross says he has not seen his horse	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_475", "sentence_476"], "communicatesContent": "I have seen nothing of my horse."}
silver-blaze	event_12_16	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Colonel Ross would recognize Silver Blaze	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_477", "sentence_478", "sentence_479", "sentence_480", "sentence_481"], "communicatesContent": "I suppose that you would know him when you saw him?"}
silver-blaze	event_12_17	event	\N	Holmes asks about the betting and learns the odds have shortened	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_482", "sentence_483", "sentence_484"], "communicatesContent": "How is the betting?"}
silver-blaze	event_12_18	event	\N	Holmes remarks that somebody knows something	11	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_12", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_485", "sentence_486", "sentence_487"], "communicatesContent": "Hum! Somebody knows something, that is clear."}
silver-blaze	event_13_1	event	\N	The race card lists the Wessex Plate entries	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_488", "sentence_489", "sentence_490", "sentence_491", "sentence_492", "sentence_493", "sentence_494", "sentence_495", "sentence_496", "sentence_497", "sentence_498", "sentence_499", "sentence_500", "sentence_501", "sentence_502", "sentence_503", "sentence_504", "sentence_505", "sentence_506"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_13_2	event	\N	The Colonel says he scratched the other horse and staked everything on Holmes's word	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_507"], "communicatesContent": "We scratched our other one, and put all hopes on your word."}
silver-blaze	event_13_3	event	\N	The ring announces odds on Silver Blaze	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_508", "sentence_509", "sentence_510", "sentence_511", "sentence_512", "sentence_513", "sentence_514"], "communicatesContent": "Five to four against Silver Blaze! Five to fifteen against Desborough! Five to four on the field!"}
silver-blaze	event_13_4	event	\N	The narrator announces that all six horses are up	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_515", "sentence_516"], "communicatesContent": "There are the numbers up. They are all six there."}
silver-blaze	event_13_5	event	\N	The Colonel reacts in agitation and says his horse is running	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_517", "sentence_518", "sentence_519", "sentence_520", "sentence_521", "sentence_522"], "communicatesContent": "Then my horse is running. But I don't see him. My colours have not passed."}
silver-blaze	event_13_6	event	\N	A bay horse with the Colonel's colors emerges from the weighing enclosure	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_523"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_13_7	event	\N	The Colonel denies that the bay horse is his	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_524", "sentence_525", "sentence_526"], "communicatesContent": "That's not my horse. That beast has not a white hair upon its body. What is this that you have done, Mr. Holmes?"}
silver-blaze	event_13_8	event	\N	Holmes tells the Colonel to wait and see how the horse gets on	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_527"], "communicatesContent": "Well, well, let us see how he gets on."}
silver-blaze	event_13_9	event	\N	Holmes watches the race through the field-glass	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_528"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_13_10	event	\N	Holmes exclaims that the start is excellent	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_529", "sentence_530", "sentence_531"], "communicatesContent": "Capital! An excellent start!"}
silver-blaze	event_13_11	event	\N	Holmes points out the horses coming round the curve	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_532"], "communicatesContent": "There they are, coming round the curve!"}
silver-blaze	event_13_12	event	\N	The horses race up the straight	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_533", "sentence_534", "sentence_535"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	yellow-face-section_6	section	\N	Section 6	5	{"wordCount": 650}
silver-blaze	event_13_13	event	\N	The Colonel says it is his race and asks Holmes to end the mystery	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_536", "sentence_537", "sentence_538"], "communicatesContent": "It's my race, anyhow. I confess that I can make neither head nor tail of it. Don't you think that you have kept up your mystery long enough, Mr. Holmes?"}
silver-blaze	event_13_14	event	\N	Holmes leads the Colonel and Watson to the weighing enclosure to see the horse	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_539", "sentence_540", "sentence_541"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_13_15	event	\N	Holmes instructs them to wash the horse's face and leg in spirits of wine	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_542"], "communicatesContent": "You have only to wash his face and his leg in spirits of wine, and you will find that he is the same old Silver Blaze as ever."}
silver-blaze	event_13_16	event	\N	Holmes says he found the horse in the hands of a faker and ran him as he was sent over	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_543", "sentence_544"], "communicatesContent": "I found him in the hands of a faker, and took the liberty of running him just as he was sent over."}
silver-blaze	event_13_17	event	\N	The Colonel thanks Holmes for recovering the horse and asks him to find Straker's murderer	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_545", "sentence_546", "sentence_547", "sentence_548", "sentence_549", "sentence_550"], "communicatesContent": "My dear sir, you have done wonders. The horse looks very fit and well. It never went better in its life. I owe you a thousand apologies for having doubted your ability. You have done me a great service by recovering my horse. You would do me a greater still if you could lay your hands on the murderer of John Straker."}
silver-blaze	event_13_18	event	\N	Holmes says he has found Straker's murderer	12	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_13", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_551", "sentence_552", "sentence_553", "sentence_554", "sentence_555", "sentence_556", "sentence_557", "sentence_558"], "communicatesContent": "I have done so."}
silver-blaze	event_14_1	event	\N	The Colonel angrily objects to Holmes's remark	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_559", "sentence_560"], "communicatesContent": "I quite recognise that I am under obligations to you, Mr. Holmes, but I must regard what you have just said as either a very bad joke or an insult."}
silver-blaze	event_14_2	event	\N	Holmes laughs and denies associating the Colonel with the crime	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_561", "sentence_562"], "communicatesContent": "I assure you that I have not associated you with the crime, Colonel."}
silver-blaze	event_14_3	event	\N	Holmes identifies the horse as the murderer and touches it	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_563", "sentence_564", "sentence_565", "sentence_566"], "communicatesContent": "The real murderer is standing immediately behind you."}
silver-blaze	event_14_4	event	\N	Holmes says the horse acted in self-defence and postpones his explanation	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_567", "sentence_568", "sentence_569"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, the horse. And it may lessen his guilt if I say that it was done in self-defence, and that John Straker was a man who was entirely unworthy of your confidence. But there goes the bell, and as I stand to win a little on this next race, I shall defer a lengthy explanation until a more fitting time."}
silver-blaze	event_14_5	event	\N	Holmes and the others travel back to London while Holmes narrates the case	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_570"], "communicatesContent": "The events which had occurred at the Dartmoor training-stables upon the Monday night and the means by which he had unravelled them."}
silver-blaze	event_14_6	event	\N	Holmes states that his earlier theories were wrong	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_571", "sentence_572"], "communicatesContent": "Any theories which I had formed from the newspaper reports were entirely erroneous."}
silver-blaze	event_14_7	event	\N	Holmes says he went to Devonshire suspecting Fitzroy Simpson	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_573"], "communicatesContent": "I went to Devonshire with the conviction that Fitzroy Simpson was the true culprit, although, of course, I saw that the evidence against him was by no means complete."}
silver-blaze	event_14_8	event	\N	Holmes explains that the curried mutton suggested the truth to him	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_574", "sentence_575", "sentence_576"], "communicatesContent": "It was while I was in the carriage, just as we reached the trainer's house, that the immense significance of the curried mutton occurred to me. You may remember that I was distrait, and remained sitting after you had all alighted. I was marvelling in my own mind how I could possibly have overlooked so obvious a clue."}
silver-blaze	event_14_9	event	\N	The Colonel says he cannot yet see the point of Holmes's reasoning	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_577"], "communicatesContent": "That even now I cannot see how it helps us."}
silver-blaze	event_14_10	event	\N	Holmes explains how opium in curry could be detected or disguised	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_578", "sentence_579", "sentence_580", "sentence_581", "sentence_582", "sentence_583", "sentence_584", "sentence_585", "sentence_586", "sentence_587"], "communicatesContent": "It was the first link in my chain of reasoning. Powdered opium is by no means tasteless. The flavour is not disagreeable, but it is perceptible. Were it mixed with any ordinary dish the eater would undoubtedly detect it, and would probably eat no more. A curry was exactly the medium which would disguise this taste. By no possible supposition could this stranger, Fitzroy Simpson, have caused curry to be served in the trainer's family that night, and it is surely too monstrous a coincidence to suppose that he happened to come along with powdered opium upon the very night when a dish happened to be served which would disguise the flavour. That is unthinkable. Therefore Simpson becomes eliminated from the case, and our attention centres upon Straker and his wife, the only two people who could have chosen curried mutton for supper that night. The opium was added after the dish was set aside for the stable-boy, for the others had the same for supper with no ill effects. Which of them, then, had access to that dish without the maid seeing them?"}
silver-blaze	event_14_11	event	\N	Holmes explains the significance of the dog's silence	13	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_588", "sentence_589", "sentence_590"], "communicatesContent": "Before deciding that question I had grasped the significance of the silence of the dog, for one true inference invariably suggests others. The Simpson incident had shown me that a dog was kept in the stables, and yet, though some one had been in and had fetched out a horse, he had not barked enough to arouse the two lads in the loft. Obviously the midnight visitor was some one whom the dog knew well."}
silver-blaze	event_15_1	event	\N	Holmes explains a suspected scheme to injure Silver Blaze with a knife	14	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_15", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_591", "sentence_593", "sentence_594", "sentence_595", "sentence_596", "sentence_597", "sentence_598"], "communicatesContent": null}
silver-blaze	event_15_2	event	\N	Holmes describes evidence from Straker's pockets and explains the motive for the crime	14	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_15", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_599", "sentence_600", "sentence_616", "sentence_617", "sentence_618", "sentence_619", "sentence_620", "sentence_621", "sentence_622"], "communicatesContent": "And they did so. You cannot have forgotten the singular knife which was found in the dead man's hand, a knife which certainly no sane man would choose for a weapon. It was, as Dr. Watson told us, a form of knife which is used for the most delicate operations known in surgery. It was to be used for a delicate operation that night. As a man of the world, Colonel, you know that men do not carry other people's bills about in their pockets. We have most of us quite enough to do to settle our own. I at once concluded that Straker was leading a double life, and keeping a second establishment. The nature of the bill showed that there was a lady in the case, and one who had expensive tastes. Liberal as you are with your servants, one can hardly expect that they can buy twenty-guinea walking dresses for their ladies. I questioned Mrs. Straker as to the dress without her knowing it, and having satisfied myself that it had never reached her, I made a note of the milliner's address, and felt that by calling there with Straker's photograph I could easily dispose of the mythical Derbyshire."}
silver-blaze	event_15_3	event	\N	Holmes explains that Straker led Silver Blaze out to a hollow and attempted the operation there	14	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_15", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_623", "sentence_624", "sentence_625", "sentence_626", "sentence_627", "sentence_628"], "communicatesContent": "From that time on all was plain. Straker had led out the horse to a hollow where his light would be invisible. Simpson in his flight had dropped his cravat, and Straker had picked it up—with some idea, perhaps, that he might use it in securing the horse's leg. Once in the hollow, he had got behind the horse and had struck a light; but the creature frightened at the sudden glare, and with the strange instinct of animals feeling that some mischief was intended, had lashed out, and the steel shoe had struck Straker full on the forehead. He had already, in spite of the rain, taken off his overcoat in order to do his delicate task, and so, as he fell, his knife gashed his thigh. Do I make it clear?"}
silver-blaze	event_16_1	event	\N	The Colonel exclaims that something is wonderful	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_629", "sentence_630", "sentence_631"], "communicatesContent": "Wonderful! Wonderful!"}
silver-blaze	event_16_2	event	\N	The speaker says Colonel Ross might have been there	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_631", "sentence_632"], "communicatesContent": "You might have been there!"}
silver-blaze	event_16_3	event	\N	The speaker explains that his final shot was a very long one	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_633"], "communicatesContent": "My final shot was, I confess a very long one."}
silver-blaze	event_16_4	event	\N	The speaker explains that Straker would have needed practice for the tendon-nicking	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_634", "sentence_635", "sentence_636"], "communicatesContent": "It struck me that so astute a man as Straker would not undertake this delicate tendon-nicking without a little practice. What could he practice on? My eyes fell upon the sheep, and I asked a question which, rather to my surprise, showed that my surmise was correct."}
silver-blaze	event_16_5	event	\N	The speaker says he called on the milliner in London and learned Straker was known as Derbyshire	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_637", "sentence_638"], "communicatesContent": "When I returned to London I called upon the milliner, who had recognised Straker as an excellent customer of the name of Derbyshire, who had a very dashing wife, with a strong partiality for expensive dresses. I have no doubt that this woman had plunged him over head and ears in debt, and so led him into this miserable plot."}
silver-blaze	event_16_6	event	\N	The Colonel asks where the horse was	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "colonel_ross", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_639", "sentence_640"], "communicatesContent": "You have explained all but one thing. Where was the horse?"}
silver-blaze	event_16_7	event	\N	The speaker says the horse bolted and was cared for by a neighbour	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_641", "sentence_642"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, it bolted, and was cared for by one of your neighbours. We must have an amnesty in that direction, I think."}
silver-blaze	event_16_8	event	\N	The speaker identifies the train location as Clapham Junction and says they will soon be in Victoria	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_643"], "communicatesContent": "This is Clapham Junction, if I am not mistaken, and we shall be in Victoria in less than ten minutes."}
silver-blaze	event_16_9	event	\N	The speaker invites Colonel Ross to smoke a cigar in their rooms	15	{"section": "silver-blaze-section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_644"], "communicatesContent": "If you care to smoke a cigar in our rooms, Colonel, I shall be happy to give you any other details which might interest you."}
yellow-face	yellow-face	story	\N	The Yellow Face	\N	{"sourceFile": "data/raw/memoirs/yellow-face.txt", "granularity": "sentence"}
yellow-face	yellow-face-section_1	section	\N	Section 1	0	{"wordCount": 644}
yellow-face	yellow-face-section_2	section	\N	Section 2	1	{"wordCount": 613}
yellow-face	yellow-face-section_3	section	\N	Section 3	2	{"wordCount": 718}
yellow-face	yellow-face-section_4	section	\N	Section 4	3	{"wordCount": 791}
yellow-face	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "In publishing these short sketches based upon the numerous cases in which my companion's singular gifts have made us the listeners to, and eventually the actors in, some strange drama, it is only natural that I should dwell rather upon his successes than upon his failures.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "And this not so much for the sake of his reputation—for, indeed, it was when he was at his wits' end that his energy and his versatility were most admirable—but because where he failed it happened too often that no one else succeeded, and that the tale was left forever without a conclusion.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "Now and again, however, it chanced that even when he erred, the truth was still discovered.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "I have noted of some half-dozen cases of the kind, of which the Affair of the Second Stain and that which I am now about to recount are the two which present the strongest features of interest.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes was a man who seldom took exercise for exercise's sake.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "Few men were capable of greater muscular effort, and he was undoubtedly one of the finest boxers of his weight that I have ever seen; but he looked upon aimless bodily exertion as a waste of energy, and he seldom bestirred himself save when there was some professional object to be served.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "Then he was absolutely untiring and indefatigable.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "That he should have kept himself in training under such circumstances is remarkable, but his diet was usually of the sparest, and his habits were simple to the verge of austerity.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "Save for the occasional use of cocaine, he had no vices, and he only turned to the drug as a protest against the monotony of existence when cases were scanty and the papers uninteresting.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "One day in early spring he had so far relaxed as to go for a walk with me in the Park, where the first faint shoots of green were breaking out upon the elms, and the sticky spear-heads of the chestnuts were just beginning to burst into their five-fold leaves.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "For two hours we rambled about together, in silence for the most part, as befits two men who know each other intimately.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "It was nearly five before we were back in Baker Street once more.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "\\"Beg pardon, sir,\\" said our page-boy, as he opened the door.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "\\"There's been a gentleman here asking for you, sir.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "Holmes glanced reproachfully at me.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "\\"So much for afternoon walks!\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "said he.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"Has this gentleman gone, then?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "\\"Yes, sir.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "\\"Didn't you ask him in?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "\\"Yes, sir; he came in.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "\\"How long did he wait?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "\\"Half an hour, sir.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "He was a very restless gentleman, sir, a-walkin' and a-stampin' all the time he was here.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "I was waitin' outside the door, sir, and I could hear him.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "' Those were his very words, sir.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "'You'll only need to wait a little longer,' says I.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "'Then I'll wait in the open air, for I feel half choked,' says he.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "' And with that he ups and he outs, and all I could say wouldn't hold him back.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "'I'll be back before long.' And with that he ups and he outs, and all I could say wouldn't hold him back.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "\\"Well, well, you did your best,\\" said Holmes, as we walked into our room.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "\\"It's very annoying, though, Watson.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "I was badly in need of a case, and this looks, from the man's impatience, as if it were of importance.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "Halloa!", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "That's not your pipe on the table.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "A nice old briar with a good long stem of what the tobacconists call amber.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "I wonder how many real amber mouthpieces there are in London.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "Some people think that a fly in it is a sign.", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "Well, he must have been disturbed in his mind to leave a pipe behind him which he evidently values highly.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_1", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "\\"How do you know that he values it highly?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "\\"Well, I should put the original cost of the pipe at seven and sixpence.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "Now it has, you see, been twice mended, once in the wooden stem and once in the amber.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "Each of these mends, done, as you observe, with silver bands, must have cost more than the pipe did originally.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "The man must value the pipe highly when he prefers to patch it up rather than buy a new one with the same money.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "\\"Anything else?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "I asked, for Holmes was turning the pipe about in his hand, and staring at it in his peculiar pensive way.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "He held it up and tapped on it with his long, thin fore-finger, as a professor might who was lecturing on a bone.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "\\"Pipes are occasionally of extraordinary interest,\\" said he.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "\\"Nothing has more individuality, save perhaps watches and bootlaces.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "The indications here, however, are neither very marked nor very important.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "The owner is obviously a muscular man, left-handed, with an excellent set of teeth, careless in his habits, and with no need to practise economy.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "My friend threw out the information in a very offhand way, but I saw that he cocked his eye at me to see if I had followed his reasoning.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "\\"You think a man must be well-to-do if he smokes a seven-shilling pipe,\\" said I.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "\\"This is Grosvenor mixture at eightpence an ounce,\\" Holmes answered, knocking a little out on his palm.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "\\"As he might get an excellent smoke for half the price, he has no need to practise economy.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "\\"And the other points?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "\\"He has been in the habit of lighting his pipe at lamps and gas-jets.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "You can see that it is quite charred all down one side.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "Of course a match could not have done that.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "Why should a man hold a match to the side of his pipe?", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "But you cannot light it at a lamp without getting the bowl charred.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "And it is all on the right side of the pipe.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "From that I gather that he is a left-handed man.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "You hold your own pipe to the lamp, and see how naturally you, being right-handed, hold the left side to the flame.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "You might do it once the other way, but not as a constancy.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "This has always been held so.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "Then he has bitten through his amber.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "It takes a muscular, energetic fellow, and one with a good set of teeth, to do that.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "But if I am not mistaken I hear him upon the stair, so we shall have something more interesting than his pipe to study.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "An instant later our door opened, and a tall young man entered the room.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "He was well but quietly dressed in a dark-grey suit, and carried a brown wide-awake in his hand.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_19	section	\N	Section 19	18	{"wordCount": 157}
yellow-face	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "I should have put him at about thirty, though he was really some years older.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "\\"I beg your pardon,\\" said he, with some embarrassment; \\"I suppose I should have knocked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "Yes, of course I should have knocked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "The fact is that I am a little upset, and you must put it all down to that.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "He passed his hand over his forehead like a man who is half dazed, and then fell rather than sat down upon a chair.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "\\"I can see that you have not slept for a night or two,\\" said Holmes, in his easy, genial way.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "\\"That tries a man's nerves more than work, and more even than pleasure.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "May I ask how I can help you?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "\\"I wanted your advice, sir.", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "I don't know what to do and my whole life seems to have gone to pieces.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_2", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "\\"You wish to employ me as a consulting detective?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "\\"Not that only.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "I want your opinion as a judicious man—as a man of the world.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "I want to know what I ought to do next.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "I hope to God you'll be able to tell me.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "He spoke in little, sharp, jerky outbursts, and it seemed to me that to speak at all was very painful to him, and that his will all through was overriding his inclinations.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "\\"It's a very delicate thing,\\" said he.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "\\"One does not like to speak of one's domestic affairs to strangers.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "It seems dreadful to discuss the conduct of one's wife with two men whom I have never seen before.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "It's horrible to have to do it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "But I've got to the end of my tether, and I must have advice.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "\\"My dear Mr. Grant Munro—\\" began Holmes.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "Our visitor sprang from his chair.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "\\"What!\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "he cried, \\"you know my name?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "\\"If you wish to preserve your _incognito_,\\" said Holmes, smiling, \\"I would suggest that you cease to write your name upon the lining of your hat, or else that you turn the crown towards the person whom you are addressing.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "I was about to say that my friend and I have listened to a good many strange secrets in this room, and that we have had the good fortune to bring peace to many troubled souls.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "I trust that we may do as much for you.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "Might I beg you, as time may prove to be of importance, to furnish me with the facts of your case without further delay?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "Our visitor again passed his hand over his forehead, as if he found it bitterly hard.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "From every gesture and expression I could see that he was a reserved, self-contained man, with a dash of pride in his nature, more likely to hide his wounds than to expose them.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "Then suddenly, with a fierce gesture of his closed hand, like one who throws reserve to the winds, he began.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "\\"The facts are these, Mr. Holmes,\\" said he.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "\\"I am a married man, and have been so for three years.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "During that time my wife and I have loved each other as fondly and lived as happily as any two that ever were joined.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "We have not had a difference, not one, in thought or word or deed.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "earth for?' I asked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "And now, since last Monday, there has suddenly sprung up a barrier between us, and I find that there is something in her life and in her thought of which I know as little as if she were the woman who brushes by me in the street.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "We are estranged, and I want to know why.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "\\"Now there is one thing that I want to impress upon you before I go any further, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "Effie loves me.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "Don't let there be any mistake about that.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "She loves me with her whole heart and soul, and never more than now.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "I know it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "I feel it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "I don't want to argue about that.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "A man can tell easily enough when a woman loves him.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "But there's this secret between us, and we can never be the same until it is cleared.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "\\"Kindly let me have the facts, Mr. Munro,\\" said Holmes, with some impatience.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "\\"I'll tell you what I know about Effie's history.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "She was a widow when I met her first, though quite young—only twenty-five.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "Her name then was Mrs. Hebron.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "She went out to America when she was young, and lived in the town of Atlanta, where she married this Hebron, who was a lawyer with a good practice.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "They had one child, but the yellow fever broke out badly in the place, and both husband and child died of it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "I have seen his death certificate.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "This sickened her of America, and she came back to live with a maiden aunt at Pinner, in Middlesex.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "I may mention that her husband had left her comfortably off, and that she had a capital of about four thousand five hundred pounds, which had been so well invested by him that it returned an average of seven per cent.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "She had only been six months at Pinner when I met her; we fell in love with each other, and we married a few weeks afterwards.", "section": "yellow-face-section_3", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "\\"I am a hop merchant myself, and as I have an income of seven or eight hundred, we found ourselves comfortably off, and took a nice eighty-pound-a-year villa at Norbury.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "Our little place was very countrified, considering that it is so close to town.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "We had an inn and two houses a little above us, and a single cottage at the other side of the field which faces us, and except those there were no houses until you got half way to the station.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "My business took me into town at certain seasons, but in summer I had less to do, and then in our country home my wife and I were just as happy as could be wished.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "I tell you that there never was a shadow between us until this accursed affair began.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "\\"There's one thing I ought to tell you before I go further.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "When we married, my wife made over all her property to me—rather against my will, for I saw how awkward it would be if my business affairs went wrong.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "However, she would have it so, and it was done.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "Well, about six weeks ago she came to me.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "\\"'Jack,' said she, 'when you took my money you said that if ever I wanted any I was to ask you for it.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "\\"'Certainly,' said I.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "'It's all your own.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "\\"'Well,' said she, 'I want a hundred pounds.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "\\"I was a bit staggered at this, for I had imagined it was simply a new dress or something of the kind that she was after.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "\\"'Oh,' said she, in her playful way, 'you said that you were only my banker, and bankers never ask questions, you know.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "\\"'If you really mean it, of course you shall have the money,' said I.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "\\"'Oh, yes, I really mean it.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "\\"'And you won't tell me what you want it for?'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "\\"'Some day, perhaps, but not just at present, Jack.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "\\"So I had to be content with that, though it was the first time that there had ever been any secret between us.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "I gave her a check, and I never thought any more of the matter.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "It may have nothing to do with what came afterwards, but I thought it only right to mention it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "\\"Well, I told you just now that there is a cottage not far from our house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "There is just a field between us, but to reach it you have to go along the road and then turn down a lane.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "Just beyond it is a nice little grove of Scotch firs, and I used to be very fond of strolling down there, for trees are always a neighbourly kind of things.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "The cottage had been standing empty this eight months, and it was a pity, for it was a pretty two-storied place, with an old-fashioned porch and honeysuckle about it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "I have stood many a time and thought what a neat little homestead it would make.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "\\"Well, last Monday evening I was taking a stroll down that way, when I met an empty van coming up the lane, and saw a pile of carpets and things lying about on the grass-plot beside the porch.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "It was clear that the cottage had at last been let.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "I walked past it, and wondered what sort of folk they were who had come to live so near us.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "And as I looked I suddenly became aware that a face was watching me out of one of the upper windows.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "\\"I don't know what there was about that face, Mr. Holmes, but it seemed to send a chill right down my back.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "I was some little way off, so that I could not make out the features, but there was something unnatural and inhuman about the face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "That was the impression that I had, and I moved quickly forwards to get a nearer view of the person who was watching me.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "But as I did so the face suddenly disappeared, so suddenly that it seemed to have been plucked away into the darkness of the room.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "I stood for five minutes thinking the business over, and trying to analyze my impressions.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "I could not tell if the face were that of a man or a woman.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "It had been too far from me for that.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "But its colour was what had impressed me most.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "It was of a livid chalky white, and with something set and rigid about it which was shockingly unnatural.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "So disturbed was I that I determined to see a little more of the new inmates of the cottage.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "I approached and knocked at the door, which was instantly opened by a tall, gaunt woman with a harsh, forbidding face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_4", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "' she asked, in a Northern accent.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "ked, in a Northern accent.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "\\"'I am your neighbour over yonder,' said I, nodding towards my house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "'I see that you have only just moved in, so I thought that if I could be of any help to you in any—'", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "\\"'Ay, we'll just ask ye when we want ye,' said she, and shut the door in my face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "Annoyed at the churlish rebuff, I turned my back and walked home.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_20	section	\N	Section 20	19	{"wordCount": 309}
yellow-face	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "All evening, though I tried to think of other things, my mind would still turn to the apparition at the window and the rudeness of the woman.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "I determined to say nothing about the former to my wife, for she is a nervous, highly strung woman, and I had no wish that she would share the unpleasant impression which had been produced upon myself.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "I remarked to her, however, before I fell asleep, that the cottage was now occupied, to which she returned no reply.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "\\"I am usually an extremely sound sleeper.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "It has been a standing jest in the family that nothing could ever wake me during the night.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "And yet somehow on that particular night, whether it may have been the slight excitement produced by my little adventure or not I know not, but I slept much more lightly than usual.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "Half in my dreams I was dimly conscious that something was going on in the room, and gradually became aware that my wife had dressed herself and was slipping on her mantle and her bonnet.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "My lips were parted to murmur out some sleepy words of surprise or remonstrance at this untimely preparation, when suddenly my half-opened eyes fell upon her face, illuminated by the candle-light, and astonishment held me dumb.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "She wore an expression such as I had never seen before—such as I should have thought her incapable of assuming.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "She was deadly pale and breathing fast, glancing furtively towards the bed as she fastened her mantle, to see if she had disturbed me.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "Then, thinking that I was still asleep, she slipped noiselessly from the room, and an instant later I heard a sharp creaking which could only come from the hinges of the front door.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "I sat up in bed and rapped my knuckles against the rail to make certain that I was truly awake.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "Then I took my watch from under the pillow.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "It was three in the morning.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "What on this earth could my wife be doing out on the country road at three in the morning?", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "\\"I had sat for about twenty minutes turning the thing over in my mind and trying to find some possible explanation.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "The more I thought, the more extraordinary and inexplicable did it appear.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "I was still puzzling over it when I heard the door gently close again, and her footsteps coming up the stairs.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "' I asked as she entered.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "you been, Effie?' I asked as she entered.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "\\"She gave a violent start and a kind of gasping cry when I spoke, and that cry and start troubled me more than all the rest, for there was something indescribably guilty about them.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "My wife had always been a woman of a frank, open nature, and it gave me a chill to see her slinking into her own room, and crying out and wincing when her own husband spoke to her.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "' she cried, with a nervous laugh.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "h a nervous laugh. 'Why, I thought that nothing could awake you.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "' I asked, more sternly.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "I asked, more sternly.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "\\"'I don't wonder that you are surprised,' said she, and I could see that her fingers were trembling as she undid the fastenings of her mantle.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "'Why, I never remember having done such a thing in my life before.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "The fact is that I felt as though I were choking, and had a perfect longing for a breath of fresh air.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "I really think that I should have fainted if I had not gone out.", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "I stood at the door for a few minutes, and now I am quite myself again.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_5", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "\\"All the time that she was telling me this story she never once looked in my direction, and her voice was quite unlike her usual tones.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "It was evident to me that she was saying what was false.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "I said nothing in reply, but turned my face to the wall, sick at heart, with my mind filled with a thousand venomous doubts and suspicions.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "What was it that my wife was concealing from me?", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "Where had she been during that strange expedition?", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "I felt that I should have no peace until I knew, and yet I shrank from asking her again after once she had told me what was false.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "All the rest of the night I tossed and tumbled, framing theory after theory, each more unlikely than the last.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "\\"I should have gone to the City that day, but I was too disturbed in my mind to be able to pay attention to business matters.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "My wife seemed to be as upset as myself, and I could see from the little questioning glances which she kept shooting at me that she understood that I disbelieved her statement, and that she was at her wits' end what to do.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "We hardly exchanged a word during breakfast, and immediately afterwards I went out for a walk, that I might think the matter out in the fresh morning air.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "\\"I went as far as the Crystal Palace, spent an hour in the grounds, and was back in Norbury by one o'clock.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "It happened that my way took me past the cottage, and I stopped for an instant to look at the windows, and to see if I could catch a glimpse of the strange face which had looked out at me on the day before.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "As I stood there, imagine my surprise, Mr. Holmes, when the door suddenly opened and my wife walked out.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "\\"I was struck dumb with astonishment at the sight of her; but my emotions were nothing to those which showed themselves upon her face when our eyes met.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "She seemed for an instant to wish to shrink back inside the house again; and then, seeing how useless all concealment must be, she came forward, with a very white face and frightened eyes which belied the smile upon her lips.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "\\"'Ah, Jack,' she said, 'I have just been in to see if I can be of any assistance to our new neighbours.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "Why do you look at me like that, Jack?", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "You are not angry with me?'", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "\\"'So,' said I, 'this is where you went during the night.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "' she cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "u mean?' she cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "\\"'You came here.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "I am sure of it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "Who are these people, that you should visit them at such an hour?'", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "\\"'I have not been here before.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "' I cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "'Your very voice changes as you speak.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "When have I ever had a secret from you?", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "peak. When have I ever had a secret from you? I shall enter that cottage, and I shall probe the matter to the bottom.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "' she gasped, in uncontrollable emotion.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "Then, as I approached the door, she seized my sleeve and pulled me back with convulsive strength.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "back with convulsive strength.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "\\"'I implore you not to do this, Jack,' she cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "' Then, as I tried to shake her off, she clung to me in a frenzy of entreaty.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "come of it if you enter that cottage.' Then, as I tried to shake her off, she clung to me in a frenzy of entreaty.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "' she cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "\\"Your child?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "'Trust me only this once.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "You will never have cause to regret it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "You know that I would not have a secret from you if it were not for your own sake.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "Our whole lives are at stake in this.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "If you come home with me, all will be well.", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "all will be well. If you force your way into that cottage, all is over between us.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_6", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "\\"There was such earnestness, such despair, in her manner that her words arrested me, and I stood irresolute before the door.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "\\"'I will trust you on one condition, and on one condition only,' said I at last.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "'It is that this mystery comes to an end from now.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "You are at liberty to preserve your secret, but you must promise me that there shall be no more nightly visits, no more doings which are kept from my knowledge.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "I am willing to forget those which are passed if you will promise that there shall be no more in the future.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "\\"'I was sure that you would trust me,' she cried, with a great sigh of relief.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "'It shall be just as you wish.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "Come away—oh, come away up to the house.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "\\"Still pulling at my sleeve, she led me away from the cottage.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "As we went I glanced back, and there was that yellow livid face watching us out of the upper window.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "What link could there be between that creature and my wife?", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "Or how could the coarse, rough woman whom I had seen the day before be connected with her?", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "It was a strange puzzle, and yet I knew that my mind could never know ease again until I had solved it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "\\"For two days after this I stayed at home, and my wife appeared to abide loyally by our engagement, for, as far as I know, she never stirred out of the house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "On the third day, however, I had ample evidence that her solemn promise was not enough to hold her back from this secret influence which drew her away from her husband and her duty.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "36, which is my usual train.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "As I entered the house the maid ran into the hall with a startled face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "train. As I entered the house the maid ran into the hall with a startled face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "your mistress?' I asked.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "\\"'I think that she has gone out for a walk,' she answered.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "\\"My mind was instantly filled with suspicion.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "I rushed upstairs to make sure that she was not in the house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "As I did so I happened to glance out of one of the upper windows, and saw the maid with whom I had just been speaking running across the field in the direction of the cottage.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "Then of course I saw exactly what it all meant.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "My wife had gone over there, and had asked the servant to call her if I should return.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "Tingling with anger, I rushed down and hurried across, determined to end the matter once and forever.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "I saw my wife and the maid hurrying back along the lane, but I did not stop to speak with them.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "In the cottage lay the secret which was casting a shadow over my life.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "I vowed that, come what might, it should be a secret no longer.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "I did not even knock when I reached it, but turned the handle and rushed into the passage.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "\\"It was all still and quiet upon the ground floor.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "In the kitchen a kettle was singing on the fire, and a large black cat lay coiled up in the basket; but there was no sign of the woman whom I had seen before.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "I ran into the other room, but it was equally deserted.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "Then I rushed up the stairs, only to find two other rooms empty and deserted at the top.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "There was no one at all in the whole house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "The furniture and pictures were of the most common and vulgar description, save in the one chamber at the window of which I had seen the strange face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "That was comfortable and elegant, and all my suspicions rose into a fierce bitter flame when I saw that on the mantelpiece stood a copy of a full-length photograph of my wife, which had been taken at my request only three months ago.", "section": "yellow-face-section_7", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "\\"I stayed long enough to make certain that the house was absolutely empty.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "Then I left it, feeling a weight at my heart such as I had never had before.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "My wife came out into the hall as I entered my house; but I was too hurt and angry to speak with her, and pushing past her, I made my way into my study.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "She followed me, however, before I could close the door.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "\\"'I am sorry that I broke my promise, Jack,' said she; 'but if you knew all the circumstances I am sure that you would forgive me.'", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "\\"'Tell me everything, then,' said I.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "\\"'I cannot, Jack, I cannot,' she cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "\\"'Until you tell me who it is that has been living in that cottage, and who it is to whom you have given that photograph, there can never be any confidence between us,' said I, and breaking away from her, I left the house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "That was yesterday, Mr. Holmes, and I have not seen her since, nor do I know anything more about this strange business.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "It is the first shadow that has come between us, and it has so shaken me that I do not know what I should do for the best.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "Suddenly this morning it occurred to me that you were the man to advise me, so I have hurried to you now, and I place myself unreservedly in your hands.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "If there is any point which I have not made clear, pray question me about it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "But, above all, tell me quickly what I am to do, for this misery is more than I can bear.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "Holmes and I had listened with the utmost interest to this extraordinary statement, which had been delivered in the jerky, broken fashion of a man who is under the influence of extreme emotions.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "My companion sat silent for some time, with his chin upon his hand, lost in thought.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "\\"Tell me,\\" said he at last, \\"could you swear that this was a man's face which you saw at the window?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "\\"Each time that I saw it I was some distance away from it, so that it is impossible for me to say.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "\\"You appear, however, to have been disagreeably impressed by it.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "\\"It seemed to be of an unnatural colour, and to have a strange rigidity about the features.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "When I approached, it vanished with a jerk.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "\\"How long is it since your wife asked you for a hundred pounds?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "\\"Nearly two months.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "\\"Have you ever seen a photograph of her first husband?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "\\"No; there was a great fire at Atlanta very shortly after his death, and all her papers were destroyed.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "\\"And yet she had a certificate of death.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_21	section	\N	Section 21	20	{"wordCount": 197}
yellow-face	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "You say that you saw it.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "\\"Yes; she got a duplicate after the fire.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "\\"Did you ever meet any one who knew her in America?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "\\"Did she ever talk of revisiting the place?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "\\"Or get letters from it?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "\\"Thank you.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "I should like to think over the matter a little now.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "If the cottage is now permanently deserted we may have some difficulty.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "If, on the other hand, as I fancy is more likely, the inmates were warned of your coming, and left before you entered yesterday, then they may be back now, and we should clear it all up easily.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "Let me advise you, then, to return to Norbury, and to examine the windows of the cottage again.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "If you have reason to believe that it is inhabited, do not force your way in, but send a wire to my friend and me.", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "We shall be with you within an hour of receiving it, and we shall then very soon get to the bottom of the business.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_8", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "\\"And if it is still empty?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "\\"In that case I shall come out to-morrow and talk it over with you.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "Good-by; and, above all, do not fret until you know that you really have a cause for it.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "\\"I am afraid that this is a bad business, Watson,\\" said my companion, as he returned after accompanying Mr. Grant Munro to the door.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "\\"What do you make of it?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "\\"It had an ugly sound,\\" I answered.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "\\"Yes.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "There's blackmail in it, or I am much mistaken.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "\\"And who is the blackmailer?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "\\"Well, it must be the creature who lives in the only comfortable room in the place, and has her photograph above his fireplace.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "Upon my word, Watson, there is something very attractive about that livid face at the window, and I would not have missed the case for worlds.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "\\"You have a theory?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "\\"Yes, a provisional one.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "But I shall be surprised if it does not turn out to be correct.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "This woman's first husband is in that cottage.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "\\"Why do you think so?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "\\"How else can we explain her frenzied anxiety that her second one should not enter it?", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "The facts, as I read them, are something like this: This woman was married in America.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "Her husband developed some hateful qualities; or shall we say that he contracted some loathsome disease, and became a leper or an imbecile?", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "She flies from him at last, returns to England, changes her name, and starts her life, as she thinks, afresh.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "She has been married three years, and believes that her position is quite secure, having shown her husband the death certificate of some man whose name she has assumed, when suddenly her whereabouts is discovered by her first husband; or, we may suppose, by some unscrupulous woman who has attached herself to the invalid.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "They write to the wife, and threaten to come and expose her.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_22	section	\N	Section 22	21	{"wordCount": 196}
yellow-face	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "She asks for a hundred pounds, and endeavours to buy them off.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "They come in spite of it, and when the husband mentions casually to the wife that there are new-comers in the cottage, she knows in some way that they are her pursuers.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "She waits until her husband is asleep, and then she rushes down to endeavour to persuade them to leave her in peace.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "Having no success, she goes again next morning, and her husband meets her, as he has told us, as she comes out.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "She promises him then not to go there again, but two days afterwards the hope of getting rid of those dreadful neighbours was too strong for her, and she made another attempt, taking down with her the photograph which had probably been demanded from her.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "In the midst of this interview the maid rushed in to say that the master had come home, on which the wife, knowing that he would come straight down to the cottage, hurried the inmates out at the back door, into the grove of fir-trees, probably, which was mentioned as standing near.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "In this way he found the place deserted.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "I shall be very much surprised, however, if it is still so when he reconnoitres it this evening.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "What do you think of my theory?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "\\"It is all surmise.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "\\"But at least it covers all the facts.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "When new facts come to our knowledge which cannot be covered by it, it will be time enough to reconsider it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "We can do nothing more until we have a message from our friend at Norbury.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "But we had not a very long time to wait for that.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "It came just as we had finished our tea.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "\\"The cottage is still tenanted,\\" it said.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "\\"Have seen the face again at the window.", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "Will meet the seven o'clock train, and will take no steps until you arrive.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_9", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "He was waiting on the platform when we stepped out, and we could see in the light of the station lamps that he was very pale, and quivering with agitation.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "\\"They are still there, Mr. Holmes,\\" said he, laying his hand hard upon my friend's sleeve.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "\\"I saw lights in the cottage as I came down.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "We shall settle it now once and for all.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "\\"What is your plan, then?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "asked Holmes, as he walked down the dark tree-lined road.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "\\"I am going to force my way in and see for myself who is in the house.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "I wish you both to be there as witnesses.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "\\"You are quite determined to do this, in spite of your wife's warning that it is better that you should not solve the mystery?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "\\"Yes, I am determined.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "\\"Well, I think that you are in the right.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "Any truth is better than indefinite doubt.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "We had better go up at once.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "Of course, legally, we are putting ourselves hopelessly in the wrong; but I think that it is worth it.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "It was a very dark night, and a thin rain began to fall as we turned from the high road into a narrow lane, deeply rutted, with hedges on either side.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "Mr. Grant Munro pushed impatiently forward, however, and we stumbled after him as best we could.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "\\"There are the lights of my house,\\" he murmured, pointing to a glimmer among the trees.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_23	section	\N	Section 23	22	{"wordCount": 153}
yellow-face	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "\\"And here is the cottage which I am going to enter.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "We turned a corner in the lane as he spoke, and there was the building close beside us.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "A yellow bar falling across the black foreground showed that the door was not quite closed, and one window in the upper story was brightly illuminated.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "As we looked, we saw a dark blur moving across the blind.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "\\"There is that creature!\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "cried Grant Munro.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "\\"You can see for yourselves that some one is there.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "Now follow me, and we shall soon know all.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "We approached the door; but suddenly a woman appeared out of the shadow and stood in the golden track of the lamp-light.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "I could not see her face in the darkness, but her arms were thrown out in an attitude of entreaty.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "\\"For God's sake, don't Jack!\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "she cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "\\"I had a presentiment that you would come this evening.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "Think better of it, dear!", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "Trust me again, and you will never have cause to regret it.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "\\"I have trusted you too long, Effie,\\" he cried, sternly.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "\\"Leave go of me!", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "I must pass you.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "My friends and I are going to settle this matter once and forever!\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "He pushed her to one side, and we followed closely after him.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "As he threw the door open an old woman ran out in front of him and tried to bar his passage, but he thrust her back, and an instant afterwards we were all upon the stairs.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "Grant Munro rushed into the lighted room at the top, and we entered at his heels.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "It was a cosey, well-furnished apartment, with two candles burning upon the table and two upon the mantelpiece.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "In the corner, stooping over a desk, there sat what appeared to be a little girl.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "Her face was turned away as we entered, but we could see that she was dressed in a red frock, and that she had long white gloves on.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "As she whisked round to us, I gave a cry of surprise and horror.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "The face which she turned towards us was of the strangest livid tint, and the features were absolutely devoid of any expression.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "An instant later the mystery was explained.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "Holmes, with a laugh, passed his hand behind the child's ear, a mask peeled off from her countenance, and there was a little coal black negress, with all her white teeth flashing in amusement at our amazed faces.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "I burst out laughing, out of sympathy with her merriment; but Grant Munro stood staring, with his hand clutching his throat.", "section": "yellow-face-section_10", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "\\"My God!\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "\\"What can be the meaning of this?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "\\"I will tell you the meaning of it,\\" cried the lady, sweeping into the room with a proud, set face.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "\\"You have forced me, against my own judgment, to tell you, and now we must both make the best of it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "My husband died at Atlanta.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "My child survived.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_24	section	\N	Section 24	23	{"wordCount": 177}
yellow-face	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "She drew a large silver locket from her bosom.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "\\"You have never seen this open.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "\\"I understood that it did not open.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "She touched a spring, and the front hinged back.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "There was a portrait within of a man strikingly handsome and intelligent-looking, but bearing unmistakable signs upon his features of his African descent.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "\\"That is John Hebron, of Atlanta,\\" said the lady, \\"and a nobler man never walked the earth.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "I cut myself off from my race in order to wed him, but never once while he lived did I for an instant regret it.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "It was our misfortune that our only child took after his people rather than mine.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "It is often so in such matches, and little Lucy is darker far than ever her father was.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "But dark or fair, she is my own dear little girlie, and her mother's pet.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "The little creature ran across at the words and nestled up against the lady's dress.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "\\"When I left her in America,\\" she continued, \\"it was only because her health was weak, and the change might have done her harm.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "She was given to the care of a faithful Scotch woman who had once been our servant.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "Never for an instant did I dream of disowning her as my child.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "But when chance threw you in my way, Jack, and I learned to love you, I feared to tell you about my child.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "God forgive me, I feared that I should lose you, and I had not the courage to tell you.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "I had to choose between you, and in my weakness I turned away from my own little girl.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "For three years I have kept her existence a secret from you, but I heard from the nurse, and I knew that all was well with her.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "At last, however, there came an overwhelming desire to see the child once more.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "I struggled against it, but in vain.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "Though I knew the danger, I determined to have the child over, if it were but for a few weeks.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "I sent a hundred pounds to the nurse, and I gave her instructions about this cottage, so that she might come as a neighbour, without my appearing to be in any way connected with her.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "I pushed my precautions so far as to order her to keep the child in the house during the daytime, and to cover up her little face and hands so that even those who might see her at the window should not gossip about there being a black child in the neighbourhood.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "If I had been less cautious I might have been more wise, but I was half crazy with fear that you should learn the truth.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "\\"It was you who told me first that the cottage was occupied.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "I should have waited for the morning, but I could not sleep for excitement, and so at last I slipped out, knowing how difficult it is to awake you.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "But you saw me go, and that was the beginning of my troubles.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "Next day you had my secret at your mercy, but you nobly refrained from pursuing your advantage.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "Three days later, however, the nurse and child only just escaped from the back door as you rushed in at the front one.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "And now to-night you at last know all, and I ask you what is to become of us, my child and me?\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "She clasped her hands and waited for an answer.", "section": "yellow-face-section_11", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "It was a long ten minutes before Grant Munro broke the silence, and when his answer came it was one of which I love to think.", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "He lifted the little child, kissed her, and then, still carrying her, he held his other hand out to his wife and turned towards the door.", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "\\"We can talk it over more comfortably at home,\\" said he.", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "\\"I am not a very good man, Effie, but I think that I am a better one than you have given me credit for being.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "Holmes and I followed them down the lane, and my friend plucked at my sleeve as we came out.", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "\\"I think,\\" said he, \\"that we shall be of more use in London than in Norbury.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "Not another word did he say of the case until late that night, when he was turning away, with his lighted candle, for his bedroom.", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
yellow-face	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "\\"Watson,\\" said he, \\"if it should ever strike you that I am getting a little over-confident in my powers, or giving less pains to a case than it deserves, kindly whisper 'Norbury' in my ear, and I shall be infinitely obliged to you.\\"", "section": "yellow-face-section_12", "entities": []}
