yellow-face	event_1_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson walk in the Park	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_12", "sentence_13"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_1_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson return to Baker Street	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_14"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_1_3	event	\N	The page-boy tells Holmes that a gentleman has asked for him	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": "page_boy", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_15", "sentence_16"], "communicatesContent": "There's been a gentleman here asking for you, sir."}
yellow-face	event_1_4	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the gentleman has gone	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_20", "sentence_21"], "communicatesContent": "Has this gentleman gone, then?"}
yellow-face	event_1_5	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the gentleman was invited in	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_22", "sentence_23"], "communicatesContent": "Didn't you ask him in?"}
yellow-face	event_1_6	event	\N	The page-boy explains that the gentleman waited half an hour and then left	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": "page_boy", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_24", "sentence_32"], "communicatesContent": "Half an hour, sir. He was a very restless gentleman, sir, a-walkin' and a-stampin' all the time he was here. I was waitin' outside the door, sir, and I could hear him. ' Those were his very words, sir. 'You'll only need to wait a little longer,' says I. 'Then I'll wait in the open air, for I feel half choked,' says he. ' And with that he ups and he outs, and all I could say wouldn't hold him back. 'I'll be back before long.' And with that he ups and he outs, and all I could say wouldn't hold him back."}
yellow-face	event_1_7	event	\N	Holmes notices the left-behind pipe on the table	0	{"section": "yellow-face-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_33", "sentence_42"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_2_1	event	\N	Watson asks how Holmes knows the man values the pipe highly	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_43", "sentence_44"], "communicatesContent": "How do you know that he values it highly?"}
yellow-face	event_2_2	event	\N	Holmes explains the pipe's cost, repairs, and the owner's valuation	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_45", "sentence_46", "sentence_47", "sentence_48"], "communicatesContent": "I should put the original cost of the pipe at seven and sixpence. Now it has been twice mended, once in the wooden stem and once in the amber. Each of these mends, done with silver bands, must have cost more than the pipe did originally. The man must value the pipe highly when he prefers to patch it up rather than buy a new one with the same money."}
yellow-face	event_2_3	event	\N	Watson asks whether Holmes has anything else to add	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_49", "sentence_50"], "communicatesContent": "Anything else?"}
yellow-face	event_2_4	event	\N	Holmes studies and taps the pipe	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_50", "sentence_51"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_2_5	event	\N	Holmes comments that pipes are individually interesting	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_52", "sentence_53", "sentence_54"], "communicatesContent": "Pipes are occasionally of extraordinary interest. Nothing has more individuality, save perhaps watches and bootlaces. The indications here, however, are neither very marked nor very important."}
yellow-face	event_2_6	event	\N	Holmes describes the pipe owner as muscular, left-handed, with good teeth, careless habits, and no need for economy	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_55", "sentence_56"], "communicatesContent": "The owner is obviously a muscular man, left-handed, with an excellent set of teeth, careless in his habits, and with no need to practise economy."}
yellow-face	event_2_7	event	\N	Watson infers that Holmes means the man is well-to-do	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_57"], "communicatesContent": "You think a man must be well-to-do if he smokes a seven-shilling pipe."}
yellow-face	event_2_8	event	\N	Holmes identifies the tobacco mixture and price	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_58"], "communicatesContent": "This is Grosvenor mixture at eightpence an ounce."}
yellow-face	event_2_9	event	\N	Holmes explains the man has no need to be economical	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_58", "sentence_59"], "communicatesContent": "As he might get an excellent smoke for half the price, he has no need to practise economy."}
yellow-face	event_2_10	event	\N	Watson asks about the other points	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_60"], "communicatesContent": "And the other points?"}
yellow-face	event_5_6	event	\N	Watson tells his wife that the cottage is occupied	4	{"section": "yellow-face-section_5", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_185"], "communicatesContent": "the cottage was now occupied"}
yellow-face	event_2_11	event	\N	Holmes explains how the pipe was lit and why the bowl is charred	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_61", "sentence_62", "sentence_63", "sentence_64", "sentence_65", "sentence_66", "sentence_67", "sentence_68", "sentence_69", "sentence_70"], "communicatesContent": "He has been in the habit of lighting his pipe at lamps and gas-jets. You can see that it is quite charred all down one side. Of course a match could not have done that. Why should a man hold a match to the side of his pipe? But you cannot light it at a lamp without getting the bowl charred. And it is all on the right side of the pipe. From that I gather that he is a left-handed man. You hold your own pipe to the lamp, and see how naturally you, being right-handed, hold the left side to the flame. You might do it once the other way, but not as a constancy. This has always been held so."}
yellow-face	event_2_12	event	\N	Holmes says the man has bitten through the amber and is muscular and strong-toothed	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_71", "sentence_72"], "communicatesContent": "Then he has bitten through his amber. It takes a muscular, energetic fellow, and one with a good set of teeth, to do that."}
yellow-face	event_2_13	event	\N	Holmes hears someone on the stair and expects a more interesting subject than the pipe	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_73"], "communicatesContent": "I hear him upon the stair, so we shall have something more interesting than his pipe to study."}
yellow-face	event_2_14	event	\N	A tall young man enters the room	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_74", "sentence_75", "sentence_76"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_2_15	event	\N	The visitor apologizes for not knocking and says he is upset	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "gentleman_visitor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_77", "sentence_78", "sentence_79"], "communicatesContent": "I beg your pardon. I suppose I should have knocked. Yes, of course I should have knocked. The fact is that I am a little upset, and you must put it all down to that."}
yellow-face	event_2_16	event	\N	The visitor sits down in a dazed way	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_80"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_2_17	event	\N	Holmes remarks that the visitor has not slept for a night or two and invites him to explain his trouble	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_81", "sentence_82", "sentence_83"], "communicatesContent": "I can see that you have not slept for a night or two. That tries a man's nerves more than work, and more even than pleasure. May I ask how I can help you?"}
yellow-face	event_2_18	event	\N	The visitor says he wants advice and that his life has gone to pieces	1	{"section": "yellow-face-section_2", "speakerId": "gentleman_visitor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_84", "sentence_85"], "communicatesContent": "I wanted your advice, sir. I don't know what to do and my whole life seems to have gone to pieces."}
yellow-face	event_3_1	event	\N	Grant Munro asks Holmes whether Holmes wishes to employ him as a consulting detective	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_86"], "communicatesContent": "You wish to employ me as a consulting detective?"}
yellow-face	event_3_2	event	\N	Grant Munro asks Holmes for his opinion and advice about what he ought to do next	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_88", "sentence_89", "sentence_90"], "communicatesContent": "I want your opinion as a judicious man—as a man of the world. I want to know what I ought to do next. I hope to God you'll be able to tell me."}
yellow-face	event_3_3	event	\N	Grant Munro speaks in painful, jerky outbursts	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_91"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_3_4	event	\N	Grant Munro states that the matter is delicate and that he must have advice	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_92", "sentence_93", "sentence_94", "sentence_95", "sentence_96"], "communicatesContent": "It's a very delicate thing. One does not like to speak of one's domestic affairs to strangers. It seems dreadful to discuss the conduct of one's wife with two men whom I have never seen before. It's horrible to have to do it. But I've got to the end of my tether, and I must have advice."}
yellow-face	event_3_5	event	\N	Holmes addresses Grant Munro by name	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_97"], "communicatesContent": "My dear Mr. Grant Munro—"}
yellow-face	event_3_6	event	\N	Grant Munro rises from his chair in surprise	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_98", "sentence_99", "sentence_100"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_3_7	event	\N	Holmes explains how he identified Grant Munro's name from the hat lining	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_101", "sentence_102", "sentence_103", "sentence_104"], "communicatesContent": "If you wish to preserve your incognito, I would suggest that you cease to write your name upon the lining of your hat, or else that you turn the crown towards the person whom you are addressing. I was about to say that my friend and I have listened to a good many strange secrets in this room, and that we have had the good fortune to bring peace to many troubled souls. I trust that we may do as much for you. Might I beg you, as time may prove to be of importance, to furnish me with the facts of your case without further delay?"}
yellow-face	event_3_8	event	\N	Grant Munro passes his hand over his forehead	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_105"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_3_9	event	\N	The narrator observes Grant Munro's reserved and proud manner	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_106"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_3_10	event	\N	Grant Munro begins to explain his case	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_107", "sentence_108"], "communicatesContent": "The facts are these, Mr. Holmes."}
yellow-face	event_3_11	event	\N	Grant Munro states that he has been married for three years	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_109"], "communicatesContent": "I am a married man, and have been so for three years."}
yellow-face	event_5_7	event	\N	Watson wakes lightly during the night and notices his wife dressing	4	{"section": "yellow-face-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_188", "sentence_189"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_3_12	event	\N	Grant Munro states that he and Effie have loved each other and lived happily for three years	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_110", "sentence_111"], "communicatesContent": "During that time my wife and I have loved each other as fondly and lived as happily as any two that ever were joined. We have not had a difference, not one, in thought or word or deed."}
yellow-face	event_3_13	event	\N	Grant Munro states that a barrier has arisen between him and Effie since last Monday	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_112", "sentence_113"], "communicatesContent": "And now, since last Monday, there has suddenly sprung up a barrier between us, and I find that there is something in her life and in her thought of which I know as little as if she were the woman who brushes by me in the street. We are estranged, and I want to know why."}
yellow-face	event_3_14	event	\N	Grant Munro emphasizes that Effie loves him and that a secret exists between them	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_114", "sentence_115", "sentence_116", "sentence_117", "sentence_118", "sentence_119", "sentence_120", "sentence_121", "sentence_122"], "communicatesContent": "Now there is one thing that I want to impress upon you before I go any further, Mr. Holmes. Effie loves me. Don't let there be any mistake about that. She loves me with her whole heart and soul, and never more than now. I know it. I feel it. I don't want to argue about that. A man can tell easily enough when a woman loves him. But there's this secret between us, and we can never be the same until it is cleared."}
yellow-face	event_3_15	event	\N	Holmes asks Grant Munro to give the facts	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_123"], "communicatesContent": "Kindly let me have the facts, Mr. Munro."}
yellow-face	event_3_16	event	\N	Grant Munro recounts Effie's history in America and in England	2	{"section": "yellow-face-section_3", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_124", "sentence_125", "sentence_126", "sentence_127", "sentence_128", "sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_131", "sentence_132"], "communicatesContent": "I'll tell you what I know about Effie's history. She was a widow when I met her first, though quite young—only twenty-five. Her name then was Mrs. Hebron. She went out to America when she was young, and lived in the town of Atlanta, where she married this Hebron, who was a lawyer with a good practice. They had one child, but the yellow fever broke out badly in the place, and both husband and child died of it. I have seen his death certificate. This sickened her of America, and she came back to live with a maiden aunt at Pinner, in Middlesex. I may mention that her husband had left her comfortably off, and that she had a capital of about four thousand five hundred pounds, which had been so well invested by him that it returned an average of seven per cent. She had only been six months at Pinner when I met her; we fell in love with each other, and we married a few weeks afterwards."}
