yellow-face	event_5_13	event	\N	Watson asks his wife where she has been	4	{"section": "yellow-face-section_5", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_201", "sentence_202"], "communicatesContent": "Where have you been, Effie?"}
yellow-face	event_5_14	event	\N	Watson's wife starts and cries out when he speaks	4	{"section": "yellow-face-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_203", "sentence_204"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_5_15	event	\N	Watson's wife says she thought he would not wake and explains why she went out	4	{"section": "yellow-face-section_5", "speakerId": "jack_wife", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_205", "sentence_206", "sentence_207", "sentence_208", "sentence_209", "sentence_210", "sentence_211", "sentence_212", "sentence_213"], "communicatesContent": "I thought that nothing could awake you. I don't wonder that you are surprised. Why, I never remember having done such a thing in my life before. The fact is that I felt as though I were choking, and had a perfect longing for a breath of fresh air. I really think that I should have fainted if I had not gone out. I stood at the door for a few minutes, and now I am quite myself again."}
yellow-face	event_6_1	event	\N	Jack's wife tells Jack she has been helping the new neighbours	5	{"section": "yellow-face-section_6", "speakerId": "jack_wife", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_229", "sentence_230", "sentence_231"], "communicatesContent": "I have just been in to see if I can be of any assistance to our new neighbours. Why do you look at me like that, Jack? You are not angry with me?"}
yellow-face	event_6_2	event	\N	Jack accuses his wife of having gone to the cottage during the night	5	{"section": "yellow-face-section_6", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_232", "sentence_235", "sentence_236", "sentence_237"], "communicatesContent": "So, this is where you went during the night. You came here. I am sure of it. Who are these people, that you should visit them at such an hour?"}
yellow-face	event_6_3	event	\N	Jack's wife denies having been there before	5	{"section": "yellow-face-section_6", "speakerId": "jack_wife", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_238", "sentence_239"], "communicatesContent": "I have not been here before."}
yellow-face	event_6_4	event	\N	Jack insists on entering the cottage and probing the matter	5	{"section": "yellow-face-section_6", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_240", "sentence_241", "sentence_242"], "communicatesContent": "Your very voice changes as you speak. When have I ever had a secret from you? I shall enter that cottage, and I shall probe the matter to the bottom."}
yellow-face	event_6_5	event	\N	Jack's wife seizes Jack's sleeve and pulls him back from the cottage door	5	{"section": "yellow-face-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_244", "sentence_245"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_6_6	event	\N	Jack's wife pleads with Jack not to enter the cottage	5	{"section": "yellow-face-section_6", "speakerId": "jack_wife", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_246", "sentence_247", "sentence_248", "sentence_249", "sentence_250", "sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253", "sentence_254", "sentence_255"], "communicatesContent": "I implore you not to do this, Jack. Then, as I tried to shake her off, she clung to me in a frenzy of entreaty. Trust me only this once. You will never have cause to regret it. You know that I would not have a secret from you if it were not for your own sake. Our whole lives are at stake in this. If you come home with me, all will be well. If you force your way into that cottage, all is over between us."}
yellow-face	event_7_1	event	\N	The speaker makes a conditional promise to end the mystery and its secret visits	6	{"section": "yellow-face-section_7", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_257", "sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260"], "communicatesContent": "I will trust you on one condition, and on one condition only. It is that this mystery comes to an end from now. You are at liberty to preserve your secret, but you must promise me that there shall be no more nightly visits, no more doings which are kept from my knowledge. I am willing to forget those which are passed if you will promise that there shall be no more in the future."}
yellow-face	event_7_2	event	\N	Jack's wife agrees to the condition and invites him back to the house	6	{"section": "yellow-face-section_7", "speakerId": "jack_wife", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_261", "sentence_262", "sentence_263"], "communicatesContent": "I was sure that you would trust me. It shall be just as you wish. Come away—oh, come away up to the house."}
yellow-face	event_7_3	event	\N	Jack and his wife leave the cottage	6	{"section": "yellow-face-section_7", "speakerId": "jack_wife", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_264", "sentence_265"], "communicatesContent": "Come away—oh, come away up to the house."}
yellow-face	event_7_4	event	\N	Jack remains at home for two days	6	{"section": "yellow-face-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_269"], "communicatesContent": null}
