yellow-face	event_8_28	event	\N	Jack says no	7	{"section": "yellow-face-section_8", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_326"], "communicatesContent": "No."}
yellow-face	event_8_29	event	\N	Holmes says he will think over the matter and advises Jack to return to Norbury and examine the cottage windows again	7	{"section": "yellow-face-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_327", "sentence_328", "sentence_329", "sentence_330", "sentence_331", "sentence_332", "sentence_333"], "communicatesContent": "Thank you. I should like to think over the matter a little now. If the cottage is now permanently deserted we may have some difficulty. If, on the other hand, as I fancy is more likely, the inmates were warned of your coming, and left before you entered yesterday, then they may be back now, and we should clear it all up easily. Let me advise you, then, to return to Norbury, and to examine the windows of the cottage again. If you have reason to believe that it is inhabited, do not force your way in, but send a wire to my friend and me. We shall be with you within an hour of receiving it, and we shall then very soon get to the bottom of the business."}
yellow-face	event_9_1	event	\N	Holmes accompanies Grant Munro to the door and speaks about the case	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_9_2	event	\N	Holmes states that the matter is a bad business and likely involves blackmail	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_341"], "communicatesContent": "I am afraid that this is a bad business, Watson. There's blackmail in it, or I am much mistaken."}
yellow-face	event_9_3	event	\N	Holmes identifies the blackmailer as the creature in the comfortable room with the photograph above the fireplace	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_342", "sentence_343"], "communicatesContent": "It must be the creature who lives in the only comfortable room in the place, and has her photograph above his fireplace."}
yellow-face	event_9_4	event	\N	Holmes presents a provisional theory about the woman in the cottage	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_345", "sentence_367"], "communicatesContent": "I have a provisional theory about the case."}
yellow-face	event_9_5	event	\N	Holmes explains that the woman's first husband is in the cottage	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_348", "sentence_350", "sentence_351", "sentence_352", "sentence_353", "sentence_354", "sentence_355", "sentence_356", "sentence_357", "sentence_358", "sentence_359", "sentence_360", "sentence_361", "sentence_362", "sentence_363"], "communicatesContent": "This woman's first husband is in that cottage."}
yellow-face	event_9_6	event	\N	Holmes recounts the woman's flight, remarriage, exposure threat, and attempts to drive the pursuers away	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_351", "sentence_352", "sentence_353", "sentence_354", "sentence_355", "sentence_356", "sentence_357", "sentence_358", "sentence_359", "sentence_360", "sentence_361", "sentence_362", "sentence_363"], "communicatesContent": "The woman married in America, fled from her husband, returned to England under another name, later showed her second husband a death certificate, was threatened by her pursuers, offered them a hundred pounds, and repeatedly tried to make them leave her in peace."}
yellow-face	event_9_7	event	\N	Holmes says the maid rushed in and the wife hurried the inmates out of the cottage	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_361", "sentence_362"], "communicatesContent": "The maid rushed in to say that the master had come home, and the wife hurried the inmates out at the back door into the grove of fir-trees."}
yellow-face	event_9_8	event	\N	A message from the friend at Norbury arrives after tea	8	{"section": "yellow-face-section_9", "speakerId": "norbury_friend", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_369", "sentence_370", "sentence_371", "sentence_372", "sentence_373"], "communicatesContent": "The cottage is still tenanted. Have seen the face again at the window. Will meet the seven o'clock train, and will take no steps until you arrive."}
yellow-face	event_10_1	event	\N	Grant Munro waits on the platform pale and agitated	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_374"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_10_2	event	\N	Grant Munro says the people are still in the house and that he saw lights in the cottage	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_375", "sentence_376", "sentence_377"], "communicatesContent": "They are still there, Mr. Holmes. I saw lights in the cottage as I came down. We shall settle it now once and for all."}
yellow-face	event_10_3	event	\N	Holmes asks Grant Munro's plan	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_378", "sentence_379"], "communicatesContent": "What is your plan, then?"}
yellow-face	event_10_4	event	\N	Grant Munro says he is going to force his way into the house and wants Holmes and Watson as witnesses	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_380", "sentence_381"], "communicatesContent": "I am going to force my way in and see for myself who is in the house. I wish you both to be there as witnesses."}
a-case-of-identity	section_26	section	\N	Section 26	25	{"wordCount": 202}
yellow-face	event_10_5	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Grant Munro is determined to act despite his wife's warning	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_382"], "communicatesContent": "You are quite determined to do this, in spite of your wife's warning that it is better that you should not solve the mystery?"}
yellow-face	event_10_6	event	\N	Grant Munro says he is determined	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_383"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, I am determined."}
yellow-face	event_10_7	event	\N	Holmes agrees that truth is better than doubt and the group goes up at once	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_384", "sentence_385", "sentence_386", "sentence_387"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I think that you are in the right. Any truth is better than indefinite doubt. We had better go up at once. Of course, legally, we are putting ourselves hopelessly in the wrong; but I think that it is worth it."}
yellow-face	event_10_8	event	\N	The group turns from the high road into the lane and follows Grant Munro toward the cottage in the rain and darkness	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_388", "sentence_389", "sentence_390", "sentence_391", "sentence_392", "sentence_393", "sentence_394"], "communicatesContent": null}
yellow-face	event_10_9	event	\N	Grant Munro sees someone in the cottage and urges the others to follow	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "grant_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_395", "sentence_396", "sentence_397", "sentence_398"], "communicatesContent": "There is that creature! You can see for yourselves that some one is there. Now follow me, and we shall soon know all."}
yellow-face	event_10_10	event	\N	A woman appears and begs Grant Munro not to go on	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": "effie_munro", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_399", "sentence_400", "sentence_401", "sentence_402", "sentence_403", "sentence_404", "sentence_405"], "communicatesContent": "For God's sake, don't Jack! I had a presentiment that you would come this evening. Think better of it, dear! Trust me again, and you will never have cause to regret it."}
yellow-face	event_10_11	event	\N	Grant Munro rejects Effie's plea, pushes past her, and enters the house with Holmes and Watson	9	{"section": "yellow-face-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_406", "sentence_407", "sentence_408", "sentence_409", "sentence_410", "sentence_411", "sentence_412"], "communicatesContent": null}
