stockbrokers-clerk	event_1_12	event	\N	Holmes asks about the practice and Watson says he covers his neighbour's practice when the neighbour goes out.	0	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_1", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_22", "sentence_23", "sentence_24"], "communicatesContent": "I do my neighbour's when he goes. He is always ready to work off the debt."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_1_13	event	\N	Holmes says Watson has been unwell lately and mentions summer colds.	0	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_25", "sentence_26", "sentence_27", "sentence_28"], "communicatesContent": "Nothing could be better. I perceive that you have been unwell lately. Summer colds are always a little trying."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_1_14	event	\N	Watson says he had been confined to the house by a severe chill for three days last week.	0	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_1", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_29", "sentence_30"], "communicatesContent": "I was confined to the house by a severe chill for three days last week. I thought, however, that I had cast off every trace of it."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_1_15	event	\N	Holmes says Watson looks robust and explains that he deduced the illness from Watson's slippers.	0	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_31", "sentence_32", "sentence_33", "sentence_34", "sentence_35", "sentence_36", "sentence_37", "sentence_38", "sentence_39", "sentence_40", "sentence_41", "sentence_42", "sentence_43", "sentence_44", "sentence_45", "sentence_46", "sentence_47"], "communicatesContent": "So you have. You look remarkably robust. My dear fellow, you know my methods. Certainly. From your slippers. Your slippers are new. You could not have had them more than a few weeks. The soles which you are at this moment presenting to me are slightly scorched. For a moment I thought they might have got wet and been burned in the drying. But near the instep there is a small circular wafer of paper with the shopman's hieroglyphics upon it. Damp would of course have removed this. You had, then, been sitting with your feet outstretched to the fire, which a man would hardly do even in so wet a June as this if he were in his full health."}
