stockbrokers-clerk	event_3_6	event	\N	Arthur Pinner speaks with Hall Pycroft and questions him about his employment and market knowledge	2	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_3", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_109", "sentence_110", "sentence_111", "sentence_112", "sentence_113", "sentence_114", "sentence_115", "sentence_116", "sentence_117", "sentence_118", "sentence_121", "sentence_122", "sentence_123", "sentence_124", "sentence_125", "sentence_126", "sentence_127", "sentence_128", "sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_131", "sentence_132", "sentence_133", "sentence_134", "sentence_135", "sentence_136", "sentence_137", "sentence_138", "sentence_139", "sentence_140", "sentence_141", "sentence_142", "sentence_143", "sentence_144", "sentence_145", "sentence_146", "sentence_147", "sentence_148"], "communicatesContent": "Pycroft, I believe? Lately engaged at Coxon & Woodhouse's? And now on the staff of Mawson's. I have heard some really extraordinary stories about your financial ability. You remember Parker, who used to be Coxon's manager? He can never say enough about it. A good memory? Have you kept in touch with the market while you have been out of work? That is the way to prosper! You won't mind my testing you, will you? Let me see. How are Ayrshires? And New Zealand Consolidated? And British Broken Hills? This quite fits in with all that I had heard. My boy, my boy, you are very much too good to be a clerk at Mawson's! Well, I should tell you how it stands with me. What I have to offer is little enough when measured by your ability, but when compared with Mawson's, it's light to dark. When do you go to Mawson's?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_1	event	\N	Arthur Pinner tells Hall Pycroft that he will become business manager of the Franco-Midland Hardware Company, Limited	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_149", "sentence_150", "sentence_151", "sentence_152", "sentence_153", "sentence_154"], "communicatesContent": "By Monday you will be the business manager of the Franco-Midland Hardware Company, Limited, with a hundred and thirty-four branches in the towns and villages of France, not counting one in Brussels and one in San Remo."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_2	event	\N	Hall Pycroft reacts with surprise at the offer	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_155", "sentence_156"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_3	event	\N	Arthur Pinner explains that the company is privately subscribed and kept quiet	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_157", "sentence_158"], "communicatesContent": "It has been kept very quiet, for the capital was all privately subscribed, and it is too good a thing to let the public into."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_4	event	\N	Arthur Pinner identifies Harry Pinner as promoter and future managing director	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_159"], "communicatesContent": "My brother, Harry Pinner, is promoter, and joins the board after allotment as managing director."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_5	event	\N	Arthur Pinner says he came because Parker spoke of Hall Pycroft	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_160", "sentence_161", "sentence_162"], "communicatesContent": "He knew I was in the swim down here, and asked me to pick up a good man cheap. A young, pushing man with plenty of snap about him. Parker spoke of you, and that brought me here to-night."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_6	event	\N	Arthur Pinner offers Hall Pycroft a salary and commission	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_163", "sentence_164", "sentence_165", "sentence_166"], "communicatesContent": "We can only offer you a beggarly five hundred a year at the beginning; but you are to have an overriding commission of one per cent on all business done by your agents."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_7	event	\N	Hall Pycroft objects that he knows nothing about hardware	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_167"], "communicatesContent": "But I know nothing about hardware."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_8	event	\N	Arthur Pinner offers Hall Pycroft a hundred-pound note as an advance	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_174", "sentence_175", "sentence_176", "sentence_177"], "communicatesContent": "You are the very man for us. Here is a note for a hundred pounds, and if you think that we can do business you may just slip it into your pocket as an advance upon your salary."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_9	event	\N	Hall Pycroft asks when he should take over his new duties	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_178", "sentence_179"], "communicatesContent": "That is very handsome. When should I take over my new duties?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_10	event	\N	Arthur Pinner instructs Hall Pycroft to be in Birmingham the next day and deliver a note to Harry Pinner	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_180", "sentence_181", "sentence_182", "sentence_183"], "communicatesContent": "Be in Birmingham to-morrow at one. I have a note in my pocket here which you will take to my brother. You will find him at 126B, Corporation Street, where the temporary offices of the company are situated. Of course he must confirm your engagement, but between ourselves it will be all right."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_11	event	\N	Hall Pycroft writes and signs a statement agreeing to serve as business manager	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_187", "sentence_188", "sentence_189", "sentence_190"], "communicatesContent": "Kindly write upon it: I am perfectly willing to act as business manager to the Franco-Midland Hardware Company, Limited, at a minimum salary of £500."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_12	event	\N	Hall Pycroft says he will resign from Mawson's	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_191", "sentence_192", "sentence_193", "sentence_194"], "communicatesContent": "I'll write and resign."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_4	event	\N	Police discover American railway bonds and scrip in the carpet bag	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_485"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "had been tattooed in the bend of the elbow.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_4_13	event	\N	Arthur Pinner says he does not want Hall Pycroft to resign because of a row with Mawson's manager	3	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_4", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_195", "sentence_196", "sentence_197", "sentence_198", "sentence_199", "sentence_200"], "communicatesContent": "Precisely what I don't want you to do. I had a row over you with Mawson's manager. I had gone up to ask him about you, and he was very offensive; accused me of coaxing you away from the service of the firm, and that sort of thing. At last I fairly lost my temper. If you want good men you should pay them a good price, I said. He would rather have our small price than your big one."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_1	event	\N	The speaker gives a promise not to write if requested not to	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_205", "sentence_206", "sentence_207", "sentence_208"], "communicatesContent": "I've never so much as seen him in my life. Why should I consider him in any way? I shall certainly not write if you would rather I didn't."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_2	event	\N	Arthur Pinner's brother accepts the promise and rises from his chair	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "aarthur_pinner_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_209", "sentence_210"], "communicatesContent": "Good! That's a promise."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_3	event	\N	Arthur Pinner's brother gives Hall Pycroft a hundred-pound advance and a letter	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "aarthur_pinner_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_211", "sentence_212", "sentence_213", "sentence_214"], "communicatesContent": "I'm delighted to have got so good a man for my brother. Here's your advance of a hundred pounds, and here is the letter. Make a note of the address, 126B, Corporation Street, and remember that one o'clock to-morrow is your appointment. Good-night; and may you have all the fortune that you deserve!"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_4	event	\N	Hall Pycroft leaves for Birmingham by train	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_216", "sentence_217"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_5	event	\N	Hall Pycroft goes to a hotel in New Street	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_218"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_6	event	\N	Hall Pycroft arrives at 126B, Corporation Street before his appointment time	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_218", "sentence_219"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_7	event	\N	Hall Pycroft finds no company name painted at the premises	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_220", "sentence_221"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_8	event	\N	A man approaches Hall Pycroft and addresses him	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_222", "sentence_223"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_9	event	\N	Arthur Pinner's brother asks Hall Pycroft whether he is Mr. Hall Pycroft	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "aarthur_pinner_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_224", "sentence_225", "sentence_226"], "communicatesContent": "Mr. Hall Pycroft?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_10	event	\N	Arthur Pinner's brother explains the new premises and invites Hall Pycroft upstairs	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "aarthur_pinner_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_227", "sentence_228", "sentence_229", "sentence_230", "sentence_231", "sentence_232"], "communicatesContent": "I was expecting you, but you are a trifle before your time. I had a note from my brother this morning in which he sang your praises very loudly. We have not got our name up yet, for we only secured these temporary premises last week. Come up with me, and we will talk the matter over."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_11	event	\N	Hall Pycroft follows the man to the upstairs rooms	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_233"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_12	event	\N	Arthur Pinner's brother asks for the letter and reassures Hall Pycroft	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "aarthur_pinner_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_234", "sentence_235", "sentence_236", "sentence_237", "sentence_238"], "communicatesContent": "Don't be disheartened, Mr. Pycroft. Rome was not built in a day, and we have lots of money at our backs, though we don't cut much dash yet in offices. Pray sit down, and let me have your letter."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_5_13	event	\N	Arthur Pinner's brother reads the letter and engages Hall Pycroft	4	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_5", "speakerId": "aarthur_pinner_brother", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_239", "sentence_240", "sentence_241"], "communicatesContent": "You seem to have made a vast impression upon my brother Arthur; and I know that he is a pretty shrewd judge. He swears by London, you know; and I by Birmingham; but this time I shall follow his advice. Pray consider yourself definitely engaged."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_1	event	\N	Mr. Harry Pinner instructs Hall Pycroft about work in Birmingham and Paris	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": "harry_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_244", "sentence_245", "sentence_247", "sentence_248", "sentence_249", "sentence_250", "sentence_253", "sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256", "sentence_257"], "communicatesContent": "You will eventually manage the great depôt in Paris, which will pour a flood of English crockery into the shops of a hundred and thirty-four agents in France. The purchase will be completed in a week, and meanwhile you will remain in Birmingham and make yourself useful. This is a directory of Paris, with the trades after the names of the people. I want you to take it home with you, and to mark off all the hardware sellers, with their addresses. Not reliable ones. Their system is different from ours. Stick at it, and let me have the lists by Monday, at twelve. Good-day, Mr. Pycroft. If you continue to show zeal and intelligence you will find the company a good master."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_2	event	\N	Hall Pycroft takes the directory home and begins the assignment	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260", "sentence_261", "sentence_262", "sentence_263", "sentence_264"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_14	event	\N	Hall Pycroft introduces the two visitors under assumed names and says they seek employment	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_324", "sentence_325"], "communicatesContent": "One is Mr. Harris, of Bermondsey, and the other is Mr. Price, of this town. They are friends of mine and gentlemen of experience, but they have been out of a place for some little time, and they hoped that perhaps you might find an opening for them in the company's employment."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_3	event	\N	Harry Pinner praises the completed list and assigns a new list of furniture shops	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": "harry_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_265", "sentence_266", "sentence_267", "sentence_268", "sentence_269", "sentence_270", "sentence_271", "sentence_272"], "communicatesContent": "Thank you very much. I fear that I underrated the difficulty of the task. This list will be of very material assistance to me. And now I want you to make a list of the furniture shops, for they all sell crockery. Very good. And you can come up to-morrow evening, at seven, and let me know how you are getting on. Don't overwork yourself."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_4	event	\N	Hall Pycroft notices Harry Pinner's badly stuffed gold tooth	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_272", "sentence_273"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_5	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes explains his identification of the man in London and his conclusion	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_274", "sentence_275", "sentence_276", "sentence_277", "sentence_278"], "communicatesContent": "You may well look surprised, Dr. Watson; but it is this way: When I was speaking to the other chap in London, at the time that he laughed at my not going to Mawson's, I happened to notice that his tooth was stuffed in this very identical fashion. The glint of the gold in each case caught my eye, you see. When I put that with the voice and figure being the same, and only those things altered which might be changed by a razor or a wig, I could not doubt that it was the same man. Of course you expect two brothers to be alike, but not that they should have the same tooth stuffed in the same way."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_6	event	\N	Hall Pycroft leaves the room and returns to the hotel	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_279", "sentence_280"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_6_7	event	\N	Hall Pycroft reflects on the situation and decides to go to London by night train	5	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_281", "sentence_282", "sentence_283", "sentence_284", "sentence_285", "sentence_286"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_1	event	\N	A pause follows the clerk's concluded experience	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_2	event	\N	Holmes comments on the experience and proposes an interview with Mr. Arthur Harry Pinner at the temporary offices	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_288", "sentence_289", "sentence_290", "sentence_291", "sentence_292"], "communicatesContent": "Rather fine, Watson, is it not? There are points in it which please me. I think that you will agree with me that an interview with Mr. Arthur Harry Pinner in the temporary offices of the Franco-Midland Hardware Company, Limited, would be a rather interesting experience for both of us."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_3	event	\N	Watson asks how they can do it	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_293", "sentence_294"], "communicatesContent": "But how can we do it?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_4	event	\N	Hall Pycroft explains a plan to bring two friends to the managing director	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_295", "sentence_296"], "communicatesContent": "You are two friends of mine who are in want of a billet, and what could be more natural than that I should bring you both round to the managing director?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_5	event	\N	Holmes agrees and speaks about wanting to examine the gentleman	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_297", "sentence_298", "sentence_299", "sentence_300"], "communicatesContent": "Quite so, of course. I should like to have a look at the gentleman, and see if I can make anything of his little game. What qualities have you, my friend, which would make your services so valuable? or is it possible that—"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_6	event	\N	The three men walk through New Street toward the offices	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_300", "sentence_301"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_7	event	\N	Hall Pycroft says it is unnecessary to arrive early and that the place is deserted until the appointed hour	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_302", "sentence_303"], "communicatesContent": "It is no use our being at all before our time. He only comes there to see me, apparently, for the place is deserted up to the very hour he names."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_8	event	\N	Holmes remarks that the situation is suggestive	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_304"], "communicatesContent": "That is suggestive."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_9	event	\N	The clerk identifies a man walking ahead of them	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_305", "sentence_306", "sentence_307"], "communicatesContent": "By Jove, I told you so! That's he walking ahead of us there."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_10	event	\N	A smallish dark well-dressed man walks along the road and buys a newspaper from a boy	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_308", "sentence_309", "sentence_310"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_11	event	\N	Hall Pycroft says the man has entered the company's offices and leads the others onward	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_313", "sentence_314", "sentence_315"], "communicatesContent": "There he goes! These are the company's offices into which he has gone. Come with me, and I'll fix it up as easily as possible."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_12	event	\N	The three men enter a bare unfurnished room	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_315", "sentence_316"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_7_13	event	\N	The man at the table is revealed with signs of distress and illness and questions the visitors	6	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_7", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_317", "sentence_318", "sentence_319", "sentence_320", "sentence_321", "sentence_322", "sentence_323"], "communicatesContent": "You look ill, Mr. Pinner! Yes, I am not very well. Who are these gentlemen whom you have brought with you?"}
gloria-scott	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "Now he sat forward in this armchair and spread out the documents upon his knees.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_8_1	event	\N	Mr. Pinner asks Hall Pycroft and Holmes about their occupations and says the company may accommodate them	7	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_8", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_329", "sentence_330", "sentence_331", "sentence_332", "sentence_333", "sentence_334", "sentence_335", "sentence_336"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, I have no doubt that we shall be able to do something for you. What is your particular line, Mr. Harris? Ah yes, we shall want something of the sort. And you, Mr. Price? I have every hope that the company may accommodate you. I will let you know about it as soon as we come to any conclusion."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_8_2	event	\N	Mr. Pinner orders the visitors to leave and goes out through the farther door	7	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_8", "speakerId": "arthur_pinner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_338", "sentence_339", "sentence_340", "sentence_341", "sentence_342", "sentence_343", "sentence_344", "sentence_345"], "communicatesContent": "And now I beg that you will go. For God's sake leave me to myself! Certainly, Mr. Pycroft, certainly. You may wait here a moment; and there is no reason why your friends should not wait with you. I will be entirely at your service in three minutes, if I might trespass upon your patience so far."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes, Watson, and Pycroft discuss Pinner's behaviour and the inner door	7	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_8", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_346", "sentence_347", "sentence_348", "sentence_349", "sentence_350", "sentence_351", "sentence_352", "sentence_353", "sentence_354", "sentence_355", "sentence_356", "sentence_357", "sentence_358", "sentence_359", "sentence_360", "sentence_361", "sentence_362", "sentence_363", "sentence_364", "sentence_365"], "communicatesContent": "Impossible. That door leads into an inner room. There is no exit. None. It was empty yesterday. Then what on earth can he be doing? There is something which I don't understand in this manner. If ever a man was three parts mad with terror, that man's name is Pinner. What can have put the shivers on him? That's it. He did not turn pale. He was pale when we entered the room."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_8_4	event	\N	A knocking sound comes from the inner door	7	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_366", "sentence_367", "sentence_368", "sentence_369"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_8_5	event	\N	Holmes and the others force open the inner door and find the inner room empty	7	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_370", "sentence_371", "sentence_372", "sentence_373", "sentence_374", "sentence_375", "sentence_376", "sentence_377", "sentence_378", "sentence_379", "sentence_380", "sentence_381"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_8_6	event	\N	The managing director is found hanging by his braces in the inner room	7	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_382", "sentence_383", "sentence_384", "sentence_385"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_1	event	\N	Watson examines the man	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_388", "sentence_389"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_2	event	\N	Watson treats the man with water and repositioning	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_391", "sentence_392", "sentence_393"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_3	event	\N	Holmes suggests calling the police	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_395", "sentence_396"], "communicatesContent": "I suppose we ought to call the police in now, and yet I confess that I'd like to give them a complete case when they come."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_4	event	\N	Holmes states that a mystery remains about the sudden move	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_399", "sentence_400", "sentence_401"], "communicatesContent": "All that is clear enough. It is this last sudden move."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_5	event	\N	Holmes says the rest is obvious and asks Watson for his view	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_402", "sentence_403", "sentence_404"], "communicatesContent": "You understand the rest, then? I think that it is fairly obvious. What do you say, Watson?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_6	event	\N	Watson says he is out of his depth	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_405", "sentence_406"], "communicatesContent": "I must confess that I am out of my depths."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_7	event	\N	Holmes explains that the events point to one conclusion	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_407", "sentence_408"], "communicatesContent": "If you consider the events at first they can only point to one conclusion. What do you make of them?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_8	event	\N	Holmes explains that Pycroft was made to sign a declaration	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_409", "sentence_410", "sentence_411"], "communicatesContent": "The whole thing hinges upon two points. The first is the making of Pycroft write a declaration by which he entered the service of this preposterous company. Do you not see how very suggestive that is?"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_9	event	\N	Holmes explains that the company wanted Pycroft's handwriting specimen	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_413", "sentence_414", "sentence_415"], "communicatesContent": "Why did they want him to do it? Not as a business matter, for these arrangements are usually verbal, and there was no earthly business reason why this should be an exception. They were very anxious to obtain a specimen of your handwriting, and had no other way of doing it."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_10	event	\N	Holmes says someone wanted to imitate Pycroft's writing	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_416", "sentence_417", "sentence_418", "sentence_419", "sentence_420", "sentence_421", "sentence_422"], "communicatesContent": "And why? Quite so. Why? When we answer that we have made some progress with our little problem. Why? There can be only one adequate reason. Some one wanted to learn to imitate your writing, and had to procure a specimen of it first."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_3	event	\N	Police discover that a daring and gigantic robbery has been committed	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_484"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "Then he lit his pipe and sat for some time smoking and turning them over.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_11	event	\N	Holmes explains the second point about Pinner's request	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_423", "sentence_424"], "communicatesContent": "If we pass on to the second point we find that each throws light upon the other. That point is the request made by Pinner that you should not resign your place, but should leave the manager of this important business in the full expectation that a Mr. Hall Pycroft, whom he had never seen, was about to enter the office upon the Monday morning."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_12	event	\N	Hall Pycroft exclaims in distress	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_425", "sentence_426"], "communicatesContent": "My God! what a blind beetle I have been!"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_9_13	event	\N	Holmes explains the handwriting ruse and the need to keep Pycroft away	8	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_427", "sentence_428", "sentence_429", "sentence_430", "sentence_431", "sentence_432", "sentence_433", "sentence_434"], "communicatesContent": "Now you see the point about the handwriting. Suppose that some one turned up in your place who wrote a completely different hand from that in which you had applied for the vacancy, of course the game would have been up. But in the interval the rogue had learned to imitate you, and his position was therefore secure. Of course it was of the utmost importance to prevent you from thinking better of it, and also to keep you from coming into contact with any one who might tell you that your double was at work in Mawson's office. Therefore they gave you a handsome advance on your salary, and ran you off to the Midlands, where they gave you enough work to do to prevent your going to London, where you might have burst their little game up. That is all plain enough."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_1	event	\N	Holmes explains that two men are involved in the plot and that one impersonates Hall Pycroft at the office.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_436", "sentence_437", "sentence_438", "sentence_439", "sentence_440", "sentence_441", "sentence_442"], "communicatesContent": "There are evidently only two of them in it. The other is impersonating you at the office. This one acted as your engager, and then found that he could not find you an employer without admitting a third person into his plot. He changed his appearance as far as he could, and trusted that the likeness would be put down to a family resemblance. But for the happy chance of the gold stuffing, your suspicions would probably never have been aroused."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_2	event	\N	Hall Pycroft reacts in alarm and asks Holmes what to do.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_443", "sentence_444", "sentence_445", "sentence_446", "sentence_447"], "communicatesContent": "Good Lord! while I have been fooled in this way, what has this other Hall Pycroft been doing at Mawson's? What should we do, Mr. Holmes? Tell me what to do."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_3	event	\N	Holmes says they must wire to Mawson's.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_448"], "communicatesContent": "We must wire to Mawson's."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_4	event	\N	Holmes and others discuss that Mawson's closes at noon on Saturdays and keeps a permanent guard.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "hall_pycroft", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_449", "sentence_450", "sentence_451", "sentence_452", "sentence_453", "sentence_454"], "communicatesContent": "They shut at twelve on Saturdays."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_5	event	\N	A voice behind them mentions the paper.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_456", "sentence_457"], "communicatesContent": "The paper!"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_6	event	\N	The wounded man sits up and rubs the red band around his throat.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_458"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_7	event	\N	Holmes cries out in excitement and recognizes the paper as the secret.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_459", "sentence_460", "sentence_461", "sentence_462", "sentence_463", "sentence_464"], "communicatesContent": "The paper! Of course! Idiot that I was! I thought so much of our visit that the paper never entered my head for an instant. To be sure, the secret must be there."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_8	event	\N	Holmes flattens out the newspaper on the table and points out the headlines.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_465", "sentence_466", "sentence_467", "sentence_468", "sentence_469", "sentence_470", "sentence_471", "sentence_472"], "communicatesContent": "Look at this, Watson. It is a London paper, an early edition of the Evening Standard. Here is what we want. Look at the headlines: 'Crime in the City. Murder at Mawson & Williams. Gigantic Attempted Robbery.'"}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_10_9	event	\N	Watson reads aloud the newspaper account to the group.	9	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_10", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_472", "sentence_473", "sentence_474", "sentence_475", "sentence_476", "sentence_477", "sentence_478", "sentence_479", "sentence_480"], "communicatesContent": "A desperate attempt at robbery, culminating in the death of one man and the capture of the criminal, occurred this afternoon in the City. For some time back Mawson & Williams, the famous financial house, have been the guardians of securities which amount in the aggregate to a sum of considerably over a million sterling. So conscious was the manager of the responsibility which devolved upon him in consequence of the great interests at stake that safes of the very latest construction have been employed, and an armed watchman has been left day and night in the building. It appears that last week a new clerk named Hall Pycroft was engaged by the firm. This person appears to have been none other than Beddington, the famous forger and cracksman, who, with his brother, had only recently emerged from a five years' spell of penal servitude. By some means, which are not yet clear, he succeeded in winning, under a false name, this official position in the office, which he utilised in order to obtain moulding of various locks, and a thorough knowledge of the position of the strong room and the safes."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_1	event	\N	Sergeant Tuson sees a gentleman with a carpet bag come down the steps after midday	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_482"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_2	event	\N	Sergeant Tuson follows the man and arrests him with Constable Pollock after desperate resistance	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_483"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_5	event	\N	Police find the watchman's body doubled up and thrust into the largest safe	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_486"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_6	event	\N	The watchman is struck from behind with a poker and killed	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_487"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_7	event	\N	Beddington gains entry by pretending to have left something behind, murders the watchman, rifles the safe, and makes off with the booty	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_488"], "communicatesContent": null}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_8	event	\N	Holmes remarks that Beddington's brother has not appeared in the job and that police are making inquiries	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_489"], "communicatesContent": "Well, we may save the police some little trouble in that direction."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_9	event	\N	Holmes speaks to Watson about human nature, the villain and murderer, the brother's suicide, and the forfeited neck	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_491", "sentence_492"], "communicatesContent": "Human nature is a strange mixture, Watson. You see that even a villain and murderer can inspire such affection that his brother turns to suicide when he learns that his neck is forfeited."}
stockbrokers-clerk	event_11_10	event	\N	Holmes and the doctor remain on guard while Mr. Pycroft is asked to go out for the police	10	{"section": "stockbrokers-clerk-section_11", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_493", "sentence_494"], "communicatesContent": "The doctor and I will remain on guard, Mr. Pycroft, if you will have the kindness to step out for the police."}
