gloria-scott	sentence_1	lexical	\N	\N	0	{"text": "V.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_2	lexical	\N	\N	1	{"text": "The \\"_Gloria Scott_\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "\\"I have some papers here,\\" said my friend Sherlock Holmes, as we sat one winter's night on either side of the fire, \\"which I really think, Watson, that it would be worth your while to glance over.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "These are the documents in the extraordinary case of the _Gloria Scott_, and this is the message which struck Justice of the Peace Trevor dead with horror when he read it.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "He had picked from a drawer a little tarnished cylinder, and, undoing the tape, he handed me a short note scrawled upon a half-sheet of slate-grey paper.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "\\"The supply of game for London is going steadily up,\\" it ran.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "\\"Head-keeper Hudson, we believe, has been now told to receive all orders for fly-paper and for preservation of your hen-pheasant's life.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "As I glanced up from reading this enigmatical message, I saw Holmes chuckling at the expression upon my face.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "\\"You look a little bewildered,\\" said he.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "\\"I cannot see how such a message as this could inspire horror.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "It seems to me to be rather grotesque than otherwise.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "\\"Very likely.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "Yet the fact remains that the reader, who was a fine, robust old man, was knocked clean down by it as if it had been the butt end of a pistol.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "\\"You arouse my curiosity,\\" said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "\\"But why did you say just now that there were very particular reasons why I should study this case?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "\\"Because it was the first in which I was ever engaged.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "I had often endeavoured to elicit from my companion what had first turned his mind in the direction of criminal research, but had never caught him before in a communicative humour.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"You never heard me talk of Victor Trevor?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "\\"He was the only friend I made during the two years I was at college.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "I was never a very sociable fellow, Watson, always rather fond of moping in my rooms and working out my own little methods of thought, so that I never mixed much with the men of my year.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "Bar fencing and boxing I had few athletic tastes, and then my line of study was quite distinct from that of the other fellows, so that we had no points of contact at all.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "Trevor was the only man I knew, and that only through the accident of his bull terrier freezing on to my ankle one morning as I went down to chapel.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "\\"It was a prosaic way of forming a friendship, but it was effective.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "I was laid by the heels for ten days, but Trevor used to come in to inquire after me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "At first it was only a minute's chat, but soon his visits lengthened, and before the end of the term we were close friends.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "He was a hearty, full-blooded fellow, full of spirits and energy, the very opposite to me in most respects, but we had some subjects in common, and it was a bond of union when I found that he was as friendless as I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "Finally, he invited me down to his father's place at Donnithorpe, in Norfolk, and I accepted his hospitality for a month of the long vacation.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "\\"Old Trevor was evidently a man of some wealth and consideration, a J.P.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "and a landed proprietor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "Donnithorpe is a little hamlet just to the north of Langmere, in the country of the Broads.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "The house was an old-fashioned, wide-spread, oak-beamed brick building, with a fine lime-lined avenue leading up to it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "There was excellent wild-duck shooting in the fens, remarkably good fishing, a small but select library, taken over, as I understood, from a former occupant, and a tolerable cook, so that he would be a fastidious man who could not put in a pleasant month there.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "\\"Trevor senior was a widower, and my friend his only son.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "\\"There had been a daughter, I heard, but she had died of diphtheria while on a visit to Birmingham.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "The father interested me extremely.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "He was a man of little culture, but with a considerable amount of rude strength, both physically and mentally.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "He knew hardly any books, but he had travelled far, had seen much of the world.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "And had remembered all that he had learned.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "In person he was a thick-set, burly man with a shock of grizzled hair, a brown, weather-beaten face, and blue eyes which were keen to the verge of fierceness.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "Yet he had a reputation for kindness and charity on the country-side, and was noted for the leniency of his sentences from the bench.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "\\"One evening, shortly after my arrival, we were sitting over a glass of port after dinner, when young Trevor began to talk about those habits of observation and inference which I had already formed into a system, although I had not yet appreciated the part which they were to play in my life.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "The old man evidently thought that his son was exaggerating in his description of one or two trivial feats which I had performed.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "\\"'Come, now, Mr. Holmes,' said he, laughing good-humoredly.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "'I'm an excellent subject, if you can deduce anything from me.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "\\"'I fear there is not very much,' I answered; 'I might suggest that you have gone about in fear of some personal attack within the last twelve months.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "\\"The laugh faded from his lips, and he stared at me in great surprise.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "\\"'Well, that's true enough,' said he.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "'You know, Victor,' turning to his son, 'when we broke up that poaching gang, they swore to knife us, and Sir Edward Holly has actually been attacked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "I've always been on my guard since then, though I have no idea how you know it.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "'By the inscription I observed that you had not had it more than a year.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "But you have taken some pains to bore the head of it and pour melted lead into the hole so as to make it a formidable weapon.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "I argued that you would not take such precautions unless you had some danger to fear.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "' he asked, smiling.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "asked, smiling.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "\\"'You have boxed a good deal in your youth.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "\\"'Right again.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "How did you know it?", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "Is my nose knocked a little out of the straight?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "\\"'No,' said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "'It is your ears.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "They have the peculiar flattening and thickening which marks the boxing man.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "\\"'Anything else?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "\\"'You have done a good deal of digging by your callosities.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "\\"'Made all my money at the gold fields.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "\\"'You have been in New Zealand.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "\\"'Right again.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "\\"'You have visited Japan.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "\\"'Quite true.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "\\"'And you have been most intimately associated with some one whose initials were J.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "A., and whom you afterwards were eager to entirely forget.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "\\"Mr. Trevor stood slowly up, fixed his large blue eyes upon me with a strange wild stare, and then pitched forward, with his face among the nutshells which strewed the cloth, in a dead faint.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "\\"You can imagine, Watson, how shocked both his son and I were.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "His attack did not last long, however, for when we undid his collar, and sprinkled the water from one of the finger-glasses over his face, he gave a gasp or two and sat up.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "\\"'Ah, boys,' said he, forcing a smile, 'I hope I haven't frightened you.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "Strong as I look, there is a weak place in my heart, and it does not take much to knock me over.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "I don't know how you manage this, Mr. Holmes, but it seems to me that all the detectives of fact and of fancy would be children in your hands.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "That's your line of life, sir, and you may take the word of a man who has seen something of the world.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "\\"And that recommendation, with the exaggerated estimate of my ability with which he prefaced it, was, if you will believe me, Watson, the very first thing which ever made me feel that a profession might be made out of what had up to that time been the merest hobby.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "At the moment, however, I was too much concerned at the sudden illness of my host to think of anything else.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "' said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "that I have said nothing to pain you?' said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "\\"'Well, you certainly touched upon rather a tender point.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "' He spoke now in a half-jesting fashion, but a look of terror still lurked at the back of his eyes.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "of terror still lurked at the back of his eyes.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "\\"'It is simplicity itself,' said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "'When you bared your arm to draw that fish into the boat I saw that J.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "A.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "The letters were still legible, but it was perfectly clear from their blurred appearance, and from the staining of the skin round them, that efforts had been made to obliterate them.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "It was obvious, then, that those initials had once been very familiar to you, and that you had afterwards wished to forget them.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "\\"What an eye you have!\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "he cried, with a sigh of relief.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "'It is just as you say.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "But we won't talk of it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "Of all ghosts the ghosts of our old lovers are the worst.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "Come into the billiard-room and have a quiet cigar.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "\\"From that day, amid all his cordiality, there was always a touch of suspicion in Mr. Trevor's manner towards me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "Even his son remarked it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "' He did not mean to show it, I am sure, but it was so strongly in his mind that it peeped out at every action.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "At last I became so convinced that I was causing him uneasiness that I drew my visit to a close.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "On the very day, however, before I left, an incident occurred which proved in the sequel to be of importance.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "t to a close. On the very day, however, before I left, an incident occurred which proved in the sequel to be of importance.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "\\"We were sitting out upon the lawn on garden chairs, the three of us, basking in the sun and admiring the view across the Broads, when a maid came out to say that there was a man at the door who wanted to see Mr. Trevor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "' asked my host.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "me?' asked my host.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "\\"'He would not give any.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "\\"'What does he want, then?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "\\"'He says that you know him, and that he only wants a moment's conversation.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "' An instant afterwards there appeared a little wizened fellow with a cringing manner and a shambling style of walking.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "He wore an open jacket, with a splotch of tar on the sleeve, a red-and-black check shirt, dungaree trousers, and heavy boots badly worn.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "His face was thin and brown and crafty, with a perpetual smile upon it, which showed an irregular line of yellow teeth, and his crinkled hands were half closed in a way that is distinctive of sailors.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "As he came slouching across the lawn I heard Mr. Trevor make a sort of hiccoughing noise in his throat, and jumping out of his chair, he ran into the house.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "He was back in a moment, and I smelt a strong reek of brandy as he passed me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "randy as he passed me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "\\"'Well, my man,' said he, 'what can I do for you?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "\\"The sailor stood looking at him with puckered eyes, and with the same loose-lipped smile upon his face.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "' he asked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "know me?' he asked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "\\"'Why, dear me, it is surely Hudson,' said Mr. Trevor in a tone of surprise.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "\\"'Hudson it is, sir,' said the seaman.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "'Why, it's thirty year and more since I saw you last.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "Here you are in your house, and me still picking my salt meat out of the harness cask.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "\\"'Tut, you will find that I have not forgotten old times,' cried Mr. Trevor, and, walking towards the sailor, he said something in a low voice.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "\\"'What power had he, then?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "'Go into the kitchen,' he continued out loud, 'and you will get food and drink.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "I have no doubt that I shall find you a situation.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "\\"'Thank you, sir,' said the seaman, touching his forelock.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "'I'm just off a two-yearer in an eight-knot tramp, short-handed at that, and I wants a rest.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "I thought I'd get it either with Mr. Beddoes or with you.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "' cried Trevor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "evor. 'You know where Mr. Beddoes is?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "\\"'Bless you, sir, I know where all my old friends are,' said the fellow with a sinister smile, and he slouched off after the maid to the kitchen.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "Mr. Trevor mumbled something to us about having been shipmate with the man when he was going back to the diggings, and then, leaving us on the lawn, he went indoors.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "An hour later, when we entered the house, we found him stretched dead drunk upon the dining-room sofa.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "The whole incident left a most ugly impression upon my mind, and I was not sorry next day to leave Donnithorpe behind me, for I felt that my presence must be a source of embarrassment to my friend.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "\\"All this occurred during the first month of the long vacation.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "I went up to my London rooms, where I spent seven weeks working out a few experiments in organic chemistry.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "One day, however, when the autumn was far advanced and the vacation drawing to a close, I received a telegram from my friend imploring me to return to Donnithorpe, and saying that he was in great need of my advice and assistance.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "Of course I dropped everything and set out for the North once more.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "\\"He met me with the dog-cart at the station, and I saw at a glance that the last two months had been very trying ones for him.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "He had grown thin and careworn, and had lost the loud, cheery manner for which he had been remarkable.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "\\"'The governor is dying,' were the first words he said.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "' I cried.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "le!' I cried. 'What is the matter?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "\\"'Apoplexy.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "Nervous shock, He's been on the verge all day.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "I doubt if we shall find him alive.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "\\"I was, as you may think, Watson, horrified at this unexpected news.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "caused it?' I asked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "\\"'Ah, that is the point.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "Jump in and we can talk it over while we drive.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "You remember that fellow who came upon the evening before you left us?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "\\"'Perfectly.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "\\"'Do you know who it was that we let into the house that day?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "\\"'I have no idea.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "\\"'It was the devil, Holmes,' he cried.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "\\"I stared at him in astonishment.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "\\"'Yes, it was the devil himself.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "We have not had a peaceful hour since—not one.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "The governor has never held up his head from that evening, and now the life has been crushed out of him and his heart broken, all through this accursed Hudson.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_28	section	\N	Section 28	27	{"wordCount": 152}
gloria-scott	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "\\"'Ah, that is what I would give so much to know.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "The kindly, charitable, good old governor—how could he have fallen into the clutches of such a ruffian!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "But I am so glad that you have come, Holmes.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "I trust very much to your judgment and discretion, and I know that you will advise me for the best.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "\\"We were dashing along the smooth white country road, with the long stretch of the Broads in front of us glimmering in the red light of the setting sun.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "From a grove upon our left I could already see the high chimneys and the flag-staff which marked the squire's dwelling.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "\\"'My father made the fellow gardener,' said my companion, 'and then, as that did not satisfy him, he was promoted to be butler.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "The house seemed to be at his mercy, and he wandered about and did what he chose in it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "The maids complained of his drunken habits and his vile language.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "The dad raised their wages all round to recompense them for the annoyance.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "The fellow would take the boat and my father's best gun and treat himself to little shooting trips.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "And all this with such a sneering, leering, insolent face that I would have knocked him down twenty times over if he had been a man of my own age.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "I tell you, Holmes, I have had to keep a tight hold upon myself all this time; and now I am asking myself whether, if I had let myself go a little more, I might not have been a wiser man.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "\\"'Well, matters went from bad to worse with us, and this animal Hudson became more and more intrusive, until at last, on making some insolent reply to my father in my presence one day, I took him by the shoulders and turned him out of the room.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "He slunk away with a livid face and two venomous eyes which uttered more threats than his tongue could do.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "I don't know what passed between the poor dad and him after that, but the dad came to me next day and asked me whether I would mind apologising to Hudson.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "I refused, as you can imagine, and asked my father how he could allow such a wretch to take such liberties with himself and his household.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "\\"'\\"Ah, my boy,\\" said he, \\"it is all very well to talk, but you don't know how I am placed.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "But you shall know, Victor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "I'll see that you shall know, come what may.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "You wouldn't believe harm of your poor old father, would you, lad?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "He was very much moved, and shut himself up in the study all day, where I could see through the window that he was writing busily.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "\\"'That evening there came what seemed to me to be a grand release, for Hudson told us that he was going to leave us.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "He walked into the dining-room as we sat after dinner, and announced his intention in the thick voice of a half-drunken man.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "\\"'\\"I've had enough of Norfolk,\\" said he.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "\\"I'll run down to Mr. Beddoes in Hampshire.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "He'll be as glad to see me as you were, I daresay.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "\\"'\\"You're not going away in an unkind spirit, Hudson, I hope,\\" said my father, with a tameness which made my blood boil.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "\\"'\\"I've not had my 'pology,\\" said he sulkily, glancing in my direction.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "\\"'\\"Victor, you will acknowledge that you have used this worthy fellow rather roughly,\\" said the dad, turning to me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "\\"'\\"On the contrary, I think that we have both shown extraordinary patience towards him,\\" I answered.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "\\"'\\"Oh, you do, do you?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "he snarls.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "We'll see about that!\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "He slouched out of the room, and half an hour afterwards left the house, leaving my father in a state of pitiable nervousness.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "Night after night I heard him pacing his room, and it was just as he was recovering his confidence that the blow did at last fall.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "' I asked eagerly.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "d eagerly.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "\\"'In a most extraordinary fashion.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "A letter arrived for my father yesterday evening, bearing the Fordingbridge postmark.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "My father read it, clapped both his hands to his head, and began running round the room in little circles like a man who has been driven out of his senses.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "When I at last drew him down on to the sofa, his mouth and eyelids were all puckered on one side, and I saw that he had a stroke.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "Dr. Fordham came over at once.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "We put him to bed; but the paralysis has spread, he has shown no sign of returning consciousness, and I think that we shall hardly find him alive.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "' I cried.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "ify me, Trevor!' I cried. 'What then could have been in this letter to cause so dreadful a result?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "\\"'Nothing.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "There lies the inexplicable part of it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "The message was absurd and trivial.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "Ah, my God, it is as I feared!'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "\\"As he spoke we came round the curve of the avenue, and saw in the fading light that every blind in the house had been drawn down.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "As we dashed up to the door, my friend's face convulsed with grief, a gentleman in black emerged from it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "' asked Trevor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "appen, doctor?' asked Trevor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "\\"'Almost immediately after you left.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "\\"'Did he recover consciousness?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "\\"'For an instant before the end.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "\\"'Any message for me?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "\\"'Only that the papers were in the back drawer of the Japanese cabinet.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "\\"My friend ascended with the doctor to the chamber of death, while I remained in the study, turning the whole matter over and over in my head, and feeling as sombre as ever I had done in my life.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "What was the past of this Trevor, pugilist, traveler, and gold-digger, and how had he placed himself in the power of this acid-faced seaman?", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "Why, too, should he faint at an allusion to the half-effaced initials upon his arm, and die of fright when he had a letter from Fordingbridge?", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "Then I remembered that Fordingbridge was in Hampshire, and that this Mr. Beddoes, whom the seaman had gone to visit and presumably to blackmail, had also been mentioned as living in Hampshire.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "The letter, then, might either come from Hudson, the seaman, saying that he had betrayed the guilty secret which appeared to exist, or it might come from Beddoes, warning an old confederate that such a betrayal was imminent.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "So far it seemed clear enough.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "But then how could this letter be trivial and grotesque, as described by the son?", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "He must have misread it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "If so, it must have been one of those ingenious secret codes which mean one thing while they seem to mean another.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "I must see this letter.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "If there were a hidden meaning in it, I was confident that I could pluck it forth.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "For an hour I sat pondering over it in the gloom, until at last a weeping maid brought in a lamp, and close at her heels came my friend Trevor, pale but composed, with these very papers which lie upon my knee held in his grasp.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "He sat down opposite to me, drew the lamp to the edge of the table, and handed me a short note scribbled, as you see, upon a single sheet of grey paper.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "'The supply of game for London is going steadily up,' it ran.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "'Head-keeper Hudson, we believe, has been now told to receive all orders for fly paper and for preservation of your hen pheasant's life.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "\\"I daresay my face looked as bewildered as yours did just now when first I read this message.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "Then I reread it very carefully.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "It was evidently as I had thought, and some secret meaning must lie buried in this strange combination of words.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "Or could it be that there was a prearranged significance to such phrases as 'fly paper' and 'hen pheasant'?", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "Such a meaning would be arbitrary and could not be deduced in any way.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "And yet I was loath to believe that this was the case, and the presence of the word 'Hudson' seemed to show that the subject of the message was as I had guessed, and that it was from Beddoes rather than the sailor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "I tried it backwards, but the combination 'life pheasant's hen' was not encouraging.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "Then I tried alternate words, but neither 'The of for' nor 'supply game London' promised to throw any light upon it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "And then in an instant the key of the riddle was in my hands, and I saw that every third word, beginning with the first, would give a message which might well drive old Trevor to despair.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "\\"It was short and terse, the warning, as I now read it to my companion:", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "\\"'The game is up.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "Hudson has told all.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "Fly for your life.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "\\"Victor Trevor sank his face into his shaking hands.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "'It must be that, I suppose,' said he.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "'This is worse than death, for it means disgrace as well.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "But what is the meaning of these \\"head-keepers\\" and \\"hen pheasants\\"?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "\\"'It means nothing to the message, but it might mean a good deal to us if we had no other means of discovering the sender.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "You see that he has begun by writing \\"The ...", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "game ...", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "is,\\" and so on.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "Afterwards he had, to fulfill the prearranged cipher, to fill in any two words in each space.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "He would naturally use the first words which came to his mind, and if there were so many which referred to sport among them, you may be tolerably sure that he is either an ardent shot or interested in breeding.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "Do you know anything of this Beddoes?'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "\\"'Why, now that you mention it,' said he, 'I remember that my poor father used to have an invitation from him to shoot over his preserves every autumn.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "\\"'Then it is undoubtedly from him that the note comes,' said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "'It only remains for us to find out what this secret was which the sailor Hudson seems to have held over the heads of these two wealthy and respected men.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "' cried my friend.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "'But from you I shall have no secrets.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_29	section	\N	Section 29	28	{"wordCount": 281}
gloria-scott	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "Here is the statement which was drawn up by my father when he knew that the danger from Hudson had become imminent.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "I found it in the Japanese cabinet, as he told the doctor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "ound it in the Japanese cabinet, as he told the doctor. Take it and read it to me, for I have neither the strength nor the courage to do it myself.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "\\"These are the very papers, Watson, which he handed to me, and I will read them to you, as I read them in the old study that night to him.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "They are endorsed outside, as you see, 'Some particulars of the voyage of the bark _Gloria Scott_, from her leaving Falmouth on the 8th October, 1855, to her destruction in N.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "lat.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "15º 20', W.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "long.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "25º 14' on Nov.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "6th.' It is in the form of a letter, and runs in this way:", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "\\"'My dear, dear son,—Now that approaching disgrace begins to darken the closing years of my life, I can write with all truth and honesty that it is not the terror of the law, it is not the loss of my position in the county, nor is it my fall in the eyes of all who have known me, which cuts me to the heart; but it is the thought that you should come to blush for me—you who love me and who have seldom, I hope, had reason to do other than respect me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "But if the blow falls which is forever hanging over me, then I should wish you to read this, that you may know straight from me how far I have been to blame.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "), then if by any chance this paper should be still undestroyed and should fall into your hands, I conjure you, by all you hold sacred, by the memory of your dear mother, and by the love which had been between us, to hurl it into the fire and to never give one thought to it again.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "ween us, to hurl it into the fire and to never give one thought to it again.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "\\"'If then your eye goes on to read this line, I know that I shall already have been exposed and dragged from my home, or as is more likely, for you know that my heart is weak, by lying with my tongue sealed forever in death.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "In either case the time for suppression is past, and every word which I tell you is the naked truth, and this I swear as I hope for mercy.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "\\"'My name, dear lad, is not Trevor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "I was James Armitage in my younger days, and you can understand now the shock that it was to me a few weeks ago when your college friend addressed me in words which seemed to imply that he had surmised my secret.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "As Armitage it was that I entered a London banking house, and as Armitage I was convicted of breaking my country's laws, and was sentenced to transportation.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "Do not think very harshly of me, laddie.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "It was a debt of honour, so called, which I had to pay, and I used money which was not my own to do it, in the certainty that I could replace it before there could be any possibility of its being missed.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "But the most dreadful ill-luck pursued me.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "The money which I had reckoned upon never came to hand, and a premature examination of accounts exposed my deficit.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "The case might have been dealt leniently with, but the laws were more harshly administered thirty years ago than now, and on my twenty-third birthday I found myself chained as a felon with thirty-seven other convicts in 'tween-decks of the barque _Gloria Scott_, bound for Australia.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "\\"'It was the year '55 when the Crimean war was at its height, and the old convict ships had been largely used as transports in the Black Sea.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "The government was compelled, therefore, to use smaller and less suitable vessels for sending out their prisoners.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "The _Gloria Scott_ had been in the Chinese tea trade, but she was an old-fashioned, heavy-bowed, broad-beamed craft, and the new clippers had cut her out.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "She was a five-hundred-ton boat, and besides her thirty-eight gaol-birds, she carried twenty-six of a crew, eighteen soldiers, a captain, three mates, a doctor, a chaplain, and four warders.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "Nearly a hundred souls were in her, all told, when we set sail from Falmouth.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "\\"'The partitions between the cells of the convicts, instead of being of thick oak, as is usual in convict-ships, were quite thin and frail.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "The man next to me, upon the aft side, was one whom I had particularly noticed when we were led down the quay.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "He was a young man with a clear, hairless face, a long, thin nose, and rather nut-cracker jaws.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "He carried his head very jauntily in the air, had a swaggering style of walking, and was, above all else, remarkable for his extraordinary height.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "I don't think any of our heads would have come up to his shoulder, and I am sure that he could not have measured less than six and a half feet.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "It was strange among so many sad and weary faces to see one which was full of energy and resolution.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "The sight of it was to me like a fire in a snowstorm.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "I was glad, then, to find that he was my neighbour, and gladder still when, in the dead of the night, I heard a whisper close to my ear, and found that he had managed to cut an opening in the board which separated us.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "\\"'\\"Hallao, chummy!\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "said he, \\"what's your name, and what are you here for?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "\\"'I answered him, and asked in turn who I was talking with.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "\\"'\\"I'm Jack Prendergast,\\" said he, \\"and by God!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "You'll learn to bless my name before you've done with me.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "\\"'I remembered hearing of his case, for it was one which had made an immense sensation throughout the country some time before my own arrest.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "He was a man of good family and of great ability, but of incurably vicious habits, who had by an ingenious system of fraud obtained huge sums of money from the leading London merchants.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "\\"'\\"Ha, ha!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "You remember my case!\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "said he proudly.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "\\"'\\"Very well, indeed.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "\\"'\\"Then maybe you remember something queer about it?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "\\"'\\"What was that, then?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "\\"'\\"I'd had nearly a quarter of a million, hadn't I?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "\\"'\\"So it was said.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "\\"'\\"But none was recovered, eh?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "\\"'\\"No.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "\\"'\\"Well, where d'ye suppose the balance is?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "\\"'\\"I have no idea,\\" said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "\\"'\\"Right between my finger and thumb,\\" he cried.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "\\"By God!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "I've got more pounds to my name than you've hairs on your head.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "_ Now, you don't think it likely that a man who could do anything is going to wear his breeches out sitting in the stinking hold of a rat-gutted, beetle-ridden, mouldy old coffin of a China coaster.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "No, sir, such a man will look after himself and will look after his chums.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "You may lay to that!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "You hold on to him, and you may kiss the book that he'll haul you through.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "ay lay to that! You hold on to him, and you may kiss the book that he'll haul you through.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "He had unlocked the door that led to the deck, and we were through it in a rush.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "\\"'That was his style of talk, and at first I thought it meant nothing; but after a while, when he had tested me and sworn me in with all possible solemnity, he let me understand that there really was a plot to gain command of the vessel.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "A dozen of the prisoners had hatched it before they came aboard, Prendergast was the leader, and his money was the motive power.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "\\"'\\"I'd a partner,\\" said he, \\"a rare good man, as true as a stock to a barrel.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "He's got the dibbs, he has, and where do you think he is at this moment?", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "Why, he's the chaplain of this ship—the chaplain, no less!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "He came aboard with a black coat, and his papers right, and money enough in his box to buy the thing right up from keel to main-truck.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "The crew are his, body and soul.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "He could buy 'em at so much a gross with a cash discount, and he did it before ever they signed on.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "He's got two of the warders and Mercer, the second mate, and he'd get the captain himself, if he thought him worth it.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "\\"'\\"What are we to do, then?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "\\"'\\"What do you think?\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "said he.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "\\"We'll make the coats of some of these soldiers redder than ever the tailor did.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "\\"'\\"But they are armed,\\" said I.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "\\"'\\"And so shall we be, my boy.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "There's a brace of pistols for every mother's son of us, and if we can't carry this ship, with the crew at our back, it's time we were all sent to a young misses' boarding-school.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "You speak to your mate upon the left to-night, and see if he is to be trusted.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "\\"'I did so, and found my other neighbour to be a young fellow in much the same position as myself, whose crime had been forgery.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "His name was Evans, but he afterwards changed it, like myself, and he is now a rich and prosperous man in the south of England.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "He was ready enough to join the conspiracy, as the only means of saving ourselves, and before we had crossed the Bay there were only two of the prisoners who were not in the secret.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "One of these was of weak mind, and we did not dare to trust him, and the other was suffering from jaundice, and could not be of any use to us.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "\\"\\"From the beginning there was really nothing to prevent us from taking possession of the ship.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "The crew were a set of ruffians, specially picked for the job.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "The sham chaplain came into our cells to exhort us, carrying a black bag, supposed to be full of tracts, and so often did he come that by the third day we had each stowed away at the foot of our beds a file, a brace of pistols, a pound of powder, and twenty slugs.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "Two of the warders were agents of Prendergast, and the second mate was his right-hand man.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "The captain, the two mates, two warders, Lieutenant Martin, his eighteen soldiers, and the doctor were all that we had against us.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "Yet, safe as it was, we determined to neglect no precaution, and to make our attack suddenly by night.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "It came, however, more quickly than we expected, and in this way.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "\\"'One evening, about the third week after our start, the doctor had come down to see one of the prisoners who was ill, and putting his hand down on the bottom of his bunk he felt the outline of the pistols.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "If he had been silent he might have blown the whole thing, but he was a nervous little chap, so he gave a cry of surprise and turned so pale that the man knew what was up in an instant and seized him.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "He was gagged before he could give the alarm, and tied down upon the bed.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "The two sentries were shot down, and so was a corporal who came running to see what was the matter.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "There were two more soldiers at the door of the state-room, and their muskets seemed not to be loaded, for they never fired upon us, and they were shot while trying to fix their bayonets.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "Then we rushed on into the captain's cabin, but as we pushed open the door there was an explosion from within, and there he lay with his brains smeared over the chart of the Atlantic which was pinned upon the table, while the chaplain stood with a smoking pistol in his hand at his elbow.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "The two mates had both been seized by the crew, and the whole business seemed to be settled.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "\\"'The state-room was next the cabin, and we flocked in there and flopped down on the settees, all speaking together, for we were just mad with the feeling that we were free once more.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "There were lockers all round, and Wilson, the sham chaplain, knocked one of them in, and pulled out a dozen of brown sherry.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "We cracked off the necks of the bottles, poured the stuff out into tumblers, and were just tossing them off, when in an instant without warning there came the roar of muskets in our ears, and the saloon was so full of smoke that we could not see across the table.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "When it cleared again the place was a shambles.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "Wilson and eight others were wriggling on the top of each other on the floor, and the blood and the brown sherry on that table turn me sick now when I think of it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "We were so cowed by the sight that I think we should have given the job up if it had not been for Prendergast.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "He bellowed like a bull and rushed for the door with all that were left alive at his heels.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "Out we ran, and there on the poop were the lieutenant and ten of his men.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "The swing skylights above the saloon table had been a bit open, and they had fired on us through the slit.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "We got on them before they could load, and they stood to it like men; but we had the upper hand of them, and in five minutes it was all over.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "My God!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "Was there ever a slaughter-house like that ship!", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "Prendergast was like a raging devil, and he picked the soldiers up as if they had been children and threw them overboard alive or dead.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "There was one sergeant that was horribly wounded and yet kept on swimming for a surprising time, until some one in mercy blew out his brains.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "When the fighting was over there was no one left of our enemies except just the warders, the mates, and the doctor.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_10", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "\\"'It was over them that the great quarrel arose.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "There were many of us who were glad enough to win back our freedom, and yet who had no wish to have murder on our souls.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "It was one thing to knock the soldiers over with their muskets in their hands, and it was another to stand by while men were being killed in cold blood.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "Eight of us, five convicts and three sailors, said that we would not see it done.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "But there was no moving Prendergast and those who were with him.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "Our only chance of safety lay in making a clean job of it, said he, and he would not leave a tongue with power to wag in a witness-box.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "It nearly came to our sharing the fate of the prisoners, but at last he said that if we wished we might take a boat and go.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "We jumped at the offer, for we were already sick of these bloodthirsty doings, and we saw that there would be worse before it was done.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "We were given a suit of sailors' togs each, a barrel of water, two casks, one of junk and one of biscuits, and a compass.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "Prendergast threw us over a chart, told us that we were shipwrecked mariners whose ship had foundered in lat.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "15º N.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sir_edward_holly	entity	character	sir edward holly	\N	{"firstSection": "gloria-scott-section_2"}
gloria-scott	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": ", and then cut the painter and let us go.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "and let us go.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "\\"'And now I come to the most surprising part of my story, my dear son.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "The seamen had hauled the foreyard aback during the rising, but now as we left them they brought it square again, and as there was a light wind from the north and east the barque began to draw slowly away from us.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "Our boat lay, rising and falling, upon the long, smooth rollers, and Evans and I, who were the most educated of the party, were sitting in the sheets working out our position and planning what coast we should make for.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "It was a nice question, for the Cape de Verds were about five hundred miles to the north of us, and the African coast about seven hundred to the east.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "On the whole, as the wind was coming round to the north, we thought that Sierra Leone might be best, and turned our head in that direction, the barque being at that time nearly hull down on our starboard quarter.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "Suddenly as we looked at her we saw a dense black cloud of smoke shoot up from her, which hung like a monstrous tree upon the sky line.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "A few seconds later a roar like thunder burst upon our ears, and as the smoke thinned away there was no sign left of the _Gloria Scott_.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "In an instant we swept the boat's head round again and pulled with all our strength for the place where the haze still trailing over the water marked the scene of this catastrophe.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "\\"'It was a long hour before we reached it, and at first we feared that we had come too late to save any one.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "A splintered boat and a number of crates and fragments of spars rising and falling on the waves showed us where the vessel had foundered; but there was no sign of life, and we had turned away in despair when we heard a cry for help, and saw at some distance a piece of wreckage with a man lying stretched across it.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "When we pulled him aboard the boat he proved to be a young seaman of the name of Hudson, who was so burned and exhausted that he could give us no account of what had happened until the following morning.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_11", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "\\"'It seemed that after we had left, Prendergast and his gang had proceeded to put to death the five remaining prisoners.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "The two warders had been shot and thrown overboard, and so also had the third mate.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "Prendergast then descended into the 'tween-decks and with his own hands cut the throat of the unfortunate surgeon.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "There only remained the first mate, who was a bold and active man.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "When he saw the convict approaching him with the bloody knife in his hand he kicked off his bonds, which he had somehow contrived to loosen, and rushing down the deck he plunged into the after-hold.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "\\"'A dozen convicts, who descended with their pistols in search of him, found him with a match-box in his hand seated beside an open powder barrel, which was one of a hundred carried on board, and swearing that he would blow all hands up if he were in any way molested.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "An instant later the explosion occurred, though Hudson thought it was caused by the misdirected bullet of one of the convicts rather than the mate's match.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "Be the cause what it may, it was the end of the _Gloria Scott_ and of the rabble who held command of her.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "\\"'Such, in a few words, my dear boy, is the history of this terrible business in which I was involved.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "Next day we were picked up by the brig _Hotspur_, bound for Australia, whose captain found no difficulty in believing that we were the survivors of a passenger ship which had foundered.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "The transport ship _Gloria Scott_ was set down by the Admiralty as being lost at sea, and no word has ever leaked out as to her true fate.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "After an excellent voyage the _Hotspur_ landed us at Sydney, where Evans and I changed our names and made our way to the diggings, where, among the crowds who were gathered from all nations, we had no difficulty in losing our former identities.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "\\"'The rest I need not relate.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "We prospered, we travelled, we came back as rich colonials to England, and we bought country estates.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	j_a	entity	character	j a	\N	{"firstSection": "gloria-scott-section_2"}
gloria-scott	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "For more than twenty years we have led peaceful and useful lives, and we hoped that our past was forever buried.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "Imagine, then, my feelings when in the seaman who came to us I recognised instantly the man who had been picked off the wreck.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "He had tracked us down somehow, and had set himself to live upon our fears.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "You will understand now how it was that I strove to keep the peace with him, and you will in some measure sympathise with me in the fears which fill me, now that he has gone from me to his other victim with threats upon his tongue.'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "\\"Underneath is written in a hand so shaky as to be hardly legible, 'Beddoes writes in cipher to say H.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "has told all.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "Sweet Lord, have mercy on our souls!'", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "\\"That was the narrative which I read that night to young Trevor, and I think, Watson, that under the circumstances it was a dramatic one.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "The good fellow was heartbroken at it, and went out to the Terai tea planting, where I hear that he is doing well.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "As to the sailor and Beddoes, neither of them was ever heard of again after that day on which the letter of warning was written.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "They both disappeared utterly and completely.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "No complaint had been lodged with the police, so that Beddoes had mistaken a threat for a deed.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "Hudson had been seen lurking about, and it was believed by the police that he had done away with Beddoes and had fled.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "For myself I believe that the truth was exactly the opposite.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "I think that it is most probable that Beddoes, pushed to desperation and believing himself to have been already betrayed, had revenged himself upon Hudson, and had fled from the country with as much money as he could lay his hands on.", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "Those are the facts of the case, Doctor, and if they are of any use to your collection, I am sure that they are very heartily at your service.\\"", "section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "entities": []}
