gloria-scott	event_1_1	event	\N	Holmes presents papers about the Gloria Scott case	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3", "sentence_4"], "communicatesContent": "I have some papers here which I really think, Watson, that it would be worth your while to glance over. These are the documents in the extraordinary case of the Gloria Scott, and this is the message which struck Justice of the Peace Trevor dead with horror when he read it."}
gloria-scott	event_1_2	event	\N	Holmes takes a cylinder from a drawer and hands Watson a note	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_5"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_1_3	event	\N	The note states its message	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": "short_note", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_6", "sentence_7"], "communicatesContent": "The supply of game for London is going steadily up. Head-keeper Hudson, we believe, has been now told to receive all orders for fly-paper and for preservation of your hen-pheasant's life."}
gloria-scott	event_1_4	event	\N	Watson reads the note and Holmes chuckles at his expression	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_8", "sentence_9"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_1_5	event	\N	Watson asks why Holmes said he should study the case	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_14", "sentence_15"], "communicatesContent": "But why did you say just now that there were very particular reasons why I should study this case?"}
gloria-scott	event_1_6	event	\N	Holmes says this was the first case he was ever engaged in	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_16"], "communicatesContent": "Because it was the first in which I was ever engaged."}
gloria-scott	event_1_7	event	\N	Holmes sits forward and spreads the documents on his knees	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_18", "sentence_19"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_1_8	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson about Victor Trevor	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_20", "sentence_21"], "communicatesContent": "You never heard me talk of Victor Trevor?"}
gloria-scott	event_1_9	event	\N	Holmes describes Victor Trevor as his only college friend	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_22", "sentence_23", "sentence_24", "sentence_25", "sentence_26", "sentence_27", "sentence_28", "sentence_29", "sentence_30"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_1_10	event	\N	Victor Trevor invites Holmes to his father's place and Holmes accepts	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_30"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_1_11	event	\N	Holmes describes Old Trevor and Donnithorpe	0	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_1", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_31", "sentence_32", "sentence_33", "sentence_34", "sentence_35"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_2_1	event	\N	Victor Trevor's father discusses his life and responds to Holmes's deductions	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_44", "sentence_45", "sentence_46", "sentence_47", "sentence_48", "sentence_49", "sentence_50", "sentence_51", "sentence_52", "sentence_53", "sentence_54", "sentence_55", "sentence_56", "sentence_57", "sentence_58", "sentence_59", "sentence_60", "sentence_61", "sentence_62", "sentence_63", "sentence_64", "sentence_65", "sentence_66", "sentence_67", "sentence_68", "sentence_69", "sentence_70", "sentence_71", "sentence_72", "sentence_73", "sentence_74", "sentence_75", "sentence_76", "sentence_77", "sentence_78", "sentence_79", "sentence_80", "sentence_81"], "communicatesContent": "Come, now, Mr. Holmes. I'm an excellent subject, if you can deduce anything from me."}
gloria-scott	event_2_2	event	\N	Holmes says Trevor has gone about in fear of a personal attack	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_48"], "communicatesContent": "I might suggest that you have gone about in fear of some personal attack within the last twelve months."}
gloria-scott	event_2_3	event	\N	Old Trevor acknowledges Holmes's deduction and explains the reason for his caution	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_49", "sentence_50", "sentence_51", "sentence_52"], "communicatesContent": "Well, that's true enough. When we broke up that poaching gang, they swore to knife us, and Sir Edward Holly has actually been attacked. I've always been on my guard since then, though I have no idea how you know it."}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "\\"'Brunton, the butler, was in the library.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
gloria-scott	event_2_4	event	\N	Holmes says Trevor's stick has been modified into a weapon	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_53", "sentence_54", "sentence_55", "sentence_56"], "communicatesContent": "You have a very handsome stick. By the inscription I observed that you had not had it more than a year. But you have taken some pains to bore the head of it and pour melted lead into the hole so as to make it a formidable weapon. I argued that you would not take such precautions unless you had some danger to fear."}
gloria-scott	event_2_5	event	\N	Holmes says Trevor boxed in his youth and points to his ears as evidence	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_59", "sentence_60", "sentence_61", "sentence_62", "sentence_63", "sentence_64", "sentence_65"], "communicatesContent": "You have boxed a good deal in your youth. No. It is your ears. They have the peculiar flattening and thickening which marks the boxing man."}
gloria-scott	event_2_6	event	\N	Holmes says Trevor dug for money, visited New Zealand, and visited Japan	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_66", "sentence_67", "sentence_68", "sentence_69", "sentence_70", "sentence_71", "sentence_72"], "communicatesContent": "You have done a good deal of digging by your callosities. You have been in New Zealand. You have visited Japan."}
gloria-scott	event_2_7	event	\N	Holmes says Trevor was closely associated with someone whose initials were J. A.	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_73", "sentence_74"], "communicatesContent": "You have been most intimately associated with some one whose initials were J. A., and whom you afterwards were eager to entirely forget."}
gloria-scott	event_2_8	event	\N	Old Trevor faints and is then revived	1	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_75", "sentence_76", "sentence_77", "sentence_78", "sentence_79", "sentence_80", "sentence_81"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_3_1	event	\N	Holmes describes how he recognized the tattooed initials and their attempted removal	2	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_89", "sentence_90", "sentence_91", "sentence_92", "sentence_93", "sentence_94"], "communicatesContent": "When you bared your arm to draw that fish into the boat I saw that J. A. had been tattooed in the bend of the elbow. The letters were still legible, but it was perfectly clear from their blurred appearance, and from the staining of the skin round them, that efforts had been made to obliterate them. It was obvious, then, that those initials had once been very familiar to you, and that you had afterwards wished to forget them."}
gloria-scott	event_3_2	event	\N	Victor Trevor speaks in relief and ends the discussion of the initials	2	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_95", "sentence_96", "sentence_97", "sentence_98", "sentence_99", "sentence_100"], "communicatesContent": "What an eye you have! It is just as you say. But we won't talk of it. Of all ghosts the ghosts of our old lovers are the worst. Come into the billiard-room and have a quiet cigar."}
gloria-scott	event_3_3	event	\N	Trevor's manner toward the narrator becomes suspicious	2	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_101", "sentence_102", "sentence_103"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_3_4	event	\N	Watson ends his visit after causing Trevor uneasiness	2	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_104", "sentence_105", "sentence_106"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_3_5	event	\N	A maid announces that a man at the door wants to see Mr. Trevor	2	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "speakerId": "hudson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_107", "sentence_108", "sentence_109", "sentence_110", "sentence_111", "sentence_112"], "communicatesContent": "There was a man at the door who wanted to see Mr. Trevor. He would not give any. He says that you know him, and that he only wants a moment's conversation."}
gloria-scott	event_3_6	event	\N	The sailor comes across the lawn to meet Trevor	2	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_113", "sentence_114", "sentence_115", "sentence_116", "sentence_117", "sentence_118", "sentence_119", "sentence_120"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_4_1	event	\N	Mr. Trevor speaks privately to the sailor and sends him to the kitchen for food and drink	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_127", "sentence_128", "sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_131", "sentence_132", "sentence_133", "sentence_134", "sentence_135"], "communicatesContent": "Go into the kitchen, and you will get food and drink. I have no doubt that I shall find you a situation."}
gloria-scott	event_4_2	event	\N	The sailor goes off to the kitchen	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_135"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_4_3	event	\N	Mr. Trevor explains to Watson and Holmes that he had been shipmate with the sailor	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_136"], "communicatesContent": "having been shipmate with the man when he was going back to the diggings"}
gloria-scott	event_4_4	event	\N	Mr. Trevor leaves the lawn and goes indoors	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_136"], "communicatesContent": null}
