gloria-scott	event_4_12	event	\N	Watson asks what the matter is	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_146", "sentence_147"], "communicatesContent": "What is the matter?"}
gloria-scott	event_4_13	event	\N	Victor Trevor says the governor has apoplexy and nervous shock and may not be found alive	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_148", "sentence_149", "sentence_150"], "communicatesContent": "Apoplexy. Nervous shock, He's been on the verge all day. I doubt if we shall find him alive."}
gloria-scott	event_4_14	event	\N	Watson asks what caused the governor's condition	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_152", "sentence_153"], "communicatesContent": "What caused it?"}
gloria-scott	event_4_15	event	\N	Victor Trevor says the evening visitor was the devil himself	3	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_4", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_154", "sentence_155", "sentence_156", "sentence_157", "sentence_158", "sentence_159", "sentence_160", "sentence_161", "sentence_162", "sentence_163", "sentence_164", "sentence_165", "sentence_166", "sentence_167", "sentence_168", "sentence_169"], "communicatesContent": "It was the devil, Holmes. Yes, it was the devil himself. We have not had a peaceful hour since—not one. The governor has never held up his head from that evening, and now the life has been crushed out of him and his heart broken, all through this accursed Hudson. Ah, that is what I would give so much to know. The kindly, charitable, good old governor—how could he have fallen into the clutches of such a ruffian! But I am so glad that you have come, Holmes. I trust very much to your judgment and discretion, and I know that you will advise me for the best."}
gloria-scott	event_5_1	event	\N	Trevor and his companion travel along the country road toward the squire's dwelling	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_170", "sentence_171"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_5_2	event	\N	Hudson explains that he was promoted from gardener to butler and mistreated the household	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "hudson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_172", "sentence_173", "sentence_174", "sentence_175"], "communicatesContent": "My father made the fellow gardener, and then, as that did not satisfy him, he was promoted to be butler. The house seemed to be at his mercy, and he wandered about and did what he chose in it. The maids complained of his drunken habits and his vile language. The dad raised their wages all round to recompense them for the annoyance."}
gloria-scott	event_5_3	event	\N	Hudson takes the boat and his father's best gun for shooting trips	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_176"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_5_4	event	\N	Trevor restrains himself from attacking Hudson	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_177", "sentence_178"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_5_5	event	\N	Hudson becomes more intrusive and is turned out of the room after an insolent reply	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_179", "sentence_180"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_5_6	event	\N	Old Trevor asks Victor to apologise to Hudson and Victor refuses	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_181", "sentence_182"], "communicatesContent": "whether I would mind apologising to Hudson"}
gloria-scott	event_5_7	event	\N	Old Trevor speaks privately with Victor and writes busily in the study	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_183", "sentence_184", "sentence_185", "sentence_186", "sentence_187"], "communicatesContent": "it is all very well to talk, but you don't know how I am placed. But you shall know, Victor. I'll see that you shall know, come what may. You wouldn't believe harm of your poor old father, would you, lad?"}
gloria-scott	event_5_8	event	\N	Hudson announces that he is leaving Norfolk for Hampshire	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "hudson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_188", "sentence_189", "sentence_190", "sentence_191", "sentence_192"], "communicatesContent": "I've had enough of Norfolk. I'll run down to Mr. Beddoes in Hampshire. He'll be as glad to see me as you were, I daresay."}
gloria-scott	event_5_9	event	\N	Old Trevor asks whether Hudson is leaving in an unkind spirit and Hudson demands an apology	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_193", "sentence_194"], "communicatesContent": "You're not going away in an unkind spirit, Hudson, I hope"}
gloria-scott	event_5_10	event	\N	Old Trevor tells Victor that he has treated Hudson roughly and Victor denies it	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_195", "sentence_196"], "communicatesContent": "Victor, you will acknowledge that you have used this worthy fellow rather roughly"}
gloria-scott	event_5_11	event	\N	Hudson threatens the household and leaves the room and house	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": "hudson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_197", "sentence_198", "sentence_199", "sentence_200", "sentence_201"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, you do, do you? Very good, mate. We'll see about that!"}
gloria-scott	event_5_12	event	\N	Old Trevor becomes nervous and paces in his room at night	4	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_201", "sentence_202"], "communicatesContent": null}
