gloria-scott	event_6_14	event	\N	The doctor reports that the papers were in the back drawer of the Japanese cabinet	5	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_225"], "communicatesContent": "Only that the papers were in the back drawer of the Japanese cabinet."}
gloria-scott	event_6_15	event	\N	Trevor brings the papers into the study	5	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_237"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_6_16	event	\N	Trevor hands over the short note	5	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_238"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_7_1	event	\N	A warning note is read aloud	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_250", "sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253"], "communicatesContent": "The game is up. Hudson has told all. Fly for your life."}
gloria-scott	event_7_2	event	\N	Victor Trevor reacts to the warning	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256", "sentence_257"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_7_3	event	\N	Holmes explains the ciphered words in the note	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260", "sentence_261", "sentence_262", "sentence_263"], "communicatesContent": "It means nothing to the message, but it might mean a good deal to us if we had no other means of discovering the sender. You see that he has begun by writing 'The game is,' and so on. Afterwards he had, to fulfill the prearranged cipher, to fill in any two words in each space. He would naturally use the first words which came to his mind, and if there were so many which referred to sport among them, you may be tolerably sure that he is either an ardent shot or interested in breeding."}
gloria-scott	event_7_4	event	\N	Victor Trevor identifies Beddoes as connected with shooting preserves	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_264", "sentence_265"], "communicatesContent": "My poor father used to have an invitation from him to shoot over his preserves every autumn."}
gloria-scott	event_7_5	event	\N	Holmes concludes the note comes from Beddoes	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_266", "sentence_267"], "communicatesContent": "It is undoubtedly from him that the note comes. It only remains for us to find out what this secret was which the sailor Hudson seems to have held over the heads of these two wealthy and respected men."}
gloria-scott	event_7_6	event	\N	Victor Trevor hands over the statement and asks for it to be read	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "victor_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_268", "sentence_269", "sentence_270", "sentence_271", "sentence_272"], "communicatesContent": "From you I shall have no secrets. Here is the statement which was drawn up by my father when he knew that the danger from Hudson had become imminent. I found it in the Japanese cabinet, as he told the doctor. Take it and read it to me, for I have neither the strength nor the courage to do it myself."}
gloria-scott	event_7_7	event	\N	Holmes produces and reads the papers	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_273", "sentence_274", "sentence_275", "sentence_276", "sentence_277", "sentence_278", "sentence_279"], "communicatesContent": "These are the very papers, Watson, which he handed to me, and I will read them to you, as I read them in the old study that night to him. They are endorsed outside: 'Some particulars of the voyage of the bark Gloria Scott, from her leaving Falmouth on the 8th October, 1855, to her destruction in N. lat. 15º 20', W. long. 25º 14' on Nov. 6th.' It is in the form of a letter."}
gloria-scott	event_7_8	event	\N	The father’s letter is read	6	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_7", "speakerId": "old_trevor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_280", "sentence_281", "sentence_282", "sentence_283"], "communicatesContent": "My dear, dear son,—Now that approaching disgrace begins to darken the closing years of my life, I can write with all truth and honesty that it is not the terror of the law, it is not the loss of my position in the county, nor is it my fall in the eyes of all who have known me, which cuts me to the heart; but it is the thought that you should come to blush for me—you who love me and who have seldom, I hope, had reason to do other than respect me. But if the blow falls which is forever hanging over me, then I should wish you to read this, that you may know straight from me how far I have been to blame. If by any chance this paper should be still undestroyed and should fall into your hands, I conjure you, by all you hold sacred, by the memory of your dear mother, and by the love which had been between us, to hurl it into the fire and to never give one thought to it again."}
gloria-scott	event_12_4	event	\N	The survivors are picked up by the Hotspur	11	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_420"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_8_1	event	\N	James Armitage says his name is not Trevor and states his earlier identity	7	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "speakerId": "james_armitage", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_286", "sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": "My name, dear lad, is not Trevor. I was James Armitage in my younger days."}
gloria-scott	event_8_2	event	\N	James Armitage enters a London banking house and is convicted and sentenced to transportation	7	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_288"], "communicatesContent": null}
