gloria-scott	event_8_7	event	\N	The young convict neighbour is placed next to James Armitage in the ship's cells	7	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_299", "sentence_300", "sentence_301", "sentence_302", "sentence_303"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_8_8	event	\N	James Armitage hears the neighbour whisper after he cuts an opening between their boards	7	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_8", "speakerId": "young_convict_neighbour", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_306", "sentence_307", "sentence_308"], "communicatesContent": "Hallao, chummy! what's your name, and what are you here for?"}
gloria-scott	event_9_1	event	\N	The speaker answers Prendergast and asks who he is talking with	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_309", "sentence_310"], "communicatesContent": "who I was talking with"}
gloria-scott	event_9_2	event	\N	Prendergast identifies himself and boasts about his name	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "prendergast", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_310", "sentence_311"], "communicatesContent": "I'm Jack Prendergast, and by God! You'll learn to bless my name before you've done with me."}
gloria-scott	event_9_3	event	\N	The speaker recalls hearing of Prendergast's case	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_312"], "communicatesContent": null}
gloria-scott	event_9_4	event	\N	Prendergast boasts that none of the stolen money was recovered	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "prendergast", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_320", "sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325", "sentence_327", "sentence_328", "sentence_329"], "communicatesContent": "I'd had nearly a quarter of a million, hadn't I? ... none was recovered, eh? ... the balance is right between my finger and thumb ... I've got more pounds to my name than you've hairs on your head."}
gloria-scott	event_9_5	event	\N	Prendergast explains that a ship plot exists and that he leads it	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "prendergast", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_335", "sentence_336"], "communicatesContent": "there really was a plot to gain command of the vessel. A dozen of the prisoners had hatched it before they came aboard, Prendergast was the leader, and his money was the motive power."}
gloria-scott	event_9_6	event	\N	Prendergast describes his partner as the ship's chaplain and says the crew, warders, Mercer, and the second mate are his	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "prendergast", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_338", "sentence_339", "sentence_340", "sentence_341", "sentence_342", "sentence_343"], "communicatesContent": "I'd a partner ... he's the chaplain of this ship ... The crew are his, body and soul ... He's got two of the warders and Mercer, the second mate ... he'd get the captain himself, if he thought him worth it."}
gloria-scott	event_9_7	event	\N	The speaker asks what they are to do next	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_344", "sentence_345"], "communicatesContent": "What are we to do, then?"}
gloria-scott	event_9_8	event	\N	Prendergast says they will make the soldiers bleed	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "prendergast", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_346", "sentence_347", "sentence_348"], "communicatesContent": "We'll make the coats of some of these soldiers redder than ever the tailor did."}
gloria-scott	event_9_9	event	\N	The speaker warns that the soldiers are armed and Prendergast answers that the prisoners will also be armed and should test their mate	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_349", "sentence_350", "sentence_351", "sentence_352"], "communicatesContent": "But they are armed."}
gloria-scott	event_9_10	event	\N	Prendergast instructs the speaker to test the prisoner on the left	8	{"section": "gloria-scott-section_9", "speakerId": "prendergast", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_352"], "communicatesContent": "You speak to your mate upon the left to-night, and see if he is to be trusted."}
