musgrave-ritual	sentence_1	lexical	\N	\N	0	{"text": "VI.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_2	lexical	\N	\N	1	{"text": "The Musgrave Ritual", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "An anomaly which often struck me in the character of my friend Sherlock Holmes was that, although in his methods of thought he was the neatest and most methodical of mankind, and although also he affected a certain quiet primness of dress, he was none the less in his personal habits one of the most untidy men that ever drove a fellow-lodger to distraction.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "Not that I am in the least conventional in that respect myself.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "The rough-and-tumble work in Afghanistan, coming on the top of a natural Bohemianism of disposition, has made me rather more lax than befits a medical man.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "But with me there is a limit, and when I find a man who keeps his cigars in the coal-scuttle, his tobacco in the toe end of a Persian slipper, and his unanswered correspondence transfixed by a jack-knife into the very centre of his wooden mantelpiece, then I begin to give myself virtuous airs.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "I have always held, too, that pistol practice should be distinctly an open-air pastime; and when Holmes, in one of his queer humours, would sit in an armchair with his hair-trigger and a hundred Boxer cartridges, and proceed to adorn the opposite wall with a patriotic V.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "R.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "done in bullet-pocks, I felt strongly that neither the atmosphere nor the appearance of our room was improved by it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "Our chambers were always full of chemicals and of criminal relics which had a way of wandering into unlikely positions, and of turning up in the butter-dish or in even less desirable places.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "But his papers were my great crux.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "He had a horror of destroying documents, especially those which were connected with his past cases, and yet it was only once in every year or two that he would muster energy to docket and arrange them; for, as I have mentioned somewhere in these incoherent memoirs, the outbursts of passionate energy when he performed the remarkable feats with which his name is associated were followed by reactions of lethargy during which he would lie about with his violin and his books, hardly moving save from the sofa to the table.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "The corridors at Hurlstone have their walls largely decorated with trophies of old weapons.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "Thus month after month his papers accumulated, until every corner of the room was stacked with bundles of manuscript which were on no account to be burned, and which could not be put away save by their owner.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "One winter's night, as we sat together by the fire, I ventured to suggest to him that, as he had finished pasting extracts into his common-place book, he might employ the next two hours in making our room a little more habitable.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "He could not deny the justice of my request, so with a rather rueful face he went off to his bedroom, from which he returned presently pulling a large tin box behind him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "This he placed in the middle of the floor and, squatting down upon a stool in front of it, he threw back the lid.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "I could see that it was already a third full of bundles of paper tied up with red tape into separate packages.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "\\"There are cases enough here, Watson,\\" said he, looking at me with mischievous eyes.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "\\"I think that if you knew all that I had in this box you would ask me to pull some out instead of putting others in.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"These are the records of your early work, then?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "\\"I have often wished that I had notes of those cases.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "\\"Yes, my boy, these were all done prematurely before my biographer had come to glorify me.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "He lifted bundle after bundle in a tender, caressing sort of way.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "\\"They are not all successes, Watson,\\" said he.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "\\"But there are some pretty little problems among them.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "Here's the record of the Tarleton murders, and the case of Vamberry, the wine merchant, and the adventure of the old Russian woman, and the singular affair of the aluminium crutch, as well as a full account of Ricoletti of the club-foot, and his abominable wife.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "And here—ah, now, this really is something a little _recherché_.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "He dived his arm down to the bottom of the chest, and brought up a small wooden box with a sliding lid, such as children's toys are kept in.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "From within he produced a crumpled piece of paper, an old-fashioned brass key, a peg of wood with a ball of string attached to it, and three rusty old disks of metal.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "\\"Well, my boy, what do you make of this lot?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "he asked, smiling at my expression.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "\\"It is a curious collection.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "\\"Very curious, and the story that hangs round it will strike you as being more curious still.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "\\"These relics have a history then?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "\\"So much so that they _are_ history.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "\\"What do you mean by that?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes picked them up one by one, and laid them along the edge of the table.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "Then he reseated himself in his chair and looked them over with a gleam of satisfaction in his eyes.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "\\"These,\\" said he, \\"are all that I have left to remind me of the adventure of the Musgrave Ritual.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "I had heard him mention the case more than once, though I had never been able to gather the details.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "\\"I should be so glad,\\" said I, \\"if you would give me an account of it.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "\\"And leave the litter as it is?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "he cried, mischievously.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "\\"Your tidiness won't bear much strain after all, Watson.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "I had, then, to find where the far end of the shadow would fall when the sun was just clear of the oak.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "But I should be glad that you should add this case to your annals, for there are points in it which make it quite unique in the criminal records of this or, I believe, of any other country.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "A collection of my trifling achievements would certainly be incomplete which contained no account of this very singular business.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "\\"You may remember how the affair of the _Gloria Scott_, and my conversation with the unhappy man whose fate I told you of, first turned my attention in the direction of the profession which has become my life's work.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "You see me now when my name has become known far and wide, and when I am generally recognised both by the public and by the official force as being a final court of appeal in doubtful cases.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "Even when you knew me first, at the time of the affair which you have commemorated in 'A Study in Scarlet,' I had already established a considerable, though not a very lucrative, connection.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "You can hardly realize, then, how difficult I found it at first, and how long I had to wait before I succeeded in making any headway.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "\\"When I first came up to London I had rooms in Montague Street, just round the corner from the British Museum, and there I waited, filling in my too abundant leisure time by studying all those branches of science which might make me more efficient.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "Now and again cases came in my way, principally through the introduction of old fellow-students, for during my last years at the University there was a good deal of talk there about myself and my methods.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "The third of these cases was that of the Musgrave Ritual, and it is to the interest which was aroused by that singular chain of events, and the large issues which proved to be at stake, that I trace my first stride towards the position which I now hold.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "\\"Reginald Musgrave had been in the same college as myself, and I had some slight acquaintance with him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "He was not generally popular among the undergraduates, though it always seemed to me that what was set down as pride was really an attempt to cover extreme natural diffidence.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "In appearance he was a man of exceedingly aristocratic type, thin, high-nosed, and large-eyed, with languid and yet courtly manners.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "He was indeed a scion of one of the very oldest families in the kingdom, though his branch was a cadet one which had separated from the northern Musgraves some time in the sixteenth century, and had established itself in western Sussex, where the Manor House of Hurlstone is perhaps the oldest inhabited building in the county.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "Something of his birthplace seemed to cling to the man, and I never looked at his pale, keen face or the poise of his head without associating him with grey archways and mullioned windows and all the venerable wreckage of a feudal keep.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "Once or twice we drifted into talk, and I can remember that more than once he expressed a keen interest in my methods of observation and inference.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_2", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "\\"For four years I had seen nothing of him until one morning he walked into my room in Montague Street.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "He had changed little, was dressed like a young man of fashion—he was always a bit of a dandy—and preserved the same quiet, suave manner which had formerly distinguished him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "' I asked, after we had cordially shaken hands.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "after we had cordially shaken hands.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "\\"'You probably heard of my poor father's death,' said he; 'he was carried off about two years ago.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "Since then I have of course had the Hurlstone estates to manage, and as I am member for my district as well, my life has been a busy one.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "But I understand, Holmes, that you are turning to practical ends those powers with which you used to amaze us?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "\\"'Yes,' said I, 'I have taken to living by my wits.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "\\"'I am delighted to hear it, for your advice at present would be exceedingly valuable to me.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "We have had some very strange doings at Hurlstone, and the police have been able to throw no light upon the matter.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "It is really the most extraordinary and inexplicable business.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "From one of these I picked a battle-axe, and then, leaving my candle behind me, I crept on tiptoe down the passage and peeped in at the open door.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "\\"You can imagine with what eagerness I listened to him, Watson, for the very chance for which I had been panting during all those months of inaction seemed to have come within my reach.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "In my inmost heart I believed that I could succeed where others failed, and now I had the opportunity to test myself.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "\\"'Pray, let me have the details,' I cried.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "\\"Reginald Musgrave sat down opposite to me, and lit the cigarette which I had pushed towards him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "\\"'You must know,' said he, 'that though I am a bachelor, I have to keep up a considerable staff of servants at Hurlstone, for it is a rambling old place, and takes a good deal of looking after.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "I preserve, too, and in the pheasant months I usually have a house-party, so that it would not do to be short-handed.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "Altogether there are eight maids, the cook, the butler, two footmen, and a boy.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "The garden and the stables of course have a separate staff.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "\\"'Of these servants the one who had been longest in our service was Brunton the butler.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "He was a young schoolmaster out of place when he was first taken up by my father, but he was a man of great energy and character, and he soon became quite invaluable in the household.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "He was a well-grown, handsome man, with a splendid forehead, and though he has been with us for twenty years he cannot be more than forty now.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "With his personal advantages and his extraordinary gifts—for he can speak several languages and play nearly every musical instrument—it is wonderful that he should have been satisfied so long in such a position, but I suppose that he was comfortable, and lacked energy to make any change.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "The butler of Hurlstone is always a thing that is remembered by all who visit us.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "\\"'But this paragon has one fault.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "He is a bit of a Don Juan, and you can imagine that for a man like him it is not a very difficult part to play in a quiet country district.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "When he was married it was all right, but since he has been a widower we have had no end of trouble with him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "A few months ago we were in hopes that he was about to settle down again for he became engaged to Rachel Howells, our second housemaid; but he has thrown her over since then and taken up with Janet Tregellis, the daughter of the head gamekeeper.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "Rachel—who is a very good girl, but of an excitable Welsh temperament—had a sharp touch of brain-fever, and goes about the house now—or did until yesterday—like a black-eyed shadow of her former self.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "That was our first drama at Hurlstone; but a second one came to drive it from our minds, and it was prefaced by the disgrace and dismissal of butler Brunton.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "\\"'This was how it came about.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "I have said that the man was intelligent, and this very intelligence has caused his ruin, for it seems to have led to an insatiable curiosity about things which did not in the least concern him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "I had no idea of the lengths to which this would carry him, until the merest accident opened my eyes to it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "\\"'I have said that the house is a rambling one.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "One day last week—on Thursday night, to be more exact—I found that I could not sleep, having foolishly taken a cup of strong _café noir_ after my dinner.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "After struggling against it until two in the morning, I felt that it was quite hopeless, so I rose and lit the candle with the intention of continuing a novel which I was reading.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "The book, however, had been left in the billiard-room, so I pulled on my dressing-gown and started off to get it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "\\"'In order to reach the billiard-room I had to descend a flight of stairs and then to cross the head of a passage which led to the library and the gun-room.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "You can imagine my surprise when, as I looked down this corridor, I saw a glimmer of light coming from the open door of the library.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "I had myself extinguished the lamp and closed the door before coming to bed.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "He was sitting, fully dressed, in an easy-chair, with a slip of paper which looked like a map upon his knee, and his forehead sunk forward upon his hand in deep thought.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "I stood dumb with astonishment, watching him from the darkness.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "A small taper on the edge of the table shed a feeble light which sufficed to show me that he was fully dressed.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "Suddenly, as I looked, he rose from his chair, and walking over to a bureau at the side, he unlocked it and drew out one of the drawers.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "From this he took a paper, and returning to his seat he flattened it out beside the taper on the edge of the table, and began to study it with minute attention.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "My indignation at this calm examination of our family documents overcame me so far that I took a step forward, and Brunton, looking up, saw me standing in the doorway.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "He sprang to his feet, his face turned livid with fear, and he thrust into his breast the chart-like paper which he had been originally studying.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "\\"'\\"So!\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "said I.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "\\"This is how you repay the trust which we have reposed in you.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "You will leave my service to-morrow.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "\\"'He bowed with the look of a man who is utterly crushed, and slunk past me without a word.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "The taper was still on the table, and by its light I glanced to see what the paper was which Brunton had taken from the bureau.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "To my surprise it was nothing of any importance at all, but simply a copy of the questions and answers in the singular old observance called the Musgrave Ritual.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "It is a sort of ceremony peculiar to our family, which each Musgrave for centuries past has gone through on his coming of age—a thing of private interest, and perhaps of some little importance to the archaeologist, like our own blazonings and charges, but of no practical use whatever.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "\\"'We had better come back to the paper afterwards,' said I.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "\\"'If you think it really necessary,' he answered, with some hesitation.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "'To continue my statement, however: I relocked the bureau, using the key which Brunton had left, and I had turned to go when I was surprised to find that the butler had returned, and was standing before me.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "\\"'\\"Mr. Musgrave, sir,\\" he cried, in a voice which was hoarse with emotion, \\"I can't bear disgrace, sir.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "I've always been proud above my station in life, and disgrace would kill me.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "My blood will be on your head, sir—it will, indeed—if you drive me to despair.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "If you cannot keep me after what has passed, then for God's sake let me give you notice and leave in a month, as if of my own free will.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "I could stand that, Mr. Musgrave, but not to be cast out before all the folk that I know so well.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "\\"'\\"You don't deserve much consideration, Brunton,\\" I answered.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "\\"Your conduct has been most infamous.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "However, as you have been a long time in the family, I have no wish to bring public disgrace upon you.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "A month, however is too long.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "Take yourself away in a week, and give what reason you like for going.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "\\"'\\"Only a week, sir?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "he cried, in a despairing voice.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "\\"A fortnight—say at least a fortnight!\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "\\"'\\"A week,\\" I repeated, \\"and you may consider yourself to have been very leniently dealt with.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "\\"'He crept away, his face sunk upon his breast, like a broken man, while I put out the light and returned to my room.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "\\"'For two days after this Brunton was most assiduous in his attention to his duties.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "I made no allusion to what had passed, and waited with some curiosity to see how he would cover his disgrace.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "On the third morning, however he did not appear, as was his custom, after breakfast to receive my instructions for the day.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "As I left the dining-room I happened to meet Rachel Howells, the maid.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "I have told you that she had only recently recovered from an illness, and was looking so wretchedly pale and wan that I remonstrated with her for being at work.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "\\"'\\"You should be in bed,\\" I said.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "\\"Come back to your duties when you are stronger.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "\\"'She looked at me with so strange an expression that I began to suspect that her brain was affected.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "\\"'\\"I am strong enough, Mr. Musgrave,\\" said she.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "\\"'\\"We will see what the doctor says,\\" I answered.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "\\"You must stop work now, and when you go downstairs just say that I wish to see Brunton.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "\\"'\\"The butler is gone,\\" said she.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "\\"'\\"Gone!", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "Gone where?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "\\"'\\"He is gone.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "No one has seen him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "He is not in his room.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "Oh, yes, he is gone, he is gone!\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "She fell back against the wall with shriek after shriek of laughter, while I, horrified at this sudden hysterical attack, rushed to the bell to summon help.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "The girl was taken to her room, still screaming and sobbing, while I made inquiries about Brunton.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "There was no doubt about it that he had disappeared.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "His bed had not been slept in, he had been seen by no one since he had retired to his room the night before, and yet it was difficult to see how he could have left the house, as both windows and doors were found to be fastened in the morning.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "His clothes, his watch, and even his money were in his room, but the black suit which he usually wore was missing.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "His slippers, too, were gone, but his boots were left behind.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "Where then could butler Brunton have gone in the night, and what could have become of him now?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "\\"'Of course we searched the house from cellar to garret, but there was no trace of him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "It is, as I have said, a labyrinth of an old house, especially the original wing, which is now practically uninhabited; but we ransacked every room and cellar without discovering the least sign of the missing man.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "It was incredible to me that he could have gone away leaving all his property behind him, and yet where could he be?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "I called in the local police, but without success.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "Rain had fallen on the night before and we examined the lawn and the paths all round the house, but in vain.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "Matters were in this state, when a new development quite drew our attention away from the original mystery.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "\\"'For two days Rachel Howells had been so ill, sometimes delirious, sometimes hysterical, that a nurse had been employed to sit up with her at night.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "\\"All right, Watson, I don't intend to meddle.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "On the third night after Brunton's disappearance, the nurse, finding her patient sleeping nicely, had dropped into a nap in the armchair, when she woke in the early morning to find the bed empty, the window open, and no signs of the invalid.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "I was instantly aroused, and, with the two footmen, started off at once in search of the missing girl.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "It was not difficult to tell the direction which she had taken, for, starting from under her window, we could follow her footmarks easily across the lawn to the edge of the mere, where they vanished close to the gravel path which leads out of the grounds.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "The lake there is eight feet deep, and you can imagine our feelings when we saw that the trail of the poor demented girl came to an end at the edge of it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "\\"'Of course, we had the drags at once, and set to work to recover the remains, but no trace of the body could we find.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "On the other hand, we brought to the surface an object of a most unexpected kind.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "It was a linen bag which contained within it a mass of old rusted and discoloured metal and several dull-coloured pieces of pebble or glass.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "This strange find was all that we could get from the mere, and, although we made every possible search and inquiry yesterday, we know nothing of the fate either of Rachel Howells or of Richard Brunton.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "The county police are at their wits' end, and I have come up to you as a last resource.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "\\"You can imagine, Watson, with what eagerness I listened to this extraordinary sequence of events, and endeavoured to piece them together, and to devise some common thread upon which they might all hang.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "The butler was gone.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "The maid was gone.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "The maid had loved the butler, but had afterwards had cause to hate him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "She was of Welsh blood, fiery and passionate.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "She had been terribly excited immediately after his disappearance.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "She had flung into the lake a bag containing some curious contents.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "These were all factors which had to be taken into consideration, and yet none of them got quite to the heart of the matter.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "What was the starting-point of this chain of events?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "There lay the end of this tangled line.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "\\"'I must see that paper, Musgrave,' said I, 'which this butler of yours thought it worth his while to consult, even at the risk of the loss of his place.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "\\"'It is rather an absurd business, this ritual of ours,' he answered.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "'But it has at least the saving grace of antiquity to excuse it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "I have a copy of the questions and answers here if you care to run your eye over them.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_6", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "\\"He handed me the very paper which I have here, Watson, and this is the strange catechism to which each Musgrave had to submit when he came to man's estate.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "I will read you the questions and answers as they stand.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "\\"'Whose was it?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "\\"'His who is gone.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "\\"'Who shall have it?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "\\"'He who will come.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "\\"'Where was the sun?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "\\"'Over the oak.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "\\"'Where was the shadow?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "\\"'Under the elm.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "\\"How was it stepped?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "\\"'North by ten and by ten, east by five and by five, south by two and by two, west by one and by one, and so under.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "\\"'What shall we give for it?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "\\"'All that is ours.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "\\"'Why should we give it?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "\\"'For the sake of the trust.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "\\"'The original has no date, but is in the spelling of the middle of the seventeenth century,' remarked Musgrave.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "'I am afraid, however, that it can be of little help to you in solving this mystery.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "\\"'At least,' said I, 'it gives us another mystery, and one which is even more interesting than the first.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "It may be that the solution of the one may prove to be the solution of the other.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "You will excuse me, Musgrave, if I say that your butler appears to me to have been a very clever man, and to have had a clearer insight than ten generations of his masters.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "\\"'I hardly follow you,' said Musgrave.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "'The paper seems to me to be of no practical importance.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "\\"'But to me it seems immensely practical, and I fancy that Brunton took the same view.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "He had probably seen it before that night on which you caught him.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "\\"'It is very possible.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "We took no pains to hide it.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "\\"'He simply wished, I should imagine, to refresh his memory upon that last occasion.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "He had, as I understand, some sort of map or chart which he was comparing with the manuscript, and which he thrust into his pocket when you appeared.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "\\"'That is true.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "But what could he have to do with this old family custom of ours, and what does this rigmarole mean?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "\\"'I don't think that we should have much difficulty in determining that,' said I; 'with your permission we will take the first train down to Sussex, and go a little more deeply into the matter upon the spot.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "\\"The same afternoon saw us both at Hurlstone.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "Possibly you have seen pictures and read descriptions of the famous old building, so I will confine my account of it to saying that it is built in the shape of an L, the long arm being the more modern portion, and the shorter the ancient nucleus, from which the other had developed.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "Over the low, heavily-lintelled door, in the centre of this old part, is chiseled the date, 1607, but experts are agreed that the beams and stonework are really much older than this.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "The enormously thick walls and tiny windows of this part had in the last century driven the family into building the new wing, and the old one was used now as a storehouse and a cellar, when it was used at all.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "A splendid park with fine old timber surrounds the house, and the lake, to which my client had referred, lay close to the avenue, about two hundred yards from the building.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "\\"I was already firmly convinced, Watson, that there were not three separate mysteries here, but one only, and that if I could read the Musgrave Ritual aright I should hold in my hand the clue which would lead me to the truth concerning both the butler Brunton and the maid Howells.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "To that then I turned all my energies.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "Why should this servant be so anxious to master this old formula?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "Evidently because he saw something in it which had escaped all those generations of country squires, and from which he expected some personal advantage.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "What was it then, and how had it affected his fate?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "\\"Arrest these men, Inspector!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "\\"It was perfectly obvious to me, on reading the Ritual, that the measurements must refer to some spot to which the rest of the document alluded, and that if we could find that spot, we should be in a fair way towards finding what the secret was which the old Musgraves had thought it necessary to embalm in so curious a fashion.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "There were two guides given us to start with, an oak and an elm.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "As to the oak there could be no question at all.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "Right in front of the house, upon the left-hand side of the drive, there stood a patriarch among oaks, one of the most magnificent trees that I have ever seen.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "\\"'That was there when your Ritual was drawn up,' said I, as we drove past it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "\\"'It was there at the Norman Conquest in all probability,' he answered.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "'It has a girth of twenty-three feet.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "any old elms?' I asked.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "\\"'There used to be a very old one over yonder but it was struck by lightning ten years ago, and we cut down the stump.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "\\"'You can see where it used to be?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "\\"'Oh, yes.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "\\"'There are no other elms?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "\\"'No old ones, but plenty of beeches.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "\\"'I should like to see where it grew.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "\\"We had driven up in a dog-cart, and my client led me away at once, without our entering the house, to the scar on the lawn where the elm had stood.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "It was nearly midway between the oak and the house.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "My investigation seemed to be progressing.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "e it is impossible to find out how high the elm was?' I asked.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "\\"'I can give you it at once.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "It was sixty-four feet.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "' I asked, in surprise.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "ow it?' I asked, in surprise.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "\\"'When my old tutor used to give me an exercise in trigonometry, it always took the shape of measuring heights.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "When I was a lad I worked out every tree and building in the estate.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "\\"This was an unexpected piece of luck.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "My data were coming more quickly than I could have reasonably hoped.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "\\"'Tell me,' I asked, 'did your butler ever ask you such a question?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "\\"Reginald Musgrave looked at me in astonishment.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "'Now that you call it to my mind,' he answered, 'Brunton _did_ ask me about the height of the tree some months ago, in connection with some little argument with the groom.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "\\"This was excellent news, Watson, for it showed me that I was on the right road.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "I looked up at the sun.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "It was low in the heavens, and I calculated that in less than an hour it would lie just above the topmost branches of the old oak.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "One condition mentioned in the Ritual would then be fulfilled.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "And the shadow of the elm must mean the farther end of the shadow, otherwise the trunk would have been chosen as the guide.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "\\"That must have been difficult, Holmes, when the elm was no longer there.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "\\"Well, at least I knew that if Brunton could do it, I could also.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "Besides, there was no real difficulty.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "I went with Musgrave to his study and whittled myself this peg, to which I tied this long string with a knot at each yard.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "Then I took two lengths of a fishing-rod, which came to just six feet, and I went back with my client to where the elm had been.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "The sun was just grazing the top of the oak.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "I fastened the rod on end, marked out the direction of the shadow, and measured it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "It was nine feet in length.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "\\"Of course the calculation now was a simple one.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "If a rod of six feet threw a shadow of nine, a tree of sixty-four feet would throw one of ninety-six, and the line of the one would of course be the line of the other.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "I measured out the distance, which brought me almost to the wall of the house, and I thrust a peg into the spot.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "You can imagine my exultation, Watson, when within two inches of my peg I saw a conical depression in the ground.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "I knew that it was the mark made by Brunton in his measurements, and that I was still upon his trail.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "\\"From this starting-point I proceeded to step, having first taken the cardinal points by my pocket-compass.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "Ten steps with each foot took me along parallel with the wall of the house, and again I marked my spot with a peg.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "Then I carefully paced off five to the east and two to the south.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "It brought me to the very threshold of the old door.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "Two steps to the west meant now that I was to go two paces down the stone-flagged passage, and this was the place indicated by the Ritual.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "\\"Never have I felt such a cold chill of disappointment, Watson.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "For a moment it seemed to me that there must be some radical mistake in my calculations.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "The setting sun shone full upon the passage floor, and I could see that the old, foot-worn grey stones with which it was paved were firmly cemented together, and had certainly not been moved for many a long year.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "Brunton had not been at work here.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "I tapped upon the floor, but it sounded the same all over, and there was no sign of any crack or crevice.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "But, fortunately, Musgrave, who had begun to appreciate the meaning of my proceedings, and who was now as excited as myself, took out his manuscript to check my calculation.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "\\"'And under,' he cried.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "'You have omitted the \\"and under.\\"'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "\\"I had thought that it meant that we were to dig, but now, of course, I saw at once that I was wrong.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "' I cried.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "a cellar under this then?' I cried.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "\\"'Yes, and as old as the house.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "Down here, through this door.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "\\"We went down a winding stone stair, and my companion, striking a match, lit a large lantern which stood on a barrel in the corner.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "In an instant it was obvious that we had at last come upon the true place, and that we had not been the only people to visit the spot recently.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	brass_key	entity	object	Old-fashioned brass key	\N	{"description": "An old-fashioned brass key taken from the box.", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_2"}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "\\"It had been used for the storage of wood, but the billets, which had evidently been littered over the floor, were now piled at the sides, so as to leave a clear space in the middle.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "In this space lay a large and heavy flagstone with a rusted iron ring in the centre to which a thick shepherd's-check muffler was attached.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "' cried my client.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "'That's Brunton's muffler.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "I have seen it on him, and could swear to it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "ear to it. What has the villain been doing here?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "\\"At my suggestion a couple of the county police were summoned to be present, and I then endeavoured to raise the stone by pulling on the cravat.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "I could only move it slightly, and it was with the aid of one of the constables that I succeeded at last in carrying it to one side.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "A black hole yawned beneath into which we all peered, while Musgrave, kneeling at the side, pushed down the lantern.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "\\"A small chamber about seven feet deep and four feet square lay open to us.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "At one side of this was a squat, brass-bound wooden box, the lid of which was hinged upwards, with this curious old-fashioned key projecting from the lock.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "It was furred outside by a thick layer of dust, and damp and worms had eaten through the wood, so that a crop of livid fungi was growing on the inside of it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "Several discs of metal, old coins apparently, such as I hold here, were scattered over the bottom of the box, but it contained nothing else.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "\\"At the moment, however, we had no thought for the old chest, for our eyes were riveted upon that which crouched beside it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "It was the figure of a man, clad in a suit of black, who squatted down upon his hams with his forehead sunk upon the edge of the box and his two arms thrown out on each side of it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "The attitude had drawn all the stagnant blood to the face, and no man could have recognised that distorted liver-coloured countenance; but his height, his dress, and his hair were all sufficient to show my client, when we had drawn the body up, that it was indeed his missing butler.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "He had been dead some days, but there was no wound or bruise upon his person to show how he had met his dreadful end.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "When his body had been carried from the cellar we found ourselves still confronted with a problem which was almost as formidable as that with which we had started.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "\\"I confess that so far, Watson, I had been disappointed in my investigation.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "I had reckoned upon solving the matter when once I had found the place referred to in the Ritual; but now I was there, and was apparently as far as ever from knowing what it was which the family had concealed with such elaborate precautions.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "It is true that I had thrown a light upon the fate of Brunton, but now I had to ascertain how that fate had come upon him, and what part had been played in the matter by the woman who had disappeared.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "I sat down upon a keg in the corner and thought the whole matter carefully over.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "\\"You know my methods in such cases, Watson.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "I put myself in the man's place and, having first gauged his intelligence, I try to imagine how I should myself have proceeded under the same circumstances.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "In this case the matter was simplified by Brunton's intelligence being quite first-rate, so that it was unnecessary to make any allowance for the personal equation, as the astronomers have dubbed it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "He knew that something valuable was concealed.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "He had spotted the place.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "He found that the stone which covered it was just too heavy for a man to move unaided.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "What would he do next?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	peg_of_wood	entity	object	Peg of wood with string	\N	{"description": "A peg of wood with a ball of string attached to it.", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_2"}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "He could not get help from outside, even if he had some one whom he could trust, without the unbarring of doors and considerable risk of detection.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "It was better, if he could, to have his helpmate inside the house.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "But whom could he ask?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "This girl had been devoted to him.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "A man always finds it hard to realize that he may have finally lost a woman's love, however badly he may have treated her.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "He would try by a few attentions to make his peace with the girl Howells, and then would engage her as his accomplice.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "Together they would come at night to the cellar, and their united force would suffice to raise the stone.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "So far I could follow their actions as if I had actually seen them.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "\\"But for two of them, and one a woman, it must have been heavy work the raising of that stone.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "A burly Sussex policeman and I had found it no light job.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "What would they do to assist them?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "Probably what I should have done myself.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "I rose and examined carefully the different billets of wood which were scattered round the floor.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "Almost at once I came upon what I expected.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "One piece, about three feet in length, had a very marked indentation at one end, while several were flattened at the sides as if they had been compressed by some considerable weight.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "Evidently, as they had dragged the stone up they had thrust the chunks of wood into the chink, until at last, when the opening was large enough to crawl through, they would hold it open by a billet placed lengthwise, which might very well become indented at the lower end, since the whole weight of the stone would press it down on to the edge of this other slab.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "So far I was still on safe ground.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "\\"And now how was I to proceed to reconstruct this midnight drama?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "Clearly, only one could fit into the hole, and that one was Brunton.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "The girl must have waited above.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "Brunton then unlocked the box, handed up the contents presumably—since they were not to be found—and then—and then what happened?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "\\"What smouldering fire of vengeance had suddenly sprung into flame in this passionate Celtic woman's soul when she saw the man who had wronged her—wronged her, perhaps, far more than we suspected—in her power?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "Was it a chance that the wood had slipped, and that the stone had shut Brunton into what had become his sepulchre?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "Had she only been guilty of silence as to his fate?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "Or had some sudden blow from her hand dashed the support away and sent the slab crashing down into its place?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "Be that as it might, I seemed to see that woman's figure still clutching at her treasure trove and flying wildly up the winding stair, with her ears ringing perhaps with the muffled screams from behind her and with the drumming of frenzied hands against the slab of stone which was choking her faithless lover's life out.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "\\"Here was the secret of her blanched face, her shaken nerves, her peals of hysterical laughter on the next morning.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "But what had been in the box?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "What had she done with that?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "Of course, it must have been the old metal and pebbles which my client had dragged from the mere.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "She had thrown them in there at the first opportunity to remove the last trace of her crime.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "\\"For twenty minutes I had sat motionless, thinking the matter out.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "Musgrave still stood with a very pale face, swinging his lantern and peering down into the hole.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "\\"'These are coins of Charles the First,' said he, holding out the few which had been in the box; 'you see we were right in fixing our date for the Ritual.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "\\"'We may find something else of Charles the First,' I cried, as the probable meaning of the first two questions of the Ritual broke suddenly upon me.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "'Let me see the contents of the bag which you fished from the mere.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "\\"We ascended to his study, and he laid the _débris_ before me.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "I could understand his regarding it as of small importance when I looked at it, for the metal was almost black and the stones lustreless and dull.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "I rubbed one of them on my sleeve, however, and it glowed afterwards like a spark in the dark hollow of my hand.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "The metal work was in the form of a double ring, but it had been bent and twisted out of its original shape.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "\\"'You must bear in mind,' said I, 'that the Royal party made head in England even after the death of the King, and that when they at last fled they probably left many of their most precious possessions buried behind them, with the intention of returning for them in more peaceful times.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "\\"'My ancestor, Sir Ralph Musgrave, was a prominent Cavalier and the right-hand man of Charles the Second in his wanderings,' said my friend.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "' I answered.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "'Well now, I think that really should give us the last link that we wanted.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "at we wanted. I must congratulate you on coming into the possession, though in rather a tragic manner of a relic which is of great intrinsic value, but of even greater importance as an historical curiosity.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "' he gasped in astonishment.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "ed in astonishment.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "\\"'It is nothing less than the ancient crown of the Kings of England.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "\\"'The crown!'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_11", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "\\"'Precisely.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "Consider what the Ritual says: How does it run?", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "\\"Whose was it?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "\\"His who is gone.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "That was after the execution of Charles.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "Then, \\"Who shall have it?\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "\\"He who will come.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "That was Charles the Second, whose advent was already foreseen.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "There can, I think, be no doubt that this battered and shapeless diadem once encircled the brows of the royal Stuarts.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "\\"'And how came it in the pond?'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "' And with that I sketched out to him the whole long chain of surmise and of proof which I had constructed.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "The twilight had closed in and the moon was shining brightly in the sky before my narrative was finished.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "hining brightly in the sky before my narrative was finished.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "' asked Musgrave, pushing back the relic into its linen bag.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "n he returned?' asked Musgrave, pushing back the relic into its linen bag.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "\\"'Ah, there you lay your finger upon the one point which we shall probably never be able to clear up.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "It is likely that the Musgrave who held the secret died in the interval, and by some oversight left this guide to his descendant without explaining the meaning of it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "From that day to this it has been handed down from father to son, until at last it came within reach of a man who tore its secret out of it and lost his life in the venture.'", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "\\"And that's the story of the Musgrave Ritual, Watson.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "They have the crown down at Hurlstone—though they had some legal bother and a considerable sum to pay before they were allowed to retain it.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "I am sure that if you mentioned my name they would be happy to show it to you.", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "Of the woman nothing was ever heard, and the probability is that she got away out of England and carried herself and the memory of her crime to some land beyond the seas.\\"", "section": "musgrave-ritual-section_12", "entities": []}
musgrave-ritual	sherlock_holmes	entity	character	Sherlock Holmes	\N	{"description": "Detective and friend of Watson", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1"}
musgrave-ritual	watson	entity	character	Watson	\N	{"description": "Narrator and companion of Holmes", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1"}
musgrave-ritual	afghanistan	entity	location	Afghanistan	\N	{"description": "Place where Watson served", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1"}
musgrave-ritual	the_musgrave_ritual	entity	case	The Musgrave Ritual	\N	{"client": "watson", "source": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "outcome": "unresolved", "crime_type": "other", "description": "An investigation referred to by name in the section", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1", "primary_location": "musgrave_hall"}
musgrave-ritual	chemicals	entity	object	Chemicals	\N	{"description": "Chemical materials kept in the room", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1"}
musgrave-ritual	criminal_relics	entity	object	Criminal relics	\N	{"description": "Items connected with criminal cases kept in the room", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1"}
musgrave-ritual	cigars	entity	object	Cigars	\N	{"description": "Cigars kept by Holmes", "firstSection": "musgrave-ritual-section_1"}
