musgrave-ritual	event_4_9	event	\N	The narrator confronts Brunton and orders him to leave service the next day	3	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_110", "sentence_111", "sentence_112", "sentence_113", "sentence_114", "sentence_115", "sentence_116"], "communicatesContent": "\\"So! This is how you repay the trust which we have reposed in you. You will leave my service to-morrow.\\""}
musgrave-ritual	event_4_10	event	\N	Brunton bows and leaves without a word	3	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_116"], "communicatesContent": null}
musgrave-ritual	event_4_11	event	\N	The narrator examines the paper Brunton took and finds the Musgrave Ritual copy	3	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_117", "sentence_118", "sentence_119"], "communicatesContent": null}
musgrave-ritual	event_5_1	event	\N	They return to the paper afterwards	4	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_120", "sentence_121"], "communicatesContent": "We had better come back to the paper afterwards."}
musgrave-ritual	event_5_2	event	\N	Watson relocks the bureau and is interrupted by the returned butler	4	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_122"], "communicatesContent": null}
musgrave-ritual	event_5_3	event	\N	Brunton pleads to avoid public disgrace and asks to resign with notice	4	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "speakerId": "brunton", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_123", "sentence_124", "sentence_125", "sentence_126", "sentence_127"], "communicatesContent": "Mr. Musgrave, sir, I can't bear disgrace, sir. I've always been proud above my station in life, and disgrace would kill me. My blood will be on your head, sir—it will, indeed—if you drive me to despair. If you cannot keep me after what has passed, then for God's sake let me give you notice and leave in a month, as if of my own free will. I could stand that, Mr. Musgrave, but not to be cast out before all the folk that I know so well."}
musgrave-ritual	event_9_2	event	\N	The detective finds a conical depression near the peg	8	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_283", "sentence_284"], "communicatesContent": null}
musgrave-ritual	event_9_3	event	\N	The detective steps off distances and marks another peg	8	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_285", "sentence_286", "sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	section_31	section	\N	Section 31	30	{"wordCount": 284}
musgrave-ritual	event_5_4	event	\N	Musgrave dismisses Brunton within a week	4	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_128", "sentence_129", "sentence_130", "sentence_131", "sentence_132", "sentence_133", "sentence_134", "sentence_135", "sentence_136"], "communicatesContent": "You don't deserve much consideration, Brunton. Your conduct has been most infamous. However, as you have been a long time in the family, I have no wish to bring public disgrace upon you. A month, however is too long. Take yourself away in a week, and give what reason you like for going. A week, and you may consider yourself to have been very leniently dealt with."}
musgrave-ritual	event_5_5	event	\N	Brunton leaves crestfallen and Musgrave returns to his room	4	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_137"], "communicatesContent": null}
