musgrave-ritual	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes examines the oak beside the house and measures its girth	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_237", "sentence_238", "sentence_239", "sentence_240", "sentence_241", "sentence_242"], "communicatesContent": "That was there when your Ritual was drawn up."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_4	event	\N	Reginald Musgrave states that the oak was likely present at the Norman Conquest and has a girth of twenty-three feet	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_240", "sentence_241"], "communicatesContent": "It was there at the Norman Conquest in all probability. It has a girth of twenty-three feet."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_5	event	\N	Holmes asks about old elms and Reginald Musgrave answers that one elm was struck by lightning and the stump was cut down	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_243", "sentence_244", "sentence_245", "sentence_246", "sentence_247", "sentence_248"], "communicatesContent": "There used to be a very old one over yonder but it was struck by lightning ten years ago, and we cut down the stump. No old ones, but plenty of beeches."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_6	event	\N	Holmes asks to see where the elm grew and is led to the scar on the lawn	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_249", "sentence_250", "sentence_251"], "communicatesContent": "I should like to see where it grew."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_7	event	\N	Reginald Musgrave states the elm had been nearly midway between the oak and the house	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_251"], "communicatesContent": "It was nearly midway between the oak and the house."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_8	event	\N	Holmes questions the elm's height and Reginald Musgrave says it was sixty-four feet	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_253", "sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256", "sentence_257", "sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260"], "communicatesContent": "It was sixty-four feet."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_9	event	\N	Reginald Musgrave explains that he had practiced measuring tree and building heights when young	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_259", "sentence_260"], "communicatesContent": "When my old tutor used to give me an exercise in trigonometry, it always took the shape of measuring heights. When I was a lad I worked out every tree and building in the estate."}
musgrave-ritual	event_8_10	event	\N	Holmes learns that Brunton had asked about the height of the tree months earlier	7	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_8", "speakerId": "reginald_musgrave", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_263", "sentence_264", "sentence_265"], "communicatesContent": "Brunton did ask me about the height of the tree some months ago, in connection with some little argument with the groom."}
