musgrave-ritual	event_10_2	event	\N	Holmes and Watson carry the body from the cellar	9	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_322"], "communicatesContent": null}
musgrave-ritual	event_10_3	event	\N	Holmes states that he had been disappointed in his investigation	9	{"section": "musgrave-ritual-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325"], "communicatesContent": "I had been disappointed in my investigation. I had reckoned upon solving the matter when once I had found the place referred to in the Ritual; but now I was there, and was apparently as far as ever from knowing what it was which the family had concealed with such elaborate precautions. It is true that I had thrown a light upon the fate of Brunton, but now I had to ascertain how that fate had come upon him, and what part had been played in the matter by the woman who had disappeared."}
