reigate-squires	sentence_1	lexical	\N	\N	0	{"text": "VII.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_2	lexical	\N	\N	1	{"text": "The Reigate Squires", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "It was some time before the health of my friend Mr. Sherlock Holmes recovered from the strain caused by his immense exertions in the spring of '87.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "The whole question of the Netherland-Sumatra Company and of the colossal schemes of Baron Maupertuis are too recent in the minds of the public, and are too intimately concerned with politics and finance to be fitting subjects for this series of sketches.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "They led, however, in an indirect fashion to a singular and complex problem which gave my friend an opportunity of demonstrating the value of a fresh weapon among the many with which he waged his life-long battle against crime.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "On referring to my notes I see that it was upon the 14th of April that I received a telegram from Lyons which informed me that Holmes was lying ill in the Hotel Dulong.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "Within twenty-four hours I was in his sick-room, and was relieved to find that there was nothing formidable in his symptoms.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "Even his iron constitution, however, had broken down under the strain of an investigation which had extended over two months, during which period he had never worked less than fifteen hours a day, and had more than once, as he assured me, kept to his task for five days at a stretch.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "Even the triumphant issue of his labours could not save him from reaction after so terrible an exertion, and at a time when Europe was ringing with his name and when his room was literally ankle-deep with congratulatory telegrams I found him a prey to the blackest depression.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "Even the knowledge that he had succeeded where the police of three countries had failed, and that he had outmanœuvred at every point the most accomplished swindler in Europe, was insufficient to rouse him from his nervous prostration.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "Three days later we were back in Baker Street together; but it was evident that my friend would be much the better for a change, and the thought of a week of spring time in the country was full of attractions to me also.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "My old friend, Colonel Hayter, who had come under my professional care in Afghanistan, had now taken a house near Reigate in Surrey, and had frequently asked me to come down to him upon a visit.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "On the last occasion he had remarked that if my friend would only come with me he would be glad to extend his hospitality to him also.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "A little diplomacy was needed, but when Holmes understood that the establishment was a bachelor one, and that he would be allowed the fullest freedom, he fell in with my plans and a week after our return from Lyons we were under the Colonel's roof.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "Hayter was a fine old soldier who had seen much of the world, and he soon found, as I had expected, that Holmes and he had much in common.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "On the evening of our arrival we were sitting in the Colonel's gun-room after dinner, Holmes stretched upon the sofa, while Hayter and I looked over his little armoury of fire-arms.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "\\"By the way,\\" said he suddenly, \\"I think I'll take one of these pistols upstairs with me in case we have an alarm.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "\\"An alarm!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "said I.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"Yes, we've had a scare in this part lately.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "Old Acton, who is one of our county magnates, had his house broken into last Monday.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "No great damage done, but the fellows are still at large.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "\\"No clue?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "asked Holmes, cocking his eye at the Colonel.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "\\"None as yet.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "But the affair is a petty one, one of our little country crimes, which must seem too small for your attention, Mr. Holmes, after this great international affair.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_1", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "Holmes waved away the compliment, though his smile showed that it had pleased him.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "\\"Was there any feature of interest?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "\\"I fancy not.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "The thieves ransacked the library and got very little for their pains.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "The whole place was turned upside down, drawers burst open, and presses ransacked, with the result that an odd volume of Pope's 'Homer,' two plated candlesticks, an ivory letter-weight, a small oak barometer, and a ball of twine are all that have vanished.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "\\"What an extraordinary assortment!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "I exclaimed.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "\\"Oh, the fellows evidently grabbed hold of everything they could get.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "Holmes grunted from the sofa.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "\\"The county police ought to make something of that,\\" said he; \\"why, it is surely obvious that—\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "But I held up a warning finger.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "\\"You are here for a rest, my dear fellow.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "For Heaven's sake don't get started on a new problem when your nerves are all in shreds.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "Holmes shrugged his shoulders with a glance of comic resignation towards the Colonel, and the talk drifted away into less dangerous channels.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "It was destined, however, that all my professional caution should be wasted, for next morning the problem obtruded itself upon us in such a way that it was impossible to ignore it, and our country visit took a turn which neither of us could have anticipated.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_32	section	\N	Section 32	31	{"wordCount": 153}
reigate-squires	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "We were at breakfast when the Colonel's butler rushed in with all his propriety shaken out of him.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "\\"Have you heard the news, sir?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "he gasped.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "\\"At the Cunningham's sir!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "\\"Burglary!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "cried the Colonel, with his coffee-cup in mid-air.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "\\"Murder!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "The Colonel whistled.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "\\"By Jove!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "\\"Who's killed, then?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "The J.P.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "or his son?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "\\"Neither, sir.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "It was William the coachman.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "Shot through the heart, sir, and never spoke again.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "\\"Who shot him, then?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "\\"The burglar, sir.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "He was off like a shot and got clean away.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "He'd just broke in at the pantry window when William came on him and met his end in saving his master's property.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "\\"What time?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "\\"It was last night, sir, somewhere about twelve.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "\\"Ah, then, we'll step over afterwards,\\" said the Colonel, coolly settling down to his breakfast again.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "\\"It's a baddish business,\\" he added when the butler had gone; \\"he's our leading man about here, is old Cunningham, and a very decent fellow too.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "He'll be cut up over this, for the man has been in his service for years and was a good servant.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "It's evidently the same villains who broke into Acton's.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "\\"And stole that very singular collection,\\" said Holmes, thoughtfully.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "\\"Precisely.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "\\"Hum!", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "It may prove the simplest matter in the world, but all the same at first glance this is just a little curious, is it not?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "A gang of burglars acting in the country might be expected to vary the scene of their operations, and not to crack two cribs in the same district within a few days.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "When you spoke last night of taking precautions I remember that it passed through my mind that this was probably the last parish in England to which the thief or thieves would be likely to turn their attention—which shows that I have still much to learn.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "\\"I fancy it's some local practitioner,\\" said the Colonel.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "\\"In that case, of course, Acton's and Cunningham's are just the places he would go for, since they are far the largest about here.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "\\"And richest?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "\\"Well, they ought to be, but they've had a lawsuit for some years which has sucked the blood out of both of them, I fancy.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "Old Acton has some claim on half Cunningham's estate, and the lawyers have been at it with both hands.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_2", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "\\"If it's a local villain there should not be much difficulty in running him down,\\" said Holmes with a yawn.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_33	section	\N	Section 33	32	{"wordCount": 154}
reigate-squires	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "\\"Inspector Forrester, sir,\\" said the butler, throwing open the door.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "The official, a smart, keen-faced young fellow, stepped into the room.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "\\"Good-morning, Colonel,\\" said he; \\"I hope I don't intrude, but we hear that Mr. Holmes of Baker Street is here.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "The Colonel waved his hand towards my friend, and the Inspector bowed.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "\\"We thought that perhaps you would care to step across, Mr. Holmes.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "\\"The fates are against you, Watson,\\" said he, laughing.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "\\"We were chatting about the matter when you came in, Inspector.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "Perhaps you can let us have a few details.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "As he leaned back in his chair in the familiar attitude I knew that the case was hopeless.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "\\"We had no clue in the Acton affair.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "But here we have plenty to go on, and there's no doubt it is the same party in each case.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "The man was seen.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "\\"Ah!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "\\"Yes, sir.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "But he was off like a deer after the shot that killed poor William Kirwan was fired.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "Mr. Cunningham saw him from the bedroom window, and Mr. Alec Cunningham saw him from the back passage.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "It was quarter to twelve when the alarm broke out.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "Mr. Cunningham had just got into bed, and Mr. Alec was smoking a pipe in his dressing-gown.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "They both heard William the coachman calling for help, and Mr. Alec ran down to see what was the matter.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "The back door was open, and as he came to the foot of the stairs he saw two men wrestling together outside.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "One of them fired a shot, the other dropped, and the murderer rushed across the garden and over the hedge.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "Mr. Cunningham, looking out of his bedroom, saw the fellow as he gained the road, but lost sight of him at once.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "Mr. Alec stopped to see if he could help the dying man, and so the villain got clean away.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "Beyond the fact that he was a middle-sized man and dressed in some dark stuff, we have no personal clue; but we are making energetic inquiries, and if he is a stranger we shall soon find him out.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "\\"What was this William doing there?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "Did he say anything before he died?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "\\"Not a word.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "He lives at the lodge with his mother, and as he was a very faithful fellow we imagine that he walked up to the house with the intention of seeing that all was right there.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "Of course this Acton business has put every one on their guard.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "The robber must have just burst open the door—the lock has been forced—when William came upon him.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "\\"Did William say anything to his mother before going out?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "\\"She is very old and deaf, and we can get no information from her.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "The shock has made her half-witted, but I understand that she was never very bright.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "There is one very important circumstance, however.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "Look at this!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "He took a small piece of torn paper from a note-book and spread it out upon his knee.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "\\"This was found between the finger and thumb of the dead man.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "It appears to be a fragment torn from a larger sheet.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "You will observe that the hour mentioned upon it is the very time at which the poor fellow met his fate.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "You see that his murderer might have torn the rest of the sheet from him or he might have taken this fragment from the murderer.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "It reads almost as though it were an appointment.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_3", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "Holmes took up the scrap of paper, a facsimile of which is here reproduced.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "scrap of paper", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "\\"Presuming that it is an appointment,\\" continued the Inspector, \\"it is of course a conceivable theory that this William Kirwan—though he had the reputation of being an honest man, may have been in league with the thief.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "He may have met him there, may even have helped him to break in the door, and then they may have fallen out between themselves.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "\\"This writing is of extraordinary interest,\\" said Holmes, who had been examining it with intense concentration.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "\\"These are much deeper waters than I had thought.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "He sank his head upon his hands, while the Inspector smiled at the effect which his case had had upon the famous London specialist.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "\\"Your last remark,\\" said Holmes, presently, \\"as to the possibility of there being an understanding between the burglar and the servant, and this being a note of appointment from one to the other, is an ingenious and not entirely impossible supposition.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "But this writing opens up—\\" He sank his head into his hands again and remained for some minutes in the deepest thought.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "When he raised his face again, I was surprised to see that his cheek was tinged with colour, and his eyes as bright as before his illness.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "He sprang to his feet with all his old energy.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "\\"I'll tell you what,\\" said he, \\"I should like to have a quiet little glance into the details of this case.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "There is something in it which fascinates me extremely.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "If you will permit me, Colonel, I will leave my friend Watson and you, and I will step round with the Inspector to test the truth of one or two little fancies of mine.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "I will be with you again in half an hour.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "An hour and half had elapsed before the Inspector returned alone.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "\\"Mr. Holmes is walking up and down in the field outside,\\" said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "\\"He wants us all four to go up to the house together.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "\\"To Mr. Cunningham's?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "\\"Yes, sir.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "\\"What for?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "The Inspector shrugged his shoulders.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "\\"I don't quite know, sir.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "Between ourselves, I think Mr. Holmes had not quite got over his illness yet.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "He's been behaving very queerly, and he is very much excited.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "\\"I don't think you need alarm yourself,\\" said I.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "\\"I have usually found that there was method in his madness.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "\\"Some folks might say there was madness in his method,\\" muttered the Inspector.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "\\"But he's all on fire to start, Colonel, so we had best go out if you are ready.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "We found Holmes pacing up and down in the field, his chin sunk upon his breast, and his hands thrust into his trousers pockets.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "\\"The matter grows in interest,\\" said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "\\"Watson, your country-trip has been a distinct success.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "I have had a charming morning.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "\\"You have been up to the scene of the crime, I understand,\\" said the Colonel.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "\\"Yes; the Inspector and I have made quite a little reconnaissance together.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "\\"Any success?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "\\"Well, we have seen some very interesting things.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "I'll tell you what we did as we walk.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "First of all, we saw the body of this unfortunate man.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "He certainly died from a revolver wound as reported.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "\\"Had you doubted it, then?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "\\"Oh, it is as well to test everything.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "Our inspection was not wasted.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "We then had an interview with Mr. Cunningham and his son, who were able to point out the exact spot where the murderer had broken through the garden-hedge in his flight.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "That was of great interest.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "\\"Naturally.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "\\"Then we had a look at this poor fellow's mother.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "We could get no information from her, however, as she is very old and feeble.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_4", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "\\"And what is the result of your investigations?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "\\"The conviction that the crime is a very peculiar one.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "Perhaps our visit now may do something to make it less obscure.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "I think that we are both agreed, Inspector that the fragment of paper in the dead man's hand, bearing, as it does, the very hour of his death written upon it, is of extreme importance.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "\\"It should give a clue, Mr. Holmes.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "\\"It _does_ give a clue.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "Whoever wrote that note was the man who brought William Kirwan out of his bed at that hour.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "But where is the rest of that sheet of paper?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "\\"I examined the ground carefully in the hope of finding it,\\" said the Inspector.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "\\"It was torn out of the dead man's hand.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "Why was some one so anxious to get possession of it?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "Because it incriminated him.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "And what would he do with it?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "Thrust it into his pocket, most likely, never noticing that a corner of it had been left in the grip of the corpse.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "If we could get the rest of that sheet it is obvious that we should have gone a long way towards solving the mystery.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "\\"Yes, but how can we get at the criminal's pocket before we catch the criminal?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "\\"Well, well, it was worth thinking over.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "Then there is another obvious point.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "The note was sent to William.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "The man who wrote it could not have taken it; otherwise, of course, he might have delivered his own message by word of mouth.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "Who brought the note, then?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "Or did it come through the post?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "\\"I have made inquiries,\\" said the Inspector.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "\\"William received a letter by the afternoon post yesterday.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "The envelope was destroyed by him.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "\\"Excellent!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "cried Holmes, clapping the Inspector on the back.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "\\"You've seen the postman.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "It is a pleasure to work with you.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "Well, here is the lodge, and if you will come up, Colonel, I will show you the scene of the crime.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "We passed the pretty cottage where the murdered man had lived, and walked up an oak-lined avenue to the fine old Queen Anne house, which bears the date of Malplaquet upon the lintel of the door.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "Holmes and the Inspector led us round it until we came to the side gate, which is separated by a stretch of garden from the hedge which lines the road.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "A constable was standing at the kitchen door.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "\\"Throw the door open, officer,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "\\"Now, it was on those stairs that young Mr. Cunningham stood and saw the two men struggling just where we are.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "Old Mr. Cunningham was at that window—the second on the left—and he saw the fellow get away just to the left of that bush.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "Then Mr. Alec ran out and knelt beside the wounded man.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "The ground is very hard, you see, and there are no marks to guide us.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "As he spoke two men came down the garden path, from round the angle of the house.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "The one was an elderly man, with a strong, deep-lined, heavy-eyed face; the other a dashing young fellow, whose bright, smiling expression and showy dress were in strange contrast with the business which had brought us there.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "\\"Still at it, then?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "said he to Holmes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "\\"I thought you Londoners were never at fault.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "You don't seem to be so very quick, after all.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "\\"Ah, you must give us a little time,\\" said Holmes good-humoredly.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "\\"You'll want it,\\" said young Alec Cunningham.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "\\"Why, I don't see that we have any clue at all.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "\\"There's only one,\\" answered the Inspector.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "\\"We thought that if we could only find—Good heavens, Mr. Holmes!", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "What is the matter?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_5", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "My poor friend's face had suddenly assumed the most dreadful expression.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "His eyes rolled upwards, his features writhed in agony, and with a suppressed groan he dropped on his face upon the ground.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "Horrified at the suddenness and severity of the attack, we carried him into the kitchen, where he lay back in a large chair, and breathed heavily for some minutes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "Finally, with a shamefaced apology for his weakness, he rose once more.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "\\"Watson would tell you that I have only just recovered from a severe illness,\\" he explained.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "\\"I am liable to these sudden nervous attacks.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "\\"Shall I send you home in my trap?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "asked old Cunningham.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "\\"Well, since I am here, there is one point on which I should like to feel sure.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "We can very easily verify it.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "\\"What was it?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "\\"Well, it seems to me that it is just possible that the arrival of this poor fellow William was not before, but after, the entrance of the burglar into the house.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "You appear to take it for granted that, although the door was forced, the robber never got in.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "\\"I fancy that is quite obvious,\\" said Mr. Cunningham, gravely.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "\\"Why, my son Alec had not yet gone to bed, and he would certainly have heard any one moving about.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "\\"Where was he sitting?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "\\"I was smoking in my dressing-room.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "\\"Which window is that?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "\\"The last on the left next my father's.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "\\"Both of your lamps were lit, of course?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "\\"Undoubtedly.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "\\"There are some very singular points here,\\" said Holmes, smiling.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "\\"Is it not extraordinary that a burglar—and a burglar who had had some previous experience—should deliberately break into a house at a time when he could see from the lights that two of the family were still afoot?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "\\"He must have been a cool hand.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "\\"Well, of course, if the case were not an odd one we should not have been driven to ask you for an explanation,\\" said young Mr. Alec.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "\\"But as to your ideas that the man had robbed the house before William tackled him, I think it a most absurd notion.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "Wouldn't we have found the place disarranged, and missed the things which he had taken?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "\\"It depends on what the things were,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "\\"You must remember that we are dealing with a burglar who is a very peculiar fellow, and who appears to work on lines of his own.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "—a ball of string, a letter-weight, and I don't know what other odds and ends.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "as it?—a ball of string, a letter-weight, and I don't know what other odds and ends.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "\\"Well, we are quite in your hands, Mr. Holmes,\\" said old Cunningham.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "\\"Anything which you or the Inspector may suggest will most certainly be done.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "\\"In the first place,\\" said Holmes, \\"I should like you to offer a reward—coming from yourself, for the officials may take a little time before they would agree upon the sum, and these things cannot be done too promptly.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "I have jotted down the form here, if you would not mind signing it.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "Fifty pounds was quite enough, I thought.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": ", taking the slip of paper and the pencil which Holmes handed to him.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "\\"This is not quite correct, however,\\" he added, glancing over the document.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "ect, however,\\" he added, glancing over the document.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "\\"I wrote it rather hurriedly.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "he gasped.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "\\"You see you begin, 'Whereas, at about a quarter to one on Tuesday morning an attempt was made,' and so on.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "It was at a quarter to twelve, as a matter of fact.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "I was pained at the mistake, for I knew how keenly Holmes would feel any slip of the kind.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "It was his specialty to be accurate as to fact, but his recent illness had shaken him, and this one little incident was enough to show me that he was still far from being himself.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "He was obviously embarrassed for an instant, while the Inspector raised his eyebrows, and Alec Cunningham burst into a laugh.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "The old gentleman corrected the mistake, however, and handed the paper back to Holmes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_6", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "\\"Get it printed as soon as possible,\\" he said; \\"I think your idea is an excellent one.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "Holmes put the slip of paper carefully away into his pocket-book.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "\\"And now,\\" said he, \\"it really would be a good thing that we should all go over the house together and make certain that this rather erratic burglar did not, after all, carry anything away with him.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "Before entering, Holmes made an examination of the door which had been forced.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "It was evident that a chisel or strong knife had been thrust in, and the lock forced back with it.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "We could see the marks in the wood where it had been pushed in.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "\\"You don't use bars, then?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "\\"We have never found it necessary.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "\\"You don't keep a dog?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "\\"Yes, but he is chained on the other side of the house.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "\\"When do the servants go to bed?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "\\"About ten.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "\\"I understand that William was usually in bed also at that hour.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "\\"Yes.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "\\"It is singular that on this particular night he should have been up.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "Now, I should be very glad if you would have the kindness to show us over the house, Mr. Cunningham.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "A stone-flagged passage, with the kitchens branching away from it, led by a wooden staircase directly to the first floor of the house.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "It came out upon the landing opposite to a second more ornamental stair which came up from the front hall.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "Out of this landing opened the drawing-room and several bedrooms, including those of Mr. Cunningham and his son.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "Holmes walked slowly, taking keen note of the architecture of the house.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "I could tell from his expression that he was on a hot scent, and yet I could not in the least imagine in what direction his inferences were leading him.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "\\"My good sir,\\" said Mr. Cunningham with some impatience, \\"this is surely very unnecessary.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "That is my room at the end of the stairs, and my son's is the one beyond it.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "I leave it to your judgment whether it was possible for the thief to have come up here without disturbing us.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "\\"You must try round and get on a fresh scent, I fancy,\\" said the son with a rather malicious smile.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "\\"Still, I must ask you to humour me a little further.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "I should like, for example, to see how far the windows of the bedrooms command the front.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "This, I understand is your son's room\\"—he pushed open the door—\\"and that, I presume, is the dressing-room in which he sat smoking when the alarm was given.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "Where does the window of that look out to?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "He stepped across the bedroom, pushed open the door, and glanced round the other chamber.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "\\"I hope that you are satisfied now?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "said Mr. Cunningham, tartly.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "\\"Thank you, I think I have seen all that I wished.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "\\"Then if it is really necessary we can go into my room.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "\\"If it is not too much trouble.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "The J.P.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "shrugged his shoulders, and led the way into his own chamber, which was a plainly furnished and commonplace room.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "As we moved across it in the direction of the window, Holmes fell back until he and I were the last of the group.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "Near the foot of the bed stood a dish of oranges and a carafe of water.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "As we passed it Holmes, to my unutterable astonishment, leaned over in front of me and deliberately knocked the whole thing over.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "The glass smashed into a thousand pieces and the fruit rolled about into every corner of the room.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "\\"You've done it now, Watson,\\" said he, coolly.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "\\"A pretty mess you've made of the carpet.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_7", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "I stooped in some confusion and began to pick up the fruit, understanding for some reason my companion desired me to take the blame upon myself.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "The others did the same, and set the table on its legs again.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "\\"Halloa!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "cried the Inspector, \\"where's he got to?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "Holmes had disappeared.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "\\"Wait here an instant,\\" said young Alec Cunningham.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "\\"The fellow is off his head, in my opinion.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "Come with me, father, and see where he has got to!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "They rushed out of the room, leaving the Inspector, the Colonel, and me staring at each other.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "\\"'Pon my word, I am inclined to agree with Master Alec,\\" said the official.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "\\"It may be the effect of this illness, but it seems to me that—\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "His words were cut short by a sudden scream of \\"Help!", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "Help!", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "Murder!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "With a thrill I recognised the voice of that of my friend.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "I rushed madly from the room on to the landing.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "The cries, which had sunk down into a hoarse, inarticulate shouting, came from the room which we had first visited.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "I dashed in, and on into the dressing-room beyond.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "The two Cunninghams were bending over the prostrate figure of Sherlock Holmes, the younger clutching his throat with both hands, while the elder seemed to be twisting one of his wrists.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "In an instant the three of us had torn them away from him, and Holmes staggered to his feet, very pale and evidently greatly exhausted.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	section_34	section	\N	Section 34	33	{"wordCount": 106}
reigate-squires	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "\\"On what charge?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "\\"That of murdering their coachman, William Kirwan!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "The Inspector stared about him in bewilderment.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "\\"Oh, come now, Mr. Holmes,\\" said he at last, \\"I'm sure you don't really mean to—\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "\\"Tut, man, look at their faces!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "cried Holmes, curtly.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "Never, certainly, have I seen a plainer confession of guilt upon human countenances.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "The older man seemed numbed and dazed with a heavy, sullen expression upon his strongly-marked face.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "The son, on the other hand, had dropped all that jaunty, dashing style which had characterized him, and the ferocity of a dangerous wild beast gleamed in his dark eyes and distorted his handsome features.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "The Inspector said nothing, but, stepping to the door, he blew his whistle.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "Two of his constables came at the call.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "\\"I have no alternative, Mr. Cunningham,\\" said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "\\"I trust that this may all prove to be an absurd mistake, but you can see that—Ah, would you?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "Drop it!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "He struck out with his hand, and a revolver which the younger man was in the act of cocking clattered down upon the floor.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "\\"Keep that,\\" said Holmes, quietly putting his foot upon it; \\"you will find it useful at the trial.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "But this is what we really wanted.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "He held up a little crumpled piece of paper.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "\\"The remainder of the sheet!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "cried the Inspector.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "\\"Precisely.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "\\"And where was it?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "\\"Where I was sure it must be.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "I'll make the whole matter clear to you presently.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "I think, Colonel, that you and Watson might return now, and I will be with you again in an hour at the furthest.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "The Inspector and I must have a word with the prisoners, but you will certainly see me back at luncheon time.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes was as good as his word, for about one o'clock he rejoined us in the Colonel's smoking-room.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "He was accompanied by a little elderly gentleman, who was introduced to me as the Mr. Acton whose house had been the scene of the original burglary.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "\\"I wished Mr. Acton to be present while I demonstrated this small matter to you,\\" said Holmes, \\"for it is natural that he should take a keen interest in the details.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "I am afraid, my dear Colonel, that you must regret the hour that you took in such a stormy petrel as I am.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_8", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "\\"On the contrary,\\" answered the Colonel, warmly, \\"I consider it the greatest privilege to have been permitted to study your methods of working.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "I confess that they quite surpass my expectations, and that I am utterly unable to account for your result.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "I have not yet seen the vestige of a clue.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "\\"I am afraid that my explanation may disillusionize you but it has always been my habit to hide none of my methods, either from my friend Watson or from any one who might take an intelligent interest in them.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "\\"Precisely so,\\" said Mr. Acton.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "But, first, as I am rather shaken by the knocking about which I had in the dressing-room, I think that I shall help myself to a dash of your brandy, Colonel.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "My strength has been rather tried of late.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "\\"I trust that you had no more of those nervous attacks.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes laughed heartily.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "\\"We will come to that in its turn,\\" said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "\\"I will lay an account of the case before you in its due order, showing you the various points which guided me in my decision.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "Pray interrupt me if there is any inference which is not perfectly clear to you.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "\\"It is of the highest importance in the art of detection to be able to recognise, out of a number of facts, which are incidental and which vital.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "Otherwise your energy and attention must be dissipated instead of being concentrated.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "Now, in this case there was not the slightest doubt in my mind from the first that the key of the whole matter must be looked for in the scrap of paper in the dead man's hand.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "\\"Before going into this, I would draw your attention to the fact that, if Alec Cunningham's narrative was correct, and if the assailant, after shooting William Kirwan, had _instantly_ fled, then it obviously could not be he who tore the paper from the dead man's hand.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "But if it was not he, it must have been Alec Cunningham himself, for by the time that the old man had descended several servants were upon the scene.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "The point is a simple one, but the Inspector had overlooked it because he had started with the supposition that these county magnates had had nothing to do with the matter.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "Now, I make a point of never having any prejudices, and of following docilely wherever fact may lead me, and so, in the very first stage of the investigation, I found myself looking a little askance at the part which had been played by Mr. Alec Cunningham.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "\\"And now I made a very careful examination of the corner of paper which the Inspector had submitted to us.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "It was at once clear to me that it formed part of a very remarkable document.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "Here it is.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "Do you not now observe something very suggestive about it?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "\\"It has a very irregular look,\\" said the Colonel.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "\\"My dear sir,\\" cried Holmes, \\"there cannot be the least doubt in the world that it has been written by two persons doing alternate words.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "When I draw your attention to the strong t's of 'at' and 'to', and ask you to compare them with the weak ones of 'quarter' and 'twelve,' you will instantly recognise the fact.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "A very brief analysis of these four words would enable you to say with the utmost confidence that the 'learn' and the 'maybe' are written in the stronger hand, and the 'what' in the weaker.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "\\"By Jove, it's as clear as day!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "cried the Colonel.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "\\"Why on earth should two men write a letter in such a fashion?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "\\"Obviously the business was a bad one, and one of the men who distrusted the other was determined that, whatever was done, each should have an equal hand in it.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "Now, of the two men, it is clear that the one who wrote the 'at' and 'to' was the ringleader.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_9", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "\\"How do you get at that?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "\\"We might deduce it from the mere character of the one hand as compared with the other.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "But we have more assured reasons than that for supposing it.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "If you examine this scrap with attention you will come to the conclusion that the man with the stronger hand wrote all his words first, leaving blanks for the other to fill up.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "These blanks were not always sufficient, and you can see that the second man had a squeeze to fit his 'quarter' in between the 'at' and the 'to,' showing that the latter were already written.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "The man who wrote all his words first is undoubtedly the man who planned the affair.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "\\"Excellent!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "cried Mr. Acton.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "\\"But very superficial,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "\\"We come now, however, to a point which is of importance.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "You may not be aware that the deduction of a man's age from his writing is one which has been brought to considerable accuracy by experts.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "In normal cases one can place a man in his true decade with tolerable confidence.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "I say normal cases, because ill-health and physical weakness reproduce the signs of old age, even when the invalid is a youth.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "In this case, looking at the bold, strong hand of the one, and the rather broken-backed appearance of the other, which still retains its legibility although the t's have begun to lose their crossing, we can say that the one was a young man and the other was advanced in years without being positively decrepit.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "\\"Excellent!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "cried Mr. Acton again.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "\\"There is a further point, however, which is subtler and of greater interest.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "There is something in common between these hands.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "They belong to men who are blood-relatives.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "It may be most obvious to you in the Greek e's, but to me there are many small points which indicate the same thing.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "I have no doubt at all that a family mannerism can be traced in these two specimens of writing.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "I am only, of course, giving you the leading results now of my examination of the paper.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "There were twenty-three other deductions which would be of more interest to experts than to you.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "They all tend to deepen the impression upon my mind that the Cunninghams, father and son, had written this letter.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "\\"Having got so far, my next step was, of course, to examine into the details of the crime, and to see how far they would help us.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "I went up to the house with the Inspector, and saw all that was to be seen.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "The wound upon the dead man was, as I was able to determine with absolute confidence, fired from a revolver at the distance of something over four yards.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "There was no powder-blackening on the clothes.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "Evidently, therefore, Alec Cunningham had lied when he said that the two men were struggling when the shot was fired.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "Again, both father and son agreed as to the place where the man escaped into the road.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "At that point, however, as it happens, there is a broadish ditch, moist at the bottom.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "As there were no indications of bootmarks about this ditch, I was absolutely sure not only that the Cunninghams had again lied, but that there had never been any unknown man upon the scene at all.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "\\"And now I have to consider the motive of this singular crime.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "To get at this, I endeavoured first of all to solve the reason of the original burglary at Mr. Acton's.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "I understood, from something which the Colonel told us, that a lawsuit had been going on between you, Mr. Acton, and the Cunninghams.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "Of course, it instantly occurred to me that they had broken into your library with the intention of getting at some document which might be of importance in the case.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_10", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "\\"There can be no possible doubt as to their intentions.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "I have the clearest claim upon half of their present estate, and if they could have found a single paper—which, fortunately, was in the strong-box of my solicitors—they would undoubtedly have crippled our case.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "\\"There you are,\\" said Holmes, smiling.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "\\"It was a dangerous, reckless attempt, in which I seem to trace the influence of young Alec.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "Having found nothing they tried to divert suspicion by making it appear to be an ordinary burglary, to which end they carried off whatever they could lay their hands upon.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "That is all clear enough, but there was much that was still obscure.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "What I wanted above all was to get the missing part of that note.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "I was certain that Alec had torn it out of the dead man's hand, and almost certain that he must have thrust it into the pocket of his dressing-gown.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "Where else could he have put it?", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "The only question was whether it was still there.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "It was worth an effort to find out, and for that object we all went up to the house.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "\\"The Cunninghams joined us, as you doubtless remember, outside the kitchen door.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "It was, of course, of the very first importance that they should not be reminded of the existence of this paper, otherwise they would naturally destroy it without delay.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "The Inspector was about to tell them the importance which we attached to it when, by the luckiest chance in the world, I tumbled down in a sort of fit and so changed the conversation.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "\\"Good heavens!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "cried the Colonel, laughing, \\"do you mean to say all our sympathy was wasted and your fit an imposture?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "\\"Speaking professionally, it was admirably done,\\" cried I, looking in amazement at this man who was forever confounding me with some new phase of his astuteness.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "\\"It is an art which is often useful,\\" said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "\\"When I recovered I managed, by a device which had perhaps some little merit of ingenuity, to get old Cunningham to write the word 'twelve,' so that I might compare it with the 'twelve' upon the paper.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "\\"Oh, what an ass I have been!\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "I exclaimed.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "\\"I could see that you were commiserating me over my weakness,\\" said Holmes, laughing.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "\\"I was sorry to cause you the sympathetic pain which I know that you felt.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "We then went upstairs together, and having entered the room and seen the dressing-gown hanging up behind the door, I contrived, by upsetting a table, to engage their attention for the moment, and slipped back to examine the pockets.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "I had hardly got the paper, however—which was, as I had expected, in one of them—when the two Cunninghams were on me, and would, I verily believe, have murdered me then and there but for your prompt and friendly aid.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "As it is, I feel that young man's grip on my throat now, and the father has twisted my wrist round in the effort to get the paper out of my hand.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "They saw that I must know all about it, you see, and the sudden change from absolute security to complete despair made them perfectly desperate.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "\\"I had a little talk with old Cunningham afterwards as to the motive of the crime.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "He was tractable enough, though his son was a perfect demon, ready to blow out his own or anybody else's brains if he could have got to his revolver.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "When Cunningham saw that the case against him was so strong he lost all heart and made a clean breast of everything.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	sentence_984	lexical	\N	\N	983	{"text": "It’s past two now.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "It seems that William had secretly followed his two masters on the night when they made their raid upon Mr. Acton's, and having thus got them into his power, proceeded, under threats of exposure, to levy blackmail upon them.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "Mr. Alec, however, was a dangerous man to play games of that sort with.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "It was a stroke of positive genius on his part to see in the burglary scare which was convulsing the country side an opportunity of plausibly getting rid of the man whom he feared.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "William was decoyed up and shot, and had they only got the whole of the note and paid a little more attention to detail in the accessories, it is very possible that suspicion might never have been aroused.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_11", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "\\"And the note?\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes placed the subjoined paper before us.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "piece of paper", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_468	lexical	\N	\N	467	{"text": "If you will only come round at quarter to twelve to the east gate you will learn what will very much surprise you and maybe be of the greatest service to you and also to Annie Morrison.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_469	lexical	\N	\N	468	{"text": "But say nothing to anyone upon the matter", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_470	lexical	\N	\N	469	{"text": "\\"It is very much the sort of thing that I expected,\\" said he.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_471	lexical	\N	\N	470	{"text": "\\"Of course, we do not yet know what the relations may have been between Alec Cunningham, William Kirwan, and Annie Morrison.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_472	lexical	\N	\N	471	{"text": "The results shows that the trap was skillfully baited.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_473	lexical	\N	\N	472	{"text": "I am sure that you cannot fail to be delighted with the traces of heredity shown in the p's and in the tails of the g's.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_474	lexical	\N	\N	473	{"text": "The absence of the i-dots in the old man's writing is also most characteristic.", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
reigate-squires	sentence_475	lexical	\N	\N	474	{"text": "Watson, I think our quiet rest in the country has been a distinct success, and I shall certainly return much invigorated to Baker Street to-morrow.\\"", "section": "reigate-squires-section_12", "entities": []}
