crooked-man	event_8_1	event	\N	Holmes explains that Wood followed the ladies, saw the quarrel, rushed in, and lost control of a creature from his box	7	{"section": "crooked-man-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_278", "sentence_279", "sentence_280"], "communicatesContent": "after the ladies parted from this man he followed them at a distance, that he saw the quarrel between husband and wife through the window, that he rushed in, and that the creature which he carried in his box got loose"}
crooked-man	event_8_2	event	\N	Watson asks whether Holmes intends to question the man	7	{"section": "crooked-man-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_281"], "communicatesContent": "And you intend to ask him?"}
crooked-man	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes says he will question Wood in the presence of a witness	7	{"section": "crooked-man-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_282", "sentence_283", "sentence_284"], "communicatesContent": "Most certainly—but in the presence of a witness. If you will be so good."}
crooked-man	event_8_4	event	\N	Holmes says they will apply for a warrant if Wood refuses to help	7	{"section": "crooked-man-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_285", "sentence_286"], "communicatesContent": "If he can clear the matter up, well and good. If he refuses, we have no alternative but to apply for a warrant."}
crooked-man	event_8_5	event	\N	Watson asks how Holmes knows Wood will still be there when they return	7	{"section": "crooked-man-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": "But how do you know he'll be there when we return?"}
crooked-man	event_8_6	event	\N	Holmes says he took precautions and placed one of his Baker Street boys to guard Wood	7	{"section": "crooked-man-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_288", "sentence_289", "sentence_290"], "communicatesContent": "You may be sure that I took some precautions. I have one of my Baker Street boys mounting guard over him who would stick to him like a burr, go where he might. We shall find him in Hudson Street to-morrow, Watson, and meanwhile I should be the criminal myself if I kept you out of bed any longer."}
