resident-patient	event_2_1	event	\N	Doctor Percy Trevelyan introduces himself to Holmes and gives his address	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_37"], "communicatesContent": "My name is Doctor Percy Trevelyan, and I live at 403, Brook Street."}
resident-patient	event_2_2	event	\N	Holmes asks Trevelyan about the obscure nervous lesions monograph	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_38", "sentence_39"], "communicatesContent": "Are you not the author of a monograph upon obscure nervous lesions?"}
resident-patient	event_2_3	event	\N	Trevelyan responds that his work was known and that his publishers reported poor sales	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_40", "sentence_41", "sentence_42", "sentence_43"], "communicatesContent": "I so seldom hear of the work that I thought it was quite dead. My publishers gave me a most discouraging account of its sale. You are yourself, I presume, a medical man?"}
resident-patient	event_2_4	event	\N	Holmes says he is a retired Army surgeon	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_44"], "communicatesContent": "A retired Army surgeon."}
resident-patient	event_2_5	event	\N	Trevelyan explains his medical interests and the recent disturbance at his house	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_45", "sentence_46", "sentence_47", "sentence_48"], "communicatesContent": "My own hobby has always been nervous disease. I should wish to make it an absolute specialty, but, of course, a man must take what he can get at first. This, however, is beside the question, Mr. Sherlock Holmes, and I quite appreciate how valuable your time is. The fact is that a very singular train of events has occurred recently at my house in Brook Street, and to-night they came to such a head that I felt it was quite impossible for me to wait another hour before asking for your advice and assistance."}
resident-patient	event_2_6	event	\N	Holmes sits down and lights his pipe	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_49"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_2_7	event	\N	Holmes invites Trevelyan to give a detailed account of the disturbance	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_50", "sentence_51"], "communicatesContent": "You are very welcome to both. Pray let me have a detailed account of what the circumstances are which have disturbed you."}
resident-patient	event_2_8	event	\N	Trevelyan says he will explain the matter and begins with his college career	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_52", "sentence_53", "sentence_54"], "communicatesContent": "One or two of them are so trivial, but the matter is so inexplicable, and the recent turn which it has taken is so elaborate, that I shall lay it all before you, and you shall judge what is essential and what is not. I am compelled, to begin with, to say something of my own college career."}
resident-patient	event_2_9	event	\N	Trevelyan describes his university and research career and mentions winning a prize	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_55", "sentence_56", "sentence_57"], "communicatesContent": "I am a London University man, and my student career was considered by my professors to be a very promising one. After I had graduated I continued to devote myself to research, occupying a minor position in King's College Hospital, and I was fortunate enough to excite considerable interest by my research into the pathology of catalepsy, and finally to win the Bruce Pinkerton prize and medal by the monograph on nervous lesions to which your friend has just alluded. There was a general impression at that time that a distinguished career lay before me."}
resident-patient	event_2_10	event	\N	Trevelyan explains that lack of capital hindered his career	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_58", "sentence_59", "sentence_60", "sentence_61"], "communicatesContent": "But the one great stumbling-block lay in my want of capital. As you will readily understand, a specialist who aims high is compelled to start in one of a dozen streets in the Cavendish Square quarter, all of which entail enormous rents and furnishing expenses. Besides this preliminary outlay, he must be prepared to keep himself for some years, and to hire a presentable carriage and horse. To do this was quite beyond my power, and I could only hope that by economy I might in ten years' time save enough to enable me to put up my plate."}
resident-patient	event_2_11	event	\N	Trevelyan says an unexpected incident opened a new prospect	1	{"section": "resident-patient-section_2", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_62"], "communicatesContent": "Suddenly, however, an unexpected incident opened up quite a new prospect to me."}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_9	section	\N	Section 9	8	{"wordCount": 605}
resident-patient	event_3_1	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan asks Holmes to answer frankly	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_68"], "communicatesContent": "Answer me frankly, for you will find it to your interest to do so."}
resident-patient	event_3_2	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan asks Holmes about bad habits and drink	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_73", "sentence_74"], "communicatesContent": "Any bad habits? Not drawn towards drink, eh?"}
resident-patient	event_3_3	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan remarks on his own proposal to start Holmes in Brook Street	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_82", "sentence_85"], "communicatesContent": "It's the old story. More in your brains than in your pocket, eh? What would you say if I were to start you in Brook Street?"}
resident-patient	event_3_4	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan offers to invest in Holmes	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_87", "sentence_89"], "communicatesContent": "It's for my sake, not for yours. I'll be perfectly frank with you, and if it suits you it will suit me very well. I have a few thousands to invest, d'ye see, and I think I'll sink them in you."}
resident-patient	event_3_5	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan explains the business arrangement	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_94", "sentence_98"], "communicatesContent": "I'll tell you. I'll take the house, furnish it, pay the maids, and run the whole place. All you have to do is just to wear out your chair in the consulting-room. I'll let you have pocket-money and everything. Then you hand over to me three quarters of what you earn, and you keep the other quarter for yourself."}
resident-patient	event_3_6	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan describes Blessington approaching him with a proposal	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_99"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_3_7	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan moves into the house and starts practice	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_100", "sentence_101"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_3_8	event	\N	Blessington comes to live with Percy Trevelyan as a resident patient	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_102"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_3_9	event	\N	Blessington uses the consulting-room to inspect accounts and take proceeds	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_107"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_3_10	event	\N	Blessington speaks of a burglary and urges stronger security	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": "blessington", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_113", "sentence_114"], "communicatesContent": "Some weeks ago a burglary had been committed in the West End, and we should add stronger bolts to our windows and doors before another day passes."}
resident-patient	event_3_11	event	\N	Blessington becomes restless and watches the windows	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_115"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_3_12	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan questions Blessington and then drops the subject	2	{"section": "resident-patient-section_3", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_116"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_1	event	\N	The narrator receives an anonymous letter	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_119", "sentence_120"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_2	event	\N	The letter asks Dr. Percy Trevelyan for medical assistance	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": "anonymous_russian_nobleman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_121", "sentence_123"], "communicatesContent": "A Russian nobleman resident in England would be glad to avail himself of the professional assistance of Dr. Percy Trevelyan. He has been for some years a victim to cataleptic attacks. He proposes to call at about quarter past six to-morrow evening if Dr. Trevelyan will make it convenient to be at home."}
resident-patient	event_4_3	event	\N	The page admits the patient into the consulting-room	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_125"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_4	event	\N	The young man helps the elderly man to a chair	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_129"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_5	event	\N	The young man explains that the elderly man is his father and asks to stay out of the consultation	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": "anonymous_young_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_130", "sentence_131", "sentence_134", "sentence_139"], "communicatesContent": "You will excuse my coming in, doctor. This is my father, and his health is a matter of the most overwhelming importance to me. Not for the world. It is more painful to me than I can express. If I were to see my father in one of these dreadful seizures I am convinced that I should never survive it. My own nervous system is an exceptionally sensitive one. With your permission, I will remain in the waiting-room while you go into my father's case."}
resident-patient	event_4_6	event	\N	Percy Trevelyan assents and the young man withdraws	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_140"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_7	event	\N	Trevelyan consults the patient and takes notes	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_141", "sentence_142"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_8	event	\N	The patient becomes rigid in cataleptic seizure	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_143", "sentence_144"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_9	event	\N	Trevelyan examines the patient's pulse, temperature, muscles, and reflexes	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_147", "sentence_148"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_10	event	\N	Trevelyan leaves to fetch nitrite of amyl from the laboratory	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_149", "sentence_150"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_11	event	\N	Trevelyan returns to the consulting-room and finds the patient gone	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_151", "sentence_152"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_12	event	\N	Trevelyan runs to the waiting-room and finds the young man gone	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_153", "sentence_154"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_4_13	event	\N	Trevelyan speaks about the page and the mystery	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_156", "sentence_157", "sentence_158"], "communicatesContent": "My page who admits patients is a new boy and by no means quick. He waits downstairs, and runs up to show patients out when I ring the consulting-room bell. He had heard nothing, and the affair remained a complete mystery."}
resident-patient	event_4_14	event	\N	Mr. Blessington comes in from his walk	3	{"section": "resident-patient-section_4", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_159"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_1	event	\N	The Russian and his son arrive in the consulting-room	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_160"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_2	event	\N	The patient apologizes for his abrupt departure and explains his clouded memory after attacks	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": "anonymous_russian_nobleman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_161", "sentence_163", "sentence_164"], "communicatesContent": "I owe you a great many apologies for my abrupt departure yesterday, doctor. The fact is that when I recover from these attacks my mind is always very clouded as to all that has gone before. I woke up in a strange room, as it seemed to me, and made my way out into the street in a sort of dazed way when you were absent."}
resident-patient	event_5_3	event	\N	The son explains why he thought the consultation had ended	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": "anonymous_young_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_165", "sentence_166"], "communicatesContent": "Seeing my father pass the door of the waiting-room, I naturally thought that the consultation had come to an end. It was not until we had reached home that I began to realize the true state of affairs."}
resident-patient	event_5_4	event	\N	The doctor resumes the consultation and prescribes treatment	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_167", "sentence_168"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_5	event	\N	Blessington enters, goes upstairs, rushes down, and bursts into the consulting-room in panic	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_169", "sentence_170", "sentence_171", "sentence_172"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_6	event	\N	Blessington demands whether anyone has been in his room and cries out in alarm	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": "blessington", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_173", "sentence_174", "sentence_175", "sentence_176", "sentence_177"], "communicatesContent": "Been in my room? No one! It's a lie! Come up and look!"}
resident-patient	event_5_7	event	\N	The doctor goes upstairs with Blessington and sees footprints on the carpet	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_179", "sentence_180", "sentence_181", "sentence_182"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_8	event	\N	The doctor reasons that an intruder ascended to the resident patient's room while he was busy	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_183", "sentence_184", "sentence_185"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_9	event	\N	Blessington becomes highly agitated and suggests consulting Holmes	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": "blessington", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_186", "sentence_187", "sentence_188", "sentence_189"], "communicatesContent": "It was his suggestion that I should come round to you, and of course I at once saw the propriety of it, for certainly the incident is a very singular one, though he appears to completely overrate its importance. If you would only come back with me in my brougham, you would at least be able to soothe him, though I can hardly hope that you will be able to explain this remarkable occurrence."}
resident-patient	event_5_10	event	\N	Holmes listens to the doctor's narrative with intense attention	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_190", "sentence_191"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_11	event	\N	Holmes leaves with the doctor and Watson and arrives at Dr. Trevelyan's residence	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_192", "sentence_193"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_5_12	event	\N	A page admits the visitors and they begin ascending the stair	4	{"section": "resident-patient-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_194"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_6_1	event	\N	A hidden man warns the others not to come nearer with a pistol	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "anonymous_young_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_196", "sentence_197", "sentence_198"], "communicatesContent": "I have a pistol. I give you my word that I'll fire if you come any nearer."}
resident-patient	event_6_2	event	\N	Dr. Trevelyan addresses Blessington by name	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "doctor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_199"], "communicatesContent": "This really grows outrageous, Mr. Blessington."}
resident-patient	event_6_3	event	\N	The hidden man identifies the doctor and asks about the other men	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "anonymous_young_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_200", "sentence_201"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, then it is you, doctor. But those other gentlemen, are they what they pretend to be?"}
resident-patient	event_6_4	event	\N	The hidden man scrutinizes the visitors from the darkness and allows them to come up	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "anonymous_young_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_202", "sentence_203", "sentence_204"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, yes, it's all right. You can come up, and I am sorry if my precautions have annoyed you."}
resident-patient	event_6_5	event	\N	The man relights the stair gas and reveals himself	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_205", "sentence_206", "sentence_207", "sentence_208"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_6_6	event	\N	Blessington greets Holmes and explains his situation	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "blessington", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_209", "sentence_210", "sentence_211", "sentence_212"], "communicatesContent": "Good-evening, Mr. Holmes. I am sure I am very much obliged to you for coming round. No one ever needed your advice more than I do. I suppose that Dr. Trevelyan has told you of this most unwarrantable intrusion into my rooms."}
resident-patient	event_6_7	event	\N	Holmes asks Blessington about the two men who intrude on him	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_213", "sentence_214"], "communicatesContent": "Who are these two men Mr. Blessington, and why do they wish to molest you?"}
resident-patient	event_6_8	event	\N	Blessington refuses to answer Holmes's question directly	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "blessington", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_215", "sentence_216", "sentence_217"], "communicatesContent": "Well, well, of course it is hard to say that. You can hardly expect me to answer that, Mr. Holmes."}
resident-patient	event_6_9	event	\N	Blessington leads Holmes into his bedroom and points out a black box	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_218", "sentence_219", "sentence_220", "sentence_221", "sentence_222", "sentence_223", "sentence_224", "sentence_225"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_6_10	event	\N	Holmes rejects Blessington's attempted deception and leaves	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_226", "sentence_227", "sentence_228", "sentence_229", "sentence_230", "sentence_231", "sentence_232", "sentence_233"], "communicatesContent": "I cannot possibly advise you if you try to deceive me. Good-night, Dr. Trevelyan. My advice to you, sir, is to speak the truth."}
resident-patient	event_6_11	event	\N	Holmes and Watson walk home from the house	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_234", "sentence_235"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_6_12	event	\N	Holmes comments that the visit was a fool's errand and analyzes the intruders	5	{"section": "resident-patient-section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_236", "sentence_237", "sentence_238", "sentence_239", "sentence_240"], "communicatesContent": "Sorry to bring you out on such a fool's errand, Watson. It is an interesting case, too, at the bottom of it. I can make little of it. Well, it is quite evident that there are two men—more, perhaps, but at least two—who are determined for some reason to get at this fellow Blessington. I have no doubt in my mind that both on the first and on the second occasion that young man penetrated to Blessington's room, while his confederate, by an ingenious device, kept the doctor from interfering."}
resident-patient	event_7_1	event	\N	Holmes dismisses the catalepsy as a fraudulent imitation	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_241", "sentence_242", "sentence_243", "sentence_244"], "communicatesContent": "A fraudulent imitation, Watson, though I should hardly dare to hint as much to our specialist. It is a very easy complaint to imitate. I have done it myself."}
resident-patient	event_7_2	event	\N	Holmes explains why Blessington was absent and why the men chose the hour	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_245", "sentence_246", "sentence_247", "sentence_248", "sentence_249", "sentence_250", "sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253"], "communicatesContent": "By the purest chance Blessington was out on each occasion. Their reason for choosing so unusual an hour for a consultation was obviously to insure that there should be no other patient in the waiting-room. It just happened, however, that this hour coincided with Blessington's constitutional, which seems to show that they were not very well acquainted with his daily routine. Of course, if they had been merely after plunder they would at least have made some attempt to search for it. Besides, I can read in a man's eye when it is his own skin that he is frightened for. It is inconceivable that this fellow could have made two such vindictive enemies as these appear to be without knowing of it. I hold it, therefore, to be certain that he does know who these men are, and that for reasons of his own he suppresses it. It is just possible that to-morrow may find him in a more communicative mood."}
resident-patient	event_7_3	event	\N	Watson suggests an alternative explanation for the catalepsy story	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256"], "communicatesContent": "Is there not one alternative, grotesquely improbable, no doubt, but still just conceivable? Might the whole story of the cataleptic Russian and his son be a concoction of Dr. Trevelyan's, who has, for his own purposes, been in Blessington's rooms?"}
resident-patient	event_7_4	event	\N	Holmes says he corroborated the doctor's tale from footprints and shoes	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_257", "sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260"], "communicatesContent": "It was one of the first solutions which occurred to me, but I was soon able to corroborate the doctor's tale. This young man has left prints upon the stair-carpet which made it quite superfluous for me to ask to see those which he had made in the room. When I tell you that his shoes were square-toed instead of being pointed like Blessington's, and were quite an inch and a third longer than the doctor's, you will acknowledge that there can be no doubt as to his individuality. But we may sleep on it now, for I shall be surprised if we do not hear something further from Brook Street in the morning."}
resident-patient	event_7_5	event	\N	Holmes appears at Watson's bedside and calls for the brougham	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_261", "sentence_262", "sentence_263", "sentence_264", "sentence_265", "sentence_266", "sentence_267", "sentence_268", "sentence_269", "sentence_270", "sentence_271"], "communicatesContent": "There's a brougham waiting for us, Watson. The Brook Street business. Tragic, but ambiguous. Our friend, the doctor, was hard put to it when he wrote this. Come along, my dear fellow, for it's an urgent call."}
resident-patient	event_7_6	event	\N	Holmes and Watson return to the physician's house	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_272"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_7_7	event	\N	The doctor meets Holmes and Watson with horror	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_273", "sentence_274", "sentence_275"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, such a business!"}
resident-patient	event_7_8	event	\N	The doctor announces that Blessington has committed suicide	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_276", "sentence_277", "sentence_278", "sentence_279"], "communicatesContent": "Blessington has committed suicide! Yes, he hanged himself during the night."}
resident-patient	event_7_9	event	\N	The doctor says police are already upstairs and the event has shaken him	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_280", "sentence_281", "sentence_282", "sentence_283"], "communicatesContent": "I really hardly know what I am doing. The police are already upstairs. It has shaken me most dreadfully."}
resident-patient	event_7_10	event	\N	The doctor explains when he found Blessington hanging and how he died	6	{"section": "resident-patient-section_7", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_284", "sentence_285", "sentence_286", "sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": "He has a cup of tea taken in to him early every morning. When the maid entered, about seven, there the unfortunate fellow was hanging in the middle of the room. He had tied his cord to the hook on which the heavy lamp used to hang, and he had jumped off from the top of the very box that he showed us yesterday."}
resident-patient	event_8_1	event	\N	Holmes asks to go upstairs and inspect the matter	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_289"], "communicatesContent": "With your permission, I should like to go upstairs and look into the matter."}
resident-patient	event_8_2	event	\N	Holmes, Watson, and the doctor ascend upstairs	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_290"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_8_3	event	\N	They enter the bedroom and find Blessington dead	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_291", "sentence_292", "sentence_293", "sentence_294", "sentence_295", "sentence_296"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_8_4	event	\N	Lanner greets Holmes and says he is delighted to see him	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_297"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, Mr. Holmes, I am delighted to see you."}
resident-patient	event_8_5	event	\N	Holmes asks Lanner about the events leading to the affair	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_298", "sentence_299"], "communicatesContent": "Good-morning, Lanner, you won't think me an intruder, I am sure. Have you heard of the events which led up to this affair?"}
resident-patient	event_8_6	event	\N	Lanner says he has heard something of the events	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_300"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, I heard something of them."}
resident-patient	event_8_7	event	\N	Holmes asks Lanner for his opinion	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_301"], "communicatesContent": "Have you formed any opinion?"}
resident-patient	event_8_8	event	\N	Lanner describes the case and the body	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_302", "sentence_303", "sentence_304", "sentence_305", "sentence_306", "sentence_307"], "communicatesContent": "As far as I can see, the man has been driven out of his senses by fright. The bed has been well slept in, you see. There's his impression deep enough. It's about five in the morning, you know, that suicides are most common. That would be about his time for hanging himself. It seems to have been a very deliberate affair."}
resident-patient	event_8_9	event	\N	Watson states that the man has been dead about three hours	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_308"], "communicatesContent": "I should say that he has been dead about three hours, judging by the rigidity of the muscles."}
resident-patient	event_8_10	event	\N	Holmes asks whether anything peculiar was noticed in the room	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_309", "sentence_310"], "communicatesContent": "Noticed anything peculiar about the room?"}
resident-patient	event_8_11	event	\N	Lanner reports objects found in the room	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_313"], "communicatesContent": "Found a screw-driver and some screws on the wash-hand stand. Seems to have smoked heavily during the night, too. Here are four cigar-ends that I picked out of the fireplace."}
resident-patient	event_8_12	event	\N	Holmes asks whether the cigar-holder has been found	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_314", "sentence_315"], "communicatesContent": "Hum! have you got his cigar-holder?"}
resident-patient	event_8_13	event	\N	Lanner says he has seen no cigar-holder	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_316"], "communicatesContent": "No, I have seen none."}
resident-patient	event_8_14	event	\N	Holmes asks about the cigar-case	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_317"], "communicatesContent": "His cigar-case, then?"}
resident-patient	event_8_15	event	\N	Lanner says the cigar-case was in the coat-pocket	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_318"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, it was in his coat-pocket."}
resident-patient	event_8_16	event	\N	Holmes opens the cigar-case and smells the cigar inside	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_319"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_8_17	event	\N	Holmes identifies the cigar types and their features	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_320", "sentence_321"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_8_18	event	\N	Holmes examines the four cigar-ends with his pocket-lens	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_322"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_8_19	event	\N	Holmes states that two cigar-ends were smoked from a holder and two without	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_323"], "communicatesContent": "Two of these have been smoked from a holder and two without."}
resident-patient	event_8_20	event	\N	Holmes states that the cigar-ends were cut or bitten	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_324"], "communicatesContent": "Two have been cut by a not very sharp knife, and two have had the ends bitten off by a set of excellent teeth."}
resident-patient	event_8_21	event	\N	Holmes declares the death to be murder rather than suicide	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_325", "sentence_326"], "communicatesContent": "This is no suicide, Mr. Lanner. It is a very deeply planned and cold-blooded murder."}
resident-patient	event_8_22	event	\N	The inspector exclaims that Holmes's claim is impossible	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "lanner", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_327", "sentence_328"], "communicatesContent": "Impossible!"}
resident-patient	event_8_23	event	\N	Holmes asks why someone would murder a man by hanging him	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_329", "sentence_330"], "communicatesContent": "And why? Why should any one murder a man in so clumsy a fashion as by hanging him?"}
resident-patient	event_8_24	event	\N	Holmes and Lanner discuss how the perpetrators entered	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_331", "sentence_332", "sentence_333", "sentence_334", "sentence_335", "sentence_336"], "communicatesContent": "How could they get in? Through the front door. It was barred in the morning. Then it was barred after them. How do you know?"}
resident-patient	event_8_25	event	\N	Holmes says he saw their traces and asks to inspect the door	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_338", "sentence_339", "sentence_340"], "communicatesContent": "I saw their traces. Excuse me a moment, and I may be able to give you some further information about it."}
resident-patient	event_8_26	event	\N	Holmes inspects the room and the body, then the body is cut down and laid under a sheet	7	{"section": "resident-patient-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_341"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_9_1	event	\N	Dr. Trevelyan draws a large coil from under the bed	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_344"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_9_2	event	\N	Dr. Trevelyan explains the rope was kept beside him for escape from fire	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_345"], "communicatesContent": "He was morbidly nervous of fire, and always kept this beside him, so that he might escape by the window in case the stairs were burning."}
resident-patient	event_9_3	event	\N	Holmes takes the photograph of Blessington from the mantelpiece	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_348"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_9_4	event	\N	Holmes states that three men were in it	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_351", "sentence_352"], "communicatesContent": "There were three of them in it: the young man, the old man, and a third, to whose identity I have no clue."}
resident-patient	event_9_5	event	\N	Holmes states that the first two men masqueraded as the Russian count and his son	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_353"], "communicatesContent": "The first two, I need hardly remark, are the same who masqueraded as the Russian count and his son, so we can give a very full description of them."}
resident-patient	event_9_6	event	\N	Holmes states that the men were admitted by a confederate inside the house	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_354"], "communicatesContent": "They were admitted by a confederate inside the house."}
resident-patient	event_9_7	event	\N	Holmes advises arresting the page	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_355"], "communicatesContent": "it would be to arrest the page, who, as I understand, has only recently come into your service, Doctor."}
resident-patient	event_9_8	event	\N	Dr. Trevelyan says the page cannot be found and the maid and cook have searched for him	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "percy_trevelyan", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_356"], "communicatesContent": "The young imp cannot be found; the maid and the cook have just been searching for him."}
resident-patient	event_9_9	event	\N	Holmes states that the page played a part in the drama	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_358"], "communicatesContent": "He has played a not unimportant part in this drama."}
resident-patient	event_9_10	event	\N	Holmes states that the three men ascended the stairs on tiptoe	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_359"], "communicatesContent": "The three men having ascended the stairs, which they did on tiptoe, the elder man first, the younger man second, and the unknown man in the rear."}
resident-patient	event_9_11	event	\N	Holmes states that the men went to Blessington's room and found the door locked	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_364"], "communicatesContent": "They ascended, then, to Mr. Blessington's room, the door of which they found to be locked."}
resident-patient	event_9_12	event	\N	The men force the key round with a wire	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_365"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_9_13	event	\N	Holmes states that the men gag Mr. Blessington on entering the room	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_367", "sentence_368", "sentence_369"], "communicatesContent": "On entering the room their first proceeding must have been to gag Mr. Blessington."}
resident-patient	event_9_14	event	\N	Holmes states that a consultation is held after Blessington is secured	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_370", "sentence_371", "sentence_372"], "communicatesContent": "Having secured him, it is evident to me that a consultation of some sort was held. Probably it was something in the nature of a judicial proceeding."}
resident-patient	event_9_15	event	\N	Holmes states that the older man sits in the wicker chair and uses the cigar-holder	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_373"], "communicatesContent": "The older man sat in that wicker chair; it was he who used the cigar-holder."}
resident-patient	event_9_16	event	\N	Holmes states that the younger man sits by the chest of drawers and knocks ash off against it	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_374"], "communicatesContent": "The younger man sat over yonder; he knocked his ash off against the chest of drawers."}
resident-patient	event_9_17	event	\N	Holmes states that the third man paces up and down	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_375"], "communicatesContent": "The third fellow paced up and down."}
resident-patient	event_9_18	event	\N	Holmes states that Blessington sits upright in the bed	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_376"], "communicatesContent": "Blessington, I think, sat upright in the bed, but of that I cannot be absolutely certain."}
resident-patient	event_9_19	event	\N	Holmes states that the men hang Blessington	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_377"], "communicatesContent": "it ended by their taking Blessington and hanging him."}
resident-patient	event_9_20	event	\N	Holmes states that the men brought a block or pulley to serve as a gallows	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_378", "sentence_379"], "communicatesContent": "The matter was so prearranged that it is my belief that they brought with them some sort of block or pulley which might serve as a gallows. That screw-driver and those screws were, as I conceive, for fixing it up."}
resident-patient	event_9_21	event	\N	Holmes states that the men avoid trouble by using the hook	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_380"], "communicatesContent": "Seeing the hook, however they naturally saved themselves the trouble."}
resident-patient	event_9_22	event	\N	Holmes states that the men make off and their confederate bars the door behind them	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_381"], "communicatesContent": "Having finished their work they made off, and the door was barred behind them by their confederate."}
resident-patient	event_9_23	event	\N	The inspector hurries away to make inquiries about the page	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_383"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_9_24	event	\N	Holmes and Watson return to Baker Street for breakfast	8	{"section": "resident-patient-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_383"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_10_1	event	\N	The visitors arrive at the appointed time	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_386"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_10_2	event	\N	Holmes arrives late	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_386", "sentence_387"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_10_3	event	\N	Holmes reports that he has identified the men	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_390", "sentence_393", "sentence_394", "sentence_395"], "communicatesContent": "You have got them! Well, at least I have got their identity. This so-called Blessington is, as I expected, well known at headquarters, and so are his assailants. Their names are Biddle, Hayward, and Moffat."}
resident-patient	event_10_4	event	\N	The inspector identifies the gang	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "inspector", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_396", "sentence_397"], "communicatesContent": "The Worthingdon bank gang."}
resident-patient	event_10_5	event	\N	Holmes confirms the identification of Blessington as Sutton	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_398", "sentence_399"], "communicatesContent": "Exactly."}
resident-patient	event_10_6	event	\N	Holmes explains the Worthingdon bank case	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_402", "sentence_403", "sentence_404", "sentence_405", "sentence_406", "sentence_407", "sentence_408", "sentence_409", "sentence_410"], "communicatesContent": "You must surely remember the great Worthingdon bank business. Five men were in it—these four and a fifth called Cartwright. Tobin, the caretaker, was murdered, and the thieves got away with seven thousand pounds. This was in 1875. They were all five arrested, but the evidence against them was by no means conclusive. This Blessington or Sutton, who was the worst of the gang, turned informer. On his evidence Cartwright was hanged and the other three got fifteen years apiece. When they got out the other day, some years before their full term, they set themselves to hunt down the traitor and to avenge the death of their comrade upon him. Twice they tried to get at him and failed; a third time, it came off."}
resident-patient	event_10_7	event	\N	The doctor says the explanation is clear	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "doctor", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_412"], "communicatesContent": "I think you have made it all remarkably clear."}
resident-patient	event_10_8	event	\N	Holmes explains Blessington's concealment	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_413", "sentence_415", "sentence_417", "sentence_418", "sentence_419"], "communicatesContent": "No doubt the day on which he was perturbed was the day when he had seen of their release in the newspapers. His talk about a burglary was the merest blind. Knowing the vindictive character of his old associates, he was trying to hide his own identity from everybody as long as he could. His secret was a shameful one, and he could not bring himself to divulge it."}
resident-patient	event_10_9	event	\N	Holmes states that the shield of British law may fail but justice remains	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_419"], "communicatesContent": "However, wretch as he was, he was still living under the shield of British law, and I have no doubt, Inspector, that you will see that, though that shield may fail to guard, the sword of justice is still there to avenge."}
resident-patient	event_10_10	event	\N	The police see nothing more of the three murderers	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_421"], "communicatesContent": null}
resident-patient	event_10_11	event	\N	The proceedings against the page break down for lack of evidence	9	{"section": "resident-patient-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_422"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter	story	\N	The Greek Interpreter	\N	{"sourceFile": "data/raw/memoirs/greek-interpreter.txt", "granularity": "sentence"}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_1	section	\N	Section 1	0	{"wordCount": 601}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_2	section	\N	Section 2	1	{"wordCount": 602}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_3	section	\N	Section 3	2	{"wordCount": 630}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_4	section	\N	Section 4	3	{"wordCount": 648}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_5	section	\N	Section 5	4	{"wordCount": 660}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_6	section	\N	Section 6	5	{"wordCount": 637}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_7	section	\N	Section 7	6	{"wordCount": 622}
greek-interpreter	greek-interpreter-section_8	section	\N	Section 8	7	{"wordCount": 620}
greek-interpreter	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "During my long and intimate acquaintance with Mr. Sherlock Holmes I had never heard him refer to his relations, and hardly ever to his own early life.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "This reticence upon his part had increased the somewhat inhuman effect which he produced upon me, until sometimes I found myself regarding him as an isolated phenomenon, a brain without a heart, as deficient in human sympathy as he was pre-eminent in intelligence.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "His aversion to women and his disinclination to form new friendships were both typical of his unemotional character, but not more so than his complete suppression of every reference to his own people.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "I had come to believe that he was an orphan with no relatives living, but one day, to my very great surprise, he began to talk to me about his brother.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "It was after tea on a summer evening, and the conversation, which had roamed in a desultory, spasmodic fashion from golf clubs to the causes of the change in the obliquity of the ecliptic, came round at last to the question of atavism and hereditary aptitudes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "The point under discussion was, how far any singular gift in an individual was due to his ancestry and how far to his own early training.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "\\"In your own case,\\" said I, \\"from all that you have told me, it seems obvious that your faculty of observation and your peculiar facility for deduction are due to your own systematic training.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "\\"To some extent,\\" he answered, thoughtfully.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "\\"My ancestors were country squires, who appear to have led much the same life as is natural to their class.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "But, none the less, my turn that way is in my veins, and may have come with my grandmother, who was the sister of Vernet, the French artist.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "Art in the blood is liable to take the strangest forms.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "\\"But how do you know that it is hereditary?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "\\"Because my brother Mycroft possesses it in a larger degree than I do.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "This was news to me indeed.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "If there were another man with such singular powers in England, how was it that neither police nor public had heard of him?", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "I put the question, with a hint that it was my companion's modesty which made him acknowledge his brother as his superior.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "Holmes laughed at my suggestion.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"My dear Watson,\\" said he, \\"I cannot agree with those who rank modesty among the virtues.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "To the logician all things should be seen exactly as they are, and to underestimate one's self is as much a departure from truth as to exaggerate one's own powers.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "When I say, therefore, that Mycroft has better powers of observation than I, you may take it that I am speaking the exact and literal truth.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "\\"Is he your junior?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "\\"Seven years my senior.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "\\"How comes it that he is unknown?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "\\"Oh, he is very well known in his own circle.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "\\"Where, then?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "\\"Well, in the Diogenes Club, for example.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "I had never heard of the institution, and my face must have proclaimed as much, for Sherlock Holmes pulled out his watch.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "\\"The Diogenes Club is the queerest club in London, and Mycroft one of the queerest men.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "He's always there from quarter to five to twenty to eight.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "It's six now, so if you care for a stroll this beautiful evening I shall be very happy to introduce you to two curiosities.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "Five minutes later we were in the street, walking towards Regent's Circus.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "\\"You wonder,\\" said my companion, \\"why it is that Mycroft does not use his powers for detective work.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "He is incapable of it.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_1", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "\\"But I thought you said—\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "\\"I said that he was my superior in observation and deduction.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "If the art of the detective began and ended in reasoning from an armchair, my brother would be the greatest criminal agent that ever lived.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "But he has no ambition and no energy.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "He will not even go out of his way to verify his own solutions, and would rather be considered wrong than take the trouble to prove himself right.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "Again and again I have taken a problem to him, and have received an explanation which has afterwards proved to be the correct one.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "And yet he was absolutely incapable of working out the practical points which must be gone into before a case could be laid before a judge or jury.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "\\"It is not his profession, then?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "\\"By no means.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "What is to me a means of livelihood is to him the merest hobby of a dilettante.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "He has an extraordinary faculty for figures, and audits the books in some of the government departments.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "Mycroft lodges in Pall Mall, and he walks round the corner into Whitehall every morning and back every evening.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "From year's end to year's end he takes no other exercise, and is seen nowhere else, except only in the Diogenes Club, which is just opposite his rooms.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "\\"I cannot recall the name.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "\\"Very likely not.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "There are many men in London, you know, who, some from shyness, some from misanthropy, have no wish for the company of their fellows.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "Yet they are not averse to comfortable chairs and the latest periodicals.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "It is for the convenience of these that the Diogenes Club was started, and it now contains the most unsociable and unclubable men in town.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "No member is permitted to take the least notice of any other one.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "Save in the Stranger's Room, no talking is, under any circumstances, allowed, and three offences, if brought to the notice of the committee, render the talker liable to expulsion.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "My brother was one of the founders, and I have myself found it a very soothing atmosphere.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "We had reached Pall Mall as we talked, and were walking down it from the St. James's end.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes stopped at a door some little distance from the Carlton, and, cautioning me not to speak, he led the way into the hall.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "Through the glass paneling I caught a glimpse of a large and luxurious room, in which a considerable number of men were sitting about and reading papers, each in his own little nook.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "Holmes showed me into a small chamber which looked out into Pall Mall, and then, leaving me for a minute, he came back with a companion whom I knew could only be his brother.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "Mycroft Holmes was a much larger and stouter man than Sherlock.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "His body was absolutely corpulent, but his face, though massive, had preserved something of the sharpness of expression which was so remarkable in that of his brother.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "His eyes, which were of a peculiarly light, watery grey, seemed to always retain that far-away, introspective look which I had only observed in Sherlock's when he was exerting his full powers.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "\\"I am glad to meet you, sir,\\" said he, putting out a broad, fat hand like the flipper of a seal.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	sentence_2323	lexical	\N	\N	2322	{"text": "“Scowrers!", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "\\"I hear of Sherlock everywhere since you became his chronicler.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "By the way, Sherlock, I expected to see you round last week, to consult me over that Manor House case.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "I thought you might be a little out of your depth.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "\\"No, I solved it,\\" said my friend, smiling.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "\\"It was Adams, of course.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "\\"Yes, it was Adams.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "\\"I was sure of it from the first.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "The two sat down together in the bow-window of the club.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "\\"To any one who wishes to study mankind this is the spot,\\" said Mycroft.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "\\"Look at the magnificent types!", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "Look at these two men who are coming towards us, for example.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "\\"The billiard-marker and the other?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "\\"Precisely.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "What do you make of the other?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "The two men had stopped opposite the window.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "Some chalk marks over the waistcoat pocket were the only signs of billiards which I could see in one of them.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "The other was a very small, dark fellow, with his hat pushed back and several packages under his arm.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "\\"An old soldier, I perceive,\\" said Sherlock.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "\\"And very recently discharged,\\" remarked the brother.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "\\"Served in India, I see.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "\\"And a non-commissioned officer.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "\\"Royal Artillery, I fancy,\\" said Sherlock.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "\\"And a widower.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "\\"But with a child.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "\\"Children, my dear boy, children.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "\\"Come,\\" said I, laughing, \\"this is a little too much.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "\\"Surely,\\" answered Holmes, \\"it is not hard to say that a man with that bearing, expression of authority, and sunbaked skin, is a soldier, is more than a private, and is not long from India.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "\\"That he has not left the service long is shown by his still wearing his ammunition boots, as they are called,\\" observed Mycroft.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "\\"He had not the cavalry stride, yet he wore his hat on one side, as is shown by the lighter skin of that side of his brow.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "His weight is against his being a sapper.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "He is in the artillery.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "\\"Then, of course, his complete mourning shows that he has lost some one very dear.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "The fact that he is doing his own shopping looks as though it were his wife.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "He has been buying things for children, you perceive.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "There is a rattle, which shows that one of them is very young.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "The wife probably died in childbed.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "The fact that he has a picture-book under his arm shows that there is another child to be thought of.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "\\"I will be at your service in an instant, Watson.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "I began to understand what my friend meant when he said that his brother possessed even keener faculties that he did himself.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "He glanced across at me and smiled.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "Mycroft took snuff from a tortoise-shell box, and brushed away the wandering grains from his coat front with a large, red silk handkerchief.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "\\"By the way, Sherlock,\\" said he, \\"I have had something quite after your own heart—a most singular problem—submitted to my judgment.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "I really had not the energy to follow it up save in a very incomplete fashion, but it gave me a basis for some pleasing speculation.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "If you would care to hear the facts—\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "\\"My dear Mycroft, I should be delighted.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "The brother scribbled a note upon a leaf of his pocket-book, and, ringing the bell, he handed it to the waiter.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "\\"I have asked Mr. Melas to step across,\\" said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "\\"He lodges on the floor above me, and I have some slight acquaintance with him, which led him to come to me in his perplexity.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "Mr. Melas is a Greek by extraction, as I understand, and he is a remarkable linguist.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "He earns his living partly as interpreter in the law courts and partly by acting as guide to any wealthy Orientals who may visit the Northumberland Avenue hotels.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "I think I will leave him to tell his very remarkable experience in his own fashion.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "A few minutes later we were joined by a short, stout man whose olive face and coal-black hair proclaimed his Southern origin, though his speech was that of an educated Englishman.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "He shook hands eagerly with Sherlock Holmes, and his dark eyes sparkled with pleasure when he understood that the specialist was anxious to hear his story.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_3", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "\\"I do not believe that the police credit me—on my word, I do not,\\" said he in a wailing voice.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "\\"Just because they have never heard of it before, they think that such a thing cannot be.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "But I know that I shall never be easy in my mind until I know what has become of my poor man with the sticking-plaster upon his face.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "\\"I am all attention,\\" said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "\\"This is Wednesday evening,\\" said Mr. Melas.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "\\"Well then, it was Monday night—only two days ago, you understand—that all this happened.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "I am an interpreter, as perhaps my neighbour there has told you.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "I interpret all languages—or nearly all—but as I am a Greek by birth and with a Grecian name, it is with that particular tongue that I am principally associated.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "For many years I have been the chief Greek interpreter in London, and my name is very well known in the hotels.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "\\"It happens not unfrequently that I am sent for at strange hours by foreigners who get into difficulties, or by travelers who arrive late and wish my services.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "I was not surprised, therefore, on Monday night when a Mr. Latimer, a very fashionably dressed young man, came up to my rooms and asked me to accompany him in a cab which was waiting at the door.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "A Greek friend had come to see him upon business, he said, and as he could speak nothing but his own tongue, the services of an interpreter were indispensable.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "He gave me to understand that his house was some little distance off, in Kensington, and he seemed to be in a great hurry, bustling me rapidly into the cab when we had descended to the street.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "\\"I say into the cab, but I soon became doubtful as to whether it was not a carriage in which I found myself.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "It was certainly more roomy than the ordinary four-wheeled disgrace to London, and the fittings, though frayed, were of rich quality.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "Mr. Latimer seated himself opposite to me and we started off through Charing Cross and up the Shaftesbury Avenue.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "We had come out upon Oxford Street and I had ventured some remark as to this being a roundabout way to Kensington, when my words were arrested by the extraordinary conduct of my companion.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "\\"He began by drawing a most formidable-looking bludgeon loaded with lead from his pocket, and switching it backward and forward several times, as if to test its weight and strength.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "Then he placed it without a word upon the seat beside him.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "Having done this, he drew up the windows on each side, and I found to my astonishment that they were covered with paper so as to prevent my seeing through them.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "\\"'I am sorry to cut off your view, Mr. Melas,' said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "'The fact is that I have no intention that you should see what the place is to which we are driving.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "It might possibly be inconvenient to me if you could find your way there again.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "\\"As you can imagine, I was utterly taken aback by such an address.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "My companion was a powerful, broad-shouldered young fellow, and, apart from the weapon, I should not have had the slightest chance in a struggle with him.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "\\"'This is very extraordinary conduct, Mr. Latimer,' I stammered.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "'You must be aware that what you are doing is quite illegal.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "\\"'It is somewhat of a liberty, no doubt,' said he, 'but we'll make it up to you.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "I must warn you, however, Mr. Melas, that if at any time to-night you attempt to raise an alarm or do anything which is against my interests, you will find it a very serious thing.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "I beg you to remember that no one knows where you are, and that, whether you are in this carriage or in my house, you are equally in my power.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "\\"His words were quiet, but he had a rasping way of saying them which was very menacing.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "I sat in silence wondering what on earth could be his reason for kidnapping me in this extraordinary fashion.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "Whatever it might be, it was perfectly clear that there was no possible use in my resisting, and that I could only wait to see what might befall.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "\\"For nearly two hours we drove without my having the least clue as to where we were going.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "Sometimes the rattle of the stones told of a paved causeway, and at others our smooth, silent course suggested asphalt; but, save by this variation in sound, there was nothing at all which could in the remotest way help me to form a guess as to where we were.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "The paper over each window was impenetrable to light, and a blue curtain was drawn across the glass work in front.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "It was a quarter-past seven when we left Pall Mall, and my watch showed me that it was ten minutes to nine when we at last came to a standstill.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "My companion let down the window, and I caught a glimpse of a low, arched doorway with a lamp burning above it.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "As I was hurried from the carriage it swung open, and I found myself inside the house, with a vague impression of a lawn and trees on each side of me as I entered.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "Whether these were private grounds, however, or _bonâ-fide_ country was more than I could possibly venture to say.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "\\"There was a coloured gas-lamp inside which was turned so low that I could see little save that the hall was of some size and hung with pictures.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "In the dim light I could make out that the person who had opened the door was a small, mean-looking, middle-aged man with rounded shoulders.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "As he turned towards us the glint of the light showed me that he was wearing glasses.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "' said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "Mr. Melas, Harold?' said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "No ill-will, Mr. Melas, I hope, but we could not get on without you.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "If you deal fair with us you'll not regret it, but if you try any tricks, God help you!'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "He spoke in a nervous, jerky fashion, and with little giggling laughs in between, but somehow he impressed me with fear more than the other.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "you want with me?' I asked.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "\\"'Only to ask a few questions of a Greek gentleman who is visiting us, and to let us have the answers.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "But say no more than you are told to say, or'—here came the nervous giggle again—'you had better never have been born.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "\\"As he spoke he opened a door and showed the way into a room which appeared to be very richly furnished, but again the only light was afforded by a single lamp half-turned down.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "The chamber was certainly large, and the way in which my feet sank into the carpet as I stepped across it told me of its richness.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "I caught glimpses of velvet chairs, a high white marble mantel-piece, and what seemed to be a suit of Japanese armour at one side of it.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "There was a chair just under the lamp, and the elderly man motioned that I should sit in it.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "The younger had left us, but he suddenly returned through another door, leading with him a gentleman clad in some sort of loose dressing-gown who moved slowly towards us.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "As he came into the circle of dim light which enables me to see him more clearly I was thrilled with horror at his appearance.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "He was deadly pale and terribly emaciated, with the protruding, brilliant eyes of a man whose spirit was greater than his strength.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "But what shocked me more than any signs of physical weakness was that his face was grotesquely criss-crossed with sticking-plaster, and that one large pad of it was fastened over his mouth.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "' cried the older man, as this strange being fell rather than sat down into a chair.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "'Are his hands loose?", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "Now, then, give him the pencil.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "You are to ask the questions, Mr. Melas, and he will write the answers.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "nd he will write the answers. Ask him first of all whether he is prepared to sign the papers?'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "\\"The man's eyes flashed fire.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "' he wrote in Greek upon the slate.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "e slate.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "' I asked, at the bidding of our tyrant.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "ing of our tyrant.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "\\"'Only if I see her married in my presence by a Greek priest whom I know.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "\\"The man giggled in his venomous way.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "\\"'You know what awaits you, then?'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "\\"'I care nothing for myself.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "\\"These are samples of the questions and answers which made up our strange half-spoken, half-written conversation.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "Again and again I had to ask him whether he would give in and sign the documents.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "Again and again I had the same indignant reply.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "But soon a happy thought came to me.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "'You perceive that we have taken you into our confidence over some very private business.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "I took to adding on little sentences of my own to each question, innocent ones at first, to test whether either of our companions knew anything of the matter, and then, as I found that they showed no signs I played a more dangerous game.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "Our conversation ran something like this:", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "\\"'You can do no good by this obstinacy.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "_Who are you?_'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "\\"'I care not.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "_I am a stranger in London._'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "\\"'Your fate will be upon your own head.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "_How long have you been here?_'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "\\"'Let it be so.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "_Three weeks._'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "\\"'The property can never be yours.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "_What ails you?_'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "\\"'It shall not go to villains.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "_They are starving me._'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "\\"'You shall go free if you sign.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "_What house is this?_'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "\\"'I will never sign.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "_I do not know._'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "\\"'You are not doing her any service.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "_What is your name?_'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "\\"'Let me hear her say so.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "_Kratides._'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "\\"'You shall see her if you sign.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "_Where are you from?_'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "\\"'Then I shall never see her.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "_Athens._'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "\\"Another five minutes, Mr. Holmes, and I should have wormed out the whole story under their very noses.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "My very next question might have cleared the matter up, but at that instant the door opened and a woman stepped into the room.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "I could not see her clearly enough to know more than that she was tall and graceful, with black hair, and clad in some sort of loose white gown.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "\\"'Harold,' said she, speaking English with a broken accent.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "'I could not stay away longer.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "It is so lonely up there with only—Oh, my God, it is Paul!'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "\\"These last words were in Greek, and at the same instant the man with a convulsive effort tore the plaster from his lips, and screaming out 'Sophy!", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "' rushed into the woman's arms.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "Their embrace was but for an instant, however, for the younger man seized the woman and pushed her out of the room, while the elder easily overpowered his emaciated victim, and dragged him away through the other door.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "For a moment I was left alone in the room, and I sprang to my feet with some vague idea that I might in some way get a clue to what this house was in which I found myself.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "Fortunately, however, I took no steps, for looking up I saw that the older man was standing in the doorway with his eyes fixed upon me.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "on me.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "We should not have troubled you, only that our friend who speaks Greek and who began these negotiations has been forced to return to the East.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "It was quite necessary for us to find some one to take his place, and we were fortunate in hearing of your powers.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "\\"I bowed.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "\\"'There are five sovereigns here,' said he, walking up to me, 'which will, I hope, be a sufficient fee.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "But remember,' he added, tapping me lightly on the chest and giggling, 'if you speak to a human soul about this—one human soul, mind—well, may God have mercy upon your soul!\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "\\"I cannot tell you the loathing and horror with which this insignificant-looking man inspired me.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "I could see him better now as the lamp-light shone upon him.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "His features were peaky and sallow, and his little pointed beard was thready and ill-nourished.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "He pushed his face forward as he spoke and his lips and eyelids were continually twitching like a man with St. Vitus's dance.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "I could not help thinking that his strange, catchy little laugh was also a symptom of some nervous malady.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "The terror of his face lay in his eyes, however, steel grey, and glistening coldly with a malignant, inexorable cruelty in their depths.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "\\"'We shall know if you speak of this,' said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "'We have our own means of information.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "Now you will find the carriage waiting, and my friend will see you on your way.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "\\"I was hurried through the hall and into the vehicle, again obtaining that momentary glimpse of trees and a garden.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "Mr. Latimer followed closely at my heels, and took his place opposite to me without a word.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "In silence we again drove for an interminable distance with the windows raised, until at last, just after midnight, the carriage pulled up.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "\\"'You will get down here, Mr. Melas,' said my companion.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "'I am sorry to leave you so far from your house, but there is no alternative.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "Any attempt upon your part to follow the carriage can only end in injury to yourself.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "\\"He opened the door as he spoke, and I had hardly time to spring out when the coachman lashed the horse and the carriage rattled away.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "I looked around me in astonishment.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "I was on some sort of a heathy common mottled over with dark clumps of furze-bushes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "Far away stretched a line of houses, with a light here and there in the upper windows.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "On the other side I saw the red signal-lamps of a railway.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "\\"The carriage which had brought me was already out of sight.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "I stood gazing round and wondering where on earth I might be, when I saw some one coming towards me in the darkness.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "As he came up to me I made out that he was a railway porter.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "tell me what place this is?' I asked.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "\\"'Wandsworth Common,' said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "\\"'Can I get a train into town?'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "\\"'If you walk on a mile or so to Clapham Junction,' said he, 'you'll just be in time for the last to Victoria.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "\\"So that was the end of my adventure, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "I do not know where I was, nor whom I spoke with, nor anything save what I have told you.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "But I know that there is foul play going on, and I want to help that unhappy man if I can.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "I told the whole story to Mr. Mycroft Holmes next morning, and subsequently to the police.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "We all sat in silence for some little time after listening to this extraordinary narrative.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "Then Sherlock looked across at his brother.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "\\"Any steps?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "Mycroft picked up the _Daily News_, which was lying on the side-table.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "\\"'Anybody supplying any information to the whereabouts of a Greek gentleman named Paul Kratides, from Athens, who is unable to speak English, will be rewarded.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "A similar reward paid to any one giving information about a Greek lady whose first name is Sophy.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "' That was in all the dailies.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "No answer.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "nswer.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "\\"How about the Greek Legation?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "\\"I have inquired.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "They know nothing.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "\\"A wire to the head of the Athens police, then?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "\\"Sherlock has all the energy of the family,\\" said Mycroft, turning to me.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "\\"Well, you take the case up by all means, and let me know if you do any good.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "\\"Certainly,\\" answered my friend, rising from his chair.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "\\"I'll let you know, and Mr. Melas also.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "In the meantime, Mr. Melas, I should certainly be on my guard, if I were you, for of course they must know through these advertisements that you have betrayed them.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "As we walked home together, Holmes stopped at a telegraph office and sent off several wires.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "\\"You see, Watson,\\" he remarked, \\"our evening has been by no means wasted.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "Some of my most interesting cases have come to me in this way through Mycroft.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "The problem which we have just listened to, although it can admit of but one explanation, has still some distinguishing features.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "\\"You have hopes of solving it?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "\\"Well, knowing as much as we do, it will be singular indeed if we fail to discover the rest.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "You must yourself have formed some theory which will explain the facts to which we have listened.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "\\"In a vague way, yes.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "\\"What was your idea, then?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "\\"It seemed to me to be obvious that this Greek girl had been carried off by the young Englishman named Harold Latimer.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "\\"Carried off from where?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "\\"Athens, perhaps.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes shook his head.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "\\"This young man could not talk a word of Greek.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "The lady could talk English fairly well.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "Inference, that she had been in England some little time, but he had not been in Greece.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "\\"Well, then, we will presume that she had come on a visit to England, and that this Harold had persuaded her to fly with him.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "\\"That is more probable.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "\\"Then the brother—for that, I fancy, must be the relationship—comes over from Greece to interfere.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "He imprudently puts himself into the power of the young man and his older associate.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "They seize him and use violence towards him in order to make him sign some papers to make over the girl's fortune—of which he may be trustee—to them.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "This he refuses to do.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "In order to negotiate with him they have to get an interpreter, and they pitch upon this Mr. Melas, having used some other one before.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "The girl is not told of the arrival of her brother, and finds it out by the merest accident.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "\\"Excellent, Watson!\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "cried Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "\\"I really fancy that you are not far from the truth.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "You see that we hold all the cards, and we have only to fear some sudden act of violence on their part.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "If they give us time we must have them.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "\\"But how can we find where this house lies?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "\\"Well, if our conjecture is correct and the girl's name is or was Sophy Kratides, we should have no difficulty in tracing her.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "That must be our main hope, for the brother is, of course, a complete stranger.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "It is clear that some time has elapsed since this Harold established these relations with the girl—some weeks, at any rate—since the brother in Greece has had time to hear of it and come across.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "If they have been living in the same place during this time, it is probable that we shall have some answer to Mycroft's advertisement.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "We had reached our house in Baker Street while we had been talking.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "Holmes ascended the stair first, and as he opened the door of our room he gave a start of surprise.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "Looking over his shoulder, I was equally astonished.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "His brother Mycroft was sitting smoking in the armchair.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "\\"Come in, Sherlock!", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "Come in, sir,\\" said he blandly, smiling at our surprised faces.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "\\"You don't expect such energy from me, do you, Sherlock?", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "But somehow this case attracts me.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "\\"How did you get here?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "\\"I passed you in a hansom.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "\\"There has been some new development?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "\\"I had an answer to my advertisement.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "\\"Ah!\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "\\"Yes, it came within a few minutes of your leaving.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "\\"And to what effect?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "Mycroft Holmes took out a sheet of paper.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "\\"Here it is,\\" said he, \\"written with a J pen on royal cream paper by a middle-aged man with a weak constitution.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "'Sir,' he says, 'in answer to your advertisement of to-day's date, I beg to inform you that I know the young lady in question very well.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "If you should care to call upon me I could give you some particulars as to her painful history.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "She is living at present at The Myrtles, Beckenham.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "Yours faithfully, J.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "Davenport.'", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "\\"He writes from Lower Brixton,\\" said Mycroft Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "\\"Do you not think that we might drive to him now, Sherlock, and learn these particulars?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "\\"My dear Mycroft, the brother's life is more valuable than the sister's story.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "I think we should call at Scotland Yard for Inspector Gregson, and go straight out to Beckenham.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "We know that a man is being done to death, and every hour may be vital.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "\\"Better pick up Mr. Melas on our way,\\" I suggested.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "\\"We may need an interpreter.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "\\"Excellent,\\" said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "\\"Send the boy for a four-wheeler, and we shall be off at once.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "He opened the table-drawer as he spoke, and I noticed that he slipped his revolver into his pocket.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "\\"Yes,\\" said he, in answer to my glance; \\"I should say from what we have heard, that we are dealing with a particularly dangerous gang.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "It was almost dark before we found ourselves in Pall Mall, at the rooms of Mr. Melas.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "A gentleman had just called for him, and he was gone.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "\\"Can you tell me where?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "asked Mycroft Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "\\"I don't know, sir,\\" answered the woman who had opened the door; \\"I only know that he drove away with the gentleman in a carriage.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "\\"Did the gentleman give a name?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "\\"No, sir.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "\\"He wasn't a tall, handsome, dark young man?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "\\"Oh, no, sir.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "He was a little gentleman, with glasses, thin in the face, but very pleasant in his ways, for he was laughing all the time that he was talking.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "\\"Come along!\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "cried Sherlock Holmes, abruptly.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "\\"This grows serious,\\" he observed, as we drove to Scotland Yard.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "\\"These men have got hold of Melas again.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "He is a man of no physical courage, as they are well aware from their experience the other night.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "This villain was able to terrorise him the instant that he got into his presence.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "No doubt they want his professional services, but, having used him, they may be inclined to punish him for what they will regard as his treachery.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "Our hope was that, by taking train, we might get to Beckenham as soon or sooner than the carriage.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "On reaching Scotland Yard, however, it was more than an hour before we could get Inspector Gregson and comply with the legal formalities which would enable us to enter the house.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "He dipped it into the test-tube and it flushed at once into a dull, dirty crimson.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "It was a quarter to ten before we reached London Bridge, and half past before the four of us alighted on the Beckenham platform.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "A drive of half a mile brought us to The Myrtles—a large, dark house standing back from the road in its own grounds.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "Here we dismissed our cab, and made our way up the drive together.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "\\"The windows are all dark,\\" remarked the inspector.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "\\"The house seems deserted.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "\\"Our birds are flown and the nest empty,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "\\"Why do you say so?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "\\"A carriage heavily loaded with luggage has passed out during the last hour.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "The inspector laughed.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "\\"I saw the wheel-tracks in the light of the gate-lamp, but where does the luggage come in?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "\\"You may have observed the same wheel-tracks going the other way.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "But the outward-bound ones were very much deeper—so much so that we can say for a certainty that there was a very considerable weight on the carriage.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "\\"You get a trifle beyond me there,\\" said the inspector, shrugging his shoulder.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "\\"It will not be an easy door to force, but we will try if we cannot make some one hear us.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "He hammered loudly at the knocker and pulled at the bell, but without any success.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "Holmes had slipped away, but he came back in a few minutes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "\\"I have a window open,\\" said he.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "\\"It is a mercy that you are on the side of the force, and not against it, Mr. Holmes,\\" remarked the inspector, as he noted the clever way in which my friend had forced back the catch.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "\\"Well, I think that under the circumstances we may enter without an invitation.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "One after the other we made our way into a large apartment, which was evidently that in which Mr. Melas had found himself.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "The inspector had lit his lantern, and by its light we could see the two doors, the curtain, the lamp, and the suit of Japanese mail as he had described them.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "On the table lay two glasses, and empty brandy-bottle, and the remains of a meal.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "\\"What is that?\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "asked Holmes, suddenly.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "We all stood still and listened.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "A low moaning sound was coming from somewhere over our heads.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "Holmes rushed to the door and out into the hall.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "The dismal noise came from upstairs.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "He dashed up, the inspector and I at his heels, while his brother Mycroft followed as quickly as his great bulk would permit.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "Three doors faced up upon the second floor, and it was from the central of these that the sinister sounds were issuing, sinking sometimes into a dull mumble and rising again into a shrill whine.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "It was locked, but the key had been left on the outside.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "Holmes flung open the door and rushed in, but he was out again in an instant, with his hand to his throat.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "\\"It's charcoal,\\" he cried.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "\\"Give it time.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "It will clear.\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "Peering in, we could see that the only light in the room came from a dull blue flame which flickered from a small brass tripod in the centre.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "It threw a livid, unnatural circle upon the floor, while in the shadows beyond we saw the vague loom of two figures which crouched against the wall.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "From the open door there reeked a horrible poisonous exhalation which set us gasping and coughing.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "Holmes rushed to the top of the stairs to draw in the fresh air, and then, dashing into the room, he threw up the window and hurled the brazen tripod out into the garden.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "\\"We can enter in a minute,\\" he gasped, darting out again.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "\\"Where is a candle?", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "I doubt if we could strike a match in that atmosphere.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "Hold the light at the door and we shall get them out, Mycroft, now!\\"", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "With a rush we got to the poisoned men and dragged them out into the well-lit hall.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "Both of them were blue-lipped and insensible, with swollen, congested faces and protruding eyes.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "Indeed, so distorted were their features that, save for his black beard and stout figure, we might have failed to recognise in one of them the Greek interpreter who had parted from us only a few hours before at the Diogenes Club.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "His hands and feet were securely strapped together, and he bore over one eye the marks of a violent blow.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "The other, who was secured in a similar fashion, was a tall man in the last stage of emaciation, with several strips of sticking-plaster arranged in a grotesque pattern over his face.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "He had ceased to moan as we laid him down, and a glance showed me that for him at least our aid had come too late.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "Mr. Melas, however, still lived, and in less than an hour, with the aid of ammonia and brandy I had the satisfaction of seeing him open his eyes, and of knowing that my hand had drawn him back from that dark valley in which all paths meet.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "It was a simple story which he had to tell, and one which did but confirm our own deductions.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "His visitor, on entering his rooms, had drawn a life-preserver from his sleeve, and had so impressed him with the fear of instant and inevitable death that he had kidnapped him for the second time.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "Indeed, it was almost mesmeric, the effect which this giggling ruffian had produced upon the unfortunate linguist, for he could not speak of him save with trembling hands and a blanched cheek.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "He had been taken swiftly to Beckenham, and had acted as interpreter in a second interview, even more dramatic than the first, in which the two Englishmen had menaced their prisoner with instant death if he did not comply with their demands.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "Finally, finding him proof against every threat, they had hurled him back into his prison, and after reproaching Melas with his treachery, which appeared from the newspaper advertisement, they had stunned him with a blow from a stick, and he remembered nothing more until he found us bending over him.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "And this was the singular case of the Grecian Interpreter, the explanation of which is still involved in some mystery.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "We were able to find out, by communicating with the gentleman who had answered the advertisement, that the unfortunate young lady came of a wealthy Grecian family, and that she had been on a visit to some friends in England.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "While there she had met a young man named Harold Latimer, who had acquired an ascendancy over her and had eventually persuaded her to fly with him.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "Her friends, shocked at the event, had contented themselves with informing her brother at Athens, and had then washed their hands of the matter.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "The brother, on his arrival in England, had imprudently placed himself in the power of Latimer and of his associate, whose name was Wilson Kemp—a man of the foulest antecedents.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "These two, finding that through his ignorance of the language he was helpless in their hands, had kept him a prisoner, and had endeavoured by cruelty and starvation to make him sign away his own and his sister's property.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "\\"Hum!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "They had kept him in the house without the girl's knowledge, and the plaster over the face had been for the purpose of making recognition difficult in case she should ever catch a glimpse of him.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "Her feminine perception, however, had instantly seen through the disguise when, on the occasion of the interpreter's visit, she had seen him for the first time.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "The poor girl, however, was herself a prisoner, for there was no one about the house except the man who acted as coachman, and his wife, both of whom were tools of the conspirators.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "Finding that their secret was out, and that their prisoner was not to be coerced, the two villains with the girl had fled away at a few hours' notice from the furnished house which they had hired, having first, as they thought, taken vengeance both upon the man who had defied and the one who had betrayed them.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "Months afterwards a curious newspaper cutting reached us from Buda-Pesth.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "It told how two Englishmen who had been traveling with a woman had met with a tragic end.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "They had each been stabbed, it seems, and the Hungarian police were of opinion that they had quarreled and had inflicted mortal injuries upon each other.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "Holmes, however, is, I fancy, of a different way of thinking, and holds to this day that, if one could find the Grecian girl, one might learn how the wrongs of herself and her brother came to be avenged.", "section": "greek-interpreter-section_11", "entities": []}
greek-interpreter	sherlock_holmes	entity	character	Sherlock Holmes	\N	{"description": "Detective and narrator's companion", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_1"}
greek-interpreter	watson	entity	character	Watson	\N	{"description": "Narrator and companion of Holmes", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_1"}
greek-interpreter	mycroft_holmes	entity	character	Mycroft Holmes	\N	{"description": "Sherlock Holmes's brother", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_1"}
greek-interpreter	vernets_sister	entity	character	Vernet's sister	\N	{"description": "Holmes's grandmother; sister of the French artist Vernet", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_1"}
greek-interpreter	vernet	entity	character	Vernet	\N	{"description": "French artist mentioned as Holmes's grandmother's brother", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_1"}
greek-interpreter	diogenes_club	entity	organisation	Diogenes Club	\N	{"org_type": "club", "description": "A club in London associated with Mycroft Holmes", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_1"}
greek-interpreter	pall_mall	entity	location	Pall Mall	\N	{"description": "A London street", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_2"}
greek-interpreter	whitehall	entity	location	Whitehall	\N	{"description": "A London district and street", "firstSection": "greek-interpreter-section_2"}
