greek-interpreter	event_4_9	event	\N	Latimer speaks to Mr. Melas and threatens him	3	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_4", "speakerId": "latimer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_137", "sentence_138", "sentence_139", "sentence_142", "sentence_143", "sentence_144", "sentence_145", "sentence_146"], "communicatesContent": "I am sorry to cut off your view, Mr. Melas. I have no intention that you should see what the place is to which we are driving. It might possibly be inconvenient to me if you could find your way there again. It is somewhat of a liberty, no doubt, but we'll make it up to you. I must warn you, however, Mr. Melas, that if at any time to-night you attempt to raise an alarm or do anything which is against my interests, you will find it a very serious thing. I beg you to remember that no one knows where you are, and that, whether you are in this carriage or in my house, you are equally in my power."}
