greek-interpreter	event_5_3	event	\N	The elderly man opens the door and greets Mr. Melas as Harold	4	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "speakerId": "elderly_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_158", "sentence_159", "sentence_160", "sentence_161", "sentence_162", "sentence_163", "sentence_164", "sentence_165"], "communicatesContent": "Mr. Melas, Harold?"}
greek-interpreter	event_5_4	event	\N	The elderly man threatens Mr. Melas with warning conditions	4	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "speakerId": "elderly_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_163", "sentence_164", "sentence_165", "sentence_166"], "communicatesContent": "Well done, well done! No ill-will, Mr. Melas, I hope, but we could not get on without you. If you deal fair with us you'll not regret it, but if you try any tricks, God help you!"}
greek-interpreter	event_5_5	event	\N	The elderly man leads Mr. Melas into a richly furnished room	4	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_171", "sentence_172", "sentence_173", "sentence_174"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_5_6	event	\N	The younger man returns leading a gentleman into the room	4	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_175", "sentence_176"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_6_1	event	\N	Mr. Melas continues a half-spoken, half-written conversation with the detained man	5	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "speakerId": "mr_melas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_193", "sentence_194", "sentence_195", "sentence_196", "sentence_197", "sentence_198", "sentence_199", "sentence_200", "sentence_201", "sentence_202", "sentence_203", "sentence_204", "sentence_205", "sentence_206", "sentence_207", "sentence_208", "sentence_209", "sentence_210", "sentence_211", "sentence_212", "sentence_213", "sentence_214", "sentence_215", "sentence_216", "sentence_217", "sentence_218", "sentence_219", "sentence_220", "sentence_221", "sentence_222"], "communicatesContent": "You can do no good by this obstinacy. Your fate will be upon your own head. The property can never be yours. You shall go free if you sign. You are not doing her any service. You shall see her if you sign. Ask him whether he will give in and sign the documents."}
greek-interpreter	event_6_2	event	\N	The detained man writes answers on the slate	5	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "speakerId": "elderly_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_185", "sentence_187", "sentence_189", "sentence_190", "sentence_191", "sentence_192"], "communicatesContent": "Only if I see her married in my presence by a Greek priest whom I know. I care nothing for myself."}
greek-interpreter	event_6_3	event	\N	A woman enters the room and speaks to the detained men	5	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "speakerId": "sophy", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_224", "sentence_225", "sentence_226", "sentence_227", "sentence_228"], "communicatesContent": "Harold, I could not stay away longer. It is so lonely up there with only—Oh, my God, it is Paul!"}
greek-interpreter	event_6_4	event	\N	The woman and Paul embrace, then he is seized and dragged away	5	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "speakerId": "paul", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_229", "sentence_230", "sentence_231"], "communicatesContent": "Sophy!"}
greek-interpreter	event_6_5	event	\N	The older man explains why Mr. Melas was brought in	5	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_6", "speakerId": "elderly_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_235", "sentence_236", "sentence_237", "sentence_238"], "communicatesContent": "That will do, Mr. Melas. We have taken you into our confidence over some very private business. Our friend who speaks Greek and who began these negotiations has been forced to return to the East. It was necessary to find someone to take his place, and we were fortunate in hearing of your powers."}
greek-interpreter	event_7_1	event	\N	Mr. Melas bows	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_239"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_7_2	event	\N	Latimer tells Melas about the fee and warns him to stay silent	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": "latimer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_240", "sentence_241"], "communicatesContent": "There are five sovereigns here, which will, I hope, be a sufficient fee. But remember, if you speak to a human soul about this—one human soul, mind—well, may God have mercy upon your soul!"}
greek-interpreter	event_7_3	event	\N	Latimer threatens Melas with discovery if he speaks	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": "latimer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_248", "sentence_249", "sentence_250"], "communicatesContent": "We shall know if you speak of this. We have our own means of information. Now you will find the carriage waiting, and my friend will see you on your way."}
greek-interpreter	event_7_4	event	\N	Melas is hurried into the carriage and departs	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_251", "sentence_252", "sentence_253", "sentence_257"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_7_5	event	\N	Latimer tells Melas to get down and warns him not to follow the carriage	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": "latimer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_254", "sentence_255", "sentence_256"], "communicatesContent": "You will get down here, Mr. Melas. I am sorry to leave you so far from your house, but there is no alternative. Any attempt upon your part to follow the carriage can only end in injury to yourself."}
greek-interpreter	event_10_7	event	\N	Holmes says they may enter without an invitation	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_397"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I think that under the circumstances we may enter without an invitation."}
greek-interpreter	event_7_6	event	\N	Melas is left on Wandsworth Common	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": "porter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_257", "sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260", "sentence_261", "sentence_262", "sentence_263", "sentence_264", "sentence_267"], "communicatesContent": "Wandsworth Common."}
greek-interpreter	event_7_7	event	\N	The railway porter tells Melas how to get a train to town	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": "railway_porter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_265", "sentence_266", "sentence_268", "sentence_269"], "communicatesContent": "If you walk on a mile or so to Clapham Junction, you'll just be in time for the last to Victoria."}
greek-interpreter	event_7_8	event	\N	Melas reports the story to Mycroft Holmes and the police	6	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_7", "speakerId": "mr_melas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_273"], "communicatesContent": "the whole story"}
greek-interpreter	event_8_1	event	\N	Mycroft says that he has inquired and they know nothing.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_285", "sentence_286"], "communicatesContent": "I have inquired. They know nothing."}
greek-interpreter	event_8_2	event	\N	Someone proposes sending a wire to the head of the Athens police.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": "A wire to the head of the Athens police, then?"}
greek-interpreter	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes sends several telegrams.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_293"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_8_4	event	\N	Watson suggests that Harold Latimer carried off a Greek girl.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_300", "sentence_301", "sentence_302"], "communicatesContent": "It seemed to me to be obvious that this Greek girl had been carried off by the young Englishman named Harold Latimer."}
greek-interpreter	event_8_5	event	\N	Watson states that the girl may have come on a visit to England and that Harold persuaded her to flee with him.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_309", "sentence_310"], "communicatesContent": "Well, then, we will presume that she had come on a visit to England, and that this Harold had persuaded her to fly with him."}
greek-interpreter	event_8_6	event	\N	Watson describes the brother coming from Greece, being seized, and being forced to sign papers for the girl's fortune.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_313", "sentence_314", "sentence_315", "sentence_316"], "communicatesContent": "Then the brother—for that, I fancy, must be the relationship—comes over from Greece to interfere. He imprudently puts himself into the power of the young man and his older associate. They seize him and use violence towards him in order to make him sign some papers to make over the girl's fortune—of which he may be trustee—to them. This he refuses to do. In order to negotiate with him they have to get an interpreter, and they pitch upon this Mr. Melas, having used some other one before. The girl is not told of the arrival of her brother, and finds it out by the merest accident."}
greek-interpreter	event_8_7	event	\N	Holmes praises Watson's account and says they hold all the cards.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_317", "sentence_318", "sentence_319", "sentence_320", "sentence_321"], "communicatesContent": "Excellent, Watson! I really fancy that you are not far from the truth. You see that we hold all the cards, and we have only to fear some sudden act of violence on their part. If they give us time we must have them."}
greek-interpreter	event_8_8	event	\N	Holmes says that if the girl's name is or was Sophy Kratides they should have no difficulty tracing her.	7	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_322", "sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325", "sentence_326"], "communicatesContent": "Well, if our conjecture is correct and the girl's name is or was Sophy Kratides, we should have no difficulty in tracing her. That must be our main hope, for the brother is, of course, a complete stranger. It is clear that some time has elapsed since this Harold established these relations with the girl—some weeks, at any rate—since the brother in Greece has had time to hear of it and come across. If they have been living in the same place during this time, it is probable that we shall have some answer to Mycroft's advertisement."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_1	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes greets Sherlock Holmes at the room	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_331", "sentence_332"], "communicatesContent": "Come in, Sherlock! Come in, sir."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_2	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes explains that he is attracted to the case	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_333", "sentence_334"], "communicatesContent": "You don't expect such energy from me, do you, Sherlock? But somehow this case attracts me."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_3	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes asks how Mycroft Holmes got there	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_335", "sentence_336"], "communicatesContent": "How did you get here?"}
greek-interpreter	event_9_4	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes says he passed them in a hansom	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_335", "sentence_336"], "communicatesContent": "I passed you in a hansom."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_5	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes asks whether there has been a new development	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_338"], "communicatesContent": "There has been some new development?"}
greek-interpreter	event_9_6	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes says an answer arrived to his advertisement	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_337", "sentence_338", "sentence_340"], "communicatesContent": "I had an answer to my advertisement. Yes, it came within a few minutes of your leaving."}
greek-interpreter	event_10_8	event	\N	Holmes, Watson, and the inspector enter the large apartment	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_398"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_10_9	event	\N	The inspector lights his lantern and the room reveals its contents	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_399", "sentence_400"], "communicatesContent": null}
naval-treaty	naval-treaty-section_2	section	\N	Section 2	1	{"wordCount": 650}
greek-interpreter	event_9_7	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes shows and reads the reply letter	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_342", "sentence_343", "sentence_344", "sentence_345", "sentence_346", "sentence_347", "sentence_348"], "communicatesContent": "Here it is: written with a J pen on royal cream paper by a middle-aged man with a weak constitution. Sir, in answer to your advertisement of to-day's date, I beg to inform you that I know the young lady in question very well. If you should care to call upon me I could give you some particulars as to her painful history. She is living at present at The Myrtles, Beckenham. Yours faithfully, J. Davenport."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_8	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes states that the letter writer writes from Lower Brixton	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_349"], "communicatesContent": "He writes from Lower Brixton."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_9	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes proposes going to Scotland Yard and then Beckenham	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_350", "sentence_351", "sentence_352", "sentence_353"], "communicatesContent": "My dear Mycroft, the brother's life is more valuable than the sister's story. I think we should call at Scotland Yard for Inspector Gregson, and go straight out to Beckenham. We know that a man is being done to death, and every hour may be vital."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_10	event	\N	Watson suggests picking up Mr. Melas	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_354", "sentence_355"], "communicatesContent": "Better pick up Mr. Melas on our way. We may need an interpreter."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_11	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes agrees and orders a four-wheeler	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_356", "sentence_357"], "communicatesContent": "Excellent. Send the boy for a four-wheeler, and we shall be off at once."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_12	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes arms himself with a revolver	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_358", "sentence_359"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_9_13	event	\N	The group arrives at Mr. Melas's rooms in Pall Mall and finds him gone	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_360", "sentence_361"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_9_14	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes asks where Mr. Melas has gone	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_362", "sentence_363"], "communicatesContent": "Can you tell me where?"}
greek-interpreter	event_9_15	event	\N	The woman says Mr. Melas drove away in a carriage with a gentleman	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "woman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_364", "sentence_365", "sentence_366"], "communicatesContent": "I only know that he drove away with the gentleman in a carriage. No, sir."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_16	event	\N	Mycroft Holmes asks about the gentleman's appearance	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_367", "sentence_368", "sentence_369"], "communicatesContent": "He wasn't a tall, handsome, dark young man?"}
greek-interpreter	event_9_17	event	\N	The woman describes the gentleman as a little man with glasses	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "woman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_368", "sentence_369"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, no, sir. He was a little gentleman, with glasses, thin in the face, but very pleasant in his ways, for he was laughing all the time that he was talking."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_18	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes orders the others to come along	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_370", "sentence_371"], "communicatesContent": "Come along!"}
greek-interpreter	event_9_19	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes says the matter has become serious and they drive to Scotland Yard	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_372", "sentence_373", "sentence_374", "sentence_375", "sentence_376"], "communicatesContent": "This grows serious. These men have got hold of Melas again. He is a man of no physical courage, as they are well aware from their experience the other night. This villain was able to terrorise him the instant that he got into his presence. No doubt they want his professional services, but, having used him, they may be inclined to punish him for what they will regard as his treachery."}
greek-interpreter	event_9_20	event	\N	The party travels by train toward Beckenham	8	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_377", "sentence_378", "sentence_379", "sentence_380", "sentence_381"], "communicatesContent": null}
greek-interpreter	event_10_1	event	\N	The inspector remarks that the windows are dark and the house seems deserted	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_382", "sentence_383"], "communicatesContent": "The windows are all dark. The house seems deserted."}
greek-interpreter	event_10_2	event	\N	Holmes states that a heavily loaded carriage has passed out during the last hour	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_384", "sentence_386"], "communicatesContent": "Our birds are flown and the nest empty. A carriage heavily loaded with luggage has passed out during the last hour."}
greek-interpreter	event_10_3	event	\N	The inspector laughs and questions Holmes about the luggage inference	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": "mycroft_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_387", "sentence_388", "sentence_389", "sentence_390", "sentence_391"], "communicatesContent": "Why do you say so?"}
greek-interpreter	event_10_4	event	\N	Holmes says the door may be forced and they will try to make someone hear them	9	{"section": "greek-interpreter-section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_392"], "communicatesContent": "It will not be an easy door to force, but we will try if we cannot make some one hear us."}
