naval-treaty	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "He was a very brilliant boy, and carried away every prize which the school had to offer, finished his exploits by winning a scholarship which sent him on to continue his triumphant career at Cambridge.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "He was, I remember, extremely well connected, and even when we were all little boys together we knew that his mother's brother was Lord Holdhurst, the great conservative politician.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "This gaudy relationship did him little good at school.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "On the contrary, it seemed rather a piquant thing to us to chevy him about the playground and hit him over the shins with a wicket.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "But it was another thing when he came out into the world.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "I heard vaguely that his abilities and the influences which he commanded had won him a good position at the Foreign Office, and then he passed completely out of my mind until the following letter recalled his existence:", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "Briarbrae, Woking.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "My dear Watson,—I have no doubt that you can remember \\"Tadpole\\" Phelps, who was in the fifth form when you were in the third.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "It is possible even that you may have heard that through my uncle's influence I obtained a good appointment at the Foreign Office, and that I was in a situation of trust and honour until a horrible misfortune came suddenly to blast my career.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "There is no use writing of the details of that dreadful event.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "In the event of your acceding to my request it is probable that I shall have to narrate them to you.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "I have only just recovered from nine weeks of brain-fever, and am still exceedingly weak.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "Do you think that you could bring your friend Mr. Holmes down to see me?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "I should like to have his opinion of the case, though the authorities assure me that nothing more can be done.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "Do try to bring him down, and as soon as possible.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "Every minute seems an hour while I live in this state of horrible suspense.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "Assure him that if I have not asked his advice sooner it was not because I did not appreciate his talents, but because I have been off my head ever since the blow fell.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "Now I am clear again, though I dare not think of it too much for fear of a relapse.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "I am still so weak that I have to write, as you see, by dictating.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "Do try to bring him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_1", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "Your old schoolfellow, Percy Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "There was something that touched me as I read this letter, something pitiable in the reiterated appeals to bring Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "So moved was I that even had it been a difficult matter I should have tried it, but of course I knew well that Holmes loved his art, so that he was ever as ready to bring his aid as his client could be to receive it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "My wife agreed with me that not a moment should be lost in laying the matter before him, and so within an hour of breakfast-time I found myself back once more in the old rooms in Baker Street.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "Holmes was seated at his side-table clad in his dressing-gown, and working hard over a chemical investigation.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "A large curved retort was boiling furiously in the bluish flame of a Bunsen burner, and the distilled drops were condensing into a two-litre measure.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "My friend hardly glanced up as I entered, and I, seeing that his investigation must be of importance, seated myself in an armchair and waited.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "He dipped into this bottle or that, drawing out a few drops of each with his glass pipette, and finally brought a test-tube containing a solution over to the table.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "In his right hand he held a slip of litmus-paper.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "\\"You come at a crisis, Watson,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "\\"If this paper remains blue, all is well.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "If it turns red, it means a man's life.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "You will find tobacco in the Persian slipper.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "He turned to his desk and scribbled off several telegrams, which were handed over to the page-boy.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "Then he threw himself down into the chair opposite, and drew up his knees until his fingers clasped round his long, thin shins.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "\\"A very commonplace little murder,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "\\"You've got something better, I fancy.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "You are the stormy petrel of crime, Watson.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "What is it?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "I handed him the letter, which he read with the most concentrated attention.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "\\"It does not tell us very much, does it?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "he remarked, as he handed it back to me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "\\"Hardly anything.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "\\"And yet the writing is of interest.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "\\"But the writing is not his own.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "\\"Precisely.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "It is a woman's.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "\\"A man's surely,\\" I cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "\\"No, a woman's, and a woman of rare character.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "You see, at the commencement of an investigation it is something to know that your client is in close contact with some one who, for good or evil, has an exceptional nature.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "My interest is already awakened in the case.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "If you are ready we will start at once for Woking, and see this diplomatist who is in such evil case, and the lady to whom he dictates his letters.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "We were fortunate enough to catch an early train at Waterloo, and in a little under an hour we found ourselves among the fir-woods and the heather of Woking.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "Briarbrae proved to be a large detached house standing in extensive grounds within a few minutes' walk of the station.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "On sending in our cards we were shown into an elegantly appointed drawing-room, where we were joined in a few minutes by a rather stout man who received us with much hospitality.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "His age may have been nearer forty than thirty, but his cheeks were so ruddy and his eyes so merry that he still conveyed the impression of a plump and mischievous boy.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "\\"I am so glad that you have come,\\" said he, shaking our hands with effusion.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "\\"Percy has been inquiring for you all morning.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "Ah, poor old chap, he clings to any straw!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "His father and his mother asked me to see you, for the mere mention of the subject is very painful to them.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_2", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "\\"We have had no details yet,\\" observed Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "\\"I perceive that you are not yourself a member of the family.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "Our acquaintance looked surprised, and then, glancing down, he began to laugh.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "' monogram on my locket,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "\\"For a moment I thought you had done something clever.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "Joseph Harrison is my name, and as Percy is to marry my sister Annie I shall at least be a relation by marriage.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "You will find my sister in his room, for she has nursed him hand-and-foot this two months back.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "Perhaps we'd better go in at once, for I know how impatient he is.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "I know how impatient he is.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "The chamber in which we were shown was on the same floor as the drawing-room.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "It was furnished partly as a sitting and partly as a bedroom, with flowers arranged daintily in every nook and corner.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "A young man, very pale and worn, was lying upon a sofa near the open window, through which came the rich scent of the garden and the balmy summer air.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "A woman was sitting beside him, who rose as we entered.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "\\"Shall I leave, Percy?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "she asked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "He clutched her hand to detain her.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "\\"How are you, Watson?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "said he, cordially.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "\\"I should never have known you under that moustache, and I daresay you would not be prepared to swear to me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "This I presume is your celebrated friend, Mr. Sherlock Holmes?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "I introduced him in a few words, and we both sat down.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "The stout young man had left us, but his sister still remained with her hand in that of the invalid.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "She was a striking-looking woman, a little short and thick for symmetry, but with a beautiful olive complexion, large, dark, Italian eyes, and a wealth of deep black hair.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "Her rich tints made the white face of her companion the more worn and haggard by the contrast.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "\\"I won't waste your time,\\" said he, raising himself upon the sofa.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "\\"I'll plunge into the matter without further preamble.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "I was a happy and successful man, Mr. Holmes, and on the eve of being married, when a sudden and dreadful misfortune wrecked all my prospects in life.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "\\"I was, as Watson may have told you, in the Foreign Office, and through the influences of my uncle, Lord Holdhurst, I rose rapidly to a responsible position.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "When my uncle became foreign minister in this administration he gave me several missions of trust, and as I always brought them to a successful conclusion, he came at last to have the utmost confidence in my ability and tact.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "\\"Nearly ten weeks ago—to be more accurate, on the 23rd of May—he called me into his private room, and, after complimenting me on the good work which I had done, he informed me that he had a new commission of trust for me to execute.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "\\"'This,' said he, taking a grey roll of paper from his bureau, 'is the original of that secret treaty between England and Italy of which, I regret to say, some rumours have already got into the public press.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "It is of enormous importance that nothing further should leak out.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "The French or the Russian embassy would pay an immense sum to learn the contents of these papers.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "They should not leave my bureau were it not that it is absolutely necessary to have them copied.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "You have a desk in your office?'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "\\"'Yes, sir.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "\\"'Then take the treaty and lock it up there.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "I shall give directions that you may remain behind when the others go, so that you may copy it at your leisure without fear of being overlooked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "When you have finished, relock both the original and the draft in the desk, and hand them over to me personally to-morrow morning.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_3", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "\\"I took the papers and—\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "\\"Excuse me an instant,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "\\"Were you alone during this conversation?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "\\"Absolutely.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "\\"In a large room?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "\\"Thirty feet each way.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "\\"In the centre?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "\\"Yes, about it.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "\\"And speaking low?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "\\"My uncle's voice is always remarkably low.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "I hardly spoke at all.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "\\"Thank you,\\" said Holmes, shutting his eyes; \\"pray go on.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "\\"I did exactly what he indicated, and waited until the other clerks had departed.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "One of them in my room, Charles Gorot, had some arrears of work to make up, so I left him there and went out to dine.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "When I returned he was gone.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "I was anxious to hurry my work, for I knew that Joseph—the Mr. Harrison whom you saw just now—was in town, and that he would travel down to Woking by the eleven o'clock train, and I wanted if possible to catch it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "\\"When I came to examine the treaty I saw at once that it was of such importance that my uncle had been guilty of no exaggeration in what he had said.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "Without going into details, I may say that it defined the position of Great Britain towards the Triple Alliance, and fore-shadowed the policy which this country would pursue in the event of the French fleet gaining a complete ascendancy over that of Italy in the Mediterranean.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "The questions treated in it were purely naval.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "At the end were the signatures of the high dignitaries who had signed it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "I glanced my eyes over it, and then settled down to my task of copying.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "\\"It was a long document, written in the French language, and containing twenty-six separate articles.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "I copied as quickly as I could, but at nine o'clock I had only done nine articles, and it seemed hopeless for me to attempt to catch my train.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "I was feeling drowsy and stupid, partly from my dinner and also from the effects of a long day's work.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "A cup of coffee would clear my brain.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "A commissionnaire remains all night in a little lodge at the foot of the stairs, and is in the habit of making coffee at his spirit-lamp for any of the officials who may be working over time.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "I rang the bell, therefore, to summon him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "\\"To my surprise, it was a woman who answered the summons, a large, coarse-faced, elderly woman, in an apron.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "She explained that she was the commissionnaire's wife, who did the charing, and I gave her the order for the coffee.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "\\"I wrote two more articles and then, feeling more drowsy than ever, I rose and walked up and down the room to stretch my legs.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "My coffee had not yet come, and I wondered what the cause of the delay could be.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "Opening the door, I started down the corridor to find out.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "There was a straight passage, dimly lighted, which led from the room in which I had been working, and was the only exit from it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "It ended in a curving staircase, with the commissionnaire's lodge in the passage at the bottom.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "Half-way down this staircase is a small landing, with another passage running into it at right angles.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "This second one leads by means of a second small stair to a side door, used by servants, and also as a short cut by clerks when coming from Charles Street.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "Here is a rough chart of the place.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "rough chart", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "\\"Thank you.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "I think that I quite follow you,\\" said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "\\"It is of the utmost importance that you should notice this point.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "I went down the stairs and into the hall, where I found the commissionnaire fast asleep in his box, with the kettle boiling furiously upon the spirit-lamp.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "I took off the kettle and blew out the lamp, for the water was spurting over the floor.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "Then I put out my hand and was about to shake the man, who was still sleeping soundly, when a bell over his head rang loudly, and he woke with a start.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_4", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "' said he, looking at me in bewilderment.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "e in bewilderment.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "\\"'I came down to see if my coffee was ready.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "' He looked at me and then up at the still quivering bell with an ever-growing astonishment upon his face.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "ll with an ever-growing astonishment upon his face.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "' he asked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "s here, sir, then who rang the bell?' he asked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "' I cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "!' I cried. 'What bell is it?'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "\\"'It's the bell of the room you were working in.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "\\"A cold hand seemed to close round my heart.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "Some one, then, was in that room where my precious treaty lay upon the table.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "I ran frantically up the stairs and along the passage.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "There was no one in the corridors, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "There was no one in the room.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "All was exactly as I left it, save only that the papers which had been committed to my care had been taken from the desk on which they lay.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "The copy was there, and the original was gone.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "Holmes sat up in his chair and rubbed his hands.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "I could see that the problem was entirely to his heart.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "\\"Pray, what did you do then?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "he murmured.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "\\"I recognised in an instant that the thief must have come up the stairs from the side door.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "Of course I must have met him if he had come the other way.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "\\"You were satisfied that he could not have been concealed in the room all the time, or in the corridor which you have just described as dimly lighted?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "\\"It is absolutely impossible.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "A rat could not conceal himself either in the room or the corridor.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "There is no cover at all.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "\\"Thank you.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "Pray proceed.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "\\"The commissionnaire, seeing by my pale face that something was to be feared, had followed me upstairs.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "Now we both rushed along the corridor and down the steep steps which led to Charles Street.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "The door at the bottom was closed, but unlocked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "We flung it open and rushed out.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "I can distinctly remember that as we did so there came three chimes from a neighbouring clock.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "It was quarter to ten.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "\\"That is of enormous importance,\\" said Holmes, making a note upon his shirt-cuff.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "\\"The night was very dark, and a thin, warm rain was falling.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "There was no one in Charles Street, but a great traffic was going on, as usual, in Whitehall, at the extremity.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "We rushed along the pavement, bare-headed as we were, and at the far corner we found a policeman standing.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "\\"'A robbery has been committed,' I gasped.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "'A document of immense value has been stolen from the Foreign Office.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "Has any one passed this way?'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "\\"'I have been standing here for a quarter of an hour, sir,' said he; 'only one person has passed during that time—a woman, tall and elderly, with a Paisley shawl.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "\\"'Ah, that is only my wife,' cried the commissionnaire; 'has no one else passed?'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "\\"'No one.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "\\"'Then it must be the other way that the thief took,' cried the fellow, tugging at my sleeve.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "\\"'But I was not satisfied, and the attempts which he made to draw me away increased my suspicions.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "' I cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "y did the woman go?' I cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "\\"'I don't know, sir.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "I noticed her pass, but I had no special reason for watching her.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "She seemed to be in a hurry.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "\\"'How long ago was it?'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "\\"'Oh, not very many minutes.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "\\"'Within the last five?'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "\\"'Well, it could not be more than five.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "\\"'You're only wasting your time, sir, and every minute now is of importance,' cried the commissionnaire; 'take my word for it that my old woman has nothing to do with it, and come down to the other end of the street.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "' And with that he rushed off in the other direction.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "off in the other direction.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_5", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "\\"But I was after him in an instant and caught him by the sleeve.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "' said I.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "o you live?' said I.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "\\"'16 Ivy Lane, Brixton,' he answered.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "'But don't let yourself be drawn away upon a false scent, Mr. Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "Come to the other end of the street and let us see if we can hear of anything.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "\\"Nothing was to be lost by following his advice.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "With the policeman we both hurried down, but only to find the street full of traffic, many people coming and going, but all only too eager to get to a place of safety upon so wet a night.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "There was no lounger who could tell us who had passed.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "\\"Then we returned to the office, and searched the stairs and the passage without result.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "The corridor which led to the room was laid down with a kind of creamy linoleum which shows an impression very easily.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "We examined it very carefully, but found no outline of any footmark.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "\\"Had it been raining all evening?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "\\"Since about seven.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "\\"How is it, then, that the woman who came into the room about nine left no traces with her muddy boots?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "\\"I am glad you raised the point.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "It occurred to me at the time.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "The charwomen are in the habit of taking off their boots at the commissionnaire's office, and putting on list slippers.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "\\"That is very clear.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "There were no marks, then, though the night was a wet one?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "The chain of events is certainly one of extraordinary interest.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "What did you do next?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "\\"We examined the room also.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "There is no possibility of a secret door, and the windows are quite thirty feet from the ground.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "Both of them were fastened on the inside.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "The carpet prevents any possibility of a trap-door, and the ceiling is of the ordinary whitewashed kind.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "I will pledge my life that whoever stole my papers could only have come through the door.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "\\"How about the fireplace?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "\\"They use none.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "There is a stove.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "The bell-rope hangs from the wire just to the right of my desk.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "Whoever rang it must have come right up to the desk to do it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "But why should any criminal wish to ring the bell?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "It is a most insoluble mystery.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "\\"Certainly the incident was unusual.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "What were your next steps?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "You examined the room, I presume, to see if the intruder had left any traces—any cigar-end or dropped glove or hairpin or other trifle?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "\\"There was nothing of the sort.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "\\"No smell?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "\\"Well, we never thought of that.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "\\"Ah, a scent of tobacco would have been worth a great deal to us in such an investigation.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "\\"I never smoke myself, so I think I should have observed it if there had been any smell of tobacco.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "There was absolutely no clue of any kind.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "The only tangible fact was that the commissionnaire's wife—Mrs. Tangey was the name—had hurried out of the place.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "He could give no explanation save that it was about the time when the woman always went home.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "The policeman and I agreed that our best plan would be to seize the woman before she could get rid of the papers, presuming that she had them.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "\\"The alarm had reached Scotland Yard by this time, and Mr. Forbes, the detective, came round at once and took up the case with a great deal of energy.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "We hired a hansom, and in half an hour we were at the address which had been given to us.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "A young woman opened the door, who proved to be Mrs. Tangey's eldest daughter.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "Her mother had not come back yet, and we were shown into the front room to wait.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_6", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "\\"About ten minutes later a knock came at the door, and here we made the one serious mistake for which I blame myself.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "Instead of opening the door ourselves, we allowed the girl to do so.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "We heard her say, 'Mother, there are two men in the house waiting to see you,' and an instant afterwards we heard the patter of feet rushing down the passage.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "Forbes flung open the door, and we both ran into the back room or kitchen, but the woman had got there before us.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "She stared at us with defiant eyes, and then, suddenly recognising me, an expression of absolute astonishment came over her face.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "' she cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "isn't Mr. Phelps, of the office!' she cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "' asked my companion.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "you think we were when you ran away from us?' asked my companion.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "\\"'I thought you were the brokers,' said she, 'we have had some trouble with a tradesman.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "\\"'That's not quite good enough,' answered Forbes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "'We have reason to believe that you have taken a paper of importance from the Foreign Office, and that you ran in here to dispose of it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "You must come back with us to Scotland Yard to be searched.'", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "\\"It was in vain that she protested and resisted.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "A four-wheeler was brought, and we all three drove back in it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "We had first made an examination of the kitchen, and especially of the kitchen fire, to see whether she might have made away with the papers during the instant that she was alone.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "There were no signs, however, of any ashes or scraps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "When we reached Scotland Yard she was handed over at once to the female searcher.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "I waited in an agony of suspense until she came back with her report.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "There were no signs of the papers.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "\\"Then for the first time the horror of my situation came in its full force.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "Hitherto I had been acting, and action had numbed thought.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "I had been so confident of regaining the treaty at once that I had not dared to think of what would be the consequence if I failed to do so.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "But now there was nothing more to be done, and I had leisure to realize my position.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "It was horrible.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "Watson there would tell you that I was a nervous, sensitive boy at school.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "It is my nature.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "I thought of my uncle and of his colleagues in the Cabinet, of the shame which I had brought upon him, upon myself, upon every one connected with me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "What though I was the victim of an extraordinary accident?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "No allowance is made for accidents where diplomatic interests are at stake.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "I was ruined, shamefully, hopelessly ruined.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "I don't know what I did.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "I fancy I must have made a scene.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "I have a dim recollection of a group of officials who crowded round me, endeavouring to soothe me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "One of them drove down with me to Waterloo, and saw me into the Woking train.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "I believe that he would have come all the way had it not been that Dr. Ferrier, who lives near me, was going down by that very train.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "The doctor most kindly took charge of me, and it was well he did so, for I had a fit in the station, and before we reached home I was practically a raving maniac.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "\\"Oh, I have heard—Coldstream Guards.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "\\"You can imagine the state of things here when they were roused from their beds by the doctor's ringing and found me in this condition.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "Poor Annie here and my mother were broken-hearted.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "Dr. Ferrier had just heard enough from the detective at the station to be able to give an idea of what had happened, and his story did not mend matters.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "It was evident to all that I was in for a long illness, so Joseph was bundled out of this cheery bedroom, and it was turned into a sick-room for me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "Here I have lain, Mr. Holmes, for over nine weeks, unconscious, and raving with brain-fever.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "If it had not been for Miss Harrison here and for the doctor's care I should not be speaking to you now.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "She has nursed me by day and a hired nurse has looked after me by night, for in my mad fits I was capable of anything.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "Slowly my reason has cleared, but it is only during the last three days that my memory has quite returned.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "Sometimes I wish that it never had.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "The first thing that I did was to wire to Mr. Forbes, who had the case in hand.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "He came out, and assures me that, though everything has been done, no trace of a clue has been discovered.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "The commissionnaire and his wife have been examined in every way without any light being thrown upon the matter.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "The suspicions of the police then rested upon young Gorot, who, as you may remember, stayed over time in the office that night.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "His remaining behind and his French name were really the only two points which could suggest suspicion; but, as a matter of fact, I did not begin work until he had gone, and his people are of Huguenot extraction, but as English in sympathy and tradition as you and I are.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "Nothing was found to implicate him in any way, and there the matter dropped.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "I turn to you, Mr. Holmes, as absolutely my last hope.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "If you fail me, then my honour as well as my position are forever forfeited.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_7", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "The invalid sank back upon his cushions, tired out by this long recital, while his nurse poured him out a glass of some stimulating medicine.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "Holmes sat silently, with his head thrown back and his eyes closed, in an attitude which might seem listless to a stranger, but which I knew betokened the most intense self-absorption.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "\\"You statement has been so explicit,\\" said he at last, \\"that you have really left me very few questions to ask.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "There is one of the very utmost importance, however.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "Did you tell any one that you had this special task to perform?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "\\"No one.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "\\"Not Miss Harrison here, for example?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "\\"No.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "I had not been back to Woking between getting the order and executing the commission.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "\\"And none of your people had by chance been to see you?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "\\"None.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "\\"Did any of them know their way about in the office?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "\\"Oh, yes, all of them had been shown over it.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "\\"Still, of course, if you said nothing to any one about the treaty these inquiries are irrelevant.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "\\"I said nothing.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "\\"Do you know anything of the commissionnaire?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "\\"Nothing except that he is an old soldier.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "\\"What regiment?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "I have no doubt I can get details from Forbes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "The authorities are excellent at amassing facts, though they do not always use them to advantage.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "What a lovely thing a rose is!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "He walked past the couch to the open window, and held up the drooping stalk of a moss-rose, looking down at the dainty blend of crimson and green.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "It was a new phase of his character to me, for I had never before seen him show any keen interest in natural objects.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "\\"There is nothing in which deduction is so necessary as in religion,\\" said he, leaning with his back against the shutters.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "\\"It can be built up as an exact science by the reasoner.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "Our highest assurance of the goodness of Providence seems to me to rest in the flowers.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "All other things, our powers our desires, our food, are all really necessary for our existence in the first instance.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "But this rose is an extra.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "Its smell and its colour are an embellishment of life, not a condition of it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "It is only goodness which gives extras, and so I say again that we have much to hope from the flowers.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "Percy Phelps and his nurse looked at Holmes during this demonstration with surprise and a good deal of disappointment written upon their faces.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "He had fallen into a reverie, with the moss-rose between his fingers.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "It had lasted some minutes before the young lady broke in upon it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "\\"Do you see any prospect of solving this mystery, Mr. Holmes?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "she asked, with a touch of asperity in her voice.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "\\"Oh, the mystery!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "he answered, coming back with a start to the realities of life.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "\\"Well, it would be absurd to deny that the case is a very abstruse and complicated one, but I can promise you that I will look into the matter and let you know any points which may strike me.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "\\"Do you see any clue?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "\\"You have furnished me with seven, but, of course, I must test them before I can pronounce upon their value.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "\\"You suspect some one?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "\\"I suspect myself.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "\\"What!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "\\"Of coming to conclusions too rapidly.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "\\"Then go to London and test your conclusions.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "\\"Your advice is very excellent, Miss Harrison,\\" said Holmes, rising.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "\\"I think, Watson, we cannot do better.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "Do not allow yourself to indulge in false hopes, Mr. Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "The affair is a very tangled one.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_8", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "\\"I shall be in a fever until I see you again,\\" cried the diplomatist.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "\\"Well, I'll come out by the same train to-morrow, though it's more than likely that my report will be a negative one.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "\\"God bless you for promising to come,\\" cried our client.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "\\"It gives me fresh life to know that something is being done.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "By the way, I have had a letter from Lord Holdhurst.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "\\"Ha!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "He repeated that the matter was of the utmost importance, and added that no steps would be taken about my future—by which he means, of course, my dismissal—until my health was restored and I had an opportunity of repairing my misfortune.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "\\"Well, that was reasonable and considerate,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "\\"Come, Watson, for we have a good day's work before us in town.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "Mr. Joseph Harrison drove us down to the station, and we were soon whirling up in a Portsmouth train.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "Holmes was sunk in profound thought, and hardly opened his mouth until we had passed Clapham Junction.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "\\"It's a very cheery thing to come into London by any of these lines which run high, and allow you to look down upon the houses like this.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "I thought he was joking, for the view was sordid enough, but he soon explained himself.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "\\"Look at those big, isolated clumps of building rising up above the slates, like brick islands in a lead-coloured sea.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "\\"The board-schools.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "\\"Light-houses, my boy!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "Beacons of the future!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "Capsules with hundreds of bright little seeds in each, out of which will spring the wise, better England of the future.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "I suppose that man Phelps does not drink?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "\\"I should not think so.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "\\"Nor should I, but we are bound to take every possibility into account.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "The poor devil has certainly got himself into very deep water, and it's a question whether we shall ever be able to get him ashore.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "What did you think of Miss Harrison?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "\\"A girl of strong character.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "\\"Yes, but she is a good sort, or I am mistaken.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "She and her brother are the only children of an iron-master somewhere up Northumberland way.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "He got engaged to her when traveling last winter, and she came down to be introduced to his people, with her brother as escort.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "Then came the smash, and she stayed on to nurse her lover, while brother Joseph, finding himself pretty snug, stayed on too.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "I've been making a few independent inquiries, you see.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "But to-day must be a day of inquiries.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "\\"My practice—\\" I began.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "\\"Oh, if you find your own cases more interesting than mine—\\" said Holmes, with some asperity.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "\\"I was going to say that my practice could get along very well for a day or two, since it is the slackest time in the year.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "\\"Excellent,\\" said he, recovering his good-humour.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "\\"Then we'll look into this matter together.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "I think that we should begin by seeing Forbes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "He can probably tell us all the details we want until we know from what side the case is to be approached.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "\\"You said you had a clue?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "\\"Well, we have several, but we can only test their value by further inquiry.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "The most difficult crime to track is the one which is purposeless.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "Now this is not purposeless.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "Who is it who profits by it?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "There is the French ambassador, there is the Russian, there is whoever might sell it to either of these, and there is Lord Holdhurst.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "\\"Lord Holdhurst!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "\\"Well, it is just conceivable that a statesman might find himself in a position where he was not sorry to have such a document accidentally destroyed.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_9", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "\\"Not a statesman with the honourable record of Lord Holdhurst?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "\\"It is a possibility and we cannot afford to disregard it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "We shall see the noble lord to-day and find out if he can tell us anything.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "Meanwhile I have already set inquiries on foot.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "\\"Already?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "\\"Yes, I sent wires from Woking station to every evening paper in London.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "This advertisement will appear in each of them.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "He handed over a sheet torn from a note-book.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "On it was scribbled in pencil:", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "—The number of the cab which dropped a fare at or about the door of the Foreign Office in Charles Street at quarter to ten in the evening of May 23rd.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "Apply 221B, Baker Street.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "ker Street.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "\\"You are confident that the thief came in a cab?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "\\"If not, there is no harm done.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "But if Mr. Phelps is correct in stating that there is no hiding-place either in the room or the corridors, then the person must have come from outside.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "If he came from outside on so wet a night, and yet left no trace of damp upon the linoleum, which was examined within a few minutes of his passing, then it is exceeding probable that he came in a cab.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "Yes, I think that we may safely deduce a cab.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "\\"It sounds plausible.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "\\"That is one of the clues of which I spoke.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "It may lead us to something.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "And then, of course, there is the bell—which is the most distinctive feature of the case.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "Why should the bell ring?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "Was it the thief who did it out of bravado?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "Or was it some one who was with the thief who did it in order to prevent the crime?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "Or was it an accident?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "Or was it—?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "He sank back into the state of intense and silent thought from which he had emerged; but it seemed to me, accustomed as I was to his every mood, that some new possibility had dawned suddenly upon him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "It was twenty past three when we reached our terminus, and after a hasty luncheon at the buffet we pushed on at once to Scotland Yard.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "Holmes had already wired to Forbes, and we found him waiting to receive us—a small, foxy man with a sharp but by no means amiable expression.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "He was decidedly frigid in his manner to us, especially when he heard the errand upon which we had come.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "\\"I've heard of your methods before now, Mr. Holmes,\\" said he, tartly.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_490	lexical	\N	\N	489	{"text": "\\"Well, we have nothing else to go upon—no evidence of any kind.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "\\"You are ready enough to use all the information that the police can lay at your disposal, and then you try to finish the case yourself and bring discredit on them.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "\\"On the contrary,\\" said Holmes, \\"out of my last fifty-three cases my name has only appeared in four, and the police have had all the credit in forty-nine.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "I don't blame you for not knowing this, for you are young and inexperienced, but if you wish to get on in your new duties you will work with me and not against me.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "\\"I'd be very glad of a hint or two,\\" said the detective, changing his manner.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "\\"I've certainly had no credit from the case so far.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "\\"What steps have you taken?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "\\"Tangey, the commissionnaire, has been shadowed.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "He left the Guards with a good character and we can find nothing against him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "His wife is a bad lot, though.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "I fancy she knows more about this than appears.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "\\"Have you shadowed her?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "\\"We have set one of our women on to her.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "Mrs. Tangey drinks, and our woman has been with her twice when she was well on, but she could get nothing out of her.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_10", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "\\"I understand that they have had brokers in the house?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "\\"Yes, but they were paid off.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "\\"Where did the money come from?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_468	lexical	\N	\N	467	{"text": "\\"That was all right.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_469	lexical	\N	\N	468	{"text": "His pension was due.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_470	lexical	\N	\N	469	{"text": "They have not shown any sign of being in funds.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_471	lexical	\N	\N	470	{"text": "\\"What explanation did she give of having answered the bell when Mr. Phelps rang for the coffee?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_472	lexical	\N	\N	471	{"text": "\\"She said that her husband was very tired and she wished to relieve him.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_473	lexical	\N	\N	472	{"text": "\\"Well, certainly that would agree with his being found a little later asleep in his chair.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_474	lexical	\N	\N	473	{"text": "There is nothing against them then but the woman's character.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_475	lexical	\N	\N	474	{"text": "Did you ask her why she hurried away that night?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_476	lexical	\N	\N	475	{"text": "Her haste attracted the attention of the police constable.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_477	lexical	\N	\N	476	{"text": "\\"She was later than usual and wanted to get home.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_478	lexical	\N	\N	477	{"text": "\\"Did you point out to her that you and Mr. Phelps, who started at least twenty minutes after her, got home before her?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_479	lexical	\N	\N	478	{"text": "\\"She explains that by the difference between a 'bus and a hansom.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_480	lexical	\N	\N	479	{"text": "\\"Did she make it clear why, on reaching her house, she ran into the back kitchen?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_481	lexical	\N	\N	480	{"text": "\\"Because she had the money there with which to pay off the brokers.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_482	lexical	\N	\N	481	{"text": "\\"She has at least an answer for everything.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_483	lexical	\N	\N	482	{"text": "Did you ask her whether in leaving she met any one or saw any one loitering about Charles Street?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_484	lexical	\N	\N	483	{"text": "\\"She saw no one but the constable.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_485	lexical	\N	\N	484	{"text": "\\"Well, you seem to have cross-examined her pretty thoroughly.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_486	lexical	\N	\N	485	{"text": "What else have you done?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_487	lexical	\N	\N	486	{"text": "\\"The clerk Gorot has been shadowed all these nine weeks, but without result.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_488	lexical	\N	\N	487	{"text": "We can show nothing against him.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_489	lexical	\N	\N	488	{"text": "\\"Anything else?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_491	lexical	\N	\N	490	{"text": "\\"Have you formed a theory about how that bell rang?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_492	lexical	\N	\N	491	{"text": "\\"Well, I must confess that it beats me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_493	lexical	\N	\N	492	{"text": "It was a cool hand, whoever it was, to go and give the alarm like that.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_494	lexical	\N	\N	493	{"text": "\\"Yes, it was a queer thing to do.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_495	lexical	\N	\N	494	{"text": "Many thanks to you for what you have told me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_496	lexical	\N	\N	495	{"text": "If I can put the man into your hands you shall hear from me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_497	lexical	\N	\N	496	{"text": "Come along, Watson.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_498	lexical	\N	\N	497	{"text": "\\"Where are we going to now?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_499	lexical	\N	\N	498	{"text": "I asked, as we left the office.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_500	lexical	\N	\N	499	{"text": "\\"We are now going to interview Lord Holdhurst, the cabinet minister and future premier of England.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_501	lexical	\N	\N	500	{"text": "We were fortunate in finding that Lord Holdhurst was still in his chambers in Downing Street, and on Holmes sending in his card we were instantly shown up.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_502	lexical	\N	\N	501	{"text": "The statesman received us with that old-fashioned courtesy for which he is remarkable, and seated us on the two luxuriant lounges on either side of the fireplace.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_503	lexical	\N	\N	502	{"text": "Standing on the rug between us, with his slight, tall figure, his sharp features, thoughtful face, and curling hair prematurely tinged with grey, he seemed to represent that not too common type, a nobleman who is in truth noble.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_504	lexical	\N	\N	503	{"text": "\\"Your name is very familiar to me, Mr. Holmes,\\" said he, smiling.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_505	lexical	\N	\N	504	{"text": "\\"And, of course, I cannot pretend to be ignorant of the object of your visit.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_506	lexical	\N	\N	505	{"text": "There has only been one occurrence in these offices which could call for your attention.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_507	lexical	\N	\N	506	{"text": "In whose interest are you acting, may I ask?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_508	lexical	\N	\N	507	{"text": "\\"In that of Mr. Percy Phelps,\\" answered Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_509	lexical	\N	\N	508	{"text": "\\"Ah, my unfortunate nephew!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_510	lexical	\N	\N	509	{"text": "You can understand that our kinship makes it the more impossible for me to screen him in any way.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_511	lexical	\N	\N	510	{"text": "I fear that the incident must have a very prejudicial effect upon his career.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_512	lexical	\N	\N	511	{"text": "\\"But if the document is found?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_513	lexical	\N	\N	512	{"text": "\\"Ah, that, of course, would be different.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_514	lexical	\N	\N	513	{"text": "\\"I had one or two questions which I wished to ask you, Lord Holdhurst.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_515	lexical	\N	\N	514	{"text": "\\"I shall be happy to give you any information in my power.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_516	lexical	\N	\N	515	{"text": "\\"Was it in this room that you gave your instructions as to the copying of the document?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_11", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_517	lexical	\N	\N	516	{"text": "\\"It was.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_518	lexical	\N	\N	517	{"text": "\\"Then you could hardly have been overheard?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_519	lexical	\N	\N	518	{"text": "\\"It is out of the question.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_520	lexical	\N	\N	519	{"text": "\\"Did you ever mention to any one that it was your intention to give any one the treaty to be copied?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_521	lexical	\N	\N	520	{"text": "\\"Never.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_522	lexical	\N	\N	521	{"text": "\\"You are certain of that?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_523	lexical	\N	\N	522	{"text": "\\"Absolutely.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_524	lexical	\N	\N	523	{"text": "\\"Well, since you never said so, and Mr. Phelps never said so, and nobody else knew anything of the matter, then the thief's presence in the room was purely accidental.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_525	lexical	\N	\N	524	{"text": "He saw his chance and he took it.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_526	lexical	\N	\N	525	{"text": "The statesman smiled.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_527	lexical	\N	\N	526	{"text": "\\"You take me out of my province there,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_528	lexical	\N	\N	527	{"text": "Holmes considered for a moment.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_529	lexical	\N	\N	528	{"text": "\\"There is another very important point which I wish to discuss with you,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_530	lexical	\N	\N	529	{"text": "\\"You feared, as I understand, that very grave results might follow from the details of this treaty becoming known.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_531	lexical	\N	\N	530	{"text": "A shadow passed over the expressive face of the statesman.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_532	lexical	\N	\N	531	{"text": "\\"Very grave results indeed.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_533	lexical	\N	\N	532	{"text": "\\"And have they occurred?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_534	lexical	\N	\N	533	{"text": "\\"Not yet.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_535	lexical	\N	\N	534	{"text": "\\"If the treaty had reached, let us say, the French or Russian Foreign Office, you would expect to hear of it?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_536	lexical	\N	\N	535	{"text": "\\"I should,\\" said Lord Holdhurst, with a wry face.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_537	lexical	\N	\N	536	{"text": "\\"Since nearly ten weeks have elapsed, then, and nothing has been heard, it is not unfair to suppose that for some reason the treaty has not reached them.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_538	lexical	\N	\N	537	{"text": "Lord Holdhurst shrugged his shoulders.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_539	lexical	\N	\N	538	{"text": "\\"We can hardly suppose, Mr. Holmes, that the thief took the treaty in order to frame it and hang it up.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_540	lexical	\N	\N	539	{"text": "\\"Perhaps he is waiting for a better price.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_541	lexical	\N	\N	540	{"text": "\\"If he waits a little longer he will get no price at all.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_542	lexical	\N	\N	541	{"text": "The treaty will cease to be secret in a few months.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_543	lexical	\N	\N	542	{"text": "\\"That is most important,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_544	lexical	\N	\N	543	{"text": "\\"Of course, it is a possible supposition that the thief has had a sudden illness—\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_545	lexical	\N	\N	544	{"text": "\\"An attack of brain-fever, for example?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_546	lexical	\N	\N	545	{"text": "asked the statesman, flashing a swift glance at him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_547	lexical	\N	\N	546	{"text": "\\"I did not say so,\\" said Holmes, imperturbably.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_548	lexical	\N	\N	547	{"text": "\\"And now, Lord Holdhurst, we have already taken up too much of your valuable time, and we shall wish you good-day.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_549	lexical	\N	\N	548	{"text": "\\"Every success to your investigation, be the criminal who it may,\\" answered the nobleman, as he bowed us out the door.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_550	lexical	\N	\N	549	{"text": "\\"He's a fine fellow,\\" said Holmes, as we came out into Whitehall.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_551	lexical	\N	\N	550	{"text": "\\"But he has a struggle to keep up his position.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_552	lexical	\N	\N	551	{"text": "He is far from rich and has many calls.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_553	lexical	\N	\N	552	{"text": "You noticed, of course, that his boots had been resoled.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_554	lexical	\N	\N	553	{"text": "Now, Watson, I won't detain you from your legitimate work any longer.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_555	lexical	\N	\N	554	{"text": "I shall do nothing more to-day, unless I have an answer to my cab advertisement.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_556	lexical	\N	\N	555	{"text": "But I should be extremely obliged to you if you would come down with me to Woking to-morrow, by the same train which we took yesterday.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_557	lexical	\N	\N	556	{"text": "I met him accordingly next morning and we travelled down to Woking together.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_558	lexical	\N	\N	557	{"text": "He had had no answer to his advertisement, he said, and no fresh light had been thrown upon the case.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_559	lexical	\N	\N	558	{"text": "He had, when he so willed it, the utter immobility of countenance of a red Indian, and I could not gather from his appearance whether he was satisfied or not with the position of the case.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_560	lexical	\N	\N	559	{"text": "His conversation, I remember, was about the Bertillon system of measurements, and he expressed his enthusiastic admiration of the French savant.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_561	lexical	\N	\N	560	{"text": "We found our client still under the charge of his devoted nurse, but looking considerably better than before.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_562	lexical	\N	\N	561	{"text": "He rose from the sofa and greeted us without difficulty when we entered.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_563	lexical	\N	\N	562	{"text": "\\"Any news?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_564	lexical	\N	\N	563	{"text": "he asked, eagerly.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_565	lexical	\N	\N	564	{"text": "\\"My report, as I expected, is a negative one,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_566	lexical	\N	\N	565	{"text": "\\"I have seen Forbes, and I have seen your uncle, and I have set one or two trains of inquiry upon foot which may lead to something.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_12", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_567	lexical	\N	\N	566	{"text": "\\"You have not lost heart, then?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_568	lexical	\N	\N	567	{"text": "\\"By no means.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_569	lexical	\N	\N	568	{"text": "\\"God bless you for saying that!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_570	lexical	\N	\N	569	{"text": "cried Miss Harrison.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_571	lexical	\N	\N	570	{"text": "\\"If we keep our courage and our patience the truth must come out.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_572	lexical	\N	\N	571	{"text": "\\"We have more to tell you than you have for us,\\" said Phelps, reseating himself upon the couch.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_573	lexical	\N	\N	572	{"text": "\\"I hoped you might have something.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_574	lexical	\N	\N	573	{"text": "\\"Yes, we have had an adventure during the night, and one which might have proved to be a serious one.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_575	lexical	\N	\N	574	{"text": "His expression grew very grave as he spoke, and a look of something akin to fear sprang up in his eyes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_576	lexical	\N	\N	575	{"text": "\\"Do you know,\\" said he, \\"that I begin to believe that I am the unconscious centre of some monstrous conspiracy, and that my life is aimed at as well as my honour?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_577	lexical	\N	\N	576	{"text": "\\"Ah!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_578	lexical	\N	\N	577	{"text": "cried Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_579	lexical	\N	\N	578	{"text": "\\"It sounds incredible, for I have not, as far as I know, an enemy in the world.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_580	lexical	\N	\N	579	{"text": "Yet from last night's experience I can come to no other conclusion.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_581	lexical	\N	\N	580	{"text": "\\"Pray let me hear it.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_582	lexical	\N	\N	581	{"text": "\\"You must know that last night was the very first night that I have ever slept without a nurse in the room.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_583	lexical	\N	\N	582	{"text": "I was so much better that I thought I could dispense with one.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_584	lexical	\N	\N	583	{"text": "I had a night-light burning, however.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_585	lexical	\N	\N	584	{"text": "Well, about two in the morning I had sunk into a light sleep when I was suddenly aroused by a slight noise.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_586	lexical	\N	\N	585	{"text": "It was like the sound which a mouse makes when it is gnawing a plank, and I lay listening to it for some time under the impression that it must come from that cause.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_587	lexical	\N	\N	586	{"text": "Then it grew louder, and suddenly there came from the window a sharp metallic snick.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_588	lexical	\N	\N	587	{"text": "I sat up in amazement.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_589	lexical	\N	\N	588	{"text": "There could be no doubt what the sounds were now.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_590	lexical	\N	\N	589	{"text": "The first ones had been caused by some one forcing an instrument through the slit between the sashes, and the second by the catch being pressed back.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_591	lexical	\N	\N	590	{"text": "\\"There was a pause then for about ten minutes, as if the person were waiting to see whether the noise had awakened me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_592	lexical	\N	\N	591	{"text": "Then I heard a gentle creaking as the window was very slowly opened.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_593	lexical	\N	\N	592	{"text": "I could stand it no longer, for my nerves are not what they used to be.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_594	lexical	\N	\N	593	{"text": "I sprang out of bed and flung open the shutters.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_595	lexical	\N	\N	594	{"text": "A man was crouching at the window.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_596	lexical	\N	\N	595	{"text": "I could see little of him, for he was gone like a flash.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_597	lexical	\N	\N	596	{"text": "He was wrapped in some sort of cloak which came across the lower part of his face.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_598	lexical	\N	\N	597	{"text": "One thing only I am sure of, and that is that he had some weapon in his hand.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_599	lexical	\N	\N	598	{"text": "It looked to me like a long knife.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_600	lexical	\N	\N	599	{"text": "I distinctly saw the gleam of it as he turned to run.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_601	lexical	\N	\N	600	{"text": "\\"This is most interesting,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_602	lexical	\N	\N	601	{"text": "\\"Pray what did you do then?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_603	lexical	\N	\N	602	{"text": "\\"I should have followed him through the open window if I had been stronger.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_604	lexical	\N	\N	603	{"text": "As it was, I rang the bell and roused the house.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_605	lexical	\N	\N	604	{"text": "It took me some little time, for the bell rings in the kitchen and the servants all sleep upstairs.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_606	lexical	\N	\N	605	{"text": "I shouted, however, and that brought Joseph down, and he roused the others.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_607	lexical	\N	\N	606	{"text": "Joseph and the groom found marks on the bed outside the window, but the weather has been so dry lately that they found it hopeless to follow the trail across the grass.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_608	lexical	\N	\N	607	{"text": "There's a place, however, on the wooden fence which skirts the road which shows signs, they tell me, as if some one had got over, and had snapped the top of the rail in doing so.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_609	lexical	\N	\N	608	{"text": "I have said nothing to the local police yet, for I thought I had best have your opinion first.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_13", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_610	lexical	\N	\N	609	{"text": "This tale of our client's appeared to have an extraordinary effect upon Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_611	lexical	\N	\N	610	{"text": "He rose from his chair and paced about the room in uncontrollable excitement.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_612	lexical	\N	\N	611	{"text": "\\"Misfortunes never come single,\\" said Phelps, smiling, though it was evident that his adventure had somewhat shaken him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_613	lexical	\N	\N	612	{"text": "\\"You have certainly had your share,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_614	lexical	\N	\N	613	{"text": "\\"Do you think you could walk round the house with me?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_615	lexical	\N	\N	614	{"text": "\\"Oh, yes, I should like a little sunshine.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_616	lexical	\N	\N	615	{"text": "Joseph will come, too.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_617	lexical	\N	\N	616	{"text": "\\"And I also,\\" said Miss Harrison.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_618	lexical	\N	\N	617	{"text": "\\"I am afraid not,\\" said Holmes, shaking his head.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_619	lexical	\N	\N	618	{"text": "\\"I think I must ask you to remain sitting exactly where you are.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_620	lexical	\N	\N	619	{"text": "The young lady resumed her seat with an air of displeasure.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_621	lexical	\N	\N	620	{"text": "Her brother, however, had joined us and we set off all four together.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_622	lexical	\N	\N	621	{"text": "We passed round the lawn to the outside of the young diplomatist's window.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_623	lexical	\N	\N	622	{"text": "There were, as he had said, marks upon the bed, but they were hopelessly blurred and vague.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_624	lexical	\N	\N	623	{"text": "Holmes stopped over them for an instant, and then rose shrugging his shoulders.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_625	lexical	\N	\N	624	{"text": "\\"I don't think any one could make much of this,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_626	lexical	\N	\N	625	{"text": "\\"Let us go round the house and see why this particular room was chosen by the burglar.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_627	lexical	\N	\N	626	{"text": "I should have thought those larger windows of the drawing-room and dining-room would have had more attractions for him.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_628	lexical	\N	\N	627	{"text": "\\"They are more visible from the road,\\" suggested Mr. Joseph Harrison.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_629	lexical	\N	\N	628	{"text": "\\"Ah, yes, of course.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_630	lexical	\N	\N	629	{"text": "There is a door here which he might have attempted.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_631	lexical	\N	\N	630	{"text": "What is it for?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_632	lexical	\N	\N	631	{"text": "\\"It is the side entrance for trades-people.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_633	lexical	\N	\N	632	{"text": "Of course it is locked at night.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_634	lexical	\N	\N	633	{"text": "\\"Have you ever had an alarm like this before?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_635	lexical	\N	\N	634	{"text": "\\"Never,\\" said our client.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_636	lexical	\N	\N	635	{"text": "\\"Do you keep plate in the house, or anything to attract burglars?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_637	lexical	\N	\N	636	{"text": "\\"Nothing of value.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_638	lexical	\N	\N	637	{"text": "Holmes strolled round the house with his hands in his pockets and a negligent air which was unusual with him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_639	lexical	\N	\N	638	{"text": "\\"By the way,\\" said he to Joseph Harrison, \\"you found some place, I understand, where the fellow scaled the fence.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_640	lexical	\N	\N	639	{"text": "Let us have a look at that!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_641	lexical	\N	\N	640	{"text": "The plump young man led us to a spot where the top of one of the wooden rails had been cracked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_642	lexical	\N	\N	641	{"text": "A small fragment of the wood was hanging down.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_643	lexical	\N	\N	642	{"text": "Holmes pulled it off and examined it critically.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_644	lexical	\N	\N	643	{"text": "\\"Do you think that was done last night?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_645	lexical	\N	\N	644	{"text": "It looks rather old, does it not?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_646	lexical	\N	\N	645	{"text": "\\"Well, possibly so.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_647	lexical	\N	\N	646	{"text": "\\"There are no marks of any one jumping down upon the other side.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_648	lexical	\N	\N	647	{"text": "No, I fancy we shall get no help here.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_649	lexical	\N	\N	648	{"text": "Let us go back to the bedroom and talk the matter over.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_650	lexical	\N	\N	649	{"text": "Percy Phelps was walking very slowly, leaning upon the arm of his future brother-in-law.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_651	lexical	\N	\N	650	{"text": "Holmes walked swiftly across the lawn, and we were at the open window of the bedroom long before the others came up.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_652	lexical	\N	\N	651	{"text": "\\"Miss Harrison,\\" said Holmes, speaking with the utmost intensity of manner, \\"you must stay where you are all day.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_653	lexical	\N	\N	652	{"text": "Let nothing prevent you from staying where you are all day.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_654	lexical	\N	\N	653	{"text": "It is of the utmost importance.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_655	lexical	\N	\N	654	{"text": "\\"Certainly, if you wish it, Mr. Holmes,\\" said the girl in astonishment.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_656	lexical	\N	\N	655	{"text": "\\"When you go to bed lock the door of this room on the outside and keep the key.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_657	lexical	\N	\N	656	{"text": "Promise to do this.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_658	lexical	\N	\N	657	{"text": "\\"But Percy?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_659	lexical	\N	\N	658	{"text": "\\"He will come to London with us.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_660	lexical	\N	\N	659	{"text": "\\"And am I to remain here?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_661	lexical	\N	\N	660	{"text": "\\"It is for his sake.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_662	lexical	\N	\N	661	{"text": "You can serve him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_663	lexical	\N	\N	662	{"text": "Quick!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_664	lexical	\N	\N	663	{"text": "Promise!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_665	lexical	\N	\N	664	{"text": "She gave a quick nod of assent just as the other two came up.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_666	lexical	\N	\N	665	{"text": "\\"Why do you sit moping there, Annie?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_667	lexical	\N	\N	666	{"text": "cried her brother.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_668	lexical	\N	\N	667	{"text": "\\"Come out into the sunshine!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_669	lexical	\N	\N	668	{"text": "\\"No, thank you, Joseph.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_670	lexical	\N	\N	669	{"text": "I have a slight headache and this room is deliciously cool and soothing.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_14", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_671	lexical	\N	\N	670	{"text": "\\"What do you propose now, Mr. Holmes?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_672	lexical	\N	\N	671	{"text": "asked our client.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_673	lexical	\N	\N	672	{"text": "\\"Well, in investigating this minor affair we must not lose sight of our main inquiry.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_674	lexical	\N	\N	673	{"text": "It would be a very great help to me if you would come up to London with us.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_675	lexical	\N	\N	674	{"text": "\\"At once?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_676	lexical	\N	\N	675	{"text": "\\"Well, as soon as you conveniently can.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_677	lexical	\N	\N	676	{"text": "Say in an hour.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_678	lexical	\N	\N	677	{"text": "\\"I feel quite strong enough, if I can really be of any help.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_679	lexical	\N	\N	678	{"text": "\\"The greatest possible.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	sentence_2693	lexical	\N	\N	2692	{"text": "cried Baldwin.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_680	lexical	\N	\N	679	{"text": "\\"Perhaps you would like me to stay there to-night?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_681	lexical	\N	\N	680	{"text": "\\"I was just going to propose it.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_682	lexical	\N	\N	681	{"text": "\\"Then, if my friend of the night comes to revisit me, he will find the bird flown.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_683	lexical	\N	\N	682	{"text": "We are all in your hands, Mr. Holmes, and you must tell us exactly what you would like done.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_684	lexical	\N	\N	683	{"text": "Perhaps you would prefer that Joseph came with us so as to look after me?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_685	lexical	\N	\N	684	{"text": "\\"Oh, no; my friend Watson is a medical man, you know, and he'll look after you.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_686	lexical	\N	\N	685	{"text": "We'll have our lunch here, if you will permit us, and then we shall all three set off for town together.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_687	lexical	\N	\N	686	{"text": "It was arranged as he suggested, though Miss Harrison excused herself from leaving the bedroom, in accordance with Holmes's suggestion.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_688	lexical	\N	\N	687	{"text": "What the object of my friend's manœuvres was I could not conceive, unless it were to keep the lady away from Phelps, who, rejoiced by his returning health and by the prospect of action, lunched with us in the dining-room.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_689	lexical	\N	\N	688	{"text": "Holmes had a still more startling surprise for us, however, for, after accompanying us down to the station and seeing us into our carriage, he calmly announced that he had no intention of leaving Woking.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_690	lexical	\N	\N	689	{"text": "\\"There are one or two small points which I should desire to clear up before I go,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_691	lexical	\N	\N	690	{"text": "\\"Your absence, Mr. Phelps, will in some ways rather assist me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_692	lexical	\N	\N	691	{"text": "Watson, when you reach London you would oblige me by driving at once to Baker Street with our friend here, and remaining with him until I see you again.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_693	lexical	\N	\N	692	{"text": "It is fortunate that you are old schoolfellows, as you must have much to talk over.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_694	lexical	\N	\N	693	{"text": "Mr. Phelps can have the spare bedroom to-night, and I will be with you in time for breakfast, for there is a train which will take me into Waterloo at eight.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_695	lexical	\N	\N	694	{"text": "\\"But how about our investigation in London?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_696	lexical	\N	\N	695	{"text": "asked Phelps, ruefully.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_697	lexical	\N	\N	696	{"text": "\\"We can do that to-morrow.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_698	lexical	\N	\N	697	{"text": "I think that just at present I can be of more immediate use here.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_699	lexical	\N	\N	698	{"text": "\\"You might tell them at Briarbrae that I hope to be back to-morrow night,\\" cried Phelps, as we began to move from the platform.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_700	lexical	\N	\N	699	{"text": "\\"I hardly expect to go back to Briarbrae,\\" answered Holmes, and waved his hand to us cheerily as we shot out from the station.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_701	lexical	\N	\N	700	{"text": "Phelps and I talked it over on our journey, but neither of us could devise a satisfactory reason for this new development.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_702	lexical	\N	\N	701	{"text": "\\"I suppose he wants to find out some clue as to the burglary last night, if a burglar it was.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_703	lexical	\N	\N	702	{"text": "For myself, I don't believe it was an ordinary thief.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_704	lexical	\N	\N	703	{"text": "\\"What is your own idea, then?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_705	lexical	\N	\N	704	{"text": "\\"Upon my word, you may put it down to my weak nerves or not, but I believe there is some deep political intrigue going on around me, and that for some reason that passes my understanding my life is aimed at by the conspirators.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_706	lexical	\N	\N	705	{"text": "It sounds high-flown and absurd, but consider the facts!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_707	lexical	\N	\N	706	{"text": "Why should a thief try to break in at a bedroom window, where there could be no hope of any plunder, and why should he come with a long knife in his hand?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_708	lexical	\N	\N	707	{"text": "\\"You are sure it was not a house-breaker's jimmy?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_15", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_709	lexical	\N	\N	708	{"text": "\\"Oh, no, it was a knife.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_710	lexical	\N	\N	709	{"text": "I saw the flash of the blade quite distinctly.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_711	lexical	\N	\N	710	{"text": "\\"But why on earth should you be pursued with such animosity?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_712	lexical	\N	\N	711	{"text": "\\"Ah, that is the question.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_713	lexical	\N	\N	712	{"text": "\\"Well, if Holmes takes the same view, that would account for his action, would it not?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	the_mare	entity	object	Black mare	\N	{"description": "Hugo Baskerville's black mare.", "firstSection": "section_8"}
naval-treaty	sentence_714	lexical	\N	\N	713	{"text": "Presuming that your theory is correct, if he can lay his hands upon the man who threatened you last night he will have gone a long way towards finding who took the naval treaty.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_715	lexical	\N	\N	714	{"text": "It is absurd to suppose that you have two enemies, one of whom robs you, while the other threatens your life.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_716	lexical	\N	\N	715	{"text": "\\"But Holmes said that he was not going to Briarbrae.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_717	lexical	\N	\N	716	{"text": "\\"I have known him for some time,\\" said I, \\"but I never knew him do anything yet without a very good reason,\\" and with that our conversation drifted off on to other topics.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_718	lexical	\N	\N	717	{"text": "But it was a weary day for me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_719	lexical	\N	\N	718	{"text": "Phelps was still weak after his long illness, and his misfortune made him querulous and nervous.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_720	lexical	\N	\N	719	{"text": "In vain I endeavoured to interest him in Afghanistan, in India, in social questions, in anything which might take his mind out of the groove.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_721	lexical	\N	\N	720	{"text": "He would always come back to his lost treaty, wondering, guessing, speculating, as to what Holmes was doing, what steps Lord Holdhurst was taking, what news we should have in the morning.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_722	lexical	\N	\N	721	{"text": "As the evening wore on his excitement became quite painful.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_723	lexical	\N	\N	722	{"text": "\\"You have implicit faith in Holmes?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_724	lexical	\N	\N	723	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_725	lexical	\N	\N	724	{"text": "\\"I have seen him do some remarkable things.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_726	lexical	\N	\N	725	{"text": "\\"But he never brought light into anything quite so dark as this?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_727	lexical	\N	\N	726	{"text": "\\"Oh, yes; I have known him solve questions which presented fewer clues than yours.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_728	lexical	\N	\N	727	{"text": "\\"But not where such large interests are at stake?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_729	lexical	\N	\N	728	{"text": "\\"I don't know that.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_730	lexical	\N	\N	729	{"text": "To my certain knowledge he has acted on behalf of three of the reigning houses of Europe in very vital matters.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_731	lexical	\N	\N	730	{"text": "\\"But you know him well, Watson.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_732	lexical	\N	\N	731	{"text": "He is such an inscrutable fellow that I never quite know what to make of him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_733	lexical	\N	\N	732	{"text": "Do you think he is hopeful?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_734	lexical	\N	\N	733	{"text": "Do you think he expects to make a success of it?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_735	lexical	\N	\N	734	{"text": "\\"He has said nothing.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_736	lexical	\N	\N	735	{"text": "\\"That is a bad sign.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_737	lexical	\N	\N	736	{"text": "\\"On the contrary, I have noticed that when he is off the trail he generally says so.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_738	lexical	\N	\N	737	{"text": "It is when he is on a scent and is not quite absolutely sure yet that it is the right one that he is most taciturn.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_739	lexical	\N	\N	738	{"text": "Now, my dear fellow, we can't help matters by making ourselves nervous about them, so let me implore you to go to bed and so be fresh for whatever may await us to-morrow.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_740	lexical	\N	\N	739	{"text": "I was able at last to persuade my companion to take my advice, though I knew from his excited manner that there was not much hope of sleep for him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_741	lexical	\N	\N	740	{"text": "Indeed, his mood was infectious, for I lay tossing half the night myself, brooding over this strange problem, and inventing a hundred theories, each of which was more impossible than the last.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_742	lexical	\N	\N	741	{"text": "Why had Holmes remained at Woking?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_743	lexical	\N	\N	742	{"text": "Why had he asked Miss Harrison to remain in the sick-room all day?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_744	lexical	\N	\N	743	{"text": "Why had he been so careful not to inform the people at Briarbrae that he intended to remain near them?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_745	lexical	\N	\N	744	{"text": "I cudgelled my brains until I fell asleep in the endeavour to find some explanation which would cover all these facts.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_746	lexical	\N	\N	745	{"text": "It was seven o'clock when I awoke, and I set off at once for Phelps's room, to find him haggard and spent after a sleepless night.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_747	lexical	\N	\N	746	{"text": "His first question was whether Holmes had arrived yet.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	sentence_3656	lexical	\N	\N	3655	{"text": "“I leave it with you.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_748	lexical	\N	\N	747	{"text": "\\"He'll be here when he promised,\\" said I, \\"and not an instant sooner or later.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_16", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_749	lexical	\N	\N	748	{"text": "And my words were true, for shortly after eight a hansom dashed up to the door and our friend got out of it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_750	lexical	\N	\N	749	{"text": "Standing in the window we saw that his left hand was swathed in a bandage and that his face was very grim and pale.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_751	lexical	\N	\N	750	{"text": "He entered the house, but it was some little time before he came upstairs.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_752	lexical	\N	\N	751	{"text": "\\"He looks like a beaten man,\\" cried Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_753	lexical	\N	\N	752	{"text": "I was forced to confess that he was right.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_754	lexical	\N	\N	753	{"text": "\\"After all,\\" said I, \\"the clue of the matter lies probably here in town.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_755	lexical	\N	\N	754	{"text": "Phelps gave a groan.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_756	lexical	\N	\N	755	{"text": "\\"I don't know how it is,\\" said he, \\"but I had hoped for so much from his return.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_757	lexical	\N	\N	756	{"text": "But surely his hand was not tied up like that yesterday.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_758	lexical	\N	\N	757	{"text": "What can be the matter?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_759	lexical	\N	\N	758	{"text": "\\"You are not wounded, Holmes?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_760	lexical	\N	\N	759	{"text": "I asked, as my friend entered the room.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_761	lexical	\N	\N	760	{"text": "\\"Tut, it is only a scratch through my own clumsiness,\\" he answered, nodding his good-mornings to us.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_762	lexical	\N	\N	761	{"text": "\\"This case of yours, Mr. Phelps, is certainly one of the darkest which I have ever investigated.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_763	lexical	\N	\N	762	{"text": "\\"I feared that you would find it beyond you.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_764	lexical	\N	\N	763	{"text": "\\"It has been a most remarkable experience.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_765	lexical	\N	\N	764	{"text": "\\"That bandage tells of adventures,\\" said I.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_766	lexical	\N	\N	765	{"text": "\\"Won't you tell us what has happened?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_767	lexical	\N	\N	766	{"text": "\\"After breakfast, my dear Watson.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_768	lexical	\N	\N	767	{"text": "Remember that I have breathed thirty miles of Surrey air this morning.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_769	lexical	\N	\N	768	{"text": "I suppose that there has been no answer from my cabman advertisement?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_770	lexical	\N	\N	769	{"text": "Well, well, we cannot expect to score every time.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_771	lexical	\N	\N	770	{"text": "The table was all laid, and just as I was about to ring Mrs. Hudson entered with the tea and coffee.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_772	lexical	\N	\N	771	{"text": "A few minutes later she brought in three covers, and we all drew up to the table, Holmes ravenous, I curious, and Phelps in the gloomiest state of depression.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_773	lexical	\N	\N	772	{"text": "\\"Mrs. Hudson has risen to the occasion,\\" said Holmes, uncovering a dish of curried chicken.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_774	lexical	\N	\N	773	{"text": "\\"Her cuisine is a little limited, but she has as good an idea of breakfast as a Scotch-woman.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_775	lexical	\N	\N	774	{"text": "What have you here, Watson?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_776	lexical	\N	\N	775	{"text": "\\"Ham and eggs,\\" I answered.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_777	lexical	\N	\N	776	{"text": "\\"Good!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_778	lexical	\N	\N	777	{"text": "What are you going to take, Mr. Phelps—curried fowl or eggs, or will you help yourself?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_779	lexical	\N	\N	778	{"text": "\\"Thank you.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_780	lexical	\N	\N	779	{"text": "I can eat nothing,\\" said Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_781	lexical	\N	\N	780	{"text": "\\"Oh, come!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_782	lexical	\N	\N	781	{"text": "Try the dish before you.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_783	lexical	\N	\N	782	{"text": "\\"Thank you, I would really rather not.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_784	lexical	\N	\N	783	{"text": "\\"Well, then,\\" said Holmes, with a mischievous twinkle, \\"I suppose that you have no objection to helping me?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_785	lexical	\N	\N	784	{"text": "Phelps raised the cover, and as he did so he uttered a scream, and sat there staring with a face as white as the plate upon which he looked.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_786	lexical	\N	\N	785	{"text": "Across the centre of it was lying a little cylinder of blue-grey paper.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_787	lexical	\N	\N	786	{"text": "He caught it up, devoured it with his eyes, and then danced madly about the room, pressing it to his bosom and shrieking out in his delight.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_788	lexical	\N	\N	787	{"text": "Then he fell back into an armchair so limp and exhausted with his own emotions that we had to pour brandy down his throat to keep him from fainting.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_789	lexical	\N	\N	788	{"text": "\\"There!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_790	lexical	\N	\N	789	{"text": "there!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_791	lexical	\N	\N	790	{"text": "said Holmes, soothing, patting him upon the shoulder.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_792	lexical	\N	\N	791	{"text": "\\"It was too bad to spring it on you like this, but Watson here will tell you that I never can resist a touch of the dramatic.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_793	lexical	\N	\N	792	{"text": "Phelps seized his hand and kissed it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_794	lexical	\N	\N	793	{"text": "\\"God bless you!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_795	lexical	\N	\N	794	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_796	lexical	\N	\N	795	{"text": "\\"You have saved my honour.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_797	lexical	\N	\N	796	{"text": "\\"Well, my own was at stake, you know,\\" said Holmes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_798	lexical	\N	\N	797	{"text": "\\"I assure you it is just as hateful to me to fail in a case as it can be to you to blunder over a commission.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_799	lexical	\N	\N	798	{"text": "Phelps thrust away the precious document into the innermost pocket of his coat.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_800	lexical	\N	\N	799	{"text": "\\"I have not the heart to interrupt your breakfast any further, and yet I am dying to know how you got it and where it was.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_17", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_801	lexical	\N	\N	800	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes swallowed a cup of coffee, and turned his attention to the ham and eggs.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_802	lexical	\N	\N	801	{"text": "Then he rose, lit his pipe, and settled himself down into his chair.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_803	lexical	\N	\N	802	{"text": "\\"I'll tell you what I did first, and how I came to do it afterwards,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_804	lexical	\N	\N	803	{"text": "\\"After leaving you at the station I went for a charming walk through some admirable Surrey scenery to a pretty little village called Ripley, where I had my tea at an inn, and took the precaution of filling my flask and of putting a paper of sandwiches in my pocket.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_805	lexical	\N	\N	804	{"text": "There I remained until evening, when I set off for Woking again, and found myself in the high-road outside Briarbrae just after sunset.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_806	lexical	\N	\N	805	{"text": "\\"Well, I waited until the road was clear—it is never a very frequented one at any time, I fancy—and then I clambered over the fence into the grounds.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_807	lexical	\N	\N	806	{"text": "\\"Surely the gate was open!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_808	lexical	\N	\N	807	{"text": "ejaculated Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_809	lexical	\N	\N	808	{"text": "\\"Yes, but I have a peculiar taste in these matters.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_810	lexical	\N	\N	809	{"text": "I chose the place where the three fir-trees stand, and behind their screen I got over without the least chance of any one in the house being able to see me.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_811	lexical	\N	\N	810	{"text": "I crouched down among the bushes on the other side, and crawled from one to the other—witness the disreputable state of my trouser knees—until I had reached the clump of rhododendrons just opposite to your bedroom window.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_812	lexical	\N	\N	811	{"text": "There I squatted down and awaited developments.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_813	lexical	\N	\N	812	{"text": "\\"The blind was not down in your room, and I could see Miss Harrison sitting there reading by the table.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_814	lexical	\N	\N	813	{"text": "It was quarter-past ten when she closed her book, fastened the shutters, and retired.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_815	lexical	\N	\N	814	{"text": "\\"I heard her shut the door, and felt quite sure that she had turned the key in the lock.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_816	lexical	\N	\N	815	{"text": "\\"The key!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_817	lexical	\N	\N	816	{"text": "ejaculated Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_818	lexical	\N	\N	817	{"text": "\\"Yes; I had given Miss Harrison instructions to lock the door on the outside and take the key with her when she went to bed.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_819	lexical	\N	\N	818	{"text": "She carried out every one of my injunctions to the letter, and certainly without her co-operation you would not have that paper in your coat-pocket.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	sentence_3812	lexical	\N	\N	3811	{"text": "“It’s him or us.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_820	lexical	\N	\N	819	{"text": "She departed then and the lights went out, and I was left squatting in the rhododendron-bush.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_821	lexical	\N	\N	820	{"text": "\\"The night was fine, but still it was a very weary vigil.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_822	lexical	\N	\N	821	{"text": "Of course it has the sort of excitement about it that the sportsman feels when he lies beside the water-course and waits for the big game.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_823	lexical	\N	\N	822	{"text": "It was very long, though—almost as long, Watson, as when you and I waited in that deadly room when we looked into the little problem of the Speckled Band.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_824	lexical	\N	\N	823	{"text": "There was a church-clock down at Woking which struck the quarters, and I thought more than once that it had stopped.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_825	lexical	\N	\N	824	{"text": "At last however about two in the morning, I suddenly heard the gentle sound of a bolt being pushed back and the creaking of a key.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_826	lexical	\N	\N	825	{"text": "A moment later the servants' door was opened, and Mr. Joseph Harrison stepped out into the moonlight.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_827	lexical	\N	\N	826	{"text": "\\"Joseph!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_828	lexical	\N	\N	827	{"text": "ejaculated Phelps.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_829	lexical	\N	\N	828	{"text": "\\"He was bare-headed, but he had a black coat thrown over his shoulder so that he could conceal his face in an instant if there were any alarm.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_830	lexical	\N	\N	829	{"text": "He walked on tiptoe under the shadow of the wall, and when he reached the window he worked a long-bladed knife through the sash and pushed back the catch.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_831	lexical	\N	\N	830	{"text": "Then he flung open the window, and putting his knife through the crack in the shutters, he thrust the bar up and swung them open.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_832	lexical	\N	\N	831	{"text": "\\"From where I lay I had a perfect view of the inside of the room and of every one of his movements.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_833	lexical	\N	\N	832	{"text": "He lit the two candles which stood upon the mantelpiece, and then he proceeded to turn back the corner of the carpet in the neighbourhood of the door.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_834	lexical	\N	\N	833	{"text": "Presently he stopped and picked out a square piece of board, such as is usually left to enable plumbers to get at the joints of the gas-pipes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_835	lexical	\N	\N	834	{"text": "This one covered, as a matter of fact, the T joint which gives off the pipe which supplies the kitchen underneath.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_836	lexical	\N	\N	835	{"text": "Out of this hiding-place he drew that little cylinder of paper, pushed down the board, rearranged the carpet, blew out the candles, and walked straight into my arms as I stood waiting for him outside the window.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_18", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_837	lexical	\N	\N	836	{"text": "\\"Well, he has rather more viciousness than I gave him credit for, has Master Joseph.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_838	lexical	\N	\N	837	{"text": "He flew at me with his knife, and I had to grasp him twice, and got a cut over the knuckles, before I had the upper hand of him.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_839	lexical	\N	\N	838	{"text": "He looked murder out of the only eye he could see with when we had finished, but he listened to reason and gave up the papers.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_840	lexical	\N	\N	839	{"text": "Having got them I let my man go, but I wired full particulars to Forbes this morning.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_841	lexical	\N	\N	840	{"text": "If he is quick enough to catch his bird, well and good.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_842	lexical	\N	\N	841	{"text": "But if, as I shrewdly suspect, he finds the nest empty before he gets there, why, all the better for the government.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_843	lexical	\N	\N	842	{"text": "I fancy that Lord Holdhurst for one, and Mr. Percy Phelps for another, would very much rather that the affair never got as far as a police-court.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_844	lexical	\N	\N	843	{"text": "\\"My God!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_845	lexical	\N	\N	844	{"text": "gasped our client.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_846	lexical	\N	\N	845	{"text": "\\"Do you tell me that during these long ten weeks of agony the stolen papers were within the very room with me all the time?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_847	lexical	\N	\N	846	{"text": "\\"So it was.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_848	lexical	\N	\N	847	{"text": "\\"And Joseph!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_849	lexical	\N	\N	848	{"text": "Joseph a villain and a thief!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_850	lexical	\N	\N	849	{"text": "\\"Hum!", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_851	lexical	\N	\N	850	{"text": "I am afraid Joseph's character is a rather deeper and more dangerous one than one might judge from his appearance.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_852	lexical	\N	\N	851	{"text": "From what I have heard from him this morning, I gather that he has lost heavily in dabbling with stocks, and that he is ready to do anything on earth to better his fortunes.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_853	lexical	\N	\N	852	{"text": "Being an absolutely selfish man, when a chance presented itself he did not allow either his sister's happiness or your reputation to hold his hand.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_854	lexical	\N	\N	853	{"text": "Percy Phelps sank back in his chair.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_855	lexical	\N	\N	854	{"text": "\\"My head whirls,\\" said he.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_856	lexical	\N	\N	855	{"text": "\\"Your words have dazed me.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_857	lexical	\N	\N	856	{"text": "\\"The principal difficulty in your case,\\" remarked Holmes, in his didactic fashion, \\"lay in the fact of there being too much evidence.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_858	lexical	\N	\N	857	{"text": "What was vital was overlaid and hidden by what was irrelevant.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_859	lexical	\N	\N	858	{"text": "Of all the facts which were presented to us we had to pick just those which we deemed to be essential, and then piece them together in their order, so as to reconstruct this very remarkable chain of events.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_860	lexical	\N	\N	859	{"text": "I had already begun to suspect Joseph, from the fact that you had intended to travel home with him that night, and that therefore it was a likely enough thing that he should call for you, knowing the Foreign Office well, upon his way.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_861	lexical	\N	\N	860	{"text": "When I heard that some one had been so anxious to get into the bedroom, in which no one but Joseph could have concealed anything—you told us in your narrative how you had turned Joseph out when you arrived with the doctor—my suspicions all changed to certainties, especially as the attempt was made on the first night upon which the nurse was absent, showing that the intruder was well acquainted with the ways of the house.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_862	lexical	\N	\N	861	{"text": "\\"How blind I have been!\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_863	lexical	\N	\N	862	{"text": "\\"The facts of the case, as far as I have worked them out, are these: this Joseph Harrison entered the office through the Charles Street door, and knowing his way he walked straight into your room the instant after you left it.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_864	lexical	\N	\N	863	{"text": "Finding no one there he promptly rang the bell, and at the instant that he did so his eyes caught the paper upon the table.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_865	lexical	\N	\N	864	{"text": "A glance showed him that chance had put in his way a State document of immense value, and in an instant he had thrust it into his pocket and was gone.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_866	lexical	\N	\N	865	{"text": "A few minutes elapsed, as you remember, before the sleepy commissionnaire drew your attention to the bell, and those were just enough to give the thief time to make his escape.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_19", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_867	lexical	\N	\N	866	{"text": "\\"He made his way to Woking by the first train, and having examined his booty and assured himself that it really was of immense value, he had concealed it in what he thought was a very safe place, with the intention of taking it out again in a day or two, and carrying it to the French embassy, or wherever he thought that a long price was to be had.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_868	lexical	\N	\N	867	{"text": "Then came your sudden return.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_869	lexical	\N	\N	868	{"text": "He, without a moment's warning, was bundled out of his room, and from that time onward there were always at least two of you there to prevent him from regaining his treasure.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_870	lexical	\N	\N	869	{"text": "The situation to him must have been a maddening one.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_871	lexical	\N	\N	870	{"text": "But at last he thought he saw his chance.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_872	lexical	\N	\N	871	{"text": "He tried to steal in, but was baffled by your wakefulness.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_873	lexical	\N	\N	872	{"text": "You remember that you did not take your usual draught that night.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_874	lexical	\N	\N	873	{"text": "\\"I remember.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_875	lexical	\N	\N	874	{"text": "\\"I fancy that he had taken steps to make that draught efficacious, and that he quite relied upon your being unconscious.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_876	lexical	\N	\N	875	{"text": "Of course, I understood that he would repeat the attempt whenever it could be done with safety.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_877	lexical	\N	\N	876	{"text": "Your leaving the room gave him the chance he wanted.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_878	lexical	\N	\N	877	{"text": "I kept Miss Harrison in it all day so that he might not anticipate us.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_879	lexical	\N	\N	878	{"text": "Then, having given him the idea that the coast was clear, I kept guard as I have described.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_880	lexical	\N	\N	879	{"text": "I already knew that the papers were probably in the room, but I had no desire to rip up all the planking and skirting in search of them.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_881	lexical	\N	\N	880	{"text": "I let him take them, therefore, from the hiding-place, and so saved myself an infinity of trouble.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_882	lexical	\N	\N	881	{"text": "Is there any other point which I can make clear?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	sentence_3925	lexical	\N	\N	3924	{"text": "“How do you know this?”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_883	lexical	\N	\N	882	{"text": "\\"Why did he try the window on the first occasion,\\" I asked, \\"when he might have entered by the door?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_884	lexical	\N	\N	883	{"text": "\\"In reaching the door he would have to pass seven bedrooms.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_885	lexical	\N	\N	884	{"text": "On the other hand, he could get out on to the lawn with ease.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_886	lexical	\N	\N	885	{"text": "Anything else?\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_887	lexical	\N	\N	886	{"text": "\\"You do not think,\\" asked Phelps, \\"that he had any murderous intention?", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_888	lexical	\N	\N	887	{"text": "The knife was only meant as a tool.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_889	lexical	\N	\N	888	{"text": "\\"It may be so,\\" answered Holmes, shrugging his shoulders.", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
naval-treaty	sentence_890	lexical	\N	\N	889	{"text": "\\"I can only say for certain that Mr. Joseph Harrison is a gentleman to whose mercy I should be extremely unwilling to trust.\\"", "section": "naval-treaty-section_20", "entities": []}
