final-problem	sentence_1	lexical	\N	\N	0	{"text": "XII.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_2	lexical	\N	\N	1	{"text": "The Final Problem", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "It is with a heavy heart that I take up my pen to write these the last words in which I shall ever record the singular gifts by which my friend Mr. Sherlock Holmes was distinguished.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "In an incoherent and, as I deeply feel, an entirely inadequate fashion, I have endeavoured to give some account of my strange experiences in his company from the chance which first brought us together at the period of the \\"Study in Scarlet,\\" up to the time of his interference in the matter of the \\"Naval Treaty\\"—an interference which had the unquestionable effect of preventing a serious international complication.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "It was my intention to have stopped there, and to have said nothing of that event which has created a void in my life which the lapse of two years has done little to fill.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "My hand has been forced, however, by the recent letters in which Colonel James Moriarty defends the memory of his brother, and I have no choice but to lay the facts before the public exactly as they occurred.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "I alone know the absolute truth of the matter, and I am satisfied that the time has come when no good purpose is to be served by its suppression.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "As far as I know, there have been only three accounts in the public press: that in the _Journal de Genève_ on May 6th, 1891, the Reuter's despatch in the English papers on May 7th, and finally the recent letter to which I have alluded.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "Of these the first and second were extremely condensed, while the last is, as I shall now show, an absolute perversion of the facts.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "It lies with me to tell for the first time what really took place between Professor Moriarty and Mr. Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "It may be remembered that after my marriage, and my subsequent start in private practice, the very intimate relations which had existed between Holmes and myself became to some extent modified.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "He still came to me from time to time when he desired a companion in his investigation, but these occasions grew more and more seldom, until I find that in the year 1890 there were only three cases of which I retain any record.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "During the winter of that year and the early spring of 1891, I saw in the papers that he had been engaged by the French government upon a matter of supreme importance, and I received two notes from Holmes, dated from Narbonne and from Nimes, from which I gathered that his stay in France was likely to be a long one.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "It was with some surprise, therefore, that I saw him walk into my consulting-room upon the evening of the 24th of April.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "It struck me that he was looking even paler and thinner than usual.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "\\"Yes, I have been using myself up rather too freely,\\" he remarked, in answer to my look rather than to my words; \\"I have been a little pressed of late.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "Have you any objection to my closing your shutters?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "The only light in the room came from the lamp upon the table at which I had been reading.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "Holmes edged his way round the wall and flinging the shutters together, he bolted them securely.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"You are afraid of something?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "\\"Well, I am.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "\\"Of what?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "\\"Of air-guns.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "\\"My dear Holmes, what do you mean?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "\\"I think that you know me well enough, Watson, to understand that I am by no means a nervous man.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "At the same time, it is stupidity rather than courage to refuse to recognise danger when it is close upon you.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "Might I trouble you for a match?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "He drew in the smoke of his cigarette as if the soothing influence was grateful to him.", "section": "final-problem-section_1", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "\\"I must apologise for calling so late,\\" said he, \\"and I must further beg you to be so unconventional as to allow me to leave your house presently by scrambling over your back garden wall.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "\\"But what does it all mean?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "He held out his hand, and I saw in the light of the lamp that two of his knuckles were burst and bleeding.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "\\"It is not an airy nothing, you see,\\" said he, smiling.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "\\"On the contrary, it is solid enough for a man to break his hand over.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "Is Mrs. Watson in?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "\\"She is away upon a visit.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "\\"Indeed!", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "You are alone?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "\\"Quite.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "\\"Then it makes it the easier for me to propose that you should come away with me for a week to the Continent.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "\\"Where?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "\\"Oh, anywhere.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "It's all the same to me.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "There was something very strange in all this.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "It was not Holmes's nature to take an aimless holiday, and something about his pale, worn face told me that his nerves were at their highest tension.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "He saw the question in my eyes, and, putting his finger-tips together and his elbows upon his knees, he explained the situation.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "\\"You have probably never heard of Professor Moriarty?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "\\"Never.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "\\"Aye, there's the genius and the wonder of the thing!\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "\\"The man pervades London, and no one has heard of him.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "That's what puts him on a pinnacle in the records of crime.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "I tell you, Watson, in all seriousness, that if I could beat that man, if I could free society of him, I should feel that my own career had reached its summit, and I should be prepared to turn to some more placid line in life.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "Between ourselves, the recent cases in which I have been of assistance to the royal family of Scandinavia, and to the French republic, have left me in such a position that I could continue to live in the quiet fashion which is most congenial to me, and to concentrate my attention upon my chemical researches.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "But I could not rest, Watson, I could not sit quiet in my chair, if I thought that such a man as Professor Moriarty were walking the streets of London unchallenged.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "\\"What has he done, then?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "\\"His career has been an extraordinary one.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "He is a man of good birth and excellent education, endowed by nature with a phenomenal mathematical faculty.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "At the age of twenty-one he wrote a treatise upon the Binomial Theorem, which has had a European vogue.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "On the strength of it he won the Mathematical Chair at one of our smaller universities, and had, to all appearances, a most brilliant career before him.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "But the man had hereditary tendencies of the most diabolical kind.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "A criminal strain ran in his blood, which, instead of being modified, was increased and rendered infinitely more dangerous by his extraordinary mental powers.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "Dark rumours gathered round him in the university town, and eventually he was compelled to resign his chair and to come down to London, where he set up as an Army coach.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "So much is known to the world, but what I am telling you now is what I have myself discovered.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "\\"As you are aware, Watson, there is no one who knows the higher criminal world of London so well as I do.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "For years past I have continually been conscious of some power behind the malefactor, some deep organizing power which forever stands in the way of the law, and throws its shield over the wrong-doer.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "Again and again in cases of the most varying sorts—forgery cases, robberies, murders—I have felt the presence of this force, and I have deduced its action in many of those undiscovered crimes in which I have not been personally consulted.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "For years I have endeavoured to break through the veil which shrouded it, and at last the time came when I seized my thread and followed it, until it led me, after a thousand cunning windings, to ex-Professor Moriarty of mathematical celebrity.", "section": "final-problem-section_2", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "\\"He is the Napoleon of crime, Watson.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "He is the organizer of half that is evil and of nearly all that is undetected in this great city.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "He is a genius, a philosopher, an abstract thinker.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "He has a brain of the first order.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "He sits motionless, like a spider in the centre of its web, but that web has a thousand radiations, and he knows well every quiver of each of them.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "He does little himself.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "He only plans.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "But his agents are numerous and splendidly organized.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "Is there a crime to be done, a paper to be abstracted, we will say, a house to be rifled, a man to be removed—the word is passed to the Professor, the matter is organized and carried out.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "The agent may be caught.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "In that case money is found for his bail or his defence.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "But the central power which uses the agent is never caught—never so much as suspected.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "This was the organization which I deduced, Watson, and which I devoted my whole energy to exposing and breaking up.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "\\"But the Professor was fenced round with safeguards so cunningly devised that, do what I would, it seemed impossible to get evidence which would convict in a court of law.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "You know my powers, my dear Watson, and yet at the end of three months I was forced to confess that I had at last met an antagonist who was my intellectual equal.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "My horror at his crimes was lost in my admiration at his skill.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "But at last he made a trip—only a little, little trip—but it was more than he could afford when I was so close upon him.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "I had my chance, and, starting from that point, I have woven my net round him until now it is all ready to close.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "In three days—that is to say, on Monday next—matters will be ripe, and the Professor, with all the principal members of his gang, will be in the hands of the police.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "Then will come the greatest criminal trial of the century, the clearing up of over forty mysteries, and the rope for all of them; but if we move at all prematurely, you understand, they may slip out of our hands even at the last moment.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "\\"Now, if I could have done this without the knowledge of Professor Moriarty, all would have been well.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "But he was too wily for that.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "He saw every step which I took to draw my toils round him.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "Again and again he strove to break away, but I as often headed him off.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "I tell you, my friend, that if a detailed account of that silent contest could be written, it would take its place as the most brilliant bit of thrust-and-parry work in the history of detection.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "Never have I risen to such a height, and never have I been so hard pressed by an opponent.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "He cut deep, and yet I just undercut him.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "This morning the last steps were taken, and three days only were wanted to complete the business.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "I was sitting in my room thinking the matter over, when the door opened and Professor Moriarty stood before me.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "\\"My nerves are fairly proof, Watson, but I must confess to a start when I saw the very man who had been so much in my thoughts standing there on my threshhold.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "His appearance was quite familiar to me.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "He is extremely tall and thin, his forehead domes out in a white curve, and his two eyes are deeply sunken in his head.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "He is clean-shaven, pale, and ascetic-looking, retaining something of the professor in his features.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "His shoulders are rounded from much study, and his face protrudes forward, and is forever slowly oscillating from side to side in a curiously reptilian fashion.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "He peered at me with great curiosity in his puckered eyes.", "section": "final-problem-section_3", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "\\"'You have less frontal development than I should have expected,' said he, at last.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "'It is a dangerous habit to finger loaded firearms in the pocket of one's dressing-gown.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "\\"The fact is that upon his entrance I had instantly recognised the extreme personal danger in which I lay.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "The only conceivable escape for him lay in silencing my tongue.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "In an instant I had slipped the revolver from the drawer into my pocket, and was covering him through the cloth.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "At his remark I drew the weapon out and laid it cocked upon the table.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "He still smiled and blinked, but there was something about his eyes which made me feel very glad that I had it there.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "\\"'You evidently don't know me,' said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "\\"'On the contrary,' I answered, 'I think it is fairly evident that I do.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "Pray take a chair.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "I can spare you five minutes if you have anything to say.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "\\"'All that I have to say has already crossed your mind,' said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "\\"'Then possibly my answer has crossed yours,' I replied.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "\\"'You stand fast?'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "\\"'Absolutely.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "\\"He clapped his hand into his pocket, and I raised the pistol from the table.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "But he merely drew out a memorandum-book in which he had scribbled some dates.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "\\"'You crossed my path on the 4th of January,' said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "'On the 23rd you incommoded me; by the middle of February I was seriously inconvenienced by you; at the end of March I was absolutely hampered in my plans; and now, at the close of April, I find myself placed in such a position through your continual persecution that I am in positive danger of losing my liberty.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "The situation is becoming an impossible one.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "any suggestion to make?' I asked.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "\\"'You must drop it, Mr. Holmes,' said he, swaying his face about.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "'You really must, you know.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "\\"'After Monday,' said I.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "\\"'Tut, tut,' said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "'I am quite sure that a man of your intelligence will see that there can be but one outcome to this affair.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "It is necessary that you should withdraw.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "You have worked things in such a fashion that we have only one resource left.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "It has been an intellectual treat to me to see the way in which you have grappled with this affair, and I say, unaffectedly, that it would be a grief to me to be forced to take any extreme measure.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "You smile, sir, but I assure you that it really would.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "\\"'Danger is part of my trade,' I remarked.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "\\"'That is not danger,' said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "'It is inevitable destruction.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "You stand in the way not merely of an individual, but of a mighty organization, the full extent of which you, with all your cleverness, have been unable to realize.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "You must stand clear, Mr. Holmes, or be trodden under foot.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "\\"'I am afraid,' said I, rising, 'that in the pleasure of this conversation I am neglecting business of importance which awaits me elsewhere.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "\\"He rose also and looked at me in silence, shaking his head sadly.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "\\"'Well, well,' said he, at last.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "'It seems a pity, but I have done what I could.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "I know every move of your game.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "You can do nothing before Monday.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "It has been a duel between you and me, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "You hope to place me in the dock.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "I tell you that I will never stand in the dock.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "You hope to beat me.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "I tell you that you will never beat me.", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "If you are clever enough to bring destruction upon me, rest assured that I shall do as much to you.'", "section": "final-problem-section_4", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "\\"'You have paid me several compliments, Mr. Moriarty,' said I.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "'Let me pay you one in return when I say that if I were assured of the former eventuality I would, in the interests of the public, cheerfully accept the latter.'", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "\\"'I can promise you the one, but not the other,' he snarled, and so turned his rounded back upon me, and went peering and blinking out of the room.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "\\"That was my singular interview with Professor Moriarty.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "I confess that it left an unpleasant effect upon my mind.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "His soft, precise fashion of speech leaves a conviction of sincerity which a mere bully could not produce.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "' The reason is that I am well convinced that it is from his agents the blow will fall.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "I have the best proofs that it would be so.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "gents the blow will fall. I have the best proofs that it would be so.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "\\"You have already been assaulted?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "\\"My dear Watson, Professor Moriarty is not a man who lets the grass grow under his feet.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "I went out about midday to transact some business in Oxford Street.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "As I passed the corner which leads from Bentinck Street on to the Welbeck Street crossing a two-horse van furiously driven whizzed round and was on me like a flash.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "I sprang for the foot-path and saved myself by the fraction of a second.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "The van dashed round by Marylebone Lane and was gone in an instant.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "I kept to the pavement after that, Watson, but as I walked down Vere Street a brick came down from the roof of one of the houses, and was shattered to fragments at my feet.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "I called the police and had the place examined.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "There were slates and bricks piled up on the roof preparatory to some repairs, and they would have me believe that the wind had toppled over one of these.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "Of course I knew better, but I could prove nothing.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "I took a cab after that and reached my brother's rooms in Pall Mall, where I spent the day.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "Now I have come round to you, and on my way I was attacked by a rough with a bludgeon.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "I knocked him down, and the police have him in custody; but I can tell you with the most absolute confidence that no possible connection will ever be traced between the gentleman upon whose front teeth I have barked my knuckles and the retiring mathematical coach, who is, I daresay, working out problems upon a blackboard ten miles away.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "\\"They must have lost my track completely after their bludgeon-man was arrested.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "You will not wonder, Watson, that my first act on entering your rooms was to close your shutters, and that I have been compelled to ask your permission to leave the house by some less conspicuous exit than the front door.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "I had often admired my friend's courage, but never more than now, as he sat quietly checking off a series of incidents which must have combined to make up a day of horror.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "\\"You will spend the night here?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "I said.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "\\"No, my friend, you might find me a dangerous guest.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "I have my plans laid, and all will be well.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "Matters have gone so far now that they can move without my help as far as the arrest goes, though my presence is necessary for a conviction.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "It is obvious, therefore, that I cannot do better than get away for the few days which remain before the police are at liberty to act.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "It would be a great pleasure to me, therefore, if you could come on to the Continent with me.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "\\"The practice is quiet,\\" said I, \\"and I have an accommodating neighbour.", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "I should be glad to come.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_5", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "\\"And to start to-morrow morning?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "\\"If necessary.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "\\"Oh yes, it is most necessary.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "Then these are your instructions, and I beg, my dear Watson, that you will obey them to the letter, for you are now playing a double-handed game with me against the cleverest rogue and the most powerful syndicate of criminals in Europe.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "Now listen!", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "You will dispatch whatever luggage you intend to take by a trusty messenger unaddressed to Victoria to-night.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "In the morning you will send for a hansom, desiring your man to take neither the first nor the second which may present itself.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "Into this hansom you will jump, and you will drive to the Strand end of the Lowther Arcade, handing the address to the cabman upon a slip of paper, with a request that he will not throw it away.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "Have your fare ready, and the instant that your cab stops, dash through the Arcade, timing yourself to reach the other side at a quarter-past nine.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "You will find a small brougham waiting close to the curb, driven by a fellow with a heavy black cloak tipped at the collar with red.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "Into this you will step, and you will reach Victoria in time for the Continental express.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "\\"Where shall I meet you?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "\\"At the station.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "The second first-class carriage from the front will be reserved for us.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "\\"The carriage is our rendezvous, then?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "\\"Yes.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "It was in vain that I asked Holmes to remain for the evening.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "It was evident to me that he thought he might bring trouble to the roof he was under, and that that was the motive which impelled him to go.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "With a few hurried words as to our plans for the morrow he rose and came out with me into the garden, clambering over the wall which leads into Mortimer Street, and immediately whistling for a hansom, in which I heard him drive away.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "In the morning I obeyed Holmes's injunctions to the letter.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "A hansom was procured with such precaution as would prevent its being one which was placed ready for us, and I drove immediately after breakfast to the Lowther Arcade, through which I hurried at the top of my speed.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "A brougham was waiting with a very massive driver wrapped in a dark cloak, who, the instant that I had stepped in, whipped up the horse and rattled off to Victoria Station.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "On my alighting there he turned the carriage, and dashed away again without so much as a look in my direction.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "So far all had gone admirably.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "My luggage was waiting for me, and I had no difficulty in finding the carriage which Holmes had indicated, the less so as it was the only one in the train which was marked \\"Engaged.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "My only source of anxiety now was the non-appearance of Holmes.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "The station clock marked only seven minutes from the time when we were due to start.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "In vain I searched among the groups of travellers and leave-takers for the lithe figure of my friend.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "There was no sign of him.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "I spent a few minutes in assisting a venerable Italian priest, who was endeavouring to make a porter understand, in his broken English, that his luggage was to be booked through to Paris.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "Then, having taken another look round, I returned to my carriage, where I found that the porter, in spite of the ticket, had given me my decrepit Italian friend as a traveling companion.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "It was useless for me to explain to him that his presence was an intrusion, for my Italian was even more limited than his English, so I shrugged my shoulders resignedly, and continued to look out anxiously for my friend.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "A chill of fear had come over me, as I thought that his absence might mean that some blow had fallen during the night.", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "Already the doors had all been shut and the whistle blown, when—", "section": "final-problem-section_6", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "\\"My dear Watson,\\" said a voice, \\"you have not even condescended to say good-morning.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "I turned in uncontrollable astonishment.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "The aged ecclesiastic had turned his face towards me.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "For an instant the wrinkles were smoothed away, the nose drew away from the chin, the lower lip ceased to protrude and the mouth to mumble, the dull eyes regained their fire, the drooping figure expanded.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "The next the whole frame collapsed again, and Holmes had gone as quickly as he had come.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "\\"Good heavens!\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "I cried.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "\\"How you startled me!\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "\\"Every precaution is still necessary,\\" he whispered.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "\\"I have reason to think that they are hot upon our trail.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "Ah, there is Moriarty himself.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "The train had already begun to move as Holmes spoke.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "Glancing back, I saw a tall man pushing his way furiously through the crowd, and waving his hand as if he desired to have the train stopped.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "It was too late, however, for we were rapidly gathering momentum, and an instant later had shot clear of the station.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "\\"With all our precautions, you see that we have cut it rather fine,\\" said Holmes, laughing.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "He rose, and throwing off the black cassock and hat which had formed his disguise, he packed them away in a hand-bag.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "\\"Have you seen the morning paper, Watson?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "\\"You haven't seen about Baker Street, then?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "\\"Baker Street?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "\\"They set fire to our rooms last night.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "No great harm was done.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "\\"Good heavens, Holmes!", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "This is intolerable.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "Otherwise they could not have imagined that I had returned to my rooms.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "They have evidently taken the precaution of watching you, however, and that is what has brought Moriarty to Victoria.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "You could not have made any slip in coming?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "\\"I did exactly what you advised.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "\\"Did you find your brougham?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "\\"Yes, it was waiting.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "\\"Did you recognise your coachman?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "\\"No.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "\\"It was my brother Mycroft.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "It is an advantage to get about in such a case without taking a mercenary into your confidence.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "But we must plan what we are to do about Moriarty now.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "\\"As this is an express, and as the boat runs in connection with it, I should think we have shaken him off very effectively.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "\\"My dear Watson, you evidently did not realize my meaning when I said that this man may be taken as being quite on the same intellectual plane as myself.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "You do not imagine that if I were the pursuer I should allow myself to be baffled by so slight an obstacle.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "Why, then, should you think so meanly of him?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "\\"What will he do?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "\\"What I should do?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "\\"What would you do, then?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "\\"Engage a special.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "\\"But it must be late.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "\\"By no means.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "This train stops at Canterbury; and there is always at least a quarter of an hour's delay at the boat.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "He will catch us there.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "\\"One would think that we were the criminals.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "Let us have him arrested on his arrival.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "\\"It would be to ruin the work of three months.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "We should get the big fish, but the smaller would dart right and left out of the net.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "On Monday we should have them all.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "No, an arrest is inadmissible.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "\\"What then?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "\\"We shall get out at Canterbury.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "\\"And then?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "\\"Well, then we must make a cross-country journey to Newhaven, and so over to Dieppe.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "Moriarty will again do what I should do.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "He will get on to Paris, mark down our luggage, and wait for two days at the depôt.", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "In the meantime we shall treat ourselves to a couple of carpet-bags, encourage the manufactures of the countries through which we travel, and make our way at our leisure into Switzerland, via Luxembourg and Basle.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_7", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "At Canterbury, therefore, we alighted, only to find that we should have to wait an hour before we could get a train to Newhaven.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "I was still looking rather ruefully after the rapidly disappearing luggage-van which contained my wardrobe, when Holmes pulled my sleeve and pointed up the line.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "\\"Already, you see,\\" said he.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "Far away, from among the Kentish woods there rose a thin spray of smoke.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "A minute later a carriage and engine could be seen flying along the open curve which leads to the station.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "We had hardly time to take our place behind a pile of luggage when it passed with a rattle and a roar, beating a blast of hot air into our faces.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "\\"There he goes,\\" said Holmes, as we watched the carriage swing and rock over the points.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "\\"There are limits, you see, to our friend's intelligence.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "It would have been a _coup-de-maître_ had he deduced what I would deduce and acted accordingly.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "\\"And what would he have done had he overtaken us?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "\\"There cannot be the least doubt that he would have made a murderous attack upon me.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "It is, however, a game at which two may play.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "The question now is whether we should take a premature lunch here, or run our chance of starving before we reach the buffet at Newhaven.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "We made our way to Brussels that night and spent two days there, moving on upon the third day as far as Strasburg.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "On the Monday morning Holmes had telegraphed to the London police, and in the evening we found a reply waiting for us at our hotel.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "Holmes tore it open, and then with a bitter curse hurled it into the grate.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "\\"I might have known it!\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "he groaned.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "\\"He has escaped!\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "\\"Moriarty?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "\\"They have secured the whole gang with the exception of him.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "He has given them the slip.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "Of course, when I had left the country there was no one to cope with him.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "But I did think that I had put the game in their hands.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "I think that you had better return to England, Watson.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "\\"Why?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "\\"Because you will find me a dangerous companion now.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "This man's occupation is gone.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "He is lost if he returns to London.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "If I read his character right he will devote his whole energies to revenging himself upon me.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "He said as much in our short interview, and I fancy that he meant it.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "I should certainly recommend you to return to your practice.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "It was hardly an appeal to be successful with one who was an old campaigner as well as an old friend.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "We sat in the Strasburg _salle-à-manger_ arguing the question for half an hour, but the same night we had resumed our journey and were well on our way to Geneva.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "For a charming week we wandered up the Valley of the Rhone, and then, branching off at Leuk, we made our way over the Gemmi Pass, still deep in snow, and so, by way of Interlaken, to Meiringen.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "It was a lovely trip, the dainty green of the spring below, the virgin white of the winter above; but it was clear to me that never for one instant did Holmes forget the shadow which lay across him.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "In the homely Alpine villages or in the lonely mountain passes, I could tell by his quick glancing eyes and his sharp scrutiny of every face that passed us, that he was well convinced that, walk where we would, we could not walk ourselves clear of the danger which was dogging our footsteps.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "The young Swiss had gone too.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "Once, I remember, as we passed over the Gemmi, and walked along the border of the melancholy Daubensee, a large rock which had been dislodged from the ridge upon our right clattered down and roared into the lake behind us.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "In an instant Holmes had raced up on to the ridge, and, standing upon a lofty pinnacle, craned his neck in every direction.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "It was in vain that our guide assured him that a fall of stones was a common chance in the spring-time at that spot.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "He said nothing, but he smiled at me with the air of a man who sees the fulfillment of that which he had expected.", "section": "final-problem-section_8", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "And yet for all his watchfulness he was never depressed.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "On the contrary, I can never recollect having seen him in such exuberant spirits.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "Again and again he recurred to the fact that if he could be assured that society was freed from Professor Moriarty he would cheerfully bring his own career to a conclusion.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "\\"I think that I may go so far as to say, Watson, that I have not lived wholly in vain,\\" he remarked.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "\\"If my record were closed to-night I could still survey it with equanimity.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "The air of London is the sweeter for my presence.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "In over a thousand cases I am not aware that I have ever used my powers upon the wrong side.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "Of late I have been tempted to look into the problems furnished by nature rather than those more superficial ones for which our artificial state of society is responsible.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "Your memoirs will draw to an end, Watson, upon the day that I crown my career by the capture or extinction of the most dangerous and capable criminal in Europe.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "I shall be brief, and yet exact, in the little which remains for me to tell.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "It is not a subject on which I would willingly dwell, and yet I am conscious that a duty devolves upon me to omit no detail.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "It was on the 3rd of May that we reached the little village of Meiringen, where we put up at the Englischer Hof, then kept by Peter Steiler the elder.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "Our landlord was an intelligent man, and spoke excellent English, having served for three years as waiter at the Grosvenor Hotel in London.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "At his advice, on the afternoon of the 4th we set off together, with the intention of crossing the hills and spending the night at the hamlet of Rosenlaui.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "We had strict injunctions, however, on no account to pass the falls of Reichenbach, which are about half-way up the hill, without making a small détour to see them.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "It is indeed, a fearful place.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "The torrent, swollen by the melting snow, plunges into a tremendous abyss, from which the spray rolls up like the smoke from a burning house.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "The shaft into which the river hurls itself is an immense chasm, lined by glistening coal-black rock, and narrowing into a creaming, boiling pit of incalculable depth, which brims over and shoots the stream onward over its jagged lip.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "The long sweep of green water roaring forever down, and the thick flickering curtain of spray hissing forever upward, turn a man giddy with their constant whirl and clamour.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "We stood near the edge peering down at the gleam of the breaking water far below us against the black rocks, and listening to the half-human shout which came booming up with the spray out of the abyss.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "The path has been cut half-way round the fall to afford a complete view, but it ends abruptly, and the traveler has to return as he came.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "We had turned to do so, when we saw a Swiss lad come running along it with a letter in his hand.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "It bore the mark of the hotel which we had just left, and was addressed to me by the landlord.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "It appeared that within a very few minutes of our leaving, an English lady had arrived who was in the last stage of consumption.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "She had wintered at Davos Platz, and was journeying now to join her friends at Lucerne, when a sudden hemorrhage had overtaken her.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "It was thought that she could hardly live a few hours, but it would be a great consolation to her to see an English doctor, and, if I would only return, etc. The good Steiler assured me in a postscript that he would himself look upon my compliance as a very great favour, since the lady absolutely refused to see a Swiss physician, and he could not but feel that he was incurring a great responsibility.", "section": "final-problem-section_9", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "The appeal was one which could not be ignored.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "It was impossible to refuse the request of a fellow-countrywoman dying in a strange land.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "Yet I had my scruples about leaving Holmes.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "It was finally agreed, however, that he should retain the young Swiss messenger with him as guide and companion while I returned to Meiringen.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "My friend would stay some little time at the fall, he said, and would then walk slowly over the hill to Rosenlaui, where I was to rejoin him in the evening.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "As I turned away I saw Holmes, with his back against a rock and his arms folded, gazing down at the rush of the waters.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "It was the last that I was ever destined to see of him in this world.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "When I was near the bottom of the descent I looked back.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "It was impossible, from that position, to see the fall, but I could see the curving path which winds over the shoulder of the hill and leads to it.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "Along this a man was, I remember, walking very rapidly.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "I could see his black figure clearly outlined against the green behind him.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "I noted him, and the energy with which he walked but he passed from my mind again as I hurried on upon my errand.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "It may have been a little over an hour before I reached Meiringen.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "Old Steiler was standing at the porch of his hotel.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "\\"Well,\\" said I, as I came hurrying up, \\"I trust that she is no worse?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "A look of surprise passed over his face, and at the first quiver of his eyebrows my heart turned to lead in my breast.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "\\"You did not write this?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "I said, pulling the letter from my pocket.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "\\"There is no sick Englishwoman in the hotel?\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "\\"Certainly not!\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "\\"But it has the hotel mark upon it!", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "Ha, it must have been written by that tall Englishman who came in after you had gone.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "He said—\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "But I waited for none of the landlord's explanations.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "In a tingle of fear I was already running down the village street, and making for the path which I had so lately descended.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "It had taken me an hour to come down.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "For all my efforts two more had passed before I found myself at the fall of Reichenbach once more.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "There was Holmes's Alpine-stock still leaning against the rock by which I had left him.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "But there was no sign of him, and it was in vain that I shouted.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "My only answer was my own voice reverberating in a rolling echo from the cliffs around me.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "It was the sight of that Alpine-stock which turned me cold and sick.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "He had not gone to Rosenlaui, then.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "He had remained on that three-foot path, with sheer wall on one side and sheer drop on the other, until his enemy had overtaken him.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "He had probably been in the pay of Moriarty, and had left the two men together.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "And then what had happened?", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "Who was to tell us what had happened then?", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "I stood for a minute or two to collect myself, for I was dazed with the horror of the thing.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "Then I began to think of Holmes's own methods and to try to practise them in reading this tragedy.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "It was, alas, only too easy to do.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "During our conversation we had not gone to the end of the path, and the Alpine-stock marked the place where we had stood.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "The blackish soil is kept forever soft by the incessant drift of spray, and a bird would leave its tread upon it.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "Two lines of footmarks were clearly marked along the farther end of the path, both leading away from me.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "There were none returning.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "A few yards from the end the soil was all ploughed up into a patch of mud, and the branches and ferns which fringed the chasm were torn and bedraggled.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "I lay upon my face and peered over with the spray spouting up all around me.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "It had darkened since I left, and now I could only see here and there the glistening of moisture upon the black walls, and far away down at the end of the shaft the gleam of the broken water.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "I shouted; but only the same half-human cry of the fall was borne back to my ears.", "section": "final-problem-section_10", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "But it was destined that I should after all have a last word of greeting from my friend and comrade.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "I have said that his Alpine-stock had been left leaning against a rock which jutted on to the path.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "From the top of this boulder the gleam of something bright caught my eye, and, raising my hand, I found that it came from the silver cigarette-case which he used to carry.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "As I took it up a small square of paper upon which it had lain fluttered down on to the ground.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "Unfolding it, I found that it consisted of three pages torn from his note-book and addressed to me.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "It was characteristic of the man that the direction was a precise, and the writing as firm and clear, as though it had been written in his study.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "\\"My dear Watson,\\" he said, \\"I write these few lines through the courtesy of Mr. Moriarty, who awaits my convenience for the final discussion of those questions which lie between us.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "He has been giving me a sketch of the methods by which he avoided the English police and kept himself informed of our movements.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "They certainly confirm the very high opinion which I had formed of his abilities.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "I am pleased to think that I shall be able to free society from any further effects of his presence, though I fear that it is at a cost which will give pain to my friends, and especially, my dear Watson, to you.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "I have already explained to you, however, that my career had in any case reached its crisis, and that no possible conclusion to it could be more congenial to me than this.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "Indeed, if I may make a full confession to you, I was quite convinced that the letter from Meiringen was a hoax, and I allowed you to depart on that errand under the persuasion that some development of this sort would follow.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "' I made every disposition of my property before leaving England, and handed it to my brother Mycroft.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "up in a blue envelope and inscribed 'Moriarty.' I made every disposition of my property before leaving England, and handed it to my brother Mycroft. Pray give my greetings to Mrs. Watson, and believe me to be, my dear fellow,", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "\\"Very sincerely yours, \\"Sherlock Holmes.\\"", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "A few words may suffice to tell the little that remains.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	marylebone_lane	entity	location	Marylebone Lane	\N	{"description": "A lane in London.", "firstSection": "final-problem-section_5"}
final-problem	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "An examination by experts leaves little doubt that a personal contest between the two men ended, as it could hardly fail to end in such a situation, in their reeling over, locked in each other's arms.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "Any attempt at recovering the bodies was absolutely hopeless, and there, deep down in that dreadful caldron of swirling water and seething foam, will lie for all time the most dangerous criminal and the foremost champion of the law of their generation.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "The Swiss youth was never found again, and there can be no doubt that he was one of the numerous agents whom Moriarty kept in his employ.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "As to the gang, it will be within the memory of the public how completely the evidence which Holmes had accumulated exposed their organization, and how heavily the hand of the dead man weighed upon them.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
final-problem	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "Of their terrible chief few details came out during the proceedings, and if I have now been compelled to make a clear statement of his career it is due to those injudicious champions who have endeavoured to clear his memory by attacks upon him whom I shall ever regard as the best and the wisest man whom I have ever known.", "section": "final-problem-section_11", "entities": []}
