final-problem	event_6_12	event	\N	Watson returns to his carriage and finds the priest as a traveling companion	5	{"section": "final-problem-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_217", "sentence_218"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_6_13	event	\N	Watson fears Holmes may have suffered a blow during the night	5	{"section": "final-problem-section_6", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_219"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_1	event	\N	Holmes speaks to Watson while disguised as a clergyman	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_221"], "communicatesContent": "My dear Watson, you have not even condescended to say good-morning."}
final-problem	event_7_2	event	\N	Watson turns in astonishment	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_222"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_3	event	\N	The priest turns his face toward Watson	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_223"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_4	event	\N	Holmes's disguise briefly changes back to his own appearance and then collapses again	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_224", "sentence_225"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_5	event	\N	Watson cries out in alarm	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_226", "sentence_227", "sentence_228"], "communicatesContent": "Good heavens! How you startled me!"}
final-problem	event_7_6	event	\N	Holmes warns Watson that precautions are still necessary	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_229", "sentence_230", "sentence_231"], "communicatesContent": "Every precaution is still necessary. I have reason to think that they are hot upon our trail. Ah, there is Moriarty himself."}
final-problem	event_7_7	event	\N	The train begins to move	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_232"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_8	event	\N	Watson sees Moriarty pushing through the crowd and waving for the train to stop	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_233"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_9	event	\N	The train leaves the station	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_234"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_10	event	\N	Holmes remarks that they have cut it rather fine and removes his disguise	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_235", "sentence_236"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_11	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson about the morning paper and Baker Street	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_237", "sentence_239", "sentence_240"], "communicatesContent": "Have you seen the morning paper, Watson? You haven't seen about Baker Street, then?"}
final-problem	event_7_12	event	\N	Watson replies that he has not seen the morning paper	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_238"], "communicatesContent": "No."}
final-problem	event_7_13	event	\N	Holmes says that their rooms were set on fire last night and that no great harm was done	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_241", "sentence_242"], "communicatesContent": "They set fire to our rooms last night. No great harm was done."}
final-problem	event_7_14	event	\N	Watson reacts with outrage	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_243", "sentence_244"], "communicatesContent": "Good heavens, Holmes! This is intolerable."}
final-problem	event_7_15	event	\N	Holmes explains that the bludgeon-man was arrested and that Moriarty came to Victoria because Watson was watched	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_245", "sentence_246", "sentence_247", "sentence_248"], "communicatesContent": "They must have lost my track completely after their bludgeon-man was arrested. Otherwise they could not have imagined that I had returned to my rooms. They have evidently taken the precaution of watching you, however, and that is what has brought Moriarty to Victoria. You could not have made any slip in coming?"}
final-problem	event_7_16	event	\N	Watson says he did exactly what Holmes advised	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_249"], "communicatesContent": "I did exactly what you advised."}
final-problem	event_7_17	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Watson found his brougham and recognised the coachman	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_250", "sentence_252"], "communicatesContent": "Did you find your brougham? Did you recognise your coachman?"}
final-problem	event_7_18	event	\N	Watson answers that the brougham was waiting and that he did not recognise the coachman	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_251", "sentence_253"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, it was waiting. No."}
final-problem	event_7_19	event	\N	Holmes identifies the coachman as his brother Mycroft	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_254", "sentence_255"], "communicatesContent": "It was my brother Mycroft. It is an advantage to get about in such a case without taking a mercenary into your confidence."}
final-problem	event_7_20	event	\N	Holmes says they must plan what to do about Moriarty	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_256"], "communicatesContent": "But we must plan what we are to do about Moriarty now."}
final-problem	event_7_21	event	\N	Watson says they have probably shaken Moriarty off	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_257"], "communicatesContent": "As this is an express, and as the boat runs in connection with it, I should think we have shaken him off very effectively."}
final-problem	event_7_22	event	\N	Holmes says Moriarty is his intellectual equal and would not be baffled so easily	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260"], "communicatesContent": "My dear Watson, you evidently did not realize my meaning when I said that this man may be taken as being quite on the same intellectual plane as myself. You do not imagine that if I were the pursuer I should allow myself to be baffled by so slight an obstacle. Why, then, should you think so meanly of him?"}
final-problem	event_7_23	event	\N	Watson asks what Moriarty will do	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_261", "sentence_263"], "communicatesContent": "What will he do? What would you do, then?"}
final-problem	event_7_24	event	\N	Holmes says he would engage a special train	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_262", "sentence_264"], "communicatesContent": "Engage a special."}
final-problem	event_7_25	event	\N	Watson comments that it must be late	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_265"], "communicatesContent": "But it must be late."}
final-problem	event_9_4	event	\N	A Swiss lad runs along the path carrying a letter	8	{"section": "final-problem-section_9", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_344"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_7_26	event	\N	Holmes says the train stops at Canterbury and that Moriarty will catch them there	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_266", "sentence_267", "sentence_268"], "communicatesContent": "By no means. This train stops at Canterbury; and there is always at least a quarter of an hour's delay at the boat. He will catch us there."}
final-problem	event_7_27	event	\N	Watson proposes having Moriarty arrested on arrival	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_269", "sentence_270"], "communicatesContent": "One would think that we were the criminals. Let us have him arrested on his arrival."}
final-problem	event_7_28	event	\N	Holmes rejects arrest as inadmissible and says it would ruin three months' work	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_271", "sentence_272", "sentence_273", "sentence_274"], "communicatesContent": "It would be to ruin the work of three months. We should get the big fish, but the smaller would dart right and left out of the net. On Monday we should have them all. No, an arrest is inadmissible."}
final-problem	event_7_29	event	\N	Watson asks what they should do	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_275"], "communicatesContent": "What then?"}
final-problem	event_7_30	event	\N	Holmes says they will get out at Canterbury and travel to the Continent by a cross-country route	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_276", "sentence_277", "sentence_278", "sentence_281"], "communicatesContent": "We shall get out at Canterbury. Well, then we must make a cross-country journey to Newhaven, and so over to Dieppe. ... make our way at our leisure into Switzerland, via Luxembourg and Basle."}
final-problem	event_7_31	event	\N	Holmes says Moriarty will track their luggage, wait at the depot, and then they will buy carpet-bags	6	{"section": "final-problem-section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_279", "sentence_280", "sentence_281"], "communicatesContent": "Moriarty will again do what I should do. He will get on to Paris, mark down our luggage, and wait for two days at the depôt. In the meantime we shall treat ourselves to a couple of carpet-bags..."}
final-problem	event_8_1	event	\N	Holmes and Watson alight at Canterbury and wait for a train	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_282"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_8_2	event	\N	Holmes points out a rapidly approaching train on the line	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_283", "sentence_284", "sentence_285", "sentence_286", "sentence_287", "sentence_288"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes says their friend has limited intelligence and would have attacked him	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_289", "sentence_290", "sentence_291", "sentence_292", "sentence_293", "sentence_294"], "communicatesContent": "There are limits, you see, to our friend's intelligence. It would have been a coup-de-maître had he deduced what I would deduce and acted accordingly. And what would he have done had he overtaken us? There cannot be the least doubt that he would have made a murderous attack upon me. It is, however, a game at which two may play. The question now is whether we should take a premature lunch here, or run our chance of starving before we reach the buffet at Newhaven."}
final-problem	event_8_4	event	\N	Holmes and Watson travel to Brussels, stay two days, and move on to Strasburg	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_295"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_8_5	event	\N	Holmes telegraphs to the London police and receives a reply at the hotel	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_296"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_8_6	event	\N	Holmes opens the reply and throws it into the grate	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_297"], "communicatesContent": null}
final-problem	event_8_7	event	\N	Holmes exclaims that Moriarty has escaped	7	{"section": "final-problem-section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_298", "sentence_299", "sentence_300", "sentence_301", "sentence_302", "sentence_303", "sentence_304", "sentence_305", "sentence_306", "sentence_307", "sentence_308", "sentence_309", "sentence_310", "sentence_311", "sentence_312", "sentence_313", "sentence_314"], "communicatesContent": "I might have known it! He has escaped! Moriarty? They have secured the whole gang with the exception of him. He has given them the slip. Of course, when I had left the country there was no one to cope with him. But I did think that I had put the game in their hands. I think that you had better return to England, Watson. Because you will find me a dangerous companion now. This man's occupation is gone. He is lost if he returns to London. If I read his character right he will devote his whole energies to revenging himself upon me. He said as much in our short interview, and I fancy that he meant it. I should certainly recommend you to return to your practice."}
