cardboard-box	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "In choosing a few typical cases which illustrate the remarkable mental qualities of my friend, Sherlock Holmes, I have endeavoured, as far as possible, to select those which presented the minimum of sensationalism, while offering a fair field for his talents.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "It is, however, unfortunately impossible entirely to separate the sensational from the criminal, and a chronicler is left in the dilemma that he must either sacrifice details which are essential to his statement and so give a false impression of the problem, or he must use matter which chance, and not choice, has provided him with.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "With this short preface I shall turn to my notes of what proved to be a strange, though a peculiarly terrible, chain of events.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "It was a blazing hot day in August.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "Baker Street was like an oven, and the glare of the sunlight upon the yellow brickwork of the house across the road was painful to the eye.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "It was hard to believe that these were the same walls which loomed so gloomily through the fogs of winter.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "Our blinds were half-drawn, and Holmes lay curled upon the sofa, reading and re-reading a letter which he had received by the morning post.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "For myself, my term of service in India had trained me to stand heat better than cold, and a thermometer at ninety was no hardship.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "But the morning paper was uninteresting.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "Parliament had risen.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "Everybody was out of town, and I yearned for the glades of the New Forest or the shingle of Southsea.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "A depleted bank account had caused me to postpone my holiday, and as to my companion, neither the country nor the sea presented the slightest attraction to him.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "He loved to lie in the very centre of five millions of people, with his filaments stretching out and running through them, responsive to every little rumour or suspicion of unsolved crime.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "Appreciation of nature found no place among his many gifts, and his only change was when he turned his mind from the evil-doer of the town to track down his brother of the country.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "Finding that Holmes was too absorbed for conversation I had tossed aside the barren paper, and leaning back in my chair I fell into a brown study.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "Suddenly my companion's voice broke in upon my thoughts:", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "\\"You are right, Watson,\\" said he.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "\\"It does seem a most preposterous way of settling a dispute.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "\\"Most preposterous!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "I exclaimed, and then suddenly realizing how he had echoed the inmost thought of my soul, I sat up in my chair and stared at him in blank amazement.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "\\"What is this, Holmes?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "I cried.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "\\"This is beyond anything which I could have imagined.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "He laughed heartily at my perplexity.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "\\"You remember,\\" he said, \\"that some little time ago when I read you the passage in one of Poe's sketches in which a close reasoner follows the unspoken thoughts of his companion, you were inclined to treat the matter as a mere _tour-de-force_ of the author.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "On my remarking that I was constantly in the habit of doing the same thing you expressed incredulity.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "\\"Oh, no!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "\\"Perhaps not with your tongue, my dear Watson, but certainly with your eyebrows.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "So when I saw you throw down your paper and enter upon a train of thought, I was very happy to have the opportunity of reading it off, and eventually of breaking into it, as a proof that I had been in rapport with you.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "But I was still far from satisfied.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "\\"In the example which you read to me,\\" said I, \\"the reasoner drew his conclusions from the actions of the man whom he observed.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "If I remember right, he stumbled over a heap of stones, looked up at the stars, and so on.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "But I have been seated quietly in my chair, and what clues can I have given you?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_1", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "\\"You do yourself an injustice.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "The features are given to man as the means by which he shall express his emotions, and yours are faithful servants.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "\\"Do you mean to say that you read my train of thoughts from my features?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "\\"Your features and especially your eyes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "Perhaps you cannot yourself recall how your reverie commenced?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "\\"No, I cannot.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "\\"Then I will tell you.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "After throwing down your paper, which was the action which drew my attention to you, you sat for half a minute with a vacant expression.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "Then your eyes fixed themselves upon your newly framed picture of General Gordon, and I saw by the alteration in your face that a train of thought had been started.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "But it did not lead very far.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "Your eyes flashed across to the unframed portrait of Henry Ward Beecher which stands upon the top of your books.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "Then you glanced up at the wall, and of course your meaning was obvious.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "You were thinking that if the portrait were framed it would just cover that bare space and correspond with Gordon's picture over there.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "\\"You have followed me wonderfully!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "I exclaimed.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "\\"So far I could hardly have gone astray.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "But now your thoughts went back to Beecher, and you looked hard across as if you were studying the character in his features.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "Then your eyes ceased to pucker, but you continued to look across, and your face was thoughtful.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "You were recalling the incidents of Beecher's career.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "I was well aware that you could not do this without thinking of the mission which he undertook on behalf of the North at the time of the Civil War, for I remember your expressing your passionate indignation at the way in which he was received by the more turbulent of our people.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "You felt so strongly about it that I knew you could not think of Beecher without thinking of that also.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "When a moment later I saw your eyes wander away from the picture, I suspected that your mind had now turned to the Civil War, and when I observed that your lips set, your eyes sparkled, and your hands clenched I was positive that you were indeed thinking of the gallantry which was shown by both sides in that desperate struggle.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "But then, again, your face grew sadder; you shook your head.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "You were dwelling upon the sadness and horror and useless waste of life.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "Your hand stole towards your own old wound and a smile quivered on your lips, which showed me that the ridiculous side of this method of settling international questions had forced itself upon your mind.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "At this point I agreed with you that it was preposterous and was glad to find that all my deductions had been correct.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "\\"Absolutely!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "said I.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "\\"And now that you have explained it, I confess that I am as amazed as before.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "\\"It was very superficial, my dear Watson, I assure you.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "I should not have intruded it upon your attention had you not shown some incredulity the other day.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "I'll be back in a moment when I have changed my dressing-gown and filled my cigar-case.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "But I have in my hands here a little problem which may prove to be more difficult of solution than my small essay in thought reading.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "Have you observed in the paper a short paragraph referring to the remarkable contents of a packet sent through the post to Miss Cushing, of Cross Street, Croydon?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "\\"No, I saw nothing.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "\\"Ah!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "then you must have overlooked it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "Just toss it over to me.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "Here it is, under the financial column.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "Perhaps you would be good enough to read it aloud.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "I picked up the paper which he had thrown back to me and read the paragraph indicated.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "It was headed, \\"A Gruesome Packet.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_2", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "\\"Miss Susan Cushing, living at Cross Street, Croydon, has been made the victim of what must be regarded as a peculiarly revolting practical joke unless some more sinister meaning should prove to be attached to the incident.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "At two o'clock yesterday afternoon a small packet, wrapped in brown paper, was handed in by the postman.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "A cardboard box was inside, which was filled with coarse salt.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "On emptying this, Miss Cushing was horrified to find two human ears, apparently quite freshly severed.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "The box had been sent by parcel post from Belfast upon the morning before.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "There is no indication as to the sender, and the matter is the more mysterious as Miss Cushing, who is a maiden lady of fifty, has led a most retired life, and has so few acquaintances or correspondents that it is a rare event for her to receive anything through the post.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "Some years ago, however, when she resided at Penge, she let apartments in her house to three young medical students, whom she was obliged to get rid of on account of their noisy and irregular habits.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "The police are of opinion that this outrage may have been perpetrated upon Miss Cushing by these youths, who owed her a grudge and who hoped to frighten her by sending her these relics of the dissecting-rooms.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "Some probability is lent to the theory by the fact that one of these students came from the north of Ireland, and, to the best of Miss Cushing's belief, from Belfast.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "In the meantime, the matter is being actively investigated, Mr. Lestrade, one of the very smartest of our detective officers, being in charge of the case.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "\\"So much for the _Daily Chronicle_,\\" said Holmes as I finished reading.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "\\"Now for our friend Lestrade.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "I had a note from him this morning, in which he says: 'I think that this case is very much in your line.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "We have every hope of clearing the matter up, but we find a little difficulty in getting anything to work upon.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "We have, of course, wired to the Belfast post-office, but a large number of parcels were handed in upon that day, and they have no means of identifying this particular one, or of remembering the sender.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "The box is a half-pound box of honeydew tobacco and does not help us in any way.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "The medical student theory still appears to me to be the most feasible, but if you should have a few hours to spare I should be very happy to see you out here.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "' What say you, Watson?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "Can you rise superior to the heat and run down to Croydon with me on the off chance of a case for your annals?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "to Croydon with me on the off chance of a case for your annals?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "\\"I was longing for something to do.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "\\"You shall have it then.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "Ring for our boots and tell them to order a cab.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "A shower of rain fell while we were in the train, and the heat was far less oppressive in Croydon than in town.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "Holmes had sent on a wire, so that Lestrade, as wiry, as dapper, and as ferret-like as ever, was waiting for us at the station.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "A walk of five minutes took us to Cross Street, where Miss Cushing resided.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "It was a very long street of two-story brick houses, neat and prim, with whitened stone steps and little groups of aproned women gossiping at the doors.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "Halfway down, Lestrade stopped and tapped at a door, which was opened by a small servant girl.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "Miss Cushing was sitting in the front room, into which we were ushered.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "She was a placid-faced woman, with large, gentle eyes, and grizzled hair curving down over her temples on each side.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "A worked antimacassar lay upon her lap and a basket of coloured silks stood upon a stool beside her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_3", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "\\"They are in the outhouse, those dreadful things,\\" said she as Lestrade entered.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "\\"I wish that you would take them away altogether.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "\\"So I shall, Miss Cushing.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "I only kept them here until my friend, Mr. Holmes, should have seen them in your presence.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "\\"Why in my presence, sir?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "\\"In case he wished to ask any questions.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "\\"What is the use of asking me questions when I tell you I know nothing whatever about it?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "\\"Quite so, madam,\\" said Holmes in his soothing way.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "\\"I have no doubt that you have been annoyed more than enough already over this business.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "\\"Indeed, I have, sir.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "I am a quiet woman and live a retired life.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "It is something new for me to see my name in the papers and to find the police in my house.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "I won't have those things in here, Mr. Lestrade.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "If you wish to see them you must go to the outhouse.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "It was a small shed in the narrow garden which ran behind the house.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "Lestrade went in and brought out a yellow cardboard box, with a piece of brown paper and some string.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "There was a bench at the end of the path, and we all sat down while Holmes examined, one by one, the articles which Lestrade had handed to him.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "\\"The string is exceedingly interesting,\\" he remarked, holding it up to the light and sniffing at it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "\\"What do you make of this string, Lestrade?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "\\"It has been tarred.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "\\"Precisely.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "It is a piece of tarred twine.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "You have also, no doubt, remarked that Miss Cushing has cut the cord with a scissors, as can be seen by the double fray on each side.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "This is of importance.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "\\"I cannot see the importance,\\" said Lestrade.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "\\"The importance lies in the fact that the knot is left intact, and that this knot is of a peculiar character.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "\\"It is very neatly tied.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "I had already made a note to that effect,\\" said Lestrade complacently.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "\\"Have you found out anything?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "\\"So much for the string, then,\\" said Holmes, smiling, \\"now for the box wrapper.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "Brown paper, with a distinct smell of coffee.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "What, did you not observe it?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "I think there can be no doubt of it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "Address printed in rather straggling characters: 'Miss S.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "' Done with a broad-pointed pen, probably a J, and with very inferior ink.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "' The parcel was directed, then, by a man—the printing is distinctly masculine—of limited education and unacquainted with the town of Croydon.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "So far, so good!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "The box is a yellow half-pound honeydew box, with nothing distinctive save two thumb marks at the left bottom corner.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "It is filled with rough salt of the quality used for preserving hides and other of the coarser commercial purposes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "And embedded in it are these very singular enclosures.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "r preserving hides and other of the coarser commercial purposes. And embedded in it are these very singular enclosures.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "He took out the two ears as he spoke, and laying a board across his knee he examined them minutely, while Lestrade and I, bending forward on each side of him, glanced alternately at these dreadful relics and at the thoughtful, eager face of our companion.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "Finally he returned them to the box once more and sat for a while in deep meditation.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "\\"You have observed, of course,\\" said he at last, \\"that the ears are not a pair.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "\\"Yes, I have noticed that.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "But if this were the practical joke of some students from the dissecting-rooms, it would be as easy for them to send two odd ears as a pair.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "\\"Precisely.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "But this is not a practical joke.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_4", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "\\"You are sure of it?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "\\"The presumption is strongly against it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "Bodies in the dissecting-rooms are injected with preservative fluid.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "These ears bear no signs of this.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "They are fresh, too.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "They have been cut off with a blunt instrument, which would hardly happen if a student had done it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "Again, carbolic or rectified spirits would be the preservatives which would suggest themselves to the medical mind, certainly not rough salt.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "I repeat that there is no practical joke here, but that we are investigating a serious crime.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "A vague thrill ran through me as I listened to my companion's words and saw the stern gravity which had hardened his features.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "This brutal preliminary seemed to shadow forth some strange and inexplicable horror in the background.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "Lestrade, however, shook his head like a man who is only half convinced.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "\\"There are objections to the joke theory, no doubt,\\" said he, \\"but there are much stronger reasons against the other.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "We know that this woman has led a most quiet and respectable life at Penge and here for the last twenty years.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "She has hardly been away from her home for a day during that time.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "Why on earth, then, should any criminal send her the proofs of his guilt, especially as, unless she is a most consummate actress, she understands quite as little of the matter as we do?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "And now she has no word hard enough for Jim Browner.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "\\"That is the problem which we have to solve,\\" Holmes answered, \\"and for my part I shall set about it by presuming that my reasoning is correct, and that a double murder has been committed.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "One of these ears is a woman's, small, finely formed, and pierced for an earring.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "The other is a man's, sun-burned, discoloured, and also pierced for an earring.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "These two people are presumably dead, or we should have heard their story before now.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "To-day is Friday.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "The packet was posted on Thursday morning.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "The tragedy, then, occurred on Wednesday or Tuesday or earlier.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "If the two people were murdered, who but their murderer would have sent this sign of his work to Miss Cushing?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "We may take it that the sender of the packet is the man whom we want.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "But he must have some strong reason for sending Miss Cushing this packet.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "What reason then?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "It must have been to tell her that the deed was done!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "or to pain her, perhaps.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "But in that case she knows who it is.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "Does she know?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "I doubt it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "If she knew, why should she call the police in?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "She might have buried the ears, and no one would have been the wiser.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "That is what she would have done if she had wished to shield the criminal.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "But if she does not wish to shield him she would give his name.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "There is a tangle here which needs straightening out.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "He had been talking in a high, quick voice, staring blankly up over the garden fence, but now he sprang briskly to his feet and walked towards the house.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "\\"I have a few questions to ask Miss Cushing,\\" said he.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "\\"In that case I may leave you here,\\" said Lestrade, \\"for I have another small business on hand.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "I think that I have nothing further to learn from Miss Cushing.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "You will find me at the police-station.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "\\"We shall look in on our way to the train,\\" answered Holmes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "A moment later he and I were back in the front room, where the impassive lady was still quietly working away at her antimacassar.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "She put it down on her lap as we entered and looked at us with her frank, searching blue eyes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_5", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "\\"I am convinced, sir,\\" she said, \\"that this matter is a mistake, and that the parcel was never meant for me at all.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "I have said this several times to the gentleman from Scotland Yard, but he simply laughs at me.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "I have not an enemy in the world, as far as I know, so why should anyone play me such a trick?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "\\"I am coming to be of the same opinion, Miss Cushing,\\" said Holmes, taking a seat beside her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "\\"I think that it is more than probable——\\" he paused, and I was surprised, on glancing round to see that he was staring with singular intentness at the lady's profile.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "Surprise and satisfaction were both for an instant to be read upon his eager face, though when she glanced round to find out the cause of his silence he had become as demure as ever.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "He tore it open, glanced his eyes over it, and crumpled it into his pocket.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "I stared hard myself at her flat, grizzled hair, her trim cap, her little gilt earrings, her placid features; but I could see nothing which could account for my companion's evident excitement.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "\\"There were one or two questions——\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "\\"Oh, I am weary of questions!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "cried Miss Cushing impatiently.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "\\"You have two sisters, I believe.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "\\"How could you know that?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "\\"I observed the very instant that I entered the room that you have a portrait group of three ladies upon the mantelpiece, one of whom is undoubtedly yourself, while the others are so exceedingly like you that there could be no doubt of the relationship.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "\\"Yes, you are quite right.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "Those are my sisters, Sarah and Mary.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "\\"And here at my elbow is another portrait, taken at Liverpool, of your younger sister, in the company of a man who appears to be a steward by his uniform.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "I observe that she was unmarried at the time.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "\\"You are very quick at observing.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "\\"That is my trade.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "\\"Well, you are quite right.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "But she was married to Mr. Browner a few days afterwards.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "He was on the South American line when that was taken, but he was so fond of her that he couldn't abide to leave her for so long, and he got into the Liverpool and London boats.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "\\"Ah, the _Conqueror_, perhaps?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "\\"No, the _May Day_, when last I heard.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "Jim came down here to see me once.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "That was before he broke the pledge; but afterwards he would always take drink when he was ashore, and a little drink would send him stark, staring mad.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "Ah!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "it was a bad day that ever he took a glass in his hand again.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "First he dropped me, then he quarrelled with Sarah, and now that Mary has stopped writing we don't know how things are going with them.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "It was evident that Miss Cushing had come upon a subject on which she felt very deeply.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "Like most people who lead a lonely life, she was shy at first, but ended by becoming extremely communicative.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "She told us many details about her brother-in-law the steward, and then wandering off on the subject of her former lodgers, the medical students, she gave us a long account of their delinquencies, with their names and those of their hospitals.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "Holmes listened attentively to everything, throwing in a question from time to time.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "\\"About your second sister, Sarah,\\" said he.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "\\"I wonder, since you are both maiden ladies, that you do not keep house together.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "\\"Ah!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "you don't know Sarah's temper or you would wonder no more.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "I tried it when I came to Croydon, and we kept on until about two months ago, when we had to part.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "I don't want to say a word against my own sister, but she was always meddlesome and hard to please, was Sarah.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_6", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "\\"You say that she quarrelled with your Liverpool relations.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "\\"Yes, and they were the best of friends at one time.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "Why, she went up there to live in order to be near them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "The last six months that she was here she would speak of nothing but his drinking and his ways.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "He had caught her meddling, I suspect, and given her a bit of his mind, and that was the start of it.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "\\"Thank you, Miss Cushing,\\" said Holmes, rising and bowing.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "\\"Your sister Sarah lives, I think you said, at New Street Wallington?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "Good-bye, and I am very sorry that you should have been troubled over a case with which, as you say, you have nothing whatever to do.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "There was a cab passing as we came out, and Holmes hailed it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "\\"How far to Wallington?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "\\"Only about a mile, sir.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "\\"Very good.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "Jump in, Watson.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "We must strike while the iron is hot.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "Simple as the case is, there have been one or two very instructive details in connection with it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "Just pull up at a telegraph office as you pass, cabby.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "Holmes sent off a short wire and for the rest of the drive lay back in the cab, with his hat tilted over his nose to keep the sun from his face.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "Our driver pulled up at a house which was not unlike the one which we had just quitted.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "My companion ordered him to wait, and had his hand upon the knocker, when the door opened and a grave young gentleman in black, with a very shiny hat, appeared on the step.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "\\"Is Miss Cushing at home?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "asked Holmes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "\\"Miss Sarah Cushing is extremely ill,\\" said he.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "\\"She has been suffering since yesterday from brain symptoms of great severity.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "As her medical adviser, I cannot possibly take the responsibility of allowing anyone to see her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "I should recommend you to call again in ten days.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "He drew on his gloves, closed the door, and marched off down the street.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "\\"Well, if we can't we can't,\\" said Holmes, cheerfully.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "\\"Perhaps she could not or would not have told you much.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "\\"I did not wish her to tell me anything.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "I only wanted to look at her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "However, I think that I have got all that I want.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "Drive us to some decent hotel, cabby, where we may have some lunch, and afterwards we shall drop down upon friend Lestrade at the police-station.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "We had a pleasant little meal together, during which Holmes would talk about nothing but violins, narrating with great exultation how he had purchased his own Stradivarius, which was worth at least five hundred guineas, at a Jew broker's in Tottenham Court Road for fifty-five shillings.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "This led him to Paganini, and we sat for an hour over a bottle of claret while he told me anecdote after anecdote of that extraordinary man.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "The afternoon was far advanced and the hot glare had softened into a mellow glow before we found ourselves at the police-station.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "Lestrade was waiting for us at the door.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "\\"A telegram for you, Mr. Holmes,\\" said he.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "\\"Ha!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "It is the answer!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "\\"I have found out everything!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "\\"What!\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "Lestrade stared at him in amazement.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "\\"You are joking.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "\\"I was never more serious in my life.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "A shocking crime has been committed, and I think I have now laid bare every detail of it.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_7", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "\\"And the criminal?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "Holmes scribbled a few words upon the back of one of his visiting cards and threw it over to Lestrade.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "\\"That is the name,\\" he said.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "\\"You cannot effect an arrest until to-morrow night at the earliest.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "I should prefer that you do not mention my name at all in connection with the case, as I choose to be only associated with those crimes which present some difficulty in their solution.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "Come on, Watson.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "We strode off together to the station, leaving Lestrade still staring with a delighted face at the card which Holmes had thrown him.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "\\"The case,\\" said Sherlock Holmes as we chatted over our cigars that night in our rooms at Baker Street, \\"is one where, as in the investigations which you have chronicled under the names of 'A Study in Scarlet' and of 'The Sign of Four,' we have been compelled to reason backward from effects to causes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "I have written to Lestrade asking him to supply us with the details which are now wanting, and which he will only get after he has secured his man.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "That he may be safely trusted to do, for although he is absolutely devoid of reason, he is as tenacious as a bulldog when he once understands what he has to do, and, indeed, it is just this tenacity which has brought him to the top at Scotland Yard.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "\\"Your case is not complete, then?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "\\"It is fairly complete in essentials.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "We know who the author of the revolting business is, although one of the victims still escapes us.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "Of course, you have formed your own conclusions.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "\\"I presume that this Jim Browner, the steward of a Liverpool boat, is the man whom you suspect?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "\\"Oh!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "it is more than a suspicion.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "\\"And yet I cannot see anything save very vague indications.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "\\"On the contrary, to my mind nothing could be more clear.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "Let me run over the principal steps.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "We approached the case, you remember, with an absolutely blank mind, which is always an advantage.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "We had formed no theories.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "We were simply there to observe and to draw inferences from our observations.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "What did we see first?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "A very placid and respectable lady, who seemed quite innocent of any secret, and a portrait which showed me that she had two younger sisters.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "It instantly flashed across my mind that the box might have been meant for one of these.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "I set the idea aside as one which could be disproved or confirmed at our leisure.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "Then we went to the garden, as you remember, and we saw the very singular contents of the little yellow box.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "\\"The string was of the quality which is used by sailmakers aboard ship, and at once a whiff of the sea was perceptible in our investigation.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "When I observed that the knot was one which is popular with sailors, that the parcel had been posted at a port, and that the male ear was pierced for an earring which is so much more common among sailors than landsmen, I was quite certain that all the actors in the tragedy were to be found among our seafaring classes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "\\"When I came to examine the address of the packet I observed that it was to Miss S.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "Cushing.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "Now, the oldest sister would, of course, be Miss Cushing, and although her initial was 'S' it might belong to one of the others as well.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "In that case we should have to commence our investigation from a fresh basis altogether.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "I therefore went into the house with the intention of clearing up this point.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "I was about to assure Miss Cushing that I was convinced that a mistake had been made when you may remember that I came suddenly to a stop.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "The fact was that I had just seen something which filled me with surprise and at the same time narrowed the field of our inquiry immensely.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_8", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "\\"As a medical man, you are aware, Watson, that there is no part of the body which varies so much as the human ear.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "Each ear is as a rule quite distinctive and differs from all other ones.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "In last year's _Anthropological Journal_ you will find two short monographs from my pen upon the subject.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "I had, therefore, examined the ears in the box with the eyes of an expert and had carefully noted their anatomical peculiarities.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "Imagine my surprise, then, when on looking at Miss Cushing I perceived that her ear corresponded exactly with the female ear which I had just inspected.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "The matter was entirely beyond coincidence.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "There was the same shortening of the pinna, the same broad curve of the upper lobe, the same convolution of the inner cartilage.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "In all essentials it was the same ear.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "\\"Of course I at once saw the enormous importance of the observation.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "It was evident that the victim was a blood relation and probably a very close one.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "I began to talk to her about her family, and you remember that she at once gave us some exceedingly valuable details.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "\\"In the first place, her sister's name was Sarah, and her address had until recently been the same, so that it was quite obvious how the mistake had occurred and for whom the packet was meant.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "Then we heard of this steward, married to the third sister, and learned that he had at one time been so intimate with Miss Sarah that she had actually gone up to Liverpool to be near the Browners, but a quarrel had afterwards divided them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "This quarrel had put a stop to all communications for some months, so that if Browner had occasion to address a packet to Miss Sarah, he would undoubtedly have done so to her old address.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "\\"And now the matter had begun to straighten itself out wonderfully.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "We had learned of the existence of this steward, an impulsive man, of strong passions—you remember that he threw up what must have been a very superior berth in order to be nearer to his wife—subject, too, to occasional fits of hard drinking.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "We had reason to believe that his wife had been murdered, and that a man—presumably a seafaring man—had been murdered at the same time.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "Jealousy, of course, at once suggests itself as the motive for the crime.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "And why should these proofs of the deed be sent to Miss Sarah Cushing?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "Probably because during her residence in Liverpool she had some hand in bringing about the events which led to the tragedy.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "You will observe that this line of boats calls at Belfast, Dublin, and Waterford; so that, presuming that Browner had committed the deed and had embarked at once upon his steamer, the _May Day_, Belfast would be the first place at which he could post his terrible packet.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "\\"A second solution was at this stage obviously possible, and although I thought it exceedingly unlikely, I was determined to elucidate it before going further.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "An unsuccessful lover might have killed Mr. and Mrs. Browner, and the male ear might have belonged to the husband.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "There were many grave objections to this theory, but it was conceivable.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "I therefore sent off a telegram to my friend Algar, of the Liverpool force, and asked him to find out if Mrs. Browner were at home, and if Browner had departed in the _May Day_.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "Then we went on to Wallington to visit Miss Sarah.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "\\"I was curious, in the first place, to see how far the family ear had been reproduced in her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "Then, of course, she might give us very important information, but I was not sanguine that she would.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "She must have heard of the business the day before, since all Croydon was ringing with it, and she alone could have understood for whom the packet was meant.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "If she had been willing to help justice she would probably have communicated with the police already.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "However, it was clearly our duty to see her, so we went.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "We found that the news of the arrival of the packet—for her illness dated from that time—had such an effect upon her as to bring on brain fever.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "It was clearer than ever that she understood its full significance, but equally clear that we should have to wait some time for any assistance from her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_9", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "\\"However, we were really independent of her help.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "Our answers were waiting for us at the police-station, where I had directed Algar to send them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "Nothing could be more conclusive.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "Mrs. Browner's house had been closed for more than three days, and the neighbours were of opinion that she had gone south to see her relatives.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "It had been ascertained at the shipping offices that Browner had left aboard of the _May Day_, and I calculate that she is due in the Thames to-morrow night.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "When he arrives he will be met by the obtuse but resolute Lestrade, and I have no doubt that we shall have all our details filled in.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes was not disappointed in his expectations.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "Two days later he received a bulky envelope, which contained a short note from the detective, and a typewritten document, which covered several pages of foolscap.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "\\"Lestrade has got him all right,\\" said Holmes, glancing up at me.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "\\"Perhaps it would interest you to hear what he says.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": ", and boarded the S.S.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "_May Day_, belonging to the Liverpool, Dublin, and London Steam Packet Company.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "On inquiry, I found that there was a steward on board of the name of James Browner and that he had acted during the voyage in such an extraordinary manner that the captain had been compelled to relieve him of his duties.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "On descending to his berth, I found him seated upon a chest with his head sunk upon his hands, rocking himself to and fro.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "He is a big, powerful chap, clean-shaven, and very swarthy— something like Aldridge, who helped us in the bogus laundry affair.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "He jumped up when he heard my business, and I had my whistle to my lips to call a couple of river police, who were round the corner, but he seemed to have no heart in him, and he held out his hands quietly enough for the darbies.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "We brought him along to the cells, and his box as well, for we thought there might be something incriminating; but, bar a big sharp knife such as most sailors have, we got nothing for our trouble.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "However, we find that we shall want no more evidence, for on being brought before the inspector at the station he asked leave to make a statement, which was, of course, taken down, just as he made it, by our shorthand man.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "We had three copies typewritten, one of which I enclose.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "The affair proves, as I always thought it would, to be an extremely simple one, but I am obliged to you for assisting me in my investigation.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "With kind regards, yours very truly,—G.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "Lestrade.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "close. The affair proves, as I always thought it would, to be an extremely simple one, but I am obliged to you for assisting me in my investigation. With kind regards, yours very truly,—G. Lestrade.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "\\"Hum!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "The investigation really was a very simple one,\\" remarked Holmes, \\"but I don't think it struck him in that light when he first called us in.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "However, let us see what Jim Browner has to say for himself.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "This is his statement as made before Inspector Montgomery at the Shadwell Police Station, and it has the advantage of being verbatim.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "\\"Have I anything to say?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "Yes, I have a deal to say.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "I have to make a clean breast of it all.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "You can hang me, or you can leave me alone.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "I don't care a plug which you do.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "I tell you I've not shut an eye in sleep since I did it, and I don't believe I ever will again until I get past all waking.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "Sometimes it's his face, but most generally it's hers.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "I'm never without one or the other before me.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "He looks frowning and black-like, but she has a kind o' surprise upon her face.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "Ay, the white lamb, she might well be surprised when she read death on a face that had seldom looked anything but love upon her before.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_10", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "\\"But it was Sarah's fault, and may the curse of a broken man put a blight on her and set the blood rotting in her veins!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "It's not that I want to clear myself.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "I know that I went back to drink, like the beast that I was.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "But she would have forgiven me; she would have stuck as close to me as a rope to a block if that woman had never darkened our door.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "For Sarah Cushing loved me—that's the root of the business—she loved me until all her love turned to poisonous hate when she knew that I thought more of my wife's footmark in the mud than I did of her whole body and soul.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "\\"There were three sisters altogether.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "The old one was just a good woman, the second was a devil, and the third was an angel.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "Sarah was thirty-three, and Mary was twenty-nine when I married.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "We were just as happy as the day was long when we set up house together, and in all Liverpool there was no better woman than my Mary.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "And then we asked Sarah up for a week, and the week grew into a month, and one thing led to another, until she was just one of ourselves.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "\\"I was blue ribbon at that time, and we were putting a little money by, and all was as bright as a new dollar.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "My God, whoever would have thought that it could have come to this?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "Whoever would have dreamed it?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "\\"I used to be home for the week-ends very often, and sometimes if the ship were held back for cargo I would have a whole week at a time, and in this way I saw a deal of my sister-in-law, Sarah.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "She was a fine tall woman, black and quick and fierce, with a proud way of carrying her head, and a glint from her eye like a spark from a flint.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "But when little Mary was there I had never a thought of her, and that I swear as I hope for God's mercy.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "\\"It had seemed to me sometimes that she liked to be alone with me, or to coax me out for a walk with her, but I had never thought anything of that.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "But one evening my eyes were opened.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "I had come up from the ship and found my wife out, but Sarah at home.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "' I was impatient and paced up and down the room.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "' says she.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "' 'That's all right, my lass,' said I, putting out my hand towards her in a kindly way, but she had it in both hers in an instant, and they burned as if they were in a fever.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "I looked into her eyes and I read it all there.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "There was no need for her to speak, nor for me either.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "I frowned and drew my hand away.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "Then she stood by my side in silence for a bit, and then put up her hand and patted me on the shoulder.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "' said she, and with a kind o' mocking laugh, she ran out of the room.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "ned and drew my hand away. Then she stood by my side in silence for a bit, and then put up her hand and patted me on the shoulder. 'Steady old Jim!' said she, and with a kind o' mocking laugh, she ran out of the room.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "\\"Well, from that time Sarah hated me with her whole heart and soul, and she is a woman who can hate, too.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "I was a fool to let her go on biding with us—a besotted fool—but I never said a word to Mary, for I knew it would grieve her.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "Things went on much as before, but after a time I began to find that there was a bit of a change in Mary herself.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "She had always been so trusting and so innocent, but now she became queer and suspicious, wanting to know where I had been and what I had been doing, and whom my letters were from, and what I had in my pockets, and a thousand such follies.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "Day by day she grew queerer and more irritable, and we had ceaseless rows about nothing.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "I was fairly puzzled by it all.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "Sarah avoided me now, but she and Mary were just inseparable.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "I can see now how she was plotting and scheming and poisoning my wife's mind against me, but I was such a blind beetle that I could not understand it at the time.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "Then I broke my blue ribbon and began to drink again, but I think I should not have done it if Mary had been the same as ever.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "She had some reason to be disgusted with me now, and the gap between us began to be wider and wider.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "And then this Alec Fairbairn chipped in, and things became a thousand times blacker.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_11", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "\\"It was to see Sarah that he came to my house first, but soon it was to see us, for he was a man with winning ways, and he made friends wherever he went.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "He was a dashing, swaggering chap, smart and curled, who had seen half the world and could talk of what he had seen.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "He was good company, I won't deny it, and he had wonderful polite ways with him for a sailor man, so that I think there must have been a time when he knew more of the poop than the forecastle.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "For a month he was in and out of my house, and never once did it cross my mind that harm might come of his soft, tricky ways.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "And then at last something made me suspect, and from that day my peace was gone forever.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "\\"It was only a little thing, too.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "I had come into the parlour unexpected, and as I walked in at the door I saw a light of welcome on my wife's face.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "But as she saw who it was it faded again, and she turned away with a look of disappointment.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "That was enough for me.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_446	lexical	\N	\N	445	{"text": "There was no one but Alec Fairbairn whose step she could have mistaken for mine.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "If I could have seen him then I should have killed him, for I have always been like a madman when my temper gets loose.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "Mary saw the devil's light in my eyes, and she ran forward with her hands on my sleeve.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "' says she.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "' I asked.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "'In the kitchen,' says she.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "' says she.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "' She was frightened by my face, I think, for she never answered a word, and the same evening she left my house.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "not?' says she. 'Because I order it.' 'Oh!' says she, 'if my friends are not good enough for this house, then I am not good enough for it either.' 'You can do what you like,' says I, 'but if Fairbairn shows his face here again I'll send you one of his ears for a keepsake.' She was frightened by my face, I think, for she never answered a word, and the same evening she left my house.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "\\"Well, I don't know now whether it was pure devilry on the part of this woman, or whether she thought that she could turn me against my wife by encouraging her to misbehave.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "Anyway, she took a house just two streets off and let lodgings to sailors.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "Fairbairn used to stay there, and Mary would go round to have tea with her sister and him.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "How often she went I don't know, but I followed her one day, and as I broke in at the door Fairbairn got away over the back garden wall, like the cowardly skunk that he was.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "I swore to my wife that I would kill her if I found her in his company again, and I led her back with me, sobbing and trembling, and as white as a piece of paper.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "There was no trace of love between us any longer.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "I could see that she hated me and feared me, and when the thought of it drove me to drink, then she despised me as well.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "\\"Well, Sarah found that she could not make a living in Liverpool, so she went back, as I understand, to live with her sister in Croydon, and things jogged on much the same as ever at home.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "And then came this last week and all the misery and ruin.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "\\"It was in this way.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "We had gone on the _May Day_ for a round voyage of seven days, but a hogshead got loose and started one of our plates, so that we had to put back into port for twelve hours.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "I left the ship and came home, thinking what a surprise it would be for my wife, and hoping that maybe she would be glad to see me so soon.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "The thought was in my head as I turned into my own street, and at that moment a cab passed me, and there she was, sitting by the side of Fairbairn, the two chatting and laughing, with never a thought for me as I stood watching them from the footpath.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_12", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_468	lexical	\N	\N	467	{"text": "\\"I tell you, and I give you my word for it, that from that moment I was not my own master, and it is all like a dim dream when I look back on it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_469	lexical	\N	\N	468	{"text": "I had been drinking hard of late, and the two things together fairly turned my brain.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_470	lexical	\N	\N	469	{"text": "There's something throbbing in my head now, like a docker's hammer, but that morning I seemed to have all Niagara whizzing and buzzing in my ears.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_471	lexical	\N	\N	470	{"text": "\\"Well, I took to my heels, and I ran after the cab.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_472	lexical	\N	\N	471	{"text": "I had a heavy oak stick in my hand, and I tell you I saw red from the first; but as I ran I got cunning, too, and hung back a little to see them without being seen.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_473	lexical	\N	\N	472	{"text": "They pulled up soon at the railway station.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_474	lexical	\N	\N	473	{"text": "There was a good crowd round the booking-office, so I got quite close to them without being seen.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_475	lexical	\N	\N	474	{"text": "They took tickets for New Brighton.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_476	lexical	\N	\N	475	{"text": "So did I, but I got in three carriages behind them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_477	lexical	\N	\N	476	{"text": "When we reached it they walked along the Parade, and I was never more than a hundred yards from them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_478	lexical	\N	\N	477	{"text": "At last I saw them hire a boat and start for a row, for it was a very hot day, and they thought, no doubt, that it would be cooler on the water.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_479	lexical	\N	\N	478	{"text": "\\"It was just as if they had been given into my hands.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_480	lexical	\N	\N	479	{"text": "There was a bit of a haze, and you could not see more than a few hundred yards.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_481	lexical	\N	\N	480	{"text": "I hired a boat for myself, and I pulled after them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_482	lexical	\N	\N	481	{"text": "I could see the blur of their craft, but they were going nearly as fast as I, and they must have been a long mile from the shore before I caught them up.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_483	lexical	\N	\N	482	{"text": "The haze was like a curtain all round us, and there were we three in the middle of it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_484	lexical	\N	\N	483	{"text": "My God, shall I ever forget their faces when they saw who was in the boat that was closing in upon them?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_485	lexical	\N	\N	484	{"text": "She screamed out.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_486	lexical	\N	\N	485	{"text": "He swore like a madman and jabbed at me with an oar, for he must have seen death in my eyes.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_487	lexical	\N	\N	486	{"text": "I got past it and got one in with my stick that crushed his head like an egg.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_488	lexical	\N	\N	487	{"text": "' I struck again, and she lay stretched beside him.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_489	lexical	\N	\N	488	{"text": "I was like a wild beast then that had tasted blood.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_490	lexical	\N	\N	489	{"text": "If Sarah had been there, by the Lord, she should have joined them.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_491	lexical	\N	\N	490	{"text": "I pulled out my knife, and—well, there!", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_492	lexical	\N	\N	491	{"text": "I've said enough.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_493	lexical	\N	\N	492	{"text": "It gave me a kind of savage joy when I thought how Sarah would feel when she had such signs as these of what her meddling had brought about.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_494	lexical	\N	\N	493	{"text": "Then I tied the bodies into the boat, stove a plank, and stood by until they had sunk.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_495	lexical	\N	\N	494	{"text": "I knew very well that the owner would think that they had lost their bearings in the haze, and had drifted off out to sea.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_496	lexical	\N	\N	495	{"text": "I cleaned myself up, got back to land, and joined my ship without a soul having a suspicion of what had passed.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_497	lexical	\N	\N	496	{"text": "That night I made up the packet for Sarah Cushing, and next day I sent it from Belfast.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_498	lexical	\N	\N	497	{"text": "ul having a suspicion of what had passed. That night I made up the packet for Sarah Cushing, and next day I sent it from Belfast.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_499	lexical	\N	\N	498	{"text": "\\"There you have the whole truth of it.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_500	lexical	\N	\N	499	{"text": "You can hang me, or do what you like with me, but you cannot punish me as I have been punished already.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_501	lexical	\N	\N	500	{"text": "I cannot shut my eyes but I see those two faces staring at me—staring at me as they stared when my boat broke through the haze.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_502	lexical	\N	\N	501	{"text": "I killed them quick, but they are killing me slow; and if I have another night of it I shall be either mad or dead before morning.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_503	lexical	\N	\N	502	{"text": "You won't put me alone into a cell, sir?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_504	lexical	\N	\N	503	{"text": "For pity's sake don't, and may you be treated in your day of agony as you treat me now.'", "section": "cardboard-box-section_13", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_505	lexical	\N	\N	504	{"text": "\\"What is the meaning of it, Watson?\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_506	lexical	\N	\N	505	{"text": "said Holmes solemnly as he laid down the paper.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_507	lexical	\N	\N	506	{"text": "\\"What object is served by this circle of misery and violence and fear?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_508	lexical	\N	\N	507	{"text": "It must tend to some end, or else our universe is ruled by chance, which is unthinkable.", "section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_509	lexical	\N	\N	508	{"text": "But what end?", "section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "entities": []}
cardboard-box	sentence_510	lexical	\N	\N	509	{"text": "There is the great standing perennial problem to which human reason is as far from an answer as ever.\\"", "section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "entities": []}
