cardboard-box	event_14_3	event	\N	Holmes states that the circle must tend to some end or the universe is ruled by chance	13	{"section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_508"], "communicatesContent": "It must tend to some end, or else our universe is ruled by chance, which is unthinkable."}
cardboard-box	event_14_4	event	\N	Holmes asks what end it is	13	{"section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_509"], "communicatesContent": "But what end?"}
cardboard-box	event_14_5	event	\N	Holmes states that the problem remains unanswered	13	{"section": "cardboard-box-section_14", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_510"], "communicatesContent": "There is the great standing perennial problem to which human reason is as far from an answer as ever."}
