hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "Chapter 1.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "Mr. Sherlock Holmes", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "Mr. Sherlock Holmes, who was usually very late in the mornings, save upon those not infrequent occasions when he was up all night, was seated at the breakfast table.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "I stood upon the hearth-rug and picked up the stick which our visitor had left behind him the night before.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "It was a fine, thick piece of wood, bulbous-headed, of the sort which is known as a “Penang lawyer.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "Just under the head was a broad silver band nearly an inch across.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": ",” was engraved upon it, with the date “1884.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "It was just such a stick as the old-fashioned family practitioner used to carry—dignified, solid, and reassuring.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "practitioner used to carry—dignified, solid, and reassuring.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "“Well, Watson, what do you make of it?”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "Holmes was sitting with his back to me, and I had given him no sign of my occupation.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "“How did you know what I was doing?", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "I believe you have eyes in the back of your head.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "“I have, at least, a well-polished, silver-plated coffee-pot in front of me,” said he.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "“But, tell me, Watson, what do you make of our visitor’s stick?", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "Since we have been so unfortunate as to miss him and have no notion of his errand, this accidental souvenir becomes of importance.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "Let me hear you reconstruct the man by an examination of it.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "“I think,” said I, following as far as I could the methods of my companion, “that Dr. Mortimer is a successful, elderly medical man, well-esteemed since those who know him give him this mark of their appreciation.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "“Good!”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "said Holmes.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "“Excellent!”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "“I think also that the probability is in favour of his being a country practitioner who does a great deal of his visiting on foot.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "“Why so?”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "“Because this stick, though originally a very handsome one has been so knocked about that I can hardly imagine a town practitioner carrying it.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "The thick-iron ferrule is worn down, so it is evident that he has done a great amount of walking with it.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "“Perfectly sound!”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "said Holmes.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "“And then again, there is the ‘friends of the C.C.H.’", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "I should guess that to be the Something Hunt, the local hunt to whose members he has possibly given some surgical assistance, and which has made him a small presentation in return.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "“Really, Watson, you excel yourself,” said Holmes, pushing back his chair and lighting a cigarette.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "“I am bound to say that in all the accounts which you have been so good as to give of my own small achievements you have habitually underrated your own abilities.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "It may be that you are not yourself luminous, but you are a conductor of light.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "Some people without possessing genius have a remarkable power of stimulating it.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "I confess, my dear fellow, that I am very much in your debt.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "He had never said as much before, and I must admit that his words gave me keen pleasure, for I had often been piqued by his indifference to my admiration and to the attempts which I had made to give publicity to his methods.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "I was proud, too, to think that I had so far mastered his system as to apply it in a way which earned his approval.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "He now took the stick from my hands and examined it for a few minutes with his naked eyes.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "Then with an expression of interest he laid down his cigarette, and carrying the cane to the window, he looked over it again with a convex lens.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "“Interesting, though elementary,” said he as he returned to his favourite corner of the settee.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "“There are certainly one or two indications upon the stick.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "It gives us the basis for several deductions.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "“Has anything escaped me?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "I asked with some self-importance.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "“I trust that there is nothing of consequence which I have overlooked?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "“I am afraid, my dear Watson, that most of your conclusions were erroneous.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "When I said that you stimulated me I meant, to be frank, that in noting your fallacies I was occasionally guided towards the truth.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "Not that you are entirely wrong in this instance.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "The man is certainly a country practitioner.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "And he walks a good deal.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "“Then I was right.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "“To that extent.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "“But that was all.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "“No, no, my dear Watson, not all—by no means all.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "I would suggest, for example, that a presentation to a doctor is more likely to come from a hospital than from a hunt, and that when the initials ‘C.C.’", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "are placed before that hospital the words ‘Charing Cross’ very naturally suggest themselves.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "“You may be right.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "“The probability lies in that direction.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "And if we take this as a working hypothesis we have a fresh basis from which to start our construction of this unknown visitor.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "“Well, then, supposing that ‘C.C.H.’", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "does stand for ‘Charing Cross Hospital,’ what further inferences may we draw?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "“Do none suggest themselves?", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "You know my methods.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "Apply them!”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "“I can only think of the obvious conclusion that the man has practised in town before going to the country.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "“I think that we might venture a little farther than this.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "Look at it in this light.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "On what occasion would it be most probable that such a presentation would be made?", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "When would his friends unite to give him a pledge of their good will?", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "Obviously at the moment when Dr. Mortimer withdrew from the service of the hospital in order to start a practice for himself.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "We know there has been a presentation.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "We believe there has been a change from a town hospital to a country practice.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "Is it, then, stretching our inference too far to say that the presentation was on the occasion of the change?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "“It certainly seems probable.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "“Now, you will observe that he could not have been on the _staff_ of the hospital, since only a man well-established in a London practice could hold such a position, and such a one would not drift into the country.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "What was he, then?", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "If he was in the hospital and yet not on the staff he could only have been a house-surgeon or a house-physician—little more than a senior student.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "And he left five years ago—the date is on the stick.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "So your grave, middle-aged family practitioner vanishes into thin air, my dear Watson, and there emerges a young fellow under thirty, amiable, unambitious, absent-minded, and the possessor of a favourite dog, which I should describe roughly as being larger than a terrier and smaller than a mastiff.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "I laughed incredulously as Sherlock Holmes leaned back in his settee and blew little wavering rings of smoke up to the ceiling.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "“As to the latter part, I have no means of checking you,” said I, “but at least it is not difficult to find out a few particulars about the man’s age and professional career.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "From my small medical shelf I took down the Medical Directory and turned up the name.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "There were several Mortimers, but only one who could be our visitor.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "I read his record aloud.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": ", 1882, Grimpen, Dartmoor, Devon.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "House-surgeon, from 1882 to 1884, at Charing Cross Hospital.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "Winner of the Jackson prize for Comparative Pathology, with essay entitled ‘Is Disease a Reversion?’", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "Corresponding member of the Swedish Pathological Society.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "Author of ‘Some Freaks of Atavism’ (_Lancet_ 1882).", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "‘Do We Progress?’", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "(_Journal of Psychology_, March, 1883).", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "Medical Officer for the parishes of Grimpen, Thorsley, and High Barrow.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "horsley, and High Barrow.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "“No mention of that local hunt, Watson,” said Holmes with a mischievous smile, “but a country doctor, as you very astutely observed.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "I think that I am fairly justified in my inferences.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "As to the adjectives, I said, if I remember right, amiable, unambitious, and absent-minded.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "It is my experience that it is only an amiable man in this world who receives testimonials, only an unambitious one who abandons a London career for the country, and only an absent-minded one who leaves his stick and not his visiting-card after waiting an hour in your room.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "“And the dog?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "“Has been in the habit of carrying this stick behind his master.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "Being a heavy stick the dog has held it tightly by the middle, and the marks of his teeth are very plainly visible.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "The dog’s jaw, as shown in the space between these marks, is too broad in my opinion for a terrier and not broad enough for a mastiff.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "It may have been—yes, by Jove, it _is_ a curly-haired spaniel.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "He had risen and paced the room as he spoke.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "Now he halted in the recess of the window.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "There was such a ring of conviction in his voice that I glanced up in surprise.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "“My dear fellow, how can you possibly be so sure of that?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "“For the very simple reason that I see the dog himself on our very door-step, and there is the ring of its owner.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "Don’t move, I beg you, Watson.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "He is a professional brother of yours, and your presence may be of assistance to me.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "Now is the dramatic moment of fate, Watson, when you hear a step upon the stair which is walking into your life, and you know not whether for good or ill.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "What does Dr. James Mortimer, the man of science, ask of Sherlock Holmes, the specialist in crime?", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "Come in!”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "The appearance of our visitor was a surprise to me, since I had expected a typical country practitioner.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "He was a very tall, thin man, with a long nose like a beak, which jutted out between two keen, grey eyes, set closely together and sparkling brightly from behind a pair of gold-rimmed glasses.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "He was clad in a professional but rather slovenly fashion, for his frock-coat was dingy and his trousers frayed.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "Though young, his long back was already bowed, and he walked with a forward thrust of his head and a general air of peering benevolence.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "As he entered his eyes fell upon the stick in Holmes’s hand, and he ran towards it with an exclamation of joy.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "“I am so very glad,” said he.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "“I was not sure whether I had left it here or in the Shipping Office.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "I would not lose that stick for the world.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "“A presentation, I see,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_135	lexical	\N	\N	134	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "“From Charing Cross Hospital?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "“From one or two friends there on the occasion of my marriage.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "“Dear, dear, that’s bad!”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "said Holmes, shaking his head.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer blinked through his glasses in mild astonishment.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "“Why was it bad?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "“Only that you have disarranged our little deductions.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "Your marriage, you say?”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "“Yes, sir.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "I married, and so left the hospital, and with it all hopes of a consulting practice.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "It was necessary to make a home of my own.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "“Come, come, we are not so far wrong, after all,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "“And now, Dr. James Mortimer—”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "“Mister, sir, Mister—a humble M.R.C.S.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "“And a man of precise mind, evidently.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "“A dabbler in science, Mr. Holmes, a picker up of shells on the shores of the great unknown ocean.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "I presume that it is Mr. Sherlock Holmes whom I am addressing and not—”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "“No, this is my friend Dr. Watson.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "“Glad to meet you, sir.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "I have heard your name mentioned in connection with that of your friend.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "You interest me very much, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "I had hardly expected so dolichocephalic a skull or such well-marked supra-orbital development.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "Would you have any objection to my running my finger along your parietal fissure?", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "A cast of your skull, sir, until the original is available, would be an ornament to any anthropological museum.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "It is not my intention to be fulsome, but I confess that I covet your skull.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes waved our strange visitor into a chair.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "“You are an enthusiast in your line of thought, I perceive, sir, as I am in mine,” said he.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "“I observe from your forefinger that you make your own cigarettes.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "Have no hesitation in lighting one.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "The man drew out paper and tobacco and twirled the one up in the other with surprising dexterity.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "He had long, quivering fingers as agile and restless as the antennæ of an insect.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "Holmes was silent, but his little darting glances showed me the interest which he took in our curious companion.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "“I presume, sir,” said he at last, “that it was not merely for the purpose of examining my skull that you have done me the honour to call here last night and again today?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "“No, sir, no; though I am happy to have had the opportunity of doing that as well.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "I came to you, Mr. Holmes, because I recognized that I am myself an unpractical man and because I am suddenly confronted with a most serious and extraordinary problem.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "Recognizing, as I do, that you are the second highest expert in Europe—”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_172	lexical	\N	\N	171	{"text": "“Indeed, sir!", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_173	lexical	\N	\N	172	{"text": "May I inquire who has the honour to be the first?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "asked Holmes with some asperity.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "“To the man of precisely scientific mind the work of Monsieur Bertillon must always appeal strongly.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "“Then had you not better consult him?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "“I said, sir, to the precisely scientific mind.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "But as a practical man of affairs it is acknowledged that you stand alone.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "I trust, sir, that I have not inadvertently—”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "“Just a little,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "“I think, Dr. Mortimer, you would do wisely if without more ado you would kindly tell me plainly what the exact nature of the problem is in which you demand my assistance.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "Chapter 2.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "The Curse of the Baskervilles", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "“I have in my pocket a manuscript,” said Dr. James Mortimer.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "“I observed it as you entered the room,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "“It is an old manuscript.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "“Early eighteenth century, unless it is a forgery.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "“How can you say that, sir?”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "“You have presented an inch or two of it to my examination all the time that you have been talking.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "It would be a poor expert who could not give the date of a document within a decade or so.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "You may possibly have read my little monograph upon the subject.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "I put that at 1730.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "“The exact date is 1742.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer drew it from his breast-pocket.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "“This family paper was committed to my care by Sir Charles Baskerville, whose sudden and tragic death some three months ago created so much excitement in Devonshire.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "I may say that I was his personal friend as well as his medical attendant.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "He was a strong-minded man, sir, shrewd, practical, and as unimaginative as I am myself.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "Yet he took this document very seriously, and his mind was prepared for just such an end as did eventually overtake him.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "Holmes stretched out his hand for the manuscript and flattened it upon his knee.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "“You will observe, Watson, the alternative use of the long _s_ and the short.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "It is one of several indications which enabled me to fix the date.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "I looked over his shoulder at the yellow paper and the faded script.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "At the head was written: “Baskerville Hall,” and below in large, scrawling figures: “1742.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "“It appears to be a statement of some sort.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "“Yes, it is a statement of a certain legend which runs in the Baskerville family.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "“But I understand that it is something more modern and practical upon which you wish to consult me?”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "“Most modern.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "A most practical, pressing matter, which must be decided within twenty-four hours.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "But the manuscript is short and is intimately connected with the affair.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "With your permission I will read it to you.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "Holmes leaned back in his chair, placed his finger-tips together, and closed his eyes, with an air of resignation.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer turned the manuscript to the light and read in a high, cracking voice the following curious, old-world narrative:", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "“Of the origin of the Hound of the Baskervilles there have been many statements, yet as I come in a direct line from Hugo Baskerville, and as I had the story from my father, who also had it from his, I have set it down with all belief that it occurred even as is here set forth.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "And I would have you believe, my sons, that the same Justice which punishes sin may also most graciously forgive it, and that no ban is so heavy but that by prayer and repentance it may be removed.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "Learn then from this story not to fear the fruits of the past, but rather to be circumspect in the future, that those foul passions whereby our family has suffered so grievously may not again be loosed to our undoing.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "“Know then that in the time of the Great Rebellion (the history of which by the learned Lord Clarendon I most earnestly commend to your attention) this Manor of Baskerville was held by Hugo of that name, nor can it be gainsaid that he was a most wild, profane, and godless man.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "This, in truth, his neighbours might have pardoned, seeing that saints have never flourished in those parts, but there was in him a certain wanton and cruel humour which made his name a by-word through the West.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "“You say it was large?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "It chanced that this Hugo came to love (if, indeed, so dark a passion may be known under so bright a name) the daughter of a yeoman who held lands near the Baskerville estate.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "But the young maiden, being discreet and of good repute, would ever avoid him, for she feared his evil name.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "So it came to pass that one Michaelmas this Hugo, with five or six of his idle and wicked companions, stole down upon the farm and carried off the maiden, her father and brothers being from home, as he well knew.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "When they had brought her to the Hall the maiden was placed in an upper chamber, while Hugo and his friends sat down to a long carouse, as was their nightly custom.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "Now, the poor lass upstairs was like to have her wits turned at the singing and shouting and terrible oaths which came up to her from below, for they say that the words used by Hugo Baskerville, when he was in wine, were such as might blast the man who said them.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "At last in the stress of her fear she did that which might have daunted the bravest or most active man, for by the aid of the growth of ivy which covered (and still covers) the south wall she came down from under the eaves, and so homeward across the moor, there being three leagues betwixt the Hall and her father’s farm.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "“It chanced that some little time later Hugo left his guests to carry food and drink—with other worse things, perchance—to his captive, and so found the cage empty and the bird escaped.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "Then, as it would seem, he became as one that hath a devil, for, rushing down the stairs into the dining-hall, he sprang upon the great table, flagons and trenchers flying before him, and he cried aloud before all the company that he would that very night render his body and soul to the Powers of Evil if he might but overtake the wench.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "And while the revellers stood aghast at the fury of the man, one more wicked or, it may be, more drunken than the rest, cried out that they should put the hounds upon her.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "Whereat Hugo ran from the house, crying to his grooms that they should saddle his mare and unkennel the pack, and giving the hounds a kerchief of the maid’s, he swung them to the line, and so off full cry in the moonlight over the moor.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "“Now, for some space the revellers stood agape, unable to understand all that had been done in such haste.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "But anon their bemused wits awoke to the nature of the deed which was like to be done upon the moorlands.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "Everything was now in an uproar, some calling for their pistols, some for their horses, and some for another flask of wine.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "But at length some sense came back to their crazed minds, and the whole of them, thirteen in number, took horse and started in pursuit.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "The moon shone clear above them, and they rode swiftly abreast, taking that course which the maid must needs have taken if she were to reach her own home.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "“They had gone a mile or two when they passed one of the night shepherds upon the moorlands, and they cried to him to know if he had seen the hunt.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "And the man, as the story goes, was so crazed with fear that he could scarce speak, but at last he said that he had indeed seen the unhappy maiden, with the hounds upon her track.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "‘But I have seen more than that,’ said he, ‘for Hugo Baskerville passed me upon his black mare, and there ran mute behind him such a hound of hell as God forbid should ever be at my heels.’", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "So the drunken squires cursed the shepherd and rode onward.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "But soon their skins turned cold, for there came a galloping across the moor, and the black mare, dabbled with white froth, went past with trailing bridle and empty saddle.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "Then the revellers rode close together, for a great fear was on them, but they still followed over the moor, though each, had he been alone, would have been right glad to have turned his horse’s head.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "Riding slowly in this fashion they came at last upon the hounds.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "These, though known for their valour and their breed, were whimpering in a cluster at the head of a deep dip or goyal, as we call it, upon the moor, some slinking away and some, with starting hackles and staring eyes, gazing down the narrow valley before them.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "“The company had come to a halt, more sober men, as you may guess, than when they started.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "The most of them would by no means advance, but three of them, the boldest, or it may be the most drunken, rode forward down the goyal.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "“Enormous.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "Now, it opened into a broad space in which stood two of those great stones, still to be seen there, which were set by certain forgotten peoples in the days of old.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "The moon was shining bright upon the clearing, and there in the centre lay the unhappy maid where she had fallen, dead of fear and of fatigue.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "But it was not the sight of her body, nor yet was it that of the body of Hugo Baskerville lying near her, which raised the hair upon the heads of these three dare-devil roysterers, but it was that, standing over Hugo, and plucking at his throat, there stood a foul thing, a great, black beast, shaped like a hound, yet larger than any hound that ever mortal eye has rested upon.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "And even as they looked the thing tore the throat out of Hugo Baskerville, on which, as it turned its blazing eyes and dripping jaws upon them, the three shrieked with fear and rode for dear life, still screaming, across the moor.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "One, it is said, died that very night of what he had seen, and the other twain were but broken men for the rest of their days.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "“Such is the tale, my sons, of the coming of the hound which is said to have plagued the family so sorely ever since.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "If I have set it down it is because that which is clearly known hath less terror than that which is but hinted at and guessed.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "Nor can it be denied that many of the family have been unhappy in their deaths, which have been sudden, bloody, and mysterious.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "Yet may we shelter ourselves in the infinite goodness of Providence, which would not forever punish the innocent beyond that third or fourth generation which is threatened in Holy Writ.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "To that Providence, my sons, I hereby commend you, and I counsel you by way of caution to forbear from crossing the moor in those dark hours when the powers of evil are exalted.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "“[This from Hugo Baskerville to his sons Rodger and John, with instructions that they say nothing thereof to their sister Elizabeth.]”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "When Dr. Mortimer had finished reading this singular narrative he pushed his spectacles up on his forehead and stared across at Mr. Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "The latter yawned and tossed the end of his cigarette into the fire.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "“Well?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "“Do you not find it interesting?”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "“To a collector of fairy tales.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer drew a folded newspaper out of his pocket.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "“Now, Mr. Holmes, we will give you something a little more recent.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "This is the _Devon County Chronicle_ of May 14th of this year.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "It is a short account of the facts elicited at the death of Sir Charles Baskerville which occurred a few days before that date.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "My friend leaned a little forward and his expression became intent.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "Our visitor readjusted his glasses and began:", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "“The recent sudden death of Sir Charles Baskerville, whose name has been mentioned as the probable Liberal candidate for Mid-Devon at the next election, has cast a gloom over the county.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "Though Sir Charles had resided at Baskerville Hall for a comparatively short period his amiability of character and extreme generosity had won the affection and respect of all who had been brought into contact with him.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "In these days of _nouveaux riches_ it is refreshing to find a case where the scion of an old county family which has fallen upon evil days is able to make his own fortune and to bring it back with him to restore the fallen grandeur of his line.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "Sir Charles, as is well known, made large sums of money in South African speculation.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "More wise than those who go on until the wheel turns against them, he realised his gains and returned to England with them.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "It is only two years since he took up his residence at Baskerville Hall, and it is common talk how large were those schemes of reconstruction and improvement which have been interrupted by his death.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "“But it had not approached the body?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "Being himself childless, it was his openly expressed desire that the whole countryside should, within his own lifetime, profit by his good fortune, and many will have personal reasons for bewailing his untimely end.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "His generous donations to local and county charities have been frequently chronicled in these columns.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "“The circumstances connected with the death of Sir Charles cannot be said to have been entirely cleared up by the inquest, but at least enough has been done to dispose of those rumours to which local superstition has given rise.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "There is no reason whatever to suspect foul play, or to imagine that death could be from any but natural causes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "Sir Charles was a widower, and a man who may be said to have been in some ways of an eccentric habit of mind.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "In spite of his considerable wealth he was simple in his personal tastes, and his indoor servants at Baskerville Hall consisted of a married couple named Barrymore, the husband acting as butler and the wife as housekeeper.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "Their evidence, corroborated by that of several friends, tends to show that Sir Charles’s health has for some time been impaired, and points especially to some affection of the heart, manifesting itself in changes of colour, breathlessness, and acute attacks of nervous depression.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "Dr. James Mortimer, the friend and medical attendant of the deceased, has given evidence to the same effect.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "“The facts of the case are simple.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "Sir Charles Baskerville was in the habit every night before going to bed of walking down the famous yew alley of Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "The evidence of the Barrymores shows that this had been his custom.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "On the fourth of May Sir Charles had declared his intention of starting next day for London, and had ordered Barrymore to prepare his luggage.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "That night he went out as usual for his nocturnal walk, in the course of which he was in the habit of smoking a cigar.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "He never returned.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "At twelve o’clock Barrymore, finding the hall door still open, became alarmed, and, lighting a lantern, went in search of his master.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "The day had been wet, and Sir Charles’s footmarks were easily traced down the alley.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "Halfway down this walk there is a gate which leads out on to the moor.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "There were indications that Sir Charles had stood for some little time here.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "He then proceeded down the alley, and it was at the far end of it that his body was discovered.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "One fact which has not been explained is the statement of Barrymore that his master’s footprints altered their character from the time that he passed the moor-gate, and that he appeared from thence onward to have been walking upon his toes.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "One Murphy, a gipsy horse-dealer, was on the moor at no great distance at the time, but he appears by his own confession to have been the worse for drink.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "He declares that he heard cries but is unable to state from what direction they came.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "No signs of violence were to be discovered upon Sir Charles’s person, and though the doctor’s evidence pointed to an almost incredible facial distortion—so great that Dr. Mortimer refused at first to believe that it was indeed his friend and patient who lay before him—it was explained that that is a symptom which is not unusual in cases of dyspnœa and death from cardiac exhaustion.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "This explanation was borne out by the post-mortem examination, which showed long-standing organic disease, and the coroner’s jury returned a verdict in accordance with the medical evidence.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "It is well that this is so, for it is obviously of the utmost importance that Sir Charles’s heir should settle at the Hall and continue the good work which has been so sadly interrupted.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "Had the prosaic finding of the coroner not finally put an end to the romantic stories which have been whispered in connection with the affair, it might have been difficult to find a tenant for Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "It is understood that the next of kin is Mr. Henry Baskerville, if he be still alive, the son of Sir Charles Baskerville’s younger brother.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "The young man when last heard of was in America, and inquiries are being instituted with a view to informing him of his good fortune.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer refolded his paper and replaced it in his pocket.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "“Those are the public facts, Mr. Holmes, in connection with the death of Sir Charles Baskerville.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "“I must thank you,” said Sherlock Holmes, “for calling my attention to a case which certainly presents some features of interest.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "I had observed some newspaper comment at the time, but I was exceedingly preoccupied by that little affair of the Vatican cameos, and in my anxiety to oblige the Pope I lost touch with several interesting English cases.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "This article, you say, contains all the public facts?”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "“It does.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "“Then let me have the private ones.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "He leaned back, put his finger-tips together, and assumed his most impassive and judicial expression.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "“In doing so,” said Dr. Mortimer, who had begun to show signs of some strong emotion, “I am telling that which I have not confided to anyone.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "My motive for withholding it from the coroner’s inquiry is that a man of science shrinks from placing himself in the public position of seeming to indorse a popular superstition.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "I had the further motive that Baskerville Hall, as the paper says, would certainly remain untenanted if anything were done to increase its already rather grim reputation.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "For both these reasons I thought that I was justified in telling rather less than I knew, since no practical good could result from it, but with you there is no reason why I should not be perfectly frank.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "“The moor is very sparsely inhabited, and those who live near each other are thrown very much together.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "For this reason I saw a good deal of Sir Charles Baskerville.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "With the exception of Mr. Frankland, of Lafter Hall, and Mr. Stapleton, the naturalist, there are no other men of education within many miles.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "Sir Charles was a retiring man, but the chance of his illness brought us together, and a community of interests in science kept us so.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "He had brought back much scientific information from South Africa, and many a charming evening we have spent together discussing the comparative anatomy of the Bushman and the Hottentot.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "“Within the last few months it became increasingly plain to me that Sir Charles’s nervous system was strained to the breaking point.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "He had taken this legend which I have read you exceedingly to heart—so much so that, although he would walk in his own grounds, nothing would induce him to go out upon the moor at night.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "Incredible as it may appear to you, Mr. Holmes, he was honestly convinced that a dreadful fate overhung his family, and certainly the records which he was able to give of his ancestors were not encouraging.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "The idea of some ghastly presence constantly haunted him, and on more than one occasion he has asked me whether I had on my medical journeys at night ever seen any strange creature or heard the baying of a hound.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "The latter question he put to me several times, and always with a voice which vibrated with excitement.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "“I can well remember driving up to his house in the evening some three weeks before the fatal event.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "He chanced to be at his hall door.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "I had descended from my gig and was standing in front of him, when I saw his eyes fix themselves over my shoulder and stare past me with an expression of the most dreadful horror.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "I whisked round and had just time to catch a glimpse of something which I took to be a large black calf passing at the head of the drive.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "So excited and alarmed was he that I was compelled to go down to the spot where the animal had been and look around for it.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "It was gone, however, and the incident appeared to make the worst impression upon his mind.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "I stayed with him all the evening, and it was on that occasion, to explain the emotion which he had shown, that he confided to my keeping that narrative which I read to you when first I came.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "I mention this small episode because it assumes some importance in view of the tragedy which followed, but I was convinced at the time that the matter was entirely trivial and that his excitement had no justification.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "“It was at my advice that Sir Charles was about to go to London.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "His heart was, I knew, affected, and the constant anxiety in which he lived, however chimerical the cause of it might be, was evidently having a serious effect upon his health.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "I thought that a few months among the distractions of town would send him back a new man.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "Mr. Stapleton, a mutual friend who was much concerned at his state of health, was of the same opinion.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "At the last instant came this terrible catastrophe.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "“On the night of Sir Charles’s death Barrymore the butler, who made the discovery, sent Perkins the groom on horseback to me, and as I was sitting up late I was able to reach Baskerville Hall within an hour of the event.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "I checked and corroborated all the facts which were mentioned at the inquest.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "I followed the footsteps down the yew alley, I saw the spot at the moor-gate where he seemed to have waited, I remarked the change in the shape of the prints after that point, I noted that there were no other footsteps save those of Barrymore on the soft gravel, and finally I carefully examined the body, which had not been touched until my arrival.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "Sir Charles lay on his face, his arms out, his fingers dug into the ground, and his features convulsed with some strong emotion to such an extent that I could hardly have sworn to his identity.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "There was certainly no physical injury of any kind.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "But one false statement was made by Barrymore at the inquest.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "He said that there were no traces upon the ground round the body.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "He did not observe any.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "But I did—some little distance off, but fresh and clear.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "“Footprints?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "“Footprints.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "“A man’s or a woman’s?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer looked strangely at us for an instant, and his voice sank almost to a whisper as he answered.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "“Mr. Holmes, they were the footprints of a gigantic hound!”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "Chapter 3.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "The Problem", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "I confess at these words a shudder passed through me.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "There was a thrill in the doctor’s voice which showed that he was himself deeply moved by that which he told us.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "Holmes leaned forward in his excitement and his eyes had the hard, dry glitter which shot from them when he was keenly interested.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "“You saw this?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "“As clearly as I see you.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "“And you said nothing?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "“What was the use?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "“How was it that no one else saw it?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "“The marks were some twenty yards from the body and no one gave them a thought.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "I don’t suppose I should have done so had I not known this legend.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "“There are many sheep-dogs on the moor?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "“No doubt, but this was no sheep-dog.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "“What sort of night was it?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "“Damp and raw.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "“But not actually raining?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "“What is the alley like?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "“There are two lines of old yew hedge, twelve feet high and impenetrable.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "The walk in the centre is about eight feet across.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "“Is there anything between the hedges and the walk?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "“Yes, there is a strip of grass about six feet broad on either side.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "“I understand that the yew hedge is penetrated at one point by a gate?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "“Yes, the wicket-gate which leads on to the moor.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "“Is there any other opening?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "“None.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "“So that to reach the yew alley one either has to come down it from the house or else to enter it by the moor-gate?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "“There is an exit through a summer-house at the far end.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "“Had Sir Charles reached this?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "“No; he lay about fifty yards from it.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "“Now, tell me, Dr. Mortimer—and this is important—the marks which you saw were on the path and not on the grass?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "“No marks could show on the grass.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "“Were they on the same side of the path as the moor-gate?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "“Yes; they were on the edge of the path on the same side as the moor-gate.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "“You interest me exceedingly.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "Another point.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "Was the wicket-gate closed?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "“Closed and padlocked.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "“How high was it?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "“About four feet high.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "“Then anyone could have got over it?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "“And what marks did you see by the wicket-gate?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "“None in particular.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "“Good heaven!", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "Did no one examine?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "“Yes, I examined, myself.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "“And found nothing?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "“It was all very confused.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_403	lexical	\N	\N	402	{"text": "Sir Charles had evidently stood there for five or ten minutes.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_404	lexical	\N	\N	403	{"text": "“How do you know that?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_405	lexical	\N	\N	404	{"text": "“Because the ash had twice dropped from his cigar.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_406	lexical	\N	\N	405	{"text": "“Excellent!", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_407	lexical	\N	\N	406	{"text": "This is a colleague, Watson, after our own heart.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_408	lexical	\N	\N	407	{"text": "But the marks?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_409	lexical	\N	\N	408	{"text": "“He had left his own marks all over that small patch of gravel.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_410	lexical	\N	\N	409	{"text": "I could discern no others.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_411	lexical	\N	\N	410	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes struck his hand against his knee with an impatient gesture.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_412	lexical	\N	\N	411	{"text": "“If I had only been there!”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_413	lexical	\N	\N	412	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_414	lexical	\N	\N	413	{"text": "“It is evidently a case of extraordinary interest, and one which presented immense opportunities to the scientific expert.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_415	lexical	\N	\N	414	{"text": "That gravel page upon which I might have read so much has been long ere this smudged by the rain and defaced by the clogs of curious peasants.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_416	lexical	\N	\N	415	{"text": "Oh, Dr. Mortimer, Dr. Mortimer, to think that you should not have called me in!", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_417	lexical	\N	\N	416	{"text": "You have indeed much to answer for.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_418	lexical	\N	\N	417	{"text": "“I could not call you in, Mr. Holmes, without disclosing these facts to the world, and I have already given my reasons for not wishing to do so.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_419	lexical	\N	\N	418	{"text": "Besides, besides—”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_420	lexical	\N	\N	419	{"text": "“Why do you hesitate?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_421	lexical	\N	\N	420	{"text": "“There is a realm in which the most acute and most experienced of detectives is helpless.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_422	lexical	\N	\N	421	{"text": "“You mean that the thing is supernatural?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_423	lexical	\N	\N	422	{"text": "“I did not positively say so.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_424	lexical	\N	\N	423	{"text": "“No, but you evidently think it.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_425	lexical	\N	\N	424	{"text": "“Since the tragedy, Mr. Holmes, there have come to my ears several incidents which are hard to reconcile with the settled order of Nature.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_426	lexical	\N	\N	425	{"text": "“For example?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_427	lexical	\N	\N	426	{"text": "“I find that before the terrible event occurred several people had seen a creature upon the moor which corresponds with this Baskerville demon, and which could not possibly be any animal known to science.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_428	lexical	\N	\N	427	{"text": "They all agreed that it was a huge creature, luminous, ghastly, and spectral.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_429	lexical	\N	\N	428	{"text": "I have cross-examined these men, one of them a hard-headed countryman, one a farrier, and one a moorland farmer, who all tell the same story of this dreadful apparition, exactly corresponding to the hell-hound of the legend.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_430	lexical	\N	\N	429	{"text": "I assure you that there is a reign of terror in the district, and that it is a hardy man who will cross the moor at night.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_431	lexical	\N	\N	430	{"text": "“And you, a trained man of science, believe it to be supernatural?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_432	lexical	\N	\N	431	{"text": "“I do not know what to believe.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_433	lexical	\N	\N	432	{"text": "Holmes shrugged his shoulders.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_434	lexical	\N	\N	433	{"text": "“I have hitherto confined my investigations to this world,” said he.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_435	lexical	\N	\N	434	{"text": "“In a modest way I have combated evil, but to take on the Father of Evil himself would, perhaps, be too ambitious a task.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_436	lexical	\N	\N	435	{"text": "Yet you must admit that the footmark is material.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_437	lexical	\N	\N	436	{"text": "“The original hound was material enough to tug a man’s throat out, and yet he was diabolical as well.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_438	lexical	\N	\N	437	{"text": "“I see that you have quite gone over to the supernaturalists.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_439	lexical	\N	\N	438	{"text": "But now, Dr. Mortimer, tell me this.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_440	lexical	\N	\N	439	{"text": "If you hold these views, why have you come to consult me at all?", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_441	lexical	\N	\N	440	{"text": "You tell me in the same breath that it is useless to investigate Sir Charles’s death, and that you desire me to do it.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_442	lexical	\N	\N	441	{"text": "“I did not say that I desired you to do it.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_443	lexical	\N	\N	442	{"text": "“Then, how can I assist you?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_444	lexical	\N	\N	443	{"text": "“By advising me as to what I should do with Sir Henry Baskerville, who arrives at Waterloo Station”—Dr. Mortimer looked at his watch—“in exactly one hour and a quarter.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_445	lexical	\N	\N	444	{"text": "“He being the heir?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_447	lexical	\N	\N	446	{"text": "On the death of Sir Charles we inquired for this young gentleman and found that he had been farming in Canada.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_448	lexical	\N	\N	447	{"text": "From the accounts which have reached us he is an excellent fellow in every way.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_449	lexical	\N	\N	448	{"text": "I speak now not as a medical man but as a trustee and executor of Sir Charles’s will.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_450	lexical	\N	\N	449	{"text": "“There is no other claimant, I presume?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_451	lexical	\N	\N	450	{"text": "“None.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_452	lexical	\N	\N	451	{"text": "The only other kinsman whom we have been able to trace was Rodger Baskerville, the youngest of three brothers of whom poor Sir Charles was the elder.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_453	lexical	\N	\N	452	{"text": "The second brother, who died young, is the father of this lad Henry.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_454	lexical	\N	\N	453	{"text": "The third, Rodger, was the black sheep of the family.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_455	lexical	\N	\N	454	{"text": "He came of the old masterful Baskerville strain and was the very image, they tell me, of the family picture of old Hugo.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_456	lexical	\N	\N	455	{"text": "He made England too hot to hold him, fled to Central America, and died there in 1876 of yellow fever.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_457	lexical	\N	\N	456	{"text": "Henry is the last of the Baskervilles.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_458	lexical	\N	\N	457	{"text": "In one hour and five minutes I meet him at Waterloo Station.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_459	lexical	\N	\N	458	{"text": "I have had a wire that he arrived at Southampton this morning.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_460	lexical	\N	\N	459	{"text": "Now, Mr. Holmes, what would you advise me to do with him?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_461	lexical	\N	\N	460	{"text": "“Why should he not go to the home of his fathers?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_462	lexical	\N	\N	461	{"text": "“It seems natural, does it not?", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_463	lexical	\N	\N	462	{"text": "And yet, consider that every Baskerville who goes there meets with an evil fate.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_464	lexical	\N	\N	463	{"text": "I feel sure that if Sir Charles could have spoken with me before his death he would have warned me against bringing this, the last of the old race, and the heir to great wealth, to that deadly place.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_465	lexical	\N	\N	464	{"text": "And yet it cannot be denied that the prosperity of the whole poor, bleak countryside depends upon his presence.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_466	lexical	\N	\N	465	{"text": "All the good work which has been done by Sir Charles will crash to the ground if there is no tenant of the Hall.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_467	lexical	\N	\N	466	{"text": "I fear lest I should be swayed too much by my own obvious interest in the matter, and that is why I bring the case before you and ask for your advice.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_468	lexical	\N	\N	467	{"text": "Holmes considered for a little time.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_469	lexical	\N	\N	468	{"text": "“Put into plain words, the matter is this,” said he.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_470	lexical	\N	\N	469	{"text": "“In your opinion there is a diabolical agency which makes Dartmoor an unsafe abode for a Baskerville—that is your opinion?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_471	lexical	\N	\N	470	{"text": "“At least I might go the length of saying that there is some evidence that this may be so.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_472	lexical	\N	\N	471	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_473	lexical	\N	\N	472	{"text": "But surely, if your supernatural theory be correct, it could work the young man evil in London as easily as in Devonshire.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_474	lexical	\N	\N	473	{"text": "A devil with merely local powers like a parish vestry would be too inconceivable a thing.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_475	lexical	\N	\N	474	{"text": "“You put the matter more flippantly, Mr. Holmes, than you would probably do if you were brought into personal contact with these things.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_476	lexical	\N	\N	475	{"text": "Your advice, then, as I understand it, is that the young man will be as safe in Devonshire as in London.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_477	lexical	\N	\N	476	{"text": "He comes in fifty minutes.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_478	lexical	\N	\N	477	{"text": "What would you recommend?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_479	lexical	\N	\N	478	{"text": "“I recommend, sir, that you take a cab, call off your spaniel who is scratching at my front door, and proceed to Waterloo to meet Sir Henry Baskerville.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_480	lexical	\N	\N	479	{"text": "“And then?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_481	lexical	\N	\N	480	{"text": "“And then you will say nothing to him at all until I have made up my mind about the matter.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_482	lexical	\N	\N	481	{"text": "“How long will it take you to make up your mind?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_483	lexical	\N	\N	482	{"text": "“Twenty-four hours.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_484	lexical	\N	\N	483	{"text": "At ten o’clock tomorrow, Dr. Mortimer, I will be much obliged to you if you will call upon me here, and it will be of help to me in my plans for the future if you will bring Sir Henry Baskerville with you.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_485	lexical	\N	\N	484	{"text": "“I will do so, Mr. Holmes.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_486	lexical	\N	\N	485	{"text": "He scribbled the appointment on his shirt-cuff and hurried off in his strange, peering, absent-minded fashion.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_487	lexical	\N	\N	486	{"text": "Holmes stopped him at the head of the stair.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_488	lexical	\N	\N	487	{"text": "“Only one more question, Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_489	lexical	\N	\N	488	{"text": "You say that before Sir Charles Baskerville’s death several people saw this apparition upon the moor?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_490	lexical	\N	\N	489	{"text": "“Three people did.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_491	lexical	\N	\N	490	{"text": "“Did any see it after?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_492	lexical	\N	\N	491	{"text": "“I have not heard of any.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_493	lexical	\N	\N	492	{"text": "“Thank you.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_494	lexical	\N	\N	493	{"text": "Good-morning.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_495	lexical	\N	\N	494	{"text": "Holmes returned to his seat with that quiet look of inward satisfaction which meant that he had a congenial task before him.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_496	lexical	\N	\N	495	{"text": "“Going out, Watson?”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_497	lexical	\N	\N	496	{"text": "“Unless I can help you.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_498	lexical	\N	\N	497	{"text": "“No, my dear fellow, it is at the hour of action that I turn to you for aid.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_499	lexical	\N	\N	498	{"text": "But this is splendid, really unique from some points of view.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_500	lexical	\N	\N	499	{"text": "When you pass Bradley’s, would you ask him to send up a pound of the strongest shag tobacco?", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_501	lexical	\N	\N	500	{"text": "Thank you.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_502	lexical	\N	\N	501	{"text": "It would be as well if you could make it convenient not to return before evening.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_503	lexical	\N	\N	502	{"text": "Then I should be very glad to compare impressions as to this most interesting problem which has been submitted to us this morning.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_504	lexical	\N	\N	503	{"text": "I knew that seclusion and solitude were very necessary for my friend in those hours of intense mental concentration during which he weighed every particle of evidence, constructed alternative theories, balanced one against the other, and made up his mind as to which points were essential and which immaterial.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_505	lexical	\N	\N	504	{"text": "I therefore spent the day at my club and did not return to Baker Street until evening.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_506	lexical	\N	\N	505	{"text": "It was nearly nine o’clock when I found myself in the sitting-room once more.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_507	lexical	\N	\N	506	{"text": "My first impression as I opened the door was that a fire had broken out, for the room was so filled with smoke that the light of the lamp upon the table was blurred by it.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_508	lexical	\N	\N	507	{"text": "As I entered, however, my fears were set at rest, for it was the acrid fumes of strong coarse tobacco which took me by the throat and set me coughing.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_509	lexical	\N	\N	508	{"text": "Through the haze I had a vague vision of Holmes in his dressing-gown coiled up in an armchair with his black clay pipe between his lips.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_510	lexical	\N	\N	509	{"text": "Several rolls of paper lay around him.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_511	lexical	\N	\N	510	{"text": "“Caught cold, Watson?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_512	lexical	\N	\N	511	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_513	lexical	\N	\N	512	{"text": "“No, it’s this poisonous atmosphere.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_514	lexical	\N	\N	513	{"text": "“I suppose it _is_ pretty thick, now that you mention it.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_515	lexical	\N	\N	514	{"text": "“Thick!", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_516	lexical	\N	\N	515	{"text": "It is intolerable.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_517	lexical	\N	\N	516	{"text": "“Open the window, then!", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_518	lexical	\N	\N	517	{"text": "You have been at your club all day, I perceive.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_519	lexical	\N	\N	518	{"text": "“My dear Holmes!”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_520	lexical	\N	\N	519	{"text": "“Am I right?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_521	lexical	\N	\N	520	{"text": "“Certainly, but how?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_522	lexical	\N	\N	521	{"text": "He laughed at my bewildered expression.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_523	lexical	\N	\N	522	{"text": "“There is a delightful freshness about you, Watson, which makes it a pleasure to exercise any small powers which I possess at your expense.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_524	lexical	\N	\N	523	{"text": "A gentleman goes forth on a showery and miry day.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_525	lexical	\N	\N	524	{"text": "He returns immaculate in the evening with the gloss still on his hat and his boots.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_526	lexical	\N	\N	525	{"text": "He has been a fixture therefore all day.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_527	lexical	\N	\N	526	{"text": "He is not a man with intimate friends.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_528	lexical	\N	\N	527	{"text": "Where, then, could he have been?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_529	lexical	\N	\N	528	{"text": "Is it not obvious?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_530	lexical	\N	\N	529	{"text": "“Well, it is rather obvious.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_531	lexical	\N	\N	530	{"text": "“The world is full of obvious things which nobody by any chance ever observes.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_532	lexical	\N	\N	531	{"text": "Where do you think that I have been?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_533	lexical	\N	\N	532	{"text": "“A fixture also.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_534	lexical	\N	\N	533	{"text": "“On the contrary, I have been to Devonshire.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_535	lexical	\N	\N	534	{"text": "“In spirit?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_536	lexical	\N	\N	535	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_537	lexical	\N	\N	536	{"text": "My body has remained in this armchair and has, I regret to observe, consumed in my absence two large pots of coffee and an incredible amount of tobacco.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_538	lexical	\N	\N	537	{"text": "After you left I sent down to Stamford’s for the Ordnance map of this portion of the moor, and my spirit has hovered over it all day.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_539	lexical	\N	\N	538	{"text": "I flatter myself that I could find my way about.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_540	lexical	\N	\N	539	{"text": "“A large-scale map, I presume?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_541	lexical	\N	\N	540	{"text": "“Very large.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_542	lexical	\N	\N	541	{"text": "He unrolled one section and held it over his knee.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_543	lexical	\N	\N	542	{"text": "“Here you have the particular district which concerns us.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_544	lexical	\N	\N	543	{"text": "That is Baskerville Hall in the middle.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_545	lexical	\N	\N	544	{"text": "“With a wood round it?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_546	lexical	\N	\N	545	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_547	lexical	\N	\N	546	{"text": "I fancy the yew alley, though not marked under that name, must stretch along this line, with the moor, as you perceive, upon the right of it.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_548	lexical	\N	\N	547	{"text": "This small clump of buildings here is the hamlet of Grimpen, where our friend Dr. Mortimer has his headquarters.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_549	lexical	\N	\N	548	{"text": "Within a radius of five miles there are, as you see, only a very few scattered dwellings.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_550	lexical	\N	\N	549	{"text": "Here is Lafter Hall, which was mentioned in the narrative.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_551	lexical	\N	\N	550	{"text": "There is a house indicated here which may be the residence of the naturalist—Stapleton, if I remember right, was his name.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_552	lexical	\N	\N	551	{"text": "Here are two moorland farmhouses, High Tor and Foulmire.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_553	lexical	\N	\N	552	{"text": "Then fourteen miles away the great convict prison of Princetown.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_554	lexical	\N	\N	553	{"text": "Between and around these scattered points extends the desolate, lifeless moor.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_555	lexical	\N	\N	554	{"text": "This, then, is the stage upon which tragedy has been played, and upon which we may help to play it again.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_556	lexical	\N	\N	555	{"text": "“It must be a wild place.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_557	lexical	\N	\N	556	{"text": "“Yes, the setting is a worthy one.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_558	lexical	\N	\N	557	{"text": "If the devil did desire to have a hand in the affairs of men—”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_559	lexical	\N	\N	558	{"text": "“Then you are yourself inclining to the supernatural explanation.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_560	lexical	\N	\N	559	{"text": "“The devil’s agents may be of flesh and blood, may they not?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_561	lexical	\N	\N	560	{"text": "There are two questions waiting for us at the outset.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_562	lexical	\N	\N	561	{"text": "The one is whether any crime has been committed at all; the second is, what is the crime and how was it committed?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_563	lexical	\N	\N	562	{"text": "Of course, if Dr. Mortimer’s surmise should be correct, and we are dealing with forces outside the ordinary laws of Nature, there is an end of our investigation.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_564	lexical	\N	\N	563	{"text": "But we are bound to exhaust all other hypotheses before falling back upon this one.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_565	lexical	\N	\N	564	{"text": "I think we’ll shut that window again, if you don’t mind.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_566	lexical	\N	\N	565	{"text": "It is a singular thing, but I find that a concentrated atmosphere helps a concentration of thought.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_567	lexical	\N	\N	566	{"text": "I have not pushed it to the length of getting into a box to think, but that is the logical outcome of my convictions.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_568	lexical	\N	\N	567	{"text": "Have you turned the case over in your mind?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_569	lexical	\N	\N	568	{"text": "“Yes, I have thought a good deal of it in the course of the day.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_570	lexical	\N	\N	569	{"text": "“What do you make of it?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_571	lexical	\N	\N	570	{"text": "“It is very bewildering.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_572	lexical	\N	\N	571	{"text": "“It has certainly a character of its own.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_573	lexical	\N	\N	572	{"text": "There are points of distinction about it.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_574	lexical	\N	\N	573	{"text": "That change in the footprints, for example.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_575	lexical	\N	\N	574	{"text": "What do you make of that?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_576	lexical	\N	\N	575	{"text": "“Mortimer said that the man had walked on tiptoe down that portion of the alley.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_577	lexical	\N	\N	576	{"text": "“He only repeated what some fool had said at the inquest.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_578	lexical	\N	\N	577	{"text": "Why should a man walk on tiptoe down the alley?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_579	lexical	\N	\N	578	{"text": "“What then?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_580	lexical	\N	\N	579	{"text": "“He was running, Watson—running desperately, running for his life, running until he burst his heart—and fell dead upon his face.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_581	lexical	\N	\N	580	{"text": "“Running from what?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_582	lexical	\N	\N	581	{"text": "“There lies our problem.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_583	lexical	\N	\N	582	{"text": "There are indications that the man was crazed with fear before ever he began to run.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_584	lexical	\N	\N	583	{"text": "“How can you say that?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_585	lexical	\N	\N	584	{"text": "“I am presuming that the cause of his fears came to him across the moor.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_586	lexical	\N	\N	585	{"text": "If that were so, and it seems most probable, only a man who had lost his wits would have run _from_ the house instead of towards it.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_587	lexical	\N	\N	586	{"text": "If the gipsy’s evidence may be taken as true, he ran with cries for help in the direction where help was least likely to be.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_588	lexical	\N	\N	587	{"text": "Then, again, whom was he waiting for that night, and why was he waiting for him in the yew alley rather than in his own house?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_589	lexical	\N	\N	588	{"text": "“You think that he was waiting for someone?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_590	lexical	\N	\N	589	{"text": "“The man was elderly and infirm.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_591	lexical	\N	\N	590	{"text": "We can understand his taking an evening stroll, but the ground was damp and the night inclement.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_592	lexical	\N	\N	591	{"text": "Is it natural that he should stand for five or ten minutes, as Dr. Mortimer, with more practical sense than I should have given him credit for, deduced from the cigar ash?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_593	lexical	\N	\N	592	{"text": "“But he went out every evening.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_594	lexical	\N	\N	593	{"text": "“I think it unlikely that he waited at the moor-gate every evening.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_595	lexical	\N	\N	594	{"text": "On the contrary, the evidence is that he avoided the moor.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_596	lexical	\N	\N	595	{"text": "That night he waited there.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_597	lexical	\N	\N	596	{"text": "It was the night before he made his departure for London.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_598	lexical	\N	\N	597	{"text": "The thing takes shape, Watson.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_599	lexical	\N	\N	598	{"text": "It becomes coherent.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_600	lexical	\N	\N	599	{"text": "Might I ask you to hand me my violin, and we will postpone all further thought upon this business until we have had the advantage of meeting Dr. Mortimer and Sir Henry Baskerville in the morning.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_601	lexical	\N	\N	600	{"text": "Chapter 4.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_602	lexical	\N	\N	601	{"text": "Sir Henry Baskerville", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_603	lexical	\N	\N	602	{"text": "Our breakfast table was cleared early, and Holmes waited in his dressing-gown for the promised interview.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_604	lexical	\N	\N	603	{"text": "Our clients were punctual to their appointment, for the clock had just struck ten when Dr. Mortimer was shown up, followed by the young baronet.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_605	lexical	\N	\N	604	{"text": "The latter was a small, alert, dark-eyed man about thirty years of age, very sturdily built, with thick black eyebrows and a strong, pugnacious face.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_606	lexical	\N	\N	605	{"text": "He wore a ruddy-tinted tweed suit and had the weather-beaten appearance of one who has spent most of his time in the open air, and yet there was something in his steady eye and the quiet assurance of his bearing which indicated the gentleman.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_607	lexical	\N	\N	606	{"text": "“This is Sir Henry Baskerville,” said Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_608	lexical	\N	\N	607	{"text": "“Why, yes,” said he, “and the strange thing is, Mr. Sherlock Holmes, that if my friend here had not proposed coming round to you this morning I should have come on my own account.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_609	lexical	\N	\N	608	{"text": "I understand that you think out little puzzles, and I’ve had one this morning which wants more thinking out than I am able to give it.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_610	lexical	\N	\N	609	{"text": "“Pray take a seat, Sir Henry.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_611	lexical	\N	\N	610	{"text": "Do I understand you to say that you have yourself had some remarkable experience since you arrived in London?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_612	lexical	\N	\N	611	{"text": "“Nothing of much importance, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_613	lexical	\N	\N	612	{"text": "Only a joke, as like as not.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_614	lexical	\N	\N	613	{"text": "It was this letter, if you can call it a letter, which reached me this morning.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_615	lexical	\N	\N	614	{"text": "He laid an envelope upon the table, and we all bent over it.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_616	lexical	\N	\N	615	{"text": "It was of common quality, greyish in colour.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_617	lexical	\N	\N	616	{"text": "The address, “Sir Henry Baskerville, Northumberland Hotel,” was printed in rough characters; the post-mark “Charing Cross,” and the date of posting the preceding evening.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_618	lexical	\N	\N	617	{"text": "“Who knew that you were going to the Northumberland Hotel?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_619	lexical	\N	\N	618	{"text": "asked Holmes, glancing keenly across at our visitor.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_620	lexical	\N	\N	619	{"text": "“No one could have known.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_621	lexical	\N	\N	620	{"text": "We only decided after I met Dr. Mortimer.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_622	lexical	\N	\N	621	{"text": "“But Dr. Mortimer was no doubt already stopping there?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_623	lexical	\N	\N	622	{"text": "“No, I had been staying with a friend,” said the doctor.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_624	lexical	\N	\N	623	{"text": "“There was no possible indication that we intended to go to this hotel.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_625	lexical	\N	\N	624	{"text": "“Hum!", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_626	lexical	\N	\N	625	{"text": "Someone seems to be very deeply interested in your movements.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_627	lexical	\N	\N	626	{"text": "Out of the envelope he took a half-sheet of foolscap paper folded into four.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_628	lexical	\N	\N	627	{"text": "This he opened and spread flat upon the table.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_629	lexical	\N	\N	628	{"text": "Across the middle of it a single sentence had been formed by the expedient of pasting printed words upon it.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_630	lexical	\N	\N	629	{"text": "It ran:", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_631	lexical	\N	\N	630	{"text": "As you value your life or your reason keep away from the moor.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_632	lexical	\N	\N	631	{"text": "The word “moor” only was printed in ink.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_633	lexical	\N	\N	632	{"text": "“Now,” said Sir Henry Baskerville, “perhaps you will tell me, Mr. Holmes, what in thunder is the meaning of that, and who it is that takes so much interest in my affairs?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_634	lexical	\N	\N	633	{"text": "“What do you make of it, Dr. Mortimer?", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_635	lexical	\N	\N	634	{"text": "You must allow that there is nothing supernatural about this, at any rate?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_636	lexical	\N	\N	635	{"text": "“No, sir, but it might very well come from someone who was convinced that the business is supernatural.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_637	lexical	\N	\N	636	{"text": "“What business?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_638	lexical	\N	\N	637	{"text": "asked Sir Henry sharply.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_639	lexical	\N	\N	638	{"text": "“It seems to me that all you gentlemen know a great deal more than I do about my own affairs.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_640	lexical	\N	\N	639	{"text": "“You shall share our knowledge before you leave this room, Sir Henry.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_641	lexical	\N	\N	640	{"text": "I promise you that,” said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_642	lexical	\N	\N	641	{"text": "“We will confine ourselves for the present with your permission to this very interesting document, which must have been put together and posted yesterday evening.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_643	lexical	\N	\N	642	{"text": "Have you yesterday’s _Times_, Watson?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_644	lexical	\N	\N	643	{"text": "“It is here in the corner.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_645	lexical	\N	\N	644	{"text": "“Might I trouble you for it—the inside page, please, with the leading articles?”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_646	lexical	\N	\N	645	{"text": "He glanced swiftly over it, running his eyes up and down the columns.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_647	lexical	\N	\N	646	{"text": "“Capital article this on free trade.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_648	lexical	\N	\N	647	{"text": "Permit me to give you an extract from it.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_649	lexical	\N	\N	648	{"text": "‘You may be cajoled into imagining that your own special trade or your own industry will be encouraged by a protective tariff, but it stands to reason that such legislation must in the long run keep away wealth from the country, diminish the value of our imports, and lower the general conditions of life in this island.’", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_650	lexical	\N	\N	649	{"text": "“What do you think of that, Watson?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_651	lexical	\N	\N	650	{"text": "cried Holmes in high glee, rubbing his hands together with satisfaction.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_652	lexical	\N	\N	651	{"text": "“Don’t you think that is an admirable sentiment?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_653	lexical	\N	\N	652	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer looked at Holmes with an air of professional interest, and Sir Henry Baskerville turned a pair of puzzled dark eyes upon me.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_654	lexical	\N	\N	653	{"text": "“I don’t know much about the tariff and things of that kind,” said he, “but it seems to me we’ve got a bit off the trail so far as that note is concerned.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_655	lexical	\N	\N	654	{"text": "“On the contrary, I think we are particularly hot upon the trail, Sir Henry.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_656	lexical	\N	\N	655	{"text": "Watson here knows more about my methods than you do, but I fear that even he has not quite grasped the significance of this sentence.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_657	lexical	\N	\N	656	{"text": "“No, I confess that I see no connection.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_658	lexical	\N	\N	657	{"text": "“And yet, my dear Watson, there is so very close a connection that the one is extracted out of the other.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_659	lexical	\N	\N	658	{"text": "‘You,’ ‘your,’ ‘your,’ ‘life,’ ‘reason,’ ‘value,’ ‘keep away,’ ‘from the.’", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_660	lexical	\N	\N	659	{"text": "Don’t you see now whence these words have been taken?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_661	lexical	\N	\N	660	{"text": "“By thunder, you’re right!", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_662	lexical	\N	\N	661	{"text": "Well, if that isn’t smart!”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_663	lexical	\N	\N	662	{"text": "cried Sir Henry.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_664	lexical	\N	\N	663	{"text": "“If any possible doubt remained it is settled by the fact that ‘keep away’ and ‘from the’ are cut out in one piece.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_665	lexical	\N	\N	664	{"text": "“Well, now—so it is!”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_666	lexical	\N	\N	665	{"text": "“Really, Mr. Holmes, this exceeds anything which I could have imagined,” said Dr. Mortimer, gazing at my friend in amazement.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_667	lexical	\N	\N	666	{"text": "“I could understand anyone saying that the words were from a newspaper; but that you should name which, and add that it came from the leading article, is really one of the most remarkable things which I have ever known.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_668	lexical	\N	\N	667	{"text": "How did you do it?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_669	lexical	\N	\N	668	{"text": "“I presume, Doctor, that you could tell the skull of a negro from that of an Esquimau?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_670	lexical	\N	\N	669	{"text": "“Most certainly.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_671	lexical	\N	\N	670	{"text": "“But how?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_672	lexical	\N	\N	671	{"text": "“Because that is my special hobby.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_673	lexical	\N	\N	672	{"text": "The differences are obvious.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_674	lexical	\N	\N	673	{"text": "The supra-orbital crest, the facial angle, the maxillary curve, the—”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_675	lexical	\N	\N	674	{"text": "“But this is my special hobby, and the differences are equally obvious.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_676	lexical	\N	\N	675	{"text": "There is as much difference to my eyes between the leaded bourgeois type of a _Times_ article and the slovenly print of an evening half-penny paper as there could be between your negro and your Esquimau.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_677	lexical	\N	\N	676	{"text": "The detection of types is one of the most elementary branches of knowledge to the special expert in crime, though I confess that once when I was very young I confused the _Leeds Mercury_ with the _Western Morning News_.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_678	lexical	\N	\N	677	{"text": "But a _Times_ leader is entirely distinctive, and these words could have been taken from nothing else.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_679	lexical	\N	\N	678	{"text": "As it was done yesterday the strong probability was that we should find the words in yesterday’s issue.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_680	lexical	\N	\N	679	{"text": "“So far as I can follow you, then, Mr. Holmes,” said Sir Henry Baskerville, “someone cut out this message with a scissors—”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_681	lexical	\N	\N	680	{"text": "“Nail-scissors,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_682	lexical	\N	\N	681	{"text": "“You can see that it was a very short-bladed scissors, since the cutter had to take two snips over ‘keep away.’”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_683	lexical	\N	\N	682	{"text": "“That is so.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_684	lexical	\N	\N	683	{"text": "Someone, then, cut out the message with a pair of short-bladed scissors, pasted it with paste—”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_685	lexical	\N	\N	684	{"text": "“Gum,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_686	lexical	\N	\N	685	{"text": "“With gum on to the paper.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_687	lexical	\N	\N	686	{"text": "But I want to know why the word ‘moor’ should have been written?”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_688	lexical	\N	\N	687	{"text": "“Because he could not find it in print.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_689	lexical	\N	\N	688	{"text": "The other words were all simple and might be found in any issue, but ‘moor’ would be less common.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_690	lexical	\N	\N	689	{"text": "“Why, of course, that would explain it.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_691	lexical	\N	\N	690	{"text": "Have you read anything else in this message, Mr. Holmes?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_692	lexical	\N	\N	691	{"text": "“There are one or two indications, and yet the utmost pains have been taken to remove all clues.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_693	lexical	\N	\N	692	{"text": "The address, you observe is printed in rough characters.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_694	lexical	\N	\N	693	{"text": "But the _Times_ is a paper which is seldom found in any hands but those of the highly educated.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_695	lexical	\N	\N	694	{"text": "We may take it, therefore, that the letter was composed by an educated man who wished to pose as an uneducated one, and his effort to conceal his own writing suggests that that writing might be known, or come to be known, by you.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_696	lexical	\N	\N	695	{"text": "Again, you will observe that the words are not gummed on in an accurate line, but that some are much higher than others.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_697	lexical	\N	\N	696	{"text": "‘Life,’ for example is quite out of its proper place.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_698	lexical	\N	\N	697	{"text": "That may point to carelessness or it may point to agitation and hurry upon the part of the cutter.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_699	lexical	\N	\N	698	{"text": "On the whole I incline to the latter view, since the matter was evidently important, and it is unlikely that the composer of such a letter would be careless.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_700	lexical	\N	\N	699	{"text": "If he were in a hurry it opens up the interesting question why he should be in a hurry, since any letter posted up to early morning would reach Sir Henry before he would leave his hotel.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_701	lexical	\N	\N	700	{"text": "Did the composer fear an interruption—and from whom?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_702	lexical	\N	\N	701	{"text": "“We are coming now rather into the region of guesswork,” said Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_703	lexical	\N	\N	702	{"text": "“Say, rather, into the region where we balance probabilities and choose the most likely.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_704	lexical	\N	\N	703	{"text": "It is the scientific use of the imagination, but we have always some material basis on which to start our speculation.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_705	lexical	\N	\N	704	{"text": "Now, you would call it a guess, no doubt, but I am almost certain that this address has been written in a hotel.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_706	lexical	\N	\N	705	{"text": "“How in the world can you say that?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_707	lexical	\N	\N	706	{"text": "“If you examine it carefully you will see that both the pen and the ink have given the writer trouble.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_708	lexical	\N	\N	707	{"text": "The pen has spluttered twice in a single word and has run dry three times in a short address, showing that there was very little ink in the bottle.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_709	lexical	\N	\N	708	{"text": "Now, a private pen or ink-bottle is seldom allowed to be in such a state, and the combination of the two must be quite rare.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_710	lexical	\N	\N	709	{"text": "But you know the hotel ink and the hotel pen, where it is rare to get anything else.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_711	lexical	\N	\N	710	{"text": "Yes, I have very little hesitation in saying that could we examine the waste-paper baskets of the hotels around Charing Cross until we found the remains of the mutilated _Times_ leader we could lay our hands straight upon the person who sent this singular message.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_712	lexical	\N	\N	711	{"text": "Halloa!", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_713	lexical	\N	\N	712	{"text": "Halloa!", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_714	lexical	\N	\N	713	{"text": "What’s this?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_715	lexical	\N	\N	714	{"text": "He was carefully examining the foolscap, upon which the words were pasted, holding it only an inch or two from his eyes.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_716	lexical	\N	\N	715	{"text": "“Well?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_717	lexical	\N	\N	716	{"text": "“Nothing,” said he, throwing it down.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_718	lexical	\N	\N	717	{"text": "“It is a blank half-sheet of paper, without even a water-mark upon it.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_719	lexical	\N	\N	718	{"text": "I think we have drawn as much as we can from this curious letter; and now, Sir Henry, has anything else of interest happened to you since you have been in London?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_720	lexical	\N	\N	719	{"text": "“Why, no, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_721	lexical	\N	\N	720	{"text": "I think not.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_722	lexical	\N	\N	721	{"text": "“You have not observed anyone follow or watch you?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_723	lexical	\N	\N	722	{"text": "“I seem to have walked right into the thick of a dime novel,” said our visitor.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_724	lexical	\N	\N	723	{"text": "“Why in thunder should anyone follow or watch me?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_725	lexical	\N	\N	724	{"text": "“We are coming to that.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_726	lexical	\N	\N	725	{"text": "You have nothing else to report to us before we go into this matter?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_727	lexical	\N	\N	726	{"text": "“Well, it depends upon what you think worth reporting.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_728	lexical	\N	\N	727	{"text": "“I think anything out of the ordinary routine of life well worth reporting.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_729	lexical	\N	\N	728	{"text": "Sir Henry smiled.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_730	lexical	\N	\N	729	{"text": "“I don’t know much of British life yet, for I have spent nearly all my time in the States and in Canada.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_731	lexical	\N	\N	730	{"text": "But I hope that to lose one of your boots is not part of the ordinary routine of life over here.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_732	lexical	\N	\N	731	{"text": "“You have lost one of your boots?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_733	lexical	\N	\N	732	{"text": "“My dear sir,” cried Dr. Mortimer, “it is only mislaid.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_734	lexical	\N	\N	733	{"text": "You will find it when you return to the hotel.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_735	lexical	\N	\N	734	{"text": "What is the use of troubling Mr. Holmes with trifles of this kind?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_736	lexical	\N	\N	735	{"text": "“Well, he asked me for anything outside the ordinary routine.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_737	lexical	\N	\N	736	{"text": "“Exactly,” said Holmes, “however foolish the incident may seem.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_738	lexical	\N	\N	737	{"text": "You have lost one of your boots, you say?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_739	lexical	\N	\N	738	{"text": "“Well, mislaid it, anyhow.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_740	lexical	\N	\N	739	{"text": "I put them both outside my door last night, and there was only one in the morning.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_741	lexical	\N	\N	740	{"text": "I could get no sense out of the chap who cleans them.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_742	lexical	\N	\N	741	{"text": "The worst of it is that I only bought the pair last night in the Strand, and I have never had them on.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_743	lexical	\N	\N	742	{"text": "“If you have never worn them, why did you put them out to be cleaned?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_744	lexical	\N	\N	743	{"text": "“They were tan boots and had never been varnished.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_745	lexical	\N	\N	744	{"text": "That was why I put them out.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_746	lexical	\N	\N	745	{"text": "“Then I understand that on your arrival in London yesterday you went out at once and bought a pair of boots?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_747	lexical	\N	\N	746	{"text": "“I did a good deal of shopping.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_748	lexical	\N	\N	747	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer here went round with me.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_749	lexical	\N	\N	748	{"text": "You see, if I am to be squire down there I must dress the part, and it may be that I have got a little careless in my ways out West.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_750	lexical	\N	\N	749	{"text": "Among other things I bought these brown boots—gave six dollars for them—and had one stolen before ever I had them on my feet.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_751	lexical	\N	\N	750	{"text": "“It seems a singularly useless thing to steal,” said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_752	lexical	\N	\N	751	{"text": "“I confess that I share Dr. Mortimer’s belief that it will not be long before the missing boot is found.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_753	lexical	\N	\N	752	{"text": "“And, now, gentlemen,” said the baronet with decision, “it seems to me that I have spoken quite enough about the little that I know.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_754	lexical	\N	\N	753	{"text": "It is time that you kept your promise and gave me a full account of what we are all driving at.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_755	lexical	\N	\N	754	{"text": "“Your request is a very reasonable one,” Holmes answered.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_756	lexical	\N	\N	755	{"text": "“Dr. Mortimer, I think you could not do better than to tell your story as you told it to us.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_757	lexical	\N	\N	756	{"text": "Thus encouraged, our scientific friend drew his papers from his pocket and presented the whole case as he had done upon the morning before.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_758	lexical	\N	\N	757	{"text": "Sir Henry Baskerville listened with the deepest attention and with an occasional exclamation of surprise.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_759	lexical	\N	\N	758	{"text": "“Well, I seem to have come into an inheritance with a vengeance,” said he when the long narrative was finished.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_760	lexical	\N	\N	759	{"text": "“Of course, I’ve heard of the hound ever since I was in the nursery.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_761	lexical	\N	\N	760	{"text": "It’s the pet story of the family, though I never thought of taking it seriously before.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_762	lexical	\N	\N	761	{"text": "But as to my uncle’s death—well, it all seems boiling up in my head, and I can’t get it clear yet.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_763	lexical	\N	\N	762	{"text": "You don’t seem quite to have made up your mind whether it’s a case for a policeman or a clergyman.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_764	lexical	\N	\N	763	{"text": "“Precisely.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_765	lexical	\N	\N	764	{"text": "“And now there’s this affair of the letter to me at the hotel.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_766	lexical	\N	\N	765	{"text": "I suppose that fits into its place.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_767	lexical	\N	\N	766	{"text": "“It seems to show that someone knows more than we do about what goes on upon the moor,” said Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_768	lexical	\N	\N	767	{"text": "“And also,” said Holmes, “that someone is not ill-disposed towards you, since they warn you of danger.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_769	lexical	\N	\N	768	{"text": "“Or it may be that they wish, for their own purposes, to scare me away.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_770	lexical	\N	\N	769	{"text": "“Well, of course, that is possible also.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_771	lexical	\N	\N	770	{"text": "I am very much indebted to you, Dr. Mortimer, for introducing me to a problem which presents several interesting alternatives.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_772	lexical	\N	\N	771	{"text": "But the practical point which we now have to decide, Sir Henry, is whether it is or is not advisable for you to go to Baskerville Hall.”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_773	lexical	\N	\N	772	{"text": "“Why should I not go?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_774	lexical	\N	\N	773	{"text": "“There seems to be danger.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_775	lexical	\N	\N	774	{"text": "“Do you mean danger from this family fiend or do you mean danger from human beings?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_776	lexical	\N	\N	775	{"text": "“Well, that is what we have to find out.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_777	lexical	\N	\N	776	{"text": "“Whichever it is, my answer is fixed.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_778	lexical	\N	\N	777	{"text": "There is no devil in hell, Mr. Holmes, and there is no man upon earth who can prevent me from going to the home of my own people, and you may take that to be my final answer.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_779	lexical	\N	\N	778	{"text": "His dark brows knitted and his face flushed to a dusky red as he spoke.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_780	lexical	\N	\N	779	{"text": "It was evident that the fiery temper of the Baskervilles was not extinct in this their last representative.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_781	lexical	\N	\N	780	{"text": "“Meanwhile,” said he, “I have hardly had time to think over all that you have told me.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_782	lexical	\N	\N	781	{"text": "It’s a big thing for a man to have to understand and to decide at one sitting.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_783	lexical	\N	\N	782	{"text": "I should like to have a quiet hour by myself to make up my mind.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_784	lexical	\N	\N	783	{"text": "Now, look here, Mr. Holmes, it’s half-past eleven now and I am going back right away to my hotel.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_785	lexical	\N	\N	784	{"text": "Suppose you and your friend, Dr. Watson, come round and lunch with us at two.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_786	lexical	\N	\N	785	{"text": "I’ll be able to tell you more clearly then how this thing strikes me.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_787	lexical	\N	\N	786	{"text": "“Is that convenient to you, Watson?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_788	lexical	\N	\N	787	{"text": "“Perfectly.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_789	lexical	\N	\N	788	{"text": "“Then you may expect us.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_790	lexical	\N	\N	789	{"text": "Shall I have a cab called?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_791	lexical	\N	\N	790	{"text": "“I’d prefer to walk, for this affair has flurried me rather.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_792	lexical	\N	\N	791	{"text": "“I’ll join you in a walk, with pleasure,” said his companion.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_793	lexical	\N	\N	792	{"text": "“Then we meet again at two o’clock.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_794	lexical	\N	\N	793	{"text": "Au revoir, and good-morning!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_795	lexical	\N	\N	794	{"text": "We heard the steps of our visitors descend the stair and the bang of the front door.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_796	lexical	\N	\N	795	{"text": "In an instant Holmes had changed from the languid dreamer to the man of action.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_797	lexical	\N	\N	796	{"text": "“Your hat and boots, Watson, quick!", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_798	lexical	\N	\N	797	{"text": "Not a moment to lose!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_799	lexical	\N	\N	798	{"text": "He rushed into his room in his dressing-gown and was back again in a few seconds in a frock-coat.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_800	lexical	\N	\N	799	{"text": "We hurried together down the stairs and into the street.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_801	lexical	\N	\N	800	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer and Baskerville were still visible about two hundred yards ahead of us in the direction of Oxford Street.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_802	lexical	\N	\N	801	{"text": "“Shall I run on and stop them?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_803	lexical	\N	\N	802	{"text": "“Not for the world, my dear Watson.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_804	lexical	\N	\N	803	{"text": "I am perfectly satisfied with your company if you will tolerate mine.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_805	lexical	\N	\N	804	{"text": "Our friends are wise, for it is certainly a very fine morning for a walk.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_806	lexical	\N	\N	805	{"text": "He quickened his pace until we had decreased the distance which divided us by about half.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_807	lexical	\N	\N	806	{"text": "Then, still keeping a hundred yards behind, we followed into Oxford Street and so down Regent Street.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_808	lexical	\N	\N	807	{"text": "Once our friends stopped and stared into a shop window, upon which Holmes did the same.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_809	lexical	\N	\N	808	{"text": "An instant afterwards he gave a little cry of satisfaction, and, following the direction of his eager eyes, I saw that a hansom cab with a man inside which had halted on the other side of the street was now proceeding slowly onward again.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_810	lexical	\N	\N	809	{"text": "“There’s our man, Watson!", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_811	lexical	\N	\N	810	{"text": "Come along!", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_812	lexical	\N	\N	811	{"text": "We’ll have a good look at him, if we can do no more.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_813	lexical	\N	\N	812	{"text": "At that instant I was aware of a bushy black beard and a pair of piercing eyes turned upon us through the side window of the cab.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_814	lexical	\N	\N	813	{"text": "Instantly the trapdoor at the top flew up, something was screamed to the driver, and the cab flew madly off down Regent Street.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_815	lexical	\N	\N	814	{"text": "Holmes looked eagerly round for another, but no empty one was in sight.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_816	lexical	\N	\N	815	{"text": "Then he dashed in wild pursuit amid the stream of the traffic, but the start was too great, and already the cab was out of sight.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_817	lexical	\N	\N	816	{"text": "“There now!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_818	lexical	\N	\N	817	{"text": "said Holmes bitterly as he emerged panting and white with vexation from the tide of vehicles.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_819	lexical	\N	\N	818	{"text": "“Was ever such bad luck and such bad management, too?", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_820	lexical	\N	\N	819	{"text": "Watson, Watson, if you are an honest man you will record this also and set it against my successes!”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_821	lexical	\N	\N	820	{"text": "“Who was the man?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_822	lexical	\N	\N	821	{"text": "“I have not an idea.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_823	lexical	\N	\N	822	{"text": "“A spy?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_824	lexical	\N	\N	823	{"text": "“Well, it was evident from what we have heard that Baskerville has been very closely shadowed by someone since he has been in town.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_825	lexical	\N	\N	824	{"text": "How else could it be known so quickly that it was the Northumberland Hotel which he had chosen?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_826	lexical	\N	\N	825	{"text": "If they had followed him the first day I argued that they would follow him also the second.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_827	lexical	\N	\N	826	{"text": "You may have observed that I twice strolled over to the window while Dr. Mortimer was reading his legend.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_828	lexical	\N	\N	827	{"text": "“Yes, I remember.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_829	lexical	\N	\N	828	{"text": "“I was looking out for loiterers in the street, but I saw none.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_830	lexical	\N	\N	829	{"text": "We are dealing with a clever man, Watson.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_831	lexical	\N	\N	830	{"text": "This matter cuts very deep, and though I have not finally made up my mind whether it is a benevolent or a malevolent agency which is in touch with us, I am conscious always of power and design.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_832	lexical	\N	\N	831	{"text": "When our friends left I at once followed them in the hopes of marking down their invisible attendant.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_833	lexical	\N	\N	832	{"text": "So wily was he that he had not trusted himself upon foot, but he had availed himself of a cab so that he could loiter behind or dash past them and so escape their notice.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_834	lexical	\N	\N	833	{"text": "His method had the additional advantage that if they were to take a cab he was all ready to follow them.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_835	lexical	\N	\N	834	{"text": "It has, however, one obvious disadvantage.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_836	lexical	\N	\N	835	{"text": "“It puts him in the power of the cabman.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_837	lexical	\N	\N	836	{"text": "“Exactly.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_838	lexical	\N	\N	837	{"text": "“What a pity we did not get the number!”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_839	lexical	\N	\N	838	{"text": "“My dear Watson, clumsy as I have been, you surely do not seriously imagine that I neglected to get the number?", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_840	lexical	\N	\N	839	{"text": "No.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_841	lexical	\N	\N	840	{"text": "2704 is our man.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_842	lexical	\N	\N	841	{"text": "But that is no use to us for the moment.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_843	lexical	\N	\N	842	{"text": "“I fail to see how you could have done more.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_844	lexical	\N	\N	843	{"text": "“On observing the cab I should have instantly turned and walked in the other direction.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_845	lexical	\N	\N	844	{"text": "I should then at my leisure have hired a second cab and followed the first at a respectful distance, or, better still, have driven to the Northumberland Hotel and waited there.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_846	lexical	\N	\N	845	{"text": "When our unknown had followed Baskerville home we should have had the opportunity of playing his own game upon himself and seeing where he made for.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_847	lexical	\N	\N	846	{"text": "As it is, by an indiscreet eagerness, which was taken advantage of with extraordinary quickness and energy by our opponent, we have betrayed ourselves and lost our man.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_848	lexical	\N	\N	847	{"text": "We had been sauntering slowly down Regent Street during this conversation, and Dr. Mortimer, with his companion, had long vanished in front of us.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_849	lexical	\N	\N	848	{"text": "“There is no object in our following them,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_850	lexical	\N	\N	849	{"text": "“The shadow has departed and will not return.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_851	lexical	\N	\N	850	{"text": "We must see what further cards we have in our hands and play them with decision.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_852	lexical	\N	\N	851	{"text": "Could you swear to that man’s face within the cab?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_853	lexical	\N	\N	852	{"text": "“I could swear only to the beard.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_854	lexical	\N	\N	853	{"text": "“And so could I—from which I gather that in all probability it was a false one.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_855	lexical	\N	\N	854	{"text": "A clever man upon so delicate an errand has no use for a beard save to conceal his features.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_856	lexical	\N	\N	855	{"text": "Come in here, Watson!”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_857	lexical	\N	\N	856	{"text": "He turned into one of the district messenger offices, where he was warmly greeted by the manager.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_858	lexical	\N	\N	857	{"text": "“Ah, Wilson, I see you have not forgotten the little case in which I had the good fortune to help you?”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_859	lexical	\N	\N	858	{"text": "“No, sir, indeed I have not.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_860	lexical	\N	\N	859	{"text": "You saved my good name, and perhaps my life.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_861	lexical	\N	\N	860	{"text": "“My dear fellow, you exaggerate.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_862	lexical	\N	\N	861	{"text": "I have some recollection, Wilson, that you had among your boys a lad named Cartwright, who showed some ability during the investigation.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_863	lexical	\N	\N	862	{"text": "“Yes, sir, he is still with us.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_864	lexical	\N	\N	863	{"text": "—thank you!", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_865	lexical	\N	\N	864	{"text": "And I should be glad to have change of this five-pound note.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_866	lexical	\N	\N	865	{"text": "this five-pound note.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_867	lexical	\N	\N	866	{"text": "A lad of fourteen, with a bright, keen face, had obeyed the summons of the manager.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_868	lexical	\N	\N	867	{"text": "He stood now gazing with great reverence at the famous detective.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_869	lexical	\N	\N	868	{"text": "“Let me have the Hotel Directory,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_870	lexical	\N	\N	869	{"text": "“Thank you!", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_871	lexical	\N	\N	870	{"text": "Now, Cartwright, there are the names of twenty-three hotels here, all in the immediate neighbourhood of Charing Cross.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_872	lexical	\N	\N	871	{"text": "Do you see?”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_873	lexical	\N	\N	872	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_874	lexical	\N	\N	873	{"text": "“You will visit each of these in turn.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_875	lexical	\N	\N	874	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_876	lexical	\N	\N	875	{"text": "“You will begin in each case by giving the outside porter one shilling.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_877	lexical	\N	\N	876	{"text": "Here are twenty-three shillings.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_878	lexical	\N	\N	877	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_879	lexical	\N	\N	878	{"text": "“You will tell him that you want to see the waste-paper of yesterday.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_880	lexical	\N	\N	879	{"text": "You will say that an important telegram has miscarried and that you are looking for it.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_881	lexical	\N	\N	880	{"text": "You understand?”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_883	lexical	\N	\N	882	{"text": "“But what you are really looking for is the centre page of the _Times_ with some holes cut in it with scissors.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_884	lexical	\N	\N	883	{"text": "Here is a copy of the _Times_.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_885	lexical	\N	\N	884	{"text": "It is this page.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_886	lexical	\N	\N	885	{"text": "You could easily recognize it, could you not?”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_887	lexical	\N	\N	886	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_888	lexical	\N	\N	887	{"text": "“In each case the outside porter will send for the hall porter, to whom also you will give a shilling.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_889	lexical	\N	\N	888	{"text": "Here are twenty-three shillings.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_890	lexical	\N	\N	889	{"text": "You will then learn in possibly twenty cases out of the twenty-three that the waste of the day before has been burned or removed.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_891	lexical	\N	\N	890	{"text": "In the three other cases you will be shown a heap of paper and you will look for this page of the _Times_ among it.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_892	lexical	\N	\N	891	{"text": "The odds are enormously against your finding it.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_893	lexical	\N	\N	892	{"text": "There are ten shillings over in case of emergencies.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_894	lexical	\N	\N	893	{"text": "Let me have a report by wire at Baker Street before evening.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_895	lexical	\N	\N	894	{"text": "And now, Watson, it only remains for us to find out by wire the identity of the cabman, No.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_896	lexical	\N	\N	895	{"text": "2704, and then we will drop into one of the Bond Street picture galleries and fill in the time until we are due at the hotel.”", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_897	lexical	\N	\N	896	{"text": "Chapter 5.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_898	lexical	\N	\N	897	{"text": "Three Broken Threads", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_899	lexical	\N	\N	898	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes had, in a very remarkable degree, the power of detaching his mind at will.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_900	lexical	\N	\N	899	{"text": "For two hours the strange business in which we had been involved appeared to be forgotten, and he was entirely absorbed in the pictures of the modern Belgian masters.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_901	lexical	\N	\N	900	{"text": "He would talk of nothing but art, of which he had the crudest ideas, from our leaving the gallery until we found ourselves at the Northumberland Hotel.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_902	lexical	\N	\N	901	{"text": "“Sir Henry Baskerville is upstairs expecting you,” said the clerk.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_903	lexical	\N	\N	902	{"text": "“He asked me to show you up at once when you came.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_904	lexical	\N	\N	903	{"text": "“Have you any objection to my looking at your register?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_905	lexical	\N	\N	904	{"text": "said Holmes.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_906	lexical	\N	\N	905	{"text": "“Not in the least.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_907	lexical	\N	\N	906	{"text": "The book showed that two names had been added after that of Baskerville.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_908	lexical	\N	\N	907	{"text": "One was Theophilus Johnson and family, of Newcastle; the other Mrs. Oldmore and maid, of High Lodge, Alton.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_909	lexical	\N	\N	908	{"text": "“Surely that must be the same Johnson whom I used to know,” said Holmes to the porter.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_910	lexical	\N	\N	909	{"text": "“A lawyer, is he not, grey-headed, and walks with a limp?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_911	lexical	\N	\N	910	{"text": "“No, sir, this is Mr. Johnson, the coal-owner, a very active gentleman, not older than yourself.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_912	lexical	\N	\N	911	{"text": "“Surely you are mistaken about his trade?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_913	lexical	\N	\N	912	{"text": "“No, sir!", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_914	lexical	\N	\N	913	{"text": "he has used this hotel for many years, and he is very well known to us.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_915	lexical	\N	\N	914	{"text": "“Ah, that settles it.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_916	lexical	\N	\N	915	{"text": "Mrs. Oldmore, too; I seem to remember the name.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_917	lexical	\N	\N	916	{"text": "Excuse my curiosity, but often in calling upon one friend one finds another.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_918	lexical	\N	\N	917	{"text": "“She is an invalid lady, sir.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_919	lexical	\N	\N	918	{"text": "Her husband was once mayor of Gloucester.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_920	lexical	\N	\N	919	{"text": "She always comes to us when she is in town.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_921	lexical	\N	\N	920	{"text": "“Thank you; I am afraid I cannot claim her acquaintance.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_922	lexical	\N	\N	921	{"text": "We have established a most important fact by these questions, Watson,” he continued in a low voice as we went upstairs together.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_923	lexical	\N	\N	922	{"text": "“We know now that the people who are so interested in our friend have not settled down in his own hotel.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_924	lexical	\N	\N	923	{"text": "That means that while they are, as we have seen, very anxious to watch him, they are equally anxious that he should not see them.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_925	lexical	\N	\N	924	{"text": "Now, this is a most suggestive fact.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_926	lexical	\N	\N	925	{"text": "“What does it suggest?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_927	lexical	\N	\N	926	{"text": "“It suggests—halloa, my dear fellow, what on earth is the matter?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_928	lexical	\N	\N	927	{"text": "As we came round the top of the stairs we had run up against Sir Henry Baskerville himself.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_929	lexical	\N	\N	928	{"text": "His face was flushed with anger, and he held an old and dusty boot in one of his hands.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_930	lexical	\N	\N	929	{"text": "So furious was he that he was hardly articulate, and when he did speak it was in a much broader and more Western dialect than any which we had heard from him in the morning.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_931	lexical	\N	\N	930	{"text": "“Seems to me they are playing me for a sucker in this hotel,” he cried.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_932	lexical	\N	\N	931	{"text": "“They’ll find they’ve started in to monkey with the wrong man unless they are careful.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_933	lexical	\N	\N	932	{"text": "By thunder, if that chap can’t find my missing boot there will be trouble.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_934	lexical	\N	\N	933	{"text": "I can take a joke with the best, Mr. Holmes, but they’ve got a bit over the mark this time.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_935	lexical	\N	\N	934	{"text": "“Still looking for your boot?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_936	lexical	\N	\N	935	{"text": "“Yes, sir, and mean to find it.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_937	lexical	\N	\N	936	{"text": "“But, surely, you said that it was a new brown boot?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_938	lexical	\N	\N	937	{"text": "“So it was, sir.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_939	lexical	\N	\N	938	{"text": "And now it’s an old black one.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_940	lexical	\N	\N	939	{"text": "“What!", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_941	lexical	\N	\N	940	{"text": "you don’t mean to say—?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_942	lexical	\N	\N	941	{"text": "“That’s just what I do mean to say.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_943	lexical	\N	\N	942	{"text": "I only had three pairs in the world—the new brown, the old black, and the patent leathers, which I am wearing.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_944	lexical	\N	\N	943	{"text": "Last night they took one of my brown ones, and today they have sneaked one of the black.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_945	lexical	\N	\N	944	{"text": "Well, have you got it?", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_946	lexical	\N	\N	945	{"text": "Speak out, man, and don’t stand staring!”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_947	lexical	\N	\N	946	{"text": "An agitated German waiter had appeared upon the scene.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_948	lexical	\N	\N	947	{"text": "“No, sir; I have made inquiry all over the hotel, but I can hear no word of it.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_949	lexical	\N	\N	948	{"text": "“Well, either that boot comes back before sundown or I’ll see the manager and tell him that I go right straight out of this hotel.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_950	lexical	\N	\N	949	{"text": "“It shall be found, sir—I promise you that if you will have a little patience it will be found.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_951	lexical	\N	\N	950	{"text": "“Mind it is, for it’s the last thing of mine that I’ll lose in this den of thieves.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_952	lexical	\N	\N	951	{"text": "Well, well, Mr. Holmes, you’ll excuse my troubling you about such a trifle—”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_953	lexical	\N	\N	952	{"text": "“I think it’s well worth troubling about.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_954	lexical	\N	\N	953	{"text": "“Why, you look very serious over it.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_955	lexical	\N	\N	954	{"text": "“How do you explain it?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_956	lexical	\N	\N	955	{"text": "“I just don’t attempt to explain it.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_957	lexical	\N	\N	956	{"text": "It seems the very maddest, queerest thing that ever happened to me.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_958	lexical	\N	\N	957	{"text": "“The queerest perhaps—” said Holmes thoughtfully.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_959	lexical	\N	\N	958	{"text": "“What do you make of it yourself?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_960	lexical	\N	\N	959	{"text": "“Well, I don’t profess to understand it yet.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_961	lexical	\N	\N	960	{"text": "This case of yours is very complex, Sir Henry.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_962	lexical	\N	\N	961	{"text": "When taken in conjunction with your uncle’s death I am not sure that of all the five hundred cases of capital importance which I have handled there is one which cuts so deep.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_963	lexical	\N	\N	962	{"text": "But we hold several threads in our hands, and the odds are that one or other of them guides us to the truth.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_964	lexical	\N	\N	963	{"text": "We may waste time in following the wrong one, but sooner or later we must come upon the right.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_965	lexical	\N	\N	964	{"text": "We had a pleasant luncheon in which little was said of the business which had brought us together.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_966	lexical	\N	\N	965	{"text": "It was in the private sitting-room to which we afterwards repaired that Holmes asked Baskerville what were his intentions.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_967	lexical	\N	\N	966	{"text": "“To go to Baskerville Hall.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_968	lexical	\N	\N	967	{"text": "“And when?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_969	lexical	\N	\N	968	{"text": "“At the end of the week.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_970	lexical	\N	\N	969	{"text": "“On the whole,” said Holmes, “I think that your decision is a wise one.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_971	lexical	\N	\N	970	{"text": "I have ample evidence that you are being dogged in London, and amid the millions of this great city it is difficult to discover who these people are or what their object can be.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_972	lexical	\N	\N	971	{"text": "If their intentions are evil they might do you a mischief, and we should be powerless to prevent it.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_973	lexical	\N	\N	972	{"text": "You did not know, Dr. Mortimer, that you were followed this morning from my house?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_974	lexical	\N	\N	973	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer started violently.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_975	lexical	\N	\N	974	{"text": "“Followed!", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_976	lexical	\N	\N	975	{"text": "By whom?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_977	lexical	\N	\N	976	{"text": "“That, unfortunately, is what I cannot tell you.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_978	lexical	\N	\N	977	{"text": "Have you among your neighbours or acquaintances on Dartmoor any man with a black, full beard?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_979	lexical	\N	\N	978	{"text": "“No—or, let me see—why, yes.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_980	lexical	\N	\N	979	{"text": "Barrymore, Sir Charles’s butler, is a man with a full, black beard.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_981	lexical	\N	\N	980	{"text": "“Ha!", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_982	lexical	\N	\N	981	{"text": "Where is Barrymore?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_983	lexical	\N	\N	982	{"text": "“He is in charge of the Hall.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_984	lexical	\N	\N	983	{"text": "“We had best ascertain if he is really there, or if by any possibility he might be in London.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_985	lexical	\N	\N	984	{"text": "“How can you do that?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_986	lexical	\N	\N	985	{"text": "“Give me a telegraph form.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_987	lexical	\N	\N	986	{"text": "‘Is all ready for Sir Henry?’", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_988	lexical	\N	\N	987	{"text": "That will do.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_989	lexical	\N	\N	988	{"text": "Address to Mr. Barrymore, Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_990	lexical	\N	\N	989	{"text": "What is the nearest telegraph-office?", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_991	lexical	\N	\N	990	{"text": "Grimpen.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_992	lexical	\N	\N	991	{"text": "Very good, we will send a second wire to the postmaster, Grimpen: ‘Telegram to Mr. Barrymore to be delivered into his own hand.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_993	lexical	\N	\N	992	{"text": "If absent, please return wire to Sir Henry Baskerville, Northumberland Hotel.’", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_994	lexical	\N	\N	993	{"text": "That should let us know before evening whether Barrymore is at his post in Devonshire or not.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_995	lexical	\N	\N	994	{"text": "“That’s so,” said Baskerville.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_996	lexical	\N	\N	995	{"text": "“By the way, Dr. Mortimer, who is this Barrymore, anyhow?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_997	lexical	\N	\N	996	{"text": "“He is the son of the old caretaker, who is dead.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_998	lexical	\N	\N	997	{"text": "They have looked after the Hall for four generations now.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_999	lexical	\N	\N	998	{"text": "So far as I know, he and his wife are as respectable a couple as any in the county.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1000	lexical	\N	\N	999	{"text": "“At the same time,” said Baskerville, “it’s clear enough that so long as there are none of the family at the Hall these people have a mighty fine home and nothing to do.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1001	lexical	\N	\N	1000	{"text": "“That is true.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1002	lexical	\N	\N	1001	{"text": "“Did Barrymore profit at all by Sir Charles’s will?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1003	lexical	\N	\N	1002	{"text": "asked Holmes.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1004	lexical	\N	\N	1003	{"text": "“He and his wife had five hundred pounds each.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1005	lexical	\N	\N	1004	{"text": "“Ha!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1006	lexical	\N	\N	1005	{"text": "Did they know that they would receive this?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1007	lexical	\N	\N	1006	{"text": "“Yes; Sir Charles was very fond of talking about the provisions of his will.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1008	lexical	\N	\N	1007	{"text": "“That is very interesting.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1009	lexical	\N	\N	1008	{"text": "“I hope,” said Dr. Mortimer, “that you do not look with suspicious eyes upon everyone who received a legacy from Sir Charles, for I also had a thousand pounds left to me.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1010	lexical	\N	\N	1009	{"text": "“Indeed!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1011	lexical	\N	\N	1010	{"text": "And anyone else?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1012	lexical	\N	\N	1011	{"text": "“There were many insignificant sums to individuals, and a large number of public charities.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1013	lexical	\N	\N	1012	{"text": "The residue all went to Sir Henry.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1014	lexical	\N	\N	1013	{"text": "“And how much was the residue?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1015	lexical	\N	\N	1014	{"text": "“Seven hundred and forty thousand pounds.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1016	lexical	\N	\N	1015	{"text": "Holmes raised his eyebrows in surprise.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1017	lexical	\N	\N	1016	{"text": "“I had no idea that so gigantic a sum was involved,” said he.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1018	lexical	\N	\N	1017	{"text": "“Sir Charles had the reputation of being rich, but we did not know how very rich he was until we came to examine his securities.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1019	lexical	\N	\N	1018	{"text": "The total value of the estate was close on to a million.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1020	lexical	\N	\N	1019	{"text": "“Dear me!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1021	lexical	\N	\N	1020	{"text": "It is a stake for which a man might well play a desperate game.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1022	lexical	\N	\N	1021	{"text": "And one more question, Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1023	lexical	\N	\N	1022	{"text": "—who would inherit the estate?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1024	lexical	\N	\N	1023	{"text": "d to our young friend here—you will forgive the unpleasant hypothesis!—who would inherit the estate?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1025	lexical	\N	\N	1024	{"text": "“Since Rodger Baskerville, Sir Charles’s younger brother died unmarried, the estate would descend to the Desmonds, who are distant cousins.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1026	lexical	\N	\N	1025	{"text": "James Desmond is an elderly clergyman in Westmoreland.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1027	lexical	\N	\N	1026	{"text": "“Thank you.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1028	lexical	\N	\N	1027	{"text": "These details are all of great interest.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1029	lexical	\N	\N	1028	{"text": "Have you met Mr. James Desmond?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1030	lexical	\N	\N	1029	{"text": "“Yes; he once came down to visit Sir Charles.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1031	lexical	\N	\N	1030	{"text": "He is a man of venerable appearance and of saintly life.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1032	lexical	\N	\N	1031	{"text": "I remember that he refused to accept any settlement from Sir Charles, though he pressed it upon him.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1033	lexical	\N	\N	1032	{"text": "“And this man of simple tastes would be the heir to Sir Charles’s thousands.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1034	lexical	\N	\N	1033	{"text": "“He would be the heir to the estate because that is entailed.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1071	lexical	\N	\N	1070	{"text": "“Then on Saturday, unless you hear to the contrary, we shall meet at the ten-thirty train from Paddington.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1035	lexical	\N	\N	1034	{"text": "He would also be the heir to the money unless it were willed otherwise by the present owner, who can, of course, do what he likes with it.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1036	lexical	\N	\N	1035	{"text": "“And have you made your will, Sir Henry?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1037	lexical	\N	\N	1036	{"text": "“No, Mr. Holmes, I have not.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1038	lexical	\N	\N	1037	{"text": "I’ve had no time, for it was only yesterday that I learned how matters stood.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1039	lexical	\N	\N	1038	{"text": "But in any case I feel that the money should go with the title and estate.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1040	lexical	\N	\N	1039	{"text": "That was my poor uncle’s idea.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1041	lexical	\N	\N	1040	{"text": "How is the owner going to restore the glories of the Baskervilles if he has not money enough to keep up the property?", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1042	lexical	\N	\N	1041	{"text": "House, land, and dollars must go together.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1043	lexical	\N	\N	1042	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1044	lexical	\N	\N	1043	{"text": "Well, Sir Henry, I am of one mind with you as to the advisability of your going down to Devonshire without delay.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1045	lexical	\N	\N	1044	{"text": "There is only one provision which I must make.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1046	lexical	\N	\N	1045	{"text": "You certainly must not go alone.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1047	lexical	\N	\N	1046	{"text": "“Dr. Mortimer returns with me.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1048	lexical	\N	\N	1047	{"text": "“But Dr. Mortimer has his practice to attend to, and his house is miles away from yours.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1049	lexical	\N	\N	1048	{"text": "With all the goodwill in the world he may be unable to help you.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1050	lexical	\N	\N	1049	{"text": "No, Sir Henry, you must take with you someone, a trusty man, who will be always by your side.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1051	lexical	\N	\N	1050	{"text": "“Is it possible that you could come yourself, Mr. Holmes?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1052	lexical	\N	\N	1051	{"text": "“If matters came to a crisis I should endeavour to be present in person; but you can understand that, with my extensive consulting practice and with the constant appeals which reach me from many quarters, it is impossible for me to be absent from London for an indefinite time.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1053	lexical	\N	\N	1052	{"text": "At the present instant one of the most revered names in England is being besmirched by a blackmailer, and only I can stop a disastrous scandal.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1054	lexical	\N	\N	1053	{"text": "You will see how impossible it is for me to go to Dartmoor.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1055	lexical	\N	\N	1054	{"text": "“Whom would you recommend, then?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1056	lexical	\N	\N	1055	{"text": "Holmes laid his hand upon my arm.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1057	lexical	\N	\N	1056	{"text": "“If my friend would undertake it there is no man who is better worth having at your side when you are in a tight place.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1058	lexical	\N	\N	1057	{"text": "No one can say so more confidently than I.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1059	lexical	\N	\N	1058	{"text": "The proposition took me completely by surprise, but before I had time to answer, Baskerville seized me by the hand and wrung it heartily.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1060	lexical	\N	\N	1059	{"text": "“Well, now, that is real kind of you, Dr. Watson,” said he.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1061	lexical	\N	\N	1060	{"text": "“You see how it is with me, and you know just as much about the matter as I do.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1062	lexical	\N	\N	1061	{"text": "If you will come down to Baskerville Hall and see me through I’ll never forget it.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1063	lexical	\N	\N	1062	{"text": "The promise of adventure had always a fascination for me, and I was complimented by the words of Holmes and by the eagerness with which the baronet hailed me as a companion.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1064	lexical	\N	\N	1063	{"text": "“I will come, with pleasure,” said I.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1065	lexical	\N	\N	1064	{"text": "“I do not know how I could employ my time better.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1066	lexical	\N	\N	1065	{"text": "“And you will report very carefully to me,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1067	lexical	\N	\N	1066	{"text": "“When a crisis comes, as it will do, I will direct how you shall act.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1068	lexical	\N	\N	1067	{"text": "I suppose that by Saturday all might be ready?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1069	lexical	\N	\N	1068	{"text": "“Would that suit Dr. Watson?”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1070	lexical	\N	\N	1069	{"text": "“Perfectly.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1072	lexical	\N	\N	1071	{"text": "We had risen to depart when Baskerville gave a cry of triumph, and diving into one of the corners of the room he drew a brown boot from under a cabinet.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1073	lexical	\N	\N	1072	{"text": "“My missing boot!”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1074	lexical	\N	\N	1073	{"text": "he cried.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1075	lexical	\N	\N	1074	{"text": "“May all our difficulties vanish as easily!”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1076	lexical	\N	\N	1075	{"text": "said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1077	lexical	\N	\N	1076	{"text": "“But it is a very singular thing,” Dr. Mortimer remarked.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1078	lexical	\N	\N	1077	{"text": "“I searched this room carefully before lunch.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1079	lexical	\N	\N	1078	{"text": "“And so did I,” said Baskerville.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1080	lexical	\N	\N	1079	{"text": "“Every inch of it.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1081	lexical	\N	\N	1080	{"text": "“There was certainly no boot in it then.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1082	lexical	\N	\N	1081	{"text": "“In that case the waiter must have placed it there while we were lunching.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1083	lexical	\N	\N	1082	{"text": "The German was sent for but professed to know nothing of the matter, nor could any inquiry clear it up.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1084	lexical	\N	\N	1083	{"text": "Another item had been added to that constant and apparently purposeless series of small mysteries which had succeeded each other so rapidly.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1085	lexical	\N	\N	1084	{"text": "Setting aside the whole grim story of Sir Charles’s death, we had a line of inexplicable incidents all within the limits of two days, which included the receipt of the printed letter, the black-bearded spy in the hansom, the loss of the new brown boot, the loss of the old black boot, and now the return of the new brown boot.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1086	lexical	\N	\N	1085	{"text": "Holmes sat in silence in the cab as we drove back to Baker Street, and I knew from his drawn brows and keen face that his mind, like my own, was busy in endeavouring to frame some scheme into which all these strange and apparently disconnected episodes could be fitted.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1087	lexical	\N	\N	1086	{"text": "All afternoon and late into the evening he sat lost in tobacco and thought.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1088	lexical	\N	\N	1087	{"text": "Just before dinner two telegrams were handed in.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1089	lexical	\N	\N	1088	{"text": "The first ran:", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1090	lexical	\N	\N	1089	{"text": "Have just heard that Barrymore is at the Hall.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1091	lexical	\N	\N	1090	{"text": "BASKERVILLE.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1092	lexical	\N	\N	1091	{"text": "The second:", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1093	lexical	\N	\N	1092	{"text": "Visited twenty-three hotels as directed, but sorry to report unable to trace cut sheet of _Times_.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1094	lexical	\N	\N	1093	{"text": "CARTWRIGHT.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1095	lexical	\N	\N	1094	{"text": "“There go two of my threads, Watson.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1096	lexical	\N	\N	1095	{"text": "There is nothing more stimulating than a case where everything goes against you.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1097	lexical	\N	\N	1096	{"text": "We must cast round for another scent.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1098	lexical	\N	\N	1097	{"text": "“We have still the cabman who drove the spy.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1099	lexical	\N	\N	1098	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1100	lexical	\N	\N	1099	{"text": "I have wired to get his name and address from the Official Registry.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1101	lexical	\N	\N	1100	{"text": "I should not be surprised if this were an answer to my question.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1102	lexical	\N	\N	1101	{"text": "The ring at the bell proved to be something even more satisfactory than an answer, however, for the door opened and a rough-looking fellow entered who was evidently the man himself.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1103	lexical	\N	\N	1102	{"text": "“I got a message from the head office that a gent at this address had been inquiring for No.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1104	lexical	\N	\N	1103	{"text": "2704,” said he.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1105	lexical	\N	\N	1104	{"text": "“I’ve driven my cab this seven years and never a word of complaint.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1106	lexical	\N	\N	1105	{"text": "I came here straight from the Yard to ask you to your face what you had against me.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1107	lexical	\N	\N	1106	{"text": "“I have nothing in the world against you, my good man,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1147	lexical	\N	\N	1146	{"text": "“This very door,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1108	lexical	\N	\N	1107	{"text": "“On the contrary, I have half a sovereign for you if you will give me a clear answer to my questions.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1109	lexical	\N	\N	1108	{"text": "“Well, I’ve had a good day and no mistake,” said the cabman with a grin.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1110	lexical	\N	\N	1109	{"text": "“What was it you wanted to ask, sir?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1111	lexical	\N	\N	1110	{"text": "“First of all your name and address, in case I want you again.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1112	lexical	\N	\N	1111	{"text": "“John Clayton, 3 Turpey Street, the Borough.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1113	lexical	\N	\N	1112	{"text": "My cab is out of Shipley’s Yard, near Waterloo Station.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1114	lexical	\N	\N	1113	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes made a note of it.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1115	lexical	\N	\N	1114	{"text": "“Now, Clayton, tell me all about the fare who came and watched this house at ten o’clock this morning and afterwards followed the two gentlemen down Regent Street.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1116	lexical	\N	\N	1115	{"text": "The man looked surprised and a little embarrassed.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1117	lexical	\N	\N	1116	{"text": "“Why, there’s no good my telling you things, for you seem to know as much as I do already,” said he.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1118	lexical	\N	\N	1117	{"text": "“The truth is that the gentleman told me that he was a detective and that I was to say nothing about him to anyone.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1119	lexical	\N	\N	1118	{"text": "“My good fellow; this is a very serious business, and you may find yourself in a pretty bad position if you try to hide anything from me.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1120	lexical	\N	\N	1119	{"text": "You say that your fare told you that he was a detective?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1121	lexical	\N	\N	1120	{"text": "“Yes, he did.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1122	lexical	\N	\N	1121	{"text": "“When did he say this?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1123	lexical	\N	\N	1122	{"text": "“When he left me.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1124	lexical	\N	\N	1123	{"text": "“Did he say anything more?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1125	lexical	\N	\N	1124	{"text": "“He mentioned his name.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1126	lexical	\N	\N	1125	{"text": "Holmes cast a swift glance of triumph at me.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1127	lexical	\N	\N	1126	{"text": "“Oh, he mentioned his name, did he?", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1128	lexical	\N	\N	1127	{"text": "That was imprudent.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1129	lexical	\N	\N	1128	{"text": "What was the name that he mentioned?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1130	lexical	\N	\N	1129	{"text": "“His name,” said the cabman, “was Mr. Sherlock Holmes.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1131	lexical	\N	\N	1130	{"text": "Never have I seen my friend more completely taken aback than by the cabman’s reply.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1132	lexical	\N	\N	1131	{"text": "For an instant he sat in silent amazement.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1133	lexical	\N	\N	1132	{"text": "Then he burst into a hearty laugh.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1134	lexical	\N	\N	1133	{"text": "“A touch, Watson—an undeniable touch!”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1135	lexical	\N	\N	1134	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1136	lexical	\N	\N	1135	{"text": "“I feel a foil as quick and supple as my own.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1137	lexical	\N	\N	1136	{"text": "He got home upon me very prettily that time.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1138	lexical	\N	\N	1137	{"text": "So his name was Sherlock Holmes, was it?”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1139	lexical	\N	\N	1138	{"text": "“Yes, sir, that was the gentleman’s name.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1140	lexical	\N	\N	1139	{"text": "“Excellent!", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1141	lexical	\N	\N	1140	{"text": "Tell me where you picked him up and all that occurred.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1142	lexical	\N	\N	1141	{"text": "“He hailed me at half-past nine in Trafalgar Square.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1143	lexical	\N	\N	1142	{"text": "He said that he was a detective, and he offered me two guineas if I would do exactly what he wanted all day and ask no questions.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1144	lexical	\N	\N	1143	{"text": "I was glad enough to agree.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1145	lexical	\N	\N	1144	{"text": "First we drove down to the Northumberland Hotel and waited there until two gentlemen came out and took a cab from the rank.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1146	lexical	\N	\N	1145	{"text": "We followed their cab until it pulled up somewhere near here.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1148	lexical	\N	\N	1147	{"text": "“Well, I couldn’t be sure of that, but I dare say my fare knew all about it.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1149	lexical	\N	\N	1148	{"text": "We pulled up halfway down the street and waited an hour and a half.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1150	lexical	\N	\N	1149	{"text": "Then the two gentlemen passed us, walking, and we followed down Baker Street and along—”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1151	lexical	\N	\N	1150	{"text": "“I know,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1152	lexical	\N	\N	1151	{"text": "“Until we got three-quarters down Regent Street.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1153	lexical	\N	\N	1152	{"text": "Then my gentleman threw up the trap, and he cried that I should drive right away to Waterloo Station as hard as I could go.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1154	lexical	\N	\N	1153	{"text": "I whipped up the mare and we were there under the ten minutes.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1155	lexical	\N	\N	1154	{"text": "Then he paid up his two guineas, like a good one, and away he went into the station.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1156	lexical	\N	\N	1155	{"text": "Only just as he was leaving he turned round and he said: ‘It might interest you to know that you have been driving Mr. Sherlock Holmes.’", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1157	lexical	\N	\N	1156	{"text": "That’s how I come to know the name.”", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1158	lexical	\N	\N	1157	{"text": "“I see.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1159	lexical	\N	\N	1158	{"text": "And you saw no more of him?”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1160	lexical	\N	\N	1159	{"text": "“Not after he went into the station.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1161	lexical	\N	\N	1160	{"text": "“And how would you describe Mr. Sherlock Holmes?”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1162	lexical	\N	\N	1161	{"text": "The cabman scratched his head.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1163	lexical	\N	\N	1162	{"text": "“Well, he wasn’t altogether such an easy gentleman to describe.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1164	lexical	\N	\N	1163	{"text": "I’d put him at forty years of age, and he was of a middle height, two or three inches shorter than you, sir.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1165	lexical	\N	\N	1164	{"text": "He was dressed like a toff, and he had a black beard, cut square at the end, and a pale face.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1166	lexical	\N	\N	1165	{"text": "I don’t know as I could say more than that.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1167	lexical	\N	\N	1166	{"text": "“Colour of his eyes?”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1168	lexical	\N	\N	1167	{"text": "“No, I can’t say that.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1169	lexical	\N	\N	1168	{"text": "“Nothing more that you can remember?”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1170	lexical	\N	\N	1169	{"text": "“No, sir; nothing.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1171	lexical	\N	\N	1170	{"text": "“Well, then, here is your half-sovereign.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1172	lexical	\N	\N	1171	{"text": "There’s another one waiting for you if you can bring any more information.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1173	lexical	\N	\N	1172	{"text": "Good-night!”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1174	lexical	\N	\N	1173	{"text": "“Good-night, sir, and thank you!”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1175	lexical	\N	\N	1174	{"text": "John Clayton departed chuckling, and Holmes turned to me with a shrug of his shoulders and a rueful smile.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1176	lexical	\N	\N	1175	{"text": "“Snap goes our third thread, and we end where we began,” said he.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1177	lexical	\N	\N	1176	{"text": "“The cunning rascal!", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1178	lexical	\N	\N	1177	{"text": "He knew our number, knew that Sir Henry Baskerville had consulted me, spotted who I was in Regent Street, conjectured that I had got the number of the cab and would lay my hands on the driver, and so sent back this audacious message.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1179	lexical	\N	\N	1178	{"text": "I tell you, Watson, this time we have got a foeman who is worthy of our steel.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1180	lexical	\N	\N	1179	{"text": "I’ve been checkmated in London.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1181	lexical	\N	\N	1180	{"text": "I can only wish you better luck in Devonshire.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1182	lexical	\N	\N	1181	{"text": "But I’m not easy in my mind about it.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1183	lexical	\N	\N	1182	{"text": "“About what?”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1184	lexical	\N	\N	1183	{"text": "“About sending you.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1185	lexical	\N	\N	1184	{"text": "It’s an ugly business, Watson, an ugly dangerous business, and the more I see of it the less I like it.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1526	lexical	\N	\N	1525	{"text": "We came shortly after Sir Charles settled.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1186	lexical	\N	\N	1185	{"text": "Yes, my dear fellow, you may laugh, but I give you my word that I shall be very glad to have you back safe and sound in Baker Street once more.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1187	lexical	\N	\N	1186	{"text": "Chapter 6.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1188	lexical	\N	\N	1187	{"text": "Baskerville Hall", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1189	lexical	\N	\N	1188	{"text": "Sir Henry Baskerville and Dr. Mortimer were ready upon the appointed day, and we started as arranged for Devonshire.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1190	lexical	\N	\N	1189	{"text": "Mr. Sherlock Holmes drove with me to the station and gave me his last parting injunctions and advice.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1191	lexical	\N	\N	1190	{"text": "“I will not bias your mind by suggesting theories or suspicions, Watson,” said he; “I wish you simply to report facts in the fullest possible manner to me, and you can leave me to do the theorizing.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1192	lexical	\N	\N	1191	{"text": "“What sort of facts?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1193	lexical	\N	\N	1192	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1194	lexical	\N	\N	1193	{"text": "“Anything which may seem to have a bearing however indirect upon the case, and especially the relations between young Baskerville and his neighbours or any fresh particulars concerning the death of Sir Charles.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1195	lexical	\N	\N	1194	{"text": "I have made some inquiries myself in the last few days, but the results have, I fear, been negative.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1196	lexical	\N	\N	1195	{"text": "One thing only appears to be certain, and that is that Mr. James Desmond, who is the next heir, is an elderly gentleman of a very amiable disposition, so that this persecution does not arise from him.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1197	lexical	\N	\N	1196	{"text": "I really think that we may eliminate him entirely from our calculations.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1198	lexical	\N	\N	1197	{"text": "There remain the people who will actually surround Sir Henry Baskerville upon the moor.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1199	lexical	\N	\N	1198	{"text": "“Would it not be well in the first place to get rid of this Barrymore couple?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1200	lexical	\N	\N	1199	{"text": "“By no means.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1201	lexical	\N	\N	1200	{"text": "You could not make a greater mistake.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1202	lexical	\N	\N	1201	{"text": "If they are innocent it would be a cruel injustice, and if they are guilty we should be giving up all chance of bringing it home to them.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1203	lexical	\N	\N	1202	{"text": "No, no, we will preserve them upon our list of suspects.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1204	lexical	\N	\N	1203	{"text": "Then there is a groom at the Hall, if I remember right.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1205	lexical	\N	\N	1204	{"text": "There are two moorland farmers.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1206	lexical	\N	\N	1205	{"text": "There is our friend Dr. Mortimer, whom I believe to be entirely honest, and there is his wife, of whom we know nothing.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1207	lexical	\N	\N	1206	{"text": "There is this naturalist, Stapleton, and there is his sister, who is said to be a young lady of attractions.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1208	lexical	\N	\N	1207	{"text": "There is Mr. Frankland, of Lafter Hall, who is also an unknown factor, and there are one or two other neighbours.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1209	lexical	\N	\N	1208	{"text": "These are the folk who must be your very special study.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1210	lexical	\N	\N	1209	{"text": "“I will do my best.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1211	lexical	\N	\N	1210	{"text": "“You have arms, I suppose?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1212	lexical	\N	\N	1211	{"text": "“Yes, I thought it as well to take them.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1213	lexical	\N	\N	1212	{"text": "“Most certainly.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1214	lexical	\N	\N	1213	{"text": "Keep your revolver near you night and day, and never relax your precautions.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1215	lexical	\N	\N	1214	{"text": "Our friends had already secured a first-class carriage and were waiting for us upon the platform.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1216	lexical	\N	\N	1215	{"text": "“No, we have no news of any kind,” said Dr. Mortimer in answer to my friend’s questions.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1217	lexical	\N	\N	1216	{"text": "“I can swear to one thing, and that is that we have not been shadowed during the last two days.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1218	lexical	\N	\N	1217	{"text": "We have never gone out without keeping a sharp watch, and no one could have escaped our notice.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1219	lexical	\N	\N	1218	{"text": "“You have always kept together, I presume?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1220	lexical	\N	\N	1219	{"text": "“Except yesterday afternoon.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1566	lexical	\N	\N	1565	{"text": "“Halloa!”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1221	lexical	\N	\N	1220	{"text": "I usually give up one day to pure amusement when I come to town, so I spent it at the Museum of the College of Surgeons.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1222	lexical	\N	\N	1221	{"text": "“And I went to look at the folk in the park,” said Baskerville.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1223	lexical	\N	\N	1222	{"text": "“But we had no trouble of any kind.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1224	lexical	\N	\N	1223	{"text": "“It was imprudent, all the same,” said Holmes, shaking his head and looking very grave.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1225	lexical	\N	\N	1224	{"text": "“I beg, Sir Henry, that you will not go about alone.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1226	lexical	\N	\N	1225	{"text": "Some great misfortune will befall you if you do.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1227	lexical	\N	\N	1226	{"text": "Did you get your other boot?”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1228	lexical	\N	\N	1227	{"text": "“No, sir, it is gone forever.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1229	lexical	\N	\N	1228	{"text": "“Indeed.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1230	lexical	\N	\N	1229	{"text": "That is very interesting.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1231	lexical	\N	\N	1230	{"text": "Well, good-bye,” he added as the train began to glide down the platform.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1232	lexical	\N	\N	1231	{"text": "“Bear in mind, Sir Henry, one of the phrases in that queer old legend which Dr. Mortimer has read to us, and avoid the moor in those hours of darkness when the powers of evil are exalted.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1233	lexical	\N	\N	1232	{"text": "I looked back at the platform when we had left it far behind and saw the tall, austere figure of Holmes standing motionless and gazing after us.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1234	lexical	\N	\N	1233	{"text": "The journey was a swift and pleasant one, and I spent it in making the more intimate acquaintance of my two companions and in playing with Dr. Mortimer’s spaniel.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1235	lexical	\N	\N	1234	{"text": "In a very few hours the brown earth had become ruddy, the brick had changed to granite, and red cows grazed in well-hedged fields where the lush grasses and more luxuriant vegetation spoke of a richer, if a damper, climate.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1236	lexical	\N	\N	1235	{"text": "Young Baskerville stared eagerly out of the window and cried aloud with delight as he recognized the familiar features of the Devon scenery.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1237	lexical	\N	\N	1236	{"text": "“I’ve been over a good part of the world since I left it, Dr. Watson,” said he; “but I have never seen a place to compare with it.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1238	lexical	\N	\N	1237	{"text": "“I never saw a Devonshire man who did not swear by his county,” I remarked.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1239	lexical	\N	\N	1238	{"text": "“It depends upon the breed of men quite as much as on the county,” said Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1240	lexical	\N	\N	1239	{"text": "“A glance at our friend here reveals the rounded head of the Celt, which carries inside it the Celtic enthusiasm and power of attachment.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1241	lexical	\N	\N	1240	{"text": "Poor Sir Charles’s head was of a very rare type, half Gaelic, half Ivernian in its characteristics.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1242	lexical	\N	\N	1241	{"text": "But you were very young when you last saw Baskerville Hall, were you not?”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1243	lexical	\N	\N	1242	{"text": "“I was a boy in my teens at the time of my father’s death and had never seen the Hall, for he lived in a little cottage on the South Coast.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1244	lexical	\N	\N	1243	{"text": "Thence I went straight to a friend in America.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1245	lexical	\N	\N	1244	{"text": "I tell you it is all as new to me as it is to Dr. Watson, and I’m as keen as possible to see the moor.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1246	lexical	\N	\N	1245	{"text": "“Are you?", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1247	lexical	\N	\N	1246	{"text": "Then your wish is easily granted, for there is your first sight of the moor,” said Dr. Mortimer, pointing out of the carriage window.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1248	lexical	\N	\N	1247	{"text": "Over the green squares of the fields and the low curve of a wood there rose in the distance a grey, melancholy hill, with a strange jagged summit, dim and vague in the distance, like some fantastic landscape in a dream.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1249	lexical	\N	\N	1248	{"text": "Baskerville sat for a long time, his eyes fixed upon it, and I read upon his eager face how much it meant to him, this first sight of that strange spot where the men of his blood had held sway so long and left their mark so deep.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1250	lexical	\N	\N	1249	{"text": "There he sat, with his tweed suit and his American accent, in the corner of a prosaic railway-carriage, and yet as I looked at his dark and expressive face I felt more than ever how true a descendant he was of that long line of high-blooded, fiery, and masterful men.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1251	lexical	\N	\N	1250	{"text": "There were pride, valour, and strength in his thick brows, his sensitive nostrils, and his large hazel eyes.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1352	lexical	\N	\N	1351	{"text": "“Do you mean that your wife and you wish to leave?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1252	lexical	\N	\N	1251	{"text": "If on that forbidding moor a difficult and dangerous quest should lie before us, this was at least a comrade for whom one might venture to take a risk with the certainty that he would bravely share it.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1253	lexical	\N	\N	1252	{"text": "The train pulled up at a small wayside station and we all descended.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1254	lexical	\N	\N	1253	{"text": "Outside, beyond the low, white fence, a wagonette with a pair of cobs was waiting.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1255	lexical	\N	\N	1254	{"text": "Our coming was evidently a great event, for station-master and porters clustered round us to carry out our luggage.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1256	lexical	\N	\N	1255	{"text": "It was a sweet, simple country spot, but I was surprised to observe that by the gate there stood two soldierly men in dark uniforms who leaned upon their short rifles and glanced keenly at us as we passed.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1257	lexical	\N	\N	1256	{"text": "The coachman, a hard-faced, gnarled little fellow, saluted Sir Henry Baskerville, and in a few minutes we were flying swiftly down the broad, white road.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1258	lexical	\N	\N	1257	{"text": "Rolling pasture lands curved upward on either side of us, and old gabled houses peeped out from amid the thick green foliage, but behind the peaceful and sunlit countryside there rose ever, dark against the evening sky, the long, gloomy curve of the moor, broken by the jagged and sinister hills.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1259	lexical	\N	\N	1258	{"text": "The wagonette swung round into a side road, and we curved upward through deep lanes worn by centuries of wheels, high banks on either side, heavy with dripping moss and fleshy hart’s-tongue ferns.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1260	lexical	\N	\N	1259	{"text": "Bronzing bracken and mottled bramble gleamed in the light of the sinking sun.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1261	lexical	\N	\N	1260	{"text": "Still steadily rising, we passed over a narrow granite bridge and skirted a noisy stream which gushed swiftly down, foaming and roaring amid the grey boulders.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1262	lexical	\N	\N	1261	{"text": "Both road and stream wound up through a valley dense with scrub oak and fir.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1263	lexical	\N	\N	1262	{"text": "At every turn Baskerville gave an exclamation of delight, looking eagerly about him and asking countless questions.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1264	lexical	\N	\N	1263	{"text": "To his eyes all seemed beautiful, but to me a tinge of melancholy lay upon the countryside, which bore so clearly the mark of the waning year.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1265	lexical	\N	\N	1264	{"text": "Yellow leaves carpeted the lanes and fluttered down upon us as we passed.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1266	lexical	\N	\N	1265	{"text": "The rattle of our wheels died away as we drove through drifts of rotting vegetation—sad gifts, as it seemed to me, for Nature to throw before the carriage of the returning heir of the Baskervilles.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1267	lexical	\N	\N	1266	{"text": "“Halloa!”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1268	lexical	\N	\N	1267	{"text": "cried Dr. Mortimer, “what is this?”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1269	lexical	\N	\N	1268	{"text": "A steep curve of heath-clad land, an outlying spur of the moor, lay in front of us.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1270	lexical	\N	\N	1269	{"text": "On the summit, hard and clear like an equestrian statue upon its pedestal, was a mounted soldier, dark and stern, his rifle poised ready over his forearm.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1271	lexical	\N	\N	1270	{"text": "He was watching the road along which we travelled.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1272	lexical	\N	\N	1271	{"text": "“What is this, Perkins?”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1273	lexical	\N	\N	1272	{"text": "asked Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1274	lexical	\N	\N	1273	{"text": "Our driver half turned in his seat.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1275	lexical	\N	\N	1274	{"text": "“There’s a convict escaped from Princetown, sir.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1276	lexical	\N	\N	1275	{"text": "He’s been out three days now, and the warders watch every road and every station, but they’ve had no sight of him yet.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1277	lexical	\N	\N	1276	{"text": "The farmers about here don’t like it, sir, and that’s a fact.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1278	lexical	\N	\N	1277	{"text": "“Well, I understand that they get five pounds if they can give information.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1279	lexical	\N	\N	1278	{"text": "“Yes, sir, but the chance of five pounds is but a poor thing compared to the chance of having your throat cut.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1280	lexical	\N	\N	1279	{"text": "You see, it isn’t like any ordinary convict.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1281	lexical	\N	\N	1280	{"text": "This is a man that would stick at nothing.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1282	lexical	\N	\N	1281	{"text": "“Who is he, then?”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1283	lexical	\N	\N	1282	{"text": "“It is Selden, the Notting Hill murderer.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1353	lexical	\N	\N	1352	{"text": "“Only when it is quite convenient to you, sir.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1284	lexical	\N	\N	1283	{"text": "I remembered the case well, for it was one in which Holmes had taken an interest on account of the peculiar ferocity of the crime and the wanton brutality which had marked all the actions of the assassin.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1285	lexical	\N	\N	1284	{"text": "The commutation of his death sentence had been due to some doubts as to his complete sanity, so atrocious was his conduct.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1286	lexical	\N	\N	1285	{"text": "Our wagonette had topped a rise and in front of us rose the huge expanse of the moor, mottled with gnarled and craggy cairns and tors.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1287	lexical	\N	\N	1286	{"text": "A cold wind swept down from it and set us shivering.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1288	lexical	\N	\N	1287	{"text": "Somewhere there, on that desolate plain, was lurking this fiendish man, hiding in a burrow like a wild beast, his heart full of malignancy against the whole race which had cast him out.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1289	lexical	\N	\N	1288	{"text": "It needed but this to complete the grim suggestiveness of the barren waste, the chilling wind, and the darkling sky.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1290	lexical	\N	\N	1289	{"text": "Even Baskerville fell silent and pulled his overcoat more closely around him.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1291	lexical	\N	\N	1290	{"text": "We had left the fertile country behind and beneath us.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1292	lexical	\N	\N	1291	{"text": "We looked back on it now, the slanting rays of a low sun turning the streams to threads of gold and glowing on the red earth new turned by the plough and the broad tangle of the woodlands.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1293	lexical	\N	\N	1292	{"text": "The road in front of us grew bleaker and wilder over huge russet and olive slopes, sprinkled with giant boulders.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1294	lexical	\N	\N	1293	{"text": "Now and then we passed a moorland cottage, walled and roofed with stone, with no creeper to break its harsh outline.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1295	lexical	\N	\N	1294	{"text": "Suddenly we looked down into a cuplike depression, patched with stunted oaks and firs which had been twisted and bent by the fury of years of storm.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1296	lexical	\N	\N	1295	{"text": "Two high, narrow towers rose over the trees.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1297	lexical	\N	\N	1296	{"text": "The driver pointed with his whip.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1298	lexical	\N	\N	1297	{"text": "“Baskerville Hall,” said he.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1299	lexical	\N	\N	1298	{"text": "Its master had risen and was staring with flushed cheeks and shining eyes.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1300	lexical	\N	\N	1299	{"text": "A few minutes later we had reached the lodge-gates, a maze of fantastic tracery in wrought iron, with weather-bitten pillars on either side, blotched with lichens, and surmounted by the boars’ heads of the Baskervilles.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1301	lexical	\N	\N	1300	{"text": "The lodge was a ruin of black granite and bared ribs of rafters, but facing it was a new building, half constructed, the first fruit of Sir Charles’s South African gold.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1302	lexical	\N	\N	1301	{"text": "Through the gateway we passed into the avenue, where the wheels were again hushed amid the leaves, and the old trees shot their branches in a sombre tunnel over our heads.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1303	lexical	\N	\N	1302	{"text": "Baskerville shuddered as he looked up the long, dark drive to where the house glimmered like a ghost at the farther end.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1304	lexical	\N	\N	1303	{"text": "“Was it here?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1305	lexical	\N	\N	1304	{"text": "he asked in a low voice.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1306	lexical	\N	\N	1305	{"text": "“No, no, the yew alley is on the other side.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1307	lexical	\N	\N	1306	{"text": "The young heir glanced round with a gloomy face.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1308	lexical	\N	\N	1307	{"text": "“It’s no wonder my uncle felt as if trouble were coming on him in such a place as this,” said he.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1309	lexical	\N	\N	1308	{"text": "“It’s enough to scare any man.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1310	lexical	\N	\N	1309	{"text": "I’ll have a row of electric lamps up here inside of six months, and you won’t know it again, with a thousand candle-power Swan and Edison right here in front of the hall door.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1311	lexical	\N	\N	1310	{"text": "The avenue opened into a broad expanse of turf, and the house lay before us.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1312	lexical	\N	\N	1311	{"text": "In the fading light I could see that the centre was a heavy block of building from which a porch projected.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1313	lexical	\N	\N	1312	{"text": "The whole front was draped in ivy, with a patch clipped bare here and there where a window or a coat of arms broke through the dark veil.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1314	lexical	\N	\N	1313	{"text": "From this central block rose the twin towers, ancient, crenelated, and pierced with many loopholes.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1315	lexical	\N	\N	1314	{"text": "To right and left of the turrets were more modern wings of black granite.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1316	lexical	\N	\N	1315	{"text": "A dull light shone through heavy mullioned windows, and from the high chimneys which rose from the steep, high-angled roof there sprang a single black column of smoke.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1317	lexical	\N	\N	1316	{"text": "“Welcome, Sir Henry!", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1318	lexical	\N	\N	1317	{"text": "Welcome to Baskerville Hall!”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1319	lexical	\N	\N	1318	{"text": "A tall man had stepped from the shadow of the porch to open the door of the wagonette.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1320	lexical	\N	\N	1319	{"text": "The figure of a woman was silhouetted against the yellow light of the hall.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1321	lexical	\N	\N	1320	{"text": "She came out and helped the man to hand down our bags.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1322	lexical	\N	\N	1321	{"text": "“You don’t mind my driving straight home, Sir Henry?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1323	lexical	\N	\N	1322	{"text": "said Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1324	lexical	\N	\N	1323	{"text": "“My wife is expecting me.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1325	lexical	\N	\N	1324	{"text": "“Surely you will stay and have some dinner?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1326	lexical	\N	\N	1325	{"text": "“No, I must go.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1327	lexical	\N	\N	1326	{"text": "I shall probably find some work awaiting me.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1328	lexical	\N	\N	1327	{"text": "I would stay to show you over the house, but Barrymore will be a better guide than I.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1329	lexical	\N	\N	1328	{"text": "Good-bye, and never hesitate night or day to send for me if I can be of service.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1330	lexical	\N	\N	1329	{"text": "The wheels died away down the drive while Sir Henry and I turned into the hall, and the door clanged heavily behind us.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1331	lexical	\N	\N	1330	{"text": "It was a fine apartment in which we found ourselves, large, lofty, and heavily raftered with huge baulks of age-blackened oak.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1332	lexical	\N	\N	1331	{"text": "In the great old-fashioned fireplace behind the high iron dogs a log-fire crackled and snapped.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1333	lexical	\N	\N	1332	{"text": "Sir Henry and I held out our hands to it, for we were numb from our long drive.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1334	lexical	\N	\N	1333	{"text": "Then we gazed round us at the high, thin window of old stained glass, the oak panelling, the stags’ heads, the coats of arms upon the walls, all dim and sombre in the subdued light of the central lamp.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1335	lexical	\N	\N	1334	{"text": "“It’s just as I imagined it,” said Sir Henry.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1336	lexical	\N	\N	1335	{"text": "“Is it not the very picture of an old family home?", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1337	lexical	\N	\N	1336	{"text": "To think that this should be the same hall in which for five hundred years my people have lived.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1338	lexical	\N	\N	1337	{"text": "It strikes me solemn to think of it.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1339	lexical	\N	\N	1338	{"text": "I saw his dark face lit up with a boyish enthusiasm as he gazed about him.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1340	lexical	\N	\N	1339	{"text": "The light beat upon him where he stood, but long shadows trailed down the walls and hung like a black canopy above him.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1341	lexical	\N	\N	1340	{"text": "Barrymore had returned from taking our luggage to our rooms.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1342	lexical	\N	\N	1341	{"text": "He stood in front of us now with the subdued manner of a well-trained servant.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1343	lexical	\N	\N	1342	{"text": "He was a remarkable-looking man, tall, handsome, with a square black beard and pale, distinguished features.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1344	lexical	\N	\N	1343	{"text": "“Would you wish dinner to be served at once, sir?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1345	lexical	\N	\N	1344	{"text": "“Is it ready?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1346	lexical	\N	\N	1345	{"text": "“In a very few minutes, sir.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1347	lexical	\N	\N	1346	{"text": "You will find hot water in your rooms.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1348	lexical	\N	\N	1347	{"text": "My wife and I will be happy, Sir Henry, to stay with you until you have made your fresh arrangements, but you will understand that under the new conditions this house will require a considerable staff.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1349	lexical	\N	\N	1348	{"text": "“What new conditions?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1350	lexical	\N	\N	1349	{"text": "“I only meant, sir, that Sir Charles led a very retired life, and we were able to look after his wants.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1351	lexical	\N	\N	1350	{"text": "You would, naturally, wish to have more company, and so you will need changes in your household.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1354	lexical	\N	\N	1353	{"text": "“But your family have been with us for several generations, have they not?", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1355	lexical	\N	\N	1354	{"text": "I should be sorry to begin my life here by breaking an old family connection.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1356	lexical	\N	\N	1355	{"text": "I seemed to discern some signs of emotion upon the butler’s white face.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1357	lexical	\N	\N	1356	{"text": "“I feel that also, sir, and so does my wife.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1358	lexical	\N	\N	1357	{"text": "But to tell the truth, sir, we were both very much attached to Sir Charles, and his death gave us a shock and made these surroundings very painful to us.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1359	lexical	\N	\N	1358	{"text": "I fear that we shall never again be easy in our minds at Baskerville Hall.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1360	lexical	\N	\N	1359	{"text": "“But what do you intend to do?”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1361	lexical	\N	\N	1360	{"text": "“I have no doubt, sir, that we shall succeed in establishing ourselves in some business.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1362	lexical	\N	\N	1361	{"text": "Sir Charles’s generosity has given us the means to do so.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1363	lexical	\N	\N	1362	{"text": "And now, sir, perhaps I had best show you to your rooms.”", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1364	lexical	\N	\N	1363	{"text": "A square balustraded gallery ran round the top of the old hall, approached by a double stair.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1365	lexical	\N	\N	1364	{"text": "From this central point two long corridors extended the whole length of the building, from which all the bedrooms opened.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1366	lexical	\N	\N	1365	{"text": "My own was in the same wing as Baskerville’s and almost next door to it.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1367	lexical	\N	\N	1366	{"text": "These rooms appeared to be much more modern than the central part of the house, and the bright paper and numerous candles did something to remove the sombre impression which our arrival had left upon my mind.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1368	lexical	\N	\N	1367	{"text": "But the dining-room which opened out of the hall was a place of shadow and gloom.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1369	lexical	\N	\N	1368	{"text": "It was a long chamber with a step separating the daïs where the family sat from the lower portion reserved for their dependents.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1370	lexical	\N	\N	1369	{"text": "At one end a minstrel’s gallery overlooked it.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1371	lexical	\N	\N	1370	{"text": "Black beams shot across above our heads, with a smoke-darkened ceiling beyond them.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1372	lexical	\N	\N	1371	{"text": "With rows of flaring torches to light it up, and the colour and rude hilarity of an old-time banquet, it might have softened; but now, when two black-clothed gentlemen sat in the little circle of light thrown by a shaded lamp, one’s voice became hushed and one’s spirit subdued.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1373	lexical	\N	\N	1372	{"text": "A dim line of ancestors, in every variety of dress, from the Elizabethan knight to the buck of the Regency, stared down upon us and daunted us by their silent company.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1374	lexical	\N	\N	1373	{"text": "We talked little, and I for one was glad when the meal was over and we were able to retire into the modern billiard-room and smoke a cigarette.", "section": "section_35", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1375	lexical	\N	\N	1374	{"text": "“My word, it isn’t a very cheerful place,” said Sir Henry.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1376	lexical	\N	\N	1375	{"text": "“I suppose one can tone down to it, but I feel a bit out of the picture at present.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1377	lexical	\N	\N	1376	{"text": "I don’t wonder that my uncle got a little jumpy if he lived all alone in such a house as this.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1378	lexical	\N	\N	1377	{"text": "However, if it suits you, we will retire early tonight, and perhaps things may seem more cheerful in the morning.”", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1379	lexical	\N	\N	1378	{"text": "I drew aside my curtains before I went to bed and looked out from my window.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1380	lexical	\N	\N	1379	{"text": "It opened upon the grassy space which lay in front of the hall door.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1381	lexical	\N	\N	1380	{"text": "Beyond, two copses of trees moaned and swung in a rising wind.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1382	lexical	\N	\N	1381	{"text": "A half moon broke through the rifts of racing clouds.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1383	lexical	\N	\N	1382	{"text": "In its cold light I saw beyond the trees a broken fringe of rocks, and the long, low curve of the melancholy moor.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1384	lexical	\N	\N	1383	{"text": "I closed the curtain, feeling that my last impression was in keeping with the rest.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1385	lexical	\N	\N	1384	{"text": "And yet it was not quite the last.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1386	lexical	\N	\N	1385	{"text": "I found myself weary and yet wakeful, tossing restlessly from side to side, seeking for the sleep which would not come.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1387	lexical	\N	\N	1386	{"text": "Far away a chiming clock struck out the quarters of the hours, but otherwise a deathly silence lay upon the old house.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1388	lexical	\N	\N	1387	{"text": "And then suddenly, in the very dead of the night, there came a sound to my ears, clear, resonant, and unmistakable.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1389	lexical	\N	\N	1388	{"text": "It was the sob of a woman, the muffled, strangling gasp of one who is torn by an uncontrollable sorrow.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1390	lexical	\N	\N	1389	{"text": "I sat up in bed and listened intently.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1391	lexical	\N	\N	1390	{"text": "The noise could not have been far away and was certainly in the house.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1392	lexical	\N	\N	1391	{"text": "For half an hour I waited with every nerve on the alert, but there came no other sound save the chiming clock and the rustle of the ivy on the wall.", "section": "section_36", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1393	lexical	\N	\N	1392	{"text": "Chapter 7.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1394	lexical	\N	\N	1393	{"text": "The Stapletons of Merripit House", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1395	lexical	\N	\N	1394	{"text": "The fresh beauty of the following morning did something to efface from our minds the grim and grey impression which had been left upon both of us by our first experience of Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1396	lexical	\N	\N	1395	{"text": "As Sir Henry and I sat at breakfast the sunlight flooded in through the high mullioned windows, throwing watery patches of colour from the coats of arms which covered them.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1397	lexical	\N	\N	1396	{"text": "The dark panelling glowed like bronze in the golden rays, and it was hard to realise that this was indeed the chamber which had struck such a gloom into our souls upon the evening before.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1398	lexical	\N	\N	1397	{"text": "“I guess it is ourselves and not the house that we have to blame!”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1399	lexical	\N	\N	1398	{"text": "said the baronet.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1400	lexical	\N	\N	1399	{"text": "“We were tired with our journey and chilled by our drive, so we took a grey view of the place.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1401	lexical	\N	\N	1400	{"text": "Now we are fresh and well, so it is all cheerful once more.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1402	lexical	\N	\N	1401	{"text": "“And yet it was not entirely a question of imagination,” I answered.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1403	lexical	\N	\N	1402	{"text": "“Did you, for example, happen to hear someone, a woman I think, sobbing in the night?”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1404	lexical	\N	\N	1403	{"text": "“That is curious, for I did when I was half asleep fancy that I heard something of the sort.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1405	lexical	\N	\N	1404	{"text": "I waited quite a time, but there was no more of it, so I concluded that it was all a dream.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1406	lexical	\N	\N	1405	{"text": "“I heard it distinctly, and I am sure that it was really the sob of a woman.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1407	lexical	\N	\N	1406	{"text": "“We must ask about this right away.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1408	lexical	\N	\N	1407	{"text": "He rang the bell and asked Barrymore whether he could account for our experience.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1409	lexical	\N	\N	1408	{"text": "It seemed to me that the pallid features of the butler turned a shade paler still as he listened to his master’s question.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1410	lexical	\N	\N	1409	{"text": "“There are only two women in the house, Sir Henry,” he answered.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1411	lexical	\N	\N	1410	{"text": "“One is the scullery-maid, who sleeps in the other wing.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1412	lexical	\N	\N	1411	{"text": "The other is my wife, and I can answer for it that the sound could not have come from her.”", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1413	lexical	\N	\N	1412	{"text": "And yet he lied as he said it, for it chanced that after breakfast I met Mrs. Barrymore in the long corridor with the sun full upon her face.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1414	lexical	\N	\N	1413	{"text": "She was a large, impassive, heavy-featured woman with a stern set expression of mouth.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1415	lexical	\N	\N	1414	{"text": "But her telltale eyes were red and glanced at me from between swollen lids.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1416	lexical	\N	\N	1415	{"text": "It was she, then, who wept in the night, and if she did so her husband must know it.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1417	lexical	\N	\N	1416	{"text": "Yet he had taken the obvious risk of discovery in declaring that it was not so.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1418	lexical	\N	\N	1417	{"text": "Why had he done this?", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1419	lexical	\N	\N	1418	{"text": "And why did she weep so bitterly?", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1420	lexical	\N	\N	1419	{"text": "Already round this pale-faced, handsome, black-bearded man there was gathering an atmosphere of mystery and of gloom.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1421	lexical	\N	\N	1420	{"text": "It was he who had been the first to discover the body of Sir Charles, and we had only his word for all the circumstances which led up to the old man’s death.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1422	lexical	\N	\N	1421	{"text": "Was it possible that it was Barrymore, after all, whom we had seen in the cab in Regent Street?", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1423	lexical	\N	\N	1422	{"text": "The beard might well have been the same.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1424	lexical	\N	\N	1423	{"text": "The cabman had described a somewhat shorter man, but such an impression might easily have been erroneous.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1425	lexical	\N	\N	1424	{"text": "How could I settle the point forever?", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1426	lexical	\N	\N	1425	{"text": "Obviously the first thing to do was to see the Grimpen postmaster and find whether the test telegram had really been placed in Barrymore’s own hands.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1427	lexical	\N	\N	1426	{"text": "Be the answer what it might, I should at least have something to report to Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1428	lexical	\N	\N	1427	{"text": "Sir Henry had numerous papers to examine after breakfast, so that the time was propitious for my excursion.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1429	lexical	\N	\N	1428	{"text": "It was a pleasant walk of four miles along the edge of the moor, leading me at last to a small grey hamlet, in which two larger buildings, which proved to be the inn and the house of Dr. Mortimer, stood high above the rest.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1430	lexical	\N	\N	1429	{"text": "The postmaster, who was also the village grocer, had a clear recollection of the telegram.", "section": "section_37", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1431	lexical	\N	\N	1430	{"text": "“Certainly, sir,” said he, “I had the telegram delivered to Mr. Barrymore exactly as directed.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1432	lexical	\N	\N	1431	{"text": "“Who delivered it?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1433	lexical	\N	\N	1432	{"text": "“My boy here.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1434	lexical	\N	\N	1433	{"text": "James, you delivered that telegram to Mr. Barrymore at the Hall last week, did you not?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1435	lexical	\N	\N	1434	{"text": "“Yes, father, I delivered it.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1436	lexical	\N	\N	1435	{"text": "“Into his own hands?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1437	lexical	\N	\N	1436	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1438	lexical	\N	\N	1437	{"text": "“Well, he was up in the loft at the time, so that I could not put it into his own hands, but I gave it into Mrs. Barrymore’s hands, and she promised to deliver it at once.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1439	lexical	\N	\N	1438	{"text": "“Did you see Mr. Barrymore?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1440	lexical	\N	\N	1439	{"text": "“No, sir; I tell you he was in the loft.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1441	lexical	\N	\N	1440	{"text": "“If you didn’t see him, how do you know he was in the loft?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1442	lexical	\N	\N	1441	{"text": "“Well, surely his own wife ought to know where he is,” said the postmaster testily.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1443	lexical	\N	\N	1442	{"text": "“Didn’t he get the telegram?", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1444	lexical	\N	\N	1443	{"text": "If there is any mistake it is for Mr. Barrymore himself to complain.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1445	lexical	\N	\N	1444	{"text": "It seemed hopeless to pursue the inquiry any farther, but it was clear that in spite of Holmes’s ruse we had no proof that Barrymore had not been in London all the time.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1446	lexical	\N	\N	1445	{"text": "Suppose that it were so—suppose that the same man had been the last who had seen Sir Charles alive, and the first to dog the new heir when he returned to England.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1447	lexical	\N	\N	1446	{"text": "What then?", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1448	lexical	\N	\N	1447	{"text": "Was he the agent of others or had he some sinister design of his own?", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1449	lexical	\N	\N	1448	{"text": "What interest could he have in persecuting the Baskerville family?", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1450	lexical	\N	\N	1449	{"text": "I thought of the strange warning clipped out of the leading article of the _Times_.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1451	lexical	\N	\N	1450	{"text": "Was that his work or was it possibly the doing of someone who was bent upon counteracting his schemes?", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1452	lexical	\N	\N	1451	{"text": "The only conceivable motive was that which had been suggested by Sir Henry, that if the family could be scared away a comfortable and permanent home would be secured for the Barrymores.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1453	lexical	\N	\N	1452	{"text": "But surely such an explanation as that would be quite inadequate to account for the deep and subtle scheming which seemed to be weaving an invisible net round the young baronet.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1454	lexical	\N	\N	1453	{"text": "Holmes himself had said that no more complex case had come to him in all the long series of his sensational investigations.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1455	lexical	\N	\N	1454	{"text": "I prayed, as I walked back along the grey, lonely road, that my friend might soon be freed from his preoccupations and able to come down to take this heavy burden of responsibility from my shoulders.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1456	lexical	\N	\N	1455	{"text": "Suddenly my thoughts were interrupted by the sound of running feet behind me and by a voice which called me by name.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1457	lexical	\N	\N	1456	{"text": "I turned, expecting to see Dr. Mortimer, but to my surprise it was a stranger who was pursuing me.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1458	lexical	\N	\N	1457	{"text": "He was a small, slim, clean-shaven, prim-faced man, flaxen-haired and lean-jawed, between thirty and forty years of age, dressed in a grey suit and wearing a straw hat.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1459	lexical	\N	\N	1458	{"text": "A tin box for botanical specimens hung over his shoulder and he carried a green butterfly-net in one of his hands.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1460	lexical	\N	\N	1459	{"text": "“You will, I am sure, excuse my presumption, Dr. Watson,” said he as he came panting up to where I stood.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1461	lexical	\N	\N	1460	{"text": "“Here on the moor we are homely folk and do not wait for formal introductions.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1462	lexical	\N	\N	1461	{"text": "You may possibly have heard my name from our mutual friend, Mortimer.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1463	lexical	\N	\N	1462	{"text": "I am Stapleton, of Merripit House.”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1464	lexical	\N	\N	1463	{"text": "“Your net and box would have told me as much,” said I, “for I knew that Mr. Stapleton was a naturalist.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1465	lexical	\N	\N	1464	{"text": "But how did you know me?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1466	lexical	\N	\N	1465	{"text": "“I have been calling on Mortimer, and he pointed you out to me from the window of his surgery as you passed.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1467	lexical	\N	\N	1466	{"text": "As our road lay the same way I thought that I would overtake you and introduce myself.", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1468	lexical	\N	\N	1467	{"text": "I trust that Sir Henry is none the worse for his journey?”", "section": "section_38", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1469	lexical	\N	\N	1468	{"text": "“He is very well, thank you.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1470	lexical	\N	\N	1469	{"text": "“We were all rather afraid that after the sad death of Sir Charles the new baronet might refuse to live here.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1471	lexical	\N	\N	1470	{"text": "It is asking much of a wealthy man to come down and bury himself in a place of this kind, but I need not tell you that it means a very great deal to the countryside.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1472	lexical	\N	\N	1471	{"text": "Sir Henry has, I suppose, no superstitious fears in the matter?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1473	lexical	\N	\N	1472	{"text": "“I do not think that it is likely.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1474	lexical	\N	\N	1473	{"text": "“Of course you know the legend of the fiend dog which haunts the family?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1475	lexical	\N	\N	1474	{"text": "“I have heard it.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1476	lexical	\N	\N	1475	{"text": "“It is extraordinary how credulous the peasants are about here!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1477	lexical	\N	\N	1476	{"text": "Any number of them are ready to swear that they have seen such a creature upon the moor.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1478	lexical	\N	\N	1477	{"text": "He spoke with a smile, but I seemed to read in his eyes that he took the matter more seriously.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1479	lexical	\N	\N	1478	{"text": "“The story took a great hold upon the imagination of Sir Charles, and I have no doubt that it led to his tragic end.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1480	lexical	\N	\N	1479	{"text": "“But how?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1481	lexical	\N	\N	1480	{"text": "“His nerves were so worked up that the appearance of any dog might have had a fatal effect upon his diseased heart.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1482	lexical	\N	\N	1481	{"text": "I fancy that he really did see something of the kind upon that last night in the yew alley.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1483	lexical	\N	\N	1482	{"text": "I feared that some disaster might occur, for I was very fond of the old man, and I knew that his heart was weak.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1484	lexical	\N	\N	1483	{"text": "“How did you know that?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1485	lexical	\N	\N	1484	{"text": "“My friend Mortimer told me.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1486	lexical	\N	\N	1485	{"text": "“You think, then, that some dog pursued Sir Charles, and that he died of fright in consequence?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1487	lexical	\N	\N	1486	{"text": "“Have you any better explanation?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1488	lexical	\N	\N	1487	{"text": "“I have not come to any conclusion.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1489	lexical	\N	\N	1488	{"text": "“Has Mr. Sherlock Holmes?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1490	lexical	\N	\N	1489	{"text": "The words took away my breath for an instant but a glance at the placid face and steadfast eyes of my companion showed that no surprise was intended.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1491	lexical	\N	\N	1490	{"text": "“It is useless for us to pretend that we do not know you, Dr. Watson,” said he.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1492	lexical	\N	\N	1491	{"text": "“The records of your detective have reached us here, and you could not celebrate him without being known yourself.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1493	lexical	\N	\N	1492	{"text": "When Mortimer told me your name he could not deny your identity.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1494	lexical	\N	\N	1493	{"text": "If you are here, then it follows that Mr. Sherlock Holmes is interesting himself in the matter, and I am naturally curious to know what view he may take.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1495	lexical	\N	\N	1494	{"text": "“I am afraid that I cannot answer that question.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1496	lexical	\N	\N	1495	{"text": "“May I ask if he is going to honour us with a visit himself?”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1497	lexical	\N	\N	1496	{"text": "“He cannot leave town at present.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1498	lexical	\N	\N	1497	{"text": "He has other cases which engage his attention.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1499	lexical	\N	\N	1498	{"text": "“What a pity!", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1500	lexical	\N	\N	1499	{"text": "He might throw some light on that which is so dark to us.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1501	lexical	\N	\N	1500	{"text": "But as to your own researches, if there is any possible way in which I can be of service to you I trust that you will command me.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1502	lexical	\N	\N	1501	{"text": "If I had any indication of the nature of your suspicions or how you propose to investigate the case, I might perhaps even now give you some aid or advice.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1503	lexical	\N	\N	1502	{"text": "“I assure you that I am simply here upon a visit to my friend, Sir Henry, and that I need no help of any kind.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1504	lexical	\N	\N	1503	{"text": "“Excellent!”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1505	lexical	\N	\N	1504	{"text": "said Stapleton.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1506	lexical	\N	\N	1505	{"text": "“You are perfectly right to be wary and discreet.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1507	lexical	\N	\N	1506	{"text": "I am justly reproved for what I feel was an unjustifiable intrusion, and I promise you that I will not mention the matter again.”", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1508	lexical	\N	\N	1507	{"text": "We had come to a point where a narrow grassy path struck off from the road and wound away across the moor.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1509	lexical	\N	\N	1508	{"text": "A steep, boulder-sprinkled hill lay upon the right which had in bygone days been cut into a granite quarry.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1510	lexical	\N	\N	1509	{"text": "The face which was turned towards us formed a dark cliff, with ferns and brambles growing in its niches.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1511	lexical	\N	\N	1510	{"text": "From over a distant rise there floated a grey plume of smoke.", "section": "section_39", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1512	lexical	\N	\N	1511	{"text": "“A moderate walk along this moor-path brings us to Merripit House,” said he.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1513	lexical	\N	\N	1512	{"text": "“Perhaps you will spare an hour that I may have the pleasure of introducing you to my sister.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1514	lexical	\N	\N	1513	{"text": "My first thought was that I should be by Sir Henry’s side.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1515	lexical	\N	\N	1514	{"text": "But then I remembered the pile of papers and bills with which his study table was littered.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1516	lexical	\N	\N	1515	{"text": "It was certain that I could not help with those.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1517	lexical	\N	\N	1516	{"text": "And Holmes had expressly said that I should study the neighbours upon the moor.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1518	lexical	\N	\N	1517	{"text": "I accepted Stapleton’s invitation, and we turned together down the path.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1519	lexical	\N	\N	1518	{"text": "“It is a wonderful place, the moor,” said he, looking round over the undulating downs, long green rollers, with crests of jagged granite foaming up into fantastic surges.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1520	lexical	\N	\N	1519	{"text": "“You never tire of the moor.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1521	lexical	\N	\N	1520	{"text": "You cannot think the wonderful secrets which it contains.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1522	lexical	\N	\N	1521	{"text": "It is so vast, and so barren, and so mysterious.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1523	lexical	\N	\N	1522	{"text": "“You know it well, then?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1524	lexical	\N	\N	1523	{"text": "“I have only been here two years.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1525	lexical	\N	\N	1524	{"text": "The residents would call me a newcomer.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1527	lexical	\N	\N	1526	{"text": "But my tastes led me to explore every part of the country round, and I should think that there are few men who know it better than I do.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1528	lexical	\N	\N	1527	{"text": "“Is it hard to know?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1529	lexical	\N	\N	1528	{"text": "“Very hard.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1530	lexical	\N	\N	1529	{"text": "You see, for example, this great plain to the north here with the queer hills breaking out of it.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1531	lexical	\N	\N	1530	{"text": "Do you observe anything remarkable about that?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1532	lexical	\N	\N	1531	{"text": "“It would be a rare place for a gallop.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1533	lexical	\N	\N	1532	{"text": "“You would naturally think so and the thought has cost several their lives before now.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1534	lexical	\N	\N	1533	{"text": "You notice those bright green spots scattered thickly over it?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1535	lexical	\N	\N	1534	{"text": "“Yes, they seem more fertile than the rest.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1536	lexical	\N	\N	1535	{"text": "Stapleton laughed.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1537	lexical	\N	\N	1536	{"text": "“That is the great Grimpen Mire,” said he.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1538	lexical	\N	\N	1537	{"text": "“A false step yonder means death to man or beast.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1539	lexical	\N	\N	1538	{"text": "Only yesterday I saw one of the moor ponies wander into it.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1540	lexical	\N	\N	1539	{"text": "He never came out.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1541	lexical	\N	\N	1540	{"text": "I saw his head for quite a long time craning out of the bog-hole, but it sucked him down at last.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1542	lexical	\N	\N	1541	{"text": "Even in dry seasons it is a danger to cross it, but after these autumn rains it is an awful place.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1543	lexical	\N	\N	1542	{"text": "And yet I can find my way to the very heart of it and return alive.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1544	lexical	\N	\N	1543	{"text": "By George, there is another of those miserable ponies!”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1545	lexical	\N	\N	1544	{"text": "Something brown was rolling and tossing among the green sedges.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1546	lexical	\N	\N	1545	{"text": "Then a long, agonised, writhing neck shot upward and a dreadful cry echoed over the moor.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1547	lexical	\N	\N	1546	{"text": "It turned me cold with horror, but my companion’s nerves seemed to be stronger than mine.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1548	lexical	\N	\N	1547	{"text": "“It’s gone!”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1549	lexical	\N	\N	1548	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1550	lexical	\N	\N	1549	{"text": "“The mire has him.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1551	lexical	\N	\N	1550	{"text": "Two in two days, and many more, perhaps, for they get in the way of going there in the dry weather and never know the difference until the mire has them in its clutches.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1552	lexical	\N	\N	1551	{"text": "It’s a bad place, the great Grimpen Mire.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1553	lexical	\N	\N	1552	{"text": "“And you say you can penetrate it?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1554	lexical	\N	\N	1553	{"text": "“Yes, there are one or two paths which a very active man can take.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1555	lexical	\N	\N	1554	{"text": "I have found them out.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1556	lexical	\N	\N	1555	{"text": "“But why should you wish to go into so horrible a place?”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1557	lexical	\N	\N	1556	{"text": "“Well, you see the hills beyond?", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1558	lexical	\N	\N	1557	{"text": "They are really islands cut off on all sides by the impassable mire, which has crawled round them in the course of years.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1559	lexical	\N	\N	1558	{"text": "That is where the rare plants and the butterflies are, if you have the wit to reach them.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1560	lexical	\N	\N	1559	{"text": "“I shall try my luck some day.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1561	lexical	\N	\N	1560	{"text": "He looked at me with a surprised face.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1562	lexical	\N	\N	1561	{"text": "“For God’s sake put such an idea out of your mind,” said he.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1563	lexical	\N	\N	1562	{"text": "“Your blood would be upon my head.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1564	lexical	\N	\N	1563	{"text": "I assure you that there would not be the least chance of your coming back alive.", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1565	lexical	\N	\N	1564	{"text": "It is only by remembering certain complex landmarks that I am able to do it.”", "section": "section_40", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1569	lexical	\N	\N	1568	{"text": "A long, low moan, indescribably sad, swept over the moor.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1570	lexical	\N	\N	1569	{"text": "It filled the whole air, and yet it was impossible to say whence it came.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1571	lexical	\N	\N	1570	{"text": "From a dull murmur it swelled into a deep roar, and then sank back into a melancholy, throbbing murmur once again.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1572	lexical	\N	\N	1571	{"text": "Stapleton looked at me with a curious expression in his face.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1573	lexical	\N	\N	1572	{"text": "“Queer place, the moor!”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1574	lexical	\N	\N	1573	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1575	lexical	\N	\N	1574	{"text": "“But what is it?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1576	lexical	\N	\N	1575	{"text": "“The peasants say it is the Hound of the Baskervilles calling for its prey.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1577	lexical	\N	\N	1576	{"text": "I’ve heard it once or twice before, but never quite so loud.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1578	lexical	\N	\N	1577	{"text": "I looked round, with a chill of fear in my heart, at the huge swelling plain, mottled with the green patches of rushes.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1579	lexical	\N	\N	1578	{"text": "Nothing stirred over the vast expanse save a pair of ravens, which croaked loudly from a tor behind us.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1580	lexical	\N	\N	1579	{"text": "“You are an educated man.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1581	lexical	\N	\N	1580	{"text": "You don’t believe such nonsense as that?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1582	lexical	\N	\N	1581	{"text": "said I.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1583	lexical	\N	\N	1582	{"text": "“What do you think is the cause of so strange a sound?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1584	lexical	\N	\N	1583	{"text": "“Bogs make queer noises sometimes.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1585	lexical	\N	\N	1584	{"text": "It’s the mud settling, or the water rising, or something.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1586	lexical	\N	\N	1585	{"text": "“No, no, that was a living voice.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1587	lexical	\N	\N	1586	{"text": "“Well, perhaps it was.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1588	lexical	\N	\N	1587	{"text": "Did you ever hear a bittern booming?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1589	lexical	\N	\N	1588	{"text": "“No, I never did.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1590	lexical	\N	\N	1589	{"text": "“It’s a very rare bird—practically extinct—in England now, but all things are possible upon the moor.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1591	lexical	\N	\N	1590	{"text": "Yes, I should not be surprised to learn that what we have heard is the cry of the last of the bitterns.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1592	lexical	\N	\N	1591	{"text": "“It’s the weirdest, strangest thing that ever I heard in my life.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1593	lexical	\N	\N	1592	{"text": "“Yes, it’s rather an uncanny place altogether.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1594	lexical	\N	\N	1593	{"text": "Look at the hillside yonder.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1595	lexical	\N	\N	1594	{"text": "What do you make of those?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1596	lexical	\N	\N	1595	{"text": "The whole steep slope was covered with grey circular rings of stone, a score of them at least.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1597	lexical	\N	\N	1596	{"text": "“What are they?", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1598	lexical	\N	\N	1597	{"text": "Sheep-pens?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1599	lexical	\N	\N	1598	{"text": "“No, they are the homes of our worthy ancestors.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1600	lexical	\N	\N	1599	{"text": "Prehistoric man lived thickly on the moor, and as no one in particular has lived there since, we find all his little arrangements exactly as he left them.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1601	lexical	\N	\N	1600	{"text": "These are his wigwams with the roofs off.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1602	lexical	\N	\N	1601	{"text": "You can even see his hearth and his couch if you have the curiosity to go inside.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1603	lexical	\N	\N	1602	{"text": "“But it is quite a town.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1604	lexical	\N	\N	1603	{"text": "When was it inhabited?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1605	lexical	\N	\N	1604	{"text": "“Neolithic man—no date.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1606	lexical	\N	\N	1605	{"text": "“What did he do?”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1607	lexical	\N	\N	1606	{"text": "“He grazed his cattle on these slopes, and he learned to dig for tin when the bronze sword began to supersede the stone axe.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1608	lexical	\N	\N	1607	{"text": "Look at the great trench in the opposite hill.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1610	lexical	\N	\N	1609	{"text": "Yes, you will find some very singular points about the moor, Dr. Watson.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1611	lexical	\N	\N	1610	{"text": "Oh, excuse me an instant!", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1612	lexical	\N	\N	1611	{"text": "It is surely Cyclopides.”", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1613	lexical	\N	\N	1612	{"text": "A small fly or moth had fluttered across our path, and in an instant Stapleton was rushing with extraordinary energy and speed in pursuit of it.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1614	lexical	\N	\N	1613	{"text": "To my dismay the creature flew straight for the great mire, and my acquaintance never paused for an instant, bounding from tuft to tuft behind it, his green net waving in the air.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1615	lexical	\N	\N	1614	{"text": "His grey clothes and jerky, zigzag, irregular progress made him not unlike some huge moth himself.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1616	lexical	\N	\N	1615	{"text": "I was standing watching his pursuit with a mixture of admiration for his extraordinary activity and fear lest he should lose his footing in the treacherous mire, when I heard the sound of steps and, turning round, found a woman near me upon the path.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1617	lexical	\N	\N	1616	{"text": "She had come from the direction in which the plume of smoke indicated the position of Merripit House, but the dip of the moor had hid her until she was quite close.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1618	lexical	\N	\N	1617	{"text": "I could not doubt that this was the Miss Stapleton of whom I had been told, since ladies of any sort must be few upon the moor, and I remembered that I had heard someone describe her as being a beauty.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1619	lexical	\N	\N	1618	{"text": "The woman who approached me was certainly that, and of a most uncommon type.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1620	lexical	\N	\N	1619	{"text": "There could not have been a greater contrast between brother and sister, for Stapleton was neutral tinted, with light hair and grey eyes, while she was darker than any brunette whom I have seen in England—slim, elegant, and tall.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1621	lexical	\N	\N	1620	{"text": "She had a proud, finely cut face, so regular that it might have seemed impassive were it not for the sensitive mouth and the beautiful dark, eager eyes.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1622	lexical	\N	\N	1621	{"text": "With her perfect figure and elegant dress she was, indeed, a strange apparition upon a lonely moorland path.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1623	lexical	\N	\N	1622	{"text": "Her eyes were on her brother as I turned, and then she quickened her pace towards me.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1624	lexical	\N	\N	1623	{"text": "I had raised my hat and was about to make some explanatory remark when her own words turned all my thoughts into a new channel.", "section": "section_41", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1625	lexical	\N	\N	1624	{"text": "“Go back!”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1626	lexical	\N	\N	1625	{"text": "she said.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1627	lexical	\N	\N	1626	{"text": "“Go straight back to London, instantly.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1628	lexical	\N	\N	1627	{"text": "I could only stare at her in stupid surprise.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1629	lexical	\N	\N	1628	{"text": "Her eyes blazed at me, and she tapped the ground impatiently with her foot.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1630	lexical	\N	\N	1629	{"text": "“Why should I go back?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1631	lexical	\N	\N	1630	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1632	lexical	\N	\N	1631	{"text": "“I cannot explain.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1633	lexical	\N	\N	1632	{"text": "She spoke in a low, eager voice, with a curious lisp in her utterance.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1634	lexical	\N	\N	1633	{"text": "“But for God’s sake do what I ask you.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1635	lexical	\N	\N	1634	{"text": "Go back and never set foot upon the moor again.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1636	lexical	\N	\N	1635	{"text": "“But I have only just come.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1637	lexical	\N	\N	1636	{"text": "“Man, man!”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1638	lexical	\N	\N	1637	{"text": "she cried.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1639	lexical	\N	\N	1638	{"text": "“Can you not tell when a warning is for your own good?", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1640	lexical	\N	\N	1639	{"text": "Go back to London!", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1641	lexical	\N	\N	1640	{"text": "Start tonight!", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1642	lexical	\N	\N	1641	{"text": "Get away from this place at all costs!", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1643	lexical	\N	\N	1642	{"text": "Hush, my brother is coming!", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1644	lexical	\N	\N	1643	{"text": "Not a word of what I have said.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1645	lexical	\N	\N	1644	{"text": "Would you mind getting that orchid for me among the mare’s-tails yonder?", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1646	lexical	\N	\N	1645	{"text": "We are very rich in orchids on the moor, though, of course, you are rather late to see the beauties of the place.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1647	lexical	\N	\N	1646	{"text": "Stapleton had abandoned the chase and came back to us breathing hard and flushed with his exertions.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1648	lexical	\N	\N	1647	{"text": "“Halloa, Beryl!”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1649	lexical	\N	\N	1648	{"text": "said he, and it seemed to me that the tone of his greeting was not altogether a cordial one.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1650	lexical	\N	\N	1649	{"text": "“Well, Jack, you are very hot.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1651	lexical	\N	\N	1650	{"text": "“Yes, I was chasing a Cyclopides.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1652	lexical	\N	\N	1651	{"text": "He is very rare and seldom found in the late autumn.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1653	lexical	\N	\N	1652	{"text": "What a pity that I should have missed him!”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1654	lexical	\N	\N	1653	{"text": "He spoke unconcernedly, but his small light eyes glanced incessantly from the girl to me.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1655	lexical	\N	\N	1654	{"text": "“You have introduced yourselves, I can see.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1656	lexical	\N	\N	1655	{"text": "“Yes.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1657	lexical	\N	\N	1656	{"text": "I was telling Sir Henry that it was rather late for him to see the true beauties of the moor.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1658	lexical	\N	\N	1657	{"text": "“Why, who do you think this is?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1659	lexical	\N	\N	1658	{"text": "“I imagine that it must be Sir Henry Baskerville.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1660	lexical	\N	\N	1659	{"text": "“No, no,” said I.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1661	lexical	\N	\N	1660	{"text": "“Only a humble commoner, but his friend.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1662	lexical	\N	\N	1661	{"text": "My name is Dr. Watson.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1663	lexical	\N	\N	1662	{"text": "A flush of vexation passed over her expressive face.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1664	lexical	\N	\N	1663	{"text": "“We have been talking at cross purposes,” said she.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1665	lexical	\N	\N	1664	{"text": "“Why, you had not very much time for talk,” her brother remarked with the same questioning eyes.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1666	lexical	\N	\N	1665	{"text": "“I talked as if Dr. Watson were a resident instead of being merely a visitor,” said she.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1667	lexical	\N	\N	1666	{"text": "“It cannot much matter to him whether it is early or late for the orchids.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1668	lexical	\N	\N	1667	{"text": "But you will come on, will you not, and see Merripit House?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1669	lexical	\N	\N	1668	{"text": "A short walk brought us to it, a bleak moorland house, once the farm of some grazier in the old prosperous days, but now put into repair and turned into a modern dwelling.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1670	lexical	\N	\N	1669	{"text": "An orchard surrounded it, but the trees, as is usual upon the moor, were stunted and nipped, and the effect of the whole place was mean and melancholy.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1671	lexical	\N	\N	1670	{"text": "We were admitted by a strange, wizened, rusty-coated old manservant, who seemed in keeping with the house.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1672	lexical	\N	\N	1671	{"text": "Inside, however, there were large rooms furnished with an elegance in which I seemed to recognize the taste of the lady.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1673	lexical	\N	\N	1672	{"text": "As I looked from their windows at the interminable granite-flecked moor rolling unbroken to the farthest horizon I could not but marvel at what could have brought this highly educated man and this beautiful woman to live in such a place.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1674	lexical	\N	\N	1673	{"text": "“Queer spot to choose, is it not?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1675	lexical	\N	\N	1674	{"text": "said he as if in answer to my thought.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1676	lexical	\N	\N	1675	{"text": "“And yet we manage to make ourselves fairly happy, do we not, Beryl?”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1677	lexical	\N	\N	1676	{"text": "“Quite happy,” said she, but there was no ring of conviction in her words.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1678	lexical	\N	\N	1677	{"text": "“I had a school,” said Stapleton.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1679	lexical	\N	\N	1678	{"text": "“It was in the north country.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1680	lexical	\N	\N	1679	{"text": "The work to a man of my temperament was mechanical and uninteresting, but the privilege of living with youth, of helping to mould those young minds, and of impressing them with one’s own character and ideals was very dear to me.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1681	lexical	\N	\N	1680	{"text": "However, the fates were against us.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1682	lexical	\N	\N	1681	{"text": "A serious epidemic broke out in the school and three of the boys died.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1683	lexical	\N	\N	1682	{"text": "It never recovered from the blow, and much of my capital was irretrievably swallowed up.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1684	lexical	\N	\N	1683	{"text": "And yet, if it were not for the loss of the charming companionship of the boys, I could rejoice over my own misfortune, for, with my strong tastes for botany and zoology, I find an unlimited field of work here, and my sister is as devoted to Nature as I am.", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1685	lexical	\N	\N	1684	{"text": "All this, Dr. Watson, has been brought upon your head by your expression as you surveyed the moor out of our window.”", "section": "section_42", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1686	lexical	\N	\N	1685	{"text": "“It certainly did cross my mind that it might be a little dull—less for you, perhaps, than for your sister.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1687	lexical	\N	\N	1686	{"text": "“No, no, I am never dull,” said she quickly.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1688	lexical	\N	\N	1687	{"text": "“We have books, we have our studies, and we have interesting neighbours.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1689	lexical	\N	\N	1688	{"text": "Dr. Mortimer is a most learned man in his own line.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1690	lexical	\N	\N	1689	{"text": "Poor Sir Charles was also an admirable companion.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1691	lexical	\N	\N	1690	{"text": "We knew him well and miss him more than I can tell.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1692	lexical	\N	\N	1691	{"text": "Do you think that I should intrude if I were to call this afternoon and make the acquaintance of Sir Henry?”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1693	lexical	\N	\N	1692	{"text": "“I am sure that he would be delighted.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1694	lexical	\N	\N	1693	{"text": "“Then perhaps you would mention that I propose to do so.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1695	lexical	\N	\N	1694	{"text": "We may in our humble way do something to make things more easy for him until he becomes accustomed to his new surroundings.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1696	lexical	\N	\N	1695	{"text": "Will you come upstairs, Dr. Watson, and inspect my collection of Lepidoptera?", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1697	lexical	\N	\N	1696	{"text": "I think it is the most complete one in the south-west of England.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1698	lexical	\N	\N	1697	{"text": "By the time that you have looked through them lunch will be almost ready.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1699	lexical	\N	\N	1698	{"text": "But I was eager to get back to my charge.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1700	lexical	\N	\N	1699	{"text": "The melancholy of the moor, the death of the unfortunate pony, the weird sound which had been associated with the grim legend of the Baskervilles, all these things tinged my thoughts with sadness.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1701	lexical	\N	\N	1700	{"text": "Then on the top of these more or less vague impressions there had come the definite and distinct warning of Miss Stapleton, delivered with such intense earnestness that I could not doubt that some grave and deep reason lay behind it.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1702	lexical	\N	\N	1701	{"text": "I resisted all pressure to stay for lunch, and I set off at once upon my return journey, taking the grass-grown path by which we had come.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1703	lexical	\N	\N	1702	{"text": "It seems, however, that there must have been some short cut for those who knew it, for before I had reached the road I was astounded to see Miss Stapleton sitting upon a rock by the side of the track.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1704	lexical	\N	\N	1703	{"text": "Her face was beautifully flushed with her exertions and she held her hand to her side.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1705	lexical	\N	\N	1704	{"text": "“I have run all the way in order to cut you off, Dr. Watson,” said she.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1706	lexical	\N	\N	1705	{"text": "“I had not even time to put on my hat.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1707	lexical	\N	\N	1706	{"text": "I must not stop, or my brother may miss me.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1708	lexical	\N	\N	1707	{"text": "I wanted to say to you how sorry I am about the stupid mistake I made in thinking that you were Sir Henry.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1709	lexical	\N	\N	1708	{"text": "Please forget the words I said, which have no application whatever to you.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1710	lexical	\N	\N	1709	{"text": "“But I can’t forget them, Miss Stapleton,” said I.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1711	lexical	\N	\N	1710	{"text": "“I am Sir Henry’s friend, and his welfare is a very close concern of mine.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1712	lexical	\N	\N	1711	{"text": "Tell me why it was that you were so eager that Sir Henry should return to London.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1713	lexical	\N	\N	1712	{"text": "“A woman’s whim, Dr. Watson.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1714	lexical	\N	\N	1713	{"text": "When you know me better you will understand that I cannot always give reasons for what I say or do.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1715	lexical	\N	\N	1714	{"text": "“No, no.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1716	lexical	\N	\N	1715	{"text": "I remember the thrill in your voice.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1717	lexical	\N	\N	1716	{"text": "I remember the look in your eyes.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1718	lexical	\N	\N	1717	{"text": "Please, please, be frank with me, Miss Stapleton, for ever since I have been here I have been conscious of shadows all round me.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1719	lexical	\N	\N	1718	{"text": "Life has become like that great Grimpen Mire, with little green patches everywhere into which one may sink and with no guide to point the track.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1720	lexical	\N	\N	1719	{"text": "Tell me then what it was that you meant, and I will promise to convey your warning to Sir Henry.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1721	lexical	\N	\N	1720	{"text": "An expression of irresolution passed for an instant over her face, but her eyes had hardened again when she answered me.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1722	lexical	\N	\N	1721	{"text": "“You make too much of it, Dr. Watson,” said she.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1723	lexical	\N	\N	1722	{"text": "“My brother and I were very much shocked by the death of Sir Charles.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1724	lexical	\N	\N	1723	{"text": "We knew him very intimately, for his favourite walk was over the moor to our house.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1725	lexical	\N	\N	1724	{"text": "He was deeply impressed with the curse which hung over the family, and when this tragedy came I naturally felt that there must be some grounds for the fears which he had expressed.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1726	lexical	\N	\N	1725	{"text": "I was distressed therefore when another member of the family came down to live here, and I felt that he should be warned of the danger which he will run.", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1727	lexical	\N	\N	1726	{"text": "That was all which I intended to convey.”", "section": "section_43", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1728	lexical	\N	\N	1727	{"text": "“But what is the danger?”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1729	lexical	\N	\N	1728	{"text": "“You know the story of the hound?”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1730	lexical	\N	\N	1729	{"text": "“I do not believe in such nonsense.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1731	lexical	\N	\N	1730	{"text": "“But I do.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1732	lexical	\N	\N	1731	{"text": "If you have any influence with Sir Henry, take him away from a place which has always been fatal to his family.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1733	lexical	\N	\N	1732	{"text": "The world is wide.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1734	lexical	\N	\N	1733	{"text": "Why should he wish to live at the place of danger?”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1735	lexical	\N	\N	1734	{"text": "“Because it _is_ the place of danger.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1736	lexical	\N	\N	1735	{"text": "That is Sir Henry’s nature.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1737	lexical	\N	\N	1736	{"text": "I fear that unless you can give me some more definite information than this it would be impossible to get him to move.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1738	lexical	\N	\N	1737	{"text": "“I cannot say anything definite, for I do not know anything definite.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1739	lexical	\N	\N	1738	{"text": "“I would ask you one more question, Miss Stapleton.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1740	lexical	\N	\N	1739	{"text": "If you meant no more than this when you first spoke to me, why should you not wish your brother to overhear what you said?", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1741	lexical	\N	\N	1740	{"text": "There is nothing to which he, or anyone else, could object.”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1742	lexical	\N	\N	1741	{"text": "“My brother is very anxious to have the Hall inhabited, for he thinks it is for the good of the poor folk upon the moor.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1743	lexical	\N	\N	1742	{"text": "He would be very angry if he knew that I have said anything which might induce Sir Henry to go away.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1744	lexical	\N	\N	1743	{"text": "But I have done my duty now and I will say no more.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1745	lexical	\N	\N	1744	{"text": "I must go back, or he will miss me and suspect that I have seen you.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1746	lexical	\N	\N	1745	{"text": "Good-bye!”", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1747	lexical	\N	\N	1746	{"text": "She turned and had disappeared in a few minutes among the scattered boulders, while I, with my soul full of vague fears, pursued my way to Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_44", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1748	lexical	\N	\N	1747	{"text": "Chapter 8.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1749	lexical	\N	\N	1748	{"text": "First Report of Dr. Watson", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1750	lexical	\N	\N	1749	{"text": "From this point onward I will follow the course of events by transcribing my own letters to Mr. Sherlock Holmes which lie before me on the table.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1781	lexical	\N	\N	1780	{"text": "It is not to be wondered at, for time hangs heavily in this lonely spot to an active man like him, and she is a very fascinating and beautiful woman.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1751	lexical	\N	\N	1750	{"text": "One page is missing, but otherwise they are exactly as written and show my feelings and suspicions of the moment more accurately than my memory, clear as it is upon these tragic events, can possibly do.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1752	lexical	\N	\N	1751	{"text": "Baskerville Hall, October 13th.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1753	lexical	\N	\N	1752	{"text": "MY DEAR HOLMES,", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1754	lexical	\N	\N	1753	{"text": "My previous letters and telegrams have kept you pretty well up to date as to all that has occurred in this most God-forsaken corner of the world.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1755	lexical	\N	\N	1754	{"text": "The longer one stays here the more does the spirit of the moor sink into one’s soul, its vastness, and also its grim charm.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1756	lexical	\N	\N	1755	{"text": "When you are once out upon its bosom you have left all traces of modern England behind you, but, on the other hand, you are conscious everywhere of the homes and the work of the prehistoric people.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1757	lexical	\N	\N	1756	{"text": "On all sides of you as you walk are the houses of these forgotten folk, with their graves and the huge monoliths which are supposed to have marked their temples.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1758	lexical	\N	\N	1757	{"text": "As you look at their grey stone huts against the scarred hillsides you leave your own age behind you, and if you were to see a skin-clad, hairy man crawl out from the low door fitting a flint-tipped arrow on to the string of his bow, you would feel that his presence there was more natural than your own.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1759	lexical	\N	\N	1758	{"text": "The strange thing is that they should have lived so thickly on what must always have been most unfruitful soil.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1760	lexical	\N	\N	1759	{"text": "I am no antiquarian, but I could imagine that they were some unwarlike and harried race who were forced to accept that which none other would occupy.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1761	lexical	\N	\N	1760	{"text": "All this, however, is foreign to the mission on which you sent me and will probably be very uninteresting to your severely practical mind.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1762	lexical	\N	\N	1761	{"text": "I can still remember your complete indifference as to whether the sun moved round the earth or the earth round the sun.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1763	lexical	\N	\N	1762	{"text": "Let me, therefore, return to the facts concerning Sir Henry Baskerville.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1764	lexical	\N	\N	1763	{"text": "If you have not had any report within the last few days it is because up to today there was nothing of importance to relate.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1765	lexical	\N	\N	1764	{"text": "Then a very surprising circumstance occurred, which I shall tell you in due course.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1766	lexical	\N	\N	1765	{"text": "But, first of all, I must keep you in touch with some of the other factors in the situation.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1767	lexical	\N	\N	1766	{"text": "One of these, concerning which I have said little, is the escaped convict upon the moor.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1768	lexical	\N	\N	1767	{"text": "There is strong reason now to believe that he has got right away, which is a considerable relief to the lonely householders of this district.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1769	lexical	\N	\N	1768	{"text": "A fortnight has passed since his flight, during which he has not been seen and nothing has been heard of him.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1770	lexical	\N	\N	1769	{"text": "It is surely inconceivable that he could have held out upon the moor during all that time.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1771	lexical	\N	\N	1770	{"text": "Of course, so far as his concealment goes there is no difficulty at all.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1772	lexical	\N	\N	1771	{"text": "Any one of these stone huts would give him a hiding-place.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1773	lexical	\N	\N	1772	{"text": "But there is nothing to eat unless he were to catch and slaughter one of the moor sheep.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1774	lexical	\N	\N	1773	{"text": "We think, therefore, that he has gone, and the outlying farmers sleep the better in consequence.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1775	lexical	\N	\N	1774	{"text": "We are four able-bodied men in this household, so that we could take good care of ourselves, but I confess that I have had uneasy moments when I have thought of the Stapletons.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1776	lexical	\N	\N	1775	{"text": "They live miles from any help.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1777	lexical	\N	\N	1776	{"text": "There are one maid, an old manservant, the sister, and the brother, the latter not a very strong man.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1778	lexical	\N	\N	1777	{"text": "They would be helpless in the hands of a desperate fellow like this Notting Hill criminal if he could once effect an entrance.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1779	lexical	\N	\N	1778	{"text": "Both Sir Henry and I were concerned at their situation, and it was suggested that Perkins the groom should go over to sleep there, but Stapleton would not hear of it.", "section": "section_45", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1780	lexical	\N	\N	1779	{"text": "The fact is that our friend, the baronet, begins to display a considerable interest in our fair neighbour.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1843	lexical	\N	\N	1842	{"text": "asked Sir Henry.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1782	lexical	\N	\N	1781	{"text": "There is something tropical and exotic about her which forms a singular contrast to her cool and unemotional brother.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1783	lexical	\N	\N	1782	{"text": "Yet he also gives the idea of hidden fires.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1784	lexical	\N	\N	1783	{"text": "He has certainly a very marked influence over her, for I have seen her continually glance at him as she talked as if seeking approbation for what she said.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1785	lexical	\N	\N	1784	{"text": "I trust that he is kind to her.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1786	lexical	\N	\N	1785	{"text": "There is a dry glitter in his eyes and a firm set of his thin lips, which goes with a positive and possibly a harsh nature.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1787	lexical	\N	\N	1786	{"text": "You would find him an interesting study.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1788	lexical	\N	\N	1787	{"text": "He came over to call upon Baskerville on that first day, and the very next morning he took us both to show us the spot where the legend of the wicked Hugo is supposed to have had its origin.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1789	lexical	\N	\N	1788	{"text": "It was an excursion of some miles across the moor to a place which is so dismal that it might have suggested the story.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1790	lexical	\N	\N	1789	{"text": "We found a short valley between rugged tors which led to an open, grassy space flecked over with the white cotton grass.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1791	lexical	\N	\N	1790	{"text": "In the middle of it rose two great stones, worn and sharpened at the upper end until they looked like the huge corroding fangs of some monstrous beast.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1792	lexical	\N	\N	1791	{"text": "In every way it corresponded with the scene of the old tragedy.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1793	lexical	\N	\N	1792	{"text": "Sir Henry was much interested and asked Stapleton more than once whether he did really believe in the possibility of the interference of the supernatural in the affairs of men.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1794	lexical	\N	\N	1793	{"text": "He spoke lightly, but it was evident that he was very much in earnest.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1795	lexical	\N	\N	1794	{"text": "Stapleton was guarded in his replies, but it was easy to see that he said less than he might, and that he would not express his whole opinion out of consideration for the feelings of the baronet.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1796	lexical	\N	\N	1795	{"text": "He told us of similar cases, where families had suffered from some evil influence, and he left us with the impression that he shared the popular view upon the matter.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1797	lexical	\N	\N	1796	{"text": "On our way back we stayed for lunch at Merripit House, and it was there that Sir Henry made the acquaintance of Miss Stapleton.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1798	lexical	\N	\N	1797	{"text": "From the first moment that he saw her he appeared to be strongly attracted by her, and I am much mistaken if the feeling was not mutual.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1799	lexical	\N	\N	1798	{"text": "He referred to her again and again on our walk home, and since then hardly a day has passed that we have not seen something of the brother and sister.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1800	lexical	\N	\N	1799	{"text": "They dine here tonight, and there is some talk of our going to them next week.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1801	lexical	\N	\N	1800	{"text": "One would imagine that such a match would be very welcome to Stapleton, and yet I have more than once caught a look of the strongest disapprobation in his face when Sir Henry has been paying some attention to his sister.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1802	lexical	\N	\N	1801	{"text": "He is much attached to her, no doubt, and would lead a lonely life without her, but it would seem the height of selfishness if he were to stand in the way of her making so brilliant a marriage.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1803	lexical	\N	\N	1802	{"text": "Yet I am certain that he does not wish their intimacy to ripen into love, and I have several times observed that he has taken pains to prevent them from being _tête-à-tête_.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1804	lexical	\N	\N	1803	{"text": "By the way, your instructions to me never to allow Sir Henry to go out alone will become very much more onerous if a love affair were to be added to our other difficulties.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1805	lexical	\N	\N	1804	{"text": "My popularity would soon suffer if I were to carry out your orders to the letter.", "section": "section_46", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1806	lexical	\N	\N	1805	{"text": "The other day—Thursday, to be more exact—Dr. Mortimer lunched with us.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1807	lexical	\N	\N	1806	{"text": "He has been excavating a barrow at Long Down and has got a prehistoric skull which fills him with great joy.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1808	lexical	\N	\N	1807	{"text": "Never was there such a single-minded enthusiast as he!", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1809	lexical	\N	\N	1808	{"text": "The Stapletons came in afterwards, and the good doctor took us all to the yew alley at Sir Henry’s request to show us exactly how everything occurred upon that fatal night.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1810	lexical	\N	\N	1809	{"text": "It is a long, dismal walk, the yew alley, between two high walls of clipped hedge, with a narrow band of grass upon either side.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1811	lexical	\N	\N	1810	{"text": "At the far end is an old tumble-down summer-house.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1812	lexical	\N	\N	1811	{"text": "Halfway down is the moor-gate, where the old gentleman left his cigar-ash.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1813	lexical	\N	\N	1812	{"text": "It is a white wooden gate with a latch.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1814	lexical	\N	\N	1813	{"text": "Beyond it lies the wide moor.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1815	lexical	\N	\N	1814	{"text": "I remembered your theory of the affair and tried to picture all that had occurred.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1816	lexical	\N	\N	1815	{"text": "As the old man stood there he saw something coming across the moor, something which terrified him so that he lost his wits and ran and ran until he died of sheer horror and exhaustion.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1817	lexical	\N	\N	1816	{"text": "There was the long, gloomy tunnel down which he fled.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1818	lexical	\N	\N	1817	{"text": "And from what?", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1819	lexical	\N	\N	1818	{"text": "A sheep-dog of the moor?", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1820	lexical	\N	\N	1819	{"text": "Or a spectral hound, black, silent, and monstrous?", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1821	lexical	\N	\N	1820	{"text": "Was there a human agency in the matter?", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1822	lexical	\N	\N	1821	{"text": "Did the pale, watchful Barrymore know more than he cared to say?", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1823	lexical	\N	\N	1822	{"text": "It was all dim and vague, but always there is the dark shadow of crime behind it.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1824	lexical	\N	\N	1823	{"text": "One other neighbour I have met since I wrote last.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1825	lexical	\N	\N	1824	{"text": "This is Mr. Frankland, of Lafter Hall, who lives some four miles to the south of us.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1826	lexical	\N	\N	1825	{"text": "He is an elderly man, red-faced, white-haired, and choleric.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1827	lexical	\N	\N	1826	{"text": "His passion is for the British law, and he has spent a large fortune in litigation.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1828	lexical	\N	\N	1827	{"text": "He fights for the mere pleasure of fighting and is equally ready to take up either side of a question, so that it is no wonder that he has found it a costly amusement.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1829	lexical	\N	\N	1828	{"text": "Sometimes he will shut up a right of way and defy the parish to make him open it.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1830	lexical	\N	\N	1829	{"text": "At others he will with his own hands tear down some other man’s gate and declare that a path has existed there from time immemorial, defying the owner to prosecute him for trespass.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1831	lexical	\N	\N	1830	{"text": "He is learned in old manorial and communal rights, and he applies his knowledge sometimes in favour of the villagers of Fernworthy and sometimes against them, so that he is periodically either carried in triumph down the village street or else burned in effigy, according to his latest exploit.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1832	lexical	\N	\N	1831	{"text": "He is said to have about seven lawsuits upon his hands at present, which will probably swallow up the remainder of his fortune and so draw his sting and leave him harmless for the future.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1833	lexical	\N	\N	1832	{"text": "Apart from the law he seems a kindly, good-natured person, and I only mention him because you were particular that I should send some description of the people who surround us.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1834	lexical	\N	\N	1833	{"text": "He is curiously employed at present, for, being an amateur astronomer, he has an excellent telescope, with which he lies upon the roof of his own house and sweeps the moor all day in the hope of catching a glimpse of the escaped convict.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1835	lexical	\N	\N	1834	{"text": "If he would confine his energies to this all would be well, but there are rumours that he intends to prosecute Dr. Mortimer for opening a grave without the consent of the next of kin because he dug up the Neolithic skull in the barrow on Long Down.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1836	lexical	\N	\N	1835	{"text": "He helps to keep our lives from being monotonous and gives a little comic relief where it is badly needed.", "section": "section_47", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1837	lexical	\N	\N	1836	{"text": "And now, having brought you up to date in the escaped convict, the Stapletons, Dr. Mortimer, and Frankland, of Lafter Hall, let me end on that which is most important and tell you more about the Barrymores, and especially about the surprising development of last night.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1838	lexical	\N	\N	1837	{"text": "First of all about the test telegram, which you sent from London in order to make sure that Barrymore was really here.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1839	lexical	\N	\N	1838	{"text": "I have already explained that the testimony of the postmaster shows that the test was worthless and that we have no proof one way or the other.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1840	lexical	\N	\N	1839	{"text": "I told Sir Henry how the matter stood, and he at once, in his downright fashion, had Barrymore up and asked him whether he had received the telegram himself.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1841	lexical	\N	\N	1840	{"text": "Barrymore said that he had.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1842	lexical	\N	\N	1841	{"text": "“Did the boy deliver it into your own hands?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1844	lexical	\N	\N	1843	{"text": "Barrymore looked surprised, and considered for a little time.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1845	lexical	\N	\N	1844	{"text": "“No,” said he, “I was in the box-room at the time, and my wife brought it up to me.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1846	lexical	\N	\N	1845	{"text": "“Did you answer it yourself?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1847	lexical	\N	\N	1846	{"text": "“No; I told my wife what to answer and she went down to write it.”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1848	lexical	\N	\N	1847	{"text": "In the evening he recurred to the subject of his own accord.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1849	lexical	\N	\N	1848	{"text": "“I could not quite understand the object of your questions this morning, Sir Henry,” said he.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1850	lexical	\N	\N	1849	{"text": "“I trust that they do not mean that I have done anything to forfeit your confidence?”", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1851	lexical	\N	\N	1850	{"text": "Sir Henry had to assure him that it was not so and pacify him by giving him a considerable part of his old wardrobe, the London outfit having now all arrived.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1852	lexical	\N	\N	1851	{"text": "Mrs. Barrymore is of interest to me.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1853	lexical	\N	\N	1852	{"text": "She is a heavy, solid person, very limited, intensely respectable, and inclined to be puritanical.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1854	lexical	\N	\N	1853	{"text": "You could hardly conceive a less emotional subject.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1855	lexical	\N	\N	1854	{"text": "Yet I have told you how, on the first night here, I heard her sobbing bitterly, and since then I have more than once observed traces of tears upon her face.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1856	lexical	\N	\N	1855	{"text": "Some deep sorrow gnaws ever at her heart.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1857	lexical	\N	\N	1856	{"text": "Sometimes I wonder if she has a guilty memory which haunts her, and sometimes I suspect Barrymore of being a domestic tyrant.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1858	lexical	\N	\N	1857	{"text": "I have always felt that there was something singular and questionable in this man’s character, but the adventure of last night brings all my suspicions to a head.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1859	lexical	\N	\N	1858	{"text": "And yet it may seem a small matter in itself.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1860	lexical	\N	\N	1859	{"text": "You are aware that I am not a very sound sleeper, and since I have been on guard in this house my slumbers have been lighter than ever.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1861	lexical	\N	\N	1860	{"text": "Last night, about two in the morning, I was aroused by a stealthy step passing my room.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1862	lexical	\N	\N	1861	{"text": "I rose, opened my door, and peeped out.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1863	lexical	\N	\N	1862	{"text": "A long black shadow was trailing down the corridor.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1864	lexical	\N	\N	1863	{"text": "It was thrown by a man who walked softly down the passage with a candle held in his hand.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1865	lexical	\N	\N	1864	{"text": "He was in shirt and trousers, with no covering to his feet.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1866	lexical	\N	\N	1865	{"text": "I could merely see the outline, but his height told me that it was Barrymore.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1867	lexical	\N	\N	1866	{"text": "He walked very slowly and circumspectly, and there was something indescribably guilty and furtive in his whole appearance.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1868	lexical	\N	\N	1867	{"text": "I have told you that the corridor is broken by the balcony which runs round the hall, but that it is resumed upon the farther side.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1869	lexical	\N	\N	1868	{"text": "I waited until he had passed out of sight and then I followed him.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1870	lexical	\N	\N	1869	{"text": "When I came round the balcony he had reached the end of the farther corridor, and I could see from the glimmer of light through an open door that he had entered one of the rooms.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1871	lexical	\N	\N	1870	{"text": "Now, all these rooms are unfurnished and unoccupied so that his expedition became more mysterious than ever.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1872	lexical	\N	\N	1871	{"text": "The light shone steadily as if he were standing motionless.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1873	lexical	\N	\N	1872	{"text": "I crept down the passage as noiselessly as I could and peeped round the corner of the door.", "section": "section_48", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1874	lexical	\N	\N	1873	{"text": "Barrymore was crouching at the window with the candle held against the glass.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1875	lexical	\N	\N	1874	{"text": "His profile was half turned towards me, and his face seemed to be rigid with expectation as he stared out into the blackness of the moor.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1876	lexical	\N	\N	1875	{"text": "For some minutes he stood watching intently.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1877	lexical	\N	\N	1876	{"text": "Then he gave a deep groan and with an impatient gesture he put out the light.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1878	lexical	\N	\N	1877	{"text": "Instantly I made my way back to my room, and very shortly came the stealthy steps passing once more upon their return journey.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1879	lexical	\N	\N	1878	{"text": "Long afterwards when I had fallen into a light sleep I heard a key turn somewhere in a lock, but I could not tell whence the sound came.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1880	lexical	\N	\N	1879	{"text": "What it all means I cannot guess, but there is some secret business going on in this house of gloom which sooner or later we shall get to the bottom of.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1881	lexical	\N	\N	1880	{"text": "I do not trouble you with my theories, for you asked me to furnish you only with facts.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1882	lexical	\N	\N	1881	{"text": "I have had a long talk with Sir Henry this morning, and we have made a plan of campaign founded upon my observations of last night.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1883	lexical	\N	\N	1882	{"text": "I will not speak about it just now, but it should make my next report interesting reading.", "section": "section_49", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1884	lexical	\N	\N	1883	{"text": "Chapter 9.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1885	lexical	\N	\N	1884	{"text": "The Light upon the Moor [Second Report of Dr. Watson]", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1886	lexical	\N	\N	1885	{"text": "Baskerville Hall, Oct.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1887	lexical	\N	\N	1886	{"text": "15th.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1888	lexical	\N	\N	1887	{"text": "MY DEAR HOLMES,", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1889	lexical	\N	\N	1888	{"text": "If I was compelled to leave you without much news during the early days of my mission you must acknowledge that I am making up for lost time, and that events are now crowding thick and fast upon us.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1890	lexical	\N	\N	1889	{"text": "In my last report I ended upon my top note with Barrymore at the window, and now I have quite a budget already which will, unless I am much mistaken, considerably surprise you.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1891	lexical	\N	\N	1890	{"text": "Things have taken a turn which I could not have anticipated.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1892	lexical	\N	\N	1891	{"text": "In some ways they have within the last forty-eight hours become much clearer and in some ways they have become more complicated.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1893	lexical	\N	\N	1892	{"text": "But I will tell you all and you shall judge for yourself.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1894	lexical	\N	\N	1893	{"text": "Before breakfast on the morning following my adventure I went down the corridor and examined the room in which Barrymore had been on the night before.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1895	lexical	\N	\N	1894	{"text": "The western window through which he had stared so intently has, I noticed, one peculiarity above all other windows in the house—it commands the nearest outlook on to the moor.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1896	lexical	\N	\N	1895	{"text": "There is an opening between two trees which enables one from this point of view to look right down upon it, while from all the other windows it is only a distant glimpse which can be obtained.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1897	lexical	\N	\N	1896	{"text": "It follows, therefore, that Barrymore, since only this window would serve the purpose, must have been looking out for something or somebody upon the moor.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1898	lexical	\N	\N	1897	{"text": "The night was very dark, so that I can hardly imagine how he could have hoped to see anyone.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1899	lexical	\N	\N	1898	{"text": "It had struck me that it was possible that some love intrigue was on foot.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1900	lexical	\N	\N	1899	{"text": "That would have accounted for his stealthy movements and also for the uneasiness of his wife.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1901	lexical	\N	\N	1900	{"text": "The man is a striking-looking fellow, very well equipped to steal the heart of a country girl, so that this theory seemed to have something to support it.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1902	lexical	\N	\N	1901	{"text": "That opening of the door which I had heard after I had returned to my room might mean that he had gone out to keep some clandestine appointment.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1903	lexical	\N	\N	1902	{"text": "So I reasoned with myself in the morning, and I tell you the direction of my suspicions, however much the result may have shown that they were unfounded.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1904	lexical	\N	\N	1903	{"text": "But whatever the true explanation of Barrymore’s movements might be, I felt that the responsibility of keeping them to myself until I could explain them was more than I could bear.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1905	lexical	\N	\N	1904	{"text": "I had an interview with the baronet in his study after breakfast, and I told him all that I had seen.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1906	lexical	\N	\N	1905	{"text": "He was less surprised than I had expected.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1907	lexical	\N	\N	1906	{"text": "“I knew that Barrymore walked about nights, and I had a mind to speak to him about it,” said he.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1908	lexical	\N	\N	1907	{"text": "“Two or three times I have heard his steps in the passage, coming and going, just about the hour you name.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1975	lexical	\N	\N	1974	{"text": "“Halloa, Watson!", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1909	lexical	\N	\N	1908	{"text": "“Perhaps then he pays a visit every night to that particular window,” I suggested.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1910	lexical	\N	\N	1909	{"text": "“Perhaps he does.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1911	lexical	\N	\N	1910	{"text": "If so, we should be able to shadow him and see what it is that he is after.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1912	lexical	\N	\N	1911	{"text": "I wonder what your friend Holmes would do if he were here.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1913	lexical	\N	\N	1912	{"text": "“I believe that he would do exactly what you now suggest,” said I.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1914	lexical	\N	\N	1913	{"text": "“He would follow Barrymore and see what he did.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1915	lexical	\N	\N	1914	{"text": "“Then we shall do it together.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1916	lexical	\N	\N	1915	{"text": "“But surely he would hear us.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1917	lexical	\N	\N	1916	{"text": "“The man is rather deaf, and in any case we must take our chance of that.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1918	lexical	\N	\N	1917	{"text": "We’ll sit up in my room tonight and wait until he passes.”", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1919	lexical	\N	\N	1918	{"text": "Sir Henry rubbed his hands with pleasure, and it was evident that he hailed the adventure as a relief to his somewhat quiet life upon the moor.", "section": "section_50", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1920	lexical	\N	\N	1919	{"text": "The baronet has been in communication with the architect who prepared the plans for Sir Charles, and with a contractor from London, so that we may expect great changes to begin here soon.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1921	lexical	\N	\N	1920	{"text": "There have been decorators and furnishers up from Plymouth, and it is evident that our friend has large ideas and means to spare no pains or expense to restore the grandeur of his family.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1922	lexical	\N	\N	1921	{"text": "When the house is renovated and refurnished, all that he will need will be a wife to make it complete.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1923	lexical	\N	\N	1922	{"text": "Between ourselves there are pretty clear signs that this will not be wanting if the lady is willing, for I have seldom seen a man more infatuated with a woman than he is with our beautiful neighbour, Miss Stapleton.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1924	lexical	\N	\N	1923	{"text": "And yet the course of true love does not run quite as smoothly as one would under the circumstances expect.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1925	lexical	\N	\N	1924	{"text": "Today, for example, its surface was broken by a very unexpected ripple, which has caused our friend considerable perplexity and annoyance.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1926	lexical	\N	\N	1925	{"text": "After the conversation which I have quoted about Barrymore, Sir Henry put on his hat and prepared to go out.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1927	lexical	\N	\N	1926	{"text": "As a matter of course I did the same.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1928	lexical	\N	\N	1927	{"text": "“What, are _you_ coming, Watson?”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1929	lexical	\N	\N	1928	{"text": "he asked, looking at me in a curious way.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1930	lexical	\N	\N	1929	{"text": "“That depends on whether you are going on the moor,” said I.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1931	lexical	\N	\N	1930	{"text": "“Yes, I am.”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1932	lexical	\N	\N	1931	{"text": "“Well, you know what my instructions are.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1933	lexical	\N	\N	1932	{"text": "I am sorry to intrude, but you heard how earnestly Holmes insisted that I should not leave you, and especially that you should not go alone upon the moor.”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1934	lexical	\N	\N	1933	{"text": "Sir Henry put his hand upon my shoulder with a pleasant smile.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1935	lexical	\N	\N	1934	{"text": "“My dear fellow,” said he, “Holmes, with all his wisdom, did not foresee some things which have happened since I have been on the moor.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1936	lexical	\N	\N	1935	{"text": "You understand me?", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1937	lexical	\N	\N	1936	{"text": "I am sure that you are the last man in the world who would wish to be a spoil-sport.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1938	lexical	\N	\N	1937	{"text": "I must go out alone.”", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1939	lexical	\N	\N	1938	{"text": "It put me in a most awkward position.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1940	lexical	\N	\N	1939	{"text": "I was at a loss what to say or what to do, and before I had made up my mind he picked up his cane and was gone.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1941	lexical	\N	\N	1940	{"text": "But when I came to think the matter over my conscience reproached me bitterly for having on any pretext allowed him to go out of my sight.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1942	lexical	\N	\N	1941	{"text": "I imagined what my feelings would be if I had to return to you and to confess that some misfortune had occurred through my disregard for your instructions.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1943	lexical	\N	\N	1942	{"text": "I assure you my cheeks flushed at the very thought.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1944	lexical	\N	\N	1943	{"text": "It might not even now be too late to overtake him, so I set off at once in the direction of Merripit House.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1945	lexical	\N	\N	1944	{"text": "I hurried along the road at the top of my speed without seeing anything of Sir Henry, until I came to the point where the moor path branches off.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1946	lexical	\N	\N	1945	{"text": "There, fearing that perhaps I had come in the wrong direction after all, I mounted a hill from which I could command a view—the same hill which is cut into the dark quarry.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1947	lexical	\N	\N	1946	{"text": "Thence I saw him at once.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1948	lexical	\N	\N	1947	{"text": "He was on the moor path about a quarter of a mile off, and a lady was by his side who could only be Miss Stapleton.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1949	lexical	\N	\N	1948	{"text": "It was clear that there was already an understanding between them and that they had met by appointment.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1950	lexical	\N	\N	1949	{"text": "They were walking slowly along in deep conversation, and I saw her making quick little movements of her hands as if she were very earnest in what she was saying, while he listened intently, and once or twice shook his head in strong dissent.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1951	lexical	\N	\N	1950	{"text": "I stood among the rocks watching them, very much puzzled as to what I should do next.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1952	lexical	\N	\N	1951	{"text": "To follow them and break into their intimate conversation seemed to be an outrage, and yet my clear duty was never for an instant to let him out of my sight.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1953	lexical	\N	\N	1952	{"text": "To act the spy upon a friend was a hateful task.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1954	lexical	\N	\N	1953	{"text": "Still, I could see no better course than to observe him from the hill, and to clear my conscience by confessing to him afterwards what I had done.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1955	lexical	\N	\N	1954	{"text": "It is true that if any sudden danger had threatened him I was too far away to be of use, and yet I am sure that you will agree with me that the position was very difficult, and that there was nothing more which I could do.", "section": "section_51", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1956	lexical	\N	\N	1955	{"text": "Our friend, Sir Henry, and the lady had halted on the path and were standing deeply absorbed in their conversation, when I was suddenly aware that I was not the only witness of their interview.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1957	lexical	\N	\N	1956	{"text": "A wisp of green floating in the air caught my eye, and another glance showed me that it was carried on a stick by a man who was moving among the broken ground.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1958	lexical	\N	\N	1957	{"text": "It was Stapleton with his butterfly-net.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1959	lexical	\N	\N	1958	{"text": "He was very much closer to the pair than I was, and he appeared to be moving in their direction.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1960	lexical	\N	\N	1959	{"text": "At this instant Sir Henry suddenly drew Miss Stapleton to his side.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1961	lexical	\N	\N	1960	{"text": "His arm was round her, but it seemed to me that she was straining away from him with her face averted.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1962	lexical	\N	\N	1961	{"text": "He stooped his head to hers, and she raised one hand as if in protest.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1963	lexical	\N	\N	1962	{"text": "Next moment I saw them spring apart and turn hurriedly round.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1964	lexical	\N	\N	1963	{"text": "Stapleton was the cause of the interruption.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1965	lexical	\N	\N	1964	{"text": "He was running wildly towards them, his absurd net dangling behind him.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1966	lexical	\N	\N	1965	{"text": "He gesticulated and almost danced with excitement in front of the lovers.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1967	lexical	\N	\N	1966	{"text": "What the scene meant I could not imagine, but it seemed to me that Stapleton was abusing Sir Henry, who offered explanations, which became more angry as the other refused to accept them.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1968	lexical	\N	\N	1967	{"text": "The lady stood by in haughty silence.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1969	lexical	\N	\N	1968	{"text": "Finally Stapleton turned upon his heel and beckoned in a peremptory way to his sister, who, after an irresolute glance at Sir Henry, walked off by the side of her brother.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1970	lexical	\N	\N	1969	{"text": "The naturalist’s angry gestures showed that the lady was included in his displeasure.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1971	lexical	\N	\N	1970	{"text": "The baronet stood for a minute looking after them, and then he walked slowly back the way that he had come, his head hanging, the very picture of dejection.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1972	lexical	\N	\N	1971	{"text": "What all this meant I could not imagine, but I was deeply ashamed to have witnessed so intimate a scene without my friend’s knowledge.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1973	lexical	\N	\N	1972	{"text": "I ran down the hill therefore and met the baronet at the bottom.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1974	lexical	\N	\N	1973	{"text": "His face was flushed with anger and his brows were wrinkled, like one who is at his wit’s ends what to do.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1976	lexical	\N	\N	1975	{"text": "Where have you dropped from?”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1977	lexical	\N	\N	1976	{"text": "said he.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1978	lexical	\N	\N	1977	{"text": "“You don’t mean to say that you came after me in spite of all?”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1979	lexical	\N	\N	1978	{"text": "I explained everything to him: how I had found it impossible to remain behind, how I had followed him, and how I had witnessed all that had occurred.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1980	lexical	\N	\N	1979	{"text": "For an instant his eyes blazed at me, but my frankness disarmed his anger, and he broke at last into a rather rueful laugh.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1981	lexical	\N	\N	1980	{"text": "“You would have thought the middle of that prairie a fairly safe place for a man to be private,” said he, “but, by thunder, the whole countryside seems to have been out to see me do my wooing—and a mighty poor wooing at that!", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1982	lexical	\N	\N	1981	{"text": "Where had you engaged a seat?”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1983	lexical	\N	\N	1982	{"text": "“I was on that hill.”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1984	lexical	\N	\N	1983	{"text": "“Quite in the back row, eh?", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1985	lexical	\N	\N	1984	{"text": "But her brother was well up to the front.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1986	lexical	\N	\N	1985	{"text": "Did you see him come out on us?”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1987	lexical	\N	\N	1986	{"text": "“Yes, I did.”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1988	lexical	\N	\N	1987	{"text": "“Did he ever strike you as being crazy—this brother of hers?”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1989	lexical	\N	\N	1988	{"text": "“I can’t say that he ever did.”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1990	lexical	\N	\N	1989	{"text": "“I dare say not.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1991	lexical	\N	\N	1990	{"text": "I always thought him sane enough until today, but you can take it from me that either he or I ought to be in a straitjacket.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1992	lexical	\N	\N	1991	{"text": "What’s the matter with me, anyhow?", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1993	lexical	\N	\N	1992	{"text": "You’ve lived near me for some weeks, Watson.", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1994	lexical	\N	\N	1993	{"text": "Tell me straight, now!", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1995	lexical	\N	\N	1994	{"text": "Is there anything that would prevent me from making a good husband to a woman that I loved?”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1996	lexical	\N	\N	1995	{"text": "“I should say not.”", "section": "section_52", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1997	lexical	\N	\N	1996	{"text": "“He can’t object to my worldly position, so it must be myself that he has this down on.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1998	lexical	\N	\N	1997	{"text": "What has he against me?", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_1999	lexical	\N	\N	1998	{"text": "I never hurt man or woman in my life that I know of.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2000	lexical	\N	\N	1999	{"text": "And yet he would not so much as let me touch the tips of her fingers.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2001	lexical	\N	\N	2000	{"text": "“Did he say so?”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2002	lexical	\N	\N	2001	{"text": "“That, and a deal more.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2003	lexical	\N	\N	2002	{"text": "I tell you, Watson, I’ve only known her these few weeks, but from the first I just felt that she was made for me, and she, too—she was happy when she was with me, and that I’ll swear.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2004	lexical	\N	\N	2003	{"text": "There’s a light in a woman’s eyes that speaks louder than words.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2005	lexical	\N	\N	2004	{"text": "But he has never let us get together and it was only today for the first time that I saw a chance of having a few words with her alone.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2006	lexical	\N	\N	2005	{"text": "She was glad to meet me, but when she did it was not love that she would talk about, and she wouldn’t have let me talk about it either if she could have stopped it.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2007	lexical	\N	\N	2006	{"text": "She kept coming back to it that this was a place of danger, and that she would never be happy until I had left it.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2008	lexical	\N	\N	2007	{"text": "I told her that since I had seen her I was in no hurry to leave it, and that if she really wanted me to go, the only way to work it was for her to arrange to go with me.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2009	lexical	\N	\N	2008	{"text": "With that I offered in as many words to marry her, but before she could answer, down came this brother of hers, running at us with a face on him like a madman.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2010	lexical	\N	\N	2009	{"text": "He was just white with rage, and those light eyes of his were blazing with fury.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2011	lexical	\N	\N	2010	{"text": "What was I doing with the lady?", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2012	lexical	\N	\N	2011	{"text": "How dared I offer her attentions which were distasteful to her?", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2013	lexical	\N	\N	2012	{"text": "Did I think that because I was a baronet I could do what I liked?", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2014	lexical	\N	\N	2013	{"text": "If he had not been her brother I should have known better how to answer him.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2015	lexical	\N	\N	2014	{"text": "As it was I told him that my feelings towards his sister were such as I was not ashamed of, and that I hoped that she might honour me by becoming my wife.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2016	lexical	\N	\N	2015	{"text": "That seemed to make the matter no better, so then I lost my temper too, and I answered him rather more hotly than I should perhaps, considering that she was standing by.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2017	lexical	\N	\N	2016	{"text": "So it ended by his going off with her, as you saw, and here am I as badly puzzled a man as any in this county.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2018	lexical	\N	\N	2017	{"text": "Just tell me what it all means, Watson, and I’ll owe you more than ever I can hope to pay.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2019	lexical	\N	\N	2018	{"text": "I tried one or two explanations, but, indeed, I was completely puzzled myself.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2020	lexical	\N	\N	2019	{"text": "Our friend’s title, his fortune, his age, his character, and his appearance are all in his favour, and I know nothing against him unless it be this dark fate which runs in his family.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2021	lexical	\N	\N	2020	{"text": "That his advances should be rejected so brusquely without any reference to the lady’s own wishes and that the lady should accept the situation without protest is very amazing.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2022	lexical	\N	\N	2021	{"text": "However, our conjectures were set at rest by a visit from Stapleton himself that very afternoon.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2023	lexical	\N	\N	2022	{"text": "He had come to offer apologies for his rudeness of the morning, and after a long private interview with Sir Henry in his study the upshot of their conversation was that the breach is quite healed, and that we are to dine at Merripit House next Friday as a sign of it.", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2024	lexical	\N	\N	2023	{"text": "“I don’t say now that he isn’t a crazy man,” said Sir Henry; “I can’t forget the look in his eyes when he ran at me this morning, but I must allow that no man could make a more handsome apology than he has done.”", "section": "section_53", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2025	lexical	\N	\N	2024	{"text": "“Did he give any explanation of his conduct?”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2026	lexical	\N	\N	2025	{"text": "“His sister is everything in his life, he says.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2027	lexical	\N	\N	2026	{"text": "That is natural enough, and I am glad that he should understand her value.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2028	lexical	\N	\N	2027	{"text": "They have always been together, and according to his account he has been a very lonely man with only her as a companion, so that the thought of losing her was really terrible to him.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2029	lexical	\N	\N	2028	{"text": "He had not understood, he said, that I was becoming attached to her, but when he saw with his own eyes that it was really so, and that she might be taken away from him, it gave him such a shock that for a time he was not responsible for what he said or did.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2030	lexical	\N	\N	2029	{"text": "He was very sorry for all that had passed, and he recognized how foolish and how selfish it was that he should imagine that he could hold a beautiful woman like his sister to himself for her whole life.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2031	lexical	\N	\N	2030	{"text": "If she had to leave him he had rather it was to a neighbour like myself than to anyone else.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2032	lexical	\N	\N	2031	{"text": "But in any case it was a blow to him and it would take him some time before he could prepare himself to meet it.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2033	lexical	\N	\N	2032	{"text": "He would withdraw all opposition upon his part if I would promise for three months to let the matter rest and to be content with cultivating the lady’s friendship during that time without claiming her love.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2034	lexical	\N	\N	2033	{"text": "This I promised, and so the matter rests.”", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2035	lexical	\N	\N	2034	{"text": "So there is one of our small mysteries cleared up.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2036	lexical	\N	\N	2035	{"text": "It is something to have touched bottom anywhere in this bog in which we are floundering.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2037	lexical	\N	\N	2036	{"text": "We know now why Stapleton looked with disfavour upon his sister’s suitor—even when that suitor was so eligible a one as Sir Henry.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2038	lexical	\N	\N	2037	{"text": "And now I pass on to another thread which I have extricated out of the tangled skein, the mystery of the sobs in the night, of the tear-stained face of Mrs. Barrymore, of the secret journey of the butler to the western lattice window.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2039	lexical	\N	\N	2038	{"text": "Congratulate me, my dear Holmes, and tell me that I have not disappointed you as an agent—that you do not regret the confidence which you showed in me when you sent me down.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2040	lexical	\N	\N	2039	{"text": "All these things have by one night’s work been thoroughly cleared.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2041	lexical	\N	\N	2040	{"text": "I have said “by one night’s work,” but, in truth, it was by two nights’ work, for on the first we drew entirely blank.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2042	lexical	\N	\N	2041	{"text": "I sat up with Sir Henry in his rooms until nearly three o’clock in the morning, but no sound of any sort did we hear except the chiming clock upon the stairs.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2043	lexical	\N	\N	2042	{"text": "It was a most melancholy vigil and ended by each of us falling asleep in our chairs.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2044	lexical	\N	\N	2043	{"text": "Fortunately we were not discouraged, and we determined to try again.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2045	lexical	\N	\N	2044	{"text": "The next night we lowered the lamp and sat smoking cigarettes without making the least sound.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2046	lexical	\N	\N	2045	{"text": "It was incredible how slowly the hours crawled by, and yet we were helped through it by the same sort of patient interest which the hunter must feel as he watches the trap into which he hopes the game may wander.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2047	lexical	\N	\N	2046	{"text": "One struck, and two, and we had almost for the second time given it up in despair when in an instant we both sat bolt upright in our chairs with all our weary senses keenly on the alert once more.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2048	lexical	\N	\N	2047	{"text": "We had heard the creak of a step in the passage.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2049	lexical	\N	\N	2048	{"text": "Very stealthily we heard it pass along until it died away in the distance.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2050	lexical	\N	\N	2049	{"text": "Then the baronet gently opened his door and we set out in pursuit.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2051	lexical	\N	\N	2050	{"text": "Already our man had gone round the gallery and the corridor was all in darkness.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2052	lexical	\N	\N	2051	{"text": "Softly we stole along until we had come into the other wing.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2053	lexical	\N	\N	2052	{"text": "We were just in time to catch a glimpse of the tall, black-bearded figure, his shoulders rounded as he tiptoed down the passage.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2054	lexical	\N	\N	2053	{"text": "Then he passed through the same door as before, and the light of the candle framed it in the darkness and shot one single yellow beam across the gloom of the corridor.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2055	lexical	\N	\N	2054	{"text": "We shuffled cautiously towards it, trying every plank before we dared to put our whole weight upon it.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2056	lexical	\N	\N	2055	{"text": "We had taken the precaution of leaving our boots behind us, but, even so, the old boards snapped and creaked beneath our tread.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2057	lexical	\N	\N	2056	{"text": "Sometimes it seemed impossible that he should fail to hear our approach.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2058	lexical	\N	\N	2057	{"text": "However, the man is fortunately rather deaf, and he was entirely preoccupied in that which he was doing.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2059	lexical	\N	\N	2058	{"text": "When at last we reached the door and peeped through we found him crouching at the window, candle in hand, his white, intent face pressed against the pane, exactly as I had seen him two nights before.", "section": "section_54", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2060	lexical	\N	\N	2059	{"text": "We had arranged no plan of campaign, but the baronet is a man to whom the most direct way is always the most natural.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2061	lexical	\N	\N	2060	{"text": "He walked into the room, and as he did so Barrymore sprang up from the window with a sharp hiss of his breath and stood, livid and trembling, before us.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2062	lexical	\N	\N	2061	{"text": "His dark eyes, glaring out of the white mask of his face, were full of horror and astonishment as he gazed from Sir Henry to me.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2063	lexical	\N	\N	2062	{"text": "“What are you doing here, Barrymore?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2064	lexical	\N	\N	2063	{"text": "“Nothing, sir.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2065	lexical	\N	\N	2064	{"text": "His agitation was so great that he could hardly speak, and the shadows sprang up and down from the shaking of his candle.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2066	lexical	\N	\N	2065	{"text": "“It was the window, sir.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2067	lexical	\N	\N	2066	{"text": "I go round at night to see that they are fastened.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2068	lexical	\N	\N	2067	{"text": "“On the second floor?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2069	lexical	\N	\N	2068	{"text": "“Yes, sir, all the windows.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2070	lexical	\N	\N	2069	{"text": "“Look here, Barrymore,” said Sir Henry sternly, “we have made up our minds to have the truth out of you, so it will save you trouble to tell it sooner rather than later.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2071	lexical	\N	\N	2070	{"text": "Come, now!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2072	lexical	\N	\N	2071	{"text": "No lies!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2073	lexical	\N	\N	2072	{"text": "What were you doing at that window?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2074	lexical	\N	\N	2073	{"text": "The fellow looked at us in a helpless way, and he wrung his hands together like one who is in the last extremity of doubt and misery.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2075	lexical	\N	\N	2074	{"text": "“I was doing no harm, sir.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2076	lexical	\N	\N	2075	{"text": "I was holding a candle to the window.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2077	lexical	\N	\N	2076	{"text": "“And why were you holding a candle to the window?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2078	lexical	\N	\N	2077	{"text": "“Don’t ask me, Sir Henry—don’t ask me!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2079	lexical	\N	\N	2078	{"text": "I give you my word, sir, that it is not my secret, and that I cannot tell it.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2080	lexical	\N	\N	2079	{"text": "If it concerned no one but myself I would not try to keep it from you.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2081	lexical	\N	\N	2080	{"text": "A sudden idea occurred to me, and I took the candle from the trembling hand of the butler.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2082	lexical	\N	\N	2081	{"text": "“He must have been holding it as a signal,” said I.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2083	lexical	\N	\N	2082	{"text": "“Let us see if there is any answer.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2084	lexical	\N	\N	2083	{"text": "I held it as he had done, and stared out into the darkness of the night.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2085	lexical	\N	\N	2084	{"text": "Vaguely I could discern the black bank of the trees and the lighter expanse of the moor, for the moon was behind the clouds.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2086	lexical	\N	\N	2085	{"text": "And then I gave a cry of exultation, for a tiny pinpoint of yellow light had suddenly transfixed the dark veil, and glowed steadily in the centre of the black square framed by the window.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2087	lexical	\N	\N	2086	{"text": "“There it is!”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2088	lexical	\N	\N	2087	{"text": "I cried.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2089	lexical	\N	\N	2088	{"text": "“No, no, sir, it is nothing—nothing at all!”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2090	lexical	\N	\N	2089	{"text": "the butler broke in; “I assure you, sir—”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2091	lexical	\N	\N	2090	{"text": "“Move your light across the window, Watson!”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2092	lexical	\N	\N	2091	{"text": "cried the baronet.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2093	lexical	\N	\N	2092	{"text": "“See, the other moves also!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2094	lexical	\N	\N	2093	{"text": "Now, you rascal, do you deny that it is a signal?", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2095	lexical	\N	\N	2094	{"text": "Come, speak up!", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2096	lexical	\N	\N	2095	{"text": "Who is your confederate out yonder, and what is this conspiracy that is going on?”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2097	lexical	\N	\N	2096	{"text": "The man’s face became openly defiant.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2098	lexical	\N	\N	2097	{"text": "“It is my business, and not yours.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2099	lexical	\N	\N	2098	{"text": "I will not tell.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2100	lexical	\N	\N	2099	{"text": "“Then you leave my employment right away.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2101	lexical	\N	\N	2100	{"text": "“Very good, sir.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2102	lexical	\N	\N	2101	{"text": "If I must I must.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2103	lexical	\N	\N	2102	{"text": "“And you go in disgrace.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2104	lexical	\N	\N	2103	{"text": "By thunder, you may well be ashamed of yourself.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2105	lexical	\N	\N	2104	{"text": "Your family has lived with mine for over a hundred years under this roof, and here I find you deep in some dark plot against me.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2106	lexical	\N	\N	2105	{"text": "“No, no, sir; no, not against you!”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2107	lexical	\N	\N	2106	{"text": "It was a woman’s voice, and Mrs. Barrymore, paler and more horror-struck than her husband, was standing at the door.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2108	lexical	\N	\N	2107	{"text": "Her bulky figure in a shawl and skirt might have been comic were it not for the intensity of feeling upon her face.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2109	lexical	\N	\N	2108	{"text": "“We have to go, Eliza.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2110	lexical	\N	\N	2109	{"text": "This is the end of it.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2111	lexical	\N	\N	2110	{"text": "You can pack our things,” said the butler.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2112	lexical	\N	\N	2111	{"text": "“Oh, John, John, have I brought you to this?", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2113	lexical	\N	\N	2112	{"text": "It is my doing, Sir Henry—all mine.", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2114	lexical	\N	\N	2113	{"text": "He has done nothing except for my sake and because I asked him.”", "section": "section_55", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2115	lexical	\N	\N	2114	{"text": "“Speak out, then!", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2116	lexical	\N	\N	2115	{"text": "What does it mean?”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2117	lexical	\N	\N	2116	{"text": "“My unhappy brother is starving on the moor.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2118	lexical	\N	\N	2117	{"text": "We cannot let him perish at our very gates.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2119	lexical	\N	\N	2118	{"text": "The light is a signal to him that food is ready for him, and his light out yonder is to show the spot to which to bring it.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2120	lexical	\N	\N	2119	{"text": "“Then your brother is—”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2121	lexical	\N	\N	2120	{"text": "“The escaped convict, sir—Selden, the criminal.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2122	lexical	\N	\N	2121	{"text": "“That’s the truth, sir,” said Barrymore.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2123	lexical	\N	\N	2122	{"text": "“I said that it was not my secret and that I could not tell it to you.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2124	lexical	\N	\N	2123	{"text": "But now you have heard it, and you will see that if there was a plot it was not against you.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2125	lexical	\N	\N	2124	{"text": "This, then, was the explanation of the stealthy expeditions at night and the light at the window.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2126	lexical	\N	\N	2125	{"text": "Sir Henry and I both stared at the woman in amazement.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2127	lexical	\N	\N	2126	{"text": "Was it possible that this stolidly respectable person was of the same blood as one of the most notorious criminals in the country?", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2128	lexical	\N	\N	2127	{"text": "“Yes, sir, my name was Selden, and he is my younger brother.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2129	lexical	\N	\N	2128	{"text": "We humoured him too much when he was a lad and gave him his own way in everything until he came to think that the world was made for his pleasure, and that he could do what he liked in it.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2130	lexical	\N	\N	2129	{"text": "Then as he grew older he met wicked companions, and the devil entered into him until he broke my mother’s heart and dragged our name in the dirt.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2131	lexical	\N	\N	2130	{"text": "From crime to crime he sank lower and lower until it is only the mercy of God which has snatched him from the scaffold; but to me, sir, he was always the little curly-headed boy that I had nursed and played with as an elder sister would.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2132	lexical	\N	\N	2131	{"text": "That was why he broke prison, sir.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2133	lexical	\N	\N	2132	{"text": "He knew that I was here and that we could not refuse to help him.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2134	lexical	\N	\N	2133	{"text": "When he dragged himself here one night, weary and starving, with the warders hard at his heels, what could we do?", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2135	lexical	\N	\N	2134	{"text": "We took him in and fed him and cared for him.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2136	lexical	\N	\N	2135	{"text": "Then you returned, sir, and my brother thought he would be safer on the moor than anywhere else until the hue and cry was over, so he lay in hiding there.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2137	lexical	\N	\N	2136	{"text": "But every second night we made sure if he was still there by putting a light in the window, and if there was an answer my husband took out some bread and meat to him.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2138	lexical	\N	\N	2137	{"text": "Every day we hoped that he was gone, but as long as he was there we could not desert him.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2139	lexical	\N	\N	2138	{"text": "That is the whole truth, as I am an honest Christian woman and you will see that if there is blame in the matter it does not lie with my husband but with me, for whose sake he has done all that he has.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2140	lexical	\N	\N	2139	{"text": "The woman’s words came with an intense earnestness which carried conviction with them.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2141	lexical	\N	\N	2140	{"text": "“Is this true, Barrymore?”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2142	lexical	\N	\N	2141	{"text": "“Yes, Sir Henry.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2143	lexical	\N	\N	2142	{"text": "Every word of it.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2144	lexical	\N	\N	2143	{"text": "“Well, I cannot blame you for standing by your own wife.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2145	lexical	\N	\N	2144	{"text": "Forget what I have said.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2146	lexical	\N	\N	2145	{"text": "Go to your room, you two, and we shall talk further about this matter in the morning.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2147	lexical	\N	\N	2146	{"text": "When they were gone we looked out of the window again.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2148	lexical	\N	\N	2147	{"text": "Sir Henry had flung it open, and the cold night wind beat in upon our faces.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2149	lexical	\N	\N	2148	{"text": "Far away in the black distance there still glowed that one tiny point of yellow light.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2150	lexical	\N	\N	2149	{"text": "“I wonder he dares,” said Sir Henry.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2151	lexical	\N	\N	2150	{"text": "“It may be so placed as to be only visible from here.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2152	lexical	\N	\N	2151	{"text": "“Very likely.", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2153	lexical	\N	\N	2152	{"text": "How far do you think it is?”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2154	lexical	\N	\N	2153	{"text": "“Out by the Cleft Tor, I think.”", "section": "section_56", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2155	lexical	\N	\N	2154	{"text": "“Not more than a mile or two off.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2156	lexical	\N	\N	2155	{"text": "“Hardly that.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2157	lexical	\N	\N	2156	{"text": "“Well, it cannot be far if Barrymore had to carry out the food to it.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2158	lexical	\N	\N	2157	{"text": "And he is waiting, this villain, beside that candle.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2159	lexical	\N	\N	2158	{"text": "By thunder, Watson, I am going out to take that man!”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2160	lexical	\N	\N	2159	{"text": "The same thought had crossed my own mind.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2161	lexical	\N	\N	2160	{"text": "It was not as if the Barrymores had taken us into their confidence.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2162	lexical	\N	\N	2161	{"text": "Their secret had been forced from them.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2163	lexical	\N	\N	2162	{"text": "The man was a danger to the community, an unmitigated scoundrel for whom there was neither pity nor excuse.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2164	lexical	\N	\N	2163	{"text": "We were only doing our duty in taking this chance of putting him back where he could do no harm.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2165	lexical	\N	\N	2164	{"text": "With his brutal and violent nature, others would have to pay the price if we held our hands.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2166	lexical	\N	\N	2165	{"text": "Any night, for example, our neighbours the Stapletons might be attacked by him, and it may have been the thought of this which made Sir Henry so keen upon the adventure.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2167	lexical	\N	\N	2166	{"text": "“I will come,” said I.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2168	lexical	\N	\N	2167	{"text": "“Then get your revolver and put on your boots.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2169	lexical	\N	\N	2168	{"text": "The sooner we start the better, as the fellow may put out his light and be off.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2170	lexical	\N	\N	2169	{"text": "In five minutes we were outside the door, starting upon our expedition.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2171	lexical	\N	\N	2170	{"text": "We hurried through the dark shrubbery, amid the dull moaning of the autumn wind and the rustle of the falling leaves.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2172	lexical	\N	\N	2171	{"text": "The night air was heavy with the smell of damp and decay.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2173	lexical	\N	\N	2172	{"text": "Now and again the moon peeped out for an instant, but clouds were driving over the face of the sky, and just as we came out on the moor a thin rain began to fall.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2174	lexical	\N	\N	2173	{"text": "The light still burned steadily in front.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2175	lexical	\N	\N	2174	{"text": "“Are you armed?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2176	lexical	\N	\N	2175	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2177	lexical	\N	\N	2176	{"text": "“I have a hunting-crop.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2178	lexical	\N	\N	2177	{"text": "“We must close in on him rapidly, for he is said to be a desperate fellow.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2179	lexical	\N	\N	2178	{"text": "We shall take him by surprise and have him at our mercy before he can resist.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2180	lexical	\N	\N	2179	{"text": "“I say, Watson,” said the baronet, “what would Holmes say to this?", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2181	lexical	\N	\N	2180	{"text": "How about that hour of darkness in which the power of evil is exalted?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2182	lexical	\N	\N	2181	{"text": "As if in answer to his words there rose suddenly out of the vast gloom of the moor that strange cry which I had already heard upon the borders of the great Grimpen Mire.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2183	lexical	\N	\N	2182	{"text": "It came with the wind through the silence of the night, a long, deep mutter, then a rising howl, and then the sad moan in which it died away.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2184	lexical	\N	\N	2183	{"text": "Again and again it sounded, the whole air throbbing with it, strident, wild, and menacing.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2185	lexical	\N	\N	2184	{"text": "The baronet caught my sleeve and his face glimmered white through the darkness.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2186	lexical	\N	\N	2185	{"text": "“My God, what’s that, Watson?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2187	lexical	\N	\N	2186	{"text": "“I don’t know.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2188	lexical	\N	\N	2187	{"text": "It’s a sound they have on the moor.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2189	lexical	\N	\N	2188	{"text": "I heard it once before.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2190	lexical	\N	\N	2189	{"text": "It died away, and an absolute silence closed in upon us.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2191	lexical	\N	\N	2190	{"text": "We stood straining our ears, but nothing came.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2192	lexical	\N	\N	2191	{"text": "“Watson,” said the baronet, “it was the cry of a hound.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2193	lexical	\N	\N	2192	{"text": "My blood ran cold in my veins, for there was a break in his voice which told of the sudden horror which had seized him.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2194	lexical	\N	\N	2193	{"text": "“What do they call this sound?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2195	lexical	\N	\N	2194	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2196	lexical	\N	\N	2195	{"text": "“Who?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2197	lexical	\N	\N	2196	{"text": "“The folk on the countryside.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2198	lexical	\N	\N	2197	{"text": "“Oh, they are ignorant people.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2199	lexical	\N	\N	2198	{"text": "Why should you mind what they call it?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2200	lexical	\N	\N	2199	{"text": "“Tell me, Watson.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2201	lexical	\N	\N	2200	{"text": "What do they say of it?”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2202	lexical	\N	\N	2201	{"text": "I hesitated but could not escape the question.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2203	lexical	\N	\N	2202	{"text": "“They say it is the cry of the Hound of the Baskervilles.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2204	lexical	\N	\N	2203	{"text": "He groaned and was silent for a few moments.", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2205	lexical	\N	\N	2204	{"text": "“A hound it was,” he said at last, “but it seemed to come from miles away, over yonder, I think.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2206	lexical	\N	\N	2205	{"text": "“It was hard to say whence it came.”", "section": "section_57", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2207	lexical	\N	\N	2206	{"text": "“It rose and fell with the wind.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2208	lexical	\N	\N	2207	{"text": "Isn’t that the direction of the great Grimpen Mire?”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2209	lexical	\N	\N	2208	{"text": "“Yes, it is.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2210	lexical	\N	\N	2209	{"text": "“Well, it was up there.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2211	lexical	\N	\N	2210	{"text": "Come now, Watson, didn’t you think yourself that it was the cry of a hound?", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2212	lexical	\N	\N	2211	{"text": "I am not a child.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2213	lexical	\N	\N	2212	{"text": "You need not fear to speak the truth.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2214	lexical	\N	\N	2213	{"text": "“Stapleton was with me when I heard it last.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2215	lexical	\N	\N	2214	{"text": "He said that it might be the calling of a strange bird.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2216	lexical	\N	\N	2215	{"text": "“No, no, it was a hound.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2217	lexical	\N	\N	2216	{"text": "My God, can there be some truth in all these stories?", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2218	lexical	\N	\N	2217	{"text": "Is it possible that I am really in danger from so dark a cause?", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2219	lexical	\N	\N	2218	{"text": "You don’t believe it, do you, Watson?”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2220	lexical	\N	\N	2219	{"text": "“No, no.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2221	lexical	\N	\N	2220	{"text": "“And yet it was one thing to laugh about it in London, and it is another to stand out here in the darkness of the moor and to hear such a cry as that.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2222	lexical	\N	\N	2221	{"text": "And my uncle!", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2223	lexical	\N	\N	2222	{"text": "There was the footprint of the hound beside him as he lay.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2224	lexical	\N	\N	2223	{"text": "It all fits together.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2225	lexical	\N	\N	2224	{"text": "I don’t think that I am a coward, Watson, but that sound seemed to freeze my very blood.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2226	lexical	\N	\N	2225	{"text": "Feel my hand!”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2227	lexical	\N	\N	2226	{"text": "It was as cold as a block of marble.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2228	lexical	\N	\N	2227	{"text": "“You’ll be all right tomorrow.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2229	lexical	\N	\N	2228	{"text": "“I don’t think I’ll get that cry out of my head.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2230	lexical	\N	\N	2229	{"text": "What do you advise that we do now?”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2231	lexical	\N	\N	2230	{"text": "“Shall we turn back?”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2232	lexical	\N	\N	2231	{"text": "“No, by thunder; we have come out to get our man, and we will do it.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2233	lexical	\N	\N	2232	{"text": "We after the convict, and a hell-hound, as likely as not, after us.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2234	lexical	\N	\N	2233	{"text": "Come on!", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2235	lexical	\N	\N	2234	{"text": "We’ll see it through if all the fiends of the pit were loose upon the moor.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2236	lexical	\N	\N	2235	{"text": "We stumbled slowly along in the darkness, with the black loom of the craggy hills around us, and the yellow speck of light burning steadily in front.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2237	lexical	\N	\N	2236	{"text": "There is nothing so deceptive as the distance of a light upon a pitch-dark night, and sometimes the glimmer seemed to be far away upon the horizon and sometimes it might have been within a few yards of us.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2238	lexical	\N	\N	2237	{"text": "But at last we could see whence it came, and then we knew that we were indeed very close.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2239	lexical	\N	\N	2238	{"text": "A guttering candle was stuck in a crevice of the rocks which flanked it on each side so as to keep the wind from it and also to prevent it from being visible, save in the direction of Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2240	lexical	\N	\N	2239	{"text": "A boulder of granite concealed our approach, and crouching behind it we gazed over it at the signal light.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2241	lexical	\N	\N	2240	{"text": "It was strange to see this single candle burning there in the middle of the moor, with no sign of life near it—just the one straight yellow flame and the gleam of the rock on each side of it.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2242	lexical	\N	\N	2241	{"text": "“What shall we do now?”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2243	lexical	\N	\N	2242	{"text": "whispered Sir Henry.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2244	lexical	\N	\N	2243	{"text": "“Wait here.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2245	lexical	\N	\N	2244	{"text": "He must be near his light.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2246	lexical	\N	\N	2245	{"text": "Let us see if we can get a glimpse of him.”", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2247	lexical	\N	\N	2246	{"text": "The words were hardly out of my mouth when we both saw him.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2248	lexical	\N	\N	2247	{"text": "Over the rocks, in the crevice of which the candle burned, there was thrust out an evil yellow face, a terrible animal face, all seamed and scored with vile passions.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2249	lexical	\N	\N	2248	{"text": "Foul with mire, with a bristling beard, and hung with matted hair, it might well have belonged to one of those old savages who dwelt in the burrows on the hillsides.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2250	lexical	\N	\N	2249	{"text": "The light beneath him was reflected in his small, cunning eyes which peered fiercely to right and left through the darkness like a crafty and savage animal who has heard the steps of the hunters.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2251	lexical	\N	\N	2250	{"text": "Something had evidently aroused his suspicions.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2252	lexical	\N	\N	2251	{"text": "It may have been that Barrymore had some private signal which we had neglected to give, or the fellow may have had some other reason for thinking that all was not well, but I could read his fears upon his wicked face.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2253	lexical	\N	\N	2252	{"text": "Any instant he might dash out the light and vanish in the darkness.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2254	lexical	\N	\N	2253	{"text": "I sprang forward therefore, and Sir Henry did the same.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2255	lexical	\N	\N	2254	{"text": "At the same moment the convict screamed out a curse at us and hurled a rock which splintered up against the boulder which had sheltered us.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2256	lexical	\N	\N	2255	{"text": "I caught one glimpse of his short, squat, strongly built figure as he sprang to his feet and turned to run.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2257	lexical	\N	\N	2256	{"text": "At the same moment by a lucky chance the moon broke through the clouds.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2258	lexical	\N	\N	2257	{"text": "We rushed over the brow of the hill, and there was our man running with great speed down the other side, springing over the stones in his way with the activity of a mountain goat.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2259	lexical	\N	\N	2258	{"text": "A lucky long shot of my revolver might have crippled him, but I had brought it only to defend myself if attacked and not to shoot an unarmed man who was running away.", "section": "section_58", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2260	lexical	\N	\N	2259	{"text": "We were both swift runners and in fairly good training, but we soon found that we had no chance of overtaking him.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2261	lexical	\N	\N	2260	{"text": "We saw him for a long time in the moonlight until he was only a small speck moving swiftly among the boulders upon the side of a distant hill.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2262	lexical	\N	\N	2261	{"text": "We ran and ran until we were completely blown, but the space between us grew ever wider.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2263	lexical	\N	\N	2262	{"text": "Finally we stopped and sat panting on two rocks, while we watched him disappearing in the distance.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2264	lexical	\N	\N	2263	{"text": "And it was at this moment that there occurred a most strange and unexpected thing.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2265	lexical	\N	\N	2264	{"text": "We had risen from our rocks and were turning to go home, having abandoned the hopeless chase.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2266	lexical	\N	\N	2265	{"text": "The moon was low upon the right, and the jagged pinnacle of a granite tor stood up against the lower curve of its silver disc.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2267	lexical	\N	\N	2266	{"text": "There, outlined as black as an ebony statue on that shining background, I saw the figure of a man upon the tor.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2268	lexical	\N	\N	2267	{"text": "Do not think that it was a delusion, Holmes.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2269	lexical	\N	\N	2268	{"text": "I assure you that I have never in my life seen anything more clearly.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2270	lexical	\N	\N	2269	{"text": "As far as I could judge, the figure was that of a tall, thin man.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2271	lexical	\N	\N	2270	{"text": "He stood with his legs a little separated, his arms folded, his head bowed, as if he were brooding over that enormous wilderness of peat and granite which lay before him.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2272	lexical	\N	\N	2271	{"text": "He might have been the very spirit of that terrible place.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2273	lexical	\N	\N	2272	{"text": "It was not the convict.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2274	lexical	\N	\N	2273	{"text": "This man was far from the place where the latter had disappeared.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2275	lexical	\N	\N	2274	{"text": "Besides, he was a much taller man.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2276	lexical	\N	\N	2275	{"text": "With a cry of surprise I pointed him out to the baronet, but in the instant during which I had turned to grasp his arm the man was gone.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2277	lexical	\N	\N	2276	{"text": "There was the sharp pinnacle of granite still cutting the lower edge of the moon, but its peak bore no trace of that silent and motionless figure.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2278	lexical	\N	\N	2277	{"text": "I wished to go in that direction and to search the tor, but it was some distance away.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2279	lexical	\N	\N	2278	{"text": "The baronet’s nerves were still quivering from that cry, which recalled the dark story of his family, and he was not in the mood for fresh adventures.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2280	lexical	\N	\N	2279	{"text": "He had not seen this lonely man upon the tor and could not feel the thrill which his strange presence and his commanding attitude had given to me.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2281	lexical	\N	\N	2280	{"text": "“A warder, no doubt,” said he.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2282	lexical	\N	\N	2281	{"text": "“The moor has been thick with them since this fellow escaped.”", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2283	lexical	\N	\N	2282	{"text": "Well, perhaps his explanation may be the right one, but I should like to have some further proof of it.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2284	lexical	\N	\N	2283	{"text": "Today we mean to communicate to the Princetown people where they should look for their missing man, but it is hard lines that we have not actually had the triumph of bringing him back as our own prisoner.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2285	lexical	\N	\N	2284	{"text": "Such are the adventures of last night, and you must acknowledge, my dear Holmes, that I have done you very well in the matter of a report.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2286	lexical	\N	\N	2285	{"text": "Much of what I tell you is no doubt quite irrelevant, but still I feel that it is best that I should let you have all the facts and leave you to select for yourself those which will be of most service to you in helping you to your conclusions.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2287	lexical	\N	\N	2286	{"text": "We are certainly making some progress.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2288	lexical	\N	\N	2287	{"text": "So far as the Barrymores go we have found the motive of their actions, and that has cleared up the situation very much.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2289	lexical	\N	\N	2288	{"text": "But the moor with its mysteries and its strange inhabitants remains as inscrutable as ever.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2290	lexical	\N	\N	2289	{"text": "Perhaps in my next I may be able to throw some light upon this also.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2291	lexical	\N	\N	2290	{"text": "Best of all would it be if you could come down to us.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2292	lexical	\N	\N	2291	{"text": "In any case you will hear from me again in the course of the next few days.", "section": "section_59", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2293	lexical	\N	\N	2292	{"text": "Chapter 10.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2294	lexical	\N	\N	2293	{"text": "Extract from the Diary of Dr. Watson", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2295	lexical	\N	\N	2294	{"text": "So far I have been able to quote from the reports which I have forwarded during these early days to Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2296	lexical	\N	\N	2295	{"text": "Now, however, I have arrived at a point in my narrative where I am compelled to abandon this method and to trust once more to my recollections, aided by the diary which I kept at the time.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2297	lexical	\N	\N	2296	{"text": "A few extracts from the latter will carry me on to those scenes which are indelibly fixed in every detail upon my memory.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2298	lexical	\N	\N	2297	{"text": "I proceed, then, from the morning which followed our abortive chase of the convict and our other strange experiences upon the moor.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2299	lexical	\N	\N	2298	{"text": "—A dull and foggy day with a drizzle of rain.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2300	lexical	\N	\N	2299	{"text": "The house is banked in with rolling clouds, which rise now and then to show the dreary curves of the moor, with thin, silver veins upon the sides of the hills, and the distant boulders gleaming where the light strikes upon their wet faces.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2301	lexical	\N	\N	2300	{"text": "It is melancholy outside and in.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2302	lexical	\N	\N	2301	{"text": "The baronet is in a black reaction after the excitements of the night.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2303	lexical	\N	\N	2302	{"text": "I am conscious myself of a weight at my heart and a feeling of impending danger—ever present danger, which is the more terrible because I am unable to define it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2304	lexical	\N	\N	2303	{"text": "ble to define it.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2305	lexical	\N	\N	2304	{"text": "And have I not cause for such a feeling?", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2306	lexical	\N	\N	2305	{"text": "Consider the long sequence of incidents which have all pointed to some sinister influence which is at work around us.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2307	lexical	\N	\N	2306	{"text": "There is the death of the last occupant of the Hall, fulfilling so exactly the conditions of the family legend, and there are the repeated reports from peasants of the appearance of a strange creature upon the moor.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2308	lexical	\N	\N	2307	{"text": "Twice I have with my own ears heard the sound which resembled the distant baying of a hound.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2309	lexical	\N	\N	2308	{"text": "It is incredible, impossible, that it should really be outside the ordinary laws of nature.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2310	lexical	\N	\N	2309	{"text": "A spectral hound which leaves material footmarks and fills the air with its howling is surely not to be thought of.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2311	lexical	\N	\N	2310	{"text": "Stapleton may fall in with such a superstition, and Mortimer also, but if I have one quality upon earth it is common sense, and nothing will persuade me to believe in such a thing.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2312	lexical	\N	\N	2311	{"text": "To do so would be to descend to the level of these poor peasants, who are not content with a mere fiend dog but must needs describe him with hell-fire shooting from his mouth and eyes.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2313	lexical	\N	\N	2312	{"text": "Holmes would not listen to such fancies, and I am his agent.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2314	lexical	\N	\N	2313	{"text": "But facts are facts, and I have twice heard this crying upon the moor.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2315	lexical	\N	\N	2314	{"text": "Suppose that there were really some huge hound loose upon it; that would go far to explain everything.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2316	lexical	\N	\N	2315	{"text": "But where could such a hound lie concealed, where did it get its food, where did it come from, how was it that no one saw it by day?", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2317	lexical	\N	\N	2316	{"text": "It must be confessed that the natural explanation offers almost as many difficulties as the other.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2318	lexical	\N	\N	2317	{"text": "And always, apart from the hound, there is the fact of the human agency in London, the man in the cab, and the letter which warned Sir Henry against the moor.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2319	lexical	\N	\N	2318	{"text": "This at least was real, but it might have been the work of a protecting friend as easily as of an enemy.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2320	lexical	\N	\N	2319	{"text": "Where is that friend or enemy now?", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2321	lexical	\N	\N	2320	{"text": "Has he remained in London, or has he followed us down here?", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2322	lexical	\N	\N	2321	{"text": "Could he—could he be the stranger whom I saw upon the tor?", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2323	lexical	\N	\N	2322	{"text": "It is true that I have had only the one glance at him, and yet there are some things to which I am ready to swear.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2324	lexical	\N	\N	2323	{"text": "He is no one whom I have seen down here, and I have now met all the neighbours.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2325	lexical	\N	\N	2324	{"text": "The figure was far taller than that of Stapleton, far thinner than that of Frankland.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2326	lexical	\N	\N	2325	{"text": "Barrymore it might possibly have been, but we had left him behind us, and I am certain that he could not have followed us.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2327	lexical	\N	\N	2326	{"text": "A stranger then is still dogging us, just as a stranger dogged us in London.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2328	lexical	\N	\N	2327	{"text": "We have never shaken him off.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2329	lexical	\N	\N	2328	{"text": "If I could lay my hands upon that man, then at last we might find ourselves at the end of all our difficulties.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2330	lexical	\N	\N	2329	{"text": "To this one purpose I must now devote all my energies.", "section": "section_60", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2331	lexical	\N	\N	2330	{"text": "My first impulse was to tell Sir Henry all my plans.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2332	lexical	\N	\N	2331	{"text": "My second and wisest one is to play my own game and speak as little as possible to anyone.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2333	lexical	\N	\N	2332	{"text": "He is silent and distrait.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2334	lexical	\N	\N	2333	{"text": "His nerves have been strangely shaken by that sound upon the moor.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2335	lexical	\N	\N	2334	{"text": "I will say nothing to add to his anxieties, but I will take my own steps to attain my own end.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2336	lexical	\N	\N	2335	{"text": "We had a small scene this morning after breakfast.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2337	lexical	\N	\N	2336	{"text": "Barrymore asked leave to speak with Sir Henry, and they were closeted in his study some little time.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2338	lexical	\N	\N	2337	{"text": "Sitting in the billiard-room I more than once heard the sound of voices raised, and I had a pretty good idea what the point was which was under discussion.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2339	lexical	\N	\N	2338	{"text": "After a time the baronet opened his door and called for me.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2340	lexical	\N	\N	2339	{"text": "“Barrymore considers that he has a grievance,” he said.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2341	lexical	\N	\N	2340	{"text": "“He thinks that it was unfair on our part to hunt his brother-in-law down when he, of his own free will, had told us the secret.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2342	lexical	\N	\N	2341	{"text": "The butler was standing very pale but very collected before us.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2343	lexical	\N	\N	2342	{"text": "“I may have spoken too warmly, sir,” said he, “and if I have, I am sure that I beg your pardon.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2344	lexical	\N	\N	2343	{"text": "At the same time, I was very much surprised when I heard you two gentlemen come back this morning and learned that you had been chasing Selden.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2345	lexical	\N	\N	2344	{"text": "The poor fellow has enough to fight against without my putting more upon his track.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2346	lexical	\N	\N	2345	{"text": "“If you had told us of your own free will it would have been a different thing,” said the baronet, “you only told us, or rather your wife only told us, when it was forced from you and you could not help yourself.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2347	lexical	\N	\N	2346	{"text": "“I didn’t think you would have taken advantage of it, Sir Henry—indeed I didn’t.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2348	lexical	\N	\N	2347	{"text": "“The man is a public danger.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2349	lexical	\N	\N	2348	{"text": "There are lonely houses scattered over the moor, and he is a fellow who would stick at nothing.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2350	lexical	\N	\N	2349	{"text": "You only want to get a glimpse of his face to see that.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2351	lexical	\N	\N	2350	{"text": "Look at Mr. Stapleton’s house, for example, with no one but himself to defend it.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2352	lexical	\N	\N	2351	{"text": "There’s no safety for anyone until he is under lock and key.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2353	lexical	\N	\N	2352	{"text": "“He’ll break into no house, sir.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2354	lexical	\N	\N	2353	{"text": "I give you my solemn word upon that.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2355	lexical	\N	\N	2354	{"text": "But he will never trouble anyone in this country again.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2356	lexical	\N	\N	2355	{"text": "I assure you, Sir Henry, that in a very few days the necessary arrangements will have been made and he will be on his way to South America.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2357	lexical	\N	\N	2356	{"text": "For God’s sake, sir, I beg of you not to let the police know that he is still on the moor.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2358	lexical	\N	\N	2357	{"text": "They have given up the chase there, and he can lie quiet until the ship is ready for him.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2359	lexical	\N	\N	2358	{"text": "You can’t tell on him without getting my wife and me into trouble.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2360	lexical	\N	\N	2359	{"text": "I beg you, sir, to say nothing to the police.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2361	lexical	\N	\N	2360	{"text": "“What do you say, Watson?”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2362	lexical	\N	\N	2361	{"text": "I shrugged my shoulders.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2363	lexical	\N	\N	2362	{"text": "“If he were safely out of the country it would relieve the tax-payer of a burden.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2364	lexical	\N	\N	2363	{"text": "“But how about the chance of his holding someone up before he goes?”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2365	lexical	\N	\N	2364	{"text": "“He would not do anything so mad, sir.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2366	lexical	\N	\N	2365	{"text": "We have provided him with all that he can want.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2367	lexical	\N	\N	2366	{"text": "To commit a crime would be to show where he was hiding.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2368	lexical	\N	\N	2367	{"text": "“That is true,” said Sir Henry.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2369	lexical	\N	\N	2368	{"text": "“Well, Barrymore—”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2370	lexical	\N	\N	2369	{"text": "“God bless you, sir, and thank you from my heart!", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2371	lexical	\N	\N	2370	{"text": "It would have killed my poor wife had he been taken again.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2372	lexical	\N	\N	2371	{"text": "“I guess we are aiding and abetting a felony, Watson?", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2373	lexical	\N	\N	2372	{"text": "But, after what we have heard I don’t feel as if I could give the man up, so there is an end of it.", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2374	lexical	\N	\N	2373	{"text": "All right, Barrymore, you can go.”", "section": "section_61", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2375	lexical	\N	\N	2374	{"text": "With a few broken words of gratitude the man turned, but he hesitated and then came back.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2376	lexical	\N	\N	2375	{"text": "“You’ve been so kind to us, sir, that I should like to do the best I can for you in return.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2377	lexical	\N	\N	2376	{"text": "I know something, Sir Henry, and perhaps I should have said it before, but it was long after the inquest that I found it out.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2378	lexical	\N	\N	2377	{"text": "I’ve never breathed a word about it yet to mortal man.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2379	lexical	\N	\N	2378	{"text": "It’s about poor Sir Charles’s death.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2380	lexical	\N	\N	2379	{"text": "The baronet and I were both upon our feet.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2381	lexical	\N	\N	2380	{"text": "“Do you know how he died?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2382	lexical	\N	\N	2381	{"text": "“No, sir, I don’t know that.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2383	lexical	\N	\N	2382	{"text": "“What then?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2384	lexical	\N	\N	2383	{"text": "“I know why he was at the gate at that hour.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2385	lexical	\N	\N	2384	{"text": "It was to meet a woman.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2386	lexical	\N	\N	2385	{"text": "“To meet a woman!", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2387	lexical	\N	\N	2386	{"text": "He?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2388	lexical	\N	\N	2387	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2389	lexical	\N	\N	2388	{"text": "“And the woman’s name?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2390	lexical	\N	\N	2389	{"text": "“I can’t give you the name, sir, but I can give you the initials.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2391	lexical	\N	\N	2390	{"text": "Her initials were L.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2392	lexical	\N	\N	2391	{"text": "L.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2393	lexical	\N	\N	2392	{"text": "“How do you know this, Barrymore?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2394	lexical	\N	\N	2393	{"text": "“Well, Sir Henry, your uncle had a letter that morning.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2395	lexical	\N	\N	2394	{"text": "He had usually a great many letters, for he was a public man and well known for his kind heart, so that everyone who was in trouble was glad to turn to him.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2396	lexical	\N	\N	2395	{"text": "But that morning, as it chanced, there was only this one letter, so I took the more notice of it.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2397	lexical	\N	\N	2396	{"text": "It was from Coombe Tracey, and it was addressed in a woman’s hand.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2398	lexical	\N	\N	2397	{"text": "“Well?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2399	lexical	\N	\N	2398	{"text": "“Well, sir, I thought no more of the matter, and never would have done had it not been for my wife.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2400	lexical	\N	\N	2399	{"text": "Only a few weeks ago she was cleaning out Sir Charles’s study—it had never been touched since his death—and she found the ashes of a burned letter in the back of the grate.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2401	lexical	\N	\N	2400	{"text": "The greater part of it was charred to pieces, but one little slip, the end of a page, hung together, and the writing could still be read, though it was grey on a black ground.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2402	lexical	\N	\N	2401	{"text": "It seemed to us to be a postscript at the end of the letter and it said: ‘Please, please, as you are a gentleman, burn this letter, and be at the gate by ten o clock.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2403	lexical	\N	\N	2402	{"text": "Beneath it were signed the initials L.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2404	lexical	\N	\N	2403	{"text": "L.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2405	lexical	\N	\N	2404	{"text": "“Have you got that slip?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2406	lexical	\N	\N	2405	{"text": "“No, sir, it crumbled all to bits after we moved it.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2407	lexical	\N	\N	2406	{"text": "“Had Sir Charles received any other letters in the same writing?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2408	lexical	\N	\N	2407	{"text": "“Well, sir, I took no particular notice of his letters.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2409	lexical	\N	\N	2408	{"text": "I should not have noticed this one, only it happened to come alone.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2410	lexical	\N	\N	2409	{"text": "“And you have no idea who L.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2411	lexical	\N	\N	2410	{"text": "L.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2412	lexical	\N	\N	2411	{"text": "is?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2413	lexical	\N	\N	2412	{"text": "“No, sir.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2414	lexical	\N	\N	2413	{"text": "No more than you have.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2415	lexical	\N	\N	2414	{"text": "But I expect if we could lay our hands upon that lady we should know more about Sir Charles’s death.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2416	lexical	\N	\N	2415	{"text": "“I cannot understand, Barrymore, how you came to conceal this important information.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2417	lexical	\N	\N	2416	{"text": "“Well, sir, it was immediately after that our own trouble came to us.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2418	lexical	\N	\N	2417	{"text": "And then again, sir, we were both of us very fond of Sir Charles, as we well might be considering all that he has done for us.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2419	lexical	\N	\N	2418	{"text": "To rake this up couldn’t help our poor master, and it’s well to go carefully when there’s a lady in the case.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2420	lexical	\N	\N	2419	{"text": "Even the best of us—”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2421	lexical	\N	\N	2420	{"text": "“You thought it might injure his reputation?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2422	lexical	\N	\N	2421	{"text": "“Well, sir, I thought no good could come of it.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2423	lexical	\N	\N	2422	{"text": "But now you have been kind to us, and I feel as if it would be treating you unfairly not to tell you all that I know about the matter.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2424	lexical	\N	\N	2423	{"text": "“Very good, Barrymore; you can go.”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2425	lexical	\N	\N	2424	{"text": "When the butler had left us Sir Henry turned to me.", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2426	lexical	\N	\N	2425	{"text": "“Well, Watson, what do you think of this new light?”", "section": "section_62", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2427	lexical	\N	\N	2426	{"text": "“It seems to leave the darkness rather blacker than before.”", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2428	lexical	\N	\N	2427	{"text": "“So I think.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2429	lexical	\N	\N	2428	{"text": "But if we can only trace L.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2430	lexical	\N	\N	2429	{"text": "L.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2431	lexical	\N	\N	2430	{"text": "it should clear up the whole business.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2432	lexical	\N	\N	2431	{"text": "We have gained that much.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2433	lexical	\N	\N	2432	{"text": "We know that there is someone who has the facts if we can only find her.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2434	lexical	\N	\N	2433	{"text": "What do you think we should do?”", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2435	lexical	\N	\N	2434	{"text": "“Let Holmes know all about it at once.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2436	lexical	\N	\N	2435	{"text": "It will give him the clue for which he has been seeking.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2437	lexical	\N	\N	2436	{"text": "I am much mistaken if it does not bring him down.”", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2438	lexical	\N	\N	2437	{"text": "I went at once to my room and drew up my report of the morning’s conversation for Holmes.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2439	lexical	\N	\N	2438	{"text": "It was evident to me that he had been very busy of late, for the notes which I had from Baker Street were few and short, with no comments upon the information which I had supplied and hardly any reference to my mission.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2440	lexical	\N	\N	2439	{"text": "No doubt his blackmailing case is absorbing all his faculties.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2441	lexical	\N	\N	2440	{"text": "And yet this new factor must surely arrest his attention and renew his interest.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2442	lexical	\N	\N	2441	{"text": "I wish that he were here.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2443	lexical	\N	\N	2442	{"text": "—All day today the rain poured down, rustling on the ivy and dripping from the eaves.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2444	lexical	\N	\N	2443	{"text": "I thought of the convict out upon the bleak, cold, shelterless moor.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2445	lexical	\N	\N	2444	{"text": "Poor devil!", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2446	lexical	\N	\N	2445	{"text": "Whatever his crimes, he has suffered something to atone for them.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2447	lexical	\N	\N	2446	{"text": "And then I thought of that other one—the face in the cab, the figure against the moon.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2448	lexical	\N	\N	2447	{"text": "Was he also out in that deluge—the unseen watcher, the man of darkness?", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2449	lexical	\N	\N	2448	{"text": "In the evening I put on my waterproof and I walked far upon the sodden moor, full of dark imaginings, the rain beating upon my face and the wind whistling about my ears.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2450	lexical	\N	\N	2449	{"text": "God help those who wander into the great mire now, for even the firm uplands are becoming a morass.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2451	lexical	\N	\N	2450	{"text": "I found the black tor upon which I had seen the solitary watcher, and from its craggy summit I looked out myself across the melancholy downs.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2452	lexical	\N	\N	2451	{"text": "Rain squalls drifted across their russet face, and the heavy, slate-coloured clouds hung low over the landscape, trailing in grey wreaths down the sides of the fantastic hills.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2453	lexical	\N	\N	2452	{"text": "In the distant hollow on the left, half hidden by the mist, the two thin towers of Baskerville Hall rose above the trees.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2454	lexical	\N	\N	2453	{"text": "They were the only signs of human life which I could see, save only those prehistoric huts which lay thickly upon the slopes of the hills.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2455	lexical	\N	\N	2454	{"text": "Nowhere was there any trace of that lonely man whom I had seen on the same spot two nights before.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2456	lexical	\N	\N	2455	{"text": "wo nights before.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2457	lexical	\N	\N	2456	{"text": "As I walked back I was overtaken by Dr. Mortimer driving in his dog-cart over a rough moorland track which led from the outlying farmhouse of Foulmire.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2458	lexical	\N	\N	2457	{"text": "He has been very attentive to us, and hardly a day has passed that he has not called at the Hall to see how we were getting on.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2459	lexical	\N	\N	2458	{"text": "He insisted upon my climbing into his dog-cart, and he gave me a lift homeward.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2460	lexical	\N	\N	2459	{"text": "I found him much troubled over the disappearance of his little spaniel.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2461	lexical	\N	\N	2460	{"text": "It had wandered on to the moor and had never come back.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2462	lexical	\N	\N	2461	{"text": "I gave him such consolation as I might, but I thought of the pony on the Grimpen Mire, and I do not fancy that he will see his little dog again.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2463	lexical	\N	\N	2462	{"text": "“By the way, Mortimer,” said I as we jolted along the rough road, “I suppose there are few people living within driving distance of this whom you do not know?”", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2464	lexical	\N	\N	2463	{"text": "“Hardly any, I think.”", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2465	lexical	\N	\N	2464	{"text": "“Can you, then, tell me the name of any woman whose initials are L.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2466	lexical	\N	\N	2465	{"text": "L.?”", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2467	lexical	\N	\N	2466	{"text": "He thought for a few minutes.", "section": "section_63", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2468	lexical	\N	\N	2467	{"text": "“No,” said he.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2469	lexical	\N	\N	2468	{"text": "“There are a few gipsies and labouring folk for whom I can’t answer, but among the farmers or gentry there is no one whose initials are those.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2470	lexical	\N	\N	2469	{"text": "Wait a bit though,” he added after a pause.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2471	lexical	\N	\N	2470	{"text": "“There is Laura Lyons—her initials are L.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2472	lexical	\N	\N	2471	{"text": "—but she lives in Coombe Tracey.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2473	lexical	\N	\N	2472	{"text": ".”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2474	lexical	\N	\N	2473	{"text": "“Who is she?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2475	lexical	\N	\N	2474	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2476	lexical	\N	\N	2475	{"text": "“She is Frankland’s daughter.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2477	lexical	\N	\N	2476	{"text": "“What!", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2478	lexical	\N	\N	2477	{"text": "Old Frankland the crank?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2479	lexical	\N	\N	2478	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2480	lexical	\N	\N	2479	{"text": "She married an artist named Lyons, who came sketching on the moor.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2481	lexical	\N	\N	2480	{"text": "He proved to be a blackguard and deserted her.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2482	lexical	\N	\N	2481	{"text": "The fault from what I hear may not have been entirely on one side.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2483	lexical	\N	\N	2482	{"text": "Her father refused to have anything to do with her because she had married without his consent and perhaps for one or two other reasons as well.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2484	lexical	\N	\N	2483	{"text": "So, between the old sinner and the young one the girl has had a pretty bad time.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2485	lexical	\N	\N	2484	{"text": "“How does she live?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2486	lexical	\N	\N	2485	{"text": "“I fancy old Frankland allows her a pittance, but it cannot be more, for his own affairs are considerably involved.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2487	lexical	\N	\N	2486	{"text": "Whatever she may have deserved one could not allow her to go hopelessly to the bad.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2488	lexical	\N	\N	2487	{"text": "Her story got about, and several of the people here did something to enable her to earn an honest living.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2489	lexical	\N	\N	2488	{"text": "Stapleton did for one, and Sir Charles for another.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2490	lexical	\N	\N	2489	{"text": "I gave a trifle myself.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2491	lexical	\N	\N	2490	{"text": "It was to set her up in a typewriting business.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2492	lexical	\N	\N	2491	{"text": "He wanted to know the object of my inquiries, but I managed to satisfy his curiosity without telling him too much, for there is no reason why we should take anyone into our confidence.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2493	lexical	\N	\N	2492	{"text": "Tomorrow morning I shall find my way to Coombe Tracey, and if I can see this Mrs. Laura Lyons, of equivocal reputation, a long step will have been made towards clearing one incident in this chain of mysteries.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2494	lexical	\N	\N	2493	{"text": "I am certainly developing the wisdom of the serpent, for when Mortimer pressed his questions to an inconvenient extent I asked him casually to what type Frankland’s skull belonged, and so heard nothing but craniology for the rest of our drive.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2495	lexical	\N	\N	2494	{"text": "I have not lived for years with Sherlock Holmes for nothing.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2496	lexical	\N	\N	2495	{"text": "I have only one other incident to record upon this tempestuous and melancholy day.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2497	lexical	\N	\N	2496	{"text": "This was my conversation with Barrymore just now, which gives me one more strong card which I can play in due time.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2498	lexical	\N	\N	2497	{"text": "Mortimer had stayed to dinner, and he and the baronet played écarté afterwards.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2499	lexical	\N	\N	2498	{"text": "The butler brought me my coffee into the library, and I took the chance to ask him a few questions.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2500	lexical	\N	\N	2499	{"text": "“Well,” said I, “has this precious relation of yours departed, or is he still lurking out yonder?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2501	lexical	\N	\N	2500	{"text": "“I don’t know, sir.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2502	lexical	\N	\N	2501	{"text": "I hope to heaven that he has gone, for he has brought nothing but trouble here!", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2503	lexical	\N	\N	2502	{"text": "I’ve not heard of him since I left out food for him last, and that was three days ago.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2504	lexical	\N	\N	2503	{"text": "“Did you see him then?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2505	lexical	\N	\N	2504	{"text": "“No, sir, but the food was gone when next I went that way.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2506	lexical	\N	\N	2505	{"text": "“Then he was certainly there?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2507	lexical	\N	\N	2506	{"text": "“So you would think, sir, unless it was the other man who took it.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2508	lexical	\N	\N	2507	{"text": "I sat with my coffee-cup halfway to my lips and stared at Barrymore.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2509	lexical	\N	\N	2508	{"text": "“You know that there is another man then?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2510	lexical	\N	\N	2509	{"text": "“Yes, sir; there is another man upon the moor.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2511	lexical	\N	\N	2510	{"text": "“Have you seen him?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2513	lexical	\N	\N	2512	{"text": "“How do you know of him then?”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2514	lexical	\N	\N	2513	{"text": "“Selden told me of him, sir, a week ago or more.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2515	lexical	\N	\N	2514	{"text": "He’s in hiding, too, but he’s not a convict as far as I can make out.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2516	lexical	\N	\N	2515	{"text": "I don’t like it, Dr. Watson—I tell you straight, sir, that I don’t like it.”", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2517	lexical	\N	\N	2516	{"text": "He spoke with a sudden passion of earnestness.", "section": "section_64", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2518	lexical	\N	\N	2517	{"text": "“Now, listen to me, Barrymore!", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2519	lexical	\N	\N	2518	{"text": "I have no interest in this matter but that of your master.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2520	lexical	\N	\N	2519	{"text": "I have come here with no object except to help him.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2521	lexical	\N	\N	2520	{"text": "Tell me, frankly, what it is that you don’t like.”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2522	lexical	\N	\N	2521	{"text": "Barrymore hesitated for a moment, as if he regretted his outburst or found it difficult to express his own feelings in words.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2523	lexical	\N	\N	2522	{"text": "“It’s all these goings-on, sir,” he cried at last, waving his hand towards the rain-lashed window which faced the moor.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2524	lexical	\N	\N	2523	{"text": "“There’s foul play somewhere, and there’s black villainy brewing, to that I’ll swear!", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2525	lexical	\N	\N	2524	{"text": "Very glad I should be, sir, to see Sir Henry on his way back to London again!”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2526	lexical	\N	\N	2525	{"text": "“But what is it that alarms you?”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2527	lexical	\N	\N	2526	{"text": "“Look at Sir Charles’s death!", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2528	lexical	\N	\N	2527	{"text": "That was bad enough, for all that the coroner said.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2529	lexical	\N	\N	2528	{"text": "Look at the noises on the moor at night.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2530	lexical	\N	\N	2529	{"text": "There’s not a man would cross it after sundown if he was paid for it.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2531	lexical	\N	\N	2530	{"text": "Look at this stranger hiding out yonder, and watching and waiting!", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2532	lexical	\N	\N	2531	{"text": "What’s he waiting for?", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2533	lexical	\N	\N	2532	{"text": "What does it mean?", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2534	lexical	\N	\N	2533	{"text": "It means no good to anyone of the name of Baskerville, and very glad I shall be to be quit of it all on the day that Sir Henry’s new servants are ready to take over the Hall.”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2535	lexical	\N	\N	2534	{"text": "“But about this stranger,” said I.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2536	lexical	\N	\N	2535	{"text": "“Can you tell me anything about him?", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2537	lexical	\N	\N	2536	{"text": "What did Selden say?", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2538	lexical	\N	\N	2537	{"text": "Did he find out where he hid, or what he was doing?”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2539	lexical	\N	\N	2538	{"text": "“He saw him once or twice, but he is a deep one and gives nothing away.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2540	lexical	\N	\N	2539	{"text": "At first he thought that he was the police, but soon he found that he had some lay of his own.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2541	lexical	\N	\N	2540	{"text": "A kind of gentleman he was, as far as he could see, but what he was doing he could not make out.”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2542	lexical	\N	\N	2541	{"text": "“And where did he say that he lived?”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2543	lexical	\N	\N	2542	{"text": "“Among the old houses on the hillside—the stone huts where the old folk used to live.”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2544	lexical	\N	\N	2543	{"text": "“But how about his food?”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2545	lexical	\N	\N	2544	{"text": "“Selden found out that he has got a lad who works for him and brings all he needs.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2546	lexical	\N	\N	2545	{"text": "I dare say he goes to Coombe Tracey for what he wants.”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2547	lexical	\N	\N	2546	{"text": "“Very good, Barrymore.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2548	lexical	\N	\N	2547	{"text": "We may talk further of this some other time.”", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2549	lexical	\N	\N	2548	{"text": "When the butler had gone I walked over to the black window, and I looked through a blurred pane at the driving clouds and at the tossing outline of the wind-swept trees.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2550	lexical	\N	\N	2549	{"text": "It is a wild night indoors, and what must it be in a stone hut upon the moor.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2551	lexical	\N	\N	2550	{"text": "What passion of hatred can it be which leads a man to lurk in such a place at such a time!", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2552	lexical	\N	\N	2551	{"text": "And what deep and earnest purpose can he have which calls for such a trial!", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2553	lexical	\N	\N	2552	{"text": "There, in that hut upon the moor, seems to lie the very centre of that problem which has vexed me so sorely.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2554	lexical	\N	\N	2553	{"text": "I swear that another day shall not have passed before I have done all that man can do to reach the heart of the mystery.", "section": "section_65", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2555	lexical	\N	\N	2554	{"text": "Chapter 11.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2556	lexical	\N	\N	2555	{"text": "The Man on the Tor", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2557	lexical	\N	\N	2556	{"text": "The extract from my private diary which forms the last chapter has brought my narrative up to the eighteenth of October, a time when these strange events began to move swiftly towards their terrible conclusion.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2558	lexical	\N	\N	2557	{"text": "The incidents of the next few days are indelibly graven upon my recollection, and I can tell them without reference to the notes made at the time.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2559	lexical	\N	\N	2558	{"text": "I start them from the day which succeeded that upon which I had established two facts of great importance, the one that Mrs. Laura Lyons of Coombe Tracey had written to Sir Charles Baskerville and made an appointment with him at the very place and hour that he met his death, the other that the lurking man upon the moor was to be found among the stone huts upon the hillside.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2560	lexical	\N	\N	2559	{"text": "With these two facts in my possession I felt that either my intelligence or my courage must be deficient if I could not throw some further light upon these dark places.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2561	lexical	\N	\N	2560	{"text": "I had no opportunity to tell the baronet what I had learned about Mrs. Lyons upon the evening before, for Dr. Mortimer remained with him at cards until it was very late.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2562	lexical	\N	\N	2561	{"text": "At breakfast, however, I informed him about my discovery and asked him whether he would care to accompany me to Coombe Tracey.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2563	lexical	\N	\N	2562	{"text": "At first he was very eager to come, but on second thoughts it seemed to both of us that if I went alone the results might be better.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2564	lexical	\N	\N	2563	{"text": "The more formal we made the visit the less information we might obtain.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2565	lexical	\N	\N	2564	{"text": "I left Sir Henry behind, therefore, not without some prickings of conscience, and drove off upon my new quest.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2566	lexical	\N	\N	2565	{"text": "When I reached Coombe Tracey I told Perkins to put up the horses, and I made inquiries for the lady whom I had come to interrogate.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2567	lexical	\N	\N	2566	{"text": "I had no difficulty in finding her rooms, which were central and well appointed.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2568	lexical	\N	\N	2567	{"text": "A maid showed me in without ceremony, and as I entered the sitting-room a lady, who was sitting before a Remington typewriter, sprang up with a pleasant smile of welcome.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2569	lexical	\N	\N	2568	{"text": "Her face fell, however, when she saw that I was a stranger, and she sat down again and asked me the object of my visit.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2570	lexical	\N	\N	2569	{"text": "The first impression left by Mrs. Lyons was one of extreme beauty.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2571	lexical	\N	\N	2570	{"text": "Her eyes and hair were of the same rich hazel colour, and her cheeks, though considerably freckled, were flushed with the exquisite bloom of the brunette, the dainty pink which lurks at the heart of the sulphur rose.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2572	lexical	\N	\N	2571	{"text": "Admiration was, I repeat, the first impression.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2573	lexical	\N	\N	2572	{"text": "But the second was criticism.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2574	lexical	\N	\N	2573	{"text": "There was something subtly wrong with the face, some coarseness of expression, some hardness, perhaps, of eye, some looseness of lip which marred its perfect beauty.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2575	lexical	\N	\N	2574	{"text": "But these, of course, are afterthoughts.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2576	lexical	\N	\N	2575	{"text": "At the moment I was simply conscious that I was in the presence of a very handsome woman, and that she was asking me the reasons for my visit.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2577	lexical	\N	\N	2576	{"text": "I had not quite understood until that instant how delicate my mission was.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2578	lexical	\N	\N	2577	{"text": "“I have the pleasure,” said I, “of knowing your father.”", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2579	lexical	\N	\N	2578	{"text": "It was a clumsy introduction, and the lady made me feel it.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2580	lexical	\N	\N	2579	{"text": "“There is nothing in common between my father and me,” she said.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2581	lexical	\N	\N	2580	{"text": "“I owe him nothing, and his friends are not mine.", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2582	lexical	\N	\N	2581	{"text": "If it were not for the late Sir Charles Baskerville and some other kind hearts I might have starved for all that my father cared.”", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2583	lexical	\N	\N	2582	{"text": "“It was about the late Sir Charles Baskerville that I have come here to see you.”", "section": "section_66", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2584	lexical	\N	\N	2583	{"text": "The freckles started out on the lady’s face.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2585	lexical	\N	\N	2584	{"text": "“What can I tell you about him?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2586	lexical	\N	\N	2585	{"text": "she asked, and her fingers played nervously over the stops of her typewriter.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2587	lexical	\N	\N	2586	{"text": "“You knew him, did you not?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2588	lexical	\N	\N	2587	{"text": "“I have already said that I owe a great deal to his kindness.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2589	lexical	\N	\N	2588	{"text": "If I am able to support myself it is largely due to the interest which he took in my unhappy situation.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2590	lexical	\N	\N	2589	{"text": "“Did you correspond with him?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2591	lexical	\N	\N	2590	{"text": "The lady looked quickly up with an angry gleam in her hazel eyes.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2592	lexical	\N	\N	2591	{"text": "“What is the object of these questions?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2593	lexical	\N	\N	2592	{"text": "she asked sharply.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2594	lexical	\N	\N	2593	{"text": "“The object is to avoid a public scandal.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2595	lexical	\N	\N	2594	{"text": "It is better that I should ask them here than that the matter should pass outside our control.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2596	lexical	\N	\N	2595	{"text": "She was silent and her face was still very pale.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2597	lexical	\N	\N	2596	{"text": "At last she looked up with something reckless and defiant in her manner.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2598	lexical	\N	\N	2597	{"text": "“Well, I’ll answer,” she said.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2599	lexical	\N	\N	2598	{"text": "“What are your questions?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2600	lexical	\N	\N	2599	{"text": "“Did you correspond with Sir Charles?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2601	lexical	\N	\N	2600	{"text": "“I certainly wrote to him once or twice to acknowledge his delicacy and his generosity.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2602	lexical	\N	\N	2601	{"text": "“Have you the dates of those letters?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2603	lexical	\N	\N	2602	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2604	lexical	\N	\N	2603	{"text": "“Have you ever met him?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2605	lexical	\N	\N	2604	{"text": "“Yes, once or twice, when he came into Coombe Tracey.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2606	lexical	\N	\N	2605	{"text": "He was a very retiring man, and he preferred to do good by stealth.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2607	lexical	\N	\N	2606	{"text": "“But if you saw him so seldom and wrote so seldom, how did he know enough about your affairs to be able to help you, as you say that he has done?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2608	lexical	\N	\N	2607	{"text": "She met my difficulty with the utmost readiness.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2609	lexical	\N	\N	2608	{"text": "“There were several gentlemen who knew my sad history and united to help me.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2610	lexical	\N	\N	2609	{"text": "One was Mr. Stapleton, a neighbour and intimate friend of Sir Charles’s.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2611	lexical	\N	\N	2610	{"text": "He was exceedingly kind, and it was through him that Sir Charles learned about my affairs.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2612	lexical	\N	\N	2611	{"text": "I knew already that Sir Charles Baskerville had made Stapleton his almoner upon several occasions, so the lady’s statement bore the impress of truth upon it.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2613	lexical	\N	\N	2612	{"text": "“Did you ever write to Sir Charles asking him to meet you?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2614	lexical	\N	\N	2613	{"text": "I continued.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2615	lexical	\N	\N	2614	{"text": "Mrs. Lyons flushed with anger again.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2616	lexical	\N	\N	2615	{"text": "“Really, sir, this is a very extraordinary question.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2617	lexical	\N	\N	2616	{"text": "“I am sorry, madam, but I must repeat it.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2618	lexical	\N	\N	2617	{"text": "“Then I answer, certainly not.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2619	lexical	\N	\N	2618	{"text": "“Not on the very day of Sir Charles’s death?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2728	lexical	\N	\N	2727	{"text": "I act entirely from a sense of public duty.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2620	lexical	\N	\N	2619	{"text": "The flush had faded in an instant, and a deathly face was before me.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2621	lexical	\N	\N	2620	{"text": "Her dry lips could not speak the “No” which I saw rather than heard.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2622	lexical	\N	\N	2621	{"text": "“Surely your memory deceives you,” said I.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2623	lexical	\N	\N	2622	{"text": "“I could even quote a passage of your letter.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2624	lexical	\N	\N	2623	{"text": "It ran ‘Please, please, as you are a gentleman, burn this letter, and be at the gate by ten o’clock.’”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2625	lexical	\N	\N	2624	{"text": "I thought that she had fainted, but she recovered herself by a supreme effort.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2626	lexical	\N	\N	2625	{"text": "“Is there no such thing as a gentleman?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2627	lexical	\N	\N	2626	{"text": "she gasped.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2628	lexical	\N	\N	2627	{"text": "“You do Sir Charles an injustice.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2629	lexical	\N	\N	2628	{"text": "He _did_ burn the letter.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2630	lexical	\N	\N	2629	{"text": "But sometimes a letter may be legible even when burned.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2631	lexical	\N	\N	2630	{"text": "You acknowledge now that you wrote it?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2632	lexical	\N	\N	2631	{"text": "“Yes, I did write it,” she cried, pouring out her soul in a torrent of words.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2633	lexical	\N	\N	2632	{"text": "“I did write it.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2634	lexical	\N	\N	2633	{"text": "Why should I deny it?", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2635	lexical	\N	\N	2634	{"text": "I have no reason to be ashamed of it.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2636	lexical	\N	\N	2635	{"text": "I wished him to help me.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2637	lexical	\N	\N	2636	{"text": "I believed that if I had an interview I could gain his help, so I asked him to meet me.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2638	lexical	\N	\N	2637	{"text": "“But why at such an hour?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2639	lexical	\N	\N	2638	{"text": "“Because I had only just learned that he was going to London next day and might be away for months.", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2640	lexical	\N	\N	2639	{"text": "There were reasons why I could not get there earlier.”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2641	lexical	\N	\N	2640	{"text": "“But why a rendezvous in the garden instead of a visit to the house?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2642	lexical	\N	\N	2641	{"text": "“Do you think a woman could go alone at that hour to a bachelor’s house?”", "section": "section_67", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2643	lexical	\N	\N	2642	{"text": "“Well, what happened when you did get there?”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2644	lexical	\N	\N	2643	{"text": "“I never went.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2645	lexical	\N	\N	2644	{"text": "“Mrs. Lyons!”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2646	lexical	\N	\N	2645	{"text": "“No, I swear it to you on all I hold sacred.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2647	lexical	\N	\N	2646	{"text": "I never went.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2648	lexical	\N	\N	2647	{"text": "Something intervened to prevent my going.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2649	lexical	\N	\N	2648	{"text": "“What was that?”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2650	lexical	\N	\N	2649	{"text": "“That is a private matter.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2651	lexical	\N	\N	2650	{"text": "I cannot tell it.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2652	lexical	\N	\N	2651	{"text": "“You acknowledge then that you made an appointment with Sir Charles at the very hour and place at which he met his death, but you deny that you kept the appointment.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2653	lexical	\N	\N	2652	{"text": "“That is the truth.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2654	lexical	\N	\N	2653	{"text": "Again and again I cross-questioned her, but I could never get past that point.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2655	lexical	\N	\N	2654	{"text": "“Mrs. Lyons,” said I as I rose from this long and inconclusive interview, “you are taking a very great responsibility and putting yourself in a very false position by not making an absolutely clean breast of all that you know.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2656	lexical	\N	\N	2655	{"text": "If I have to call in the aid of the police you will find how seriously you are compromised.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2657	lexical	\N	\N	2656	{"text": "If your position is innocent, why did you in the first instance deny having written to Sir Charles upon that date?”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2658	lexical	\N	\N	2657	{"text": "“Because I feared that some false conclusion might be drawn from it and that I might find myself involved in a scandal.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2659	lexical	\N	\N	2658	{"text": "“And why were you so pressing that Sir Charles should destroy your letter?”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2660	lexical	\N	\N	2659	{"text": "“If you have read the letter you will know.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2661	lexical	\N	\N	2660	{"text": "“I did not say that I had read all the letter.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2662	lexical	\N	\N	2661	{"text": "“You quoted some of it.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2663	lexical	\N	\N	2662	{"text": "“I quoted the postscript.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2664	lexical	\N	\N	2663	{"text": "The letter had, as I said, been burned and it was not all legible.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2665	lexical	\N	\N	2664	{"text": "I ask you once again why it was that you were so pressing that Sir Charles should destroy this letter which he received on the day of his death.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2666	lexical	\N	\N	2665	{"text": "“The matter is a very private one.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2667	lexical	\N	\N	2666	{"text": "“The more reason why you should avoid a public investigation.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2668	lexical	\N	\N	2667	{"text": "“I will tell you, then.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2669	lexical	\N	\N	2668	{"text": "If you have heard anything of my unhappy history you will know that I made a rash marriage and had reason to regret it.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2670	lexical	\N	\N	2669	{"text": "“I have heard so much.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2671	lexical	\N	\N	2670	{"text": "“My life has been one incessant persecution from a husband whom I abhor.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2672	lexical	\N	\N	2671	{"text": "The law is upon his side, and every day I am faced by the possibility that he may force me to live with him.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2673	lexical	\N	\N	2672	{"text": "At the time that I wrote this letter to Sir Charles I had learned that there was a prospect of my regaining my freedom if certain expenses could be met.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2674	lexical	\N	\N	2673	{"text": "It meant everything to me—peace of mind, happiness, self-respect—everything.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2675	lexical	\N	\N	2674	{"text": "I knew Sir Charles’s generosity, and I thought that if he heard the story from my own lips he would help me.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2676	lexical	\N	\N	2675	{"text": "“Then how is it that you did not go?”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2677	lexical	\N	\N	2676	{"text": "“Because I received help in the interval from another source.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2678	lexical	\N	\N	2677	{"text": "“Why then, did you not write to Sir Charles and explain this?”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2679	lexical	\N	\N	2678	{"text": "“So I should have done had I not seen his death in the paper next morning.”", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2680	lexical	\N	\N	2679	{"text": "The woman’s story hung coherently together, and all my questions were unable to shake it.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2681	lexical	\N	\N	2680	{"text": "I could only check it by finding if she had, indeed, instituted divorce proceedings against her husband at or about the time of the tragedy.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2682	lexical	\N	\N	2681	{"text": "It was unlikely that she would dare to say that she had not been to Baskerville Hall if she really had been, for a trap would be necessary to take her there, and could not have returned to Coombe Tracey until the early hours of the morning.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2683	lexical	\N	\N	2682	{"text": "Such an excursion could not be kept secret.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2684	lexical	\N	\N	2683	{"text": "The probability was, therefore, that she was telling the truth, or, at least, a part of the truth.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2685	lexical	\N	\N	2684	{"text": "I came away baffled and disheartened.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2686	lexical	\N	\N	2685	{"text": "Once again I had reached that dead wall which seemed to be built across every path by which I tried to get at the object of my mission.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2687	lexical	\N	\N	2686	{"text": "And yet the more I thought of the lady’s face and of her manner the more I felt that something was being held back from me.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2688	lexical	\N	\N	2687	{"text": "Why should she turn so pale?", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2689	lexical	\N	\N	2688	{"text": "Why should she fight against every admission until it was forced from her?", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2690	lexical	\N	\N	2689	{"text": "Why should she have been so reticent at the time of the tragedy?", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2691	lexical	\N	\N	2690	{"text": "Surely the explanation of all this could not be as innocent as she would have me believe.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2692	lexical	\N	\N	2691	{"text": "For the moment I could proceed no farther in that direction, but must turn back to that other clue which was to be sought for among the stone huts upon the moor.", "section": "section_68", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2693	lexical	\N	\N	2692	{"text": "And that was a most vague direction.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2694	lexical	\N	\N	2693	{"text": "I realised it as I drove back and noted how hill after hill showed traces of the ancient people.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2695	lexical	\N	\N	2694	{"text": "Barrymore’s only indication had been that the stranger lived in one of these abandoned huts, and many hundreds of them are scattered throughout the length and breadth of the moor.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2696	lexical	\N	\N	2695	{"text": "But I had my own experience for a guide since it had shown me the man himself standing upon the summit of the Black Tor.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2697	lexical	\N	\N	2696	{"text": "That, then, should be the centre of my search.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2698	lexical	\N	\N	2697	{"text": "From there I should explore every hut upon the moor until I lighted upon the right one.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2699	lexical	\N	\N	2698	{"text": "If this man were inside it I should find out from his own lips, at the point of my revolver if necessary, who he was and why he had dogged us so long.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2700	lexical	\N	\N	2699	{"text": "He might slip away from us in the crowd of Regent Street, but it would puzzle him to do so upon the lonely moor.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2701	lexical	\N	\N	2700	{"text": "On the other hand, if I should find the hut and its tenant should not be within it I must remain there, however long the vigil, until he returned.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2702	lexical	\N	\N	2701	{"text": "Holmes had missed him in London.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2703	lexical	\N	\N	2702	{"text": "It would indeed be a triumph for me if I could run him to earth where my master had failed.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2704	lexical	\N	\N	2703	{"text": "Luck had been against us again and again in this inquiry, but now at last it came to my aid.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2705	lexical	\N	\N	2704	{"text": "And the messenger of good fortune was none other than Mr. Frankland, who was standing, grey-whiskered and red-faced, outside the gate of his garden, which opened on to the highroad along which I travelled.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2706	lexical	\N	\N	2705	{"text": "“Good-day, Dr. Watson,” cried he with unwonted good humour, “you must really give your horses a rest and come in to have a glass of wine and to congratulate me.”", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2707	lexical	\N	\N	2706	{"text": "My feelings towards him were very far from being friendly after what I had heard of his treatment of his daughter, but I was anxious to send Perkins and the wagonette home, and the opportunity was a good one.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2708	lexical	\N	\N	2707	{"text": "I alighted and sent a message to Sir Henry that I should walk over in time for dinner.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2709	lexical	\N	\N	2708	{"text": "Then I followed Frankland into his dining-room.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2710	lexical	\N	\N	2709	{"text": "“It is a great day for me, sir—one of the red-letter days of my life,” he cried with many chuckles.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2711	lexical	\N	\N	2710	{"text": "“I have brought off a double event.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2712	lexical	\N	\N	2711	{"text": "I mean to teach them in these parts that law is law, and that there is a man here who does not fear to invoke it.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2713	lexical	\N	\N	2712	{"text": "I have established a right of way through the centre of old Middleton’s park, slap across it, sir, within a hundred yards of his own front door.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2714	lexical	\N	\N	2713	{"text": "What do you think of that?", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2715	lexical	\N	\N	2714	{"text": "We’ll teach these magnates that they cannot ride roughshod over the rights of the commoners, confound them!", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2716	lexical	\N	\N	2715	{"text": "And I’ve closed the wood where the Fernworthy folk used to picnic.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2717	lexical	\N	\N	2716	{"text": "These infernal people seem to think that there are no rights of property, and that they can swarm where they like with their papers and their bottles.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2718	lexical	\N	\N	2717	{"text": "Both cases decided, Dr. Watson, and both in my favour.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2719	lexical	\N	\N	2718	{"text": "I haven’t had such a day since I had Sir John Morland for trespass because he shot in his own warren.”", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2720	lexical	\N	\N	2719	{"text": "“How on earth did you do that?”", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2721	lexical	\N	\N	2720	{"text": "“Look it up in the books, sir.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2722	lexical	\N	\N	2721	{"text": "It will repay reading—Frankland _v_.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2723	lexical	\N	\N	2722	{"text": "Morland, Court of Queen’s Bench.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2724	lexical	\N	\N	2723	{"text": "It cost me £200, but I got my verdict.”", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2725	lexical	\N	\N	2724	{"text": "“Did it do you any good?”", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2726	lexical	\N	\N	2725	{"text": "“None, sir, none.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2727	lexical	\N	\N	2726	{"text": "I am proud to say that I had no interest in the matter.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2729	lexical	\N	\N	2728	{"text": "I have no doubt, for example, that the Fernworthy people will burn me in effigy tonight.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2730	lexical	\N	\N	2729	{"text": "I told the police last time they did it that they should stop these disgraceful exhibitions.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2731	lexical	\N	\N	2730	{"text": "The County Constabulary is in a scandalous state, sir, and it has not afforded me the protection to which I am entitled.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2732	lexical	\N	\N	2731	{"text": "The case of Frankland _v_.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2733	lexical	\N	\N	2732	{"text": "Regina will bring the matter before the attention of the public.", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2734	lexical	\N	\N	2733	{"text": "I told them that they would have occasion to regret their treatment of me, and already my words have come true.”", "section": "section_69", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2735	lexical	\N	\N	2734	{"text": "“How so?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2736	lexical	\N	\N	2735	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2737	lexical	\N	\N	2736	{"text": "The old man put on a very knowing expression.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2738	lexical	\N	\N	2737	{"text": "“Because I could tell them what they are dying to know; but nothing would induce me to help the rascals in any way.”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2739	lexical	\N	\N	2738	{"text": "I had been casting round for some excuse by which I could get away from his gossip, but now I began to wish to hear more of it.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2740	lexical	\N	\N	2739	{"text": "I had seen enough of the contrary nature of the old sinner to understand that any strong sign of interest would be the surest way to stop his confidences.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2741	lexical	\N	\N	2740	{"text": "“Some poaching case, no doubt?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2742	lexical	\N	\N	2741	{"text": "said I with an indifferent manner.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2743	lexical	\N	\N	2742	{"text": "“Ha, ha, my boy, a very much more important matter than that!", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2744	lexical	\N	\N	2743	{"text": "What about the convict on the moor?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2745	lexical	\N	\N	2744	{"text": "I stared.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2746	lexical	\N	\N	2745	{"text": "“You don’t mean that you know where he is?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2747	lexical	\N	\N	2746	{"text": "said I.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2748	lexical	\N	\N	2747	{"text": "“I may not know exactly where he is, but I am quite sure that I could help the police to lay their hands on him.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2749	lexical	\N	\N	2748	{"text": "Has it never struck you that the way to catch that man was to find out where he got his food and so trace it to him?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2750	lexical	\N	\N	2749	{"text": "He certainly seemed to be getting uncomfortably near the truth.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2751	lexical	\N	\N	2750	{"text": "“No doubt,” said I; “but how do you know that he is anywhere upon the moor?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2752	lexical	\N	\N	2751	{"text": "“I know it because I have seen with my own eyes the messenger who takes him his food.”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2753	lexical	\N	\N	2752	{"text": "My heart sank for Barrymore.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2754	lexical	\N	\N	2753	{"text": "It was a serious thing to be in the power of this spiteful old busybody.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2755	lexical	\N	\N	2754	{"text": "But his next remark took a weight from my mind.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2756	lexical	\N	\N	2755	{"text": "“You’ll be surprised to hear that his food is taken to him by a child.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2757	lexical	\N	\N	2756	{"text": "I see him every day through my telescope upon the roof.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2758	lexical	\N	\N	2757	{"text": "He passes along the same path at the same hour, and to whom should he be going except to the convict?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2759	lexical	\N	\N	2758	{"text": "Here was luck indeed!", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2760	lexical	\N	\N	2759	{"text": "And yet I suppressed all appearance of interest.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2761	lexical	\N	\N	2760	{"text": "A child!", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2762	lexical	\N	\N	2761	{"text": "Barrymore had said that our unknown was supplied by a boy.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2763	lexical	\N	\N	2762	{"text": "It was on his track, and not upon the convict’s, that Frankland had stumbled.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2764	lexical	\N	\N	2763	{"text": "If I could get his knowledge it might save me a long and weary hunt.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2765	lexical	\N	\N	2764	{"text": "But incredulity and indifference were evidently my strongest cards.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2804	lexical	\N	\N	2803	{"text": "Nothing would induce me to help the police in any way.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2766	lexical	\N	\N	2765	{"text": "“I should say that it was much more likely that it was the son of one of the moorland shepherds taking out his father’s dinner.”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2767	lexical	\N	\N	2766	{"text": "The least appearance of opposition struck fire out of the old autocrat.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2768	lexical	\N	\N	2767	{"text": "His eyes looked malignantly at me, and his grey whiskers bristled like those of an angry cat.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2769	lexical	\N	\N	2768	{"text": "“Indeed, sir!”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2770	lexical	\N	\N	2769	{"text": "said he, pointing out over the wide-stretching moor.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2771	lexical	\N	\N	2770	{"text": "“Do you see that Black Tor over yonder?", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2772	lexical	\N	\N	2771	{"text": "Well, do you see the low hill beyond with the thornbush upon it?", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2773	lexical	\N	\N	2772	{"text": "It is the stoniest part of the whole moor.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2774	lexical	\N	\N	2773	{"text": "Is that a place where a shepherd would be likely to take his station?", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2775	lexical	\N	\N	2774	{"text": "Your suggestion, sir, is a most absurd one.”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2776	lexical	\N	\N	2775	{"text": "I meekly answered that I had spoken without knowing all the facts.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2777	lexical	\N	\N	2776	{"text": "My submission pleased him and led him to further confidences.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2778	lexical	\N	\N	2777	{"text": "“You may be sure, sir, that I have very good grounds before I come to an opinion.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2779	lexical	\N	\N	2778	{"text": "I have seen the boy again and again with his bundle.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2780	lexical	\N	\N	2779	{"text": "Every day, and sometimes twice a day, I have been able—but wait a moment, Dr. Watson.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2781	lexical	\N	\N	2780	{"text": "Do my eyes deceive me, or is there at the present moment something moving upon that hillside?”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2782	lexical	\N	\N	2781	{"text": "It was several miles off, but I could distinctly see a small dark dot against the dull green and grey.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2783	lexical	\N	\N	2782	{"text": "“Come, sir, come!”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2784	lexical	\N	\N	2783	{"text": "cried Frankland, rushing upstairs.", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2785	lexical	\N	\N	2784	{"text": "“You will see with your own eyes and judge for yourself.”", "section": "section_70", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2786	lexical	\N	\N	2785	{"text": "The telescope, a formidable instrument mounted upon a tripod, stood upon the flat leads of the house.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2787	lexical	\N	\N	2786	{"text": "Frankland clapped his eye to it and gave a cry of satisfaction.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2788	lexical	\N	\N	2787	{"text": "“Quick, Dr. Watson, quick, before he passes over the hill!”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2789	lexical	\N	\N	2788	{"text": "There he was, sure enough, a small urchin with a little bundle upon his shoulder, toiling slowly up the hill.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2790	lexical	\N	\N	2789	{"text": "When he reached the crest I saw the ragged uncouth figure outlined for an instant against the cold blue sky.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2791	lexical	\N	\N	2790	{"text": "He looked round him with a furtive and stealthy air, as one who dreads pursuit.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2792	lexical	\N	\N	2791	{"text": "Then he vanished over the hill.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2793	lexical	\N	\N	2792	{"text": "“Well!", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2794	lexical	\N	\N	2793	{"text": "Am I right?”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2795	lexical	\N	\N	2794	{"text": "“Certainly, there is a boy who seems to have some secret errand.”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2796	lexical	\N	\N	2795	{"text": "“And what the errand is even a county constable could guess.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2797	lexical	\N	\N	2796	{"text": "But not one word shall they have from me, and I bind you to secrecy also, Dr. Watson.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2798	lexical	\N	\N	2797	{"text": "Not a word!", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2799	lexical	\N	\N	2798	{"text": "You understand!”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2800	lexical	\N	\N	2799	{"text": "“Just as you wish.”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2801	lexical	\N	\N	2800	{"text": "“They have treated me shamefully—shamefully.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2802	lexical	\N	\N	2801	{"text": "When the facts come out in Frankland _v_.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2803	lexical	\N	\N	2802	{"text": "Regina I venture to think that a thrill of indignation will run through the country.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2805	lexical	\N	\N	2804	{"text": "For all they cared it might have been me, instead of my effigy, which these rascals burned at the stake.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2806	lexical	\N	\N	2805	{"text": "Surely you are not going!", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2807	lexical	\N	\N	2806	{"text": "You will help me to empty the decanter in honour of this great occasion!”", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2808	lexical	\N	\N	2807	{"text": "But I resisted all his solicitations and succeeded in dissuading him from his announced intention of walking home with me.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2809	lexical	\N	\N	2808	{"text": "I kept the road as long as his eye was on me, and then I struck off across the moor and made for the stony hill over which the boy had disappeared.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2810	lexical	\N	\N	2809	{"text": "Everything was working in my favour, and I swore that it should not be through lack of energy or perseverance that I should miss the chance which fortune had thrown in my way.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2811	lexical	\N	\N	2810	{"text": "The sun was already sinking when I reached the summit of the hill, and the long slopes beneath me were all golden-green on one side and grey shadow on the other.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2812	lexical	\N	\N	2811	{"text": "A haze lay low upon the farthest sky-line, out of which jutted the fantastic shapes of Belliver and Vixen Tor.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2813	lexical	\N	\N	2812	{"text": "Over the wide expanse there was no sound and no movement.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2814	lexical	\N	\N	2813	{"text": "One great grey bird, a gull or curlew, soared aloft in the blue heaven.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2815	lexical	\N	\N	2814	{"text": "He and I seemed to be the only living things between the huge arch of the sky and the desert beneath it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2816	lexical	\N	\N	2815	{"text": "The barren scene, the sense of loneliness, and the mystery and urgency of my task all struck a chill into my heart.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2817	lexical	\N	\N	2816	{"text": "The boy was nowhere to be seen.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2818	lexical	\N	\N	2817	{"text": "But down beneath me in a cleft of the hills there was a circle of the old stone huts, and in the middle of them there was one which retained sufficient roof to act as a screen against the weather.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2819	lexical	\N	\N	2818	{"text": "My heart leaped within me as I saw it.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2820	lexical	\N	\N	2819	{"text": "This must be the burrow where the stranger lurked.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2821	lexical	\N	\N	2820	{"text": "At last my foot was on the threshold of his hiding place—his secret was within my grasp.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2822	lexical	\N	\N	2821	{"text": "As I approached the hut, walking as warily as Stapleton would do when with poised net he drew near the settled butterfly, I satisfied myself that the place had indeed been used as a habitation.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2823	lexical	\N	\N	2822	{"text": "A vague pathway among the boulders led to the dilapidated opening which served as a door.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2824	lexical	\N	\N	2823	{"text": "All was silent within.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2825	lexical	\N	\N	2824	{"text": "The unknown might be lurking there, or he might be prowling on the moor.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2826	lexical	\N	\N	2825	{"text": "My nerves tingled with the sense of adventure.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2827	lexical	\N	\N	2826	{"text": "Throwing aside my cigarette, I closed my hand upon the butt of my revolver and, walking swiftly up to the door, I looked in.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2828	lexical	\N	\N	2827	{"text": "The place was empty.", "section": "section_71", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2829	lexical	\N	\N	2828	{"text": "But there were ample signs that I had not come upon a false scent.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2830	lexical	\N	\N	2829	{"text": "This was certainly where the man lived.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2831	lexical	\N	\N	2830	{"text": "Some blankets rolled in a waterproof lay upon that very stone slab upon which Neolithic man had once slumbered.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2832	lexical	\N	\N	2831	{"text": "The ashes of a fire were heaped in a rude grate.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2833	lexical	\N	\N	2832	{"text": "Beside it lay some cooking utensils and a bucket half-full of water.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2834	lexical	\N	\N	2833	{"text": "A litter of empty tins showed that the place had been occupied for some time, and I saw, as my eyes became accustomed to the checkered light, a pannikin and a half-full bottle of spirits standing in the corner.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2835	lexical	\N	\N	2834	{"text": "In the middle of the hut a flat stone served the purpose of a table, and upon this stood a small cloth bundle—the same, no doubt, which I had seen through the telescope upon the shoulder of the boy.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2836	lexical	\N	\N	2835	{"text": "It contained a loaf of bread, a tinned tongue, and two tins of preserved peaches.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2837	lexical	\N	\N	2836	{"text": "As I set it down again, after having examined it, my heart leaped to see that beneath it there lay a sheet of paper with writing upon it.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2838	lexical	\N	\N	2837	{"text": "I raised it, and this was what I read, roughly scrawled in pencil: “Dr. Watson has gone to Coombe Tracey.”", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2839	lexical	\N	\N	2838	{"text": "For a minute I stood there with the paper in my hands thinking out the meaning of this curt message.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2840	lexical	\N	\N	2839	{"text": "It was I, then, and not Sir Henry, who was being dogged by this secret man.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2841	lexical	\N	\N	2840	{"text": "He had not followed me himself, but he had set an agent—the boy, perhaps—upon my track, and this was his report.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2842	lexical	\N	\N	2841	{"text": "Possibly I had taken no step since I had been upon the moor which had not been observed and reported.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2843	lexical	\N	\N	2842	{"text": "Always there was this feeling of an unseen force, a fine net drawn round us with infinite skill and delicacy, holding us so lightly that it was only at some supreme moment that one realised that one was indeed entangled in its meshes.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2844	lexical	\N	\N	2843	{"text": "If there was one report there might be others, so I looked round the hut in search of them.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2845	lexical	\N	\N	2844	{"text": "There was no trace, however, of anything of the kind, nor could I discover any sign which might indicate the character or intentions of the man who lived in this singular place, save that he must be of Spartan habits and cared little for the comforts of life.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2846	lexical	\N	\N	2845	{"text": "When I thought of the heavy rains and looked at the gaping roof I understood how strong and immutable must be the purpose which had kept him in that inhospitable abode.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2847	lexical	\N	\N	2846	{"text": "Was he our malignant enemy, or was he by chance our guardian angel?", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2848	lexical	\N	\N	2847	{"text": "I swore that I would not leave the hut until I knew.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2849	lexical	\N	\N	2848	{"text": "Outside the sun was sinking low and the west was blazing with scarlet and gold.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2850	lexical	\N	\N	2849	{"text": "Its reflection was shot back in ruddy patches by the distant pools which lay amid the great Grimpen Mire.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2851	lexical	\N	\N	2850	{"text": "There were the two towers of Baskerville Hall, and there a distant blur of smoke which marked the village of Grimpen.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2852	lexical	\N	\N	2851	{"text": "Between the two, behind the hill, was the house of the Stapletons.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2853	lexical	\N	\N	2852	{"text": "All was sweet and mellow and peaceful in the golden evening light, and yet as I looked at them my soul shared none of the peace of Nature but quivered at the vagueness and the terror of that interview which every instant was bringing nearer.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2854	lexical	\N	\N	2853	{"text": "With tingling nerves but a fixed purpose, I sat in the dark recess of the hut and waited with sombre patience for the coming of its tenant.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2855	lexical	\N	\N	2854	{"text": "And then at last I heard him.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2856	lexical	\N	\N	2855	{"text": "Far away came the sharp clink of a boot striking upon a stone.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2857	lexical	\N	\N	2856	{"text": "Then another and yet another, coming nearer and nearer.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2858	lexical	\N	\N	2857	{"text": "I shrank back into the darkest corner and cocked the pistol in my pocket, determined not to discover myself until I had an opportunity of seeing something of the stranger.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2859	lexical	\N	\N	2858	{"text": "There was a long pause which showed that he had stopped.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2860	lexical	\N	\N	2859	{"text": "Then once more the footsteps approached and a shadow fell across the opening of the hut.", "section": "section_72", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2861	lexical	\N	\N	2860	{"text": "“It is a lovely evening, my dear Watson,” said a well-known voice.", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2862	lexical	\N	\N	2861	{"text": "“I really think that you will be more comfortable outside than in.”", "section": "section_73", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2863	lexical	\N	\N	2862	{"text": "Chapter 12.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2864	lexical	\N	\N	2863	{"text": "Death on the Moor", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2865	lexical	\N	\N	2864	{"text": "For a moment or two I sat breathless, hardly able to believe my ears.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2866	lexical	\N	\N	2865	{"text": "Then my senses and my voice came back to me, while a crushing weight of responsibility seemed in an instant to be lifted from my soul.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2867	lexical	\N	\N	2866	{"text": "That cold, incisive, ironical voice could belong to but one man in all the world.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2868	lexical	\N	\N	2867	{"text": "“Holmes!”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2869	lexical	\N	\N	2868	{"text": "I cried—“Holmes!”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2870	lexical	\N	\N	2869	{"text": "“Come out,” said he, “and please be careful with the revolver.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2871	lexical	\N	\N	2870	{"text": "I stooped under the rude lintel, and there he sat upon a stone outside, his grey eyes dancing with amusement as they fell upon my astonished features.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2872	lexical	\N	\N	2871	{"text": "He was thin and worn, but clear and alert, his keen face bronzed by the sun and roughened by the wind.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2873	lexical	\N	\N	2872	{"text": "In his tweed suit and cloth cap he looked like any other tourist upon the moor, and he had contrived, with that catlike love of personal cleanliness which was one of his characteristics, that his chin should be as smooth and his linen as perfect as if he were in Baker Street.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2874	lexical	\N	\N	2873	{"text": "“I never was more glad to see anyone in my life,” said I as I wrung him by the hand.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2875	lexical	\N	\N	2874	{"text": "“Or more astonished, eh?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2876	lexical	\N	\N	2875	{"text": "“Well, I must confess to it.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2877	lexical	\N	\N	2876	{"text": "“The surprise was not all on one side, I assure you.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2878	lexical	\N	\N	2877	{"text": "I had no idea that you had found my occasional retreat, still less that you were inside it, until I was within twenty paces of the door.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2879	lexical	\N	\N	2878	{"text": "“My footprint, I presume?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2880	lexical	\N	\N	2879	{"text": "“No, Watson, I fear that I could not undertake to recognize your footprint amid all the footprints of the world.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2881	lexical	\N	\N	2880	{"text": "If you seriously desire to deceive me you must change your tobacconist; for when I see the stub of a cigarette marked Bradley, Oxford Street, I know that my friend Watson is in the neighbourhood.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2882	lexical	\N	\N	2881	{"text": "You will see it there beside the path.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2883	lexical	\N	\N	2882	{"text": "You threw it down, no doubt, at that supreme moment when you charged into the empty hut.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2884	lexical	\N	\N	2883	{"text": "“Exactly.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2885	lexical	\N	\N	2884	{"text": "“I thought as much—and knowing your admirable tenacity I was convinced that you were sitting in ambush, a weapon within reach, waiting for the tenant to return.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2886	lexical	\N	\N	2885	{"text": "So you actually thought that I was the criminal?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2887	lexical	\N	\N	2886	{"text": "“I did not know who you were, but I was determined to find out.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2888	lexical	\N	\N	2887	{"text": "“Excellent, Watson!", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2889	lexical	\N	\N	2888	{"text": "And how did you localise me?", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2890	lexical	\N	\N	2889	{"text": "You saw me, perhaps, on the night of the convict hunt, when I was so imprudent as to allow the moon to rise behind me?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2891	lexical	\N	\N	2890	{"text": "“Yes, I saw you then.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2892	lexical	\N	\N	2891	{"text": "“And have no doubt searched all the huts until you came to this one?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2893	lexical	\N	\N	2892	{"text": "“No, your boy had been observed, and that gave me a guide where to look.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2894	lexical	\N	\N	2893	{"text": "“The old gentleman with the telescope, no doubt.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2895	lexical	\N	\N	2894	{"text": "I could not make it out when first I saw the light flashing upon the lens.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2896	lexical	\N	\N	2895	{"text": "He rose and peeped into the hut.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2897	lexical	\N	\N	2896	{"text": "“Ha, I see that Cartwright has brought up some supplies.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2898	lexical	\N	\N	2897	{"text": "What’s this paper?", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2899	lexical	\N	\N	2898	{"text": "So you have been to Coombe Tracey, have you?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2900	lexical	\N	\N	2899	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2901	lexical	\N	\N	2900	{"text": "“To see Mrs. Laura Lyons?”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2902	lexical	\N	\N	2901	{"text": "“Exactly.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2903	lexical	\N	\N	2902	{"text": "“Well done!", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2904	lexical	\N	\N	2903	{"text": "Our researches have evidently been running on parallel lines, and when we unite our results I expect we shall have a fairly full knowledge of the case.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2905	lexical	\N	\N	2904	{"text": "“Well, I am glad from my heart that you are here, for indeed the responsibility and the mystery were both becoming too much for my nerves.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2906	lexical	\N	\N	2905	{"text": "But how in the name of wonder did you come here, and what have you been doing?", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2907	lexical	\N	\N	2906	{"text": "I thought that you were in Baker Street working out that case of blackmailing.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2908	lexical	\N	\N	2907	{"text": "“That was what I wished you to think.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2909	lexical	\N	\N	2908	{"text": "“Then you use me, and yet do not trust me!”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2910	lexical	\N	\N	2909	{"text": "I cried with some bitterness.", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2911	lexical	\N	\N	2910	{"text": "“I think that I have deserved better at your hands, Holmes.”", "section": "section_74", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2912	lexical	\N	\N	2911	{"text": "“My dear fellow, you have been invaluable to me in this as in many other cases, and I beg that you will forgive me if I have seemed to play a trick upon you.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2913	lexical	\N	\N	2912	{"text": "In truth, it was partly for your own sake that I did it, and it was my appreciation of the danger which you ran which led me to come down and examine the matter for myself.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2914	lexical	\N	\N	2913	{"text": "Had I been with Sir Henry and you it is confident that my point of view would have been the same as yours, and my presence would have warned our very formidable opponents to be on their guard.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2915	lexical	\N	\N	2914	{"text": "As it is, I have been able to get about as I could not possibly have done had I been living in the Hall, and I remain an unknown factor in the business, ready to throw in all my weight at a critical moment.”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2916	lexical	\N	\N	2915	{"text": "“But why keep me in the dark?”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2917	lexical	\N	\N	2916	{"text": "“For you to know could not have helped us and might possibly have led to my discovery.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2918	lexical	\N	\N	2917	{"text": "You would have wished to tell me something, or in your kindness you would have brought me out some comfort or other, and so an unnecessary risk would be run.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2919	lexical	\N	\N	2918	{"text": "I brought Cartwright down with me—you remember the little chap at the express office—and he has seen after my simple wants: a loaf of bread and a clean collar.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2920	lexical	\N	\N	2919	{"text": "What does man want more?", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2921	lexical	\N	\N	2920	{"text": "He has given me an extra pair of eyes upon a very active pair of feet, and both have been invaluable.”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2922	lexical	\N	\N	2921	{"text": "”—My voice trembled as I recalled the pains and the pride with which I had composed them.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2923	lexical	\N	\N	2922	{"text": "pride with which I had composed them.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2924	lexical	\N	\N	2923	{"text": "Holmes took a bundle of papers from his pocket.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2925	lexical	\N	\N	2924	{"text": "“Here are your reports, my dear fellow, and very well thumbed, I assure you.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2926	lexical	\N	\N	2925	{"text": "I made excellent arrangements, and they are only delayed one day upon their way.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2927	lexical	\N	\N	2926	{"text": "I must compliment you exceedingly upon the zeal and the intelligence which you have shown over an extraordinarily difficult case.”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2928	lexical	\N	\N	2927	{"text": "I was still rather raw over the deception which had been practised upon me, but the warmth of Holmes’s praise drove my anger from my mind.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2929	lexical	\N	\N	2928	{"text": "I felt also in my heart that he was right in what he said and that it was really best for our purpose that I should not have known that he was upon the moor.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2930	lexical	\N	\N	2929	{"text": "“That’s better,” said he, seeing the shadow rise from my face.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2931	lexical	\N	\N	2930	{"text": "“And now tell me the result of your visit to Mrs. Laura Lyons—it was not difficult for me to guess that it was to see her that you had gone, for I am already aware that she is the one person in Coombe Tracey who might be of service to us in the matter.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2932	lexical	\N	\N	2931	{"text": "In fact, if you had not gone today it is exceedingly probable that I should have gone tomorrow.”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2933	lexical	\N	\N	2932	{"text": "The sun had set and dusk was settling over the moor.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2934	lexical	\N	\N	2933	{"text": "The air had turned chill and we withdrew into the hut for warmth.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2935	lexical	\N	\N	2934	{"text": "There, sitting together in the twilight, I told Holmes of my conversation with the lady.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2936	lexical	\N	\N	2935	{"text": "So interested was he that I had to repeat some of it twice before he was satisfied.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2937	lexical	\N	\N	2936	{"text": "“This is most important,” said he when I had concluded.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2938	lexical	\N	\N	2937	{"text": "“It fills up a gap which I had been unable to bridge in this most complex affair.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2976	lexical	\N	\N	2975	{"text": "Your interview with the lady has cleared the situation very much.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2939	lexical	\N	\N	2938	{"text": "You are aware, perhaps, that a close intimacy exists between this lady and the man Stapleton?”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2940	lexical	\N	\N	2939	{"text": "“I did not know of a close intimacy.”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2941	lexical	\N	\N	2940	{"text": "“There can be no doubt about the matter.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2942	lexical	\N	\N	2941	{"text": "They meet, they write, there is a complete understanding between them.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2943	lexical	\N	\N	2942	{"text": "Now, this puts a very powerful weapon into our hands.", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2944	lexical	\N	\N	2943	{"text": "If I could only use it to detach his wife—”", "section": "section_75", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2945	lexical	\N	\N	2944	{"text": "“His wife?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2946	lexical	\N	\N	2945	{"text": "“I am giving you some information now, in return for all that you have given me.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2947	lexical	\N	\N	2946	{"text": "The lady who has passed here as Miss Stapleton is in reality his wife.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2948	lexical	\N	\N	2947	{"text": "“Good heavens, Holmes!", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2949	lexical	\N	\N	2948	{"text": "Are you sure of what you say?", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2950	lexical	\N	\N	2949	{"text": "How could he have permitted Sir Henry to fall in love with her?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2951	lexical	\N	\N	2950	{"text": "“Sir Henry’s falling in love could do no harm to anyone except Sir Henry.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2952	lexical	\N	\N	2951	{"text": "He took particular care that Sir Henry did not make love to her, as you have yourself observed.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2953	lexical	\N	\N	2952	{"text": "I repeat that the lady is his wife and not his sister.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2954	lexical	\N	\N	2953	{"text": "“But why this elaborate deception?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2955	lexical	\N	\N	2954	{"text": "“Because he foresaw that she would be very much more useful to him in the character of a free woman.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2956	lexical	\N	\N	2955	{"text": "All my unspoken instincts, my vague suspicions, suddenly took shape and centred upon the naturalist.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2957	lexical	\N	\N	2956	{"text": "In that impassive colourless man, with his straw hat and his butterfly-net, I seemed to see something terrible—a creature of infinite patience and craft, with a smiling face and a murderous heart.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2958	lexical	\N	\N	2957	{"text": "“It is he, then, who is our enemy—it is he who dogged us in London?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2959	lexical	\N	\N	2958	{"text": "“So I read the riddle.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2960	lexical	\N	\N	2959	{"text": "“And the warning—it must have come from her!”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2961	lexical	\N	\N	2960	{"text": "“Exactly.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2962	lexical	\N	\N	2961	{"text": "The shape of some monstrous villainy, half seen, half guessed, loomed through the darkness which had girt me so long.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2963	lexical	\N	\N	2962	{"text": "“But are you sure of this, Holmes?", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2964	lexical	\N	\N	2963	{"text": "How do you know that the woman is his wife?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2965	lexical	\N	\N	2964	{"text": "“Because he so far forgot himself as to tell you a true piece of autobiography upon the occasion when he first met you, and I dare say he has many a time regretted it since.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2966	lexical	\N	\N	2965	{"text": "He was once a schoolmaster in the north of England.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2967	lexical	\N	\N	2966	{"text": "Now, there is no one more easy to trace than a schoolmaster.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2968	lexical	\N	\N	2967	{"text": "There are scholastic agencies by which one may identify any man who has been in the profession.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2969	lexical	\N	\N	2968	{"text": "A little investigation showed me that a school had come to grief under atrocious circumstances, and that the man who had owned it—the name was different—had disappeared with his wife.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2970	lexical	\N	\N	2969	{"text": "The descriptions agreed.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2971	lexical	\N	\N	2970	{"text": "When I learned that the missing man was devoted to entomology the identification was complete.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2972	lexical	\N	\N	2971	{"text": "The darkness was rising, but much was still hidden by the shadows.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2973	lexical	\N	\N	2972	{"text": "“If this woman is in truth his wife, where does Mrs. Laura Lyons come in?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2974	lexical	\N	\N	2973	{"text": "I asked.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2975	lexical	\N	\N	2974	{"text": "“That is one of the points upon which your own researches have shed a light.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2977	lexical	\N	\N	2976	{"text": "I did not know about a projected divorce between herself and her husband.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2978	lexical	\N	\N	2977	{"text": "In that case, regarding Stapleton as an unmarried man, she counted no doubt upon becoming his wife.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2979	lexical	\N	\N	2978	{"text": "“And when she is undeceived?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2980	lexical	\N	\N	2979	{"text": "“Why, then we may find the lady of service.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2981	lexical	\N	\N	2980	{"text": "It must be our first duty to see her—both of us—tomorrow.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2982	lexical	\N	\N	2981	{"text": "Don’t you think, Watson, that you are away from your charge rather long?", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2983	lexical	\N	\N	2982	{"text": "Your place should be at Baskerville Hall.”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2984	lexical	\N	\N	2983	{"text": "The last red streaks had faded away in the west and night had settled upon the moor.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2985	lexical	\N	\N	2984	{"text": "A few faint stars were gleaming in a violet sky.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2986	lexical	\N	\N	2985	{"text": "“One last question, Holmes,” I said as I rose.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2987	lexical	\N	\N	2986	{"text": "“Surely there is no need of secrecy between you and me.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2988	lexical	\N	\N	2987	{"text": "What is the meaning of it all?", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2989	lexical	\N	\N	2988	{"text": "What is he after?”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2990	lexical	\N	\N	2989	{"text": "Holmes’s voice sank as he answered:", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2991	lexical	\N	\N	2990	{"text": "“It is murder, Watson—refined, cold-blooded, deliberate murder.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2992	lexical	\N	\N	2991	{"text": "Do not ask me for particulars.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2993	lexical	\N	\N	2992	{"text": "My nets are closing upon him, even as his are upon Sir Henry, and with your help he is already almost at my mercy.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2994	lexical	\N	\N	2993	{"text": "There is but one danger which can threaten us.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2995	lexical	\N	\N	2994	{"text": "It is that he should strike before we are ready to do so.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2996	lexical	\N	\N	2995	{"text": "Another day—two at the most—and I have my case complete, but until then guard your charge as closely as ever a fond mother watched her ailing child.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2997	lexical	\N	\N	2996	{"text": "Your mission today has justified itself, and yet I could almost wish that you had not left his side.", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2998	lexical	\N	\N	2997	{"text": "Hark!”", "section": "section_76", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_2999	lexical	\N	\N	2998	{"text": "A terrible scream—a prolonged yell of horror and anguish—burst out of the silence of the moor.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3000	lexical	\N	\N	2999	{"text": "That frightful cry turned the blood to ice in my veins.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3001	lexical	\N	\N	3000	{"text": "“Oh, my God!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3002	lexical	\N	\N	3001	{"text": "I gasped.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3003	lexical	\N	\N	3002	{"text": "“What is it?", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3004	lexical	\N	\N	3003	{"text": "What does it mean?”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3005	lexical	\N	\N	3004	{"text": "Holmes had sprung to his feet, and I saw his dark, athletic outline at the door of the hut, his shoulders stooping, his head thrust forward, his face peering into the darkness.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3006	lexical	\N	\N	3005	{"text": "“Hush!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3007	lexical	\N	\N	3006	{"text": "he whispered.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3008	lexical	\N	\N	3007	{"text": "“Hush!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3009	lexical	\N	\N	3008	{"text": "The cry had been loud on account of its vehemence, but it had pealed out from somewhere far off on the shadowy plain.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3010	lexical	\N	\N	3009	{"text": "Now it burst upon our ears, nearer, louder, more urgent than before.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3011	lexical	\N	\N	3010	{"text": "“Where is it?”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3012	lexical	\N	\N	3011	{"text": "Holmes whispered; and I knew from the thrill of his voice that he, the man of iron, was shaken to the soul.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3013	lexical	\N	\N	3012	{"text": "“Where is it, Watson?”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3014	lexical	\N	\N	3013	{"text": "“There, I think.”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3015	lexical	\N	\N	3014	{"text": "I pointed into the darkness.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3016	lexical	\N	\N	3015	{"text": "“No, there!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3017	lexical	\N	\N	3016	{"text": "Again the agonised cry swept through the silent night, louder and much nearer than ever.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3018	lexical	\N	\N	3017	{"text": "And a new sound mingled with it, a deep, muttered rumble, musical and yet menacing, rising and falling like the low, constant murmur of the sea.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3019	lexical	\N	\N	3018	{"text": "“The hound!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3020	lexical	\N	\N	3019	{"text": "cried Holmes.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3021	lexical	\N	\N	3020	{"text": "“Come, Watson, come!", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3022	lexical	\N	\N	3021	{"text": "Great heavens, if we are too late!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3023	lexical	\N	\N	3022	{"text": "He had started running swiftly over the moor, and I had followed at his heels.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3024	lexical	\N	\N	3023	{"text": "But now from somewhere among the broken ground immediately in front of us there came one last despairing yell, and then a dull, heavy thud.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3025	lexical	\N	\N	3024	{"text": "We halted and listened.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3026	lexical	\N	\N	3025	{"text": "Not another sound broke the heavy silence of the windless night.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3027	lexical	\N	\N	3026	{"text": "I saw Holmes put his hand to his forehead like a man distracted.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3028	lexical	\N	\N	3027	{"text": "He stamped his feet upon the ground.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3029	lexical	\N	\N	3028	{"text": "“He has beaten us, Watson.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3030	lexical	\N	\N	3029	{"text": "We are too late.”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3031	lexical	\N	\N	3030	{"text": "“No, no, surely not!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3032	lexical	\N	\N	3031	{"text": "“Fool that I was to hold my hand.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3033	lexical	\N	\N	3032	{"text": "And you, Watson, see what comes of abandoning your charge!", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3034	lexical	\N	\N	3033	{"text": "But, by Heaven, if the worst has happened we’ll avenge him!”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3035	lexical	\N	\N	3034	{"text": "Blindly we ran through the gloom, blundering against boulders, forcing our way through gorse bushes, panting up hills and rushing down slopes, heading always in the direction whence those dreadful sounds had come.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3036	lexical	\N	\N	3035	{"text": "At every rise Holmes looked eagerly round him, but the shadows were thick upon the moor, and nothing moved upon its dreary face.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3037	lexical	\N	\N	3036	{"text": "“Can you see anything?”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3038	lexical	\N	\N	3037	{"text": "“Nothing.”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3039	lexical	\N	\N	3038	{"text": "“But, hark, what is that?”", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3040	lexical	\N	\N	3039	{"text": "A low moan had fallen upon our ears.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3041	lexical	\N	\N	3040	{"text": "There it was again upon our left!", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3042	lexical	\N	\N	3041	{"text": "On that side a ridge of rocks ended in a sheer cliff which overlooked a stone-strewn slope.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3043	lexical	\N	\N	3042	{"text": "On its jagged face was spread-eagled some dark, irregular object.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3044	lexical	\N	\N	3043	{"text": "As we ran towards it the vague outline hardened into a definite shape.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3045	lexical	\N	\N	3044	{"text": "It was a prostrate man face downward upon the ground, the head doubled under him at a horrible angle, the shoulders rounded and the body hunched together as if in the act of throwing a somersault.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3046	lexical	\N	\N	3045	{"text": "So grotesque was the attitude that I could not for the instant realise that that moan had been the passing of his soul.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3047	lexical	\N	\N	3046	{"text": "Not a whisper, not a rustle, rose now from the dark figure over which we stooped.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3048	lexical	\N	\N	3047	{"text": "Holmes laid his hand upon him and held it up again with an exclamation of horror.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3049	lexical	\N	\N	3048	{"text": "The gleam of the match which he struck shone upon his clotted fingers and upon the ghastly pool which widened slowly from the crushed skull of the victim.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3050	lexical	\N	\N	3049	{"text": "And it shone upon something else which turned our hearts sick and faint within us—the body of Sir Henry Baskerville!", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3051	lexical	\N	\N	3050	{"text": "There was no chance of either of us forgetting that peculiar ruddy tweed suit—the very one which he had worn on the first morning that we had seen him in Baker Street.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3052	lexical	\N	\N	3051	{"text": "We caught the one clear glimpse of it, and then the match flickered and went out, even as the hope had gone out of our souls.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3053	lexical	\N	\N	3052	{"text": "Holmes groaned, and his face glimmered white through the darkness.", "section": "section_77", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3054	lexical	\N	\N	3053	{"text": "“The brute!", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3055	lexical	\N	\N	3054	{"text": "The brute!”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3056	lexical	\N	\N	3055	{"text": "I cried with clenched hands.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3057	lexical	\N	\N	3056	{"text": "“Oh Holmes, I shall never forgive myself for having left him to his fate.”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3058	lexical	\N	\N	3057	{"text": "“I am more to blame than you, Watson.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3059	lexical	\N	\N	3058	{"text": "In order to have my case well rounded and complete, I have thrown away the life of my client.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3060	lexical	\N	\N	3059	{"text": "It is the greatest blow which has befallen me in my career.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3061	lexical	\N	\N	3060	{"text": "But how could I know—how _could_ I know—that he would risk his life alone upon the moor in the face of all my warnings?”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3062	lexical	\N	\N	3061	{"text": "—and yet have been unable to save him!", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3063	lexical	\N	\N	3062	{"text": "Where is this brute of a hound which drove him to his death?", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3064	lexical	\N	\N	3063	{"text": "It may be lurking among these rocks at this instant.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3065	lexical	\N	\N	3064	{"text": "And Stapleton, where is he?", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3066	lexical	\N	\N	3065	{"text": "He shall answer for this deed.”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3067	lexical	\N	\N	3066	{"text": ". And Stapleton, where is he? He shall answer for this deed.”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3068	lexical	\N	\N	3067	{"text": "“He shall.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3069	lexical	\N	\N	3068	{"text": "I will see to that.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3070	lexical	\N	\N	3069	{"text": "Uncle and nephew have been murdered—the one frightened to death by the very sight of a beast which he thought to be supernatural, the other driven to his end in his wild flight to escape from it.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3071	lexical	\N	\N	3070	{"text": "But now we have to prove the connection between the man and the beast.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3072	lexical	\N	\N	3071	{"text": "Save from what we heard, we cannot even swear to the existence of the latter, since Sir Henry has evidently died from the fall.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3073	lexical	\N	\N	3072	{"text": "But, by heavens, cunning as he is, the fellow shall be in my power before another day is past!”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3074	lexical	\N	\N	3073	{"text": "We stood with bitter hearts on either side of the mangled body, overwhelmed by this sudden and irrevocable disaster which had brought all our long and weary labours to so piteous an end.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3075	lexical	\N	\N	3074	{"text": "Then as the moon rose we climbed to the top of the rocks over which our poor friend had fallen, and from the summit we gazed out over the shadowy moor, half silver and half gloom.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3076	lexical	\N	\N	3075	{"text": "Far away, miles off, in the direction of Grimpen, a single steady yellow light was shining.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3077	lexical	\N	\N	3076	{"text": "It could only come from the lonely abode of the Stapletons.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3078	lexical	\N	\N	3077	{"text": "With a bitter curse I shook my fist at it as I gazed.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3079	lexical	\N	\N	3078	{"text": "“Why should we not seize him at once?”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3080	lexical	\N	\N	3079	{"text": "“Our case is not complete.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3081	lexical	\N	\N	3080	{"text": "The fellow is wary and cunning to the last degree.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3082	lexical	\N	\N	3081	{"text": "It is not what we know, but what we can prove.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3083	lexical	\N	\N	3082	{"text": "If we make one false move the villain may escape us yet.”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3084	lexical	\N	\N	3083	{"text": "“What can we do?”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3085	lexical	\N	\N	3084	{"text": "“There will be plenty for us to do tomorrow.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3086	lexical	\N	\N	3085	{"text": "Tonight we can only perform the last offices to our poor friend.”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3087	lexical	\N	\N	3086	{"text": "Together we made our way down the precipitous slope and approached the body, black and clear against the silvered stones.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3088	lexical	\N	\N	3087	{"text": "The agony of those contorted limbs struck me with a spasm of pain and blurred my eyes with tears.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3089	lexical	\N	\N	3088	{"text": "“We must send for help, Holmes!", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3388	lexical	\N	\N	3387	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3090	lexical	\N	\N	3089	{"text": "We cannot carry him all the way to the Hall.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3091	lexical	\N	\N	3090	{"text": "Good heavens, are you mad?”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3092	lexical	\N	\N	3091	{"text": "He had uttered a cry and bent over the body.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3093	lexical	\N	\N	3092	{"text": "Now he was dancing and laughing and wringing my hand.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3094	lexical	\N	\N	3093	{"text": "Could this be my stern, self-contained friend?", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3095	lexical	\N	\N	3094	{"text": "These were hidden fires, indeed!", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3096	lexical	\N	\N	3095	{"text": "“A beard!", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3097	lexical	\N	\N	3096	{"text": "A beard!", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3098	lexical	\N	\N	3097	{"text": "The man has a beard!”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3099	lexical	\N	\N	3098	{"text": "“A beard?”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3100	lexical	\N	\N	3099	{"text": "“It is not the baronet—it is—why, it is my neighbour, the convict!”", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3101	lexical	\N	\N	3100	{"text": "With feverish haste we had turned the body over, and that dripping beard was pointing up to the cold, clear moon.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3102	lexical	\N	\N	3101	{"text": "There could be no doubt about the beetling forehead, the sunken animal eyes.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3103	lexical	\N	\N	3102	{"text": "It was indeed the same face which had glared upon me in the light of the candle from over the rock—the face of Selden, the criminal.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3104	lexical	\N	\N	3103	{"text": "Then in an instant it was all clear to me.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3105	lexical	\N	\N	3104	{"text": "I remembered how the baronet had told me that he had handed his old wardrobe to Barrymore.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3106	lexical	\N	\N	3105	{"text": "Barrymore had passed it on in order to help Selden in his escape.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3107	lexical	\N	\N	3106	{"text": "Boots, shirt, cap—it was all Sir Henry’s.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3108	lexical	\N	\N	3107	{"text": "The tragedy was still black enough, but this man had at least deserved death by the laws of his country.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3109	lexical	\N	\N	3108	{"text": "I told Holmes how the matter stood, my heart bubbling over with thankfulness and joy.", "section": "section_78", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3110	lexical	\N	\N	3109	{"text": "“Then the clothes have been the poor devil’s death,” said he.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3111	lexical	\N	\N	3110	{"text": "“It is clear enough that the hound has been laid on from some article of Sir Henry’s—the boot which was abstracted in the hotel, in all probability—and so ran this man down.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3112	lexical	\N	\N	3111	{"text": "There is one very singular thing, however: How came Selden, in the darkness, to know that the hound was on his trail?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3113	lexical	\N	\N	3112	{"text": "“He heard him.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3114	lexical	\N	\N	3113	{"text": "“To hear a hound upon the moor would not work a hard man like this convict into such a paroxysm of terror that he would risk recapture by screaming wildly for help.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3115	lexical	\N	\N	3114	{"text": "By his cries he must have run a long way after he knew the animal was on his track.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3116	lexical	\N	\N	3115	{"text": "How did he know?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3117	lexical	\N	\N	3116	{"text": "“A greater mystery to me is why this hound, presuming that all our conjectures are correct—”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3118	lexical	\N	\N	3117	{"text": "“I presume nothing.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3119	lexical	\N	\N	3118	{"text": "“Well, then, why this hound should be loose tonight.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3120	lexical	\N	\N	3119	{"text": "I suppose that it does not always run loose upon the moor.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3121	lexical	\N	\N	3120	{"text": "Stapleton would not let it go unless he had reason to think that Sir Henry would be there.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3122	lexical	\N	\N	3121	{"text": "“My difficulty is the more formidable of the two, for I think that we shall very shortly get an explanation of yours, while mine may remain forever a mystery.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3123	lexical	\N	\N	3122	{"text": "The question now is, what shall we do with this poor wretch’s body?", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3124	lexical	\N	\N	3123	{"text": "We cannot leave it here to the foxes and the ravens.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3125	lexical	\N	\N	3124	{"text": "“I suggest that we put it in one of the huts until we can communicate with the police.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3126	lexical	\N	\N	3125	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3497	lexical	\N	\N	3496	{"text": "he asked.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3127	lexical	\N	\N	3126	{"text": "I have no doubt that you and I could carry it so far.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3128	lexical	\N	\N	3127	{"text": "Halloa, Watson, what’s this?", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3129	lexical	\N	\N	3128	{"text": "It’s the man himself, by all that’s wonderful and audacious!", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3130	lexical	\N	\N	3129	{"text": "Not a word to show your suspicions—not a word, or my plans crumble to the ground.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3131	lexical	\N	\N	3130	{"text": "A figure was approaching us over the moor, and I saw the dull red glow of a cigar.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3132	lexical	\N	\N	3131	{"text": "The moon shone upon him, and I could distinguish the dapper shape and jaunty walk of the naturalist.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3133	lexical	\N	\N	3132	{"text": "He stopped when he saw us, and then came on again.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3134	lexical	\N	\N	3133	{"text": "“Why, Dr. Watson, that’s not you, is it?", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3135	lexical	\N	\N	3134	{"text": "You are the last man that I should have expected to see out on the moor at this time of night.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3136	lexical	\N	\N	3135	{"text": "But, dear me, what’s this?", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3137	lexical	\N	\N	3136	{"text": "Somebody hurt?", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3138	lexical	\N	\N	3137	{"text": "Not—don’t tell me that it is our friend Sir Henry!”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3139	lexical	\N	\N	3138	{"text": "He hurried past me and stooped over the dead man.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3140	lexical	\N	\N	3139	{"text": "I heard a sharp intake of his breath and the cigar fell from his fingers.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3141	lexical	\N	\N	3140	{"text": "“Who—who’s this?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3142	lexical	\N	\N	3141	{"text": "he stammered.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3143	lexical	\N	\N	3142	{"text": "“It is Selden, the man who escaped from Princetown.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3144	lexical	\N	\N	3143	{"text": "Stapleton turned a ghastly face upon us, but by a supreme effort he had overcome his amazement and his disappointment.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3145	lexical	\N	\N	3144	{"text": "He looked sharply from Holmes to me.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3146	lexical	\N	\N	3145	{"text": "“Dear me!", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3147	lexical	\N	\N	3146	{"text": "What a very shocking affair!", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3148	lexical	\N	\N	3147	{"text": "How did he die?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3149	lexical	\N	\N	3148	{"text": "“He appears to have broken his neck by falling over these rocks.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3150	lexical	\N	\N	3149	{"text": "My friend and I were strolling on the moor when we heard a cry.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3151	lexical	\N	\N	3150	{"text": "“I heard a cry also.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3152	lexical	\N	\N	3151	{"text": "That was what brought me out.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3153	lexical	\N	\N	3152	{"text": "I was uneasy about Sir Henry.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3154	lexical	\N	\N	3153	{"text": "“Why about Sir Henry in particular?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3155	lexical	\N	\N	3154	{"text": "I could not help asking.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3156	lexical	\N	\N	3155	{"text": "“Because I had suggested that he should come over.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3157	lexical	\N	\N	3156	{"text": "When he did not come I was surprised, and I naturally became alarmed for his safety when I heard cries upon the moor.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3158	lexical	\N	\N	3157	{"text": "By the way”—his eyes darted again from my face to Holmes’s—“did you hear anything else besides a cry?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3159	lexical	\N	\N	3158	{"text": "“No,” said Holmes; “did you?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3160	lexical	\N	\N	3159	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3161	lexical	\N	\N	3160	{"text": "“What do you mean, then?”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3162	lexical	\N	\N	3161	{"text": "“Oh, you know the stories that the peasants tell about a phantom hound, and so on.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3163	lexical	\N	\N	3162	{"text": "It is said to be heard at night upon the moor.", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3164	lexical	\N	\N	3163	{"text": "I was wondering if there were any evidence of such a sound tonight.”", "section": "section_79", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3165	lexical	\N	\N	3164	{"text": "“We heard nothing of the kind,” said I.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3166	lexical	\N	\N	3165	{"text": "“And what is your theory of this poor fellow’s death?”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3167	lexical	\N	\N	3166	{"text": "“I have no doubt that anxiety and exposure have driven him off his head.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3168	lexical	\N	\N	3167	{"text": "He has rushed about the moor in a crazy state and eventually fallen over here and broken his neck.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3169	lexical	\N	\N	3168	{"text": "“That seems the most reasonable theory,” said Stapleton, and he gave a sigh which I took to indicate his relief.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3170	lexical	\N	\N	3169	{"text": "“What do you think about it, Mr. Sherlock Holmes?”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3171	lexical	\N	\N	3170	{"text": "My friend bowed his compliments.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3172	lexical	\N	\N	3171	{"text": "“You are quick at identification,” said he.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3173	lexical	\N	\N	3172	{"text": "“We have been expecting you in these parts since Dr. Watson came down.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3174	lexical	\N	\N	3173	{"text": "You are in time to see a tragedy.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3175	lexical	\N	\N	3174	{"text": "“Yes, indeed.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3176	lexical	\N	\N	3175	{"text": "I have no doubt that my friend’s explanation will cover the facts.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3177	lexical	\N	\N	3176	{"text": "I will take an unpleasant remembrance back to London with me tomorrow.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3178	lexical	\N	\N	3177	{"text": "“Oh, you return tomorrow?”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3179	lexical	\N	\N	3178	{"text": "“That is my intention.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3180	lexical	\N	\N	3179	{"text": "“I hope your visit has cast some light upon those occurrences which have puzzled us?”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3181	lexical	\N	\N	3180	{"text": "Holmes shrugged his shoulders.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3182	lexical	\N	\N	3181	{"text": "“One cannot always have the success for which one hopes.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3183	lexical	\N	\N	3182	{"text": "An investigator needs facts and not legends or rumours.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3184	lexical	\N	\N	3183	{"text": "It has not been a satisfactory case.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3185	lexical	\N	\N	3184	{"text": "My friend spoke in his frankest and most unconcerned manner.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3186	lexical	\N	\N	3185	{"text": "Stapleton still looked hard at him.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3187	lexical	\N	\N	3186	{"text": "Then he turned to me.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3188	lexical	\N	\N	3187	{"text": "“I would suggest carrying this poor fellow to my house, but it would give my sister such a fright that I do not feel justified in doing it.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3189	lexical	\N	\N	3188	{"text": "I think that if we put something over his face he will be safe until morning.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3190	lexical	\N	\N	3189	{"text": "And so it was arranged.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3191	lexical	\N	\N	3190	{"text": "Resisting Stapleton’s offer of hospitality, Holmes and I set off to Baskerville Hall, leaving the naturalist to return alone.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3192	lexical	\N	\N	3191	{"text": "Looking back we saw the figure moving slowly away over the broad moor, and behind him that one black smudge on the silvered slope which showed where the man was lying who had come so horribly to his end.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3193	lexical	\N	\N	3192	{"text": "“We’re at close grips at last,” said Holmes as we walked together across the moor.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3194	lexical	\N	\N	3193	{"text": "“What a nerve the fellow has!", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3195	lexical	\N	\N	3194	{"text": "How he pulled himself together in the face of what must have been a paralyzing shock when he found that the wrong man had fallen a victim to his plot.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3196	lexical	\N	\N	3195	{"text": "I told you in London, Watson, and I tell you now again, that we have never had a foeman more worthy of our steel.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3197	lexical	\N	\N	3196	{"text": "“I am sorry that he has seen you.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3198	lexical	\N	\N	3197	{"text": "“And so was I at first.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3199	lexical	\N	\N	3198	{"text": "But there was no getting out of it.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3200	lexical	\N	\N	3199	{"text": "“What effect do you think it will have upon his plans now that he knows you are here?”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3201	lexical	\N	\N	3200	{"text": "“It may cause him to be more cautious, or it may drive him to desperate measures at once.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3202	lexical	\N	\N	3201	{"text": "Like most clever criminals, he may be too confident in his own cleverness and imagine that he has completely deceived us.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3203	lexical	\N	\N	3202	{"text": "“Why should we not arrest him at once?”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3204	lexical	\N	\N	3203	{"text": "“My dear Watson, you were born to be a man of action.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3205	lexical	\N	\N	3204	{"text": "Your instinct is always to do something energetic.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3206	lexical	\N	\N	3205	{"text": "But supposing, for argument’s sake, that we had him arrested tonight, what on earth the better off should we be for that?", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3207	lexical	\N	\N	3206	{"text": "We could prove nothing against him.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3208	lexical	\N	\N	3207	{"text": "There’s the devilish cunning of it!", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3209	lexical	\N	\N	3208	{"text": "If he were acting through a human agent we could get some evidence, but if we were to drag this great dog to the light of day it would not help us in putting a rope round the neck of its master.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3210	lexical	\N	\N	3209	{"text": "“Surely we have a case.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3211	lexical	\N	\N	3210	{"text": "“Not a shadow of one—only surmise and conjecture.", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3212	lexical	\N	\N	3211	{"text": "We should be laughed out of court if we came with such a story and such evidence.”", "section": "section_80", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3213	lexical	\N	\N	3212	{"text": "“There is Sir Charles’s death.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3214	lexical	\N	\N	3213	{"text": "“Found dead without a mark upon him.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3215	lexical	\N	\N	3214	{"text": "You and I know that he died of sheer fright, and we know also what frightened him, but how are we to get twelve stolid jurymen to know it?", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3216	lexical	\N	\N	3215	{"text": "What signs are there of a hound?", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3217	lexical	\N	\N	3216	{"text": "Where are the marks of its fangs?", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3218	lexical	\N	\N	3217	{"text": "Of course we know that a hound does not bite a dead body and that Sir Charles was dead before ever the brute overtook him.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3219	lexical	\N	\N	3218	{"text": "But we have to prove all this, and we are not in a position to do it.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3220	lexical	\N	\N	3219	{"text": "“Well, then, tonight?”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3221	lexical	\N	\N	3220	{"text": "“We are not much better off tonight.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3222	lexical	\N	\N	3221	{"text": "Again, there was no direct connection between the hound and the man’s death.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3223	lexical	\N	\N	3222	{"text": "We never saw the hound.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3224	lexical	\N	\N	3223	{"text": "We heard it, but we could not prove that it was running upon this man’s trail.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3225	lexical	\N	\N	3224	{"text": "There is a complete absence of motive.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3226	lexical	\N	\N	3225	{"text": "No, my dear fellow; we must reconcile ourselves to the fact that we have no case at present, and that it is worth our while to run any risk in order to establish one.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3227	lexical	\N	\N	3226	{"text": "“And how do you propose to do so?”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3228	lexical	\N	\N	3227	{"text": "“I have great hopes of what Mrs. Laura Lyons may do for us when the position of affairs is made clear to her.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3229	lexical	\N	\N	3228	{"text": "And I have my own plan as well.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3230	lexical	\N	\N	3229	{"text": "Sufficient for tomorrow is the evil thereof; but I hope before the day is past to have the upper hand at last.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3231	lexical	\N	\N	3230	{"text": "I could draw nothing further from him, and he walked, lost in thought, as far as the Baskerville gates.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3232	lexical	\N	\N	3231	{"text": "“Are you coming up?”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3233	lexical	\N	\N	3232	{"text": "“Yes; I see no reason for further concealment.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3234	lexical	\N	\N	3233	{"text": "But one last word, Watson.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3235	lexical	\N	\N	3234	{"text": "Say nothing of the hound to Sir Henry.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3236	lexical	\N	\N	3235	{"text": "Let him think that Selden’s death was as Stapleton would have us believe.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3237	lexical	\N	\N	3236	{"text": "He will have a better nerve for the ordeal which he will have to undergo tomorrow, when he is engaged, if I remember your report aright, to dine with these people.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3238	lexical	\N	\N	3237	{"text": "“And so am I.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3239	lexical	\N	\N	3238	{"text": "“Then you must excuse yourself and he must go alone.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3240	lexical	\N	\N	3239	{"text": "That will be easily arranged.", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3498	lexical	\N	\N	3497	{"text": "“The biggest thing for years,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3241	lexical	\N	\N	3240	{"text": "And now, if we are too late for dinner, I think that we are both ready for our suppers.”", "section": "section_81", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3242	lexical	\N	\N	3241	{"text": "Chapter 13.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3243	lexical	\N	\N	3242	{"text": "Fixing the Nets", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3244	lexical	\N	\N	3243	{"text": "Sir Henry was more pleased than surprised to see Sherlock Holmes, for he had for some days been expecting that recent events would bring him down from London.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3245	lexical	\N	\N	3244	{"text": "He did raise his eyebrows, however, when he found that my friend had neither any luggage nor any explanations for its absence.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3246	lexical	\N	\N	3245	{"text": "Between us we soon supplied his wants, and then over a belated supper we explained to the baronet as much of our experience as it seemed desirable that he should know.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3247	lexical	\N	\N	3246	{"text": "But first I had the unpleasant duty of breaking the news to Barrymore and his wife.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3248	lexical	\N	\N	3247	{"text": "To him it may have been an unmitigated relief, but she wept bitterly in her apron.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3249	lexical	\N	\N	3248	{"text": "To all the world he was the man of violence, half animal and half demon; but to her he always remained the little wilful boy of her own girlhood, the child who had clung to her hand.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3250	lexical	\N	\N	3249	{"text": "Evil indeed is the man who has not one woman to mourn him.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3251	lexical	\N	\N	3250	{"text": "“I’ve been moping in the house all day since Watson went off in the morning,” said the baronet.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3252	lexical	\N	\N	3251	{"text": "“I guess I should have some credit, for I have kept my promise.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3253	lexical	\N	\N	3252	{"text": "If I hadn’t sworn not to go about alone I might have had a more lively evening, for I had a message from Stapleton asking me over there.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3254	lexical	\N	\N	3253	{"text": "“I have no doubt that you would have had a more lively evening,” said Holmes drily.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3255	lexical	\N	\N	3254	{"text": "“By the way, I don’t suppose you appreciate that we have been mourning over you as having broken your neck?”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3256	lexical	\N	\N	3255	{"text": "Sir Henry opened his eyes.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3257	lexical	\N	\N	3256	{"text": "“How was that?”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3258	lexical	\N	\N	3257	{"text": "“This poor wretch was dressed in your clothes.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3259	lexical	\N	\N	3258	{"text": "I fear your servant who gave them to him may get into trouble with the police.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3260	lexical	\N	\N	3259	{"text": "“That is unlikely.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3261	lexical	\N	\N	3260	{"text": "There was no mark on any of them, as far as I know.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3262	lexical	\N	\N	3261	{"text": "“That’s lucky for him—in fact, it’s lucky for all of you, since you are all on the wrong side of the law in this matter.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3263	lexical	\N	\N	3262	{"text": "I am not sure that as a conscientious detective my first duty is not to arrest the whole household.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3264	lexical	\N	\N	3263	{"text": "Watson’s reports are most incriminating documents.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3265	lexical	\N	\N	3264	{"text": "“But how about the case?”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3266	lexical	\N	\N	3265	{"text": "asked the baronet.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3267	lexical	\N	\N	3266	{"text": "“Have you made anything out of the tangle?", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3268	lexical	\N	\N	3267	{"text": "I don’t know that Watson and I are much the wiser since we came down.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3269	lexical	\N	\N	3268	{"text": "“I think that I shall be in a position to make the situation rather more clear to you before long.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3270	lexical	\N	\N	3269	{"text": "It has been an exceedingly difficult and most complicated business.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3271	lexical	\N	\N	3270	{"text": "There are several points upon which we still want light—but it is coming all the same.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3272	lexical	\N	\N	3271	{"text": "“We’ve had one experience, as Watson has no doubt told you.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3273	lexical	\N	\N	3272	{"text": "We heard the hound on the moor, so I can swear that it is not all empty superstition.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3274	lexical	\N	\N	3273	{"text": "I had something to do with dogs when I was out West, and I know one when I hear one.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3275	lexical	\N	\N	3274	{"text": "If you can muzzle that one and put him on a chain I’ll be ready to swear you are the greatest detective of all time.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3533	lexical	\N	\N	3532	{"text": "“Yes, we shall make our little ambush here.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3276	lexical	\N	\N	3275	{"text": "“I think I will muzzle him and chain him all right if you will give me your help.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3277	lexical	\N	\N	3276	{"text": "“Whatever you tell me to do I will do.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3278	lexical	\N	\N	3277	{"text": "“Very good; and I will ask you also to do it blindly, without always asking the reason.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3279	lexical	\N	\N	3278	{"text": "“Just as you like.”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3280	lexical	\N	\N	3279	{"text": "“If you will do this I think the chances are that our little problem will soon be solved.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3281	lexical	\N	\N	3280	{"text": "I have no doubt—”", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3282	lexical	\N	\N	3281	{"text": "He stopped suddenly and stared fixedly up over my head into the air.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3283	lexical	\N	\N	3282	{"text": "The lamp beat upon his face, and so intent was it and so still that it might have been that of a clear-cut classical statue, a personification of alertness and expectation.", "section": "section_82", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3284	lexical	\N	\N	3283	{"text": "“What is it?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3285	lexical	\N	\N	3284	{"text": "we both cried.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3286	lexical	\N	\N	3285	{"text": "I could see as he looked down that he was repressing some internal emotion.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3287	lexical	\N	\N	3286	{"text": "His features were still composed, but his eyes shone with amused exultation.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3288	lexical	\N	\N	3287	{"text": "“Excuse the admiration of a connoisseur,” said he as he waved his hand towards the line of portraits which covered the opposite wall.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3289	lexical	\N	\N	3288	{"text": "“Watson won’t allow that I know anything of art but that is mere jealousy because our views upon the subject differ.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3290	lexical	\N	\N	3289	{"text": "Now, these are a really very fine series of portraits.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3291	lexical	\N	\N	3290	{"text": "“Well, I’m glad to hear you say so,” said Sir Henry, glancing with some surprise at my friend.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3292	lexical	\N	\N	3291	{"text": "“I don’t pretend to know much about these things, and I’d be a better judge of a horse or a steer than of a picture.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3293	lexical	\N	\N	3292	{"text": "I didn’t know that you found time for such things.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3294	lexical	\N	\N	3293	{"text": "“I know what is good when I see it, and I see it now.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3295	lexical	\N	\N	3294	{"text": "That’s a Kneller, I’ll swear, that lady in the blue silk over yonder, and the stout gentleman with the wig ought to be a Reynolds.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3296	lexical	\N	\N	3295	{"text": "They are all family portraits, I presume?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3297	lexical	\N	\N	3296	{"text": "“Every one.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3298	lexical	\N	\N	3297	{"text": "“Do you know the names?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3299	lexical	\N	\N	3298	{"text": "“Barrymore has been coaching me in them, and I think I can say my lessons fairly well.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3300	lexical	\N	\N	3299	{"text": "“Who is the gentleman with the telescope?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3301	lexical	\N	\N	3300	{"text": "“That is Rear-Admiral Baskerville, who served under Rodney in the West Indies.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3302	lexical	\N	\N	3301	{"text": "The man with the blue coat and the roll of paper is Sir William Baskerville, who was Chairman of Committees of the House of Commons under Pitt.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3303	lexical	\N	\N	3302	{"text": "“And this Cavalier opposite to me—the one with the black velvet and the lace?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3304	lexical	\N	\N	3303	{"text": "“Ah, you have a right to know about him.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3305	lexical	\N	\N	3304	{"text": "That is the cause of all the mischief, the wicked Hugo, who started the Hound of the Baskervilles.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3306	lexical	\N	\N	3305	{"text": "We’re not likely to forget him.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3307	lexical	\N	\N	3306	{"text": "I gazed with interest and some surprise upon the portrait.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3308	lexical	\N	\N	3307	{"text": "“Dear me!”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3309	lexical	\N	\N	3308	{"text": "said Holmes, “he seems a quiet, meek-mannered man enough, but I dare say that there was a lurking devil in his eyes.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3310	lexical	\N	\N	3309	{"text": "I had pictured him as a more robust and ruffianly person.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3311	lexical	\N	\N	3310	{"text": "“There’s no doubt about the authenticity, for the name and the date, 1647, are on the back of the canvas.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3312	lexical	\N	\N	3311	{"text": "Holmes said little more, but the picture of the old roysterer seemed to have a fascination for him, and his eyes were continually fixed upon it during supper.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3313	lexical	\N	\N	3312	{"text": "It was not until later, when Sir Henry had gone to his room, that I was able to follow the trend of his thoughts.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3314	lexical	\N	\N	3313	{"text": "He led me back into the banqueting-hall, his bedroom candle in his hand, and he held it up against the time-stained portrait on the wall.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3315	lexical	\N	\N	3314	{"text": "“Do you see anything there?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3316	lexical	\N	\N	3315	{"text": "I looked at the broad plumed hat, the curling love-locks, the white lace collar, and the straight, severe face which was framed between them.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3317	lexical	\N	\N	3316	{"text": "It was not a brutal countenance, but it was prim, hard, and stern, with a firm-set, thin-lipped mouth, and a coldly intolerant eye.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3318	lexical	\N	\N	3317	{"text": "“Is it like anyone you know?”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3319	lexical	\N	\N	3318	{"text": "“There is something of Sir Henry about the jaw.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3320	lexical	\N	\N	3319	{"text": "“Just a suggestion, perhaps.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3321	lexical	\N	\N	3320	{"text": "But wait an instant!”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3322	lexical	\N	\N	3321	{"text": "He stood upon a chair, and, holding up the light in his left hand, he curved his right arm over the broad hat and round the long ringlets.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3323	lexical	\N	\N	3322	{"text": "“Good heavens!”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3324	lexical	\N	\N	3323	{"text": "I cried in amazement.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3325	lexical	\N	\N	3324	{"text": "The face of Stapleton had sprung out of the canvas.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3326	lexical	\N	\N	3325	{"text": "“Ha, you see it now.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3327	lexical	\N	\N	3326	{"text": "My eyes have been trained to examine faces and not their trimmings.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3328	lexical	\N	\N	3327	{"text": "It is the first quality of a criminal investigator that he should see through a disguise.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3329	lexical	\N	\N	3328	{"text": "“But this is marvellous.", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3330	lexical	\N	\N	3329	{"text": "It might be his portrait.”", "section": "section_83", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3331	lexical	\N	\N	3330	{"text": "“Yes, it is an interesting instance of a throwback, which appears to be both physical and spiritual.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3332	lexical	\N	\N	3331	{"text": "A study of family portraits is enough to convert a man to the doctrine of reincarnation.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3333	lexical	\N	\N	3332	{"text": "The fellow is a Baskerville—that is evident.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3334	lexical	\N	\N	3333	{"text": "“With designs upon the succession.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3335	lexical	\N	\N	3334	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3336	lexical	\N	\N	3335	{"text": "This chance of the picture has supplied us with one of our most obvious missing links.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3337	lexical	\N	\N	3336	{"text": "We have him, Watson, we have him, and I dare swear that before tomorrow night he will be fluttering in our net as helpless as one of his own butterflies.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3338	lexical	\N	\N	3337	{"text": "A pin, a cork, and a card, and we add him to the Baker Street collection!”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3339	lexical	\N	\N	3338	{"text": "He burst into one of his rare fits of laughter as he turned away from the picture.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3340	lexical	\N	\N	3339	{"text": "I have not heard him laugh often, and it has always boded ill to somebody.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3341	lexical	\N	\N	3340	{"text": "I was up betimes in the morning, but Holmes was afoot earlier still, for I saw him as I dressed, coming up the drive.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3342	lexical	\N	\N	3341	{"text": "“Yes, we should have a full day today,” he remarked, and he rubbed his hands with the joy of action.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3343	lexical	\N	\N	3342	{"text": "“The nets are all in place, and the drag is about to begin.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3344	lexical	\N	\N	3343	{"text": "We’ll know before the day is out whether we have caught our big, lean-jawed pike, or whether he has got through the meshes.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3345	lexical	\N	\N	3344	{"text": "“Have you been on the moor already?”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3346	lexical	\N	\N	3345	{"text": "“I have sent a report from Grimpen to Princetown as to the death of Selden.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3347	lexical	\N	\N	3346	{"text": "I think I can promise that none of you will be troubled in the matter.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3348	lexical	\N	\N	3347	{"text": "And I have also communicated with my faithful Cartwright, who would certainly have pined away at the door of my hut, as a dog does at his master’s grave, if I had not set his mind at rest about my safety.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3349	lexical	\N	\N	3348	{"text": "“What is the next move?”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3350	lexical	\N	\N	3349	{"text": "“To see Sir Henry.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3351	lexical	\N	\N	3350	{"text": "Ah, here he is!”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3352	lexical	\N	\N	3351	{"text": "“Good-morning, Holmes,” said the baronet.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3353	lexical	\N	\N	3352	{"text": "“You look like a general who is planning a battle with his chief of the staff.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3354	lexical	\N	\N	3353	{"text": "“That is the exact situation.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3355	lexical	\N	\N	3354	{"text": "Watson was asking for orders.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3356	lexical	\N	\N	3355	{"text": "“And so do I.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3357	lexical	\N	\N	3356	{"text": "“Very good.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3358	lexical	\N	\N	3357	{"text": "You are engaged, as I understand, to dine with our friends the Stapletons tonight.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3359	lexical	\N	\N	3358	{"text": "“I hope that you will come also.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3360	lexical	\N	\N	3359	{"text": "They are very hospitable people, and I am sure that they would be very glad to see you.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3361	lexical	\N	\N	3360	{"text": "“I fear that Watson and I must go to London.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3362	lexical	\N	\N	3361	{"text": "“To London?”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3363	lexical	\N	\N	3362	{"text": "“Yes, I think that we should be more useful there at the present juncture.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3364	lexical	\N	\N	3363	{"text": "The baronet’s face perceptibly lengthened.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3365	lexical	\N	\N	3364	{"text": "“I hoped that you were going to see me through this business.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3366	lexical	\N	\N	3365	{"text": "The Hall and the moor are not very pleasant places when one is alone.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3367	lexical	\N	\N	3366	{"text": "“My dear fellow, you must trust me implicitly and do exactly what I tell you.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3368	lexical	\N	\N	3367	{"text": "You can tell your friends that we should have been happy to have come with you, but that urgent business required us to be in town.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3369	lexical	\N	\N	3368	{"text": "We hope very soon to return to Devonshire.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3370	lexical	\N	\N	3369	{"text": "Will you remember to give them that message?”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3371	lexical	\N	\N	3370	{"text": "“If you insist upon it.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3372	lexical	\N	\N	3371	{"text": "“There is no alternative, I assure you.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3373	lexical	\N	\N	3372	{"text": "I saw by the baronet’s clouded brow that he was deeply hurt by what he regarded as our desertion.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3374	lexical	\N	\N	3373	{"text": "“When do you desire to go?”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3375	lexical	\N	\N	3374	{"text": "he asked coldly.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3376	lexical	\N	\N	3375	{"text": "“Immediately after breakfast.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3377	lexical	\N	\N	3376	{"text": "We will drive in to Coombe Tracey, but Watson will leave his things as a pledge that he will come back to you.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3378	lexical	\N	\N	3377	{"text": "Watson, you will send a note to Stapleton to tell him that you regret that you cannot come.”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3379	lexical	\N	\N	3378	{"text": "“I have a good mind to go to London with you,” said the baronet.", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3380	lexical	\N	\N	3379	{"text": "“Why should I stay here alone?”", "section": "section_84", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3381	lexical	\N	\N	3380	{"text": "“Because it is your post of duty.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3382	lexical	\N	\N	3381	{"text": "Because you gave me your word that you would do as you were told, and I tell you to stay.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3383	lexical	\N	\N	3382	{"text": "“All right, then, I’ll stay.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3384	lexical	\N	\N	3383	{"text": "“One more direction!", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3385	lexical	\N	\N	3384	{"text": "I wish you to drive to Merripit House.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3386	lexical	\N	\N	3385	{"text": "Send back your trap, however, and let them know that you intend to walk home.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3387	lexical	\N	\N	3386	{"text": "“To walk across the moor?”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3389	lexical	\N	\N	3388	{"text": "“But that is the very thing which you have so often cautioned me not to do.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3390	lexical	\N	\N	3389	{"text": "“This time you may do it with safety.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3391	lexical	\N	\N	3390	{"text": "If I had not every confidence in your nerve and courage I would not suggest it, but it is essential that you should do it.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3392	lexical	\N	\N	3391	{"text": "“Then I will do it.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3393	lexical	\N	\N	3392	{"text": "“And as you value your life do not go across the moor in any direction save along the straight path which leads from Merripit House to the Grimpen Road, and is your natural way home.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3394	lexical	\N	\N	3393	{"text": "“I will do just what you say.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3395	lexical	\N	\N	3394	{"text": "“Very good.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3396	lexical	\N	\N	3395	{"text": "I should be glad to get away as soon after breakfast as possible, so as to reach London in the afternoon.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3397	lexical	\N	\N	3396	{"text": "I was much astounded by this programme, though I remembered that Holmes had said to Stapleton on the night before that his visit would terminate next day.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3398	lexical	\N	\N	3397	{"text": "It had not crossed my mind however, that he would wish me to go with him, nor could I understand how we could both be absent at a moment which he himself declared to be critical.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3399	lexical	\N	\N	3398	{"text": "There was nothing for it, however, but implicit obedience; so we bade good-bye to our rueful friend, and a couple of hours afterwards we were at the station of Coombe Tracey and had dispatched the trap upon its return journey.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3400	lexical	\N	\N	3399	{"text": "A small boy was waiting upon the platform.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3401	lexical	\N	\N	3400	{"text": "“Any orders, sir?”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3402	lexical	\N	\N	3401	{"text": "“You will take this train to town, Cartwright.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3403	lexical	\N	\N	3402	{"text": "The moment you arrive you will send a wire to Sir Henry Baskerville, in my name, to say that if he finds the pocketbook which I have dropped he is to send it by registered post to Baker Street.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3404	lexical	\N	\N	3403	{"text": "“Yes, sir.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3405	lexical	\N	\N	3404	{"text": "“And ask at the station office if there is a message for me.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3406	lexical	\N	\N	3405	{"text": "The boy returned with a telegram, which Holmes handed to me.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3407	lexical	\N	\N	3406	{"text": "It ran:", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3408	lexical	\N	\N	3407	{"text": "Wire received.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3409	lexical	\N	\N	3408	{"text": "Coming down with unsigned warrant.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3410	lexical	\N	\N	3409	{"text": "Arrive five-forty.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3411	lexical	\N	\N	3410	{"text": "Lestrade.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3412	lexical	\N	\N	3411	{"text": "“That is in answer to mine of this morning.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3413	lexical	\N	\N	3412	{"text": "He is the best of the professionals, I think, and we may need his assistance.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3414	lexical	\N	\N	3413	{"text": "Now, Watson, I think that we cannot employ our time better than by calling upon your acquaintance, Mrs. Laura Lyons.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3415	lexical	\N	\N	3414	{"text": "His plan of campaign was beginning to be evident.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3416	lexical	\N	\N	3415	{"text": "He would use the baronet in order to convince the Stapletons that we were really gone, while we should actually return at the instant when we were likely to be needed.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3417	lexical	\N	\N	3416	{"text": "That telegram from London, if mentioned by Sir Henry to the Stapletons, must remove the last suspicions from their minds.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3418	lexical	\N	\N	3417	{"text": "Already I seemed to see our nets drawing closer around that lean-jawed pike.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3419	lexical	\N	\N	3418	{"text": "Mrs. Laura Lyons was in her office, and Sherlock Holmes opened his interview with a frankness and directness which considerably amazed her.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3420	lexical	\N	\N	3419	{"text": "“I am investigating the circumstances which attended the death of the late Sir Charles Baskerville,” said he.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3421	lexical	\N	\N	3420	{"text": "“My friend here, Dr. Watson, has informed me of what you have communicated, and also of what you have withheld in connection with that matter.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3422	lexical	\N	\N	3421	{"text": "“What have I withheld?”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3423	lexical	\N	\N	3422	{"text": "she asked defiantly.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3424	lexical	\N	\N	3423	{"text": "“You have confessed that you asked Sir Charles to be at the gate at ten o’clock.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3425	lexical	\N	\N	3424	{"text": "We know that that was the place and hour of his death.", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3426	lexical	\N	\N	3425	{"text": "You have withheld what the connection is between these events.”", "section": "section_85", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3427	lexical	\N	\N	3426	{"text": "“There is no connection.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3428	lexical	\N	\N	3427	{"text": "“In that case the coincidence must indeed be an extraordinary one.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3429	lexical	\N	\N	3428	{"text": "But I think that we shall succeed in establishing a connection, after all.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3430	lexical	\N	\N	3429	{"text": "I wish to be perfectly frank with you, Mrs. Lyons.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3431	lexical	\N	\N	3430	{"text": "We regard this case as one of murder, and the evidence may implicate not only your friend Mr. Stapleton but his wife as well.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3432	lexical	\N	\N	3431	{"text": "The lady sprang from her chair.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3433	lexical	\N	\N	3432	{"text": "“His wife!”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3434	lexical	\N	\N	3433	{"text": "she cried.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3435	lexical	\N	\N	3434	{"text": "“The fact is no longer a secret.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3436	lexical	\N	\N	3435	{"text": "The person who has passed for his sister is really his wife.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3437	lexical	\N	\N	3436	{"text": "Mrs. Lyons had resumed her seat.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3438	lexical	\N	\N	3437	{"text": "Her hands were grasping the arms of her chair, and I saw that the pink nails had turned white with the pressure of her grip.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3439	lexical	\N	\N	3438	{"text": "“His wife!”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3440	lexical	\N	\N	3439	{"text": "she said again.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3441	lexical	\N	\N	3440	{"text": "“His wife!", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3442	lexical	\N	\N	3441	{"text": "He is not a married man.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3443	lexical	\N	\N	3442	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes shrugged his shoulders.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3444	lexical	\N	\N	3443	{"text": "“Prove it to me!", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3445	lexical	\N	\N	3444	{"text": "Prove it to me!", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3446	lexical	\N	\N	3445	{"text": "And if you can do so—!”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3447	lexical	\N	\N	3446	{"text": "The fierce flash of her eyes said more than any words.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3448	lexical	\N	\N	3447	{"text": "“I have come prepared to do so,” said Holmes, drawing several papers from his pocket.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3449	lexical	\N	\N	3448	{"text": "“Here is a photograph of the couple taken in York four years ago.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3450	lexical	\N	\N	3449	{"text": "It is indorsed ‘Mr. and Mrs. Vandeleur,’ but you will have no difficulty in recognizing him, and her also, if you know her by sight.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3451	lexical	\N	\N	3450	{"text": "Here are three written descriptions by trustworthy witnesses of Mr. and Mrs. Vandeleur, who at that time kept St. Oliver’s private school.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3452	lexical	\N	\N	3451	{"text": "Read them and see if you can doubt the identity of these people.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3453	lexical	\N	\N	3452	{"text": "She glanced at them, and then looked up at us with the set, rigid face of a desperate woman.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3454	lexical	\N	\N	3453	{"text": "“Mr. Holmes,” she said, “this man had offered me marriage on condition that I could get a divorce from my husband.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3455	lexical	\N	\N	3454	{"text": "He has lied to me, the villain, in every conceivable way.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3456	lexical	\N	\N	3455	{"text": "Not one word of truth has he ever told me.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3457	lexical	\N	\N	3456	{"text": "And why—why?", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3458	lexical	\N	\N	3457	{"text": "I imagined that all was for my own sake.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3459	lexical	\N	\N	3458	{"text": "But now I see that I was never anything but a tool in his hands.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3460	lexical	\N	\N	3459	{"text": "Why should I preserve faith with him who never kept any with me?", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3461	lexical	\N	\N	3460	{"text": "Why should I try to shield him from the consequences of his own wicked acts?", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3462	lexical	\N	\N	3461	{"text": "Ask me what you like, and there is nothing which I shall hold back.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3463	lexical	\N	\N	3462	{"text": "One thing I swear to you, and that is that when I wrote the letter I never dreamed of any harm to the old gentleman, who had been my kindest friend.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3464	lexical	\N	\N	3463	{"text": "“I entirely believe you, madam,” said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3465	lexical	\N	\N	3464	{"text": "“The recital of these events must be very painful to you, and perhaps it will make it easier if I tell you what occurred, and you can check me if I make any material mistake.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3466	lexical	\N	\N	3465	{"text": "The sending of this letter was suggested to you by Stapleton?”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3467	lexical	\N	\N	3466	{"text": "“He dictated it.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3468	lexical	\N	\N	3467	{"text": "“I presume that the reason he gave was that you would receive help from Sir Charles for the legal expenses connected with your divorce?”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3469	lexical	\N	\N	3468	{"text": "“Exactly.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3470	lexical	\N	\N	3469	{"text": "“And then after you had sent the letter he dissuaded you from keeping the appointment?”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3471	lexical	\N	\N	3470	{"text": "“He told me that it would hurt his self-respect that any other man should find the money for such an object, and that though he was a poor man himself he would devote his last penny to removing the obstacles which divided us.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3472	lexical	\N	\N	3471	{"text": "“He appears to be a very consistent character.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3473	lexical	\N	\N	3472	{"text": "And then you heard nothing until you read the reports of the death in the paper?”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3474	lexical	\N	\N	3473	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3475	lexical	\N	\N	3474	{"text": "“And he made you swear to say nothing about your appointment with Sir Charles?”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3476	lexical	\N	\N	3475	{"text": "“He did.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3477	lexical	\N	\N	3476	{"text": "He said that the death was a very mysterious one, and that I should certainly be suspected if the facts came out.", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3478	lexical	\N	\N	3477	{"text": "He frightened me into remaining silent.”", "section": "section_86", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3479	lexical	\N	\N	3478	{"text": "“Quite so.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3480	lexical	\N	\N	3479	{"text": "But you had your suspicions?”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3481	lexical	\N	\N	3480	{"text": "She hesitated and looked down.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3482	lexical	\N	\N	3481	{"text": "“I knew him,” she said.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3483	lexical	\N	\N	3482	{"text": "“But if he had kept faith with me I should always have done so with him.”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3484	lexical	\N	\N	3483	{"text": "“I think that on the whole you have had a fortunate escape,” said Sherlock Holmes.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3485	lexical	\N	\N	3484	{"text": "“You have had him in your power and he knew it, and yet you are alive.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3486	lexical	\N	\N	3485	{"text": "You have been walking for some months very near to the edge of a precipice.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3487	lexical	\N	\N	3486	{"text": "We must wish you good-morning now, Mrs. Lyons, and it is probable that you will very shortly hear from us again.”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3488	lexical	\N	\N	3487	{"text": "“Our case becomes rounded off, and difficulty after difficulty thins away in front of us,” said Holmes as we stood waiting for the arrival of the express from town.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3489	lexical	\N	\N	3488	{"text": "“I shall soon be in the position of being able to put into a single connected narrative one of the most singular and sensational crimes of modern times.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3490	lexical	\N	\N	3489	{"text": "Students of criminology will remember the analogous incidents in Godno, in Little Russia, in the year ’66, and of course there are the Anderson murders in North Carolina, but this case possesses some features which are entirely its own.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3491	lexical	\N	\N	3490	{"text": "Even now we have no clear case against this very wily man.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3492	lexical	\N	\N	3491	{"text": "But I shall be very much surprised if it is not clear enough before we go to bed this night.”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3493	lexical	\N	\N	3492	{"text": "The London express came roaring into the station, and a small, wiry bulldog of a man had sprung from a first-class carriage.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3494	lexical	\N	\N	3493	{"text": "We all three shook hands, and I saw at once from the reverential way in which Lestrade gazed at my companion that he had learned a good deal since the days when they had first worked together.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3495	lexical	\N	\N	3494	{"text": "I could well remember the scorn which the theories of the reasoner used then to excite in the practical man.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3496	lexical	\N	\N	3495	{"text": "“Anything good?”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3499	lexical	\N	\N	3498	{"text": "“We have two hours before we need think of starting.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3500	lexical	\N	\N	3499	{"text": "I think we might employ it in getting some dinner and then, Lestrade, we will take the London fog out of your throat by giving you a breath of the pure night air of Dartmoor.", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3501	lexical	\N	\N	3500	{"text": "Never been there?", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3502	lexical	\N	\N	3501	{"text": "Ah, well, I don’t suppose you will forget your first visit.”", "section": "section_87", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3503	lexical	\N	\N	3502	{"text": "Chapter 14.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3504	lexical	\N	\N	3503	{"text": "The Hound of the Baskervilles", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3505	lexical	\N	\N	3504	{"text": "One of Sherlock Holmes’s defects—if, indeed, one may call it a defect—was that he was exceedingly loath to communicate his full plans to any other person until the instant of their fulfilment.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3506	lexical	\N	\N	3505	{"text": "Partly it came no doubt from his own masterful nature, which loved to dominate and surprise those who were around him.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3507	lexical	\N	\N	3506	{"text": "Partly also from his professional caution, which urged him never to take any chances.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3508	lexical	\N	\N	3507	{"text": "The result, however, was very trying for those who were acting as his agents and assistants.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3509	lexical	\N	\N	3508	{"text": "I had often suffered under it, but never more so than during that long drive in the darkness.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3510	lexical	\N	\N	3509	{"text": "The great ordeal was in front of us; at last we were about to make our final effort, and yet Holmes had said nothing, and I could only surmise what his course of action would be.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3511	lexical	\N	\N	3510	{"text": "My nerves thrilled with anticipation when at last the cold wind upon our faces and the dark, void spaces on either side of the narrow road told me that we were back upon the moor once again.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3512	lexical	\N	\N	3511	{"text": "Every stride of the horses and every turn of the wheels was taking us nearer to our supreme adventure.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3513	lexical	\N	\N	3512	{"text": "Our conversation was hampered by the presence of the driver of the hired wagonette, so that we were forced to talk of trivial matters when our nerves were tense with emotion and anticipation.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3514	lexical	\N	\N	3513	{"text": "It was a relief to me, after that unnatural restraint, when we at last passed Frankland’s house and knew that we were drawing near to the Hall and to the scene of action.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3515	lexical	\N	\N	3514	{"text": "We did not drive up to the door but got down near the gate of the avenue.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3516	lexical	\N	\N	3515	{"text": "The wagonette was paid off and ordered to return to Coombe Tracey forthwith, while we started to walk to Merripit House.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3517	lexical	\N	\N	3516	{"text": "“Are you armed, Lestrade?”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3518	lexical	\N	\N	3517	{"text": "The little detective smiled.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3519	lexical	\N	\N	3518	{"text": "“As long as I have my trousers I have a hip-pocket, and as long as I have my hip-pocket I have something in it.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3520	lexical	\N	\N	3519	{"text": "“Good!", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3521	lexical	\N	\N	3520	{"text": "My friend and I are also ready for emergencies.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3522	lexical	\N	\N	3521	{"text": "“You’re mighty close about this affair, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3523	lexical	\N	\N	3522	{"text": "What’s the game now?”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3524	lexical	\N	\N	3523	{"text": "“A waiting game.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3525	lexical	\N	\N	3524	{"text": "“My word, it does not seem a very cheerful place,” said the detective with a shiver, glancing round him at the gloomy slopes of the hill and at the huge lake of fog which lay over the Grimpen Mire.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3526	lexical	\N	\N	3525	{"text": "“I see the lights of a house ahead of us.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3527	lexical	\N	\N	3526	{"text": "“That is Merripit House and the end of our journey.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3528	lexical	\N	\N	3527	{"text": "I must request you to walk on tiptoe and not to talk above a whisper.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3529	lexical	\N	\N	3528	{"text": "We moved cautiously along the track as if we were bound for the house, but Holmes halted us when we were about two hundred yards from it.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3530	lexical	\N	\N	3529	{"text": "“This will do,” said he.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3531	lexical	\N	\N	3530	{"text": "“These rocks upon the right make an admirable screen.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3532	lexical	\N	\N	3531	{"text": "“We are to wait here?”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3534	lexical	\N	\N	3533	{"text": "Get into this hollow, Lestrade.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3535	lexical	\N	\N	3534	{"text": "You have been inside the house, have you not, Watson?", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3536	lexical	\N	\N	3535	{"text": "Can you tell the position of the rooms?", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3537	lexical	\N	\N	3536	{"text": "What are those latticed windows at this end?”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3538	lexical	\N	\N	3537	{"text": "“I think they are the kitchen windows.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3539	lexical	\N	\N	3538	{"text": "“And the one beyond, which shines so brightly?”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3540	lexical	\N	\N	3539	{"text": "“That is certainly the dining-room.”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3541	lexical	\N	\N	3540	{"text": "“The blinds are up.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3542	lexical	\N	\N	3541	{"text": "You know the lie of the land best.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3543	lexical	\N	\N	3542	{"text": "Creep forward quietly and see what they are doing—but for heaven’s sake don’t let them know that they are watched!”", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3544	lexical	\N	\N	3543	{"text": "I tiptoed down the path and stooped behind the low wall which surrounded the stunted orchard.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3545	lexical	\N	\N	3544	{"text": "Creeping in its shadow I reached a point whence I could look straight through the uncurtained window.", "section": "section_88", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3546	lexical	\N	\N	3545	{"text": "There were only two men in the room, Sir Henry and Stapleton.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3547	lexical	\N	\N	3546	{"text": "They sat with their profiles towards me on either side of the round table.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3548	lexical	\N	\N	3547	{"text": "Both of them were smoking cigars, and coffee and wine were in front of them.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3549	lexical	\N	\N	3548	{"text": "Stapleton was talking with animation, but the baronet looked pale and distrait.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3550	lexical	\N	\N	3549	{"text": "Perhaps the thought of that lonely walk across the ill-omened moor was weighing heavily upon his mind.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3551	lexical	\N	\N	3550	{"text": "As I watched them Stapleton rose and left the room, while Sir Henry filled his glass again and leaned back in his chair, puffing at his cigar.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3552	lexical	\N	\N	3551	{"text": "I heard the creak of a door and the crisp sound of boots upon gravel.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3553	lexical	\N	\N	3552	{"text": "The steps passed along the path on the other side of the wall under which I crouched.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3554	lexical	\N	\N	3553	{"text": "Looking over, I saw the naturalist pause at the door of an out-house in the corner of the orchard.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3555	lexical	\N	\N	3554	{"text": "A key turned in a lock, and as he passed in there was a curious scuffling noise from within.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3556	lexical	\N	\N	3555	{"text": "He was only a minute or so inside, and then I heard the key turn once more and he passed me and reentered the house.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3557	lexical	\N	\N	3556	{"text": "I saw him rejoin his guest, and I crept quietly back to where my companions were waiting to tell them what I had seen.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3558	lexical	\N	\N	3557	{"text": "“You say, Watson, that the lady is not there?”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3559	lexical	\N	\N	3558	{"text": "Holmes asked when I had finished my report.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3560	lexical	\N	\N	3559	{"text": "“No.”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3561	lexical	\N	\N	3560	{"text": "“Where can she be, then, since there is no light in any other room except the kitchen?”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3562	lexical	\N	\N	3561	{"text": "“I cannot think where she is.”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3563	lexical	\N	\N	3562	{"text": "I have said that over the great Grimpen Mire there hung a dense, white fog.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3564	lexical	\N	\N	3563	{"text": "It was drifting slowly in our direction and banked itself up like a wall on that side of us, low but thick and well defined.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3565	lexical	\N	\N	3564	{"text": "The moon shone on it, and it looked like a great shimmering ice-field, with the heads of the distant tors as rocks borne upon its surface.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3566	lexical	\N	\N	3565	{"text": "Holmes’s face was turned towards it, and he muttered impatiently as he watched its sluggish drift.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3567	lexical	\N	\N	3566	{"text": "“It’s moving towards us, Watson.”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3568	lexical	\N	\N	3567	{"text": "“Is that serious?”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3569	lexical	\N	\N	3568	{"text": "“Very serious, indeed—the one thing upon earth which could have disarranged my plans.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3570	lexical	\N	\N	3569	{"text": "He can’t be very long, now.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3571	lexical	\N	\N	3570	{"text": "It is already ten o’clock.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3572	lexical	\N	\N	3571	{"text": "Our success and even his life may depend upon his coming out before the fog is over the path.”", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3573	lexical	\N	\N	3572	{"text": "The night was clear and fine above us.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3574	lexical	\N	\N	3573	{"text": "The stars shone cold and bright, while a half-moon bathed the whole scene in a soft, uncertain light.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3575	lexical	\N	\N	3574	{"text": "Before us lay the dark bulk of the house, its serrated roof and bristling chimneys hard outlined against the silver-spangled sky.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3576	lexical	\N	\N	3575	{"text": "Broad bars of golden light from the lower windows stretched across the orchard and the moor.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3577	lexical	\N	\N	3576	{"text": "One of them was suddenly shut off.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3578	lexical	\N	\N	3577	{"text": "The servants had left the kitchen.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3579	lexical	\N	\N	3578	{"text": "There only remained the lamp in the dining-room where the two men, the murderous host and the unconscious guest, still chatted over their cigars.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3580	lexical	\N	\N	3579	{"text": "Every minute that white woolly plain which covered one-half of the moor was drifting closer and closer to the house.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3581	lexical	\N	\N	3580	{"text": "Already the first thin wisps of it were curling across the golden square of the lighted window.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3582	lexical	\N	\N	3581	{"text": "The farther wall of the orchard was already invisible, and the trees were standing out of a swirl of white vapour.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3583	lexical	\N	\N	3582	{"text": "As we watched it the fog-wreaths came crawling round both corners of the house and rolled slowly into one dense bank on which the upper floor and the roof floated like a strange ship upon a shadowy sea.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3584	lexical	\N	\N	3583	{"text": "Holmes struck his hand passionately upon the rock in front of us and stamped his feet in his impatience.", "section": "section_89", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3585	lexical	\N	\N	3584	{"text": "“If he isn’t out in a quarter of an hour the path will be covered.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3586	lexical	\N	\N	3585	{"text": "In half an hour we won’t be able to see our hands in front of us.”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3587	lexical	\N	\N	3586	{"text": "“Shall we move farther back upon higher ground?”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3588	lexical	\N	\N	3587	{"text": "“Yes, I think it would be as well.”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3589	lexical	\N	\N	3588	{"text": "So as the fog-bank flowed onward we fell back before it until we were half a mile from the house, and still that dense white sea, with the moon silvering its upper edge, swept slowly and inexorably on.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3590	lexical	\N	\N	3589	{"text": "“We are going too far,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3591	lexical	\N	\N	3590	{"text": "“We dare not take the chance of his being overtaken before he can reach us.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3592	lexical	\N	\N	3591	{"text": "At all costs we must hold our ground where we are.”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3593	lexical	\N	\N	3592	{"text": "He dropped on his knees and clapped his ear to the ground.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3594	lexical	\N	\N	3593	{"text": "“Thank God, I think that I hear him coming.”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3595	lexical	\N	\N	3594	{"text": "A sound of quick steps broke the silence of the moor.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3596	lexical	\N	\N	3595	{"text": "Crouching among the stones we stared intently at the silver-tipped bank in front of us.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3597	lexical	\N	\N	3596	{"text": "The steps grew louder, and through the fog, as through a curtain, there stepped the man whom we were awaiting.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3598	lexical	\N	\N	3597	{"text": "He looked round him in surprise as he emerged into the clear, starlit night.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3599	lexical	\N	\N	3598	{"text": "Then he came swiftly along the path, passed close to where we lay, and went on up the long slope behind us.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3600	lexical	\N	\N	3599	{"text": "As he walked he glanced continually over either shoulder, like a man who is ill at ease.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3601	lexical	\N	\N	3600	{"text": "“Hist!”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3602	lexical	\N	\N	3601	{"text": "cried Holmes, and I heard the sharp click of a cocking pistol.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3603	lexical	\N	\N	3602	{"text": "“Look out!", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3604	lexical	\N	\N	3603	{"text": "It’s coming!”", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3605	lexical	\N	\N	3604	{"text": "There was a thin, crisp, continuous patter from somewhere in the heart of that crawling bank.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3678	lexical	\N	\N	3677	{"text": "A faint moaning and rustling came from within.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3606	lexical	\N	\N	3605	{"text": "The cloud was within fifty yards of where we lay, and we glared at it, all three, uncertain what horror was about to break from the heart of it.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3607	lexical	\N	\N	3606	{"text": "I was at Holmes’s elbow, and I glanced for an instant at his face.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3608	lexical	\N	\N	3607	{"text": "It was pale and exultant, his eyes shining brightly in the moonlight.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3609	lexical	\N	\N	3608	{"text": "But suddenly they started forward in a rigid, fixed stare, and his lips parted in amazement.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3610	lexical	\N	\N	3609	{"text": "At the same instant Lestrade gave a yell of terror and threw himself face downward upon the ground.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3611	lexical	\N	\N	3610	{"text": "I sprang to my feet, my inert hand grasping my pistol, my mind paralyzed by the dreadful shape which had sprung out upon us from the shadows of the fog.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3612	lexical	\N	\N	3611	{"text": "A hound it was, an enormous coal-black hound, but not such a hound as mortal eyes have ever seen.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3613	lexical	\N	\N	3612	{"text": "Fire burst from its open mouth, its eyes glowed with a smouldering glare, its muzzle and hackles and dewlap were outlined in flickering flame.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3614	lexical	\N	\N	3613	{"text": "Never in the delirious dream of a disordered brain could anything more savage, more appalling, more hellish be conceived than that dark form and savage face which broke upon us out of the wall of fog.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3615	lexical	\N	\N	3614	{"text": "With long bounds the huge black creature was leaping down the track, following hard upon the footsteps of our friend.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3616	lexical	\N	\N	3615	{"text": "So paralyzed were we by the apparition that we allowed him to pass before we had recovered our nerve.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3617	lexical	\N	\N	3616	{"text": "Then Holmes and I both fired together, and the creature gave a hideous howl, which showed that one at least had hit him.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3618	lexical	\N	\N	3617	{"text": "He did not pause, however, but bounded onward.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3619	lexical	\N	\N	3618	{"text": "Far away on the path we saw Sir Henry looking back, his face white in the moonlight, his hands raised in horror, glaring helplessly at the frightful thing which was hunting him down.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3620	lexical	\N	\N	3619	{"text": "But that cry of pain from the hound had blown all our fears to the winds.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3621	lexical	\N	\N	3620	{"text": "If he was vulnerable he was mortal, and if we could wound him we could kill him.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3622	lexical	\N	\N	3621	{"text": "Never have I seen a man run as Holmes ran that night.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3623	lexical	\N	\N	3622	{"text": "I am reckoned fleet of foot, but he outpaced me as much as I outpaced the little professional.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3624	lexical	\N	\N	3623	{"text": "In front of us as we flew up the track we heard scream after scream from Sir Henry and the deep roar of the hound.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3625	lexical	\N	\N	3624	{"text": "I was in time to see the beast spring upon its victim, hurl him to the ground, and worry at his throat.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3626	lexical	\N	\N	3625	{"text": "But the next instant Holmes had emptied five barrels of his revolver into the creature’s flank.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3627	lexical	\N	\N	3626	{"text": "With a last howl of agony and a vicious snap in the air, it rolled upon its back, four feet pawing furiously, and then fell limp upon its side.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3628	lexical	\N	\N	3627	{"text": "I stooped, panting, and pressed my pistol to the dreadful, shimmering head, but it was useless to press the trigger.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3629	lexical	\N	\N	3628	{"text": "The giant hound was dead.", "section": "section_90", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3630	lexical	\N	\N	3629	{"text": "Sir Henry lay insensible where he had fallen.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3631	lexical	\N	\N	3630	{"text": "We tore away his collar, and Holmes breathed a prayer of gratitude when we saw that there was no sign of a wound and that the rescue had been in time.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3632	lexical	\N	\N	3631	{"text": "Already our friend’s eyelids shivered and he made a feeble effort to move.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3633	lexical	\N	\N	3632	{"text": "Lestrade thrust his brandy-flask between the baronet’s teeth, and two frightened eyes were looking up at us.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3634	lexical	\N	\N	3633	{"text": "“My God!”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3635	lexical	\N	\N	3634	{"text": "he whispered.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3636	lexical	\N	\N	3635	{"text": "“What was it?", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3637	lexical	\N	\N	3636	{"text": "What, in heaven’s name, was it?”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3638	lexical	\N	\N	3637	{"text": "“It’s dead, whatever it is,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3639	lexical	\N	\N	3638	{"text": "“We’ve laid the family ghost once and forever.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3640	lexical	\N	\N	3639	{"text": "In mere size and strength it was a terrible creature which was lying stretched before us.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3641	lexical	\N	\N	3640	{"text": "It was not a pure bloodhound and it was not a pure mastiff; but it appeared to be a combination of the two—gaunt, savage, and as large as a small lioness.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3642	lexical	\N	\N	3641	{"text": "Even now in the stillness of death, the huge jaws seemed to be dripping with a bluish flame and the small, deep-set, cruel eyes were ringed with fire.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3643	lexical	\N	\N	3642	{"text": "I placed my hand upon the glowing muzzle, and as I held them up my own fingers smouldered and gleamed in the darkness.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3644	lexical	\N	\N	3643	{"text": "“Phosphorus,” I said.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3645	lexical	\N	\N	3644	{"text": "“A cunning preparation of it,” said Holmes, sniffing at the dead animal.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3646	lexical	\N	\N	3645	{"text": "“There is no smell which might have interfered with his power of scent.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3647	lexical	\N	\N	3646	{"text": "We owe you a deep apology, Sir Henry, for having exposed you to this fright.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3648	lexical	\N	\N	3647	{"text": "I was prepared for a hound, but not for such a creature as this.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3649	lexical	\N	\N	3648	{"text": "And the fog gave us little time to receive him.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3650	lexical	\N	\N	3649	{"text": "“You have saved my life.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3651	lexical	\N	\N	3650	{"text": "“Having first endangered it.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3652	lexical	\N	\N	3651	{"text": "Are you strong enough to stand?”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3653	lexical	\N	\N	3652	{"text": "“Give me another mouthful of that brandy and I shall be ready for anything.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3654	lexical	\N	\N	3653	{"text": "So!", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3655	lexical	\N	\N	3654	{"text": "Now, if you will help me up.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3656	lexical	\N	\N	3655	{"text": "What do you propose to do?”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3657	lexical	\N	\N	3656	{"text": "“To leave you here.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3658	lexical	\N	\N	3657	{"text": "You are not fit for further adventures tonight.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3659	lexical	\N	\N	3658	{"text": "If you will wait, one or other of us will go back with you to the Hall.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3660	lexical	\N	\N	3659	{"text": "He tried to stagger to his feet; but he was still ghastly pale and trembling in every limb.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3661	lexical	\N	\N	3660	{"text": "We helped him to a rock, where he sat shivering with his face buried in his hands.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3662	lexical	\N	\N	3661	{"text": "“We must leave you now,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3663	lexical	\N	\N	3662	{"text": "“The rest of our work must be done, and every moment is of importance.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3664	lexical	\N	\N	3663	{"text": "We have our case, and now we only want our man.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3665	lexical	\N	\N	3664	{"text": "“It’s a thousand to one against our finding him at the house,” he continued as we retraced our steps swiftly down the path.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3666	lexical	\N	\N	3665	{"text": "“Those shots must have told him that the game was up.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3667	lexical	\N	\N	3666	{"text": "“We were some distance off, and this fog may have deadened them.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3668	lexical	\N	\N	3667	{"text": "“He followed the hound to call him off—of that you may be certain.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3669	lexical	\N	\N	3668	{"text": "No, no, he’s gone by this time!", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3670	lexical	\N	\N	3669	{"text": "But we’ll search the house and make sure.”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3671	lexical	\N	\N	3670	{"text": "The front door was open, so we rushed in and hurried from room to room to the amazement of a doddering old manservant, who met us in the passage.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3672	lexical	\N	\N	3671	{"text": "There was no light save in the dining-room, but Holmes caught up the lamp and left no corner of the house unexplored.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3673	lexical	\N	\N	3672	{"text": "No sign could we see of the man whom we were chasing.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3674	lexical	\N	\N	3673	{"text": "On the upper floor, however, one of the bedroom doors was locked.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3675	lexical	\N	\N	3674	{"text": "“There’s someone in here,” cried Lestrade.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3676	lexical	\N	\N	3675	{"text": "“I can hear a movement.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3677	lexical	\N	\N	3676	{"text": "Open this door!”", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3679	lexical	\N	\N	3678	{"text": "Holmes struck the door just over the lock with the flat of his foot and it flew open.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3680	lexical	\N	\N	3679	{"text": "Pistol in hand, we all three rushed into the room.", "section": "section_91", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3681	lexical	\N	\N	3680	{"text": "But there was no sign within it of that desperate and defiant villain whom we expected to see.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3682	lexical	\N	\N	3681	{"text": "Instead we were faced by an object so strange and so unexpected that we stood for a moment staring at it in amazement.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3683	lexical	\N	\N	3682	{"text": "The room had been fashioned into a small museum, and the walls were lined by a number of glass-topped cases full of that collection of butterflies and moths the formation of which had been the relaxation of this complex and dangerous man.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3684	lexical	\N	\N	3683	{"text": "In the centre of this room there was an upright beam, which had been placed at some period as a support for the old worm-eaten baulk of timber which spanned the roof.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3685	lexical	\N	\N	3684	{"text": "To this post a figure was tied, so swathed and muffled in the sheets which had been used to secure it that one could not for the moment tell whether it was that of a man or a woman.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3686	lexical	\N	\N	3685	{"text": "One towel passed round the throat and was secured at the back of the pillar.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3687	lexical	\N	\N	3686	{"text": "Another covered the lower part of the face, and over it two dark eyes—eyes full of grief and shame and a dreadful questioning—stared back at us.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3688	lexical	\N	\N	3687	{"text": "In a minute we had torn off the gag, unswathed the bonds, and Mrs. Stapleton sank upon the floor in front of us.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3689	lexical	\N	\N	3688	{"text": "As her beautiful head fell upon her chest I saw the clear red weal of a whiplash across her neck.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3690	lexical	\N	\N	3689	{"text": "“The brute!”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3691	lexical	\N	\N	3690	{"text": "cried Holmes.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3692	lexical	\N	\N	3691	{"text": "“Here, Lestrade, your brandy-bottle!", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3693	lexical	\N	\N	3692	{"text": "Put her in the chair!", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3694	lexical	\N	\N	3693	{"text": "She has fainted from ill-usage and exhaustion.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3695	lexical	\N	\N	3694	{"text": "She opened her eyes again.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3696	lexical	\N	\N	3695	{"text": "“Is he safe?”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3697	lexical	\N	\N	3696	{"text": "she asked.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3698	lexical	\N	\N	3697	{"text": "“Has he escaped?”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3699	lexical	\N	\N	3698	{"text": "“He cannot escape us, madam.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3700	lexical	\N	\N	3699	{"text": "“No, no, I did not mean my husband.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3701	lexical	\N	\N	3700	{"text": "Sir Henry?", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3702	lexical	\N	\N	3701	{"text": "Is he safe?”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3703	lexical	\N	\N	3702	{"text": "“Yes.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3704	lexical	\N	\N	3703	{"text": "“And the hound?”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3705	lexical	\N	\N	3704	{"text": "“It is dead.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3706	lexical	\N	\N	3705	{"text": "She gave a long sigh of satisfaction.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3707	lexical	\N	\N	3706	{"text": "“Thank God!", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3708	lexical	\N	\N	3707	{"text": "Thank God!", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3709	lexical	\N	\N	3708	{"text": "Oh, this villain!", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3710	lexical	\N	\N	3709	{"text": "See how he has treated me!”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3711	lexical	\N	\N	3710	{"text": "She shot her arms out from her sleeves, and we saw with horror that they were all mottled with bruises.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3712	lexical	\N	\N	3711	{"text": "“But this is nothing—nothing!", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3713	lexical	\N	\N	3712	{"text": "It is my mind and soul that he has tortured and defiled.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3714	lexical	\N	\N	3713	{"text": "I could endure it all, ill-usage, solitude, a life of deception, everything, as long as I could still cling to the hope that I had his love, but now I know that in this also I have been his dupe and his tool.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3715	lexical	\N	\N	3714	{"text": "She broke into passionate sobbing as she spoke.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3716	lexical	\N	\N	3715	{"text": "“You bear him no good will, madam,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3717	lexical	\N	\N	3716	{"text": "“Tell us then where we shall find him.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3718	lexical	\N	\N	3717	{"text": "If you have ever aided him in evil, help us now and so atone.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3719	lexical	\N	\N	3718	{"text": "“There is but one place where he can have fled,” she answered.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3720	lexical	\N	\N	3719	{"text": "“There is an old tin mine on an island in the heart of the mire.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3721	lexical	\N	\N	3720	{"text": "It was there that he kept his hound and there also he had made preparations so that he might have a refuge.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3722	lexical	\N	\N	3721	{"text": "That is where he would fly.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3723	lexical	\N	\N	3722	{"text": "The fog-bank lay like white wool against the window.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3724	lexical	\N	\N	3723	{"text": "Holmes held the lamp towards it.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3725	lexical	\N	\N	3724	{"text": "“See,” said he.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3726	lexical	\N	\N	3725	{"text": "“No one could find his way into the Grimpen Mire tonight.”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3727	lexical	\N	\N	3726	{"text": "She laughed and clapped her hands.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3728	lexical	\N	\N	3727	{"text": "Her eyes and teeth gleamed with fierce merriment.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3729	lexical	\N	\N	3728	{"text": "“He may find his way in, but never out,” she cried.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3730	lexical	\N	\N	3729	{"text": "“How can he see the guiding wands tonight?", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3731	lexical	\N	\N	3730	{"text": "We planted them together, he and I, to mark the pathway through the mire.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3732	lexical	\N	\N	3731	{"text": "Oh, if I could only have plucked them out today.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3733	lexical	\N	\N	3732	{"text": "Then indeed you would have had him at your mercy!”", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3734	lexical	\N	\N	3733	{"text": "It was evident to us that all pursuit was in vain until the fog had lifted.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3735	lexical	\N	\N	3734	{"text": "Meanwhile we left Lestrade in possession of the house while Holmes and I went back with the baronet to Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3736	lexical	\N	\N	3735	{"text": "The story of the Stapletons could no longer be withheld from him, but he took the blow bravely when he learned the truth about the woman whom he had loved.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3737	lexical	\N	\N	3736	{"text": "But the shock of the night’s adventures had shattered his nerves, and before morning he lay delirious in a high fever under the care of Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3738	lexical	\N	\N	3737	{"text": "The two of them were destined to travel together round the world before Sir Henry had become once more the hale, hearty man that he had been before he became master of that ill-omened estate.", "section": "section_92", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3739	lexical	\N	\N	3738	{"text": "And now I come rapidly to the conclusion of this singular narrative, in which I have tried to make the reader share those dark fears and vague surmises which clouded our lives so long and ended in so tragic a manner.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3740	lexical	\N	\N	3739	{"text": "On the morning after the death of the hound the fog had lifted and we were guided by Mrs. Stapleton to the point where they had found a pathway through the bog.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3741	lexical	\N	\N	3740	{"text": "It helped us to realise the horror of this woman’s life when we saw the eagerness and joy with which she laid us on her husband’s track.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3742	lexical	\N	\N	3741	{"text": "We left her standing upon the thin peninsula of firm, peaty soil which tapered out into the widespread bog.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3743	lexical	\N	\N	3742	{"text": "From the end of it a small wand planted here and there showed where the path zigzagged from tuft to tuft of rushes among those green-scummed pits and foul quagmires which barred the way to the stranger.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3744	lexical	\N	\N	3743	{"text": "Rank reeds and lush, slimy water-plants sent an odour of decay and a heavy miasmatic vapour onto our faces, while a false step plunged us more than once thigh-deep into the dark, quivering mire, which shook for yards in soft undulations around our feet.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3745	lexical	\N	\N	3744	{"text": "Its tenacious grip plucked at our heels as we walked, and when we sank into it it was as if some malignant hand was tugging us down into those obscene depths, so grim and purposeful was the clutch in which it held us.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3746	lexical	\N	\N	3745	{"text": "Once only we saw a trace that someone had passed that perilous way before us.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3747	lexical	\N	\N	3746	{"text": "From amid a tuft of cotton grass which bore it up out of the slime some dark thing was projecting.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3748	lexical	\N	\N	3747	{"text": "Holmes sank to his waist as he stepped from the path to seize it, and had we not been there to drag him out he could never have set his foot upon firm land again.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3749	lexical	\N	\N	3748	{"text": "He held an old black boot in the air.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3750	lexical	\N	\N	3749	{"text": "“Meyers, Toronto,” was printed on the leather inside.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3751	lexical	\N	\N	3750	{"text": "“It is worth a mud bath,” said he.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3752	lexical	\N	\N	3751	{"text": "“It is our friend Sir Henry’s missing boot.”", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3753	lexical	\N	\N	3752	{"text": "“Thrown there by Stapleton in his flight.”", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3754	lexical	\N	\N	3753	{"text": "“Exactly.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3755	lexical	\N	\N	3754	{"text": "He retained it in his hand after using it to set the hound upon the track.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3756	lexical	\N	\N	3755	{"text": "He fled when he knew the game was up, still clutching it.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3757	lexical	\N	\N	3756	{"text": "And he hurled it away at this point of his flight.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3758	lexical	\N	\N	3757	{"text": "We know at least that he came so far in safety.”", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3759	lexical	\N	\N	3758	{"text": "But more than that we were never destined to know, though there was much which we might surmise.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3760	lexical	\N	\N	3759	{"text": "There was no chance of finding footsteps in the mire, for the rising mud oozed swiftly in upon them, but as we at last reached firmer ground beyond the morass we all looked eagerly for them.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3761	lexical	\N	\N	3760	{"text": "But no slightest sign of them ever met our eyes.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3762	lexical	\N	\N	3761	{"text": "If the earth told a true story, then Stapleton never reached that island of refuge towards which he struggled through the fog upon that last night.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3763	lexical	\N	\N	3762	{"text": "Somewhere in the heart of the great Grimpen Mire, down in the foul slime of the huge morass which had sucked him in, this cold and cruel-hearted man is forever buried.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3764	lexical	\N	\N	3763	{"text": "Many traces we found of him in the bog-girt island where he had hid his savage ally.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3765	lexical	\N	\N	3764	{"text": "A huge driving-wheel and a shaft half-filled with rubbish showed the position of an abandoned mine.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3766	lexical	\N	\N	3765	{"text": "Beside it were the crumbling remains of the cottages of the miners, driven away no doubt by the foul reek of the surrounding swamp.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3767	lexical	\N	\N	3766	{"text": "In one of these a staple and chain with a quantity of gnawed bones showed where the animal had been confined.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3768	lexical	\N	\N	3767	{"text": "A skeleton with a tangle of brown hair adhering to it lay among the _débris_.", "section": "section_93", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3769	lexical	\N	\N	3768	{"text": "“A dog!”", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3770	lexical	\N	\N	3769	{"text": "said Holmes.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3771	lexical	\N	\N	3770	{"text": "“By Jove, a curly-haired spaniel.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3772	lexical	\N	\N	3771	{"text": "Poor Mortimer will never see his pet again.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3773	lexical	\N	\N	3772	{"text": "Well, I do not know that this place contains any secret which we have not already fathomed.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3774	lexical	\N	\N	3773	{"text": "He could hide his hound, but he could not hush its voice, and hence came those cries which even in daylight were not pleasant to hear.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3775	lexical	\N	\N	3774	{"text": "On an emergency he could keep the hound in the out-house at Merripit, but it was always a risk, and it was only on the supreme day, which he regarded as the end of all his efforts, that he dared do it.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3776	lexical	\N	\N	3775	{"text": "This paste in the tin is no doubt the luminous mixture with which the creature was daubed.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3777	lexical	\N	\N	3776	{"text": "It was suggested, of course, by the story of the family hell-hound, and by the desire to frighten old Sir Charles to death.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3778	lexical	\N	\N	3777	{"text": "No wonder the poor devil of a convict ran and screamed, even as our friend did, and as we ourselves might have done, when he saw such a creature bounding through the darkness of the moor upon his track.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3779	lexical	\N	\N	3778	{"text": "It was a cunning device, for, apart from the chance of driving your victim to his death, what peasant would venture to inquire too closely into such a creature should he get sight of it, as many have done, upon the moor?", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3780	lexical	\N	\N	3779	{"text": "I said it in London, Watson, and I say it again now, that never yet have we helped to hunt down a more dangerous man than he who is lying yonder”—he swept his long arm towards the huge mottled expanse of green-splotched bog which stretched away until it merged into the russet slopes of the moor.", "section": "section_94", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3781	lexical	\N	\N	3780	{"text": "Chapter 15.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3782	lexical	\N	\N	3781	{"text": "A Retrospection", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	the_house	entity	location	The house	\N	{"description": "Hugo Baskerville's house.", "firstSection": "section_8"}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3783	lexical	\N	\N	3782	{"text": "It was the end of November, and Holmes and I sat, upon a raw and foggy night, on either side of a blazing fire in our sitting-room in Baker Street.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3784	lexical	\N	\N	3783	{"text": "Since the tragic upshot of our visit to Devonshire he had been engaged in two affairs of the utmost importance, in the first of which he had exposed the atrocious conduct of Colonel Upwood in connection with the famous card scandal of the Nonpareil Club, while in the second he had defended the unfortunate Mme.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3785	lexical	\N	\N	3784	{"text": "Montpensier from the charge of murder which hung over her in connection with the death of her step-daughter, Mlle.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3786	lexical	\N	\N	3785	{"text": "Carére, the young lady who, as it will be remembered, was found six months later alive and married in New York.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3787	lexical	\N	\N	3786	{"text": "My friend was in excellent spirits over the success which had attended a succession of difficult and important cases, so that I was able to induce him to discuss the details of the Baskerville mystery.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3788	lexical	\N	\N	3787	{"text": "I had waited patiently for the opportunity for I was aware that he would never permit cases to overlap, and that his clear and logical mind would not be drawn from its present work to dwell upon memories of the past.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3789	lexical	\N	\N	3788	{"text": "Sir Henry and Dr. Mortimer were, however, in London, on their way to that long voyage which had been recommended for the restoration of his shattered nerves.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3790	lexical	\N	\N	3789	{"text": "They had called upon us that very afternoon, so that it was natural that the subject should come up for discussion.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3791	lexical	\N	\N	3790	{"text": "“The whole course of events,” said Holmes, “from the point of view of the man who called himself Stapleton was simple and direct, although to us, who had no means in the beginning of knowing the motives of his actions and could only learn part of the facts, it all appeared exceedingly complex.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3792	lexical	\N	\N	3791	{"text": "I have had the advantage of two conversations with Mrs. Stapleton, and the case has now been so entirely cleared up that I am not aware that there is anything which has remained a secret to us.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3793	lexical	\N	\N	3792	{"text": "You will find a few notes upon the matter under the heading B in my indexed list of cases.”", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3794	lexical	\N	\N	3793	{"text": "“Perhaps you would kindly give me a sketch of the course of events from memory.”", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3795	lexical	\N	\N	3794	{"text": "“Certainly, though I cannot guarantee that I carry all the facts in my mind.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3796	lexical	\N	\N	3795	{"text": "Intense mental concentration has a curious way of blotting out what has passed.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3797	lexical	\N	\N	3796	{"text": "The barrister who has his case at his fingers’ ends and is able to argue with an expert upon his own subject finds that a week or two of the courts will drive it all out of his head once more.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3798	lexical	\N	\N	3797	{"text": "So each of my cases displaces the last, and Mlle.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3799	lexical	\N	\N	3798	{"text": "Carére has blurred my recollection of Baskerville Hall.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3800	lexical	\N	\N	3799	{"text": "Tomorrow some other little problem may be submitted to my notice which will in turn dispossess the fair French lady and the infamous Upwood.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3801	lexical	\N	\N	3800	{"text": "So far as the case of the hound goes, however, I will give you the course of events as nearly as I can, and you will suggest anything which I may have forgotten.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3802	lexical	\N	\N	3801	{"text": "“My inquiries show beyond all question that the family portrait did not lie, and that this fellow was indeed a Baskerville.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3803	lexical	\N	\N	3802	{"text": "He was a son of that Rodger Baskerville, the younger brother of Sir Charles, who fled with a sinister reputation to South America, where he was said to have died unmarried.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3804	lexical	\N	\N	3803	{"text": "He did, as a matter of fact, marry, and had one child, this fellow, whose real name is the same as his father’s.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3805	lexical	\N	\N	3804	{"text": "He married Beryl Garcia, one of the beauties of Costa Rica, and, having purloined a considerable sum of public money, he changed his name to Vandeleur and fled to England, where he established a school in the east of Yorkshire.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3806	lexical	\N	\N	3805	{"text": "His reason for attempting this special line of business was that he had struck up an acquaintance with a consumptive tutor upon the voyage home, and that he had used this man’s ability to make the undertaking a success.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3807	lexical	\N	\N	3806	{"text": "Fraser, the tutor, died however, and the school which had begun well sank from disrepute into infamy.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3808	lexical	\N	\N	3807	{"text": "The Vandeleurs found it convenient to change their name to Stapleton, and he brought the remains of his fortune, his schemes for the future, and his taste for entomology to the south of England.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3868	lexical	\N	\N	3867	{"text": "Eventually, as we know, she adopted the expedient of cutting out the words which would form the message, and addressing the letter in a disguised hand.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3809	lexical	\N	\N	3808	{"text": "I learned at the British Museum that he was a recognized authority upon the subject, and that the name of Vandeleur has been permanently attached to a certain moth which he had, in his Yorkshire days, been the first to describe.", "section": "section_95", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3810	lexical	\N	\N	3809	{"text": "“We now come to that portion of his life which has proved to be of such intense interest to us.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3811	lexical	\N	\N	3810	{"text": "The fellow had evidently made inquiry and found that only two lives intervened between him and a valuable estate.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3812	lexical	\N	\N	3811	{"text": "When he went to Devonshire his plans were, I believe, exceedingly hazy, but that he meant mischief from the first is evident from the way in which he took his wife with him in the character of his sister.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3813	lexical	\N	\N	3812	{"text": "The idea of using her as a decoy was clearly already in his mind, though he may not have been certain how the details of his plot were to be arranged.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3814	lexical	\N	\N	3813	{"text": "He meant in the end to have the estate, and he was ready to use any tool or run any risk for that end.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3815	lexical	\N	\N	3814	{"text": "His first act was to establish himself as near to his ancestral home as he could, and his second was to cultivate a friendship with Sir Charles Baskerville and with the neighbours.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3816	lexical	\N	\N	3815	{"text": "“The baronet himself told him about the family hound, and so prepared the way for his own death.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3817	lexical	\N	\N	3816	{"text": "Stapleton, as I will continue to call him, knew that the old man’s heart was weak and that a shock would kill him.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3818	lexical	\N	\N	3817	{"text": "So much he had learned from Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3819	lexical	\N	\N	3818	{"text": "He had heard also that Sir Charles was superstitious and had taken this grim legend very seriously.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3820	lexical	\N	\N	3819	{"text": "His ingenious mind instantly suggested a way by which the baronet could be done to death, and yet it would be hardly possible to bring home the guilt to the real murderer.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3821	lexical	\N	\N	3820	{"text": "“Having conceived the idea he proceeded to carry it out with considerable finesse.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3822	lexical	\N	\N	3821	{"text": "An ordinary schemer would have been content to work with a savage hound.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3823	lexical	\N	\N	3822	{"text": "The use of artificial means to make the creature diabolical was a flash of genius upon his part.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3824	lexical	\N	\N	3823	{"text": "The dog he bought in London from Ross and Mangles, the dealers in Fulham Road.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3825	lexical	\N	\N	3824	{"text": "It was the strongest and most savage in their possession.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3826	lexical	\N	\N	3825	{"text": "He brought it down by the North Devon line and walked a great distance over the moor so as to get it home without exciting any remarks.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3827	lexical	\N	\N	3826	{"text": "He had already on his insect hunts learned to penetrate the Grimpen Mire, and so had found a safe hiding-place for the creature.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3828	lexical	\N	\N	3827	{"text": "Here he kennelled it and waited his chance.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3829	lexical	\N	\N	3828	{"text": "“But it was some time coming.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3830	lexical	\N	\N	3829	{"text": "The old gentleman could not be decoyed outside of his grounds at night.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3831	lexical	\N	\N	3830	{"text": "Several times Stapleton lurked about with his hound, but without avail.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3832	lexical	\N	\N	3831	{"text": "It was during these fruitless quests that he, or rather his ally, was seen by peasants, and that the legend of the demon dog received a new confirmation.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3833	lexical	\N	\N	3832	{"text": "He had hoped that his wife might lure Sir Charles to his ruin, but here she proved unexpectedly independent.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3834	lexical	\N	\N	3833	{"text": "She would not endeavour to entangle the old gentleman in a sentimental attachment which might deliver him over to his enemy.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3835	lexical	\N	\N	3834	{"text": "Threats and even, I am sorry to say, blows refused to move her.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3836	lexical	\N	\N	3835	{"text": "She would have nothing to do with it, and for a time Stapleton was at a deadlock.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3837	lexical	\N	\N	3836	{"text": "“He found a way out of his difficulties through the chance that Sir Charles, who had conceived a friendship for him, made him the minister of his charity in the case of this unfortunate woman, Mrs. Laura Lyons.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3838	lexical	\N	\N	3837	{"text": "By representing himself as a single man he acquired complete influence over her, and he gave her to understand that in the event of her obtaining a divorce from her husband he would marry her.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3869	lexical	\N	\N	3868	{"text": "It reached the baronet, and gave him the first warning of his danger.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3839	lexical	\N	\N	3838	{"text": "His plans were suddenly brought to a head by his knowledge that Sir Charles was about to leave the Hall on the advice of Dr. Mortimer, with whose opinion he himself pretended to coincide.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3840	lexical	\N	\N	3839	{"text": "He must act at once, or his victim might get beyond his power.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3841	lexical	\N	\N	3840	{"text": "He therefore put pressure upon Mrs. Lyons to write this letter, imploring the old man to give her an interview on the evening before his departure for London.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3842	lexical	\N	\N	3841	{"text": "He then, by a specious argument, prevented her from going, and so had the chance for which he had waited.", "section": "section_96", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3843	lexical	\N	\N	3842	{"text": "“Driving back in the evening from Coombe Tracey he was in time to get his hound, to treat it with his infernal paint, and to bring the beast round to the gate at which he had reason to expect that he would find the old gentleman waiting.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3844	lexical	\N	\N	3843	{"text": "The dog, incited by its master, sprang over the wicket-gate and pursued the unfortunate baronet, who fled screaming down the yew alley.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3845	lexical	\N	\N	3844	{"text": "In that gloomy tunnel it must indeed have been a dreadful sight to see that huge black creature, with its flaming jaws and blazing eyes, bounding after its victim.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3846	lexical	\N	\N	3845	{"text": "He fell dead at the end of the alley from heart disease and terror.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3847	lexical	\N	\N	3846	{"text": "The hound had kept upon the grassy border while the baronet had run down the path, so that no track but the man’s was visible.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3848	lexical	\N	\N	3847	{"text": "On seeing him lying still the creature had probably approached to sniff at him, but finding him dead had turned away again.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3849	lexical	\N	\N	3848	{"text": "It was then that it left the print which was actually observed by Dr. Mortimer.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3850	lexical	\N	\N	3849	{"text": "The hound was called off and hurried away to its lair in the Grimpen Mire, and a mystery was left which puzzled the authorities, alarmed the countryside, and finally brought the case within the scope of our observation.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3851	lexical	\N	\N	3850	{"text": "“So much for the death of Sir Charles Baskerville.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3852	lexical	\N	\N	3851	{"text": "You perceive the devilish cunning of it, for really it would be almost impossible to make a case against the real murderer.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3853	lexical	\N	\N	3852	{"text": "His only accomplice was one who could never give him away, and the grotesque, inconceivable nature of the device only served to make it more effective.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3854	lexical	\N	\N	3853	{"text": "Both of the women concerned in the case, Mrs. Stapleton and Mrs. Laura Lyons, were left with a strong suspicion against Stapleton.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3855	lexical	\N	\N	3854	{"text": "Mrs. Stapleton knew that he had designs upon the old man, and also of the existence of the hound.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3856	lexical	\N	\N	3855	{"text": "Mrs. Lyons knew neither of these things, but had been impressed by the death occurring at the time of an uncancelled appointment which was only known to him.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3857	lexical	\N	\N	3856	{"text": "However, both of them were under his influence, and he had nothing to fear from them.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3858	lexical	\N	\N	3857	{"text": "The first half of his task was successfully accomplished but the more difficult still remained.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3859	lexical	\N	\N	3858	{"text": "“It is possible that Stapleton did not know of the existence of an heir in Canada.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3860	lexical	\N	\N	3859	{"text": "In any case he would very soon learn it from his friend Dr. Mortimer, and he was told by the latter all details about the arrival of Henry Baskerville.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3861	lexical	\N	\N	3860	{"text": "Stapleton’s first idea was that this young stranger from Canada might possibly be done to death in London without coming down to Devonshire at all.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3862	lexical	\N	\N	3861	{"text": "He distrusted his wife ever since she had refused to help him in laying a trap for the old man, and he dared not leave her long out of his sight for fear he should lose his influence over her.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3863	lexical	\N	\N	3862	{"text": "It was for this reason that he took her to London with him.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3864	lexical	\N	\N	3863	{"text": "They lodged, I find, at the Mexborough Private Hotel, in Craven Street, which was actually one of those called upon by my agent in search of evidence.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3865	lexical	\N	\N	3864	{"text": "Here he kept his wife imprisoned in her room while he, disguised in a beard, followed Dr. Mortimer to Baker Street and afterwards to the station and to the Northumberland Hotel.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3866	lexical	\N	\N	3865	{"text": "His wife had some inkling of his plans; but she had such a fear of her husband—a fear founded upon brutal ill-treatment—that she dare not write to warn the man whom she knew to be in danger.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3867	lexical	\N	\N	3866	{"text": "If the letter should fall into Stapleton’s hands her own life would not be safe.", "section": "section_97", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3870	lexical	\N	\N	3869	{"text": "“It was very essential for Stapleton to get some article of Sir Henry’s attire so that, in case he was driven to use the dog, he might always have the means of setting him upon his track.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3871	lexical	\N	\N	3870	{"text": "With characteristic promptness and audacity he set about this at once, and we cannot doubt that the boots or chamber-maid of the hotel was well bribed to help him in his design.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3872	lexical	\N	\N	3871	{"text": "By chance, however, the first boot which was procured for him was a new one and, therefore, useless for his purpose.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3873	lexical	\N	\N	3872	{"text": "He then had it returned and obtained another—a most instructive incident, since it proved conclusively to my mind that we were dealing with a real hound, as no other supposition could explain this anxiety to obtain an old boot and this indifference to a new one.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3874	lexical	\N	\N	3873	{"text": "The more _outré_ and grotesque an incident is the more carefully it deserves to be examined, and the very point which appears to complicate a case is, when duly considered and scientifically handled, the one which is most likely to elucidate it.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3875	lexical	\N	\N	3874	{"text": "“Then we had the visit from our friends next morning, shadowed always by Stapleton in the cab.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3876	lexical	\N	\N	3875	{"text": "From his knowledge of our rooms and of my appearance, as well as from his general conduct, I am inclined to think that Stapleton’s career of crime has been by no means limited to this single Baskerville affair.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3877	lexical	\N	\N	3876	{"text": "It is suggestive that during the last three years there have been four considerable burglaries in the west country, for none of which was any criminal ever arrested.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3878	lexical	\N	\N	3877	{"text": "The last of these, at Folkestone Court, in May, was remarkable for the cold-blooded pistolling of the page, who surprised the masked and solitary burglar.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3879	lexical	\N	\N	3878	{"text": "I cannot doubt that Stapleton recruited his waning resources in this fashion, and that for years he has been a desperate and dangerous man.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3880	lexical	\N	\N	3879	{"text": "“We had an example of his readiness of resource that morning when he got away from us so successfully, and also of his audacity in sending back my own name to me through the cabman.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3881	lexical	\N	\N	3880	{"text": "From that moment he understood that I had taken over the case in London, and that therefore there was no chance for him there.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3882	lexical	\N	\N	3881	{"text": "He returned to Dartmoor and awaited the arrival of the baronet.”", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3883	lexical	\N	\N	3882	{"text": "“One moment!”", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3884	lexical	\N	\N	3883	{"text": "said I.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3885	lexical	\N	\N	3884	{"text": "“You have, no doubt, described the sequence of events correctly, but there is one point which you have left unexplained.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3886	lexical	\N	\N	3885	{"text": "What became of the hound when its master was in London?”", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3887	lexical	\N	\N	3886	{"text": "“I have given some attention to this matter and it is undoubtedly of importance.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3888	lexical	\N	\N	3887	{"text": "There can be no question that Stapleton had a confidant, though it is unlikely that he ever placed himself in his power by sharing all his plans with him.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3889	lexical	\N	\N	3888	{"text": "There was an old manservant at Merripit House, whose name was Anthony.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3890	lexical	\N	\N	3889	{"text": "His connection with the Stapletons can be traced for several years, as far back as the school-mastering days, so that he must have been aware that his master and mistress were really husband and wife.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3891	lexical	\N	\N	3890	{"text": "This man has disappeared and has escaped from the country.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3892	lexical	\N	\N	3891	{"text": "It is suggestive that Anthony is not a common name in England, while Antonio is so in all Spanish or Spanish-American countries.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3893	lexical	\N	\N	3892	{"text": "The man, like Mrs. Stapleton herself, spoke good English, but with a curious lisping accent.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3894	lexical	\N	\N	3893	{"text": "I have myself seen this old man cross the Grimpen Mire by the path which Stapleton had marked out.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3895	lexical	\N	\N	3894	{"text": "It is very probable, therefore, that in the absence of his master it was he who cared for the hound, though he may never have known the purpose for which the beast was used.", "section": "section_98", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3896	lexical	\N	\N	3895	{"text": "“The Stapletons then went down to Devonshire, whither they were soon followed by Sir Henry and you.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3897	lexical	\N	\N	3896	{"text": "One word now as to how I stood myself at that time.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3898	lexical	\N	\N	3897	{"text": "It may possibly recur to your memory that when I examined the paper upon which the printed words were fastened I made a close inspection for the water-mark.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3899	lexical	\N	\N	3898	{"text": "In doing so I held it within a few inches of my eyes, and was conscious of a faint smell of the scent known as white jessamine.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3900	lexical	\N	\N	3899	{"text": "There are seventy-five perfumes, which it is very necessary that a criminal expert should be able to distinguish from each other, and cases have more than once within my own experience depended upon their prompt recognition.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3901	lexical	\N	\N	3900	{"text": "The scent suggested the presence of a lady, and already my thoughts began to turn towards the Stapletons.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3902	lexical	\N	\N	3901	{"text": "Thus I had made certain of the hound, and had guessed at the criminal before ever we went to the west country.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3903	lexical	\N	\N	3902	{"text": "“It was my game to watch Stapleton.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3904	lexical	\N	\N	3903	{"text": "It was evident, however, that I could not do this if I were with you, since he would be keenly on his guard.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3905	lexical	\N	\N	3904	{"text": "I deceived everybody, therefore, yourself included, and I came down secretly when I was supposed to be in London.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3906	lexical	\N	\N	3905	{"text": "My hardships were not so great as you imagined, though such trifling details must never interfere with the investigation of a case.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3907	lexical	\N	\N	3906	{"text": "I stayed for the most part at Coombe Tracey, and only used the hut upon the moor when it was necessary to be near the scene of action.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3908	lexical	\N	\N	3907	{"text": "Cartwright had come down with me, and in his disguise as a country boy he was of great assistance to me.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3909	lexical	\N	\N	3908	{"text": "I was dependent upon him for food and clean linen.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3910	lexical	\N	\N	3909	{"text": "When I was watching Stapleton, Cartwright was frequently watching you, so that I was able to keep my hand upon all the strings.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3911	lexical	\N	\N	3910	{"text": "“I have already told you that your reports reached me rapidly, being forwarded instantly from Baker Street to Coombe Tracey.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3912	lexical	\N	\N	3911	{"text": "They were of great service to me, and especially that one incidentally truthful piece of biography of Stapleton’s.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3913	lexical	\N	\N	3912	{"text": "I was able to establish the identity of the man and the woman and knew at last exactly how I stood.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3914	lexical	\N	\N	3913	{"text": "The case had been considerably complicated through the incident of the escaped convict and the relations between him and the Barrymores.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3915	lexical	\N	\N	3914	{"text": "This also you cleared up in a very effective way, though I had already come to the same conclusions from my own observations.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3916	lexical	\N	\N	3915	{"text": "“By the time that you discovered me upon the moor I had a complete knowledge of the whole business, but I had not a case which could go to a jury.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3917	lexical	\N	\N	3916	{"text": "Even Stapleton’s attempt upon Sir Henry that night which ended in the death of the unfortunate convict did not help us much in proving murder against our man.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3918	lexical	\N	\N	3917	{"text": "There seemed to be no alternative but to catch him red-handed, and to do so we had to use Sir Henry, alone and apparently unprotected, as a bait.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3919	lexical	\N	\N	3918	{"text": "We did so, and at the cost of a severe shock to our client we succeeded in completing our case and driving Stapleton to his destruction.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3920	lexical	\N	\N	3919	{"text": "That Sir Henry should have been exposed to this is, I must confess, a reproach to my management of the case, but we had no means of foreseeing the terrible and paralyzing spectacle which the beast presented, nor could we predict the fog which enabled him to burst upon us at such short notice.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3921	lexical	\N	\N	3920	{"text": "We succeeded in our object at a cost which both the specialist and Dr. Mortimer assure me will be a temporary one.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3922	lexical	\N	\N	3921	{"text": "A long journey may enable our friend to recover not only from his shattered nerves but also from his wounded feelings.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3923	lexical	\N	\N	3922	{"text": "His love for the lady was deep and sincere, and to him the saddest part of all this black business was that he should have been deceived by her.", "section": "section_99", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3924	lexical	\N	\N	3923	{"text": "“It only remains to indicate the part which she had played throughout.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3925	lexical	\N	\N	3924	{"text": "There can be no doubt that Stapleton exercised an influence over her which may have been love or may have been fear, or very possibly both, since they are by no means incompatible emotions.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3926	lexical	\N	\N	3925	{"text": "It was, at least, absolutely effective.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3927	lexical	\N	\N	3926	{"text": "At his command she consented to pass as his sister, though he found the limits of his power over her when he endeavoured to make her the direct accessory to murder.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3928	lexical	\N	\N	3927	{"text": "She was ready to warn Sir Henry so far as she could without implicating her husband, and again and again she tried to do so.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3929	lexical	\N	\N	3928	{"text": "Stapleton himself seems to have been capable of jealousy, and when he saw the baronet paying court to the lady, even though it was part of his own plan, still he could not help interrupting with a passionate outburst which revealed the fiery soul which his self-contained manner so cleverly concealed.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3930	lexical	\N	\N	3929	{"text": "By encouraging the intimacy he made it certain that Sir Henry would frequently come to Merripit House and that he would sooner or later get the opportunity which he desired.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3931	lexical	\N	\N	3930	{"text": "On the day of the crisis, however, his wife turned suddenly against him.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3932	lexical	\N	\N	3931	{"text": "She had learned something of the death of the convict, and she knew that the hound was being kept in the outhouse on the evening that Sir Henry was coming to dinner.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3933	lexical	\N	\N	3932	{"text": "She taxed her husband with his intended crime, and a furious scene followed in which he showed her for the first time that she had a rival in his love.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3934	lexical	\N	\N	3933	{"text": "Her fidelity turned in an instant to bitter hatred, and he saw that she would betray him.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3935	lexical	\N	\N	3934	{"text": "He tied her up, therefore, that she might have no chance of warning Sir Henry, and he hoped, no doubt, that when the whole countryside put down the baronet’s death to the curse of his family, as they certainly would do, he could win his wife back to accept an accomplished fact and to keep silent upon what she knew.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3936	lexical	\N	\N	3935	{"text": "In this I fancy that in any case he made a miscalculation, and that, if we had not been there, his doom would none the less have been sealed.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3937	lexical	\N	\N	3936	{"text": "A woman of Spanish blood does not condone such an injury so lightly.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3938	lexical	\N	\N	3937	{"text": "And now, my dear Watson, without referring to my notes, I cannot give you a more detailed account of this curious case.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3939	lexical	\N	\N	3938	{"text": "I do not know that anything essential has been left unexplained.”", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3940	lexical	\N	\N	3939	{"text": "“He could not hope to frighten Sir Henry to death as he had done the old uncle with his bogie hound.”", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3941	lexical	\N	\N	3940	{"text": "“The beast was savage and half-starved.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3942	lexical	\N	\N	3941	{"text": "If its appearance did not frighten its victim to death, at least it would paralyze the resistance which might be offered.”", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3943	lexical	\N	\N	3942	{"text": "“No doubt.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3944	lexical	\N	\N	3943	{"text": "There only remains one difficulty.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3945	lexical	\N	\N	3944	{"text": "If Stapleton came into the succession, how could he explain the fact that he, the heir, had been living unannounced under another name so close to the property?", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3946	lexical	\N	\N	3945	{"text": "How could he claim it without causing suspicion and inquiry?”", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3947	lexical	\N	\N	3946	{"text": "“It is a formidable difficulty, and I fear that you ask too much when you expect me to solve it.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3948	lexical	\N	\N	3947	{"text": "The past and the present are within the field of my inquiry, but what a man may do in the future is a hard question to answer.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3949	lexical	\N	\N	3948	{"text": "Mrs. Stapleton has heard her husband discuss the problem on several occasions.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3950	lexical	\N	\N	3949	{"text": "There were three possible courses.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3951	lexical	\N	\N	3950	{"text": "He might claim the property from South America, establish his identity before the British authorities there and so obtain the fortune without ever coming to England at all, or he might adopt an elaborate disguise during the short time that he need be in London; or, again, he might furnish an accomplice with the proofs and papers, putting him in as heir, and retaining a claim upon some proportion of his income.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3952	lexical	\N	\N	3951	{"text": "We cannot doubt from what we know of him that he would have found some way out of the difficulty.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3953	lexical	\N	\N	3952	{"text": "And now, my dear Watson, we have had some weeks of severe work, and for one evening, I think, we may turn our thoughts into more pleasant channels.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3954	lexical	\N	\N	3953	{"text": "I have a box for _Les Huguenots_.", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3955	lexical	\N	\N	3954	{"text": "Have you heard the De Reszkes?", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3956	lexical	\N	\N	3955	{"text": "Might I trouble you then to be ready in half an hour, and we can stop at Marcini’s for a little dinner on the way?”", "section": "section_100", "entities": []}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	sentence_3957	lexical	\N	\N	3956	{"text": "THE END", "section": "section_101", "entities": []}
