hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_48_1	event	\N	Watson discusses the test telegram and Barrymore's receipt of it	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1838", "sentence_1839"], "communicatesContent": "the test telegram was sent from London in order to make sure that Barrymore was really here; the testimony of the postmaster showed that the test was worthless and there was no proof one way or the other."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_48_2	event	\N	Sir Henry questions Barrymore about the telegram	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1840", "sentence_1841", "sentence_1842", "sentence_1843", "sentence_1844", "sentence_1845", "sentence_1846", "sentence_1847"], "communicatesContent": "Did the boy deliver it into your own hands?"}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_48_3	event	\N	Barrymore says his wife brought him the telegram and answered it for him	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "barrymore", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1841", "sentence_1845", "sentence_1847"], "communicatesContent": "I had the telegram; I was in the box-room at the time, and my wife brought it up to me. I told my wife what to answer and she went down to write it."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_48_4	event	\N	Barrymore raises concern about losing Sir Henry's confidence	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "barrymore", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1848", "sentence_1849", "sentence_1850"], "communicatesContent": "I could not quite understand the object of your questions this morning, Sir Henry; I trust that they do not mean that I have done anything to forfeit your confidence?"}
