hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_6	event	\N	Watson tells Sir Henry about what he saw	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1905"], "communicatesContent": "all that I had seen"}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_7	event	\N	Sir Henry says he knew Barrymore walked about at night and had intended to speak to him	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1906", "sentence_1907"], "communicatesContent": "I knew that Barrymore walked about nights, and I had a mind to speak to him about it."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_8	event	\N	Sir Henry says he has heard Barrymore's steps in the passage	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1908"], "communicatesContent": "Two or three times I have heard his steps in the passage, coming and going, just about the hour you name."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_9	event	\N	Watson suggests Barrymore may visit the particular window every night	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1909"], "communicatesContent": "Perhaps then he pays a visit every night to that particular window."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_10	event	\N	Sir Henry proposes shadowing Barrymore	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1910", "sentence_1911", "sentence_1912"], "communicatesContent": "If so, we should be able to shadow him and see what it is that he is after. I wonder what your friend Holmes would do if he were here."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_11	event	\N	Watson says Holmes would follow Barrymore	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1913", "sentence_1914"], "communicatesContent": "I believe that he would do exactly what you now suggest. He would follow Barrymore and see what he did."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_12	event	\N	Sir Henry agrees to do it together	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1915"], "communicatesContent": "Then we shall do it together."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_13	event	\N	Watson says Barrymore is rather deaf and they must take their chance	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1916", "sentence_1917"], "communicatesContent": "But surely he would hear us. The man is rather deaf, and in any case we must take our chance of that."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_50_14	event	\N	Sir Henry plans to sit in his room and wait for Barrymore to pass	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1918", "sentence_1919"], "communicatesContent": "We’ll sit up in my room tonight and wait until he passes."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_51_1	event	\N	The baronet communicates with the architect and a contractor from London	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1920"], "communicatesContent": "The baronet has been in communication with the architect who prepared the plans for Sir Charles, and with a contractor from London."}
