hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_2	event	\N	Holmes and the others tear away Sir Henry's collar and examine him	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3631"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_3	event	\N	Sir Henry shows signs of returning to consciousness and tries to move	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3632"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_4	event	\N	Lestrade puts a brandy-flask between Sir Henry's teeth	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3633"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_5	event	\N	Sir Henry whispers in alarm	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3634", "sentence_3635"], "communicatesContent": "My God! What was it? What, in heaven's name, was it?"}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_6	event	\N	Holmes says the creature is dead and the family ghost has been laid	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3638", "sentence_3639"], "communicatesContent": "It's dead, whatever it is. We've laid the family ghost once and forever."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_7	event	\N	The dead hound lies stretched before the group	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3640", "sentence_3641", "sentence_3642"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_8	event	\N	Watson places his hand on the glowing muzzle and his fingers smoulder	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3643", "sentence_3644"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_9	event	\N	Holmes sniffs the dead animal and explains the preparation	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3645", "sentence_3646"], "communicatesContent": "A cunning preparation of it. There is no smell which might have interfered with his power of scent."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_10	event	\N	Holmes apologizes to Sir Henry for exposing him to the fright	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3647", "sentence_3648", "sentence_3649"], "communicatesContent": "We owe you a deep apology, Sir Henry, for having exposed you to this fright. I was prepared for a hound, but not for such a creature as this. And the fog gave us little time to receive him."}
valley-of-fear	section_32	section	\N	Section 32	31	{"wordCount": 705}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_12	event	\N	Sir Henry asks to be helped up and says he is ready for anything	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sir_henry_baskerville", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3652", "sentence_3653", "sentence_3654", "sentence_3655", "sentence_3656"], "communicatesContent": "Give me another mouthful of that brandy and I shall be ready for anything. So! Now, if you will help me up. What do you propose to do?"}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_13	event	\N	Holmes says they will leave Sir Henry there and return with him to the Hall	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3657", "sentence_3658", "sentence_3659"], "communicatesContent": "To leave you here. You are not fit for further adventures tonight. If you will wait, one or other of us will go back with you to the Hall."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_14	event	\N	Sir Henry staggers to his feet and is helped to a rock	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3660", "sentence_3661"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_15	event	\N	Holmes says they must leave Sir Henry and continue their work	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3662", "sentence_3663", "sentence_3664"], "communicatesContent": "We must leave you now. The rest of our work must be done, and every moment is of importance. We have our case, and now we only want our man."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_91_16	event	\N	The three men retrace their steps down the path and search the house	90	{"section": "section_91", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3665", "sentence_3666", "sentence_3667", "sentence_3668", "sentence_3669", "sentence_3670", "sentence_3671", "sentence_3672", "sentence_3673", "sentence_3674", "sentence_3675", "sentence_3676", "sentence_3677", "sentence_3678", "sentence_3679", "sentence_3680"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_1	event	\N	The room appears as a small museum full of butterfly and moth cases	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3682", "sentence_3683"], "communicatesContent": null}
