hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_3	event	\N	Holmes and the others tear off the gag and unswathe the bonds from Mrs. Stapleton	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3688"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_4	event	\N	Mrs. Stapleton sinks to the floor	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3688"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_5	event	\N	Holmes orders Lestrade to give brandy and place Mrs. Stapleton in a chair	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3690", "sentence_3691", "sentence_3692", "sentence_3693", "sentence_3694"], "communicatesContent": "Here, Lestrade, your brandy-bottle! Put her in the chair! She has fainted from ill-usage and exhaustion."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_6	event	\N	Mrs. Stapleton regains consciousness and asks about Sir Henry and the hound	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": "mrs_stapleton", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3695", "sentence_3696", "sentence_3697", "sentence_3698", "sentence_3699", "sentence_3700", "sentence_3701", "sentence_3702", "sentence_3703", "sentence_3704", "sentence_3705"], "communicatesContent": "Is he safe? Has he escaped? No, no, I did not mean my husband. Sir Henry? Is he safe? And the hound?"}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_7	event	\N	Mrs. Stapleton describes her mistreatment by her husband	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": "mrs_stapleton", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3707", "sentence_3708", "sentence_3709", "sentence_3710", "sentence_3711", "sentence_3712", "sentence_3713", "sentence_3714", "sentence_3715"], "communicatesContent": "Thank God! Thank God! Oh, this villain! See how he has treated me! But this is nothing—nothing! It is my mind and soul that he has tortured and defiled. I could endure it all, ill-usage, solitude, a life of deception, everything, as long as I could still cling to the hope that I had his love, but now I know that in this also I have been his dupe and his tool."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_8	event	\N	Holmes asks Mrs. Stapleton where to find the villain and urges her to help	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3716", "sentence_3717", "sentence_3718"], "communicatesContent": "You bear him no good will, madam. Tell us then where we shall find him. If you have ever aided him in evil, help us now and so atone."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_9	event	\N	Mrs. Stapleton identifies the old tin mine as his likely refuge	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": "mrs_stapleton", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3719", "sentence_3720", "sentence_3721", "sentence_3722"], "communicatesContent": "There is but one place where he can have fled. There is an old tin mine on an island in the heart of the mire. It was there that he kept his hound and there also he had made preparations so that he might have a refuge. That is where he would fly."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_10	event	\N	Holmes holds the lamp toward the fog-bank	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3723", "sentence_3724", "sentence_3725", "sentence_3726"], "communicatesContent": null}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_92_11	event	\N	Mrs. Stapleton laughs and describes the guiding wands through the mire	91	{"section": "section_92", "speakerId": "mrs_stapleton", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3727", "sentence_3728", "sentence_3729", "sentence_3730", "sentence_3731", "sentence_3732", "sentence_3733"], "communicatesContent": "He may find his way in, but never out. How can he see the guiding wands tonight? We planted them together, he and I, to mark the pathway through the mire. Oh, if I could only have plucked them out today. Then indeed you would have had him at your mercy!"}
