hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_95_13	event	\N	Holmes explains that the man married Beryl Garcia, took public money, renamed himself Vandeleur, and fled to England	94	{"section": "section_95", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3805"], "communicatesContent": "He married Beryl Garcia, one of the beauties of Costa Rica, and, having purloined a considerable sum of public money, he changed his name to Vandeleur and fled to England, where he established a school in the east of Yorkshire."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_95_14	event	\N	Holmes explains that the man used a consumptive tutor's ability to run his school	94	{"section": "section_95", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3806"], "communicatesContent": "His reason for attempting this special line of business was that he had struck up an acquaintance with a consumptive tutor upon the voyage home, and that he had used this man's ability to make the undertaking a success."}
