hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_100_8	event	\N	Mrs. Stapleton hears Stapleton discuss possible ways to claim the property	99	{"section": "section_100", "speakerId": "stapleton", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3949", "sentence_3950", "sentence_3951"], "communicatesContent": "There were three possible courses: claim the property from South America, establish his identity before the British authorities there and obtain the fortune without coming to England, adopt an elaborate disguise in London, or furnish an accomplice with the proofs and papers and retain a claim upon some proportion of the income."}
hound-of-the-baskervilles	event_100_9	event	\N	Holmes and Watson turn their thoughts to a more pleasant evening	99	{"section": "section_100", "speakerId": "mr_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3953", "sentence_3954", "sentence_3955", "sentence_3956"], "communicatesContent": "We have had some weeks of severe work, and for one evening we may turn our thoughts into more pleasant channels. I have a box for Les Huguenots. Have you heard the De Reszkes? Might I trouble you then to be ready in half an hour, and we can stop at Marcini's for a little dinner on the way?"}
