valley-of-fear	event_4_2	event	\N	Holmes identifies the writing as Porlock's writing	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_26", "sentence_27", "sentence_28", "sentence_29"], "communicatesContent": "It is Porlock’s writing."}
valley-of-fear	event_4_3	event	\N	Watson asks who Porlock is	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_31", "sentence_32"], "communicatesContent": "Who then is Porlock?"}
valley-of-fear	event_4_4	event	\N	Holmes describes Porlock and Moriarty to Watson	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_33", "sentence_34", "sentence_35", "sentence_36", "sentence_37", "sentence_38"], "communicatesContent": "Porlock is a nom-de-plume, a mere identification mark; behind it lies a shifty and evasive personality. In a former letter he informed me that the name was not his own. Porlock is important for the great man with whom he is in touch. You have heard me speak of Professor Moriarty?"}
valley-of-fear	event_14_10	event	\N	John Douglas's wife becomes popular with acquaintances	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_534"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_4_5	event	\N	Watson refers to Moriarty as a famous scientific criminal and unknown to the public	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_39", "sentence_42"], "communicatesContent": "The famous scientific criminal, as famous among crooks as... unknown to the public."}
valley-of-fear	event_4_6	event	\N	Holmes praises Watson's humor and extols Moriarty	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_40", "sentence_41", "sentence_43", "sentence_44", "sentence_45", "sentence_46", "sentence_47", "sentence_48", "sentence_49", "sentence_50", "sentence_51", "sentence_52", "sentence_53", "sentence_54"], "communicatesContent": "My blushes, Watson! A touch! A distinct touch! You are developing a certain unexpected vein of pawky humour, Watson, against which I must learn to guard myself. But in calling Moriarty a criminal you are uttering libel in the eyes of the law—and there lie the glory and the wonder of it! The greatest schemer of all time, the organizer of every deviltry, the controlling brain of the underworld, a brain which might have made or marred the destiny of nations—that’s the man! But so aloof is he from general suspicion, so immune from criticism, so admirable in his management and self-effacement, that for those very words that you have uttered he could hale you to a court and emerge with your year’s pension as a solatium for his wounded character. Is he not the celebrated author of The Dynamics of an Asteroid, a book which ascends to such rarefied heights of pure mathematics that it is said that there was no man in the scientific press capable of criticizing it? Is this a man to traduce? Foul-mouthed doctor and slandered professor—such would be your respective rôles! That’s genius, Watson. But if I am spared by lesser men, our day will surely come."}
valley-of-fear	event_4_7	event	\N	Watson expresses a wish to be present for that day	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_55", "sentence_56"], "communicatesContent": "May I be there to see!"}
valley-of-fear	event_4_8	event	\N	Holmes says Porlock is a link in the chain and the only flaw so far	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_57", "sentence_58", "sentence_59", "sentence_60"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, yes—the so-called Porlock is a link in the chain some little way from its great attachment. Porlock is not quite a sound link—between ourselves. He is the only flaw in that chain so far as I have been able to test it."}
valley-of-fear	event_5_1	event	\N	Holmes explains the importance of Porlock	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_63", "sentence_64", "sentence_65"], "communicatesContent": "Hence the extreme importance of Porlock. He has once or twice given me advance information which has been of value. If we had the cipher, we should find that this communication is of the nature that I indicate."}
valley-of-fear	event_5_2	event	\N	Holmes examines the paper and Watson looks at the inscription	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_66", "sentence_67", "sentence_68"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_5_3	event	\N	Holmes identifies the inscription as secret information	4	{"section": "section_5", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_69", "sentence_70", "sentence_71", "sentence_72", "sentence_73", "sentence_74", "sentence_75", "sentence_76", "sentence_77", "sentence_78", "sentence_79", "sentence_80", "sentence_81", "sentence_82", "sentence_83", "sentence_84"], "communicatesContent": "It is obviously an attempt to convey secret information. In this instance, the cipher has no use at all. The message is a reference to the words in a page of some book, and I am powerless until I am told which page and which book. Douglas and Birlstone are words not contained in the page in question. One should not include cipher and message in the same envelope because if it miscarried one would be undone. Our second post is overdue, and I shall be surprised if it does not bring us either a further letter of explanation or the volume to which these figures refer."}
