valley-of-fear	event_14_14	event	\N	John Douglas's wife shows uneasiness when her husband is late returning	13	{"section": "section_14", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_539"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_10_6	event	\N	Holmes compares Moriarty to Jonathan Wild	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_402", "sentence_407", "sentence_408"], "communicatesContent": "Have you ever read of Jonathan Wild? Jonathan Wild wasn’t a detective, and he wasn’t in a novel. He was a master criminal, and he lived last century—1750 or thereabouts."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_1	event	\N	Holmes describes Jonathan Wild as the hidden force of London's criminals	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_413", "sentence_414"], "communicatesContent": "Jonathan Wild was the hidden force of the London criminals, to whom he sold his brains and his organization on a fifteen per cent commission."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_2	event	\N	Holmes says Moriarty has a criminal chain with himself at one end and many criminals at the other	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_419"], "communicatesContent": "Moriarty is the first link in his chain, with this Napoleon-gone-wrong at one end, and a hundred broken fighting men, pickpockets, blackmailers, and card sharpers at the other, with every sort of crime in between."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_3	event	\N	Holmes identifies Colonel Sebastian Moran as Moriarty's chief of staff	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_420"], "communicatesContent": "His chief of staff is Colonel Sebastian Moran, as aloof and guarded and inaccessible to the law as himself."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_4	event	\N	Holmes states that Moran is paid six thousand a year	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_421", "sentence_423", "sentence_424"], "communicatesContent": "Six thousand a year."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_5	event	\N	Holmes reports that Moriarty's checks were drawn on six different banks	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_428", "sentence_429"], "communicatesContent": "I hunted down some of Moriarty's checks lately; they were drawn on six different banks."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_6	event	\N	Holmes says Moriarty has many banking accounts and most of his fortune abroad	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_433", "sentence_435"], "communicatesContent": "He wanted no gossip about his wealth. No single man should know what he had. I have no doubt that he has twenty banking accounts; the bulk of his fortune abroad in the Deutsche Bank or the Crédit Lyonnais as likely as not."}
valley-of-fear	event_11_7	event	\N	MacDonald grows impressed during the conversation	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_437", "sentence_438", "sentence_439"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_11_8	event	\N	MacDonald remarks that Holmes has sidetracked them and asks about the connection to the crime	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_440", "sentence_441", "sentence_442", "sentence_443", "sentence_444"], "communicatesContent": "You've got us side-tracked with your interesting anecdotes, Mr. Holmes. What really counts is your remark that there is some connection between the professor and the crime. That you get from the warning received through the man Porlock. Can we for our present practical needs get any further than that?"}
valley-of-fear	event_11_9	event	\N	Holmes proposes that Moriarty may have ordered a murder to enforce discipline or as ordinary business	10	{"section": "section_11", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_445", "sentence_446", "sentence_447", "sentence_448", "sentence_449", "sentence_450", "sentence_451", "sentence_452", "sentence_453", "sentence_454", "sentence_455", "sentence_456", "sentence_457", "sentence_458", "sentence_459", "sentence_460", "sentence_461", "sentence_462"], "communicatesContent": "We may form some conception as to the motives of the crime. There might be two different motives. Moriarty rules with a rod of iron over his people. His discipline is tremendous. There is only one punishment in his code. It is death. The murdered man Douglas may have betrayed the chief, and his punishment followed to put the fear of death into them. The other is that it has been engineered by Moriarty in the ordinary course of business. If there was robbery, it would be against the first hypothesis and in favour of the second. Moriarty may have been engaged to engineer it on a promise of part spoils, or he may have been paid so much down to manage it. Whichever it may be, it is down at Birlstone that we must seek the solution. I know our man too well to suppose that he has left anything up here which may lead us to him."}
valley-of-fear	event_12_1	event	\N	MacDonald urges the group to go to Birlstone	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_463", "sentence_464"], "communicatesContent": "Then to Birlstone we must go!"}
valley-of-fear	event_12_2	event	\N	MacDonald says he has five minutes for preparation	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_465", "sentence_466", "sentence_467"], "communicatesContent": "it’s later than I thought. I can give you, gentlemen, five minutes for preparation, and that is all."}
valley-of-fear	event_12_3	event	\N	Holmes rises and changes from his dressing gown to his coat	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_468"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_12_4	event	\N	Holmes asks MacDonald to tell him all about it while they travel	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_469"], "communicatesContent": "While we are on our way, Mr. Mac, I will ask you to be good enough to tell me all about it."}
valley-of-fear	event_12_5	event	\N	MacDonald explains that the case details are meagre but remarkable	11	{"section": "section_12", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_470", "sentence_471", "sentence_472", "sentence_473", "sentence_474", "sentence_475"], "communicatesContent": "All about it proved to be disappointingly little, and yet there was enough to assure us that the case before us might well be worthy of the expert’s closest attention."}
