valley-of-fear	event_16_2	event	\N	The sergeant says nothing will be touched until his superiors arrive	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sergeant_wilson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_576"], "communicatesContent": "We will touch nothing until my superiors arrive."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_3	event	\N	Cecil Barker says nothing has been touched	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "cecil_james_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_577", "sentence_578", "sentence_579"], "communicatesContent": "Nothing has been touched up to now. I’ll answer for that. You see it all exactly as I found it."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_4	event	\N	Barker answers questions about the time of the shot	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "cecil_james_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_580", "sentence_581", "sentence_582", "sentence_583", "sentence_584", "sentence_585"], "communicatesContent": "It was just half-past eleven. I had not begun to undress, and I was sitting by the fire in my bedroom when I heard the report. It was not very loud—it seemed to be muffled. I rushed down—I don’t suppose it was thirty seconds before I was in the room."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_5	event	\N	Barker answers that the door was open	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "cecil_james_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_586", "sentence_587"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, it was open."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_6	event	\N	Barker describes Douglas lying in the room and the candle burning	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "cecil_james_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_588", "sentence_589", "sentence_590"], "communicatesContent": "Poor Douglas was lying as you see him. His bedroom candle was burning on the table. It was I who lit the lamp some minutes afterward."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_7	event	\N	Barker says he saw no one and intercepted Mrs. Douglas	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "cecil_james_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_591", "sentence_592", "sentence_593", "sentence_594", "sentence_595"], "communicatesContent": "No. I heard Mrs. Douglas coming down the stair behind me, and I rushed out to prevent her from seeing this dreadful sight. Mrs. Allen, the housekeeper, came and took her away. Ames had arrived, and we ran back into the room once more."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_8	event	\N	The sergeant asks about the drawbridge and Barker lowers it	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sergeant_wilson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_596", "sentence_597"], "communicatesContent": "I have heard that the drawbridge is kept up all night."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_9	event	\N	The sergeant suggests Douglas shot himself	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sergeant_wilson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_598", "sentence_599", "sentence_600"], "communicatesContent": "Then how could any murderer have got away? It is out of the question! Mr. Douglas must have shot himself."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_10	event	\N	Barker shows the open window and blood mark	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_601", "sentence_602", "sentence_603", "sentence_604", "sentence_605", "sentence_606"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_16_11	event	\N	The sergeant and Barker discuss the moat escape	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sergeant_wilson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_607", "sentence_608", "sentence_609", "sentence_610", "sentence_611", "sentence_612", "sentence_613", "sentence_614"], "communicatesContent": "You mean that someone waded across the moat? Then if you were in the room within half a minute of the crime, he must have been in the water at that very moment."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_12	event	\N	The doctor comments on the injuries	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "dr_wood", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_615", "sentence_616", "sentence_617"], "communicatesContent": "Horrible enough! I’ve never seen such injuries since the Birlstone railway smash."}
valley-of-fear	event_16_13	event	\N	The sergeant questions how an outside person entered while the bridge was up	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sergeant_wilson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_618", "sentence_619", "sentence_620"], "communicatesContent": "It’s all very well your saying that a man escaped by wading this moat, but what I ask you is, how did he ever get into the house at all if the bridge was up?"}
valley-of-fear	event_16_14	event	\N	Ames answers when the bridge was raised	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "ames", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_621", "sentence_622", "sentence_623", "sentence_624", "sentence_625", "sentence_626", "sentence_627"], "communicatesContent": "It was nearly six o’clock. I’ve heard that it was usually raised at sunset. That would be nearer half-past four than six at this time of year. Mrs. Douglas had visitors to tea. I couldn’t raise it until they went. Then I wound it up myself."}
valley-of-fear	event_17_23	event	\N	The doctor scrutinizes the body and notices a mark on the dead man's arm	16	{"section": "section_17", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_680", "sentence_681", "sentence_682", "sentence_683", "sentence_684", "sentence_685"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_16_15	event	\N	The sergeant states how an outside killer must have entered and waited	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sergeant_wilson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_628", "sentence_629", "sentence_630", "sentence_631", "sentence_632", "sentence_633", "sentence_634"], "communicatesContent": "If anyone came from outside—they must have got in across the bridge before six and been in hiding ever since, until Mr. Douglas came into the room after eleven. Mr. Douglas went round the house every night the last thing before he turned in to see that the lights were right. That brought him in here. The man was waiting and shot him. Then he got away through the window and left his gun behind him. That’s how I read it; for nothing else will fit the facts."}
