valley-of-fear	event_26_1	event	\N	MacDonald asks Barker how long he was with Douglas in California	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1102", "sentence_1103"], "communicatesContent": "How long were you with Douglas in California?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_2	event	\N	Barker says he was with Douglas for five years altogether	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1104"], "communicatesContent": "Five years altogether."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_3	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether Douglas was a bachelor	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1105", "sentence_1106"], "communicatesContent": "He was a bachelor, you say?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_4	event	\N	Barker states that Douglas was a widower	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1106"], "communicatesContent": "A widower."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_5	event	\N	MacDonald asks where Douglas's first wife came from	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1107"], "communicatesContent": "Have you ever heard where his first wife came from?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_6	event	\N	Barker reports Douglas's account of his first wife's German extraction and mentions her portrait and death	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1108", "sentence_1109", "sentence_1110"], "communicatesContent": "No, I remember his saying that she was of German extraction, and I have seen her portrait. She was a very beautiful woman. She died of typhoid the year before I met him."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_7	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether Douglas is associated with any part of America	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1111"], "communicatesContent": "You don’t associate his past with any particular part of America?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_8	event	\N	Barker mentions Chicago and the coal and iron districts and says Douglas travelled a good deal	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1112", "sentence_1113", "sentence_1114", "sentence_1115"], "communicatesContent": "I have heard him talk of Chicago. He knew that city well and had worked there. I have heard him talk of the coal and iron districts. He had travelled a good deal in his time."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_9	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether Douglas was a politician and whether the secret society related to politics	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1116", "sentence_1117"], "communicatesContent": "Was he a politician? Had this secret society to do with politics?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_10	event	\N	Barker denies that Douglas cared about politics	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1118"], "communicatesContent": "No, he cared nothing about politics."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_11	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether Barker has reason to think the matter was criminal	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1119"], "communicatesContent": "You have no reason to think it was criminal?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_12	event	\N	Barker describes Douglas as a straight man	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1120"], "communicatesContent": "On the contrary, I never met a straighter man in my life."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_13	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether anything curious happened in Douglas's California life	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1121"], "communicatesContent": "Was there anything curious about his life in California?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_14	event	\N	Barker says Douglas preferred to stay and work at their claim in the mountains and avoided other men	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1122", "sentence_1123"], "communicatesContent": "He liked best to stay and to work at our claim in the mountains. He would never go where other men were if he could help it."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_15	event	\N	Barker says he first thought someone was after Douglas, then became sure after Douglas left for Europe	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1124", "sentence_1125"], "communicatesContent": "That’s why I first thought that someone was after him. Then when he left so suddenly for Europe I made sure that it was so."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_16	event	\N	Barker says he believes Douglas had some warning and that men inquired after him within a week	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1126", "sentence_1127"], "communicatesContent": "I believe that he had a warning of some sort. Within a week of his leaving half a dozen men were inquiring for him."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_17	event	\N	MacDonald asks what sort of men they were	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1128"], "communicatesContent": "What sort of men?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_18	event	\N	Barker describes the men who inquired for Douglas	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1129", "sentence_1130", "sentence_1131", "sentence_1132"], "communicatesContent": "Well, they were a mighty hard-looking crowd. They came up to the claim and wanted to know where he was. I told them that he was gone to Europe and that I did not know where to find him. They meant him no good—it was easy to see that."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_19	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether the men were Americans or Californians	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1133"], "communicatesContent": "Were these men Americans—Californians?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_20	event	\N	Barker says the men were Americans but not miners	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1134", "sentence_1135", "sentence_1136", "sentence_1137"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I don’t know about Californians. They were Americans, all right. But they were not miners. I don’t know what they were, and was very glad to see their backs."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_21	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether the events date back six years	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1138"], "communicatesContent": "That was six years ago?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_22	event	\N	Barker says it was nearer seven years	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1139"], "communicatesContent": "Nearer seven."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_23	event	\N	MacDonald restates the timeline as at least eleven years	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1140", "sentence_1141"], "communicatesContent": "And then you were together five years in California, so that this business dates back not less than eleven years at the least?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_24	event	\N	MacDonald says the feud must be very serious and long-lasting	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1142", "sentence_1143"], "communicatesContent": "It must be a very serious feud that would be kept up with such earnestness for as long as that. It would be no light thing that would give rise to it."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_25	event	\N	Barker says the matter shadowed Douglas's whole life and was never out of his mind	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1144", "sentence_1145"], "communicatesContent": "I think it shadowed his whole life. It was never quite out of his mind."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_26	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether Douglas would have turned to the police for protection	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1146"], "communicatesContent": "But if a man had a danger hanging over him, and knew what it was, don’t you think he would turn to the police for protection?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_27	event	\N	Barker says the danger may have been unprotectable	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1147"], "communicatesContent": "Maybe it was some danger that he could not be protected against."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_28	event	\N	Barker says Douglas always went about armed and left his revolver in the bedroom last night	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1148", "sentence_1149", "sentence_1150", "sentence_1151", "sentence_1152"], "communicatesContent": "There’s one thing you should know. He always went about armed. His revolver was never out of his pocket. But, by bad luck, he was in his dressing gown and had left it in the bedroom last night. Once the bridge was up, I guess he thought he was safe."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_29	event	\N	MacDonald asks for clearer dates	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1153"], "communicatesContent": "I should like these dates a little clearer,"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_30	event	\N	MacDonald states that Douglas left California six years ago and Barker followed him the next year	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1154", "sentence_1155", "sentence_1156"], "communicatesContent": "It is quite six years since Douglas left California. You followed him next year, did you not?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_31	event	\N	MacDonald states Douglas had been married five years and Barker returned about the time of the marriage	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1157", "sentence_1158"], "communicatesContent": "And he had been married five years. You must have returned about the time of his marriage."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_32	event	\N	Barker says he returned about a month before Douglas's marriage and was his best man	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1159", "sentence_1160"], "communicatesContent": "About a month before. I was his best man."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_33	event	\N	MacDonald asks whether Barker knew Mrs. Douglas before her marriage	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1161"], "communicatesContent": "Did you know Mrs. Douglas before her marriage?"}
valley-of-fear	event_26_34	event	\N	Barker says he did not know Mrs. Douglas before her marriage and had been away from England for ten years	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1162", "sentence_1163"], "communicatesContent": "No, I did not. I had been away from England for ten years."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_35	event	\N	MacDonald says Barker has seen a good deal of Mrs. Douglas since	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1164"], "communicatesContent": "But you have seen a good deal of her since."}
valley-of-fear	event_26_36	event	\N	Barker objects that he has seen Douglas since and that any visits to Douglas also involved seeing his wife	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "gary_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1165", "sentence_1166", "sentence_1167", "sentence_1168"], "communicatesContent": "I have seen a good deal of him since. If I have seen her, it is because you cannot visit a man without knowing his wife. If you imagine there is any connection—"}
valley-of-fear	event_27_1	event	\N	Barker refuses to answer whether Mr. Douglas approved his friendship with Mrs. Douglas	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1175", "sentence_1176", "sentence_1177", "sentence_1178", "sentence_1179", "sentence_1180", "sentence_1181", "sentence_1182", "sentence_1183", "sentence_1184"], "communicatesContent": "You have no right to ask such questions! What has this to do with the matter you are investigating? Well, I refuse to answer."}
valley-of-fear	event_27_2	event	\N	Barker explains Douglas's jealousy and his own friendship with the Douglas household	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1185", "sentence_1186", "sentence_1187", "sentence_1188", "sentence_1189", "sentence_1190", "sentence_1191", "sentence_1192", "sentence_1193"], "communicatesContent": "Poor Douglas had just one fault in the world, and that was his jealousy. He was fond of me. He was devoted to his wife. He loved me to come here, and was forever sending for me. If his wife and I talked together or there seemed any sympathy between us, a kind of wave of jealousy would pass over him. More than once I’ve sworn off coming for that reason, and then he would write me such penitent, imploring letters that I just had to. No man ever had a more loving, faithful wife, and no friend could be more loyal than I."}
valley-of-fear	event_27_3	event	\N	MacDonald questions Barker about the dead man's wedding ring	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1194", "sentence_1195", "sentence_1196", "sentence_1197", "sentence_1198", "sentence_1199", "sentence_1200", "sentence_1201", "sentence_1202", "sentence_1203", "sentence_1204", "sentence_1205"], "communicatesContent": "You are aware that the dead man’s wedding ring has been taken from his finger?"}
valley-of-fear	event_27_4	event	\N	Holmes asks Barker about the candle, the lamp, and the arrival of help	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1206", "sentence_1207", "sentence_1208", "sentence_1209", "sentence_1210", "sentence_1211", "sentence_1212", "sentence_1213", "sentence_1214", "sentence_1215", "sentence_1216"], "communicatesContent": "When you entered the room there was only a candle lighted on the table, was there not? By its light you saw that some terrible incident had occurred? You at once rang for help? And it arrived very speedily? And yet when they arrived they found that the candle was out and that the lamp had been lighted."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_1	event	\N	Barker explains why he lit the lamp and blew out the candle	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1217", "sentence_1218", "sentence_1219", "sentence_1220", "sentence_1221", "sentence_1222", "sentence_1223"], "communicatesContent": "I don’t see that it was remarkable, Mr. Holmes. The candle threw a very bad light. My first thought was to get a better one. The lamp was on the table; so I lit it. Exactly."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_2	event	\N	Barker leaves the room	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1224"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_28_3	event	\N	Inspector MacDonald sends a note to Mrs. Douglas	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1225"], "communicatesContent": "he would wait upon Mrs. Douglas in her room"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_4	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas replies that she will meet them in the dining room	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1225"], "communicatesContent": "she would meet us in the dining room"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_5	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas enters the dining room	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1226", "sentence_1227", "sentence_1228"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_28_6	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas asks whether anything has been found out	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1229", "sentence_1230", "sentence_1231"], "communicatesContent": "Have you found anything out yet?"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_7	event	\N	The inspector states that every possible step has been taken and nothing will be neglected	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1233", "sentence_1234"], "communicatesContent": "We have taken every possible step, Mrs. Douglas. You may rest assured that nothing will be neglected."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_8	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas asks that no expense be spared and every effort be made	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1235", "sentence_1236"], "communicatesContent": "Spare no money. It is my desire that every possible effort should be made."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_9	event	\N	The inspector asks Mrs. Douglas for information about the matter	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1237"], "communicatesContent": "Perhaps you can tell us something which may throw some light upon the matter."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_10	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas says she knows nothing else but offers all she knows	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1238"], "communicatesContent": "I fear not; but all I know is at your service."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_11	event	\N	The inspector questions Mrs. Douglas about whether she saw the room of the tragedy	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1239"], "communicatesContent": "We have heard from Mr. Cecil Barker that you did not actually see—that you were never in the room where the tragedy occurred?"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_12	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas says Barker turned her back on the stairs and begged her to return to her room	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1240", "sentence_1241"], "communicatesContent": "No, he turned me back upon the stairs. He begged me to return to my room."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_13	event	\N	The inspector confirms that Mrs. Douglas heard the shot and came down at once	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1242", "sentence_1243"], "communicatesContent": "Quite so. You had heard the shot, and you had at once come down."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_14	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas says she put on her dressing gown and came down	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1244"], "communicatesContent": "I put on my dressing gown and then came down."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_15	event	\N	The inspector asks how long after the shot Barker stopped Mrs. Douglas on the stair	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1245"], "communicatesContent": "How long was it after hearing the shot that you were stopped on the stair by Mr. Barker?"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_16	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas says Barker stopped her after a couple of minutes and urged her not to go on	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1246", "sentence_1247", "sentence_1248", "sentence_1249", "sentence_1250", "sentence_1251"], "communicatesContent": "It may have been a couple of minutes. It is so hard to reckon time at such a moment. He implored me not to go on. He assured me that I could do nothing. Then Mrs. Allen, the housekeeper, led me upstairs again. It was all like some dreadful dream."}
valley-of-fear	event_28_17	event	\N	The inspector asks how long Mr. Douglas had been downstairs before the shot	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1252"], "communicatesContent": "Can you give us any idea how long your husband had been downstairs before you heard the shot?"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_18	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas says she cannot say when her husband went downstairs and that he made his nightly round of the house	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1253", "sentence_1254", "sentence_1255", "sentence_1256"], "communicatesContent": "No, I cannot say. He went from his dressing room, and I did not hear him go. He did the round of the house every night, for he was nervous of fire. It is the only thing that I have ever known him nervous of."}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_171	lexical	\N	\N	170	{"text": "And then I think that what he foresaw happened.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	event_28_19	event	\N	The inspector asks about danger from America	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1257", "sentence_1258", "sentence_1260"], "communicatesContent": "That is just the point which I want to come to, Mrs. Douglas. You have known your husband only in England, have you not? Have you heard him speak of anything which occurred in America and might bring some danger upon him?"}
valley-of-fear	event_28_20	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas says she and her husband had been married five years and that he kept the danger from her	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1259", "sentence_1261", "sentence_1262", "sentence_1263", "sentence_1264", "sentence_1265"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, we have been married five years. Yes, I have always felt that there was a danger hanging over him. He refused to discuss it with me. It was not from want of confidence in me—there was the most complete love and confidence between us—but it was out of his desire to keep all alarm away from me. He thought I should brood over it if I knew all, and so he was silent."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_1	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas explains how she learned of her husband's secret past	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1266", "sentence_1267", "sentence_1268", "sentence_1269", "sentence_1270", "sentence_1271", "sentence_1272", "sentence_1273", "sentence_1274"], "communicatesContent": "Can a husband ever carry about a secret all his life and a woman who loves him have no suspicion of it? I knew it by his refusal to talk about some episodes in his American life. I knew it by certain precautions he took. I knew it by certain words he let fall. I knew it by the way he looked at unexpected strangers. I was perfectly certain that he had some powerful enemies, that he believed they were on his track, and that he was always on his guard against them. I was so sure of it that for years I have been terrified if ever he came home later than was expected."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_2	event	\N	Holmes asks Mrs. Douglas about the words that attracted her attention	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1275"], "communicatesContent": "what the words were which attracted your attention"}
valley-of-fear	event_29_3	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas identifies and quotes the phrase 'The Valley of Fear'	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1276", "sentence_1277", "sentence_1278", "sentence_1279", "sentence_1280", "sentence_1281", "sentence_1282"], "communicatesContent": "The Valley of Fear. That was an expression he has used when I questioned him. 'I have been in the Valley of Fear.' 'Are we never to get out of the Valley of Fear?' I have asked him when I have seen him more serious than usual. 'Sometimes I think that we never shall,' he has answered."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_4	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Mrs. Douglas questioned her husband about the Valley of Fear	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1283"], "communicatesContent": "Surely you asked him what he meant by the Valley of Fear?"}
valley-of-fear	event_29_5	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas describes her husband's grave reaction and quoted words about the Valley of Fear	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1284", "sentence_1285", "sentence_1286", "sentence_1287"], "communicatesContent": "I did; but his face would become very grave and he would shake his head. 'It is bad enough that one of us should have been in its shadow,' he said. 'Please God it shall never fall upon you!' It was some real valley in which he had lived and in which something terrible had occurred to him, of that I am certain; but I can tell you no more."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_6	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas reports that Mr. Douglas once spoke the name Bodymaster McGinty while delirious	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1288", "sentence_1289", "sentence_1290", "sentence_1291", "sentence_1292", "sentence_1293", "sentence_1294", "sentence_1295", "sentence_1296"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, he was delirious with fever once when he had his hunting accident three years ago. Then I remember that there was a name that came continually to his lips. He spoke it with anger and a sort of horror. McGinty was the name—Bodymaster McGinty. I asked him when he recovered who Bodymaster McGinty was, and whose body he was master of. 'Never of mine, thank God!' he answered with a laugh, and that was all I could get from him. But there is a connection between Bodymaster McGinty and the Valley of Fear."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_7	event	\N	Inspector MacDonald asks about Mrs. Douglas's engagement and wedding	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1297", "sentence_1298", "sentence_1299"], "communicatesContent": "You met Mr. Douglas in a boarding house in London, did you not, and became engaged to him there? Was there any romance, anything secret or mysterious, about the wedding?"}
valley-of-fear	event_29_8	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas answers questions about the engagement and wedding	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1300", "sentence_1301", "sentence_1302", "sentence_1303", "sentence_1304"], "communicatesContent": "There was romance. There is always romance. There was nothing mysterious. No, I was quite free."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_9	event	\N	MacDonald raises the question of the missing wedding ring and a possible enemy	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1305", "sentence_1306", "sentence_1307"], "communicatesContent": "You have heard, no doubt, that his wedding ring has been taken. Does that suggest anything to you? Suppose that some enemy of his old life had tracked him down and committed this crime, what possible reason could he have for taking his wedding ring?"}
valley-of-fear	event_29_10	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas responds to the question about the wedding ring	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1308", "sentence_1310", "sentence_1311"], "communicatesContent": "I really cannot tell. It is certainly a most extraordinary thing."}
valley-of-fear	event_29_11	event	\N	MacDonald ends the interview and dismisses Mrs. Douglas	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1312", "sentence_1313", "sentence_1314", "sentence_1315", "sentence_1316", "sentence_1317"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_30_1	event	\N	MacDonald remarks on Barker, the wedding ring, and asks Holmes what he makes of it	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1318", "sentence_1319", "sentence_1320", "sentence_1321", "sentence_1322", "sentence_1323", "sentence_1324"], "communicatesContent": "She’s a beautiful woman—a very beautiful woman. This man Barker has certainly been down here a good deal. He is a man who might be attractive to a woman. He admits that the dead man was jealous, and maybe he knew best himself what cause he had for jealousy. Then there’s that wedding ring. You can’t get past that. The man who tears a wedding ring off a dead man’s—What do you say to it, Mr. Holmes?"}
valley-of-fear	event_30_2	event	\N	Holmes rings for Ames and asks where Cecil Barker is	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1325", "sentence_1326", "sentence_1327", "sentence_1328", "sentence_1329"], "communicatesContent": "where is Mr. Cecil Barker now?"}
valley-of-fear	event_30_3	event	\N	Ames reports that Barker is in the garden	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "ames", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1328", "sentence_1329"], "communicatesContent": "Barker was in the garden."}
valley-of-fear	event_30_4	event	\N	Holmes asks Ames what Barker wore on his feet and Ames answers	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1330", "sentence_1331", "sentence_1332", "sentence_1333"], "communicatesContent": "Can you remember, Ames, what Mr. Barker had on his feet last night when you joined him in the study?"}
valley-of-fear	event_30_5	event	\N	Holmes asks where the slippers are and Ames replies	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1334", "sentence_1335", "sentence_1336", "sentence_1337"], "communicatesContent": "Where are the slippers now?"}
valley-of-fear	event_30_6	event	\N	Ames states that he noticed the slippers were stained with blood	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "ames", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1338", "sentence_1339", "sentence_1340", "sentence_1341", "sentence_1342"], "communicatesContent": "I may say that I noticed that the slippers were stained with blood—so indeed were my own."}
valley-of-fear	event_30_7	event	\N	Holmes and the others examine the slippers in the study and compare them with the blood mark on the sill	29	{"section": "section_30", "speakerId": "macdonald", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1343", "sentence_1344", "sentence_1345", "sentence_1346", "sentence_1347", "sentence_1348", "sentence_1349", "sentence_1350", "sentence_1351", "sentence_1352", "sentence_1353", "sentence_1354", "sentence_1355", "sentence_1356", "sentence_1357", "sentence_1358", "sentence_1359", "sentence_1360", "sentence_1361", "sentence_1362", "sentence_1363", "sentence_1364"], "communicatesContent": "there’s not a doubt of it! Barker has just marked the window himself. It’s a good deal broader than any bootmark. I mind that you said it was a splay-foot, and here’s the explanation. But what’s the game, Mr. Holmes—what’s the game?"}
