valley-of-fear	event_31_9	event	\N	Watson greets Mrs. Douglas with reserve	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1391"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_31_10	event	\N	Watson speaks dismissively to Mrs. Douglas	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1395", "sentence_1396", "sentence_1401"], "communicatesContent": "It is no business of mine."}
valley-of-fear	event_31_11	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas asks Watson to answer a question about Holmes and the police	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1402", "sentence_1403", "sentence_1404", "sentence_1405"], "communicatesContent": "One question which you can answer with more authority than anyone else in the world, and it may make a very great difference to me. You know Mr. Holmes and his relations with the police better than anyone else can. Supposing that a matter were brought confidentially to his knowledge, is it absolutely necessary that he should pass it on to the detectives?"}
valley-of-fear	event_31_12	event	\N	Barker agrees with Mrs. Douglas's question	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "cecil_james_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1406", "sentence_1407"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, that’s it. Is he on his own or is he entirely in with them?"}
valley-of-fear	event_31_13	event	\N	Mrs. Douglas implores Watson to guide them	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "mrs_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1409", "sentence_1410"], "communicatesContent": "I beg—I implore that you will, Dr. Watson! I assure you that you will be helping us—helping me greatly if you will guide us on that point."}
