valley-of-fear	event_31_14	event	\N	Watson describes Holmes as an independent investigator and declines to say more	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1412", "sentence_1413", "sentence_1414", "sentence_1415"], "communicatesContent": "Mr. Holmes is an independent investigator. He is his own master, and would act as his own judgment directed. At the same time, he would naturally feel loyalty towards the officials who were working on the same case, and he would not conceal from them anything which would help them in bringing a criminal to justice. Beyond this I can say nothing, and I would refer you to Mr. Holmes himself if you wanted fuller information."}
