valley-of-fear	event_32_6	event	\N	Holmes states that Barker's story is a lie and that Barker and Mrs. Douglas are both lying in conspiracy	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1435", "sentence_1436", "sentence_1437", "sentence_1438", "sentence_1439", "sentence_1440", "sentence_1441", "sentence_1442", "sentence_1443"], "communicatesContent": "The whole story told by Barker is a lie. But Barker’s story is corroborated by Mrs. Douglas. Therefore she is lying also. They are both lying, and in a conspiracy. Why are they lying, and what is the truth which they are trying so hard to conceal?"}
valley-of-fear	event_32_7	event	\N	Holmes argues that the ring, card, and timing in the story make the account impossible	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1444", "sentence_1445", "sentence_1446", "sentence_1447", "sentence_1448", "sentence_1449", "sentence_1450", "sentence_1451", "sentence_1452", "sentence_1453", "sentence_1454", "sentence_1455", "sentence_1456", "sentence_1457"], "communicatesContent": "the assassin had less than a minute after the murder had been committed to take that ring, which was under another ring, from the dead man’s finger, to replace the other ring and to put that singular card beside his victim; the ring could not have been taken before the man was killed; the assassin was alone with the dead man for some time with the lamp lit; the shot must have been fired some time earlier than we are told; there was a deliberate conspiracy upon the part of the two people who heard the gunshot"}
valley-of-fear	event_32_8	event	\N	Holmes says that Barker placed the blood mark on the windowsill to mislead the police	31	{"section": "section_32", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1458"], "communicatesContent": "the blood mark on the windowsill was deliberately placed there by Barker, in order to give a false clue to the police"}
valley-of-fear	event_33_1	event	\N	The servants move about the house until half-past ten	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1460"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_33_2	event	\N	Ames remains in the pantry while the other servants go to their rooms	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1461"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_33_3	event	\N	Holmes conducts experiments after Watson and the others leave	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1462"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_33_4	event	\N	Holmes hears a voice from the housekeeper's room when it is loudly raised	32	{"section": "section_33", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1463", "sentence_1464"], "communicatesContent": null}
