valley-of-fear	event_45_11	event	\N	The card meant for the narrator lies beside the dead man's body	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1982"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_45_12	event	\N	The narrator puts his rings on the dead man's finger and leaves the wedding ring in place	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1983", "sentence_1984", "sentence_1985", "sentence_1986"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_45_13	event	\N	The narrator puts plaster on the spot where he is wearing one	44	{"section": "section_45", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1987", "sentence_1988"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_46_1	event	\N	The narrator describes the situation and says they need to hide and escape with the widow to live in peace	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "john_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1989", "sentence_1990", "sentence_1991"], "communicatesContent": "Well, that was the situation. If I could lie low for a while and then get away where I could be joined by my 'widow' we should have a chance at last of living in peace for the rest of our lives. These devils would give me no rest so long as I was above ground; but if they saw in the papers that Baldwin had got his man, there would be an end of all my troubles."}
valley-of-fear	event_46_2	event	\N	Douglas says he had little time to explain the plan, but Barker and his wife understood enough to help him	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "john_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1992"], "communicatesContent": "I hadn’t much time to make it all clear to Barker and to my wife; but they understood enough to be able to help me."}
valley-of-fear	event_46_3	event	\N	Douglas says Ames also knew about the hiding place but failed to connect it with the matter	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "john_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1993"], "communicatesContent": "I knew all about this hiding place, so did Ames; but it never entered his head to connect it with the matter."}
valley-of-fear	event_46_4	event	\N	Douglas retires into the hiding place and Barker takes over the remainder of the plan	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "john_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1994"], "communicatesContent": "I retired into it, and it was up to Barker to do the rest."}
valley-of-fear	event_46_5	event	\N	Barker opens the window and marks the sill to suggest how the murderer escaped	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1996", "sentence_1997"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_46_6	event	\N	Barker rings the bell when everything is fixed	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1998"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_46_7	event	\N	Douglas tells the gentlemen that he has told the truth and asks how he stands by English law	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "john_douglas", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2000", "sentence_2001"], "communicatesContent": "And so, gentlemen, you can do what you please; but I’ve told you the truth and the whole truth, so help me God! What I ask you now is how do I stand by the English law?"}
valley-of-fear	event_46_8	event	\N	Holmes breaks the silence and answers Douglas about English law and future danger	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2002", "sentence_2003", "sentence_2004", "sentence_2005", "sentence_2008", "sentence_2009", "sentence_2010", "sentence_2011"], "communicatesContent": "The English law is in the main a just law. You will get no worse than your deserts from that, Mr. Douglas. But I would ask you how did this man know that you lived here, or how to get into your house, or where to hide to get you? The story is not over yet, I fear. You may find worse dangers than the English law, or even than your enemies from America. I see trouble before you, Mr. Douglas. You’ll take my advice and still be on your guard."}
valley-of-fear	event_46_9	event	\N	The narration shifts away from Birlstone Manor House and the present journey back twenty years and westward	45	{"section": "section_46", "speakerId": "arthur_conan_doyle", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2012", "sentence_2013", "sentence_2014", "sentence_2015", "sentence_2016"], "communicatesContent": "I will ask you to come away with me for a time, far from the Sussex Manor House of Birlstone, and far also from the year of grace in which we made our eventful journey... I wish you to journey back some twenty years in time, and westward some thousands of miles in space... Do not think that I intrude one story before another is finished. As you read on you will find that this is not so. And when I have detailed those distant events and you have solved this mystery of the past, we shall meet once more in those rooms on Baker Street."}
valley-of-fear	event_47_1	event	\N	The evening train travels up the steep railroad gradients toward Vermissa	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2021", "sentence_2027"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_47_2	event	\N	Steam ploughs keep the railroad open	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2021"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_47_3	event	\N	The oil lamps are lit in the leading passenger car	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2028"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_47_4	event	\N	Workmen, miners, policemen, women, travelers, and one young Irishman occupy the leading passenger car	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2028", "sentence_2029", "sentence_2030", "sentence_2031", "sentence_2032"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_47_5	event	\N	The traveller makes tentative remarks to the nearest miner	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": "young_irishman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2040"], "communicatesContent": "tentative remarks"}
valley-of-fear	event_47_6	event	\N	The traveller resigns himself to silence and stares out of the window	46	{"section": "section_47", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2040"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_48_1	event	\N	The young traveller gazes out over the dismal industrial country	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2045", "sentence_2046", "sentence_2047"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_48_2	event	\N	The young traveller draws out a bulky letter and writes notes on its margins	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2048"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_174	lexical	\N	\N	173	{"text": "“One more question.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	event_48_3	event	\N	The young traveller produces a navy revolver and shows that it is fully loaded	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2049", "sentence_2050", "sentence_2051"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_48_4	event	\N	The young traveller restores the revolver to a secret pocket and a working man observes it	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2052"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_48_5	event	\N	The working man greets the young traveller and comments on the revolver	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "working_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2053", "sentence_2054", "sentence_2055"], "communicatesContent": "Hullo, mate! You seem heeled and ready."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_6	event	\N	The young traveller says he sometimes needs weapons where he comes from	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "young_traveller", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2056", "sentence_2057"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, we need them sometimes in the place I come from."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_7	event	\N	The young traveller says he is last from Chicago	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "young_traveller", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2058", "sentence_2059"], "communicatesContent": "I’m last from Chicago."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_8	event	\N	The working man asks whether the young traveller is a stranger in the district and warns that he may need the revolver there	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "working_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2060", "sentence_2061", "sentence_2062"], "communicatesContent": "A stranger in these parts? You may find you need it here."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_9	event	\N	The young traveller asks whether the country is full of doings and says he has heard there is always work for a willing man	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "young_traveller", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2063", "sentence_2064", "sentence_2065", "sentence_2066", "sentence_2067", "sentence_2068", "sentence_2069", "sentence_2070", "sentence_2071"], "communicatesContent": "Ah! is that so? Have you heard nothing of doings hereabouts? Why, I thought the country was full of it. You’ll hear quick enough. What made you come here? I heard there was always work for a willing man."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_10	event	\N	The young traveller says he is a member of the union	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "young_traveller", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2072", "sentence_2073"], "communicatesContent": "Sure."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_11	event	\N	The working man says the traveller will get his job and asks whether he has friends	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "working_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2074", "sentence_2075"], "communicatesContent": "Then you’ll get your job, I guess. Have you any friends?"}
valley-of-fear	event_48_12	event	\N	The young traveller says he can make friends and identifies himself as a Freemen brother	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "young_traveller", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2076", "sentence_2077", "sentence_2078", "sentence_2079"], "communicatesContent": "Not yet; but I have the means of making them. I am one of the Eminent Order of Freemen. There’s no town without a lodge, and where there is a lodge I’ll find my friends."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_13	event	\N	The working man reacts, moves close, and initiates a secret brotherhood handshake and sign	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "working_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2080", "sentence_2081", "sentence_2082", "sentence_2083", "sentence_2084", "sentence_2085", "sentence_2086", "sentence_2087", "sentence_2088", "sentence_2089", "sentence_2090", "sentence_2091", "sentence_2092", "sentence_2093"], "communicatesContent": "Put it there. I see you speak the truth. But it’s well to make certain. Dark nights are unpleasant."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_14	event	\N	The working man identifies himself as Brother Scanlan of Lodge 341 and the traveller identifies himself as Brother John McMurdo of Lodge 29 Chicago	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2094", "sentence_2095", "sentence_2096", "sentence_2097", "sentence_2098", "sentence_2099", "sentence_2100"], "communicatesContent": "I’m Brother Scanlan, Lodge 341, Vermissa Valley. Glad to see you in these parts. Thank you. I’m Brother John McMurdo, Lodge 29, Chicago. Bodymaster J.H. Scott. But I am in luck to meet a brother so early."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_15	event	\N	Scanlan says the order is flourishing and asks why McMurdo left Chicago	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2101", "sentence_2102", "sentence_2103", "sentence_2104", "sentence_2105", "sentence_2106"], "communicatesContent": "Well, there are plenty of us about. You won’t find the order more flourishing anywhere in the States than right here in Vermissa Valley. But we could do with some lads like you. I can’t understand a spry man of the union finding no work to do in Chicago. Then why did you leave?"}
valley-of-fear	event_48_16	event	\N	McMurdo nods toward the policemen and implies they would be glad to know the reason for his departure	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2107", "sentence_2108"], "communicatesContent": "I guess those chaps would be glad to know."}
valley-of-fear	event_48_17	event	\N	Scanlan asks whether McMurdo is in trouble and whether it is a penitentiary job or a killing	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2109", "sentence_2110", "sentence_2111", "sentence_2112", "sentence_2113", "sentence_2114", "sentence_2115"], "communicatesContent": "In trouble? A penitentiary job? Not a killing!"}
valley-of-fear	event_48_18	event	\N	McMurdo rebukes Scanlan for asking and says it is too early to speak of such things	47	{"section": "section_48", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2116", "sentence_2117", "sentence_2118", "sentence_2119"], "communicatesContent": "It’s early days to talk of such things. I’ve my own good reasons for leaving Chicago, and let that be enough for you. Who are you that you should take it on yourself to ask such things?"}
valley-of-fear	event_49_1	event	\N	Scanlan asks McMurdo where he is bound for and where he is staying	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2122", "sentence_2123", "sentence_2125", "sentence_2127", "sentence_2128"], "communicatesContent": "Where are you bound for now? Where are you staying?"}
valley-of-fear	event_49_2	event	\N	McMurdo shows an envelope and gives an address	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2126", "sentence_2127", "sentence_2128"], "communicatesContent": "Here is the address—Jacob Shafter, Sheridan Street. It’s a boarding house that was recommended by a man I knew in Chicago."}
valley-of-fear	event_60_7	event	\N	McMurdo continues to dine at Shafter's and see Ettie	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2752", "sentence_2753"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_49_3	event	\N	The policeman gives McMurdo advice about Vermissa and Boss McGinty	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "local_police_sergeant", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2129", "sentence_2130", "sentence_2131", "sentence_2132", "sentence_2134", "sentence_2135"], "communicatesContent": "Vermissa is out of my beat. I live at Hobson’s Patch, and that’s here where we are drawing up. If you’re in trouble in Vermissa, go straight to the Union House and see Boss McGinty. He is the Bodymaster of Vermissa Lodge, and nothing can happen in these parts unless Black Jack McGinty wants it. Maybe we’ll meet in lodge one of these evenings. But mind my words: If you are in trouble, go to Boss McGinty."}
valley-of-fear	event_49_4	event	\N	Scanlan descends from the carriage	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2136"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_49_5	event	\N	McMurdo remains in the carriage as night falls and the train moves through the furnace district	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2137", "sentence_2138"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_49_6	event	\N	A policeman remarks on the appearance of the fiery district	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "local_police_sergeant", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2139", "sentence_2140", "sentence_2141", "sentence_2142", "sentence_2143"], "communicatesContent": "I guess hell must look something like that. For that matter, I allow that hell must be something like that. If there are worse devils down yonder than some we could name, it’s more than I’d expect. I guess you are new to this part, young man?"}
valley-of-fear	event_49_7	event	\N	McMurdo answers the policeman rudely	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2144", "sentence_2145", "sentence_2148", "sentence_2149", "sentence_2150", "sentence_2151", "sentence_2152"], "communicatesContent": "Well, what if I am? What the hell is it to you who are my friends? Did I ask you for your advice, or did you think me such a sucker that I couldn’t move without it? You speak when you are spoken to, and by the Lord you’d have to wait a long time if it was me!"}
valley-of-fear	event_49_8	event	\N	The policemen react to McMurdo’s hostility	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "local_police_sergeant", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2153", "sentence_2154", "sentence_2155", "sentence_2156", "sentence_2157", "sentence_2158", "sentence_2159", "sentence_2160", "sentence_2161", "sentence_2162"], "communicatesContent": "No offense, stranger. It was a warning for your own good, seeing that you are, by your own showing, new to the place. Maybe we’ll see more of you before very long. You’re a real hand-picked one, if I am a judge. I guess we may meet again."}
valley-of-fear	event_49_9	event	\N	McMurdo declares his name and where he can be found	48	{"section": "section_49", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2163", "sentence_2164", "sentence_2165", "sentence_2166", "sentence_2167"], "communicatesContent": "I’m not afraid of you, and don’t you think it! My name’s Jack McMurdo—see? If you want me, you’ll find me at Jacob Shafter’s on Sheridan Street, Vermissa; so I’m not hiding from you, am I? Day or night I dare to look the like of you in the face—don’t make any mistake about that!"}
valley-of-fear	event_50_1	event	\N	The train arrives at the ill-lit station and the passengers clear off the platform.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2169"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_50_2	event	\N	McMurdo picks up his gripsack and starts to leave the platform.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2170"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_50_3	event	\N	A miner accosts McMurdo and offers to carry his grip and show him the road.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "young_irishman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2170", "sentence_2171", "sentence_2172", "sentence_2173", "sentence_2174", "sentence_2175"], "communicatesContent": "By Gar, mate! you know how to speak to the cops. It was grand to hear you. Let me carry your grip and show you the road. I’m passing Shafter’s on the way to my own shack."}
valley-of-fear	event_50_4	event	\N	The miners give McMurdo friendly good-nights as they leave the platform.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "miners", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2176"], "communicatesContent": "Good-nights"}
valley-of-fear	event_50_5	event	\N	McMurdo becomes a notable figure in Vermissa before setting foot in the town.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2177"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_50_6	event	\N	McMurdo and the miner walk through Vermissa toward the centre of town.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2184", "sentence_2185", "sentence_2186", "sentence_2212", "sentence_2213"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_50_7	event	\N	The miner identifies the Union House, names Jack McGinty as the boss there, and warns McMurdo about the Scowrers and McGinty.	49	{"section": "section_50", "speakerId": "young_irishman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2185", "sentence_2186", "sentence_2187", "sentence_2188", "sentence_2189", "sentence_2190", "sentence_2191", "sentence_2192", "sentence_2193", "sentence_2194", "sentence_2195", "sentence_2196", "sentence_2197", "sentence_2198", "sentence_2199", "sentence_2200", "sentence_2201", "sentence_2202", "sentence_2203", "sentence_2204", "sentence_2205", "sentence_2206", "sentence_2207", "sentence_2208", "sentence_2209", "sentence_2210", "sentence_2211"], "communicatesContent": "That’s the Union House. Jack McGinty is the boss there. I thought his name was known clear across the country. It’s been in the papers often enough. There’s only one set of affairs that you’ll hear of in these parts, and that’s the affairs of the Scowrers. Man, you won’t live long in these parts if you speak in the open street like that. Many a man has had the life beaten out of him for less. If killing is murder, then God knows there is murder and to spare. Don’t you dare to breathe the name of Jack McGinty in connection with it, stranger; for every whisper goes back to him, and he is not one that is likely to let it pass. Now, that’s the house you’re after, that one standing back from the street. You’ll find old Jacob Shafter that runs it as honest a man as lives in this township."}
valley-of-fear	event_51_1	event	\N	McMurdo reaches Shafter's house and knocks at the door	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2214"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_51_2	event	\N	Ettie Shafter opens the door	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2215", "sentence_2216"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_51_3	event	\N	Ettie Shafter speaks to McMurdo about expecting her father back	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2221", "sentence_2222", "sentence_2223", "sentence_2224"], "communicatesContent": "I thought it was father. Did you come to see him? He is down town. I expect him back every minute."}
valley-of-fear	event_51_4	event	\N	McMurdo speaks to Ettie Shafter about board	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2226", "sentence_2227", "sentence_2228"], "communicatesContent": "No, miss. I’m in no hurry to see him. But your house was recommended to me for board. I thought it might suit me—and now I know it will."}
valley-of-fear	event_51_5	event	\N	Ettie Shafter invites McMurdo inside and introduces herself	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2232", "sentence_2233", "sentence_2234", "sentence_2235", "sentence_2236"], "communicatesContent": "Come right in, sir. I’m Miss Ettie Shafter, Mr. Shafter’s daughter. My mother’s dead, and I run the house. You can sit down by the stove in the front room until father comes along—Ah, here he is! So you can fix things with him right away."}
valley-of-fear	event_51_6	event	\N	Mr. Shafter arrives at the house	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2237"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_51_7	event	\N	McMurdo explains his business to Mr. Shafter and gives his Chicago referral chain	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2238", "sentence_2239", "sentence_2240"], "communicatesContent": "A man named Murphy gave me the address in Chicago. He in turn had had it from someone else."}
valley-of-fear	event_51_8	event	\N	Mr. Shafter agrees to board McMurdo for seven dollars a week in advance	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2241", "sentence_2242", "sentence_2243"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_51_9	event	\N	McMurdo takes up board and lodging at Shafter's house	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2244"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_51_10	event	\N	McMurdo becomes prominent among the boarders	50	{"section": "section_51", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2246", "sentence_2247", "sentence_2248", "sentence_2249", "sentence_2250", "sentence_2251", "sentence_2252", "sentence_2253"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_52_1	event	\N	The young Irishman openly admires the daughter of the house and wins her heart	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2254", "sentence_2255"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_52_2	event	\N	The young Irishman tells Ettie that he loves her and keeps repeating it despite discouragement	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "young_irishman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2256"], "communicatesContent": "I love you."}
valley-of-fear	event_52_3	event	\N	The young Irishman responds to the idea of someone else and says Ettie will eventually say yes	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "young_irishman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2257", "sentence_2258", "sentence_2259", "sentence_2260", "sentence_2261", "sentence_2262"], "communicatesContent": "Someone else? Well, the worse luck for someone else! Let him look out for himself! Am I to lose my life’s chance and all my heart’s desire for someone else? You can keep on saying no, Ettie: the day will come when you will say yes, and I’m young enough to wait."}
valley-of-fear	event_52_4	event	\N	The young Irishman speaks charmingly and with mystery to Ettie	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2263", "sentence_2264", "sentence_2265", "sentence_2266", "sentence_2267", "sentence_2268"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_52_5	event	\N	McMurdo gets a temporary job as a bookkeeper	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2269"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_52_6	event	\N	McMurdo does not yet report himself to the lodge head	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2270"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_52_7	event	\N	Mike Scanlan visits McMurdo and asks why he has not reported to the Bodymaster	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2271", "sentence_2272", "sentence_2273", "sentence_2274", "sentence_2275", "sentence_2276"], "communicatesContent": "Say, McMurdo, I remembered your address, so I made bold to call. I’m surprised that you’ve not reported to the Bodymaster. Why haven’t you seen Boss McGinty yet?"}
valley-of-fear	event_52_8	event	\N	McMurdo says he had to find a job and has been busy	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2277", "sentence_2278"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I had to find a job. I have been busy."}
valley-of-fear	event_52_9	event	\N	Scanlan warns McMurdo to make time for the Bodymaster and to avoid running against him	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2279", "sentence_2280", "sentence_2281", "sentence_2282"], "communicatesContent": "You must find time for him if you have none for anything else. Good Lord, man! you’re a fool not to have been down to the Union House and registered your name the first morning after you came here! If you run against him—well, you mustn’t, that’s all!"}
valley-of-fear	event_52_10	event	\N	McMurdo says he has been a lodge member for over two years and that duties were not so pressing in Chicago	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2283", "sentence_2284", "sentence_2285", "sentence_2286"], "communicatesContent": "I’ve been a member of the lodge for over two years, Scanlan, but I never heard that duties were so pressing as all that. Well, it’s the same society here."}
valley-of-fear	event_52_11	event	\N	Scanlan questions McMurdo and looks at him fixedly	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2287", "sentence_2288", "sentence_2289", "sentence_2290", "sentence_2291"], "communicatesContent": "Is it? Isn’t it? You’ll tell me that in a month’s time."}
valley-of-fear	event_52_12	event	\N	Scanlan says he heard McMurdo talked with the patrolmen after leaving the train	51	{"section": "section_52", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2292", "sentence_2293", "sentence_2294"], "communicatesContent": "I hear you had a talk with the patrolmen after I left the train. Oh, it got about—things do get about for good and for bad in this district."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_1	event	\N	Scanlan laughs and urges McMurdo to visit Shafter at once	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa_valley", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2299", "sentence_2300", "sentence_2301", "sentence_2302"], "communicatesContent": "You go and see him, my lad. It’s not the police but you that he’ll hate if you don’t. Now, take a friend’s advice and go at once!"}
valley-of-fear	event_60_8	event	\N	McMurdo shows the coining moulds to lodge brothers and they take examples of false money	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2754", "sentence_2755"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_53_2	event	\N	McMurdo meets Shafter in Shafter's private room and they speak about Ettie	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "jake_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2303", "sentence_2304", "sentence_2305", "sentence_2306", "sentence_2307", "sentence_2308", "sentence_2309", "sentence_2310", "sentence_2311", "sentence_2312", "sentence_2313"], "communicatesContent": "It seems to me, mister, that you are gettin’ set on my Ettie. Ain’t that so, or am I wrong? Vell, I vant to tell you right now that it ain’t no manner of use. There’s someone slipped in afore you. Vell, you can lay that she told you truth. But did she tell you who it vas? I dare say not, the leetle baggage! Perhaps she did not vish to frighten you avay."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_3	event	\N	McMurdo admits his interest in Ettie	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2307"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, that is so."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_4	event	\N	Shafter names Teddy Baldwin as the rival for Ettie	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "jake_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2316", "sentence_2317", "sentence_2318", "sentence_2319", "sentence_2320"], "communicatesContent": "It is Teddy Baldwin."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_5	event	\N	McMurdo asks who Teddy Baldwin is and Shafter explains that he is a boss of the Scowrers	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2321", "sentence_2322"], "communicatesContent": "And who the devil is he?"}
valley-of-fear	event_53_6	event	\N	McMurdo asks what the Scowrers are and Shafter identifies them as the Eminent Order of Freemen	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "jake_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2323", "sentence_2324", "sentence_2325", "sentence_2326", "sentence_2327", "sentence_2328", "sentence_2329"], "communicatesContent": "The Scowrers are the Eminent Order of Freemen!"}
valley-of-fear	event_53_7	event	\N	McMurdo states that he is a member of the order	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2330", "sentence_2331"], "communicatesContent": "Why, I am a member of that order myself."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_8	event	\N	Shafter says he would not have kept McMurdo in his house if he had known he was in the order	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "jake_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2332", "sentence_2333"], "communicatesContent": "I vould never have had you in my house if I had known it—not if you vere to pay me a hundred dollar a veek."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_9	event	\N	McMurdo defends the order as one for charity and good fellowship	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2334", "sentence_2335", "sentence_2336"], "communicatesContent": "What’s wrong with the order? It’s for charity and good fellowship. The rules say so."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_10	event	\N	Shafter says the order is a murder society in this place	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "jake_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2337", "sentence_2338", "sentence_2339", "sentence_2340"], "communicatesContent": "It’s a murder society, that’s vat it is."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_11	event	\N	McMurdo challenges Shafter to prove the claim and demands an apology or explanation	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2341", "sentence_2342", "sentence_2343", "sentence_2349", "sentence_2350", "sentence_2351", "sentence_2352", "sentence_2353", "sentence_2354", "sentence_2355", "sentence_2356", "sentence_2357", "sentence_2358"], "communicatesContent": "See here! I want you to take back what you’ve said, or else make it good. One or the other you must do before I quit this room. Put yourself in my place. Here am I, a stranger in the town. I belong to a society that I know only as an innocent one. You’ll find it through the length and breadth of the States, but always as an innocent one. Now, when I am counting upon joining it here, you tell me that it is the same as a murder society called the Scowrers. I guess you owe me either an apology or else an explanation, Mr. Shafter."}
valley-of-fear	event_53_12	event	\N	Shafter states that the bosses of the order and the Scowrers are the same and that offenders are struck by the other group	52	{"section": "section_53", "speakerId": "jake_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2359", "sentence_2360", "sentence_2361", "sentence_2362"], "communicatesContent": "I can but tell you vat the whole vorld knows, mister. The bosses of the one are the bosses of the other. If you offend the one, it is the other vat vill strike you. We have proved it too often."}
valley-of-fear	event_54_1	event	\N	McMurdo demands proof of the gossip.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2363", "sentence_2364"], "communicatesContent": "That’s just gossip—I want proof!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_2	event	\N	Mr. Shafter tells McMurdo he must leave and cannot stay there.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mr_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2365", "sentence_2366", "sentence_2367", "sentence_2368", "sentence_2369", "sentence_2370", "sentence_2371"], "communicatesContent": "If you live here long you vill get your proof. But I forget that you are yourself one of them. You vill soon be as bad as the rest. But you vill find other lodgings, mister. I cannot have you here. Is it not bad enough that one of these people come courting my Ettie, and that I dare not turn him down, but that I should have another for my boarder? Yes, indeed, you shall not sleep here after to-night!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_3	event	\N	McMurdo is placed under banishment from his room and from Ettie.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2372"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_54_4	event	\N	McMurdo speaks privately with Ettie in the sitting-room.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2373", "sentence_2374", "sentence_2375"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, your father is after giving me notice. It’s little I would care if it was just my room, but indeed, Ettie, though it’s only a week that I’ve known you, you are the very breath of life to me, and I can’t live without you!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_5	event	\N	Ettie tells McMurdo that he is too late and that another man exists.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2376", "sentence_2377", "sentence_2378", "sentence_2379"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, hush, Mr. McMurdo, don’t speak so! I have told you, have I not, that you are too late? There is another, and if I have not promised to marry him at once, at least I can promise no one else."}
valley-of-fear	event_54_6	event	\N	McMurdo proposes that Ettie choose him instead of keeping the promise.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2380", "sentence_2381", "sentence_2382", "sentence_2383"], "communicatesContent": "Suppose I had been first, Ettie, would I have had a chance?"}
valley-of-fear	event_76_4	event	\N	Jack embraces and kisses Ettie	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3458", "sentence_3459"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_54_7	event	\N	McMurdo kneels before Ettie and asks her to choose him and leave with him.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2384", "sentence_2385", "sentence_2386", "sentence_2387", "sentence_2388", "sentence_2389", "sentence_2390", "sentence_2391"], "communicatesContent": "For God’s sake, Ettie, let it stand at that! Will you ruin your life and my own for the sake of this promise? Follow your heart, acushla! ’Tis a safer guide than any promise before you knew what it was that you were saying. Say that you will be mine, and we will face it out together!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_8	event	\N	Ettie refuses to say yes while they are there.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2392", "sentence_2393", "sentence_2394"], "communicatesContent": "Not here? No, no, Jack!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_9	event	\N	McMurdo holds Ettie in his arms and insists that it must be here.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2395", "sentence_2396", "sentence_2397", "sentence_2398", "sentence_2399", "sentence_2400"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, here. It could not be here. Could you take me away? No, here. I’ll hold you against the world, Ettie, right here where we are!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_10	event	\N	Ettie asks why they should not leave together and McMurdo refuses to leave.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2401", "sentence_2402", "sentence_2403", "sentence_2404", "sentence_2405", "sentence_2406", "sentence_2407"], "communicatesContent": "Why should we not leave together?"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_11	event	\N	Ettie names Baldwin, McGinty, and the Scowrers as people McMurdo does not know.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2408", "sentence_2409", "sentence_2410", "sentence_2411"], "communicatesContent": "You don’t know, Jack. You’ve been here too short a time. You don’t know this Baldwin. You don’t know McGinty and his Scowrers."}
valley-of-fear	event_54_12	event	\N	McMurdo rejects fear of Baldwin, McGinty, and the Scowrers.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2412", "sentence_2413", "sentence_2414", "sentence_2415", "sentence_2416", "sentence_2417"], "communicatesContent": "No, I don’t know them, and I don’t fear them, and I don’t believe in them! I’ve lived among rough men, my darling, and instead of fearing them it has always ended that they have feared me—always, Ettie. It’s mad on the face of it! If these men, as your father says, have done crime after crime in the valley, and if everyone knows them by name, how comes it that none are brought to justice? You answer me that, Ettie!"}
valley-of-fear	event_54_13	event	\N	Ettie explains that no witness dares testify and that the accused are protected by alibis.	53	{"section": "section_54", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2418", "sentence_2419", "sentence_2420", "sentence_2421", "sentence_2422"], "communicatesContent": "Because no witness dares to appear against them. He would not live a month if he did. Also because they have always their own men to swear that the accused one was far from the scene of the crime. But surely, Jack, you must have read all this. I had understood that every paper in the United States was writing about it."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_1	event	\N	Ettie tells Jack that she loathes Baldwin, fears him, and has been using half-promises to put him off.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2430", "sentence_2431", "sentence_2432", "sentence_2433", "sentence_2434", "sentence_2435"], "communicatesContent": "now I can tell you the truth. I loathe him with all my heart; but I fear him also. I fear him for myself; but above all I fear him for father. I know that some great sorrow would come upon us if I dared to say what I really felt. That is why I have put him off with half-promises. It was in real truth our only hope."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_2	event	\N	Ettie asks Jack to flee with her and take her father away from the power of the wicked men.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2436"], "communicatesContent": "if you would fly with me, Jack, we could take father with us and live forever far from the power of these wicked men."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_3	event	\N	Baldwin enters the room swaggering and confronts McMurdo and Ettie.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2447", "sentence_2448", "sentence_2449", "sentence_2450"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_55_4	event	\N	Ettie greets Baldwin, says he has arrived earlier than expected, and invites him to sit down.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2451", "sentence_2452", "sentence_2453"], "communicatesContent": "I'm glad to see you, Mr. Baldwin. You're earlier than I had thought. Come and sit down."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_5	event	\N	Baldwin asks who McMurdo is.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2454", "sentence_2455", "sentence_2456"], "communicatesContent": "Who is this?"}
valley-of-fear	event_55_6	event	\N	Ettie introduces McMurdo to Baldwin as a friend and a new boarder.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2457", "sentence_2458"], "communicatesContent": "It's a friend of mine, Mr. Baldwin, a new boarder here. Mr. McMurdo, may I introduce you to Mr. Baldwin?"}
valley-of-fear	event_55_7	event	\N	McMurdo and Baldwin nod surlily to each other.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2459"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_55_8	event	\N	Baldwin asserts that Ettie belongs to him and orders McMurdo to take a walk.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2460", "sentence_2461", "sentence_2462", "sentence_2463", "sentence_2464", "sentence_2465"], "communicatesContent": "Maybe Miss Ettie has told you how it is with us? I didn't understand that there was any relation between you. Didn't you? Well, you can understand it now. You can take it from me that this young lady is mine, and you'll find it a very fine evening for a walk."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_9	event	\N	McMurdo refuses Baldwin's suggestion of a walk.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2466"], "communicatesContent": "Thank you, I am in no humour for a walk."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_10	event	\N	Baldwin challenges McMurdo to a fight.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2467", "sentence_2468", "sentence_2469"], "communicatesContent": "Maybe you are in a humour for a fight, Mr. Boarder!"}
valley-of-fear	event_55_11	event	\N	McMurdo accepts Baldwin's challenge.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2470", "sentence_2471", "sentence_2472"], "communicatesContent": "That I am! You never said a more welcome word."}
valley-of-fear	event_55_12	event	\N	Ettie begs Jack and Ted to stop fighting and urges Ted to be forgiving.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2473", "sentence_2474", "sentence_2475", "sentence_2476", "sentence_2477", "sentence_2478", "sentence_2479", "sentence_2480", "sentence_2481"], "communicatesContent": "For God's sake, Jack! Oh, for God's sake! Oh, Jack, Jack, he will hurt you! Oh, it's Jack, is it? You've come to that already, have you? Oh, Ted, be reasonable—be kind! For my sake, Ted, if ever you loved me, be big-hearted and forgiving!"}
valley-of-fear	event_55_13	event	\N	McMurdo tells Ettie to leave so that he and Baldwin can settle the matter.	54	{"section": "section_55", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2482", "sentence_2483", "sentence_2484"], "communicatesContent": "I think, Ettie, that if you were to leave us alone we could get this thing settled. Or maybe, Mr. Baldwin, you will take a turn down the street with me. It's a fine evening, and there's some open ground beyond the next block."}
valley-of-fear	event_56_1	event	\N	His enemy threatens revenge without using his hands	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2485", "sentence_2486"], "communicatesContent": "I’ll get even with you without needing to dirty my hands. You’ll wish you had never set foot in this house before I am through with you!"}
valley-of-fear	event_56_2	event	\N	McMurdo challenges the enemy to act at once	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2487"], "communicatesContent": "No time like the present."}
valley-of-fear	event_56_3	event	\N	The enemy responds and shows a branded sign on his forearm	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2488", "sentence_2499", "sentence_2491", "sentence_2492"], "communicatesContent": "I’ll choose my own time, mister. You can leave the time to me. See here! D’you know what that means? Well, you will know, I’ll promise you that. You won’t be much older, either. Perhaps Miss Ettie can tell you something about it. —on your knees—and then I’ll tell you what your punishment may be. You’ve sowed—and by the Lord, I’ll see that you reap!"}
valley-of-fear	event_56_4	event	\N	The enemy leaves the house in fury	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2500", "sentence_2501", "sentence_2502"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_56_5	event	\N	McMurdo and the girl stand in silence	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2503"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_56_6	event	\N	The girl embraces McMurdo and urges him to flee that night	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2504", "sentence_2505", "sentence_2506", "sentence_2507", "sentence_2508", "sentence_2509", "sentence_2510", "sentence_2511"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, Jack, how brave you were! But it is no use, you must fly! To-night—Jack—to-night! It’s your only hope. He will have your life. I read it in his horrible eyes. What chance have you against a dozen of them, with Boss McGinty and all the power of the lodge behind them?"}
valley-of-fear	event_56_7	event	\N	McMurdo disengages her hands, kisses her, and sets her back into a chair	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2512"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_56_8	event	\N	McMurdo says he is a Freeman and plans to sleep there that night	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2513", "sentence_2514", "sentence_2515", "sentence_2516", "sentence_2517", "sentence_2518", "sentence_2525", "sentence_2526", "sentence_2527"], "communicatesContent": "There, acushla, there! Don’t be disturbed or fear for me. I’m a Freeman myself. I’m after telling your father about it. Maybe I am no better than the others; so don’t make a saint of me. Perhaps you hate me too, now that I’ve told you as much? I was thinking the same thing. I’ll go right now and fix it. You can tell your father that I’ll sleep here to-night and find some other quarters in the morning."}
valley-of-fear	event_56_9	event	\N	The girl reassures McMurdo and urges him to seek McGinty first	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2519", "sentence_2520", "sentence_2521", "sentence_2522", "sentence_2523", "sentence_2524"], "communicatesContent": "Hate you, Jack? While life lasts I could never do that! I’ve heard that there is no harm in being a Freeman anywhere but here; so why should I think the worse of you for that? But if you are a Freeman, Jack, why should you not go down and make a friend of Boss McGinty? Oh, hurry, Jack, hurry! Get your word in first, or the hounds will be on your trail."}
valley-of-fear	event_56_10	event	\N	McMurdo goes to McGinty’s saloon	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2528"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_56_11	event	\N	McGinty is described as a popular but feared official whose bar is crowded	55	{"section": "section_56", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2529", "sentence_2530", "sentence_2531", "sentence_2532"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_57_1	event	\N	Boss McGinty's saloon grows larger and more ornate over time	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2533"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_57_2	event	\N	McMurdo enters the saloon and moves through the crowd	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2534", "sentence_2535", "sentence_2536"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_57_3	event	\N	McMurdo approaches McGinty at the far end of the saloon	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2537", "sentence_2538", "sentence_2539", "sentence_2540"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_57_4	event	\N	McMurdo pushes through the courtiers toward McGinty	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2543"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_57_5	event	\N	McMurdo and McGinty exchange greetings and remarks	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2545", "sentence_2546", "sentence_2547", "sentence_2548", "sentence_2549", "sentence_2550", "sentence_2551", "sentence_2552", "sentence_2553", "sentence_2554", "sentence_2555", "sentence_2556", "sentence_2558", "sentence_2559", "sentence_2560", "sentence_2561", "sentence_2562", "sentence_2563", "sentence_2564", "sentence_2565", "sentence_2566", "sentence_2567", "sentence_2568", "sentence_2569", "sentence_2570", "sentence_2571"], "communicatesContent": "Well, young man, I can’t call your face to mind."}
valley-of-fear	event_57_6	event	\N	A voice identifies McGinty as Councillor McGinty	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "courtiers", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2548"], "communicatesContent": "He’s Councillor McGinty, young man."}
valley-of-fear	event_57_7	event	\N	McMurdo states that he is new there and was advised to see McGinty	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2546", "sentence_2549", "sentence_2550", "sentence_2551"], "communicatesContent": "I’m new here, Mr. McGinty. I’m sorry, Councillor. I’m strange to the ways of the place. But I was advised to see you."}
valley-of-fear	event_57_8	event	\N	McGinty asks who advised McMurdo to see him	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2562", "sentence_2563", "sentence_2564", "sentence_2565"], "communicatesContent": "And who told you?"}
valley-of-fear	event_57_9	event	\N	McMurdo identifies Brother Scanlan of Lodge 341, Vermissa as the adviser and drinks McGinty's health	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2565", "sentence_2566", "sentence_2567"], "communicatesContent": "Brother Scanlan of Lodge 341, Vermissa. I drink your health Councillor, and to our better acquaintance."}
valley-of-fear	event_57_10	event	\N	McGinty reacts to McMurdo's manner	56	{"section": "section_57", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2568", "sentence_2569", "sentence_2570", "sentence_2571"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, it’s like that, is it? I’ll have to look a bit closer into this, Mister—"}
valley-of-fear	event_58_1	event	\N	McGinty calls McMurdo into the room behind the bar	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2573", "sentence_2574"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_58_2	event	\N	McGinty closes the door and sits on a barrel while inspecting McMurdo in silence	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2575", "sentence_2576", "sentence_2577", "sentence_2578"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_58_3	event	\N	McGinty produces a revolver and threatens McMurdo	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2579", "sentence_2580"], "communicatesContent": "See here, my joker, if I thought you were playing any game on us, it would be short work for you."}
valley-of-fear	event_58_4	event	\N	McMurdo says he is a stranger brother and McGinty demands proof of lodge membership	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2581", "sentence_2582", "sentence_2583"], "communicatesContent": "This is a strange welcome, for the Bodymaster of a lodge of Freemen to give to a stranger brother."}
valley-of-fear	event_58_5	event	\N	McMurdo answers McGinty's lodge questions about his initiation details	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2584", "sentence_2585", "sentence_2586", "sentence_2587", "sentence_2588", "sentence_2589", "sentence_2590", "sentence_2591"], "communicatesContent": "Lodge 29, Chicago. June 24, 1872. James H. Scott. Bartholomew Wilson."}
valley-of-fear	event_58_6	event	\N	McGinty questions McMurdo about his work, his lodge, and why he left Chicago	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2594", "sentence_2595", "sentence_2596", "sentence_2597", "sentence_2598", "sentence_2599", "sentence_2600", "sentence_2601", "sentence_2602", "sentence_2603", "sentence_2604", "sentence_2605", "sentence_2606", "sentence_2607", "sentence_2608", "sentence_2609", "sentence_2610", "sentence_2611", "sentence_2612", "sentence_2613"], "communicatesContent": "What are you doing here? What are you doing here? Have you heard anything of the lodge in these parts? Why did you leave Chicago?"}
valley-of-fear	event_58_7	event	\N	McMurdo shows McGinty a newspaper cutting about Jonas Pinto	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2614", "sentence_2615", "sentence_2616", "sentence_2623", "sentence_2624"], "communicatesContent": "You wouldn't squeal on a fellow? Look at that clipping."}
valley-of-fear	event_58_8	event	\N	McGinty reacts angrily to McMurdo's wording and then examines the clipping	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2617", "sentence_2618", "sentence_2619", "sentence_2620", "sentence_2621", "sentence_2622", "sentence_2624", "sentence_2625", "sentence_2626", "sentence_2627"], "communicatesContent": "You are right, Councillor."}
valley-of-fear	event_58_9	event	\N	McMurdo explains that he shot Jonas Pinto and fled to the coal country	57	{"section": "section_58", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2628", "sentence_2629", "sentence_2630", "sentence_2631", "sentence_2632", "sentence_2633", "sentence_2634", "sentence_2635", "sentence_2636", "sentence_2637", "sentence_2638", "sentence_2639", "sentence_2640", "sentence_2641", "sentence_2642", "sentence_2643", "sentence_2644"], "communicatesContent": "I was helping Uncle Sam to make dollars. This man Pinto helped me to shove the queer. Then he said he would split. Maybe he did split. I didn't wait to see. I just killed him and lighted out for the coal country. 'Cause I'd read in the papers that they weren't too particular in those parts. That's about the size of it."}
valley-of-fear	event_59_1	event	\N	McMurdo takes half a dozen coins from his pocket	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2645"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_59_2	event	\N	McGinty holds the coins to the light in his hand	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2648"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_59_3	event	\N	McGinty praises McMurdo as a useful brother and says the lodge can use bad men	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2651", "sentence_2652", "sentence_2653"], "communicatesContent": "you’ll be a mighty useful brother; we can do with a bad man or two among us, Friend McMurdo; for there are times when we have to take our own part; we’d soon be against the wall if we didn’t shove back at those that were pushing us"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_4	event	\N	McMurdo agrees to do his share of shoving	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2654"], "communicatesContent": "I’ll do my share of shoving with the rest of the boys"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_5	event	\N	McGinty says McMurdo has good nerve and mentions the gun he shoved at him	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2655", "sentence_2656"], "communicatesContent": "You seem to have a good nerve. You didn’t squirm when I shoved this gun at you."}
valley-of-fear	event_59_6	event	\N	McMurdo says he was covering McGinty with a cocked pistol	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2657", "sentence_2658", "sentence_2659", "sentence_2660", "sentence_2661", "sentence_2662"], "communicatesContent": "It was not me that was in danger. It was you, Councillor. I was covering you all the time. I guess my shot would have been as quick as yours."}
valley-of-fear	event_59_7	event	\N	McGinty laughs after flushing angry red	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2664"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_59_8	event	\N	The bartender reports that Ted Baldwin must see McGinty at once	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "bartender", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2669", "sentence_2670", "sentence_2671", "sentence_2672"], "communicatesContent": "it’s Ted Baldwin. He says he must see you this very minute"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_9	event	\N	Ted Baldwin enters, pushes the bartender out, and closes the door	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2672", "sentence_2673"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_59_10	event	\N	Ted Baldwin says he has a word to say to McGinty about McMurdo	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2674", "sentence_2675"], "communicatesContent": "you got here first, did you? I’ve a word to say to you, Councillor, about this man"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_11	event	\N	McMurdo challenges Baldwin to say it in front of him	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2676"], "communicatesContent": "Then say it here and now before my face"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_12	event	\N	McGinty tries to reconcile McMurdo and Baldwin	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2680", "sentence_2681", "sentence_2682", "sentence_2683"], "communicatesContent": "This will never do. We have a new brother here, Baldwin, and it’s not for us to greet him in such fashion. Hold out your hand, man, and make it up"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_13	event	\N	McMurdo says he will fight Baldwin in any manner Baldwin chooses	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2686", "sentence_2687", "sentence_2688"], "communicatesContent": "I’ve offered to fight him if he thinks I have wronged him. I’ll fight him with fists, or, if that won’t satisfy him, I’ll fight him any other way he chooses. Now, I’ll leave it to you, Councillor, to judge between us as a Bodymaster should"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_14	event	\N	McMurdo says the dispute concerns a young lady who is free to choose for herself	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2689", "sentence_2690", "sentence_2691"], "communicatesContent": "A young lady. She’s free to choose for herself"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_15	event	\N	McGinty rules that the young lady is free as between two lodge brothers	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2692", "sentence_2693", "sentence_2694", "sentence_2695", "sentence_2696", "sentence_2697"], "communicatesContent": "As between two brothers of the lodge I should say that she was. Yes, it is, Ted Baldwin. Is it you that would dispute it?"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_16	event	\N	Baldwin accuses McGinty of choosing McMurdo over him	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2698", "sentence_2699", "sentence_2700"], "communicatesContent": "You would throw over one that has stood by you this five years in favour of a man that you never saw before in your life? You’re not Bodymaster for life, Jack McGinty, and by God! when next it comes to a vote—"}
valley-of-fear	event_59_17	event	\N	McGinty attacks Baldwin and hurls him across a barrel	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2701", "sentence_2702", "sentence_2703"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_59_18	event	\N	McMurdo pulls McGinty back to stop him from killing Baldwin	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2703", "sentence_2704", "sentence_2705", "sentence_2706"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_59_19	event	\N	McGinty releases Baldwin and Baldwin sits up on the barrel, shaken and gasping	58	{"section": "section_59", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2707"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_60_1	event	\N	McGinty confronts Baldwin and then briefly reconciles with him over lodge discipline	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2708", "sentence_2714", "sentence_2728"], "communicatesContent": "You’ve been asking for it this many a day, Ted Baldwin—now you’ve got it! Maybe you think if I was voted down from Bodymaster you would find yourself in my shoes. It’s for the lodge to say that. But so long as I am the chief I’ll have no man lift his voice against me or my rulings. Well, then, we are all good friends again and there’s an end of the matter. That’s the end of the black blood. You come under lodge discipline if it goes further, and that’s a heavy hand in these parts, as Brother Baldwin knows—and as you will damn soon find out, Brother McMurdo, if you ask for trouble!"}
valley-of-fear	event_60_2	event	\N	Baldwin answers McGinty	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2713", "sentence_2721", "sentence_2722", "sentence_2723"], "communicatesContent": "I have nothing against you. The clouds are heavy. But they will forever brighten. And this I swear!"}
valley-of-fear	event_60_3	event	\N	McGinty pours champagne and the men drink a reconciliation toast	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2715", "sentence_2716", "sentence_2717", "sentence_2718", "sentence_2724"], "communicatesContent": "See now. Let us drink the quarrelling toast of the lodge. After that, as you know, there can be no bad blood between us. Now, then the left hand on the apple of my throat. I say to you, Ted Baldwin, what is the offense, sir?"}
valley-of-fear	event_60_4	event	\N	McMurdo responds and takes Baldwin's hand	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2729", "sentence_2730", "sentence_2731", "sentence_2732", "sentence_2733", "sentence_2734"], "communicatesContent": "Faith, I’d be slow to do that. I’m quick to quarrel and quick to forgive. It’s my hot Irish blood, they tell me. But it’s over for me, and I bear no grudge."}
valley-of-fear	event_60_5	event	\N	McGinty explains the women are outside lodge jurisdiction and tells McMurdo to join Lodge 341	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2736", "sentence_2737", "sentence_2741", "sentence_2743", "sentence_2745", "sentence_2746", "sentence_2747"], "communicatesContent": "Tut! These girls! These girls! To think that the same petticoats should come between two of my boys! It’s the devil’s own luck! Well, it’s the colleen inside of them that must settle the question; for it’s outside the jurisdiction of a Bodymaster—and the Lord be praised for that! We have enough on us, without the women as well. You’ll have to be affiliated to Lodge 341, Brother McMurdo. We have our own ways and methods, different from Chicago. Saturday night is our meeting, and if you come then, we’ll make you free forever of the Vermissa Valley."}
valley-of-fear	event_60_6	event	\N	McMurdo moves his lodgings to Widow MacNamara's and later lodges with Scanlan	59	{"section": "section_60", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2749", "sentence_2750", "sentence_2751"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_61_1	event	\N	A mine police captain enters McGinty's saloon and orders whisky	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": "teddy_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2760", "sentence_2762", "sentence_2763", "sentence_2764", "sentence_2765", "sentence_2766", "sentence_2767", "sentence_2768", "sentence_2769"], "communicatesContent": "A straight whisky; for the night is bitter."}
valley-of-fear	event_61_2	event	\N	McGinty speaks coldly to Captain Marvin about township police and capitalists	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2770", "sentence_2771"], "communicatesContent": "We’d do better without you, Captain Marvin, for we have our own police of the township, and no need for any imported goods. What are you but the paid tool of the capitalists, hired by them to club or shoot your poorer fellow citizen?"}
valley-of-fear	event_61_3	event	\N	Marvin replies that they will not argue about the matter	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": "teddy_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2772", "sentence_2773"], "communicatesContent": "Well, well, we won’t argue about that. I expect we all do our duty same as we see it; but we can’t all see it the same."}
valley-of-fear	event_61_4	event	\N	Marvin recognizes Jack McMurdo and addresses him as an old acquaintance	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": "teddy_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2774", "sentence_2775", "sentence_2776", "sentence_2777", "sentence_2778"], "communicatesContent": "Hullo! Hullo! Here’s an old acquaintance!"}
valley-of-fear	event_61_5	event	\N	McMurdo rejects friendship with Marvin and denies shame over his name	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2779", "sentence_2780", "sentence_2781", "sentence_2782", "sentence_2783", "sentence_2784", "sentence_2785", "sentence_2786", "sentence_2787", "sentence_2788"], "communicatesContent": "I was never a friend to you nor any other cursed copper in my life. I'm not denying it. D’ye think I’m ashamed of my own name? What the devil d’you mean by that?"}
valley-of-fear	event_61_6	event	\N	Marvin says he had been a Chicago officer and calls McMurdo a Chicago crook	60	{"section": "section_61", "speakerId": "teddy_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2789", "sentence_2790", "sentence_2791", "sentence_2792", "sentence_2793", "sentence_2794", "sentence_2795", "sentence_2796", "sentence_2797", "sentence_2798", "sentence_2799", "sentence_2800"], "communicatesContent": "No, no, Jack, bluster won’t do with me. I was an officer in Chicago before ever I came to this darned coal bunker, and I know a Chicago crook when I see one. Just the same old Teddy Marvin, at your service. We haven’t forgotten the shooting of Jonas Pinto up there. Did you not? That’s good impartial evidence, ain’t it? Well, his death came in uncommon handy for you, or they would have had you for shoving the queer. Well, we can let that be bygones; for, between you and me—and perhaps I’m going further than my duty in saying it—they could get no clear case against you, and Chicago’s open to you to-morrow."}
valley-of-fear	event_62_1	event	\N	McMurdo is spoken to by the captain and replies politely enough	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2801", "sentence_2802", "sentence_2803", "sentence_2804", "sentence_2807"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I suppose you mean well, and I do thank you."}
valley-of-fear	event_62_2	event	\N	The captain warns McMurdo about living on the straight and leaves the bar-room	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2804", "sentence_2805", "sentence_2806", "sentence_2807", "sentence_2808"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_62_3	event	\N	McMurdo becomes a local hero in the bar-room	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2808", "sentence_2809", "sentence_2810", "sentence_2811", "sentence_2812", "sentence_2813"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_62_4	event	\N	The bar loafers crowd round McMurdo and shake his hand	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2812"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_62_5	event	\N	McMurdo is introduced to the lodge	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2815", "sentence_2816", "sentence_2817"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_62_6	event	\N	The lodge assembly meets at the Union House	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2817"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_62_7	event	\N	Members assemble in the lodge room around the long table	61	{"section": "section_62", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2820", "sentence_2821", "sentence_2822", "sentence_2823", "sentence_2824", "sentence_2825", "sentence_2826", "sentence_2827", "sentence_2828"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_1	event	\N	McMurdo is led into an outer room by two solemn brothers	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2832"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_2	event	\N	McMurdo hears voices from the assembly inside the partition	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2833", "sentence_2834"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_3	event	\N	An inner guard enters and delivers the Bodymaster's order to truss, blind, and enter McMurdo	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2835", "sentence_2836"], "communicatesContent": "that he shall be trussed, blinded, and entered"}
valley-of-fear	event_63_4	event	\N	Three men remove McMurdo's coat, turn up his sleeve, and bind his arms with a rope	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2837"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_5	event	\N	A thick black cap is placed over McMurdo's head and face	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2838"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_6	event	\N	McMurdo is led into the assembly hall	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2839"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_7	event	\N	McGinty asks McMurdo whether he is already a member of the Ancient Order of Freemen	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2842", "sentence_2843"], "communicatesContent": "John McMurdo, are you already a member of the Ancient Order of Freemen?"}
valley-of-fear	event_63_8	event	\N	McGinty asks McMurdo whether his lodge is No. 29, Chicago	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2844", "sentence_2845", "sentence_2846"], "communicatesContent": "Is your lodge No. 29, Chicago?"}
valley-of-fear	event_63_9	event	\N	McGinty and McMurdo exchange remarks about dark nights and heavy clouds	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2847", "sentence_2848", "sentence_2849", "sentence_2850"], "communicatesContent": "Dark nights are unpleasant."}
valley-of-fear	event_63_10	event	\N	McGinty asks whether the brethren are satisfied	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2851", "sentence_2852", "sentence_2853"], "communicatesContent": "Are the brethren satisfied?"}
valley-of-fear	event_63_11	event	\N	McGinty states that they know McMurdo is one of them by his sign and countersign and asks if he is ready to be tested	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2854", "sentence_2855", "sentence_2856", "sentence_2857", "sentence_2858", "sentence_2859", "sentence_2860", "sentence_2861", "sentence_2862", "sentence_2863", "sentence_2864", "sentence_2865", "sentence_2866", "sentence_2867", "sentence_2868", "sentence_2869", "sentence_2871"], "communicatesContent": "We know, Brother, by your sign and by your countersign that you are indeed one of us. We would have you know, however, that in this county and in other counties of these parts we have certain rites, and also certain duties of our own which call for good men. Are you ready to be tested?"}
valley-of-fear	event_63_12	event	\N	McMurdo steps forward to prove his stout heart	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2858", "sentence_2859", "sentence_2860", "sentence_2861", "sentence_2862", "sentence_2863", "sentence_2864"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_63_13	event	\N	McMurdo is subjected to a pain test on his forearm	62	{"section": "section_63", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2865", "sentence_2866", "sentence_2867", "sentence_2868", "sentence_2869", "sentence_2871"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_64_1	event	\N	The lodge audience applauds McMurdo's first appearance	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2872", "sentence_2873", "sentence_2874", "sentence_2875"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_64_2	event	\N	McGinty questions McMurdo about the oath and the Bodymaster's rule	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2876", "sentence_2877", "sentence_2878", "sentence_2879", "sentence_2880"], "communicatesContent": "You have already sworn the oath of secrecy and fidelity, and you are aware that the punishment for any breach of it is instant and inevitable death? And you accept the rule of the Bodymaster for the time being under all circumstances?"}
valley-of-fear	event_64_3	event	\N	McGinty welcomes McMurdo to Lodge 341 and orders liquor to be brought	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2881", "sentence_2882"], "communicatesContent": "In the name of Lodge 341, Vermissa, I welcome you to its privileges and debates. You will put the liquor on the table, Brother Scanlan, and we will drink to our worthy brother."}
valley-of-fear	event_64_4	event	\N	McMurdo examines his branded forearm after receiving his coat	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2883", "sentence_2884", "sentence_2885", "sentence_2886", "sentence_2887", "sentence_2888"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_64_5	event	\N	The lodge proceeds with business after the initiation drinks are finished	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2889", "sentence_2890"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_64_6	event	\N	McGinty reads Windle's letter about a job on Andrew Rae	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2891", "sentence_2892", "sentence_2893", "sentence_2894", "sentence_2895", "sentence_2896", "sentence_2897", "sentence_2898", "sentence_2899"], "communicatesContent": "There is a job to be done on Andrew Rae of Rae & Sturmash, coal owners near this place. You will remember that your lodge owes us a return, having had the service of two brethren in the matter of the patrolman last fall. You will send two good men, they will be taken charge of by Treasurer Higgins of this lodge, whose address you know. He will show them when to act and where."}
valley-of-fear	event_64_7	event	\N	McGinty asks for volunteers and several young fellows offer themselves	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2900", "sentence_2901", "sentence_2902", "sentence_2903", "sentence_2904"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_64_8	event	\N	McGinty selects Tiger Cormac and Wilson for the job and discusses their participation	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2905", "sentence_2906", "sentence_2907", "sentence_2908", "sentence_2909", "sentence_2910", "sentence_2911", "sentence_2912", "sentence_2913", "sentence_2914"], "communicatesContent": "You’ll do, Tiger Cormac. If you handle it as well as you did the last, you won’t be wrong. And you, Wilson. It’s your first, is it not? Well, you have to be blooded some time. It will be a great start for you. As to the pistol, you’ll find it waiting for you, or I’m mistaken. If you report yourselves on Monday, it will be time enough. You’ll get a great welcome when you return."}
valley-of-fear	event_64_9	event	\N	Cormac asks about a reward for the job	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2915", "sentence_2916"], "communicatesContent": "Any reward this time?"}
valley-of-fear	event_64_10	event	\N	McGinty replies that the job is for honour and may yield a few dollars	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2917", "sentence_2918", "sentence_2919"], "communicatesContent": "Never mind the reward. You just do it for the honour of the thing. Maybe when it is done there will be a few odd dollars at the bottom of the box."}
valley-of-fear	event_64_11	event	\N	Wilson asks what the man has done and McGinty refuses to explain	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2920", "sentence_2921", "sentence_2922", "sentence_2923", "sentence_2924", "sentence_2925"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, it’s not for the likes of you to ask what the man has done. He has been judged over there. That’s no business of ours. All we have to do is to carry it out for them, same as they would for us."}
valley-of-fear	event_64_12	event	\N	McGinty says two brothers from the Merton lodge will come next week to do business	63	{"section": "section_64", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2926"], "communicatesContent": "Two brothers from the Merton lodge are coming over to us next week to do some business in this quarter."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_1	event	\N	Someone asks who they are.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2927", "sentence_2928"], "communicatesContent": "Who are they?"}
valley-of-fear	event_65_2	event	\N	A speaker warns that it is wiser not to ask and says the men will make a clean job when they are about it.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2929", "sentence_2930", "sentence_2931"], "communicatesContent": "Faith, it is wiser not to ask. If you know nothing, you can testify nothing, and no trouble can come of it. But they are men who will make a clean job when they are about it."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_3	event	\N	Ted Baldwin speaks about people getting out of hand and mentions three men being turned off by Foreman Blaker.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2933", "sentence_2934", "sentence_2935", "sentence_2936"], "communicatesContent": "Folk are gettin’ out of hand in these parts. It was only last week that three of our men were turned off by Foreman Blaker. It’s been owing him a long time, and he’ll get it full and proper."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_4	event	\N	McMurdo whispers to his neighbour and asks what is meant by the reference to 'the business end of a buckshot cartridge'.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2937", "sentence_2938", "sentence_2939", "sentence_2940"], "communicatesContent": "Get what?"}
valley-of-fear	event_65_5	event	\N	A man answers with a loud laugh.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2939", "sentence_2940"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_65_6	event	\N	McMurdo says he likes the lodge ways and that it is a proper place for a lad of mettle.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2941", "sentence_2942", "sentence_2943", "sentence_2944"], "communicatesContent": "I like it well. ’Tis a proper place for a lad of mettle."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_7	event	\N	Those around him applaud McMurdo's words.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2945"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_65_8	event	\N	The black-maned Bodymaster from the end of the table reacts to McMurdo's words.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2946", "sentence_2947", "sentence_2948"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_65_9	event	\N	McMurdo rises and offers to help the lodge if a man should be wanted.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2949", "sentence_2950", "sentence_2951"], "communicatesContent": "I would say, Eminent Bodymaster, that if a man should be wanted I should take it as an honour to be chosen to help the lodge."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_10	event	\N	The meeting applauds McMurdo's offer.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2951", "sentence_2952"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_65_11	event	\N	The secretary moves that Brother McMurdo should wait until the lodge chooses to employ him.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "harraway", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2953", "sentence_2954"], "communicatesContent": "that Brother McMurdo should wait until it is the good pleasure of the lodge to employ him."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_12	event	\N	McMurdo accepts waiting for the lodge's decision.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2955"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, that was what I meant; I’m in your hands."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_13	event	\N	The chairman tells McMurdo his time will come and that he may come to a small matter that night.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2956", "sentence_2957", "sentence_2958", "sentence_2959", "sentence_2960", "sentence_2961", "sentence_2962"], "communicatesContent": "Your time will come, Brother. We have marked you down as a willing man, and we believe that you will do good work in these parts. There is a small matter to-night in which you may take a hand if it so please you. You can come to-night, anyhow, and it will help you to know what we stand for in this community. I will make the announcement later."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_14	event	\N	The chairman announces that he will ask the treasurer about the bank balance and mentions the pension to Jim Carnaway's widow.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2962", "sentence_2963", "sentence_2964", "sentence_2965"], "communicatesContent": "First of all, I will ask the treasurer as to our bank balance. There is the pension to Jim Carnaway’s widow. He was struck down doing the work of the lodge, and it is for us to see that she is not the loser."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_15	event	\N	McMurdo's neighbour explains that Jim was shot when men tried to kill Chester Wilcox of Marley Creek.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "james_h_scott", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2966"], "communicatesContent": "Jim was shot last month when they tried to kill Chester Wilcox of Marley Creek."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_16	event	\N	The treasurer reports the funds are good and lists payments and threats against firms.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "treasurer_higgins", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2967", "sentence_2968", "sentence_2969", "sentence_2970", "sentence_2971", "sentence_2972", "sentence_2973", "sentence_2974", "sentence_2975"], "communicatesContent": "The funds are good at the moment. The firms have been generous of late. Max Linder & Co. paid five hundred to be left alone. Walker Brothers sent in a hundred; but I took it on myself to return it and ask for five. If I do not hear by Wednesday, their winding gear may get out of order. We had to burn their breaker last year before they became reasonable. Then the West Section Coaling Company has paid its annual contribution. We have enough on hand to meet any obligations."}
valley-of-fear	event_65_17	event	\N	A brother asks about Archie Swindon.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2976", "sentence_2977"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_65_18	event	\N	The treasurer says Archie Swindon sold out and left the district and left a note.	64	{"section": "section_65", "speakerId": "treasurer_higgins", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2978", "sentence_2979", "sentence_2980", "sentence_2981", "sentence_2982"], "communicatesContent": "He has sold out and left the district. The old devil left a note for us to say that he had rather be a free crossing sweeper in New York than a large mine owner under the power of a ring of blackmailers. By Gar! it was as well that he made a break for it before the note reached us! I guess he won’t show his face in this valley again."}
valley-of-fear	event_66_1	event	\N	Brother Morris rises from the table end and asks who bought the property of the man driven out of the district	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2983", "sentence_2984"], "communicatesContent": "may I ask who has bought the property of this man that we have driven out of the district?"}
valley-of-fear	event_66_2	event	\N	The treasurer answers that the State & Merton County Railroad Company bought the property	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "treasurer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2985", "sentence_2986"], "communicatesContent": "It has been bought by the State & Merton County Railroad Company."}
valley-of-fear	event_66_3	event	\N	Brother Morris asks who bought the mines of Todman and Lee	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2987"], "communicatesContent": "And who bought the mines of Todman and of Lee that came into the market in the same way last year?"}
valley-of-fear	event_66_4	event	\N	The treasurer answers that the same company bought the mines of Todman and Lee	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "treasurer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2988"], "communicatesContent": "The same company, Brother Morris."}
valley-of-fear	event_66_5	event	\N	Brother Morris asks who bought several ironworks that were given up of late	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2989"], "communicatesContent": "And who bought the ironworks of Manson and of Shuman and of Van Deher and of Atwood, which have all been given up of late?"}
valley-of-fear	event_66_6	event	\N	The treasurer answers that the West Gilmerton General Mining Company bought the ironworks	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "treasurer", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2990"], "communicatesContent": "They were all bought by the West Gilmerton General Mining Company."}
valley-of-fear	event_66_7	event	\N	Brother Morris argues that the lodge has driven small men out of trade and is making itself dangerous	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_2992", "sentence_2993", "sentence_2994", "sentence_2995", "sentence_2996", "sentence_2997", "sentence_2998", "sentence_2999", "sentence_3000", "sentence_3001", "sentence_3002"], "communicatesContent": "With all respect to you, Eminent Bodymaster, I think it may matter very much to us. This process has been going on now for ten long years. We are gradually driving all the small men out of trade. What is the result? We find in their places great companies like the Railroad or the General Iron, who have their directors in New York or Philadelphia, and care nothing for our threats. We can take it out of their local bosses; but it only means that others will be sent in their stead. And we are making it dangerous for ourselves. The small men could not harm us. They had not the money nor the power. So long as we did not squeeze them too dry, they would stay on under our power. But if these big companies find that we stand between them and their profits, they will spare no pains and no expense to hunt us down and bring us to court."}
valley-of-fear	event_66_8	event	\N	The speaker resumes his seat and the lodge reacts with angry cries	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3003", "sentence_3008", "sentence_3009"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_66_9	event	\N	McGinty rises and speaks to the lodge about unity and business for the evening	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3010", "sentence_3011", "sentence_3012", "sentence_3013", "sentence_3014", "sentence_3015", "sentence_3016"], "communicatesContent": "Brother Morris, you were always a croaker. So long as the members of this lodge stand together there is no power in the United States that can touch them. Sure, have we not tried it often enough in the lawcourts? I expect the big companies will find it easier to pay than to fight, same as the little companies do. And now, Brethren, this lodge has finished its business for the evening, save for one small matter which may be mentioned when we are parting. The time has now come for fraternal refreshment and for harmony."}
valley-of-fear	event_66_10	event	\N	McMurdo sings for the lodge and wins its good will	65	{"section": "section_66", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3018", "sentence_3019"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_67_1	event	\N	The new recruit becomes popular among the brethren and is marked for advancement	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3020"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_67_2	event	\N	McGinty addresses the men about James Stanger and his article	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3022", "sentence_3023", "sentence_3024", "sentence_3025", "sentence_3027", "sentence_3028", "sentence_3029", "sentence_3030", "sentence_3031", "sentence_3032", "sentence_3033", "sentence_3034", "sentence_3035", "sentence_3036", "sentence_3037", "sentence_3038", "sentence_3039", "sentence_3040", "sentence_3041"], "communicatesContent": "there is one man in this town that wants trimming up; James Stanger of the Herald has been opening his mouth against us again; the paper heads an article 'Law and Order!' and quotes 'Reign of Terror in the Coal and Iron District' describing our organization as responsible for assassinations, outrages, tyranny, terrorism, and lawlessness; the men are known; the organization is patent and public; the question is what shall we say to him?"}
valley-of-fear	event_67_3	event	\N	The men murmur assent and mutter oaths	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3026"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_67_4	event	\N	McGinty reads from the newspaper cutting and dismisses it	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3027", "sentence_3028", "sentence_3029", "sentence_3030", "sentence_3031", "sentence_3032", "sentence_3033", "sentence_3034", "sentence_3035", "sentence_3036", "sentence_3037", "sentence_3038", "sentence_3039", "sentence_3040", "sentence_3041"], "communicatesContent": "Law and Order! Reign of Terror in the Coal and Iron District. Twelve years have now elapsed since the first assassinations which proved the existence of a criminal organization in our midst. From that day these outrages have never ceased, until now they have reached a pitch which makes us the opprobrium of the civilized world. Is it for such results as this that our great country welcomes to its bosom the alien who flies from the despotisms of Europe? Is it that they shall themselves become tyrants over the very men who have given them shelter, and that a state of terrorism and lawlessness should be established under the very shadow of the sacred folds of the starry Flag of Freedom which would raise horror in our minds if we read of it as existing under the most effete monarchy of the East? The men are known. The organization is patent and public. How long are we to endure it? Can we forever live—"}
valley-of-fear	event_67_5	event	\N	A dozen men cry out to kill James Stanger	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "freeman_organisation", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3042", "sentence_3043"], "communicatesContent": "Kill him!"}
valley-of-fear	event_67_6	event	\N	Brother Morris protests against killing James Stanger	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3044", "sentence_3045", "sentence_3046", "sentence_3047", "sentence_3048", "sentence_3049"], "communicatesContent": "our hand is too heavy in this valley, and there will come a point where in self-defense every man will unite to crush us out. James Stanger is an old man. He is respected in the township and the district. His paper stands for all that is solid in the valley. If that man is struck down, there will be a stir through this state that will only end with our destruction."}
valley-of-fear	event_69_3	event	\N	Baldwin shouts abuse and orders McMurdo to stand back.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3111", "sentence_3112", "sentence_3113", "sentence_3114"], "communicatesContent": "Curse you! Who are you to interfere—you that are new to the lodge? Stand back!"}
valley-of-fear	event_67_7	event	\N	McGinty challenges Morris on how destruction would come about	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3050", "sentence_3051", "sentence_3052", "sentence_3053", "sentence_3054", "sentence_3055"], "communicatesContent": "Is it by the police? Sure, half of them are in our pay and half of them afraid of us. Or is it by the law courts and the judge? Haven't we tried that before now, and what ever came of it?"}
valley-of-fear	event_67_8	event	\N	Brother Morris mentions Judge Lynch	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3056", "sentence_3057"], "communicatesContent": "There is a Judge Lynch that might try the case."}
valley-of-fear	event_67_9	event	\N	McGinty threatens Morris and says he has him under watch	66	{"section": "section_67", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3058", "sentence_3059", "sentence_3060", "sentence_3061"], "communicatesContent": "I have but to raise my finger, and I could put two hundred men into this town that would clear it out from end to end. See here, Brother Morris, I have my eye on you, and have had for some time! You’ve no heart yourself, and you try to take the heart out of others. It will be an ill day for you, Brother Morris, when your own name comes on our agenda paper, and I’m thinking that it’s just there that I ought to place it."}
valley-of-fear	event_68_1	event	\N	Morris recoils and sits back in his chair	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3062"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_2	event	\N	Morris drinks from his glass before answering	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3063"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_3	event	\N	Morris apologizes to the Eminent Bodymaster and the lodge brethren and promises not to offend again	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3064", "sentence_3065", "sentence_3066"], "communicatesContent": "I apologize, Eminent Bodymaster, to you and to every brother in this lodge if I have said more than I should. I am a faithful member—you all know that—and it is my fear lest evil come to the lodge which makes me speak in anxious words. But I have greater trust in your judgment than in my own, Eminent Bodymaster, and I promise you that I will not offend again."}
valley-of-fear	event_68_4	event	\N	The Bodymaster relaxes his scowl while listening	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3067"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_5	event	\N	The Bodymaster responds that the lodge will remain united and that Stanger should receive a severe warning	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3068", "sentence_3069", "sentence_3070", "sentence_3071", "sentence_3072", "sentence_3073", "sentence_3074"], "communicatesContent": "Very good, Brother Morris. It’s myself that would be sorry if it were needful to give you a lesson. But so long as I am in this chair we shall be a united lodge in word and in deed. And now, boys, I’ll say this much, that if Stanger got his full deserts there would be more trouble than we need ask for. These editors hang together, and every journal in the state would be crying out for police and troops. But I guess you can give him a pretty severe warning. Will you fix it, Brother Baldwin?"}
valley-of-fear	event_68_6	event	\N	Ted Baldwin agrees to fix the matter	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3075", "sentence_3076"], "communicatesContent": "Sure!"}
valley-of-fear	event_68_7	event	\N	The chairman says the new brother may come	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3080", "sentence_3081", "sentence_3082"], "communicatesContent": "I promised the new brother he should go."}
valley-of-fear	event_68_8	event	\N	The chairman orders the group to get to work	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3083", "sentence_3084"], "communicatesContent": "That’s enough. The sooner we get to work the better."}
valley-of-fear	event_68_9	event	\N	The company breaks up in shouts, yells, and drunken song	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3085"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_10	event	\N	The duty band leaves the bar and goes out into the street	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3086", "sentence_3087"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_11	event	\N	The men gather in a yard facing a high building and see the Vermissa Herald sign and hear printing from within	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3089", "sentence_3090", "sentence_3091"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_12	event	\N	Baldwin assigns McMurdo to stand below at the door while he takes the others inside	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3092", "sentence_3093", "sentence_3094", "sentence_3095"], "communicatesContent": "You can stand below at the door and see that the road is kept open for us. Arthur Willaby can stay with you. You others come with me. Have no fears, boys; for we have a dozen witnesses that we are in the Union Bar at this very moment."}
valley-of-fear	event_68_13	event	\N	The party crosses the road and Baldwin's men rush into the newspaper office	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3096", "sentence_3097"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_14	event	\N	McMurdo and another man remain below	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3098"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_15	event	\N	A struggle erupts upstairs and a gray-haired man rushes onto the landing, is seized, struck down, and beaten	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3099", "sentence_3100", "sentence_3101", "sentence_3102", "sentence_3103", "sentence_3104", "sentence_3105", "sentence_3106"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_68_16	event	\N	McMurdo rushes up the stair and pushes Baldwin back	67	{"section": "section_68", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3107"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_1	event	\N	Baldwin warns that the man will be killed and orders the weapon dropped.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3108", "sentence_3109"], "communicatesContent": "You’ll kill the man. Drop it!"}
valley-of-fear	event_69_2	event	\N	Baldwin looks at McMurdo in amazement.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3110"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_4	event	\N	The man raises his stick and McMurdo draws his pistol.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3115"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_5	event	\N	McMurdo warns the man to stand back and threatens to shoot him.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3116", "sentence_3117", "sentence_3118", "sentence_3119"], "communicatesContent": "Stand back yourself! I’ll blow your face in if you lay a hand on me. As to the lodge, wasn’t it the order of the Bodymaster that the man was not to be killed—and what are you doing but killing him?"}
valley-of-fear	event_69_6	event	\N	One of the men remarks that McMurdo is speaking the truth.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "one_of_the_men", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3120"], "communicatesContent": "It’s truth he says."}
valley-of-fear	event_69_7	event	\N	The man below urges the others to hurry because the windows are lighting up and the town will soon arrive.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "the_dead_man", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3121", "sentence_3122", "sentence_3123", "sentence_3124"], "communicatesContent": "By Gar! you’d best hurry yourselves! The windows are all lighting up, and you’ll have the whole town here inside of five minutes."}
valley-of-fear	event_69_8	event	\N	Shouting breaks out in the street and a group of compositors and pressmen gathers in the hall below.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3125"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_9	event	\N	The criminals leave the editor's body and flee down the stairs into the street.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3126"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_10	event	\N	Some of the men mix with the crowd in McGinty's saloon and whisper to the Boss that the job was carried through.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": "some_of_the_men", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3127"], "communicatesContent": "the job had been well carried through"}
valley-of-fear	event_69_11	event	\N	Others, including McMurdo, break away into side streets and go home by devious paths.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3128"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_12	event	\N	McMurdo wakes the next morning after his initiation into the lodge.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3130"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_13	event	\N	McMurdo has a headache and a hot, swollen branded arm.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3131"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_14	event	\N	McMurdo stays at home for the morning, writes a long letter, and later reads the Daily Herald.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3132", "sentence_3133"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_15	event	\N	McMurdo reads the Herald report about the office outrage and Stanger's injuries.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3134", "sentence_3135", "sentence_3136", "sentence_3137", "sentence_3138", "sentence_3139", "sentence_3140", "sentence_3141"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_16	event	\N	McMurdo lays down the paper and lights his pipe when his landlady brings him an unsigned note.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3142", "sentence_3143"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_69_17	event	\N	McMurdo reads the note directing him to Miller Hill by the flagstaff.	68	{"section": "section_69", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3144", "sentence_3145", "sentence_3146", "sentence_3147", "sentence_3148", "sentence_3149", "sentence_3150"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_70_1	event	\N	McMurdo strolls up the path to the restaurant on Miller Hill	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3154"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_70_2	event	\N	McMurdo meets Brother Morris at Miller Hill and they exchange the lodge sign	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3155", "sentence_3156", "sentence_3157"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_70_3	event	\N	Brother Morris speaks privately with McMurdo	69	{"section": "section_70", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3158", "sentence_3159", "sentence_3160", "sentence_3161", "sentence_3162", "sentence_3163", "sentence_3164", "sentence_3165", "sentence_3166", "sentence_3167", "sentence_3168", "sentence_3169", "sentence_3170", "sentence_3171", "sentence_3172", "sentence_3173", "sentence_3174", "sentence_3175", "sentence_3176", "sentence_3177", "sentence_3178", "sentence_3179", "sentence_3180", "sentence_3181", "sentence_3182", "sentence_3183", "sentence_3184", "sentence_3185", "sentence_3186", "sentence_3187", "sentence_3188"], "communicatesContent": "I wanted to have a word with you, Mr. McMurdo. It was kind of you to come. Why did you not put your name to the note? One has to be cautious, mister. One never knows in times like these how a thing may come back to one. One never knows either who to trust or who not to trust. No, no, not always. Whatever we say, even what we think, seems to go back to that man McGinty. Look here! It was only last night, as you know well, that I swore good faith to our Bodymaster. Would you be asking me to break my oath? If that is the view you take, I can only say that I am sorry I gave you the trouble to come and meet me. Things have come to a bad pass when two free citizens cannot speak their thoughts to each other. And to take it back to Boss McGinty! Indeed, then, you do me injustice there. For myself I am loyal to the lodge, and so I tell you straight; but I would be a poor creature if I were to repeat to any other what you might say to me in confidence. It will go no further than me; though I warn you that you may get neither help nor sympathy. I have given up looking for either the one or the other. I may be putting my very life in your hands by what I say; but, bad as you are—and it seemed to me last night that you were shaping to be as bad as the worst—still you are new to it, and your conscience cannot yet be as hardened as theirs. That was why I thought to speak with you. Well, what have you to say? If you give me away, may a curse be on you! Sure, I said I would not. I would ask you, then, when you joined the Freeman’s society in Chicago and swore vows of charity and fidelity, did ever it cross your mind that you might find it would lead you to crime?"}
valley-of-fear	event_71_1	event	\N	McMurdo responds that if it is called crime, then it is called crime.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3189"], "communicatesContent": "If you call it crime."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_2	event	\N	Morris insists that the violence should be called crime.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3190", "sentence_3191", "sentence_3192", "sentence_3193", "sentence_3194"], "communicatesContent": "Call it crime! You have seen little of it if you can call it anything else. Was it crime last night when a man old enough to be your father was beaten till the blood dripped from his white hairs? Was that crime—or what else would you call it?"}
valley-of-fear	event_71_3	event	\N	McMurdo describes the violence as a war between two classes.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3195"], "communicatesContent": "There are some would say it was war, a war of two classes with all in, so that each struck as best it could."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_4	event	\N	Morris asks whether McMurdo expected violence when he joined the Freeman’s society at Chicago.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3196"], "communicatesContent": "Well, did you think of such a thing when you joined the Freeman’s society at Chicago?"}
valley-of-fear	event_71_5	event	\N	McMurdo denies that he thought of such violence when he joined.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3197"], "communicatesContent": "No, I’m bound to say I did not."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_6	event	\N	Morris says he joined the society in Philadelphia as a benefit club and meeting place.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3198", "sentence_3199"], "communicatesContent": "Nor did I when I joined it at Philadelphia. It was just a benefit club and a meeting place for one’s fellows."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_7	event	\N	Morris says he came to better himself, brought his family, started a drygoods store, and prospered.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3200", "sentence_3201", "sentence_3202", "sentence_3203", "sentence_3204"], "communicatesContent": "and I came to better myself! My wife and three children came with me. I started a drygoods store on Market Square, and I prospered well."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_8	event	\N	Morris says the word spread that he was a Freeman and he was forced to join the local lodge.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3205"], "communicatesContent": "The word had gone round that I was a Freeman, and I was forced to join the local lodge, same as you did last night."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_9	event	\N	Morris says he bears the lodge badge and an inner mark of shame.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3206"], "communicatesContent": "I’ve the badge of shame on my forearm and something worse branded on my heart."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_10	event	\N	Morris says he was under the orders of a black villain and caught in a meshwork of crime.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3207"], "communicatesContent": "I found that I was under the orders of a black villain and caught in a meshwork of crime."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_11	event	\N	Morris says every attempt to improve matters was treated as treason.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3208", "sentence_3209"], "communicatesContent": "What could I do? Every word I said to make things better was taken as treason, same as it was last night."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_12	event	\N	Morris says he cannot leave because his store contains all he owns and departure would mean murder to him and possibly to his family.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3210", "sentence_3211", "sentence_3212"], "communicatesContent": "I can’t get away; for all I have in the world is in my store. If I leave the society, I know well that it means murder to me, and God knows what to my wife and children. Oh, man, it is awful—awful!"}
valley-of-fear	event_71_13	event	\N	Morris breaks down sobbing.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3213", "sentence_3214"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_71_14	event	\N	McMurdo tells Morris he was too soft for the job and the wrong sort for the work.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3215", "sentence_3216", "sentence_3217"], "communicatesContent": "You were too soft for the job. You are the wrong sort for such work."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_15	event	\N	Morris says his conscience and religion made him a criminal among them.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3218"], "communicatesContent": "I had a conscience and a religion; but they made me a criminal among them."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_16	event	\N	Morris says he was chosen for a job and went along despite fear of consequences.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3219", "sentence_3220", "sentence_3221", "sentence_3222", "sentence_3223", "sentence_3224"], "communicatesContent": "I was chosen for a job. If I backed down I knew well what would come to me. Maybe I’m a coward. Maybe it’s the thought of my poor little woman and the children that makes me one. Anyhow I went. I guess it will haunt me forever."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_17	event	\N	Morris describes a lonely house and says he was assigned to the door while others went in.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3225", "sentence_3226", "sentence_3227", "sentence_3228"], "communicatesContent": "It was a lonely house, twenty miles from here, over the range yonder. I was told off for the door, same as you were last night. They could not trust me with the job. The others went in."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_18	event	\N	Morris says the others came out with bloody hands and a child screamed from the house.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3229", "sentence_3230", "sentence_3231"], "communicatesContent": "When they came out their hands were crimson to the wrists. As we turned away a child was screaming out of the house behind us. It was a boy of five who had seen his father murdered."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_19	event	\N	Morris says he had to hide his horror to avoid retaliation against his family.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3232"], "communicatesContent": "I nearly fainted with the horror of it, and yet I had to keep a bold and smiling face; for well I knew that if I did not it would be out of my house that they would come next with their bloody hands and it would be my little Fred that would be screaming for his father."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_20	event	\N	Morris says he became a criminal, a sharer in murder, and was cut off from his faith.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3233", "sentence_3234", "sentence_3235"], "communicatesContent": "But I was a criminal then, part sharer in a murder, lost forever in this world, and lost also in the next. I am a good Catholic; but the priest would have no word with me when he heard I was a Scowrer, and I am excommunicated from my faith. That’s how it stands with me."}
valley-of-fear	event_71_21	event	\N	Morris warns McMurdo that he is going down the same road and asks how it will end.	70	{"section": "section_71", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3236", "sentence_3237"], "communicatesContent": "I see you going down the same road, and I ask you what the end is to be. Are you ready to be a cold-blooded murderer also, or can we do anything to stop it?"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_1	event	\N	McMurdo asks Morris what he would do and whether he would inform on someone; Morris rejects the idea of informing	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3238", "sentence_3239", "sentence_3240", "sentence_3241", "sentence_3242", "sentence_3243"], "communicatesContent": "What would you do? You would not inform?"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_2	event	\N	McMurdo warns Morris that he is weak, says Morris should sell out sooner, and says Morris's statements are safe with him unless he is an informer	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3244", "sentence_3245", "sentence_3246", "sentence_3247", "sentence_3248", "sentence_3249", "sentence_3250", "sentence_3251", "sentence_3252", "sentence_3253", "sentence_3254", "sentence_3255", "sentence_3256", "sentence_3257"], "communicatesContent": "I’m thinking that you are a weak man and that you make too much of the matter. Too much! Wait till you have lived here longer. Look down the valley! See the cloud of a hundred chimneys that overshadows it! I tell you that the cloud of murder hangs thicker and lower than that over the heads of the people. It is the Valley of Fear, the Valley of Death. The terror is in the hearts of the people from the dusk to the dawn. Wait, young man, and you will learn for yourself. What is very clear is that you are not the man for the place, and that the sooner you sell out—if you only get a dime a dollar for what the business is worth—the better it will be for you. What you have said is safe with me; but, by Gar! if I thought you were an informer—"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_3	event	\N	Morris pleads with McMurdo not to accuse him of being an informer	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3258", "sentence_3259"], "communicatesContent": "No, no!"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_4	event	\N	McMurdo ends the talk, says he will remember it, says Morris meant kindly, and leaves for home	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3260", "sentence_3261", "sentence_3262", "sentence_3263"], "communicatesContent": "Well, let it rest at that. I’ll bear what you have said in mind, and maybe some day I’ll come back to it. I expect you meant kindly by speaking to me like this. Now I’ll be getting home."}
valley-of-fear	event_72_5	event	\N	Morris warns McMurdo that they may have been seen together and that others may ask what they spoke about	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3264", "sentence_3265", "sentence_3266"], "communicatesContent": "One word before you go. We may have been seen together. They may want to know what we have spoken about."}
valley-of-fear	event_72_6	event	\N	Morris offers McMurdo a clerkship in his store and McMurdo refuses it	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3267", "sentence_3268", "sentence_3269", "sentence_3270", "sentence_3271", "sentence_3272"], "communicatesContent": "I offer you a clerkship in my store."}
valley-of-fear	event_72_7	event	\N	Boss McGinty visits McMurdo at his home and sits opposite him	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "boss_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3273", "sentence_3274", "sentence_3275", "sentence_3276", "sentence_3277", "sentence_3278", "sentence_3279"], "communicatesContent": "I’m not much of a visitor, Brother McMurdo. I guess I am too busy over the folk that visit me. But I thought I’d stretch a point and drop down to see you in your own house."}
valley-of-fear	event_72_8	event	\N	McMurdo greets McGinty and brings out whisky	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3278", "sentence_3279"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_72_9	event	\N	McGinty asks about McMurdo's arm and McMurdo says he is not forgetting it but it is worth it	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "boss_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3280", "sentence_3281", "sentence_3282", "sentence_3283"], "communicatesContent": "How’s the arm?"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_10	event	\N	McGinty says the arm is worth it for loyal men who help the lodge	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "boss_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3284"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, it’s worth it, to those that are loyal and go through with it and are a help to the lodge."}
valley-of-fear	event_72_11	event	\N	McGinty asks what McMurdo was speaking to Brother Morris about on Miller Hill	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "boss_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3285", "sentence_3286"], "communicatesContent": "What were you speaking to Brother Morris about on Miller Hill this morning?"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_12	event	\N	McMurdo explains that Morris offered him a clerkship because Morris thought he was at a loose end, and that he refused it	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3287", "sentence_3288", "sentence_3289", "sentence_3290", "sentence_3291", "sentence_3292", "sentence_3293", "sentence_3294", "sentence_3295", "sentence_3296"], "communicatesContent": "Morris didn’t know I could earn a living here at home. He shan’t know either; for he has got too much conscience for the likes of me. But he’s a good-hearted old chap. It was his idea that I was at a loose end, and that he would do me a good turn by offering me a clerkship in a drygoods store. Yes, that was it. Sure. Couldn’t I earn ten times as much in my own bedroom with four hours’ work?"}
valley-of-fear	event_72_13	event	\N	McGinty agrees and tells McMurdo not to associate too much with Morris	71	{"section": "section_72", "speakerId": "boss_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3297", "sentence_3298"], "communicatesContent": "That’s so. But I wouldn’t get about too much with Morris."}
valley-of-fear	event_73_1	event	\N	McMurdo and McGinty argue in the room.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3299", "sentence_3300", "sentence_3301", "sentence_3302", "sentence_3303", "sentence_3304", "sentence_3305", "sentence_3306", "sentence_3307", "sentence_3308", "sentence_3309", "sentence_3310", "sentence_3311", "sentence_3312", "sentence_3313", "sentence_3314", "sentence_3315", "sentence_3316", "sentence_3317", "sentence_3318", "sentence_3319", "sentence_3320", "sentence_3321", "sentence_3322", "sentence_3323", "sentence_3324", "sentence_3325", "sentence_3326", "sentence_3327", "sentence_3328"], "communicatesContent": "Why not? Well, I guess because I tell you not. That’s enough for most folk in these parts. Well, if you want reasons, I’ll give them. Did Morris say nothing to you against the lodge? No. Nor against me? No. Well, that’s because he daren’t trust you. But in his heart he is not a loyal brother. We know that well. So we watch him and we wait for the time to admonish him. I’m thinking that the time is drawing near. There’s no room for scabby sheep in our pen. But if you keep company with a disloyal man, we might think that you were disloyal, too. See? Well, that’s enough. I came down to give you a word in season, and you’ve had it. It’s my business to know what goes on in this township. I guess you’d best reckon on my hearing all that passes. Well, time’s up, and I’ll just say—"}
valley-of-fear	event_73_2	event	\N	McMurdo says he dislikes Morris and denies disloyalty.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3320", "sentence_3321", "sentence_3324"], "communicatesContent": "There’s no chance of my keeping company with him; for I dislike the man. As to being disloyal, if it was any man but you he would not use the word to me twice. I’d like to know how you ever came to learn that I had spoken with Morris at all?"}
valley-of-fear	event_73_3	event	\N	McGinty finishes his drink and is interrupted by police entering the room.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3322", "sentence_3323", "sentence_3325", "sentence_3326", "sentence_3327", "sentence_3328", "sentence_3329", "sentence_3330"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_73_4	event	\N	Captain Marvin and armed constables enter and confront McMurdo.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "captain_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3330", "sentence_3331", "sentence_3332", "sentence_3333", "sentence_3334", "sentence_3335", "sentence_3336", "sentence_3337"], "communicatesContent": "I thought you’d be getting into trouble, Mr. Crooked McMurdo of Chicago. Can’t keep out of it, can you? Take your hat and come along with us."}
valley-of-fear	event_73_5	event	\N	McGinty protests the police action and challenges Captain Marvin.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3338", "sentence_3339", "sentence_3340", "sentence_3341", "sentence_3342", "sentence_3343", "sentence_3344", "sentence_3345", "sentence_3346"], "communicatesContent": "I guess you’ll pay for this, Captain Marvin. Who are you, I’d like to know, to break into a house in this fashion and molest honest, law-abiding men? He is a friend of mine, and I’ll answer for his conduct. By Gar! a man might as well live in Russia as in Vermissa while folk like you are running the police. It’s a capitalist outrage, and you’ll hear more of it, I reckon."}
valley-of-fear	event_73_6	event	\N	Captain Marvin states that the police are after McMurdo and orders him covered.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "captain_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3340", "sentence_3341", "sentence_3342", "sentence_3344", "sentence_3345", "sentence_3346"], "communicatesContent": "You’re standing out in this deal, Councillor McGinty. We are not out after you, but after this man McMurdo. It is for you to help, not to hinder us in our duty. By all accounts, Mr. McGinty, you may have to answer for your own conduct some of these days. This man McMurdo was a crook before ever he came here, and he’s a crook still. Cover him, Patrolman, while I disarm him."}
valley-of-fear	event_73_7	event	\N	McMurdo shows his pistol and taunts Captain Marvin.	72	{"section": "section_73", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3347", "sentence_3348", "sentence_3349"], "communicatesContent": "There’s my pistol. Maybe, Captain Marvin, if you and I were alone and face to face you would not take me so easily. Where’s your warrant?"}
valley-of-fear	event_74_1	event	\N	McMurdo asks what he is accused of	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3356", "sentence_3357"], "communicatesContent": "What am I accused of?"}
valley-of-fear	event_74_2	event	\N	An accusation of involvement in the beating of Editor Stanger is stated	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3358", "sentence_3359"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_3	event	\N	McGinty says McMurdo was with him in the saloon playing poker until midnight	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3360", "sentence_3361"], "communicatesContent": "This man was with me in my saloon playing poker up to midnight, and I can bring a dozen to prove it."}
valley-of-fear	event_74_4	event	\N	The captain orders McMurdo to come quietly under arrest	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3362", "sentence_3363", "sentence_3364", "sentence_3365"], "communicatesContent": "Meanwhile, come on, McMurdo, and come quietly if you don’t want a gun across your head."}
valley-of-fear	event_74_5	event	\N	McMurdo and McGinty accept the situation	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3365"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_6	event	\N	The boss whispers with McMurdo before they part	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3366", "sentence_3367", "sentence_3368", "sentence_3369", "sentence_3370", "sentence_3371"], "communicatesContent": "What about—"}
valley-of-fear	event_74_7	event	\N	McMurdo indicates a safe hiding place under the floor	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3367", "sentence_3368"], "communicatesContent": "All right"}
valley-of-fear	event_74_8	event	\N	The boss says good-bye and promises to see Reilly the lawyer	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3369", "sentence_3370", "sentence_3371"], "communicatesContent": "I’ll bid you good-bye. I’ll see Reilly the lawyer and take the defense upon myself. Take my word for it that they won’t be able to hold you."}
valley-of-fear	event_74_9	event	\N	The captain orders the prisoner guarded and searches the house	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3373", "sentence_3374", "sentence_3375"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_10	event	\N	McMurdo is escorted to headquarters	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3376"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_11	event	\N	Loiterers shout for McMurdo to be lynched	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3377", "sentence_3378", "sentence_3379", "sentence_3380", "sentence_3381"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_12	event	\N	McMurdo is pushed into the police station	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3381", "sentence_3382"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_13	event	\N	The inspector formally examines McMurdo	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3382"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_14	event	\N	McMurdo is put into the common cell	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3382", "sentence_3383"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_15	event	\N	A jailer brings bedding and hidden whisky, glasses, and cards to the prisoners	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": "freeman_organisation", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3385", "sentence_3386"], "communicatesContent": ""}
valley-of-fear	event_74_16	event	\N	The prisoners spend a hilarious night	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3386", "sentence_3387"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_17	event	\N	The magistrate fails to hold the prisoners for a higher court	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3388"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_18	event	\N	The compositors and pressmen give uncertain evidence about the attack	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3389", "sentence_3390"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_19	event	\N	The injured man deposes about the attack and the moustache of the first striker	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3391"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_74_20	event	\N	Six citizens, including McGinty, give evidence that the men were at a card party at the Union House	73	{"section": "section_74", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3393"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_1	event	\N	The court discharges the ex-prisoners with near-apology and implied censure of Captain Marvin and the police	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3394"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_2	event	\N	The verdict is greeted with loud applause in the court	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3395"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_3	event	\N	Members of the lodge smile and wave as the ex-prisoners leave the dock	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3396", "sentence_3397"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_4	event	\N	A little dark-bearded man shouts threats at the passing ex-prisoners	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3398", "sentence_3399", "sentence_3400", "sentence_3401"], "communicatesContent": "You damned murderers! We’ll fix you yet!"}
valley-of-fear	event_75_5	event	\N	McMurdo's arrest and acquittal increase his popularity among his fellows	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3403"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_6	event	\N	McMurdo joins the lodge and is brought before the magistrate the same night	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3404"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_7	event	\N	McMurdo earns a reputation among his fellows as a good boon companion, cheery reveller, and high-tempered man	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3405"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_8	event	\N	McMurdo impresses his comrades as capable of devising and carrying out a bloodthirsty scheme	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3406"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_9	event	\N	The oldsters say McMurdo will be the man for the clean job and wait to set him to work	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3407"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_10	event	\N	McGinty recognizes McMurdo as a supremely able instrument	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3408"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_11	event	\N	McGinty feels as if he holds a fierce bloodhound in leash	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3409", "sentence_3410"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_12	event	\N	A few lodge members, including Ted Baldwin, resent and hate McMurdo but keep clear of him	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3411"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_13	event	\N	Ettie Shafter's father refuses further contact with McMurdo and bars him from the house	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3412", "sentence_3413"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_14	event	\N	Ettie Shafter remains attached to McMurdo but warns herself against marriage to a man regarded as a criminal	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3414"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_15	event	\N	Ettie Shafter goes to McMurdo's house to see him	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3415", "sentence_3416"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_16	event	\N	McMurdo sits at a table with a letter in front of him in his sitting-room	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3417"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_17	event	\N	Ettie enters quietly and lays her hand on McMurdo's shoulders	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3418", "sentence_3419", "sentence_3420"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_18	event	\N	McMurdo turns on Ettie and reaches for her throat while crumpling the paper before him	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3421", "sentence_3422", "sentence_3423"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_75_19	event	\N	McMurdo stands glaring, then changes from ferocity to astonishment and joy	74	{"section": "section_75", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3424", "sentence_3425"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_76_1	event	\N	Jack greets Ettie and reaches out to her	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3426", "sentence_3427", "sentence_3428", "sentence_3429"], "communicatesContent": "It’s you! And to think that you should come to me, heart of my heart, and I should find nothing better to do than to want to strangle you! Come then, darling, let me make it up to you."}
valley-of-fear	event_76_2	event	\N	Ettie questions Jack about his fear and the letter	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3433", "sentence_3434", "sentence_3435", "sentence_3436", "sentence_3437", "sentence_3438", "sentence_3439", "sentence_3440", "sentence_3441", "sentence_3442", "sentence_3443", "sentence_3444", "sentence_3445", "sentence_3446", "sentence_3447"], "communicatesContent": "What’s come over you, Jack? Why were you so scared of me? Oh, Jack, if your conscience was at ease, you would not have looked at me like that! Let me see that letter you were writing. It’s to another woman. I know it! Why else should you hold it from me? Was it to your wife that you were writing? How am I to know that you are not a married man—you, a stranger, that nobody knows?"}
valley-of-fear	event_76_3	event	\N	Jack denies being married and explains that the letter is secret lodge business	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3448", "sentence_3449", "sentence_3450", "sentence_3451", "sentence_3453", "sentence_3454", "sentence_3455", "sentence_3456", "sentence_3457"], "communicatesContent": "I am not married, Ettie. See now, I swear it! You’re the only one woman on earth to me. By the cross of Christ I swear it! I’ll tell you, acushla. I’m under oath not to show it, and just as I wouldn’t break my word to you so I would keep it to those who hold my promise. It’s the business of the lodge, and even to you it’s secret. And if I was scared when a hand fell on me, can’t you understand it when it might have been the hand of a detective?"}
valley-of-fear	event_76_5	event	\N	Jack invites Ettie to sit beside him and speaks of her as his queen and lover	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3460", "sentence_3461", "sentence_3462", "sentence_3463"], "communicatesContent": "Sit here by me, then. It’s a queer throne for such a queen; but it’s the best your poor lover can find. He’ll do better for you some of these days, I’m thinking. Now your mind is easy once again, is it not?"}
valley-of-fear	event_76_6	event	\N	Ettie says Jack is a criminal among criminals and begs him to give it up	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3464", "sentence_3465", "sentence_3466", "sentence_3467", "sentence_3468", "sentence_3469", "sentence_3470", "sentence_3471", "sentence_3472", "sentence_3473", "sentence_3474", "sentence_3475", "sentence_3476", "sentence_3478"], "communicatesContent": "How can it ever be at ease, Jack, when I know that you are a criminal among criminals, when I never know the day that I may hear you are in court for murder? ‘McMurdo the Scowrer,’ that’s what one of our boarders called you yesterday. It went through my heart like a knife. But they were true. Give it up, Jack! For my sake, for God’s sake, give it up! It was to ask you that I came here to-day. Oh, Jack, see—I beg it of you on my bended knees! Kneeling here before you I implore you to give it up!"}
valley-of-fear	event_76_7	event	\N	Jack refuses to abandon the oath and the lodge	75	{"section": "section_76", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3479", "sentence_3480", "sentence_3481", "sentence_3482", "sentence_3483"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, my darlin’, you don’t know what it is you are asking. How could I give it up when it would be to break my oath and to desert my comrades? If you could see how things stand with me you could never ask it of me. Besides, if I wanted to, how could I do it? You don’t suppose that the lodge would let a man go free with all its secrets?"}
valley-of-fear	event_77_1	event	\N	Ettie says she has planned an escape with her father to a safer place	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3484", "sentence_3485", "sentence_3486", "sentence_3487", "sentence_3488", "sentence_3489"], "communicatesContent": "I’ve thought of that, Jack. I’ve planned it all. Father has saved some money. He is weary of this place where the fear of these people darkens our lives. He is ready to go. We would fly together to Philadelphia or New York, where we would be safe from them."}
valley-of-fear	event_77_2	event	\N	McMurdo laughs and warns that the lodge can reach distant places	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3490", "sentence_3491", "sentence_3492"], "communicatesContent": "The lodge has a long arm. Do you think it could not stretch from here to Philadelphia or New York?"}
valley-of-fear	event_77_3	event	\N	Ettie proposes leaving for the West, England, Germany, or anywhere beyond the valley	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3493"], "communicatesContent": "Well, then, to the West, or to England, or to Germany, where father came from—anywhere to get away from this Valley of Fear!"}
valley-of-fear	event_77_4	event	\N	McMurdo thinks of old Brother Morris	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3494"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_77_5	event	\N	McMurdo speaks about the valley being so named and the shadow on some people	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3495", "sentence_3496"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, it is the second time I have heard the valley so named. The shadow does indeed seem to lie heavy on some of you."}
valley-of-fear	event_77_6	event	\N	Ettie says the valley darkens their lives and mentions Ted Baldwin	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3497", "sentence_3498", "sentence_3499", "sentence_3500"], "communicatesContent": "It darkens every moment of our lives. Do you suppose that Ted Baldwin has ever forgiven us? If it were not that he fears you, what do you suppose our chances would be? If you saw the look in those dark, hungry eyes of his when they fall on me!"}
valley-of-fear	event_77_7	event	\N	McMurdo says he would punish Ted Baldwin if he caught him	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3501", "sentence_3502"], "communicatesContent": "By Gar! I’d teach him better manners if I caught him at it!"}
valley-of-fear	event_77_8	event	\N	McMurdo refuses to leave immediately but offers to try to arrange an honorable departure	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3503", "sentence_3504", "sentence_3505", "sentence_3506", "sentence_3507", "sentence_3508", "sentence_3509"], "communicatesContent": "But see here, little girl. I can’t leave here. I can’t—take that from me once and for all. But if you will leave me to find my own way, I will try to prepare a way of getting honourably out of it. Well, well, it’s just how you look at it. But if you’ll give me six months, I’ll work it so that I can leave without being ashamed to look others in the face."}
valley-of-fear	event_77_9	event	\N	Ettie reacts with joy and asks whether McMurdo's offer is a promise	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3510", "sentence_3511", "sentence_3512", "sentence_3513"], "communicatesContent": "Six months! Is it a promise?"}
valley-of-fear	event_77_10	event	\N	McMurdo says the departure may take seven or eight months but will happen within a year	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3514", "sentence_3515"], "communicatesContent": "Well, it may be seven or eight. But within a year at the furthest we will leave the valley behind us."}
valley-of-fear	event_77_11	event	\N	Ettie returns to her father's house more light-hearted	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3516", "sentence_3517", "sentence_3518"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_77_12	event	\N	McMurdo discovers that the organization is wider and more complex than the simple lodge	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3519"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_77_13	event	\N	McMurdo sees Evans Pott and notes his intimidating manner	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3521", "sentence_3522"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_79_11	event	\N	Some miners surge forward, but strangers fire over the crowd and the miners scatter	78	{"section": "section_79", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3581"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_79_12	event	\N	The murderous gang vanishes in the mists of morning	78	{"section": "section_79", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3582"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_175	lexical	\N	\N	174	{"text": "How did your mother take the matter?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
valley-of-fear	event_77_14	event	\N	Scanlan receives a note from McGinty enclosing a note from Evans Pott	76	{"section": "section_77", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3523", "sentence_3524", "sentence_3525"], "communicatesContent": "He is sending over two good men, Lawler and Andrews, who have instructions to act in the neighbourhood; though it is best for the cause that no particulars as to their objects should be given. Would the Bodymaster see to it that suitable arrangements be made for their lodgings and comfort until the time for action should arrive? It is impossible for anyone to remain secret at the Union House and, therefore, McMurdo and Scanlan should put the strangers up for a few days in their boarding house."}
valley-of-fear	event_78_1	event	\N	Lawler and Andrews arrive carrying gripsacks	77	{"section": "section_78", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3526"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_78_2	event	\N	Lawler and Andrews are described as elderly and youthful, respectively, and dressed in specific clothing	77	{"section": "section_78", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3527", "sentence_3528"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_78_3	event	\N	Lawler and Andrews are described as total abstainers and assassins for the society	77	{"section": "section_78", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3529", "sentence_3530"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_78_4	event	\N	Lawler explains why they were chosen	77	{"section": "section_78", "speakerId": "lawler", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3533", "sentence_3535"], "communicatesContent": "They chose us because neither I nor the boy here drink. They can count on us saying no more than we should. You must not take it amiss, but it is the orders of the County Delegate that we obey."}
valley-of-fear	event_78_5	event	\N	Scanlan speaks about past killings and keeping silent until the work is done	77	{"section": "section_78", "speakerId": "scanlan_lodge_341_vermissa", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3536", "sentence_3537", "sentence_3538"], "communicatesContent": "We are all in it together. That’s true enough, and we’ll talk till the cows come home of the killing of Charlie Williams or of Simon Bird, or any other job in the past. But till the work is done we say nothing."}
valley-of-fear	event_78_6	event	\N	McMurdo says he wants to speak to several people	77	{"section": "section_78", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3539"], "communicatesContent": "There are half a dozen about here that I have a word to say to."}
