valley-of-fear	event_82_9	event	\N	Rumours reach the lodge of secret gatherings in the Herald office and distribution of firearms among the law-abiding people	81	{"section": "section_82", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3696"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_82_10	event	\N	McMurdo leaves his house to attend the lodge	81	{"section": "section_82", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3703"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_82_11	event	\N	Morris comes to see McMurdo and speaks to him about a secret	81	{"section": "section_82", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3703", "sentence_3704", "sentence_3705", "sentence_3706", "sentence_3707", "sentence_3708", "sentence_3709", "sentence_3710", "sentence_3711", "sentence_3712", "sentence_3713", "sentence_3714", "sentence_3715", "sentence_3716"], "communicatesContent": "I can’t forget that I spoke my heart to you once, and that you kept it to yourself, even though the Boss himself came to ask you about it. I’ve a secret here, and it is just burning the life out of me. I wish it had come to any one of you but me. If I tell it, it will mean murder, for sure. If I don’t, it may bring the end of us all."}
valley-of-fear	event_83_5	event	\N	Morris drinks whisky and his face takes colour	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3722"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_83_6	event	\N	Morris tells McMurdo that a detective is on their trail	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3723", "sentence_3724"], "communicatesContent": "There’s a detective on our trail."}
valley-of-fear	event_83_7	event	\N	McMurdo stares at Morris in astonishment	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3725"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_83_8	event	\N	McMurdo calls Morris crazy and asks about police and detectives	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3726", "sentence_3727"], "communicatesContent": "Why, man, you’re crazy. Isn’t the place full of police and detectives and what harm did they ever do us?"}
valley-of-fear	event_83_9	event	\N	Morris explains that the detective is not a man of the district and asks about Pinkerton's	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3728", "sentence_3729", "sentence_3730"], "communicatesContent": "No, no, it’s no man of the district. As you say, we know them, and it is little that they can do. But you’ve heard of Pinkerton’s?"}
valley-of-fear	event_83_10	event	\N	McMurdo says he has read of some folk of that name	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3731"], "communicatesContent": "I’ve read of some folk of that name."}
valley-of-fear	event_83_11	event	\N	Morris warns that they have no chance if Pinkerton's are on their trail	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3732", "sentence_3733", "sentence_3734", "sentence_3735"], "communicatesContent": "Well, you can take it from me you’ve no show when they are on your trail. It’s not a take-it-or-miss-it government concern. It’s a dead earnest business proposition that’s out for results and keeps out till by hook or crook it gets them. If a Pinkerton man is deep in this business, we are all destroyed."}
valley-of-fear	event_83_12	event	\N	McMurdo says they must kill him	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3736"], "communicatesContent": "We must kill him."}
valley-of-fear	event_83_13	event	\N	Morris objects to identifying the man to be murdered and says it would end in murder	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3737", "sentence_3738", "sentence_3739", "sentence_3740", "sentence_3741", "sentence_3742", "sentence_3743", "sentence_3744", "sentence_3745"], "communicatesContent": "Ah, it’s the first thought that came to you! So it will be up at the lodge. Didn’t I say to you that it would end in murder? Sure, what is murder? Isn’t it common enough in these parts? It is, indeed; but it’s not for me to point out the man that is to be murdered. I’d never rest easy again. And yet it’s our own necks that may be at stake. In God’s name what shall I do?"}
valley-of-fear	event_83_14	event	\N	Morris rocks to and fro in indecision	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3746"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_83_15	event	\N	McMurdo is moved by Morris's words and grips his shoulder	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3747", "sentence_3748", "sentence_3749"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_83_16	event	\N	McMurdo urges Morris to give the facts and asks who the fellow is, where he is, how he heard of him, and why he came	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3750", "sentence_3751", "sentence_3752", "sentence_3753", "sentence_3754", "sentence_3755"], "communicatesContent": "See here, man, you won’t gain anything by sitting keening like an old wife at a wake. Let’s have the facts. Who is the fellow? Where is he? How did you hear of him? Why did you come to me?"}
valley-of-fear	event_83_17	event	\N	Morris explains why he came to McMurdo and gives the source of the letter	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "bodymaster_morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3756", "sentence_3757", "sentence_3758", "sentence_3759", "sentence_3760", "sentence_3761"], "communicatesContent": "I came to you; for you are the one man that would advise me. I told you that I had a store in the East before I came here. I left good friends behind me, and one of them is in the telegraph service. Here’s a letter that I had from him yesterday. It’s this part from the top of the page. You can read it yourself."}
valley-of-fear	event_83_18	event	\N	McMurdo reads the letter from Morris's friend	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3762", "sentence_3763", "sentence_3764", "sentence_3765", "sentence_3766", "sentence_3767", "sentence_3768", "sentence_3769", "sentence_3770", "sentence_3771", "sentence_3772", "sentence_3773"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_83_19	event	\N	McMurdo sits in silence holding the letter and then asks whether anyone else knows of it	82	{"section": "section_83", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3774", "sentence_3775", "sentence_3776", "sentence_3777"], "communicatesContent": "Does anyone else know of this?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_1	event	\N	Morris asks whether the man has any other person he would likely write to	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3779"], "communicatesContent": "But this man—your friend—has he any other person that he would be likely to write to?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_2	event	\N	McMurdo says the man likely knows one or two more	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3780"], "communicatesContent": "Well, I dare say he knows one or two more."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_3	event	\N	Morris asks whether the people are of the lodge	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3781"], "communicatesContent": "Of the lodge?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_4	event	\N	McMurdo says that is likely enough	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3782"], "communicatesContent": "It’s likely enough."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_5	event	\N	McMurdo explains that he asked because the man may have given a description of Birdy Edwards	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3783"], "communicatesContent": "I was asking because it is likely that he may have given some description of this fellow Birdy Edwards—then we could get on his trail."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_6	event	\N	McMurdo says it is possible but he should not think the man knew Birdy Edwards	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3784", "sentence_3785"], "communicatesContent": "Well, it’s possible. But I should not think he knew him."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_7	event	\N	McMurdo says the man is only telling him news that came by way of business	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3786"], "communicatesContent": "He is just telling me the news that came to him by way of business."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_8	event	\N	McMurdo asks how the man would know the Pinkerton man	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3787"], "communicatesContent": "How would he know this Pinkerton man?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_9	event	\N	McMurdo starts violently	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3788"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_84_10	event	\N	McMurdo says he has got him and asks Morris to leave the matter in his hands	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3789", "sentence_3790", "sentence_3795"], "communicatesContent": "By Gar! I’ve got him. What a fool I was not to know it. Lord! but we’re in luck! We will fix him before he can do any harm. See here, Morris, will you leave this thing in my hands?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_11	event	\N	Morris agrees to leave the matter in McMurdo's hands	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3796", "sentence_3802"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, if you will only take it off mine. It’s just what I would ask."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_12	event	\N	McMurdo says he will take responsibility and tells Morris to keep silent	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3797", "sentence_3798", "sentence_3799", "sentence_3800", "sentence_3801", "sentence_3803", "sentence_3804"], "communicatesContent": "I’ll do that. You can stand right back and let me run it. Even your name need not be mentioned. I’ll take it all on myself, as if it were to me that this letter has come. Will that content you? Then leave it at that and keep your head shut. Now I’ll get down to the lodge, and we’ll soon make old man Pinkerton sorry for himself."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_13	event	\N	Morris asks whether McMurdo would kill the man	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "morris", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3805"], "communicatesContent": "You wouldn’t kill this man?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_14	event	\N	McMurdo tells Morris not to ask questions and says he has hold of the matter	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3806", "sentence_3807", "sentence_3808"], "communicatesContent": "The less you know, Friend Morris, the easier your conscience will be, and the better you will sleep. Ask no questions, and let these things settle themselves. I have hold of it now."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_15	event	\N	Morris leaves sadly	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3809"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_84_16	event	\N	McMurdo says self-protection is no murder and that it is him or us	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3811", "sentence_3812", "sentence_3813", "sentence_3814"], "communicatesContent": "Self-protection is no murder, anyhow. It’s him or us. I guess this man would destroy us all if we left him long in the valley. Why, Brother Morris, we’ll have to elect you Bodymaster yet; for you’ve surely saved the lodge."}
valley-of-fear	event_84_17	event	\N	McMurdo destroys papers that would incriminate him	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3817"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_84_18	event	\N	McMurdo stops at Shafter's house and Ettie comes out to him	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3819", "sentence_3820"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_84_19	event	\N	Ettie says something has happened and that Jack is in danger	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3823", "sentence_3824", "sentence_3825"], "communicatesContent": "Something has happened! Oh, Jack, you are in danger!"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_20	event	\N	McMurdo says it may be wise to make a move before it is worse	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3826", "sentence_3827", "sentence_3828"], "communicatesContent": "Sure, it is not very bad, my sweetheart. And yet it may be wise that we make a move before it is worse. Make a move?"}
valley-of-fear	event_84_21	event	\N	McMurdo says he promised to go some day, had bad news, and sees trouble coming	83	{"section": "section_84", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3829", "sentence_3830", "sentence_3831", "sentence_3832", "sentence_3833", "sentence_3834", "sentence_3835", "sentence_3836"], "communicatesContent": "I promised you once that I would go some day. I think the time is coming. I had news to-night, bad news, and I see trouble coming. Well, a Pinkerton. But, sure, you wouldn’t know what that is, acushla, nor what it may mean to the likes of me. I’m too deep in this thing, and I may have to get out of it quick. You said you would come with me if I went."}
valley-of-fear	event_85_1	event	\N	Jack asks Ettie to trust him and promises not to harm her	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3838", "sentence_3839", "sentence_3840", "sentence_3841"], "communicatesContent": "I’m an honest man in some things, Ettie. I wouldn’t hurt a hair of your bonny head for all that the world can give, nor ever pull you down one inch from the golden throne above the clouds where I always see you. Would you trust me?"}
valley-of-fear	event_85_2	event	\N	Ettie places her hand in Jack's hand	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3841"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_85_3	event	\N	Jack orders Ettie to accompany him if he leaves	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3842", "sentence_3843", "sentence_3844", "sentence_3845", "sentence_3846", "sentence_3847"], "communicatesContent": "Well, then, listen to what I say, and do as I order you, for indeed it’s the only way for us. Things are going to happen in this valley. I feel it in my bones. There may be many of us that will have to look out for ourselves. I’m one, anyhow. If I go, by day or night, it’s you that must come with me!"}
valley-of-fear	event_85_4	event	\N	Ettie says she would come after Jack	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3848"], "communicatesContent": "I’d come after you, Jack."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_10	event	\N	McGinty asks what they have to fear and what Birdy Edwards can know of their affairs	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3896", "sentence_3897"], "communicatesContent": "What have we to fear, anyhow? What can he know of our affairs?"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_4	event	\N	Holmes answers that he had expected as much	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4276"], "communicatesContent": "I feared as much"}
valley-of-fear	event_85_5	event	\N	Jack insists Ettie must come with him and explains his plan to leave her until marriage	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3849", "sentence_3850", "sentence_3851", "sentence_3852", "sentence_3853"], "communicatesContent": "No, no, you shall come with me. If this valley is closed to me and I can never come back, how can I leave you behind, and me perhaps in hiding from the police with never a chance of a message? It’s with me you must come. I know a good woman in the place I come from, and it’s there I’d leave you till we can get married. Will you come?"}
valley-of-fear	event_85_6	event	\N	Ettie agrees to come with Jack	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3854"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, Jack, I will come."}
valley-of-fear	event_85_7	event	\N	Jack blesses Ettie and instructs her to go to the depot waiting room when signaled	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "jack", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3855", "sentence_3856", "sentence_3857"], "communicatesContent": "God bless you for your trust in me! It’s a fiend out of hell that I should be if I abused it. Now, mark you, Ettie, it will be just a word to you, and when it reaches you, you will drop everything and come right down to the waiting room at the depot and stay there till I come for you."}
valley-of-fear	event_85_8	event	\N	Ettie says she will come at the word	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "ettie_shafter", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3858"], "communicatesContent": "Day or night, I’ll come at the word, Jack."}
valley-of-fear	event_85_9	event	\N	McMurdo goes to the lodge	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3859"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_85_10	event	\N	McMurdo passes through lodge guards using signs and countersigns	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3860"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_85_11	event	\N	The lodge welcomes McMurdo	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3861"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_85_12	event	\N	McMurdo sees lodge leaders assembled in the crowded room	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3862", "sentence_3863"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_85_13	event	\N	The chairman speaks to McMurdo about business that needs judgment	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3864", "sentence_3865", "sentence_3866"], "communicatesContent": "Indeed, it’s glad we are to see you, Brother! There’s business here that wants a Solomon in judgment to set it right."}
valley-of-fear	event_85_14	event	\N	A neighbour explains the dispute over the head money for Crabbe's shooting	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3867", "sentence_3868"], "communicatesContent": "It’s Lander and Egan. They both claim the head money given by the lodge for the shooting of old man Crabbe over at Stylestown, and who’s to say which fired the bullet?"}
valley-of-fear	event_85_15	event	\N	McMurdo claims urgency before the lodge	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3869", "sentence_3870", "sentence_3871", "sentence_3872", "sentence_3873", "sentence_3874", "sentence_3875"], "communicatesContent": "Eminent Bodymaster, I claim urgency!"}
valley-of-fear	event_85_16	event	\N	McMurdo presents ill news to the lodge about a planned destruction campaign and a Pinkerton detective in the valley	84	{"section": "section_85", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3876", "sentence_3877", "sentence_3878", "sentence_3879"], "communicatesContent": "Eminent Bodymaster and Brethren, I am the bearer of ill news this day; but it is better that it should be known and discussed, than that a blow should fall upon us without warning which would destroy us all. I have information that the most powerful and richest organizations in this state have bound themselves together for our destruction, and that at this very moment there is a Pinkerton detective, one Birdy Edwards, at work in the valley collecting the evidence which may put a rope round the necks of many of us, and send every man in this room into a felon’s cell. That is the situation for the discussion of which I have made a claim of urgency."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_1	event	\N	The chairman breaks the dead silence in the room	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3880", "sentence_3881"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_86_2	event	\N	The chairman asks McMurdo for his evidence	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3882", "sentence_3883"], "communicatesContent": "What is your evidence for this, Brother McMurdo?"}
valley-of-fear	event_86_3	event	\N	McMurdo says the evidence is in a letter that has come into his hands	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3884"], "communicatesContent": "It is in this letter which has come into my hands."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_4	event	\N	McMurdo reads the passage from the letter aloud	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3885", "sentence_3886", "sentence_3887"], "communicatesContent": "It is a matter of honour with me that I can give no further particulars about the letter, nor put it into your hands; but I assure you that there is nothing else in it which can affect the interests of the lodge. I put the case before you as it has reached me."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_5	event	\N	An older brother says Birdy Edwards has the reputation of being the best man in the Pinkerton service	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3888"], "communicatesContent": "I have heard of Birdy Edwards, and that he has the name of being the best man in the Pinkerton service."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_6	event	\N	McGinty asks whether anyone knows Birdy Edwards by sight	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3889", "sentence_3890"], "communicatesContent": "Does anyone know him by sight?"}
valley-of-fear	event_86_7	event	\N	McMurdo says that he knows Birdy Edwards by sight	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3891"], "communicatesContent": "I do."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_8	event	\N	The hall reacts with astonishment	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3892"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_86_9	event	\N	McMurdo says they can hold Birdy Edwards in their power and act quickly to end the matter	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3893", "sentence_3894", "sentence_3895"], "communicatesContent": "I believe we hold him in the hollow of our hands. If we act quickly and wisely, we can cut this thing short. If I have your confidence and your help, it is little that we have to fear."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_11	event	\N	McMurdo warns that Birdy Edwards has capitalist backing, may buy weaker brethren, and may already have their secrets	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3898", "sentence_3899", "sentence_3900", "sentence_3901", "sentence_3902"], "communicatesContent": "You might say so if all were as stanch as you, Councillor. But this man has all the millions of the capitalists at his back. Do you think there is no weaker brother among all our lodges that could not be bought? He will get at our secrets—maybe has got them already. There’s only one sure cure."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_12	event	\N	Baldwin says Birdy Edwards must never leave the valley	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "ted_baldwin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3903"], "communicatesContent": "That he never leaves the valley."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_13	event	\N	McMurdo approves Baldwin’s suggestion	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3904", "sentence_3905", "sentence_3906"], "communicatesContent": "Good for you, Brother Baldwin. You and I have had our differences, but you have said the true word to-night."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_14	event	\N	McMurdo says the matter is too vital to discuss in open lodge and proposes a committee	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3909", "sentence_3910", "sentence_3911", "sentence_3912"], "communicatesContent": "I would put it to you that this is too vital a thing for us to discuss in open lodge. God forbid that I should throw a doubt on anyone here; but if so much as a word of gossip got to the ears of this man, there would be an end of any chance of our getting him. I would ask the lodge to choose a trusty committee, Mr. Chairman—yourself, if I might suggest it, and Brother Baldwin here, and five more. Then I can talk freely of what I know and of what I advise should be done."}
valley-of-fear	event_86_15	event	\N	The lodge adopts the proposition and chooses a committee	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3913", "sentence_3914"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_86_16	event	\N	The lodge’s revelry becomes short and subdued and the men break up early	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3915", "sentence_3916", "sentence_3917"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_86_17	event	\N	McGinty and McMurdo speak alone after the others leave	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3918", "sentence_3919", "sentence_3920"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_86_18	event	\N	McMurdo explains that Birdy Edwards is not present under that name and is lodging at Hobson’s Patch as Steve Wilson	85	{"section": "section_86", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3921", "sentence_3922", "sentence_3923", "sentence_3924"], "communicatesContent": "I said just now that I knew Birdy Edwards. I need not tell you that he is not here under that name. He’s a brave man, but not a crazy one. He passes under the name of Steve Wilson, and he is lodging at Hobson’s Patch."}
valley-of-fear	event_87_1	event	\N	A man tells how he met another man on the cars and took him for a reporter	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3926", "sentence_3928", "sentence_3929", "sentence_3930", "sentence_3931", "sentence_3932", "sentence_3933", "sentence_3934", "sentence_3935", "sentence_3936"], "communicatesContent": "Because I fell into talk with him. I met him on the cars when I went down the line on Wednesday. He said he was a reporter. Wanted to know all he could about the Scowrers and what he called the outrages for a New York paper. He paid me twenty dollars for information and offered ten times that if I could find more."}
valley-of-fear	event_87_2	event	\N	A man says he gave the other man false information	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3937", "sentence_3938"], "communicatesContent": "Any stuff I could make up."}
valley-of-fear	event_87_3	event	\N	A man explains how he later saw the other man at the telegraph bureau	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3940", "sentence_3941", "sentence_3942", "sentence_3944", "sentence_3945", "sentence_3946", "sentence_3947", "sentence_3948"], "communicatesContent": "He got out at Hobson's Patch, and so did I. I chanced into the telegraph bureau, and he was leaving it. He had filled the form with stuff that might have been Chinese. The clerk said he fired a sheet of this off every day. I said it was special news for his paper, and he was scared that the others should tap it."}
valley-of-fear	event_87_4	event	\N	McGinty agrees that the suspicion is right and asks what should be done	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3949", "sentence_3950", "sentence_3951"], "communicatesContent": "By Gar! I believe you are right. But what do you allow that we should do about it?"}
valley-of-fear	event_87_5	event	\N	Someone suggests going at once to attack the man	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3952", "sentence_3953", "sentence_3954"], "communicatesContent": "Why not go right down now and fix him?"}
valley-of-fear	event_87_6	event	\N	McMurdo says he would leave at once if he knew where to find him	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3955", "sentence_3956", "sentence_3957"], "communicatesContent": "I'd start this next minute if I knew where we could find him. He's in Hobson's Patch; but I don't know the house. I've got a plan, though, if you'll only take my advice."}
valley-of-fear	event_87_7	event	\N	McMurdo describes a plan to lure the man to Widow MacNamara's house	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3958", "sentence_3959", "sentence_3960", "sentence_3961", "sentence_3962", "sentence_3963", "sentence_3964", "sentence_3965", "sentence_3966", "sentence_3967", "sentence_3968", "sentence_3969", "sentence_3970", "sentence_3971", "sentence_3972", "sentence_3973", "sentence_3974", "sentence_3975", "sentence_3976"], "communicatesContent": "I'll go to the Patch tomorrow morning. I'll find him through the operator. Then I'll tell him that I'm a Freeman myself. I'll offer him all the secrets of the lodge for a price. I'll tell him the papers are at my house, and that it's as much as my life would be worth to let him come while folk were about. Let him come at ten o'clock at night, and he shall see everything. Widow MacNamara's is a lonely house. She's as true as steel and as deaf as a post. There's only Scanlan and me in the house. If I get his promise, I'd have the whole seven of you come to me by nine o'clock. We’ll get him in. If ever he gets out alive, he can talk of Birdy Edwards's luck for the rest of his days."}
valley-of-fear	event_94_3	event	\N	Cecil Barker arrives and reports bad news to Holmes	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4273", "sentence_4275"], "communicatesContent": "I’ve had bad news—terrible news, Mr. Holmes"}
a-case-of-identity	section_13	section	\N	Section 13	12	{"wordCount": 162}
valley-of-fear	event_87_8	event	\N	McGinty agrees to wait until the next night	86	{"section": "section_87", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3977", "sentence_3978", "sentence_3979", "sentence_3980"], "communicatesContent": "There’s going to be a vacancy at Pinkerton's or I’m mistaken. Leave it at that, McMurdo. At nine tomorrow we’ll be with you. You once get the door shut behind him, and you can leave the rest with us."}
valley-of-fear	event_88_1	event	\N	Conspirators plan to question a detective once he is in their power	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3982", "sentence_3984", "sentence_3988", "sentence_3989", "sentence_3990"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_88_2	event	\N	McMurdo goes to Hobson’s Patch as agreed	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3991"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_88_3	event	\N	Captain Marvin addresses McMurdo at the station	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "captain_marvin", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3992"], "communicatesContent": "(not specified)"}
valley-of-fear	event_88_4	event	\N	McMurdo refuses to speak with Captain Marvin	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3993"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_88_5	event	\N	McMurdo meets McGinty at the Union House and tells him that someone is coming	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_3994", "sentence_3995", "sentence_3996", "sentence_3997"], "communicatesContent": "He is coming."}
valley-of-fear	event_88_6	event	\N	McGinty asks whether the man knows much	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4001", "sentence_4002"], "communicatesContent": "Do you reckon he knows much?"}
valley-of-fear	event_88_7	event	\N	McMurdo answers that the man has been there about six weeks and may have passed on results	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4003", "sentence_4004", "sentence_4005", "sentence_4006"], "communicatesContent": "He’s been here some time—six weeks at the least. I guess he didn’t come into these parts to look at the prospect. If he has been working among us all that time with the railroad money at his back, I should expect that he has got results, and that he has passed them on."}
valley-of-fear	event_88_8	event	\N	McGinty proposes sending men to beat Morris and question him	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4007", "sentence_4008", "sentence_4009", "sentence_4010", "sentence_4011", "sentence_4012", "sentence_4013"], "communicatesContent": "If any man gives us away, it would be he. I’ve a mind to send a couple of the boys round before evening to give him a beating up and see what they can get from him."}
valley-of-fear	event_88_9	event	\N	McMurdo agrees that there would be no harm in that	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4014", "sentence_4015", "sentence_4016", "sentence_4017"], "communicatesContent": "Well, there would be no harm in that."}
valley-of-fear	event_88_10	event	\N	McGinty declares that he will fix Morris and has watched him for a year	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "bodymaster_mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4018", "sentence_4019", "sentence_4020"], "communicatesContent": "I’ll fix the old devil! I’ve had my eye on him this year past."}
valley-of-fear	event_88_11	event	\N	McMurdo says the beating must wait until tomorrow and the Pinkerton affair is settled	87	{"section": "section_88", "speakerId": "mc_murdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4021", "sentence_4022", "sentence_4023"], "communicatesContent": "But whatever you do must be to-morrow; for we must lie low until the Pinkerton affair is settled up. We can’t afford to set the police buzzing, to-day of all days."}
valley-of-fear	event_89_1	event	\N	McMurdo says Birdy Edwards will be given fake papers after he sees all of McMurdo's papers	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4028", "sentence_4029", "sentence_4030", "sentence_4031", "sentence_4032", "sentence_4033", "sentence_4034"], "communicatesContent": "I guess I took him on his weak point. If he could get on a good trail of the Scowrers, he’s ready to follow it into hell. I took his money and as much more when he has seen all my papers. What papers? Well, there are no papers. But I filled him up about constitutions and books of rules and forms of membership. He expects to get right down to the end of everything before he leaves."}
valley-of-fear	event_89_2	event	\N	McGinty says Birdy Edwards is right about wanting to get to the end of everything	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4035"], "communicatesContent": "Faith, he’s right there."}
valley-of-fear	event_89_3	event	\N	McMurdo says Captain Marvin spoke to him at the depot that day	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4036", "sentence_4037", "sentence_4038"], "communicatesContent": "As if I would carry such things, and me a suspected man, and Captain Marvin after speaking to me this very day at the depot!"}
valley-of-fear	event_89_4	event	\N	McGinty says the burden of the plan is falling on McMurdo and identifies a location obstacle	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4039", "sentence_4040"], "communicatesContent": "I guess the heavy end of this business is coming on to you. We could put him down an old shaft when we’ve done with him; but however we work it we can’t get past the man living at Hobson’s Patch and you being there to-day."}
valley-of-fear	event_89_5	event	\N	McMurdo says they can prevent proof of the killing	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4041", "sentence_4042", "sentence_4043", "sentence_4044", "sentence_4045", "sentence_4046", "sentence_4047", "sentence_4048", "sentence_4049", "sentence_4050"], "communicatesContent": "If we handle it right, they can never prove the killing. No one can see him come to the house after dark, and I’ll lay to it that no one will see him go. Now see here, Councillor, I’ll show you my plan and I’ll ask you to fit the others into it. You will all come in good time. Very well. He comes at ten. He is to tap three times, and me to open the door for him. Then I’ll get behind him and shut it. He’s our man then."}
valley-of-fear	event_93_21	event	\N	Holmes writes to the wife to get her husband out of England at any cost	92	{"section": "section_93", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4260", "sentence_4261", "sentence_4262"], "communicatesContent": "Get him out of England at any cost. There are forces here which may be more dangerous than those he has escaped. There is no safety for your husband in England."}
valley-of-fear	event_94_1	event	\N	An enigmatic note is slipped into the letter box	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4264"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_89_6	event	\N	McMurdo describes the next step of the ambush and the risk of shooting	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4051", "sentence_4052", "sentence_4053", "sentence_4054", "sentence_4055", "sentence_4056", "sentence_4057", "sentence_4058", "sentence_4059", "sentence_4060"], "communicatesContent": "That’s all easy and plain. Yes; but the next step wants considering. He’s a hard proposition. He’s heavily armed. I’ve fooled him proper, and yet he is likely to be on his guard. Suppose I show him right into a room with seven men in it where he expected to find me alone. There is going to be shooting, and somebody is going to be hurt. That’s so. And the noise is going to bring every damned copper in the township on top of it. I guess you are right."}
valley-of-fear	event_89_7	event	\N	McMurdo explains how he will lure Birdy Edwards into the parlour and seize his pistol arm	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcmurdo", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4061", "sentence_4062", "sentence_4063", "sentence_4064", "sentence_4065", "sentence_4066", "sentence_4067", "sentence_4068", "sentence_4069"], "communicatesContent": "This is how I should work it. You will all be in the big room—same as you saw when you had a chat with me. I’ll open the door for him, show him into the parlour beside the door, and leave him there while I get the papers. That will give me the chance of telling you how things are shaping. Then I will go back to him with some faked papers. As he is reading them I will jump for him and get my grip on his pistol arm. You’ll hear me call and in you will rush. The quicker the better; for he is as strong a man as I, and I may have more than I can manage. But I allow that I can hold him till you come."}
valley-of-fear	event_89_8	event	\N	McGinty approves the plan and says the lodge will owe McMurdo a debt	88	{"section": "section_89", "speakerId": "mcginty", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4070", "sentence_4071", "sentence_4072", "sentence_4073"], "communicatesContent": "It’s a good plan. The lodge will owe you a debt for this. I guess when I move out of the chair I can put a name to the man that’s coming after me."}
valley-of-fear	event_90_1	event	\N	McMurdo prepares a revolver for the evening	89	{"section": "section_90", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4074", "sentence_4075"], "communicatesContent": null}
