valley-of-fear	event_94_5	event	\N	Barker asks whether Holmes has had a cable	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4277"], "communicatesContent": "You have not had a cable, have you?"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_6	event	\N	Holmes says he has had a note from someone who has had a cable	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4278"], "communicatesContent": "I have had a note from someone who has"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_7	event	\N	Barker identifies Douglas and says they started for South Africa on the Palmyra	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4279", "sentence_4281"], "communicatesContent": "It’s poor Douglas. They tell me his name is Edwards; but he will always be Jack Douglas of Benito Canyon to me. I told you that they started together for South Africa in the Palmyra three weeks ago."}
valley-of-fear	event_94_8	event	\N	Barker reports that the ship reached Cape Town and reads Mrs. Douglas's cable	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4283", "sentence_4284", "sentence_4285", "sentence_4286", "sentence_4287"], "communicatesContent": "The ship reached Cape Town last night. I received this cable from Mrs. Douglas this morning: Jack has been lost overboard in gale off St. Helena. No one knows how accident occurred. IVY DOUGLAS."}
valley-of-fear	event_94_9	event	\N	Holmes states that the report was stage-managed and that Jack Douglas was murdered	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4289", "sentence_4291", "sentence_4293", "sentence_4294", "sentence_4295"], "communicatesContent": "It came like that, did it? Well, I’ve no doubt it was well stage-managed. None in the world. Surely!"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_10	event	\N	Barker agrees that Jack Douglas was murdered	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4296"], "communicatesContent": "So I think also"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_11	event	\N	Holmes rejects the Scowrers as the perpetrators and points to Moriarty	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4297", "sentence_4298", "sentence_4299", "sentence_4300", "sentence_4301", "sentence_4302", "sentence_4303"], "communicatesContent": "No, no, my good sir. There is a master hand here. It is no case of sawed-off shotguns and clumsy six-shooters. You can tell an old master by the sweep of his brush. I can tell a Moriarty when I see one. This crime is from London, not from America."}
valley-of-fear	event_94_12	event	\N	Barker asks about the motive	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4304"], "communicatesContent": "But for what motive?"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_13	event	\N	Holmes explains that the crime was done by a man who cannot afford to fail and that a great brain and organization were used to destroy one man	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4305", "sentence_4306", "sentence_4307"], "communicatesContent": "Because it is done by a man who cannot afford to fail, one whose whole unique position depends upon the fact that all he does must succeed. A great brain and a huge organization have been turned to the extinction of one man. It is crushing the nut with the triphammer—an absurd extravagance of energy—but the nut is very effectually crushed all the same."}
valley-of-fear	event_94_14	event	\N	Barker asks how the man came to have anything to do with it	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4308"], "communicatesContent": "How came this man to have anything to do with it?"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_15	event	\N	Holmes says the first word of the business came from one of Moriarty's lieutenants and describes the criminal method	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4309", "sentence_4310", "sentence_4311", "sentence_4312", "sentence_4313", "sentence_4314", "sentence_4315", "sentence_4316", "sentence_4317"], "communicatesContent": "I can only say that the first word that ever came to us of the business was from one of his lieutenants. These Americans were well advised. Having an English job to do, they took into partnership, as any foreign criminal could do, this great consultant in crime. From that moment their man was doomed. At first he would content himself by using his machinery in order to find their victim. Then he would indicate how the matter might be treated. Finally, when he read in the reports of the failure of this agent, he would step in himself with a master touch. You heard me warn this man at Birlstone Manor House that the coming danger was greater than the past. Was I right?"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_16	event	\N	Barker strikes his head with his clenched fist in anger	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4318"], "communicatesContent": null}
valley-of-fear	event_94_17	event	\N	Barker asks whether they must accept the situation	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "cecil_barker", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4319", "sentence_4320"], "communicatesContent": "Do not tell me that we have to sit down under this? Do you say that no one can ever get level with this king devil?"}
valley-of-fear	event_94_18	event	\N	Holmes says the man can be beaten but asks for time	93	{"section": "section_94", "speakerId": "holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4321", "sentence_4322", "sentence_4323"], "communicatesContent": "No, I don’t say that. I don’t say that he can’t be beat. But you must give me time—you must give me time!"}
valley-of-fear	event_95_1	event	\N	They sit in silence for some minutes	94	{"section": "section_95", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4324"], "communicatesContent": null}
