a-case-of-identity	sentence_1	lexical	\N	\N	0	{"text": "y dear fellow,” said Sherlock Holmes as we sat on either side of the ﬁre in his lodgings at Baker Street, “life is inﬁnitely stranger than anything which the mind of man could invent.", "section": "section_1", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_2	lexical	\N	\N	1	{"text": "We would not dare to conceive the things which are really mere commonplaces of existence.", "section": "section_1", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_3	lexical	\N	\N	2	{"text": "If we could ﬂy out of that window hand in hand, hover over this great city, gently remove the roofs, and peep in at the queer things which are going on, the strange coincidences, the plannings, the cross-purposes, the wonderful chains of events, working through generations, and leading to the most outr´e results, it would make all ﬁction with its con- ventionalities and foreseen conclusions most stale and unproﬁtable.”", "section": "section_1", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_4	lexical	\N	\N	3	{"text": "“And yet I am not convinced of it,” I answered.", "section": "section_1", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_5	lexical	\N	\N	4	{"text": "“The cases which come to light in the papers are, as a rule, bald enough, and vulgar enough.", "section": "section_1", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_6	lexical	\N	\N	5	{"text": "We have in our police reports realism pushed to its extreme lim- its, and yet the result is, it must be confessed, neither fascinating nor artistic.”", "section": "section_1", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_7	lexical	\N	\N	6	{"text": "“A certain selection and discretion must be used in producing a realistic effect,” remarked Holmes.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_8	lexical	\N	\N	7	{"text": "“This is wanting in the police report, where more stress is laid, perhaps, upon the platitudes of the magistrate than upon the details, which to an observer contain the vital essence of the whole matter.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_9	lexical	\N	\N	8	{"text": "Depend upon it, there is nothing so unnatural as the commonplace.”", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_10	lexical	\N	\N	9	{"text": "I smiled and shook my head.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_11	lexical	\N	\N	10	{"text": "“I can quite un- derstand your thinking so.”", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_12	lexical	\N	\N	11	{"text": "I said.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_13	lexical	\N	\N	12	{"text": "“Of course, in your position of unofﬁcial adviser and helper to ev- erybody who is absolutely puzzled, throughout three continents, you are brought in contact with all that is strange and bizarre.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_14	lexical	\N	\N	13	{"text": "But here”—I picked up the morning paper from the ground—“let us put it to a practical test.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_15	lexical	\N	\N	14	{"text": "Here is the ﬁrst heading upon which I come.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_16	lexical	\N	\N	15	{"text": "‘A husband’s cruelty to his wife.’", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_17	lexical	\N	\N	16	{"text": "There is half a column of print, but I know without reading it that it is all perfectly familiar to me.", "section": "section_2", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_18	lexical	\N	\N	17	{"text": "There is, of course, the other woman, the drink, the push, the blow, the bruise, the sympathetic sister or landlady.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_19	lexical	\N	\N	18	{"text": "The crudest of writers could invent nothing more crude.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_20	lexical	\N	\N	19	{"text": "“Indeed, your example is an unfortunate one for your argument,” said Holmes, taking the paper and glancing his eye down it.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_21	lexical	\N	\N	20	{"text": "“This is the Dundas sep- aration case, and, as it happens, I was engaged in clearing up some small points in connection with it.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_22	lexical	\N	\N	21	{"text": "The husband was a teetotaler, there was no other woman, and the conduct complained of was that he had drifted into the habit of winding up every meal by taking out his false teeth and hurling them at his wife, which, you will allow, is not an action likely to occur to the imagination of the average story-teller.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_23	lexical	\N	\N	22	{"text": "Take a pinch of snuff, Doctor, and acknowledge that I have scored over you in your example.”", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_24	lexical	\N	\N	23	{"text": "He held out his snuffbox of old gold, with a great amethyst in the centre of the lid.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_25	lexical	\N	\N	24	{"text": "Its splendour was in such contrast to his homely ways and simple life that I could not help commenting upon it.", "section": "section_3", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_26	lexical	\N	\N	25	{"text": "“Ah,” said he, “I forgot that I had not seen you for some weeks.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_27	lexical	\N	\N	26	{"text": "It is a little souvenir from the King of Bohemia in return for my assistance in the case of the Irene Adler papers.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_28	lexical	\N	\N	27	{"text": "“And the ring?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_29	lexical	\N	\N	28	{"text": "I asked, glancing at a remarkable brilliant which sparkled upon his ﬁnger.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_30	lexical	\N	\N	29	{"text": "“It was from the reigning family of Holland, though the matter in which I served them was of such delicacy that I cannot conﬁde it even to you, who have been good enough to chronicle one or two of my little problems.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_31	lexical	\N	\N	30	{"text": "“And have you any on hand just now?”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_32	lexical	\N	\N	31	{"text": "I asked with interest.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_33	lexical	\N	\N	32	{"text": "“Some ten or twelve, but none which present any feature of interest.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_34	lexical	\N	\N	33	{"text": "They are important, you under- stand, without being interesting.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_35	lexical	\N	\N	34	{"text": "Indeed, I have found that it is usually in unimportant matters that there is a ﬁeld for the observation, and for the quick analysis of cause and effect which gives the charm to an inves- tigation.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_36	lexical	\N	\N	35	{"text": "The larger crimes are apt to be the simpler, for the bigger the crime the more obvious, as a rule, is the motive.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_37	lexical	\N	\N	36	{"text": "In these cases, save for one rather intricate matter which has been referred to me from Marseilles, there is nothing which presents any features of inter- est.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_38	lexical	\N	\N	37	{"text": "It is possible, however, that I may have something better before very many minutes are over, for this is one of my clients, or I am much mistaken.”", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_39	lexical	\N	\N	38	{"text": "He had risen from his chair and was standing be- tween the parted blinds gazing down into the dull neutral-tinted London street.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_40	lexical	\N	\N	39	{"text": "Looking over his shoul- der, I saw that on the pavement opposite there stood a large woman with a heavy fur boa round her neck, and a large curling red feather in a broad-brimmed hat which was tilted in a coquettish Duchess of De- vonshire fashion over her ear.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_41	lexical	\N	\N	40	{"text": "From under this great panoply she peeped up in a nervous, hesitating fash- ion at our windows, while her body oscillated back- ward and forward, and her ﬁngers ﬁdgeted with her glove buttons.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_42	lexical	\N	\N	41	{"text": "Suddenly, with a plunge, as of the swimmer who leaves the bank, she hurried across the road, and we heard the sharp clang of the bell.", "section": "section_4", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_43	lexical	\N	\N	42	{"text": "“I have seen those symptoms before,” said Holmes, throwing his cigarette into the ﬁre.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_44	lexical	\N	\N	43	{"text": "“Oscillation upon the pavement always means an affaire de coeur .", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_45	lexical	\N	\N	44	{"text": "She would like advice, but is not sure that the matter is not too delicate for communication.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_46	lexical	\N	\N	45	{"text": "And yet even here we may discriminate.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_47	lexical	\N	\N	46	{"text": "When a woman has been seriously wronged by a man she no longer oscillates, and the usual symptom is a broken bell wire.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_48	lexical	\N	\N	47	{"text": "Here we may take it that there is a love matter, but that the maiden is not so much angry as perplexed, or grieved.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_49	lexical	\N	\N	48	{"text": "But here she comes in person to resolve our doubts.”", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_50	lexical	\N	\N	49	{"text": "As he spoke there was a tap at the door, and the boy in buttons entered to announce Miss Mary Suther- land, while the lady herself loomed behind his small black ﬁgure like a full-sailed merchant-man behind a tiny pilot boat.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_51	lexical	\N	\N	50	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes welcomed her with the easy courtesy for which he was remarkable, and, having closed the door and bowed her into an armchair, he looked her over in the minute and yet abstracted fashion which was peculiar to him.", "section": "section_5", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_52	lexical	\N	\N	51	{"text": "“Do you not ﬁnd,” he said, “that with your short sight it is a little trying to do so much typewriting?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_53	lexical	\N	\N	52	{"text": "“I did at ﬁrst,” she answered, “but now I know where the letters are without looking.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_54	lexical	\N	\N	53	{"text": "Then, sud- denly realising the full purport of his words, she gave a violent start and looked up, with fear and astonish- ment upon her broad, good-humoured face.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_55	lexical	\N	\N	54	{"text": "“You’ve heard about me, Mr. Holmes,” she cried, “else how could you know all that?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_56	lexical	\N	\N	55	{"text": "“Never mind,” said Holmes, laughing; “it is my business to know things.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_57	lexical	\N	\N	56	{"text": "Perhaps I have trained my- self to see what others overlook.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_58	lexical	\N	\N	57	{"text": "If not, why should you come to consult me?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_59	lexical	\N	\N	58	{"text": "“I came to you, sir, because I heard of you from Mrs. Etherege, whose husband you found so easy when the police and everyone had given him up for dead.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_60	lexical	\N	\N	59	{"text": "Oh, Mr. Holmes, I wish you would do as much for me.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_61	lexical	\N	\N	60	{"text": "I’m not rich, but still I have a hundred a year in my own right, besides the little that I make by the machine, and I would give it all to know what has become of Mr. Hosmer Angel.”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_62	lexical	\N	\N	61	{"text": "“Why did you come away to consult me in such a hurry?”", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_63	lexical	\N	\N	62	{"text": "asked Sherlock Holmes, with his ﬁnger-tips together and his eyes to the ceiling.", "section": "section_6", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_64	lexical	\N	\N	63	{"text": "Again a startled look came over the somewhat vac- uous face of Miss Mary Sutherland.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_65	lexical	\N	\N	64	{"text": "“Yes, I did bang out of the house,” she said, “for it made me angry to see the easy way in which Mr. Windibank—that is, my father—took it all.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_66	lexical	\N	\N	65	{"text": "He would not go to the police, and he would not go to you, and so at last, as he would do nothing and kept on saying that there was no harm done, it made me mad, and I just on with my things and came right away to you.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_67	lexical	\N	\N	66	{"text": "“Your father,” said Holmes, “your stepfather, surely, since the name is different.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_68	lexical	\N	\N	67	{"text": "“Yes, my stepfather.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_69	lexical	\N	\N	68	{"text": "I call him father, though it sounds funny, too, for he is only ﬁve years and two months older than myself.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_70	lexical	\N	\N	69	{"text": "“And your mother is alive?”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_71	lexical	\N	\N	70	{"text": "“Oh, yes, mother is alive and well.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_72	lexical	\N	\N	71	{"text": "I wasn’t best pleased, Mr. Holmes, when she married again so soon after father’s death, and a man who was nearly ﬁfteen years younger than herself.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_73	lexical	\N	\N	72	{"text": "Father was a plumber in the Tottenham Court Road, and he left a tidy business behind him, which mother carried on with Mr. Hardy, the foreman; but when Mr. Windibank came he made her sell the business, for he was very superior, being a traveller in wines.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_74	lexical	\N	\N	73	{"text": "They got £4700 for the goodwill and interest, which wasn’t near as much as father could have got if he had been alive.”", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_75	lexical	\N	\N	74	{"text": "I had expected to see Sherlock Holmes impatient under this rambling and inconsequential narrative, but, on the contrary, he had listened with the greatest concentration of attention.", "section": "section_7", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_76	lexical	\N	\N	75	{"text": "“Your own little income,” he asked, “does it come out of the business?”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_77	lexical	\N	\N	76	{"text": "“Oh, no, sir.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_78	lexical	\N	\N	77	{"text": "It is quite separate and was left me by my uncle Ned in Auckland.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_79	lexical	\N	\N	78	{"text": "It is in New Zealand stock, paying 41/2 per cent.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_80	lexical	\N	\N	79	{"text": "Two thousand ﬁve hun- dred pounds was the amount, but I can only touch the interest.”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_81	lexical	\N	\N	80	{"text": "“You interest me extremely,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_82	lexical	\N	\N	81	{"text": "“And since you draw so large a sum as a hundred a year, with what you earn into the bargain, you no doubt travel a little and indulge yourself in every way.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_83	lexical	\N	\N	82	{"text": "I believe that a single lady can get on very nicely upon an income of about £60.”", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_84	lexical	\N	\N	83	{"text": "“I could do with much less than that, Mr. Holmes, but you understand that as long as I live at home I don’t wish to be a burden to them, and so they have the use of the money just while I am staying with them.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_85	lexical	\N	\N	84	{"text": "Of course, that is only just for the time.", "section": "section_8", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_86	lexical	\N	\N	85	{"text": "Mr. Windibank draws my interest every quarter and pays it over to mother, and I ﬁnd that I can do pretty well with what I earn at typewriting.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_87	lexical	\N	\N	86	{"text": "It brings me twopence a sheet, and I can often do from ﬁfteen to twenty sheets in a day.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_88	lexical	\N	\N	87	{"text": "“You have made your position very clear to me,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_89	lexical	\N	\N	88	{"text": "“This is my friend, Dr. Watson, be- fore whom you can speak as freely as before myself.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_90	lexical	\N	\N	89	{"text": "Kindly tell us now all about your connection with Mr.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_91	lexical	\N	\N	90	{"text": "Hosmer Angel.”", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_92	lexical	\N	\N	91	{"text": "A ﬂush stole over Miss Sutherland’s face, and she picked nervously at the fringe of her jacket.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_93	lexical	\N	\N	92	{"text": "“I met him ﬁrst at the gasﬁtters’ ball,” she said.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_94	lexical	\N	\N	93	{"text": "“They used to send father tickets when he was alive, and then afterwards they remembered us, and sent them to mother.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_95	lexical	\N	\N	94	{"text": "Mr. Windibank did not wish us to go.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_96	lexical	\N	\N	95	{"text": "He never did wish us to go anywhere.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_97	lexical	\N	\N	96	{"text": "He would get quite mad if I wanted so much as to join a Sunday- school treat.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_98	lexical	\N	\N	97	{"text": "But this time I was set on going, and I would go; for what right had he to prevent?", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_99	lexical	\N	\N	98	{"text": "He said the folk were not ﬁt for us to know, when all father’s friends were to be there.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_100	lexical	\N	\N	99	{"text": "And he said that I had nothing ﬁt to wear, when I had my purple plush that I had never so much as taken out of the drawer.", "section": "section_9", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_101	lexical	\N	\N	100	{"text": "At last, when nothing else would do, he went off to France upon the business of the ﬁrm, but we went, mother and I, with Mr. Hardy, who used to be our foreman, and it was there I met Mr. Hosmer Angel.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_102	lexical	\N	\N	101	{"text": "“I suppose,” said Holmes, “that when Mr.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_103	lexical	\N	\N	102	{"text": "Windibank came back from France he was very an- noyed at your having gone to the ball.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_104	lexical	\N	\N	103	{"text": "“Oh, well, he was very good about it.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_105	lexical	\N	\N	104	{"text": "He laughed, I remember, and shrugged his shoulders, and said there was no use denying anything to a woman, for she would have her way.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_106	lexical	\N	\N	105	{"text": "“I see.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_107	lexical	\N	\N	106	{"text": "Then at the gasﬁtters’ ball you met, as I understand, a gentleman called Mr. Hosmer Angel.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_108	lexical	\N	\N	107	{"text": "“Yes, sir.", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_109	lexical	\N	\N	108	{"text": "I met him that night, and he called next day to ask if we had got home all safe, and after that we met him—that is to say, Mr. Holmes, I met him twice for walks, but after that father came back again, and Mr. Hosmer Angel could not come to the house any more.”", "section": "section_10", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_110	lexical	\N	\N	109	{"text": "“No?”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_111	lexical	\N	\N	110	{"text": "“Well, you know father didn’t like anything of the sort.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_112	lexical	\N	\N	111	{"text": "He wouldn’t have any visitors if he could help it, and he used to say that a woman should be happy in her own family circle.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_113	lexical	\N	\N	112	{"text": "But then, as I used to say to mother, a woman wants her own circle to begin with, and I had not got mine yet.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_114	lexical	\N	\N	113	{"text": "“But how about Mr. Hosmer Angel?", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_115	lexical	\N	\N	114	{"text": "Did he make no attempt to see you?”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_116	lexical	\N	\N	115	{"text": "“Well, father was going off to France again in a week, and Hosmer wrote and said that it would be safer and better not to see each other until he had gone.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_117	lexical	\N	\N	116	{"text": "We could write in the meantime, and he used to write every day.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_118	lexical	\N	\N	117	{"text": "I took the letters in in the morning, so there was no need for father to know.”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_119	lexical	\N	\N	118	{"text": "“Were you engaged to the gentleman at this time?”", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_120	lexical	\N	\N	119	{"text": "“Oh, yes, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "section_11", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_121	lexical	\N	\N	120	{"text": "We were engaged after the ﬁrst walk that we took.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_122	lexical	\N	\N	121	{"text": "Hosmer—Mr. Angel—was a cashier in an ofﬁce in Leadenhall Street—and—” “What ofﬁce?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_123	lexical	\N	\N	122	{"text": "“That’s the worst of it, Mr. Holmes, I don’t know.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_124	lexical	\N	\N	123	{"text": "“Where did he live, then?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_125	lexical	\N	\N	124	{"text": "“He slept on the premises.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_126	lexical	\N	\N	125	{"text": "“And you don’t know his address?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_127	lexical	\N	\N	126	{"text": "“No—except that it was Leadenhall Street.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_128	lexical	\N	\N	127	{"text": "“Where did you address your letters, then?”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_129	lexical	\N	\N	128	{"text": "“To the Leadenhall Street Post Ofﬁce, to be left till called for.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_130	lexical	\N	\N	129	{"text": "He said that if they were sent to the ofﬁce he would be chaffed by all the other clerks about hav- ing letters from a lady, so I offered to typewrite them, like he did his, but he wouldn’t have that, for he said that when I wrote them they seemed to come from me, but when they were typewritten he always felt that the machine had come between us.", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_131	lexical	\N	\N	130	{"text": "That will just show you how fond he was of me, Mr. Holmes, and the little things that he would think of.”", "section": "section_12", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_132	lexical	\N	\N	131	{"text": "“It was most suggestive,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_133	lexical	\N	\N	132	{"text": "“It has long been an axiom of mine that the little things are inﬁnitely the most important.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_134	lexical	\N	\N	133	{"text": "Can you remember any other little things about Mr. Hosmer Angel?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_136	lexical	\N	\N	135	{"text": "He would rather walk with me in the evening than in the day- light, for he said that he hated to be conspicuous.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_137	lexical	\N	\N	136	{"text": "Very retiring and gentlemanly he was.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_138	lexical	\N	\N	137	{"text": "Even his voice was gentle.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_139	lexical	\N	\N	138	{"text": "He’d had the quinsy and swollen glands when he was young, he told me, and it had left him with a weak throat, and a hesitating, whispering fashion of speech.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_140	lexical	\N	\N	139	{"text": "He was always well dressed, very neat and plain, but his eyes were weak, just as mine are, and he wore tinted glasses against the glare.”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_141	lexical	\N	\N	140	{"text": "“Well, and what happened when Mr. Windibank, your stepfather, returned to France?”", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_142	lexical	\N	\N	141	{"text": "“Mr. Hosmer Angel came to the house again and proposed that we should marry before father came back.", "section": "section_13", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_143	lexical	\N	\N	142	{"text": "He was in dreadful earnest and made me swear, with my hands on the Testament, that whatever hap- pened I would always be true to him.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_144	lexical	\N	\N	143	{"text": "Mother said he was quite right to make me swear, and that it was a sign of his passion.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_145	lexical	\N	\N	144	{"text": "Mother was all in his favour from the ﬁrst and was even fonder of him than I was.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_146	lexical	\N	\N	145	{"text": "Then, when they talked of marrying within the week, I began to ask about father; but they both said never to mind about father, but just to tell him afterwards, and mother said she would make it all right with him.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_147	lexical	\N	\N	146	{"text": "I didn’t quite like that, Mr. Holmes.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_148	lexical	\N	\N	147	{"text": "It seemed funny that I should ask his leave, as he was only a few years older than me; but I didn’t want to do anything on the sly, so I wrote to father at Bordeaux, where the company has its French ofﬁces, but the letter came back to me on the very morning of the wedding.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_149	lexical	\N	\N	148	{"text": "“It missed him, then?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_150	lexical	\N	\N	149	{"text": "“Yes, sir; for he had started to England just before it arrived.”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_151	lexical	\N	\N	150	{"text": "“Ha!", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_152	lexical	\N	\N	151	{"text": "that was unfortunate.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_153	lexical	\N	\N	152	{"text": "Your wedding was arranged, then, for the Friday.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_154	lexical	\N	\N	153	{"text": "Was it to be in church?”", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_155	lexical	\N	\N	154	{"text": "“Yes, sir, but very quietly.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_156	lexical	\N	\N	155	{"text": "It was to be at St.", "section": "section_14", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_157	lexical	\N	\N	156	{"text": "Saviour’s, near King’s Cross, and we were to have breakfast afterwards at the St. Pancras Hotel.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_158	lexical	\N	\N	157	{"text": "Hosmer came for us in a hansom, but as there were two of us he put us both into it and stepped himself into a four-wheeler, which happened to be the only other cab in the street.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_159	lexical	\N	\N	158	{"text": "We got to the church ﬁrst, and when the four-wheeler drove up we waited for him to step out, but he never did, and when the cabman got down from the box and looked there was no one there!", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_160	lexical	\N	\N	159	{"text": "The cabman said that he could not imagine what had be- come of him, for he had seen him get in with his own eyes.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_161	lexical	\N	\N	160	{"text": "That was last Friday, Mr. Holmes, and I have never seen or heard anything since then to throw any light upon what became of him.”", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_162	lexical	\N	\N	161	{"text": "“It seems to me that you have been very shame- fully treated,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_15", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_163	lexical	\N	\N	162	{"text": "“Oh, no, sir!", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_164	lexical	\N	\N	163	{"text": "He was too good and kind to leave me so.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_165	lexical	\N	\N	164	{"text": "Why, all the morning he was saying to me that, whatever happened, I was to be true; and that even if something quite unforeseen occurred to separate us, I was always to remember that I was pledged to him, and that he would claim his pledge sooner or later.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_166	lexical	\N	\N	165	{"text": "It seemed strange talk for a wedding-morning, but what has happened since gives a meaning to it.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_167	lexical	\N	\N	166	{"text": "“Most certainly it does.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_168	lexical	\N	\N	167	{"text": "Your own opinion is, then, that some unforeseen catastrophe has occurred to him?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_169	lexical	\N	\N	168	{"text": "“Yes, sir.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_170	lexical	\N	\N	169	{"text": "I believe that he foresaw some danger, or else he would not have talked so.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_176	lexical	\N	\N	175	{"text": "“She was angry, and said that I was never to speak of the matter again.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_177	lexical	\N	\N	176	{"text": "“And your father?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_178	lexical	\N	\N	177	{"text": "Did you tell him?”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_179	lexical	\N	\N	178	{"text": "“Yes; and he seemed to think, with me, that some- thing had happened, and that I should hear of Hos- mer again.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_180	lexical	\N	\N	179	{"text": "As he said, what interest could anyone have in bringing me to the doors of the church, and then leaving me?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_181	lexical	\N	\N	180	{"text": "Now, if he had borrowed my money, or if he had married me and got my money settled on him, there might be some reason, but Hosmer was very independent about money and never would look at a shilling of mine.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_182	lexical	\N	\N	181	{"text": "And yet, what could have hap- pened?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_183	lexical	\N	\N	182	{"text": "And why could he not write?", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_184	lexical	\N	\N	183	{"text": "Oh, it drives me half-mad to think of it, and I can’t sleep a wink at night.”", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_185	lexical	\N	\N	184	{"text": "She pulled a little handkerchief out of her muff and began to sob heavily into it.", "section": "section_16", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_186	lexical	\N	\N	185	{"text": "“I shall glance into the case for you,” said Holmes, rising, “and I have no doubt that we shall reach some deﬁnite result.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_187	lexical	\N	\N	186	{"text": "Let the weight of the matter rest upon me now, and do not let your mind dwell upon it fur- ther.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_188	lexical	\N	\N	187	{"text": "Above all, try to let Mr. Hosmer Angel vanish from your memory, as he has done from your life.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_189	lexical	\N	\N	188	{"text": "“Then you don’t think I’ll see him again?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_190	lexical	\N	\N	189	{"text": "“I fear not.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_191	lexical	\N	\N	190	{"text": "“Then what has happened to him?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_192	lexical	\N	\N	191	{"text": "“You will leave that question in my hands.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_193	lexical	\N	\N	192	{"text": "I should like an accurate description of him and any letters of his which you can spare.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_194	lexical	\N	\N	193	{"text": "“I advertised for him in last Saturday’s Chronicle,” said she.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_195	lexical	\N	\N	194	{"text": "“Here is the slip and here are four letters from him.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_196	lexical	\N	\N	195	{"text": "“Thank you.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_197	lexical	\N	\N	196	{"text": "And your address?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_198	lexical	\N	\N	197	{"text": "“No.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_199	lexical	\N	\N	198	{"text": "31 Lyon Place, Camberwell.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_200	lexical	\N	\N	199	{"text": "“Mr. Angel’s address you never had, I understand.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_201	lexical	\N	\N	200	{"text": "Where is your father’s place of business?”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_202	lexical	\N	\N	201	{"text": "“He travels for Westhouse & Marbank, the great claret importers of Fenchurch Street.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_203	lexical	\N	\N	202	{"text": "“Thank you.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_204	lexical	\N	\N	203	{"text": "You have made your statement very clearly.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_205	lexical	\N	\N	204	{"text": "You will leave the papers here, and remember the advice which I have given you.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_206	lexical	\N	\N	205	{"text": "Let the whole incident be a sealed book, and do not allow it to affect your life.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_207	lexical	\N	\N	206	{"text": "“You are very kind, Mr. Holmes, but I cannot do that.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_208	lexical	\N	\N	207	{"text": "I shall be true to Hosmer.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_209	lexical	\N	\N	208	{"text": "He shall ﬁnd me ready when he comes back.”", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_210	lexical	\N	\N	209	{"text": "For all the preposterous hat and the vacuous face, there was something noble in the simple faith of our visitor which compelled our respect.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_211	lexical	\N	\N	210	{"text": "She laid her little bundle of papers upon the table and went her way, with a promise to come again whenever she might be summoned.", "section": "section_17", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_212	lexical	\N	\N	211	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes sat silent for a few minutes with his ﬁngertips still pressed together, his legs stretched out in front of him, and his gaze directed upward to the ceiling.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_213	lexical	\N	\N	212	{"text": "Then he took down from the rack the old and oily clay pipe, which was to him as a counsellor, and, having lit it, he leaned back in his chair, with the thick blue cloud-wreaths spinning up from him, and a look of inﬁnite languor in his face.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_214	lexical	\N	\N	213	{"text": "“Quite an interesting study, that maiden,” he ob- served.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_215	lexical	\N	\N	214	{"text": "“I found her more interesting than her little problem, which, by the way, is rather a trite one.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_216	lexical	\N	\N	215	{"text": "You will ﬁnd parallel cases, if you consult my index, in Andover in ’77, and there was something of the sort at The Hague last year.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_217	lexical	\N	\N	216	{"text": "Old as is the idea, however, there were one or two details which were new to me.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_218	lexical	\N	\N	217	{"text": "But the maiden herself was most instructive.”", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_219	lexical	\N	\N	218	{"text": "“You appeared to read a good deal upon her which was quite invisible to me,” I remarked.", "section": "section_18", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_220	lexical	\N	\N	219	{"text": "“Not invisible but unnoticed, Watson.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_221	lexical	\N	\N	220	{"text": "You did not know where to look, and so you missed all that was important.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_222	lexical	\N	\N	221	{"text": "I can never bring you to realise the impor- tance of sleeves, the suggestiveness of thumb-nails, or the great issues that may hang from a boot-lace.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_223	lexical	\N	\N	222	{"text": "Now, what did you gather from that woman’s appearance?", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_224	lexical	\N	\N	223	{"text": "Describe it.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_225	lexical	\N	\N	224	{"text": "“Well, she had a slate-coloured, broad-brimmed straw hat, with a feather of a brickish red.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_226	lexical	\N	\N	225	{"text": "Her jacket was black, with black beads sewn upon it, and a fringe of little black jet ornaments.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_227	lexical	\N	\N	226	{"text": "Her dress was brown, rather darker than coffee colour, with a little purple plush at the neck and sleeves.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_228	lexical	\N	\N	227	{"text": "Her gloves were greyish and were worn through at the right foreﬁnger.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_229	lexical	\N	\N	228	{"text": "Her boots I didn’t observe.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_230	lexical	\N	\N	229	{"text": "She had small round, hang- ing gold earrings, and a general air of being fairly well-to-do in a vulgar, comfortable, easy-going way.”", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_231	lexical	\N	\N	230	{"text": "Sherlock Holmes clapped his hands softly together and chuckled.", "section": "section_19", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_232	lexical	\N	\N	231	{"text": "“’Pon my word, Watson, you are coming along wonderfully.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_233	lexical	\N	\N	232	{"text": "You have really done very well indeed.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_234	lexical	\N	\N	233	{"text": "It is true that you have missed everything of impor- tance, but you have hit upon the method, and you have a quick eye for colour.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_235	lexical	\N	\N	234	{"text": "Never trust to general impressions, my boy, but concentrate yourself upon details.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_236	lexical	\N	\N	235	{"text": "My ﬁrst glance is always at a woman’s sleeve.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_237	lexical	\N	\N	236	{"text": "In a man it is perhaps better ﬁrst to take the knee of the trouser.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_238	lexical	\N	\N	237	{"text": "As you observe, this woman had plush upon her sleeves, which is a most useful material for showing traces.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_239	lexical	\N	\N	238	{"text": "The double line a little above the wrist, where the typewritist presses against the table, was beautifully deﬁned.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_240	lexical	\N	\N	239	{"text": "The sewing-machine, of the hand type, leaves a similar mark, but only on the left arm, and on the side of it farthest from the thumb, instead of being right across the broadest part, as this was.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_241	lexical	\N	\N	240	{"text": "I then glanced at her face, and, observing the dint of a pince-nez at either side of her nose, I ventured a remark upon short sight and typewriting, which seemed to surprise her.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_242	lexical	\N	\N	241	{"text": "“It surprised me.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_243	lexical	\N	\N	242	{"text": "“But, surely, it was obvious.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_244	lexical	\N	\N	243	{"text": "I was then much sur- prised and interested on glancing down to observe that, though the boots which she was wearing were not unlike each other, they were really odd ones; the one having a slightly decorated toe-cap, and the other a plain one.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_245	lexical	\N	\N	244	{"text": "One was buttoned only in the two lower buttons out of ﬁve, and the other at the ﬁrst, third, and ﬁfth.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_246	lexical	\N	\N	245	{"text": "Now, when you see that a young lady, other- wise neatly dressed, has come away from home with odd boots, half-buttoned, it is no great deduction to say that she came away in a hurry.”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_247	lexical	\N	\N	246	{"text": "“And what else?”", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_248	lexical	\N	\N	247	{"text": "I asked, keenly interested, as I always was, by my friend’s incisive reasoning.", "section": "section_20", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_249	lexical	\N	\N	248	{"text": "“I noted, in passing, that she had written a note before leaving home but after being fully dressed.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_250	lexical	\N	\N	249	{"text": "You observed that her right glove was torn at the foreﬁnger, but you did not apparently see that both glove and ﬁnger were stained with violet ink.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_251	lexical	\N	\N	250	{"text": "She had written in a hurry and dipped her pen too deep.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_252	lexical	\N	\N	251	{"text": "It must have been this morning, or the mark would not remain clear upon the ﬁnger.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_253	lexical	\N	\N	252	{"text": "All this is amus- ing, though rather elementary, but I must go back to business, Watson.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_254	lexical	\N	\N	253	{"text": "Would you mind reading me the advertised description of Mr. Hosmer Angel?”", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_255	lexical	\N	\N	254	{"text": "I held the little printed slip to the light.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_256	lexical	\N	\N	255	{"text": "“Missing,” it said, “on the morning of the fourteenth, a gentleman named Hos- mer Angel.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_257	lexical	\N	\N	256	{"text": "About ﬁve ft.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_258	lexical	\N	\N	257	{"text": "seven in.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_259	lexical	\N	\N	258	{"text": "in height; strongly built, sallow complex- ion, black hair, a little bald in the cen- tre, bushy, black side-whiskers and mous- tache; tinted glasses, slight inﬁrmity of speech.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_260	lexical	\N	\N	259	{"text": "Was dressed, when last seen, in black frock-coat faced with silk, black waistcoat, gold Albert chain, and grey Har- ris tweed trousers, with brown gaiters over elastic-sided boots.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_261	lexical	\N	\N	260	{"text": "Known to have been employed in an ofﬁce in Leadenhall Street.", "section": "section_21", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_262	lexical	\N	\N	261	{"text": "Anybody bringing—” “That will do,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_263	lexical	\N	\N	262	{"text": "“As to the letters,” he continued, glancing over them, “they are very com- monplace.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_264	lexical	\N	\N	263	{"text": "Absolutely no clue in them to Mr. Angel, save that he quotes Balzac once.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_265	lexical	\N	\N	264	{"text": "There is one remark- able point, however, which will no doubt strike you.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_266	lexical	\N	\N	265	{"text": "“They are typewritten,” I remarked.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_267	lexical	\N	\N	266	{"text": "“Not only that, but the signature is typewritten.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_268	lexical	\N	\N	267	{"text": "Look at the neat little ‘Hosmer Angel’ at the bottom.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_269	lexical	\N	\N	268	{"text": "There is a date, you see, but no superscription except Leadenhall Street, which is rather vague.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_270	lexical	\N	\N	269	{"text": "The point about the signature is very suggestive—in fact, we may call it conclusive.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_271	lexical	\N	\N	270	{"text": "“Of what?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_272	lexical	\N	\N	271	{"text": "“My dear fellow, is it possible you do not see how strongly it bears upon the case?”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_273	lexical	\N	\N	272	{"text": "“I cannot say that I do unless it were that he wished to be able to deny his signature if an action for breach of promise were instituted.”", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_274	lexical	\N	\N	273	{"text": "“No, that was not the point.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_275	lexical	\N	\N	274	{"text": "However, I shall write two letters, which should settle the matter.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_276	lexical	\N	\N	275	{"text": "One is to a ﬁrm in the City, the other is to the young lady’s stepfather, Mr. Windibank, asking him whether he could meet us here at six o’clock tomorrow evening.", "section": "section_22", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_277	lexical	\N	\N	276	{"text": "It is just as well that we should do business with the male relatives.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_278	lexical	\N	\N	277	{"text": "And now, Doctor, we can do nothing until the answers to those letters come, so we may put our little problem upon the shelf for the interim.”", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_279	lexical	\N	\N	278	{"text": "I had had so many reasons to believe in my friend’s subtle powers of reasoning and extraordinary energy in action that I felt that he must have some solid grounds for the assured and easy demeanour with which he treated the singular mystery which he had been called upon to fathom.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_280	lexical	\N	\N	279	{"text": "Once only had I known him to fail, in the case of the King of Bohemia and of the Irene Adler photograph; but when I looked back to the weird business of the Sign of Four, and the extraordinary circumstances connected with the Study in Scarlet, I felt that it would be a strange tangle indeed which he could not unravel.", "section": "section_23", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_281	lexical	\N	\N	280	{"text": "I left him then, still pufﬁng at his black clay pipe, with the conviction that when I came again on the next evening I would ﬁnd that he held in his hands all the clues which would lead up to the identity of the disappearing bridegroom of Miss Mary Sutherland.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_282	lexical	\N	\N	281	{"text": "A professional case of great gravity was engaging my own attention at the time, and the whole of next day I was busy at the bedside of the sufferer.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_283	lexical	\N	\N	282	{"text": "It was not until close upon six o’clock that I found myself free and was able to spring into a hansom and drive to Baker Street, half afraid that I might be too late to assist at the d ´enouement of the little mystery.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_284	lexical	\N	\N	283	{"text": "I found Sherlock Holmes alone, however, half asleep, with his long, thin form curled up in the recesses of his armchair.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_285	lexical	\N	\N	284	{"text": "A formidable array of bottles and test-tubes, with the pungent cleanly smell of hydrochloric acid, told me that he had spent his day in the chemical work which was so dear to him.", "section": "section_24", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_286	lexical	\N	\N	285	{"text": "“Well, have you solved it?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_287	lexical	\N	\N	286	{"text": "I asked as I entered.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_288	lexical	\N	\N	287	{"text": "“Yes.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_289	lexical	\N	\N	288	{"text": "It was the bisulphate of baryta.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_290	lexical	\N	\N	289	{"text": "“No, no, the mystery!”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_291	lexical	\N	\N	290	{"text": "I cried.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_292	lexical	\N	\N	291	{"text": "“Oh, that!", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_293	lexical	\N	\N	292	{"text": "I thought of the salt that I have been working upon.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_294	lexical	\N	\N	293	{"text": "There was never any mystery in the matter, though, as I said yesterday, some of the details are of interest.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_295	lexical	\N	\N	294	{"text": "The only drawback is that there is no law, I fear, that can touch the scoundrel.”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_296	lexical	\N	\N	295	{"text": "“Who was he, then, and what was his object in deserting Miss Sutherland?”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_297	lexical	\N	\N	296	{"text": "The question was hardly out of my mouth, and Holmes had not yet opened his lips to reply, when we heard a heavy footfall in the passage and a tap at the door.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_298	lexical	\N	\N	297	{"text": "“This is the girl’s stepfather, Mr. James Windibank,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_299	lexical	\N	\N	298	{"text": "“He has written to me to say that he would be here at six.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_300	lexical	\N	\N	299	{"text": "Come in!”", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_301	lexical	\N	\N	300	{"text": "The man who entered was a sturdy, middle-sized fellow, some thirty years of age, clean-shaven, and sallow-skinned, with a bland, insinuating manner, and a pair of wonderfully sharp and penetrating grey eyes.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_302	lexical	\N	\N	301	{"text": "He shot a questioning glance at each of us, placed his shiny top-hat upon the sideboard, and with a slight bow sidled down into the nearest chair.", "section": "section_25", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_303	lexical	\N	\N	302	{"text": "“Good-evening, Mr. James Windibank,” said Holmes.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_304	lexical	\N	\N	303	{"text": "“I think that this typewritten letter is from you, in which you made an appointment with me for six o’clock?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_305	lexical	\N	\N	304	{"text": "“Yes, sir.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_306	lexical	\N	\N	305	{"text": "I am afraid that I am a little late, but I am not quite my own master, you know.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_307	lexical	\N	\N	306	{"text": "I am sorry that Miss Sutherland has troubled you about this little matter, for I think it is far better not to wash linen of the sort in public.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_308	lexical	\N	\N	307	{"text": "It was quite against my wishes that she came, but she is a very excitable, impulsive girl, as you may have noticed, and she is not easily con- trolled when she has made up her mind on a point.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_309	lexical	\N	\N	308	{"text": "Of course, I did not mind you so much, as you are not connected with the ofﬁcial police, but it is not pleasant to have a family misfortune like this noised abroad.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_310	lexical	\N	\N	309	{"text": "Besides, it is a useless expense, for how could you possibly ﬁnd this Hosmer Angel?”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_311	lexical	\N	\N	310	{"text": "“On the contrary,” said Holmes quietly; “I have ev- ery reason to believe that I will succeed in discovering Mr. Hosmer Angel.”", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_312	lexical	\N	\N	311	{"text": "Mr. Windibank gave a violent start and dropped his gloves.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_313	lexical	\N	\N	312	{"text": "“I am delighted to hear it,” he said.", "section": "section_26", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_314	lexical	\N	\N	313	{"text": "“It is a curious thing,” remarked Holmes, “that a typewriter has really quite as much individuality as a man’s handwriting.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_315	lexical	\N	\N	314	{"text": "Unless they are quite new, no two of them write exactly alike.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_316	lexical	\N	\N	315	{"text": "Some letters get more worn than others, and some wear only on one side.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_317	lexical	\N	\N	316	{"text": "Now, you remark in this note of yours, Mr. Windibank, that in every case there is some little slurring over of the ‘e,’ and a slight defect in the tail of the ‘r.’", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_318	lexical	\N	\N	317	{"text": "There are fourteen other characteristics, but those are the more obvious.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_319	lexical	\N	\N	318	{"text": "“We do all our correspondence with this machine at the ofﬁce, and no doubt it is a little worn,” our visitor answered, glancing keenly at Holmes with his bright little eyes.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_320	lexical	\N	\N	319	{"text": "“And now I will show you what is really a very interesting study, Mr. Windibank,” Holmes continued.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_321	lexical	\N	\N	320	{"text": "“I think of writing another little monograph some of these days on the typewriter and its relation to crime.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_322	lexical	\N	\N	321	{"text": "It is a subject to which I have devoted some little attention.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_323	lexical	\N	\N	322	{"text": "I have here four letters which purport to come from the missing man.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_324	lexical	\N	\N	323	{"text": "They are all type- written.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_325	lexical	\N	\N	324	{"text": "In each case, not only are the ‘e’s’ slurred and the ‘r’s’ tailless, but you will observe, if you care to use my magnifying lens, that the fourteen other characteristics to which I have alluded are there as well.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_326	lexical	\N	\N	325	{"text": "Mr. Windibank sprang out of his chair and picked up his hat.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_327	lexical	\N	\N	326	{"text": "“I cannot waste time over this sort of fantastic talk, Mr. Holmes,” he said.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_328	lexical	\N	\N	327	{"text": "“If you can catch the man, catch him, and let me know when you have done it.”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_329	lexical	\N	\N	328	{"text": "“Certainly,” said Holmes, stepping over and turn- ing the key in the door.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_330	lexical	\N	\N	329	{"text": "“I let you know, then, that I have caught him!”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_331	lexical	\N	\N	330	{"text": "“What!", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_332	lexical	\N	\N	331	{"text": "where?”", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_333	lexical	\N	\N	332	{"text": "shouted Mr. Windibank, turning white to his lips and glancing about him like a rat in a trap.", "section": "section_27", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_334	lexical	\N	\N	333	{"text": "“Oh, it won’t do—really it won’t,” said Holmes suavely.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_335	lexical	\N	\N	334	{"text": "“There is no possible getting out of it, Mr.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_336	lexical	\N	\N	335	{"text": "Windibank.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_337	lexical	\N	\N	336	{"text": "It is quite too transparent, and it was a very bad compliment when you said that it was im- possible for me to solve so simple a question.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_338	lexical	\N	\N	337	{"text": "That’s right!", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_339	lexical	\N	\N	338	{"text": "Sit down and let us talk it over.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_340	lexical	\N	\N	339	{"text": "Our visitor collapsed into a chair, with a ghastly face and a glitter of moisture on his brow.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_341	lexical	\N	\N	340	{"text": "“It—it’s not actionable,” he stammered.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_342	lexical	\N	\N	341	{"text": "“I am very much afraid that it is not.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_343	lexical	\N	\N	342	{"text": "But between ourselves, Windibank, it was as cruel and selﬁsh and heartless a trick in a petty way as ever came before me.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_344	lexical	\N	\N	343	{"text": "Now, let me just run over the course of events, and you will contradict me if I go wrong.”", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_345	lexical	\N	\N	344	{"text": "The man sat huddled up in his chair, with his head sunk upon his breast, like one who is utterly crushed.", "section": "section_28", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_346	lexical	\N	\N	345	{"text": "Holmes stuck his feet up on the corner of the mantel- piece and, leaning back with his hands in his pockets, began talking, rather to himself, as it seemed, than to us.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_347	lexical	\N	\N	346	{"text": "“The man married a woman very much older than himself for her money,” said he, “and he enjoyed the use of the money of the daughter as long as she lived with them.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_348	lexical	\N	\N	347	{"text": "It was a considerable sum, for people in their position, and the loss of it would have made a se- rious difference.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_349	lexical	\N	\N	348	{"text": "It was worth an effort to preserve it.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_350	lexical	\N	\N	349	{"text": "The daughter was of a good, amiable disposition, but affectionate and warm-hearted in her ways, so that it was evident that with her fair personal advantages, and her little income, she would not be allowed to remain single long.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_351	lexical	\N	\N	350	{"text": "Now her marriage would mean, of course, the loss of a hundred a year, so what does her stepfather do to prevent it?", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_352	lexical	\N	\N	351	{"text": "He takes the obvious course of keeping her at home and forbidding her to seek the company of people of her own age.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_353	lexical	\N	\N	352	{"text": "But soon he found that that would not answer forever.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_354	lexical	\N	\N	353	{"text": "She became restive, insisted upon her rights, and ﬁnally announced her positive intention of going to a certain ball.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_355	lexical	\N	\N	354	{"text": "What does her clever stepfather do then?", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_356	lexical	\N	\N	355	{"text": "He conceives an idea more creditable to his head than to his heart.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_357	lexical	\N	\N	356	{"text": "With the connivance and assistance of his wife he disguised himself, covered those keen eyes with tinted glasses, masked the face with a moustache and a pair of bushy whiskers, sunk that clear voice into an insinuating whisper, and doubly secure on account of the girl’s short sight, he appears as Mr.", "section": "section_29", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_358	lexical	\N	\N	357	{"text": "Hosmer Angel, and keeps off other lovers by making love himself.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_359	lexical	\N	\N	358	{"text": "“It was only a joke at ﬁrst,” groaned our visitor.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_360	lexical	\N	\N	359	{"text": "“We never thought that she would have been so car- ried away.”", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_361	lexical	\N	\N	360	{"text": "“Very likely not.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_362	lexical	\N	\N	361	{"text": "However that may be, the young lady was very decidedly carried away, and, having quite made up her mind that her stepfather was in France, the suspicion of treachery never for an instant entered her mind.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_363	lexical	\N	\N	362	{"text": "She was ﬂattered by the gentle- man’s attentions, and the effect was increased by the loudly expressed admiration of her mother.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_364	lexical	\N	\N	363	{"text": "Then Mr.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_365	lexical	\N	\N	364	{"text": "Angel began to call, for it was obvious that the matter should be pushed as far as it would go if a real effect were to be produced.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_366	lexical	\N	\N	365	{"text": "There were meetings, and an engagement, which would ﬁnally secure the girl’s affections from turning towards anyone else.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_367	lexical	\N	\N	366	{"text": "But the deception could not be kept up forever.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_368	lexical	\N	\N	367	{"text": "These pre- tended journeys to France were rather cumbrous.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_369	lexical	\N	\N	368	{"text": "The thing to do was clearly to bring the business to an end in such a dramatic manner that it would leave a per- manent impression upon the young lady’s mind and prevent her from looking upon any other suitor for some time to come.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_370	lexical	\N	\N	369	{"text": "Hence those vows of ﬁdelity ex- acted upon a Testament, and hence also the allusions to a possibility of something happening on the very morning of the wedding.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_371	lexical	\N	\N	370	{"text": "James Windibank wished Miss Sutherland to be so bound to Hosmer Angel, and so uncertain as to his fate, that for ten years to come, at any rate, she would not listen to another man.", "section": "section_30", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_372	lexical	\N	\N	371	{"text": "As far as the church door he brought her, and then, as he could go no farther, he conveniently vanished away by the old trick of stepping in at one door of a four-wheeler and out at the other.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_373	lexical	\N	\N	372	{"text": "I think that was the chain of events, Mr. Windibank!”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_374	lexical	\N	\N	373	{"text": "Our visitor had recovered something of his assur- ance while Holmes had been talking, and he rose from his chair now with a cold sneer upon his pale face.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_375	lexical	\N	\N	374	{"text": "“It may be so, or it may not, Mr. Holmes,” said he, “but if you are so very sharp you ought to be sharp enough to know that it is you who are breaking the law now, and not me.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_376	lexical	\N	\N	375	{"text": "I have done nothing action- able from the ﬁrst, but as long as you keep that door locked you lay yourself open to an action for assault and illegal constraint.”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_377	lexical	\N	\N	376	{"text": "“The law cannot, as you say, touch you,” said Holmes, unlocking and throwing open the door, “yet there never was a man who deserved punishment more.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_378	lexical	\N	\N	377	{"text": "If the young lady has a brother or a friend, he ought to lay a whip across your shoulders.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_379	lexical	\N	\N	378	{"text": "By Jove!”", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_380	lexical	\N	\N	379	{"text": "he continued, ﬂushing up at the sight of the bitter sneer upon the man’s face, “it is not part of my duties to my client, but here’s a hunting crop handy, and I think I shall just treat myself to—” He took two swift steps to the whip, but before he could grasp it there was a wild clatter of steps upon the stairs, the heavy hall door banged, and from the window we could see Mr. James Windibank running at the top of his speed down the road.", "section": "section_31", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_381	lexical	\N	\N	380	{"text": "“There’s a cold-blooded scoundrel!”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_382	lexical	\N	\N	381	{"text": "said Holmes, laughing, as he threw himself down into his chair once more.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_383	lexical	\N	\N	382	{"text": "“That fellow will rise from crime to crime until he does something very bad, and ends on a gal- lows.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_384	lexical	\N	\N	383	{"text": "The case has, in some respects, been not entirely devoid of interest.”", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_385	lexical	\N	\N	384	{"text": "“I cannot now entirely see all the steps of your reasoning,” I remarked.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_386	lexical	\N	\N	385	{"text": "“Well, of course it was obvious from the ﬁrst that this Mr. Hosmer Angel must have some strong object for his curious conduct, and it was equally clear that the only man who really proﬁted by the incident, as far as we could see, was the stepfather.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_387	lexical	\N	\N	386	{"text": "Then the fact that the two men were never together, but that the one always appeared when the other was away, was suggestive.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_388	lexical	\N	\N	387	{"text": "So were the tinted spectacles and the curi- ous voice, which both hinted at a disguise, as did the bushy whiskers.", "section": "section_32", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_389	lexical	\N	\N	388	{"text": "My suspicions were all conﬁrmed by his peculiar action in typewriting his signature, which, of course, inferred that his handwriting was so familiar to her that she would recognise even the smallest sample of it.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_390	lexical	\N	\N	389	{"text": "You see all these isolated facts, together with many minor ones, all pointed in the same direction.”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_391	lexical	\N	\N	390	{"text": "“And how did you verify them?”", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_392	lexical	\N	\N	391	{"text": "“Having once spotted my man, it was easy to get corroboration.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_393	lexical	\N	\N	392	{"text": "I knew the ﬁrm for which this man worked.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_394	lexical	\N	\N	393	{"text": "Having taken the printed description, I eliminated everything from it which could be the result of a disguise—the whiskers, the glasses, the voice, and I sent it to the ﬁrm, with a request that they would inform me whether it answered to the description of any of their travellers.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_395	lexical	\N	\N	394	{"text": "I had already noticed the peculiarities of the typewriter, and I wrote to the man himself at his business address asking him if he would come here.", "section": "section_33", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_396	lexical	\N	\N	395	{"text": "As I expected, his reply was typewritten and revealed the same trivial but char- acteristic defects.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_397	lexical	\N	\N	396	{"text": "The same post brought me a letter from Westhouse & Marbank, of Fenchurch Street, to say that the description tallied in every respect with that of their employee, James Windibank.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_398	lexical	\N	\N	397	{"text": "Voil `a tout!”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_399	lexical	\N	\N	398	{"text": "“And Miss Sutherland?”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_400	lexical	\N	\N	399	{"text": "“If I tell her she will not believe me.", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_401	lexical	\N	\N	400	{"text": "You may remember the old Persian saying, ‘There is danger for him who taketh the tiger cub, and danger also for whoso snatches a delusion from a woman.’", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
a-case-of-identity	sentence_402	lexical	\N	\N	401	{"text": "There is as much sense in Haﬁz as in Horace, and as much knowledge of the world.”", "section": "section_34", "entities": []}
