a-case-of-identity	event_1_1	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes speaks about life and fiction	0	{"section": "section_1", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_1", "sentence_2", "sentence_3"], "communicatesContent": "life is infinitely stranger than anything which the mind of man could invent; we would not dare to conceive the things which are really mere commonplaces of existence; if we could fly out of that window hand in hand, hover over this great city, gently remove the roofs, and peep in at the queer things which are going on, the strange coincidences, the plannings, the cross-purposes, the wonderful chains of events, working through generations, and leading to the most outré results, it would make all fiction with its conventionalities and foreseen conclusions most stale and unprofitable."}
a-case-of-identity	event_1_2	event	\N	The speaker answers that he is not convinced	0	{"section": "section_1", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_4"], "communicatesContent": "And yet I am not convinced of it."}
a-case-of-identity	event_1_3	event	\N	The speaker states that cases in papers are bald and vulgar	0	{"section": "section_1", "speakerId": "unknown", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_5", "sentence_6"], "communicatesContent": "The cases which come to light in the papers are, as a rule, bald enough, and vulgar enough; we have in our police reports realism pushed to its extreme limits, and yet the result is, it must be confessed, neither fascinating nor artistic."}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_1	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes remarks that realistic effect requires selection and discretion	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_7"], "communicatesContent": "A certain selection and discretion must be used in producing a realistic effect."}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_2	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes remarks that the police report lacks details and stresses platitudes	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_8"], "communicatesContent": "This is wanting in the police report, where more stress is laid, perhaps, upon the platitudes of the magistrate than upon the details, which to an observer contain the vital essence of the whole matter."}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_3	event	\N	Sherlock Holmes says the commonplace is unnatural	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_9"], "communicatesContent": "Depend upon it, there is nothing so unnatural as the commonplace."}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_4	event	\N	The speaker smiles and shakes his head	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_10"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_5	event	\N	The speaker says he can understand Holmes's thinking	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_11", "sentence_12"], "communicatesContent": "I can quite understand your thinking so."}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_6	event	\N	The speaker says Holmes is brought into contact with strange and bizarre things	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_13"], "communicatesContent": "Of course, in your position of unofficial adviser and helper to everybody who is absolutely puzzled, throughout three continents, you are brought in contact with all that is strange and bizarre."}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_7	event	\N	The speaker picks up the morning paper from the ground and presents it for a practical test	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_14", "sentence_15"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_2_8	event	\N	The speaker identifies the newspaper heading about a husband's cruelty to his wife	1	{"section": "section_2", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_16", "sentence_17"], "communicatesContent": "Here is the first heading upon which I come. 'A husband's cruelty to his wife.' There is half a column of print, but I know without reading it that it is all perfectly familiar to me."}
a-case-of-identity	event_3_1	event	\N	Holmes says the Dundas separation case is an unfortunate example for the argument	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_20", "sentence_21"], "communicatesContent": "Indeed, your example is an unfortunate one for your argument."}
