a-case-of-identity	event_10_4	event	\N	Holmes states that Windibank may have been annoyed when he returned from France	9	{"section": "section_10", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_102", "sentence_103"], "communicatesContent": "I suppose that when Mr. Windibank came back from France he was very annoyed at your having gone to the ball."}
a-case-of-identity	event_3_3	event	\N	Holmes describes the husband, wife, and conduct complained of in the Dundas separation case	2	{"section": "section_3", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_22"], "communicatesContent": "The husband was a teetotaler, there was no other woman, and the conduct complained of was that he had drifted into the habit of winding up every meal by taking out his false teeth and hurling them at his wife, which, you will allow, is not an action likely to occur to the imagination of the average story-teller."}
