a-case-of-identity	event_4_1	event	\N	Holmes mentions a souvenir from the King of Bohemia	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_27"], "communicatesContent": "It is a little souvenir from the King of Bohemia in return for my assistance in the case of the Irene Adler papers."}
a-case-of-identity	event_4_2	event	\N	Holmes mentions a ring from the reigning family of Holland	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_30"], "communicatesContent": "It was from the reigning family of Holland, though the matter in which I served them was of such delicacy that I cannot confide it even to you, who have been good enough to chronicle one or two of my little problems."}
a-case-of-identity	event_4_3	event	\N	Holmes states that he has several matters on hand	3	{"section": "section_4", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_33", "sentence_34", "sentence_35", "sentence_36", "sentence_37", "sentence_38"], "communicatesContent": "Some ten or twelve, but none which present any feature of interest. They are important, you understand, without being interesting. Indeed, I have found that it is usually in unimportant matters that there is a field for the observation, and for the quick analysis of cause and effect which gives the charm to an investigation. The larger crimes are apt to be the simpler, for the bigger the crime the more obvious, as a rule, is the motive. In these cases, save for one rather intricate matter which has been referred to me from Marseilles, there is nothing which presents any features of interest. It is possible, however, that I may have something better before very many minutes are over, for this is one of my clients, or I am much mistaken."}
