a-case-of-identity	event_6_5	event	\N	Holmes laughs and replies that knowing things is his business	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_56", "sentence_57", "sentence_58"], "communicatesContent": "Never mind. It is my business to know things. Perhaps I have trained myself to see what others overlook. If not, why should you come to consult me?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_6_6	event	\N	The woman explains why she came to Holmes and asks him to help find Hosmer Angel	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "large_woman", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_59", "sentence_60", "sentence_61"], "communicatesContent": "I came to you, sir, because I heard of you from Mrs. Etherege, whose husband you found so easy when the police and everyone had given him up for dead. Oh, Mr. Holmes, I wish you would do as much for me. I’m not rich, but still I have a hundred a year in my own right, besides the little that I make by the machine, and I would give it all to know what has become of Mr. Hosmer Angel."}
a-case-of-identity	event_6_7	event	\N	Holmes asks why she came away to consult him in such a hurry	5	{"section": "section_6", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_62", "sentence_63"], "communicatesContent": "Why did you come away to consult me in such a hurry?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_1	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says she bangs out of the house and comes right away to Holmes	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_65", "sentence_66"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, I did bang out of the house, for it made me angry to see the easy way in which Mr. Windibank—that is, my father—took it all. He would not go to the police, and he would not go to you, and so at last, as he would do nothing and kept on saying that there was no harm done, it made me mad, and I just on with my things and came right away to you."}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_2	event	\N	Holmes remarks that Windibank is Mary Sutherland's stepfather	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_67", "sentence_68"], "communicatesContent": "Your father, your stepfather, surely, since the name is different."}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_3	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says Windibank is her stepfather and that she calls him father	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_68", "sentence_69"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, my stepfather. I call him father, though it sounds funny, too, for he is only five years and two months older than myself."}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_4	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Mary Sutherland's mother is alive	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_70"], "communicatesContent": "And your mother is alive?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_5	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says her mother is alive and well	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_71"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, yes, mother is alive and well."}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_6	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says her mother remarried soon after her father's death	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_72"], "communicatesContent": "I wasn’t best pleased, Mr. Holmes, when she married again so soon after father’s death, and a man who was nearly fifteen years younger than herself."}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_7	event	\N	Mary Sutherland describes her father, mother, Mr. Hardy, and Mr. Windibank's role in the business	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_73", "sentence_74"], "communicatesContent": "Father was a plumber in the Tottenham Court Road, and he left a tidy business behind him, which mother carried on with Mr. Hardy, the foreman; but when Mr. Windibank came he made her sell the business, for he was very superior, being a traveller in wines. They got £4700 for the goodwill and interest, which wasn’t near as much as father could have got if he had been alive."}
a-case-of-identity	event_7_8	event	\N	Holmes listens to Mary Sutherland's narrative with concentration	6	{"section": "section_7", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_75"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_8_1	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says her income is separate from the business and was left to her by her uncle	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_77", "sentence_78", "sentence_79", "sentence_80"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, no, sir. It is quite separate and was left me by my uncle Ned in Auckland. It is in New Zealand stock, paying 41/2 per cent. Two thousand five hundred pounds was the amount, but I can only touch the interest."}
a-case-of-identity	event_8_2	event	\N	Holmes remarks that Mary Sutherland interests him extremely	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_81"], "communicatesContent": "You interest me extremely."}
a-case-of-identity	event_8_3	event	\N	Holmes comments on Mary Sutherland's income and travel habits	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_82", "sentence_83"], "communicatesContent": "And since you draw so large a sum as a hundred a year, with what you earn into the bargain, you no doubt travel a little and indulge yourself in every way. I believe that a single lady can get on very nicely upon an income of about £60."}
a-case-of-identity	event_8_4	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says she could live on less and does not wish to be a burden while staying at home	7	{"section": "section_8", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_84", "sentence_85"], "communicatesContent": "I could do with much less than that, Mr. Holmes, but you understand that as long as I live at home I don’t wish to be a burden to them, and so they have the use of the money just while I am staying with them. Of course, that is only just for the time."}
