a-case-of-identity	event_16_1	event	\N	Mary Sutherland says Hosmer was too good and kind to leave her and recalls his wedding-morning warning.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_163", "sentence_164", "sentence_165", "sentence_166"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, no, sir! He was too good and kind to leave me so. Why, all the morning he was saying to me that, whatever happened, I was to be true; and that even if something quite unforeseen occurred to separate us, I was always to remember that I was pledged to him, and that he would claim his pledge sooner or later. It seemed strange talk for a wedding-morning, but what has happened since gives a meaning to it."}
a-case-of-identity	event_16_2	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Mary thinks an unforeseen catastrophe occurred to Hosmer.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_167", "sentence_168"], "communicatesContent": "Your own opinion is, then, that some unforeseen catastrophe has occurred to him?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_16_3	event	\N	Mary says she believes Hosmer foresaw danger and that what he foresaw happened.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "mary_sutherland", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_169", "sentence_170", "sentence_171"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, sir. I believe that he foresaw some danger, or else he would not have talked so. And then I think that what he foresaw happened."}
a-case-of-identity	event_16_4	event	\N	Holmes asks what happened to Hosmer and whether Mary has any notion of it.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_172", "sentence_173"], "communicatesContent": "But you have no notion as to what it could have been?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_16_5	event	\N	Holmes asks how Mary’s mother reacted and Mary says her mother became angry and forbade further discussion.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_174", "sentence_175", "sentence_176"], "communicatesContent": "One more question. How did your mother take the matter?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_16_6	event	\N	Holmes asks whether Mary told her father and Mary says he seemed to think something had happened and that she should hear of Hosmer again.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_177", "sentence_178", "sentence_179", "sentence_180", "sentence_181", "sentence_182", "sentence_183", "sentence_184"], "communicatesContent": "And your father? Did you tell him?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_16_7	event	\N	Mary sobs into her handkerchief.	15	{"section": "section_16", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_185"], "communicatesContent": null}
