a-case-of-identity	event_21_5	event	\N	Holmes asks Watson to read the advertised description of Mr. Hosmer Angel	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_253", "sentence_254"], "communicatesContent": "Would you mind reading me the advertised description of Mr. Hosmer Angel?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_21_6	event	\N	Watson reads the printed slip by the light	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_255"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_21_7	event	\N	The advertised slip describes Hosmer Angel as missing and gives his appearance and employment	20	{"section": "section_21", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_256", "sentence_257", "sentence_258", "sentence_259", "sentence_260", "sentence_261"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_22_1	event	\N	Holmes stops Watson from speaking and continues discussing the letters	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_262", "sentence_263", "sentence_264", "sentence_265"], "communicatesContent": "As to the letters, they are very commonplace. Absolutely no clue in them to Mr. Angel, save that he quotes Balzac once. There is one remarkable point, however, which will no doubt strike you."}
a-case-of-identity	event_22_2	event	\N	Watson remarks that the letters are typewritten	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_266"], "communicatesContent": "They are typewritten."}
a-case-of-identity	event_22_3	event	\N	Holmes points out that the signature is typewritten and makes a suggestion about its significance	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_267", "sentence_268", "sentence_269", "sentence_270"], "communicatesContent": "Not only that, but the signature is typewritten. Look at the neat little 'Hosmer Angel' at the bottom. There is a date, you see, but no superscription except Leadenhall Street, which is rather vague. The point about the signature is very suggestive—in fact, we may call it conclusive."}
a-case-of-identity	event_22_4	event	\N	Watson asks what Holmes means	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_271"], "communicatesContent": "Of what?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_22_5	event	\N	Holmes explains that Watson has not seen how strongly the point bears on the case	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_272", "sentence_273", "sentence_274"], "communicatesContent": "My dear fellow, is it possible you do not see how strongly it bears upon the case? No, that was not the point. However, I shall write two letters, which should settle the matter."}
a-case-of-identity	event_22_6	event	\N	Holmes says he will write two letters to settle the matter	21	{"section": "section_22", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_275", "sentence_276"], "communicatesContent": "I shall write two letters, which should settle the matter. One is to a firm in the City, the other is to the young lady’s stepfather, Mr. Windibank, asking him whether he could meet us here at six o’clock tomorrow evening."}
a-case-of-identity	event_23_1	event	\N	The speaker says business is done with the male relatives.	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_277"], "communicatesContent": "It is just as well that we should do business with the male relatives."}
a-case-of-identity	event_23_2	event	\N	The speaker says nothing can be done until the letters are answered.	22	{"section": "section_23", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_278"], "communicatesContent": "And now, Doctor, we can do nothing until the answers to those letters come, so we may put our little problem upon the shelf for the interim."}
