a-case-of-identity	event_25_1	event	\N	Watson asks Holmes whether he has solved the mystery	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_286", "sentence_287"], "communicatesContent": "Well, have you solved it?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_25_2	event	\N	Holmes answers that he has solved it and identifies the substance as bisulphate of baryta	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_288", "sentence_289"], "communicatesContent": "Yes. It was the bisulphate of baryta."}
a-case-of-identity	event_25_3	event	\N	Watson clarifies that he means the mystery	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_290", "sentence_291"], "communicatesContent": "No, no, the mystery!"}
a-case-of-identity	event_25_4	event	\N	Holmes explains that he was thinking of the salt he had been working upon and says there had never been any mystery	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_292", "sentence_293", "sentence_294", "sentence_295"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, that! I thought of the salt that I have been working upon. There was never any mystery in the matter, though, as I said yesterday, some of the details are of interest. The only drawback is that there is no law, I fear, that can touch the scoundrel."}
a-case-of-identity	event_25_5	event	\N	Watson asks who the man was and what his object was in deserting Miss Sutherland	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "watson", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_296"], "communicatesContent": "Who was he, then, and what was his object in deserting Miss Sutherland?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_25_6	event	\N	Holmes identifies the arriving man as Mr. James Windibank and says he had written to say he would be there at six	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_297", "sentence_298", "sentence_299", "sentence_300"], "communicatesContent": "This is the girl’s stepfather, Mr. James Windibank. He has written to me to say that he would be here at six. Come in!"}
a-case-of-identity	event_25_7	event	\N	Mr. James Windibank enters the room	24	{"section": "section_25", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_297", "sentence_301", "sentence_302"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_26_1	event	\N	Holmes greets Mr. James Windibank	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_303"], "communicatesContent": "Good-evening, Mr. James Windibank."}
a-case-of-identity	event_26_2	event	\N	Holmes refers to a typewritten letter and an appointment for six o’clock	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_304"], "communicatesContent": "I think that this typewritten letter is from you, in which you made an appointment with me for six o’clock?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_26_3	event	\N	Mr. Windibank replies to Holmes	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "mr_james_windibank", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_305", "sentence_306", "sentence_307", "sentence_308", "sentence_309", "sentence_310"], "communicatesContent": "Yes, sir. I am afraid that I am a little late, but I am not quite my own master, you know. I am sorry that Miss Sutherland has troubled you about this little matter, for I think it is far better not to wash linen of the sort in public. It was quite against my wishes that she came, but she is a very excitable, impulsive girl, as you may have noticed, and she is not easily controlled when she has made up her mind on a point. Of course, I did not mind you so much, as you are not connected with the official police, but it is not pleasant to have a family misfortune like this noised abroad. Besides, it is a useless expense, for how could you possibly find this Hosmer Angel?"}
a-case-of-identity	event_26_4	event	\N	Holmes states that he will succeed in discovering Mr. Hosmer Angel	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_311"], "communicatesContent": "On the contrary, I have every reason to believe that I will succeed in discovering Mr. Hosmer Angel."}
a-case-of-identity	event_26_5	event	\N	Mr. Windibank startles and drops his gloves	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_312"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_26_6	event	\N	Mr. Windibank says he is delighted to hear it	25	{"section": "section_26", "speakerId": "mr_james_windibank", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_313"], "communicatesContent": "I am delighted to hear it."}
a-case-of-identity	event_27_1	event	\N	Holmes remarks on typewriter individuality and wear patterns	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_314", "sentence_315", "sentence_316", "sentence_317", "sentence_318"], "communicatesContent": "It is a curious thing that a typewriter has really quite as much individuality as a man’s handwriting. Unless they are quite new, no two of them write exactly alike. Some letters get more worn than others, and some wear only on one side. In every case there is some little slurring over of the ‘e,’ and a slight defect in the tail of the ‘r.’ There are fourteen other characteristics, but those are the more obvious."}
a-case-of-identity	event_27_2	event	\N	Mr. Windibank states that the office correspondence is done on the machine	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "mr_windibank", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_319"], "communicatesContent": "We do all our correspondence with this machine at the office, and no doubt it is a little worn."}
a-case-of-identity	event_27_3	event	\N	Holmes says he will show Mr. Windibank a study of the typewriter and crime	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_320", "sentence_321", "sentence_322"], "communicatesContent": "I will show you what is really a very interesting study, Mr. Windibank. I think of writing another little monograph some of these days on the typewriter and its relation to crime. It is a subject to which I have devoted some little attention."}
a-case-of-identity	event_27_4	event	\N	Holmes presents four letters said to come from the missing man	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_323", "sentence_324", "sentence_325"], "communicatesContent": "I have here four letters which purport to come from the missing man. They are all type-written. In each case, not only are the ‘e’s’ slurred and the ‘r’s’ tailless, but the fourteen other characteristics to which I have alluded are there as well."}
a-case-of-identity	event_27_5	event	\N	Mr. Windibank rises, takes his hat, and dismisses Holmes's talk	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "mr_windibank", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_326", "sentence_327", "sentence_328"], "communicatesContent": "I cannot waste time over this sort of fantastic talk, Mr. Holmes. If you can catch the man, catch him, and let me know when you have done it."}
a-case-of-identity	event_27_6	event	\N	Holmes locks the door and announces that he has caught the man	26	{"section": "section_27", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_329", "sentence_330", "sentence_331", "sentence_332", "sentence_333"], "communicatesContent": "Certainly. I let you know, then, that I have caught him!"}
a-case-of-identity	event_28_1	event	\N	Holmes tells Windibank the situation cannot be escaped and asks him to sit down	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_334", "sentence_335", "sentence_336", "sentence_337", "sentence_338", "sentence_339"], "communicatesContent": "Oh, it won’t do—really it won’t. There is no possible getting out of it, Mr. Windibank. It is quite too transparent, and it was a very bad compliment when you said that it was impossible for me to solve so simple a question. That’s right! Sit down and let us talk it over."}
