a-case-of-identity	event_28_3	event	\N	Windibank says the matter is not actionable	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "mr_james_windibank", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_341"], "communicatesContent": "It—it’s not actionable."}
a-case-of-identity	event_28_4	event	\N	Holmes says he fears the matter is not actionable and condemns the trick	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_342", "sentence_343", "sentence_344"], "communicatesContent": "I am very much afraid that it is not. But between ourselves, Windibank, it was as cruel and selfish and heartless a trick in a petty way as ever came before me. Now, let me just run over the course of events, and you will contradict me if I go wrong."}
a-case-of-identity	event_28_5	event	\N	Windibank sits huddled in his chair with his head sunk	27	{"section": "section_28", "speakerId": null, "sourceNodes": ["sentence_345"], "communicatesContent": null}
a-case-of-identity	event_29_1	event	\N	Holmes speaks about the man's marriage and the daughter's money	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_346", "sentence_347", "sentence_348", "sentence_349"], "communicatesContent": "The man married a woman very much older than himself for her money, and he enjoyed the use of the money of the daughter as long as she lived with them. It was a considerable sum, for people in their position, and the loss of it would have made a serious difference. It was worth an effort to preserve it."}
a-case-of-identity	event_29_2	event	\N	Holmes describes the daughter's character and the effect of her marriage	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_350", "sentence_351"], "communicatesContent": "The daughter was of a good, amiable disposition, but affectionate and warm-hearted in her ways, so that with her fair personal advantages and her little income she would not be allowed to remain single long. Her marriage would mean the loss of a hundred a year, so the stepfather would need to prevent it."}
a-case-of-identity	event_29_3	event	\N	Holmes says the stepfather keeps the daughter at home and forbids her company	28	{"section": "section_29", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_352"], "communicatesContent": "He takes the obvious course of keeping her at home and forbidding her to seek the company of people of her own age."}
