a-case-of-identity	event_31_5	event	\N	Holmes says the law cannot touch Mr. Windibank and that he deserves punishment more than anyone	30	{"section": "section_31", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_377", "sentence_378", "sentence_379", "sentence_380"], "communicatesContent": "The law cannot, as you say, touch you, yet there never was a man who deserved punishment more. If the young lady has a brother or a friend, he ought to lay a whip across your shoulders. By Jove! it is not part of my duties to my client, but here’s a hunting crop handy, and I think I shall just treat myself to—"}
