a-case-of-identity	event_34_4	event	\N	Holmes quotes a Persian saying and comments on Hafiz and Horace	33	{"section": "section_34", "speakerId": "sherlock_holmes", "sourceNodes": ["sentence_401", "sentence_402"], "communicatesContent": "You may remember the old Persian saying, ‘There is danger for him who taketh the tiger cub, and danger also for whoso snatches a delusion from a woman.’ There is as much sense in Hafiz as in Horace, and as much knowledge of the world."}
